              "description": "<p><strong>豁免检定</strong> @Check[fortitude|dc:22]</p>\n<p><strong>最长持续时间</strong> 6 轮</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 1</strong> @Damage[1d8[poison]] 伤害（1 轮）</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 2</strong> @Damage[1d8[poison]] 伤害并获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drain 1}（1 轮）</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 3</strong> @Damage[2d6[poison]] 伤害并获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drain 2}（1 轮）</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> @Check[fortitude|dc:22]</p>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> @Damage[1d8[poison]] damage (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> @Damage[1d8[poison]] damage and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1} (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> @Damage[2d6[poison]] damage and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2} (1 round)</p>"
            },
            "Flare Hood": {
              "name": "耀光兜帽 Flare Hood",
              "description": "<p>帝王眼镜蛇张开其颈部兜帽。每个处于@Template[type:emanation|distance:20]内的非帝王眼镜蛇生物必须尝试一次 @Check[will|dc:22] 意志豁免。随后该生物在1分钟内暂时免疫。</p><hr /><p><strong>大成功</strong> 该生物不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 该生物陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 1}。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 该生物陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 2}。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 该生物陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 3}。</p>\n<p>The emperor cobra flares its hood. Each non–emperor cobra creature within a @Template[type:emanation|distance:20] must attempt a @Check[will|dc:22] save. The creature is then temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 3}.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>这些强大的巨蛇侵扰沼泽与低地。尽管它们体长超过16英尺、体重超过200磅，却能在数秒内攀爬上树。帝王眼镜蛇会通过张开颈罩并向袭击者嘶嘶作声来护阻掠食者。和许多有毒蛇类一样，它们通过用带毒素的咬击强击猎物来狩猎，随后撤退直到受害者死亡，再返回将其整只吞下。</p><hr /><p>在每一种非北极生态系统中，都有某种蛇类繁衍兴盛，各自拥有其特定的狩猎模式与防御机制。</p>\n<p>These powerful serpents infest bogs and lowlands. Despite being over 16 feet long and weighing more than 200 pounds, they can climb trees in seconds. Emperor cobras ward off predators by flaring their hoods and hissing at attackers. Like many venomous snakes, they hunt by striking prey with their poison bite, retreating until their victims die, and then returning to swallow them whole.</p><hr /><p>Snakes of some variety thrive in every non-arctic ecosystem, each with their own particular hunting patterns and defense mechanisms.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "帝王眼镜蛇 Emperor Cobra"
        },
        "Silkwasp Bandit": {
          "name": "绢黄蜂强盗 Silkwasp Bandit",
          "tokenName": "绢蜂强盗 Silkwasp Bandit",
          "items": {
            "Composite Longbow": {
              "name": "复合长弓 Composite Longbow"
            },
            "Greataxe": {
              "name": "巨斧 Greataxe"
            },
            "Hide Armor": {
              "name": "皮甲 Hide Armor",
              "description": "<p>这种护甲由毛皮、结实的皮革，有时还有成型的煮制皮革混合而成。它依靠多层皮革提供防护，但其笨重会减慢穿戴者的速度并降低机动性。</p>\n<p>A mix of furs, sturdy hide, and sometimes molded boiled leather, this armor provides protection due to its layers of leather, though its bulkiness slows the wearer down and decreases mobility.</p>"
            },
            "Arrows": {
              "name": "箭矢 Arrows",
              "description": "<p>这些弹体是弓用的弹药。箭杆由木头制成。它在飞行时由一端的羽翎保持稳定，另一端则装有金属箭头。</p>\n<p>These projectiles are the ammunition for bows. The shaft of an arrow is made of wood. It is stabilized in flight by fletching at one end and bears a metal head on the other.</p>"
            },
            "Explosive Arrow": {
              "name": "爆炸箭 Explosive Arrow",
              "description": "<p><strong>弹药</strong> 任意</p>\n<p><strong>启动</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">A</span>（操作）</p>\n<hr />\n<p>这发弹药涂覆着粗粝的黑色烟灰。启动后，<em>爆炸弹药</em>命中目标时，弹体会在 @Template[burst|distance:10] 内爆炸，对区域内每个生物（包括目标）造成 @Damage[6d6[fire]|options:area-damage] 伤害。每个生物必须进行一次 @Check[reflex|dc:25|basic|options:area-effect] 豁免。</p>\n<p><strong>Ammunition</strong> any</p>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">A</span> (manipulate)</p>\n<hr />\n<p>This piece of ammunition is coated in gritty black soot. When activated <em>explosive ammunition</em> hits a target, the missile explodes in a @Template[burst|distance:10], dealing @Damage[6d6[fire]|options:area-damage] damage to each creature in the area (including the target). Each creature must attempt a @Check[reflex|dc:25|basic|options:area-effect] save.</p>"
            },
            "Attack of Opportunity": {
              "name": "借机攻击 Attack of Opportunity",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.AttackOfOpportunity]</p>"
            },
            "Rage": {
              "name": "狂暴 Rage",
              "description": "<p><strong>需求</strong> 怪物猎人未处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏} 状态，且未在狂暴中</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 怪物猎人获得 9 点临时生命值，持续到狂暴结束。在狂暴期间，其近战攻击造成额外 8 点伤害，速度获得 +10 尺状态加值，并对 AC 承受 -1 减值。怪物猎人不能使用具有“专注”特质的动作，除 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.BlAOM2X92SI6HMtJ]{搜索} 和狂暴动作外。</p>\n<p>狂暴持续 1 分钟，直到没有怪物猎人能够感知到的敌人，或直到怪物猎人陷入昏迷为止。</p>\n<p>一旦狂暴结束，怪物猎人在 1 分钟内不能再次狂暴。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.z3uyCMBddrPK5umr]{效果：狂暴}</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster hunter isn't @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} or raging</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster hunter gains 9 temporary Hit Points that last until the rage ends. While raging, they deal 8 additional damage with melee attacks, gain a +10-foot status bonus to their Speed, and take a -1 penalty to AC. The monster hunter can't use concentrate actions except @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.BlAOM2X92SI6HMtJ]{Seek} and rage actions.</p>\n<p>The rage lasts for 1 minute, until there are no enemies the monster hunter can perceive, or until the monster hunter falls unconscious.</p>\n<p>Once the rage ends, the monster hunter can't again for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.z3uyCMBddrPK5umr]{Effect: Rage}</p>"
            },
            "Sudden Charge": {
              "name": "突袭 Sudden Charge",
              "description": "<p>怪物猎人行走两次并进行一次近战打击。</p>\n<p>The monster hunter Strides twice and makes a melee Strike.</p>"
            },
            "Monster Lore": {
              "name": "怪物学识 Monster Lore"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>有些佣兵避开政治、效忠誓言与臣属关系的种种复杂纠葛，只收钱去狩猎怪物。这是一种直截了当的佣兵差事，往往危险至极，但也可能带来荣耀与名声。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>这是一个宽泛的类别，囊括那些挥舞武器、施展法术，甚至凭借诡计与机敏行事的人；佣兵会将自己与自身专长雇佣给那些付得起金币的人。</p>\n<p>Some mercenaries eschew the complications of politics, oaths of service, and fealty and just get paid to hunt monsters. It's a straightforward form of mercenary service, often dangerous in the extreme, but one that can yield glory and fame.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>A broad category that includes those wielding arms, spells, or even guile and cunning, mercenaries hire themselves and their expertise to those with the gold to pay for it.</p>",
          "blurb": "变体怪物猎人\nvariant monster hunter",
          "prototypeToken": "丝黄蜂强盗 Silkwasp Bandit"
        },
        "Kagekuma": {
          "name": "痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔） Kagekuma",
          "tokenName": "痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔） Kagekuma",
          "items": {
            "Occult Innate Spells": {
              "name": "异能内在法术 Occult Innate Spells"
            },
            "Rewrite Memory": {
              "name": "重写记忆 Rewrite Memory",
              "description": "<p>你通过抹除一段记忆、增强一段记忆的清晰度、改变一段记忆，或添加一段虚假记忆来改动目标的记忆。目标可以尝试一次意志豁免以抗拒该法术。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响，并意识到你试图改变它的记忆。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标不受影响，但会认为你的法术是某种无害的东西而非<em>改写记忆</em>，除非它识别出该法术。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 在该法术持续时间的最初5分钟内，你可以维持该法术以在每轮修改一次记忆。当你这么做时，你构想最多6秒的记忆进行修改，最多可达连续5分钟的记忆。</p>\n<p>只要该法术仍处于生效中，你改变过的任何记忆都会保持改变。如果在这5分钟结束前目标移出射程，你就无法再改变任何后续记忆。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（6环）</strong> 你可以对一个自愿的目标施放该法术，以压制所有关于某个特定主题的记忆，该主题需用不超过50个词详细描述。该效果是永久的，并会用一团模糊不清的迷雾来填补这些缺失。</p>\n<p>You alter the target's memories by erasing a memory, enhancing a memory's clarity, altering a memory, or adding a false memory. The target can attempt a Will save to resist the spell.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and realizes you tried to alter its memory.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected but thinks your spell was something harmless instead of <em>rewrite memory</em>, unless it identifies the spell.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> During the first 5 minutes of the spell's duration, you can Sustain the spell to modify a memory once each round. When you do, you imagine up to 6 seconds of memory to modify, to a maximum of 5 continuous minutes of memory.</p>\n<p>Any memories you've altered remain changed as long as the spell is active. If the target moves out of range before the 5 minutes is up, you can't alter any further memories.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (6th)</strong> You can Cast the Spell on a willing target to suppress all memory of a particular topic, detailed in 50 words or fewer. The effect is permanent, and it patches these omissions with an indistinct haze.</p>"
            },
            "Translocate": {
              "name": "传送 Translocate",
              "description": "<p>你会立刻将自己以及你穿戴和持握的所有物品从你当前的空间传送至射程内一处你能看见的未被占据的空间。若这会让另一名生物随你一同被带走——即使你正将其装在一个异次元容器中携带——该法术会失效。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（5环）</strong> 射程提升至1英里。你不必能看见目的地，只要你过去曾到过那里，并且知道其相对你的位置与距离。随后你在1小时内暂时免疫。</p>\n<p>You instantly transport yourself and any items you're wearing and holding from your current space to an unoccupied space within range you can see. If this would bring another creature with you—even if you're carrying it in an extradimensional container—the spell is lost.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (5th)</strong> The range increases to 1 mile. You don't need to be able to see your destination, as long as you have been there in the past and know its relative location and distance from you. You are then temporarily immune for 1 hour.</p>"
            },
            "Veil of Privacy": {
              "name": "隐私之幕 Veil of Privacy",
              "description": "<p>你建立起防护性的护，使目标难以被魔法侦测到。<em>隐私帷幕</em>在持续时间内尝试反制所有用于针对目标或目标道具的侦测、揭示与探知效果；为此，将戏法视为1环法术。若成功反制一个以区域或多个目标为目标的法术，则仅对<em>隐私帷幕</em>的目标抵消其效果。</p>\n<p>You erect protective wards that make the target difficult to detect via magic. <em>Veil of privacy</em> attempts to counteract all detection, revelation, and scrying effects used against the target or the target's gear throughout the duration, counting cantrips as 1st-rank spells for this purpose. Successfully counteracting a spell that targets an area or multiple targets negates the effects for only <em>veil of privacy's</em> target.</p>"
            },
            "Blur": {
              "name": "朦胧术 Blur",
              "description": "<p>目标的形体看起来模糊不清。它变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{隐蔽}。由于此效果的性质仍然使目标的位置显而易见，目标无法使用此隐蔽来躲藏或潜行。</p>\n<p>The target's form appears blurry. It becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{Concealed}. As the nature of this effect still leaves the target's location obvious, the target can't use this concealment to Hide or Sneak.</p>"
            },
            "Daze": {
              "name": "晕眩术 Daze",
              "description": "<p>你侵入目标的心智，以一道心灵冲击使其陷入晕眩。冲击造成1d6点心灵伤害，进行一次基础意志豁免。若目标豁免大失败，则它还会陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{震慑 1}。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>强化（+2）</strong> 伤害提高1d6。</p>\n<p>You push into the target's mind and daze it with a mental jolt. The jolt deals 1d6 mental damage, with a basic Will save. If the target critically fails the save, it is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 1}.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+2)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p>"
            },
            "Fear": {
              "name": "恐惧术 Fear",
              "description": "<p>你在目标心中种下恐惧；它必须进行一次意志豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 1}。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 目标获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 2}。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 目标获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 3}，并获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.sDPxOjQ9kx2RZE8D]{逃跑}，持续 1 轮。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（3环）</strong> 你最多可以以五个生物为目标。</p>\n<p>You plant fear in the target; it must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 3} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.sDPxOjQ9kx2RZE8D]{Fleeing} for 1 round.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> You can target up to five creatures.</p>"
            },
            "Item Facade": {
              "name": "伪装物件 Item Facade",
              "description": "<p>你使目标物体看起来、摸起来仿佛其物理状况要好得多或差得多。当你施放此法术时，决定你要让该物体看起来破败不堪还是完美无瑕。被伪装成破败的物品看起来处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.6dNUvdb1dhToNDj3]{破损}状态且做工粗劣。完好的物品若被伪装得更好，看起来就像崭新的一样，并且高度抛光或保养良好。一件破损物品看起来仿佛完好且可正常使用。被摧毁的物品不能受此法术影响。与该物品进行交互的生物可以尝试识破该幻觉。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（2环）</strong> 持续时间为24小时。</p>\n<p><strong>升阶（3环）</strong> 持续时间为无限。</p>\n<p>You make the target object look and feel as though it were in much better or worse physical condition. When you cast this spell, decide whether you want to make the object look decrepit or perfect. An item made to look decrepit appears @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.6dNUvdb1dhToNDj3]{Broken} and shoddy. An intact item made to look better appears as though it's brand new and highly polished or well maintained. A Broken item appears to be intact and functional. Destroyed items can't be affected by this spell. A creature that Interacts with the item can attempt to disbelieve the illusion.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (2nd)</strong> The duration is 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> The duration is unlimited.</p>"
            },
            "Message": {
              "name": "传讯术 Message",
              "description": "<p>你轻声地用口型说出词句，但它们并不会从你的口中发出，而是直接传到目标的耳中。其他人听不到你的话语，效果并不会比你平常只做口型更好；但目标能听见你的话语，就仿佛他们正站在你身旁。目标可以以反应动作给出简短回应，或在他们的下个回合以自由动作（）回应（若他们愿意），但他们必须能看见你且在射程内才能这么做。若他们回应，他们的回应也会像原本的传讯术一样，直接传到你的耳中。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（3环）</strong> 该法术的射程增加至500英尺。</p>\n<p>You mouth words quietly, but instead of coming out of your mouth, they're transferred directly to the ears of the target. While others can't hear your words any better than if you normally mouthed them, the target can hear your words as if they were standing next to you. The target can give a brief response as a reaction, or as a free action on their next turn if they wish, but they must be able to see you and be within range to do so. If they respond, their response is delivered directly to your ear, just like the original message.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> The spell's range increases to 500 feet.</p>"
            },
            "Telekinetic Projectile": {
              "name": "念动射弹 Telekinetic Projectile",
              "description": "<p>你将射程内一件松散、无人持用且负载为1或更低的物体掷向目标。对目标进行一次法术攻击掷骰。若命中，你造成2d6钝击、穿刺或挥砍伤害——取决于你掷出的物体。被掷出的物品不具有任何会影响该次攻击或伤害的特征或魔法属性。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 你造成双倍伤害。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 你造成全额伤害。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（+1）</strong> 伤害增加1d6。</p>\n<p>You hurl a loose, unattended object that is within range and that has 1 Bulk or less at the target. Make a spell attack roll against the target. If you hit, you deal 2d6 bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage—as appropriate for the object you hurled. No specific traits or magic properties of the hurled item affect the attack or the damage.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> You deal double damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> You deal full damage.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p>"
            },
            "Broken Kusarigama": {
              "name": "破损的锁镰 Broken Kusarigama",
              "description": "<p>这把令人印象深刻的武器由一段链条将一枚重锤连接到一把镰刀（kama）上组成，便于缴械对手或从远处发起攻击。</p>\n<p>This impressive weapon consists of a weight attached to a kama via a length of chain, which aids with disarming an opponent or attacking from a distance.</p>"
            },
            "Kusarigama": {
              "name": "锁镰 Kusarigama"
            },
            "Bite": {
              "name": "啃咬 Bite"
            },
            "Soul Shred": {
              "name": "灵魂撕裂 Soul Shred",
              "description": "<p>被痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）杀死的生物很难被复活或作为不死被唤起。痂苦魔会自动尝试反制任何复活或将其所杀死的任一生物唤起为不死的尝试（反制调整值 [[/r 1d20+16 #Counteract]]{+16}，反制位阶 4）。如果杀死该生物的痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）被杀死，该生物便可正常地从死亡中被带回或成为不死。</p>\n<p>Creatures killed by a kagekuma are difficult to bring back to life or animate as undead. The kagekuma automatically attempts to counteract any attempt to resurrect or animate as undead any creature that it has killed (counteract modifier [[/r 1d20+16 #Counteract]]{+16}, counteract rank 4). If the kagekuma who slew the creature is slain, the creature can be brought back from death or become undead normally.</p>"
            },
            "Manifest Bundle": {
              "name": "具现捆子 Manifest Bundle",
              "description": "<p><strong>频率</strong> 每小时一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）显现出一大捆稻草、芦苇、绳索、纱线、毛发或类似物品，全部用细绳捆扎在一起并固定在它背上。只要这捆物品仍保持显现，痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）的 AC 提升至 27，但其速度降至 15 尺。</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The kagekuma manifests a large bundle of straw, reeds, rope, yarn, hair, or the like, all lashed together with cords and strapped to its back. The kagekuma's AC increases to 27 as long as its bundle remains manifested, but its Speed is reduced to 15 feet.</p>"
            },
            "Ruin Wielder": {
              "name": "持骸者 Ruin Wielder",
              "description": "<p>当痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）挥舞一把破损的非魔法武器时，它不会承受该武器处于破损状态的任何劣势。当痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）挥舞该武器时，该武器变为一把<em>+1 强击武器</em>，并且在成功命中时额外造成 1d6 心灵伤害。</p>\n<p>When a kagekuma wields a broken, non-magical weapon, they don't take any of the disadvantages of the weapon being broken. While the kagekuma wields it, the weapon becomes a <em>+1 striking weapon</em>, and it deals an additional 1d6 mental damage on a successful hit.</p>"
            },
            "Shadow Bite": {
              "name": "阴影啃咬 Shadow Bite",
              "description": "<p><strong>需求</strong> 痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）正在投下阴影</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）以一个相邻且正在投下阴影的生物为目标，然后它的阴影会吞食该生物的阴影。若痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）拥有显现的捆束，观察者（包括阴影正被啃咬的生物）只有在成功通过一次 @Check[perception|dc:38] 检定后，才能注意到痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）的阴影啃咬。目标必须成功通过一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:26] 豁免，否则变为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1}（大失败时为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2}）。</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kagekuma is casting a shadow</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The kagekuma targets an adjacent creature that's casting a shadow, then its shadow feeds on that creature's shadow. If the kagekuma has a manifested bundle, observers (including the creature whose shadow is being bitten) can notice the kagekuma's Shadow Bite only if they succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:38] check. The target must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:26] save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1} (@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2} on a critical failure).</p>"
            },
            "Shed Bundle": {
              "name": "摘下捆子 Shed Bundle",
              "description": "<p><strong>需求</strong> 痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）拥有一捆已显现的束</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每日一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）使其束消失，行走，然后尝试一次锁镰打击和一次啃咬打击。</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kagekuma has a manifested bundle</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The kagekuma causes its bundle to vanish, Strides, and then attempts a kusarigama Strike and a bite Strike.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）栖身于边缘地带，潜伏在猎物最深的阴影之中。在某些地区，它们被称为“影魔”，而这种灵堕魔能够在拥挤的人群里伪装成毫不起眼的身影，使其即便在有人居住的区域也能进食。痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）外表如同一名佝偻的人形生物，长颈獠口；但当它披着一捆束物时，生物的头与颈会紧紧缩回双肩之间，因而被完全遮蔽。痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）将复杂关系中信任被反复建立又反复破坏的循环具象化。</p>\n<h2>痂苦魔的捆子</h2>\n<p>痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）的捆子不仅仅是伪装与护甲——它更是一个物理性的标记，昭示着它们夺走了多少条性命、吞啜了多少转世的灵魂。无论捆子由稻草、绳索、毛发或其他材料构成，其中一段段独立的长度都象征某种“死神的收割”；捆子里的每一缕都代表着这只灵堕魔斩断并收集的一条隐喻性的生命线——以至于被夺取的无数生命，反过来淹没了这只灵堕魔在世间自身的存在感。</p>\n<p>Kagekumas exist in the periphery, lurking in the very shadows of their prey. Known in some regions as \"shadefiends,\" this nindoru's ability to appear as uninteresting figures in the crowd allows them to feed even in populated areas. A kagekuma appears as a hunched over humanoid with a long neck and a fanged mouth, but when wearing a bundle, the creature's head and neck tuck in tight between its shoulders to become entirely obscured. The kagekuma personifies the cycle of trust being built and broken over and over again through the course of a complex relationship.</p>\n<h2>Kagekuma Bundles</h2>\n<p>A kagekuma's bundle is more than just a disguise and armor—it's a physical indication of how many lives they've cut short and how many souls they've supped upon. Whether the bundle is composed of straw, ropes, hair, or other materials, the individual lengths symbolize a sort of \"reaper's harvest,\" with each strand in the bundle representing a metaphorical lifeline that the nindoru has severed and collected—to an extent that the multitude of lives taken overwhelms the nindoru's own presence in the world.</p>",
          "ac": "27 with bundle",
          "prototypeToken": "痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔） Kagekuma",
          "speed": "or 15 feet with bundle"
        },
        "Shinzo's Gifts": {
          "name": "神藏的赋礼 Shinzo's Gifts",
          "tokenName": "神藏的赋礼 Shinzo's Gifts",
          "items": {
            "Injigo's Loving Embrace": {
              "name": "莓莓的怀抱 Injigo's Loving Embrace",
              "description": "<p>这张@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.T8EopYZLT137CsdW]{网}由络新妇因吉戈编织，她将其作为赋礼送给她的侏儒爱人玛拉，以便在因吉戈外出狩猎远征时，让玛拉在他们的山中小屋里保持安全。<em>莓莓的怀抱</em>如同一张典型的网般运作。你使用这张网进行@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.PMbdMWc2QroouFGD]{擒拿}的运动检定时，获得+1物品加值。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>启动</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> 构想，交互</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每日一次</p>\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 你将网朝30尺内你能看见的一个虚体生物的方向旋转。丝织的力线飞甩而出，抽打着缠绕住该虚体生物；该生物必须尝试一次@Check[reflex|dc:25]豁免骰，以避免在直到你下一回合结束前变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{禁足}。你可以维持此启动至多1分钟，且该生物必须在DC 25检定中成功才能@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.SkZAQRkLLkmBQNB9]{逃脱}这张网。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>启动</strong> 10分钟（构想，交互）</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每周一次</p>\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 你准备入睡时，将网像毯子一样裹在身上。只要你获得8小时的睡眠或等同的休息，你便会梦见给你所爱慕的某人写爱情信：这可以是真实的情人、你感兴趣的对象，或是某个陌生人——你醒来后不会记得其身份。醒来时，你会因那些未寄出的信而充满忧郁之感，但这些情绪会分散你对其他更不愉快念头的注意力，使你在接下来的8小时内获得对心灵伤害的抗力5，并且在对抗心灵效果的豁免骰上获得+1物品加值。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.EeU33F3eBq5OPYp0]{效果：莓莓的怀抱}</p>\n<p>This @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.T8EopYZLT137CsdW]{Net} was woven by the jorogumo Injigo, who presented it as a gift to her gnome sweetheart, Mara, to keep her safe in their mountain cottage when Injigo left on hunting expeditions. <em>Injigo's Loving Embrace</em> functions as a typical net. You gain a +1 item bonus to Athletics checks made to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.PMbdMWc2QroouFGD]{Grapple} with the net.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> envision, Interact</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You spin the net in the direction of an incorporeal creature within 30 feet that you can see. Lines of silken force whip out to lash around the incorporeal creature, who must attempt a @Check[reflex|dc:25] save to avoid becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{Immobilized} until the end of your next turn. You can Sustain this activation for up to 1 minute, and the creature must succeed at a DC 25 check to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.SkZAQRkLLkmBQNB9]{Escape} the net.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> 10 minutes (envision, Interact)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per week</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You wrap the net around you like a blanket as you prepare to sleep. As long as you get 8 hours of sleep or analogous rest, you dream of writing love letters to someone you adore: this could be an actual paramour, someone you're interested in, or someone unknown whose identity you don't recall after waking. When you wake, you're filled with a sense of melancholia about those unsent letters, but these feelings distract you from other, more unpleasant thoughts, granting you resistance 5 to mental damage and a +1 item bonus to saving throws against mental effects for the next 8 hours.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.EeU33F3eBq5OPYp0]{Effect: Injigo's Loving Embrace}</p>"
            },
            "Kinburi's Sandals of Bounding": {
              "name": "金布里的弹跳木屐 Kinburi's Sandals of Bounding",
              "description": "<p>这双高底木屐曾属于一位傲慢的狐妖，名叫金布里。众所周知，她的迅捷与优雅无人能及，旁观者形容她每一步都仿佛在地面之上滑行。她常常挑战他人押注自己的速度，但当人们逐渐变得精明后，她被迫隐藏身份，或承诺若自己落败便没收她的木屐。</p>\n<p>这双木屐使你在进行用于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.2HJ4yuEFY1Cast4h]{High Jump}与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.JUvAvruz7yRQXfz2]{Long Jump}的运动检定时，获得+1物品加值。此外，当你使用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.d5I6018Mci2SWokk]{Leap}动作时，若为水平跳跃，你可以多移动5尺；若为垂直跳跃，你可以多跳高3尺。</p>\n<p><strong>启动</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span>（命令术）</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每小时一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 你高声吹嘘自己的优雅与敏捷，然后以任意组合进行两次High Jump或Long Jump。你不需要先行走，并且在两次跳跃之间，你只需要在进行第二次跳跃前与一个实体物体接触；该物体不必能承受你的重量，甚至也不必连接在地面上——需要时，你可以从一片漂浮的羽毛、一根细枝，甚至一堵纸墙上借力起跳。对于这些跳跃，木屐的物品加值提升至+2。</p>\n<p>These elevated wooden sandals once belonged to a haughty kitsune named Kinburi. It was well known that her swiftness and grace were unmatched, and observers described her as seeming to glide above the earth with each step. She often challenged others to wager on her speed, but as people began to grow wise, she was forced to conceal her identity or promise to forfeit her sandals if she lost.</p>\n<p>These sandals give you a +1 item bonus to Athletics checks to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.2HJ4yuEFY1Cast4h]{High Jump} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.JUvAvruz7yRQXfz2]{Long Jump}. In addition, when you use the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.d5I6018Mci2SWokk]{Leap} action, you can move 5 feet further if jumping horizontally or 3 feet higher if jumping vertically.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (command)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You loudly boast about your grace and agility, then take any combination of two High Jumps or Long Jumps. You do not need to Stride first, and between the two jumps, you need only to come into contact with a physical object before making the second jump; this object doesn't need to be one that can bear your weight, or even be attached to the ground—you can jump off from a floating feather or a thin branch or even off a paper wall as needed. The sandals' item bonus increases to +2 for these jumps.</p>"
            },
            "Vashu's Ninth Life": {
              "name": "瓦修的第九条命 Vashu's Ninth Life",
              "description": "<p>这把<em>+1 强击 幽冥 武士刀</em>由三百多年前，一名名叫瓦修·维加鲁的猫人游荡者从猫王那里偷来的胡须制成。他寻求胡须的魔法，以超自然地延长自己的寿命；而有些人相信他至今仍活着——最终他成功摆脱了这把剑，从而逃过了猫王的怒火。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>启动</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">f</span>（观想）</p>\n<p><strong>触发</strong> 你的回合结束</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每小时一次</p>\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 你将感官延伸至刀刃之中，使你能够对附近的移动作出反应。<em>瓦修的第九条命</em>获得招架特征，并自行抬起至招架姿势，在你下个回合开始前给予你 AC +1 环境加值。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.05mIW5FMX2socBY9]{Effect: Vashu's Ninth Life}</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>启动</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">r</span>（观想）</p>\n<p><strong>触发</strong> 你使用<em>瓦修的第九条命</em>杀死一个活着的生物</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每日一次</p>\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 被杀死生物的一部分生命力沿着刀刃流入你的灵魂，强化你自身的生命。你获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.I0BhPWqYf1bbzEYg]{死硬} 专长的益处，持续 1 分钟。这会使你在濒死（状态）达到濒死 5 时才会死亡，而非濒死 4。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.p0piyFHae9uBfNRa]{Effect: Vashu's Ninth Life (Diehard)}</p>\n<p>This <em>+1 striking ghost touch katana</em> is made from a whisker stolen from the king of cats over three hundred years ago by a catfolk rogue named Vashu Vigaru. He sought the magic of the whisker to preternaturally extend his life, and some believe he still lives, having successfully divested himself of the sword to escape the king's wrath in the end.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">f</span> (envision)</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Your turn ends</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You extend your senses through the blade, allowing you to react to nearby movement. <em>Vashu's Ninth Life</em> gains the parry trait and raises itself into parrying position, granting you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.05mIW5FMX2socBY9]{Effect: Vashu's Ninth Life}</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">r</span> (envision)</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You slay a living creature with <em>Vashu's Ninth Life</em></p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> A portion of the slain creature's life force travels through the blade and into your soul, bolstering your own life. You gain the benefits of the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.I0BhPWqYf1bbzEYg]{Diehard} feat for 1 minute. This causes you to die from the dying condition at dying 5 rather than dying 4.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.p0piyFHae9uBfNRa]{Effect: Vashu's Ninth Life (Diehard)}</p>"
            },
            "Juubun's One Thousand Poems": {
              "name": "重文的千篇诗 Juubun's One Thousand Poems",
              "description": "<p>这份磨损明显的手稿用褪色的淡紫色线侧边装订。其内收录了哲学家清寺重文在很久以前写下的诗篇，蕴含一生的智慧，就极其广泛的主题呈现信息与建议。</p>\n<p><strong>启动</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> 构想（情绪，心灵，法术塑形）</p>\n<p><strong>频率</strong> 每日一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 若你的下一个动作是施放一个具有语言（特征）且以1个生物为目标的法术，你会被重文的魂魄所攫取，使你法术的口述成分变得极具诗意且富有感染力。若目标是盟友，你的话语将激励对方，使其获得10点临时生命值，持续1分钟。若目标生物是敌人且该法术需要进行豁免检定，并且该敌人豁免失败，则其会因绝望与悲伤而获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1}。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.Rn2Nl2iXlRMijTNb]{效果：重文的千篇诗}</p>\n<p>This well-worn manuscript is side stitched with fading lilac-colored thread. It is filled with poems written long ago by a philosopher named Seiji Juubun, which contain a lifetime of wisdom, presenting information and advice on a tremendous breadth of topics.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> envision (emotion, mental, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a Spell that has the linguistic trait and that targets 1 creature, you are overtaken by Juubun's spirit, and the spoken elements of your spell become impactfully poetic. If the target is an ally, your words inspire them and they gain 10 temporary Hit Points, which last for 1 minute. If the targeted creature is an enemy and the spell requires a saving throw, and if the enemy fails its saving throw, they become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1} as a result of despair and sadness.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-effects.Item.Rn2Nl2iXlRMijTNb]{Effect: Juubun's One Thousand Poems}</p>"
            }
          },
          "prototypeToken": "神藏的赋礼 Shinzo's Gifts"
        },
        "Kugaptee's Anger": {
          "name": "苦迦菩提的愤怒 Kugaptee's Anger",
          "tokenName": "苦迦菩提之怒 Kugaptee's Anger",
          "items": {
            "Terrifying Roar": {
              "name": "骇魂咆哮 Terrifying Roar",
              "description": "<p><strong>触发</strong> 一名PC拾起隋镜的心脏</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 一声雷霆般的咆哮在森林中回荡。所有PC必须尝试进行一次 @Check[will|dc:22] 意志豁免。该作祟掷先攻。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 该角色不受影响，并在24小时内暂时免疫骇魂咆哮。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 该角色不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 该角色获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 1（状态）}。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 该角色的惊惧状态值增加2。若这会使该角色的惊惧状态值超过4，则该角色改为获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.sDPxOjQ9kx2RZE8D]{逃跑}，持续至其下一回合结束。</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A PC picks up Sui-Jing's heart</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> A thunderous roar ripples through the forest. All of the PCs must attempt a @Check[will|dc:22] save. The haunt rolls initiative.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The character is unaffected and is temporally immune to Terrifying Roar for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The character is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The character is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The character's frightened condition increases by 2. If this would increase the character's frightened condition value above 4, the character is instead @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.sDPxOjQ9kx2RZE8D]{Fleeing} until the end of their next turn.</p>"
            }
          },
          "disable": "<p>@Check[nature|dc:23] 或 @Check[religion|dc:23] 以进行祷告以对抗邪恶，使苦迦菩提之怒在其例行流程中的动作减少至1（见下文），持续1轮；将穗静的心脏放入她在区域 <strong>A2</strong> 的尸体中，是解除该危害的唯一方法</p>\n<p>@Check[nature|dc:23] or @Check[religion|dc:23] to offer prayers against the evil to reduce Kugaptee's Anger's actions during its routine to 1 (see below) for 1 round; Placing Sui-Jing's heart into her corpse at area <strong>A2</strong> is the only way to disable this hazard</p>",
          "hazarddescription": "<p>树木倾倒的声响与雷鸣般的脚步声充斥空气，仿佛某个巨大的巨人注意到了这里，正缓缓穿过森林逼近。</p>\n<p>The sound of toppling trees and thunderous footsteps fills the air, as if some immense giant had taken notice and now slowly approaches through the forest.</p>",
          "routine": "<p>（2 动作）某个庞然巨物在森林、黑暗与浓雾中踏步前行、却仍在视线之外的声响充斥空气。此作祟的第一个动作是释放一次骇魂咆哮（@Check[will|dc:22]，其效果与上文的骇魂咆哮相同）。第二个动作是将整个思维空间的树木灌注以邪恶生命，使利爪般的枝条抽打向每名PC。这些利爪对每个角色造成 @Damage[4d6[slashing]] 伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:22|basic] 豁免）。站在小径上或空地中的角色在此次豁免检定中获得+1 环境加值，而携带穗静之心的角色在此次豁免检定中获得+4 物品加值。在PC的回合中，他们可以采取进一步动作来保护自己免受爪状枝条的伤害。通过举起盾牌或趴下，PC在其反射豁免检定中获得+2 环境加值。处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{倒地} 状态的PC可以 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.ust1jJSCZQUhBZIz]{寻找掩蔽} 以获得对利爪的强效掩蔽的好处（将其此次反射豁免的环境加值提高至+4）。在其回合中进行翻滚并在一次 @Check[acrobatics|dc:22] 检定中成功的PC，在对抗爪状枝条的反射豁免中获得+2 状态加值。成功通过一次 @Check[stealth|dc:22] 检定来 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.VMozDqMMuK5kpoX4]{潜行} 的PC，将其反射豁免的结果提升一个成功等级。</p>\n<p>如果某名PC在上一轮成功使用自然或宗教来祈祷以抵御邪恶，则苦迦菩提之怒仅有1个动作；随机决定它用此动作释放骇魂咆哮，或以树木抽打。</p>\n<p>(2 actions) The sound of something immense striding just out of sight through the forest, darkness, and fog fills the air. The haunt's first action is to unleash a Terrifying Roar (@Check[will|dc:22] with the same effects as Terrifying Roar above). The second action is to infuse the trees of the entire mindscape with malevolent life, causing clawlike branches to lash out at each PC. These claws inflict @Damage[4d6[slashing]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:22|basic] save) to each character. A character standing on the path or in a clearing gets a +1 circumstance bonus to this saving throw, and the character who carries Sui-Jing's heart gains a +4 item bonus to this saving throw. On a PC's turn, they can take further action to protect themselves from the clawed branches. By Raising a Shield or by Dropping Prone, a PC gains a +2 circumstance bonus to their Reflex saving throw. A @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{Prone} PC can @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.ust1jJSCZQUhBZIz]{Take Cover} to gain the benefits of greater cover against the claws (increasing their circumstance bonus to this Reflex save to +4). A PC who Tumbles Through on their turn and succeeds at a @Check[acrobatics|dc:22] check gains a +2 status bonus to their Reflex saves against the clawed branches. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[stealth|dc:22] check to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.VMozDqMMuK5kpoX4]{Sneak} improves the result of their Reflex save by one degree of success.</p>\n<p>If a PC successfully used Nature or Religion to pray against the evil on the previous round, Kugaptee's Anger has only 1 action; randomly determine if it uses its Terrifying Roar or lashes out with trees with this action.</p>",
          "stealthdetails": "<p>（专家）</p>\n<p>(expert)</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "苦迦菩提之怒 Kugaptee's Anger"
        },
        "Noppera-bo Grunt": {
          "name": "无面鬼士兵 Noppera-bo Grunt",
          "tokenName": "无面鬼士兵 Noppera-bo Grunt",
          "items": {
            "Spear": {
              "name": "矛 Spear"
            },
            "Leather Armor": {
              "name": "皮甲 Leather Armor",
              "description": "<p>由柔软与定型的熟皮混合制成，这种护甲能在提供一定防护的同时保持最大的灵活性。</p>\n<p>A mix of flexible and molded boiled leather, a suit of this type of armor provides some protection with maximum flexibility.</p>"
            },
            "Telepathy 30 feet": {
              "name": "心灵感应 30英尺 Telepathy 30 feet",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Telepathy]</p>"
            },
            "No Face": {
              "name": "无面 No Face",
              "description": "<p>无脸法师没有视觉，但听觉十分敏锐。他们不需要呼吸，并且免疫于那些需要呼吸的效果。他们通过皮肤吸收液体来获得养分——传统上是把双手或无脸的头部浸入液体中，通过渗透作用来“饮用”；他们也能以这种方式从消耗品（如药水或灵药）中获益。</p>\n<p>Noppera-bos have no sense of vision, but their sense of hearing is precise. They don't breathe and are immune to effects that require breathing. They gain sustenance by absorbing fluids through their skin—traditionally by immersing their hands or faceless head into the fluid to \"drink\" through osmosis; they can also benefit from consumables, such as potions or elixirs, in this way.</p>"
            },
            "Sensitive Hearing": {
              "name": "听觉感官 Sensitive Hearing",
              "description": "<p>只要无面鬼处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9PR9y0bi4JPKnHPR]{失聪}，它们就会处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢 1}。</p>\n<p>As long as a noppera-bo is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9PR9y0bi4JPKnHPR]{Deafened}, they are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1}.</p>"
            },
            "Impersonate Shape": {
              "name": "乔装变形 Impersonate Shape",
              "description": "<p>无面鬼士兵会变成其在过去24小时内触碰过的一名小型或中型类人生物的无面版本。变形期间且其面部被覆盖时，该士兵在对该生物进行 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.AJstokjdG6iDjVjE]{乔装} 时获得+2环境加值。无面鬼士兵可以再次使用该能力变回原形。</p>\n<p>The noppera-bo grunt changes into a faceless version of a Small or Medium humanoid they've touched during the last 24 hours. While transformed and their face is covered, the grunt gains a +2 circumstance bonus to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.AJstokjdG6iDjVjE]{Impersonate} that creature. The noppera-bo grunt can change back by using this ability again.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>无面鬼士兵缺乏足够的社交礼仪，因此无法靠另一张人脸把自己彻底伪装起来。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>无面鬼从背后看起来像普通人类，甚至可能长得像你认识的某个人——直到他们转过身，露出一张毫无五官的脸。</p>\n<h2>老练的行家</h2>\n<p>典型的无面鬼残忍无情，并以惊吓或折磨类人生物为乐，但并非所有无面鬼都沉溺于邪恶。中立的无面鬼往往是恶作剧者，利用其能力来欺骗与戏弄；而罕见的善良无面鬼则改以其能力来致敬并崇拜他们所钦佩之人，同时把自己的时间投入到磨练其在艺术或手工制作方面的技能上。</p>\n<h2>无面鬼起源</h2>\n<p>关于无面鬼的起源有许多理论——从变形能力失控的化狸，到被诅咒扭曲的类人生物，再到自然诞生的妖怪。有些人甚至推测，这种状态是一种可传播的诅咒，就像兽化症一样。大多数无面鬼不记得自己的来历，并且往往更感兴趣的是假扮成完全不同的他人。</p>\n<p>Noppera-bo grunts lack the social graces necessary to fully disguise themselves with another person's face.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Noppera-bos appear to be regular humans from behind, and might even resemble someone you know, until they turn to reveal a featureless face.</p>\n<h2>Consummate Professionals</h2>\n<p>While the typical noppera-bo is cruel and revels in the act of frightening or tormenting humanoid creatures, not all of them wallow in evil. Neutral noppera-bos tend to be pranksters who use their abilities to trick and tease, while the rare good noppera- bos instead use their abilities to honor and idolize those they admire while focusing their own time on developing their skills at art or crafting.</p>\n<h2>Noppera-bo Origins</h2>\n<p>There are many theories on the origins of noppera-bos—from tanuki whose change shape ability went wrong, to humanoids who were warped by curses, to naturally spawning yokai. Some even theorize this condition is a transmissible curse like lycanthropy. Most noppera-bos don't recall their origins, and are often more interested in pretending to be someone else entirely.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "无面鬼士兵 Noppera-bo Grunt"
        },
        "Wolf": {
          "name": "狼 Wolf",
          "tokenName": "狼 Wolf",
          "items": {
            "Jaws": {
              "name": "颚 Jaws"
            },
            "Pack Attack": {
              "name": "群体攻击 Pack Attack",
              "description": "<p>狼的打击对至少处于狼的两名盟友触及范围内的生物造成额外1d4伤害。</p>\n<p>The wolf's Strikes deal 1d4 extra damage to creatures within reach of at least two of the wolf's allies.</p>"
            },
            "Knockdown": {
              "name": "击倒 Knockdown",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Knockdown]</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>狼群居并以群体方式狩猎。与大众的普遍看法相反，狼群并非由群体中最强壮的个体领导；它们通常由一对配偶、它们的幼崽，以及来自先前繁殖季的亚成体后代组成。后代一般在成年后离开父母的狼群，随后会寻找自己的配偶，在别处组建新的狼群。</p>\n<p>狼通常不把类人生物视为传统意义上的猎物动物，但在特殊情况下，这些动物也可能会攻击人，尤其是在冬季月份以及其他传统猎物（主要是鹿与麋鹿）稀少的情形下。一些存在，例如强大的吸血鬼，能够召唤狼在战斗中协助它们。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>狼在森林、丘陵及其他荒野地带游荡，在那里它们以群体狩猎，先困扰并包围猎物，再上前完成击杀。和大多数掠食性动物一样，狼更倾向于攻击它们能找到的最虚弱或最易受害的猎物。</p>\n<p>Wolves live and hunt in packs, which, contrary to popular belief, are not led by the strongest in the group, but typically consist of a mated pair, their pups, and juvenile offspring from previous mating seasons. Offspring generally leave their parents' pack upon reaching maturity, at which point they seek out mates of their own to form their own packs elsewhere.</p>\n<p>Humanoids are not traditionally viewed as prey animals by wolves, but extraordinary circumstances can lead these animals to attack people, especially in winter months and other situations where traditional prey (deer and elk mainly) is scarce. Some beings, such as powerful vampires, can call upon wolves to aid them in combat.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Wolves roam forests, hills, and other wild lands, where they hunt in packs to beleaguer and surround their prey before going in for the kill. Like most predatory animals, wolves prefer to attack the weakest or most vulnerable prey they can find.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "狼 Wolf"
        },
        "Heart-Eating Vulture": {
          "name": "食心秃鹫 Heart-Eating Vulture",
          "tokenName": "噬心秃鹫 Heart-Eating Vulture",
          "items": {
            "Beak": {
              "name": "喙 Beak"
            },
            "Talon": {
              "name": "利爪 Talon"
            },
            "Death Burst": {
              "name": "死亡绽放 Death Burst",
              "description": "<p>当食心秃鹫被杀死时，它的躯体在坠地时痉挛抽搐，红光开始从它皮肉的裂口间透出。到该轮结束时，食心秃鹫爆炸成一团由红色灵堕魔蝴蝶组成的@Template[emanation|distance:10]{10-foot radius}爆发，它们刀锋般锋利的翅膀与利爪造成@Damage[5d6[slashing]|options:area-damage]伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:18|basic|options:area-effect]豁免），现场只留下它曾用一只爪子紧攥的那颗心脏。</p>\n<p>When the heart-eating vulture is slain, its body spasms and thrashes as it falls to the ground while red light begins to shine through splits in its flesh. At the end of the round, the heart-eating vulture explodes into a @Template[emanation|distance:10]{10-foot radius} blast of red nindoru butterflies, their razor-sharp wings and claws inflicting @Damage[5d6[slashing]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:18|basic|options:area-effect] save), leaving behind only the heart it clutched in one of its talons.</p>"
            },
            "Carrion Fever": {
              "name": "腐尸热 Carrion Fever",
              "description": "<p>腐尸热导致的恶心（状态）在该苦难持续期间无法降低</p>\n<p><strong>豁免检定</strong> @Check[fortitude|dc:21]</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>潜伏期</strong> 1天</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 1</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1} 和 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}（1天）</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 2</strong> 恶心 1，@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢 1}，以及疲乏（1天）</p>\n<p>The sickened condition from carrion fever can't be reduced while the affliction remains</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> @Check[fortitude|dc:21]</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Onset</strong> 1 day</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> sickened 1, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1}, and fatigued (1 day)</p>"
            },
            "Projectile Vomit": {
              "name": "喷射性呕吐 Projectile Vomit",
              "description": "<p><strong>频率</strong> 每小时一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 巨型秃鹫将上一顿吃下的食物呕吐到10英尺内的一名生物身上。该生物受到 @Damage[3d6[acid]] 伤害，并进行一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:20|basic] 豁免。豁免失败时，该目标还会 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1}。</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The giant vulture vomits up its last meal on a creature within 10 feet. The creature takes @Damage[3d6[acid]] damage with a @Check[fortitude|dc:20|basic] save. On a failed save, the target is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1}.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>秃鹫凭借黑色羽毛与光秃的脖颈，即使在远处也很容易辨认。它们沿着气流滑翔，寻找腐肉作为下一餐。它们常以四五只为一组结成“委员会”，在战场与瘟疫肆虐的城镇上空盘旋，渴望进食。这样的取食循环扮演着重要角色，尤其是在炎热地区：它们格外强效的胃酸能中和食物中的危险细菌，从而将其从环境中清除。</p>\n<p>巨型秃鹫翼展可达25英尺，体重可达600磅。它们比起体型更小的近亲要少见得多，通常生活在能支撑多种巨型动物物种的区域。它们外形骇人，受挑衅时确实危险，但即便是巨型秃鹫本性也并不敌对，更偏好享用他者的猎获。它们更可能在逃跑时吐出上一餐来分散注意力，而不是攻击其他生物。然而，在特别艰难的时期，饥饿的巨型秃鹫群可能会协同合作，把家畜当作食物。</p>\n<p>巨型秃鹫偶尔会与更大的生物（如龙或巨人）形成寄生关系，啄食那些无人看管或被遗忘的一餐残余。以骨骼为工作材料的工匠已开始重视这种行为。把一具生物正确地剥皮剔肉要慢得多，不如让一群秃鹫把尸体啄得只剩骨头，留下干净的骷髅。作为以食物为驱动力的捕食者，用这种方式养大的年幼秃鹫可以被训练得对主人形成印刻，从而带动了把它们当作不寻常宠物饲养的风潮。</p>\n<p>尽管并无魔法本质，秃鹫的爪子传统上被用作护符，用于治疗与祛除疾病；这源自一种古老信念，认为这些猛禽对它们所踏行的污秽免疫。这个信念并不完全正确，但秃鹫确实有若干独特的适应性，能避免常见疾病——这些疾病足以击倒捕食者，甚至其他食腐者。由于体型缘故，尤其是巨型秃鹫的爪子，有时会在其他资源匮乏的地区被用来制作武器。</p>\n<p>Recognizable at a distance by their black feathers and bald necks, vultures drift along air currents looking for carrion to serve as their next meal. Often grouping in committees of four or five, these scavengers wheel above battles and plague-stricken towns, eager to feed. This feeding cycle plays an important role, especially in hot regions, as their particularly potent stomach acid neutralizes dangerous bacteria in their meals and thus removes it from the environment.</p>\n<p>A giant vulture has a wingspan of up to 25 feet across and weighs up to 600 pounds. Less common than their smaller cousins, they typically live in areas that support a number of megafauna species. While imposing and certainly dangerous when provoked, even giant vultures are not hostile by nature, preferring to feast on the kills of others. They are more likely to vomit their last meal as a distraction while they flee than to attack other creatures. However, during particularly lean times, starving groups of giant vultures might work in unison to make a meal of livestock.</p>\n<p>Giant vultures occasionally form parasitic relationships with larger creatures such as dragons or giants, picking at the remains of an unattended or forgotten meal. Crafters who use bones in their work have come to value this type of behavior. Flensing a creature properly is far slower than letting a committee of vultures strip the carcass and leave behind a clean skeleton. As food-motivated predators, younger vultures raised this way can be made to imprint upon owners, leading to a trend of keeping them as unusual pets.</p>\n<p>While not magical in nature, vulture talons are traditionally used as charms in healing and removing disease, stemming from an old belief that the raptors were immune to the filth in which they strode. While this belief isn't strictly true, vultures do have several unique adaptations to avoid common diseases that would take out predators or even other scavengers. Due to their size, giant vulture talons in particular are sometimes used to craft weapons in regions where other resources are scarce.</p>",
          "blurb": "变体巨型秃鹫\nVariant giant vulture",
          "prototypeToken": "食心秃鹫 Heart-Eating Vulture"
        },
        "Sumika": {
          "name": "澄香 Sumika",
          "tokenName": "澄香 Sumika",
          "items": {
            "Composite Shortbow": {
              "name": "复合短弓 Composite Shortbow"
            },
            "Light Mace": {
              "name": "轻型钉头锤 Light Mace"
            },
            "Padded Armor": {
              "name": "软甲 Padded Armor",
              "description": "<p>这种护甲只是一层厚实的绗缝布料，但有时因其非常便宜而被使用。软垫护甲比其他类型的护甲更容易受损并被毁坏。重甲的价格中包含一件软垫护甲内衬，不过当它穿在重甲下面时会失去“舒适”特征。如果你的重甲被毁，或在其他未穿着完整重甲的情况下，你可以只穿那件软垫护甲内衬来睡觉。这样你就能让魔法护甲维持灌注状态，并从与之对应的重甲上的任何符文力量中获益，但没有软垫护甲内衬，其他人无法穿上你的重甲。</p>\n<p>This armor is simply a layer of heavy, quilted cloth, but it is sometimes used because it's so inexpensive. Padded armor is easier to damage and destroy than other types of armor. Heavy armor comes with a padded armor undercoat included in its Price, though it loses the comfort trait when worn under heavy armor. You can wear just that padded armor undercoat to sleep in, if your heavy armor is destroyed, or when otherwise not wearing the full heavy armor. This allows you to keep magic armor invested and benefit from the power of any runes on the associated heavy armor, but no one else can wear your heavy armor without the padded undercoat.</p>"
            },
            "Snare Toolkit (Functions as Artisan's Toolkit)": {
              "name": "陷阱工具包（功能等同于工匠工具包） Snare Toolkit (Functions as Artisan's Toolkit)",
              "description": "<p>你需要这些工具才能用制作技能将原材料制成物品。不同的工作需要不同的套装，由GM决定；例如，铁匠的工具包不同于木匠的工具包。如果你佩戴着你的工匠工具包，你可以将其作为使用它的动作的一部分抽出并收回。</p>\n<p>You need these tools to create items from raw materials with the Craft skill. Different sets are needed for different work, as determined by the GM; for example, a blacksmith's toolkit differs from a woodworker's toolkit. If you wear your artisan's toolkit, you can draw and replace it as part of the action that uses it.</p>"
            },
            "Arrows": {
              "name": "箭矢 Arrows",
              "description": "<p>这些投射物是弓的弹药。箭杆由木头制成。一端的箭羽使其在飞行中保持稳定，另一端则装有金属箭头。</p>\n<p>These projectiles are the ammunition for bows. The shaft of an arrow is made of wood. It is stabilized in flight by fletching at one end and bears a metal head on the other.</p>"
            },
            "Fist": {
              "name": "拳头 Fist"
            },
            "Expert Subsistence": {
              "name": "专家级生存技能 Expert Subsistence",
              "description": "<p>在使用“生存”进行[[/act subsist statistic=survival]]时，若偷猎者掷出任何比成功更差的结果，他们都会得到成功。成功时，他们可以为自己和额外4个生物提供求生所需的生活供给；大成功时，他们可以照料的生物数量是成功时的两倍。</p>\n<p>While using Survival to [[/act subsist statistic=survival]], if the poacher rolls any result worse than a success, they get a success. On a success, they can provide subsistence living for themselves and four additional creatures, and on a critical success, they can take care of twice as many creatures as on a success.</p>"
            },
            "Snare Crafting": {
              "name": "陷阱制作 Snare Crafting",
              "description": "<p>偷猎者知道如何制作以下圈套：</p><ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.AFX1V0Go9DqPWBlN]{警报圈套}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Km4lSOsyrip5q6iD]{妨碍圈套}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.oplQpQSTyTvHDDtq]{标记圈套}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.XcD8p1o71tPohZWT]{信号圈套}</li></ul><p>偷猎者每天最多可以制造四个圈套而无需支付材料费用，并使用3个交互动作来布置一个圈套。该圈套在24小时后会失效。</p>\n<p>The poacher knows how to craft the following snares:</p><ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.AFX1V0Go9DqPWBlN]{Alarm Snare}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Km4lSOsyrip5q6iD]{Hampering Snare}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.oplQpQSTyTvHDDtq]{Marking Snare}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.XcD8p1o71tPohZWT]{Signaling Snare}</li></ul><p>The poacher can create up to four snares each day without paying for the materials, using 3 Interact actions to deploy a snare. The snare becomes inert after 24 hours.</p>"
            },
            "On the Hunt": {
              "name": "狩猎中 On the Hunt",
              "description": "<p>偷猎者将其正在观察或追踪的一个生物指定为其猎物。偷猎者在对该猎物进行[[/act seek]]的察觉检定以及对该猎物进行[[/act track]]的生存检定时，获得+2环境加值。每轮中，偷猎者第一次命中被指定的猎物时，会额外造成1d4精准伤害。这些效果持续到偷猎者再次使用“狩猎中”为止。</p>\n<p>The poacher designates one creature they're observing or tracking as their prey. The poacher gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to [[/act seek]] the prey and to Survival checks to [[/act track]] the prey. The first time the poacher hits the designated prey in a round, they deal an additional 1d4 precision damage. These effects last until the poacher uses On the Hunt again.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>禁止狩猎的规定可能会保护贵族的私人保留地，或在特定季节维护共有森林中动物种群的可持续性。偷猎者违反这些法律——有时出于贪婪，有时出于绝望，有时则为了取乐。</p><hr /><p>探险者通常装备精良、训练有素，能够应对任何类型的危害，并渴望带领他人进入荒野。</p>\n<p>Rules against hunting may insulate the private reserves of nobles or guard the viability of animal populations in shared forests during specific seasons. Poachers violate those laws—sometimes out of greed, sometimes out of desperation, and sometimes for sport.</p><hr /><p>Explorers are often well-equipped and well-trained for any type of hazard and are eager to lead others into the wild.</p>",
          "blurb": "女偷猎者\nfemale Poacher",
          "prototypeToken": "澄香 Sumika"
        },
        "Enko": {
          "name": "恩科 Enko",
          "tokenName": "恩科 Enko",
          "items": {
            "Claw": {
              "name": "爪击 Claw"
            },
            "Head Bowl": {
              "name": "头碗 Head Bowl",
              "description": "<p>河童头顶的凹陷处盛满了水。将河童头顶的水洒出、蒸发或以其他方式全部移除，会使其所有速度降至5尺，直到该水盆再次被水装满为止。陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{Prone}的河童必须在一次@Check[reflex|dc:15]豁免中获得成功，否则会洒出其水；而陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}的河童会自动洒出其水。</p>\n<p>如果河童被擒抱、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.VcDeM8A5oI6VqhbM]{Restrained}或震慑，另一名生物可以花费单动作来尝试从其水盆中洒出水；此动作具有攻击与操作（特征）特征，用以进行一次对抗河童强韧DC的运动检定。成功时，该生物洒出河童的水。</p>\n<p>The depression atop a kappa's head is filled with water. Spilling, evaporating, or otherwise removing all the water from the top of a kappa's head reduces all their Speeds to 5 feet until the basin is again filled with water. A kappa who becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{Prone} must succeed at a @Check[reflex|dc:15] save or spill their water, and a kappa who becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious} automatically spills their water.</p>\n<p>If a kappa is grappled, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.VcDeM8A5oI6VqhbM]{Restrained}, or stunned, another creature can attempt to spill the water from their bowl by spending a single action, which has the attack and manipulate traits, to attempt an Athletics check against the kappa's Fortitude DC. On a success, the creature spills the kappa's water.</p>"
            },
            "Pull Arm": {
              "name": "拉拽手臂 Pull Arm",
              "description": "<p>河童拉拽他们的一只手臂，使那只手臂获得10英尺触及。另一只相对的手臂会缩小，几乎只剩下一只手从他们的龟壳中伸出。河童仍然可以用缩短的手来握持物品，但不能用那只手持用护盾术或武器。河童花费一个单动作来拉拽其相对的手臂，便可让双臂恢复到原本的长度。</p>\n<p>The kappa pulls one of their arms, gaining 10-foot reach with that arm. The opposing arm shrinks to little more than a hand extending from their shell. The kappa can still use their shortened hand to hold things, but they can't use that hand to wield a shield or weapon. By spending a single action to pull their opposing arm, the kappa can return their arms to their original length.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>河童天性顽皮，喜欢对毫无防备的旅人恶作剧。虽然它们通常并非明显恶毒，却也能造成相当大的困扰：从不设防的沐浴者那里偷走衣物，或从营火旁抢走无人看管的食物。河童也乐于在比拼力量的竞赛中证明自己的价值；尽管它们爱耍花招，却以在赛场上讲荣誉、守信用、交谈时保持礼貌而闻名。</p>\n<p>尽管不同地区的河童在体貌上各有差异，但它们全都是两栖的、形似海龟的人形生物：长着喙状口器，手脚有蹼，覆有黏滑的鳞片，颜色从蓝绿色到淡黄色不等。它们常有黑发，围成一圈，以便让头顶中央的凹陷露出来。来自河童栖居的湖泊、溪流或河流的水会填满这处凹陷——也就是它们的头碗——人们相信那是其力量的来源。年幼的河童很容易被哄骗得鞠躬，从而不小心把自己头碗里的水倒空。失去这水会让河童变得倦怠无力；头碗空着的时间越久，它们就越虚弱。对生活在自家水域附近的河童而言，这很少会造成严重危险；但对更爱冒险、远游在外的河童来说，却可能致命。</p>\n<p>河童并非天生敌对；据说它们会与孤独的孩子交朋友，也会通过指路或进行简单的医疗处理来帮助受困的冒险者。尽管如此，许多河童栖居的区域都会张贴告示，警告人们它们的存在，并鼓励靠近水边的旅人丢下一根黄瓜——河童最爱的食物——以换取平安通行。有时这些告示还是河童自己挂出来的，好提高它们收到美味点心的机会。</p>\n<p>Mischievous by nature, kappas delight in playing pranks on unsuspecting travelers. While usually not overtly malicious, they can be a significant nuisance, stealing clothes from unsuspecting bathers or snatching unattended food from campfires. Kappas also enjoy proving their worth in competitions of strength and, despite their propensity for trickery, are known to be honorable competitors who keep their word and remain polite in conversation.</p>\n<p>While kappas vary in physical attributes from region to region, they're all amphibious, turtle-like humanoids with beaked mouths, webbed hands and feet, and slimy scales that range in color from bluish green to pale yellow. They often have black hair, arranged in a ring to accommodate the central depression atop their head. Water from a kappa's home lake, stream, or river fills this depression, or head bowl, which is believed to be the source of their strength. Younger kappas are easily tricked into bowing and accidentally emptying the water from their own head bowls. Losing this water makes a kappa lethargic. The longer a kappa's head bowl remains empty, the weaker they grow. While this rarely poses a serious danger for a kappa living near their home body of water, it can prove fatal to a more adventurous kappa wandering afar.</p>\n<p>Kappas aren't inherently hostile and have been known to befriend lonely children and lend aid to stranded adventurers by providing directions or minor medical treatment. Still, many areas where kappas dwell feature posted signs warning of their presence that encourage travelers venturing near water to toss in a cucumber—kappas' favorite food—in exchange for safe passage. Kappas sometimes put up these signs themselves to increase the likelihood of receiving a tasty treat.</p>",
          "blurb": "雄性河童\nMale Kappa",
          "prototypeToken": "恩科 Enko"
        },
        "Sumika's Thanks": {
          "name": "澄香的感谢 Sumika's Thanks",
          "tokenName": "澄香的感谢 Sumika's Thanks",
          "items": {
            "Additional materials to craft two other common 1st-level snares of the PCs’ choice": {
              "name": "用于制作另外两个由PC自选的常见1级陷阱的额外材料 Additional materials to craft two other common 1st-level snares of the PCs’ choice"
            },
            "Supplies for Spirit Traps": {
              "name": "精魂陷阱的补给品 Supplies for Spirit Traps",
              "description": "<p>精魂陷阱由一张浸过水的网组成，该水中浸泡了圣草，以便更好地对抗魅影。此陷阱的组件在未设置时可作为一张网使用。你将此陷阱设置在一个10尺×10尺的区域内。第一个具有精魂（特征）的生物踏入该区域时，必须尝试一次@Check[fortitude|dc:16] 豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 该生物不受影响</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 该生物获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard}状态，持续1轮。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 该生物获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{禁足}状态，持续1轮。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 该生物陷入禁足，直到它逃脱（DC 16）。</p>\n<p>A spirit trap consists of a net dipped in water that has been steeped with sacred herbs to better combat phantoms. This snare's components function as a net when not set up. You set this snare up in a 10-foot-by-10-foot area. The first creature with the spirit trait that steps into the area must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:16] save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard} for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{Immobilized} for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is immobilized until it Escapes (DC 16).</p>"
            }
          },
          "prototypeToken": "澄香的感谢 Sumika's Thanks"
        },
        "Phantom Boar": {
          "name": "魅影野猪 Phantom Boar",
          "tokenName": "魅影野猪 Phantom Boar",
          "items": {
            "Occult Innate Spells": {
              "name": "异能内在法术 Occult Innate Spells"
            },
            "Daze": {
              "name": "晕眩术 Daze",
              "description": "<p>你使目标的心智变得混乱，并用一次心灵冲击令其眩晕。冲击造成等同于你施法能力调整值的心灵伤害；目标必须尝试一次基础意志豁免。若目标在豁免中大失败，它还会获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{震慑 1}。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>强化（+2）</strong> 伤害增加 1d6。</p>\n<p>You cloud the target's mind and daze it with a mental jolt. The jolt deals mental damage equal to your spellcasting ability modifier; the target must attempt a basic Will save. If the target critically fails the save, it is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 1}.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+2)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p>"
            },
            "Fear": {
              "name": "恐惧 Fear",
              "description": "<p>你向目标心中种下恐惧；它必须尝试一次意志豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 1}。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 目标获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 2}。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 目标获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 3}，并在1轮内获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.sDPxOjQ9kx2RZE8D]{逃跑}。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（3环）</strong> 你最多可以指定五个生物为目标。</p>\n<p>You plant fear in the target; it must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 3} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.sDPxOjQ9kx2RZE8D]{Fleeing} for 1 round.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> You can target up to five creatures.</p>"
            },
            "Ghost Sound": {
              "name": "幻音术 Ghost Sound",
              "description": "<p>你创造一个由简单声音构成的听觉幻象，其最大音量相当于四个普通人同时喊叫。声音从你在射程内指定的一个方格发出。你无法创造可理解的词语或其他复杂的声音（如音乐）。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>高度强化（3环）</strong> 射程增加至60英尺。</p>\n<p><strong>高度强化（5环）</strong> 射程增加至120英尺。</p>\n<p>You create an auditory illusion of simple sounds that has a maximum volume equal to four normal humans shouting. The sounds emanate from a square you designate within range. You can't create intelligible words or other intricate sounds (such as music).</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> The range increases to 60 feet.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (5th)</strong> The range increases to 120 feet.</p>"
            },
            "Tusk": {
              "name": "獠牙 Tusk"
            },
            "Walk the Ethereal Line": {
              "name": "游于两界 Walk the Ethereal Line",
              "description": "<p>魅影行走于灵界与物质位面之间的细微界线之上，以便同时存在于两个位面。</p>\n<p>他们可以再次使用此能力，将自身转回仅存在于灵界。</p>\n<p>The phantom walks the thin line between the Ethereal and Material Planes in order to exist on both planes simultaneously.</p>\n<p>They can shift back to solely the Ethereal Plane by using this ability again.</p>"
            },
            "Susceptible to Death": {
              "name": "易于死亡 Susceptible to Death",
              "description": "<p>尽管魅影并非活物，但它们也不是不死，并且会以独特的方式易受死亡效果的影响。</p>\n<p>若某个魅影的生命值因死亡效果（例如由类似 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Z9OrRXKgAPv6Hn5l]{Execute} 的法术所致）而降至 0，它会立刻被送往灵魂之河，在那里其灵魂将重新踏上通往来世的通常道路。</p>\n<p>Though phantoms aren't alive, neither are they undead, and they are uniquely vulnerable to the effects of death.</p>\n<p>A phantom whose Hit Points are reduced to 0 as a result of a death effect (such as from a spell like @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Z9OrRXKgAPv6Hn5l]{Execute}) is immediately whisked away to the River of Souls, where their soul resumes the usual path to the afterlife.</p>"
            },
            "Vulnerable to Kindness": {
              "name": "友善易伤 Vulnerable to Kindness",
              "description": "<p>魅影能看见并听见的30尺内任何生物，都可以用带有听觉、专注、语言和心灵（特征）的两行动行动向它发出平静且友善的问候。以这种方式向魅影问候的生物必须尝试一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:18]检定。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 魅影受到@Damage[4d8[mental]]伤害，并陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{震慑 1}。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 魅影受到@Damage[2d8[mental]]伤害。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 魅影受到@Damage[1d8[mental]]伤害。</p>\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 魅影不受影响，并在1轮内不再受此弱点影响。</p>\n<p>Any creature within 30 feet that the phantom can see and hear can issue a calm and friendly greeting to it as a two-action activity with the auditory, concentrate, linguistic, and mental traits. A creature greeting the phantom in this manner must attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:18] check.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The phantom takes @Damage[4d8[mental]] damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The phantom takes @Damage[2d8[mental]] damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The phantom takes @Damage[1d8[mental]] damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The phantom is unaffected, and is not affected by this weakness for 1 round.</p>"
            },
            "Boar Charge": {
              "name": "猪突 Boar Charge",
              "description": "<p>魅影野猪行走两次，然后进行一次獠牙打击。只要它移动了至少20英尺，它的攻击掷骰获得+2环境加值。</p>\n<p>The phantom boar Strides twice and then makes a tusk Strike. As long as it moved at least 20 feet, it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to its attack roll.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>根据大多数神学家的说法，转世的灵魂前往来世的典型轨迹相当直接明了。当一个凡人死去时，他们的魂魄会进入灵魂之河，并最终抵达骨园，在那里接受法莱斯玛的审判。被审判的魂魄随后前往其相应的最终安息之地——天堂、地狱、阿巴顿等等——并在那里成为祈求者。</p>\n<p>然而，当一枚排队等待审判的魂魄过早地离开灵魂之河并被转移至灵界时，情况就会变得复杂。无论是由于夜鬼婆之类的险恶闯入者、恶毒的位面魔法，甚至是命运使然，这些魂魄都会从生死的自然秩序中脱离，并在某种炼狱状态中徘徊。与祈求者不同，这些灵界魅影保留着他们死前的生前记忆；而与幽灵等魂魄不同，魅影并未染上不死之身那种污秽的影响——至少起初如此，尽管堕落的威胁始终沉重地笼罩着魅影的存在。有些最终屈服于那样的命运，而另一些则最终重新回到灵魂之河。在那之前，这些游荡的转世的灵魂自成一类——没有真正的家园、议程或目的。</p>\n<p>许多魅影并不想继续停留在这种诡异的炼狱状态中，或是因为他们渴望继续在灵魂之河中的旅程，或是因为他们畏惧不死之身的腐化。为了完成自然的灵性循环并接受审判以继续前往来世，魅影只需设法回到灵魂之河即可。然而，这样的追寻绝非易事——灵界朦胧的雾霭足以让最有经验的旅者也迷失方向，而诸多掠食者在此位面徘徊，寻找离群的转世的灵魂以将其束缚或吞噬。</p>\n<p>The typical trajectory for souls passing to the afterlife is fairly straightforward, according to most theologians. When a mortal dies, their soul enters the River of Souls and eventually reaches the Boneyard, where it is judged by Pharasma. The judged soul moves onto its appropriate domain of final rest-Heaven, Hell, Abaddon, and so forth-where it becomes a petitioner.</p>\n<p>Complications arise, however, when a soul in queue for judgment prematurely departs from the River of Souls and is shunted into the Ethereal Plane. Whether as a result of nefarious interlopers like night hags, malignant planar magic, or even fate, these souls become dislodged from the natural order of life and death and linger in a sort of purgatory. Unlike petitioners, these ethereal phantoms retain memories of their life before death, and unlike spirits such as ghosts, phantoms aren't tinged with the foul influences of undeath-at least, not at first, though the threat of corruption hangs heavy over a phantom's existence. Some eventually succumb to that fate, while others eventually rejoin the River of Souls. Until then, these wandering souls are a kind unto themselves-one without a true home, agenda, or purpose.</p>\n<p>Many phantoms have no desire to remain in their strange state of purgatory, either because they seek to continue their journey through the River of Souls or because they fear the corruption of undeath. In order to complete the natural spiritual cycle and become judged so they can continue to the afterlife, a phantom must simply find a way back into the River of Souls. Such a quest is no easy feat, however-the hazy mists of the Ethereal Plane can befuddle even the most experienced traveler, and numerous predators prowl the realm in search of stray souls to bind or devour.</p>",
          "blurb": "变体魅影\nVariant phantom",
          "prototypeToken": "魅影野猪 Phantom Boar"
        },
        "Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Martial)": {
          "name": "无面鬼模仿者（武技） Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Martial)",
          "tokenName": "无面鬼模仿者（武技） Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Martial)",
          "items": {
            "False Weapon": {
              "name": "虚假武器 False Weapon",
              "description": "<p>无面鬼模仿者携带一把<em>+1 强击</em>武器，其外观与被模仿PC偏好的武器完全相同。若该PC偏好徒手打击，则它看起来像是一副缠手布。若该PC偏好远程武器，则无面鬼模仿者没有近战武器，转而使用上文的远程武器规则；否则，无面鬼模仿者没有远程武器。若PC不偏好任何武器，则无面鬼会挥舞一根木棒作为其虚假武器。该虚假武器仅部分真实，命中时只造成心灵伤害；它不会获得原本武器的任何特征或魔法强化。若无面鬼模仿者的虚假武器破损、被缴械或被放下，它就会消散。无面鬼模仿者可以花费10分钟重新创造一把，以制作一把替代的虚假武器。</p>\n<p>A noppera-bo impersonator carries a <em>+1 striking</em> weapon that looks identical to the favored weapon of the PC being impersonated. If the PC favors unarmed strikes, it appears as hand wraps. If the PC favors a ranged weapon, then the noppera-bo impersonator has no melee weapon and instead uses the ranged weapon rules above; otherwise, the noppera-bo impersonator has no ranged weapon. If the PCs favors no weapon, then the noppera-bo wields a club as its false weapon. This false weapon is only partially real and inflicts only mental damage when it hits; it gains none of the original weapon's traits or magical enhancements. If a noppera-bo impersonator's false weapon is broken, disarmed, or set down, it fades away. The noppera-bo impersonator can craft a replacement false weapon by spending 10 minutes to recreate one.</p>"
            },
            "Telepathy 30 feet": {
              "name": "心灵感应 30 尺 Telepathy 30 feet",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Telepathy]</p>"
            },
            "No Face": {
              "name": "无面 No Face",
              "description": "<p>无面鬼没有视觉，但听觉十分敏锐。它们不需要呼吸，并免疫于需要呼吸的效果。它们通过皮肤吸收液体来获取养分——传统做法是把双手或无面的头浸入液体中，通过渗透作用来“饮用”；它们也能以这种方式从消耗品（如药水或炼金灵药）中获益。</p>\n<p>The noppera-bo has no sense of vision, but their hearing is precise. They don't breathe and are immune to effects that require breathing. They gain sustenance by absorbing fluids through their skin—traditionally by immersing their hands or faceless head into the fluid to \"drink\" through osmosis; they can also benefit from consumables, such as potions or elixirs, in this way.</p>"
            },
            "Sensitive Hearing": {
              "name": "听觉感官 Sensitive Hearing",
              "description": "<p>只要无面鬼处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9PR9y0bi4JPKnHPR]{耳聋} 状态，他们就会 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢 1}。</p>\n<p>As long as the noppera-bo is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9PR9y0bi4JPKnHPR]{Deafened}, they're @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1}.</p>"
            },
            "Impersonated Abilities": {
              "name": "模仿能力 Impersonated Abilities",
              "description": "<p>无面鬼模仿者获得以下能力之一，由你选择。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.kkP0tagXmAYuSH3u]{效果：被模仿的能力}</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>着甲</strong> 无面鬼看起来穿着重甲，并将其AC提高至24。</li>\n<li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.hFtNbo1LKYCoDy2O]{借机攻击}</li>\n<li><strong>持盾者</strong> 无面鬼携带一面次级坚固护盾（若其被摧毁、掉落或无面鬼死亡时，会变成无用的道具），并获得“盾牌格挡”通用专长。</li>\n<li><strong>武器提升</strong> 无面鬼从以下武器特征中选择一项加入其虚假武器：灵巧、致命 d8、强势、格挡、触及、推撞、横扫或绊摔。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The noppera-bo impersonator gains one of the following abilities of your choice.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.kkP0tagXmAYuSH3u]{Effect: Impersonated Ability}</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Armored</strong> The noppera-bo appears to be heavily armored, and they increase their AC to 24.</li>\n<li>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.hFtNbo1LKYCoDy2O]{Attack of Opportunity}</li>\n<li><strong>Shield Carrier</strong> The noppera-bo carries a minor sturdy shield (that transforms into a useless prop if it's destroyed, dropped, or upon the noppera-bo's death), and they gain the Shield Block general feat.</li>\n<li><strong>Weapon Perk</strong> The noppera-bo chooses one of these weapon traits to add to their false weapon: agile, deadly d8, forceful, parry, reach, shove, sweep, or trip.</li>\n</ul>"
            }
          },
          "prototypeToken": "无面鬼模仿者（武艺） Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Martial)"
        },
