        "Injured Kappa": {
          "name": "受伤的河童 Injured Kappa",
          "tokenName": "受伤的河童 Injured Kappa",
          "items": {
            "Claw": {
              "name": "爪击 Claw"
            },
            "Head Bowl": {
              "name": "头碗 Head Bowl",
              "description": "<p>河童头顶的凹陷处盛满了水。将河童头顶的水泼洒出去、使其蒸发，或以其他方式移除全部水后，河童的所有速度都降至5尺，直到水盆再次被水填满为止。河童陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{倒地}时，必须在一次@Check[reflex|dc:15]豁免中成功，否则会洒出头顶的水；而陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}的河童会自动洒出头顶的水。</p>\n<p>如果河童被擒抱、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.VcDeM8A5oI6VqhbM]{束缚}或震慑，另一名生物可以花费单动作来尝试把水从其水盆中洒出；该动作具有攻击与操作（特征）特征，进行一次运动检定，对抗河童的强韧DC。成功时，该生物洒出了河童的水。</p>\n<p>The depression atop a kappa's head is filled with water. Spilling, evaporating, or otherwise removing all the water from the top of a kappa's head reduces all their Speeds to 5 feet until the basin is again filled with water. A kappa who becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{Prone} must succeed at a @Check[reflex|dc:15] save or spill their water, and a kappa who becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious} automatically spills their water.</p>\n<p>If a kappa is grappled, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.VcDeM8A5oI6VqhbM]{Restrained}, or stunned, another creature can attempt to spill the water from their bowl by spending a single action, which has the attack and manipulate traits, to attempt an Athletics check against the kappa's Fortitude DC. On a success, the creature spills the kappa's water.</p>"
            },
            "Pull Arm": {
              "name": "拉拽手臂 Pull Arm",
              "description": "<p>河童拉拽自己的一只手臂，使那只手臂获得10尺触及。对侧手臂会缩小到几乎只剩一只手从其甲壳中伸出。河童仍可用缩短的手拿取物品，但不能用那只手持用护盾术或武器。河童可以花费一个单动作拉拽对侧手臂，使双臂恢复原本长度。</p>\n<p>The kappa pulls one of their arms, gaining 10-foot reach with that arm. The opposing arm shrinks to little more than a hand extending from their shell. The kappa can still use their shortened hand to hold things, but they can't use that hand to wield a shield or weapon. By spending a single action to pull their opposing arm, the kappa can return their arms to their original length.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>河童天性顽皮，最爱对毫无戒心的旅人恶作剧。虽然通常并非公然怀有恶意，但它们也会造成不小的麻烦：从不知情的洗浴者那里偷走衣物，或从营火旁抢走无人看守的食物。河童也喜欢在力气比拼中证明自身价值；尽管它们爱耍花招，却以讲信用、比赛时守礼并在交谈中保持礼貌而闻名。</p>\n<p>河童的外貌会因地区而异，但它们全都是两栖的、形似乌龟的人形生物：有喙状的嘴、带蹼的手脚，以及黏滑的鳞片，颜色从蓝绿色到淡黄色不等。它们常有黑色头发，围成一圈，以便让头顶中央的凹陷露出来。来自河童栖身的湖泊、溪流或河流的水会灌满这个凹陷——也就是它们的头碗——而人们相信这正是它们力量的来源。年轻的河童很容易被骗得鞠躬，从而不小心把自己头碗里的水倒空。失去这水会让河童变得萎靡不振；头碗空着的时间越久，它们就越虚弱。对生活在栖身水域附近的河童来说，这很少会构成严重危险，但对那些更爱冒险、远离家乡四处游荡的河童而言，却可能致命。</p>\n<p>河童并非天生敌对；人们也知道它们会与孤独的孩子交朋友，并通过指路或进行些许医疗处理来帮助受困的冒险者。不过，许多河童出没的区域都会张贴告示，警告它们的存在，并鼓励靠近水边的旅人丢下一根黄瓜——河童最爱的食物——以换取平安通行。有时这些告示还是河童自己挂的，为的是提高自己收到美味点心的概率。</p>\n<p>Mischievous by nature, kappas delight in playing pranks on unsuspecting travelers. While usually not overtly malicious, they can be a significant nuisance, stealing clothes from unsuspecting bathers or snatching unattended food from campfires. Kappas also enjoy proving their worth in competitions of strength and, despite their propensity for trickery, are known to be honorable competitors who keep their word and remain polite in conversation.</p>\n<p>While kappas vary in physical attributes from region to region, they're all amphibious, turtle-like humanoids with beaked mouths, webbed hands and feet, and slimy scales that range in color from bluish green to pale yellow. They often have black hair, arranged in a ring to accommodate the central depression atop their head. Water from a kappa's home lake, stream, or river fills this depression, or head bowl, which is believed to be the source of their strength. Younger kappas are easily tricked into bowing and accidentally emptying the water from their own head bowls. Losing this water makes a kappa lethargic. The longer a kappa's head bowl remains empty, the weaker they grow. While this rarely poses a serious danger for a kappa living near their home body of water, it can prove fatal to a more adventurous kappa wandering afar.</p>\n<p>Kappas aren't inherently hostile and have been known to befriend lonely children and lend aid to stranded adventurers by providing directions or minor medical treatment. Still, many areas where kappas dwell feature posted signs warning of their presence that encourage travelers venturing near water to toss in a cucumber—kappas' favorite food—in exchange for safe passage. Kappas sometimes put up these signs themselves to increase the likelihood of receiving a tasty treat.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "受伤的河童 Injured Kappa"
        },
