            "Anathematic Reprisal": {
              "name": "破戒处罚 Anathematic Reprisal",
              "description": "<p><strong>触发</strong> 一名生物执行了对你神祇而言属禁忌的行为。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>你惩罚一名违背你神祇的生物，借由目睹他人犯下你神祇的禁忌时你所感到的痛苦来汲取力量。只有当某名生物主动犯下一项独特的禁忌行为时，你才能施放此法术。例如，若制造不死对你的神祇而言属于禁忌，你可以对一名刚在你面前制造了不死的死灵法师使用破戒处罚，但不能仅因某个不死生物的存在就对其使用。你对目标造成4d6点心灵伤害，但一次基础意志豁免可以减少此伤害。若其豁免失败，它还会获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}，持续1轮。随后该生物在1分钟内暂时免疫。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（+1）</strong> 伤害增加1d6。</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature performs an act anathema to your deity.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You punish a creature that transgresses against your deity, drawing upon the anguish you feel upon seeing one of your deity's anathema committed. You can cast this spell only when a creature actively commits a unique act of anathema. For example, if creating undead were anathema to your deity, you could use anathematic reprisal on a necromancer who had just created undead in front of you, but not on an undead creature just for existing. You deal 4d6 mental damage to the target, but a basic Will save can reduce this damage. If it fails, it is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 round. The creature is then temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p>"
            },
            "Crisis of Faith": {
              "name": "信念崩塌 Crisis of Faith",
              "description": "<p>你攻击目标的信仰，以疑虑与心灵动荡折磨该生物，造成6d6心灵伤害；若其能施放神圣法术，则改为造成6d8心灵伤害。其效果由其意志豁免决定。</p>\n<p>对许多神祇而言，若你在没有充分理由的情况下对你自身神祇的追随者施放此法术，即为禁忌。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标承受一半伤害。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 目标承受全部伤害；若目标能施放神圣法术，则其获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}，持续1轮。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 目标承受双倍伤害，获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}，持续1轮，且1轮内无法施放神圣法术。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（+1）</strong> 伤害增加2d6（若目标为神圣施法者，则改为增加2d8）。</p>\n<p>You assault the target's faith, riddling the creature with doubt and mental turmoil that deal 6d6 mental damage, or 6d8 mental damage if it can cast divine spells. The effects are determined by its Will save.</p>\n<p>To many deities, casting this spell on a follower of your own deity without significant cause is anathema.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full damage; if the target can cast divine spells, it's @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double damage, is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 round, and can't cast divine spells for 1 round.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 2d6 (or by 2d8 if the target is a divine spellcaster).</p>"
            },
            "Fangs": {
              "name": "尖牙 Fangs"
