            "Blinding Spittle": {
              "name": "致盲唾液 Blinding Spittle",
              "description": "<p>被双头蛇的喷吐打击重击的生物会@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.XgEqL1kFApUbl5Z2]{目盲}1轮。</p>\n<p>A creature critically hit by an amphisbaena's spit Strike is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.XgEqL1kFApUbl5Z2]{Blinded} for 1 round.</p>"
            },
            "Twin Bites": {
              "name": "双重撕咬 Twin Bites",
              "description": "<p>一条双头蛇用它每个头各进行一次獠牙打击，每次分别针对不同的目标。两次打击都计入它的多重攻击减值，但在它完成两次攻击之后减值才会提高。</p>\n<p>An amphisbaena makes a fangs Strike with each of its heads, each against a different target. Both Strikes count toward its multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after it has made both attacks.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>双头蛇是一种极其好斗、带有毒性的蝰蛇，体型惊人，身体两端各长着一颗头。它的移动方式与更常见的侧行蛇相似：将身体向前抛成一个环并向前推进，同时始终让其中一颗头贴地，以此固定自身。</p>\n<p>双头蛇的典型猎物包括兔子、狐狸、各类鸟、小型鹿，若有机会甚至也会捕食类人。它们天性领地意识极强，几乎会攻击任何靠近巢穴的东西，不论入侵者体型大小。许多孩子都被告诫不要独自深入森林太远，以免游荡得离双头蛇的巢穴太近，成了这生物的下一顿饭。</p>\n<p>双头蛇的毒液效力惊人，若不治疗，甚至能在数分钟内放倒一个强壮的矮人。然而，这种毒液也可用于多种治疗药方，因此若能采集到便是极有价值的商品。例如，可能会建议孕妇少量、稀释后饮用毒液，以帮助保障妊娠。将少量毒液与各种草药和油混合可制成敷剂，用于减轻酸痛。正因如此，双头蛇的形象常出现在许多与治疗和炼金主题相关的场合，比如酊剂的标签、草药师记录中的注释，以及医学教科书里的插图。</p>\n<p>据说第一条双头蛇是由美杜莎的头颅被斩下时滴落的血形成的。这个故事的起源很可能源于这样一个事实：双头蛇对石化有着异乎寻常的免疫力，因此有时会被美杜莎当作宠物饲养。饲养双头蛇为宠物的美杜莎，可能会将这条蝰蛇视为自己最珍贵的伴侣，甚至当作自己的孩子。尽管有这些传说中的超自然起源，也偶尔会受到特殊对待，但双头蛇完全是寻常的动物，只有粗浅的智能，并且完全没有任何与生俱来的魔法能力。</p>\n<p>An amphisbaena is an exceedingly aggressive, venomous viper of remarkable size that bears two heads-one on each end of its body. It moves in a manner similar to that of the more common sidewinder snake, throwing its body forward in a loop and anchoring itself by keeping one head or the other on the ground at all times.</p>\n<p>Amphisbaenas' typical prey includes rabbits, foxes, various birds, small deer, and even humanoids if presented the opportunity. Fiercely territorial by nature, they attack just about anything that gets near their lairs, regardless of the intruder's size. Many a child has been warned about going too far into the woods alone, lest they wander too close to an amphisbaena den and become the creature's next meal.</p>\n<p>The venom of an amphisbaena is incredibly potent, able to take down a stout dwarf within minutes if left untreated. However, it also has uses in a variety of healing remedies, which makes it a valuable commodity if collected. For example, a pregnant person might be advised to drink the venom in small, dilute doses to help safeguard the pregnancy. Mixing small amounts of the venom with various herbs and oil creates a poultice which dulls aches and pains. As a result, the image of an amphisbaena appears in many contexts associated with healing and alchemical subjects, such as labels for tinctures, annotations in herbalists' records, and illustrations in textbooks of medicine.</p>\n<p>The first amphisbaena is said to have formed from the blood that fell as a medusa's head was severed. This story's origin most likely stems from the fact that amphisbaenas are oddly immune to petrification, which in turn leads to them sometimes being kept as pets by a medusa. A medusa who keeps an amphisbaena as a pet might regard the viper as their most treasured companion or perhaps even as their own child. Despite these fabled supernatural origins and the occasional special treatment they receive, however, amphisbaenas are entirely mundane animals with only rudimentary intelligence and no innate magical abilities whatsoever.</p>",
          "ac": "all-around vision",
          "prototypeToken": "双头蛇 Amphisbaena"
        },
