        },
        "Mountain Oni": {
          "name": "山岳恶鬼 Mountain Oni",
          "tokenName": "山岳恶鬼 Mountain Oni",
          "items": {
            "Primal Innate Spells": {
              "name": "原能内在法术 Primal Innate Spells"
            },
            "Invisibility (At Will, Self Only)": {
              "name": "隐形（随意施放，仅自身） Invisibility (At Will, Self Only)",
              "description": "<p>幻术扭曲目标周围的光线，使其变为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.zJxUflt9np0q4yML]{隐形}。这会使其对所有生物而言处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.VRSef5y1LmL2Hkjf]{无踪} 状态，不过这些生物可以尝试寻找目标，使其改为对他们而言处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.iU0fEDdBp3rXpTMC]{藏匿} 状态。若目标使用敌对动作，则法术在该敌对动作完成后结束。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（4环）</strong> 该法术持续 1 分钟，但目标使用敌对动作时不会结束。</p>\n<p>Illusions bend light around the target, rendering it @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.zJxUflt9np0q4yML]{Invisible}. This makes it @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.VRSef5y1LmL2Hkjf]{Undetected} to all creatures, though the creatures can attempt to find the target, making it @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.iU0fEDdBp3rXpTMC]{Hidden} to them instead. If the target uses a hostile action, the spell ends after that hostile action is completed.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (4th)</strong> The spell lasts 1 minute, but it doesn't end if the target uses a hostile action.</p>"
            },
            "Tetsubo": {
              "name": "铁棒 Tetsubo"
            },
            "Jaws": {
              "name": "颚 Jaws"
            },
            "Bean Panic": {
              "name": "豆子恐慌 Bean Panic",
              "description": "<p>恶鬼会奇怪地害怕豆子，尤其是在季节开始更替时尤甚。若一名生物以交互将一把豆子掷向恶鬼，恶鬼会陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 2}。以这种方式陷入惊惧时，其对魂魄伤害的弱点增加5。随后，恶鬼在24小时内免疫豆子恐慌。</p>\n<p>Oni are curiously afraid of beans, especially as the seasons begin to change. If a creature Interacts to throw a handful of beans at the oni, the oni becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}. While frightened this way, their weakness to spirit damage is increased by 5. The oni then becomes immune to bean panic for 24 hours.</p>"
            },
            "Reactive Strike": {
              "name": "反应打击 Reactive Strike",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ReactiveStrike]</p>"
            },
            "Change Shape": {
              "name": "变形 Change Shape",
              "description": "<p>山岳恶鬼可以变成任何中型或大型类人生物的外表。这不会改变它们的速度或它们以打击进行攻击与伤害的加值，但可能会改变它们的打击所造成的伤害类型（通常变为钝击）。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ChangeShape]</p>\n<p>The mountain oni can take on the appearance of any Medium or Large humanoid creature. This doesn't change their Speed or their attack and damage bonuses with their Strikes but might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ChangeShape]</p>"
            },
            "Thundering Iron": {
              "name": "雷鸣铁 Thundering Iron",
              "description": "<p>恶鬼举起他们的铁棒，以震耳欲聋的巨响猛然砸下。他们进行一次铁棒打击。成功时，目标额外受到 1d10 点音波伤害。</p>\n<p>除恶鬼外，目标周围 @Template[emanation|distance:10] 内的每个生物也会受到此伤害，并被从目标处推开 5 尺。</p>\n<p>The oni lifts their tetsubo and brings it down in a deafening peal. They make a tetsubo Strike. On a success, the target takes an additional 1d10 sonic damage.</p>\n<p>Each creature in a @Template[emanation|distance:10] around the target, other than the oni, take this damage as well and is pushed 5 feet away from the target.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>山地恶鬼是最常见的恶鬼，也常被认为是最不精明的一类。其他恶鬼或许与魂魄世界联系更紧密，而山地恶鬼对满足其永无止境的食欲之外的事几乎毫无兴趣。怠惰与暴食是山地恶鬼常见的恶习，只要喂得饱，它们便能与附近村庄共存；但更有野心的山地恶鬼往往会被发现带领食人魔战团，或策划残暴的强盗劫掠。山地恶鬼很少过着孤身独居的生活；不过那些真的独来独往者，往往更喜欢在乡野间劫掠，或榨取村庄并把战利品囤为己有。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>恶鬼是源自天夏的巨大而残暴的生物，外形像类人生物，拥有鲜艳的肤色、獠牙与犄角。尽管常被误认为是邪魔，最初的恶鬼原本是神灵，是守护自然的守护魂魄。这些神灵遭受了可怕的创伤：它们的神圣之护因剧烈的灾害或他人的冷酷无情而失落，于是转化成了如今这般暴戾的生物。尽管有人相信，通过恰当的仪式崇拜可以在魂魄层面安抚恶鬼，使其变回神灵，但这些自诩的救世主中有许多人都倒在了恶鬼臭名昭著的蛮力、撕裂血肉的利齿，以及对风暴的掌控之下。</p>\n<p>恶鬼具备将自己伪装成其他类人生物的能力。它们在伪装上很少有创意，往往选择一种与其恶鬼形态相近的特定外貌并一直保持。可这种简单反而令许多人措手不及，因为人们以为恶鬼只限于一种替代形态，而事实绝非如此。</p>\n<p>Mountain oni are the most common oni and often considered the least sophisticated. While other oni might have a stronger connection to the spiritual world, mountain oni have little interest in anything beyond satisfying their relentless appetites. Sloth and gluttony are common vices among mountain oni, which can allow them to coexist with nearby villages so long as they're well fed, but more ambitious mountain oni can often be found leading ogre war parties or orchestrating violent bandit raids. It's rare for mountain oni to live solitary existences, but those who do prefer to maraud the countryside or exploit villages and hoard the spoils for themselves.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Oni are large, brutal creatures originating in Tian Xia who resemble humanoids with brightly colored skin, tusks, and horns. Though commonly mistaken for fiends, the first oni were originally kami, tutelary nature spirits. These kami suffered a terrible trauma, losing their sacred wards to dramatic disasters or the callousness of others, and as a result transformed into the violent creatures they are today. While some believe that oni can be spiritually placated through proper ritual worship that transforms them back into kami, many of these would-be saviors fall to oni's notorious brute strength, flesh-rending teeth, and command of storms.</p>\n<p>Oni possess the ability to disguise themselves as other humanoids. They are rarely creative in their disguises, often choosing a specific appearance similar to their oni form and sticking with it. This simplicity catches many by surprise, however, as people assume oni are limited to a single alternate form, which is by no means the case.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "山岳恶鬼 Mountain Oni"
        },
        "Arms of the Drowned": {
