        "Fluffy Whiskers": {
          "name": "毛须 Fluffy Whiskers",
          "tokenName": "毛须 Fluffy Whiskers",
          "items": {
            "Jaws": {
              "name": "颌骨 Jaws"
            },
            "Lithe": {
              "name": "轻盈 Lithe",
              "description": "<p>黄鼠狼将任何它仅能把头勉强伸进去或更宽的狭窄空间视为困难地形，并且不需要进行 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.kMcV8e5EZUxa6evt]{挤入} 就能穿过其中进行移动。</p>\n<p>A weasel treats any tight space it can barely fit its head in or wider as difficult terrain and doesn't need to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.kMcV8e5EZUxa6evt]{Squeeze} to move through it.</p>"
            },
            "Constrict": {
              "name": "紧勒 Constrict",
              "description": "<p>@Damage[1d4[穿刺]], @Check[强韧|dc:15|基础]</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Constrict]</p>\n<p>@Damage[1d4[piercing]], @Check[fortitude|dc:15|basic]</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Constrict]</p>"
            },
            "Grab": {
              "name": "抓取 Grab",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Grab]</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>尽管体型矮小，黄鼠狼却是技艺高超的猎手。它们在觅食时几乎毫无畏惧，经常杀死体型可达自身五倍的生物。它们偏爱的战术是咬住受害者后颈并用颌部紧紧勒住，直到目标死亡。为了让自己始终吃得饱，黄鼠狼会杀死比所需更多的生物，并把猎物塞进空心原木或废弃的洞穴里，留待日后食用。</p>\n<p>学者们观察到，黄鼠狼无论在野外还是在圈养环境中，都会在猎物面前表现出一种怪异的行为：它们不可预测地四处乱窜，扑倒在地，在洞穴中钻进钻出，整体看起来完全是在胡乱行动。作为回应，猎物会变得困惑，甚至仿佛被催眠，这就给了黄鼠狼一个机会，猛冲上前并给予致命一击。</p>\n<p>一只典型的黄鼠狼体长12英寸，体重不到一磅。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>黄鼠狼是身形矫健、聪明的掠食者，以漂亮、光滑的皮毛以及钻入狭窄空间的能力而闻名。按体重比例而言，很少有动物像黄鼠狼一样贪食。它们饥不择食，几乎每天要吃下接近自身体重一半的食物，因此会不断猎捕新的猎物来满足饥饿。</p>\n<p>Despite their small stature, weasels are skilled hunters. Nearly fearless in pursuit of food, they frequently kill creatures up to five times their own size. Their preferred tactic is to latch onto the back of their victim's neck and constrict with their jaws until the target dies. To keep themselves well fed, weasels kill more creatures than they need and stuff their victims into hollow logs or empty dens to eat later.</p>\n<p>Scholars have observed weasels, both in the wild and captivity, perform a bizarre behavior in front of their prey. They rush about unpredictably, throw themselves to the ground, wriggle into and out of burrows, and generally appear to behave entirely irrationally. In response, their prey becomes confused or seemingly hypnotized, which gives the weasel an opportunity to dash forward and strike a killing blow.</p>\n<p>A typical weasel is 12 inches long and weighs less than a pound.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Weasels are lithe, clever predators known for both their beautiful, sleek fur and their ability to crawl into tight spaces. Pound for pound, few animals are as voracious as weasels. Insatiably hungry, they eat almost half their own weight each day, leading them to constantly hunt for new prey to satisfy their hunger.</p>",
          "blurb": "黄鼠狼\nWeasel",
          "prototypeToken": "毛须 Fluffy Whiskers"
        },
