            "Void Healing": {
              "name": "虚空治疗 Void Healing",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.NegativeHealing]</p>"
            },
            "Black Apoxia": {
              "name": "黑色缺氧症 Black Apoxia",
              "description": "<p>目标在疾病治愈前，无法从由黑色缺氧症造成的疲乏（状态）中恢复</p>\n<p><strong>豁免检定</strong> @Check[fortitude|dc:24]</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>阶段 1</strong> 携带者，无不良效果（1天）</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 2</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1} 和 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued}（1天）</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 3</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2} 和疲乏（1天）</p>\n<p><strong>阶段 4</strong> 死亡</p>\n<p>The target can't recover from the fatigued condition caused by black apoxia until the disease is cured</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> @Check[fortitude|dc:24]</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> carrier with no ill effect (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2} and fatigued (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> dead</p>"
            },
            "Brawling Critical": {
              "name": "徒手战斗大成功或大失败 Brawling Critical",
              "description": "<p>当黑坊主用徒手攻击造成一次大成功时，目标必须成功通过一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:22] 豁免，否则将获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢 1} 状态，直到其下个回合结束。</p>\n<p>When the kurobozu scores a critical hit with an unarmed attack, the target must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:22] save or be @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} until the end of its next turn.</p>"
            },
            "Sagebane": {
              "name": "贤者祸根 Sagebane",
              "description": "<p>当黑坊主用徒手打击对一名活体生物造成伤害时，目标必须在一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:24] 豁免中成功，否则将陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}，持续 1 分钟。</p>\n<p>黑坊主造成的进一步伤害会将持续时间重置为 1 分钟，并在豁免失败时将呆滞值增加 1，最高至呆滞 4。</p>\n<p>When the kurobozu damages a living creature with an unarmed Strike, the target must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:24] save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>Further damage dealt by the kurobozu resets the duration to 1 minute and increases the stupefied value by 1 on a failed save, to a maximum of stupefied 4.</p>"
            },
            "Steal Breath": {
              "name": "窃息 Steal Breath",
              "description": "<p><strong>需求</strong> 黑坊主与一个活着的生物相邻，该生物处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.6uEgoh53GbXuHpTF]{Paralyzed}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned}或@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}状态</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 黑坊主俯身从目标口中吸走气息，目标必须尝试一次@Check[fortitude|dc:22]豁免。无论结果如何，该生物都会暴露于黑色缺氧之中，且其呼吸散发腐肉恶臭，持续1分钟。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 该生物不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 该生物在1分钟内无法说话。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 该生物变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2}，且在1分钟内无法说话。</p>\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 如失败，且该生物倒下并陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}，并开始窒息。</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kurobozu is adjacent to a living creature that is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.6uEgoh53GbXuHpTF]{Paralyzed}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned}, or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The kurobozu leans over and sucks the breath from the target, who must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:22] save. Regardless of the result, the creature is exposed to black apoxia and its breath reeks of carrion for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature can't speak for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2} and can't speak for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, plus the creature falls @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious} and begins suffocating.</p>"
            },
            "Stunning Flurry": {
              "name": "震慑连击 Stunning Flurry",
              "description": "<p><strong>频率</strong> 每轮一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 黑坊主进行两次徒手打击。若两次都命中同一个生物，则为了计算抗力与弱点，将它们的伤害合并，且目标必须在一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:22|traits:incapacitation] 豁免中成功，否则将陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{震慑 1}（大失败则为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{震慑 3}）；此豁免具有失能（特征）。</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The kurobozu makes two unarmed Strikes. If both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses, and the target must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:22|traits:incapacitation] save or be @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 1} (or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 3} on a critical failure); this save has the incapacitation trait.</p>"
            },
            "Monastic Lore": {
              "name": "僧院学识 Monastic Lore"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>生前违背戒律的武僧，死后可能会复起成为一种被称为黑坊主的不死恐怖。这些捕食者以凡人的气息为食，用扭曲的四肢悄然爬入卧室，从沉睡的受害者身上窃取生命。这样的进食会在受害者身上留下痕迹——其呼气带有令人作呕的腐臭气味，并染上一种使人衰弱的疾病，最终导致精疲力竭，继而死亡。</p>\n<p>黑坊主仍保留着其苦修训练的残响，使它们能在战斗中从虚弱的敌人身上吸走气息。它们的恶毒狡黠与苦修般的纪律相结合，使其能够炮制复杂而漫长的阴谋，以实现其嫉妒的复仇。很少有黑坊主足够具有说服力，能劝诱曾经的盟友违背自己的誓言，但这并不会阻止它们尝试。</p>\n<p>A monk who violated their monastic vows in life might arise after death to become an undead horror known as a kurobozu. These predators feast upon the breath of mortals, creeping on twisted limbs into bedrooms to steal the life from sleeping victims. This act of feeding leaves its mark on the victim in the form of a vile scent of rot on the victim's breath and a debilitating disease that eventually results in exhaustion and finally death.</p>\n<p>Kurobozus retain echoes of their ascetic training, enabling them to suck the breath from debilitated foes in the midst of battle. Their malevolent cunning combined with ascetic discipline helps them concoct elaborate and lengthy schemes to enact their jealous revenge. Few kurobozus are convincing enough to persuade their onetime allies to break their own oaths, but this doesn't stop them from making the attempt.</p>",
          "blurb": "异体雄性黑坊主\nVariant male kurobozu",
          "hp": "void healing",
          "prototypeToken": "咀嚼者 The Chewer"
        },
        "Awakened Tree": {
          "name": "觉醒树木 Awakened Tree",
          "tokenName": "觉醒树 Awakened Tree",
          "items": {
            "Branch": {
              "name": "分支 Branch"
            },
            "Root": {
              "name": "根源 Root"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>树栖摄政者与其他强大原初魔法的操使者，会为了保护森林而赋予树木短暂的知觉。这些觉醒的树被灌注了一套可用的本能与动员和攻击的能力，便会听从其主人的命令，为守护家园而战。下列数据同样适用于以其他方式变得可动的植被，例如来自异界的神秘影响、反复无常的妖精魂魄之类。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>树栖者是森林的守护者，也是树木的代言者。它们的寿命与所守望的林地一样漫长；树栖者将自己视为树木的父母与牧者，而非园丁。因此，尽管树栖者往往行动缓慢而谨慎，但当被迫为林地防御而战时，它们会快得令人胆寒。虽然它们很少主动寻求短命族群的陪伴——即便精灵在树栖者眼中也转瞬即逝——且天生不信任变化，但人们也知道树栖者会容忍那些愿意从它们冗长、散漫的独白中学习的人，尤其是这些学生也表达出守护林地的意愿。面对威胁其领地之人，例如急于采伐木材的伐木工，或意图开垦农田、建立城镇的移民，树栖者的怒火坚定不移且毁灭性十足。或许颇具讽刺意味的是，树栖者擅长拆毁他人建造之物——这一特征对其族群中怀抱复仇之心的成员尤为有用。</p>\n<p>Arboreal regents and other wielders of powerful primal magic grant temporary sentience to trees in order to protect the forest. Invested with a workable set of instincts and the ability to mobilize and attack, these awakened trees follow the commands of their master and fight to protect their home. The statistics below work just as well for foliage that has become animate via other methods, such as a mystical influence from another dimension, a capricious fey spirit, or the like.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Arboreals are guardians of the forest and representatives of the trees. As long-lived as the woods they watch over, arboreals consider themselves parents and shepherds of trees rather than their gardeners. Consequently, while arboreals tend to be slow and methodical, they are terrifyingly swift when forced to fight in defense of the woods. Though they rarely seek out the companionship of short-lived folk—even elves are fugacious in the eyes of arboreals—and have an inherent distrust of change, arboreals have been known to tolerate those who seek to learn from their long-winded, rambling monologues, especially if such pupils also express a desire to protect the timberlands. Against those who threaten their realm, such as loggers eager to harvest lumber or settlers aiming to establish croplands or a town, arboreals' wrath is unwavering and devastating. Perhaps ironically, arboreals are gifted at tearing down what others build—a trait that serves vengeful members of their kind well.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "觉醒树 Awakened Tree"
        },
