        "Thatchling": {
          "name": "草人 Thatchling",
          "tokenName": "草人 Thatchling",
          "items": {
            "Frond": {
              "name": "叶状体 Frond"
            },
            "Distracting Giggle": {
              "name": "分神讪笑 Distracting Giggle",
              "description": "<p>15尺。草人的咯咯笑在脑海深处回荡。处于该灵光内的生物进行意志豁免时承受–1状态减值。</p>\n<p>15 feet. The thatchling's giggle echoes in the back of the mind. Creatures within the aura take a –1 status penalty to Will saves.</p>"
            },
            "Rejuvenation": {
              "name": "复苏 Rejuvenation",
              "description": "<p>当草人被除火焰以外的伤害摧毁时，它会尝试一次@Check[flat|dc:11]。成功时，它会在[[/br 2d4 #days]]{2d4天}后于其被摧毁之处120尺内重组，并完全恢复。若草人因火焰伤害降至0生命值，或阻止其灵魂转生的障碍被移除，则它总会被永久摧毁。</p>\n<p>When a thatchling is destroyed by damage other than fire, it attempts a @Check[flat|dc:11]. On a success, it reforms after [[/br 2d4 #days]]{2d4 days} within 120 feet of where it was destroyed, fully healed. A thatchling is always permanently destroyed if reduced to 0 Hit Points by fire damage or if the obstacle preventing the soul from reincarnating is removed.</p>"
            },
            "Void Healing": {
              "name": "虚空治疗 Void Healing",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.NegativeHealing]</p>"
            },
            "Thatchling's Curse": {
              "name": "草人诅咒 Thatchling's Curse",
              "description": "<p>草人将注意力集中在其30尺内一名可见的单一目标上，然后开始喃喃自语并低声念着胡言乱语。目标必须尝试一次 @Check[will|dc:16] 意志豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响，并在24小时内暂时免疫草人诅咒。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标短暂迷失方向，难以朝正确方向移动。目标的各项速度在1轮内受到–5尺的状态减值。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 同成功，但其各项速度的减值持续1分钟。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 同失败，但其各项速度的减值持续至诅咒被移除，或直至制造该效果的草人被永久摧毁为止，以先发生者为准。此外，当受诅咒的生物尝试进行用于辨别方向或 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.EA5vuSgJfiHH7plD]{追踪} 的生存检定时，他们使用比其检定结果低一级成功度的结果，并且他们不能采取侦查（探索行动）。</p>\n<p>The thatchling focuses its attention on a single target within 30 feet that it can see, and then begins muttering and whispering nonsense. The target must attempt a @Check[will|dc:16] save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Thatchling's Curse for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is momentarily disoriented and has difficulty moving in the right direction. The target takes a –5-foot status penalty to its Speeds for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, but the penalty to its Speeds lasts for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the penalty to its Speeds lasts until the curse is removed or until the thatchling that created the effect is permanently destroyed, whichever comes first. In addition, when the cursed creature attempts a Survival check to Sense Direction or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.EA5vuSgJfiHH7plD]{Track}, they use the outcome for one degree of success worse than the result of their check, and they can't take the Scout exploration activity.</p>"
            },
            "Thicket Walker": {
              "name": "灌木行者 Thicket Walker",
              "description": "<p>草人会无视由荆棘、纠缠的草丛和矮丛环境中造成的困难地形，即使这些地形是被魔法操控的也一样。</p>\n<p>Thatchlings ignore difficult terrain caused by brambles, tangled grass, and undergrowth, even those manipulated by magic.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>典型的草人看起来像一捆干草与树枝拼成的人形，由一圈圈看似发着蓝光的头发般物质缠绕固定。这些次等不死无法形成比小人类孩童更大的躯体。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>在神门的乡间，善解的一些分支警告人们：若一个注定要转世的灵魂被阻止进入灵魂之河、无法重新加入轮回，会发生什么。这些灵魂会变得沮丧、困惑，继而因自觉被剥夺了应得的肉身而狂怒，并迫使植物充当它们的新身体。也有人推测：当遗体被浅埋时，向下生长到残骸里的草根会将灵魂缠住并捕获。</p>\n<p>草人很聪明，也有说话的能力，但很少开口——它们通常没什么想对那些它们觊觎其生命的人说的。偶尔，有的草人会尝试呼喊求助来把某人引到高草地或茂密的矮丛环境中，但它们几乎不擅长欺骗，因此这种伎俩并不能有效地让它们看起来像是真正需要帮助的活物。</p>\n<h2>老友</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的草人来源很简单：那些本应在死亡后转世的灵魂无法转世，于是以草人的形态复起。当然，由于每一年都会“重置”一切，那些在一年中死去并变成草人的人，会在每个夏季第一天再次以活人之身重生，并且不记得自己先前那段注定毁灭的存在。尽管仍受本能驱使去攻击活物，柳岸镇的草人确实会感到一丝懊悔——若GM认为特别合适，它们对生前认识的生物进行的攻击检定与豁免骰会承受–2环境减值。</p>\n<h2>永远无感</h2>\n<p>草人诅咒会夺走受其影响者的方向感，进而在神门催生出一整类侮辱用语，用来把某人把事情办成的能力比作“草人感”。例如，一个很难交到朋友的人，可能会被说成有“草人感的友情”；而一个总把饭菜做砸的人，可能会被说成有“草人感的厨房手感”。</p>\n<p>The typical thatchling appears as a humanoid bundle of dry grass and twigs, held together by coils of what looks like glowing blue hair. These minor undead can't form bodies larger than those of a small human child.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>In rural Shenmen, some branches of Sangpotshi warn of what can happen if a soul bound for reincarnation is prevented from entering the River of Souls and rejoining the cycle. These souls become frustrated, confused, and then furious at what they feel is a denial of the body they deserve, and in turn, they force vegetation to serve as their new body. Others theorize that when a body is buried in a shallow grave, the roots of grass growing down into the remains can tangle the soul and capture it.</p>\n<p>Thatchlings are intelligent and capable of speaking but rarely do so—they generally have little to say to those whose lives they covet. Rarely, one might attempt to lure someone into an area of tall grass or dense undergrowth by calling out to them for aid, but they have little skill at deception, so such tactics aren't particularly effective at making them seem like actual living creatures in need of help.</p>\n<h2>Old Friends</h2>\n<p>The source of Willowshore's thatchlings is the simple fact that the souls who would normally have been reincarnated upon death can't do so, thus rising as thatchlings. Of course, since each year \"resets\" things, those who died during the year and became thatchlings are reborn alive once more on every first day of summer, with no memories of their previous doomed existence. While still driven by instinct to attack the living, Willowshore's thatchlings do feel a sense of remorse—if the GM judges it especially appropriate, they might take a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and saving throws against creatures they knew in life.</p>\n<h2>Forever Senseless</h2>\n<p>The thatchling's curse robs the sense of direction from those it falls upon, leading to a whole category of insults in Shenmen that compare someone's ability to get something done to \"a thatchling's sense.\" For example, someone who has a hard time making friends might be said to have \"a thatchling's sense of friendship,\" while someone who constantly ruins meals might be said to have \"a thatchling's kitchen sense.\"</p>",
          "hp": "void healing",
          "prototypeToken": "草人 Thatchling",
          "speed": "thicket walker"
        },
