        "Kohoshi": {
          "name": "小星 Kohoshi",
          "tokenName": "小星 Kohoshi",
          "items": {
            "Spade": {
              "name": "铁锹 Spade"
            },
            "Fist": {
              "name": "拳头 Fist"
            },
            "Ward": {
              "name": "护 Ward",
              "description": "<p>每个神灵都与一处护相绑定：一种特定的动物、植物、物体或地点。神灵可以以一个带有专注（特征）的单动作与其护融合或从中现身。融合期间，神灵可以用其通常的感官以及其护的感官来观察周遭，但不能移动、与其护交流或控制其护。此外，与其护融合的神灵每分钟恢复生命值，如同其花费了一整天休息一般。</p>\n<p>式神的护通常是一件小型艺术品或文明的象征，例如里程碑、小路标志、私人花园或超小型雕像。</p>\n<p>Every kami is bound to a ward: a specific animal, plant, object, or location. A kami can merge with or emerge from their ward as a single action, which has the concentrate trait. While merged, the kami can observe their surroundings with their usual senses as well as the senses of their ward, but can't move, communicate with, or control their ward. Additionally, a kami merged with their ward recovers Hit Points each minute as if they spent an entire day resting.</p>\n<p>A shikigami's ward is typically a minor work of art or symbol of civilization, such as a milestone, trail sign, personal garden, or tiny statue.</p>"
            },
            "Flatten": {
              "name": "压平 Flatten",
              "description": "<p>式神变得扁平，如同一张纸的厚度。处于扁平化时，他们可以随风飘浮，获得20英尺飞行速度，并且可以穿过细小的裂缝与缝隙而无需挤入；但他们会变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{笨拙 2}。式神可以解除该效果。</p>\n<p>The shikigami flattens to the width of a sheet of paper. While Flattened, they can float on the wind, gaining a 20-foot fly Speed, and they can slip through small cracks and gaps without needing to Squeeze; however, they become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{Clumsy 2}. The shikigami can Dismiss this effect.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>式神由纸构成，能够在扁平的剪纸形态与由纸浆塑形的立体纸偶之间轻易变换。与大多数其他神灵不同——后者往往由更强大的魂魄或神祇将其束缚于自身的护——式神是较弱小的魂魄，有时连凡人修行者也能将其束缚进一个超小型的纸形体内，并指派它守护一些小型工作物，例如花园雕像与花瓶。地主们乐于让式神守护自家花园：无论是他们付钱请一位云游施法者去恳求式神，还是仅仅走运，恰好有另一位魂魄将某个式神指派到他们的土地上。旅人若遇见被式神眷顾的里程碑或路标，便相信这样的遭遇是旅途的吉兆。</p>\n<p>至于式神自身，它们对文明以及栖居其中的人形生物看法不一。式神会为了保护自己的护而与入侵者和亵渎者战斗，但若当地人开始污染区域或对自然表现出漠视，这些神灵也同样可能选择离开——并带走它们的护。大多数有能力束缚式神的修行者并不会做出这类不敬之举；然而，一旦神灵听闻此类行径，遍布各地的式神便可能成批放弃契约并出走，留下令人不安的真空。由此，式神体现了文明扩张与自然世界保存之间那种岌岌可危的保持平衡。</p>\n<p>并非所有式神都守护花园，因此你可以将式神的铲子替换为任何一种对式神任务与其护有用的日常工具。神灵挥舞任何此类武器时，使用与其铲子打击所列相同的伤害骰、调整值与特征，但应根据新武器适当地更改伤害类型。</p><hr /><p>神灵是来自天夏诸国的神圣自然之灵，位于内海地区以东的遥远之地。它们作为守护者，守卫自己所保护的自然物体与地点——它们的护——也是恶鬼（Pathfinder Monster Core 252–255）的古老宿敌。神灵能够与自己的护融合，使其得以暗中观察任何踏入其圣地之人。神灵会放过那些它们认为无害的人，但会警觉地战斗，以吓退任何被视作威胁者。</p>\n<p>Shikigami are made of paper and can easily transform between a flat cutout form and a three-dimensional doll of molded paper. Unlike most other kami, who are bound to their wards by a more powerful spirit or deity, shikigami are minor spirits that even mortal practitioners can sometimes bind into a tiny paper form and task with guarding small works, such as garden statues and vases. Landowners delight in having shikigami protect their gardens, whether they paid a wandering spellcaster to entreat the shikigami or simply had the fortune of another spirit assigning a shikigami to their land. Travelers who come across a shikigami-graced milestone or waypost believe that such encounters are good omens for the journey.</p>\n<p>For their part, shikigami have mixed opinions on civilization and the humanoids who dwell therein. While shikigami will fight to protect their ward against invaders and desecrators, these kami are just as likely to leave—their ward in tow—if locals begin to despoil the area or show a disregard for nature. Most practitioners capable of binding a shikigami wouldn't engage in this type of disrespect, but should the kami catch wind of such practices, shikigami across the land might abandon their contracts en masse, leaving behind an uncomfortable vacuum with their exodus. In this way, shikigami exemplify the precarious balance between the expansion of civilization and the preservation of the natural world.</p>\n<p>Not all shikigami protect gardens, so you can substitute the shikigami's spade for any sort of mundane tool that's useful to the shikigami's task and their ward. The kami wields any such weapon with the same damage dice, modifiers, and traits listed for their spade Strike, but change the damage type as appropriate for the new weapon.</p><hr /><p>Kami are divine nature spirits from the lands of Tian Xia, far to the east of the Inner Sea region. They serve as guardians of natural objects and places they protect—their wards—and are ancient enemies of oni (Pathfinder Monster Core 252–255). Kami can merge with their wards, allowing them to surreptitiously watch anyone who treads upon their sacred grounds. Kami leave those who they deem harmless alone, but fight vigilantly to scare away anyone perceived as a threat.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "小星 Kohoshi",
          "speed": "flatten"
