            "Create Thatchling Spawn": {
              "name": "创造草人衍体 Create Thatchling Spawn",
              "description": "<p>一个活着的人形生物若在受到草人诅咒效果影响期间被红头草人杀死，会在[[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4轮}后作为一只草人复生。该衍生体受杀死它的红头草人的命令控制。如果一只红头草人同时控制的数量过多（由GM决定），则在其回合开始时，一些草人可以通过一次@Check[will|dc:18]意志豁免来挣脱控制。如果创造该衍生体的红头草人被摧毁，该衍生体会成为一只自主的草人。</p>\n<p>A living humanoid who's slain by a red-hooded thatchling while under the effects of Thatchling's Curse rises as a thatchling after [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}. This spawn is under the command of the red-hooded thatchling that killed it. If a red-hooded thatchling controls too many at once (as determined by the GM), some thatchlings can free themselves with a @Check[will|dc:18] saving throw at the start of their turn. If the red-hooded thatchling who created the spawn is destroyed, the spawn becomes an autonomous thatchling.</p>"
            },
            "Howl of Vengeful Fury": {
              "name": "复仇怒嚎 Howl of Vengeful Fury",
              "description": "<p><strong>频率</strong> 每小时一次</p><hr /><p><strong>效果</strong> 红头草人可怜地抽泣，随后释放出一声骇人的尖叫。所有位于 @Template[emanation|distance:30] 内的非草人生物受到 @Damage[2d10[sonic]|options:area-damage] 伤害（@Check[fortitude|dc:18|basic|options:area-effect] 豁免），并在1分钟内对所有草人的分神讪笑免疫。区域内的草人获得5点临时生命值，并在1分钟内其打击与豁免骰获得+1状态加值。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.X1Q1uBiylZoJg3Co]{效果：复仇怒嚎}</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The red-hooded thatchling sobs pitifully before unleashing a terrifying scream. All non-thatchling creatures within a @Template[emanation|distance:30] take @Damage[2d10[sonic]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[fortitude|dc:18|basic|options:area-effect] save) and become immune to all thatchlings' distracting giggle for 1 minute. Thatchlings in the area gain 5 temporary Hit Points and a +1 status bonus to their Strikes and saving throws for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.X1Q1uBiylZoJg3Co]{Effect: Howl of Vengeful Fury}</p>"
            },
            "Thatchling's Curse": {
              "name": "草人诅咒 Thatchling's Curse",
              "description": "<p>草人将注意力集中在其可见的、30尺内的单一目标身上，然后开始咕哝并低声念着毫无意义的胡言乱语。目标必须尝试一次 @Check[will|dc:18] 豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 目标不受影响，并在24小时内暂时免疫草人诅咒。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标短暂迷失方向，难以朝正确方向移动。目标的速度在1轮内受到–5尺状态减值。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 同成功，但其速度的减值持续1分钟。</p>\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 同失败，但其速度的减值持续到诅咒被移除，或直到制造该效果的草人被永久摧毁为止，以先发生者为准。此外，当受诅咒的生物尝试进行用于辨别方向或 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.EA5vuSgJfiHH7plD]{追踪} 的生存检定时，他们使用比其检定结果差一级成功度的结果，且他们不能进行侦查（探索行动）。</p>\n<p>The thatchling focuses its attention on a single target within 30 feet that it can see, and then begins muttering and whispering nonsense. The target must attempt a @Check[will|dc:18] save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Thatchling's Curse for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is momentarily disoriented and has difficulty moving in the right direction. The target takes a –5-foot status penalty to its Speeds for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, but the penalty to its Speeds lasts for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the penalty to its Speeds lasts until the curse is removed or until the thatchling that created the effect is permanently destroyed, whichever comes first. In addition, when the cursed creature attempts a Survival check to Sense Direction or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.EA5vuSgJfiHH7plD]{Track}, they use the outcome for one degree of success worse than the result of their check, and they can't take the Scout exploration activity.</p>"
            },
            "Thicket Walker": {
              "name": "灌木行者 Thicket Walker",
              "description": "<p>草人无视由荆棘、纠缠的草以及矮丛环境中造成的困难地形，即使这些地形是由魔法操纵的也一样。</p>\n<p>Thatchlings ignore difficult terrain caused by brambles, tangled grass, and undergrowth, even those manipulated by magic.</p>"
            },
            "Fan Hongrui True Form": {
              "name": "范宏瑞真身 Fan Hongrui True Form"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>当一个注定会变成草人的灵魂在巨大痛苦的折磨中死去时，他们可能会在死后以红头草人的形态归来。这些复仇的草人从远处看似戴着红色兜帽，但一旦靠近，便会揭露骇人的真相——他们的头颅被鲜血浸透。与其他草人不同，红头草人精于诡计；他们能借由幻术魔法伪装成活着的类人生物，这种能力使他们更容易把毫无防备者引诱进伏击。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>在神门的乡间，善解的某些支派警告人们：若一个本该转世的灵魂被阻止进入灵魂之河、无法重新回到轮回，会发生什么事。这些灵魂会先变得挫败与困惑，随后因自觉被剥夺了自己应得的躯体而暴怒；作为回应，他们强迫植被充当自己的新身体。也有人推测，当尸体被埋在浅墓中时，向下生长、扎入遗骸的草根会将灵魂缠住并把它困住。</p>\n<p>草人具有智慧，也有说话的能力，但他们很少开口——对那些他们觊觎其生命的人，他们通常没什么可说的。极少数情况下，某个草人可能会试图呼救，诱使他人走入高草区或矮丛环境中；但他们几乎不擅长欺骗，因此这种手段并不能有效让他们看起来像真正需要帮助的活生物。</p>\n<h2>老友</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇草人的来源很简单：那些正常情况下会在死亡后转世的灵魂无法如此，于是以草人的形态复苏。当然，由于每一年都会“重置”一切，那些在一年中死去并变成草人的人，会在每个夏季第一天再次以活人之身重生，且没有任何关于此前毁灭的存在的记忆。尽管他们仍受本能驱使去攻击活物，柳岸镇的草人确实会感到一丝懊悔——若GM判断这尤其合适，他们在对抗生前认识的生物时，其攻击检定与豁免骰会承受–2环境减值。</p>\n<h2>永远无感</h2>\n<p>草人诅咒会夺走受其影响者的方向感，以至于神门出现了一整类侮辱用语，会把某人做成一件事的能力拿来和“草人感”相比。比如，一个很难交到朋友的人可能会被说成拥有“草人感的友谊”，而一个总把饭菜做砸的人可能会被说成拥有“草人感的厨房”。</p>\n<p>When a soul doomed to become a thatchling dies in the throes of great anguish, they can return after death as a red-hooded thatchling. These vengeful thatchlings appear to wear red hoods when viewed at a distance, but up close, the grisly truth—that their heads are blood-soaked—is revealed. Unlike other thatchlings, red-hooded thatchlings are skilled at trickery, and their ability to appear as a living humanoid through illusion magic allows them to lure the unexpected into ambushes much more easily.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>In rural Shenmen, some branches of Sangpotshi warn of what can happen if a soul bound for reincarnation is prevented from entering the River of Souls and rejoining the cycle. These souls become frustrated, confused, and then furious at what they feel is a denial of the body they deserve, and in turn, they force vegetation to serve as their new body. Others theorize that when a body is buried in a shallow grave, the roots of grass growing down into the remains can tangle the soul and capture it.</p>\n<p>Thatchlings are intelligent and capable of speaking but rarely do so—they generally have little to say to those whose lives they covet. Rarely, one might attempt to lure someone into an area of tall grass or dense undergrowth by calling out to them for aid, but they have little skill at deception, so such tactics aren't particularly effective at making them seem like actual living creatures in need of help.</p>\n<h2>Old Friends</h2>\n<p>The source of Willowshore's thatchlings is the simple fact that the souls who would normally have been reincarnated upon death can't do so, thus rising as thatchlings. Of course, since each year \"resets\" things, those who died during the year and became thatchlings are reborn alive once more on every first day of summer, with no memories of their previous doomed existence. While still driven by instinct to attack the living, Willowshore's thatchlings do feel a sense of remorse—if the GM judges it especially appropriate, they might take a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and saving throws against creatures they knew in life.</p>\n<h2>Forever Senseless</h2>\n<p>The thatchling's curse robs the sense of direction from those it falls upon, leading to a whole category of insults in Shenmen that compare someone's ability to get something done to \"a thatchling's sense.\" For example, someone who has a hard time making friends might be said to have \"a thatchling's sense of friendship,\" while someone who constantly ruins meals might be said to have \"a thatchling's kitchen sense.\"</p>",
          "blurb": "变体女性红头草人\nVariant female red-hooded thatchling",
          "hp": "void healing",
          "prototypeToken": "范宏瑞 Fan Hongrui",
          "speed": "thicket walker"
        },
