            "Soul Lock": {
              "name": "灵魂锁 Soul Lock",
              "description": "<p><strong>频率</strong> 每日一次</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>效果</strong> 狂躁邪魔吞噬30英尺内一名在过去1分钟内死亡的有感知生物的灵魂。如此做时，狂躁邪魔的腹中会长出一枚拳头大小的灵魂宝石（硬度2，HP 8），并且可以在任何时候以一个交互动作将其反刍出来。摧毁该宝石会释放其中的灵魂，但不会使死去的生物复活。若施法者试图使灵魂被困在灵魂宝石中的生物复生，则会失败，除非其在一次 @Check[religion|dc:30] 检定中成功。一次成功会使灵魂宝石粉碎音波，使该生物如同该法术正常效果般复活。</p>\n<p>一名邪魔可以交互以吞下其持有的灵魂宝石，将该灵魂判入邪魔的家乡位面。该邪魔获得快速治疗5，持续1分钟。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.JgJ4Iw8BvJ4tWkah]{效果：灵魂锁（治疗）}</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The cacodaemon ingests the soul of a sentient creature within 30 feet that died within the last minute. When they do, the cacodaemon grows a fist-sized soul gem (Hardness 2, HP 8) in their gut and can regurgitate it at any time as an Interact action. Destroying the gem frees the soul within but doesn't return the deceased creature to life. If a caster attempts to return to life a creature whose soul is trapped within a soul gem, they fail unless they succeed at a @Check[religion|dc:30] check. A success causes the soul gem to shatter so the creature is returned to life as normal for the spell.</p>\n<p>A fiend can Interact to ingest a soul gem it is holding, condemning the soul to the fiend's home plane. The fiend gains fast healing 5 for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.JgJ4Iw8BvJ4tWkah]{Effect: Soul Lock (Healing)}</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>这些扭曲的暴力与恨意化身诞生于阿巴顿迷雾中翻涌的愤怒而畸变的转世的灵魂漩涡。狂躁邪魔始终渴求凡人的灵魂，并渴望制造痛苦。它们是由牙齿、鳍与棘刺构成的咬噬球体，是邪魔族类中最弱的一支：由各种琐碎的死亡形态拼合而成，却缺乏将自身专注于单一死因所带来的力量。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>邪魔是阴郁而可怖的阿巴顿位面的居民，被塑造出来并奉献于摧毁一切形式的生命。它们侍奉天启骑士，追求以尽可能痛苦且骇人的方式杀死每一个凡人。每一种邪魔都代表一种不同的死法，而它们的力量几乎总是用于散播那种特定的死亡。凭借这些力量，它们试图将一切存在拖入绝望与无望的深坑，并让所有灵魂归于虚无。</p>\n<p>凡人召唤邪魔时，通常是想把这些生物的毁灭与腐化之力为己所用；但邪魔无论走到哪里，总会寻找散播恐惧、怀疑与绝望的办法。它们常常将阴谋伪装成其他邪魔外道所为，因为它们知道这种混淆会加深凡人的恐惧，并让凡人无法携带最有效的武器。因此，博学的凡人有时会以其首领为名，将邪魔称为“骑手”，或以其最大产业为名，称之为“灵魂贩子”。</p>\n<p>许多邪魔外道会引诱凡人过上虚无主义的邪恶生活，以在其原生位面增加自身数量与力量；而邪魔还受到对凡人灵魂的超自然饥渴所驱使，并用多种手段——其中尤以狂躁邪魔的灵魂宝石为甚——来囚陷它们。在阿巴顿以及多元宇宙其他阴森之地，灵魂既是美馔，也是商品，也是魔法力量的源泉；而邪魔则是这种灵性“资源”最贪婪的暴食者、最活跃的商人，以及最恶劣的滥用者之一。</p>\n<p>These twisted embodiments of violence and spite are spawned from eddies of angry and warped souls amid Abaddon's mists. Cacodaemons constantly hunger for mortal souls and yearn to create suffering. As gnashing spheres of teeth, fins, and spines, they are the weakest of daemonkind, an amalgam of various petty forms of death without the strength that comes from focusing on a single cause of demise.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Denizens of the bleak and terrible plane of Abaddon, daemons are shaped by and devoted to the destruction of life in all its forms. They seek the death of every mortal being by the most painful and horrible means possible, in service to the Apocalypse Riders. Each kind of daemon represents a different way to die, and their powers are nearly always aimed at spreading that particular form of death. Through the use of these powers, they seek to drag all existence down into a pit of hopelessness and despair, and to commit all souls to oblivion.</p>\n<p>While mortals who summon daemons usually seek to use the creatures' destructive and corrupting powers for their own ends, daemons always look for ways to spread fear, doubt, and despair wherever they go. Often, daemons disguise their plots as the workings of other fiends, knowing that such confusion compounds mortals' fear and keeps those mortals from bringing the most effective weapons. As a result, learned mortals sometimes refer to daemons as \"riders\" after their leaders or \"soul mongers\" after their largest industry.</p>\n<p>While many fiends seek to tempt mortals into lives of nihilistic evil to increase their own numbers and power on their native planes, daemons are further driven by a supernatural hunger for mortal souls and use a variety of methods—not least of which is the cacodaemons' soul gems—to entrap them. On Abaddon and in other forbidding places across the multiverse, souls are simultaneously a delicacy, a trade good, and a source of magical power, and the daemons are among the greatest gluttons, merchants, and abusers of this spiritual \"resource.\"</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "狂躁邪魔 Cacodaemon"
        },
