            "Touch of Idiocy": {
              "name": "愚者之触 Touch of Idiocy",
              "description": "<p>你使目标的心智变得迟钝，效果取决于其意志豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}，持续至你下个回合开始。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 目标获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 2}，持续1分钟。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 目标获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 3}，持续1分钟。</p>\n<p>You dull the target's mind, depending on its Will save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} until the start of your next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 2} for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 3} for 1 minute.</p>"
            },
            "Daze": {
              "name": "晕眩术 Daze",
              "description": "<p>你侵入目标的心智，用一次心灵冲击使其陷入恍惚。这次冲击造成1d6心灵伤害，目标进行一次基础意志豁免。若目标在豁免中大失败，它还会获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{震慑 1}。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（+2）</strong> 伤害增加1d6。</p>\n<p>You push into the target's mind and daze it with a mental jolt. The jolt deals 1d6 mental damage, with a basic Will save. If the target critically fails the save, it is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 1}.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+2)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p>"
            },
            "Item Facade": {
              "name": "伪装物件 Item Facade",
              "description": "<p>你让目标物体看起来和摸起来仿佛处于好得多或差得多的物理状态。施放该法术时，决定你要让该物体看起来破败不堪还是完美无瑕。一件被伪装成破败的物品看起来处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.6dNUvdb1dhToNDj3]{Broken}状态且粗制滥造。一件完好的物品若被伪装得更好，看起来就像崭新的一样并被高度抛光或保养良好。一件Broken物品看起来像是完好且可正常使用。被摧毁的物品无法受该法术影响。与该物品进行交互的生物可以尝试识破该幻觉。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（2环）</strong> 持续时间为24小时。</p>\n<p><strong>升阶（3环）</strong> 持续时间为无限。</p>\n<p>You make the target object look and feel as though it were in much better or worse physical condition. When you cast this spell, decide whether you want to make the object look decrepit or perfect. An item made to look decrepit appears @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.6dNUvdb1dhToNDj3]{Broken} and shoddy. An intact item made to look better appears as though it's brand new and highly polished or well maintained. A Broken item appears to be intact and functional. Destroyed items can't be affected by this spell. A creature that Interacts with the item can attempt to disbelieve the illusion.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (2nd)</strong> The duration is 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> The duration is unlimited.</p>"
            },
            "Phantom Pain": {
              "name": "幻痛术 Phantom Pain",
              "description": "<p>幻觉般的痛苦折磨着目标，造成2d4点心灵伤害以及@Damage[(@item.level)d4[persistent,mental]]伤害。目标必须进行一次意志豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 目标不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 目标承受全部初始伤害但不承受持续伤害，且该法术立即结束。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 目标承受全部初始伤害与持续伤害，且目标获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1}。如果目标从恶心中恢复，持续伤害结束且该法术结束。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 同失败，但目标获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 2}。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>升阶（+1）</strong> 伤害增加2d4，持续伤害增加1d4。</p>\n<p>Illusory pain wracks the target, dealing 2d4 mental damage and @Damage[(@item.level)d4[persistent,mental]] damage. The target must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes full initial damage but no persistent damage, and the spell ends immediately.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full initial and persistent damage, and the target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1}. If the target recovers from being Sickened, the persistent damage ends and the spell ends.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2}.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 2d4 and the persistent damage by 1d4.</p>"
            },
            "True Strike": {
              "name": "真实打击 True Strike",
              "description": "<p>对未来的一瞥确保你的下一击精准命中。直到你的回合结束前，你下一次进行攻击掷骰时，将该次攻击掷骰掷两次并取较佳结果。该次攻击无视攻击掷骰的环境减值，以及因目标处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{隐蔽}或@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.iU0fEDdBp3rXpTMC]{藏匿}而需要进行的任何纯骰检定。</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spell-effects.Item.fpGDAz2v5PG0zUSl]{法术效果：必中打击}</p>\n<p>A glimpse into the future ensures your next blow strikes true. The next time you make an attack roll before the end of your turn, roll the attack twice and use the better result. The attack ignores circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the target being @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{Concealed} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.iU0fEDdBp3rXpTMC]{Hidden}.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spell-effects.Item.fpGDAz2v5PG0zUSl]{Spell Effect: Sure Strike}</p>"
            },
            "Broken Katana": {
              "name": "破损打刀 Broken Katana"
            },
            "Aura of Forgetfulness": {
              "name": "健忘灵光 Aura of Forgetfulness",
              "description": "<p>30英尺。任何在灵光中开始其回合的生物都必须尝试一次 @Check[will|dc:21] 意志豁免。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 该生物不受影响，并在24小时内暂时免疫健忘灵光。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 该生物不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 该生物获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢 1} 直到其下一回合结束，因为它难以记起自己原本打算做什么。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 同失败，但为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢 2}。</p>\n<p>30 feet. A creature who begins its turn in the aura must attempt a @Check[will|dc:21] save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Aura of Forgetfulness for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} until the end of its next turn, as it has trouble remembering what it intended to do.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 2}.</p>"
            },
            "Soul Shred": {
              "name": "灵魂撕裂 Soul Shred",
              "description": "<p>被伊德加杀死的生物很难复活，或作为不死生物被唤起。伊德加会自动尝试反制任何复活或唤起任何其所杀死生物的尝试（反制调整值 [[/r 1d20+14 #Counteract]]{+14}，反制阶级 3）。如果杀死该生物的伊德加本身被杀死，则该生物可以正常从死亡中被带回或成为不死生物。</p>\n<p>Creatures killed by a idja are difficult to bring back to life or animate as undead. The idja automatically attempts to counteract any attempt to resurrect or animate any creature that it has killed (counteract modifier [[/r 1d20+14 #Counteract]]{+14}, counteract rank 3). If the idja who slew the creature is itself slain, the creature can be brought back from death or become undead normally.</p>"
            },
            "Manifest False Memories": {
              "name": "具现虚假记忆 Manifest False Memories",
              "description": "<p>伊吉达从体内释放出一团红色蝴蝶云，每一只都携带着一段虚假记忆，会感染被其拂过者。所有位于伊吉达@Template[emanation|distance:10]{10英尺内}的非灵堕魔生物都必须尝试一次@Check[will|dc:21]意志豁免。伊吉达在接下来的[[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4轮}内无法使用具现虚假记忆。</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>大成功</strong> 该生物不受影响。</p>\n<p><strong>成功</strong> 该生物获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}，直到其下一回合结束。</p>\n<p><strong>失败</strong> 该生物获得呆滞 1和@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.yblD8fOR1J8rDwEQ]{困惑}，直到其下一回合结束。</p>\n<p><strong>大失败</strong> 该生物获得呆滞 1和困惑，持续1分钟。该生物可在其每个回合结束时尝试一次新的豁免以结束这些效果。</p>\n<p>The ijda releases a cloud of red butterflies from its body, each of which carries a false memory that infects those they brush against. All non-nindoru creatures @Template[emanation|distance:10]{within 10 feet} of the ijda must attempt a @Check[will|dc:21] save. The ijda can't Manifest False Memories for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} until the end of its next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is stupefied 1 and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.yblD8fOR1J8rDwEQ]{Confused} until the end of its next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is stupefied 1 and confused for 1 minute. It can attempt a new save at the end of each of its turns to end the effects.</p>"
            },
            "Ruin Wielder": {
              "name": "持骸者 Ruin Wielder",
              "description": "<p>当伊吉达挥舞一把破损的非魔法武器时，他们不会承受该武器处于破损状态的任何不利影响。当伊吉达挥舞它时，该武器变为一把+1强击武器，并在成功命中时额外造成1d6点心灵伤害。</p>\n<p>When a ijda wields a broken non-magical weapon, they do not take any of the disadvantages of the weapon being broken. While the ijda wields it, the weapon becomes a +1 striking weapon that deals an additional 1d6 mental damage on a successful hit.</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>伊迦达是遗忘的生物。它们诞生于曾经开悟、却又背弃了开悟以及自己在转世轮回中职责的灵魂；它们诅咒自身存在的徒劳，并以将他人引向同样命运为乐。</p>\n<p>伊迦达外形如高耸的人形，其躯体臃肿，且不断迸裂出细小的红色蝴蝶；这些蝴蝶飞散开后便融化成薄雾。它们的手臂异常修长，扭曲断折到更像触手般蠕动，使其战斗方式令人不安，触及范围甚至超过多数大型生物。它们披着由霉烂稻草制成的衣物与斗篷，挥舞着断剑——碎裂的剑刃仍大致悬浮在原位。它们最令人毛骨悚然的特征，是完全没有头颅；取而代之的，是本应为头的位置上放着一只柳条编成的笼子，里面塞满翻涌的蝴蝶云团。然而它们依旧能视、能听、能言，仿佛头颅仍在原处一般。</p>\n<p>伊迦达形成时没有头、甚至没有大脑；它们的心智由头笼中的蝴蝶群，或从体内爆裂而出的蝴蝶群所共享。每当这些昆虫逃逸并消散，健忘的邪魔就失去一个潜在的念头。它们无法学习新事物，所做的一切要么源自刻入灵魂的记忆，要么来自它们对其他灵堕魔或其所认可为上级的生物所盲从的指令。它们的动作、言语与反应，全凭一种肌肉记忆来完成——这种记忆基于它们的灵魂相信自己应如何回应外界刺激。因此，如今大多数伊迦达都成了残暴的守卫，因为它们的遗忘也使它们无法入睡。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>当一个多次转世的邪恶凡人灵魂被从灵魂轮回中硬生生扯出并遭到腐化时，它可能经历可怖的蜕变，化为一种名为灵堕魔的邪魔。作为熵增与破坏循环之力，灵堕魔是丑恶的生物，躯体常显得扭曲变形；它们挥舞已然破碎却仍能运作的武器，而其真正面容也往往隐匿不见。它们呈现出人们在不死生物身上可能见到的特征，例如腐烂的血肉或裸露的骨骼，但灵堕魔确确实实仍是活物。</p>\n<p>每一只灵堕魔都体现着某一种特定循环的断裂——无论那循环源自自然界还是社会传统。对灵堕魔而言，没有什么比吞食一名多次转世的生物更为美味；而理论上即将真正登临开悟者，则是最可口的一餐。被灵堕魔杀死者也会被撕离轮回——幸运者会前往白骨原接受裁决，但更多人会被腐化，化为更多此等可怖邪魔。</p>\n<p>善解的追随者认为灵堕魔尤为可憎，并将其列为最可怕的威胁之一。灵堕魔最常见于转世轮回之力最强盛的世界区域；并且如同罗刹与鬼（oni）一般，它们与物质位面的关联最为紧密。</p>\n<h2>转世的灵魂</h2>\n<p>在某些情况下，你会知道灵堕魔所攻击的生物是否拥有转世的灵魂。诸如轮回族（samsarans）之类的族裔总是转世的灵魂，而玩家角色的背景故事，甚至他们的背景，往往也能表明存在前世。鬼季中的所有玩家角色都符合“转世的灵魂”，因为他们在数十年间一次又一次地重历人生。若你需要为裁定灵堕魔的能力而判断某个生物的灵魂是否转世，进行一次 @Check[flat|dc:11]——成功则表示它拥有转世的灵魂。</p>\n<h2>灵堕魔半神</h2>\n<p>最强大的灵堕魔是半神，尽管它们的邪教相当罕见。死后易于再度转世的灵堕魔半神（例如库伽普提 Kugaptee），更恰当的称呼是“灵堕魔苦行者”。</p>\n<h2>灵堕魔叛徒</h2>\n<p>尽管大多数灵堕魔本质上都是纯粹的混乱邪恶，但传说中存在极其罕见的灵堕魔，能够挣脱自身天性并得以超升；它们死后会转世为神使（kami）或其他更为仁善的灵体，并在此过程中褪去灵堕魔特征。当然，对那些被留下的灵堕魔而言，这些“叛徒”被视作想象得到的最美味佳肴。</p>\n<h2>灵堕魔蝴蝶</h2>\n<p>各类灵堕魔最离奇的共同特征之一，是那些似乎总在它们周围盘旋、栖落于其躯体之上，或周期性地从其伤口中涌出的血红蝴蝶。这些令人不安的昆虫是灵堕魔思想的物质显化，象征着它们曾经经历却又背弃的无数前世。一旦灵堕魔蝴蝶离开其源头飞出几尺之外，便从不会存留太久，而是淡化成烟，迅速消散在空气中。</p>\n<h2>其他灵堕魔</h2>\n<p>除这几页所呈现的四种之外，还存在许多其他类型的灵堕魔。其他例子包括：会复制尸体的恪尸魔（哭泣灵堕魔）；作为社会渗透者的痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）；亵渎亡者的煞星魔（畸形灵堕魔）；以及强大而残暴的稽折魔（无头灵堕魔）。</p>\n<p>Ijdas are creatures of forgetfulness. Born from souls who were once enlightened but then renounced it and their role in the cycle of reincarnation, they curse the futility of their existence and find pleasure in leading others to the same fate.</p>\n<p>Ijdas appear as towering humanoids, their bodies bloated and constantly bursting with small red butterflies that flitter away before melting into mist. Their arms are overly long and so broken as to writhe more like tentacles, affording them an unsettling combat style with greater reach than most large creatures enjoy. They wear clothing and capes made of moldy straw and wield broken swords whose shattered blades still float roughly in place. Their most unsettling features are their complete lack of heads; instead, where a head should be sits a wicker cage filled with a writhing cloud of butterflies. Yet still, they see, hear, and speak without issue, as if their heads remained in place.</p>\n<p>Formed without heads or even brains, an idja's mind is shared among the flocks of butterflies in their head cages or bursting from their bodies, and as each of these insects escapes and fades away, these forgetful fiends lose another potential thought. Unable to learn new things, any actions they take stem from memories etched into their souls or directives they blindly follow from other nindorus or creatures they've come to accept as superiors. Their movements, words, and reactions are all conducted via a type of muscle memory based on how their souls believe they should respond to their external stimuli. As a result, most now serve as brutal guardians, since their forgetfulness also prevents them from being able to sleep.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>When an evil mortal soul that has been reincarnated multiple times is wrenched from the cycle of souls and corrupted, it can undergo a horrific transformation into a fiend known as a nindoru. A force for entropy and the breaking of cycles, nindorus are hideous creatures whose bodies often appear distorted, who wield weapons that have been shattered yet still function, and whose true face is often hidden from view. They display traits one might expect to see in an undead creature, such as decaying flesh or exposed bones, yet a nindoru is very much still alive.</p>\n<p>Each nindoru epitomizes the fracture of a specific cycle, be it one from the natural world or from societal traditions. To the nindoru, nothing is more delicious than the consumption of a creature who has reincarnated multiple times, with those who are theoretically about to ascend to true enlightenment presenting the tastiest meal. Those slain by a nindoru are themselves torn from the cycle—the lucky ones move on to the Boneyard for judgment, but many are instead corrupted to form more of these horrific fiends.</p>\n<p>Followers of Sangpotshi find nindoru to be particularly abhorrent and count them among the greatest threats imaginable. Most commonly found in regions of the world where the reincarnation cycle is strongest, nindorus are, like rakshasas and oni, associated most strongly with the Material Plane.</p>\n<h2>Reincarnated Souls</h2>\n<p>In some cases, you'll know if a creature a nindoru attacks has a reincarnated soul. Ancestries like samsarans are always reincarnated souls, and a PC's backstory or even their background can often indicate the presence of a previous life. All of the PCs in Season of Ghosts qualify as reincarnated souls, as they've relived their lives over and over for decades. If you ever need to determine if a creature's soul is reincarnated for the purpose of adjudicating a nindoru's ability, attempt a @Check[flat|dc:11]—on a success, it has a reincarnated soul.</p>\n<h2>Nindoru Demigods</h2>\n<p>The most powerful nindorus are demigods, although their cults are quite rare. Prone to reincarnation after death, nindoru demigods like Kugaptee are more properly known as \"nindoru ascetics.\"</p>\n<h2>Nindoru Traitors</h2>\n<p>While most nindorus are purely chaotic evil in nature, legends tell of exceptionally rare nindorus who manage to escape their own nature and ascend, reincarnating after death into kami or other more benevolent spirits and shedding the nindoru trait as they do so. Of course, these \"traitors\" are regarded as the most delicious meals imaginable by the nindorus left behind.</p>\n<h2>Nindoru Butterflies</h2>\n<p>One of the strangest shared traits of the various types of nindoru are the blood-red butterflies that seem to follow them around, nest on their bodies, or periodically emerge from their wounds. These unnerving insects are physical manifestations of the nindorus' thoughts and symbolize the countless past lives they once lived but turned their backs on. Nindoru butterflies never last long once they flutter more than a few feet from their source, fading away into smoke that quickly dissipates into the air.</p>\n<h2>Other Nindorus</h2>\n<p>Many other types of nindorus exist beyond the four presented on these pages. Others include the corpse-copying akashtis (sobbing nindorus), infiltrators of society known as kagekumas (lurking nindorus), the dead defiling shisagishins (crooked nindorus), and the powerful and brutal argyrzeis (headless nindorus).</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "Ijda"
        },
