            "Slurp Something Shiny": {
              "name": "啜食闪亮之物 Slurp Something Shiny",
              "description": "<p>疣儿用他的舌头打击对触及范围内一名目标持有的闪亮物体进行一次[[/act disarm]]尝试。</p>\n<p>Warty makes a [[/act disarm]] attempt with his tongue Strike against a shiny object held by a target in reach.</p>"
            },
            "Swallow Whole": {
              "name": "整个吞下 Swallow Whole",
              "description": "<p>中型，@Damage[(1d8)[bludgeoning]] 伤害，[[/act escape dc=18]] 逃脱 破裂 8</p><hr /><p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.SwallowWhole]</p>\n<p>Medium, @Damage[(1d8)[bludgeoning]] damage, [[/act escape dc=18]] Rupture 8</p><hr /><p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.SwallowWhole]</p>"
            },
            "Tongue Grab": {
              "name": "伸舌擒抓 Tongue Grab",
              "description": "<p>被疣儿的舌头命中的生物会被这只巨蟾蜍@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.kWc1fhmv9LBiTuei]{受擒}。该生物并未@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{禁足}，但它无法移动到蟾蜍舌头的触及范围之外。</p>\n<p>生物可以用一次成功的打击对 AC 15 发动攻击并造成至少 6 点挥砍伤害来切断舌头。这不会对疣儿造成伤害，但会阻止他使用舌头打击，直到他重新长出舌头为止，这需要一周。</p>\n<p>A creature hit by Warty's tongue becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.kWc1fhmv9LBiTuei]{Grabbed} by the giant toad. The creature isn't @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{Immobilized}, but it can't move beyond the reach of the toad's tongue.</p>\n<p>A creature can sever the tongue with a successful Strike against AC 15 that deals at least 6 slashing damage. This deals no damage to Warty, but prevents him from using his tongue Strike until he regrows his tongue, which takes a week.</p>"
            },
            "Grab": {
              "name": "抓取 Grab",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Grab]</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>大多数巨蟾蜍生活在干旱环境中，尤其是沙漠，并且热衷于吞食几乎任何比自己小的生物。它们以吃巨鼠而闻名，随后会接管鼠类的洞穴作为巢穴。巨蟾蜍的眼后有巨大的毒素腺体，使它们能够用毒素覆盖皮肤。这使得它们几乎没有天敌，若不加以控制，其种群数量会迅速激增。尽管大多数人认为巨蟾蜍是危险的害兽，但一些食人魔与山丘巨人群体会饲养它们，以收集其毒素供消遣之用。</p>\n<p>Most giant toads live in dry environments, particularly deserts, and eagerly eat almost any creature smaller than themselves. They're known to eat giant rats, then take over the rats' burrows as homes. Giant toads have large poison glands behind their eyes that enable them to coat their skin with poison. This leads to them having very few natural predators, and populations can quickly explode if left unchecked. While most consider giant toads dangerous pests, some groups of ogres and hill giants cultivate them to collect their poison for recreational use.</p>",
          "blurb": "变体巨蟾蜍\nVariant giant toad",
          "prototypeToken": "疣儿 Warty"
        },
        "First Home": {
          "name": "第一之家 First Home",
