        "Ittan-Momen": {
          "name": "一反木绵 Ittan-Momen",
          "tokenName": "一反木绵 Ittan-Momen",
          "items": {
            "Body": {
              "name": "身体 Body"
            },
            "Tremorsense (Imprecise) 30 feet": {
              "name": "震动感知（不精确）30 尺 Tremorsense (Imprecise) 30 feet",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Tremorsense]</p>"
            },
            "Mundane Appearance": {
              "name": "平凡外表 Mundane Appearance",
              "description": "<p>当它不移动时，例如在白天，一反木绵几乎与普通布料难以区分。它们在用于伪装成普通布料的欺骗检定和DC上，自动结果为26。</p>\n<p>When not moving, such as during the day, the ittan-momen is nearly indistinguishable from normal cloth. They have an automatic result of 26 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as normal cloth.</p>"
            },
            "Constrict": {
              "name": "绞勒 Constrict",
              "description": "<p>@Damage[1d8[bludgeoning]], @Check[fortitude|dc:18|basic]</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Constrict]</p>\n<p>@Damage[1d8[bludgeoning]], @Check[fortitude|dc:18|basic]</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Constrict]</p>"
            },
            "Engulf": {
              "name": "吞没 Engulf",
              "description": "<p>@Check[reflex|dc:18]，@Damage[(1d8+2)[bludgeoning]] 伤害，逃脱 DC 18，破裂 5</p>\n<p>一反木绵一次只能吞没一个生物。只要该生物的头部在实际上能够被一反木绵的身体覆盖，一反木绵就可以吞没比自身更大体型的生物。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Engulf]</p>\n<p>@Check[reflex|dc:18], @Damage[(1d8+2)[bludgeoning]] damage, Escape DC 18, Rupture 5</p>\n<p>The ittan-momen can Engulf only one creature. They can Engulf a creature of a larger size so long as the creature's head can feasibly be covered by the ittan-momen's body.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Engulf]</p>"
            },
            "Grab": {
              "name": "抓取 Grab",
              "description": "<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Grab]</p>"
            }
          },
          "publicNotes": "<p>诞生于大块布料之中，一反木绵在空中飘舞，捕捉着落日的最后余晖。一反木绵能从任何足够大的布料中苏醒，许多美丽却遭受残酷对待的挂毯曾将毫无防备的受害者引诱至过早的死亡。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>付丧神是由一件一百年老物体与神灵结合而成、具备智慧且能自主行动的物体。付丧神的范围从无害到恶毒不等，每个个体的性格都源自其在觉醒前被如何对待。被悉心照料的物体往往会诞生乐于帮助、友善的付丧神，而遭受虐待或被遗弃的物体则会扭曲成邪恶而暴力的存在。大多数付丧神天性顽皮，常常只想占据活着的生物的注意力。</p>\n<p>付丧神通常能在那些对爱护物体的价值抱有强烈文化信念的区域中找到；这种观念能帮助物品存续得足够久，从而成为付丧神。拥有大量付丧神的城镇与村庄因夜间付丧神的庆典而被称为“无眠之镇”；这些庆典可能喧闹到足以让活着的居民无法安然入睡。</p>\n<p>Born from large pieces of cloth, ittan-momen flutter in the air, catching the last rays of the setting sun. Ittan-momen can awaken from any sufficiently large cloth, and many beautiful but cruelly-treated tapestries have lured unsuspecting victims to an untimely end.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Tsukumogami are intelligent, mobile objects formed from the union between a 100-year-old object and a kami. Tsukumogami range from harmless to malicious, each individual personality a result of how the object was treated before its awakening. Well-cared-for objects tend to birth helpful, friendly tsukumogami, while mistreated or abandoned objects twist into malevolent and violent beings. Most tsukumogami are, by nature, mischievous, and oftentimes want nothing more than to occupy the attention of living creatures.</p>\n<p>Tsukumogami can commonly be found in areas with a strong cultural belief in the value of caring for objects, which helps items survive long enough to become tsukumogami. Towns and villages with large tsukumogami populations are referred to as \"sleepless towns\" due to the nightly tsukumogami celebrations, which can become so raucous that they prevent the living residents from sleeping peacefully.</p>",
          "prototypeToken": "一反木绵 Ittan-Momen"
        },
