          "publicNotes": "<p>这些巨大而骇人的蛛形纲生物通常从头到尾根有8英尺长。巨蝎是多种沙漠栖居生物偏爱的驮兽与战争猛兽，尤其受寇洛斯青睐。不过，它们最常见的还是出没于荒野之中。在那里，它们会在山坡洞穴中筑巢，或钻入浅薄的沙层之下潜伏，等待猎物徘徊靠近。</p>\n<hr />\n<p>蝎子是沙漠、森林、稀树草原与荒地中的甲壳天灾；它们是致命的蛛形纲生物，拥有强有力的螯与疼痛的毒刺。几乎在所有气候中都能找到蝎子，它们以耐心的潜行与蛮力相结合的方式猎捕猎物。大多数蝎子生活在地下洞穴中，要么独自狩猎，要么作为更大群落的一部分。这些蛛形纲生物令人极度畏惧且危险，以至于在许多文化中，它们被视作神祇，或被当作兼具死亡与免于该死亡之庇护的二元象征。</p>\n<p>These massive, terrifying arachnids are typically 8 feet long from head to the base of the tail. Giant scorpions are the favored pack animals and war beasts of various desert-dwelling creatures, particularly kholos. They are most commonly encountered in the wild, however. There they lair in mountainside caves or burrow beneath shallow layers of sand where they lie in wait for prey to wander near.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Chitinous scourges of deserts, forests, savannas, and badlands, scorpions are deadly arachnids with powerful pincers and a painful sting. Scorpions can be found in nearly every climate, where they hunt their prey with a mixture of patient stealth and raw strength. Most scorpions live in underground burrows, either as lone hunters or part of a larger colony. These arachnids are so feared and dangerous that in many cultures, they are treated as deities or dualistic symbols of both death and protection from said death.</p>",
          "blurb": "变体巨型蝎子\nVariant giant scorpion",
