          "publicNotes": "<p>这些源自邪恶军阀或嗜血将军的险恶灵性残骸，是由阴影与死亡构成的高大幽影。与其他缚灵一样，战争缚灵会在世界的幽暗之处作祟，但它们更可能远行更长距离以播撒恐怖或积聚影响，穿越阳光斑驳的土地时也常停留在阴暗的林间空地或不祥的废墟。战争缚灵往往傲慢，很少与同类结成群体，反而更喜欢支配由普通缚灵组成的队伍。尤其强大的死灵法师可能会强迫成群的战争缚灵为其效劳。然而，一个格外恶毒的目标——例如铲除一处光明与生命的堡垒——也可能将数只战争缚灵吸引到一起，共同为同一目的而行动。</p><h2>战争缚灵的起源</h2><p>并非每一只战争缚灵都曾是一个个体。它们中的许多会随着时间凝聚成形：在失落的灵魂不断聚积之处，多只缚灵相互融合，那些魂魄与意识被以某种方式剪断或削弱。这样的战争缚灵思考与交流时并非作为一个强大的存在，而更像是一阵喧嚣的众声——常常彼此冲突，但当它们同意协同工作时，便真正令人毛骨悚然。在虚无能量汇聚的地点，例如在虚无或在恐惧之岛，战争缚灵经常以这种方式形成。</p>\n<p>These menacing spiritual remnants of wicked warlords or bloodthirsty generals are towering specters of shadow and death. Like other wraiths, war wraiths haunt the shadowy places of the world but are more likely to travel greater distances to sow terror or amass influence, often sticking to dark glades or sinister ruins when journeying across sun-dappled lands. War wraiths tend to be arrogant and rarely form a pack with others of their kind, preferring instead to dominate groups of ordinary wraiths. A particularly powerful necromancer might compel packs of war wraiths into service. However, a particularly malevolent goal—such as eradicating a bastion of light and life—might draw several war wraiths together in a common purpose.</p><h2>War Wraith Origins</h2><p>Not every war wraith was once an individual. Many of them coalesce over time, merging from multiple wraiths where lost souls accumulate and have their spirits and consciousnesses shorn apart or undermined in some way. These war wraiths tend to think and communicate not as one potent being, but as a riot of voices—often conflicting but truly bone-chilling when they agree to work in unison. In locations where void energy focuses, such as in the Void or on the Isle of Terror, war wraiths form in this way frequently.</p>",
