            "Act 1: The Summer that never Was": {
              "name": "第一幕：从未到来的夏天 Act 1: The Summer that never Was",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Summer that never Was\">第一幕：从未存在的夏天</h1>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1>柳岸镇之死</h1>\n  <p>尽管本《冒险》路径的大部分内容发生在思维空间中，被杀死的PC仍可像往常一样通过@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.IkGYwHRLhkuoGReG]{死者复活}及类似法术复活。被杀死的PC甚至可能成为不死生物，尽管镇民不太可能欢迎如此阴森的发展。玩家也总能选择直接创建一个新角色来替代倒下的角色。这个新PC应当来自柳岸镇，从小镇“储备”的未命名NPC中挑选；不过，如果某位玩家有兴趣把一名已命名的NPC改作替补角色，这同样可行。当然，你会想要确保这个NPC不会在后续的脚本化遭遇或事件中登场——而如果他们确实会登场，那就用另一名NPC替换他们！当你到达本战役的最终幕时，PC们将会“追上”当前日期，而替补角色也可以自由加入，无需再设法把他们编进柳岸镇居民之中。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第1章：点亮长夜</h2>\n<p>PC们在森林中醒来，但他们很快发现自己的家乡已被诡异的超自然天气吞没，并遭到怪物入侵。PC们设法返回镇内并向长者们请教后，将展开数项任务以侦察局势，并采取措施重新点亮柳岸镇中央的<em>长明灯</em>。这应能驱退超自然天气，并且（但愿）为小镇恢复和平！</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第2章：夺回柳岸镇</h2>\n<p>PC们将注意力转向柳岸镇镇区，怪物们已在此盘踞固守。这里，许多镇民需要救援；而在小镇再次能够安全居住之前，同样多的诡异而阴险的生物必须被直面并击退。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第3章：柳岸镇的诅咒</h2>\n<p>PC们发现，一团被诅咒的雾墙笼罩着荒野，阻止一切试图远离城镇的旅行。被迫只能依靠手头现有之物，PC们一边帮助柳岸镇镇民从怪物入侵中恢复，一边调查那将他们困在此地的诡异诅咒可能源自何处。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第4章：鬼打墙</h2>\n<p>PC们向西行进，以直面诅咒的源头。随后他们发现，如今栖身于一处废弃旧伐木营地的那群无面怪物，不过是一股更古老、更为阴险力量的崇拜者。该实体的影响或许才是柳岸镇的诅咒真正的源头——然而那一切都位于一道无法穿透的鬼打墙之后。</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">升级进度</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">“从未存在的夏天”按四名角色进行设计。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">1</span> PC们以1级开始本次冒险。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">2</span> PC们应当在他们尝试解放柳岸镇镇区期间升至2级——如果你使用里程碑升级，那么当PC们击败目前控制柳岸镇中心地带的三名怪物头目中的第二名时，PC们应当达到2级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">3</span> PC们在开始第4章之前应当为3级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">4</span> PC们在完成第一幕时应当达到4级。</p>\n</section>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dawnstep-bridge.webp\" alt=\"Dawnstep Bridge\" data-tooltip=\"Dawnstep Bridge\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Summer that never Was\">Act 1: The Summer That Never Was</h1>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1>Death in Willowshore</h1>\n  <p>Though much of this Adventure Path takes place within a mindscape, slain PCs can be revived as usual through @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.IkGYwHRLhkuoGReG]{Raise Dead} and similar spells. A slain PC can even become undead, though the townsfolk are unlikely to welcome such a sinister development. A player can always choose to just create a new character to take the place of a fallen character. This new PC should be from Willowshore, drawn from the town's \"bank\" of unnamed NPCs, although if a player is interested in turning a named NPC into a replacement character, this could work just as well. You'll want to make sure this NPC doesn't feature in a scripted encounter or event later, of course—and if they do, to replace them with a different NPC! Once you reach the final act of this campaign, the PCs will have \"caught up\" to the current date, and replacement characters can be introduced freely without having to work them in as citizens of Willowshore.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 1: To Light the Night</h2>\n<p>The PCs wake in the forest, but they soon discover their hometown has been engulfed in eerie supernatural weather and invaded by monsters. After making their way back into town and consulting with elders, the PCs pursue several missions to scout out the situation and take steps to relight the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> in the middle of Willowshore, which should drive back the supernatural weather and, hopefully, restore peace to the town!</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 2: Reclaiming Willowshore</h2>\n<p>The PCs turn their attention to downtown Willowshore, where monsters have entrenched their position. Here, many townsfolk need rescue, and just as many strange and sinister creatures must be confronted before the town can be safely inhabited once again.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 3: The Willowshore Curse</h2>\n<p>The PCs discover that a cursed fog bank enshrouds the hinterlands, preventing all attempts to travel too far from town. Forced to rely upon what they have at hand, the PCs help the townsfolk of Willowshore recover from the monstrous invasion while investigating what could be the source of the strange curse that has trapped them in the region.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 4: The Wall of Ghosts</h2>\n<p>The PCs head west to confront the source of the curse. They then discover that the band of faceless monsters that now dwell in an abandoned lumber camp are merely worshippers of an older, more sinister force. This entity’s influence might be the actual source of the Willowshore curse—yet that lies beyond an impenetrable Wall of Ghosts.</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">Advancement Track</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">\"The Summer That Never Was\" is designed for four characters.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">1</span> The PCs begin this adventure at 1st level.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">2</span> The PCs should become 2nd level during their attempt to liberate downtown Willowshore—if you're using milestones to level up, the PCs should reach 2nd level upon defeating the second of the three monstrous ringleaders that now control central Willowshore.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">3</span> The PCs should be 3rd level before they begin Chapter 4.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">4</span> The PCs should reach 4th level by the time they complete Act 1.</p>\n</section>"
            },
