            "Act 4: To Bloom Below the Web": {
              "name": "第四幕：在蛛网之下绽放 Act 4: To Bloom Below the Web",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"To Bloom Below the Web\">第四幕：在蛛网之下绽放</h1>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第11章：柳岸镇归来</h2>\n<p>PC们已摆脱时间循环的思维空间，并将柳岸镇带回了活人的世界。然而，他们的麻烦并未就此结束。此前被困在自身思维空间中的总督官邸也一并回归——而其中潜伏着某种邪恶之物。PC们必须探索这座阴森的宅邸，同时还要保护柳岸镇，抵御一群同样怀有不祥图谋的强盗。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第12章：公主之网</h2>\n<p>络新妇公主任美璃被柳岸镇的突然再现以及PC们成为强大工具（甚至盟友）的潜力所吸引，主动与他们接触。尽管她是一位令人不安的资助者，但她的帮助与指引成为理解并击败已开始在柳岸镇让无辜者血染街巷之邪恶的关键——而这股邪恶很快会以一连串骇人听闻的残忍谋杀案显现。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第13章：横跨两界的恶魔</h2>\n<p>在任美璃的帮助下，PC们得知，早已死去的总督和善保——其失败的仪式在115年前创造了受诅咒的思维空间——相信自己注定要成为转世的灵魂：恶魔苦迦菩提。更糟的是，他的举动威胁到释放真正的苦迦菩提，而后者正处于重返生命的边缘。唯有在柳岸镇最终、骇人的思维空间中直面那已异变的总督——一个让PC们得以窥见若苦迦菩提转世后生活将会如何的思维空间——他们才能拯救自己的家园。</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">进度追踪</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">“第四幕：在蛛网之下绽放”是为四名角色设计的。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">10</span> PC们以10级开始本幕。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">11</span> PC们应在开始寻找“五季宝藏”之前达到11级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">12</span> PC们应在进入苦迦菩提的领域之前达到12级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">13</span> PC们应在冒险结束时触及13级。</p>\n</section>\n<aside>\n  <h2>孙海的命运</h2>\n  <p>木材大亨孙海是上一幕的主要反派，PC们在作为转生的魂魄踏上前往活人世界的旅程时曾与他对峙。若他被杀死，任何残余的驱魔人、巫女与佣兵都会迅速抛下唐入，任其交由村民处理，因而导致第四幕中所呈现的局势。</p>\n  <p>PC们也可能与这位木材大亨谈判出了较不暴力的解决方案。在这种情况下，孙海不仅可能仍然活着，甚至仍可能控制唐入，并试图将柳岸镇用作其伐木需求的行动基地。然而，若柳岸镇奇迹般地从废墟中崛起，他的追随者会因恐惧而抛弃他；届时孙海可以由你酌情安排，成为一名心怀怨恨、迫使PC们不得不再次面对的劲敌。</p>\n  <p>如果PC们让孙海相信移除谭杉所带来的危险，或以其他方式成功就柳岸镇的安全进行充分谈判，他会自愿放弃唐入。他送给PC们的“礼物”就是无视他们与他们的城镇，把目光投向神门的其他地方。他并不是个好人，因此“不干涉”的承诺差不多就是人们所能奢望的最好结果了。</p>\n</aside>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kugaptees-grasp.webp\" alt=\"Kugaptee's Grasp\" data-tooltip=\"Kugaptee's Grasp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"To Bloom Below the Web\">Act 4: To Bloom Below the Web</h1>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 11: Willowshore's Return</h2>\n<p>The PCs are free of the time-looped mindscape and have returned Willowshore to the living world. However, their troubles don’t end here. The governor’s manor, previously trapped in its own mindscape, has returned as well—and something evil lurks within it. The PCs must explore the sinister manor while also protecting Willowshore from a group of bandits who have an equally ominous agenda.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 12: The Princess's Web</h2>\n<p>The jorogumo princess Ren Mei Li, intrigued by Willowshore’s sudden reappearance and the PCs’ potential to become powerful instruments (or even allies), initiates contact with them. Although she’s an unsettling benefactor, her help and guidance prove key to understanding and defeating the evil that has begun spilling the blood of innocents in Willowshore—evil that soon manifests in a string of grisly murders.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 13: A Fiend in Two Worlds</h2>\n<p>With Ren Mei Li’s help, the PCs learn that the long-dead governor Heh Shan-Bao, whose botched ritual created the cursed mindscape 115 years ago, believes he’s destined to become the reincarnated fiend Kugaptee. Worse, his efforts threaten to free the actual Kugaptee, who’s on the cusp of returning to life. Only by confronting the transformed governor in a final, horrific mindscape of Willowshore—one that gives the PCs a glimpse of what life might be like should Kugaptee reincarnate—can they save their home.</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">Advancement Track</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">\"Act 4: To Bloom Below the Web\" is designed for four characters.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">10</span> The PCs begin this act at 10th level.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">11</span> The PCs should be 11th level before they begin seeking the Five-Season Treasures.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">12</span> The PCs should be 12th level before they enter Kugaptee's realm.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">13</span> The PCs should reach 13th level by the end of the adventure.</p>\n</section>\n<aside>\n  <h2>Mago Kai's Fate</h2>\n  <p>The lumber baron Mago Kai was the previous act's primary antagonist, and the PCs confronted him during their journey into the living world as transmigrated spirits. If he was slain, any remaining exorcists, shrine maidens, and mercenaries swiftly abandon Karahai to its villagers, resulting in the situation as presented in Act 4.</p>\n  <p>It's possible that the PCs negotiated a less violent solution with the lumber baron. In this case, not only might Mago Kai still be alive, he could even still control Karahai and seek to use Willowshore as a base of operations for his logging needs. If Willowshore has miraculously risen from ruins, though, his followers abandon him out of fear, and Mago Kai can, at your discretion, become a bitter rival the PCs will be forced to confront once more.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs convinced Mago Kai of the danger posed by removing the Tan Sugi or otherwise managed to negotiate fully for Willowshore's safety, he abandons Karahai willingly. His gift to the PCs is to ignore them and their town, setting his sights elsewhere in Shenmen. He isn't a very good person, so a promise of noninterference is about the best one can hope for.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Act 3: No Breath to Cry": {
              "name": "第三幕：欲泣无息 Act 3: No Breath to Cry",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"No Breath to Cry\">第三幕：欲泣无息</h1>\n\n<h2 data-no-toc>第8章：真相的湮灭</h2>\n<p>英雄们远征归来，返回柳岸镇，试图找到失踪的总督和善保，并解开他们被囚禁在神秘思维空间中的最终秘密。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第9章：直面死亡</h2>\n<p>英雄们手握一项前景可期、或能解救他们的仪式，必须帮助柳岸镇熬过神门残酷的寒冬，以及前来造访小镇的更残忍的生物。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第10章：此地归我</h2>\n<p>英雄们终于有机会直面那些试图抹除他们及其所知一切的势力，终于为柳岸镇的救赎开辟出一条道路。</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">升级进度</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">“欲泣无息”是为四名角色设计的。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">7</span>PC应以第7等级开始本幕。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">8</span>PC应在击败他们的无面鬼替身时达到第8等级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">9</span>PC应在抵达孙海的要塞时达到第9等级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">10</span>PC应在完成第三幕时达到第10等级。</p>\n</section>\n<aside>\n  <h2>我们真的死了吗？</h2>\n  <p>在本幕第一章末尾，PC发现一个令人震惊的真相：他们不仅被困在思维空间中——他们已经死了。总督和善保以一种可能让他们觉得他在撒谎、或只是搞错了的方式，将这件事揭示给PC。随着剧情推进到第9章，这个真相会愈发明显；到了第10章展开时，PC应当接受这一发展，并将注意力放在如何纠正它上。</p>\n  <p>尽管如此，有些团可能会被这一剧情反转分散注意力。如果你发现你的团因为“他们的PC已死，并且这段时间基本一直是幽灵（特征）”这一揭示而跑偏或感到挫败，可以考虑把情况解释得更像是：他们曾被杀死，但又在这个新区域中复活或以转世的灵魂的形式重获新生；并且只要继续研究和善保已着手的解决方案，他们就能修复他造成的局面。</p>\n</aside>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-risen-from-death.webp\" alt=\"Risen from Death\" data-tooltip=\"Risen from Death\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"No Breath to Cry\">Act 3: No Breath to Cry</h1>\n\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 8: Oblivion of Truth</h2>\n<p>Returning to Willowshore from their expedition, the heroes attempt to find the missing governor, Heh Shan-Bao, and unlock the final secrets to their imprisonment within their mysterious mindscape.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 9: Face-to-Face with Death</h2>\n<p>With a promising ritual that could free them in hand, the heroes must help Willowshore survive Shenmen’s cruel winter and the crueler creatures that come to visit their town.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 10: This Place Is Ours</h2>\n<p>The heroes finally have a chance to confront the forces that seek to erase them and everything they know, opening a path for Willowshore’s salvation at last.</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">Advancement Track</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">\"No Breath to Cry\" is designed for four characters.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">7</span> The PCs should begin this act at 7th level.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">8</span> The PCs should be 8th level by the time they defeat their noppera-bo doubles.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">9</span> The PCs should be 9th level by the time they reach Mago Kai's fort.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">10</span> The PCs should reach 10th level by the time they complete Act 3.</p>\n</section>\n<aside>\n  <h2>Are We Really Dead?</h2>\n  <p>At the end of this act's first chapter, the PCs discover an astonishing truth: they aren't just trapped in a mindscape—they're dead. Governor Heh Shan-Bao reveals this truth to the PCs in a way that might make them think he's lying to them, or perhaps that he's simply wrong. As the act progresses into Chapter 9, this truth becomes increasingly apparent; by the time Chapter 10 takes place, the PCs should accept this development and be focused on fixing it.</p>\n  <p>Still, some groups might become distracted by this plot twist. If you find that your group is side-tracked or frustrated by the revelation that their PCs are dead and have essentially been ghosts this whole time, consider explaining the situation to be more akin to them having been killed only to be resurrected or reincarnated in this new area, and that by continuing to research the solution Heh Shan-Bao started, they'll be able to fix the situation he caused.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Act 2: Let the Leaves Fall": {
              "name": "第二幕：任叶飘落 Act 2: Let the Leaves Fall",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Let the Leaves Fall\">第二幕：任落叶飘零</h1>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第5章：四时更迭</h2>\n<p>PC们与镇上的长者合作，制定——并付诸实施——一项计划，为柳岸镇即将到来的冬季做准备。然而，随着数周过去，诡异的超自然事件开始困扰镇民，而想要找到答案，就不可避免地必须把目光投向鬼打墙之外。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第6章：踏险斩祸一道清</h2>\n<p>PC们设计出一项仪式来洞开鬼打墙，并在迈步穿过之后，踏上朝圣之径：这是一段从柳岸镇前往谭杉寺的传统冥想之旅，他们希望答案就在彼端等候。然而，诅咒也延伸到了这里，并且力量更加强大。在PC们完成旅程之前，他们将直面超自然风暴、可怕的怪物威胁，以及闹鬼的神龛。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第7章：睿智遗墟</h2>\n<p>谭杉寺已成废墟，但更糟的是，它还被邪魔怪物与背弃根源的不死僧侣所掌控。为了得知关于折磨他们城镇之诅咒本质的宝贵秘密，PC们必须净化寺院，并击败在其内部生根的邪恶。</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">进度追踪</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">“任落叶飘零”以四名角色为设计基准。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">4</span> PC们以第4等级开始本幕。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">5</span> PC们在尝试踏上朝圣之径之前应达到第5等级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">6</span> PC们在探索谭杉寺之前应达到第6等级。</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">7</span> PC们应在完成第二幕时达到第7等级。</p>\n</section>\n<aside>\n  <h1>让他们打起来！</h1>\n  <p>尽管本冒险的第2章与第3章包含大量经典战斗与探索内容，但“任落叶飘零”的第1章则完全聚焦于PC们必须推进的多种休整模式活动，以在他们为柳岸镇备冬并进一步了解折磨城镇的诅咒的征程中取得进展。因此，在本冒险时间线的大部分阶段，战斗机会并不多；第2章与第3章的事件甚至可能只占据短短几周。虽然有些队伍会乐于抓住机会进行角色扮演并推进休整模式活动，但你也可能发现你的队伍会不时渴望打一场。在这种情况下，你可以在荒野中加入与危险生物的遭遇，甚至安排某个怪物或一群怪物对镇内某处地点发动潜在的突袭。你也可以按需将第1章后半段出现的一些闹鬼事件调整为与不死的战斗。</p>\n</aside>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-spider-tree.webp\" alt=\"Spider Tree\" data-tooltip=\"Spider Tree\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Let the Leaves Fall\">Act 2: Let the Leaves Fall</h1>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 5: Turning of the Seasons</h2>\n<p>The PCs work with the town elder to create—and then act on—a plan to prepare the town of Willowshore for the coming winter. As the weeks roll on, though, strange supernatural events begin to trouble townsfolk, and the need to look beyond the Wall of Ghosts for answers becomes unavoidable.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 6: The Enlightened Path</h2>\n<p>The PCs devise a ritual to open the Wall of Ghosts and, upon stepping through, set foot upon the Pilgrim’s Path: the traditional meditative journey from Willowshore to the Tan Sugi monastery, where they hope answers await. The curse extends here, however, and with even greater power. Before the PCs finish the journey, they’ll face supernatural storms, monstrous threats, and haunted shrines.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>Chapter 7: In the Ruins of Wisdom</h2>\n<p>The Tan Sugi monastery lies in ruins, but worse, it’s also in the grips of fiendish monsters and undead monks who have turned their backs on tradition. In order to learn valuable secrets about the nature of the curse afflicting their town, the PCs must purify the monastery and defeat the evil that has taken root within.</p>\n<section class=\"advancement-track\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc style=\"margin-left:2ch\">Advancement Track</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin-left:2ch\">\"Let the Leaves Fall\" is designed for four characters.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">4</span> The PCs begin this act at 4th level.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">5</span> The PCs should be 5th level before they attempt to walk the Pilgrim's Path.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">6</span> The PCs should be 6th level before they explore Tan Sugi Monastery.</p>\n  <p><span class=\"level\">7</span> The PCs should reach 7th level by the time they complete Act 2.</p>\n</section>\n<aside>\n  <h1>Let Them Fight!</h1>\n  <p>While Chapters 2 and 3 of this adventure feature plenty of classic combat and exploration, the first chapter of “Let the Leaves Fall” is focused entirely on a wide range of downtime activities the PCs must pursue in their quest to prepare Willowshore for winter and to learn more about the curse afflicting the town. As such, there are few opportunities for combat during the bulk of this adventure’s timeline, with the events of Chapters 2 and 3 potentially filling only a few weeks. While some groups will welcome the chance to roleplay and pursue downtime activities, you might find your group is eager for a fight now and then. In this case, you can add encounters with dangerous creatures in the wilds, or even a potential raid from a monster or group of monsters against a location in town. You can also adjust some of the hauntings found in the later part of Chapter 1 into combats against undead if you wish.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Kishotenketsu": {
              "name": "起承转合 Kishotenketsu",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Kishotenketsu\">起承转合</h1>\n<p>在<em>《鬼季》冒险道</em>中，PC们成为柳岸镇的救星，带领同为镇民的伙伴从被困于生与死之间的境地脱身，再度迈入现代时代——前提是他们能在一名贪婪木材大亨的阴谋算计与一名尚未完全死去的邪魔之影响下幸存。</p>\n<p>这条冒险道并非建立在遵循“开端–发展–结局”模式的三幕式故事结构上（许多Paizo的冒险道都采用这种三幕式模型），而是采用被称为起承转合的经典四幕框架——这是一种源自中国、韩国与日本叙事传统的故事结构。本冒险道的四幕也据此进行编排：第一幕介绍故事、设定与角色，同时呈现核心问题与关键剧情点。第二幕让剧情行动走到台前，故事逐步升级。第三幕引入出人意料的转折或关键节点，并作为剧情的高潮。最后一幕聚焦故事的结果与余波，收束事件，并探讨从中得到的教训。为了帮助管理预期，在开玩之前让你的玩家熟悉这种幕结构会很有帮助！</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Kishotenketsu\">Kishotenketsu</h1>\n<p>In the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em>, the PCs become saviors of the town of Willowshore and lead their fellow townsfolk from being trapped between life and death to emerge once more into the modern era—provided they can survive the machinations of a greedy lumber baron and the influence of a not-quite-dead fiend.</p>\n<p>This Adventure Path isn’t built on a three-act story structure that follows a “beginning–middle–end” pattern (a three-act model that is used for many of Paizo’s Adventure Paths), but instead on the classic four-act framework known as kishotenketsu, which is a traditional story structure of Chinese, Korean, and Japanese narratives. The four acts of this Adventure Path are organized accordingly. The first act introduces the story, setting, and characters while presenting the central issues and plot points. The second act is when the action of the plot takes center stage and the story escalates. The third introduces an unexpected twist or turning point in the storyline and serves as the plot’s climax. Finally, the last act focuses on the results and ramifications of the story, concludes the events, and explores lessons learned. It can be helpful to familiarize your players with this act structure before play in order to help manage expectations!</p>"
            },
            "Campaign Timeline": {
              "name": "战役时间线 Campaign Timeline",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Campaign Timeline\">战役时间线</h1>\n<p>以下列出了导致<em>鬼季冒险路径</em>开始的关键事件。注意：这些日期使用的是帝国历，而非艾巴萨罗姆纪年。要将日期换算为艾巴萨罗姆纪年，将年份减去2,500。</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>日期</th>\n      <th>事件</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6223 IC</td>\n      <td>一位名为谭隋靖的英雄冒险者击败了强大的邪魔苦迦菩提，但在战斗结束时她也随之死去。她的遗体在苦迦菩提的残骸上长出一棵杉树，将邪魔困在树根之下，阻止他复活归来。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7020</td>\n      <td>偏远村落柳岸镇由一位名为@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}的追随者@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}建立。她在山地腹地修建了一座善解修道院，并将谭隋靖的杉树（也因此是苦迦菩提的坟墓）纳入修道院庭院的中心。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7054</td>\n      <td>智惠因自然原因去世。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7060</td>\n      <td>柳岸镇成为一座伐木城镇。本地的善解传统日渐式微。谭杉寺的僧侣失去了智惠的指引，彼此争吵并弃寺离去。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7062</td>\n      <td>赭城的领袖周冥瑕将其子送往柳岸镇，试图采伐那棵辉煌的杉树。他的尝试失败了，但却使苦迦菩提的影响得以扩散，导致一场神秘悲剧，后来被称为断刀夜。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7102</td>\n      <td>和善保受龙瓦任命，入主柳岸镇，成为总督。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7106</td>\n      <td>预言破灭之年开始。龙瓦帝国崩溃。神门的官员与中央断绝联系，转而屈从于贪婪，变得残酷并虐待平民。和善保总督竭力让柳岸镇免受这些事件波及。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7107</td>\n      <td>神门落入络新妇“琅珞伊”之手。年迈的周冥瑕仍为赭城统治者，却遭杀害，但以幽魂之身归来。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7108</td>\n      <td>和善保试图施行仪式以治愈谭杉寺并封印苦迦菩提，希望借此保护村落免受邪魔日益增长的影响与力量侵袭，但仪式失败，柳岸镇的人民在睡梦中死去。柳岸镇的两处平行思维空间由此生成，其中一处将被杀的镇民困在生死之间的领域里。和善保尝试作最后的挣扎以自救，却反而独自被困在第二处思维空间中——它卡在柳岸镇与生者领域之间：闹鬼之中又套着闹鬼。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7223</td>\n      <td>当下。马戈·凯开始策划将柳岸镇变为新的旧伐木营地，并着手安排对柳岸镇进行大规模驱魔与净化。这些行动对柳岸镇思维空间的循环造成了足够的扰动，使得PC们在115年来第一次有可能挣脱他们所承受的时间回路。</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>保留惊喜</h1>\n  <p>这条冒险路径中有数个惊喜等待玩家在游玩过程中揭开，最显著的是：他们一直被困在生死之间的时间回路中；并且如果他们想回到现实世界，就必须通过转生术回到旧躯体里，或进入全新的躯体。即便这些惊喜有一部分或全部提前被玩家得知，这条冒险路径仍然完全可以顺利运作；但你或许会希望在战役开始时就让玩家知道，这条冒险路径包含一些剧情反转，并且如果某位玩家碰巧知道其中一部分或全部，请将这些信息保留在自己心中，以为同桌的其他人保留惊喜。</p>\n  <p>如果你的玩家有一部分或全部很早就推理出了真相，或这些剧情反转已被剧透，请克制住在最后一刻为了“保留惊喜”而更改走向的冲动，因为体验一条被你正确预料的故事线同样令人满足。取而代之的是，既不要确认也不要否定正确的猜测；只需提醒玩家：“我们到最后看看事情会如何发展，不就知道了吗？”</p>\n</aside>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Campaign Timeline\">Campaign Timeline</h1>\n<p>Key events that led to the start of the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em> are presented below. Note that these dates use the Imperial Calendar, not Absalom Reckoning. To convert a date to Absalom Reckoning, subtract 2,500 from the year.</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Date</th>\n      <th>Event</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6223 IC</td>\n      <td>A heroic adventurer named Tan Sui-Jing defeats the powerful fiend Kugaptee but dies herself as the battle concludes. Her body sprouts a sugi tree over Kugaptee’s remains, trapping the fiend below the roots and preventing him from returning to life.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7020</td>\n      <td>The remote village of Willowshore is founded by a follower of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi} named @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}. She builds a Sangpotshi monastery in the mountain hinterlands, incorporating Tan Sui-Jing’s sugi tree (and thus Kugaptee’s grave) at the heart of the monastery’s courtyard.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7054</td>\n      <td>Zhi Hui passes away of natural causes.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7060</td>\n      <td>Willowshore becomes a lumber town. Local Sangpotshi traditions dwindle. The monks of the Tan Sugi monastery, bereft of Zhi Hui’s guidance, bicker and abandon the monastery.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7062</td>\n      <td>Chou Mingxia, the leader of the city of Sze, sends her son to Willowshore, where he attempts to harvest the glorious sugi tree. His attempt fails but does allow Kugaptee’s influence to spread, resulting in a mysterious tragedy that would come to be known as the Night of Broken Blades.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7102</td>\n      <td>Governor Heh Shan-Bao is installed at Willowshore by Lung Wa.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7106</td>\n      <td>Age of Lost Omens begins. Lung Wa empire collapses. Government officials in Shenmen are cut off, and they succumb to greed, becoming cruel and abusive to the common folk. Governor Heh does his best to shelter Willowshore from these events.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7107</td>\n      <td>Shenmen falls under the control of the jorogumo Lang Loi. Elderly Chou Mingxia, still the ruler of Sze, is slain but returns as a ghost.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7108</td>\n      <td>The people of Willowshore perish in their sleep when Heh Shan-Bao attempts and fails to perform a ritual to heal the Tan Sugi and seal off Kugaptee in hopes of protecting the village from the fiend’s growing influence and power. Two parallel mindscapes of Willowshore are created, one trapping the slain townsfolk in a realm between life and death. Heh Shan-Bao tries a last-ditch effort to save himself but instead becomes trapped alone in the second mindscape lodged between Willowshore and the living realm—a haunting within a haunting.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7223</td>\n      <td>Present day. Mago Kai begins his plans to turn Willowshore into a new lumber camp and starts orchestrating a mass exorcism and cleansing of Willowshore. These efforts cause enough of a disruption in the cycle of the Willowshore mindscape that, for the first time in 115 years, the PCs are potentially able to break free from the time loop they’ve endured.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Preserving Surprises</h1>\n  <p>This Adventure Path has several surprises for the players to uncover as they play, most notably that they’ve been trapped in a time loop in between life and death, and that if they want to return to the real world, they’ll have to reincarnate back into either their old bodies or entirely new ones. The Adventure Path still works fine if some or all of these surprises are spoiled for players, but you might want to let your players know when the campaign begins that the Adventure Path includes some plot twists, and that if a player happens to know some or all of them, to please keep that knowledge to themselves to preserve the surprise for the others at the table.</p>\n  <p>If some or all of your players figure things out early or have had these plot twists spoiled, resist the urge to change the developments at the last minute to “preserve surprise,” since it can be just as satisfying to experience a storyline that you’ve correctly anticipated. Instead, neither confirm nor deny correct guesses; simply remind the players, “We’ll see how it all plays out by the end, won’t we?”</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Arachnophobia Advice": {
              "name": "蜘蛛恐惧症建议 Arachnophobia Advice",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Arachnophobia Advice\">蜘蛛恐惧症建议</h3>\n<p>和所有恐怖主题的游戏一样，在一开始就开诚布公地讨论战役内容很重要。并不是每个人对每一种恐怖套路都同样自在；如果能提前知道你的一些玩家是否希望某些元素被弱化或彻底移除，那么当你作为GM努力为整个桌面呈现愉快的体验时，这将对你有极大的帮助！</p>\n<p>尤其需要注意的是蜘蛛及蜘蛛主题的意象与要素的使用。神门是一片由络新妇统治的土地——这些怪物将蜘蛛令人不安的特征与人类熟悉的形态融合在一起。在这场冒险中，蜘蛛会经常出现，既可能是盟友，也可能是敌人。如果你的玩家有人深受蜘蛛恐惧症困扰，考虑将本战役中的插画藏匿起来，并用一些不那么令人不适的生物来替换蜘蛛主题的生物。在这种情况下，最好选择一种仍然令人不安的动物，以便保留战役的恐怖氛围；但当你在蟾蜍、蛇、秃鹫、蠕虫、苍蝇以及其他所有可能的替代选项之间做选择时，始终要把玩家的感受放在心上。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Arachnophobia Advice\">Arachnophobia Advice</h3>\n<p>As with all horror-themed games, it’s important at the onset to have an open talk about the campaign’s contents. Not every person is equally comfortable with every horror trope, and knowing in advance if some of your players prefer certain elements to be downplayed or removed entirely is an immense help to you as the GM when you’re working to present an enjoyable experience for the table!</p>\n<p>Of particular note is the use of spiders and spider-themed imagery and themes. Shenmen is a land ruled by jorogumo—monsters that blend the unsettling features of spiders with the familiar shapes of humanity. Spiders feature often in this adventure as both allies and foes as well. If you have players who struggle with arachnophobia, consider keeping the artwork in this campaign hidden, and replace the spider-themed creatures with something less upsetting. In this case, it’s best to choose an animal that’s still unsettling so as to preserve the horror of the campaign, but when you’re choosing between toads and snakes and vultures and worms and flies and all the rest of the potential substitutions, always keep the considerations of your players in mind.</p>"
            },
            "Fearful Moods vs. Frustrating Foes": {
              "name": "恐惧情绪 vs. 令人沮丧的对手 Fearful Moods vs. Frustrating Foes",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Fearful Moods vs. Frustrating Foes\">恐惧氛围 vs. 令人沮丧的敌人</h3>\n<p><em>鬼季冒险路径</em>是一场恐怖主题的战役，但其恐怖的根源与营造恐惧的方法来自战役的氛围，而非战斗——这条冒险路径更接近哥特式恐怖的传统，而非生存恐怖的传统。因此，本战役中的战斗并非旨在特别严苛，尤其是在第一幕期间。如果你和你的玩家希望战斗更具挑战性，并想在每场战斗中调高危险的感受，可以考虑在部分战斗中加入额外敌人，或通过安排让PC们更少时间休息与恢复，或在收集资源方面更为吃力。多数情况下你应避免提高生物等级，因为这可能会让战斗变得比你预期更严苛。但在你进行任何这些调整之前，先按原文方式运行看看——让情境的恐怖从主题与氛围中自然浮现。随着玩家逐渐认识居住在柳岸镇的众多NPC，对那些并非英雄之人的安危产生担忧，也能进一步提升紧张感。</p>\n<p>如果你确实选择调整战斗难度，请与团体保持沟通，确保你没有把强度推得太过头。记住，对“难”与“不难”的感受取决于你坐在GM屏风的哪一侧！</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Fearful Moods vs. Frustrating Foes\">Fearful Moods vs. Frustrating Foes</h3>\n<p>The <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em> is a horror-themed campaign, but its traditions of horror and methods of building fear come from the campaign’s mood, not from its combats—this Adventure Path is more akin to gothic horror traditions than survival horror traditions. As such, the combats in this campaign are not intended to be particularly punishing, especially during the first act. If you and your players seek more challenging combats and want to dial up the perception of danger in every battle, consider adding additional foes to some of the battles or staging things so that the PCs have less time to rest and recover or struggle more to gather resources. You should avoid increasing creature levels for the most part, since this can skew battles to be more punishing than you might expect. But before you make any of these adjustments, consider running things the way they’re written first—let the horror of the situation arise from the themes and mood. As the players get to know the many NPCs who dwell in the town of Willowshore, fear for the safety of those who aren’t heroes can further build the intensity.</p>\n<p>If you do choose to adjust the combat difficulty, maintain a dialogue with your group to make sure you’re not pushing things too far. Remember, the perception of what’s difficult or not depends on which side of the GM Screen you’re sitting at!</p>"
            },
            "Playing Season of Ghosts": {
              "name": "游玩《鬼季》 Playing Season of Ghosts",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Playing Season of Ghosts\">游玩鬼季</h2>\n<p>《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》是一份可在 paizo.com 获取的免费 PDF。本冒险假定玩家会使用该文档来协助构建他们的角色，但如果你选择在战役中不使用《玩家指南》，请让你的玩家知道：这条冒险路径并非设定在当代时代——而是发生在预言破灭之年潜伏期开始后的数年，即 7108 年。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Playing Season of Ghosts\">Playing Season of Ghosts</h2>\n<p>The <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em> is a free PDF available at paizo.com. This adventure assumes the players use that document to help build their characters, but if you choose not to use the Player’s Guide in your campaign, let your players know that this Adventure Path isn’t set in a contemporary time—it instead takes place a few years after the onset of the Age of Lost Omens, in the year of 7108.</p>"
            },
            "Welcome to Willowshore": {
              "name": "欢迎来到柳岸镇 Welcome to Willowshore",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Welcome to Willowshore\">欢迎来到柳岸镇</h1>\n<p>“第一幕：从未存在过的夏天”始于柳岸镇，这是一处与世隔绝、自给自足的聚居地，年复一年靠着定期的供奉与仪式勉强维生，以此抵御鬼魂与怪物。如今，柳岸镇已被遗弃且闹鬼，但在<em>《鬼季》冒险路径</em>的大部分游玩时间里，行动发生在小镇那如幻似真的思维空间中——PC与村民的灵魂都被困在那里，已逾一个世纪。在这里，他们在不知情的情况下，一遍又一遍地重复同样阴郁的一年，并未意识到自己曾被他们的总督和善保意外杀死。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>神门</h1>\n  <p>天夏的一些国家更直接地受到某些现实文化的启发，而神门的灵感则主要来自取材于大量现实故事的恐怖传统。它是一个虚构国家，并不意在代表这些超自然恐怖传统之外的任何事物。在这个国家的历史中，它曾被龙瓦征服，接纳了来自花国的移民，并曾被络新妇夺取统治。因此，它呈现出文化混融，其人民在姓名与地名上也吸收了多种语言的词汇。在神门，鬼魂与怪物是生活中非常真实的一部分，而人们所采取的种种做法并非出于迷信，而是出于必要。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>当这些被困住的灵魂在不自知中一遍又一遍地重复 ic 7108 年时，活人的世界却继续前行。一个世纪之间，柳岸镇逐渐荒废成废墟，尽管曾有几次敷衍却注定失败的尝试想要收复这处聚居地。直到当下这一年——ic 7223 年——一项真正有分量的重建柳岸镇的行动才终于开始。</p>\n<p>在周冥瑕——泽城幽魂统治者——的命令下，一位名为孙海的木材大亨将目光投向了柳岸镇。孙海是泽城残酷成功范例之一，但当数场灾害导致他在其他旧伐木营地被迫停业时，为了履行他对周冥瑕作出的承诺，他不得不把视野投向远离泽城的地方。孙海的斥候发现柳岸镇的废墟后，他以迅疾而迫切的态势着手接管这处聚居地；在发现柳岸镇破败到无法居住后，他在附近一座名为唐入的海岸要塞建立了行动基地。然而，孙海在这座废弃小镇中看到了潜力——只要动用他手头尚存的资源重建柳岸镇，他就知道自己能赶在明年春天向周冥瑕供奉之前开始获利。</p>\n<p>但只有一个问题：柳岸镇的废墟闹鬼。村落的幽灵居民包括那些早已死去、也早已被困住的镇民……以及PC。</p>\n<p>对身处柳岸镇思维空间的人而言，那是 ic 7108 年夏季的第一天，正处在所谓鬼季的开端；此时幽魂之森的闹鬼现象、不安的灵体与亡灵活动都会变得更加频繁。每一年，当 ic 7109 年春季的最后一天结束时，思维空间及其被困住的居民都会重置回 ic 7108 年夏季的第一天。随着生者领域的时间不断向前，这一循环反复上演，直到 ic 7223 年孙海到来——距离柳岸镇的覆灭整整 115 年。</p>\n<p>正是在柳岸镇的那个夏日第一天——同一个夏天的第 115 个“第一天”，而思维空间的居民对此一无所知——这场战役由此开始。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Welcome to Willowshore\">Welcome to Willowshore</h1>\n<p>“Act 1: The Summer That Never Was” begins in Willowshore, an isolated, self-sufficient settlement that scrapes by year after year with regular offerings and rituals designed to keep the ghosts and monsters at bay. Today, Willowshore is abandoned and haunted, but for much of the playtime of the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em>, the action takes place in a phantasmagoric mindscape of the town where the souls of the PCs and villagers alike have been trapped for over a century. Here, they unwittingly repeat the same dismal year again and again, unaware that they were accidentally slain by their governor, Heh Shan-Bao.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Shenmen</h1>\n  <p>While some nations in Tian Xia are inspired more closely by certain real-life cultures, Shenmen is instead primarily inspired by horror traditions taken from a wide range of real-world stories. It’s a fictional nation and isn’t meant to represent more than these traditions of supernatural horror. During this nation’s history, it was conquered by Lung Wa, picked up immigrants from Hwanggot, and was taken over by jorogumo. It has a mix of cultures as a result, and its people have adopted words from multiple languages for their names and places. In Shenmen, ghosts and monsters are a very real part of life, and the practices employed by its people arise not from superstition but from necessity.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>While these trapped souls unknowingly repeat the year 7108 ic over and over, the living world moved on. Over the course of a century, Willowshore fell into ruin, despite a few half-hearted but doomed attempts to reclaim the settlement. It isn’t until the current year, 7223 ic, that a significant effort to reclaim Willowshore finally begins.</p>\n<p>At the command of Chou Mingxia, the ghostly ruler of the city of Sze, a lumber baron named Mago Kai turned his sights to Willowshore. Mago Kai is one of Sze’s cruel success stories, but when several disasters caused closures at his other lumber camps, he was forced to look further afield from Sze to honor the commitments he’d made to Chou Mingxia. When Mago’s scouts discovered the ruins of Willowshore, he set upon the settlement with swift urgency, establishing a base of operations at a nearby coastal fortress named Karahai after finding Willowshore to be in an unlivable state of disrepair. However, Mago Kai sees potential in the abandoned town—if he uses what resources he still has to rebuild Willowshore, he knows he can turn a profit in time for next spring’s offering to Chou Mingxia.</p>\n<p>There’s only one problem: the ruins of Willowshore are haunted. The village’s spectral inhabitants include its long-dead and long-trapped citizens... and the PCs.</p>\n<p>To those within Willowshore’s mindscape, it’s the first day of summer in the year 7108, just at the beginning of the so-called season of ghosts, when Specterwood sees an increase in activity from hauntings, restless spirits, and undead. Every year, on the final day of spring in 7109, the mindscape and its trapped inhabitants reset back to that first day of summer in 7108. This cycle has repeated itself over and over as time in the living realm marched onward, until the arrival of Mago Kai in the year 7223, a full 115 years after Willowshore’s doom.</p>\n<p>It’s that first day of summer in Willowshore—the 115th first day of that same summer, unknown to the mindscape’s inhabitants—when this campaign begins.</p>"
            },
            "Campaign Overview": {
              "name": "战役概览 Campaign Overview",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Campaign Overview\"><span>战役概览</span></h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Heh Shan-Bao\" alt=\"middle aged male noble\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp')\" />\n<p>神门并不总是一片闹鬼之地。不久前，怪物与幽灵还只是睡前故事；这片人口稀少的省份的居民以祖先口耳相传的历史为傲，讲述他们在面对所遭遇的恐怖时依然坚韧不屈。然而，他们自己的日常生活面对的却是一种不那么超自然的威胁：来自龙华帝国的压迫。</p>\n<p>龙华并非有意苛待神门，但帝国把派驻神门当作惩罚政客与士兵的手段——这是一份“被打发到穷乡僻壤的不受欢迎差事”——从而造成了一个压迫的循环。只要白银与上等木材仍不断出口到上龙华地区，神门被任命的总督与守卫便大多任其自行其是。</p>\n<p>多年下来，地方政府愈发腐败。龙华把他们送来此省，本是要教训他们学会谦卑；可他们反倒明白了：只要能为上级产出货物，便可以用任何最有利于自己的方式经营各自的采邑。</p>\n<p>龙华崩溃后，这种局面只变得更加糟糕。再无上位者约束，神门的领袖们露出了真面目，成了专制者与暴君——但这并未持续太久。神门历史中的幽灵与怪物从未真正离去——它们只是一直在等待。当它们自罗网山脉席卷而下，并从幽魂之森最深的山谷中现身时，神门的腐败统治者最先倒下。</p>\n<p>这次复苏并未给神门人民带来喘息。它不过是换了一批看守者而已，因为许多被屠戮的领袖死后化作幽灵，或干脆变成了怪物。如今，人们在恐惧中度日，并以年度传统（例如柳岸镇的“鬼季”）来确保定期献上合宜的供品，以换取在惶惶不安中再苟活一年。</p>\n<img class=\"chapter-image\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-death-comes-to-willowshore.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-death-comes-to-willowshore.webp')\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Campaign Overview\"><span>Campaign Overview</span></h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Heh Shan-Bao\" alt=\"middle aged male noble\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp')\" />\n<p>Shenmen wasn’t always a haunted land. Not so long ago, monsters and ghosts were bedtime stories; the citizens of the sparsely populated province had a proud oral history of their ancestors’ resilience despite the terrors they faced. But their own day-to-day lives instead faced a less supernatural threat: oppression from the empire of Lung Wa.</p>\n<p>Lung Wa didn’t intentionally treat Shenmen poorly, but the empire’s practice of using postings to Shenmen to punish politicians and soldiers with an “undesirable assignment in the backwoods” created a cycle of oppression. As long as silver and fine lumber continued to be exported to greater Lung Wa, Shenmen’s appointed governors and guards were mostly left to their own devices.</p>\n<p>Over the years, the local government grew more corrupt. Those whom Lung Wa had sent to the province to be taught a lesson in humility instead learned that, as long as they produced goods for their superiors, they could run their own fiefdoms in whatever way best served themselves.</p>\n<p>This situation only grew worse after Lung Wa’s collapse. With no one above them, the leaders of Shenmen showed their true colors and became despots and tyrants—but not for long. The ghosts and monsters of Shenmen’s history had never truly left—they’d merely been waiting. When they swept down from the Gossamer Mountains and emerged from the deepest vales of Specterwood, Shenmen’s corrupt leaders were the first to fall.</p>\n<p>This resurgence was no reprieve for the people of Shenmen. It was merely a changing of the guard, as many of the slaughtered leaders rose from death as ghosts or transformed into monsters themselves. Today, the people live lives of fear, with annual traditions (such as Willowshore’s “season of ghosts”) in place to ensure proper offerings are regularly given in return for one more year of fearful subsistence.</p>"
            },
            "Contents": {
              "name": "内容 Contents",
              "text": "<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo14008-hc-cover.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pf2logo.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" style=\"position:absolute;top:20px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:100%\" />\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/season-of-ghosts-logo.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" style=\"position:absolute;bottom:20px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:100%\" />\n</div>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Contents\">\n  <span>鬼季</span>\n</h1>\n\n<h3 data-no-toc>Pathfinder 冒险路径</h3>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog01frontm.JournalEntryPage.01campaignover00]{战役概览}</h2>\n<p>作者：James Jacobs</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow]{柳岸镇}</h2>\n<p>作者：Sen H.H.S.</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第一幕：不曾存在的夏日</h2>\n<p>作者：Sen H.H.S.</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第1章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh]{点亮长夜}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第2章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{收复柳岸镇}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第3章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{柳岸镇的诅咒}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第4章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{第一幕4：鬼打墙}</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第二幕：任落叶飘零</h2>\n<p>作者：Joan Hong</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第5章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin]{四季更迭}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第6章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{踏险斩祸一道清}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第7章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{智慧遗迹之中}</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第三幕：欲泣无息</h2>\n<p>作者：Dan Cascone 与 Eleanor Ferron</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第8章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi]{真相的湮灭}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第9章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto]{直面死亡}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第10章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{此地归我们所有}</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>第四幕：于蛛网之下绽放</h2>\n<p>作者：Liane Merciel</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第11章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow]{柳岸镇的归来}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第12章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri]{公主的蛛网}</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:2ch\"><strong>第13章：</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend]{双界之魔}</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog16contin]{继续战役}</h2>\n<p>作者：Liane Merciel</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl]{首长夜}</h2>\n<p>作者：Tan Shao Han</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}</h2>\n<p>作者：Grady Wang</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog19cycles]{毁灭的轮回}</h2>\n<p>作者：Jeremy Blum</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent]{冒险工具箱}</h2>\n<p>作者：Jeremy Blum、Dana Ebert、Eleanor Ferron、Sen H.H.S.、Joan Hong、James Jacobs、Joshua Kim 与 Tan Shao Han</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia]{怪物图鉴与NPC}</h2>\n<p>作者：Eleanor Ferron、Sen H.H.S.、Joan Hong、Michelle Y. Kim 与 Liane Merciel</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-left\">\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pf2logo.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pf2logo.webp');scale:1.2\" />\n  <p><strong>作者</strong></p>\n  <p>Dan Cascone、Eleanor Ferron、Sen H.H.S.、Joan Hong 与 Liane Merciel</p>\n  <p><strong>补充撰稿</strong></p>\n  <p>Jeremy Blum、Dana Ebert、James Jacobs、Joshua Kim、Michelle Y. Kim、Tan Shao Han 与 Grady Wang</p>\n  <p><strong>开发</strong></p>\n  <p>James Jacobs</p>\n  <p><strong>编辑负责人</strong></p>\n  <p>Priscilla N. Lagares 与 Ianara Natividad</p>\n  <p><strong>编辑</strong></p>\n  <p>Felix Dritz、Patrick Hurley、Avi Kool、Priscilla N. Lagares、Zac Moran、Ianara Natividad、Solomon St. John、Simone D. Sallé 与 Tan Shao Han</p>\n  <p><strong>封面画师</strong></p>\n  <p>Rodrigo Gonzalez Toledo</p>\n  <p><strong>内页画师</strong></p>\n  <p>Shafi Adams、M