        "Willowshore": {
          "name": "柳岸镇 Willowshore",
          "pages": {
            "Willowshore’s Hinterlands": {
              "name": "柳岸腹地 Willowshore’s Hinterlands",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore’s Hinterlands\">柳岸腹地</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇思维空间的地图出现在对页。如果你在使用《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》，玩家们会有一张该地区的地图。如果你没有使用这本指南，考虑提供一张你自己设计的地图供团队使用，帮助他们辨明方位。PC们直到 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章} 才会开始分散开来并探索这些地区，但在此之后，他们常常会沿着腹地的道路与荒野旅行，以跟进线索、追逐机会，或前往重要地点。</p>\n<p>没有道路的森林六角格属于困难地形，腹地南部崎岖多岩的旷野也是如此。这些地区栖息着许多危险的野生动物和怪物，但这些危险并不会随着PC们一同提升强度。作为一般规则，柳岸腹地中的大多数遭遇都以PC为2级为前提来呈现，因为该地区探索的大部分内容发生在第3章。该章也提供了一张游荡怪物表，可用于为旅行或露营过夜增添变化（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05exploringthe00]{此处}）。</p>\n<p>在后续的幕中，PC们将会周期性地面对更危险的遭遇。你应避免让这些后续幕的遭遇在PC达到预期等级之前就被触发。同样地，也要抵制“强化”游荡怪物表的诱惑——尽管这样做能让这些遭遇对PC仍具挑战性，但也可能破坏真实感：会让该地区显得越来越危险，以至于像柳岸镇这样的城镇别说繁荣，连生存都显得不可能。当你进入第2幕后，最好的做法是要么干脆停止使用游荡怪物，要么仅以叙事方式描述这些遭遇，而不强迫PC去进行一场场越来越简单的战斗。这既能帮助玩家感受到其角色在变强，也能随着战役推进加快游戏节奏。</p>\n<p>对页的地图标注了两组不同的遭遇。位于腹地中央、被思维空间边界包围的那些，属于第3章中详述的遭遇（从 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d1willowshor00]{此处} 开始），并包含区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d1willowshor00]{D1}–@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d13theroadto00]{D13}。发生在区域 <strong>D13</strong> 西北侧、沿着朝圣之径的那些，则在第2幕的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{第6章} 中详述，并包含区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b1tormentedk00]{B}–@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e1grandgate000]{E}。如果其他章节中的某个遭遇引用了腹地中的某个地点，将会标注其章节与幕，以便查找。</p>\n<p>关于环绕整个腹地的思维空间边界的完整细节，从 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05themindscape00]{此处} 开始。关于鬼打墙的细节见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05wallofghosts00]{此处}，而关于突破它的细节见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08throughthewa00]{此处}。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore’s Hinterlands\">Willowshore’s Hinterlands</h1>\n<p>A map of the Willowshore mindscape appears on the facing page. If you’re using the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>, the players have a map of the region. If you aren’t using this guide, consider providing a map of your own design for the group to use to help them orient themselves. The PCs won’t begin to spread out and explore these regions until @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}, but after this point, they’ll often be traveling the roads and wilds of the hinterlands to follow up on clues, pursue opportunities, or travel to important locations.</p>\n<p>Forest hexes without roads are difficult terrain, as are rough and rocky fields in the southern hinterlands. These regions harbor many dangerous wild animals and monsters, but these perils won’t scale up in power along with the PCs. As a general rule, most of the encounters in Willowshore’s Hinterlands are presented with the assumption that the PCs are 2nd level, since the bulk of the region’s exploration takes place in Chapter 3. That chapter also presents a wandering monster table for use in spicing up travel or nights spent camping (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05exploringthe00]{Here}).</p>\n<p>In later acts, the PCs will periodically face encounters that are more dangerous. You should avoid having these later act encounters trigger before the PCs are the expected level. Likewise, resist the temptation to “power up” the wandering monster table—while doing so does keep these encounters a challenge for the PCs, it can damage verisimilitude by making the region feel increasingly too dangerous for a town like Willowshore to thrive in, much less survive in. Once you’ve moved on to Act 2, it’s best if you either just stop using wandering monsters, or simply describe these encounters narratively without forcing the PCs to play through increasingly simple combats. This can help the players to feel like their characters are growing in power, but also helps to speed gameplay as the campaign progresses.</p>\n<p>The map on the facing page has two different sets of encounters marked. Those within the central portion of the hinterlands surrounded by the mindscape’s border comprise encounters that are detailed in Chapter 3 (beginning @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d1willowshor00]{Here}) and comprise areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d1willowshor00]{D1}–@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d13theroadto00]{D13}. Those that take place along the Pilgrim’s Path to the northwest of area <strong>D13</strong> are detailed in Act 2, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{Chapter 6} and comprise areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b1tormentedk00]{B}–@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e1grandgate000]{E}. In the event an encounter in a different chapter references a location in the Hinterlands, the chapter and act will be included to aid in navigation.</p>\n<p>Full details on the Mindscape Border that encircles the entire hinterlands can be found beginning @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05themindscape00]{Here}. Details on the Wall of Ghosts appear @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05wallofghosts00]{Here}, and details on breaking through it appear @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08throughthewa00]{Here}.</p>"
            },
            "The Willowshore Rumormill": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的传闻集散地 The Willowshore Rumormill",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Willowshore Rumormill\">柳岸镇的流言集散地</h1>\n<p>一旦在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}末尾，PC们为柳岸镇恢复秩序并赶走占据此地的怪物，小镇便会迅速回归常态——或者说，尽可能接近“常态”。请记住：尽管柳岸镇的人民已经重复经历思维空间的年度循环超过一个世纪，但每次循环的最初几周都是最难熬的，因为镇民必须重新学习这套新现实的规则。</p>\n<p>在<em>鬼季冒险路径</em>中，PC们将结识许多柳岸镇的居民。他们中的一些人会很早就与PC们相遇，而另一些人的重要作用可能要到很久之后才会显露出来。随着PC们执行各项任务，柳岸镇的居民也照常过着日常生活。这些日常事务的性质会随季节而变化，但有一件事始终不变——小镇居民对闲聊八卦与散布流言的热衷。</p>\n<p>PC们可以通过多种方式听到传闻——例如在镇上花上几小时搜集信息，并进行一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:15|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]检定；又或者作为帮助某位当地人的“回报”，对方急于以睿智的建议来偿还这些服务；甚至只是由于在本地商店或食肆里闲坐而顺带听到。某些能够推动剧情发展的传闻已直接写在冒险文本之中，但你也可以使用如下表所列的闲聊传闻，为PC们增添些许地方风味，并为那些在战役中要到年内较晚时段才真正开始发挥作用的NPC提前埋下伏笔。传闻后标注（T）表示为真，（F）表示为假。</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>d20</th>\n      <th>传闻</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–3</td>\n      <td>去年春天，松的家里至少来过六位不同的女访客——他该不会终于在找老婆了吧？（F）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4–6</td>\n      <td>去年首长夜的制作天灯优胜者尤素珍，用幽灵（特征）帮忙，才让她的天灯亮得格外耀眼。（F）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7–9</td>\n      <td>大抵是一只顽皮的野生家猫，有时能在蔚蓝茶馆附近见到的亚弥，可不只是只猫那么简单。（T）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10–11</td>\n      <td>我朋友的朋友又在林子里看见那只巨锹甲虫了；看样子它的地盘越来越靠近镇子！不禁让人怀疑，是不是有人一直在喂它……（F）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>12–13</td>\n      <td>每到冬天，总有人说在林子里见到狐狸幽灵（特征）。我才不信——以前不信，以后也不会信。那些老说看见她的猎人和捕兽人，不过是想博关注罢了。（F）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>14–15</td>\n      <td>要是在林子里看见仙鹤，别招惹它。看见它是好运，但杀了它就是坏运！（T）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>16–17</td>\n      <td>朝圣之径尽头那座老修道院闹鬼的传闻？全都是真的——所以现在才没人再去！（T）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>18–19</td>\n      <td>大尊柳是个喜怒无常的神灵，但有时也会把礼物赠与那些令他们高兴的人。（T）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>20</td>\n      <td>给PC抛出一条为另一名PC量身定做、且完全荒诞离谱的传闻，内容是他/她据称在镇上做过的某些动作。（F）</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Willowshore Rumormill\">The Willowshore Rumormill</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs restore order to Willowshore and drive out the occupying monsters at the end of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2}, the town swiftly returns to normal—or as close to “normal” as it can get. Remember that even though the people of Willowshore have repeated the mindscape’s annual cycle for over a century, the first few weeks of each repetition are the hardest as the townspeople must re-learn the rules of their new reality.</p>\n<p>During the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em>, the PCs will come to know many of Willowshore’s citizens. Some of them they’ll meet early while others might not have their important roles revealed until much later. As the PCs go about their missions, the citizens of Willowshore pursue their day to day activities. While the nature of these efforts changes with each season, one thing remains constant—the popular pursuit of small-town gossiping and rumormongering.</p>\n<p>The PCs can hear rumors in many ways—as the result of spending a few hours Gathering Information in town with a @Check[diplomacy|dc:15|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] check, as a “reward” for aiding a local who becomes eager to repay those services with sage advice, or simply as a side-effect of hanging out in a local shop or eatery. Certain rumors that help to propel the storyline forward are built into the adventure text itself, but you can use idle rumors like those listed in the following table to give the PCs a bit of local flavor and to foreshadow the existence of NPCs whose role in the campaign won’t really kick in until later in the year. A (T) following a rumor indicates it’s true, while an (F) indicates it’s false.</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>d20</th>\n      <th>Rumor</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–3</td>\n      <td>Matsu has had no fewer than six different lady visitors to his home last spring—perhaps he’s finally looking for a wife? (F)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4–6</td>\n      <td>Last year’s lantern making winner during First Long Night, You So-Jin, used a ghost to help make her lantern glow extra bright. (F)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7–9</td>\n      <td>Yami, a playful feral house cat sometimes seen living near the Ceruleant Teahouse, is more than just a cat. (T)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10–11</td>\n      <td>A friend of a friend spotted that giant stag beetle out in the woods again; seems like it’s territory is getting closer and closer to town! Makes you wonder if someone’s been feeding it... (F)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>12–13</td>\n      <td>Every winter, sightings of the Fox Ghost out in the woods happen. I don’t believe it—never have, never will. The hunters and trappers who keep seeing her are just looking for attention. (F)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>14–15</td>\n      <td>If you see a crane out in the woods, leave it alone. They’re good luck to see, but bad luck to kill! (T)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>16–17</td>\n      <td>Those stories about the old monastery at the far end of the Pilgrim’s Path being haunted? All true—that’s why no one visits anymore! (T)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>18–19</td>\n      <td>Great Willow is a moody kami, but he gives gifts sometimes to those who please them. (T)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>20</td>\n      <td>Present the PC with a custom-created and completely outrageous rumor about one of the other PCs’ supposed actions in town. (F)</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
            },
            "Wooded Clearing": {
              "name": "林间空地 Wooded Clearing",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W38. Wooded Clearing\">W38. 林间空地</h2>\n<p>每年在<em>鬼季</em>开始之际的重现节结束时，组织者都会挑选一个不同的地点，把他们选中的被绑架者带到那里。这个地点从不远离城镇，但总在视线之外。今年，PC们正是那些被绑架者，他们被带到城镇正东方的这处林中小空地。战役便从这里开始。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W38. Wooded Clearing\">W38. Wooded Clearing</h2>\n<p>At the end of each year’s Reenactment Festival at the start of the <em>Season of Ghosts</em>, the organizers choose a different place to bring their chosen abductees. This location is never far from town, but always out of sight. This year, the PCs are those abductees, and they are brought to this small clearing in the woods just east of town. It is here that the campaign begins.</p>"
            },
            "The Great Willow": {
              "name": "大尊柳 The Great Willow",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W37. The Great Willow\">W37. 大尊柳</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇坐落在一片地理上被称为三山的山地区域脚下，因该区域有三座主要山峰而得名。在她的回忆录中，智惠大师在记述她如何在这些山中最低那座的峰顶发现了一棵体型异常巨大的古老柳树。与守护这棵树的木灵神结为朋友后，智惠大师得知了关键情报，最终引领她前往西边的谭杉林。凭借这份知识，所谓“大尊柳”的木灵神多年来一直受到柳岸镇居民与来访朝圣者的崇敬，直到柳岸镇总督在那场注定失败的行动中未能保护城镇免受苦迦菩提的影响之日。</p>\n<p>当三山地区成为思维空间后，大尊柳被卷入其中，并与区域内其他居民一同重生。每当思维空间重置，大尊柳都会觉得自己与现实“更遥远”了一点，变得越来越心不在焉，与世界愈发疏离。他们知道自己是这片区域里唯一的神灵，而随着每一次新的循环，也越来越确信自己同样是世界上最后的神灵。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">大尊柳</span> <span class=\"keepme\">荒野 6</span></h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无归属</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大尊柳</strong>（忧郁的无性别木灵神），察觉 DC 26，意志 DC 24</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>货物</strong> 采集来的食物与非金属的原始材料</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W37. The Great Willow\">W37. The Great Willow</h2>\n<p>Willowshore rests at the foot of a mountainous region known geographically as the Trimountains, named due to the three major peaks in the area. In her memoir, Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} noted how on the summit of the lowest of these mountains she found an ancient willow tree of unusual size. After befriending the kodama kami who protected the tree, Master Zhi Hui learned vital information that eventually led her to the Tan Sugi grove to the west. For this knowledge, the kodama of the so-called “Great Willow” received much reverence from both Willowshore and visiting pilgrims for many years, until the day Willowshore’s governor failed in his fateful attempt to protect the town from Kugaptee’s influence.</p>\n<p>When the Trimountain region became a mindscape, Great Willow was drawn in and was reborn along with the rest of the region’s inhabitants. Each time the mindscape resets, Great Willow feels just a bit more “distant” from reality, growing more and more distracted and detached from the world. They’re aware of the fact that they’re the only kami in the region, and with each new cycle, grow more and more convinced they’re also the last kami in the world.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Great Willow</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Wilderness 6</span></h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Great Willow</strong> (morose agender kodama), Perception DC 26, Will DC 24</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> foraged foods and non-metallic raw materials</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Bones of the Forgotten": {
              "name": "受弃者之骨 Bones of the Forgotten",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W36. Bones of the Forgotten\">W36. 受弃者之骨</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇和许多偏远村落一样，有自己的一套法律。重罪通常以放逐来惩处；若此人的技能或知识仍有用处，则会改为监禁。处决十分罕见，因为被放逐进幽魂之森本身往往就等同于死刑。</p>\n<p>尤其卑劣的罪犯会在头皮上刺上罪印；而死后，这个纹身会通过刻痕转移到骨头上，因此即便尸体死亡、腐朽，印记仍会保留。带有罪印的尸体——无论来自柳岸镇、其他村落，还是龙华之类的帝国势力——都只能埋葬在这片杂草丛生、无人打理的区域中。</p>\n<p>过去坟墓都没有标记，但最近立起了几根木桩，并在上面挂着纸手里剑，仿佛是在无声地抗议：埋在下面的人或许死得并不公正。又或者，这是为了阻止一个充满怨恨、复仇心切的幽灵（特征）出现。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W36. Bones of the Forgotten\">W36. Bones of the Forgotten</h2>\n<p>Willowshore, like many remote villages, has its own set of laws. Grievous crimes are punished via exile, or imprisonment if the individual’s skill or knowledge was needed. Executions were rare, as being exiled into the Specterwood was often a death sentence in itself.</p>\n<p>Particularly vile criminals had a Mark of Crime tattooed onto their scalp, and after death, this tattoo was transferred to the bones through carving, meaning even in death and decomposition, the mark remained. Bodies with a Mark of Crime—be it from Willowshore, another village, or an imperial force such as Lung Wa—can only be buried in this overgrown and unkept area.</p>\n<p>While graves were unmarked in the past, a few wooden posts have been erected recently and paper shuriken hung off them, seemingly in silent protest that the ones buried beneath might have died an unjust death. Or perhaps this is an attempt to stave off the rise of a bitter, vengeful ghost.</p>"
            },
            "The Leshy’s Salon": {
              "name": "莱西茶铺 The Leshy’s Salon",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W35. The Leshy’s Salon\">W35. 莱西茶铺</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>柳岸腹地</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇周边一向是一片田园诗般的荒野，除了少数众所周知的危险区域外，相对适合进行探索。不幸的是，对PC们而言，腹地的安全已成往事，因为在这片区域的思维空间版本中，幽灵（特征）与怪物潜伏其间。用不了多久，镇上的居民就会普遍知晓此事。对柳岸腹地的探索在本次冒险中扮演关键角色——其许多遭遇的细节见于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>当地的莱西们不记得自己何时来到这片地区，只知道那是在柳岸镇建立之前很久。他们直到聚落扩张、使其难以置身事外时，才正式加入柳岸镇。在盟友家族阻止贪婪的伐木领主靠近后，莱西们建立了自己的茶场生意，背着矩形的竹制背包上路，里面装着煮好的茶和茶具。有些会高喊口号，另一些则用简单的木鱼来告知顾客他们已到来。这些行商很快成了柳岸镇生活中的一大景观与常见风景。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">莱西茶铺</span> <span class=\"keepme\">农场 3</span></h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>山峰草</strong>（亵渎礼制的无性别莱西制茶师3），察觉 DC 19，意志 DC 19，制作 +9</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong>陶土茶具、茶叶</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W35. The Leshy’s Salon\">W35. The Leshy’s Salon</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Willowshore Hinterlands</h1>\n  <p>Willowshore’s immediate surroundings are traditionally an idyllic wilderness, one that’s relatively safe to explore save for a few well-known dangerous areas. Unfortunately for the PCs, the hinterlands’ safety is a thing of the past, for here in the mindscape version of the region, ghosts and monsters lurk. It shouldn’t be long before this becomes common knowledge among the town locals. Exploration of the Willowshore hinterlands plays a key role in the adventure—details on many of its encounters are found in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>The local leshies don’t recall when they came to the region, just that it was long before Willowshore was founded. They didn’t officially join Willowshore until the expansion of the settlement made it inevitable. With allied families keeping the greedy lumber lords away, the leshies built their own tea farm business, taking to the roads with brewed tea and tea ware stashed in rectangular bamboo backpacks. Some would shout slogans, while others used a simple temple block to inform customers of their arrival. These traveling merchants soon became an attraction and staple of Willowshore life.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Leshy’s Salon</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Farm 3</span></h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Mountain Summit Grass</strong> (irreverent agender leshy teamaker 3), Perception DC 19, Will DC 19, Crafting +9</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> clay pottery tea ware, tea leaves</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Kawaka’s Home": {
              "name": "川冈的家 Kawaka’s Home",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W34. Kawaka’s Home\">W34. 川冈的家</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的大多数居民都住在自己的营业场所里，或至少住在附近。云纸屋的主人迈纳·川冈也不例外；他住在造纸厂上层的一套小房间里，而自从几年前父母去世后，他就一直让这里——他的家宅——空着无人居住。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W34. Kawaka’s Home\">W34. Kawaka’s Home</h2>\n<p>Most of Willowshore’s citizens live in or at least near to their place of business. The owner of Cloud Paper House, Myna Kawaka is no exception; he lives in a small suite of rooms on an upper floor of the paper mill, and has left this, his family home, unoccupied since his parents’ deaths a few years ago.</p>"
            },
            "Spider Gate": {
              "name": "蜘蛛门 Spider Gate",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W33. Spider Gate\">W33. 蜘蛛门</h2>\n<p>在一次试图采收谭杉而引发的屠杀之后，柳岸镇的总督屈服于要求在村口设置一盏新灯笼的呼声。原本的计划是让柳岸镇的木匠修建一座鸟居或嬛族语式的门楼，以便悬挂灯笼；但一位龙华贵族反而提出免费赠送他花园里的一尊石制守护蜘蛛，因为它已经不再符合花园的装饰风格。</p>\n<p>巨像运抵时，大多数柳岸镇的人民都觉得那是他们见过最丑的东西。尽管如此，他们仍认为雕像里寄宿着一位守护的魂魄，并因此对其敬重有加。随着时代推移，村民们接纳了这位独特的入口守护者，甚至称它为他们“丑小乖”的吉祥物。守护的魂魄虽不太情愿接受这个称呼，但整座村庄的猝然覆灭让它孤苦了一个多世纪；而当它死去并与自己誓言守护的人民重聚时，这段经历也随之被它遗忘。丑小乖用獠牙叼着的灯笼只是一盏普通灯笼，不同于晨步桥上发现的<em>长明灯</em>；但柳岸镇的人民同样珍视它，并竭力让它始终保持点亮。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W33. Spider Gate\">W33. Spider Gate</h2>\n<p>After the slaughter caused by an attempt to harvest the Tan Sugi, Willowshore’s governor caved to the demand for a new lantern for the entrance of the village. While the original plan was for the carpenters of Willowshore to build a tori gate or Tian-shu gateway on which lanterns could be hung, a Lung Wa aristocrat offered a free stone guardian spider from his garden instead, since it no longer fit in with the garden’s decorations.</p>\n<p>Most Willowshorers thought the giant statue was the ugliest thing they’d ever seen when it arrived. Nevertheless, they assumed the statue housed a guardian spirit and respected it accordingly. In time, villagers accepted their unique entrance guardian, even calling it their “ugly but cute” mascot. While the guardian spirit is reluctant to accept that title, the sudden death of the whole village left it forlorn for over a century, an experience it forgot when it died and reunited with the people it vowed to protect. The lantern Ugly Cute holds in its fangs is a regular lantern, unlike the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> found at Dawnstep Bridge, but the people of Willowshore value it just as much and strive to keep it lit at all times.</p>"
            },
            "The Mushroom House": {
              "name": "蘑菇房 The Mushroom House",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W32. The Mushroom House\">W32. 蘑菇房</h2>\n<p>这座偏僻的砖砌农舍散发着腐败和粪肥的气味。不过，人人都知道农舍里生长的不只有蘑菇。只要价格合适，蘑菇房几乎什么都能“种”出来。卢达·巴马是一位精干的年迈半身人女性，她是这个非法市场的头目；她在胡太婆的明确许可下经营此处。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">蘑菇房</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">非法市场 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>卢达·巴马</strong>（善于操纵的女性半身人走私者 3）察觉 DC 20，意志 DC 18，工艺 +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> PC可以为卢达担任“收款人”，使用威吓来赚取收入。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 冒险道具、毒品、毒素、纹身</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W32. The Mushroom House\">W32. The Mushroom House</h2>\n<p>This remote brick farmhouse smells of decay and manure. Everyone knows that mushrooms aren’t the only things growing in the farmhouse, though. For the right price, the Mushroom House can grow almost anything. Luda Bama, a spry, elderly halfling woman, is the head of this illicit market, which she runs with the explicit permission of Granny Hu.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">The Mushroom House</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Illicit Market 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Luda Bama</strong> (manipulative female halfling smuggler 3) Perception DC 20, Will DC 18, Crafting +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> A PC can act as a “collector” for Luda, using Intimidation to Earn Income.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> adventuring gear, drugs, poisons, tattoos</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Dock": {
              "name": "码头 Dock",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W31. Dock\">W31. 码头</h2>\n<p>在大坝建成后，柳岸镇在木筏湖上的旧码头被封闭，因此需要在木棉河河口修建一座新码头。新码头规模更大、更为开阔，由拉祖尔·萨姆杜拉运营管理；他是木棉河-杜月江瓦市专门因其造船技艺而雇用的。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">柳岸镇码头</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">码头 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>拉祖尔·萨姆杜拉</strong>（沉静的男性娜迦裔造船匠 3）察觉 DC 19，意志 DC 19，工艺 +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 队伍可以以每天 5 cp 的价格租用一艘 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.vehicles.Actor.l0RfYgabnbNoHnkS]{划艇}，或以 15 gp 直接购买一艘。拉祖尔也为他的划艇提供极佳的手工桨。这些桨使你使用划艇进行载具操作检定时获得 +1 物品加值，价格为 50 gp。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>货物</strong> 河船租赁与售卖</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W31. Dock\">W31. Dock</h2>\n<p>After the construction of the dam, Willowshore’s old dock in Woodraft Lake was blocked off, thus requiring the construction of a new dock at the mouth of the Ceiba River. The new dock is larger and more expansive, and is operated and managed by Rajul, who was hired by the Ceiba-Duyue Exchange specifically for his boatbuilding skills.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Willowshore Dock</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Dock 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Rajul Samudra</strong> (serene male nagaji shipwright 3) Perception DC 19, Will DC 19, Crafting +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> The party can rent a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.vehicles.Actor.l0RfYgabnbNoHnkS]{Rowboat} for 5 cp a day or purchase one outright for 15 gp. Rajul also offers excellent handcrafted oars for his rowboats. These oars grant a +1 item bonus to Piloting checks with rowboats and cost 50 gp.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> riverboat rentals and sales</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Fisheries": {
              "name": "渔场 Fisheries",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W30. Fisheries\">W30. 渔场</h2>\n<p>淡水鱼是柳岸镇的重要食物来源。当地人传统上会捕捞整群的鱼，将超过一定尺寸的鱼加以保存，并把小鱼养在自家后院的池塘里。如今，这种做法已得到扩展，不过渔民们仍未达到让这里的渔场池塘能够无限期维持的程度。</p>\n<p>多年来，座泽一直是柳岸镇最出色的养鱼人；她感知天气变化的能力，让她在职业上拥有完美优势。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">渔夫农场与码头</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">公会 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>座泽</strong>（警觉的女性鼠人渔夫 3）察觉 DC 19，意志 DC 19，自然 +9</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 若PC受到北岭人的喜爱，他们可以参考座泽的天气预报，在1天内获得对抗天气效果的检定与豁免的+1环境加值。他们每周只能从该效果中获益一次。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 风干或熏制的鱼与虾、肥料、钓鱼道具、昆虫饵料</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> PC可以在渔场巡逻以防掠食者，或检查竿钓渔夫使用的简易码头是否有损坏，使其能够以生存检定来赚取收入。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W30. Fisheries\">W30. Fisheries</h2>\n<p>Freshwater fish is an important food source for Willowshore. Locals traditionally capture entire schools of fish, preserve those above a certain size, and raise small ones in their backyard ponds. Today, this practice has been expanded, though the fishers have yet to reach a point where the fishery ponds here can be maintained indefinitely.</p>\n<p>Zataku has been Willowshore’s foremost fish keeper for many years; her ability to sense weather changes gives her the perfect edge in her occupation.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Fisher’s Farms and Docks</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Guild 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Zataku</strong> (observant female ratfolk fisher 3) Perception DC 19, Will DC 19, Nature +9</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> If the PCs are liked by Northridge, they can confer with Zataku’s weather forecasts to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks and saves against weather effects for 1 day. They can benefit from this effect once per week.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> Dried or smoked fish and shrimp, fertilizer, fishing gear, insect bait</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> A PC can patrol the fisheries for predators or inspect the simple docks used by the pole fishers for damage, allowing them to Earn Income with Survival checks.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Trade Office": {
              "name": "贸易栈 Trade Office",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W29. Trade Office\">W29. 贸易栈</h2>\n<p>当总督和善保最初在柳岸镇上任时，他下令在此修建数座新仓库与一处贸易栈，希望将小镇的产业与其同沿海要塞唐入的联系扩展为更有利可图的事业。在胡太婆的建议下，和善保亲自挑选了当地的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{国府幸}祭司金具元担任瓦市经理。金具元勉强接受了这份工作，因为他知道，凭胡太婆掌握的把柄，只要她开口要他在账目上动点手脚，或对往返蘑菇房的几件包裹睁一只眼闭一只眼，他都无法拒绝。胡太婆本人就住在这里的一间私人套房中。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-gu-won.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kim Gu-won\" alt=\"金具元，一个光头人类男性，身穿绿色长袍。\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-gu-won.webp')\" />\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">木棉河-杜月江瓦市</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">贸易栈 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>金具元</strong>（耐心的人类男性、国府幸的牧师 5）察觉 DC 23，意志 DC 23，制作 +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 金具元的书法出类拔萃，这项技能使他在制作符箓与卷轴时更具优势。他只需用 4 小时工作即可制作持续 1 个月的符箓，并能在 2 天内制作持续 1 年的符箓。他也能在 2 天内制作卷轴。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>货物</strong> 饮料、神圣卷轴、食物与香料、符箓、未加工矿物、纺织品</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> PC 可以在此协助整理物流，并使用社交检定来赚取收入。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W29. Trade Office\">W29. Trade Office</h2>\n<p>When Governor Heh Shan-Bao originally took office in Willowshore, he ordered several new warehouses and a trade office to be built here, hoping to expand the town’s industry and connection with the coastal fortress of Karahai into something more profitable. On Granny Hu’s advice, Shan-Bao handpicked the local @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{Kofusachi} priest, Kim Gu-won, to take the post of Exchange Manager. Gu-won reluctantly accepted the job, knowing that with what Granny Hu has on him, he wouldn’t be able to refuse if she asked him to shift a few numbers here and there or ignore a few packages going to or coming from the Mushroom House. Granny Hu herself lives in a private suite of rooms here.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-gu-won.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kim Gu-won\" alt=\"Kim Gu-won, a bald human man wearing a green robe.\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-gu-won.webp')\" />\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">The Ceiba-Duyue Exchange</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Trade Office 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Kim Gu-won</strong> (patient male human cleric of Kofusachi 5) Perception DC 23, Will DC 23, Crafting +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Gu-won is exceptional at calligraphy, a skill that gives him an advantage in crafting fulus and scrolls. He can craft fulus that last a month with 4 hours of work and fulus that last a year in 2 days. He can also craft scrolls in 2 days.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> beverages, divine scrolls, foods and spices, fulus, raw mineral, textiles</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> A PC can help organize logistics here and use Society checks to Earn Income.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Mother’s Coil": {
              "name": "主母之绾 Mother’s Coil",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W28. Mother’s Coil\">W28. 主母之绾</h2>\n<p>在柳岸镇，传统上人们将魔法视为神明祝福的显现、与魂魄世界的联系，或只是手与心的把戏。直到苏萨杜斯的安贾尔——一位年迈的那伽族法师——到来之前，大多数人并不真正理解魔法是一门需要研究与学习的学问。大约十五年前安贾尔来到此地，发现柳岸镇的天气对他们的干鳞症颇为温和，于是从一位打算搬去城市的农民手中买下一块地。几乎一夜之间，一座那伽佐尔风格的黑色玄武岩高塔拔地而起，令村民们叹为观止。</p>\n<p>尽管对魔法感到好奇，但大多数村民觉得钻研这门学问艰深难近，更别提不切实际。因此，安贾尔只有一位学徒——十兵卫。她是安贾尔在柳岸镇抚养长大的孩子：当年她被一对不负责任的“父母”遗弃在此，那两人冒充富裕商人，却在欠下账单后逃之夭夭。安贾尔因他们让一个孩子陷入危险而勃然大怒，在其那林尼瓦提亚信仰的驱使下，这位老法师将惊恐的十兵卫收为己出。</p>\n<p>尽管安贾尔去年的去世令人悲痛，十兵卫仍怀着决心，要通过养父母留下的书籍继续研习奥术之道。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">主母之绾</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">法师塔 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>井川十兵卫</strong>（好学的女性人类法师 3）察觉DC 19，意志DC 19，奥秘学+10，制作+10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong>十兵卫在战役开始时只知道如何制作1环与2环法术卷轴，以及1环魔杖。每周，她会将一件与PC等级相同的非消耗品魔法物品加入自己已知的魔法物品配方清单。PC可以请求她每周至多1次，研究某个特定配方。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong>奥术与隐秘卷轴、魔法物品与法术的公式与配方、魔杖</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W28. Mother’s Coil\">W28. Mother’s Coil</h2>\n<p>Magic was seen traditionally in Willowshore as a manifestation of divine blessing, one’s connection to the Spirit World, or just a trick of the hand and mind. Most folks didn’t quite understand it as a topic studied and learned until the arrival of Anjal of Thulsadus, an old nagaji wizard. Arriving about fifteen years ago, Anjal found the weather of Willowshore to be gentle on their dryscale condition and thus bought a plot of land from a farmer looking to relocate to the city. Overnight, a Nagajor-styled tower of dark basalt appeared, much to the awe of the villagers.</p>\n<p>Though curious about magic, most villagers find studying the topic to be formidable and unapproachable, not to mention impractical. Thus, Anjal had only one apprentice, Jubei, a child they raised after she was abandoned in Willowshore by a pair of irresponsible “parents” who posed as well-off merchants but then fled without paying their bills. Infuriated that they endangered a child, Anjal’s Nalinivatian beliefs prompted the old wizard to take the terrified Jubei in as their own.</p>\n<p>While Anjal’s death last year was tragic, Jubei is determined to continue studying the arcane arts through the books her adopted parent left behind.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Mother’s Coil</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Wizard’s Tower 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Igawa Jubei</strong> (studious female human wizard 3) Perception DC 19, Will DC 19, Arcana +10, Crafting +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Jubei begins the campaign knowing only how to craft 1st-level and 2nd-level spell scrolls and 1st-level wands. Each week, she adds one non-consumable magical item of the PCs’ level to her known list of magical item recipes. The PCs can Request her to research a specific recipe up to once per week.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> arcane and occult scrolls, formulas and recipes for magic items and spells, wands</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Hand of Spring": {
              "name": "妙手回春 The Hand of Spring",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W27. The Hand of Spring\">W27. 妙手回春</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇在达米汗辛哥大夫到来之前，医疗护理主要依赖民间偏方、草药煎剂和巡游祭司。大家都简称他为达米。达米用针灸、提纯化学制剂与外科手术相结合的方式来提供照护。尽管他的治疗方法并非柳岸镇所习惯，达米却因其乐善好施、比起金钱更在乎病人的大夫名声在外。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">妙手回春</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">诊所 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>达米汗辛哥“达米”玛玛邦罗欧布</strong>（和蔼的男性人类大夫 4）察觉 DC 22，意志 DC 22，制作 +12，医术 +14</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 除了向PC出售或制作治疗物品外，达米还可以尝试未受训与受训的医术检定来为每天至多8名不同的病人进行治疗，每人每次治疗收费5 cp。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 炼金治疗物品、医疗包补给品、非魔法治疗物品</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W27. The Hand of Spring\">W27. The Hand of Spring</h2>\n<p>Willowshore relied heavily on home remedies, herbal droughts, and traveling priests for medical care until the arrival of Doctor Damihansig, whom everyone calls Dami for short. Dami uses a mix of acupuncture, purified chemicals, and surgery to provide care. Though his treatments aren’t what Willowshore is used to, Dami has developed quite a reputation for being a charitable doctor who cares more about his patients than monetary gain.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">The Hand of Spring</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Clinic 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Damihansig “Dami” Mababangloob</strong> (kindly male human doctor 4) Perception DC 22, Will DC 22, Crafting +12, Medicine +14</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Other than selling or making healing items for the PCs, Dami can attempt untrained and trained Medicine checks to treat up to 8 different patients a day, charging 5 cp per person per treatment.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> alchemical healing items, healer’s kit supplies, non-magical healing items</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Second Best": {
              "name": "二等优 Second Best",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W26. Second Best\">W26. 二等优</h2>\n<p>大约五年前，霍天哲与其来自唐入的铁匠父亲一同来到柳岸镇，协助维护柳岸镇大坝。这个在城里长大的儿子原以为自己马上就能教会“乡下的二流铁匠”该怎么把事办好。然而很快，天哲就意识到，自己的手艺甚至不如永焰会最年轻的学徒；而他那些设计花哨的农具小装置，在真正的农田里与其说是奇妙机器，不如说更像玩具。受到打击后，天哲请求父亲留在柳岸镇，好让自己学习成为“一名有用的铁匠”。天哲的父亲不情不愿地答应了这突如其来的请求，但还是给了儿子一把金币，好让他去订做一块新的店招。为了提醒自己，天哲大胆地把工坊命名为“二等优”。</p>\n<p>在过去五年里，天哲的产品积累了一批忠实顾客；他对机械的见识也打动了雍武秀，使这位老铁匠将大坝维护的职责交给了他。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">二等优</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">铁匠 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>霍天哲</strong>（谦逊的男性人类发明家 4）察觉 DC 18，意志 DC 18，制作 +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 除了常规金属物品外，天哲也能制作炼金弹药和炸弹。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 冒险工具、炼金弹药、炼金炸弹、发条小装置，以及简易护甲、金属武器与盾牌，</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W26. Second Best\">W26. Second Best</h2>\n<p>When Huo Tian-Zhe arrived in Willowshore with his blacksmith father from Karahai about five years ago to assist with the maintenance of Willowshore’s dam, the urban-born son thought he was about to show the “second-rate smiths of the countryside” how to get things done. Quickly, Tian-Zhe realized his own skills were subpar to even the youngest apprentice of the Eternal Blaze and that his fancily-designed farm gadgets were more toys than machines of marvels out in the actual farm fields. Humbled, Tian-Zhe asked his father to stay in Willowshore so he could learn to be a “smith of use.” Begrudgingly accepting the abrupt request, Tian-Zhe’s father nevertheless gave his son a handful of gold to order a new shop sign. As a reminder to himself, Tian-Zhe boldly named his workshop “Second Best.”</p>\n<p>In the last five years, Tian-Zhe’s products have garnered some loyal customers, and his knowledge of machinery won over Yong Wu-Xiu such that the old smith tasked him with the maintenance of the dam.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Second Best</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Smith 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Huo Tian-Zhe</strong> (humble male human inventor 4) Perception DC 18, Will DC 18, Crafting +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Tian-Zhe can craft alchemical ammunition and bombs in addition to regular metal items.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> adventuring tools, alchemical ammunition, alchemical bombs, clockwork gadgets, and simple armor, metal weapons, and shields,</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Woodcarver’s Guild": {
              "name": "木雕师行会 Woodcarver’s Guild",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W25. Woodcarver’s Guild\">W25. 木雕师行会</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇较新的商号，尤其是与木雕有关的那些，大多位于商业街旁两层高的红砖建筑内。为了确保木材大亨永远不会偏袒任何人，木雕师们联合起来成立了一个行会，让年轻学徒在学徒期内有机会到不同的店铺实习。木雕师现任民选行会领袖梦昂便是这种训练的产物。尽管她的作品备受赞誉，也全心投入于培训这条街上临街店铺里的众多匠人，梦昂却更想成为一名画家或珠宝匠。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">木雕师行会</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">公会 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>云梦昂</strong>（才华横溢的女性人类公会领袖 4）察觉 DC 22，意志 DC 20，制作 +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 艺术品、木制物品、木制宗教象征物</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 木雕师行会可以按PC的请求制作任何非魔法、非武器的木制或硬木物品。若PC提供该物品所需的原始材料，梦昂也能制作绘画作品与珠宝。行会一旦拥有桃木供应（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#collecting-peachwood]{采集桃木}），角色就能制作桃木纸，这能让云梦昂制作符箓（包括稀有的区域符箓 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20willowshoref00]{此处}）。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W25. Woodcarver’s Guild\">W25. Woodcarver’s Guild</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s newer businesses, particularly those associated with woodcarving, are mostly found in one of the two-storied red-brick buildings along Mercantile Street. To ensure the lumber lords would never favor anyone, the woodcarvers came together to form a guild, through which young apprentices have the opportunity to intern at different shops during their apprenticeship. Mong-Un, the woodcarver’s current elected guild leader, is a product of such training. Though heaped with praises for her work and devoted to the training of the many artisans whose shops front this street, Mong-Un would rather be a painter or jewelry maker.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Woodcarver’s Guild</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Guild 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Yun Mong-un</strong> (talented female human guild leader 4) Perception DC 22, Will DC 20, Crafting +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> artwork, wood items, wooden religious symbols</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> The woodcarver’s guild can craft any non-magical, non-weapon wood or hardwood items for the PCs upon request. Mong-Un can also craft painted artworks and jewelry if the PCs provide the raw materials necessary for the item. Once the guild has peachwood supplies (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#collecting-peachwood]{Collecting Peachwood}), the characters can craft peachwood paper, which allows Yun Mong-un to craft fulus (including the rare regional fulus @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20willowshoref00]{Here}).</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Ho Jeong-hui’s Home": {
              "name": "洪正辉的家 Ho Jeong-hui’s Home",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W24. Ho Jeong-hui’s Home\">W24. 洪正辉的家</h2>\n<p><strong>洪正辉</strong>（人类男性平民城镇守卫 2）最近用薪水攒够了钱后搬进了这间小屋。在这里，他可以花时间烹饪他最爱的、气味浓烈（但很美味）的晚餐，而不会惹恼营房里的同僚守卫。不过更重要的是，他拥有所需的隐私，能花时间招待那群虽小却热情、令他心动的访客。作为柳岸镇最受追捧的单身汉之一，他的名声确保很少有人会无视他发出的到家中做客的邀请。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W24. Ho Jeong-hui’s Home\">W24. Ho Jeong-hui’s Home</h2>\n<p><strong>Ho Jeong-hui</strong> (popular male human town guard 2) recently moved into this small home after saving up enough money from his salary. Here, he gets to spend time cooking the pungent (but delicious) dinners he loves so much without vexing fellow guards in the barracks. Though more importantly, he has the privacy he needs to spend time entertaining the small but eager cast of visitors who catch his eye. His reputation as one of Willowshore’s most eligible bachelors ensures that few invitations to his home are ignored.</p>"
            },
            "Abandoned Estates": {
              "name": "被遗弃的庄园 Abandoned Estates",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W23. Abandoned Estates\">W23. 被遗弃的庄园</h2>\n<p>这两座被遗弃的木材大亨庄园在被彻底洗劫一空后，被留作偶尔的发泄室或胆量挑战。东侧庄园后方的一小片树林中坐落着一座献给 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna} 的废弃神龛（区域 <strong>W23b</strong>），许多人都在质疑，是否应该有人把这位女神接入家中，而不是让她孤零零地留在庄园的废墟里。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W23. Abandoned Estates\">W23. Abandoned Estates</h2>\n<p>These two abandoned lumber lords’ estates, after being thoroughly picked clean, were left to serve as the occasional rage room or dare challenge. An abandoned shrine to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna} sits in a small copse of trees behind the eastern estate (area <strong>W23b</strong>), and many have questioned if someone should accept the goddess into their home instead of leaving her bereft in the estate ruins.</p>"
            },
            "The Cerulean Teahouse": {
              "name": "青天茶馆 The Cerulean Teahouse",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W22. The Cerulean Teahouse\">W22. 青天茶馆</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的木材老板们自视甚高，一想到要与“平民百姓”厮混就觉得别扭。贵族庆麦莱的解决办法，是在这些木材领主的庄园附近建立了这座精致的建筑。</p>\n<p>青天茶馆凭借奢华的餐食、饮品与表演迅速走红。然而，新鲜劲一过，生意很快就冷了下来。尽管如此，麦莱仍坚持不懈：先把茶馆的重心改为茶饭外烩，接着与莱西茶铺合作，将此处作为门面店，最后又转为可灵活经营的住宿加早餐旅店。就在麦莱终于还清这处房产的贷款仅仅几天后，龙华崩溃的消息传到了柳岸镇。</p>\n<p>麦莱在那时选择收手，并宣布退休；但当她试图把茶馆的控制权交给家人时，却遇到了麻烦——显然，她的亲属中没有人想搬到柳岸镇。去年初冬，麦莱去世，生意的归属仍未确定，因为麦莱从未提交遗嘱。在本幕中，当PC们探索这间茶馆时，他们会发现麦莱留下的一件奇特遗物；随着时间推移，这件遗物将使他们成为茶馆的新主人。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W22. The Cerulean Teahouse\">W22. The Cerulean Teahouse</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s lumber bosses thought very highly of themselves, and the idea of mingling with the “common folk” rankled them. Aristocrat Qing Mai-Lai’s solution was the establishment of this fine structure, close to the lumber lords’ estates.</p>\n<p>The Cerulean Teahouse took off quickly, thanks to its offerings of extravagant food, drinks, and performances. However, once the novelty wore off, business quickly died. Still, Mai-Lai persevered, first by changing the teahouse’s focus to banquet catering, then by collaborating with The Leshy’s Salon as a storefront, and finally as a flexible bed-and-breakfast. Just days after Mai-Lai finally paid off the loan on the property, news of Lung Wa’s collapse reached Willowshore.</p>\n<p>Mai-Lai called it quits at that point and announced her retirement, but her attempts to pass on control of the Teahouse to family met with complications when it became apparent none of her relations wanted to move to Willowshore. When Mai-Lai passed away early in the previous winter, ownership of the business was undetermined, for Mai-Lai never submitted a will. When the PCs explore the teahouse in this act, they’ll find a curious remnant left behind by Mai-Lai that, in time, will result in them becoming the teahouse’s new owners.</p>"
            },
            "Mama Bao’s": {
              "name": "包子嫲嫲的 Mama Bao’s",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W21. Mama Bao’s\">W21. 包子嫲嫲的小店</h2>\n<p>中村玉茗，亲切地被称为“包子嫲嫲”，多年来一直经营着这家小小的蒸包铺——这是许多本地人最爱光顾的一站。店内令人放松的氛围与舒适感，足以弥补菜单选择有限的不足。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">包子嫲嫲的小店</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">餐馆 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>中村玉茗</strong>（友善的女性人类厨师 4）察觉 DC 21，意志 DC 23，烹饪学识 +14</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 蒸包</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 只要队伍至少被北岭人喜爱，一名在烹饪学识上至少为专家的 PC 就能在这里帮忙。该 PC 在为了赚取收入而进行的食物学识检定上获得 +1 环境加值。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W21. Mama Bao’s\">W21. Mama Bao’s</h2>\n<p>Nakamura Yu Ming, known affectionately as “Mama Bao,” has run this small steamed bun shop for years—it’s a favorite stop for many locals. The relaxing ambiance and comfort of the restaurant more than make up for the limited menu offerings.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Mama Bao’s Shop</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Restaurant 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Nakamura Yu Ming</strong> (friendly female human cook 4) Perception DC 21, Will DC 23, Cooking Lore +14</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> steamed buns</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> As long as the party is at least liked by Northridge, a PC who is at least expert in Cooking Lore can help out here. The PC gains a +1 circumstance bonus to Food Lore checks made to Earn Income.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Luo and Laws": {
              "name": "骆氏状所 Luo and Laws",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W20. Luo and Laws\">W20. 骆氏状所</h2>\n<p>龙华的法律在一次又一次被自私自利的统治者修订后，成了一团自相矛盾的乱麻，使得像骆熙旸这样的独立律师，得以靠着努力理清这些条文而过上不错的生活。邀请她来此的木材大亨们向她保证乡村生活压力会更小；因此熙旸到来时只带了那套必需的10卷《帝国律摘要》。这位律师很快发现，柳岸镇的法律问题并不比她先前在伺城遇到的简单，甚至可能更复杂，于是她的图书馆规模一路扩张，最终比她旧居中的那座大了一倍。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">骆氏状所</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">律师事务所 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无派系</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>骆熙旸</strong>（热切的女性人类律师 4）察觉DC 23，意志DC 21，交涉 +12，法律学识 +14，社会 +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 若熙旸乐于帮助，PC可以利用她那套杂糅而丰富的藏书、案例研究与记录，在事务所内进行研究时，对与柳岸镇相关的回忆知识检定获得+1环境加值。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 熙旸总是需要人帮忙归档文件、誊写契约，以及裁断争端。PC可以在此使用交涉或法律学识来赚取收入。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W20. Luo and Laws\">W20. Luo and Laws</h2>\n<p>Lung Wa’s laws, after being revised time and time again by self-serving rulers, are a bag of contradictions, allowing independent lawyers, such as Luo Xi Yang, to make a decent living attempting to make sense of them. Promised by the lumber lords who invited her here that rural life would be less stressful, Xi Yang arrived with only the essential 10-volume Imperial Compendium. Quickly, the lawyer discovered that Willowshore’s legal issues were as complicated, if not more so, than what she’d previously encountered in the city of Sze, and thus her library grew to a size that doubled the one in her former home.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Luo &amp; Laws</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Law Office 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Luo Xi Yang</strong> (eager female human lawyer 4) Perception DC 23, Will DC 21, Diplomacy +12, Law Lore +14, Society +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> If Xi Yang is helpful, the PCs can make use of her eclectic collection of books, case studies, and records to gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge checks associated with Willowshore while researching in the office.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> Xi Yang is always in need of help with filing documents, scribing contracts, and adjudicating disagreements. A PC can Earn Income here with Diplomacy or Law Lore.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Downtown Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇镇区 Downtown Willowshore",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W19. Downtown Willowshore\">W19. 柳岸镇镇区</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇镇区仍是镇上的主要行动中心。东北方曾经矗立着总督的住所与办公处，也兼作村子的银行与金库——但如今这整片区域都成了一块神秘的空地。总督及其宅邸究竟发生了什么，是PC们最终会在本条冒险路径中解开的重大谜团之一。这块空地以南是帝国营房。十字路口以北、与一处空旷广场相对的位置，是村里每周舒剧演出的舞台。附近的道路两侧，分别是柳岸镇最繁忙的店铺之一树雀居，以及柳岸镇唯一的公共澡堂乐天河童。</p>\n<p>更为详细的柳岸镇镇区探索内容见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}，但下列四处设施构成了该区域最重要的地点。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">七彩鸣鸟</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">剧院 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大野和马</strong>（合群的男性狐妖导演 5）察觉 DC 22，意志 DC 20，交涉 +13，表演 +13，雪琳传说 +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 每月一次，PC可以尝试一次 @Check[performance|dc:25] 检定，试镜大野和马某部作品中的一个角色。成功时，该PC在当月以表演进行的赚取收入检定，其任务等级上限等同于柳岸镇的等级或该PC的等级（取较高者）。</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">树雀居</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">商号 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>三美奈户弥</strong>（友善的女性人类家族女族长 3）察觉 DC 18，意志 DC 20，制造 +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 多亏三美家事先规划，柳岸镇储备了足够的食物，能够让全村以勉强糊口的生活水平支撑到冬季。若PC们至少被南岸所喜爱，他们便可在此免费食宿以利用这些储备。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>货物</strong> 酒类、谷物、腌渍食品、口粮</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">乐天河童</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">商号 1</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>华德哥</strong>（健谈的男性半身人澡堂老板 1）察觉 DC 17，意志 DC 17，交涉 +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 一旦澡堂修复完成，PC们便可免费使用设施。每天一次，在温水中浸泡1小时可帮助强化该PC的免疫系统——接下来24小时内对该PC进行治疗疾病的尝试获得+1物品加值。</p>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp\" data-tooltip=\"郑鹏\" alt=\"郑鹏，一名戴着铁制护卫头盔的男性人类。\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp')\" />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">澡堂的经营者德哥几乎知道镇上所有流言蜚语，但他会把嘴闭得很紧。只要PC们搜集信息是为了正当理由，且德哥至少对他们是友善的，与他闲聊即可让PC们的搜集信息检定投掷两次并取较佳结果。这是一次命运效果，每周可用一次。</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">守卫署</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">营房 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>郑鹏</strong>（沉着的男性人类守卫军官 3）察觉 DC 18，意志 DC 18，威吓 +9</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>货物</strong> 护甲、装备维护工具、武器</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 只要队伍至少被北岭人所喜爱，PC就可以在此协助约束守卫纪律。如此一来，便可用威吓来赚取收入。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W19. Downtown Willowshore\">W19. Downtown Willowshore</h2>\n<p>Downtown Willowshore remains a major hub of activity in town. To the northeast once stood the governor’s home and office, which also served as the village’s bank and treasury—but today, this entire area is a mysterious empty lot. What happened to the governor and his estate is one of the great mysteries the PCs will eventually solve during this Adventure Path. South of this empty lot lie the imperial barracks. To the north of the crossroad, opposite an empty square, is the stage for the village’s weekly Shu Opera performance. Nearby, on opposite sides of the road are one of Willowshore’s busiest stores, the Treesparrow’s Rest, and Willowshore’s only public bathhouse, the Happy Kappa.</p>\n<p>See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2} for a more detailed exploration of downtown Willowshore, but the following four establishments comprise the most important locations in the area.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">The Seven-Colored Songbird</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Theater 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Kazuma Oono</strong> (gregarious male kitsune director 5) Perception DC 22, Will DC 20, Diplomacy +13, Performance +13, Shelyn Lore +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> Once a month, a PC can audition for a role in one of Kazuma Oono’s productions by attempting a @Check[performance|dc:25] check. On a success, the task level limit for Earn Income checks using Performance for that PC during that month is equal to Willowshore’s level or the PC’s level, whichever is higher.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Treesparrow’s Rest</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Business 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Nadoya Sanmi</strong> (friendly female human family matriarch 3) Perception DC 18, Will DC 20, Crafting +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Thanks to the Sanmi family’s pre-planning, Willowshore has enough food stores to support the village on a subsistence level of living until winter. If the PCs are at least liked by Southbank, they can stay here free of charge to take advantage of this.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> alcohol, grains, preserved foods, rations</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">The Happy Kappa</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Business 1</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Hua De-ge</strong> (chatty male halfling bathhouse owner 1) Perception DC 17, Will DC 17, Diplomacy +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Once the bathhouse has been restored, the PCs can use the facilities free of charge. Once per day, a 1-hour soak in the warm waters helps to bolster the PC’s immune system—attempts to Treat Disease on that PC during the next 24 hours gain a +1 item bonus.</p>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zheng Peng\" alt=\"Zheng Peng, a male human wearing an iron guard helmet.\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp')\" />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">The bathhouse’s proprietor, De-ge, knows just about every bit of gossip in town, though he keeps his mouth shut about it. Providing the PCs are collecting information for a good cause and De-ge is at least friendly, chatting with him allows the PCs to roll Gather Information checks twice and take the better result. This is a fortune effect and can be used once per week.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Guard Office</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Barracks 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Zheng Peng</strong> (stoic male human watch officer 3) Perception DC 18, Will DC 18, Intimidation +9</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> armor, gear maintenance equipment, weapons</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> As long as the party is at least liked by Northridge, a PC can help to keep guards in line here. Doing so allows one to Earn Income using Intimidation.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Willowshore Dam": {
              "name": "柳岸镇大坝 Willowshore Dam",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W18. Willowshore Dam\">W18. 柳岸镇大坝</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的大坝是一项小型的工程奇迹。它的主体由精确拼合的深灰色大理石板构成，并雕刻出经过仔细计算的弧度。大坝有两扇巨大的木闸门，可以关闭或开启，以降低湖面的水位。转动控制闸门的轮盘会自动让铃铛响起，向下游的人发出信号，让他们移动到安全地带。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W18. Willowshore Dam\">W18. Willowshore Dam</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s dam is a minor engineering marvel. Its main body is constructed out of precisely fitted slabs of dark-gray marble, carved with a carefully calculated curvature. The dam has two giant wooden gates that can be closed or opened to lower the level of the lake. Turning the wheel that controls the gates automatically causes a bell to ring, signaling those downriver to move away to safety.</p>"
            },
            "Woodraft Lake": {
              "name": "木筏湖 Woodraft Lake",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W17. Woodraft Lake\">W17. 木筏湖</h2>\n<p>龙华任命到柳岸镇的首任总督曾试图通过各种工程壮举来驯服臭名昭著的木棉河。这项努力的一部分，再加上对木材湿储的需求，促成了柳岸镇大坝的修建——以及随之而来的木筏湖。</p>\n<p>起初许多人抗议这项工程，因为形成的湖泊会淹没一些房屋与农田——其中包括村里供奉难婆的神龛。随后又关了几个人，所有抱怨便都停止了。大坝按时竣工。那位总督也因此获得升迁，并在不久后离开柳岸镇，但他没享受多久，便在一个阳光明媚的日子里被山体滑坡掩埋。尽管这故事的真实性颇为可疑，此后的总督从未阻止柳岸镇的村民将这座湖当作苦难寡妇的圣地来供奉。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W17. Woodraft Lake\">W17. Woodraft Lake</h2>\n<p>The first governor appointed to Willowshore by Lung Wa made an effort to tame the notorious Ceiba River through various engineering feats. Part of that effort, plus the demand for wet storage for wood, led to the construction of the Willowshore Dam—and by extension, Woodraft Lake.</p>\n<p>Many protested the construction at first, as the resulting lake would submerge some homes and farmlands—including the village’s shrine to Lady Nanbyo. A few imprisonments later, all complaints ceased. The dam was completed in due time. While the governor earned themself a promotion and left Willowshore soon after, they didn’t get to enjoy it for long before a landslide buried them on a bright sunny day. While the story’s veracity is somewhat dubious, subsequent governors have never stopped Willowshore’s villagers from treating the lake as a shrine to the Widow of Suffering.</p>"
            },
            "Nine Ear Shrine": {
              "name": "九耳神社 Nine Ear Shrine",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W16. Nine Ear Shrine\">W16. 九耳神社</h2>\n<p>这座泥墙小屋从外面看像一间粮仓。其内部向地下延伸10英尺，进入一个四壁以石材衬砌的封闭空间；正中央矗立着一尊15英尺高的九尾狐大理石雕像。它的脖子上挂着一条用干草编成的巨大魂魄之绳。地下室的墙面装饰着彩绘雕刻，描绘了@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{大狐女}的故事。</p>\n<p>十五年前，欧家一位绝望的母亲在一家人被一名腐败的守卫聚拢起来准备处决时，把她的婴儿藏在了这里。等守卫们发现少了一个孩子时，一大群狐狸已经包围了神社。守卫们不愿冒着触怒神圣狂怒的风险，便撤退了。家族的盟友很快赶到并救走了婴儿；就在那时，狐狸们也随之消失。</p>\n<p>那个婴儿——欧巴明——在远房亲戚的照料下长大。尽管她显露出欧家崇敬自然的倾向，巴明仍希望通过侍奉大狐女来偿还这份救命之恩。虽然有人质疑她的意图，但大多数柳岸居民都支援她的奉献。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">九耳神社</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">神殿 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>欧巴明</strong>（虔诚的女性人类祭司3）察觉 DC 18，意志 DC 20，制作 +5（受训），宗教 +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 巴明只会在她的态度乐于帮助时提供服务。她能制作最高至2环的符箓（<em>宝藏宝库</em> 76–79）、来自神圣或原初法术表的1环法术卷轴，以及@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.clyXfh0aVXgij2Hb]{狼之牙}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Yew9oddFsH0KeDLh]{猎手之灾}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.jdDDqv9LbEYX2wAE]{猿猴徽章}与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.nXStoLxPrrP2b6WB]{青铜牛垂饰}护符。</p>\n</section>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">售卖：符箓、卷轴、护符</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W16. Nine Ear Shrine\">W16. Nine Ear Shrine</h2>\n<p>This mud-wall hut looks like a grain storage hut on the outside. Its interior descends 10 feet underground into an enclosed space lined with stone, in the middle of which sits a 15-foot-tall marble statue of a nine-tailed fox. A large spiritual rope made of hay hangs off its neck. The walls of the basement are decorated with painted carvings that depict stories of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{Daikitsu}.</p>\n<p>Fifteen years ago, a desperate mother of the Ouh family hid her baby here as the family was rounded up for execution by a corrupt guard. By the time the guards knew about the missing offspring, a large skulk of foxes had surrounded the temple. Unwilling to tempt divine wrath, the guards retreated. Allies of the family soon arrived to rescue the baby, at which point the foxes vanished.</p>\n<p>That baby, Ouh Ba-Ming, grew up under the care of distant relatives. While she shows signs of the Ouh family’s inclinations toward the veneration of nature, Ba-Ming wishes to return her life debt by serving Daikitsu. While some question her intentions, most Willowshorers support her dedication.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Nine Ear Shrine</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Temple 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Ouh Ba-Ming</strong> (devoted female human priest 3) Perception DC 18, Will DC 20, Crafting +5 (Trained), Religion +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Ba-ming only provides her services if her attitude is helpful. She can craft fulus up to 2nd level (<em>Treasure Vault</em> 76–79), 1st-level spell scrolls from the divine or primal spell list, and the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.clyXfh0aVXgij2Hb]{Wolf Fang}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Yew9oddFsH0KeDLh]{Hunter's Bane}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.jdDDqv9LbEYX2wAE]{Monkey Pin}, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.nXStoLxPrrP2b6WB]{Bronze Bull Pendant} talismans.</p>\n</section>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">Wares fulus, scrolls, talismans</p>"
            },
            "Rebel’s Leatherworks": {
              "name": "里氏制革厂 Rebel’s Leatherworks",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W15. Rebel’s Leatherworks\">W15. 里氏制革厂</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇对皮革与兽皮制品的需求一直很高，主要原因是这家本地作坊一直难以留住足够的雇员来满足这份需求。制革厂的老板维图姆尼亚尔在这些困境持续之下变得越来越乖戾、越来越暴躁——讽刺的是，这些困境最初正是由他糟糕的态度所导致的。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">里氏制革厂</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">制革厂 1</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>维图姆尼亚尔</strong>（脾气暴躁的男性纳迦吉制革工 3）察觉 DC 18，意志 DC 20，制作 +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 兽皮与皮革物品</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 若一名PC至少被南岸与北岭人喜爱，便能在此协助制作皮革制品，并且可以尝试进行一项等级等于柳岸镇等级+1或更低的任务。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W15. Rebel’s Leatherworks\">W15. Rebel’s Leatherworks</h3>\n<p>Demand for leather and hide goods has been high throughout Willowshore, primarily as a result of this local workshop’s struggles with keeping enough employees in order to keep up with said demand. Vitumniar, the leatherworks’ owner, has only grown more surly and short-tempered as these struggles continue—struggles ironically caused by his bad attitude in the first place.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Rebel’s Leatherworks</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Tannery 1</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Vitumniar</strong> (cantankerous male nagaji tanner 3) Perception DC 18, Will DC 20, Crafting +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> hide and leather items</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> A PC who’s at least liked by Southbank and Northridge, can help craft leather goods here and can attempt a task of a level equal to Willowshore’s level +1 or less.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Cloud Paper House": {
              "name": "云纸屋 Cloud Paper House",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W14. Cloud Paper House\">W14. 云纸屋</h3>\n<p>在柳岸镇的工业区仍在营业的三家商号之中，云纸屋是唯一称得上“兴旺”的。这在很大程度上要归功于其主人川冈·迈娜所付出的辛勤与尽责：他不仅致力于支持与保护自己的雇员，还及时调整工厂的生产重点，以满足城镇不断变化的需求，或为本店生产的各式纸制品开发新的用途。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">云纸屋</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">造纸厂 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>川冈·迈娜</strong>（忠诚的男性天狗公会领袖 3）察觉 DC 20，意志 DC 20，制作 +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 纸张与纸制品，例如法术书与配方簿</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 柳岸镇需要大量纸张来修复那些推拉门。一名至少受到南岸喜爱的PC可以在此协助制作纸张，并在以赚取收入为目的进行制作检定时，获得制作检定的+1物品加值。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W14. Cloud Paper House\">W14. Cloud Paper House</h3>\n<p>Of the three businesses that remain open in Willowshore’s industrial district, Cloud Paper House is the only one that could be called “thriving.” This is in no small part due to the hard work and diligence its owner, Myna Kawaka has put into not only supporting and protecting his employees, but in pivoting to adjust the focus of the factory to either meet the town’s changing needs or to develop new roles for the wide range of paper products this establishment produces.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Cloud Paper House</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Paper Mill 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Myna Kawaka</strong> (devoted male tengu guild leader 3) Perception DC 20, Will DC 20, Crafting +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> paper and paper products such as spellbooks and formula books</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> Willowshore is going to need a lot of paper to fix all those sliding doors. A PC who’s at least liked by Southbank can help craft paper here and gains a +1 item bonus to Crafting checks to Earn Income.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Jadeite Essentials": {
              "name": "玉液琼浆 Jadeite Essentials",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W13. Jadeite Essentials\">W13. 玉液琼浆</h3>\n<p>这家独特的店铺曾经容纳过两门彼此相辅相成的生意——一家蒸馏厂和一处吹制玻璃工坊。不幸的是，最近的攻击中，大部分蒸馏装备都被怪物摧毁，令店主诗织里一时不知该何去何从，并在考虑是否要收拾行装返回精瑛，与那里的家人团聚。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">玉液琼浆</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">蒸馏厂 2</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">北岭人</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>诗织里</strong>（心烦意乱的女性艾尤瓦林酿酒师 2）察觉 DC 19，意志 DC 19，酒精学识 +10，制作 +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 酒精、精油与香水、玻璃器皿与玻璃物品</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 由于蒸馏装备大多已被怪物摧毁，这家工坊仅剩店内的吹制玻璃设施。一名至少受北岭人喜爱的 PC 可以在此协助制作玻璃器皿，并在以制作检定赚取收入时获得 +1 物品加值。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W13. Jadeite Essentials\">W13. Jadeite Essentials</h3>\n<p>This unique establishment once housed two different businesses that supported each other—a distillery and a glassblowing facility. Unfortunately, much of the distilling equipment was destroyed by the monsters during the recent attack, leaving owner Shioli not quite sure what to do next and considering the option of pulling up stakes and heading back to Jinin to reunite with family there.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Jadeite Essentials</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Distillery 2</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Northridge</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Shioli</strong> (distraught female aiuvarin brewer 2) Perception DC 19, Will DC 19, Alcohol Lore +10, Crafting +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> alcohol, essential oils and perfume, glassware and glass items</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> With the distilling equipment mostly destroyed by the monsters, all that’s left of the plant is its in-house glassblowing facilities. A PC who’s at least liked by Northridge can help craft glassware here and gains a +1 item bonus to Crafting checks to Earn Income.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Industrial District": {
              "name": "工业区 Industrial District",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W13—W15. Industrial District\">W13—W15. 工业区</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的龙华木材老板还经营着许多与从林中取来的材料相关的其他生意。许多产业工人明确是为这份工作来到柳岸镇的，把家人和朋友留在身后。</p>\n<p>木材老板离开后，何总督夺取了控制权，并命令工人继续工作。工人们因自己在此事上毫无选择而愤怒，近来一直在深夜聚集，在资深造纸与制书人川冈的带领下，讨论他们应如何与总督谈判：放行那些想离开的人，并公平支付选择留下的人。因此，川冈被视为工业区非官方的“公会会长”。</p>\n<p>随着龙华的崩溃，许多曾在此繁荣的商号纷纷关门歇业，只剩下三家仍以不同程度维持运作；下文将对它们分别作更详细的介绍。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W13—W15. Industrial District\">W13—W15. Industrial District</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s Lung Wa lumber bosses had a host of other businesses related to materials taken from the woods. Many industrial workers came to Willowshore explicitly for this work, leaving family and friends behind.</p>\n<p>After the lumber bosses left, Governor Heh seized control and ordered the workers to continue working. Upset that they had no choice in the matter, the workers have been gathering late at night under the guidance of Kawaka, a senior paper and bookmaker, to discuss how they should negotiate with the governor to release those who want to leave and fairly pay those who elect to stay. As a result, Kawaka is viewed as an unofficial “guild master” of the Industrial District.</p>\n<p>With the collapse of Lung Wa, many of the businesses that once thrived here closed up shop, leaving only three in various levels of activity, each of which is presented in greater detail below.</p>"
            },
            "Matsu’s Home": {
              "name": "马苏的家 Matsu’s Home",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W12. Matsu’s Home\">W12. 马苏的家</h2>\n<p><strong>马苏 </strong>（退休的人类厨师 1 级）算得上是南岸一个颇有名气的本地“招牌”人物——一位健谈的老者，似乎乐于把自己往那种吵闹又暴躁、怀念“过去美好时光”的刻板老头形象上靠。其实，马苏知道自己最好的日子已经过去了。作为终身单身汉，他从未抽出时间经营社交生活（更别说成家），每一天的流逝都让他对自己认为被虚度的青春更加懊悔。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W12. Matsu’s Home\">W12. Matsu’s Home</h2>\n<p><strong>Matsu </strong>(retired human chef 1) is something of a notorious local establishment in Southbank—a gregarious elderly man who seems to enjoy leaning in to the cliche of the loud and cranky oldster who longs for the “good old days.” In truth, Matsu knows his best days are behind him, and as a lifelong bachelor who never found the time to focus on a social life (much less build a family), each passing day brings him more regret for what he regards as a wasted youth.</p>"
            },
            "Dawnstep Bridge": {
              "name": "晨步桥 Dawnstep Bridge",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W11. Dawnstep Bridge\">W11. 晨步桥</h2>\n<p>在早期，晨步桥不过是一系列漂浮的木制平台，并配有导向绳索，以便协助通行，或收回部分桥段让河流船只通过；但当钱开始大量涌入城镇时，一座真正的石桥建成，使城镇两岸之间的联系更加牢固。桥墩将桥面支撑在下方水面上方七英尺处，留出了足够空间，让从旧伐木营地顺流放下的原木漂入木筏湖，但也阻止了比木筏或小艇更大的船只通行——这点不便很快就被柳岸镇的人民抛诸脑后，因为他们逐渐体会到这条更为坚固的两岸连接所带来的好处。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W11. Dawnstep Bridge\">W11. Dawnstep Bridge</h2>\n<p>In the early days, Dawnstep Bridge was little more than a series of floating wooden platforms with guidelines to aid in crossing or in retracting sections to allow for river traffic to pass, but by the time money began pouring into town, the construction of a proper stone bridge helped create a stronger link between the town’s two shores. The bridge’s pilings support the bridge seven feet above the water below, enough room for logs floated downriver from the lumber camp to float into Woodraft Lake, but prevented the passage of watercraft larger than rafts or skiffs—an inconvenience that the people of Willowshore swiftly got over as they grew to appreciate the benefits the much more solid link between shores provided.</p>"
            },
            "Eternal Lantern": {
              "name": "长明灯 Eternal Lantern",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W10. Eternal Lantern\">W10. 长明灯</h2>\n<p>三福青楼建立之后（但在它成为旅店之前），柳岸镇的人口规模已增长到足以按神门的标准被视为一座城镇；这意味着必须在城镇入口附近、某处重要的十字路口或一座桥上，始终维持一盏点亮的灯笼。若这些地点之一没有点亮的灯笼，就表明该城镇已被遗弃；人们相信这会招来诸如害兽、幽灵（特征）、野兽，以及更糟的东西。在柳岸镇，一件名为<em>长明灯</em>的小型神器承担了这一用途——这是 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}大师本人传下来的珍贵传家宝。这盏灯笼在本冒险的第1幕中扮演重要角色，并能为PC提供持久的加值（见第40页）。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W10. Eternal Lantern\">W10. Eternal Lantern</h2>\n<p>After the Thrice-Blessed Brothel was established (but before it became an inn), Willowshore’s population had grown enough in size to be considered a town by Shenmen standards, meaning that a lit lantern must be maintained at all times within the town near the entrance, at a major crossroads, or at a bridge. The lack of a lit lantern at one of these locations suggests that the town is abandoned, which is believed to invite the likes of vermin, ghosts, beasts, and worse. In Willowshore, a minor artifact known as the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> serves this purpose—a treasured heirloom from Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} herself. This lantern plays a major role in Act 1 of the adventure, and can grant long-lasting bonuses to the PCs (see page 40).</p>"
            },
            "Lady of Souls": {
              "name": "司魂娘娘 Lady of Souls",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W9. Lady of Souls\">W9. 司魂娘娘</h2>\n<p>龙华最初扩展到柳岸镇时的主要关切之一，是降低不死生物起义的可能性。他们通过建造一座供奉@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}的大教堂解决了这个问题。</p>\n<p>伊丽丝·堪多拉是一位来自果卡的第二代塔尔丹人，是这里现任的女祭司。伊丽丝小时候曾来过柳岸镇和谭杉寺，她从未想过成为法莱斯玛的牧师，会让她有机会永久回到这座她记忆犹新的村庄。她将这一巧合视为法莱斯玛之手安排的命运，因此一直恪尽职守、勤勉服务。她喜欢独自带着长笛待在墓园里，并常在那里演奏，以帮助安抚术那些最近葬于此地者的魂魄。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">司魂娘娘庙</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">神殿 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">无隶属</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>伊丽丝·堪多拉</strong>（富有同理心的人类女性，法莱斯玛牧师 5）察觉 DC 25，意志 DC 25，制作 +13，表演 +13，宗教 +13</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 由于大教堂在怪物攻击中受损，在本幕期间伊丽丝只能提供最高至2环的神圣卷轴。到第二幕夏末入秋后，伊丽丝每4天可按正常价格制作或铭刻一次@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.JQdwHECogcTzdd8R]{幽冥}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.r28DjJEjF6jvCcfb]{仁慈}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.DKWuJb2rSgiotOG7]{+1 强度}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.DxCuJKynlnMQZHgp]{强击}以及@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.LwQb7ryTC8FlOXgX]{活化}武器符文。在此之前，如果PC向她提出请求、请求她帮忙，伊丽丝可以制作以下物品：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.HHELOoN5GVonUiIa]{泪天使垂饰}、镇魂炸药（@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.LNd5u19GqC51ngby]{次级}与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Wf94e8YNhZdIvWc9]{中级}），以及治疗药水（@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.2RuepCemJhrpKKao]{轻微}and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.e0vSAQfxhHauiAoD]{次级}）。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 消耗品类宗教物品，神圣卷轴</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W9. Lady of Souls\">W9. Lady of Souls</h2>\n<p>One of Lung Wa’s chief concerns when they first expanded into Willowshore was to reduce the likelihood of an undead uprising. They solved it by building a cathedral to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}.</p>\n<p>Elizeth Candora, a second-generation Taldan from Goka, is the current priestess here. Having once visited Willowshore and the Tan Sugi monastery as a child, Elizeth never imagined that becoming a cleric of Pharasma would lead to an opportunity for her to permanently return to the village she so vividly recalls. She sees this coincidence as fate arranged by Pharasma’s hands and therefore serves dutifully and diligently. She’s fond of spending time alone in the graveyard with her flute and often plays the instrument there to help soothe the spirits of those recently buried therein.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Her Fluvial Lady of Souls</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Temple 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unaffiliated</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Elizeth Candora</strong> (empathetic female human cleric of Pharasma 5) Perception DC 25, Will DC 25, Crafting +13, Performance +13, Religion +13</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> As the cathedral was damaged during the monster attack, Elizeth can only provide divine scrolls up to 2nd-level during this act. Once summer ends and fall begins in Act 2, Elizeth can create or inscribe the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.JQdwHECogcTzdd8R]{Ghost Touch}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.r28DjJEjF6jvCcfb]{Merciful}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.DKWuJb2rSgiotOG7]{+1 Potency}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.DxCuJKynlnMQZHgp]{Striking}, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.LwQb7ryTC8FlOXgX]{Vitalizing} weapon runes once every 4 days at normal cost. Before that, Elizeth can create the following items if the PCs Request her help: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.HHELOoN5GVonUiIa]{Crying Angel Pendant}, ghost charges (@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.LNd5u19GqC51ngby]{Lesser} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Wf94e8YNhZdIvWc9]{Moderate}), and healing potions (@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.2RuepCemJhrpKKao]{Minor}and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.e0vSAQfxhHauiAoD]{Lesser}).</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> consumable religious items, divine scrolls</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Milling Houses": {
              "name": "磨坊 Milling Houses",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W8. Milling Houses\">W8. 磨坊</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇有许多磨坊，其中包括两座水力驱动、三座风力驱动，以及10座由人力或役用动物驱动。充足的磨坊运作确保即便有一两座磨坊因例行维护或故障而停摆，也绝不会危及村子的需求。</p>\n<p>在磨坊工作强度很大，而且由于每天需求不同，工时也可能不规律。磨坊工人的领头人乔春虎通过鼓励、顶回不合理的要求、保持工资稳定以及午夜啃食来维持高昂士气。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">磨坊</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">生意 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>乔春虎</strong>（乐于支持的男性人类磨坊工人 4）察觉 DC 20，意志 DC 20，阿巴达尔学识 +10，制造 +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 去壳谷物、谷物面粉、石制物体</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>工作</strong> 磨坊总是在找额外人手来帮忙让磨盘不停转动。PC可以在这里使用运动来赚取收入。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W8. Milling Houses\">W8. Milling Houses</h2>\n<p>Willowshore has numerous milling houses, including two powered by water, three by wind, and 10 powered by people or draft animals. The abundance of milling operations ensures that losing one or two mills to routine maintenance or malfunction never jeopardizes the village’s needs.</p>\n<p>Working at the mills is intense, and the hours can be irregular due to the demand each day. The millers’ leader, Chung-hu, keeps morale high with encouragement, pushing back against unreasonable demands, keeping wages stable, and midnight snacks.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Milling Houses</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Business 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Choe Chung-hu</strong> (supportive male human miller 4) Perception DC 20, Will DC 20, Abadar Lore +10, Crafting +12</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> De-husked grain, grain flour, stone objects</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Work</strong> The mills are always looking for extra hands to help keep the stones turning. A PC can use Athletics to Earn Income here.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Silvermist Lodges": {
              "name": "银雾斋 Silvermist Lodges",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W7. Silvermist Lodges\">W7. 银雾斋</h2>\n<p>\n  银雾斋分布在镇南的三处院落中。在每个地点（区域\n  <strong>W7a–W7c</strong>），斋舍的木作顺应木纹走向，使建筑呈现出一种与精灵建筑相关的自然有机之感。早些年柳岸镇初次尝试实现自给自足时，八名精灵冒险者定居于此；鉴于他们更长的寿命，他们寻求的是一份短期契约。尽管这最初的八名精灵如今都已不再居住在柳岸镇，但他们留下了许多子嗣与后裔，其中包括艾欧梅娜，她现在在中央院落（区域 <strong>W7b</strong>）经营这些斋舍。\n</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">银雾斋</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">狩猎小屋 2</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>艾欧梅娜</strong>（耐心的非二元精灵游侠 2）察觉 DC 21，意志 DC 19，制作 +7，自然 +8，生存 +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 动物部位、套索补给</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W7. Silvermist Lodges\">W7. Silvermist Lodges</h2>\n<p>\n  The Silvermist Lodges are split between three compounds south of town. At each location (areas\n  <strong>W7a–W7c</strong>), the lodges’ woodwork conforms to the grain of the wood, giving the buildings an organic look associated with elven architecture. In the days when Willowshore first tried to become self-sufficient, eight elven adventurers settled here, seeking a short-term contract given their longer life spans. Though none of these original eight elves live in Willowshore anymore, they left many offspring and descendants behind, including Aiomena, who now runs the lodges from the central compound (area <strong>W7b</strong>).\n</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Silvermist Lodges</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Hunting Lodge 2</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Aiomena</strong> (patient nonbinary elf ranger 2) Perception DC 21, Will DC 19, Crafting +7, Nature +8, Survival +8</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> animal parts, snare supplies</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Thrice-Blessed Inn": {
              "name": "三福客栈 Thrice-Blessed Inn",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W6. Thrice-Blessed Inn\">W6. 三福客栈</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-otis.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Reverent Mother Otis\" alt=\"奥蒂丝，一位穿着蓝色长袍的性别流动半精灵。\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-otis.webp')\" />\n<p>柳岸镇的三福客栈最初是三福青楼，由三位分别信奉@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{国府幸}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{卡莉丝翠}与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{莎琳}的牧师建立。旧青楼为隐私而设的厚重窗板——以及三位不同神祇的祝福——都是极佳的防御，有助于在遭受攻击时保护这座建筑。</p>\n<p>政治上的复杂状况迫使青楼的老板奥蒂丝妈妈在龙华崩溃前的几年就关闭了这家店。在柳岸镇本地律师骆熙旸的帮助下，她得以援引一条鲜为人知的法律，使他们免于被驱逐，并允许他们继续将这栋建筑作为客栈经营。这座前青楼非常适合一次性安置并供养大量人群；在怪物入侵之后的修复工作完成前，它正好能成为那些失去家园者的理想栖身之所。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">三福客栈</span> <span class=\"keepme\">居住区 4</span></h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>虔敬的奥蒂丝妈妈</strong>（精明的性别流动艾乌瓦林客栈掌柜 4），察觉DC 20，意志DC 20，交涉+12，卡莉丝翠学识+10，柳岸镇学识+10</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> PC可以花费1 gp雇用一名客栈雇员协助进行一次搜集信息检定——这么做会使PC在进行搜集信息的检定时获得+1状态加值。任何缺乏住宿或食物的PC都可以在柳岸镇从怪物入侵中恢复期间在此获得维持生存水准的食宿，除非他们曾严重冒犯过虔敬的奥蒂丝妈妈本人。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W6. Thrice-Blessed Inn\">W6. Thrice-Blessed Inn</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-otis.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Reverent Mother Otis\" alt=\"Otis, a genderfluid half-elf wearing a blue robe.\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-otis.webp')\" />\n<p>Willowshore’s Thrice-Blessed Inn began as the Thrice-Blessed Brothel, and was founded by three clerics of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{Kofusachi}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{Calistria}, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{Shelyn}. The former brothel’s heavy shutters for privacy—and the blessing of three different gods—are great defenses that help protect the building during attacks.</p>\n<p>Political complications forced the brothel’s owner, Mother Otis, to shut down the establishment only a few years before Lung Wa’s collapse. With the aid of Willowshore’s local lawyer, Luo Xi Yang, she was able to rely upon an obscure law that prevented their eviction and allowed them to continue to operate the building as an inn. Well suited for housing and feeding large numbers of people all at once, the former brothel is perfect for those who lost their homes until repairs in the wake of the monster invasion are completed.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">Thrice-Blessed Inn</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Living Quarters 4</span></h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Reverent Mother Otis</strong> (canny genderfluid aiuvarin innkeeper 4), Perception DC 20, Will DC 20, Diplomacy +12, Calistria Lore +10, Willowshore Lore +10</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> A PC can hire one of the inn’s employees to assist in a Gather Information check at a cost of 1 gp—doing so grants the PC a +1 status bonus to their check to Gather Information. Any PCs who lack lodging or food can receive subsistence levels of living here while Willowshore recovers from the monster invasion unless they’ve greatly offended Reverent Mother Otis personally.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Matsuki Estate": {
              "name": "松木宅 Matsuki Estate",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W5. Matsuki Estate\">W5. 松木宅</h2>\n<p>“老松木”曾在谭杉寺的首席木匠门下当学徒。在告别师父后，他带领家人建造了一座大型宅邸，以容纳他们全家二十来口人。迷信的家主随后确保外墙用含有受祝福盐与圣水的石灰岩加固，这帮助宅邸挺过了怪物入侵。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">松木宅</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">居住区 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>松木胜</strong>（怀旧的男性人类木匠 5）察觉 DC 22（若为视觉则为 20），意志 DC 22，制作 +13，柳岸镇学识 +16</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W5. Matsuki Estate\">W5. Matsuki Estate</h2>\n<p>“Old Matsuki” once apprenticed to the head carpenter of the Tan Sugi monastery. After taking leave from his master, he led his family to construct a large estate to house all two dozen of them. The superstitious patriarch then made sure that the outer walls were bolstered with limestone containing blessed salts and holy water, which helped the estate weather the monster invasion.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Matsuki Estate</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Living Quarters 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Matsuki Shou</strong> (nostalgic male human carpenter 5) Perception DC 22 (20 if visual), Will DC 22, Crafting +13, Willowshore Lore +16</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Abadar Shrine": {
              "name": "财神爷神龛 Abadar Shrine",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W4. Abadar Shrine\">W4. 财神爷神龛</h2>\n<p>这座以暮木镶边装饰的神龛内，供奉着一尊3英尺高的石灰岩@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{阿巴达尔}雕像；它一手握着铁锹，另一手拿着泥铲。据说，这尊雕像曾先被送往过峡，在大银行举行仪式以迎请阿巴达尔的神圣祝福，随后再用渡船运回柳岸镇。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W4. Abadar Shrine\">W4. Abadar Shrine</h2>\n<p>This duskwood-trimmed shrine houses a 3-foot-tall limestone statue of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{Abadar} that holds a shovel in one hand and a trowel in the other. The statue was reportedly taken to Goka first to ritualistically invite Abadar’s divine blessings at the Grand Bank before being ferried back to Willowshore.</p>"
            },
            "Graveside Manners": {
              "name": "坟边居 Graveside Manners",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W3. Graveside Manners\">W3. 坟边居</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的居民在早期实行火葬以防止不死生物的出现。这片老墓园中的坟墓安置着许多早期定居者的骨灰瓮。如今，只有少数家族仍将坟边居用作墓地。多亏了墓园看守人尤素珍，墓碑上依然不生地衣与苔藓。</p>\n<p>尤素珍曾是谭杉寺的常客朝圣者，在寺院崩塌后定居柳岸镇并开了这家店。她初到镇上时，古怪的习惯与异乎寻常的信仰使一位特别令人厌恶的本地牧师（此人早已不在）在毫无证据的情况下指控她是死灵法师，但随着时间推移，她凭借药物的疗效赢得了全镇的认可。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">坟边居</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">草药店 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>尤素珍</strong>（神秘的女性精灵草药师 4）察觉 DC 21，意志 DC 21，制作 +14（大师）</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> PC可以以每天 1 sp 的价格租用尤素珍的专家级炼金实验室，用来制作他们自己的炼金物品</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 炼金灵药与工具、炼金试剂、新鲜与干燥的草药</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W3. Graveside Manners\">W3. Graveside Manners</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s residents practiced cremation in its early days to prevent undeath. The tombs in this old cemetery house the urns of many of those early settlers. Today, only a few families use Graveside Manners as a burial ground. The headstones remain free of lichen and moss, thanks to the graveyard’s keeper, So-Jin.</p>\n<p>Once a pilgrim who frequented the Tan Sugi monastery, So-Jin settled in Willowshore after the monastery’s collapse and opened this shop. When she first arrived in town, her strange habits and unusual beliefs compelled one particularly unpleasant local priest (a man now long gone) to accuse her (with no evidence) of being a necromancer, but in time she won the town over with the effectiveness of her medicine.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Graveside Manners</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Herbal Store 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>You So-Jin</strong> (mysterious female elf herbalist 4) Perception DC 21, Will DC 21, Crafting +14 (Master)</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> The PCs can rent usage of So-Jin’s expanded alchemist’s lab for 1 sp per day to craft their own alchemical items</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> alchemical elixirs and tools, alchemical reagents, fresh and dried herbs</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Willowshore Stables": {
              "name": "柳岸镇马场 Willowshore Stables",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W2. Willowshore Stables\">W2. 柳岸镇马场</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇马场是镇上为家养动物、宠物与牲畜提供兽医服务的设施。柳岸镇将牲畜作为役畜使用的习惯影响了当地的饮食文化，使许多人避免食用牛肉。</p>\n<p>夏季第一天怪物入侵柳岸镇时，柳岸镇马场及其诱人的牛群牧场成了不可能被忽视的目标。到黎明时分，牧场大多数围栏都被毁坏，几乎所有的牛与公牛都逃入了荒野。马场主人昆舜重和他十几岁的儿子蒙松一直在忙着抢修。这些问题是舜重在能为其他动物提供帮助之前必须先解决的。（PC可以在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}中协助牧场。）</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">柳岸镇马场</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">马场 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>昆舜重</strong>（关怀备至的男性人类兽医 3）察觉 DC 19，意志 DC 16，自然 +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 一旦牧场修复完毕，舜重便能以自然替代医疗，来对具有动物（特征）的生物执行医疗的未受训或受训动作，例如对目标进行治疗伤势。他每天最多可治疗六只动物，且每日每次治疗费用为1 sp。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 动物租赁、坐骑护甲、鞍袋、陆上载具</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W2. Willowshore Stables\">W2. Willowshore Stables</h2>\n<p>Willowshore Stables is the town’s veterinary facility for household animals, pets, and livestock. Willowshore’s use of livestock as beasts of burden influenced the local food culture, causing many to avoid eating beef.</p>\n<p>When monsters invaded Willowshore on the first day of summer, the Willowshore Stables and its tempting fields of cattle were an impossible target to ignore. By dawn, most of the ranch’s fences were destroyed and nearly all of the cattle and oxen had fled into the wilderness. The owner, Kum Soon-chong, and his teenage son, Meng-sung, have been scrambling to get things fixed. These are problems Soon-chong must solve first before he can provide help to other animals. (The PCs can help ranch in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}.)</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Willowshore Stables</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Stables 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Kum Soon-chong</strong> (caring male human veterinarian 3) Perception DC 19, Will DC 16, Nature +10</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> Once the ranch is repaired, Soon-chong can treat creatures with the animal trait using Nature in place of Medicine to perform Medicine untrained or trained actions, such as Treat Wounds, on the target. He can treat up to six animals per day, and each treatment per day costs 1 sp.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> animal rentals, barding, saddle bags, land vehicles</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Eternal Blaze Ironworks": {
              "name": "永火铁厂 Eternal Blaze Ironworks",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W1. Eternal Blaze Ironworks\">W1. 永火铁厂</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wu-xiuyong.webp\" data-tooltip=\"雍武秀\" alt=\"雍武秀，一名狐形的狐妖，身穿铁制护甲。\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wu-xiuyong.webp')\" />\n<p>在修道院建造期间，永火铁厂负责制作各种金属物品，从炊具、木工工具，到诸如合页、锁与箱子钥匙等小型金属零件。</p>\n<p>约十年前，雍武秀从父亲手中继承了这门生意。她以“铁锅匠”闻名；在柳岸镇不景气的那些年里，武秀走遍天夏各地，一边谋生，一边学习新技艺。除了精通打造武器与护甲之外，她还学会了加工一些非传统金属（如冷铁与银）的技能，不过她很少把这件事告诉别人。</p>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">永火铁厂</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">铁匠 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">南岸</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>雍武秀</strong>（勤勉的女性狐妖铁匠 3）察觉 DC 21，意志 DC 21，制作 +13</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>服务</strong> 除了常规金属物品外，武秀也能用冷铁或银来制作物体，但通常只会为至少对她而言算是友善的人这么做——她在自己的熔炉里藏匿着250 gp 的冷铁与250 gp 的银，可用于制作。</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>商品</strong> 金属制品，冒险道具（尤其是炊具），金属护甲，金属武器，金属盾牌</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"W1. Eternal Blaze Ironworks\">W1. Eternal Blaze Ironworks</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wu-xiuyong.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yong Wu-Xiu\" alt=\"Yong Wu-Xiu, a fox-like Kitsune wearing iron armor.\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wu-xiuyong.webp')\" />\n<p>In the days of the monastery’s construction, the Eternal Blaze Ironworks was responsible for creating metal items from cookware, woodworking tools, and small metal parts, such as hinges, locks, and keys for chests.</p>\n<p>Yong Wu-Xiu inherited the business from her father about a decade ago. Known as the Iron Pot Blacksmith, Wu spent Willowshore’s unprosperous years traveling throughout Tian Xia, both to earn a living and to learn new techniques. Other than mastering how to make weapons and armor, she also picked up the skill of working unconventional metals such as cold iron and silver, though she rarely shares this fact with anyone.</p>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Eternal Blaze Ironworks</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Blacksmith 3</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Southbank</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Yong Wu-Xiu</strong> (industrious female kitsune blacksmith 3) Perception DC 21, Will DC 21, Crafting +13</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Services</strong> In addition to regular metal items, Wu-Xiu can also craft objects out of cold iron or silver but generally does so only for those she’s at least friendly with—she has 250 gp of cold iron and 250 gp of silver on hand hidden in her forge that she can use to craft with.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Wares</strong> metalworks, adventuring gear (especially cookware), metal armor, metal weapons, metal shields</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Location Support": {
              "name": "地点支持 Location Support",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Location Support\">地点支持</h2>\n<p>以下页面中介绍的部分地点，会在末尾附上一段简短的数据表，汇总该地点的名称、等级（用于确定进行“赚取收入”任务的DC——记得每当柳岸镇自身等级提升时，都要相应提高这些DC，详见对页 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02peopleofwill00#growing-the-town]{小镇成长}）、货物与服务，以及在此工作或居住的重要NPC信息。这些地点还具有两种特征之一——南岸或北岭人。</p>\n<p>PC可以通过将负责该地点的NPC的态度调整为乐于帮助，从而获得这些地点的支援。PC第一次获得带有上述任一特征的地点的支援时，会获得与该特征对应派系的1点声望点数，除非他们已被该派系钦佩或尊敬；若已如此，则不再获得额外点数。（要在此之外获得更多声望点数，需要在冒险过程中采取特定动作。）</p>\n<p><strong>服务：</strong>许多NPC或地点可以制作特定物品。请求NPC制作一件物品，等同于以全价购买该物品，但会有4天的延迟。</p>\n<p><strong>态度：</strong>除非另有说明，NPC对PC的初始态度为不关心。若PC被某派系喜爱，则所有与该派系相关且原本不关心的NPC，其初始态度改为友善。若PC被某派系尊敬，则所有与该派系相关且原本不关心或友善的NPC，其初始态度改为乐于帮助，并会自动给予其地点的支援。</p>\n<p><strong>工作：</strong>其中一些地点会为“赚取收入”的休整模式活动提供加值。除非另有说明，在柳岸镇进行任何“赚取收入”尝试时，任务等级必须等于或低于柳岸镇的等级（冒险路径开始时为4级）。注意：通过被相关派系钦佩或尊敬，以及提高柳岸镇的聚落等级，都可以提升该任务等级上限。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Location Support\">Location Support</h2>\n<p>Some of the locations presented on the following pages end with a short stat block that summarizes the location’s name, level (for the purpose of determining DCs for Earn Income tasks—remember to adjust these up whenever Willowshore itself increases its level, as detailed in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02peopleofwill00#growing-the-town]{Growing the Town} on the facing page), wares and services, and information about significant NPCs who work or live there. These locations also have one of two traits—Southbank or Northridge.</p>\n<p>The PCs can gain the support of these locations by adjusting the attitude of the NPC who runs the site to be helpful. The first time a PC gains the support of a site with one of these traits, they earn 1 Reputation Point with the matching faction unless they’re already admired or revered by that faction, in which case no additional points are earned. (Earning Reputation Points beyond this requires specific actions taken during the course of the adventure itself.)</p>\n<p><strong>Services:</strong> Many NPCs or locations can craft specific items. Requesting an NPC to craft an item is equivalent to buying an item at full price with a four-day delay.</p>\n<p><strong>Attitudes:</strong> Unless otherwise specified, an NPC’s initial attitude toward the PCs is indifferent. If a PC becomes liked by a faction, all indifferent associated NPCs shift their initial attitude to friendly. If a PC becomes revered by a faction, all indifferent or friendly associated NPCs shift their initial attitude to helpful and automatically grant the support of their site.</p>\n<p><strong>Work:</strong> Some of these locations allow bonuses to Earn Income downtime activities. Unless otherwise indicated, any attempt to Earn Income in Willowshore must be of a task level equal to or less than Willowshore’s level (level 4 as the Adventure Path begins). Note that this maximum task level can be increased by becoming admired or revered with the associated faction, and also by raising Willowshore’s settlement level.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore’s Rivers and Creeks": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的河流与溪流 Willowshore’s Rivers and Creeks",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore’s Rivers and Creeks\">柳岸镇的河流与溪流</h2>\n<p>木棉河从柳岸镇的中心流过，河水向东奔流，最终汇入更大的杜月江。木棉河的水深在20到25英尺之间变化，但在柳岸镇大坝以西，这条河上唯一的水上交通工具是小艇和类似的小型划艇。木棉溪更为浅薄，水深很少超过6英尺。关于这些水道的更多信息，会出现在发生在其中或其附近的遭遇中。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore’s Rivers and Creeks\">Willowshore’s Rivers and Creeks</h2>\n<p>The Ceiba River flows through the center of Willowshore, its waters running to the east to eventually flow into the larger Duyue River. While the depth of the Ceiba varies between 20 and 25 feet, west of Willowshore Dam, the only watercraft on the river are skiffs and similar small rowboats. Ceiba Creek is even more shallow, rarely more than six feet deep. Additional information on these waterways appears in the encounters that take place within or nearby them.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Locations": {
              "name": "柳岸镇地点 Willowshore Locations",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore Locations\">柳岸镇地点</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇中的重要建筑与关键人物详见后续页面，其编号与第 10 页地图上的地点相对应。未标注的建筑为木结构，可能是商铺、住宅、农舍、储藏间，或依据其所处位置而定的其他杂项用途。在游戏过程中，追踪你在这些未标注建筑中新增的地点——这是让你们团的柳岸镇版本真正独具特色的绝佳方式！</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore Locations\">Willowshore Locations</h1>\n<p>Significant buildings and important people found in Willowshore are detailed on the following pages, with numbers corresponding to the locations on the map on page 10. Unlabeled buildings are wooden structures that might be shops, homes, farmhouses, storerooms, or other miscellaneous usage depending on their location. As you play, keep track of any new locations you place in these unlabeled buildings—this is an excellent way to make your table’s version of Willowshore truly your own!</p>"
            },
            "Building Reputation": {
              "name": "建立声望 Building Reputation",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Building Reputation\">建立声望</h1>\n<p>当PC们帮助镇民时，他们的声望会增长。所有NPC都有一个默认的起始态度，取决于队伍当前在其阵营中的声望。</p>\n<p>在开始时，队伍在两个阵营中的声望点数均为0。随着他们在这场战役中达成目标，他们会获得点数——或者在更少见的情况下，失去点数。下表进一步总结了声望的影响，并使用以下特性。</p>\n<p><strong>默认态度：</strong>这表示当PC们首次遭遇与该阵营相关的NPC时，该NPC的默认态度。无隶属关系的NPC始终具有不关心的默认态度。注意，对PC们变得敌对的NPC不会一见面就攻击他们（除非被挑衅），而是仅仅拒绝与PC们做生意或来往。</p>\n<p><strong>社交DC 修正：</strong>本栏中的调整值会应用于与该阵营NPC进行任何社交遭遇技能检定的DC。社交遭遇的基础DC总是包含在遭遇文本中。</p>\n<p><strong>赚取收入：</strong>这些阶层提供的环境加值与减值，适用于所有与该阵营的地点或NPC相关、为赚取收入而进行的检定。当PC们受到钦佩时，他们在该阵营处可尝试用来赚取收入的最大任务等级提高1；当他们受到尊敬时，则改为将最大任务等级提高2。</p>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>声望</th>\n      <th>点数</th>\n      <th>默认态度</th>\n      <th>社交DC 修正</th>\n      <th>赚取收入加值/减值</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>尊敬</td>\n      <td>31或更多</td>\n      <td>乐于帮助</td>\n      <td>–10</td>\n      <td>+3（视为高2级）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>钦佩</td>\n      <td>15到30</td>\n      <td>友善</td>\n      <td>–5</td>\n      <td>+2（视为高1级）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>喜爱</td>\n      <td>5到14</td>\n      <td>友善</td>\n      <td>–2</td>\n      <td>+1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>被无视</td>\n      <td>–4到4</td>\n      <td>不关心</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>不受欢迎</td>\n      <td>–5到–14</td>\n      <td>不友善</td>\n      <td>+2</td>\n      <td>–1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>憎恨</td>\n      <td>–15到–29</td>\n      <td>不友善</td>\n      <td>+5</td>\n      <td>–3</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>被追猎</td>\n      <td>–30或更少</td>\n      <td>敌对</td>\n      <td>+10</td>\n      <td>无法赚取收入</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Building Reputation\">Building Reputation</h1>\n<p>As the PCs aid the townspeople, their reputation grows. All NPCs have a default starting attitude based on the party’s current reputation with their faction.</p>\n<p>At the start, the party has 0 Reputation Points with both factions. As they accomplish goals during this campaign, they’ll gain points—or, more rarely, lose points. The table below summarizes the effects of reputation further, using the following qualities.</p>\n<p><strong>Default Attitude:</strong> This indicates the default attitude of an NPC associated with the faction when the PCs first encounter that NPC. Unaffiliated NPCs always have a default attitude of indifferent. Note that NPCs who become hostile to the PCs don’t attack them on sight (unless provoked), but instead, they simply refuse to do business or associate with the PCs.</p>\n<p><strong>Social DC Mod:</strong> The modifier in this column is applied to the DC of any social encounter skill check with an NPC of that faction. The base DCs for social encounters are always included in the encounter text.</p>\n<p><strong>Earn Income:</strong> The circumstance bonuses and penalties granted by these tiers apply to all checks attempted to Earn Income associated with locations or NPCs of the faction. When the PCs are admired, they increase the maximum task level they can attempt to Earn Income at with that faction by 1, and when they’re revered, they instead increase the maximum task level by 2.</p>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Reputation</th>\n      <th>Points</th>\n      <th>Default Attitude</th>\n      <th>Social DC Mod</th>\n      <th>Earn Income Bonus/Penalty</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Revered</td>\n      <td>31 or more</td>\n      <td>Helpful</td>\n      <td>–10</td>\n      <td>+3 (treat as 2 levels higher)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Admired</td>\n      <td>15 to 30</td>\n      <td>Friendly</td>\n      <td>–5</td>\n      <td>+2 (treat as 1 level higher)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Liked</td>\n      <td>5 to 14</td>\n      <td>Friendly</td>\n      <td>–2</td>\n      <td>+1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Ignored</td>\n      <td>–4 to 4</td>\n      <td>Indifferent</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Disliked</td>\n      <td>–5 to –14</td>\n      <td>Unfriendly</td>\n      <td>+2</td>\n      <td>–1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Hated</td>\n      <td>–15 to –29</td>\n      <td>Unfriendly</td>\n      <td>+5</td>\n      <td>–3</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Hunted</td>\n      <td>–30 or less</td>\n      <td>Hostile</td>\n      <td>+10</td>\n      <td>Can’t Earn Income</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
            },
            "People of Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的人民 People of Willowshore",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"People of Willowshore\">柳岸镇的人民</h1>\n<p>一个多世纪以来，被杀害的镇民灵魂在一个每年都会把时间循环回自身起点的思维空间里反复经历着同一年。就这些居民（包括PC）而言，这场冒险始于7108年的初夏——距龙瓦覆亡仅仅两年。当前最受关注的话题包括：伐木领主的近期出走、络新妇夺取国家控制权的消息，以及为即将到来的鬼季所做的准备。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>柳岸镇之名</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇的人民来自形形色色的文化与国度，因此，本镇NPC、传说与背景知识的灵感来源也借鉴了大量现实世界的亚洲素材。尽管在柳岸镇能遇到的各个NPC，其命名习惯可能受到现实世界亚洲国家的启发，但小镇本身的名字在英文中以复合词呈现。这是有意为之，旨在捕捉一种属于广泛亚洲文化、却不被其中任何一种所主导的地点氛围。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>许多柳岸镇人会以自家族最初定居本镇的时间来表明身份，这往往也会影响他们住在木棉河的哪一岸。第一波镇民要么是在修院里劳作之人，要么是由修院出资、受雇来柳岸镇定居之人。这些人最初居住在河的南岸，因此被称为南岸人。与此同时，龙瓦掌控此地之后才来到的人则定居在河的北岸；那里因坡势显著而被称为北岭人。这些移民包括为伐木头目效力的工人、希望便捷获取木材的商号，以及帝国卫队。</p>\n<p>尽管如今柳岸镇的这两派使用“南岸”和“北岭”这两个名称，但一个人的立场并不完全由其居住或工作的地点决定。南岸人偏向传统主义，热衷于维持柳岸镇的文化，并以土地的馈赠过着朴素生活。北岭人则更注重现代的务实与城镇发展。许多北岭人对络新妇统治申门的想法持开放态度；而南岸人则原则上认为络新妇是邪恶怪物，最好避而远之。</p>\n<p>尽管存在分歧，双方仍一致认同应将柳岸镇的生存与安全置于首位。许多居民自有看法，既不偏向任何一方，并认为自己不隶属于两派中的任何一派。总体而言，柳岸镇崇尚尽其所能地付出。在许多方面，村子别无选择，尤其当这场冒险的事件逐步发展之时。</p>\n<p>以下数据块呈现的是本战役开始时的柳岸镇现状。随着冒险之路推进，柳岸镇的等级将因PC们对抗困扰此地的邪恶势力而提高——更多细节见“小镇成长”边栏。</p>\n<p>请注意，柳岸镇数据块中的人口数值，统计的是PC们完成@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}后、诸事终于开始“恢复正常”时的小镇人口。若你的PC在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh]{第1章}与第2章中设法从死亡中拯救了出乎意料数量的本地人，你可以酌情略微提高该人口总数；但PC在前两章遭遇的尸体与遇难者，都是不幸的亡魂，不计入这些总数之中。若这并非思维空间所要承受的最终循环（要么因为Kugaptee现身现实世界并将一切吞噬，要么因为PC们成功阻止该邪魔并让柳岸镇回归现实），这些受害者会在一年后复活。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>小镇成长</h2>\n  <p>从@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}开始时起，柳岸镇是一处4级定居点，刚刚挺过一场残酷的怪物袭击。帮助镇民复原、让柳岸镇重新“站稳脚跟”，是贯穿本战役的反复主题。随着PC完成各幕所详述的里程碑事件，他们将有效提升柳岸镇的等级。虽说这不会影响小镇人口总数，却会提高镇上可购买物品的基准上限，并提高镇上以“谋生收入”进行多数任务时可用的基础最高任务等级。柳岸镇的NPC也会随着PC帮助重振士气并重建生活而变得更强。每当柳岸镇在4级之上再获得1级时，将柳岸镇内所有NPC的DC与技能调整值都提高1。此外，每当柳岸镇提高1级时，各地点的等级也提高1，这能让PC在“谋生收入”时接取更高等级的任务。</p>\n  <p>柳岸镇提升等级的速度不会像PC那样快。小镇阶段性的等级提升，与其说是小镇规模变大，不如说是PC在恢复士气、帮助本地人从近期事件中复原，使柳岸镇回到一切变糟之前的旧日高度。</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">柳岸镇</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">定居点 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">城镇</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">被困在循环思维空间中的偏远城镇</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>政府</strong> 委任总督（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}，失踪）</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>人口</strong> 225（73%人类、6%半精灵、4%半身人、4%狐人、3%精灵、3%天狗、2%那迦裔、5%其他）</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>语言</strong> 通用语（天语）、精灵语、半身人语、米纳坦语、那迦裔语、天狗语、天华语、天民语</p>\n\n  <hr />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>宗教</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{阿巴达尔}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{大狐津}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.r6SFB1PzKsagDXff]{难婆}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法拉丝玛}、@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}，其他（以小型神龛呈现）</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>威胁</strong> 恶意灵体、饥狂害虫、艰难的自给自足、超自然影响、领地性野兽</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>共克时艰</strong> 柳岸镇的居民尽管彼此有分歧，仍会互相扶持。即使另一位柳岸镇居民对你不关心或不友善，你仍可以尝试向其发出请求以获得帮助，但你这样做时承受–2环境减值。</p>\n\n  <hr />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“老奶奶”胡板娘</strong>（守序中立 女性 天殊 守卫）退休的帝国卫队长</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>和善保</strong>（守序中立 男性 天殊 总督）柳岸镇的委任行政长官；目前失踪</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“老”松木胜</strong>（中立善良 男性 天殊 家族族长）退休木匠与柳岸镇的活历史</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"People of Willowshore\">People of Willowshore</h1>\n<p>For over a century, the souls of the slain townspeople repeated the same year in a mindscape that annually loops time back on itself. As far as these residents—including the PCs—are concerned, this adventure begins at the onset of summer in 7108, a mere two years after the fall of Lung Wa. Current trending topics are the recent exodus of the lumber lords, news of the jorogumo seizing control of the nation, and preparations for the upcoming season of ghosts.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Willowshore’s Name</h1>\n  <p>The people of Willowshore come from a wide range of cultures and nations, and as such, the inspirations for the NPCs, legends, and lore of the town are inspired by a widespread number of real-world Asian sources. While individual NPCs found in Willowshore might have naming conventions inspired by real-world Asian countries, the name of the town itself is presented as a compound word in English. This is a deliberate attempt to capture the feel of a place that belongs to a wide range of Asian cultures but isn’t dominated by one.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Many Willowshorers identify by when their family first settled in town, which often affects which bank of the Ceiba River they live on. The first wave of townspeople are either those who worked on the monastery or who were paid to settle in Willowshore by the monastery. These folks originally lived south of the river and are thus referred to as Southbankers. Those who arrived after Lung Wa took control, meanwhile, settled on the river’s northern banks, called Northridge due to its prominent incline. These settlers included workers for the lumber bosses, businesses that wanted convenient access to the lumber, and imperial guards.</p>\n<p>Though these two factions in Willowshore today use the names Southbank and Northridge, one’s allegiance isn’t solely determined by where they live or work. Southbank folks are traditionalists, keen on maintaining Willowshore’s culture and living simply off the land. Northridge folks, meanwhile, focus on modern pragmatism and urban growth. Many Northridge folks are open to the idea of jorogumo ruling Shenmen, while Southbankers on principle think jorogumo are evil monsters and best avoided.</p>\n<p>Despite disagreements, both sides have a consensus on putting Willowshore’s survival and safety first. Plenty of residents have their own opinions that lean in neither direction and consider themselves unaffiliated with either faction. Overall, Willowshore values giving all one has to offer. In many ways, the village has no choice, especially as the events of this adventure evolve.</p>\n<p>The following stat block presents the town of Willowshore as it stands at the start of this campaign. As the Adventure Path continues, Willowshore’s level will grow as a result of the PCs’ work fighting against the sinister forces plaguing the region—see the “Growing the Town” sidebar for more details.</p>\n<p>Note that the population figure in the Willowshore stat block accounts for the town’s population after the PCs finish @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2} and things finally start to “get back to normal.” Feel free to increase this population total slightly if your PCs manage to save an unexpected number of locals from death during @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh]{Chapter 1} and 2, but the dead bodies and victims the PCs encounter during those first two chapters are poor souls who are not included in these totals. If this weren’t destined to be the final cycle the mindscape endures (either because Kugaptee emerges into the real world and consumes it all, or because the PCs manage to stop the fiend and return Willowshore to reality), these victims would return to life in a year.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Growing the Town</h2>\n  <p>As of the start of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}, Willowshore is a 4th-level settlement that has just endured a brutal monster attack. Helping the townspeople recover and getting Willowshore back “on its feet” is a recurring theme throughout this campaign. As the PCs accomplish milestone events, as detailed in each act, they effectively increase Willowshore’s level. While this doesn’t impact the town’s population total, it does increase the baseline for what items can be purchased in town and the baseline maximum for most task levels for Earning Income in town. Willowshore’s NPCs also grow in power as the PCs help build morale and reestablish themselves. Increase all NPC DCs and skill modifiers in Willowshore by 1 each time Willowshore gains a level above 4. Additionally, the level of each location increases by 1 each time Willowshore increases a level, which allows the PCs to take higher-level tasks when Earning Income.</p>\n  <p>Willowshore won’t gain levels as fast as the PCs. The town’s periodic level increases are less about the town itself growing in size and more about the PCs restoring morale and helping locals recover from recent events to bring Willowshore back to its previous height, before everything went bad.</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Willowshore</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Settlement 4</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Town</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">Isolated town trapped in a cyclic mindscape</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Government</strong> Appointed governor (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao}, missing)</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Population</strong> 225 (73% humans, 6% half-elves, 4% halflings, 4% kitsune, 3% elves, 3% tengu, 2% nagaji, 5% others)</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Languages</strong> Common (Tien), Elven, Halfling, Minatan, Nagaji, Tengu, Tian-hwa, Tian-min</p>\n\n  <hr />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Religions</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{Abadar}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{Daikitsu}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.r6SFB1PzKsagDXff]{Lady Nanbyo}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi}, others (represented by small shrines)</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Threats</strong> malicious spirits, ravenous vermin, struggling self-sufficiency, supernatural influences, territorial beasts</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Teeth-Clenching Teamwork</strong> Willowshore’s residents help one another despite their differences. You can attempt to Request help from another Willowshore resident even if they’re indifferent or unfriendly, but you do so with a –2 circumstance penalty.</p>\n\n  <hr />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“Granny” Hu Ban-niang</strong> (LN female Tian-shu guard) retired imperial guard captain</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Heh Shan-Bao</strong> (LN male Tian-shu governor) appointed administrator of Willowshore; currently missing</p>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“Old” Matsuki Shou</strong> (NG male Tian-shu family patriarch) retired carpenter and Willowshore’s living history</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Willowshore Mindscape": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的思维空间 The Willowshore Mindscape",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Willowshore Mindscape\">柳岸镇的思维空间</h1>\n<p>对那些被困在思维空间中的人而言，它与真实的生者世界毫无区别。魔法如人所料般运作，而从其他位面召唤来的生物也会以为自己被召至凡人界。任何信息上的出入——比如如今是哪一年、曾发生过哪些事件——都很容易被柳岸镇的偏远所掩盖。尽管柳岸镇的人民在现实世界中于7108年被杀害，但在柳岸镇的思维空间内，他们依旧活得好好的。不可避免地，环绕该地区的超自然边界终将被发现，迫使柳岸镇的居民正视他们新的非自然处境；但每年春季的最后一天，时间都会重置，所有记忆以及对理解思维空间本质所取得的进展也会一并重置，让循环再次从头开始。115年来一直如此。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>柳岸腹地</span> <span>思维空间</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">有限</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">循环时间</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">柳岸镇的思维空间是一个拟真思维空间，如《Pathfinder Dark Archives》第199页所述，但你在主持<em>鬼季</em>时不必查阅那本书。思维空间的居民（包括PC）在冒险路径的后期之前一直不会意识到他们所处的现实。</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">柳岸镇的思维空间具有循环时间（特征），并被锁定在一个“时间循环”之中。该思维空间在时间上有一个固定的起点，并在一年流逝后抵达终点。当时间到达这一年度终点时，思维空间内的一切（包括所有思维空间原生者）都会在时间上回退。上一年的所有发展、成就与记忆都会消失，一切都重置回起始时的状态。这会让所有原生生物恢复到先前的年龄，将他们的生命值与位置重置到起始时的状态，甚至会复活那些在过去一年中死亡者。循环思维空间原生者死去后，其灵魂不会进入灵魂之河，而是保持停滞状态，等待思维空间当前循环的终结。在某些情况下，先前循环的诡异回声会以奇异而独特的方式积累，导致出现类似作祟的显现或不死生物，例如@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21thatchling0000]{草人}。</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">在每个循环中，事件会以完全相同的方式推进，除非某种外来影响（例如来自另一种现实、前来造访的生物）打乱这些事件，从而可能在该循环剩余时间里引发一个显著不同的局面。当循环思维空间重置时，外来物品或访客会连同他们对先前循环的记忆一并保留，他们可以按自己的意愿利用这些记忆。这类事件以前从未在柳岸镇的思维空间中发生过，但这一次，事情将会不同。</p>\n</section>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>思维空间的居民</h2>\n  <p>柳岸镇中居住着四类居民。</p>\n  <p><strong>被困住的灵魂：</strong>柳岸镇的居民（包括PC），以及腹地中大多数智慧生物，都在7108年死去，随后便被困在思维空间里；他们以活着的状态存在，却没有自己死亡的任何记忆。</p>\n  <p><strong>非智慧生物：</strong>诸如动物伙伴或魔宠之类的生物在灵性上与PC相连，因此被视为被困住的灵魂；但思维空间中其余的非智慧野生动物与植物则如同其物种的正常个体般活动，却缺乏任何类似灵魂的东西——它们被杀死时会如常腐烂，但无法成为不死生物，也无法被恢复生命。</p>\n  <p><strong>怪物化身：</strong>邪魔库加普提的影响引入了具备实体且拥有自由意志的怪物化身——它们是在思维空间上一个循环终结时出现，并延续到了这一循环。它们没有在思维空间形成之前存在过的真实记忆，也不具备灵魂，但在其他方面的表现与其种类的典型怪物无异。它们无法被复活或变为不死生物，但其尸体会在死亡后留下并如常腐烂。</p>\n  <p><strong>访客：</strong>思维空间中极少数居民是来自其边界之外的访客。名为伸藏的死神商人就是一个例子，PC从第二幕开始将会遭遇的宁多鲁邪魔也是如此。</p>\n</aside>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Willowshore Mindscape\">The Willowshore Mindscape</h1>\n<p>For those trapped within the mindscape, it’s indistinguishable from the living world. Magic functions as one expects, and creatures conjured from other planes assume they’ve been called into the mortal realm. Any discrepancy in information, such as what year it is and what events took place, can easily be dismissed due to Willowshore’s remoteness. While the people of Willowshore were slain in the real world in 7108, they remain very much alive within Willowshore’s mindscape. Inevitably, the supernatural borders that surround the region are discovered, forcing the citizens of Willowshore to come to terms with their new unnatural situation, but every year on the last day of spring, time resets and all memory and progress toward understanding the nature of the mindscape resets, starting the cycle over again. And so it has been for 115 years.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>Willowshore Hinterlands</span> <span>Mindscape</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Finite</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Cyclic Time</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The Willowshore mindscape is an immersive mindscape, as detailed on page 199 of <em>Pathfinder Dark Archives</em>, but you won’t need to reference that book to run <em>Season of Ghosts</em>. The mindscape’s inhabitants, including the PCs, remain unaware of their reality until later in the Adventure Path.</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">Willowshore’s mindscape has the cyclic time trait and is locked into a “time loop.” The mindscape has a set point in time when it starts and when it ends after the passage of a year. When time reaches this yearly end point, everything within the mindscape (including all natives of the mindscape) revert in time. All developments, accomplishments, and memories of the previous year are lost, and everything resets to the state things were at the start. This restores all native creatures to their previous age, resets their health and location to where they were at the start, and even resurrects those who died during the past year. The soul of a cyclic mindscape native who dies doesn’t enter the River of Souls but instead remains in stasis awaiting the end of the mindscape’s current cycle. In some cases, eerie echoes of previous cycles can accumulate in strange and unique ways, resulting in haunt-like manifestations or undead creatures, such as @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21thatchling0000]{Thatchlings}.</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">During each cycle, events proceed identically unless an outside influence (such as a visiting creature from another reality) disrupts these events, potentially setting up a significantly different scenario for the rest of that cycle’s remaining time. When a cyclic mindscape resets, foreign objects or visitors remain, along with their memories of previous cycles, and they can use these memories to their advantage as they see fit. Such events have never happened in Willowshore’s mindscape before, but this time, things will be different.</p>\n</section>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Mindscape Inhabitants</h2>\n  <p>Four types of inhabitants dwell in Willowshore.</p>\n  <p><strong>Trapped Souls:</strong> The citizens of Willowshore (including the PCs), as well as most of the sapient creatures in the hinterlands, perished in 7108 and then became trapped, alive and with no memories of their deaths, in the mindscape.</p>\n  <p><strong>Non-Sapient Creatures:</strong> Creatures like animal companions or familiars are linked spiritually to PCs and are considered to be trapped souls, but the rest of the non-sapient wildlife and plant life that dwells in the mindscape function as normal animals of their kind but lack anything akin to a soul—when they’re slain, they decay as normal but can’t become undead, nor can they be restored to life.</p>\n  <p><strong>Monstrous Manifestations:</strong> The influence of the fiend Kugaptee introduces physical and free-willed manifestations of monsters whose appearance at the end of the mindscape’s previous cycle have persisted into this one. They have no true memories of their existence before the mindscape’s formation, nor do they possess a soul, but they otherwise function as typical monsters of their kind. They can’t be brought back to life or become undead, but their bodies remain after death and decay as normal.</p>\n  <p><strong>Visitors:</strong> A very few inhabitants of the mindscape are visitors from beyond its border. The shinigami merchant named Shinzo is one example here, as are nindoru fiends the PCs will encounter starting in the second act.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇 Willowshore",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Willowshore\">柳岸镇</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇的建立深受@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}苦修传统影响。6223 ic，谭隋靖以凯旋般的自我牺牲之举击败了邪魔苦迦菩提后，善解修行者之间兴起一项挑战：找出谭隋靖化为的那棵杉树。7020年，一位以河名为号、名为@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠大师}的善解大师完成了这一壮举。为确保后来者也能安全地亲自前往树所在的林地，智惠大师决定将这棵杉树供奉在谭杉寺之中，使善解修行者能够前来思索其哲理。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围 / 宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.x5igH32eFlcD1P5V]{柳岸镇} | @UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{更换季节}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>林木密布且群山环绕的地形使得施工异常艰难，即便对最老练的建造者亦然。有些人拒绝在此地歇息，因为在他人殒命之处附近睡觉（哪怕是为崇高的缘由）被视为禁忌。智惠大师欣然安置了这些工人，并筹措资金为他们修建住处与其他设施——地点在山脚下、补给从河畔一处便捷的港湾卸下之处。运送补给的商人们开始把这处偏远聚落称作“柳树盈岸”，这是一种本地的隐喻，意为“根本不可能找到”。久而久之，这个名字便与聚落联系起来，并简化为“柳岸镇”。</p>\n<p>寺院历经五年艰苦建造后，工人们将重心转向扩建柳岸镇，兴建旅店、农舍与其他建筑，以支撑不断增长的长期访客。在寺院最鼎盛之时，几乎每一家店铺或农场都会为朝圣者提供一餐与一宿。7054年智惠大师去世后，这股经济繁荣便逐渐消退；随着谭杉寺步入漫长衰落，许多柳岸镇居民开始把技艺与货物带往更远处谋生。</p>\n<p>7060年，神门征召该村，令其加入龙华的伐木采收大计。起初进展顺利，基础设施相继兴建，包括桥梁与一座水坝。然而，经营采伐作业的伐木头目很快便因剥削柳岸镇的苦修往事而遭人憎恶。更糟的是，他们开始把这处聚落（此时已名副其实成为一座镇子）包装成龙华贵族的“度假胜地”，让其来此以狩猎取乐，并恣意享用那些以帝国之名强行征收来的食物与美酒。</p>\n<p>伐木头目与官府几乎不在意那座早已废弃的寺院，直到他们贪婪扩张的触角在7062年伸向谭杉林；一次试图采伐神圣之树的行动以血腥屠戮告终。唯一幸存者的证词，使废弃寺院在柳岸镇内彻底坐实了恶名。其后数周乃至数月间，怪物目击事件与日俱增；受任命的总督随即以土地或财产为许诺，诱使帝国军队进驻镇中，作为其所能提供保护的补偿。最终，这些士兵中有许多人在此地退役，成为镇里新一波定居者。</p>\n<p>7106年龙华崩溃后，柳岸镇的伐木领主们带着财富弃庄而逃。大多数士兵返回神门首都或擅离职守，只留下那些已在本地扎根的人。柳岸镇的偏远使其免于猖獗的匪患与外部政治冲突，但这种隔绝也延误了重大消息的传入。直到7108年晚春，柳岸镇才得知络新妇接管整个神门的消息；这则新闻迫使镇长和善保尝试一场危险仪式，以恢复谭杉寺的护佑之力。仪式却适得其反，反而唤醒了邪魔苦迦菩提的遗产，引发一股毁灭性的力量浪潮，悲剧性地杀死了全镇所有人。</p>\n<p>次日，太阳升起，照见一座已无生命的柳岸镇；在更广阔的世人眼中，这座城镇在一百多年来始终只是鬼故事的荒废源头。然而，在这场事件中丧生的人从未意识到自己的结局，因为他们被杀的灵魂被困在一个平行现实里。他们滞留在生死之间的诡异边狱中，栖居于一处思维空间；对身处其界域中的人而言，此地与现实几乎无从分辨。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-willowshore.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"chapter-image\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-willowshore.webp')\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Willowshore\">Willowshore</h1>\n<p>Willowshore’s founding is steeped in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi} asceticism. After Tan Sui-Jing’s triumphant act of self-sacrifice defeated the fiend Kugaptee in 6223 ic, there rose a challenge among Sangpotshi practitioners to locate the sugi tree Sui-Jing transformed into. In 7020, a Sangpotshi master under the Fluvial name of Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} accomplished this feat. To ensure that others could safely visit the tree’s grove themselves, Master Zhi Hui decided to enshrine the sugi within the Tan Sugi monastery, where Sangpotshi practitioners could come to reflect upon the philosophy.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance / Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.x5igH32eFlcD1P5V]{Willowshore} | @UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{Change Season}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>The wooded and mountainous terrain made construction immensely difficult, even for the most seasoned of builders. Some refused to rest there, as the idea of sleeping near a place where another died (even for a noble cause) was taboo. Master Zhi Hui gladly accommodated these workers and sought funds to build them living quarters and other facilities at the foot of the mountain where supplies were dropped off at a convenient harbor along the riverside. The merchants ferrying in the supplies took to calling the remote settlement “the shore of willows,” a local metaphor meaning “impossible to find.” In time, the name became associated with the settlement, shortened to Willowshore.</p>\n<p>After five years of hard work on the monastery, the workers turned their focus to expanding Willowshore, building inns, farmhouses, and other structures to support a growing stream of long-term visitors. At the height of the monastery’s popularity, almost every shop or farm offered a meal and bed for pilgrims. This economic boom faded with Master Zhi Hui’s death in 7054, and many Willowshore residents began to ply their skills and wares further afield to earn a living as the Tan Sugi monastery began its slow decline.</p>\n<p>In 7060, Shenmen enlisted the village to become part of Lung Wa’s lumber harvesting ambitions. Things started out well, with the construction of infrastructure, including bridges and a dam. However, the lumber bosses who ran the harvesting operation soon became loathed for their exploitation of Willowshore’s ascetic past. Worse, they began to present the settlement (now properly called a town) as a “getaway” for Lung Wa aristocrats to hunt for sport and indulge in food and drinks forcefully seized in the empire’s name.</p>\n<p>The lumber bosses and government cared little for the long-abandoned monastery until their greedy expansion reached for the Tan Sugi grove in 7062 and an attempt to harvest the sacred trees ended in grisly slaughter. The sole survivor’s testimony cemented an ill reputation within Willowshore of the abandoned monastery. As monster sightings grew in the weeks and months after, the appointed governor responded by enticing imperial forces to move into the town with the promise of land or property in compensation for the protection they could offer. Many of these soldiers would ultimately retire in the region, becoming a new wave of settlers in the town.</p>\n<p>When Lung Wa collapsed in 7106, Willowshore’s lumber lords took their wealth, abandoned their estates, and fled. Most soldiers returned to Shenmen’s capital or deserted their posts, leaving behind those who had put down local roots. Though Willowshore’s remoteness saved it from the rampant banditry and external political conflicts, the isolation also delayed major news. Willowshore didn’t learn of the jorogumo takeover of all Shenmen until late spring of 7108, news that compelled the town’s governor, Heh Shan-Bao, to attempt a dangerous ritual to restore the protective power of the Tan Sugi monastery. The ritual backfired and instead awakened the fiend Kugaptee’s legacy, resulting in a devastating wave of power that tragically killed the entire town.</p>\n<p>The sun rose the next day on a Willowshore devoid of life, and to the world at large, the town has remained an abandoned source of ghost stories for over a hundred years. However, those who perished in this event never realized their fate, for their slain souls became trapped in an alternate reality. Stuck in a strange limbo between life and death, they reside in a mindscape largely indistinguishable from reality to those who live within its realm.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 1.1: To Light the Night": {
          "name": "第一幕 1.1：点亮黑夜 Act 1.1: To Light the Night",
          "pages": {
            "Light the Night": {
              "name": "点亮夜晚 Light the Night",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Light the Night\">点亮长夜</h1>\n<p><em>长明灯</em>是一件固定不动的15级魔法物品，位于晨步桥的南侧。这盏石灯笼高5英尺，由产自罗网山脉、带有银色纹理的花岗岩雕刻而成。其内部装有一只冷铁笼，笼内有一座莲花状底座，底座上曾放着三枚发光的铜币。据说，这盏灯的光芒能保护柳岸镇免受各种邪恶侵害。多年前，智惠大师@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}将其赠与柳岸镇；镇上无人记得它曾熄灭过。然而，当怪物入侵城镇时，武僧辘肠注意到了那三枚发光的钱币并将其抢走——可当他把这些“魔法”钱币从碗中取出后，它们立刻黯淡无光，让他大失所望。</p>\n<p>要重新点亮灯笼，所有PC需要做的只是打开<em>长明灯</em>南侧的栅格，将三枚受祝福的铜币放入内部的冷铁笼中，然后关上栅格。以上每一步各为一个交互动作；当最后一步完成后，灯笼便会再次点燃。当<em>长明灯</em>点亮且三枚钱币仍在其中时，它会在30英尺半径内提供光照（并在接下来的30英尺提供昏暗光照）。但更重要的是，点亮它会让笼罩柳岸镇的迷踪蜃雾、绯红之月与血雨效果立刻终止。任何被赋予残酷智慧与说话能力的动物也会恢复为普通动物，并自行离开城镇。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.8KtgPGYgJdlDgXwI]{Light Eternal Lantern}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>每当PC在灯笼中使用与柳岸镇各神龛相关的祝福时，与之相连的各类神圣力量便会有所察觉；祂们的关注与认可会在灯光亮起的瞬间化为赐福，赐予PC一项恩惠。此恩惠使PC在尝试使用该神祇的神圣技能进行技能检定时，获得+1物品加值。举例来说，如果PC放入由@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{卡莉丝翠}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna}与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.s9opv94lGDRKnw6W]{Shizuru}祝福过的钱币，他们将分别在欺瞒、特技与社交检定上获得+1物品加值。由于这些都是物品加值，使用来自同一神龛的多枚受祝福钱币，或使用来自共享同一神圣技能的多位神祇的受祝福钱币，都不会带来额外优势。同样地，PC最终也可能发现，他们在战役剩余部分获得的魔法物品能够提供比这些恩惠更高的物品加值。每名PC都会获得这些恩惠的效果，无论是谁放入了钱币，因为众神知道PC在协力合作，而能拯救或毁灭柳岸镇的命运系于他们。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC第一次点亮<em>长明灯</em>时，给予他们80 XP。这也会提升PC在镇中的声望。PC第一次点亮灯笼时，会在柳岸镇的两个派系中各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Light the Night\">Light the Night</h1>\n<p>The <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is an immobile 15th-level magical item located on the southern side of Dawnstep Bridge. This stone lantern is a 5-foot-tall stone lamp carved from silver-laced granite from the Gossamer Mountains. Its interior contains a cold iron cage with a lotus-shaped pedestal on which three glowing copper coins once sat. It’s said that the light from this lamp protects Willowshore from all manners of evil. Gifted to Willowshore many years ago by Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}, the lantern has never been extinguished for as long as anyone in town can remember, but when the monsters invaded the town, the buso Gurglegut spotted the glowing coins and snatched them up, only to be disappointed when the “magic” coins went dark after he took them from the bowl.</p>\n<p>To relight the lantern, all the PCs need to do is open the grill on the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>’s southern face, place three blessed copper coins in the cold iron cage within, and then close the grill. Each of these is a single Interact action, and once the last is completed, the lantern ignites once more. While the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is lit and the three coins remain inside, it sheds light in a 30-foot radius (and dim light for the next 30 feet), but more importantly, lighting it causes the mirage mist, crimson moon, and blood rain effects that have settled over Willowshore to immediately end. Any animals that had been granted cruel sapience and the ability to speak revert to normal animals as well and make their way back out of town.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.8KtgPGYgJdlDgXwI]{Light Eternal Lantern}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>The various divine forces associated with Willowshore’s shrines take note whenever their blessings are used in the lantern by the PCs, and their interest and approval results in a boon granted to the PCs as soon as the lantern’s light shines out. This boon grants the PCs a +1 item bonus to skill checks they attempt with the deity’s divine skill. For example, if the PCs place coins blessed by @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{Calistria}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna}, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.s9opv94lGDRKnw6W]{Shizuru}, they’ll receive a +1 item bonus to Deception, Acrobatics, and Society respectively. Since these are all item bonuses, there’s no advantage to using multiple blessed coins from the same shrine or from deities who share the same divine skill. Likewise, the PCs might eventually find that magic items they gain during the rest of the campaign could provide greater item bonuses than those granted by these boons. Each PC gains the effects of these boons, regardless of who placed the coins, as the gods know the PCs are working together, and that it’s their destiny that can save or damn Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP the first time they light the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>. This also increases the PCs’ reputation in town. They gain 1 Reputation Point with both of Willowshore’s factions the first time they light the lantern.</p>"
            },
            "Retaking Dawnstep": {
              "name": "重夺黎明阶梯 Retaking Dawnstep",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">夺回晨步</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇使用晨步桥的地图。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ootora.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Gurglegut\" alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ootora.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>坐在晨步桥上临时王座上的庞大身影，是名叫辘肠的笨重布索；而较小的一群则是数只金金，它们竭尽所能逗乐自己那暴力的首领。对PC们而言幸运的是，他们不必一次对付所有这些怪物——任何接近桥的举动都会很快引起它们的注意，但只有辘肠会走上前，在桥的南端与PC们对峙。金金们会退在后方对PC们嘲笑挑衅，但若有人真的把攻击指向它们，小魔怪（特征）便会尖叫着惊慌逃窜。</p>\n<p>如果PC们带着一份下了毒的酒作为礼物靠近，辘肠会高兴地大笑，迅速夺过礼物一饮而尽，并挥手把PC们赶走。若他因饮酒而昏迷，金金们会以为他死了而惊慌逃散；但如果PC们在他仍有意识时再次靠近（或一开始就拒不离开），他会立刻发动攻击。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-ootora.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">夺回晨步</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.EFX5AOuSEa0cxcj1]{辘肠}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>辘肠醉得够呛，以至于在本次遭遇中他等同于处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心（状态） 2}。他在战斗开始时会先用第一个动作尝试一次@Check[fortitude|dc:15]豁免来降低自己的恶心数值，随后用第二个动作尝试对看起来最强悍的PC进行挫败士气。他的第三个动作要么是行走到该PC身边，要么是用他的库克力对邻接的角色进行打击。之后的每个回合，他都会先花费一个动作尝试降低自己的恶心（状态），直到完全恢复为止。不管怎样，他都会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.GQ5mt29CNdfsJZyz]{辘肠的宝藏} <br />\n  辘肠收集了一些宝藏，并把它们放在他的临时王座附近——一柄镶有半宝石、价值15 gp的银质权杖，以及一个价值5 gp的精致银质首饰盒，里面装着一枚<em>谨慎之戒</em>。此外，这名布索还在口袋里带着三枚古老的铜币——一名角色若成功进行一次@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识，便能正确辨认出这三枚钱币正是长久以来维持<em>长明灯</em>点亮的那三枚。这三枚钱币如今不再带有祝福，其价值也恰如其分——3 cp。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们将辘肠逐出柳岸镇，从而重新开放晨步桥，他们将从每个派系各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Retaking Dawnstep</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Use the map for Dawnstep Bridge for this encounter.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ootora.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Gurglegut\" alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ootora.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures: </strong>The large figure seated on the improvised throne on Dawnstep Bridge is a lumbering buso named Gurglegut, while the smaller crowd are several jinkins who are doing their best to keep their violent leader entertained. Fortunately for the PCs, they don’t need to fight all of these monsters at once—any approach to the bridge quickly attracts their attention, but only Gurglegut steps forward to confront the PCs at the south end of the bridge. The jinkins hang back to jeer and taunt the PCs, but any actual attack directed toward them causes the gremlins to shriek and flee in panic.</p>\n<p>If the PCs approach with a gift of poisoned wine, Gurglegut laughs in delight and quickly snatches up the gift and drinks it, waving the PCs away. If he falls unconscious from the drink, the jinkins panic and flee, thinking he died, but if the PCs approach again (or refuse to leave in the first place) while he’s still conscious, he attacks at once.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-ootora.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Retaking Dawnstep</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.EFX5AOuSEa0cxcj1]{Gurglegut}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Gurglegut is drunk enough that he’s effectively @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2} during this encounter. He opens the fight by spending his first action to attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save to reduce his sickened value, then uses his second action to try to Demoralize the toughest-looking PC. His third action is either to Stride up to that PC or to Strike an adjacent character with his kukri. He starts each following round with an action to try to reduce his sickened condition until he’s fully recovered. In any event, he fights to the death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.GQ5mt29CNdfsJZyz]{Gurglegut's Treasures} <br />\n  Gurglegut has gathered a few treasures that he keeps near his impromptu throne—a silver scepter set with semi-precious stones worth 15 gp and an elegant silver jewelry case worth 5 gp that contains a <em>ring of discretion</em>. In addition, the buso carries three ancient copper coins in a pocket—a character who succeeds at a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge correctly identifies these three coins as those that, for so long, kept the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> lit. These three coins no longer bear blessings and are worth precisely that—3 cp.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs rid Willowshore of Gurglegut and thus reopen Dawnstep Bridge, they earn 1 Reputation Point with each faction.</p>"
            },
            "Liberating the Bridge": {
              "name": "解放桥梁 Liberating the Bridge",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Liberating the Bridge\">解放晨步桥</h1>\n<p>晨步桥（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w11dawnstepb00]{W11}）是连接城镇两岸的重要通道，但如果PC此时决定进行调查，他们会发现桥上有一只武僧与数只金金守卫。等PC靠近到100英尺内，且雾气中或诡异的月光下细节变得可见时，宣读以下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>鲜血涂抹在晨步桥的灰色石面上，证明这里不久前发生过战斗。柳岸镇标志性的石灯笼之火——记忆中第一次——熄灭了。桥上堆着被偷来的家具，形成一座王座；一名高大的类人生物坐在其上。他从一口酿造锅里饮酒，周围几名小得多的类人生物蹦跳打闹，似乎在模仿并嘲弄近期受害者临死时的抽搐与反应动作（）。</p>\n</div>\n<p>PC可以花些时间观察这些怪物；它们嬉闹得足够喧闹，使PC无需进行潜行检定就能在远处观看它们的丑态。不过，他们仍需尝试一次秘密的 @Check[perception|dc:15|traits:secret] 检定，以从10分钟的观察中捕捉线索。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> PC注意到金金会说通用语（小魔怪（特征）大多只是在扮演滑稽地惊惧的镇民的角色），但那个更大、独眼的身影并未留意。那大个子偶尔开口，也只是（用妖精语）醉醺醺地哼唱几句关于酒精的蹩脚打油诗，或吹嘘他对本地人的暴力胜利。聆听10分钟后，PC得知入侵势力中似乎有三名头目——辘肠、灰屠与莫都求——但没有迹象表明谁是谁，或这三只生物究竟是什么。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> PC得知金金和那个大个子似乎不共享同一种语言。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 除了确认敌人数目外，PC从观察中没有获得任何值得一提的信息。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> PC得出错误结论：那个大个子正处于快要昏睡过去的边缘。</p>\n<p>PC在最初的10分钟之后仍可继续尝试额外的 @Check[perception|dc:15|traits:secret] 检定，但每额外观察10分钟，若PC未能通过潜行检定以保持藏匿，怪物就有机会注意到他们。若PC被注意到，金金会兴奋地尖叫，随后有四只小魔怪（特征）追赶上来。</p>\n<p>与四只金金的战斗是一场极端1级遭遇——PC明智的做法是逃跑。金金会咯咯怪笑、尖声嚎叫，追逐几轮后便会放弃，满足于吓到人类；但如果它们与PC交战并击败了队伍，那么在辘肠介入之前，队伍可能需要本地人出手营救。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>因侦察怪物，给予PC 10 XP，以及在两个阵营中各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Liberating the Bridge\">Liberating the Bridge</h1>\n<p>Dawnstep Bridge (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w11dawnstepb00]{W11}) is an important link between the town’s two shores, but if the PCs decide to investigate at this time, they find the bridge guarded by a buso and several jinkins. Read the following once the PCs come within 100 feet and the details become visible through the mist or under the eerie moonlight.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Blood smears the gray stone of Dawnstep Bridge, evidence of a recent fight. The flame of Willowshore’s iconic stone lantern is—for the first time in memory—extinguished. A large humanoid figure sits on a throne made of stolen furniture heaped on the bridge. As he drinks from a brewing pot, several much smaller humanoids around him caper about, apparently mimicking and mocking death throes and reactions of recent victims.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The PCs can spend some time observing the monsters, who are cavorting loudly enough that the PCs can watch their antics from a distance without needing to roll Stealth checks. However, they do need to attempt a secret @Check[perception|dc:15|traits:secret] check to pick up on clues from 10 minutes of observation.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The PC notes that the jinkins speak Common (the gremlins are mostly just play-acting roles of comically frightened townsfolk), but the larger, one-eyed figure isn’t paying attention. The few times the larger figure speaks, it’s to drunkenly sing out (in Fey) a few rhymes of bad poetry about alcohol or to boast of his violent triumphs against the locals. After listening for 10 minutes, the PC learns the names of what appear to be the three ringleaders of the invading force—Gurglegut, Gray Butcher, and Mo Douqiu—although there’s no indication who’s who or what these three creatures are.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The PC learns that the jinkins and larger figure don’t seem to share a language.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The PC learns nothing of note from their observations other than confirming numbers of foes.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The PC comes to the incorrect conclusion that the large figure is on the verge of passing out.</p>\n<p>The PCs can attempt additional @Check[perception|dc:15|traits:secret] checks beyond the first 10 minutes, but each additional 10 minutes they do so, the monsters get a chance to notice the PCs if they don’t succeed at their Stealth checks to remain hidden. If the PCs are noticed, the jinkins shriek in excitement, and four of the gremlins give chase.</p>\n<p>A fight against four jinkins is an Extreme 1 encounter—one from which the PCs would be wise to flee. The jinkins hoot and shriek and give up the chase after a few rounds, pleased to have scared the humans, but if they fight and defeat the PCs, the party might need to be rescued by locals before Gurglegut gets involved.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 10 XP and 1 Reputation Point with both factions for spying on the monsters.</p>"
            },
            "Shrine Locations": {
              "name": "圣所位置 Shrine Locations",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shrine Locations\">神龛位置</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Dami\" alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp')\" />\n<p>一名崇拜相关神祇的PC会自动知晓其神祇神龛的位置。PC们也可以通过探索城镇或与各种NPC交谈，得知其中一些更为隐秘的神龛所在。由你酌情决定：若某位PC崇拜或信奉下表未列出的神祇或信仰，他们可能会在自己家中设立一个小型的个人信仰神龛。</p>\n<p>当PC尝试进行一次关于地点的@Check[willowshore-lore|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定以回忆知识时，他们掷骰一次，并得知所有“发现DC”等于或低于该次检定结果的神龛位置。表格条目按发现DC由低到高排列，以便一眼看出角色在众多神龛中发现了哪些。</p>\n<h1 class=\"table\">柳岸镇的神龛</h1>\n<br />\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>神祇</th>\n      <th>位置</th>\n      <th>发现</th>\n      <th>替代祝福技能</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{阿巴达尔}</td>\n      <td>财神爷神龛（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w4abadarshri00]{W4}）</td>\n      <td>自动</td>\n      <td>@Check[society]或@Check[willowshore-lore]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{黛姬缇}</td>\n      <td>九耳神社（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w16nineearsh00]{W16}）</td>\n      <td>自动</td>\n      <td>@Check[farming-lore]或@Check[survival]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{科福萨奇}</td>\n      <td>贸易栈（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w29tradeoffi00]{W29}）</td>\n      <td>自动</td>\n      <td>@Check[mercantile-lore]或@Check[performance]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法拉丝玛}</td>\n      <td>司魂娘娘（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w9ladyofsoul00]{W9}）</td>\n      <td>自动</td>\n      <td>@Check[fortune-telling-lore]或@Check[medicine]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{莎伦}</td>\n      <td>市中心（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b17shelynshr00]{B17}）</td>\n      <td>DC 12</td>\n      <td>@Check[art-lore|dc:12]或@Check[performance|dc:12]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.giAsBYiL2omr0x2L]{齐仲}</td>\n      <td>妙手回春（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}）</td>\n      <td>DC 13</td>\n      <td>@Check[herbalism-lore|dc:13]或@Check[medicine|dc:13]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.wjXNXFWBLbJaeZQR]{刻特菲斯}</td>\n      <td>银雾斋西区（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7a}）</td>\n      <td>DC 14</td>\n      <td>@Check[hunting-lore|dc:14]或@Check[survival|dc:14]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gsFaxWHbZmc1moY6]{纳利妮瓦蒂}</td>\n      <td>主母之绾（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}）</td>\n      <td>DC 15</td>\n      <td>@Check[midwifery-lore|dc:15]或@Check[nature|dc:15]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.s9opv94lGDRKnw6W]{诗祖鲁}</td>\n      <td>主母之绾（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}）</td>\n      <td>DC 15</td>\n      <td>@Check[diplomacy|dc:15]或@Check[warfare-lore|dc:15]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.aTYy1WHwAZiuei4h]{月夜}</td>\n      <td>主母之绾（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}）</td>\n      <td>DC 15</td>\n      <td>@Check[genealogy-lore|dc:15]或@Check[occultism|dc:15]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{蝶娜}</td>\n      <td>被遗弃的庄园（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w23abandoned00]{W23b}）</td>\n      <td>DC 16</td>\n      <td>@Check[scouting-lore|dc:16]或@Check[survival|dc:16]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.MbJ93Nw39h2cBYi5]{老鼠婆}</td>\n      <td>蘑菇房（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}）</td>\n      <td>DC 17</td>\n      <td>@Check[thievery|dc:17]或@Check[underworld-lore|dc:17]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.83jKKHQPoqVylmrF]{耶真姬}</td>\n      <td>受弃者之骨（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w36bonesofth00]{W36}）</td>\n      <td>DC 18</td>\n      <td>@Check[intimidation|dc:18]或@Check[legal-lore|dc:18]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{卡丽丝翠雅}</td>\n      <td>三福客栈（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w6thricebles00]{W6}）</td>\n      <td>DC 19</td>\n      <td>@Check[deception|dc:19]或@Check[guild-lore|dc:19]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.r6SFB1PzKsagDXff]{难婆}</td>\n      <td>木筏湖*（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w17woodraftl00]{W17}）</td>\n      <td>DC 20</td>\n      <td>@Check[nature|dc:20]或@Check[river-lore|dc:20]</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"no-indent\">*该神龛位于水下25英尺处。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shrine Locations\">Shrine Locations</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Dami\" alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp')\" />\n<p>A PC who worships the deity in question automatically knows the location of their deity’s shrine. The PCs can also learn of some of these more obscure shrine locations by exploring the town or by speaking to various NPCs. At your discretion, if a PC worships a deity or follows a faith not listed on the following table, they might have a small personal shrine to their faith set up in their own home.</p>\n<p>When a PC attempts a @Check[willowshore-lore|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge about locations, they roll once and learn the locations of all shrines with a Discover DC equal to or less than the result of their check. The table entries are organized in ascending order of Discover DC value to make it easier to tell at a glance which of the many shrines a character discovered.</p>\n<h1 class=\"table\">Willowshore’s Shrines</h1>\n<br />\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Deity</th>\n      <th>Location</th>\n      <th>Discover</th>\n      <th>Alternate Blessing Skills</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{Abadar}</td>\n      <td>Abadar Shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w4abadarshri00]{W4})</td>\n      <td>Automatic</td>\n      <td>@Check[society] or @Check[willowshore-lore]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{Daikitsu}</td>\n      <td>Nine Ear Shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w16nineearsh00]{W16})</td>\n      <td>Automatic</td>\n      <td>@Check[farming-lore] or @Check[survival]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{Kofusachi}</td>\n      <td>Trade Office (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w29tradeoffi00]{W29})</td>\n      <td>Automatic</td>\n      <td>@Check[mercantile-lore] or @Check[performance]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}</td>\n      <td>Lady of Souls (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w9ladyofsoul00]{W9})</td>\n      <td>Automatic</td>\n      <td>@Check[fortune-telling-lore] or @Check[medicine]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{Shelyn}</td>\n      <td>Downtown (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b17shelynshr00]{B17})</td>\n      <td>DC 12</td>\n      <td>@Check[art-lore|dc:12] or @Check[performance|dc:12]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.giAsBYiL2omr0x2L]{Qi Zhong}</td>\n      <td>The Hand of Spring (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27})</td>\n      <td>DC 13</td>\n      <td>@Check[herbalism-lore|dc:13] or @Check[medicine|dc:13]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.wjXNXFWBLbJaeZQR]{Ketephys}</td>\n      <td>Western Silvermist Lodge (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7a})</td>\n      <td>DC 14</td>\n      <td>@Check[hunting-lore|dc:14] or @Check[survival|dc:14]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gsFaxWHbZmc1moY6]{Nalinivati}</td>\n      <td>Mother’s Coil (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28})</td>\n      <td>DC 15</td>\n      <td>@Check[midwifery-lore|dc:15] or @Check[nature|dc:15]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.s9opv94lGDRKnw6W]{Shizuru}</td>\n      <td>Mother’s Coil (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28})</td>\n      <td>DC 15</td>\n      <td>@Check[diplomacy|dc:15] or @Check[warfare-lore|dc:15]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.aTYy1WHwAZiuei4h]{Tsukiyo}</td>\n      <td>Mother’s Coil (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28})</td>\n      <td>DC 15</td>\n      <td>@Check[genealogy-lore|dc:15] or @Check[occultism|dc:15]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna}</td>\n      <td>Abandoned Estates (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w23abandoned00]{W23b})</td>\n      <td>DC 16</td>\n      <td>@Check[scouting-lore|dc:16] or @Check[survival|dc:16]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.MbJ93Nw39h2cBYi5]{Lao Shu Po}</td>\n      <td>Mushroom House (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32})</td>\n      <td>DC 17</td>\n      <td>@Check[thievery|dc:17] or @Check[underworld-lore|dc:17]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.83jKKHQPoqVylmrF]{Yaezhing}</td>\n      <td>Bones of the Forgotten (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w36bonesofth00]{W36})</td>\n      <td>DC 18</td>\n      <td>@Check[intimidation|dc:18] or @Check[legal-lore|dc:18]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{Calistria}</td>\n      <td>Thrice-Blessed Inn (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w6thricebles00]{W6})</td>\n      <td>DC 19</td>\n      <td>@Check[deception|dc:19] or @Check[guild-lore|dc:19]</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.r6SFB1PzKsagDXff]{Lady Nanbyo}</td>\n      <td>Woodraft Lake* (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w17woodraftl00]{W17})</td>\n      <td>DC 20</td>\n      <td>@Check[nature|dc:20] or @Check[river-lore|dc:20]</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"no-indent\">*This shrine is 25 feet underwater.</p>"
