            "Blessing the Coins": {
              "name": "祝福钱币 Blessing the Coins",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Blessing the Coins\">祝圣钱币</h1>\n<p>为了点亮<em>长明灯</em>，PC必须将三枚祝福过的铜币放入灯笼的燃料容器中。要祝圣一枚铜币，PC必须前往柳岸镇镇界内的数处圣龛之一，并进行以下行动。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>祈请圣龛祝福</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>需求</strong>你手持一枚未祝圣的铜币，且与柳岸镇的一处圣龛相邻。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你向圣龛献上祷告，并恳求其所奉的神祇祝圣一枚铜币。将铜币放在圣龛前，然后在圣龛前花费10分钟祈祷。尝试一次@Check[religion|dc:15]或神祇学识检定，或尝试一次与该神祇教义相关的DC 17技能检定——每处圣龛都提供两项可替代的技能，详见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03shrinelocati00]{柳岸镇的圣龛}表。若你崇拜该神祇，则将你的检定结果提高一级成功度。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败 成功</strong>神祇祝圣了这枚铜币，同时也向你灌注额外的神圣能量与洞见。你恢复@Damage[1d8+8[healing]]生命值，并且在接下来24小时内可以将@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.izcxFQFwf3woCnFs]{神导术}以神圣法术的方式施放1次。此后你在祈请圣龛祝福时获得的所有大成功或大失败成功都改为视为普通成功。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>神祇祝圣了这枚铜币。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>你失败了，并且在接下来24小时内无法再在这座特定圣龛处尝试祈请祝福。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败 失败</strong>你惹怒了神祇。铜币消失，你在接下来1周内无法再在这座圣龛处尝试祈请祝福，并且你会在1小时内陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Blessing the Coins\">Blessing the Coins</h1>\n<p>In order to light the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, the PCs must place three blessed copper coins into the lantern’s fuel receptacle. To bless a copper coin, the PCs must seek out one of several shrines found in Willowshore’s town limits and perform the following activity.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Invoke Shrine Blessing</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requirements</strong> You are holding an unblessed copper coin and are adjacent to one of Willowshore's shrines.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You offer prayers to a shrine and implore its associated deity to bless a copper coin. Place the copper coin before the shrine, then spend 10 minutes in prayer before the shrine. Attempt a @Check[religion|dc:15] or Deity Lore check or a DC 17 skill check associated with the deity's teachings—two alternate skills are available for each shrine, as detailed in the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03shrinelocati00]{Willowshore's Shrines table}. If you worship the deity in question, increase the result of your check by one degree of success.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The deity blesses the copper coin but also imbues you with additional divine energy and insight. You heal @Damage[1d8+8[healing]] Hit Points and can cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.izcxFQFwf3woCnFs]{Guidance} once in the next 24 hours as a divine spell. You treat all further critical successes at Invoking Shrine Blessing as regular successes instead.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The deity blesses the copper coin.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> You fail, and can't attempt to invoke a blessing at this specific shrine again for 24 hours.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> You anger the deity. The copper coin vanishes, you can't attempt to invoke a blessing at this shrine again for 1 week, and you become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 hour.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Worst Puzzle": {
              "name": "最糟糕的谜题 The Worst Puzzle",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">最糟糕的谜题</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>正如胡太婆所怀疑的那样，她的三个孙辈和他们一个爱惹麻烦的朋友在重现节当晚，在蘑菇房附近的一处木材烘干场里（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}）自办了一场派对。他们喝到不省人事，在场地里过了一夜；而到了早上，一群金金怪发现了他们，并决定在这些小魔怪转去镇上别处之前，残忍地把这些年轻人困起来。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/reveler-1.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">最糟糕的谜题</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.UVGcrrlk3ejOlNOy]{濒危的狂欢者（4）} @UUID[Actor.bX3fzfr47WnGjiT0]{杂乱的木堆}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC们抵达时，他们发现四名濒危的狂欢者被困在木材烘干场中央的一小块区域里——那群金金怪把这里布置成了一个危险的陷阱。当四人听到PC们靠近时，他们会呼救，同时也警告PC们小心——“到处都是绊线和触发装置！那些卑鄙的小东西特意这么干的！”这四名本地人蜷缩在几摞木材的中央，而在他们周围，令人不安数量的沉重木梁与削尖的木桩被摆放得密密麻麻，并与一团纠结的绊线、以及承受拉力的木钉（木销）交织在一起。</p>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>只要这四名村民保持相对静止，他们就能在该危害的核心位置保持安全。为了让他们逃脱，PC们必须解除金金怪搭建的陷阱，否则这些平民很可能会受到伤害。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>每有一名狂欢者存活，PC们获得20 XP；若四人全部存活，则额外获得北岭人声望点数1点。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Worst Puzzle</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As Granny Hu suspected, three of her grandchildren and one of their troublemaking friends held their own party on the night of the Reenactment Festival in a lumber drying yard near the Mushroom House (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}). They passed out and spent the night in the yard, and that morning, a group of jinkins found them and decided to cruelly trap the youths before the gremlins moved on to other parts of town.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/reveler-1.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">The Worst Puzzle</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.UVGcrrlk3ejOlNOy]{Endangered Revelers (4)} @UUID[Actor.bX3fzfr47WnGjiT0]{Haphazard Wood Pile}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When the PCs arrive, they find the four endangered revelers trapped in a small area at the center of a lumber drying yard that the jinkins rigged into a dangerous trap. As the four hear the PCs approach, they call out for help but also warn the PCs to watch out—“There’s all sorts of trip lines and triggers set! Those nasty little creatures made sure of that!” The four locals huddle in the middle of several stacks of lumber, and an unnerving amount of heavy timbers and sharpened stakes have been arranged all around them within a tangled web of trip lines and tension-bearing wood dowels.</p>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> As long as the four villagers remain relatively still, they’ll be safe at the heart of this hazard. In order for them to escape, the PCs must disarm the trap the jinkins built, otherwise the commoners are likely to come to harm.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> The PCs gain 20 XP for each surviving reveler, and 1 Reputation Point with Northridge if all four survive.</p>"
            },
            "Clash at the Clinic": {
              "name": "诊所冲突 Clash at the Clinic",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A2. 诊所冲突</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇唯一的诊所——妙手回春（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}）——已成了一个临时避难所，收容那些不隶属于任一派系的镇民。有些人，例如井川十兵卫（主母之绾出身的法师学徒，区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}）与霍天哲（二等优的修补匠，区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w26secondbes00]{W26}），则是因伤来此。十兵卫在躲避一台 jinkin 装置时严重扭伤了脚踝，而天哲身上则有一道因炼金爆炸回火造成的大面积烧伤。</p>\n<p>使用妙手回春的地图来进行这场遭遇。随着 PC 接近（区域 <strong>A2a</strong>），他们能明显听见来自庭院（区域 <strong>A2b</strong>）的嘶嘶声、低吼声以及战斗的闷响。他们可透过将庭院与外侧小径隔开的木格栅，清楚看见几只巨蜈蚣正在攻击一只体型如人般大小的幽灵壁虎。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/phantom-beast-gecko.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">A2. 诊所冲突</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.pPxs70qB838Wn1YC]{巨蜈蚣（3）} @UUID[Actor.DOL44mzpaqGxmhLn]{幽影壁虎}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>尽管达米大夫已做了预防措施，巨蜈蚣仍被吸引到了此处。这只幽灵般的壁虎，是一位长期守护诊所的守护灵的显现。PC 接近时，壁虎正尽力对付两只蜈蚣，但当 PC 一靠近（在区域 <strong>A2a</strong>），又有三只蜈蚣从格栅的缝隙里攀爬进来，立刻转而攻击 PC。</p>\n  <p>蜈蚣会战斗至死。尽管幽影壁虎本身并非那股灌注于思维空间中的邪恶的显现，它仍将 PC 视为潜在入侵者。一旦 PC 击败了在 A2a 区域攻击他们的三只蜈蚣，壁虎便会在 A2b 区域解决它最后一只蜈蚣，随后尝试以【挫败士气】来威胁 PC。它不会主动发动攻击；在最后一只蜈蚣被杀死后的 1 个回合，达米大夫会从西侧建筑（区域 A2c）现身，并脱口而出：“别杀它！”希望能阻止 PC 攻击幽影壁虎。若在所有蜈蚣被杀死后，PC 经过 1 个回合仍未采取任何敌对动作，幽影壁虎便会淡回灵界。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>与大夫交谈：</strong> @UUID[Actor.6BT2JpPWi2191MLF]{达米的感谢} @UUID[Actor.ogwwP9izSObpJFqv]{达米的额外感谢} @UUID[Actor.zSekgt0ROU35Tf3Y]{达米的毒药} <br />\n  若 PC 协助击败蜈蚣，达米大夫会以两剂次等解毒剂作为谢礼。若他们也设法让壁虎免于被杀，他还会赠予他们一瓶次等黑暗视觉灵药。他另有五瓶次等黑暗视觉灵药，若 PC 有兴趣也可购买或以物易物取得更多。他也会在怪物仍盘踞镇中期间，提供 PC 随时来诊所免费使用【治疗伤势】的服务。\n</p>\n<p>如果 PC 提到他们打算重新点亮<em>长明灯</em>，达米大夫会为他们开放他供奉 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.giAsBYiL2omr0x2L]{齐仲} 的神龛（区域 <strong>A2d</strong>），让他们寻求神祇祝福。此外，十兵卫也会告知 PC：主母之绾（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}）还有一处供奉 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gsFaxWHbZmc1moY6]{莲花天女} 的神龛。</p>\n<p>至于胡婆婆担心他的安危一事，达米大夫挥挥手便打发了，表示他对她的摆姿态与政治手腕毫无兴趣。尽管发生了蜈蚣袭击，他仍觉得待在诊所里很安全，并拒绝离开；他指出搬动伤者可能对他们弊大于利。若 PC 真想帮忙，就该设法夺回柳岸镇。</p>\n<p>最后，若 PC 提到计划在晨步桥给 buso 下毒或下药，达米大夫神情凝重地点头，承认自己能帮忙，但也明确表示他平时并不赞同投毒。他会提供 PC 一剂迟钝毒药，并警告他们务必小心，只能用来对付那只怪物（他手边留着这点少量存货，是为了缓解痛苦难耐的病患）。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若 PC 让幽影壁虎活下来，他们获得的 XP 视同击败了它，按全额计算。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A2. Clash at the Clinic</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s only clinic, the Hand of Spring (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}), has become an impromptu haven for townsfolk who are unaffiliated with either faction. Some, such as Igawa Jubei (a wizard’s apprentice from Mother’s Coil, area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}) and Huo Tian-Zhe (a tinkerer from Second Best, area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w26secondbes00]{W26}) are here due to injuries. Jubei badly sprained her ankle escaping from a jinkin contraption, while Tian-Zhe sports a large burn wound from a backfired alchemical explosion.</p>\n<p>Use the map for Hand of Spring to play out this encounter. As the PCs approach (area <strong>A2a</strong>), sounds of hissing, growling, and the thumping of a battle are apparent, coming from the courtyard (area <strong>A2b</strong>). They can plainly see several giant centipedes attacking a ghostly gecko the size of a human by peering through the wooden lattice separating the courtyard from the exterior path.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/phantom-beast-gecko.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">A2. Clash at the Clinic</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.pPxs70qB838Wn1YC]{Giant Centipede (3)} @UUID[Actor.DOL44mzpaqGxmhLn]{Phantom Gecko}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Despite Doctor Dami’s precautions, giant centipedes have been attracted to the area. The ghostly gecko is the manifestation of a guardian spirit that has long protected the clinic. As the PCs approach, the gecko does its best against two centipedes, but three more clamber through gaps in the lattice to attack the PCs as soon as they approach (at area <strong>A2a</strong>).</p>\n  <p>The centipedes fight to the death. While the phantom gecko itself isn’t a manifestation of the evil infusing the mindscape, it still regards the PCs as potential intruders. Once the PCs defeat the three centipedes that attack them in area A2a, the gecko finishes off its last centipede in area A2b and then threatens the PCs by attempting to Demoralize them. It doesn’t initiate an attack, and one round after the last centipede is slain, Doctor Dami emerges from the western building (area A2c) and blurts out, “Don’t kill it!” with the hope of preventing the PCs from attacking the phantom gecko. If a round passes without any hostile action from the PCs after all the centipedes have been slain, the phantom gecko fades back into the Ethereal Plane.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Speaking to the Doctor:</strong> @UUID[Actor.6BT2JpPWi2191MLF]{Dami's Thanks} @UUID[Actor.ogwwP9izSObpJFqv]{Dami's Extra Thanks} @UUID[Actor.zSekgt0ROU35Tf3Y]{Dami's Poison} <br />\n  If the PCs help defeat the centipedes, Doctor Dami gives them two lesser antidotes in thanks. If they managed to spare the gecko from being killed as well, he also gives them a lesser darkvision elixir. He has five more vials of lesser darkvision elixirs, should the PCs be interested in buying or bartering for more. He also offers to use Treat Wounds on the PCs whenever they come to the clinic at no cost, so long as the monsters are still in town.\n</p>\n<p>If the PCs mention their intention to relight the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, Doctor Dami opens his shrine to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.giAsBYiL2omr0x2L]{Qi Zhong} (area <strong>A2d</strong>) for them to seek the god’s blessing. Also, Jubei informs the PCs about the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gsFaxWHbZmc1moY6]{Nalinivati} shrine in Mother’s Coil (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w28mothersco00]{W28}).</p>\n<p>As for Granny Hu’s concerns for his safety, Doctor Dami dismisses that concern with a wave of the hand, noting his disinterest in her posturing and politics. Despite the centipede attack, he still feels safe in his clinic and refuses to abandon it, noting that moving the wounded may do them more harm than good. If the PCs really want to help, they should work toward reclaiming Willowshore.</p>\n<p>Finally, if the PCs mention a plan to poison or drug the buso at Dawnstep Bridge, Doctor Dami nods grimly and admits he can help, although he makes it clear that he doesn’t normally condone poisoning. He supplies the PCs with a dose of lethargy poison, warning them to be careful with it and to use it only against the monster (he keeps this small supply of the poison on hand to soothe patients who are in great pain).</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs let the phantom gecko live, they receive full XP as if they defeated it.</p>"
            },
            "The Trapped Hunter": {
              "name": "受困的猎手 The Trapped Hunter",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A1. 被困的猎人</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">极难 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>如果PC们同意去找一名银雾斋成员，转达老松木希望有猎人能在条件允许时追踪丑小乖的请求，那么PC们需要在南岸花费1小时进行搜寻。之后，每位参与搜寻的PC都可以尝试一次@Check[perception|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]或@Check[survival|dc:15|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定。成功时，他们找到一座小农庄，那里的局势正一片骚动。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>两只名叫米多莉与紫的金金怪，再加上两只心术不正的动物（名叫面条的鼬鼠和名叫麻雀的乌鸦），困住了一名银雾斋猎人——名叫澄香的女性。澄香被这些生物的声音骗来调查这座农庄；她把它们误认为是在哭泣的孩子。澄香在农舍西南侧公共房间里被小妖精们布置的弹簧长矛陷阱重创后，爬进卧室（区域<strong>A1a</strong>）并用东西堵住了门。</p>\n<p>这四个家伙现在聚集在西南建筑的入口附近，对澄香叫嚣嘲弄。“蓝如晨曦！紫而奇迹！快似小鹿！合起来，我们就是钱币兜姐妹！”两只金金怪高喊道。它们那句无意义的押韵结束并笑作一团时，面条补充道：“这意思是我们来偷光你所有的牛！”麻雀则停在入口上方的屋顶上，用尖细的声音对澄香叫着，像是在引诱一只被困的猫：“来呀，小猫咪、小猫咪！出来吃点心呀！”</p>\n<p>这四个恶作剧的折磨者并不怎么想和PC们战斗。相反，它们想通过强抢的方式去“结交”动物，并把澄香误认为这座农庄的牧场主。若有任何PC拥有伙伴动物、魔宠、坐骑或幻灵，该团伙会盯上其中看起来最强的那一个，混合使用明显不可信的食物承诺与赤裸裸的威胁，试图让那只动物加入它们。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/murasaki.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">A1. 被困的猎人</span> <span class=\"keepme\">极难 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.VLVw77FyEkhBM3og]{Midori} @UUID[Actor.oBy8cJvJblCMd8xW]{Murasaki} @UUID[Actor.Uwfc3kP631bILlPx]{Noodles} @UUID[Actor.7iu3BpmtW0fFAoUu]{Sparrow} @UUID[Actor.1or0C3ZqZm9dC54P]{Sumika}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img class=\"float-right\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-sumika.webp\" alt=\"A young woman with dark hair in a long braid\" title=\"Sumika\" style=\"z-index:5;shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-sumika.webp')\" />\n  <p>PC们当然可以与钱币兜姐妹战斗，但这将是一场危险的遭遇。若有PC改为在攻击前先对这四个家伙喊话，这群怪人会开心地咯咯直笑。米多莉向队伍做了个夸张的敬礼，而紫说：“哦！所以你们是一群爱聊天的家伙？觉得自己有本事在钱币兜姐妹面前取胜？”麻雀用尖刻的语气啾啾叫道：“我不信！我信！我不信！你说呢？”一旦它们意识到有访客，澄香便撑起身子，从房间的窗户向外窥探，在向PC们挥手、悄悄引起他们注意后，无声地对他们做出口型：“救我！”</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>攻击这些折磨者确实能帮助澄香逃脱，但PC们也可以改为与钱币兜姐妹进行一场“斗智”。允许玩家以任何他们想要的方式交谈，然后让他们各自按意愿尝试一次@Check[deception|dc:13]、@Check[diplomacy|dc:13]或@Check[intimidation|dc:13]检定。若成功者超过半数，他们便能迷惑并分散钱币兜姐妹的注意力。你也应允许每位PC尝试一次秘密@Check[society|dc:17|traits:secret]或@Check[farming-lore|dc:15|traits:secret]检定，以意识到这四个家伙犯下的一个错误——如果他们指出“abactor”这个词才是“偷牛者”的意思，而不是“abacus”，这四个家伙会立刻为这个揭示互相争吵不休，使PC们自动赢得这场斗智。</p>\n<p>若PC们成功分散了钱币兜姐妹的注意力，澄香便能从窗户爬出去，一瘸一拐地逃往安全处。PC们随后可以跟上，在那些争吵不休的生物来得及发动攻击前离开。否则，钱币兜姐妹会变得不耐烦并决定攻击PC们。战斗中，每个成员在生命值降到4点以下时都会因恐惧而尖叫，并为保命而逃跑。</p>\n<p>若米多莉与紫在本次遭遇中存活，她们（可能还包括面条）之后可能会再次登场；见区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e13guesthous00]{E13}。</p>\n\n<p><strong>营救猎人：</strong> @UUID[Actor.2JY79N5rcJU8e8I8]{澄香的感谢} <br />获救后，澄香以足够的补给感谢PC们：这些补给能制作两件<em>精魂陷阱</em>，并额外提供材料，用于制作PC们自选的另外两件常见1级圈套。若她得知点燃<em>长明灯</em>的计划，她会建议PC们前往银雾斋最西端狩猎小屋（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7a}）的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.wjXNXFWBLbJaeZQR]{克忒菲斯}神龛。</p>\n<p>若PC们转达老松木希望猎人们去寻找丑小乖的请求，澄香会理解地点头，并承诺很快把这条信息带给她的同伴。若PC们提供治疗，澄香有信心自己能安全返回松木宅，但她也不会拒绝PC们提出护送她的提议。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>无论PC们以何种方式解决本次遭遇，都给予他们如同在战斗中击败钱币兜姐妹一样的全额XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A1. The Trapped Hunter</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>If the PCs agree to seek out a Silvermist lodge member to deliver Old Matsuki’s request for a hunter to track Ugly Cute when possible, the PCs will need to spend an hour Searching in Southbank, after which each PC who took part in the Search can attempt a @Check[perception|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] or a @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check. On a success, they find their way to a small farm where a strange commotion is taking place.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of jinkins by the names of Midori and Murasaki, plus two mean-spirited animals (a weasel named Noodles and a raven named Sparrow), have trapped one of the Silvermist hunters, a woman named Sumika. She was tricked into investigating this farm by the creatures’ voices, which she mistook for crying children. After being critically wounded by a spring-loaded spear trap the gremlins rigged in the farmhouse’s southwest communal room, Sumika crawled into the bedroom (area <strong>A1a</strong>) and barricaded the door.</p>\n<p>The four are now gathered near the entrance to the southwest building, calling out taunts to Sumika. “Blue like the dawn! Purple and miraculous! Swift like a fawn! Together, we are the Abacus Sisters!” cry out the two jinkins. As their nonsense rhyme concludes and they fall into a fit of cackling, Noodles elaborates, “That means we’re here to steal all your cattle!” Sparrow remains perched on the roof above the entrance, calling out to Sumika as if trying to lure out a trapped cat with a high-pitched, “Here, kitty, kitty! Come on out and get a treat!”</p>\n<p>These four mischievous tormentors aren’t particularly interested in fighting the PCs. Rather, they seek to “befriend” animals by taking them by force and have mistaken Sumika for this farm’s rancher. If any PCs have a companion animal, familiar, mount, or eidolon, the group fixates on the most powerful-looking of them, using a combination of obviously untrustworthy promises of food and outright threats to try to get the animal to join them.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/murasaki.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">A1. The Trapped Hunter</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.VLVw77FyEkhBM3og]{Midori} @UUID[Actor.oBy8cJvJblCMd8xW]{Murasaki} @UUID[Actor.Uwfc3kP631bILlPx]{Noodles} @UUID[Actor.7iu3BpmtW0fFAoUu]{Sparrow} @UUID[Actor.1or0C3ZqZm9dC54P]{Sumika}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img class=\"float-right\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-sumika.webp\" alt=\"A young woman with dark hair in a long braid\" title=\"Sumika\" style=\"z-index:5;shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-sumika.webp')\" />\n  <p>While the PCs can certainly fight the Abacus Sisters, this is a dangerous encounter. If instead a PC calls out to the four before attacking, the strange group cackles in delight. Midori gives the party a mock salute, and Murasaki says, “Oh! So you’re a chatty bunch then? Think you’ve got the wits to win out against the Abacus Sisters?” Sparrow chirps out a snarky, “I doubt it! I do! I doubt it! Don’t you?” Once it becomes obvious there are visitors, Sumika leans up to peer out of a window in the room and mouths the words “Help me!” to the PCs after waving a hand to quietly attract their attention.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>While attacking the tormentors can certainly help Sumika make her escape, the PCs can instead engage with the Abacus Sisters in a “battle of wits.” Allow the players to engage in any sort of conversation they wish, then have each of them attempt a @Check[deception|dc:13], @Check[diplomacy|dc:13], or @Check[intimidation|dc:13] check, as they see fit. If more than half of the PCs are successful, they confuse and distract the Abacus Sisters. You should also allow each PC to attempt a secret @Check[society|dc:17|traits:secret] or a @Check[farming-lore|dc:15|traits:secret] check to realize a mistake the four made—if they point out that the word “abactor” is the one that means “one who steals cattle,” not “abacus,” the four immediately fall to bickering and arguing among themselves about the revelation, allowing the PCs to automatically win the battle of wits.</p>\n<p>If the PCs manage to distract the Abacus Sisters, Sumika can clamber out through the window to limp away to safety. The PCs can then follow, leaving the bickering creatures behind before they can attack. Otherwise, the Abacus Sisters grow impatient and decide to attack the PCs. In combat, each member squeals in fear if reduced to fewer than 4 Hit Points and flees for their life.</p>\n<p>If Midori and Murasaki survive this encounter, they (potentially along with Noodles) might be encountered again later; see area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e13guesthous00]{E13}.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rescuing the Hunter:</strong> @UUID[Actor.2JY79N5rcJU8e8I8]{Sumika's Thanks} <br />Once rescued, Sumika thanks the PCs with enough supplies to craft two <em>spirit traps</em> along with additional materials to craft two other common 1st-level snares of the PCs’ choice. If she learns about the plan to light the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, she suggests the PCs visit the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.wjXNXFWBLbJaeZQR]{Ketephys} shrine at the westernmost Silvermist hunting lodge (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7a}).</p>\n<p>If the PCs convey Old Matsuki’s request that the hunters seek out Ugly Cute, Sumika nods in understanding and promises to deliver that information to her allies soon. If the PCs provide healing, Sumika is confident that she can make her way back to the Matsuki estate safely on her own but won’t turn down an offer by the PCs to escort her.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Reward the PCs full XP as if they defeated the Abacus Sisters in combat, no matter how they resolve this encounter.</p>"
            },
            "First Missions": {
              "name": "首次任务 First Missions",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"First Missions\">首次任务</h1>\n<p>在PC们着手应对柳岸镇镇区的生物或设法重新点亮<em>长明灯</em>这两项更大的任务之前，镇上的长者们先让他们尝试完成以下使命。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"First Missions\">First Missions</h1>\n<p>Before the PCs get to the larger task of confronting the creatures in downtown Willowshore or seeking to relight the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, the town’s elders have the following missions for them to attempt.</p>"
            },
            "Additional Requests": {
              "name": "额外请求 Additional Requests",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Additional Requests\">额外请求</h3>\n<p>胡太婆的首要目标是夺回市中心的营房，以取得其中的军械库，但她相信自己的女婿、现任卫队队长郑鹏，能够独自支撑一周。因此，除非PC们在她之前设法触及并解放营房，否则她不会向PC们提及这个任务。</p>\n<p>尽管胡太婆勉强同意老松木交给PC们的任务很重要，但还有其他事务在她看来更为紧迫。胡太婆请求PC们在着手处理寿的任务之前，先帮忙处理以下事项。</p>\n<p><strong>确认大夫情况：</strong>尽管胡太婆邀请达米汉西格·马巴邦洛布医生（简称“达米大夫”）到贸易栈与她会合，这位医生仍拒绝抛下自己的诊所——妙手回春。作为柳岸镇唯一的大夫，胡太婆希望确保等这一切结束后，村里仍有医生——而如果她还能亲自为医生的安全承担部分责任，那就更好不过了（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03a2clashatthe00]{Clash at the Clinic}）。</p>\n<p><strong>失踪的孙辈：</strong>在更私人的层面上，胡太婆担心自己有几个失踪的孙辈。他们最后一次被人看见，是在重现节当晚朝着蘑菇房附近北面的晾晒场走去（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}）。胡太婆推测，他们在那里办了自己的小聚会，结果不知怎的就没法回家了（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03theworstpuzz00]{The Worst Puzzle}）。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们与胡太婆取得联系时，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Additional Requests\">Additional Requests</h3>\n<p>Granny Hu’s primary objective is to retake the downtown barracks for its armory, but she trusts her son-in-law and current guard captain, Zheng Peng, to be able to hold his own for a week. Therefore, she only mentions this quest to the PCs if they manage to reach and liberate the barracks before she does.</p>\n<p>While she begrudgingly agrees that the missions given to the PCs by Old Matsuki are important, there are other tasks that she feels are more pressing. Granny Hu asks the PCs to help with the following first before they look to Shou’s tasks.</p>\n<p><strong>Checking the Doctor:</strong> Despite Granny Hu’s invitation to Dr. Damihansig Mababangloob (“Doctor Dami” for short) to join her at the trade office, the doctor refused to abandon his clinic, the Hand Of Spring. Being the only doctor in Willowshore, Granny Hu wants to ensure that when this is all over, the village still has a physician—and if she can personally claim some of the responsibility for the doctor’s safety, so much the better (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03a2clashatthe00]{Clash at the Clinic}).</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Grandchildren:</strong> On a more personal level, Granny Hu is worried about some of her missing grandchildren. They were last seen heading toward the northern drying yards near the Mushroom House (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}) on the evening of the Reenactment Festival. Granny Hu speculates they hosted their own private party there and somehow ended up unable to return home (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03theworstpuzz00]{The Worst Puzzle}).</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 40 XP for making contact with Granny Hu.</p>"
            },
            "Meeting Granny Hu": {
              "name": "会见胡太婆 Meeting Granny Hu",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Meeting Granny Hu\">会见胡太婆</h2>\n<p>新的贸易栈（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w29tradeoffi00]{W29}）确实是 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{胡太婆}和大多数北岭人难民逃到的地方。附近有几座仓库已被改造成供本地人暂住的临时收容所，但PC们交谈过的每个人都指引他们去贸易栈——木棉河-杜月江瓦市。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景笔记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.s74EKIg52mIxhfNp]{室内}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>在贸易栈里，胡太婆正仔细端详一张柳岸镇的地图，用一副八步棋的棋子标记怪物被目击的地点，以及人们可能被困的地方。PC们的到来让她和她目前的得力助手——@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{国府幸}的牧师金具元——都大吃一惊。胡太婆追问PC们是如何渡河的，担心他们可能被迫与怪物达成交易。PC们解释清楚后，胡太婆摇头失笑，嘲笑队伍愚蠢却勇敢。她请他们坐下，向她汇报一路经历，并假装关心南边的人们。</p>\n<p>胡太婆被迫、却又不情愿地在接下来必须采取的三项最重要举措上同意老松木的看法；但如果PC们先来找她，她会兴致勃勃地主动提出下列任务，并给出略有不同的建议。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Granny Hu\" alt=\"An elderly woman with salt and pepper hair\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>入侵的怪物：</strong>胡太婆听说，入侵柳岸镇的怪物的“脑子”是个名为莫都求的人（或某种东西）。她认为他要么是拥有秘术力量的人类，要么是某种类人的妖怪。她觉得北岭人更能自给自足；在她看来，恢复晨步桥的许可远不如击败那些如今控制柳岸镇镇区的生物重要。</p>\n<p><strong>丑小乖：</strong>胡太婆确实从一些幸存者那里听说蜘蛛雕像失踪了，但她觉得“石像自己醒来”这种说法纯属荒唐迷信。真要说的话，她怀疑那雕像可能是被魔法赋予了行动力，或许已经闹鬼。由于其能行动的来源未知，她警告不要想当然地认为丑小乖是友善的，不过她也不把它视为需要优先处理的首要威胁。</p>\n<p><strong>未点燃的灯笼：</strong>胡太婆对<em>长明灯</em>的传说只略知一二；但具元可以复述 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智辉}大师如何用受到 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{卡莉丝翠}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{国府幸}与 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{雪琳}祝福的硬币点亮灯笼，并建议前去寻访她们的神龛以求赐福，或许是最好的策略。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Meeting Granny Hu\">Meeting Granny Hu</h2>\n<p>The new trade office (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w29tradeoffi00]{W29}) is indeed where @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{Granny Hu} and most of Northridge’s refugees have fled to. Several of the nearby warehouses have been converted into temporary shelters for locals, but everyone the PCs speak to directs them to the trade office, called the Ceiba-Duyue Exchange.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.s74EKIg52mIxhfNp]{Indoors}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>At the trade office, Granny Hu scrutinizes a map of Willowshore, using game pieces from an Eight Paces set to mark where monsters have been sighted and where people might be trapped. The PCs’ arrival comes as quite a shock to her and her current right-hand aide, the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{Kofusachi} cleric Kim Gu-won. Granny Hu questions how the PCs managed to cross the river, fearing they might have been forced to strike a bargain with the monsters. Once the PCs explain, Granny Hu shakes her head and chuckles at the party’s foolish bravery. She asks them to sit and update her on what they’ve been through, feigning concern for the folks in the south.</p>\n<p>Granny Hu is forced to reluctantly agree with Old Matsuki about the three most important steps that must be taken next, but if the PCs come to her first, she eagerly suggests the following tasks on her own, providing somewhat different advice.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Granny Hu\" alt=\"An elderly woman with salt and pepper hair\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>The Invading Monsters:</strong> Granny Hu has heard rumors that the “brain” of the monsters that invaded Willowshore is someone (or something) named Mo Douqiu. She believes he might either be a human with occult powers or some sort of human-like yokai. She sees Northridge as being more self-sufficient, and restoring access to Dawnstep Bridge is, to her, less important than defeating the creatures that now control downtown Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Ugly Cute:</strong> Granny Hu did hear from some survivors that the spider statue has gone missing, but she finds the idea of the stone statue “waking up on its own” to be ridiculous superstition. If anything, she suspects the statue might have been animated by magic, or perhaps it has become haunted. Since the source of its mobility is unknown, she warns against assumptions that Ugly Cute is friendly, though she doesn’t see it as a foremost threat that needs to be handled.</p>\n<p><strong>The Unlit Lantern:</strong> While Granny Hu only vaguely knows the legend of the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, Gu-won can recount how Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} lit the lantern with coins blessed by @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AlL9GtlTldbqNoVm]{Calistria}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.AIcDyoff265z9285]{Kofusachi}, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{Shelyn} and suggests that seeking their shrines for blessings might be the best tactic.</p>"
            },
            "Crossing the Water": {
              "name": "渡水 Crossing the Water",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">渡水</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>只要怪物仍控制着晨步桥（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w11dawnstepb00]{W11}），在北岭人与南岸之间旅行就很棘手，因为木筏湖与木棉河的水域构成了一道显著的障碍。</p>\n<p><strong>木棉河：</strong>木棉河的深度在20至25英尺之间变化，两岸几乎没有浅滩——这一特征在传统上使这条河非常适合运输木材。PC可以通过一次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim]检定在河水中游泳渡过，或通过载具操作检定乘坐划艇横渡（见《Pathfinder GM Core》第212页，但注意：载具操作检定大失败会导致翻船并使船只下沉）。务必提醒玩家鬼季的第三条规矩——“当附近有鬼时，应避免进入水体。”在此情况下，“进入水体”既可能指亲身下水，也可能包括试图驾驶船只横渡水面。虽然没有任何游戏机制来支撑这种暗示的危险，但你只要提醒他们这一迷信，就能让玩家在过河时感到些许不安与紧张。</p>\n<p><strong>柳岸镇大坝：</strong>这座大坝（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w18willowsho00]{W18}）目前处于开启状态。角色可以花费一个10分钟的行动，在任一岸边与大坝的机械装置进行交互，并在一次@Check[athletics|dc:15]或@Check[engineering-lore|dc:13]检定中成功以将其关闭。每次尝试关闭（或开启）大坝都会为一次遭遇进行一次纯骰检定（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03randomencoun00]{随机遭遇}），而大成功或大失败中的大失败表示机构卡住，除非经过数天的修理工作，否则再也无法开启或关闭。</p>\n<p>一旦大坝关闭，其东侧的木棉河水位会下降到10英尺深，游泳或驾驶船只的DC降低5，持续2小时；之后木筏湖的水位上升到足以从大坝溢洪道漫过的程度，水域会恢复到先前的深度与流速。此时开启大坝会使河深恢复正常，并使横渡所需的检定在15分钟内增加5。</p>\n<p>PC可以将大坝本身视作一座临时桥梁，但其表面湿滑且局部狭窄，因此要这么做，PC必须在紧张的5分钟横渡过程中，成功通过五次@Check[acrobatics|dc:17|traits:move,skill,action:balance|name:Balance]检定以保持平衡。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span>横渡水域</span>\n      <span>中等 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.vYxo1QtbmrQNTjc3]{Grasping Currents}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>木筏湖：</strong>木筏湖（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w17woodraftl00]{W17}）的水面较为平静（游泳与载具操作检定降低5），但死去的镇民尸体漂浮在水中——要么是怪物随意丢在此处，要么更为悲惨地，是那些惊惧之人试图横渡水域而失败的结果。这些死亡，再加上诡异迷雾与猩红月光的影响，使得湖泊变得闹鬼。在<em>长明灯</em>点亮之前，任何试图横渡湖泊的尝试都会触发以下危害。</p>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>寻找船只</h2>\n  <p>在晨步桥的布索被击败之前，划艇也许是横渡木棉河最安全的方式，但在南岸找到一艘并不容易，因为多数与航运相关的城镇基础设施都位于河的北岸。更糟的是，镇上许多划艇都被破坏性的金肯斯弄坏了。角色若沿南岸搜索10分钟，并在一次@Check[perception|dc:13|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定中成功，便能找到一艘破损的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.vehicles.Actor.l0RfYgabnbNoHnkS]{划艇}；若大成功，则可找到一艘完好的划艇。</p>\n  <p>更大的船只与驳船停泊在北岸的多个地点，但这些载具很可能超出低等级队伍的驾驶能力。幸运的是，角色只要花10分钟搜索，就能在河的北岸自动找到一艘可用的划艇。</p>\n  <p>载具规则见《Pathfinder GM Core》（第210–213页）。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Crossing the Water</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As long as monsters retain control of Dawnstep Bridge (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w11dawnstepb00]{W11}), traveling between Northridge and Southbank is tricky, as the waters of Woodraft Lake and the Ceiba River present a significant barrier.</p>\n<p><strong>Ceiba River:</strong> The Ceiba River varies between 20 and 25 feet deep with very little shallows along either shore—a feature that traditionally made the river very well suited for the transport of lumber. A PC can Swim the river’s waters with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim] check or cross in a rowboat via Piloting checks (see page 212 in <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>, but note that a critical failure on a Piloting check results in a capsize and the boat sinking). Make sure to remind the players of the third practice of the season of ghosts—that one should “avoid entering bodies of water when a ghost is nearby.” In this case, entering a body of water could mean physically entering it or even attempting to pilot a boat across water. While there are no game mechanics in play to back up this implied danger, you can make your players a bit uneasy and nervous about crossing the river simply by reminding them of this superstition.</p>\n<p><strong>Willowshore Dam:</strong> The dam (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w18willowsho00]{W18}) is currently open. A character can close it as a 10-minute activity to Interact with the dam’s mechanisms on either shore by succeeding at a @Check[athletics|dc:15] or @Check[engineering-lore|dc:13] check. Each attempt to close (or open) the dam incurs a flat check for an encounter (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03randomencoun00]{Random Encounters}), and a critical failure indicates the mechanism has become stuck and can’t be opened or closed again until it’s repaired with several days of work.</p>\n<p>Once the dam is closed, the waters of the Ceiba River to the east lower to a depth of 10 feet, and the DC to Swim or Pilot a boat is reduced by 5 for 2 hours, after which the water level of Woodraft Lake rises enough to drain over the dam’s spillways, reverting the waters to their former depth and speed. Opening the dam at this point increases the river depth back to normal and increases checks to cross it by 5 for 15 minutes.</p>\n<p>A PC can treat the dam itself as an improvised bridge, but its slick surface and narrow spots mean that to do so requires that PC to succeed at five @Check[acrobatics|dc:17|traits:move,skill,action:balance|name:Balance] checks to balance during an intense 5-minute crossing.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span>Crossing the Waters</span>\n      <span>Moderate 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.vYxo1QtbmrQNTjc3]{Grasping Currents}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Woodraft Lake:</strong> While the waters of Woodraft Lake (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w17woodraftl00]{W17}) are calmer (reduce checks to Swim and Pilot by 5), the bodies of dead townsfolk float in the waters, either tossed here unceremoniously by monsters or, more tragically, the results of failed attempts by frightened people trying to cross the waters. These deaths, combined with the influence of the eerie mists and crimson moonlight, have caused the lake to become haunted. Any attempt to cross the lake before the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is lit runs afoul of the following hazard.</p>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Finding a Boat</h2>\n  <p>Until the buso at Dawnstep Bridge is defeated, rowboats are perhaps the safest way to cross the Ceiba River, but finding one on the southern shoreline isn’t particularly easy since most of the urban infrastructure for boating exists along the river’s northern banks. Worse, many of the rowboats in town have been damaged by destructive jinkins. A character who Searches for 10 minutes along the southern bank and succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:13|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check can find a broken @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.vehicles.Actor.l0RfYgabnbNoHnkS]{Rowboat}, while with a critical success, they locate an undamaged rowboat.</p>\n  <p>Larger boats and barges are moored at various places along the northern shore, but these vehicles are likely beyond the capacity of a low-level party to pilot. Fortunately, characters can automatically find a functional rowboat on the river’s northern bank after taking 10 minutes to Search.</p>\n  <p>See <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> for vehicle rules (pages 210–213).</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Making Contact: Northridge": {
              "name": "建立联系：北岭人 Making Contact: Northridge",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Making Contact: Northridge\">建立联系：北岭人</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇新建的贸易栈（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w29tradeoffi00]{W29}）及其仓库已在数周前完工。这一点，再加上它们位于柳岸镇中心以东相当一段距离，使其成为理想的临时避难所。渔场（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w30fisheries00]{W30}）甚至连蘑菇房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}）也敞开大门，以安置涌入的村民。与松木宅相比，贸易栈里的难民更少，既因为镇中心的 NPC 们被困住了，也因为有些本地人刻意与胡太婆保持距离；但与躲在贸易栈里的人建立联系，仍是从怪物手中夺回柳岸镇的重要一步。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Making Contact: Northridge\">Making Contact: Northridge</h1>\n<p>Willowshore’s new trade office (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w29tradeoffi00]{W29}) and its warehouses were completed weeks ago. This, plus the fact that they’re located a fair distance to the east of central Willowshore, makes them perfect makeshift shelters. The fisheries (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w30fisheries00]{W30}) and even the Mushroom House (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w32themushro00]{W32}) have also opened their doors to accommodate the influx of villagers. Compared to the Matsuki estate, there are fewer refugees at the trade office, both because the NPCs downtown are trapped and because several locals have intentionally distanced themselves from Granny Hu, but making contact with those holed up at the trade office is still an important step toward reclaiming Willowshore from the monsters.</p>"
            },
            "Meeting Old Matsuki": {
              "name": "会见老松木 Meeting Old Matsuki",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Meeting Old Matsuki\">会见老松木</h2>\n<p>松木宅一片忙乱。许多房间已被清空并改造成工坊、医疗站或睡铺。唯一相对平静的一隅在茶饭厅。在这里，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{老松木}与柳岸镇南部的其他重要人物同坐，耐心聆听不断送来的各类报告。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景笔记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.s74EKIg52mIxhfNp]{室内}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>他注意到PC们后，老松木暂停了当前的会谈，招手示意PC们过去，并为队伍提供热食与饮品。PC们休整时，老松木询问他们在森林里醒来之后发生了什么。PC们讲述完自己的经历后，他深表同情，并鼓励那些家人失踪的人保持乐观。若PC们觉得自家不够安全不便居住，他也愿意提供住处。</p>\n<p>待PC们稍作放松后，老松木请求他们协助夺回柳岸镇。具体来说，他提出以下四个主题，作为希望PC们去处理的目标。PC们以何种顺序尝试这些任务，由他们自行决定。</p>\n<p><strong>联络北岭人：</strong>由于怪物在晨步桥扎营，前往北岭人的便捷通道被切断。老松木承认他与胡太婆之间有些分歧，但与她取得联系并向北岭人提供力所能及的援助非常重要。若PC们愿意承担此事，老松木建议去贸易栈寻找胡太婆（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03makingcontac01]{取得联系——北岭人}）。</p>\n<p><strong>丑小乖：</strong>老松木提到，有数名难民声称看见一只马匹大小、由石头构成的蜘蛛在薄雾中大步穿行；他相信柳岸镇的石制守护者已苏醒以保卫城镇。PC们可以通过汇报那座失踪的雕像来证实这一推测。他计划招募银雾斋（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7}）的猎人去追踪丑小乖，为这头守护巨兽提供支援，但眼下猎人们正忙于在街上营救镇民。若PC们能联系上一位猎人，老松木请他们将此情报转告对方（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03a1thetrapped00]{被困的猎人}）。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Old Matsuki\" alt=\"Elderly man\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>入侵的怪物：</strong>老松木提醒PC们注意晨步桥上的武僧与金金斯（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w11dawnstepb00]{W11}；见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03liberatingth00]{解放桥梁}）。他转述幸存者的报告：金金斯似乎害怕与武僧并肩作战；而直接与武僧对峙，或点名向其发起挑战，或许是无需同时对付小魔怪（特征）便能击败怪物的一种办法。他还指出武僧似乎嗜酒，并建议若PC们自认能骗过这怪物，可以带着掺毒的酒作为供品接近它，让战斗更容易取胜。若PC们想走这条路，老松木建议去妙手回春（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}）拜访（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03a2clashatthe00]{诊所冲突}）。</p>\n<p><strong>未点亮的长明灯：</strong>老松木怀疑，影响柳岸镇的诡异天气与<em>长明灯</em>熄灭有关。他了解<em>长明灯</em>的历史，并向PC们讲述@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智辉}大师当初如何用三枚受祝福的铜币首次点燃灯火。要重新点亮灯笼、终结诡异浓雾与令人不安的猩红月光，PC们必须拜访三处不同的神龛，向三位神祇各献上一枚铜币以获得祝福。老松木只需10分钟就能教会PC们如何进行祈祷；他还提供三枚铜币作为献上的信物（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03blessingthec00]{祝福铜币}）。一旦PC们获得三枚受祝福的铜币，就应尽快前往晨步桥重新点亮<em>长明灯</em>（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03lightthenigh00]{点亮夜色}）。</p>\n<p><strong>柳岸镇镇区：</strong>最后，他迅速确认夺回镇区极其重要，但老松木警告PC们此时不要进入柳岸镇镇区，因为报告显示该地区已尤其被怪物大肆侵占。待上述四项任务完成后（尤其是点亮<em>长明灯</em>），再推进处理镇区的计划。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们与老松木取得联系后，给予40 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Meeting Old Matsuki\">Meeting Old Matsuki</h2>\n<p>The Matsuki estate is a blur of activity. Many rooms have been cleared and converted into workshops, medical stations, or sleeping quarters. The only pocket of relative calm is in the banquet hall. Here, sitting with other major figures of south Willowshore, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{Old Matsuki} listens patiently to all the reports coming in.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.s74EKIg52mIxhfNp]{Indoors}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>When he notices the PCs, Old Matsuki pauses his current meeting and beckons the PCs to join him, providing warm food and drinks for the party. While the PCs recuperate, Old Matsuki asks them what happened after they woke up in the forest. After the PCs recount their experience, he is sympathetic and encourages anyone with missing family members to stay optimistic. He offers lodgings if the PCs feel their homes aren’t secure enough to stay in.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs have had a chance to relax a bit, Old Matsuki asks for their help in retaking Willowshore. In particular, he mentions the following four topics as goals for the PCs to tackle. The order in which they attempt these quests is left to the PCs to decide.</p>\n<p><strong>Contacting Northridge:</strong> With monsters encamped on Dawnstep Bridge, easy access to Northridge is denied. Old Matsuki admits he has his differences with Granny Hu, but making contact with her and providing available aid to Northridge is important. If the PCs feel up to the task, Old Matsuki suggests seeking Granny Hu out at the trade office (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03makingcontac01]{Making Contact - Northridge}).</p>\n<p><strong>Ugly Cute: </strong>Old Matsuki notes that several refugees claim to have seen a horse-sized spider made of stone striding through the mist, and he believes Willowshore’s stone guardian has awakened to defend the town; the PCs can confirm this theory by reporting the missing statue. He plans on recruiting the hunters from the Silvermist Lodges (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7}) to track down Ugly Cute to provide aid to the guardian beast, but currently, the hunters are busy saving townsfolk in the streets. If the PCs can contact one of the hunters, Old Matsuki asks them to convey this information to them (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03a1thetrapped00]{The Trapped Hunter}).</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Old Matsuki\" alt=\"Elderly man\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>The Invading Monsters:</strong> Old Matsuki warns the PCs about the buso and jinkins on Dawnstep Bridge (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w11dawnstepb00]{W11}; see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03liberatingth00]{Liberating the Bridge}). He shares survivor reports that the jinkins appear to be afraid of fighting beside the buso, and that directly confronting the buso or calling it out specifically for a challenge might be one way to defeat the monster without having to contend with the gremlins simultaneously. He also notes that the buso seems taken with drink, and he suggests that if the PCs think they can trick the monster, they could approach it with an offering of poisoned wine to make it easier to defeat. Old Matsuki suggests paying a visit to the Hand of Spring (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}) if the PCs are interested in pursuing this option (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03a2clashatthe00]{Clash at the Clinic}).</p>\n<p><strong>The Unlit Lantern:</strong> Old Matsuki suspects that the cause of the strange weather affecting Willowshore is tied to the fact that the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> has gone dark. He knows the history of the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> and shares with the PCs the story of how Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} first lit the lantern using three blessed copper coins. To relight the lantern and bring an end to the strange mist and unsettling crimson moonlight, the PCs must obtain the blessing of three gods by visiting three different shrines and offering a copper coin to receive the blessing. It only takes 10 minutes for Old Matsuki to teach the PCs how to perform the prayer; he provides the PCs with three copper coins as tokens to offer (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03blessingthec00]{Blessing the Coins}). Once the PCs have three blessed coins, they should make haste to Dawnstep Bridge to relight the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03lightthenigh00]{Light the Night}).</p>\n<p><strong>Downtown Willowshore:</strong> In closing, and while he’s quick to confirm that retaking downtown is very important, Old Matsuki warns the PCs against entering downtown Willowshore at this time, for reports indicate that this part of town has become particularly infested with monsters. Once the four tasks above have been accomplished (in particular, the lighting of the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>), plans for dealing with downtown can proceed.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 40 XP for making contact with Old Matsuki.</p>"
            },
            "Making Contact: Southbank": {
              "name": "建立联系：南岸 Making Contact: Southbank",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Making Contact: Southbank\">建立联络：南岸</h1>\n<p>由于怪物入侵，柳岸镇南部的许多镇民在拂晓前就撤退到了松木宅（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w5matsukiest00]{W5}）或三福客栈（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w6thricebles00]{W6}），除非别无选择，否则不敢前往他们的工坊与店铺。因此，大多数通常会在河流以南出没的NPC，通常都会在松木宅或客栈里避难，直到<em>长明灯</em>被点亮为止。如果玩家没有想到要自行去拜访松木宅，一名友方NPC应该很快提出这个建议——或者你也可以让PC们都尝试进行一次社交或柳岸镇学识检定，并将这一建议告诉掷骰结果最高的那名角色。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Making Contact: Southbank\">Making Contact: Southbank</h1>\n<p>Many of the townsfolk in South Willowshore retreated to the Matsuki estate (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w5matsukiest00]{W5}) or the Thrice-Blessed Inn (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w6thricebles00]{W6}) in the predawn hours due to the monstrous invasion, only braving their workshops and stores if they had no other choice. As a result, most NPCs who are usually found south of the river are generally sheltering at the estate or the inn until the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is lit. If the players don’t think of paying a visit to the Matsuki estate on their own, an allied NPC should suggest it before long—or you can simply have the PCs all attempt Society or Willowshore Lore checks and give this suggestion to whichever character rolls highest.</p>"
            },
            "Returning Home": {
              "name": "返回家园 Returning Home",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Returning Home\">返回家中</h2>\n<p>一名或所有PC可能在镇上有家或亲人，因此他们可能会担心并希望回家确认一切平安。如果你的玩家使用《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》，他们可能已经为自己的住所选好了建筑。</p>\n<p>使用你选择的任意地图中的建筑来代表PC的宅地；或者，你也可以绘制自己设计的地图，甚至邀请玩家协助绘制他们家的地图。每个家中都有一处小危机在等待——在柳岸镇 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03randomencoun00]{随机遭遇}表上掷骰[[/r 1d12]]，以决定PC在家中将面对什么（或者，你也可以直接从这些选项中挑选威胁，并根据每名PC的过往经历在主题上进行匹配）。如果有任何朋友或家人在场，只要PC能解决屋内的状况，他们就应当是安全的（但也许会被危险吓得心神不宁）。</p>\n<p><strong>宝藏：</strong>PC每造访一处住家，都能找回一些补给——要么是PC遗留在那里的物品，要么是来自朋友或家人的赠礼。如果你使用《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》，那么在创建角色、并选择他们在镇上的住所时，玩家自己就有机会从以下宝藏组合中挑选其一。否则，为PC从下列清单中选择一项宝藏作为奖励，但除非队伍中PC多于4名，否则不要重复发放奖励。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.mmymLAkn6BxKfcv9]{第一处住家}<br />\n    两瓶<em>下等治疗药水</em>以及一件由PC自行选择、价值不超过2 gp的常见冒险道具。\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.W9P30CgccOAZixkh]{第二处住家}<br />\n    一枚<em>可预见的银币</em>以及一只小瓶，内含一剂量的<em>潜能油</em>。\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.6kd0a00CZtadgAyn]{第三处住家} <br />\n    一套用于制作<em>警报圈套</em>的材料、10 sp，以及两枚<em>次级镇魂炸药</em>。\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.Q4C0JMv8PywRl3Rt]{第四处住家} <br />\n    一块冷铁。\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC造访了他们所有的住家，给予他们10 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Returning Home\">Returning Home</h2>\n<p>One or all of the PCs might have homes or family in town, in which case they might be concerned and wish to return home to ensure all is safe. If your players are using the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>, they might have already selected buildings for their homes.</p>\n<p>Use buildings from any map of your choice to represent the PC’s homestead; alternatively, you can create maps of your own design or even recruit the aid of the players in creating maps of their homes. In each home, a minor peril awaits—roll [[/r 1d12]] on the Willowshore @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03randomencoun00]{Random Encounters} table to determine what the PCs face in their homes (alternatively, you can simply pick threats from these options, matching them thematically to each PC’s history). If any friends or family are present, they should be safe (but perhaps rattled by the danger), provided the PCs can solve the situation found within.</p>\n<p><strong>Treasure:</strong> For each home the PCs visit, they can recover some supplies—either items left behind by the PC, or gifts from friends or family. If you’re using the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>, the players themselves will have had the chance to pick one of the following sets of treasure during character creation when they selected their homes in town. Otherwise, choose a treasure from the following list for the PCs as a reward, but don’t duplicate rewards unless there are more than 4 PCs in the party.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.mmymLAkn6BxKfcv9]{First Home}<br />\n    Two <em>minor healing potions</em> and one piece of common adventuring gear worth 2 gp or less of the PC’s choice.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.W9P30CgccOAZixkh]{Second Home}<br />\n    One <em>predictable silver piece</em> and a vial with one dose of <em>oil of potency</em>.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.6kd0a00CZtadgAyn]{Third Home} <br />\n    Supplies for an <em>alarm snare</em>, 10 sp, and two <em>lesser ghost charges</em>.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    @UUID[Actor.Q4C0JMv8PywRl3Rt]{Fourth Home} <br />\n    One chunk of cold iron.\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 10 XP if they visit all of their homes.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Features": {
              "name": "柳岸镇特征 Willowshore Features",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore Features\">柳岸镇特征</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的大多数门都是拉门，只有厕所上的门例外（是带铰链的木门）。外部拉门由整块木材制成，提供标准掩蔽，并且角色在进行 @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定成功后，可以将其破拆打开。室内拉门或隔断不提供掩蔽，但会提供隐蔽，并且角色在进行 @Check[athletics|dc:5|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定成功后，可以将其破拆打开。你可以以一个交互动作在许多室内门的纸面上戳出一个洞来往里窥视，不过你必须通过一次潜行检定，才能不被另一侧的生物察觉。武器和弹药很容易贯穿室内门。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore Features\">Willowshore Features</h2>\n<p>Most doors in Willowshore are sliding doors, with the exception of those found on outhouses (which are hinged wooden doors). Exterior sliding doors are made of solid wood, grant standard cover, and can be Forced Open by a character who succeeds at a @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check. Indoor sliding doors or room partitions provide no cover, do provide concealment, and can be Forced Open by a character who succeeds at a @Check[athletics|dc:5|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check. You can poke a hole in the paper of many interior doors to peek inside as an Interact action, though you must pass a Stealth check to remain undetected by creatures on the other side. Weapons and ammunition can easily pierce through interior doors.</p>"
            },
            "Random Encounters": {
              "name": "随机遭遇 Random Encounters",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Random Encounters\">随机遭遇</h2>\n<p>PC们在镇中以探索模式旅行时（或如遭遇文本所指示），每经过4到8小时进行一次 @Check[flat|dc:10] 检定。每位正在避人耳目或斥候的PC会使该DC增加1，但每位正在疾行或搜索的PC会使该DC降低2。随机遭遇发生的频率不应高于每天一次。</p>\n<p>若成功，PC们会遇到一次随机遭遇。若结果为魅影但PC们在白天的户外，则视为没有遭遇。当PC们在夜间旅行时，在柳岸镇随机遭遇表上掷骰时加上+5调整值，将高于20的结果视为20。</p>\n<p>与所有随机遭遇一样，你应避免过度使用——你希望这些遭遇能帮助营造镇中不安全、令人不安的氛围，而不是把从一个地点移动到另一个地点这件事变成苦差事。每个团对这类额外遭遇的接受度都不同，所以不要害怕调整这些遭遇的频率（甚至是它们的威胁等级），以符合你们游戏的偏好。</p>\n<p>这些随机遭遇会在<em>长明灯</em>被点亮后结束。</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>d20 Roll</th>\n      <th>Encounter</th>\n      <th>Threat</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–2</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.y5YgKcEykcOKGQlP]{巨蟑螂}</td>\n      <td>琐碎 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3–4</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Actor.FiB6WdhAjxuMWV05]{萦绕存在}</td>\n      <td>琐碎 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5–6</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.G92kyODOgw9u6yGN]{Jinkin}</td>\n      <td>琐碎 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7–8</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.8asvo7Li4K4rfkW3]{蜘蛛群}</td>\n      <td>琐碎 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>9–10</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Actor.FiB6WdhAjxuMWV05]{萦绕存在}</td>\n      <td>琐碎 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>11–12</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Actor.FiB6WdhAjxuMWV05]{萦绕存在（2）}</td>\n      <td>低 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>13–14</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.G92kyODOgw9u6yGN]{Jinkin} and 1 @UUID[Actor.kNZii0Kz5EclXOpy]{Viper}</td>\n      <td>低 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>15–16</td>\n      <td>3 @UUID[Actor.vrZuNziqZsQBmZVN]{魅影渡鸦}</td>\n      <td>低 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>17–18</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.2LKqnJCxIrW5Xy8s]{魅影野猪}</td>\n      <td>低 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>19–20+</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.EhuhCIknwwTKScfv]{魅影狼}</td>\n      <td>中等 1</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>好斗的野生动物：</strong>巨蟑螂或蜘蛛群通常胆小，但这些生物在苦迦菩提日益增长的影响下变得更具攻击性，这些害虫会战斗至死。如同在 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03strangeaggre00]{Strange Aggression} 中那样，成功通过一次秘密的 @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:secret] 或 @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret] 检定的角色会注意到这些生物如此暴戾是多么反常。而且就像那场遭遇里的蜈蚣一样，这些野生动物既凶残又能说话——但它们说话多半只是为了发出威胁或嘲弄受害者；它们对真正的交谈毫无兴趣。</p>\n<p><strong>萦绕存在：</strong>如果PC们同时遭遇两个萦绕存在，则会有两名不同的角色被“鬼魅威胁”锁定为目标。</p>\n\n<p><strong>Jinkin：</strong>与这些小鬼的遭遇要么是单独一个jinkin，要么是一个jinkin和它的宠物毒蛇。若jinkin的生命值降到5点以下，它会逃跑，但宠物毒蛇会战斗至死。许多jinkin从当地人那里偷走了寻常物件，要么以怪异的方式把它们穿戴在身上，要么正在毁坏该物件。本冒险中遭遇到的所有jinkin说的都是通用语，而非Sakvroth语。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-phantomwolf.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Phantom Wolf\" alt=\"Phantom Wolf\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-phantomwolf.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p><strong>魅影：</strong>这些生物是在冒险路径如此早期阶段，PC们最有可能面对的、最接近真实鬼魂的存在。它们既是苦迦菩提影响的显现，也是柳岸镇集体恐惧的显现。因此，当PC们把头转开时，这些魅影可能会呼唤某位PC的名字；又或者，当PC进入一片水域，或在夜里胆敢吹口哨时，它们便会现身。PC们最重要需要注意的是：通过使用第一项做法，以友善的问候来与这些魅影交谈，PC们可以让它们失去力量，甚至使其消散。如果PC们在遭遇魅影后仍未自行想到这一策略，则允许他们尝试一次秘密的 @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:secret] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:secret] 检定来意识到这一战术。这些魅影呈现为现实动物的幽灵般、淡绿色版本，拥有诡异发光的眼睛，并且能说通用语。魅影在被遭遇时更渴望惊吓PC们而非战斗；在它们遭到攻击之前，它们只会使用其先天的奥术法术或通过威吓检定来挫败士气。一旦魅影遭到攻击，它就会用近战打击还击。这些游荡的魅影无法追逐受害者进入建筑物，并且在任意一个轮次结束时，只要它们在街道的户外看不到任何可行目标，它们就会消失回到灵界。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Random Encounters\">Random Encounters</h2>\n<p>Once every four to eight hours as the PCs travel in town using exploration mode (or as directed in an encounter’s text), attempt a @Check[flat|dc:10] check. Each PC who’s Avoiding Notice or Scouting increases this DC by 1, but each PC who’s Hustling or Searching decreases the DC by 2. A random encounter should occur no more often than once per day.</p>\n<p>On a success, the PCs come across a random encounter. If the result is a phantom but the PCs are outdoors during the day, treat it as no encounter. When the PCs are traveling at night, add a +5 modifier when rolling on the Willowshore Random Encounters table, treating results above 20 as a 20.</p>\n<p>As with all random encounters, you should avoid overdoing them—you want these encounters to help establish that things are unsafe and unsettling in town, not turn the mere act of moving from one place to the next into a slog. Each table’s appetite for additional encounters like these will vary, so don’t be afraid to adjust the frequency of these encounters (or even their threat levels) to suit your game’s preferences.</p>\n<p>These random encounters end once the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> has been lit.</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>d20 Roll</th>\n      <th>Encounter</th>\n      <th>Threat</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–2</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.y5YgKcEykcOKGQlP]{Giant Cockroach}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3–4</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Actor.FiB6WdhAjxuMWV05]{Haunting Presence}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5–6</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.G92kyODOgw9u6yGN]{Jinkin}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7–8</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.8asvo7Li4K4rfkW3]{Spider Swarm}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>9–10</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Actor.FiB6WdhAjxuMWV05]{Haunting Presence}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>11–12</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Actor.FiB6WdhAjxuMWV05]{Haunting Presences (2)}</td>\n      <td>Low 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>13–14</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.G92kyODOgw9u6yGN]{Jinkin} and 1 @UUID[Actor.kNZii0Kz5EclXOpy]{Viper}</td>\n      <td>Low 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>15–16</td>\n      <td>3 @UUID[Actor.vrZuNziqZsQBmZVN]{Phantom Ravens}</td>\n      <td>Low 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>17–18</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.2LKqnJCxIrW5Xy8s]{Phantom Boar}</td>\n      <td>Low 1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>19–20+</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.EhuhCIknwwTKScfv]{Phantom Wolves}</td>\n      <td>Moderate 1</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Aggressive Wildlife:</strong> Giant cockroaches or spider swarms are normally skittish, but these creatures have become more aggressive from Kugaptee’s growing influence, and these vermin fight to the death. As in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03strangeaggre00]{Strange Aggression}, a character who succeeds at a secret @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:secret] or @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret] check notes how strange it is for these creatures to be so violent. And as with the centipedes in that encounter, these wild animals are vicious and can speak—but do so mostly to issue threats or taunt their victims; they have no interest in actual conversations.</p>\n<p><strong>Haunting Presence:</strong> If the PCs encounter two haunting presences simultaneously, then two different characters are targeted by Ghostly Menace.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Jinkin:</strong> Encounters with these gremlins are either with a lone jinkin or with a jinkin and their pet viper. A jinkin flees if reduced to fewer than 5 Hit Points, but a pet viper fights to the death. Many of these jinkins have stolen mundane objects from locals and either wear them in strange ways or are in the process of destroying the object. All of the jinkins encountered in this adventure speak Common rather than Sakvroth.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-phantomwolf.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Phantom Wolf\" alt=\"Phantom Wolf\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-phantomwolf.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p><strong>Phantoms:</strong> These creatures are the closest thing to actual ghosts the PCs are likely to face this early in the Adventure Path. These are manifestations of Kugaptee’s influence as much as they are of Willowshore’s collective fears. As such, these phantoms might call out a PC’s name when they’re looking away, or might appear as the result of a PC entering a body of water or daring to whistle at night. The most important thing for the PCs to note is that by using the first practice and addressing these phantoms with friendly greetings, the PCs can cause them to lose their power and even discorporate. Allow the PCs to attempt a secret @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:secret] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:secret] check to realize this tactic if they don’t come up with it themselves after encountering a phantom. These phantoms appear as ghostly, pale green versions of the real animal, but have eerie glowing eyes and can speak Common. Phantoms, when encountered, are more eager to frighten the PCs than to fight, and until they’re attacked, they’ll only use their innate occult spells or Intimidation checks to Demoralize. Once a phantom is attacked, it fights back with its melee strikes. These wandering phantoms can’t pursue victims into buildings, and they vanish back into the Ethereal Plane at the end of any round in which they see no viable targets outside on the streets.</p>"
            },
            "Back to Town": {
              "name": "返回城镇 Back to Town",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Back to Town\">回到城镇</h1>\n<p>一旦PC们抵达柳岸镇，他们的目标应当是探索这座怪物盘踞的城镇，积累资源与声望，并设法点亮<em>长明灯</em>，从而消除迷雾与月光的效果。</p>\n<p>如果玩家需要指引，你可以让海儿请求他们护送她前往松木宅（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03makingcontac00]{建立联系 - 南岸}）或去见胡太婆（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03makingcontac01]{建立联系 - 北岭人}）——无论哪条路，都能让队伍与柳岸镇的两位长者之一取得联系。任何在镇上有家人、朋友或住所的PC也可能希望回到那里——此时参见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03returninghom00]{回家}。</p>\n<p>PC们也可以自行开始探索柳岸镇镇区，但这一带如今潜伏着入侵怪物的大部分，最好先与其中一位长者建立联系。如果队伍坚持前往镇区，请继续至@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}。那里的遭遇更具挑战性，但仍为1级PC做了平衡。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Back to Town\">Back to Town</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs reach Willowshore, their goal should be to explore the monster-infested town, build up their resources and reputation, and work toward lighting the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> so they can neutralize the effects of the mist and moonlight.</p>\n<p>If the players need guidance, you can have Hai-er ask them to escort her to either the Matsuki estate (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03makingcontac00]{Making Contact - Southbank}) or to Granny Hu (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03makingcontac01]{Making Contact - Northridge})—either will put the party in contact with one of Willowshore’s two elders. Any PC who has family, friends, or a home in town might wish to return there as well—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03returninghom00]{Returning Home} in this case.</p>\n<p>The PCs can also begin exploring downtown Willowshore on their own, but this area is where the bulk of the invading monsters now lurk, and it’s best if the PCs first make contact with one of the elders. If the party persists in heading downtown, proceed to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2}. While encounters there are more challenging, they’re still balanced for 1st-level PCs.</p>"
            },
            "Eastern Watchtower": {
              "name": "东侧瞭望塔 Eastern Watchtower",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Eastern Watchtower\">东侧瞭望塔</h2>\n<p>从失踪的蜘蛛雕像再往西走约一英里后，PC们抵达柳岸镇的东侧瞭望塔。空气中弥漫着血腥味，地上横七竖八躺着四具尸体。其中两具属于城镇卫兵，他们的腿部肿胀，痛苦的表情凝固在脸上。另两具尸体看起来是体型矮小的蓝灰色类人生物，长着尖牙和巨大的耳朵，似乎死于剑伤。</p>\n<p>任意PC若成功通过一次 @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来进行回忆知识，便能辨认出那两具矮小类人生物的尸体是蹑影小魔怪。任意角色若检查两名人类卫兵并成功通过一次 @Check[medicine|dc:13] 检定，就会意识到他们死于腿部蛇咬注入的毒素。PC若搜索此区域，会发现附近草丛里有两条死掉的蝰蛇。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hai-erha.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ha Hai-er\" alt=\"A woman in oriental style armored helmet\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hai-erha.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>在瞭望塔上，一名名叫哈·海儿的城镇卫兵设法逃过一死。她看到PC们后，会要求他们背诵至少四条 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03easternwatch00#the-eight-practices]{鬼季的八项守则}，以证明他们不是伪装成怪物。这八项守则列在下方侧栏中，也收录于《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》。如果你没有使用该指南，或者玩家很难记住这些守则，角色可以通过一次成功的 @Check[religion|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]、@Check[society|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来回忆知识，随机回忆起两条守则（危急成功则四条，失败则一条，危急失败则一条也想不起）。PC也可以通过一次成功的 @Check[diplomacy|dc:15|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression] 检定来建立印象，让海儿放松，将她的态度从不友善提升到至少不关心。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>八项守则</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇的人民在鬼季遵循这八条信条。这些信念被视为抵御小型邪灵或恶作剧精怪关注的护身符，因此在故事初期可用来对付困扰柳岸镇的幻影。然而，它们通常对队伍在后续冒险将面对的更强大的不死生物或真正的鬼魂并不奏效；任何了解这些守则的当地人或PC也同样知道这一点。</p>\n  <p><strong>1.</strong> 不要称鬼为“鬼”；若非得提及，就用友善的问候来称呼它们。</p>\n  <p><strong>2.</strong> 不要拍人的头或肩膀。</p>\n  <p><strong>3.</strong> 附近有鬼时，避免进入水域。</p>\n  <p><strong>4.</strong> 不要吃有两根棒状物从中伸出的食物。</p>\n  <p><strong>5.</strong> 白天不要倚靠墙壁。</p>\n  <p><strong>6.</strong> 夜里不要吹口哨。</p>\n  <p><strong>7.</strong> 夜里不要把洗好的衣物晾在外面。</p>\n  <p><strong>8.</strong> 夜里若听到有人从身后喊你的名字，不要回头。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>一旦她被说服，如果她原本还不是不关心态度，她的态度就会变为不关心；随后她从塔上爬下来，如释重负地迎接PC们。尽管她并不认识他们任何一人，但她清楚记得昨晚：在重现节临近尾声时，钟虎叔与他的同伴戴着鬼魅般的纸面具，把PC们抬到了林子里。她也证实他们不久后就从林子里返回，却没带回PC们——那时正好是她开始值守的时候。午夜过后很久，那些“可怕的小蓝怪物”才从南边的林子里出来，带着它们训练过的蛇。另两名值班卫兵设法击败了那些生物，却随后因蛇咬而死。从那以后，海儿一直待在瞭望塔里，饱受恐惧与愧疚交织的折磨；而笼罩柳岸镇的浓雾更令她胆寒。如果之前没有PC想起关于“懒阿豆”的童谣，她可以把那首童谣告诉他们。</p>\n\n<p>她警告PC们，镇子方向一直有尖叫、咆哮与其他可怕的声音在空中回荡，但从黎明起，一切又归于寂静。若PC告诉她丑萌的雕像不见了，她会难以置信。海儿更愿意留在塔里，“直到这古怪的雾散掉为止”，并承诺若发现任何危险就会敲响塔钟。若已经过去超过24小时，她的食物也快见底，将会试着进镇——在本遭遇中，她的命运由GM决定。</p>\n<p>PC离开瞭望塔前，海儿会给他们一些建议。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“回家去，看看朋友和家人，确认大家都没事。要不是这雾，我也会这么做。法拉丝玛保佑我们，我希望我女儿没事。虽然我请胡奶奶照看她，但我还是担心。还有我丈夫……希望他现在在松木宅很安全。那地方简直像堡垒一样！”</p>\n</div>\n<p>所有PC都知道，“胡奶奶”指的是胡板娘，而松木宅是寿的家——不过他更常被称为“老松木”。这两位分别是柳岸镇北岭人与南岸两派的精神领袖。PC可以邀请海儿同行，但她起初会因对周遭事态的恐惧与对岗位的坚守而拒绝。若能让她至少变为友善态度，她便同意陪同PC。她鼓励他们要么去拜访胡奶奶（这样她能确认女儿的情况），要么去松木宅（追寻她丈夫的下落）——若PC在夜幕降临前忽略了这两种选择中的任何一个，她就会自行出发与女儿团聚。只要她与PC同行，海儿就会用她的弩在战斗中提供支援；只有在弹药用尽后，她才会靠近进入近战。若她的生命值降到6点以下，她会惊慌逃跑，希望先找到安全的地方躲藏，然后再继续寻找女儿。一旦她与女儿或丈夫中的任何一人团聚，她便不再陪同PC。</p>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:2ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.PyCdl79pLeQbhSDg]{Ha Hai-er}</span>\n    <span>生物 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.jlVLrlDxDn6eCo6C]{Ha Hai-er's Supplies} <br />\n  哈·海儿会从瞭望塔里拿出两件可能派得上用场的小型魔法补给品交给队伍——一件<em>奇妙缩微梯子</em>与一枚<em>闪耀弩矢</em>。这里还存放着一小桶灯油，若PC希望点亮丑萌被遗弃栖位东侧的灯笼，也可取用。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC与哈·海儿成为朋友，则给予PC等同于在战斗中击败哈·海儿所获得的XP。若他们帮助她与家人团聚，则队伍在北岭人与南岸各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">声望追踪</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.sOoLKv6nUesBfTyK]{Point Tracking} @UUID[Item.ncrOOOY5hyJIX14r]{Northridge Reputation} @UUID[Item.JP2qia0jUHA0VTtK]{Southbank Reputation}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>将这些效果添加到Point Tracking角色上，以追踪声望点数。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Eastern Watchtower\">Eastern Watchtower</h2>\n<p>After traveling about a mile further west from the missing spider statue, the PCs reach Willowshore’s eastern watchtower. The tang of blood fills the air, and four bodies lie sprawled on the ground. Two belong to town guards, their legs swollen and expressions of pain frozen on their faces. The other two bodies appear to be tiny blue-gray humanoids with sharp teeth and giant ears, seemingly slain by sword blows.</p>\n<p>A PC who succeeds at a @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge identifies the two tiny humanoid bodies as jinkin gremlins. Any character who examines the two human guards and succeeds at a @Check[medicine|dc:13] check realizes they perished from poison delivered from snake bites to the legs. A PC who Searches the area reveals two dead vipers in the grass nearby.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hai-erha.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ha Hai-er\" alt=\"A woman in oriental style armored helmet\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hai-erha.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Up in the guard tower, a town guard named Ha Hai-er managed to escape death. When she sees the PCs, she demands they recite at least four of the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03easternwatch00#the-eight-practices]{Eight Practices} of the season of ghosts to prove they aren’t monsters in disguise. These eight practices are listed in the sidebar below and in the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>. If you’re not using the guide, or if the players have trouble remembering the practices, a character can recall two randomly rolled practices with a successful @Check[religion|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge], @Check[society|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge], or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge (or four on a critical success, one on a failure, and none on a critical failure). A PC can also get Hai-er to relax by Making an Impression with a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:15|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression] check to shift her attitude from unfriendly to at least indifferent.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>The Eight Practices</h1>\n  <p>The people of Willowshore follow these eight tenets during the season of ghosts. These beliefs are held as protections against the attentions of minor evil or mischievous spirits and, as such, can be used against the phantoms that plague Willowshore early on. However, they’re generally ineffective against more powerful undead or actual ghosts the party will face in later adventures, and any local or PC who knows these practices would know this as well.</p>\n  <p><strong>1.</strong> Do not call a ghost a ghost; instead, address them with friendly greetings if you must.</p>\n  <p><strong>2.</strong> Do not pat people on the head or shoulders.</p>\n  <p><strong>3.</strong> Avoid entering bodies of water when a ghost is nearby.</p>\n  <p><strong>4.</strong> Do not eat food that has two stick-like objects protruding from it.</p>\n  <p><strong>5.</strong> Do not lean against walls during the day.</p>\n  <p><strong>6.</strong> Do not whistle at night.</p>\n  <p><strong>7.</strong> Do not leave laundry out at night.</p>\n  <p><strong>8.</strong> If you hear someone call your name from behind you at night, do not turn around.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Once she’s convinced, her attitude shifts to indifferent if it wasn’t there already, and she clambers down from the tower to greet the PCs with relief. While she doesn’t know any of them personally, she certainly remembers yesterday evening when Uncle Chung-hu and his crew in their ghostly paper masks carried the PCs out to the woods at the culmination of the Reenactment Festival. She also confirms they returned from the woods without the PCs a short time later, just at the beginning of her watch. It was well after midnight that those “horrible little blue monsters” came out of the woods to the south with their trained serpents. The other two guards on duty managed to defeat the creatures but then perished to snake bites. Hai-er has remained in the watchtower, plagued by a mix of fear and guilt ever since, and the dense fog that has descended on Willowshore frightens her all the more. If no PC recalled the rhyme about Lazy Adou earlier, she could share it with them.</p>\n\n<p>She warns the PCs that screams, roars, and other frightening sounds have been echoing through the air from town, but that since dawn, things have been silent. She’s incredulous if the PCs tell her Ugly Cute’s statue is missing. Hai-er prefers to stay here in the tower “until this weird fog lifts,” and she promises to ring the tower bell if she spots any danger. If more than 24 hours have passed, she is running low on food and will make her way into town—her fate is left to the GM to determine in this encounter.</p>\n<p>Hai-er has some advice for the PCs before they leave the watchtower.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Go home, check on friends and family, make sure everyone is all right. That’s what I would do if not for this fog. Pharasma bless us, I hope my daughter is okay. Even though I asked Granny Hu to babysit, I worry. And my husband... hopefully he’s safe at the Matsuki estate right now. That place is nearly a fortress!”</p>\n</div>\n<p>All PCs know that “Granny Hu” refers to Hu Ban-niang, and the Matsuki estate is Shou’s home—though he’s more commonly called “Old Matsuki.” These two individuals are the spiritual leaders of Willowshore’s Northridge and Southbank factions, respectively. The PCs can invite Hai-er to join them, though she initially resists due to a combination of her fear of what’s happening all around her and her dedication to her post. If she can be made at least friendly, she agrees to accompany the PCs. She encourages them to either visit Granny Hu (so she can check on her daughter) or the Matsuki estate (to track down her husband)—if the PCs neglect either of these options before nightfall, she’ll set off to reunite with her daughter on her own. As long as she’s accompanying the PCs, Hai-er provides support in combat with her crossbow, closing to melee only once she runs out of ammunition. If reduced to fewer than 6 Hit Points, she panics and flees, hoping to find somewhere safe to hide before moving on to seek out her daughter. Once she’s reunited with either her daughter or husband, she no longer accompanies the PCs.</p>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:2ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.PyCdl79pLeQbhSDg]{Ha Hai-er}</span>\n    <span>Creature 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.jlVLrlDxDn6eCo6C]{Ha Hai-er's Supplies} <br />\n  Ha Hai-er provides the party with two minor magical supplies from the watchtower that might be of use to them—a <em>ladder marvelous miniature</em> and a single <em>shining crossbow bolt</em>. A small cask of lantern oil is stored here as well, should the PCs wish to light the lantern to the east at Ugly Cute’s abandoned perch.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward: </strong>Grant the PCs XP as if they defeated Ha Hai-er in combat if they befriend her. If they help reunite her with her family, grant the party 1 Reputation Point with Northridge and Southbank.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Reputation Tracking</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.sOoLKv6nUesBfTyK]{Point Tracking} @UUID[Item.ncrOOOY5hyJIX14r]{Northridge Reputation} @UUID[Item.JP2qia0jUHA0VTtK]{Southbank Reputation}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Add these effects to the Point Tracking actor to keep track of Reputation Points.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Spiderless Gate": {
              "name": "无蛛之门 The Spiderless Gate",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Spiderless Gate\">无蛛之门</h2>\n<p>穿过杜月江上的桥后，PC们抵达柳岸镇的东入口。此处原本在路旁有一座神龛，里面立着一尊守护蜘蛛的石像，但当PC们在薄雾中走近时，却发现情况不对——蜘蛛石像不见了，只剩下空荡荡的神龛。柳岸镇东入口的灯笼原先叼在蜘蛛的獠牙间，如今侧倒在草地里。</p>\n<p>允许PC进行一次@Check[society|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定，以回忆知识来了解这尊石蜘蛛雕像，如区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w33spidergat00]{W33}所述。同一次检定也会提醒他们：<em>长明灯</em>——柳岸镇最初的入口灯笼——位于晨步桥附近（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w10eternalla00]{W10}）。</p>\n<p><strong>消失的蜘蛛：</strong>这只被当地人带着几分喜爱地称作“丑小乖”的石蜘蛛，有马那么大，由整块石头雕成，因此不太可能有人把它直接偷走。它原本栖坐的岩石上看不出任何凿刻或伤害的痕迹，但周围地面却被深深犁开，留下大片沟痕。若成功通过@Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]检定，PC可以确认这些痕迹与“若雕像活化并沿道路向东行进”时会留下的追踪一致。随后，这些追踪进入河流，变得无法继续追踪。PC此刻无从得知真相，但在之后的冒险中，他们将发现“丑小乖”遭遇了什么——见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05searchingfor00]{Searching for Ugly Cute}（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}）。</p>\n<p>未点燃的灯笼：入口灯笼里没有灯油。即便再次点燃，这盏灯也无法驱散薄雾与月光；但若PC为其重新加注灯油（如果他们此时没有灯油，可在下一场遭遇中找到灯油），则他们对抗猩红月光的豁免骰获得+2物品加值，同时血雨的纯骰检定提升为@Check[flat|dc:18]。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC点亮灯笼，给予他们20 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Spiderless Gate\">The Spiderless Gate</h2>\n<p>After crossing the bridge over the Duyue River, the PCs arrive at the eastern entrance to Willowshore. Here, a stone statue of a guardian spider once stood in a shrine next to the road, but as the PCs approach, something looks off in the mist—the spider statue is missing, with only an empty shrine left behind. Willowshore’s eastern entrance lantern, once held in the spider’s fangs, now lies on its side in the grass.</p>\n<p>Allow the PCs a @Check[society|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge about the stone spider statue, as detailed in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w33spidergat00]{W33}. The same check also reminds them that the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>—Willowshore’s original entrance lantern—is located near Dawnstep Bridge (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w10eternalla00]{W10}).</p>\n<p><strong>The Missing Spider:</strong> The stone spider somewhat affectionately known by the locals as “Ugly Cute” is the size of a horse and made of solid stone, which makes it unlikely that someone simply made off with it. No sign of chiseling or damage to the rock on which it once perched upon is evident, but large furrows scar the ground surrounding it. With a successful @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] check, a PC confirms these marks are consistent with tracks the statue would’ve left if it animated and headed east down the road. The tracks then enter the river and become impossible to follow. The PCs have no way of knowing it at the moment, but later in the adventure, they’ll discover what happened to Ugly Cute—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05searchingfor00]{Searching for Ugly Cute} in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}.</p>\n<p>The Unlit Lantern: The entrance lantern is empty of oil. While this lantern won’t drive back the mist and moonlight if it’s lit again, if the PCs refill it (they can find lantern oil in the next encounter if they don’t have any at this time), they gain a +2 item bonus to saving throws against the crimson moonlight, and the flat check for blood rain increases to @Check[flat|dc:18].</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Give the PCs 20 XP for lighting the lantern.</p>"
            },
            "Maze of Mist, Rain of Blood": {
              "name": "迷雾迷宫，血雨 Maze of Mist, Rain of Blood",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Maze of Mist, Rain of Blood\">迷雾迷宫，血雨倾盆</h2>\n<p>当PC们沿着兽径前行时，天气变得愈发诡异。雾气从林间翻涌而来；等PC们走出森林、踏上熟悉的河岸道路时，这雾已浓成一片大雾——而距离他们离开醒来的那片空地，仅仅过去了10分钟。</p>\n<p>前方，在这不寻常的浓雾中望见杜月江大桥令人欣慰，因为这座桥证实PC们已抵达柳岸镇的最东端。然而，当他们穿过大桥时，雾气依旧不散。允许每名PC尝试一次秘密的 @Check[society|dc:13|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:13|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定以进行回忆知识。大失败时，PC会错记一则古老传说：夏雾会带来夏疫。成功时，PC会想起一首古老童谣，暗示柳岸镇的<em>长明灯</em>已经熄灭。参见下方的灯谣。</p>\n<blockquote class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>懒阿豆歇了歇，</p>\n  <p>那天不把灯点燃。</p>\n  <p>这可真是大错事，</p>\n  <p>鬼儿出来闹着玩！</p>\n  <p>迷雾昏昏血月悬，</p>\n  <p>只因他呀就放弃。</p>\n  <p>灯谣</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>只要柳岸镇的<em>长明灯</em>仍然熄灭，白昼与夜晚都会更危险、更令人不安。白天，城镇始终笼罩在一种名为迷踪蜃雾的浓雾之中。夜晚雾气消散，但代价是：绯红月光与血雨会洒遍大地。</p>\n<p><strong>迷踪蜃雾：</strong>这股阴森的浓雾厚到足以遮蔽500尺以外的视野。距离超过100尺所观察到的生物处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{隐蔽}状态。此外，雾气会扭曲周边视觉，使人不时在视野边缘注意到怪异的形状在极限处移动与变幻。处于迷踪蜃雾中的所有基于视觉的察觉检定因此承受–1状态减值；同时，所有用于辨别方向的生存检定DC增加5。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.ffY3ybPo0ZvpfCUL]{Mist Urban} @UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.2089R8LUFfxhJMM0]{Mist Nature}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-crimson-moon.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Crimson Moon\" alt=\"A Red moon Rises bathin a river and frest in red light\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-crimson-moon.webp')\" />\n\n<p><strong>绯红之月：</strong>夜晚，迷踪蜃雾散去，天空恢复为局部多云。月亮偶尔透过云层显现时，会以诡异的绯红色泽照耀。这一效果具有情绪、恐惧与心灵（特征）。生物在绯红之月下度过任何一小时的起始时刻，都必须尝试一次 @Check[will|dc:15|traits:emotion,fear,mental] 豁免，以避免其@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧}状态的数值提高。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 该生物将其由月光引发的惊惧状态值降低1。若因此将数值降至0，则该生物在当晚余下时间内对绯红之月的影响暂时免疫。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 该生物由月光引发的惊惧状态不会提高。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 该生物的惊惧状态值提高1，最高至4。该惊惧状态持续至黎明，或直到足够多次大成功将该数值降至0为止。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 同失败，但该状态值提高2。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏 / 氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.DxD2BgVlVgehVnuO]{Enable Blood Moon} @UUID[Macro.Jz8MIw7gUsCW19TY]{Reset Willowshore} | @UUID[Macro.u7NLULMdAcyTWq1c]{Enable Rain} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.nezy4qHmtlstrXAe]{Rain}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>将@UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{柳岸镇}场景的照明改为绯红色。</p>\n</section>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>邪恶动物</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇的野生动物异常凶暴这一点，足以让任何在一次秘密的 @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:secret] 或 @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret] 检定中成功的PC感到担忧（成功时，该PC会意识到：像巨蜈蚣这类生物如此迅速地变得富有攻击性、并在面对更强的对手时仍不选择逃离，是多么反常——尤其是在白天）。但当这些动物还具备令人不安的说话能力时，更立刻暴露出某种超自然力量正在作祟。一名在回忆知识的 @Check[occultism|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定中成功的PC会知道：这些动物正以某种方式受到邪灵的影响。这些动物——以及在本次冒险中于思维空间遭遇的许多其他攻击性动物——是库加普提对该地区影响的物质显现。它们不同寻常的智力（其智力调整值为+0，且能说通用语）以及残忍、嗜虐的性格，是这头邪魔在本轮思维空间循环中存在感增强的副作用；但除此之外，它们仍具有该类生物的标准数据。</p>\n</aside>\n<p><strong>血雨：</strong>每天日落、绯红之月升起时，进行一次 @Check[flat|dc:14]。成功时，云层覆盖加重（这并不免除每小时对抗绯红之月而进行意志豁免的需求），并且在夜晚某个时刻（由GM决定），看似鲜血的雨水会倾泻在柳岸镇上。这“血”似乎会把一切都覆上一层血污。任何目睹血雨的PC必须立刻进行一次对抗绯红之月效果的豁免；若他们正淋在雨中，该次豁免承受–4环境减值。若某PC因这次豁免而使其惊惧状态提高，则其将陷入逃跑1分钟，并必须尝试逃至室内地点。血雨在几分钟后结束，天空在当晚余下时间转为阴云密布。血雨结束后，落下的雨水会恢复为普通的水。</p>\n<p><strong>解决这些显现：</strong>PC们可以通过在晨步桥点燃<em>长明灯</em>来终止这些库加普提影响所带来的诡异显现（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03lightthenigh00]{Light the Night}）。若PC们没有想起那首旧谣，你可以让他们从你选择的一名被救下的NPC处得知这首童谣。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Maze of Mist, Rain of Blood\">Maze of Mist, Rain of Blood</h2>\n<p>As the PCs travel down the game trail, the weather grows stranger. Mist rolls in through the trees, growing into a full-fledged fog by the time the PCs step out of the forest and onto a familiar riverside road, a mere 10 minutes after they left the clearing they awoke in.</p>\n<p>Up ahead, the sight of the Duyue River bridge through the unusual fog is a welcome sight, for this bridge confirms that the PCs have arrived at the easternmost edge of Willowshore. As they cross the bridge, though, the fog persists. Allow each PC to attempt a secret @Check[society|dc:13|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:13|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge. On a critical failure, a PC misremembers an old legend that claims summer fog brings summer sickness. On a success, a PC recalls an old nursery rhyme that suggests Willowshore’s <em>Eternal Lantern</em> has been extinguished. See the lantern poem below for this rhyme.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Lazy Adou took a break, and</p>\n  <p>did not light the lamp that day.</p>\n  <p>This proved to be a big mistake, for</p>\n  <p>then the ghosts came out to play!</p>\n  <p>Hazy mist and moon of blood,</p>\n  <p>all because he just gave up.</p>\n  <p>Lantern Poem</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>As long as Willowshore’s <em>Eternal Lantern</em> remains extinguished, day and night are more dangerous and unsettling. During the day, the town is constantly bathed in a thick fog known as mirage mist. The mist dissipates at night, but at the cost of crimson moonlight and blood rain bathing the land.</p>\n<p><strong>Mirage Mist:</strong> The eerie fog is thick enough to obscure visibility beyond a range of 500 feet. Creatures viewed from more than 100 feet away are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{Concealed}. In addition, the mist distorts peripheral vision, causing one to periodically notice strange shapes moving and shifting about at the limits of their vision. All vision-based Perception checks attempted within mirage mist suffer a –1 status penalty as a result, and all DCs for Survival checks to Sense Direction are increased by 5.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.ffY3ybPo0ZvpfCUL]{Mist Urban} @UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.2089R8LUFfxhJMM0]{Mist Nature}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-crimson-moon.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Crimson Moon\" alt=\"A Red moon Rises bathin a river and frest in red light\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-crimson-moon.webp')\" />\n\n<p><strong>Crimson Moon:</strong> At night, the mirage mist clears and the sky reverts to partially overcast. When the moon is glimpsed through the clouds, it shines with an eerie crimson hue. This effect has the emotion, fear, and mental traits. At the start of any hour a creature spends under this crimson moon, it must attempt a @Check[will|dc:15|traits:emotion,fear,mental] save to avoid having the value of its @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened} condition increase.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature reduces its moon-induced frightened condition by 1. If this reduces the value to 0, the creature is temporarily immune to the crimson moon’s effects for the rest of the night.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The creature’s moon-induced frightened condition doesn’t increase.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The creature’s frightened condition value increases by 1, to a maximum value of 4. This frightened condition persists until dawn, or until enough critical success results reduce the value to 0.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the condition’s value increases by 2.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macros / Ambience</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.DxD2BgVlVgehVnuO]{Enable Blood Moon} @UUID[Macro.Jz8MIw7gUsCW19TY]{Reset Willowshore} | @UUID[Macro.u7NLULMdAcyTWq1c]{Enable Rain} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.nezy4qHmtlstrXAe]{Rain}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Change the @UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{Willowshore} Scene lighting to crimson.</p>\n</section>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Sinister Animals</h1>\n  <p>The fact that Willowshore’s wildlife is unusually aggressive should concern any PC who succeeds at a secret @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:secret] or @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret] check (on a success, that PC realizes how unusual it is for creatures like giant centipedes to be so quickly aggressive and to avoid fleeing upon facing superior foes, especially during daylight hours), but the addition of their disturbing ability to speak reveals immediately that something supernatural is afoot. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[occultism|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge knows these animals are being influenced in some way by an evil spirit. These animals—along with many other aggressive animals encountered in the mindscape during this adventure—are physical manifestations of Kugaptee’s influence over the region. Their unusual intellect (they have Int +0 and can speak Common) and cruel, sadistic personalities are a side effect of the fiend’s increased presence in this cycle of the mindscape, but they otherwise have standard statistics for their kind.</p>\n</aside>\n<p><strong>Blood Rain:</strong> Every sunset as the crimson moon rises, attempt a @Check[flat|dc:14]. On a success, the cloud cover increases (this doesn’t negate the need to make hourly Will saves against the crimson moon), and at some point during the night (as decided by the GM), what appears to be blood rains down on Willowshore. This “blood” seemingly coats everything with a layer of gore. Any PC who witnesses the blood rain must immediately attempt a save against the effects of the crimson moon, taking a –4 circumstance penalty to the save if they’re out in the rain. A PC whose frightened condition increases as the result of this saving throw becomes fleeing for 1 minute and must attempt to escape to an indoor location. The blood rain ends after a few minutes, transitioning back to overcast skies for the remainder of the night. Fallen rain reverts to normal water once the blood rain ends.</p>\n<p><strong>Resolving the Manifestations:</strong> The PCs can stop these eerie manifestations of Kugaptee’s influence by lighting the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> at Dawnstep Bridge (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03lightthenigh00]{Light the Night}). If the PCs don’t recall the old rhyme, you can have them learn of the rhyme by a rescued NPC of your choice.</p>"
            },
            "Strange Aggression": {
              "name": "奇异侵略性 Strange Aggression",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">奇异的侵略性</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇周边的林地里不乏危险的掠食者，但在离镇子这么近的地方，这些威胁通常微乎其微。当PC们返回镇上——或者他们决定在空地上等上一段时间——附近矮丛环境中的一阵窸窣声引起了他们的注意。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/giant-centipede.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">奇异的侵略性</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.h319yBCL0AmUKXAB]{巨蜈蚣（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>苦迦菩提日益增长的影响导致柳岸腹地的野生动物变得异常好斗，并带有超自然的发声能力——PC们现在将会发现这一点。在他们听到窸窣声片刻之后，两只巨蜈蚣从矮丛环境中窜出。这些亮橙色的生物起初在发现PC们时会发出令人不安的嘶嘶声，但当它们疾冲上前发动攻击时，这些嘶声开始组成词语：“肉……血肉……骨头……手指……头发……皮肤……眼睛……”随着战斗推进，蜈蚣的低语逐渐变成简短的句子，显然它们正喘息着念出自己希望很快就能啃食的PC们的部位。</p>\n</section>\n<p>当战斗结束后，让PC们有机会解读这些巨蜈蚣采取的奇怪动作，详见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03mazeofmistra00#sinister-animals]{邪恶动物} 侧栏。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Strange Aggression</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The woodlands surrounding Willowshore have their share of dangerous predators, but this close to town, those threats are usually minimal. As the PCs head back to town—or if instead they decide to wait for a time in the clearing—the sound of something rustling in the nearby undergrowth attracts their attention.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/giant-centipede.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Strange Aggression</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 1</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.h319yBCL0AmUKXAB]{Giant Centipedes (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Kugaptee’s growing influence causes wildlife in the Willowshore hinterlands to grow unusually aggressive and supernaturally vocal, as the PCs now discover. A few moments after they hear the rustling, two giant centipedes scuttle out from the undergrowth. The bright orange creatures initially make unnerving hissing sounds upon spotting the PCs, but as they scurry forth to attack, these hisses begin forming words: “meat... flesh... bones... fingers... hair... skin... eyes...” As the fight progresses, the centipedes’ whispering grows into short sentences, making it apparent that they’re gasping out the parts of the PCs they hope to soon feed upon.</p>\n</section>\n<p>As the combat concludes, allow the PCs a chance to interpret the strange actions taken by the giant centipedes, as detailed in the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03mazeofmistra00#sinister-animals]{Sinister Animals} sidebar.</p>"
            },
            "The First Day of Summer": {
              "name": "夏日第一天 The First Day of Summer",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The First Day of Summer\">夏季的第一天</h1>\n<p>本次冒险假定PC们从森林空地向西旅行，越过杜月江大桥并沿道路进入柳岸镇，在接近城镇时会经过石蜘蛛和东侧瞭望塔。接下来的页面将这段旅程以一系列遭遇呈现；但如果你的玩家选择偏离这条预设路线，可按需使用@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow]{柳岸镇}的地志。你应尽量将他们本会从前四个遭遇中获得的信息（富攻击性的野生动物、诡异的迷雾与猩红之月、失踪的石蜘蛛，以及哈亥尔的故事）尽快融入他们前往荒野腹地的旅途中，以便PC们仍能对后续事件有所背景认识。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The First Day of Summer\">The First Day of Summer</h1>\n<p>This adventure assumes the PCs travel west from the forest clearing, over the Duyue River bridge and up the road into Willowshore, passing by the stone spider and the eastern watchtower as they approach town. This journey is presented on the following pages as a series of encounters, but if your players choose to diverge from this assumed path, use the gazetteer of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow]{Willowshore} as needed. You should strive to include the information they would’ve gained from the first four encounters (the aggressive wildlife, the strange mist and crimson moon, the missing stone spider, and Ha Hai-er’s tale) into their journey into the hinterlands as soon as possible so that the PCs still have some context for events to follow.</p>"
            },
            "Getting Started": {
              "name": "冒险开始 Getting Started",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">冒险开始</h1>\n<p>当你准备开始这个战役时，告诉玩家：在夏季的第一天醒来时，他们发现自己身处诡异的境况。前一晚的记忆随之浮现，他们记得在重现节最热闹的时刻，自己被镇民拖出城镇；他们仍戴着红色眼罩，睡在“绑匪”放置的稻草席卷里。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.Xe84RQtKEyZoQ1yp]{Woods}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>每年，重现节的组织者都会选择一个不同的地点，把“被绑走的人”丢在离镇子不远、却无法立刻看到文明踪迹的地方。允许PC尝试进行@Check[survival|dc:10]或@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:10]检定——任何成功者都会意识到：他们其实是在柳岸镇以东的一片空地醒来（柳岸镇地图上的区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w38woodedcle00]{W38}），而附近有一条兽径向西延伸，通往镇子方向。若没有PC尝试该检定，这条小径也很容易被注意到；它一路下坡，朝向河流的水声延伸，这一点足以暗示它很可能通往回家的路。</p>\n<p>今天早晨的天气符合神门初夏的典型：多云间晴，清晨空气带着爽利的凉意；到中午时，PC大概会觉得这股凉意会退去，转为更舒适、却不闷热的温度。随着时间推移，云层只会变得更加阴沉，不久便下起雨来。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>PC所知道的事</h1>\n  <p>如果你使用了<em>鬼季 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog22sogpgh]{《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》}</em>，玩家应当已经知道以下三个关键点。若没有，或你想提醒他们一些关键要素，请在开始这段冒险前确保他们知晓以下内容。</p>\n  <p><strong>什么是鬼季？</strong>鬼季是初夏的一段时期，此时幽魂之森的闹鬼、游魂与不死生物活动会增加。其原因尚不确定，但这些鬼魂经常引诱人们走向死亡。</p>\n  <p><strong>什么是重现节？</strong>在柳岸镇，人们会在春季最后一天、庆祝季节终结的宴会之后，重演“鬼魂”掳走居民的事件（“鬼魂”由戴纸面具的村民扮演）；随后镇民假装陷入集体恐慌，由指定的哭号者放声哀悼，而其他人则表演搜寻与营救行动。这场闹剧被认为能欺骗真正的鬼魂，让它们以为已有某个幽灵纠缠过此聚落，从而说服它们去寻找另一个更“开心”的村子施加苦难。PC记得自己扮演的是被掳者：他们必须整夜蒙着眼、裹在草席里，直到早晨被当年负责重现节的当地负责人用“赎金”把他们“赎回”。</p>\n  <p><strong>PC身上有什么物品？</strong>在林中过夜有风险，而PC提前得到时间做准备。他们目前带着自己所有物品，并与他们在创建角色期间已选择的任何伙伴同行。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>如果玩家还没介绍过自己的角色，给他们一个机会这么做。若PC选择了<em>《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》</em>中的背景，他们会自带理由解释自己为何会被选中在重现节中扮演“被掳者”，同时也可能与其他PC或柳岸镇有一些潜在联系。</p>\n<p>在PC聊了一会儿之后，他们会注意到有些不对劲。今年仪式的主要组织者——磨坊主乔春虎——说好会在日出时带着食物前来“赎回”PC，并带他们回家。这个步骤并非必需；它更像是一份早餐外送，用来感谢那些参与重演的人。PC知道即使没有这份赎金，他们也可以自行回到柳岸镇，就好像他们安全地“从绑匪手中逃脱”。然而，乔春虎的缺席很反常，因为这位磨坊主很少食言。</p>\n<p>如果PC打算返回镇子，记得询问每位PC使用何种探索行动。若他们决定在空地里再等一阵子，他们可以用诸如调查或侦测魔法等行动探索此地，查看是否有任何不对劲之处。无论他们怎么选，接下来的“奇异的攻击性”遭遇都会在此时发生。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">Getting Started</h1>\n<p>When you’re ready to start this campaign, inform the players that as they wake on the first day of summer, they do so in strange circumstances. Memories of the previous night return, and they can recall being dragged from town by townsfolk during the height of the Reenactment Festival, still wearing their red blindfolds and asleep in straw mat bundles placed by their “abductors.”</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.Xe84RQtKEyZoQ1yp]{Woods}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>Each year, the organizers of the Reenactment Festival choose a different place to drop off their abductees in a location not far from town, yet without any immediate line of sight to civilization. Allow the PCs to attempt @Check[survival|dc:10] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:10] checks—anyone who succeeds realizes that they’ve instead awoken in a clearing east of Willowshore (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w38woodedcle00]{W38} on the map of Willowshore), and that a nearby game trail leads west back toward town. If no PC attempts this check, the trail is easy to notice, and the fact that it leads downhill toward the sound of a river is enough to suggest that it likely leads back toward home.</p>\n<p>The weather this morning is typical for Shenmen in the early summer—partially overcast with a crisp early morning chill to the air that, by noon, the PCs might expect to give way to a more pleasant but not overbearing heat. As the day draws on, the clouds only grow more ominous, and rain begins to fall.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>What the PCs Know</h1>\n  <p>If you’re using the <em>Season of Ghosts @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog22sogpgh]{Player's Guide}</em>, the players should already know the following three key points. If not, or if you wish to remind them of some key elements, make sure they know the following before starting this adventure.</p>\n  <p><strong>What is the season of ghosts?</strong> The season of ghosts is a time during early summer when Specterwood sees an increase in hauntings, spirits, and undead. While the cause is uncertain, these ghosts often lure folks to their deaths.</p>\n  <p><strong>What is the Reenactment Festival?</strong> In Willowshore, following a feast to celebrate the end of the season on the last day of spring, the town reenacts people being snatched away by “ghosts” (played by villagers in paper masks); the townsfolk then pretend to plunge into collective panic as designated wailers mourn loudly, while others play out a search and rescue effort. This farce is believed to trick real ghosts into thinking that someone has already haunted the settlement and thus convince them to seek a happier village to inflict misery upon. The PCs recall playing the role of the abductees, who must spend the night blindfolded and wrapped in straw mats until they’re “ransomed” in the morning by the local in charge of that year’s Reenactment Festival.</p>\n  <p><strong>What items do the PCs have?</strong> Staying overnight in the woods is risky, and the PCs were given time to prepare in advance. They currently have all of their items and are accompanied by any companions they already selected during character creation.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Give the players a chance to introduce their characters if they haven’t done so already. If the PCs chose backgrounds from the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>, they’ll have built-in reasons why they were among those selected for the role of abductee for the Reenactment Festival, as well as some potential links to the other PCs or Willowshore.</p>\n<p>After the PCs talk for a bit, they notice something is amiss. The main organizer of the ritual this year, the miller Choe Chung-hu, said he would arrive by sunrise with food to “ransom” the PCs and lead them back home. This step isn’t essential; it’s more of a breakfast delivery to thank those who helped with the reenactment. The PCs know that they can go back to Willowshore without this ransom being delivered, as if they safely “escaped from their kidnappers.” However, Chung-hu’s absence is strange since the miller seldom goes back on his word.</p>\n<p>If the PCs head back to town, remember to ask each PC what Exploration Activity they use. If instead they decide to wait a while in the clearing, they can explore the location with activities such as Investigate or Detect Magic to check for anything out of place. Regardless of their choice, the “Strange Aggression” encounter that follows takes place at this time.</p>"
            },
            "To Light the Night": {
              "name": "点亮黑夜 To Light the Night",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"To Light the Night\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第1章：</span>\n  <span>点亮长夜</span>\n</h1>\n<p>在7223 ic年初冬时节，一位名叫马戈·凯的木材大亨在翻阅祖先的日记时发现了一些耐人寻味的内容——其中提到一片非同寻常的杉树林，据说隐藏在一座名为柳岸镇的偏远小镇附近。</p>\n<p>春季的第一周，凯带着一队手下前往柳岸镇，准备评估并调查一片地区——根据找回的日记记载，那片地方已超过一百年无人采伐。探险队抵达后发现那里是一片被藤蔓吞噬、闹鬼的废墟，但仍充满潜力。这地方能否被收复成一处旧伐木营地？正当他们开始规划时，废墟仅存的守护者之一——一头石蜘蛛守护兽——袭击了这群未来的伐木工。数人丧生后，马戈·凯击败了石蜘蛛，并决定队伍应向东撤退以休整并疗伤。他在沿海要塞卡拉海安顿下来，开始为更有组织的重建行动做准备，集结清理柳岸镇废墟并将其从闹鬼过往中夺回所需的物资、士兵与驱魔师。</p>\n<p>马戈·凯并不知道，他和手下在柳岸镇废墟中遭遇的闹鬼现象并非仅仅来自不安的亡灵。这些现象是灵性的回响与影响，源自一个“思维空间”中的柳岸镇——那处思维空间版的柳岸镇在115年前诞生，当时城镇总督试图（却失败了）施行一场复杂仪式，意在保护小镇免受名为苦迦菩提的古老恶魔的影响。那次失败导致柳岸镇所有人死亡，并使他们的灵魂被困在思维空间中。后来，柳岸镇的石蜘蛛守护灵被马戈·凯的人杀死，这一近期之死引发了一连串事件，可能会让马戈·凯将柳岸镇收为己用的目标变得不可能。</p>\n<p>在过去的岁月里，思维空间的年度循环在结束时会将一切重置回前一年夏季第一天，所有被困在思维空间中的人都会在床上再次醒来，对前一年发生的事毫无记忆。但在春季最后几天“丑可爱”死亡后，怪事发生了。由于失去了守护兽所提供的灵性庇护，苦迦菩提的影响增长得更快。它在柳岸腹地更深处的区域周围制造出一层幽魂外壳，在思维空间中显现为令人胆寒的“鬼打墙”。随着苦迦菩提从死亡般的沉睡中缓慢苏醒，这恶魔的念头以实体形态显现，让思维空间滋生出各种骇人的怪物。许多怪物在春季最后几天入侵柳岸镇并淹没了小镇，命源了镇民为即将到来的鬼季所做的准备，并摧毁了许多建筑。其中有三只生物尤为突出——一只贪吃的布索，名为辘肠；一只虚荣的一反木绵，名为灰屠；以及一只纵欲的辘轳首，名为莫·斗秋——它们成了这些显现怪物的头目，而它们横行霸道的领导正是小镇覆灭的关键。</p>\n<p>这场灾难后的几天里，思维空间回退到夏季第一天时，一切都永远改变了，因为这些源自苦迦菩提念头的新显现并不会随着思维空间其他部分一起重置。115年来第一次，柳岸镇的人民醒来时发现小镇已被怪物侵染、被暴行蹂躏——却对这些事如何发生毫无记忆。</p>\n<p>当循环重置时，“丑可爱”也再次活了过来，但这一次他被困在思维空间本身。石蜘蛛迅速行动，攻击并反击入侵的怪物。随着太阳升起，PC们在一处熟悉的林间空地醒来，同时带着与他们即将面对的现实相矛盾的前一夜记忆。此后他们的去向，可能会引向思维空间的毁灭与柳岸镇被困住的灵魂重返生命——也可能会引向他们真正的死亡，在一次被拖延许久的骨园之旅之后。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-attacked-by-centipedes.webp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"To Light the Night\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 1:</span>\n  <span>To Light the Night</span>\n</h1>\n<p>During the winter of early 7223 ic, a lumber baron named Mago Kai discovered something intriguing while looking back through his ancestor’s journals—mentions of a grove of incredible sugi trees said to be hidden near a remote town called Willowshore.</p>\n<p>During the first week of spring, Kai and a group of his agents traveled to Willowshore, ready to appraise and investigate a region that, according to the recovered journals, hadn’t been harvested in well over a hundred years. The expedition arrived to find an overgrown and haunted ruin, but it was still full of potential. Could the place be reclaimed as a lumber camp? As they began planning, one of the ruin’s remaining guardians—a stone spider guardian beast—attacked the group of prospective loggers. Several people perished before Mago Kai defeated the stone spider, and he decided the group should retreat east to recuperate after their losses. He settled into the coastal fortress of Karahai and began to prepare for a more organized reconstruction effort, gathering the supplies, soldiers, and exorcists needed to cleanse Willowshore’s ruins and reclaim it from its haunted past.</p>\n<p>Unbeknownst to Mago Kai, the haunting effects he and his people experienced in the ruins of Willowshore were from more than merely unquiet spirits. These phenomena were the spiritual echoes and influences that reached out from within a mindscape version of Willowshore that came into existence 115 years before, when the city’s governor attempted (and failed) to perform a complex ritual meant to protect the town from the influence of an ancient fiend named Kugaptee. That failure resulted in the deaths of everyone in Willowshore, and left their souls trapped in a mindscape. The more recent death of the town’s stone spider guardian spirit at the hands of Mago Kai’s people set into motion a series of events that might make Mago Kai’s goal of reclaiming Willowshore for his own use impossible.</p>\n<p>In previous years, the end of the mindscape’s annual cycle reset everything back to the previous year’s first day of summer, and all those trapped within the mindscape woke again in their beds with no memories of the previous year’s events. But with Ugly Cute’s death during the final days of spring, something strange happened. Without the spiritual protection afforded by the guardian beast, Kugaptee’s influence grew even more quickly. It created a ghostly shell around the deeper regions of Willowshore’s hinterlands, manifesting in the mindscape as a frightening “Wall of Ghosts.” As Kugaptee slowly woke from his death slumber, the fiend’s thoughts manifested in physical form, infesting the mindscape with all manner of monstrous creatures. Many of these monsters invaded Willowshore and overran the town in the final days of spring, disrupting the townsfolk’s preparations for the upcoming season of ghosts and devastating many of the town’s structures. Three of these creatures in particular—a gluttonous buso named Gurglegut, a vain ittan-momen named Gray Butcher, and a hedonistic rokurokubi named Mo Douqiu—became ringleaders for these manifested monstrosities, and their bullying leadership proved key to the town’s fall.</p>\n<p>When the mindscape reverted back to the first day of summer a few days after this catastrophe, things had changed forever, for these new manifestations born from Kugaptee’s thoughts didn’t reset with the rest of the mindscape. For the first time in 115 years, the people of Willowshore woke to a town infested with monsters and savaged by mayhem—but without any memories of how these events had come to pass.</p>\n<p>Ugly Cute found himself alive once again when the cycle reset, but this time he was trapped in the mindscape itself. The stone spider quickly went into action, attacking and fighting back against the invading monsters. With the rising of the sun, the PCs awaken in a familiar forest clearing along with memories of the previous night that are at odds with the reality they shall soon face. Where they go from here could lead to the mindscape’s destruction and the return of Willowshore’s trapped souls to life—or to their true deaths after a long-delayed trip to the Boneyard.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 1.2: Reclaiming Willowshire": {
          "name": "第一幕 1.2：夺回柳郡 Act 1.2: Reclaiming Willowshire",
          "pages": {
            "Bathhouse Foyer": {
              "name": "澡堂前厅 Bathhouse Foyer",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B13. Bathhouse Foyer\">B13. 浴场门厅</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>乐天河童的门厅和往常一样温馨朴素，不过地面潮湿，仿佛刚拖过。空气中弥漫着某种消毒剂那种明显的、类似碱液的气味。</p>\n</div>\n<p>当一群五只河童浑身沾满马匹的血肉残渣，若无其事地走进这家浴场来清洗时，这家浴场疑病症的主人德-格就知道，最好把这些怪物访客当作受尊敬的客人来招待。不过，在他们安顿进浴池之后，他立刻着手清理他们血淋淋的脚印，并在藏进更衣室（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b14bathhouse00]{B14}）之前给门厅消毒。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B13. Bathhouse Foyer\">B13. Bathhouse Foyer</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The Happy Kappa’s foyer is as homely as it’s always been, though the floor is damp as if recently mopped. A distinct lye-like smell of some disinfectant hangs in the air.</p>\n</div>\n<p>When a group of five kappas, covered in horse-gore, casually strolled into this bathhouse to clean up, the bathhouse’s hypochondriac owner, De-ge knew it was best to treat the monstrous visitors as respected guests. Once they were settled into the baths, though, he immediately set about cleaning their bloody footprints and disinfecting the foyer before hiding in the locker room (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b14bathhouse00]{B14}).</p>"
            },
            "Backyard Storage": {
              "name": "后院储物间 Backyard Storage",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B12. Backyard Storage\">B12. 后院储藏间</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间后院储藏间装着铸铁门，建得几乎像银行金库一样，只开了一个圆形小窗，让外面的空气能流进来。后院的小菜园里黄瓜长得格外茂盛。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>纳多娅和三见家其余成员奉命待在这里，除非灰屠或吉金斯来叫他们。PC们见到这家人时，纳多娅会问@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11}区域里的吉金斯是否还在，以及尤莉和“另一个年轻人”是否安全。如果PC们还没清理该区域，她会请他们去清理并豁免那两人。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.glTZmc0Dbilj1yeH]{纳多娅的感谢} <br />\n  如果@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b10sanmihous00]{B10}区域的小魔怪（特征）已被赶走，纳多娅会出于感激赠予PC们一枚<em>泪天使垂饰</em>\n  护符。此外，后院还有一排新鲜黄瓜——在纳多娅允许下，PC们想拿多少都可以。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们护送三见一家安全穿过晨步桥，他们将获得20 XP，并在南岸获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B12. Backyard Storage\">B12. Backyard Storage</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Built almost like a bank vault with its cast-iron doors, this backyard storage has only a single round window that allows in air from the outside. The small vegetable garden in the backyard has an abundance of cucumbers.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Nadoya and the rest of the Sanmi family have been ordered to stay here unless Gray Butcher or the jinkins call on them. When the PCs meet the family, Nadoya asks if the jinkins in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11} are still there and whether Yuli and “the other young man” are safe. If the PCs haven’t cleared the area, she asks them to do so and save the two.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.glTZmc0Dbilj1yeH]{Nadoya's Thanks} <br />\n  If the gremlins from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b10sanmihous00]{B10} have been evicted, Nadoya gives the PCs a <em>crying angel pendant</em>\n  talisman in gratitude. Out in the backyard, there’s also a row of fresh cucumbers—the PCs can take as many as they want with Nadoya’s permission.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> The PCs gain 20 XP and 1 Reputation Point with Southbank if they see the Sanmi family to safety past the Dawnstep Bridge.</p>"
            },
            "Mudwall House": {
              "name": "泥墙屋 Mudwall House",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B11. 泥墙屋</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这栋房子有一层双层泥墙，用以调节热度、寒冷与声响——然而要压住屋内那群尖细嗓音的喧闹，它就力有未逮了。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>这里曾是寡妇三美奈户弥的家，如今却被小魔怪（特征）侵占。一群六只金金强迫奈户弥和三美家大多数人住进后院的储藏室（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b12backyards00]{B12}），同时指定<strong>三美裕里</strong>（富有创意的年轻女性人类村民）与<strong>胡乐龙</strong>（保护欲强的年轻男性人类村民）做它们的贴身侍从。这对秘密恋人在PC到来前不久拟定了反抗计划：怂恿看守们越喝越醉。如今，这里的金金都被灌下的米酒灌得酩酊大醉。裕里与乐龙原本希望小魔怪会昏睡过去，好让他们有机会逃走（或者说，私奔），但这份希望正在减退——这些小魔怪越喝越醉，反倒越发闹腾。尤其有两只金金在用一堆偷来的珠宝玩“接抛”游戏（更准确地说，是“丢、掉、再扑上去捡回来”的游戏）。</p>\n<p>当PC进入时，他们会发现金金把屋里搞得一团糟，而裕里与乐龙蜷缩在角落瑟瑟发抖。醉醺醺的金金把PC误认作鬼（oni），一见面就立刻争相博取队伍注意，高声喊道：“哦哦！鬼来了！”然后竭尽所能把破坏行为升级，一边喊“看我！”或“看这个！”</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/very-drunken-jinkin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">泥墙屋</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.RvxqKciwytdawfpb]{醉得不省人事的金金（6）} @UUID[Actor.i5Ygd16VV8NqZ7Na]{三美裕里} @UUID[Actor.JWT8JfQoCEodLmL3]{胡乐龙}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>由于醉酒，所有金金都带有弱化的生物调整。若一名角色成功通过一次 @Check[intimidation|dc:17] 检定，便可迫使六只金金全都逃离房屋。否则，让金金停止破坏此地的唯一方法，就是要么等它们醉倒（但这需要足够长的时间，其中一只会点燃房屋，从而把室内彻底烧毁），要么攻击它们。一旦战斗开始，醉醺醺的金金会欢快地嚎叫，并且愚蠢地战至死方休。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>命运多舛的恋人：</strong>若醉酒的金金被击败，乐龙会询问PC是否愿意让他拿走小魔怪刚才在玩的一条项链。若PC追问缘由，他会笨拙地撒谎，声称自己想让他的叔叔（卫队长郑鹏）或胡太婆来理清谁才是合法主人。PC可以通过一次成功的 @Check[diplomacy|dc:13] 或 @Check[intimidation|dc:13] 检定逼他说出真相：他想弄到资金来支援他与恋人私奔。他拒绝透露恋人是裕里，不过PC可能早已从区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b10sanmihous00]{B10} 的信件中得知（任何对乐龙或裕里进行察言观色并成功通过 @Check[perception|dc:13|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] 检定的人也会知道）。</p>\n<p>这段恋情也解释了乐龙为何在镇中心：怪物袭击时他正偷偷来访，结果被困在此处。无论是否拿到资金，裕里与乐龙都坚定要逃走，希望家人会以为他们在入侵中丧生。PC要阻止还是放任这对年轻人私奔，由他们决定；但如果让他们逃走，PC之后可以在荒野的猎户小屋与他们遭遇（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d6huntershut00]{D6}）。裕里会记得取回区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b10sanmihous00]{B10} 的信件，或在离开前请PC把往来书信还给他们。</p>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.DvjLaZbukPhBGGoh]{被盗珠宝} <br />\n  在这些被盗珠宝中，有一名PC发现了一条属于自己家族、很容易辨认的项链，并可将其取回。这条项链价值10 gp，但金金在醉到忘了怎么摆弄之前对它下了诅咒。只要佩戴或携带这条项链，就会让人散发腐烂大蒜的恶臭，使交涉与隐匿检定承受–1物品减值。\n</p>\n<p>其余被盗珠宝总价值75 gp，但这两打首饰分别属于柳岸镇的不同居民。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC击败金金或以常规方式将其驱逐后，给予XP奖励，最高总计80 XP，以反映它们造成的威胁较小。若PC采取措施归还被盗珠宝，他们获得北岭人阵营的1点声望点数。若PC积极鼓励、甚至协助这对年轻人私奔，他们失去南岸阵营的1点声望点数；并且当三美奈户弥得知这段关系后，在 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章} 开始时，她的态度会自动变为不友善。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B11. Mudwall House</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This house has a double-layered mud wall that regulates heat, cold, and sound—though it isn’t up to the task of dampening the rabble of high-pitched voices within.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Once home to the widowed Nadoya Sanmi, this house is now infested with gremlins. A group of six jinkins forced Nadoya and most of the Sanmi family to live in the backyard storage room (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b12backyards00]{B12}) while designating <strong>Yuli Sanmi</strong> (creative female human young villager) and <strong>Hu Lelong</strong> (protective male human young villager) to be their personal attendants. The two secret lovers hatched a plan shortly before the PCs arrive to fight back against their captors by encouraging them to get increasingly drunk, and now the jinkins here are quite blasted on the rice wine they’ve been plied with. Yuli and Lelong’s hopes that the gremlins would pass out and allow them the chance to escape (or rather, elope) are diminishing, for the gremlins have only grown rowdier as they got drunker. Two jinkins in particular are playing a game of catch with a collection of stolen jewelry (more accurately, a game of “toss, drop, and then scramble to pick back up”).</p>\n<p>As the PCs enter, they find the jinkins making a mess of the place while Yuli and Lelong cower in a corner. The drunken jinkins mistake the PCs for oni when they arrive and immediately begin to vie for the attention of the party, crying out, “Ooh! The oni are here!” and then doing their best to up their destructive antics, crying out “Look at me!” or “Watch this!”</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/very-drunken-jinkin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Mudwall House</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.RvxqKciwytdawfpb]{Very Drunken Jinkins (6)} @UUID[Actor.i5Ygd16VV8NqZ7Na]{Yuli Sanmi} @UUID[Actor.JWT8JfQoCEodLmL3]{Hu Lelong}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The jinkins all have the weak creature adjustments as a result of their drunkenness. A character who succeeds at a @Check[intimidation|dc:17] check compels all six jinkins to flee the house. Otherwise, the only way to get the jinkins to stop wrecking the place is to either wait for them to pass out (which will take long enough for one of them to light the place on fire, thereby destroying the interior completely) or to attack them. Once a fight starts, the drunk jinkins howl in delight and, foolishly, fight to the death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Star-Crossed Lovers:</strong> If the drunken jinkins are defeated, Lelong asks if the PCs would let him take one of the necklaces the gremlins were playing with. If the PCs inquires why, he clumsily lies, claiming that he wants to let his uncle (guard captain Zheng Peng) or Granny Hu sort out who the rightful owner is. The PCs can press the truth of out him with a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:13] or @Check[intimidation|dc:13] check: he wants funds to support an elopement for himself and his lover. He refuses to reveal Yuli is the lover, though the PCs might already know from the letters in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b10sanmihous00]{B10} (as will anyone who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:13|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] check to Sense Motive with either Lelong or Yuli).</p>\n<p>This romance also explains why Lelong is downtown: he was secretly visiting when monsters attacked, trapping him here. Regardless of whether they receive the funds, Yuli and Lelong are steadfast about running away, hoping their families will think they died during the invasion. Whether the PCs stop or allow the young couple to elope is up to them, but if they’re allowed to run away, the PCs can encounter them later at the Hunter’s Hut in the hinterlands (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d6huntershut00]{D6}). Yuli remembers to retrieve the letters from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b10sanmihous00]{B10} or asks the PCs to return the correspondences to them before they leave.</p>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.DvjLaZbukPhBGGoh]{Stolen Jewelry} <br />\n  Among the stolen jewelry, one of the PCs discovers a recognizable necklace that belongs to their family, and they can reclaim it. This necklace is worth 10 gp, but the jinkins cursed it before they got too drunk to remember how to Tinker. As long as the necklace is worn or carried, it makes a person stink of rotting garlic, imparting a –1 item penalty to Diplomacy and Stealth checks.\n</p>\n<p>The rest of the stolen jewelry is worth a total of 75 gp, but these two dozen pieces belong to various citizens of Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs XP for defeating the jinkins or chasing them off normally, to a maximum total of 80 XP to account for the lesser threat they posed. If the PCs take steps to return the stolen jewelry, they gain 1 Reputation Point with Northridge. If the PCs actively encouraged or even aided the young couple in their elopement, they lose 1 Reputation Point with Southbank, and Nadoya’s attitude automatically becomes unfriendly at the start of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3} as she finds out about the relationship.</p>"
            },
            "Sanmi Household": {
              "name": "桑米家族 Sanmi Household",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B10. Sanmi Household\">B10. 三美家宅</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这处家庭住宅几乎所有值钱的东西都被彻底洗劫一空，从他们所有的炊具到古董抽屉里存放的衣物或贵重物品，无一幸免。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  如果PC在此房间进行搜寻并在一次@Check[perception|dc:20|traits:secret,action:search|name:Search]检定中成功，他们会发现一叠信件藏在梳妆台抽屉下方的夹层里（@UUID[Actor.sBfmm8I2Cm470xIl]{Hidden Compartment}）。阅读这些信件会揭示三美家与胡家年轻一代之间一段秘密且日渐加深的关系：三美裕里与胡乐龙。\n</p>\n<p>一旦PC发现这些便条，允许他们尝试进行一次@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定或@Check[society|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识：极为传统的三美家不会赞同这段关系。这些便条可能会在解决区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11}中的局势时派上用场。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B10. Sanmi Household\">B10. Sanmi Household</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This family home has been thoroughly robbed of nearly everything of worth, from all their cookware to whatever clothing or valuables they had in their antique drawers.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  If the PCs Search this room and succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:secret,action:search|name:Search] check, they discover a stack of letters hidden in a compartment beneath a dresser drawer (@UUID[Actor.sBfmm8I2Cm470xIl]{Hidden Compartment}). Reading the letters reveals a secret and blossoming relationship between the youngest generation of the Sanmi and Hu families, Yuli Sanmi and Hu Lelong.\n</p>\n<p>Once the PCs discover these notes, allow them to attempt a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check or @Check[society|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge that the highly traditional Sanmi family wouldn’t approve of this relationship. These notes might prove useful in resolving the situation in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11}.</p>"
            },
            "Treesparrow’s Rest": {
              "name": "树雀居 Treesparrow’s Rest",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B9. Treesparrow’s Rest\">B9. 树雀居</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间店铺里的米、黍米或荞麦的麻袋与箱子都没有受损。架子上那些正在发酵的豆酱、米酒或腌菜的陶罐与瓶子也同样完好无损、未被动过。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这家粮店的正门没有上锁。PC可以用这里进行一次10分钟的休息（可能会进行一次@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.qc0VsZ0UesnurUUB]{小憩一刻}行动）；不过，如果他们停留超过一小时，就有可能遭遇一名从区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11}穿过后院游荡过来的金奇人，它正四处寻找可以破坏的东西。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B9. Treesparrow’s Rest\">B9. Treesparrow’s Rest</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>None of the sacks or chests of rice, millet, or buckwheat in this storefront have been damaged. The pots and vases of fermenting bean paste, rice wine, or pickled vegetables on the shelves also remain untouched.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The front doors of the grain shop are unlocked. The PCs can use this place to take a 10-minute rest (potentially taking a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.qc0VsZ0UesnurUUB]{Take a Breather} activity), though if they stay longer than an hour, they risk facing a jinkin who wanders over from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11} through the backyard on the hunt for something to ruin.</p>"
            },
            "Infested Stables": {
              "name": "虫害马厩 Infested Stables",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B8. 受虫害侵扰的马厩</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低级1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>内脏与腐肉的恶臭凝滞不散。里面躺着十来匹马。大多死时双眼圆睁，仿佛仍在分担它们生命最后时刻的痛苦。</p>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/cockroach-swarm.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">受虫害侵扰的马厩</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低级1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.JNWxfQmsosE4fWpK]{蟑螂虫群}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>一群蟑螂把家安在尸体被剖开的空腔里。它们一旦在马厩里侦测到生物，便会聚成虫群并立刻发动攻击。尽管这群虫群在点亮<em>长明灯</em>后会失去其残酷的群体心智（以及说话的能力），它仍旧饥肠辘辘，会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B8. Infested Stables</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The smell of offal and rotten meat stagnates. Inside lay a dozen horses. Most died with their eyes wide open, sharing the pain of their last moments.</p>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/cockroach-swarm.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Infested Stables</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.JNWxfQmsosE4fWpK]{Cockroach Swarm}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A swarm of cockroaches made their home inside the corpses’ eviscerated cavities. They converge into a swarm and attack as soon as they detect a creature in the stables. While this swarm loses its cruel hive mind (along with the ability to speak) once the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is lit, it remains ravenous and fights to the death.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Training Yard": {
              "name": "训练场 Training Yard",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B7. Training Yard\">B7. 训练场</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一串带血的脚印从马厩延伸出来，穿过沙地训练场的北门。</p>\n</div>\n<p>如果PC以一次成功的@Check[survival|dc:9|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]检定追踪这条踪迹，他们最终会到达乐天河童（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b15mostlyhap00]{B15}），河童们正在愉快地泡澡。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B7. Training Yard\">B7. Training Yard</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A trail of bloody prints extends from the stables out through the northern gates of the sandy training yard.</p>\n</div>\n<p>If the PCs Track this trail with a successful @Check[survival|dc:9|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] check, they end up at the Happy Kappa (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b15mostlyhap00]{B15}), where the kappas are enjoying a good bath.</p>"
            },
            "Armory": {
              "name": "军械库 Armory",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B6. Armory\">B6. 军械库</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>通往该区域的门被牢牢锁住。没有任何缝隙或窗户可以窥视内部。</p>\n</div>\n<p>军械库门上的锁质量上乘，需要进行五次成功的 @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] 检定才能开锁，但也可以用藏匿在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b4prison000000]{B4} 的钥匙把门打开。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.qFIXf0T7EUPSL2rm]{Armory} <br />\n  这座军械库内有各十二套标准的鳞甲和铆钉皮甲，以及10把弩、一桶100支弩矢、十二把匕首、六根木棒和四根短棒。除这些普通物品外，这里的补给还包括四个次等寒霜瓶、一把冷铁匕首、一面冷铁小圆盾、一把银制短剑，以及一把<em>+1 矛</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B6. Armory\">B6. Armory</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The doors to this area are locked tight. There are no cracks or windows to peek inside.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The locks on the door to the armory are of good quality, which requires five successful @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock, but the doors can also be unlocked by the key hidden in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b4prison000000]{B4}.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.qFIXf0T7EUPSL2rm]{Armory} <br />\n  This armory contains a dozen standard suits of scale mail and studded leather armor each, along with 10 crossbows, a barrel of 100 bolts, a dozen daggers, six clubs, and four saps. In addition to these mundane items, the supplies here include four lesser frost vials, a cold iron dagger, a cold iron buckler, a silver shortsword, and a <em>+1 spear</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Outdoor Prison Cell": {
              "name": "户外监牢囚室 Outdoor Prison Cell",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B5. Outdoor Prison Cell\">B5. 户外牢房</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这个竹笼用来关押犯下轻罪的人。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>四名村民被扔在这里“悔过”，否则就有被送去茶馆的风险——这是他们可以与PC们分享的情报。PC们可以通过以下方式解救这些村民：以一次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:22|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]检定来破拆笼子、强行打开竹笼；或直接把笼子砸开（AC 16，硬度 5，HP 20）。另外，他们也可以使用来自区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b4prison000000]{B4}的钥匙，打开铁制笼门的锁。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.ZkBlrAL6nOMVjuH2]{被囚禁的村民（4名）}</span>\n    <span>生物 –1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人形</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们救出囚犯并护送他们到安全地点，给予PC们20 XP以及在南岸的1点声望点数。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B5. Outdoor Prison Cell\">B5. Outdoor Prison Cell</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This bamboo cage serves as a holding cell for those who commit petty crimes.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Four villagers have been thrown in here to “repent” or risk being sent to the teahouse, a piece of information they can share with the PCs. The PCs can free these villagers by either breaking through the bamboo with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:22|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check to Force Open the cage or by smashing the cage open (AC 16, Hardness 5, HP 20). Alternately, they can unlock the iron cage door using the keys from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b4prison000000]{B4}.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.ZkBlrAL6nOMVjuH2]{Imprisoned Villagers (4)}</span>\n    <span>Creature –1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs rescue the prisoners and escort them to safety, grant the PCs 20 XP and 1 Reputation Point with Southbank.</p>"
            },
            "Prison": {
              "name": "监狱 Prison",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B4. Prison\">B4. 监狱</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间阴暗的房间里设有柳岸镇的牢房。这里共有七间牢房，装着铁栏杆，砌着砖墙。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>怪物入侵时，10名守卫被俘并被关进这里的七间牢房里；守卫队长郑鹏被单独锁在最东北的一间牢房中。每间牢房都有一把普通质量的锁（进行四次 @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] 成功即可开锁），但郑鹏预先藏好的牢房与军械库备用钥匙的应急计划终于派上了用场。PC到来时，他会呼喊他们，并告知牢房的一套备用钥匙藏在房间西南角一块松动的砖头下面。他请求PC取回钥匙，立刻释放他和其他守卫。若没有他的帮助，PC在此房间内进行搜寻时，成功通过一次 @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 检定即可发现藏起来的钥匙。</p>\n<p>郑鹏描述说，有一个看起来像人类的身影——一个光头、尖牙、披着兜帽斗篷的男子，而且他的脖子似乎能旋转到超乎常理的程度——与数个吉金一同组织了对营房的攻击。他不知道那名男子和他的小魔怪（特征）在袭击之后去了哪里。</p>\n<p>在恢复之前，郑鹏和他的守卫们都因折磨而处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏} 状态，生命值为1，并陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{力竭 3}；他们也都没有武器与护甲。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.dMbrraAblnkaazSJ]{郑鹏}</span>\n    <span>生物 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.xOHpHLI3Cb5R8xcS]{城镇守卫（10）}</span>\n    <span>生物 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.HiAo9BtbmXPhEnfU]{角落} @UUID[Actor.YsV46C0wpDNnFaQS]{郑鹏的钥匙} <br />\n  郑鹏会把军械库钥匙交给PC，并邀请他们从房间里取走任何他们需要的东西，以帮助他们解放市中心的行动。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC救出守卫，他们获得40 XP，并获得与北岭人的1点声望点数。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B4. Prison\">B4. Prison</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This dingy room is where Willowshore’s prison cells are located. The seven cells have iron bars and brick walls.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When the monsters invaded, 10 guards were captured and thrown into the seven cells here, with guard Captain Zheng Peng, locked away in the northeastern-most cell on his own. While each of the cells has a lock of average quality (four @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] successes can Pick the Lock), Zheng Peng’s contingency plan of hiding backup keys to the cells and armory finally pays off. When the PCs arrive, he calls over to them and informs them that a spare set of keys for the cells are hidden under a loose brick in the southwest corner of the room. He asks the PCs to retrieve the keys and release him and the other guards at once. Without his aid, a PC who Searches this room can discover the hidden keys with a successful @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check.</p>\n<p>Zheng Peng describes how one human-looking figure—a bald man with sharp teeth who wore a hooded cloak and whose neck seemed capable of rotating more than it should—organized the attack on the barracks along with several jinkins. He’s unaware of where the man and his gremlins headed after the attack.</p>\n<p>Until they recover, Zheng Peng and his guards are all @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued}, at 1 Hit Point, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 3} from their torments; they’re also all unarmed and unarmored.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.dMbrraAblnkaazSJ]{Zheng Peng}</span>\n    <span>Creature 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.xOHpHLI3Cb5R8xcS]{Town Guards (10)}</span>\n    <span>Creature 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.HiAo9BtbmXPhEnfU]{Corner} @UUID[Actor.YsV46C0wpDNnFaQS]{Zheng's Key} <br />\n  Zheng gives the PCs the armory key and invites them to take whatever they need from the room to aid them in their attempt to liberate downtown.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> The PCs gain 40 XP and 1 Reputation Point with Northridge if they rescue the guards.</p>"
            },
            "Guard House Courtyard": {
              "name": "卫兵房庭院 Guard House Courtyard",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B3. Guard House Courtyard\">B3. 警卫房庭院</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这座下沉式的小庭院从上方看被一片盛开的紫藤花架遮蔽，难以察觉。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这座庭院过去是警卫们放松休息的地方，不过许多人都指出，他们其实更希望这片空间能有更实际的用途。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B3. Guard House Courtyard\">B3. Guard House Courtyard</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This small sunken courtyard is hidden from above by a canopy of wisteria in full bloom.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This courtyard used to be a place for guards to relax, though many have pointed out how they would much rather have a practical use for the space.</p>"
            },
            "Imperial Guard Office": {
              "name": "帝国卫队办公室 Imperial Guard Office",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B2. Imperial Guard Office\">B2. 帝国卫队办公室</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间办公室看起来像是被飓风扫荡过一般，文件散落得满屋都是。房间里几乎没剩下什么家具。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这间办公室里的家具被用来在晨步桥上搭建辘肠的王座，只留下一个摇摇欲坠的书架、一张桌子，以及几把破损的椅子；而犯罪记录如今散落得满地都是。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B2. Imperial Guard Office\">B2. Imperial Guard Office</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The office looks like a hurricane has been through it, with documents strewn about the room. Very few furnishings remain in the room at all.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The furniture from this office was used to build Gurglegut’s throne on Dawnstep Bridge, leaving only one flimsy bookshelf, a desk, and a couple of broken chairs behind among the criminal records now scattered all over the floor.</p>"
            },
            "Empty Lot": {
              "name": "空地 Empty Lot",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B1. Empty Lot\">B1. 空地</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>就在昨天还曾是市中心明珠的总督府邸，如今已消失无踪。这片空地上唯一能证明这里曾有一座建筑的线索，是那两尊曾守卫府邸入口的石狮守卫。它们都已被涂毁并受损。</p>\n</div>\n<p>何总督与他的整座府邸一起，被困在一个平行的思维空间中。每当柳岸镇的思维空间重置，镇民们就不得不一次又一次地面对他们失踪的领袖，以及他消失的府邸被发现这一事实。关于这场谜团给城镇带来的更多后续影响，见第一幕开头 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B1. Empty Lot\">B1. Empty Lot</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The Governor’s Manor, just yesterday the crowning jewel of downtown, has vanished. The only indication that there was once a building in this empty lot are the two guardian stone lions that once guarded the entrance of the manor. Both have been defaced and damaged.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Governor Heh became trapped in a parallel mindscape, along with his entire manor. Each time Willowshore’s mindscape resets, the townspeople must contend all over again with the discovery of their missing leader and his vanished manor. See the start of Act 1, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3} for a few additional repercussions to the town in the wake of this mystery.</p>"
            },
            "Downtown Locations": {
              "name": "市中心地点 Downtown Locations",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Downtown Locations\">镇区地点</h2>\n<p>已提供柳岸镇镇区（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w19downtownw00]{W19}）的一般细节，但那些信息对应的是更安全的时期下的该区域。目前，镇区的街道空无一人。暴力的痕迹随处可见——街道与墙上溅着血迹，排水沟里有破损的武器，还有被砸烂的门窗。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.AV28Lyw8ARMP1tny]{被占据的柳岸镇}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>镇区地图（见封面内侧）上的许多地点缺少数字编码。这些未标注的建筑要么是空置民居、废弃店铺，要么是部分完工的建筑结构。它们可以为PC提供藏身处或庇护所。如果你的一位玩家选择了一栋镇区建筑作为他们的家，那么在与该玩家确定哪栋建筑属于他们之后，使用 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03returninghom00]{回家} 来解决那个遭遇。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Downtown Locations\">Downtown Locations</h2>\n<p>General details on downtown Willowshore (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w19downtownw00]{W19}) are provided, but that information relates to the area during safer times. Currently, the streets of downtown are empty. Evidence of violence lies everywhere—splashes of blood on the streets and walls, broken weapons in gutters, and smashed doors and windows.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.AV28Lyw8ARMP1tny]{Occupied Willowshore}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>Many of the locations on the map of downtown (see inside front cover) lack numerical codes. These unlabeled buildings are either empty homes, abandoned shops, or partially completed structures. They can provide the PCs with hiding spots or shelter. If one of your players has selected a downtown building as their home, then use @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03returninghom00]{Returning Home} to resolve that encounter after working with that player to determine which building is theirs.</p>"
            },
            "Liberating Downtown": {
              "name": "解放市中心 Liberating Downtown",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Liberating Downtown\">解放镇区</h1>\n<p>无论PC与谁结盟，请求都是一样的——必须解放柳岸镇镇区。PC很可能已经击败了三个怪物头目中的一个（辘肠，队伍里的“打手”），但另外两个（灰屠和莫都求）牢牢盘踞在镇区，击败他们会更困难。</p>\n<p>随着辘肠被击败、<em>长明灯</em>被点亮，灰屠与莫都求意识到他们对柳岸镇的掌控已变得岌岌可危。灰屠开始在镇区街道上巡逻，PC随时都可能与其发生遭遇。要对付莫都求（他是怪物们的幕后主使），PC必须潜入他选作堡垒的那栋建筑——已成废墟的青天茶馆。</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.ZKqa4lSnhV2XmtnH]{赞助人的支援} <br />\n  无论PC与胡太婆还是老松木结盟，他们的赞助人都不会在缺乏支援的情况下把他们派往镇区。当PC在处理@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh]{第1章}中的遭遇时，他们的赞助人收集了一批补给：十瓶<em>下等治疗药水</em>与八枚<em>潜能水晶</em>护符，并将这些物品交给PC，供他们自行决定如何使用。\n</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Liberating Downtown\">Liberating Downtown</h1>\n<p>Whomever the PCs ally with, the request is the same—downtown Willowshore must be liberated. It’s likely that the PCs have already defeated one of the three monster ringleaders (Gurglegut, the “muscle” of the group), but the other two (Gray Butcher and Mo Douqiu) are firmly ensconced in downtown and will be more difficult to defeat.</p>\n<p>With Gurglegut defeated and the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> lit, Gray Butcher and Mo Douqiu realize that their grip on Willowshore has grown tenuous. Gray Butcher takes to patrolling downtown’s streets, and the PCs could encounter them at any time. To confront Mo Douqiu (who serves as the mastermind of the monsters), the PCs must infiltrate the building he has chosen as his fortress—the ruined Cerulean Teahouse.</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.ZKqa4lSnhV2XmtnH]{Patron's Support} <br />\n  Regardless of whether the PCs ally with Granny Hu or Old Matsuki, their patron doesn’t send them into downtown without support. While the PCs were handling the encounters in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh]{Chapter 1}, their patron gathered up a supply of ten\n  <em>minor healing potions</em> and eight <em>potency crystal</em> talismans and delivers the items to the PCs for them to use as they see fit.\n</p>"
            },
            "Reclaiming Willowshire": {
              "name": "夺回柳郡 Reclaiming Willowshire",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Reclaiming Willowshire\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第2章：</span>\n  <span>收复柳岸镇</span>\n</h1>\n<p>一旦<em>长明灯</em>被点亮，那些诡异的超自然迷雾与月光被驱散，柳岸镇大部分地区的怪物与险患也随之平息。一直躲在家中或聚集在安全地带的市民们小心翼翼地现身，但柳岸镇的人民仍然惊惧。此前从未发生过类似的事，镇上的领袖们忙得不可开交，竭力让市民感到舒适、安全与安定。不过，镇上仍有一处显著区域处于危险之中：柳岸镇镇区依旧被怪物控制，而任何被困在那里的人仍是囚徒，甚至更糟。更令人不安的是，如今迷雾散去，白昼之光揭示出一件真正令人心神不宁的事。总督的庄园——曾坐落于柳岸镇镇区东北角——消失了！</p>\n<p>到此时，PC们应当已经会见了柳岸镇最具影响力的长者：“胡太婆”（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{胡板娘}，代表北岭人）以及“老松木”（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{松木胜}，代表南岸）。这两位NPC在本次冒险末尾都有完整介绍，包括PC可用来获取额外好处的影响数据表。两人都希望PC尽其所能解放镇区，而长者们则专注于在这段动荡时期保护各自的民众安全。PC选择与哪位长者合作由他们自己决定，但他们选择支援哪一派系，将有助于决定柳岸镇在本战役剩余部分中的未来。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-kappa-bath.webp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Reclaiming Willowshire\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 2:</span>\n  <span>Reclaiming Willowshore</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Once the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is lit and the eerie supernatural mists and moonlight are banished, the monsters and perils in most of Willowshore abate as well. Citizens who have been hiding in their homes or gathering in safe zones emerge cautiously, yet the people of Willowshore remain frightened. Nothing like this has happened before, and the town’s leaders have their hands full keeping the citizens comfortable, safe, and calm. One notable part of town is still in danger, though: downtown Willowshore remains controlled by monsters, and any citizens who were trapped there remain prisoners or worse. More disturbing, now that the mists are gone, the light of day reveals something truly unsettling. The governor’s manor, once situated at the northeastern corner of downtown Willowshore, has vanished!</p>\n<p>At this point, the PCs should have met with Willowshore’s most influential elders, “Granny Hu” (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{Hu Ban-niang}, representing Northridge) and “Old Matsuki” (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{Matsuki Shou}, representing Southbank). Both of these NPCs have full write-ups at the end of the adventure, including influence stat blocks the PCs can use to gain additional benefits. Both want the PCs to do what they can to liberate downtown while the elders focus on keeping their constituents safe during these troubled times. Which elder the PCs choose to work with is up to them, but their choice of which faction to support will help decide Willowshore’s future throughout the remainder of this campaign.</p>"
            },
            "Concluding the Chapter": {
              "name": "本章总结 Concluding the Chapter",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding the Chapter\">本章收尾</h1>\n<p>当三个怪物头目被击败，且<em>长明灯</em>再次点亮后，本章便告结束。柳岸镇中剩余的怪物会逃回周边的荒野，但如果你愿意，其中一些也可能躲藏到镇上的其他地方，随着冒险继续进行，给PC们增添需要处理的额外任务。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.x5igH32eFlcD1P5V]{柳岸镇}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding the Chapter\">Concluding the Chapter</h1>\n<p>This chapter ends once the three monstrous ringleaders are defeated and the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> is once again lit. The remaining monsters in Willowshore flee back into the surrounding wilderness, but if you want, some of them could end up hiding somewhere else in town, giving the PCs additional tasks to deal with as the adventure continues.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.x5igH32eFlcD1P5V]{Willowshore}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "Second Floor": {
              "name": "二楼 Second Floor",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C4. 二楼</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房间曾是供客人品茶并安静交谈的放松区域，如今家具与墙壁都被人蓄意破坏，布满深深的抓痕。东北面的墙上被砸出了一个洞。</p>\n</div>\n<p>青天茶馆的二楼离地10尺，由于缺乏维护，通往二楼的楼梯很吵。任何攀爬楼梯的人都会自动让楼梯发出吱呀声，并惊动栖居在此的生物。试图以隐匿通过楼梯时，会受到–4物品减值。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/stingy.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">二楼</span> <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.osxHAxPAbowaFn1b]{刺仔}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>莫都求的最后一只宠物——一只名为刺仔的森林蝎，体型与人类相当，颜色暗绿夹杂脏黄——栖息于此。这只森林蝎比疣儿要隐蔽得多。若被入侵者惊动，刺仔不会立刻爬下楼梯加入战斗；相反，它会在这里的椽梁上躲藏，希望让PC们先用几轮时间探索此处，然后再突然从上方扑下发动出其不意的攻击。战斗开始时，刺仔以隐匿掷骰进行先攻，并战至死方休。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C4. Second Floor</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Once a relaxing area in which guests could enjoy tea and quiet conversation, the furniture and walls of this room have been vandalized and bear deep scratches. A hole has been smashed into the wall to the northeast.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The second floor of the Cerulean Teahouse is 10 feet aboveground, and the stairs leading up are noisy from lack of maintenance. Someone who climbs the stairs automatically causes them to creak and alerts the creature that dwells up here. Attempts to traverse the stairs via Stealth suffer a –4 item penalty.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/stingy.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Second Floor</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.osxHAxPAbowaFn1b]{Stingy}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Mo Douqiu’s final pet, a dull green and dirty yellow human-sized forest scorpion named Stingy, dwells here. The forest scorpion is far more subtle than Warty. If alerted to intruders, Stingy doesn’t immediately clamber down the stairs to join the fight but instead Hides in the rafters here, hoping to drop on the PCs and attack unexpectedly after allowing them a few rounds to explore the place. When combat begins, Stingy rolls for initiative with Stealth and fights to the death.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Private Banquet Hall": {
              "name": "私人宴会厅 Private Banquet Hall",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C3. 私人茶饭厅</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间曾经装饰考究的茶饭厅如今已成污秽巢穴，遍地都是没洗的餐具、食物污渍，以及仿佛经历过多次骇人屠杀后的残迹。被剥皮或被部分消化到难以辨认的尸体堆在角落里，或从上方木梁上系着的绳索间摇晃垂落。房间中央还有一堆肮脏污秽的坐垫与毯子，像巢穴般堆成一团。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-doiqiu.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Mo Douqiu\" alt=\"Long necked humanoid lounging on cushions with a large jug of sake\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-doiqiu.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>莫都求是个毫不掩饰的享乐主义者，仅凭在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c1publicfloo00]{C1} 或楼上区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c4secondfloo00]{C4} 传来的战斗声，还不足以让他对PC有所反应；但只要南侧墙上的拉门被打开，这只辘轳首便会沉重地叹一口气，承认自己得亲自处理入侵者了。</p>\n<p>PC一旦与他对峙，莫都求便从房间中央那堆肮脏坐垫上懒散趴着的姿势，挪成更直立一些的坐姿，随后漫不经心地表示：虽然他没叫表演者，但愿意接纳“新的娱乐”。他靠回去等待PC“开始表演”，同时又仰头猛灌另一大壶酒精。若有人问他所谓表演是什么意思，莫都求会简短地说道如下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“跳舞！唱歌！打架！什么好玩就做什么！活着不就是为了这个吗，所以活起来！不然，就把自己派上用场，去喂疣儿。也就是把宝藏留下，让那饿鬼小畜生把你一口吞了。反正大多数人当蟾蜍饲料更合适。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>若PC问他为何入侵柳岸镇，莫都求回答：</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“因为这镇子无聊到爆！人人日复一日地干活，就为了糊口。年年如此，永远重复同一套。费尽力气就为了活下去。你看到所有人永远陷在这种可怕的套路里，难道不也想让这里热闹点吗？”</p>\n</div>\n<p>若PC质疑他的理念并指出他造成的暴力行为，这只辘轳首会说：</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“但那也是变化，对吧？没有什么比被扔进恐怖故事的正中央更能改变一个人！人们就爱听那些吓人的故事，你知道的，那为什么不亲身体验一回？”他爆发出震耳欲聋的大笑，然后问道：“承认吧。你们难道玩得不开心吗？！”</p>\n</div>\n<p>与莫都求的进一步交谈也会沿着同样的思路继续，这只辘轳首对肆意破坏、向他人灌输恐惧与痛苦表现出明显的快意。他几乎像是想挑衅PC先动手。他不会率先发动攻击，但一旦战斗开始，他便会命令自己剩余的宠物起来护卫他。这包括疣儿（若巨蟾蜍仍活着）以及刺仔（若蝎子仍活着）；但若PC已经击败了这两只动物，莫都求仍可仰仗他的宠物黄鼠狼毛须从他袖中爬出、从他肩头跃下，与他并肩作战。由于他一番高谈阔论且不急于开战，这只辘轳首以社交掷先攻。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-doiqiu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">私人茶饭厅</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.tSkFiv7gwtb8xEaA]{享乐主义者莫都求} @UUID[Actor.WZzYaUwCfKNV4U1q]{毛须}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>莫都求偏好以挫志PC为核心的战术，尤其是使用威吓猛扑。他也不介意在战斗中“浪费”一个动作来咯咯怪笑，或从一碟清酒里慢吞吞又邋遢地猛灌一大口。沉醉于暴力之中，莫都求会战至死亡。他甚至在死时也会发笑，最终带着癫狂的笑容死去。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.kb81yBug06ZyJjSE]{私人茶饭厅} @UUID[Actor.vpTjs5jRg5a21TCm]{莫都求} <br />\n  尽管莫都求毁掉了这间茶馆里大部分值钱物件，但仍有一件物品——一条不知为何没被弄脏、且状况相对良好的<em>戏法手帕</em>——逃过了他的注意。莫都求身上还带着通往区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c2pantrypris00]{C2} 的门锁钥匙。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>击败莫都求后，给予PC与柳岸镇各派系各1点声望点。若PC还确保护将本房间所有尸体从梁上取下，并恭敬地覆盖或以其他方式整理得体，以便向镇上其余人展示并为其准备正式葬礼，则再给予队伍与各派系各1点额外声望点。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C3. Private Banquet Hall</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This once-elaborate banquet room has become a den of filth, littered with unwashed dishes, food stains, and what looks to be the aftermath of many grisly slaughters. Bodies flayed or partially digested to the point of being unrecognizable lie heaped in corners or sway from ropes tied to wooden beams above. A pile of filthy, soiled cushions and blankets lies in a nest-like heap in the middle of the room.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-doiqiu.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Mo Douqiu\" alt=\"Long necked humanoid lounging on cushions with a large jug of sake\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-doiqiu.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Mo Douqiu is an unabashed hedonist, and it’ll take more than the sounds of battle in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c1publicfloo00]{C1} or upstairs in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c4secondfloo00]{C4} to get him to respond to the PCs, but as soon as the sliding doors on the south wall are opened, the rokurokubi gives a heavy sigh, conceding that he’ll need to handle the intruders himself.</p>\n<p>Once confronted by the PCs, Mo Douqiu shifts into a more upright position on the filthy cushions he’s sprawled on in the middle of the room, then casually notes that while he didn’t call for performers, he accepts the “new entertainment.” He sits back to wait for the PCs to “start their performance” as he begins chugging yet another large jug of alcohol. If asked what he means by a performance, Mo Douqiu curtly states the following.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Dance! Sing! Fight! Whatever is entertaining! It’s what living is all about, so LIVE! Otherwise, make use of yourself and go feed Warty. As in, leave your treasure here and let that hungry critter just gobble you down. Most people are better as toad food anyway.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>If the PCs ask why he invaded Willowshore, Mo Douqiu replies:</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Because this town is the most boring place ever! Everyone’s working day in, day out, just to make ends meet. Every single year, doing the same thing over and over again. All that work just to survive. Wouldn’t you want to liven this up too if you see everyone forever mired in the same dreadful routine?”</p>\n</div>\n<p>If the PCs question his philosophy and point out the violence he’s caused, the rokurokubi says:</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“But it was a change, right? Nothing changes you more than being thrown into the middle of a horror story! People love those terrifying tales, you know, so why not live through one?” He breaks into a roaring laugh, then asks, “Admit it. Haven’t you been having fun?!”</p>\n</div>\n<p>Any further conversation with Mo Douqiu’s proceeds along the same line, with the rokurokubi showing a distinct delight for wanton destruction and instilling fear and distress in others. It’s almost as if he wants to provoke the PCs into starting a fight. He won’t make the first attack, but once combat begins, he commands his remaining pets to rise to his defense. This includes Warty (if the giant toad still lives) and Stingy (if the scorpion still lives), but if the PCs have already defeated these two animals, Mo Douqiu can still rely upon his pet weasel, Fluffy Whiskers, to clamber out of his sleeves, launch off his shoulders, and fight at his side. As a result of his philosophizing and hesitance to start the fight, the rokurokubi rolls for initiative with Society.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-doiqiu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Private Banquet Hall</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.tSkFiv7gwtb8xEaA]{Mo Douqiu the Hedonist} @UUID[Actor.WZzYaUwCfKNV4U1q]{Fluffy Whiskers}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Mo Douqiu favors tactics focused on Demoralizing the PCs, particularly by using Threatening Lunge. He’s not above “wasting” an action during combat to cackle or take a long, sloppy gulp from a dish of sake. Reveling in the violence, Mo Douqiu fights to the death. He even laughs as he dies, ending with an unhinged grin on his face in death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.kb81yBug06ZyJjSE]{Private Banquet Hall} @UUID[Actor.vpTjs5jRg5a21TCm]{Mo Douqiu} <br />\n  While Mo Douqiu has ruined most of the objects of value in the teahouse, one item—a somehow-unsoiled and in relatively good condition <em>legerdemain handkerchief</em>—has escaped his attention. Mo Douqiu also carries the keys to the locks on the doors to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c2pantrypris00]{C2}.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> For defeating Mo Douqiu, grant the PCs 1 Reputation Point with each of Willowshore’s factions. If the PCs also ensure all the bodies in this room are removed from the beams and respectfully covered or otherwise made presentable to the rest of the town so they can be prepared for proper funerals, grant the party 1 additional Reputation Point with each faction.</p>"
            },
            "Pantry Prison": {
              "name": "储藏室监狱 Pantry Prison",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C2. Pantry Prison\">C2. 食品储藏室监牢</h2>\n<p>通往该房间的两扇门都用重型挂锁锁住。莫都求带着这些锁的钥匙；否则，一名角色可以通过进行三次@Check[thievery|dc:20|traits:action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick the Lock]检定来开锁。或者，一名角色也可以对每扇坚固的门各进行一次@Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:action:force-open|name:Force Open]检定来破拆。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间食品储藏室储备匮乏，仅存的任何物资也早已腐坏。房间里弥漫着一股氨气的臭味。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这股刺鼻的氨气味来自储藏室中数种腐坏原料缓慢发生的反应——在此房间结束其回合的角色必须成功通过一次@Check[fortitude|dc:15]豁免，否则将变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1}。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>莫都求几乎不把这房间当作食品储藏室使用，而是将其临时改造成一间监牢，用来关押他与其怪物爪牙迄今为止抓到的12名村民。这12名男女都惊恐万分，被绳索一圈圈捆住手脚，为自己的性命担忧。囚犯们安静却满怀希望地看着任何PC，他们害怕呼救会惊动莫都求，因此不敢出声。这12人目前全部处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}状态。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.rkTSYIcQYB0CtWxW]{被囚禁的村民（12人）}</span>\n    <span>生物 –1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人生物</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC解救这些俘虏，给予PC 40 XP，并且每个阵营各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C2. Pantry Prison\">C2. Pantry Prison</h2>\n<p>Both doors to this room are locked with heavy-duty padlocks. Mo Douqiu carries the key to these locks; otherwise, a character can open them with three @Check[thievery|dc:20|traits:action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick the Lock] checks to Pick the Lock. Alternately, a character can Force Open these sturdy doors with a single @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:action:force-open|name:Force Open] check each.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This pantry is poorly stocked, with any remaining supplies having spoiled long ago. The stink of ammonia lingers in the room.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The pungent smell of ammonia comes from a slow reaction of several spoiled ingredients in the pantry—a character who ends their turn in this room must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Mo Douqiu has little use for this room as a pantry and instead has turned it into an impromptu prison to hold the 12 villagers he and his monstrous agents have captured so far. All 12 of these men and women are terrified, bound hand and foot with coils of rope and fearful for their lives. The prisoners look quietly but hopefully at any PCs, too afraid to cry out for help in fear of alerting Mo Douqiu. All 12 are currently @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued}.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.rkTSYIcQYB0CtWxW]{Imprisoned Villagers (12)}</span>\n    <span>Creature –1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 40 XP and 1 Reputation Point with each faction if they free these captives.</p>"
            },
            "Public Floor": {
              "name": "公共楼层 Public Floor",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C1. 公共楼层</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房间曾经被精心上漆的木墙如今满是暴力痕迹，布满凿痕与刮擦。茶馆的前台一片狼藉，破碎的壶、瓶与杯子散落其上。一张桌子被掀翻在侧，连同当时放在上面的餐具一起倒下。东南角还有另一张桌子仍然竖立着，这张桌子却诡异地摆放整齐、桌面也已布置妥当，仿佛在等客上门。东北方向的楼梯通往二楼的阳台。北侧墙边是一条抬高两尺的木质平台，沿墙延伸；平台上有数扇拉门都紧闭着，只有西北角例外：那里的壁龛中摆着两座未点燃的炉灶，旁边还有一扇较小的木门。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这里已荒废数月，莫都求的到来对青天茶馆毫无助益。他的金鬼仆从造成了这里的大部分破坏，不过它们此后已经离开。莫都求把时间都花在私密的茶饭厅（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c3privateban00]{C3}）里，但他也动过念头，或许会与如今栖身在西边旧伐木营地的一些无面鬼碰面（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{第4章}）。西南方那张摆好的桌子正是为这种会面而准备的，但在他确信自己已完全掌控柳岸镇之前，这名辘轳首尚未向无面鬼发出邀请。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>生物：</strong>莫都求让他的宠物巨蟾蜍“疣疣”在这间屋里自由活动。当<em>长明灯</em>\n  还未点亮时，疣疣性格粗鄙、满口脏话，喜欢用舌头去拨弄任何引起它兴趣的东西（尤其是闪亮的物件）；但一旦PC点亮灯笼，苦迦菩提对这只巨蟾蜍的影响就会减弱（尽管它仍然对闪亮的东西感兴趣）。疣疣依旧忠于莫都求，但更满足于趴在通往阳台的楼梯旁睡觉。若被入侵者惊醒，它会兴奋地呱呱叫，蹒跚向前发动攻击。\n</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/warty-1.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">公共楼层</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.mmI62LfQ2mvhj7Xa]{疣疣}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>只要外头制造噪音的只有疣疣一个，莫都求就会以为这只巨蟾蜍只是在闹腾，便从区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c3privateban00]{C3} 大喊：“安分点，疣疣！我一会儿给你弄点吃的！”即便PC在这间屋里战斗的明显声响也无法惊动这名辘轳首——只有当他们进入他的房间时，他才会作出回应。</p>\n  <p>除非被命令“跟上”，否则疣疣也不懂得收手，会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.6ROWduPklUTF6Bdr]{前台} <br />\n  如果PC花至少几分钟搜寻前台，他们会自动发现一叠文件，清楚表明茶馆的财务困境早在龙华崩塌之前就已开始。这些纸张中还包括一份题为《庆麦莱的最后遗嘱与遗言》的文件；PC知道麦莱是青天茶馆的最后一任经营者。这份文件是PC若想将茶馆作为生意经营、并使其对茶馆的主张合法化的关键。更多信息见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#the-teahouse-owners-will]{茶馆主人的遗嘱}。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C1. Public Floor</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The once finely lacquered wooden walls of this room bear evidence of violence, covered now with gouges and scrapes. The front counter of the teahouse is a mess of broken pots, bottles, and cups. A table has been turned on its side, along with whatever dishes were on it at the time. Another table still stands in the southeast corner, this one strangely well placed and set, as if expecting guests. Stairs lead up to an upstairs balcony to the northeast. Steps lead up two feet to an upraised wooden platform running along the northern wall, where several sliding doors stand closed save for the northwest corner, in which two unlit stoves sit in an alcove near a smaller wooden door.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Abandoned for months, Mo Douqiu’s arrival did no favors to the Cerulean Teahouse. His jinkin minions did most of the damage here, although they’ve moved on since then. While Mo Douqiu spends his time in the private banquet hall (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c3privateban00]{C3}), he has entertained the notion of potentially meeting with some of the noppera-bos who now dwell in the lumber camp to the west (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{Chapter 4}). The set table to the southwest has been prepared for just such a meeting, but until he can be sure he has full control of Willowshore, the rokurokubi hasn’t yet contacted the noppera-bos with his invitation.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Creatures:</strong> Mo Douqiu lets his pet giant toad, Warty, wander about this room freely. While the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>\n  was unlit, Warty had a foul-mouthed personality and enjoyed using his tongue to mess with anything that caught his interest (particularly shiny things), but once the PCs light the lantern, Kugaptee’s influence over the giant toad diminishes (although he retains his interest in shiny things). Warty remains loyal to Mo Douqiu, but is more content to spend his time sleeping near the stairs leading up to the balcony. If he’s awoken by intruders, he begins to croak eagerly and lumbers forward to attack.\n</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/warty-1.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Public Floor</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.mmI62LfQ2mvhj7Xa]{Warty}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>As long as Warty is the only one making noise out here, Mo Douqiu assumes the giant toad is just being frisky and yells out from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c3privateban00]{C3}, “Settle down, Warty! I’ll get you some food in a bit!” Even the obvious sound of PCs fighting in this room fails to rouse the rokurokubi—he’ll only respond to them once they enter his chamber.</p>\n  <p>Unless commanded to heel, Warty, not knowing any better, fights to the death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.6ROWduPklUTF6Bdr]{Front Counter} <br />\n  If the PCs Search the front counter for at least a few minutes, they automatically discover paperwork that lays bare the fact that the teahouse’s financial troubles began long before Lung Wa collapsed. The papers also include a document titled “The Last Will and Testament of Qing Mai-Lai”; the PCs know Mai-Lai was the last proprietor of the Cerulean Teahouse. This document is key to the PCs legitimizing their claim over the teahouse if they want to run it as a business. See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#the-teahouse-owners-will]{The Teahouse Owner’s Will} for more information.\n</p>"
            },
            "Cerulean Teahouse": {
              "name": "青天茶馆 Cerulean Teahouse",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Cerulean Teahouse\">青天茶馆</h1>\n<p>青天茶馆（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w22thecerule00]{W22}）位于市中心北侧不远处；从市中心地图沿西北方向的街道向前走大约再100英尺即可到达。PC们可能早在从区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b4prison000000]{B4} 或 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b5outdoorpri00]{B5} 解救囚犯时，就得知这座被废弃的茶馆正被莫都求当作“总部”使用。然而，如果他们在解放市中心的过程中没有发现这条消息，务必让他们从某个人口中得知，因为在莫都求被击败之前，柳岸镇都无法摆脱怪物的影响。当然，他们也可能在探索柳岸镇时意外闯入莫都求的地盘。无论他们是如何来到茶馆的，都会在其中发现骇人的景象——因为莫都求可以说是三名怪物头目中最可怕的一个。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Cerulean Teahouse\">Cerulean Teahouse</h1>\n<p>The Cerulean Teahouse (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w22thecerule00]{W22}) is located just north of downtown and can be approached by heading up the northwestern street from the downtown map for about 100 more feet. The PCs might learn that the abandoned teahouse is being used as Mo Douqiu’s “headquarters” as early as when they free prisoners from areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b4prison000000]{B4} or @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b5outdoorpri00]{B5}. However, if they don’t discover this news through the course of liberating downtown, make sure they learn about it from someone since Willowshore won’t be free of monstrous influence until Mo Douqiu is defeated. Of course, they might also simply stumble into Mo Douqiu’s domain accidentally while they’re exploring Willowshore. However they come to the teahouse, they’ll find horrors within, for Mo Douqiu is arguably the worst of the three monstrous ringleaders.</p>"
            },
            "A Parade of Cookware": {
              "name": "炊具游行 A Parade of Cookware",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">炊具游行</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>虽然莫都求与辘肠都宣称了特定地点作为自己的领域，但第三个怪物头目还没真正选定一个“家”。相反，那名形似屠夫围裙的一反木绵，名为灰屠，正带领着一群在苦迦菩提影响下活化、叮当作响的炊具穿行于柳岸镇的街道。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-chimisha.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Gray Butcher\" alt=\"由屠夫围裙诞生的一反木绵付丧神\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-chimisha.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>灰屠的炊具游行何时与PC们遭遇，由你决定。本次遭遇开始时，PC们会在看到游行队伍之前先听见它：数百件炊具相互碰撞的声响，加上灰屠跑调的哼唱与歌声，想不注意都难。灰屠是一反木绵付丧神，由屠夫围裙诞生。它体内携带着源自一个世纪浸染血与痛的恶意残忍，并在巷弄与街道间带领一群活化的菜刀、肉锤、水壶、平底锅、筷子等等，组成叮当作响的行列。</p>\n<p>如果灰屠注意到PC们，这名一反木绵会命令游行队伍停下，并对队伍厉声喝道：“什么人？”给他们一个解释自己的机会。PC们在回答时可以尝试对灰屠撒谎或建立印象（灰屠在遭遇开始时为不友善）。若PC们将灰屠的态度改善到不关心或更好，一反木绵会命令PC们加入游行15分钟，作为他们庆祝柳岸镇新统治者的“义务”。在这段令人精疲力竭、往返穿行于柳岸镇街道的行程后，每名PC都必须成功通过一次@Check[fortitude|dc:15]豁免，以抵抗陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}。无论结果如何，一旦他们的义务履行完毕，灰屠就会把他们丢在原地离去。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/animated-cookware-swarm.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">炊具游行</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.XL1a1FkujCi3ij2x]{灰屠} @UUID[Actor.Uvh3rWOqENlqsv0A]{活化炊具虫群（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>如果PC们拒绝加入，他们的无礼会激怒灰屠，它会命令活化炊具发动攻击。在这场战斗中，灰屠会先退后观望；但如果PC们击败了两个虫群，这名一反木绵会沮丧地叹气，然后俯冲上前来完成收尾。</p>\n  <p>如果PC们与灰屠一起完成过一次游行，那么他们在不超过一小时后就应当第二次遭遇这群家伙。这一次，灰屠看到PC们仍在街上“磨磨蹭蹭”会感到挫败与恼火，并发动攻击。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.gBc1GctQWfpgcukT]{灰屠} <br />\n  灰屠在其围裙般的身体口袋里藏了几件宝藏：两瓶<em>潜能油</em>、两枚<em>迷心蛋白石护符</em>、一对<em>潜能水晶护符</em>，以及一把置于丝绸包裹的皮革刀鞘中的<em>+1 银 匕首</em>（刀鞘价值10 gp）。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>击败灰屠后，使PC们在每个阵营中各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A Parade of Cookware</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span>\n</h2>\n<p>While Mo Douqiu and Gurglegut both claimed specific locations as their domains, the third monstrous ringleader hasn’t quite yet settled on a “home.” Instead, the butcher-apron-resembling ittan-momen named Gray Butcher has been leading swarms of clattering cookware that have become animated by Kugaptee’s influence through the streets of Willowshore.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-chimisha.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Gray Butcher\" alt=\"A ittan-momen tsukumogami born from a butcher’s apron\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-chimisha.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The timing of when Gray Butcher’s parade of cookware encounters the PCs is left to you. When this encounter begins, the PCs hear the parade before they spot it, as the sound of hundreds of pieces of cookware clattering together, combined with Gray Butcher’s off-key humming and singing, is impossible to miss. Gray Butcher is an ittan-momen tsukumogami born from a butcher’s apron. They carry within themself a malicious cruelty born from a century of exposure to blood and pain as they lead a swarm of animated cleavers, meat tenderizers, kettles, pans, chopsticks, and more on a clattering procession along alleys and streets.</p>\n<p>If Gray Butcher notices the PCs, the ittan-momen orders a stop to the parade and shouts a stern “Who goes there?” at the party, giving them a chance to explain themselves. The PCs can attempt to Lie or Make an Impression on Gray Butcher (who begins the encounter unfriendly) when they answer. If the PCs improve Gray Butcher’s attitude to indifferent or better, the ittan-momen orders the PCs to join the parade for 15 minutes as their “duty” to celebrate Willowshore’s new rulers. After this exhausting trip back and forth through the streets of Willowshore, each PC must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save to resist becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued}. Regardless, Gray Butcher leaves them behind once their duty is fulfilled.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/animated-cookware-swarm.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">A Parade of Cookware</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.XL1a1FkujCi3ij2x]{Gray Butcher} @UUID[Actor.Uvh3rWOqENlqsv0A]{Animated Cookware Swarms (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If the PCs refuse to join, their impertinence enrages Gray Butcher, who orders the animated cookware to attack. During this fight, Gray Butcher hangs back, but if the PCs defeat both swarms, the ittan-momen sighs in frustration before swooping in to finish the job.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs perform one parade with Gray Butcher, it should be no more than an hour before they encounter the group a second time. This time, Gray Butcher is frustrated and annoyed to see the PCs are still “lollygagging” on the street and attacks.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.gBc1GctQWfpgcukT]{Gray Butcher} <br />\n  Gray Butcher has several treasures stashed away in the pockets of their apron body. This treasure consists of two vials of <em>oil of potency</em>, two <em>mesmerizing opal talismans</em>, a pair of <em>potency crystal talismans</em>, and a <em>+1 silver dagger</em> in a silk-wrapped leather sheath (the sheath is worth 10 gp).\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> For defeating Gray Butcher, grant the PCs 1 Reputation Point with each faction.</p>"
            },
            "Shelyn Shrine": {
              "name": "莎琳圣坛 Shelyn Shrine",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B17. Shelyn Shrine\">B17. 莎琳神龛</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>有人有先见之明，把永恒玫瑰的神龛用木板封了起来。透过木板的缝隙，可以看出里面的莎琳陶制雕像完好无损。</p>\n</div>\n<p>如果PC想为他们的钱币寻求@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{Shelyn}的祝福，他们得先以5次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]检定破拆木板。如果他们这么做了却没有恢复神龛的路障，怪物会在24小时后注意到神龛并将其摧毁（使PC从神龛获得的铜币祝福结束）。虽然神龛能在之后重建，但这次破坏行为会使PC从每个派系各失去2点声望。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B17. Shelyn Shrine\">B17. Shelyn Shrine</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Someone had the foresight to board up the shrine to the Eternal Rose. Through the cracks of the board, it’s apparent that the ceramic statue of Shelyn inside is intact and well.</p>\n</div>\n<p>If the PCs seek @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.gxwmzxUWBOhdgFSN]{Shelyn}’s blessing for their coins, they’ll need to Force Open the boards first with five successful @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] checks. If they do so and don’t restore the shrine’s barricade, monsters notice the shrine 24 hours later and destroy it (causing any blessing the PCs got from the shrine on a copper coin to end). While the shrine can be rebuilt in time, this vandalism costs the PCs 2 Reputation points from each faction.</p>"
            },
            "Public Stage": {
              "name": "公共阶段 Public Stage",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B16. 公共舞台</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">极难 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这座露天舞台后墙上的壁画已被严重凿碎并遭到涂改。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/very-drunken-jinkin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">公共舞台</span> <span class=\"keepme\">极难 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.g6gxVjIHPXPIfPw6]{金金（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC们第一次接近这座舞台时，三只金金正在屋顶上嬉闹，穿着他们从后台偷来的戏服并拿着道具。发现PC后，两只小魔怪欢呼并大喊，要求PC观看他们即兴演出一出嘲笑柳岸镇市民怯懦与愚蠢的短剧。演出既侮辱人又刻薄，但金金们投入到只要观众还在看，他们就会一直演下去。若他们注意到PC即将离开该区域，就会朝“忘恩负义的观众”喊话，开始向PC投掷松动的屋瓦。然而，一旦其中任何一只金金真的受到伤害，三只都会惊叫着逃跑，彻底离开城镇。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B16. Public Stage</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The mural on the back wall of this open-air stage has been heavily chipped and defaced.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/very-drunken-jinkin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Public Stage</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.g6gxVjIHPXPIfPw6]{Jinkins (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When PCs first approach this stage, three jinkins are roughhousing on the roof, wearing costumes and props they stole from backstage. Upon spotting the PCs, the two gremlins cheer and shout, demanding the PCs watch them perform an impromptu play about the cowardice and foolishness of Willowshore’s citizens. The performance is insulting and mean-spirited, but the jinkins are invested enough that they’ll keep at it as long as their audience keeps watching. If they notice the PCs are about to leave the area, they call out to the “ungrateful audience” and begin hurling loose shingles at the PCs. As soon as any of the jinkins actually take damage, though, all three scream in surprise and flee the town entirely.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Mostly Happy Kappas": {
              "name": "大多快乐的河童 Mostly Happy Kappas",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B15. 大多挺开心的河童</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">极限 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这处露天、由树篱围成的庭院里，有两座石砌浴池，池中热水蒸腾。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>并非所有被吸引到柳岸镇的怪物都天生邪恶，但即便是正在池中放松的这五只河童，也称不上心地善良。虽然杀死马厩里马匹的不是它们（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b8infestedst00]{B8}），但它们仍为这顿新鲜的餐食而欣喜。它们在那里把自己弄得一团糟后，便转移到这里来清洗并休息。</p>\n<p>五只河童对于1级PC而言是远超极限的遭遇，但这里并不打算作为战斗遭遇。当河童发现PC后，会邀请队伍一起泡澡。无论PC是否接受，它们都承认柳岸镇发生的事“令人遗憾”，但坚持表示自己并非问题的源头。河童透露，它们是被一名名叫莫都求的辘轳首邀请到此，对方请求它们协助接管柳岸镇。它们确认是自己吃了马匹的内脏，不过杀死动物的是金金斯——并承认莫都求的这份贿赂足以让它们与他同流合污。自那之后，它们开始感到后悔。尤其是，河童意识到，一旦城镇的守卫集结反击，这样的入侵只会给它们自身带来悲苦与伤害，此时它们会礼貌地点头致意。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/kappa.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">大多挺开心的河童</span> <span class=\"keepme\">极限 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.edclGnYWtl1fU7yo]{河童（5）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>起初它们为不关心；如果PC能够以一次成功的 @Check[diplomacy|dc:17|action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression] 检定来建立印象，从而使河童变为友善，河童就同意和平离开城镇并返回葫芦湖（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d2gourdlake000]{D2}）；否则，它们会一直待到莫都求被击败为止。若PC身上带有黄瓜（也许是来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b12backyards00]{B12} 的奖励），则允许每位PC各有一次机会，尝试进行 @Check[arcana|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[nature|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来回忆知识：黄瓜是河童最喜欢的食物。在任何试图建立印象的过程中向河童提供黄瓜，可使该次掷骰结果提高一个成功等级。若它们变为敌对，或PC发起攻击，河童会咒骂着、愤愤地喷着气逃走，而不是还手战斗。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.TTTgAKNlZmQ2BMjU]{河童的小费} <br />\n  若PC以友善的方式说服河童离开，河童会给PC一颗价值50 gp的珍珠作为小费（就好像PC是澡堂雇员一样）。在不太可能发生的情况下，如果PC与五只河童对峙并将其杀死，他们也可以将这颗珍珠作为宝藏。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC通过使河童变为友善而说服它们离开，给予60 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B15. Mostly Happy Kappas</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Extreme 1</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A pair of stone-lined baths of steaming water sit within this open-air, hedge-walled yard.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Not all the monsters drawn into Willowshore are inherently evil, but even the five kappas who are relaxing in the pools are hardly kindhearted. While they weren’t the ones who killed the horses in the stables (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b8infestedst00]{B8}), they still delighted in the fresh meal. After making a mess of themselves there, they relocated here to wash up and relax.</p>\n<p>A group of five kappas is beyond an extreme encounter for 1st level PCs, but this isn’t intended to be a combat encounter. As they spot the PCs, the kappas invite the party to join them in the bath. Whether or not the PCs do, they concede that what has happened in Willowshore is “unfortunate” but maintain that they aren’t the source of the problem. The kappas reveal that they were invited here by a rokurokubi named Mo Douqiu who asked for help taking over Willowshore. They confirm that they were the ones who ate the horses’ innards, though it was the jinkins who killed the animals—admitting this bribe from Mo Douqiu was enough to get them to join with him. Since then, they’ve begun to regret things. Particularly, the kappas realize that such an invasion can only bring woe and harm to themselves once the town’s defenders rally, giving the PCs polite nods at this time.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/kappa.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Mostly Happy Kappas</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Extreme 1</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.edclGnYWtl1fU7yo]{Kappas (5)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Initially indifferent, if the PCs can make the kappas friendly with a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:17|action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression] check to Make an Impression, the kappas agree to leave town peacefully and return to Gourd Lake (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d2gourdlake000]{D2}); otherwise, they’ll remain until Mo Douqiu is defeated. If the PCs have any cucumbers on them (perhaps as a reward from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b12backyards00]{B12}), allow each PC a chance to attempt a @Check[arcana|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[nature|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge that cucumbers are a kappa’s favorite food. Offering cucumbers to the kappas during any attempt to Make an Impression improves the result of the roll by one degree of success. If they’re made hostile, or if the PCs attack, the kappas curse and sputter in indignation and flee rather than fight back.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.TTTgAKNlZmQ2BMjU]{Kappa's Tip} <br />\n  If the PCs convince the kappas to leave on friendly terms, they give the PCs a pearl worth 50 gp as a tip (as if the PCs are bathhouse employees). In the unlikely event that the PCs confront and kill the five kappas, they can claim this pearl as treasure.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs convince the kappas to leave by making them friendly, grant them 60 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Bathhouse Lockers": {
              "name": "澡堂储物柜 Bathhouse Lockers",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B14. Bathhouse Lockers\">B14. 浴场更衣柜</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间更衣室整洁有序，每个格子里都放着拖鞋和毛巾。所有更衣柜都敞开着，只有一个例外。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-de-ge.webp\" data-tooltip=\"De-ge\" alt=\"De-ge, a male halfling innkeeper holding his finger to his lips\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-de-ge.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>德格慌乱中想躲起来，把自己硬塞进一个更衣柜里，结果被卡住了。他努力保持冷静，但恐慌正在加剧——每一轮，只要某位PC在此房间开始其回合，就可以尝试一次 @Check[perception|dc:10] 察觉检定，以听到那只关着的更衣柜里传出的窸窣挪动声与轻微的呜咽声。更衣柜门可以用一次 @Check[athletics|dc:17|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定破拆打开，或用一次 @Check[thievery|dc:15|traits:manipulate,skill,action:disable-a-device|name:Disable a Device] 检定解除而不伤到德格；但任何试图破坏更衣柜（AC 13，硬度 5，HP 24 [BT 12]）的行为，都会使对更衣柜造成的伤害有一半也转移到德格身上。他会痛得嚎叫，并恳求袭击者停手离开。</p>\n<p>若被救出，德格会心怀感激，但他表示自己受够了市中心，想去更干净的地方，比如妙手回春诊所（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}）。他恳求PC们带他过去。</p>\n<p>他还会告知PC们，他的“客人”仍在这里——五只河童穿过中间的门，朝西面的浴池方向去了，至今尚未出来。虽然他确信只要礼貌地说几句就能让它们离开，但他太害怕不敢面对它们，于是请求PC们代劳。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.nzFjwNK9VxDZFiXq]{De-ge}</span>\n    <span>生物 1</span>\n  </h2>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们护送德格前往诊所，给予他们20 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"B14. Bathhouse Lockers\">B14. Bathhouse Lockers</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This locker room is orderly, with slippers and towels in each cubby. All the lockers are open, save for one.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-de-ge.webp\" data-tooltip=\"De-ge\" alt=\"De-ge, a male halfling innkeeper holding his finger to his lips\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-de-ge.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> In his panic to hide, De-ge squeezed himself into a locker but ended up stuck. He’s trying to remain calm, but his panic is growing—every round a PC starts their turn in this room, they can attempt a @Check[perception|dc:10] check to hear the sound of shuffling and soft whimpering within the closed locker. The locker door can either be Forced Open with a @Check[athletics|dc:17|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check or Disabled with a @Check[thievery|dc:15|traits:manipulate,skill,action:disable-a-device|name:Disable a Device] check without harm to De-ge, but any attempt to damage the locker (AC 13, Hardness 5, HP 24 [BT 12]) transfers half the damage inflicted to the locker to De-ge as well, who howls in pain and begs for his assailants to stop and go away.</p>\n<p>If he’s freed, De-ge is grateful, but he expresses he’s had enough of downtown and wants to head to a more sanitized place, such as the Hand of Spring clinic (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w27thehandof00]{W27}). He begs the PCs to bring him there.</p>\n<p>He also informs the PCs that his “guests” are still here—the five kappas went through the middle door toward the baths to the west and have yet to emerge. While he’s certain that a few polite words would get them to leave, he’s too afraid to face them and asks the PCs to do it instead.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.nzFjwNK9VxDZFiXq]{De-ge}</span>\n    <span>Creature 1</span>\n  </h2>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 20 XP if they escort De-ge to the clinic.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 1.3: The Willowshore Curse": {
          "name": "第一幕 1.3：柳岸镇的诅咒 Act 1.3: The Willowshore Curse",
          "pages": {
            "Who Leads Willowshore?": {
              "name": "谁来领导柳岸镇？ Who Leads Willowshore?",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Who Leads Willowshore?\">谁来领导柳岸镇？</h1>\n<p>被困在柳岸镇，镇长失踪，又担心怪物随时可能回来，只能彼此作伴的处境，使镇上北岭人与南岸两大派系间的紧张局势不断升级。夏季第三个月的某个夜晚，这种紧张终于崩断——@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{老松木}在众目睽睽之下，公开向@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{胡太婆}发起挑战，争夺柳岸镇的领导权。</p>\n<p>长老们决定依照柳岸镇用来解决公开纠纷的一项传统，以双方选出的斗士进行决斗来裁定领导权之争。两人将决斗日期定在七天后便分道扬镳，留下在场其余人开始议论：谁会代表谁出战、谁还对谁怀有怨念，甚至猜测是否会有第三方介入北岭人与南岸之间的冲突。随着消息在镇里传开，人们逐渐意识到这场决斗很可能会演变为一场血腥屠杀，恐惧也随之蔓延。很快，一名与PC们关系亲近的NPC会请求他们缓和局势、坚定站到某一派系一边，或作为集体自荐为第三名候选人。由你决定是哪位NPC接触队伍，但应当是玩家信任的人。</p>\n<p>距离决斗还有七天，PC们有时间决定自己站在哪一边。老松木与胡太婆都邀请PC们在当天结束前与自己面谈。两人都清楚，那些重燃<em>长明灯</em>之人的支援，将大大有助于确立各自派系的领导权主张，即便PC不愿直接参与决斗亦然。为了说服两位长老之一退让、让另一位担任领导者，PC们必须在该长老处获得7点影响点。PC们在游戏过程中可能已经与一位或两位长老达到了这一水平；若是如此，他们只需决定由谁在最终查明赫赫镇长的命运之前担任柳岸镇的临时镇长即可解决此事。每位长老的影响数据表都在本书末尾其NPC条目中。</p>\n<p>如果PC们未能解决这个问题，那么你应当决定由哪位长老赢得领导权，并选择队伍较不支持的那一位。或者，若PC们对决斗感兴趣，你甚至可以允许他们担任某位长老的斗士，使用决斗规则（<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 202–203）。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们说服其中一位长老让位于另一位，并达成和平解决方案，则给予PC们80 XP，以及在其长老成为城镇领袖的派系中获得2点声望点。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Who Leads Willowshore?\">Who Leads Willowshore?</h1>\n<p>Being stuck in Willowshore with a missing governor, under a fear that the monsters could return at any moment, and with only each other for company causes tension to escalate between the town’s two factions of Northridge and Southbank. One evening during the third month of summer, this tension finally snaps as @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{Old Matsuki} very publicly challenges @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{Granny Hu} for Willowshore’s leadership.</p>\n<p>The elders resolve to settle the question of leadership via a duel between chosen champions, drawing upon a Willowshore tradition for solving public disputes. The two set the date for this duel as seven days hence and part ways, leaving the rest of those present to begin gossiping about who might be representing whom and who yet holds a grudge against another, and even wondering if a third party might step into the conflict between Northridge and Southbank. As word spreads through town, dread grows as folks realize that a duel will likely lead to a bloodbath. Soon enough, an NPC close to the PCs asks them to de-escalate the situation, to stoutly stand with one of the factions, or to put themselves forward as a collective third candidate. Which NPC approaches the party is left to you to decide, but it should be someone the players trust.</p>\n<p>With seven days before the duel, the PCs have time to make a decision as to where they stand. Both Old Matsuki and Granny Hu extend invitations to the PCs to speak to them by the end of the day. Both know the support of those who relit the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> will go a long way toward establishing their faction’s claims of leadership, even if a PC doesn’t wish to be directly involved in the duel itself. In order to convince one of the two elders to step aside and let the other assume the leadership role, the PCs must reach 7 Influence Points with that elder. It’s possible that the PCs have already reached this level with one or both elders during play, in which case they can solve the issue by making the decision of who should be Willowshore’s interim governor until Governor Heh’s fate can finally be determined. Each elder’s influence stat block appears in their NPC entry at the end of this book.</p>\n<p>If the PCs fail to solve this problem, then you should select which elder wins the leadership, picking the one that the party is less in favor with. At your option, if the PCs are intrigued by a duel, you could even allow them to serve as one of the elders’ champions, using the rules for dueling (<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 202–203).</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs convince one of the elders to cede to the other and achieve a peaceful resolution, grant the PCs 80 XP and 2 Reputation Points with the faction whose elder becomes the town’s leader.</p>"
            },
            "Speaking with Ugly Cute": {
              "name": "与丑小乖说话 Speaking with Ugly Cute",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Speaking with Ugly Cute\">与丑小乖交谈</h3>\n<p>一旦PC们击败元素生物，丑小乖便用它的八条腿撑起身子，摇摇晃晃，身上布满缺口与裂纹（剩余5点生命值），但仍然确确实实地活着。石蜘蛛感谢PC们的帮助，并打算留在这处峡谷直到恢复为止（石蜘蛛对治疗的免疫不适用于在此地通过休息获得的治疗），不过它迫不及待想从PC们口中得知柳岸镇的近况。丑小乖知道每位PC的名字，并且在得知他们已接过守护小镇的职责后欣喜不已。</p>\n<p>在对话中，丑小乖是个兴高采烈的守护魂魄，渴望来一场像样的聊天。和PC们一样，丑小乖并未意识到自己在现实世界中已经死亡；而且尽管它的死亡（从PC们的视角）发生在115年后的未来，丑小乖仍认为自己度过的这115年更像是一场梦或幻景，而不是实际经历，因此它不应当给PC们任何关于这段时间流逝的线索或洞见；这一揭示将在本冒险路径后续的篇章中出现。当PC们与丑小乖交谈时，务必传达以下要点，可作为丑小乖的评论或对PC提问的具体回答。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>丑小乖透露，它曾与一群无面怪物对峙，那些怪物正在折磨柳岸镇郊外的人们。它攻击并追逐那些生物，但最后迷失方向且身受重伤，只得返回此处疗养。它为自己弃镇而去道歉，并对PC们正在帮助守护柳岸镇感到如释重负、欣喜万分。</li>\n  <li>丑小乖声称自己曾看到幻象：在某种怪物入侵之后，柳岸镇被遗弃，逐渐崩毁成残垣断壁，又被森林重新吞没；正是这个幻象让它苏醒，并在冒险开始时前来援助PC们。</li>\n  <li>尽管丑小乖不认为重现节是诅咒的源头，但导致诅咒的事件确实发生在仪式本身最高潮之时。</li>\n  <li>环绕柳岸镇的迷雾是小镇覆灭的开端，是某个未知力量给此地带来的诅咒——丑小乖感知到这与它曾对峙的无面怪物有关。那些无面怪物占据了镇子以西的一处旧伐木营地，靠近木棉河源头。也许能在那里找到关于诅咒的线索？在更西边，丑小乖能感知到更强烈的邪恶源头，但由于该源头位于它从柳岸镇出发所能旅行的范围之外，它尚无法亲自观测。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>对话结束后，丑小乖告诉PC们，它打算回到柳岸镇东缘的蜘蛛门岗位。守护魂魄将在那里安顿下来，负责监视与观察，并把小镇的主动防御交给PC们。如果丑小乖在自省式的守护期间获得任何启示，它将再次醒来提醒队伍。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.AxXh7yuCqXIP7U16]{丑小乖}</span>\n    <span>生物 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">大型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">天界</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">神圣</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">虚体</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>无性别 石蜘蛛</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.uAPxF3uakY7mWUnW]{丑小乖的感谢与歉意} <br />\n  为感谢救援，并为自己为了追捕无面绑架者而抛下PC们道歉，丑小乖赠予PC们一片它的石质甲壳，可帮助PC们获得用于守护柳岸镇的工具。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>拯救丑小乖后，给予PC们等同于在战斗中击败它所获得的XP。此外，一旦丑小乖回到蜘蛛门岗位，PC们在两个阵营中各获得2点声望点数。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Speaking with Ugly Cute\">Speaking with Ugly Cute</h3>\n<p>Once the PCs defeat the elementals, Ugly Cute rises up on their eight legs, a bit wobbly and bearing plenty of chips and cracks to their body (with 5 Hit Points remaining), but still very much alive. The stone spider is thankful for the PCs’ help and intends to remain here in the gorge until they recover (the stone spider’s immunity to healing doesn’t apply to healing gained from rest in this location), but they’re eager to learn from the PCs how things are faring in Willowshore. Ugly Cute knows them all by name and is delighted to find out they’ve taken up the mantle of protectors of the town.</p>\n<p>During conversation, Ugly Cute is a chipper guardian spirit who’s starving for a proper chat. Like the PCs, Ugly Cute doesn’t realize they died in the real world, and even though their death occurred (from the PCs’ perspective) 115 years in the future, Ugly Cute believes that the past 115 years it spent were something more like a dream or a vision than an actual experience, and shouldn’t give the PCs any clues or insights into this passage of time; this revelation will take place in a future act of the Adventure Path. As the PCs and Ugly Cute speak, make sure to convey the following points, either as comments by Ugly Cute or as specific answers to the PCs’ questions.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Ugly Cute reveals that they confronted a group of faceless monsters who were tormenting people in Willowshore’s outskirts. They attacked and pursued the creatures, but ended up lost and wounded and had to return here to recover. They apologize for abandoning the town, and they express relief and delight that the PCs are helping to protect Willowshore.</li>\n  <li>Ugly Cute claims to have had visions of an abandoned Willowshore left to crumble into ruins reclaimed by the forest after some sort of monstrous invasion, and it was this vision that allowed it to awaken and come to the PCs’ aid at the start of the adventure.</li>\n  <li>While Ugly Cute doesn’t think that the Reenactment Festival was the source of the curse, whatever caused the curse did take place during the height of the ceremony itself.</li>\n  <li>The mists surrounding Willowshore are the beginning of the town’s doom, a curse brought upon the region by an unknown force—and one that Ugly Cute senses is tied to the faceless monsters who they confronted. These faceless monsters have claimed an old lumber camp to the west of town, near Ceiba River’s source. Perhaps clues about the curse can be found there? Further west, Ugly Cute can sense a stronger source of evil, but they haven’t been able to observe this source themself as it lies beyond the range it can travel from Willowshore.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Once the conversation is over, Ugly Cute tells the PCs they intend to return to their post at Spider Gate on the eastern edge of Willowshore. There, the guardian spirit will settle in to watch and observe, leaving the active defense of the town to the PCs. If Ugly Cute has any revelations during their time of introspective guardianship, they’ll waken again to alert the party.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.AxXh7yuCqXIP7U16]{Ugly Cute}</span>\n    <span>Creature 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Large</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Celestial</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Holy</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Incorporeal</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>Agender Stone Spider</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.uAPxF3uakY7mWUnW]{Ugly Cute's Thanks &amp; Apology} <br />\n  In thanks for the rescue, and as an apology for abandoning the PCs to chase down the faceless abductors, Ugly Cute gifts the PCs a piece of their stony carapace, which can help supply the PCs with tools to protect Willowshore.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> For rescuing Ugly Cute, grant the PCs XP as if they’d defeated them in combat. In addition, they earn 2 Reputation Points with both factions once Ugly Cute resumes their post at Spider Gate.</p>"
            },
            "Rescuing Ugly Cute": {
              "name": "拯救丑小乖 Rescuing Ugly Cute",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">营救丑小乖</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>丑小乖在思维空间中苏醒，并与附近数只无脸妖交战后，他们向南追赶逃跑的怪物一段时间，最终追上并摧毁了这些生物。石蜘蛛在战斗中受了损伤，也因自己所处的诡异新现实而愈发痛苦不安。丑小乖并未返回岗位，而是本能地回到了他们的石头“诞生”之地——尖牙峡。在那里，丑小乖能够汲取创造自身的石头之力，慢慢修复身体。自那之后，这只守护兽对无脸妖与鬼打墙尤为执着，并将时间分配在峡谷中反复思索与在镇子南面和西面的区域巡逻之间，寻找无脸妖的源头——丑小乖相信它们与笼罩这片土地的“诅咒”有关。</p>\n<p>一旦PC接近区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10} 的 1 个六角格范围内，追踪丑小乖会变得更容易（降至一次 @Check[survival|dc:10|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]），但无论他们是否成功，他们在进入该区域后不久都会撞上这片地域中的一些危险住民。</p>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在一片开阔的岩石地带。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>正如苦迦菩提的影响在柳岸镇肆虐、并使南方柳树林发生虫害一般，这位古老邪魔与毁灭和腐朽的关联，也与此地长期以来作为用于制作雕塑与建筑的原始材料来源地之传统相冲突。其结果，是数个活化巨石的显现，它们在峡谷中发出刺耳的刮磨声并来回冲刷穿行。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/living-boulder.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">营救丑小乖</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.neZX16GagSV8zxYh]{活化巨石（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ugly-cute.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ugly Cute\" alt=\"一只东方雕像风格的蜘蛛\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ugly-cute.webp');width:60%\" />\n  <p>PC进入峡谷后不久就会遭遇其中两块活化巨石，发现它们正碾磨着、爬行在一座奇怪的石堆上。尽管这些元素生物与标准活化巨石使用相同数据，它们的个性却大不相同——它们拥有远高于典型活化巨石的智力；而且虽然它们自己不能说话，却能理解阿克洛语。聪明到足以以残虐的追猎为乐，自从石蜘蛛退到这里后，活化巨石便一直以折磨并追逐丑小乖为乐。随着PC靠近，两块活化巨石便移动来发动攻击，并揭示它们一直爬行其上的那些石头，实际上正是丑小乖！</p>\n  <p>在本次遭遇的持续时间内，丑小乖始终遍体鳞伤、几乎无法移动——他们已被活化巨石折磨得近乎毁灭。如果PC在击败这两只元素生物时遇到困难，你可以让丑小乖出手力挽狂澜，但最好还是让PC成为这里的英雄！活化巨石会战斗到被摧毁为止；它们在死亡时会碎裂开来，释放出小团红色蝴蝶云，随即迅速化作烟雾消散。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Rescuing Ugly Cute</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>After Ugly Cute woke into the mindscape and clashed with several noppera-bos in the area, they chased the fleeing monsters south for a time before catching up to and destroying the creatures. The stone spider was damaged in the fight, but was also increasingly distraught over the strange new reality they found themself in. Rather than return to their post, Ugly Cute instinctively returned to the place where their stones were “born,” the Gorge of Fangs and Teeth. Here, Ugly Cute was able to draw upon the stones of their creation to slowly repair their body. Since then, the guardian beast has been particularly obsessed over the noppera-bos and the Wall of Ghosts, and has split their time between thinking things over in the Gorge and patrolling the region south and west of town, searching for the source of the noppera-bos, who Ugly Cute believes have something to do with the “curse” that has settled over the land.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs approach within 1 hex of area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}, it becomes easier to Track Ugly Cute (dropping to a @Check[survival|dc:10|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]), but regardless of their success, they’ll run into some dangerous denizens of the region soon after entering the area.</p>\n<p>This encounter takes place in an open area of rocky ground.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Just as Kugaptee’s influence wreaked havoc on Willowshore and brought infestation to the southern willow grove, the ancient fiend’s association with destruction and decay clashed against the long traditions held in this region as being a source for raw materials used to create sculptures and structures. The result was the manifestation of several living boulders that rasp and scour through the gorge.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/living-boulder.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Rescuing Ugly Cute</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.neZX16GagSV8zxYh]{Living Boulders (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ugly-cute.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ugly Cute\" alt=\"A spider in oriental statue style\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-ugly-cute.webp');width:60%\" />\n  <p>The PCs encounter two of these living boulders soon after they enter the gorge, finding them grinding and crawling over a strange mound of stones. While these elemental creatures have the same statistics as the standard living boulder, their personalities are much different—they possess a far greater intellect than the typical living boulder, and while they cannot speak themselves, they understand Aklo. Smart enough to enjoy the pursuit of cruelty, the living boulders have had a delightful time tormenting and chasing Ugly Cute ever since the stone spider retreated here. As the PCs draw near, the two living boulders move to attack, revealing that the stones they’d been crawling upon are, in fact, Ugly Cute!</p>\n  <p>For the duration of this encounter, Ugly Cute remains battered and barely able to move, having been taken near to the point of destruction by the living boulders. If the PCs have trouble defeating the two elementals, you can have Ugly Cute step in to save the day, but it’s best if the PCs are the heroes here! The living boulders fight until they’re destroyed, cracking open to release small clouds of red butterflies that swiftly fade into smoke on each of their deaths.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Searching the Hinterlands": {
              "name": "在腹地搜寻 Searching the Hinterlands",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Searching the Hinterlands\">搜寻荒野腹地</h2>\n<p>这并不高效，但PC也可以干脆去探索荒野腹地，并搜寻丑小乖经过的迹象。尝试在柳岸镇以东、以北或以西寻找丑小乖的证据会自动失败，但每当一名PC在柳岸镇以南的荒野腹地花费4小时搜寻一个六角格时，进行一次@Check[flat|dc:16]（或者，如果该PC是在尖牙峡或任何与该区域相邻的六角格中搜寻，则进行@Check[flat|dc:3]）。成功时，该PC可以尝试一次@Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]来追踪，以发现丑小乖经过的迹象。一旦发现这些迹象，任何人都可以通过成功的@Check[survival|dc:16|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]来追踪丑小乖的小路。随着足够多的成功次数，小路会直接通往区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}。</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>及时介入</h1>\n  <p>一种可以自动触发发现丑小乖小路的方法是：当PC们尚未达到3级时，就开始接近旧伐木营地（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d11lumbercam00]{D11}）或鬼打墙。如果PC们进入区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d11lumbercam00]{D11}所在六角格的一格范围内，或即将触及鬼打墙，他们就应自动发现丑小乖的小路。他们可以追踪这条小路向南到区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}，但如果他们无视它并继续前往伐木营地，你就应让丑小乖反过来找到他们。此时，石制守卫会以警告PC们营地住民为开端来开始遭遇，而不是与之接近；除此之外，你可以用与“营救丑小乖”相同的方式来演绎这次会面（不过不需要从残忍的活岩石巨砾手中营救石蜘蛛）。通过这种方式，你可以把丑小乖作为拖延PC们抵达伐木营地的手段（伐木营地本身详见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{第4章}），以便在他们更有可能准备好面对其中威胁之前先缓一缓。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Searching the Hinterlands\">Searching the Hinterlands</h2>\n<p>It’s inefficient, but the PCs could simply explore the hinterlands and Search for signs of Ugly Cute’s passage. Attempts to find evidence of Ugly Cute east, north, or west of Willowshore automatically fail, but each time a PC spends 4 hours Searching a hex in the hinterlands south of Willowshore, attempt a @Check[flat|dc:16] (or, if the PC is Searching in the Gorge of Fangs and Teeth or any hex that borders this region, a @Check[flat|dc:3]). On a success, that PC can attempt a @Check[survival|dc:15|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] to Track to discover signs of Ugly Cute’s passage. Once these signs are found, anyone can Track Ugly Cute’s trail with a successful @Check[survival|dc:16|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]. With enough successes, the trail leads directly to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>A Timely Intervention</h1>\n  <p>One way to automatically trigger the discovery of Ugly Cute’s trail is if the PCs begin to draw close to the old lumber camp (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d11lumbercam00]{D11}) or the Wall of Ghosts while they aren’t yet 3rd level. If the PCs come within a hex of area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d11lumbercam00]{D11}, or are about to reach the Wall of Ghosts, they should automatically discover Ugly Cute’s trail. They can Track this trail south to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}, but if they ignore it and continue on toward the lumber camp, you should have Ugly Cute find them instead. In this case, the stone guardian begins the encounter by warning the PCs about the denizens of the camp rather than closing with it, but otherwise, you can play this meeting out the same way as Rescuing Ugly Cute does (although without the need to rescue the stone spider from cruel living boulders). In this way, you can use Ugly Cute as a way to delay the PCs’ arrival at the lumber camp (itself detailed in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{Chapter 4}) before they’re likely ready to face the threats found therein.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Consulting Silvermist": {
              "name": "咨询银雾 Consulting Silvermist",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Consulting Silvermist\">向银雾斋请教</h2>\n<p>当PC们造访银雾斋（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7}）时，如果PC们在本幕较早之前救过澄香，可以考虑让她作为与他们会面的狩猎者。不论PC们见到的是谁，答案都一样：追踪丑小乖的尝试毫无头绪；暴雨以及狩猎者们从怪物入侵中恢复所耗费的时间，都让情况雪上加霜。澄香（或PC们联系到的任何人）沉吟道，就连老猎人的把戏——“回到猎物的家”以试图重新拾起小路——也没能奏效。尽管他们多次返回蜘蛛门（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w33spidergat00]{W33}），仍未出现任何新的线索。</p>\n<p>此时允许PC们尝试一次 @Check[hunting-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来回忆知识。成功时，一名PC会注意到：蜘蛛门与其说像丑小乖的家，不如说更像一个驻点；因此按这个逻辑，如果丑小乖选择逃往巢穴，它就不会返回那里。大成功时，一名PC灵光乍现——丑小乖是由本地采出的石料“诞生”的，那么这只生物的“家”岂不是更像它的组成材料最初被开采出来的源头？如果没有任何PC想到这一点，若队伍几天后仍未自行取得进展，你也可以让澄香或另一名狩猎者意识到这种可能性，并联系PC们提出请求，希望他们帮忙。</p>\n<p>通过一次成功的 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[society|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来回忆知识，PC还会记得：丑小乖的材料最初采自南方的尖牙峡（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}）。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Consulting Silvermist\">Consulting Silvermist</h2>\n<p>When the PCs visit the Silvermist Lodges (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{W7}), consider having Sumika be the hunter who meets with them if the PCs rescued her earlier in the act. Regardless of whom the PCs meet with, the answer is the same: attempts to track Ugly Cute have yielded no leads; the rainstorms and the amount of time that passed while the hunters were recovering from the monster invasion did them no favors. Sumika (or whoever the PCs contact) muses that even the old hunter’s trick of “returning to the quarry’s home” to try to pick up the trail anew hasn’t worked. Despite several visits back to Spider Gate (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w33spidergat00]{W33}), no fresh clues have manifested.</p>\n<p>Allow the PCs to attempt a @Check[hunting-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge at this point. On a success, a PC notes that Spider Gate is less akin to Ugly Cute’s home, but more like a posting, so following this logic, Ugly Cute wouldn’t return there if they chose to flee to a lair. On a critical success, a PC has a flash of insight—Ugly Cute was “born” from locally quarried stone, so wouldn’t the creature’s “home” be akin to the source from which its components were originally harvested? If no PC comes up with this insight, feel free to have Sumika or another hunter realize this possibility and contact the PCs with a request to help after several days have passed if the party hasn’t made progress on their own.</p>\n<p>With a successful @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[society|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC also remembers that Ugly Cute’s materials were originally quarried from the Gorge of Fangs and Teeth to the south (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d10gorgeoffa00]{D10}).</p>"
            },
            "Searching for Ugly Cute": {
              "name": "搜索“丑小乖” Searching for Ugly Cute",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Searching for Ugly Cute\">寻找丑小乖</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇的守护魂魄——多年来一直在镇子东缘守望、被人亲昵地称为“丑小乖”的石蜘蛛——突然消失，这件事看起来也许不像失踪的总督或诡异的迷雾那样紧迫，然而在这三项任务中，追踪丑小乖是唯一能让PC获得可靠线索、以便逆转笼罩大地的“诅咒”的任务。</p>\n<p>当PC最初经过丑小乖被遗弃的岗位时，地上的足迹显示那只蜘蛛曾起身走向附近的河流，之后那条小路便再也无法追踪。PC正在合作的镇中长者告诉他们，自从<em>长明灯</em>被点亮后，银雾斋的追踪者就一直在寻找线索，但到目前为止仍未发现任何丑小乖的踪迹。尽管如此，如果PC想要亲自开始追踪失踪的守护者，那么与斋中的猎人会面便是合乎逻辑的第一步。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Searching for Ugly Cute\">Searching for Ugly Cute</h1>\n<p>The vanishing of Willowshore’s guardian spirit—the stone spider affectionately called “Ugly Cute” who has stood vigil for many years at the eastern edge of town—might not seem as urgent a mystery to follow up on as the missing governor or the strange mists, but tracking down Ugly Cute is the only mission of the three that will give the PCs a solid lead for reversing the “curse” that has settled over the land.</p>\n<p>When the PCs first passed by Ugly Cute’s abandoned post, tracks on the ground suggested that the spider got up and walked away toward the nearby river, after which that particular trail became impossible to follow. The town elder the PCs are working with informs them that trackers from the Silvermist Lodges have been looking for clues ever since the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> was lit, but so far, no trace of Ugly Cute has been found. Still, meeting with hunters from the lodges is a logical first step if the PCs want to start tracking down the missing guardian themselves.</p>"
            },
            "Returning to Great Willow": {
              "name": "重返大尊柳 Returning to Great Willow",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Returning to Great Willow\">返回大尊柳</h2>\n<p>大尊柳能感知到蕈菇被击败，并已准备好在队伍下次造访山顶时，以更为愉快的态度迎接归来的PC。木灵神如今变得乐于帮助；如果任何PC正因从蕈菇那里感染的紫痘而受苦，大尊柳会提出帮助该角色康复（它会尝试一次自然检定以进行治疗疾病）。得知林地里没有任何木灵神存在的消息让大尊柳感到失望，但没有发现尸体或木灵神遭到伤害的迹象，也让它将此视为仍有希望的理由。</p>\n<p>作为对PC所提供援助的回报，大尊柳确认柳岸镇周边区域似乎受到了诅咒。它感知不到附近还有其他木灵神；并且在PC击败蕈菇返回时，大尊柳已经开始冥想诅咒的边界。它能给PC一个他们被困区域体型的大致估计，描述为以柳岸镇为中心、向各个方向约10到16英里的范围。更重要的是，大尊柳提到西边似乎存在某种更为强大的东西——木灵神感知到了鬼打墙，但不确定那究竟是什么。尽管大尊柳的这些揭示都无法帮助PC击败影响他们的“诅咒”，但应该能让他们对自己被困区域的规模有所概念。不过，大尊柳可以确认一件事——似乎没有办法穿越迷雾，因此在可预见的时间内，应当优先把目标放在让聚落变得更加自给自足上。</p>\n<p>在《鬼季》的其余部分，大尊柳在PC造访山顶时仍会对他们保持乐于帮助；你可以按需要让木灵神为队伍提供下一步行动的建议，或提供线索，以便在你认为合适时让事情回到正轨。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Returning to Great Willow\">Returning to Great Willow</h2>\n<p>Great Willow can sense when Xungu is defeated and is ready to receive the returning PCs in a much more pleasant manner upon the party’s next visit to their hilltop. The kodama is now helpful, and if any of the PCs are suffering from purple pox caught from Xungu, Great Willow offers to help the character recover (they do so by attempting a Nature check to Treat Disease). The news that no kodama were present in the grove disappoints Great Willow, but they take the fact that there were no bodies or evidence that the kodama were harmed as a reason for hope.</p>\n<p>In return for the aid the PCs provided, Great Willow confirms that the region surrounding Willowshore appears to be cursed. They can sense no other kodama in the vicinity, and by the time the PCs return from defeating Xungu, Great Willow has already started to meditate upon the curse’s boundaries. They can give the PCs a rough estimate of the size of the region they’re trapped in, describing it as a region about 10 to 16 miles or so in every direction from Willowshore. More importantly, Great Willow mentions that something even more potent seems to lie to the west—the kodama is sensing the Wall of Ghosts, but isn’t sure what it might be. While none of Great Willow’s revelations will help the PCs defeat the “curse” that affects them, it should give them an idea of the scope of the region they’re trapped in. One thing Great Willow can confirm, though—there seems to be no way to go beyond the mists, so for the time being, goals to become more self-sufficient as a settlement should be prioritized.</p>\n<p>For the rest of <em>Season of Ghosts</em>, Great Willow remains helpful to the PCs on their visits to the hilltop; you can use the kodama to give the party advice on what to do next or to provide clues as needed to get things back on track as you see fit.</p>"
            },
            "Into the Infestation": {
              "name": "深入虫患 Into the Infestation",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">深入侵染</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>受侵染的柳树林位于蜻蜓溪西岸，柳岸镇以南（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d7infestedgr00]{D7}）。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>溪畔道路在此处渐渐缩成一条小径，通向那片曾经田园诗般的柳树林；但如今，枝叶间蔓延着一层层灰色与淡黄色的真菌。灌木丛曾经生长的地方，现在冒出了更为鲜艳的斑点蘑菇或长满疣状突起的毒蕈。</p>\n</div>\n<p>尽管外观令人不适，而且无疑会伤害此处的柳树与其他植被，但占据这片林地的真菌总体上大多无害——只有一个重大的例外。本次遭遇发生在森林中一处开阔却被真菌侵染的空地里。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>当这一轮循环在柳岸镇的思维空间中开始时，一场真菌入侵蔓延到了这片柳树林。这里曾是当地人亲近自然、追求浪漫之处，而苦迦菩提的影响像寄生虫一样黏附在那些积极的情绪上，导致危险真菌的大量涌入。这些真菌大多表现为黏菌怪，立刻蠕动着爬向周围的荒野（如今也可能作为游荡怪物周期性遭遇到），但其中有一个名为循咕的菌体人仍留在这里。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xungu.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Xungu\" alt=\"Tall mushroom-like creature with a humanoid face\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xungu.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p>循咕是苦迦菩提影响的直接物质结果；虽然他们有着“统治”这片林地数十年的记忆，但在这轮思维空间循环开始之前，他们并不存在。这名菌体人把大部分时间都花在巡逻侵染区域的边缘，寻找可以捕获的肉食来准备餐食。面对PC时，循咕起初更倾向于狡诈而非暴力。作为苦迦菩提思绪的显现，循咕说的是通用语而非萨克弗罗斯语，但这并不妨碍他们在发现PC后，讲述一段可怜（却在不自知的情况下完全虚假）的故事：他们如何被从地下菌落中驱逐出来。菌体人解释说，曾居住于此的木灵神欢迎循咕进入他们的家，但随后大家全都消失了，现在循咕又再次孤身一人。接着循咕请求一名PC留下过夜并共进一餐，这样他们就不会感到孤独。菌体人解释说自己有“秘密”要分享，但人太多时会害羞，不敢一次对太多人说。</p>\n<p>当然，这些说法全是谎言；而对PC来说幸运的是，循咕并不是特别擅长撒谎。如果队伍同意这个请求，那么一旦循咕与那名PC独处，他们就会向PC揭示所谓的秘密：其实他们非常饿，而他们要“分享”的那顿饭，就是循咕要把PC吃掉——菌体人会立刻发动攻击，试图压制落单的PC。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-xungu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">深入侵染</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.dqFdd9XhC9awkWYE]{Xungu}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>当循咕讲述这个故事时，他们会尝试一次+0的欺瞒检定以撒谎；但即使这个故事成功对抗了每名PC的察觉DC，玩家仍应自行决定要怎么做。若被指出在说谎，循咕会恼怒地哼一声，然后说道：“哼，那我想我只能将就来顿茶饭，而不是点心了！”随即发动攻击，打算捕获并吃掉整支队伍。循咕发动攻击时会试图捕获PC，希望把战斗拖得足够久，让PC因紫痘而死去，因为带痘的肉更美味。这应当能给队伍时间去救出被捕的PC，或（如果整队都被抓住）让NPC改为前来营救。无论如何，循咕都会战至死；而对逃跑的PC也只会追击几个回合，随后便返回受侵染的柳树林。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>随着循咕死亡，林地中的真菌侵染立刻开始消退，蘑菇与霉菌萎缩、融化并蒸发。仅仅一小时后，柳树林就会完全恢复。此时，正在遭受紫痘的PC会将所有针对循咕所造成之该苦难的豁免骰视为自动成功（不过，受苦难的PC仍应掷骰以确定自己是否达成大成功）。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Into the Infestation</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The infested willow grove is located on the western bank of Dragonfly Creek, south of Willowshore (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d7infestedgr00]{D7}).</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The creek-side road diminishes to a trail here as it approaches the once-idyllic grove of willow trees, but today, the foliage has become overgrown with sheets of gray and pale yellow fungi. More colorful spotted mushrooms or warty toadstools grow where underbrush once did.</p>\n</div>\n<p>While unpleasant looking and certainly harmful to the willow trees and other foliage here, the fungus that has taken over this grove is largely harmless—with one significant exception. This encounter takes place in an open but fungus-infested clearing in a forest.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When this cycle began in the Willowshore mindscape, a fungal invasion spread through this patch of willow trees. Once a place where locals came to enjoy nature and pursue romance, Kugaptee’s influence clung to those positive emotions like a parasite, resulting in an influx of dangerous fungi. The fungi mostly manifested as slime molds that immediately slithered out into the surrounding hinterlands (and that can now be periodically encountered as wandering monsters), but one, a myceloid named Xungu, remains here.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xungu.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Xungu\" alt=\"Tall mushroom-like creature with a humanoid face\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xungu.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p>Xungu is a direct physical result of Kugaptee’s influence, and while they have memories of “ruling” this grove for decades, they didn’t exist before this mindscape cycle began. The myceloid spends most of their time patrolling the perimeter of the infested patch, looking for meat to catch to prepare for meals. Faced with the PCs, Xungu is initially more duplicitous than violent. As a manifestation from Kugaptee’s thoughts, Xungu speaks Common rather than Sakvroth, but this doesn’t stop them, upon spotting the PCs, from recounting a pitiful (if unknowingly false) tale of how they were chased out from their underground colony. The myceloid explains how the kodama who dwelled here welcomed Xungu into their home, but then they all vanished, and now Xungu is all alone again. Xungu then asks one of the PCs to stay overnight and share a meal so that they won’t feel lonely. The myceloid explains they have “secrets” to share but are bashful about sharing with too many people at once.</p>\n<p>All of these claims are falsehoods, of course, and fortunately for the PCs, Xungu isn’t a particularly skilled liar. If the party agrees to this request, once Xungu and the PC are alone, they reveal to the PC that the secret is that they’re really hungry and that the meal they’ll “share” will be Xungu eating the PC—the myceloid attacks at once, hoping to overpower the lone PC.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-xungu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Into the Infestation</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.dqFdd9XhC9awkWYE]{Xungu}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>When Xungu tells this story, they attempt a +0 Deception check to Lie, but even if this story is successful against every PC’s Perception DC, the players should still make their own decisions as to what to do. Called out as a liar, Xungu huffs in frustration, then says, “Well, I suppose I’ll have to settle for a banquet instead of a snack!” and attacks, intending to capture and eat the entire party. When Xungu attacks, they try to capture PCs, hoping to draw things out long enough for PCs to perish from purple pox, since poxy meat is tastier. This should give the party time to rescue a captured PC or (if the whole party gets caught) for NPCs to come rescue them instead. Xungu fights to the death, in any event, and pursues fleeing PCs for only a few rounds before returning to the infested grove.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> With Xungu’s death, the fungus infestation in the grove immediately begins to recede, with mushrooms and mold shrinking, melting, and evaporating. After just an hour, the grove is restored fully. At this point, a PC who’s suffering from purple pox treats all saving throws against the affliction caused by Xungu as automatic successes (afflicted PCs should still roll the save to determine if they achieve a critical success, though).</p>"
            },
            "Talking with Great Willow": {
              "name": "与大尊柳交谈 Talking with Great Willow",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Talking with Great Willow\">与大尊柳交谈</h3>\n<p>一旦PC们确保了大尊柳的合作，这位木灵神便会稍微放松一些，并同意与PC们交谈。祂说话的声音细小，几乎像孩子一样，但语速缓慢且非常有条理，仿佛在谨慎斟酌用词。随着一年又一年的重复（尽管祂不明白也记不得原因），大尊柳的心智变得愈发支离破碎，而如今与他人交谈这件事，对这位木灵神而言需要刻意的专注。</p>\n<p>若有人问起树根上生长的真菌，大尊柳会略显戒备，随后又平静下来，说道：“我从南边去探望一位朋友、顺道去查看情况时带回来的感染。我正在把它压下去，但我担心我的朋友。”</p>\n<p>如果PC们询问他们试图触及唐入时所遭遇的那道雾气边界，大尊柳会会意地点点头，如下回应。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“是的。我也感应到了。那是一道诅咒。一道强大的诅咒。我能感觉到它的边缘在四面八方。我们现在被关在笼子里。夏季第一天发生时，我很困惑。我独自一人。我听不见朋友们的声音。我跳去探望我最亲近的朋友，可她不在那里，那里却有一朵脾气恶劣的蘑菇，我不得不一路逃回这里。独自一人。我不知道该怎么办。我不敢在这诅咒环绕之下再离开这棵树，但我可以从这里寻找它的边缘。我会告诉你们更多，但在那之前，我需要知道我的朋友是安全的。你们要去把她从那愤怒的蘑菇手中救出来，然后我就会帮忙。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>每到夏季第一天，当思维空间的年度循环重置时，大尊柳都能感应到环境的变化，但每一次都弄不清其原因。并且每一年，祂都会使用通身入林从自己这棵柳树的守护之地旅行到柳岸镇以南近5英里的一片柳树林，去探望那里的柳树群落之神灵——一位与大尊柳不同、并未被卷入思维空间的神灵。今年，事情变得更糟：苦迦菩提的影响使一场敌对真菌的侵染得以在这片林地中滋生蔓延。</p>\n<p>当大尊柳使用通身入林旅行到那片林地时，发现那里已被真菌侵占，却不见居住于此的木灵神的踪影（这些木灵神避开了被拖入思维空间——见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05visitinggrea00#the-last-kodama]{最后的木灵神}）。面对一株敌对真菌的攻击，又已用掉当天唯一一次通身入林的施放，大尊柳被迫徒步、不太体面地一路返回这座山丘顶端的守护之地——而在此过程中，也将入侵性的真菌孢子一并带了回来。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果一名PC在一次@Check[nature|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定中成功以回忆知识，他们可以与大尊柳分享一些对抗真菌侵染的乐于帮助技巧。即便没有这份协助，在PC们返回之前，大尊柳仍会清除侵染，但祂会对这条建议心怀感激——因这份帮助，给予队伍20 XP。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Talking with Great Willow\">Talking with Great Willow</h3>\n<p>Once the PCs secure Great Willow’s cooperation, the kodama relaxes somewhat and agrees to talk to the PCs. They speak in a tiny, almost childlike voice, but in a slow and very methodical manner, as if taking care with their word selection. Great Willow’s mind has grown increasingly fractured with each repetition of the year (even though they don’t understand or remember why), and the act of speaking with others requires deliberate concentration for the kodama these days.</p>\n<p>If asked about the fungus growing on the tree roots, Great Willow bristles a bit, then calms and says, “An infection I brought back from a visit to check on a friend to the south. I am fighting it back, but I fear for my friend.”</p>\n<p>If the PCs ask about the misty border that they faced when they attempted to reach Karahai, Great Willow nods in understanding, replying as follows.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Yes. I sense it too. It is a curse. A powerful one. I can feel its edges all around. We are in a cage now. When it happened on the first day of summer, I was confused. I was alone. I could not hear my friends’ voices. I jumped to visit my closest friend and they were not there, but a foul-tempered mushroom was, and I had to run away all the way back to here. Alone. I don’t know what to do. I dare not leave this tree again when this curse is all around, but I can look for its edges from here. I will tell you more, but before I do, I need to know my friend is safe. You will go to save her from the angry mushroom, and then I will help.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>Every first day of summer, when the mindscape’s yearly cycle resets, Great Willow senses the change to the environment but is, each time, at a loss as to its cause. And every year, they use nature’s pathway to travel from their willow tree ward to a willow grove nearly 5 miles to the south of Willowshore to check up on the kami of a grove of willow trees located there—a kami who, unlike Great Willow, wasn’t pulled into the mindscape. This year, things have changed for the worse: Kugaptee’s influence allowed an infestation of hostile fungi to bloom in this grove.</p>\n<p>When Great Willow used nature’s pathway to travel to the grove, they found the place infested with fungi, with no sign of the kodama who dwelt there (these kodama avoided being drawn into the mindscape—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05visitinggrea00#the-last-kodama]{The Last Kodama}). Faced with aggression from a hostile fungus and having used their only casting of nature’s pathway for the day, Great Willow was forced to make the undignified trek back home to their ward atop this hill on foot—and in so doing, tracked invasive fungal spores with them.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If a PC succeeds at a @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, they can share some helpful techniques with Great Willow on how to fight back against the fungal infestation. Without this aid, Great Willow still removes the infestation by the time the PCs return, but they’re grateful for the suggestion—grant the party 20 XP for the help.</p>"
            },
            "Visiting Great Willow": {
              "name": "造访大尊柳 Visiting Great Willow",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">拜访大尊柳</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的大尊柳（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w37thegreatw00]{W37}）坐落在俯瞰城镇的一座山丘之上，是一处醒目的地标，也是许多当地人引以为傲的象征。据说，在慧智大师 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} 寻找昙杉木的旅途中，这棵树是她到访的第一站；多年来，这棵树作为城镇象征之一屹立至今，然而通往山顶的道路或小径从未被修建过。人人都知道树中栖居着一位灵——一位自称“大尊柳”的神灵（kami），守望着柳岸镇，但很少有人认为去打扰或可能惹恼这位灵明智。因此，拜访大尊柳往往极为罕见，而且只会发生在柳岸镇需要向灵界寻求建议之时——比如如今聚落正面临的这种时刻。</p>\n<p>除了向大尊柳求取智慧外，长老们还建议PC们组织柳岸镇的人民准备一份供奉带去树前，希望借此博得那位灵在守护柳岸镇时的垂青。至少，带上供奉应当能让与灵交谈更为顺利。长老们建议供奉美酒或清酒；任何在进行 @Check[nature|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 的回忆知识检定时成功的PC也会得出同样的建议。若PC在该检定中大成功，则会意识到更好的供奉是一条定制的、手工编制的扭绞绳索——一条注连绳（shimenawa）——木灵（kodama）可以用它披挂在树枝上，或用来协助自己制作魂魄之绳。</p>\n<p>美酒或清酒可在镇上购买，但若PC决定供奉注连绳，最好由其中一人亲手编制这条绳索；若这份礼物并非出自制作者之手，木灵很可能会觉得受辱。注连绳不必特别长——PC只需花费3 gp的材料并成功通过一次 @Check[crafting|dc:16] 检定，即可用1小时行动制作出合适的供奉（大失败表示材料被毁，无法在下一次尝试中再次使用）。</p>\n<p>抵达大尊柳需要穿过约1英里的较稀疏林地徒步前行，但由于途中有时需要攀行陡坡，此行程被视为困难地形。移动速度为25尺的一行人，从柳岸镇到大尊柳大约需要20分钟。当PC接近山顶时，森林逐渐稀疏，显露出一片空地。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>山顶四周的树林变得稀薄，在顶端留下了一片直径八十尺的空地。山丘之巅、空地中央生长着大尊柳——在这片森林的大部分区域里唯一的一棵柳树。大尊柳高近九十尺，对同类而言也格外巨大。然而，大尊柳在柳岸镇历史中受人敬畏的原因，更多在于据说栖居其中的那位灵。至少已有数年无人拜访大尊柳，但即便站在空地边缘，也能看出这棵树似乎出了问题：某种灰色的真菌生长物仿佛侵染了它较低处的根系。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-great-willow.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Great Willow\" alt=\"A creature that looks like a stack of rocks\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-great-willow.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC踏入空地时，大尊柳从树中现身，在树根间摆出防御姿态，双拳高举。他们向PC发出挑战，要求解释为何胆敢靠近。注意：进入树与其木灵30尺范围内的PC将处于大尊柳的扰乱凝视影响范围之内。</p>\n<p>当PC说明来意后，给予他们一次机会，尝试进行 @Check[diplomacy|dc:24|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression] 检定，以对大尊柳建立印象；大尊柳的初始态度为不友善。若PC表明他们为大尊柳带来了供奉，则DC降低10，改为 @Check[diplomacy|dc:14|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression]。若PC带来的供奉是手工制作的注连绳，则他们的检定结果还会提高一个成功等级。</p>\n<p>若大尊柳仍为不友善，他们会要求PC立刻离开，并“明天再来”；若PC照做，他们就必须带来一份全新的供奉。每次他们返回时，建立印象的DC降低2。</p>\n<p>若大尊柳变为敌对，他们会愤怒尖啸，指责PC是“诅咒的源头”，并发动攻击。大尊柳并不以杀死PC为目标，而是想把他们吓退；若PC呼吁停战，他们便会脱离战斗。他们不会追击PC越过空地边缘；若其生命值降至30点以下，他们会撤回到树中与之融合。若PC逃走并在日后再次返回，则对大尊柳建立印象的DC提高2。</p>\n<p>若大尊柳被提升至不关心或友善，他们会平静下来，同意与PC交谈，细节见下文“与大尊柳交谈”。</p>\n<p>在PC解决南方的真菌侵染事件之前（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05intotheinfes00]{Into the Infestation}），大尊柳无法被变为友善。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.xYiOzfdmf5NPIw9g]{大尊柳}</span><span>生物 5</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">小型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">神灵</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵体</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">木质</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.QcuXRcsJJZsAZlBk]{Willow's Parting Gift} <br />\n  若PC让大尊柳变为友善，那么当他们准备离开时，感激的木灵会赠予他们一份临别礼物——一条由超自然柔韧的编织柳枝制成的<em>次级扭结细绳</em>。\n</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>最后的木灵</h1>\n  <p>大尊柳尚未意识到、但很快就会明白（正如他们在此前每一个思维空间循环中都曾如此）的事实是：他们是这一地区唯一还在的木灵。作为靠近赫总督仪式的副作用，他们与柳岸镇的居民一同死去，如今也同样被困在此处。该地区其他木灵朋友在现实世界中继续前行，只留下大尊柳独自一人（他们每一个也都在哀悼大尊柳的消失）。如果PC在本战役的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow]{第四幕} 开始时成功让柳岸镇的人民回到现代时代，大尊柳也会随之复原；但在那之前，随着冒险之路的推进，这位木灵会变得越来越退缩、越来越抑郁。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Visiting Great Willow</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Willowshore’s Great Willow (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w37thegreatw00]{W37}) sits atop a hill overlooking town, a visible landmark and a source of pride among many locals. Said to be the first place Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} visited on her search for the Tan Sugi, the tree has endured through the years as one of the town’s symbols, yet no road or trail has ever been laid to the hill’s summit. Everyone knows that a spirit dwells within the tree, a kami who calls themself Great Willow and who watches over the town, yet few feel it’s wise to disturb or potentially annoy the spirit. As such, visits to Great Willow tend to happen rarely, and only at times when Willowshore needs advice from the spirit world—times such as those now facing the settlement.</p>\n<p>In addition to seeking wisdom from Great Willow, the elders suggest to the PCs that they organize an offering from the townspeople to bring to the tree, in hopes of currying the spirit’s favor in protecting Willowshore. At the very least, bringing an offering should help make conversing with the spirit easier. The elders suggest an offering of wine or sake, as can any PC who succeeds at a @Check[nature|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge. A PC who critically succeeds at this check realizes an even better offering would be a custom-made, hand-crafted twisted rope—a shimenawa—that a kodama could use to drape over the tree’s branches or to aid in their own creation of spiritual ropes.</p>\n<p>Wine or sake can be purchased in town, but if the PCs decide to offer a shimenawa, it’s best for one of them to craft the braided rope themselves, as the kodama will likely be insulted if such a gift is delivered by hands that didn’t craft it. The shimenawa need not be particularly long—a PC can craft an appropriate offering with an expenditure of 3 gp on materials and a successful @Check[crafting|dc:16] check as a 1-hour activity (a critical failure indicates the materials are ruined and can’t be reused on another attempt).</p>\n<p>It’s about a 1-mile walk through relatively light forest to reach the Great Willow, but since the terrain involves navigating a steep slope at times, this trip is considered difficult terrain. A party that moves at a speed of 25 feet can make the trip from Willowshore to the Great Willow in about 20 minutes. As the PCs approach the hilltop, the forest thins into a clearing.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The forest thins around the hilltop, leaving an eighty-foot-diameter clearing at its summit. Atop the hill in the center of the clearing grows the Great Willow—the only willow tree present in much of the forest. Looming at a height of nearly ninety feet, the Great Willow is also quite large for its kind. Yet the reason the Great Willow has held such a place of reverence in Willowshore’s history has more to do with the spirit said to dwell within it. At least a few years have passed since anyone has visited the Great Willow, but even from the clearing’s edge, it’s apparent that something seems amiss with the tree, for some sort of gray fungal growth has seemingly infested its lower roots.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-great-willow.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Great Willow\" alt=\"A creature that looks like a stack of rocks\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-great-willow.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> As the PCs enter the clearing, Great Willow emerges from the tree to adopt a defensive pose among its roots, fists upraised. They call out a challenge to the PCs, demanding they explain why they dare approach. Note that PCs who come within 30 feet of the tree and its kodama will be in range of Great Willow’s Distracting Gaze.</p>\n<p>When the PCs explain themselves, allow them a chance to attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:24|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression] check to Make an Impression on Great Willow, whose starting attitude is unfriendly. If the PCs reveal that they have an offering for Great Willow, the DC drops by 10 to @Check[diplomacy|dc:14|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make an Impression]. If the offering the PCs bring is a handmade shimenawa, then they also increase the result of their check by one degree of success.</p>\n<p>If Great Willow remains unfriendly, they demand the PCs leave at once and “come back tomorrow”; if the PCs do so, they’ll need to bring a brand new offering. Each time they return, the DC to Make an Impression is reduced by 2.</p>\n<p>If Great Willow becomes hostile, they shriek in rage, accuse the PCs of being “the source of the curse,” and attack. Great Willow doesn’t aim to kill PCs as much as to frighten them away and breaks off from combat if the PCs call for a truce. They won’t pursue the PCs beyond the edge of the clearing, and they retreat to the tree to merge with it if reduced to fewer than 30 Hit Points. If the PCs flee and then return at a later date, the DC to Make an Impression on Great Willow increases by 2.</p>\n<p>If Great Willow is made indifferent or friendly, they calm down and agree to speak to the PCs, as detailed below under Talking with Great Willow.</p>\n<p>Great Willow can’t be made friendly until the PCs solve the fungus infestation situation down south (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05intotheinfes00]{Into the Infestation}).</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.xYiOzfdmf5NPIw9g]{Great Willow}</span><span>Creature 5</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Small</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Kami</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Spirit</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Wood</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.QcuXRcsJJZsAZlBk]{Willow's Parting Gift} <br />\n  If the PCs made Great Willow friendly, once they prepare to leave, the grateful kodama gives them a parting gift—a <em>lesser twisting twine</em> made of supernaturally supple woven willow branches.\n</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>The Last Kodama</h1>\n  <p>What Great Willow doesn’t yet realize, but will soon enough (as they’ve done so in every mindscape cycle before), is that they’re the only kodama present in the region. As a side effect of their proximity to Governor Heh’s ritual, they perished along with the citizens of Willowshore and are now trapped here as well. Great Willow’s other kodama friends throughout the region have gone on in the real world, leaving Great Willow alone (each of them mourning Great Willow’s disappearance as well). If the PCs succeed at restoring the people of Willowshore to the modern age at the beginning of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow]{Act 4} of this campaign, Great Willow will be restored as well, but until then, the kodama grows more and more withdrawn and depressed as the Adventure Path progresses.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "The Mists": {
              "name": "迷雾 The Mists",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Mists\">迷雾</h1>\n<p>总督及其宅邸与仆从的消失固然令人忧心，但很快，镇民们最担心的事变成了：一种诡异的迷雾正阻止任何人从柳岸镇出发走得太远。小镇相对自给自足，但一旦失去贸易，来临的冬天将会很艰难。随着这片神秘迷雾带来的新现实在镇上逐渐定型，人们需要有英雄可供仰望——而PC们在未来数月里正好能承担这个角色。眼下，镇中长老对PC们有一项非常明确的请求：他们希望查明笼罩柳岸镇的这种效果究竟扩展到什么程度。这些诡异的迷雾只是阻止人们前往海岸与唐入吗？还是会将整个地区完全包围——若是如此，又到底包围到什么范围？</p>\n<p>单纯通过探索这“诅咒”的边界、沿着迷雾绕行一圈来确定其触及范围，固然是一种方法，但那将是一段漫长、潜在危险的跋涉，要穿越无路可循的荒野。相较之下，PC们所信任的那位镇中长老建议他们去拜访镇子北面山丘顶上的大尊柳。那里栖居着一位本地魂魄，其与边地荒野的联系应能让他们对眼下发生之事提供宝贵的洞见。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>沿边界前行</h2>\n  <p>思维空间的迷雾边界只有在肉身穿越时才会显现；一旦越界，旅行者会迷惘困惑、失去方向片刻，随即又会退回思维空间，回到自己最初跨越边界的那个位置。由于没有任何视觉线索可供追踪，除非反复进行这一过程，否则无法沿着边界前进；因此通过探索来绘制思维空间边界会显得重复而复杂。一旦某名PC抵达一处边界穿过的六角格，他们可以通过在该六角格内花费4小时进行搜索，以穷尽式探索与反复折返、一次又一次地与边界交互的方式，绘制出边界在该六角格内的走向。因此，PC在一天的工作中最多能绘制出两个相邻六角格的边界，随后便会陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>注意：鬼打墙作为思维空间西侧额外的一道边界，确实是一道实体且可见的屏障——参见第60页以了解该地貌的更多信息，以及PC可以如何与其交互。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Mists\">The Mists</h1>\n<p>While the disappearance of the governor and his manor and staff is worrisome, the discovery that a strange mist is preventing anyone from traveling too far from Willowshore quickly becomes the major concern of its citizens. The town is relatively self-sufficient, but without trade, the coming winter will be difficult. While the new reality of this mysterious mist settles in on the town, its people will need heroes to look up to—a role the PCs are primed to fill in the coming months. For now, the town elders have a very specific request for the PCs: they’d like to determine the extent of the effect that surrounds Willowshore. Do these strange mists merely prevent travel to the coast and to Karahai? Or do they completely encircle the region—and if so, to what extent?</p>\n<p>While simply exploring the limits of the “curse” and following the mist in a circuit around the region is one way to determine its reach, this would be a long, potentially dangerous slog through trackless wilderness. Instead, the town elder favored by the PCs suggests they pay a visit to the Great Willow that stands on the hilltop just north of town. There dwells a local spirit whose connection to the hinterland wilderness should allow them to provide valuable insight into what’s going on.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Following the Border</h2>\n  <p>The mindscape’s misty border doesn’t manifest until one physically crosses it, at which point the traveler spends a few moments confused and disoriented, only to step back into the mindscape at the point they crossed the border in the first place. Since there’s no visual cue to follow without repeating this process, mapping out the mindscape’s borders by exploring is repetitive and complicated. Once a PC reaches a hex through which the border runs, they can map out the border’s path through that hex by spending 4 hours Searching that hex through a process of exhaustive exploration and backtracking to interact with the border over and over. A PC can thus map out the border of two adjacent hexes in a day’s work before becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued}.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Note that the Wall of Ghosts, which serves as an additional border along the mindscape’s western side, is very much a physical and visual barrier—see page 60 for more information about this feature and how the PCs can interact with it.</p>"
            },
            "Songs at Canary Inn": {
              "name": "玉鸟客栈的歌曲 Songs at Canary Inn",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">玉鸟客栈的歌声</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>当PC们接近玉鸟客栈的废墟时，他们会听见一个甜美的嗓音唱着一首关于蝴蝶与梦的歌。越靠近客栈，歌声就越清晰。一旦PC们进入能看见破败客栈的距离，向他们宣读以下内容（注意第二段包含对生物的描述——如果PC们的行动会影响这些生物正在做的事，请按需调整这段文字）。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">声音</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.zLGowtHaJW7U2VZM.PlaylistSound.exPXrONS2vLVacTT]{歌声}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>本遭遇使用玉鸟客栈地图。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>林间道路在此与岔路相接，其北侧坐落着数间部分被烧毁的单卧小屋。这六七座平房曾组成玉鸟客栈，但如今多数建筑已被烧成瓦砾，尽管周围林地已从火灾中恢复。最北边那间看上去大体完好。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hongrui-fan.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Fan Hongrui\" alt=\"A dark haired woman in a red cap holds out two hands and appears to be yelling\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hongrui-fan.webp')\" />\n<p>有三道身影坐在那栋建筑南边的空地上。其中两道身影披着长长的灰色兜帽斗篷，背对着来路而坐，全部注意力都被第三道身影吸引——一个披着红兜帽斗篷的小孩站在他们面前，唱着关于蝴蝶与梦的歌；然而那旋律比起其天真主题所暗示的轻快，更显得忧郁低沉。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>那名红兜帽小孩是范弘蕊，她用<strong>幻象伪装</strong>法术掩盖了自己草人的真实面貌。当PC们靠近时，允许他们进行@Check[perception|dc:22]检定以看穿魔法伪装，并意识到这孩子其实是一个沾满鲜血、能够活动的稻草塑像，由干草编成，靠缕缕幽灵般的<strong>灵质</strong>黏合。另两道身影则是普通草人，生前是弘蕊的旅行<strong>伙伴</strong>——迟宏心与南哲宏伴。从背后看，他们像披斗篷的小型类人生物；但一旦他们对PC们做出反应（或从正面被看到），其真正的超自然本质便再也无法忽视。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">效果</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">拖拽@UUID[Item.ZIXn4CFpQ9ySzVPr]{Fan Hongrui True Form}效果以关闭她的伪装</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>尽管这些草人对活人充满嫉妒的怒火，他们并不会一见到PC们就攻击。相反，当弘蕊注意到他们时，她会停止歌唱，沉默地打量队伍。另两名草人发出草叶摩挲的窸窣声，慌忙站起，分别站到她两侧，准备保卫她。</p>\n<p>弘蕊很好奇PC们为何来此。若PC中有人携带乐器或明显是表演者，她会指向那名角色，用凄楚的声音问：“你们是来取悦我们的吗？已经很久没人为我们表演了。”若有PC为她表演，该PC必须尝试一次@Check[performance|dc:17]检定。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong>表演抚平了草人的怒意，让他们以一种不会引发嫉妒或失落的方式忆起生命之美。弘蕊的幻象消散，显露出她真实的模样；她感谢表演者送出的美好礼物，然后询问PC们为何来拜访她。她允许每位PC各问她一个问题，她会尽其所能作答。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>弘蕊的怒意稍稍被安抚。她不会解除幻象，但仍会询问PC们为何来拜访她。她允许队伍提出一个问题，她会尽其所能作答。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>表演未能打动她，弘蕊的神情变得更阴沉——她警告队伍不该在此，必须立刻离开。若PC们不立刻照办，草人便会发动攻击。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong>表演尚未结束，草人们就已开始讥笑着咯咯作声，并立刻发动攻击。</p>\n<p>如果弘蕊被安抚到愿意回答问题，你可以按自己意愿作答。她对环绕柳岸镇的思维空间一无所知；但若被问及总督，她的表情会阴沉下来，并说他是龙华的哈巴狗，是个人的敌人。她不知道龙华已经崩溃，也不知道贺总督已经失踪；但若她得知他不见了，她会说：“掌权者终会滥用或抛弃自己的责任，只要时间够久——庆幸你们的总督选择离开你们，而不是给你们的城镇带来更糟的东西。”</p>\n<p>在回答完问题后，若有PC在表演检定中取得大成功，她会如释重负地叹息——她与另外两名草人一同淡去，他们的芦苇般身躯坍倒在地。若柳岸镇的思维空间最终被允许重置，这三者会在明年归来；但在那之前，这三个草人不会再生。反之，若PC们仅取得成功，她会要求队伍立刻离开——任何留下的人都会遭到攻击。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-hongrui-fan.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">玉鸟客栈的歌声</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.ZcDfbztikxszO9uG]{Fan Hongrui} @UUID[Actor.k8gFEY6O5PdKBCEL]{Thatchlings (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>若草人发动攻击，三者都用察觉投掷先攻，并在其回合开始时施展分心咯咯笑。弘蕊留在远处，对PC们使用<strong>念动射弹</strong>，而另外两名草人则逼近进行近战。若其中任意一名草人被摧毁，或有PC与弘蕊进行近战交战，她便会释放<strong>复仇怒嚎</strong>。草人会战斗到被摧毁为止，但不会追击逃跑的PC超过离废墟半英里的距离。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.X9LtEF98l2AMbaMS]{弘蕊酬恩} @UUID[Actor.ne1myAHotXIWtfLL]{Shallow Grave} <br />在那场悲剧般的大火摧毁玉鸟客栈之后，两名叛乱者的遗体被草草埋进庭院中央的浅墓中，位置正是PC们初次造访时三名草人所在之处（弘蕊的遗体从未被找回）。在此区域进行搜索且在一次@Check[perception|dc:16|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定中成功的PC，会注意到焦黑土壤中的异常之处，并辨认出那是浅墓。</p>\n<p>若PC们掘出遗体，他们会发现两具骷髅——那是宏心与宏伴仅存的残骸。若PC们确实让这两具遗体得到妥善安葬，则在本次思维空间循环中，这三名草人不会再次再生。</p>\n<p>奇怪的是，一件曾属于弘蕊的红色斗篷也躺在坟中。若PC们确保遗体得到妥善安葬，有一名PC（最好是进行表演检定的那位）会突然感到一阵谢意，并明白弘蕊希望他们带走她的斗篷以表达谢意。同样地，若某PC在表演检定中大成功，当草人淡去时，那名PC会感到想去掘开坟墓并取走斗篷作为奖赏。</p>\n<p>若弘蕊以谢意将斗篷赠与PC们，它会作为一件名为<em>弘蕊酬恩</em>的独特魔法物品发挥作用。若PC们在未获得她的感激之下取走斗篷，它会变成诅咒物品：若穿戴超过1分钟，它会突然增重至5容纳，并与PC融合（关于诅咒物品的更多信息见<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>第306页）。该诅咒可照常解除，但也会在两具骷髅得到妥善且庄重的安葬后立刻消退，届时斗篷会变为弘蕊酬恩。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们让三名草人得以安息，除他们在战斗中击败这些草人本应获得的奖励外，再额外给予40 XP。柳岸镇的思维空间中将不再遭遇草人，任何随机遭遇若结果为草人，则视为无遭遇。此外，该地区整体感觉会稍微没那么闹鬼。这能提升镇民士气，且PC们在北岭人与南岸获得1点声望点数。</p>\n<p>尽管这条调查线索对PC们而言走到了尽头，镇中长者仍鼓励他们继续追查另外两条线索，并希望他们最终能协助解开总督失踪之谜。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Songs at Canary Inn</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As the PCs approach the ruins of Canary Inn, they’ll hear a sweet voice singing a song about butterflies and dreams. The closer they get to the inn, the clearer the song gets. Once the PCs come in sight of the ruined inn, read them the following (note that the second paragraph includes descriptions of the creatures—make sure to adjust this text as necessary if the PCs’ actions would impact the creatures’ activities).</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Sound</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.zLGowtHaJW7U2VZM.PlaylistSound.exPXrONS2vLVacTT]{Singing}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>Use the Canary Inn map for this encounter.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The forest road comes to a junction here, just north of which sit several partially burned single-bedroom structures. These half-dozen bungalows once comprised the Canary Inn, but today most of the buildings are burned to rubble, although the surrounding woodland has recovered from the fire. The northernmost structure seems mostly intact.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hongrui-fan.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Fan Hongrui\" alt=\"A dark haired woman in a red cap holds out two hands and appears to be yelling\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-hongrui-fan.webp')\" />\n<p>Three figures sit in the clearing just south of that structure. Two of the figures wear long gray hooded cloaks and sit facing away, their attention rapt on the third figure who stands before them—a young child wearing a red-hooded cloak whose song about butterflies and dreams floats along on a melody that feels much more maudlin and downbeat than its whimsical topic would suggest.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The red-hooded child is Hongrui, who has disguised her thatchling reality using an illusory disguise spell. As the PCs approach, allow them @Check[perception|dc:22] checks to see through the magical disguise and to realize the child is, in fact, a blood-soaked, mobile effigy made of dried grass held together by wisps of ghostly ectoplasm. The other two figures are regular thatchlings who, in life, were Hongrui’s traveling companions Chi Hongxin and Nanzhe Hongban. Viewed from behind, they appear as Small cloaked humanoids, but once they react to the PCs (or are viewed from the front), their true supernatural nature is impossible to miss.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">Drag on the @UUID[Item.ZIXn4CFpQ9ySzVPr]{Fan Hongrui True Form} Effect to turn off her disguise</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>While the thatchlings are filled with jealous anger toward the living, they don’t attack the PCs on sight. Instead, once Hongrui notices them, she stops her song and regards the party silently. The other two thatchlings scramble to their feet with the sound of rustling grass to stand at either side, ready to defend her.</p>\n<p>Hongrui is curious to find out why the PCs are here. If any of the PCs carry a musical instrument or are otherwise obviously a performer, she points to that character and asks in a forlorn voice, “Are you here to entertain us? It’s been so long since we’ve had others to perform for us.” If a PC does perform for her, that PC must attempt a @Check[performance|dc:17] check.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The performance soothes the thatchlings’ anger and reminds them of the beauty of life in a way that doesn’t evoke feelings of jealousy or loss. Hongrui’s illusion fades to reveal what she actually is, and she thanks the performer for the beautiful gift before asking why the PCs have come to visit her. She allows each PC to ask her one question that she’ll answer to the best of her ability.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> Hongrui’s anger is soothed somewhat. She doesn’t lower her illusion but still asks the PCs why they’ve come to visit her. She allows the party to ask one question that she’ll answer to the best of her ability.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The performance fails to impress, and Hongrui’s expression grows darker—she warns the party that they shouldn’t be here and should leave at once. If the PCs don’t comply immediately, the thatchlings attack.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The thatchlings begin giggling in mockery well before the performance ends and attack at once.</p>\n<p>If Hongrui is soothed enough that she answers questions, feel free to reply to questions as you see fit. She knows nothing about the mindscape surrounding Willowshore, but if asked about the governor, her expression darkens and she says he was a lapdog of Lung Wa and an enemy to the individual. She has no idea that Lung Wa has collapsed, or that Governor Heh has vanished, but if she learns that he has gone missing, she says, “Those in power will always abuse or abandon their responsibility, given time—be grateful your governor chose to leave you rather than inflict upon your town something worse.”</p>\n<p>Once she has answered their questions, if a PC achieved a critical success on the Performance check, she sighs in relief—she and the other thatchlings fade away, their reed bodies collapsing to the ground. If the Willowshore mindscape is allowed to eventually reset, the three return next year, but until then, these three thatchlings won’t rejuvenate. If instead the PCs only achieved a success, she asks the party to leave at once—those who remain are attacked.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-hongrui-fan.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Songs at Canary Inn</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.ZcDfbztikxszO9uG]{Fan Hongrui} @UUID[Actor.k8gFEY6O5PdKBCEL]{Thatchlings (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If the thatchlings attack, all three roll Perception for initiative and begin to Giggle Distractingly as their turn begins. Hongrui remains at range, using telekinetic projectile against the PCs while the other two thatchlings move into melee. If either of those thatchlings are destroyed, or if a PC engages Hongrui in melee, she unleashes a Howl of Vengeful Fury. The thatchlings fight until they’re destroyed but don’t pursue fleeing PCs further than a half mile from the ruins.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.X9LtEF98l2AMbaMS]{Hongrui’s Gratitude} @UUID[Actor.ne1myAHotXIWtfLL]{Shallow Grave} <br />After the tragic fire destroyed Canary Inn, the bodies of two of the rebels were given unceremonious shallow graves in the middle of the courtyard, exactly where the three thatchlings were located when the PCs first visit (Hongrui’s body was never recovered). A PC who Searches in this area and succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:16|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check notices irregularities in the charred soil that they recognize as shallow graves.</p>\n<p>If the PCs exhume the bodies, they’ll find two skeletons—all that remains of Hongxin and Hongban. If the PCs see that these two bodies are given proper burials, the three thatchlings don’t rejuvenate again during this mindscape cycle.</p>\n<p>Curiously, a red cloak that once belonged to Hongrui lies in the graves as well. If the PCs see to it that the bodies receive proper burials, one PC (the one who attempted the Performance check, preferably) feels a sudden sense of gratitude and understands that Hongrui wants them to take her cloak as thanks for the kindness. Likewise, if a PC critically succeeded at the Performance check, when the thatchlings fade, that PC feels the urge to exhume the grave and claim the cloak as a reward.</p>\n<p>If Hongrui offers the cloak to the PCs as thanks, it functions as a unique magic item called <em>Hongrui’s Gratitude</em>. If the PCs claim the cloak without her gratitude, it becomes cursed, suddenly increasing to 5 Bulk if worn for longer than 1 minute at which point it fuses with the PC (see <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> page 306 for more information about cursed items). This curse can be lifted normally but also fades as soon as the two skeletons are given a proper, respectful burial, whereupon the cloak becomes Hongrui’s Gratitude.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs bring rest to the three thatchlings, grant them 40 XP in addition to what they would’ve earned for defeating them in combat. Thatchlings are no longer encountered in the Willowshore mindscape, and any random encounter resulting in a thatchling is treated as no encounter. Additionally, the region feels slightly less haunted overall. This improves the townsfolk’s morale and the PCs gain 1 Reputation Point with Northridge and Southbank.</p>\n<p>While this line of investigation ends at a dead end for the PCs, the town elder encourages them to pursue the other two leads and hopes that they might ultimately help solve the mystery of the vanished governor.</p>"
            },
            "Ghosts in the Grass": {
              "name": "草丛中的幽灵 Ghosts in the Grass",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">草丛中的幽魂</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低级 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>洪蕊之死的确切经过使她扭曲成了一名不死生物——一只@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21redhoodedtha00]{红头草人}。早在柳岸镇的思维空间形成之前，她就一直把那些无法转生的灵魂转化为草人；这些草人愈发频繁地在柳岸腹地的森林中出没。PC们甚至可能在被长老们联系、要求他们调查此事之前，就已经在林中遭遇过其中一些亡魂。</p>\n<p>一旦长老们要求PC们前往玉鸟客栈的废墟（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d4canaryinn000]{D4}），他们就需要向西北行进，沿着小径或穿越森林前进，因为连接玉鸟客栈与柳岸镇的主路在葫芦湖以东被思维空间的边缘截断。长老们建议先沿着杜月江东岸向北顺着道路走，然后再走一条更往东的旧猎人小径，尝试抵达客栈。长老们还指出，如果事实证明玉鸟客栈位于“诅咒”的边缘之外，那就说明他们关于此事与贺知府失踪有关联的理论是错误的。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-thatchling.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">草丛中的幽魂</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低级 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.k8gFEY6O5PdKBCEL]{草人（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>无论PC们选择哪条路线，在前往玉鸟客栈的途中都会遭遇一群草人。这场遭遇发生在道路较宽的一段、或森林中一片空地附近；那里生长着一大片高草。PC们穿过此处时，会在风声或细雨的沙沙声之上，隐约听到怪异的咯咯笑声——也可能听到一声轻轻的“救救我”的耳语，但那听起来更像威胁而不是求援。无论PC们是否调查，藏在草丛中的三只草人都会窜出来攻击他们，并战斗至被摧毁为止。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>遭遇结束后，让PC们可以尝试进行@Check[religion|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定，以回忆知识了解有关草人的信息。请记住，尽管这些怪物是在本幕中才首次登场、玩家也对它们不熟悉，但在神门，关于草人的传闻与故事属于当地民俗的一部分。若该检定获得大成功或大失败，则角色必然知道：草人以草构成的替代身躯使其惧怕火焰；而草人的出现也意味着该地区可能还存在一只红头草人——一种能够制造草人衍体的不死生物。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Ghosts in the Grass</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The exact circumstances of Hongrui’s death twisted her into an undead creature—a @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21redhoodedtha00]{Red-Hooded Thatchling}. Since even before the formation of Willowshore’s mindscape, she has been converting the souls of those unable to reincarnate into the thatchlings that increasingly haunt the forests of the Willowshore hinterlands. The PCs might even have encountered some of these spirits out in the forest before being contacted by the elders to investigate this situation.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs are asked by the elders to travel to the ruins of Canary Inn (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d4canaryinn000]{D4}), they’ll need to make the journey northwest using trails or traveling through the forest, as the primary road that connects Canary Inn to Willowshore is interrupted just east of Gourd Lake by the edge of the mindscape. The elders suggest following the road up north along the east bank of the Duyue River, then taking one of the old hunter’s trails further east to try to reach the inn. If it turns out that Canary Inn lies beyond the edge of the “curse,” the elders note, then that suggests their theory of the link to Governor Heh’s disappearance is false.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-thatchling.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Ghosts in the Grass</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.k8gFEY6O5PdKBCEL]{Thatchlings (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Regardless of the route the PCs take, they encounter a group of thatchlings during their journey to the Canary Inn. This encounter takes place in an area where a wide spot in the road or a clearing in the forest allows for a large clearing of tall grass to grow. As the PCs pass through the area, the sound of strange giggling, or perhaps even a single whispered cry of “help me” that sounds more like a threat than a call for aid, becomes apparent just over the sound of wind or soft rainfall. Whether or not the PCs investigate, the three thatchlings hiding in the grass scurry out to attack them, fighting until destroyed.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>In the aftermath of the encounter, allow the PCs to attempt @Check[religion|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] checks to Recall Knowledge about thatchlings. Remember that while these monsters are newly introduced in this act and that players are unfamiliar with them, in Shenmen, rumors and stories of thatchlings are a part of local folklore. With a critical success at this check, a character certainly knows that thatchlings, with their surrogate bodies made of grass, are vulnerable to fire and that the presence of thatchlings suggests a red-hooded thatchling—an undead capable of creating thatchling spawn—is present in the region as well.</p>"
            },
            "The Missing Governor": {
              "name": "失踪的总督 The Missing Governor",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Missing Governor\">失踪的总督</h1>\n<p>不同于迷雾或丑小乖，寻找失踪总督并没有明显的切入点。对他曾经宅邸所在地点的勘查毫无所获——甚至没有任何迹象表明那里曾经矗立过一座建筑，这也让一种流行理论更显可信：不管是什么把宅邸一并夺走，确实是一股强大的超自然力量。</p>\n<p>在缺乏任何明显线索的情况下，胡太婆与老松木得出结论：某种对总督怀有怨念的超自然力量必定在这场神秘消失中扮演了某种角色。两位长者都想不出镇上有谁同时具备足够的力量与动机，能把这种事做成，但随后他们想起了上一年末发生的一件事：当时，贺赫总督逮捕了一些逃犯。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>失去一切是什么滋味</h2>\n  <p>这件事发生在三年前，也就是7105年的冬天。贺赫总督收到一封来自伺城的公文，要求他留意据称曾试图诅咒皇室的“危险逃犯”。当其中一名逃犯——名叫樊鸿瑞的歌者——出现在柳岸镇，并声称自己是在为处理朋友的蛇咬伤而寻求协助时，总督试图逮捕她。</p>\n  <p>樊鸿瑞施展魔法分散守卫注意并伤了他们，随后逃离。守卫一恢复，总督便带领他们追捕那名女子。他们一路追踪到玉鸟客栈——一处位于柳岸镇东北方的路边避所——但在随后紧张的对峙中，火灾爆发。官方说法认为大火是逃犯引起的，但也有不少人声称，总督与其守卫为逼迫逃犯及其同伙现身，才点燃了火势。</p>\n  <p>无可争议的是：当建筑在火焰中燃烧时，鸿瑞唱出的最后一句话似乎令贺赫总督心神不宁，因为她承诺道：“所有侍奉龙华之人，很快就会知道失去一切是什么滋味！”</p>\n</aside>\n<p>当时，这听起来不过是罪犯临死前的誓言；但事后回想，随着龙华在一年之内崩塌，PC们的资助者不禁怀疑，这誓言或许蕴含着比众人当时所想更多的魔法。不管怎样，樊鸿瑞的两名同伙尸体被寻回，并埋葬在那座化为废墟的建筑附近，但她的遗骸始终未曾找到。</p>\n<p>尽管两位长者也承认，将这件事与三年后贺赫总督的失踪联系起来显得牵强，但这仍是他们目前能想到的、最接近解释真相的线索。他们请求PC们前往玉鸟客栈调查现场，哪怕只是为了确认这则离奇故事不过是与总督失踪无关的巧合。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Missing Governor\">The Missing Governor</h1>\n<p>Unlike the mists or Ugly Cute, there are no obvious starting points to begin the search for the missing governor. Examinations of the plot on which his manor once stood lead nowhere—nothing even indicates that a building once stood there, lending weight to the prevailing theory that whatever snatched away the manor was a powerful supernatural force indeed.</p>\n<p>With the lack of any obvious leads, both Granny Hu and Old Matsuki came to the conclusion that some supernatural force with a grudge against the governor must have had some role in the mysterious vanishing. Neither elder knows anyone in town who has the right combination of power and motivation to pull something like this off, but then they recall an event that happened near the end of the previous year, when Governor Heh had some fugitives arrested.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>How it Feels to Lose It all</h2>\n  <p>This event took place three years ago, in the winter of 7105. Governor Heh received a missive from Sze to be on the lookout for “dangerous fugitives” said to have attempted to curse the imperial family. When one of these fugitives, a singer named Fan Hongrui, showed up in Willowshore claiming to be searching for aid in dealing with a friend’s snakebite, the governor attempted to arrest her.</p>\n  <p>Fan Hongrui used magic to distract and injure his guards and then fled. As soon as the guards recovered, the governor led them in pursuit of the woman. They tracked her to Canary Inn, a roadside shelter to the northeast of Willowshore, but in the tense standoff that followed, a fire erupted. Officially, the fire is believed to have been triggered by the fugitive, but there are more than a few who claim the governor and his guards started the blaze in an attempt to force the fugitive and her allies out into the open.</p>\n  <p>What none contest is that the final words Hongrui sung out as the building burned seemed to unsettle Governor Heh, for she promised that “All those who serve Lung Wa will soon know how it feels to lose it all!”</p>\n</aside>\n<p>At the time, it seemed little more than the dying oath of a criminal, but in hindsight, with Lung Wa collapsing within a year, the PCs’ patron wonders if there was more magic to the oath than they suspected. In any case, the bodies of Fan Hongrui’s two accomplices were recovered and buried near the ruined building, but her remains were never found.</p>\n<p>While the elders admit the connection to Governor Heh’s disappearance three years later seems tenuous, it’s the closest thing they’ve come up with to explain what could have happened. They ask the PCs to travel to Canary Inn to investigate the site, if only to confirm this strange story is merely a coincidence to the governor’s disappearance.</p>"
            },
            "Investigating the Curse": {
              "name": "调查诅咒 Investigating the Curse",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Investigating the Curse\">调查诅咒</h1>\n<p>在柳岸镇，当地人有许多请求足以让PC们忙个不停，但镇子当前所面对的最重要之事，是在鬼季潜伏期降临柳岸镇的怪异“诅咒”。在PC们从未能触及唐入的失败尝试返回后的几天里，他们被两位镇中长老——胡太婆与老松木——邀请前往司魂娘娘（当地供奉@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}的神殿）与他们会面。</p>\n<p>在这里，两位长老暂且搁置各自的私怨，感谢PC们迄今为柳岸镇提供的服务——并请求他们继续工作，查明究竟是什么导致镇子遭受诅咒。虽然怪物入侵柳岸镇无疑是这道诅咒的一种性相，但随着点亮<em>长明灯</em>以及PC们的动作，其问题似乎已在很大程度上得到解决。然而，正如长老们指出的那样，镇子还面临另外三桩谜团：贺赫总督及其宅邸的消失、环绕荒野并阻止旅行的诡异迷雾，以及被称为丑小乖的石蜘蛛的失踪。</p>\n<p>长老们请PC们调查这三项事态发展——处理的顺序无关紧要，不过总督的失踪似乎是最紧迫的问题。毕竟，若能找到贺赫总督，也许他会更了解到底发生了什么！这些谜团中的每一项，都在后续页面中以各自的一组遭遇呈现，供PC们探索。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Investigating the Curse\">Investigating the Curse</h1>\n<p>While there are plenty of requests from locals to keep the PCs busy in Willowshore, the most important thing facing the town is the strange “curse” that descended on Willowshore at the onset of the season of ghosts. A few days after the PCs return from their failed attempt to reach Karahai, they’re asked by both town elders—Granny Hu and Old Matsuki—to meet with them at the Lady of Souls, the local temple of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}.</p>\n<p>Here, the two elders set aside their personal grievances to thank the PCs for the services they’ve provided to Willowshore so far—and to then request that they continue their work to determine what has caused the town to become cursed. While the monstrous invasion of Willowshore was certainly an aspect of this curse, it seems to have been largely solved by lighting the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> and as a result of the PCs’ actions. Yet, as the elders point out, there are three other mysteries facing the town: the vanishing of Governor Heh and his estate, the strange mists that surround the hinterlands and prevent travel, and the disappearance of the stone spider known as Ugly Cute.</p>\n<p>The elders ask the PCs to investigate all three of these developments—the order in which they’re tackled is irrelevant, although the disappearance of the governor seems to be the most pressing matter. If Governor Heh can be found, perhaps he’ll know more about what’s going on, after all! Each of these mysteries is presented on the following pages as its own set of encounters for the PCs to explore.</p>"
            },
            "Opportunities": {
              "name": "机会 Opportunities",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Opportunities\">机会</h2>\n<p>\n  随着PC们越来越出名，他们将会遇到许多机会。这些任务、悬赏与请求在此汇总，并大致按可获得的先后顺序呈现，但你也可以根据你游戏的进展自由组合、穿插这些请求。本幕中未去处理的机会，随时都可以在后续幕中使用！\n</p>\n<p>\n  这些机会都以简化格式呈现。它们原本意在以探索模式解决，但如果其中某些激发了你的灵感，也可以随意扩展，让它们能够以遭遇模式解决。其中若干机会会用到胜利点来解决情境——关于如何累积胜利点的规则，见<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>第184页。\n</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>失踪的船只</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Rajul Samudra（柳岸镇码头，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w31dock0000000]{W31}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> Rajul气喘吁吁地冲向PC们，报告说河童刚从柳岸镇码头偷走了两条船，并顺流而下逃走。他请求PC们设法追上并把船夺回来。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> 河童把船带到葫芦湖的南岸（区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d2gourdlake000]{D2}），因此PC们一到该区域就可以与河童盗贼对质。船本身漂在离岸十余尺的水面上，几只河童在船上嬉闹。一名河童长者会上前向PC们为年轻河童的恶作剧道歉，并请求队伍通过“相扑试炼”给年轻河童一个教训。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    为了教训它们，PC们必须在五场相扑比赛中至少赢下三场。每场比赛由一名PC进行一次@Check[athletics|dc:17]检定以蛮力取胜，或进行一次@Check[deception|dc:17]检定以诱使河童鞠躬或用其他方式让其头顶碗中的水洒出。运动检定大失败表示该PC拉伤肌肉，并在24小时内获得\n    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{虚弱 1}。欺骗检定大失败表示该PC出尽洋相，并在本次竞赛中其之后尝试的所有欺骗检定都承受–2环境减值。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    若爆发暴力冲突，或PC们未能至少赢下三场比赛，河童会嘶嘶咒骂并逃入水中，丢下船只不管——但它们很可能几天后又会把船偷走。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    这些河童中可能有PC们在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}中遇到过的那几只。若PC们当时以和平方式解决了那次遭遇，则PC们只需在五场相扑比赛中至少赢下一场，就足以达到上述教训的目的。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 若PC们赢下足够多的比赛，河童会吸取教训，不再偷船。给予PC们40 XP以及1点Northridge声望点数。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>修复牧场</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-soon-chongkum.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kum Soon-chong\" alt=\"An alderly man in a wide brimmed conical hat.\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-soon-chongkum.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Kum Soon-chong（柳岸镇马场，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w2willowshor00]{W2}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> 帮助经营者修复在怪物入侵期间严重受损的柳岸镇马场。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong></strong>挑战 每日一次，每名PC可以选择花费8小时在附近荒野中追踪并带回逃散的牲畜，进行@Check[survival|dc:15]检定；或帮助修复牧场围栏，进行@Check[crafting|dc:15]检定。这些检定可获得胜利点。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 一旦PC们获得10点胜利点，柳岸镇马场的服务将重新开放；PC们获得10 XP与1点Southbank声望点数。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>迁移蝶神圣坛</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Choe Chung-hu（磨坊，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w8millinghou00]{W8}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> Chung-hu请求PC们帮助他为目前被搁置在镇上被遗弃的庄园地段的\n    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{蝶神}圣坛寻找一处新归宿（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w23abandoned00]{W23b}）。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> 一位名为@UUID[Actor.Yhph6WPW4ErtIP6s]{Kohoshi}的式神神灵守卫着此圣坛。PC们必须成功通过一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:19]检定，说服Kohoshi允许他们迁移圣坛。随后，PC们必须要么尝试@Check[athletics|dc:15]检定以搬运其部件，要么尝试@Check[religion|dc:16]检定以确保圣坛各构件保持完好。这些检定每次耗时4小时，并累积胜利点。若PC们在未获得Kohoshi许可的情况下尝试迁移圣坛，则这些检定都承受–2环境减值。蝶神的信徒在本挑战中进行的所有检定获得+2环境加值。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 一旦PC们获得5点胜利点，圣坛将迁移至磨坊（区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w8millinghou00]{W8}），由Chung-hu照料；PC们获得20 XP与1点Southbank声望点数。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>调查旧扩建区</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Matsuki Shou（松木宅，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w5matsukiest00]{W5}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> 年迈的Matsuki已经开始担忧：如果柳岸镇的人民被某种诅咒困住，他们将没有足够的食物熬过冬天。他请求PC们向北前往一处废弃村落，确认是否仍能抵达——若能抵达，则探索该地并收集足够信息，以便村民能在那里种植应急作物。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> PC们前往旧扩建村落（区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d8oldvillage00]{D8}），途中可能遭遇一次随机遭遇。该废弃村落位于心景的雾气边界之内。PC们抵达后，可以花费4小时并尝试@Check[nature|dc:16]或@Check[farming-lore|dc:16]检定来调查周边田地、评估其可用性，或尝试@Check[society|dc:18]检定来规划在废墟中开垦新作物的最佳方法，以此累积胜利点。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 获得8点胜利点足以将此处确立为柳岸镇的补充农业地点。这将在第2幕产生后续影响。给予PC们20 XP与1点Southbank声望点数。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>铁匠的麻烦</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>触发 </strong>冒险进入第二个月。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Yong Wu-Xiu（永火铁厂，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w1eternalbla00]{W1}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> 与Northridge结盟的帝国卫兵开始施压永火铁厂，要求其放下其他工作，转而无偿打造武器与护甲，以武装守卫——因为看起来柳岸镇可能会与世界其他地区断绝联系。Wu-Xiu请求PC们去柳岸镇守卫办公室（区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w13w15indust00]{W15}）与Zheng Peng交涉。或者，他们也可以尝试说服Wu-Xiu：支援城镇卫兵是个好主意。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> 无论PC们选择与Zheng Peng还是与Yong Wu-Xiu交谈，都不会是一次简单迅速的谈话就能左右对方。为说服两人之一向另一人的需求让步，PC们必须选择与某位NPC进行若干次、每次2小时的讨论以累积胜利点。他们可以用@Check[intimidation|dc:21]检定，以讲述柳岸镇面临的危险来恐吓Yong Wu-Xiu（甚至以威胁迫使她遵从Zheng Peng的要求）；或用@Check[diplomacy|dc:18]检定，诉诸Zheng Peng的社区责任感（并可能承诺PC们自己也将更积极地参与柳岸镇防务）。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 获得6点胜利点足以说服该NPC接受PC们偏好的解决方案。PC们获得20 XP与1点声望点数：若他们站在Yong Wu-Xiu一方，则为Southbank；若他们站在Zheng Peng一方，则为Northridge。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>收集桃木</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>触发</strong>冒险进入第二个月。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Yun Mong-un（木雕师行会，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w25woodcarve00]{W25}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> Mong-un请求PC们收集落下的桃木枝条，以便她制作适合绘制稀有符箓的纸张。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> 传统上，制作桃木纸的材料是进口的，因为当地普遍相信三处区域性桃林有助于保护柳岸镇免受邪灵影响；但由于补给线被切断，PC们必须前往这三处桃林，为Mong-un取得材料。她可以告诉PC们三处本地桃林的位置（它们在柳岸腹地地图上以“P”标示）。柳岸镇无人具备正确采伐桃木所需的高级木工技能与工具，因此Mong-un要求PC们不要动树，只采集他们能找到的落枝。尽管这些落枝不具备经过妥善处理的桃木所拥有的内在超自然特质（因此价值也较低；见<em>Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide</em>第129页），落枝仍是Mong-un制作符箓的可行且有用的材料。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    为了采集材料，一名PC必须在该区域尝试“挣取收入”，以确定所收集落枝的价值。该PC必须尝试一次\n    @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:downtime,skill|name:Earn Income]或\n    @Check[survival|dc:18|traits:downtime,skill|name:Earn Income]检定来挣取收入，且任务最高可按4级任务处理（DC按等级设定）。若大失败，则在明年之前无法再从这处桃林尝试采集材料（PC们此时尚未知晓，这会导致该桃林在战役剩余部分完全无用）。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 只要材料尚未枯竭，PC们就可以持续采集落枝。首次成功采集并交付总计价值10 gp的材料时，给予他们20 XP与1点Northridge声望点数。作为对这份支持的答谢，Yun Mong-un提出愿意传授PC们任意一种\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20willowshoref00]{稀有符箓}\n    的公式，并额外赠予每名PC总计价值8 gp的这些符箓以示感谢。在柳岸镇于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow]{第4幕}开始时回归现代时代之前，无法尝试采集经过妥善处理的桃木。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>茶馆主人的遗嘱</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Luo Xi Yang\" alt=\"A dark haired woman in a purple kimono holding a paint brush\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp')\" />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>触发</strong> PC们在青天茶馆的\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c1publicfloo00]{C1}\n    区域发现“Qing Mai-Lai的最后遗嘱与遗言”，或夏季第三个月开始。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> Luo Xi Yang（Luo &amp; Laws，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w20luoandlaw00]{W20}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> 若PC们自行发现该文件，则他们一旦读完并理解其要求，便可立即开始挑战。否则，在夏季第三个月的第一天，当文件落入她手中后，Luo Xi Yang会主动找上PC们。她将文件交给PC们，并指出“柳岸镇最新的英雄们”应当拥有优先机会来完成文件的要求，以取得青天茶馆的所有权。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> 阅读文件可知，古怪的贵族Qing Mai-Lai希望在自己过世后，确保继承人具备继续经营茶馆所需的胆识与奉献精神，因此为继承设下了一项略带危险的要求。由于如今已无后裔存活，茶馆的所有权将依法转移给第一个完成文件要求的个人或团体：取回“我扔进@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{文业}双眼里的两颗珍珠。”\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    成功通过一次\n    @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]\n    检定或@Check[social|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]\n    检定的角色知道：镇子北边有两处小池塘在当地被称为“文业双眼”。若PC们都未能联系到这一点，Xi Yang（或你选择的其他NPC）可以提醒他们。为了满足遗嘱中不同寻常的条款，必须从这些池塘中取回珍珠。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    要取回一颗珍珠，一名PC必须成功通过一次@Check[athletics|dc:16]检定以抵达池塘（详见区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d9eyesoffume00]{D9}），随后花时间在水中搜寻单颗珍珠。（注意：在搜寻文业右眼（区域D9b）之前，必须先处理栖息在其岸边的两只猎蛛。）每次尝试寻找珍珠需要4小时的搜寻、一次@Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim]\n    检定（以在搜寻期间成功在水下游泳），以及一次@Check[perception|dc:15]检定（仅当游泳的运动检定至少成功时才可尝试）以发现珍珠。每当重复进行发现珍珠的察觉检定时，其DC降低2。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">更多信息见区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d9eyesoffume00]{D9}。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 每颗珍珠价值10 gp。若PC们取回两颗珍珠，他们便有资格将青天茶馆作为一门生意来经营；重开茶馆并经营它的规则，是鬼季中一项重要追求，并在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00]{第2幕}中详细呈现。PC们在成功取得青天茶馆所有权后，获得40 XP。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>茶园虫害</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>触发</strong> PC们完成“茶馆主人的遗嘱”后过了一周。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请求者</strong> 山峰草（莱西茶铺，区域\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w35theleshys00]{W35}）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>任务</strong> 一旦消息传开，PC们已取得青天茶馆的所有权，莱西制茶师山峰草便会带着提议前来拜访。一种令人头疼的枯萎病正在莱西茶铺的植物间蔓延，莱西们需要协助来阻止其扩散。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>挑战</strong> 辨识枯萎病并治疗这种病害需要细致检查、修剪、除草，以及将受污染的土壤轮换为新土。PC们开始后，可以花费8小时并尝试@Check[nature|dc:18]检定或@Check[farming-lore|dc:16]检定来取得进展，以此累积胜利点。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>奖励</strong> 一旦PC们达成10点胜利点，他们就已将枯萎病从莱西茶铺彻底清除。给予他们20 XP。此外，在莱西茶铺赢得的感激，将在队伍经营青天茶馆时帮助他们获取茶叶供应，如下一幕所述。\n  </p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Opportunities\">Opportunities</h2>\n<p>\n  As the PCs become better known, they’ll be presented with many opportunities. These tasks, bounties, and requests\n  are summarized here, presented roughly in order of availability, but you should feel free to mix and match these\n  requests as you see fit to match your game’s progression. Opportunities not pursued in this act can always be used\n  in upcoming acts!\n</p>\n<p>\n  Each of these opportunities is presented in abridged format. They’re meant to be resolved in exploration mode, but\n  if some of them inspire you, feel free to expand upon them so that they can be resolved in encounter mode. Several\n  of these opportunities use Victory Points to resolve situations—see page 184 of the <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> for\n  rules on\n  how to accumulate Victory Points.\n</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Missing Boats</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Rajul Samudra (Willowshore Dock, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w31dock0000000]{W31})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Rajul breathlessly approaches the PCs with a report that kappas just stole two boats from\n    Willowshore Dock and\n    fled downriver with them. He asks the PCs to try to catch up with them and get the boats back.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> The kappas bring the boats to the southern shores of Gourd Lake (area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d2gourdlake000]{D2}), so as soon as the PCs reach\n    that area, they can confront the kappa thieves. The boats themselves float a dozen feet offshore while several\n    kappas play on them. A kappa elder approaches the PCs to apologize for the youngsters’ pranks, and asks the party to\n    teach the younger kappas a lesson through “trial by sumo wrestling.”\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    In order to teach the lesson, the PCs must win at least three out of five sumo wrestling matches. Each match is\n    resolved by a PC attempting a @Check[athletics|dc:17] check to use brute force or a @Check[deception|dc:17] check to\n    trick a kappa into bowing or otherwise causing it to spill the water in its head bowl. A critical failure on an\n    Athletics check\n    indicates that PC has strained a muscle and becomes\n    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 1} for 24 hours. A critical failure on a\n    Deception check indicates that PC made a fool of themselves and takes a –2 circumstance penalty to all future\n    Deception checks\n    they attempt in this contest.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    If violence breaks out, or if the PCs fail to win at least three matches, the kappas hiss and curse and flee into\n    the water, abandoning the boats—but they’ll likely just steal the boats again a few days later.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    Some of these kappas might be those the PCs encountered in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2}. If the\n    PCs resolved that encounter on peaceful terms, then the PCs must only win at least one of the five sumo wrestling\n    matches to teach the above lesson.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> If the PCs win enough matches, the kappas learn their lesson and will no longer steal boats.\n    Grant the PCs 40\n    XP and 1 Reputation Point with Northridge.\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Fixing the Ranch</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-soon-chongkum.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kum Soon-chong\" alt=\"An alderly man in a wide brimmed conical hat.\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-soon-chongkum.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Kum Soon-chong (Willowshore Stables, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w2willowshor00]{W2})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Help the proprietor repair Willowshore Stables, which was heavily damaged during the monster\n    invasion.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong></strong>Challenge Once per day, each PC can either spend 8 hours chasing down and returning\n    livestock that fled into the\n    nearby wilderness with @Check[survival|dc:15] checks, or helping to repair the ranch’s fencing with\n    @Check[crafting|dc:15] checks. These checks earn Victory Points.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> Once the PCs gain 10 Victory Points, services at Willowshore Stables become available again;\n    the PCs earn 10\n    XP and 1 Reputation Point with Southbank.\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Moving Desna’s Shrine</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Choe Chung-hu (Milling Houses, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w8millinghou00]{W8})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Chung-hu asks the PCs to help him find a new home for the\n    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna} shrine currently languishing in the Abandoned\n    Estates part of town (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w23abandoned00]{W23b}).\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> A Shikigami Kami named @UUID[Actor.Yhph6WPW4ErtIP6s]{Kohoshi} guards this shrine. The PCs\n    must succeed at\n    a @Check[diplomacy|dc:19] check to convince Kohoshi to let them move the shrine. The PCs must then either attempt\n    @Check[athletics|dc:15] checks to physically move parts of it, or @Check[religion|dc:16] checks to ensure the\n    shrine’s components remain\n    intact. These checks each take 4 hours and accumulate Victory Points. The PCs take a –2 circumstance penalty to\n    these checks if they attempt to move the shrine without Kohoshi’s permission. A worshipper of Desna gains a +2\n    circumstance bonus to all checks they attempt during this challenge.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> Once the PCs gain 5 Victory Points, the shrine is relocated to the Milling Houses (area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w8millinghou00]{W8}), where Chung-hu\n    will attend to it; the PCs earn 20 XP and 1 Reputation Point with Southbank.\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Investigate the Old Expansion</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Matsuki Shou (Matsuki Estate, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w5matsukiest00]{W5})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Old Matsuki has already started to worry that if the people of Willowshore are trapped by some\n    sort of curse,\n    they won’t have enough food to last the winter. He asks the PCs to head north to an abandoned village and determine\n    if it can still be reached—and if so, to explore it and gather enough information so that villagers can plant\n    emergency crops there.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> The PCs travel to the old village expansion (area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d8oldvillage00]{D8}), potentially facing a random encounter.\n    The\n    abandoned village lies just within the mindscape’s fog border. Once the PCs arrive, they can accumulate Victory\n    Points by spending 4 hours and then attempting @Check[nature|dc:16] or @Check[farming-lore|dc:16] checks to\n    investigate the surrounding\n    fields and appraise their viability for use, or @Check[society|dc:18] checks to plan out the best methods for\n    starting new\n    crops in the ruins.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> Reaching 8 Victory Points is enough to secure the location as a supplemental agricultural\n    site for\n    Willowshore. This will have repercussions in Act 2. Grant the PCs 20 XP and 1 Reputation Point with Southbank.\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Smith Troubles</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Trigger </strong>The adventure has entered its second month.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Yong Wu-Xiu (Eternal Blaze Ironworks, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w1eternalbla00]{W1})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Imperial guards allied with Northridge have begun pressuring Eternal Blaze Ironworks to set\n    aside other work to\n    focus on crafting weapons and armor, free of charge, to help arm guards now that it looks like Willowshore might be\n    cut off from the rest of the world. Wu-Xiu asks the PCs to speak to Zheng Peng at Willowshore’s Guard Office (area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w13w15indust00]{W15}). Alternatively, they could try to\n    convince Wu-Xiu that supporting the town’s guards is a good idea.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> Whether the PCs decide to speak to Zheng Peng or Yong Wu-Xiu, it won’t be a simple and\n    quick discussion to\n    sway one or the other. To convince one of the two to capitulate to the other’s needs, the PCs must accumulate\n    Victory Points by spending several 2-hour discussions with the NPC of their choice. They can either frighten Yong\n    Wu-Xiu with stories of the dangers facing Willowshore (or even threaten her into complying with Zheng Peng’s\n    requests) with @Check[intimidation|dc:21] checks or appeal to Zheng Peng’s sense of community (and perhaps promise\n    to serve\n    a more active role in helping to defend Willowshore themselves) with @Check[diplomacy|dc:18] checks.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> Reaching 6 Victory Points is enough to convince the NPC to acquiesce to the solution favored\n    by the PCs. This\n    earns them 20 XP and 1 Reputation Point with either Southbank (if they sided with Yong Wu-Xiu) or Northridge (if\n    they sided with Zheng Peng).\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Collecting Peachwood</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Trigger</strong> The adventure has entered its second month.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Yun Mong-un (Woodcarver’s Guild, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w25woodcarve00]{W25})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Mong-un asks the PCs to gather fallen peachwood branches so she can craft paper suitable for\n    creating rare fulus.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> Traditionally, supplies for making peachwood paper are imported since there’s a strong\n    local belief that\n    the three regional groves help to protect Willowshore from the influence of evil spirits, but with supply lines cut\n    off, the PCs must visit these three groves to secure supplies for Mong-un. She can indicate to the PCs where the\n    three local groves are located (they’re indicated with a “P” on the Willowshore Hinterlands). No one\n    in Willowshore has the advanced carpentry skill or tools required to properly harvest peachwood, so Mong-un asks the\n    PCs to leave the trees alone and simply harvest what fallen branches they can. While these fallen branches don’t\n    carry the same intrinsic supernatural quality (and thus, value) that properly treated peachwood does (see\n    <em>Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide</em> 129), the fallen branches remain a viable and useful component to\n    Mong-un’s fulu\n    production.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    To harvest supplies, a PC must attempt to Earn Income in the area to determine the value of fallen branches\n    gathered. A PC must attempt a @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:downtime,skill|name:Earn Income] or\n    @Check[survival|dc:18|traits:downtime,skill|name:Earn Income] check to Earn Income, and it can be up to a 4th-level\n    task\n    (with a DC set by level). On a critical failure, no further attempts to harvest supplies from this grove can be\n    attempted until next year (which, unknown to the PCs at this time, renders this grove useless for the remainder of\n    the campaign).\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> The PCs can continue to harvest fallen branches as long as the supplies hold out. The first\n    time they manage\n    to harvest and hand over a total of 10 gp in supplies, grant them 20 XP and 1 Reputation Point with Northridge. In\n    thanks for this support, Yun Mong-un offers to teach the PCs the formula for any of the\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20willowshoref00]{Rare Fulus}\n    and also gives each PC 8 gp worth of these fulus as thanks. Until Willowshore returns to the modern era at the\n    start of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow]{Act 4}, no attempt to harvest properly treated peachwood can be made.\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>The Teahouse Owner’s Will</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Luo Xi Yang\" alt=\"A dark haired woman in a purple kimono holding a paint brush\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp')\" />\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs discover “The Last Will and Testament of Qing Mai-Lai” in area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04c1publicfloo00]{C1} of the Cerulean Teahouse, or the\n    third month of summer begins.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Luo Xi Yang (Luo &amp; Laws, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w20luoandlaw00]{W20})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> If the PCs discover this document on their own, they can begin its challenge as soon as they\n    read it and\n    understand the requirement. Otherwise, on the first day of the third month of summer, Luo Xi Yang approaches the PCs\n    after the document has come into her hands. She presents the document to the PCs, noting that “Willowshore’s newest\n    heroes” should have the first chance to fulfill the document’s requirements to take ownership of the Cerulean\n    Teahouse.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> A reading of the document reveals that eccentric aristocrat Qing Mai-Lai wanted to ensure\n    her heirs would\n    have the gumption and devotion needed to continue running the teahouse once she passed away, and set a somewhat\n    dangerous requirement for its inheritance. With no descendants surviving today, ownership of the teahouse will\n    legally transfer to the first person or group that fulfills the document’s requirement: to recover the “two pearls\n    I’ve thrown into @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{Fumeiyoshi's} eyes.”\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    A character who succeeds at a\n    @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]\n    check or @Check[social|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] knows\n    that two\n    small ponds north of town are known locally as the “Eyes of Fumeiyoshi.” Xi Yang (or another NPC of your choice) can\n    point this out to the PCs if none of them make the connection. In order to comply with the will’s unusual\n    stipulation, the pearls must be retrieved from these pools.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">\n    To retrieve a pearl, a PC must succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:16] to reach the pond (as detailed in area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d9eyesoffume00]{D9}) and\n    must then spend time searching the waters for a single pearl. (Note that before a search of the Right Eye of\n    Fumeiyoshi, area D9b, the two hunting spiders that dwell on its shores must be dealt with.) Each attempt to find a\n    pearl takes 4 hours of Searching, a @Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim]\n    check (to successfully Swim underwater during the search), and a\n    @Check[perception|dc:15] check (which can only be attempted if the Athletics check to Swim was at least a success)\n    to discover the pearl. The DC of the Perception check to discover the pearl decreases by 2 each time the Perception\n    check is repeated.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">See area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d9eyesoffume00]{D9} for more information.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> Each of the pearls is worth 10 gp. If the PCs recover both of them, they become eligible to\n    claim the\n    Cerulean Teahouse as a business to run; rules for restoring the teahouse and running it are a significant pursuit\n    presented in detail in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00]{Act 2} of Season of\n    Ghosts. Grant the PCs 40 XP once they have successfully claimed ownership\n    of the Cerulean Teahouse.\n  </p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Tea Farm Infestation</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Trigger</strong> A week has passed since the PCs completed The Teahouse Owner’s\n    Will.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requester</strong> Mountain Summit Grass (The Leshy’s Salon, area\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w35theleshys00]{W35})</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Task</strong> Once word spreads that the PCs have taken ownership of the Cerulean Teahouse, the leshy tea\n    maker Mountain Summit Grass approaches them with a proposition. A frustrating blight has been spreading through the Leshy’s Salon’s\n    plants, and the leshies could use help in stopping its progress.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Challenge</strong> Identifying the blight and treating the affliction requires careful examination, pruning,\n    weeding, and rotation of tainted soil for fresh soil. Once the PCs get started, they can accumulate Victory Points by spending 8\n    hours and then attempting @Check[nature|dc:18] checks or @Check[farming-lore|dc:16] checks to make progress.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Reward</strong> Once the PCs achieve 10 Victory Points, they’ve scoured the blight from the Leshy’s Salon.\n    Grant them 20 XP. In addition, the gratitude earned at the Leshy’s Salon will aid the party in supplying tea when running business at\n    the Cerulean Teahouse, as detailed in the next act.\n  </p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Wall of Ghosts": {
              "name": "鬼打墙 Wall of Ghosts",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Wall of Ghosts\">鬼打墙</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wall-of-ghosts.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Wall of Ghosts\" alt=\"扭曲的形状在迷雾中荡漾\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wall-of-ghosts.webp')\" />\n<p>思维空间最西北端的边缘位于一片无法穿透的不透明白雾区域之外，这片白雾横切整片区域，形成一堵垂直的墙，似乎高耸入空中50英尺。时不时地，一些看起来像是无声尖叫的人形幽灵的扭曲身影会在雾中荡起涟漪，仿佛被困在浓雾之中。一名能够飞行并试图从墙上方掠过的PC，会发现自己能向更西边望见林木覆盖的群山景色，但任何试图接近下方这堵墙所在位置10英尺以内的举动，都会使更多迷雾在他们面前猛然翻涌升起。这就是鬼打墙——一道防御屏障，直接源自苦迦菩提那阴森的力量，用以保护通往他坟墓的道路。</p>\n<p>移除鬼打墙是第二幕的重要内容。目前，任何试图进入鬼打墙的PC都会发现自己不仅会被迫掉头，重新从进入处出现（方式与他们在别处试图越过思维空间边界时相同），还会因为墙中的幽灵穿过他们而暴露在排山倒海般的恐惧与惊骇之中，使他们的心智被惊恐与强烈、迫近的末日感所玷污。受影响的PC必须在一次@Check[will|dc:24]中成功。若失败，他们从鬼打墙中回到起点时将处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 1}；若大失败，他们将处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 3}，并在保持惊惧状态期间处于逃跑状态。</p>\n<p>关于鬼打墙及其彼方的更多细节，见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08throughthewa00]{第二幕：任叶飘落}。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Wall of Ghosts\">Wall of Ghosts</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wall-of-ghosts.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Wall of Ghosts\" alt=\"Distorted shapes ripple through the mist\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-wall-of-ghosts.webp')\" />\n<p>The northwesternmost reaches of the mindscape lie beyond an impenetrable field of opaque white mist that cuts through the region, forming a vertical wall that appears to rise 50 feet into the air. Now and then, the distorted shapes of what look like silently screaming humanoid ghosts ripple through the mist, as if trapped within the fog. A PC who can fly and who attempts to soar above the wall finds that they can look further west upon the view of the forested mountains, but any attempt to approach within 10 feet of the wall’s position below causes more mist to flare up before them. This is the Wall of Ghosts—a defensive barrier that sprang directly from Kugaptee’s sinister power to protect the approach to his grave.</p>\n<p>Removing the Wall of Ghosts is an important part of Act 2. For now, any PC who attempts to enter the Wall of Ghosts finds they are not only turned around to reemerge where they entered (in the same manner as if they press beyond the mindscape’s border elsewhere), but are also exposed to an overwhelming sense of fear and horror as the ghosts in the wall flow through them, tainting their mind with terror and feelings of overwhelming, impending doom. Affected PCs must succeed at a @Check[will|dc:24]. On a failure, they are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1} upon emerging from the Wall of Ghosts back where they started, and on a critical failure, they’re @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 3} and fleeing as long as they remain frightened.</p>\n<p>See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08throughthewa00]{Act 2: Let the Leaves Fall} for more details on the Wall of Ghosts and what lies beyond.</p>"
            },
            "Peachwood Grove": {
              "name": "桃木林地 Peachwood Grove",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"P. Peachwood Grove\">P. 桃木林</h2>\n<p>每个此类区域中都生长着一片桃木树。这些树可以采收，用于制作符箓的材料（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#collecting-peachwood]{采集桃木}）。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"P. Peachwood Grove\">P. Peachwood Grove</h2>\n<p>A grove of peachwood trees grows in each of these areas. These trees can be harvested for fulu creation supplies (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#collecting-peachwood]{Collecting Peachwood}).</p>"
            },
            "The Road to Enlightenment": {
              "name": "《通往启蒙之路》 The Road to Enlightenment",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D13. The Road to Enlightenment\">D13. 通往开悟之路</h2>\n<p>这条狭窄的道路继续向上延伸，越过鬼打墙，进入西面的群山之中。在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{第二幕}中，当PC们启程前往柳岸镇西北方那座废弃的修道院时，这条路最有可能是他们选择的路线。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D13. The Road to Enlightenment\">D13. The Road to Enlightenment</h2>\n<p>This narrow roadway leads further up past the Wall of Ghosts into the mountains to the west. This road is the most likely route the PCs will take in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{Act 2} when they make the journey out to the abandoned monastery northwest of Willowshore.</p>"
            },
            "Ritual Site": {
              "name": "仪式场地 Ritual Site",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D12. Ritual Site\">D12. 仪式场地</h2>\n<p>这里的一处林间空地被鬼打墙一分为二——关于这处仪式场地的更多细节，见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06theritualsit00]{第4章}。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D12. Ritual Site\">D12. Ritual Site</h2>\n<p>A forest clearing is bisected here by the Wall of Ghosts—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06theritualsit00]{Chapter 4} for more details about this ritual site.</p>"
            },
            "Lumber Camp": {
              "name": "旧伐木营地 Lumber Camp",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D11. Lumber Camp\">D11. 旧伐木营地</h2>\n<p>这座曾被遗弃的旧伐木营地如今成了怪物的巢穴——更多信息见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{第4章}。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D11. Lumber Camp\">D11. Lumber Camp</h2>\n<p>This once-abandoned lumber camp is now the home of monsters—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{Chapter 4} for more information.</p>"
            },
            "Gorge of Fangs and Teeth": {
              "name": "尖牙峡 Gorge of Fangs and Teeth",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D10. Gorge of Fangs and Teeth\">D10. 尖牙峡</h2>\n<p>这处石质断崖位于森林边缘数英里外，这里开采的石料曾用于铺设柳岸镇的道路，以及建造其地基与石制建筑结构。石蜘蛛“丑小乖”撤退到了这里（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05searchingfor00]{Searching for Ugly Cute}）。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D10. Gorge of Fangs and Teeth\">D10. Gorge of Fangs and Teeth</h2>\n<p>Located a few miles from the edge of the forest, this escarpment of stone was where most of the materials used to pave Willowshore’s roads and build its foundations and stone structures were quarried. The stone spider Ugly Cute retreated here (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05searchingfor00]{Searching for Ugly Cute}).</p>"
            },
            "Eyes of Fumeiyoshi": {
              "name": "文业双眼 Eyes of Fumeiyoshi",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D9. 文业双眼</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这些水池位于碗状的凹地中，被称为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{文业王}之眼。大多数腹地都长满了葱郁的植被，但填满这两处盆地的灰色砂砾土中却寸草不生。当地传言称，数百年前，掌管坟墓与耻辱之神文业王曾透过这两口半咸的水池注视世间，随后他的注意力被别处吸引；而在他离去之后，这里便再也无法生长任何植物。这两处凹地不过是土壤贫瘠之地，然而关于文业王的故事根深蒂固，关于他的目光“诅咒”了此处土地的传说仍在流传。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hunting-spider.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">文业双眼</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.PckLz0BWyLcbvuZQ]{猎蛛（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>西侧水池（区域 <strong>D9a</strong>）被称为“文业王的左眼”，而东侧水池（区域 <strong>D9b</strong>）被称为“文业王的右眼”。左眼深达25尺，而右眼相当浅，从未超过10尺深。任一凹地陡峭的坡壁都可以通过一次 @Check[athletics|dc:16] 检定来攀行（失败表示轻微滑倒，受到 @Damage[5[bludgeoning]] 伤害）。左眼除此之外相对安全，但有一对猎蛛将右眼的岸边当作它们的巢穴。</p>\n</section>\n<p>若PC们想成为青天茶馆的新主人，他们就需要探索这些地点（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#the-teahouse-owners-will]{《茶馆主人的遗嘱》}）。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D9. Eyes of Fumeiyoshi</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 2</span>\n</h2>\n<p>These pools, located in bowl-shaped depressions, are known as the Eyes of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{Fumeiyoshi}. Most of the hinterlands are filled with verdant vegetation, but nothing grows in the gritty gray soil that fills both of these basins. Local rumor holds that centuries ago, Fumeiyoshi, the god of graves and dishonor, looked out into the world through these two brackish pools before his attention was diverted elsewhere, and in the wake of his passing, no plant life can grow here. These two hollows are simply places with bad soil, yet the story about Fumeiyoshi is strong and the lore that his attention has “cursed” the land here persists.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hunting-spider.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Eyes of Fumeiyoshi</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.PckLz0BWyLcbvuZQ]{Hunting Spiders (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The western pool (area <strong>D9a</strong>) is known as “The Left Eye of Fumeiyoshi,” while the eastern pool (area <strong>D9b</strong>) is known as “The Right Eye of Fumeiyoshi.” The Left Eye is 25 feet deep, while the Right Eye is quite shallow and never reaches a depth in excess of 10 feet. The steep sides of either depression can be navigated with a @Check[athletics|dc:16] check (a failure indicates a minor slip for @Damage[5[bludgeoning]] damage). While the Left Eye is otherwise safe, a pair of hunting spiders has claimed the shores of the Right Eye as their lair.</p>\n</section>\n<p>The PCs will need to explore these locations if they wish to become the new owners of the Cerulean Teahouse (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#the-teahouse-owners-will]{The Teahouse Owner’s Will}).</p>"
            },
            "Old Village Expansion": {
              "name": "老村庄扩展 Old Village Expansion",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D8. Old Village Expansion\">D8. 老村扩建区</h2>\n<p>几栋建筑的荒废遗迹淹没在这片辽阔的草原中，周围是杂草丛生、几乎被野草堵塞的田地。只要PC们帮忙推动事情进展（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#investigate-the-old-expansion]{调查老扩建区}），这个地点就能在接下来的章节里为柳岸镇提供一处极佳的额外作物种植地。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D8. Old Village Expansion\">D8. Old Village Expansion</h2>\n<p>The overgrown ruins of several buildings lie slumped in this large grassland, surrounded by weed-choked fields. This site could serve Willowshore as an excellent location to grow additional crops in the next act, provided the PCs help to get things moving (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00#investigate-the-old-expansion]{Investigate the Old Expansion}).</p>"
            },
            "Infested Grove": {
              "name": "虫群侵染林地 Infested Grove",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D7. Infested Grove\">D7. 受侵染的林地</h2>\n<p>这片林地曾是遍布柳树的田园幽林，年轻的恋人们会聚集在此野餐，如今却已被一只真菌怪物侵占（更多细节见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05intotheinfes00]{Into the Infestation}）。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D7. Infested Grove\">D7. Infested Grove</h2>\n<p>Once an idyllic grove of willow trees where young lovers would gather for picnics, this grove has become infested by a fungal monster (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05intotheinfes00]{Into the Infestation} for more details).</p>"
            },
            "Hunter’s Hut": {
              "name": "猎户小屋 Hunter’s Hut",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D6. Hunter’s Hut\">D6. 猎户小屋</h2>\n<p>这座小小的猎户小屋在一年前被遗弃，如今已显得杂草丛生，但仍可为被风雨困在野外的PC提供遮蔽之所。</p>\n<p>如果在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11}）中，年轻的情侣尤莉与勒隆被允许私奔，他们在发现自己无法离开该地区后，最终会到这里避难。他们不确定该如何看待这诡异的迷雾，但眼下决定先在这里躲着。他们恳求PC不要让柳岸镇的任何人知道他们躲在这里。不过，如果PC向他们强调这段陌生的时代与他们可能面对的危险（并成功进行一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:13]或@Check[intimidation|dc:13]检定），这对情侣也会同意回到镇上，并羞怯地返家。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若让恋人们继续留在这里，他们可能遭遇何种命运由你决定；但若PC救下他们或支援他们，给予20 XP。若成功说服这对情侣回到镇上（或PC告知他们的家人他们在这里，从而使家人前来接回），则PC还获得南岸1点声望点数，作为寻回失踪青年的回报。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D6. Hunter’s Hut\">D6. Hunter’s Hut</h2>\n<p>Abandoned a year ago, this small hunter’s hut is already looking overgrown but can still serve as a shelter for PCs caught out in the elements.</p>\n<p>If the young couple Yuli and Lelong were allowed to elope in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2} (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai.JournalEntryPage.04b11mudwallho00]{B11}), they end up taking shelter here after they discover they can’t leave the region. They aren’t sure what to make of the strange mist, but for the time being, they’ve decided to shelter here. They beg the PCs not to let anyone in Willowshore know they’re staying here. However, the couple consents to return to town if the PCs impress upon them the strange times and dangers that they might face (along with a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:13] or @Check[intimidation|dc:13] check), and they sheepishly return home.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> What fate the lovers might meet if they’re left out here is up to you to decide, but if the PCs save them or support them, grant them 20 XP. If the couple is convinced to return to town (or if the PCs inform their families they’re up here so they can be retrieved), also grant the PCs 1 Reputation Point with Southbank for the return of the missing youths.</p>"
            },
            "Green Silk Peak": {
              "name": "青丝峰 Green Silk Peak",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D5. Green Silk Peak\">D5. 青丝峰</h2>\n<p>青丝峰海拔接近2,000英尺，其山坡令人疲惫不堪（将该区域视为高等困难地形），但从山顶望去的景色令人屏息，可将东侧的幽海尽收眼底。攀爬至峰顶的PC在晴朗的日子里能看见唐入的要塞，且看不到任何包围该区域的诡异迷雾的迹象。然而，即使试图从峰顶直接飞往要塞，也会遭遇思维空间的屏障。试图用远距离信号（例如烟雾信号或夜间强光）吸引唐入注意的尝试也不会得到回应，因为眼前的唐入以及其后的幽海景象，不过是思维空间边界之外曾经存在之物的强力幻象。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D5. Green Silk Peak\">D5. Green Silk Peak</h2>\n<p>At nearly 2,000 feet in elevation, Green Silk Peak’s slopes make for a tiring ascent (treat this area as greater difficult terrain), but the view from its summit is breathtaking, affording an expansive view of the Sea of Ghosts to the east. A PC who climbs to the peak can see the fortress of Karahai on clear days, with no evidence of the strange mist that encloses the region. Yet even attempts to fly directly to the fortress from the peak will encounter the mindscape’s barrier. Attempts to attract attention from Karahai using long-distance signals, such as smoke signals or powerful lights at night, won’t result in responses, for this view of Karahai and the Sea of Ghosts beyond is little more than a potent illusion of what once lay beyond the mindscape’s borders.</p>"
            },
            "Canary Inn": {
              "name": "玉鸟客栈 Canary Inn",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D4. Canary Inn\">D4. 玉鸟客栈</h2>\n<p>这家客栈曾是一处驿站，供在唐入与北方需数日旅行的其他村庄之间往来的旅人歇脚。然而在几年前，柳岸镇的守卫与一群从龙华逃亡、正在逃窜的逃犯之间发生了一场剑拔弩张的对峙；其后续影响之下，这间客栈被焚毁殆尽。更多细节见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05themissinggo00]{失踪的总督}。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D4. Canary Inn\">D4. Canary Inn</h2>\n<p>Once a roadhouse used by travelers journeying between Karahai and other villages a few days’ travel to the north, this inn burned to the ground a few years back in the aftermath of a tense standoff between Willowshore’s guards and a group of fugitives on the run from Lung Wa. See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05themissinggo00]{The Missing Governor} for more details.</p>"
            },
            "Treacherous Trail": {
              "name": "危机四伏的小路 Treacherous Trail",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D3. 危险小路</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 2</span>\n</h2>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/snapping-flytrap.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">危险小路</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Lc4Jk2X9KM645duw]{猛咬捕蝇草}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>这条小路曾更常被用作一条捷径，用来绕过南侧的河流弯道；众所周知，如今它已杂草丛生，并且到处都是猛咬捕蝇草。小路两端各立着一块牌子，上面写着：“警告：危险植物！”至于胆敢走这条小路的PC是否会遭遇一株猛咬捕蝇草，则由你决定。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D3. Treacherous Trail</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 2</span>\n</h2>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/snapping-flytrap.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Treacherous Trail</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 2</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Lc4Jk2X9KM645duw]{Snapping Flytrap}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Once used more often as a shortcut to bypass the southern river bend, it’s well known that this trail has become quite overgrown and infested with snapping flytraps. A sign posted at either end reads, “Warning: Dangerous plants!” Whether or not PCs who dare to take this trail encounter a snapping flytrap is up to you, though.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Gourd Lake": {
              "name": "葫芦湖 Gourd Lake",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D2. Gourd Lake\">D2. 葫芦湖</h2>\n<p>这座相对较浅的湖泊四周环绕着沼泽般的湖岸，使其不适合用来建造村庄。湖泊本身非常适合钓鱼——只要渔民小心避开南岸即可，因为那里被几名河童宣称为它们的领地。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D2. Gourd Lake\">D2. Gourd Lake</h2>\n<p>Marshy shores surround this relatively shallow lake, making it a poor site for building a village. The lake itself is excellent for fishing—as long as fishers take care to avoid the southern shores, which are claimed as the territory of several kappas.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇 Willowshore",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D1. Willowshore\">D1. 柳岸镇</h2>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow]{柳岸镇}位于此处，横跨木棉河两岸。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"D1. Willowshore\">D1. Willowshore</h2>\n<p>The town of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow]{Willowshore} is located here, straddling the banks of the Ceiba River.</p>"
            },
            "Exploring the Hinterlands": {
              "name": "探索荒野边境 Exploring the Hinterlands",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Exploring the Hinterlands\">探索柳岸腹地</h2>\n<p>本模组提供一张思维空间地图。若你使用《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》，玩家已经拥有一张该地区地图。若你不使用本指南，考虑提供一张由你自行设计的地图，让玩家作为他们探索时的指引。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注释</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.YbqD7ILHwWtGUF2P]{Hinterlands Control}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>控制 @UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{柳岸腹地} 场景上的所有图块。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/sog-party-token.webp\" alt=\"Party Token\" title=\"Party Token\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注释</span><span class=\"keepme\">指示物</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\"><a href=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/sog-party-token.webp\">队伍指示物</a></span>\n  </div>\n  <p>你可以在本次六角探索中，将这个队伍指示物用于你的队伍角色。</p>\n</section>\n<p>如 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02willowshores01]{柳岸腹地} 中所述，没有道路的森林六角格属于困难地形，南部腹地中崎岖多石的田野同样如此。PC旅行时，确保你清楚他们在进行哪些探索活动。PC在腹地度过的每一天，进行一次 @Check[flat|dc:17] 以确定是否发生遭遇。若成功，则当PC位于柳岸镇2个六角格范围内时，在下表掷 [[/r 1d12]]；否则，掷一次 [[/r 1d20]] 以确定他们在荒野中遇到什么。若发生遭遇，你应决定遭遇发生在他们旅行途中还是露营时。</p>\n\n<h1 class=\"table\">腹地随机遭遇</h1>\n<hr />\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>[[/r 1d12]]{d12}/[[/r 1d20]]{d20}</th>\n      <th>遭遇</th>\n      <th>威胁</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–3</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.nuup7VijH5sidWgW]{巨蜈蚣}</td>\n      <td>微不足道2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4–6</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.IUvO1RsdI8ECHJZv]{黏菌怪}</td>\n      <td>微不足道2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7–9</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.Yc41IEb5kKayrMgN]{草人}</td>\n      <td>微不足道2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10–11</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.PckLz0BWyLcbvuZQ]{猎蛛}</td>\n      <td>低2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>12–13</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.1b4T5NeX6Oy8Fii5]{狼}</td>\n      <td>低2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>14–15</td>\n      <td>3 @UUID[Actor.Yc41IEb5kKayrMgN]{草人}</td>\n      <td>低2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>16–17</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.rVHaUobZlIE1txxP]{金金斯}</td>\n      <td>低2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>18</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.bszU2NHYzIFKkn6R]{巨锹甲虫}</td>\n      <td>中等2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>19</td>\n      <td>4 @UUID[Actor.XIgSrA8HGoQsxfAw]{无面鬼士兵}</td>\n      <td>中等2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>20</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.SxEWCTkiVM0OYB1B]{野猪}</td>\n      <td>中等2</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>动物：</strong>PC遇到的野生动物对队伍十分警惕，只有在先遭到攻击时才会还击。该地区只有一只巨锹甲虫。</p>\n<p><strong>金金斯：</strong>这些金金斯是柳岸镇入侵事件的幸存者。若金金斯受到任何伤害，它会惊恐尖叫并逃入荒野。</p>\n<p><strong>无面鬼：</strong>这些无面鬼士兵是被排斥者，他们始终未能被旧伐木营地中那支更大的聚落接纳（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d11lumbercam00]{D11}）。他们会战斗至死，希望若能将PC作为战利品，便能以此作为筹码买通自己进入更大的团体。由你决定：若PC即将达到3级，你可以让他们得知旧伐木营地里有无面鬼出没——更多细节见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{第4章}。</p>\n<p><strong>黏菌怪：</strong>这些饥渴的真菌斑块源自柳岸镇以南区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d7infestedgr00]{D7} 的真菌侵染，并蠕动着进入周围腹地，四处游荡，漫无目的地捕食野生动物。整个腹地里一共只有六只黏菌怪。</p>\n<p><strong>草人：</strong>这些不死生物并非玉鸟客栈（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d4canaryinn000]{D4}）里的草人之一。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Exploring the Hinterlands\">Exploring the Hinterlands</h2>\n<p>A map of the mindscape is available for this module. If you’re using the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>, the players have a map of the region. If you aren’t using this guide, consider providing a map of your own design for the players to use as a guide to their exploration.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.YbqD7ILHwWtGUF2P]{Hinterlands Control}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Controls all Tiles on the @UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{Willowshore Hinterlands} Scene.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/sog-party-token.webp\" alt=\"Party Token\" title=\"Party Token\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Token</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\"><a href=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/sog-party-token.webp\">Party Token</a></span>\n  </div>\n  <p>You can use this party token for your Party Actor in this hexploration.</p>\n</section>\n<p>As mentioned in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02willowshores01]{Willowshore Hinterlands}, forest hexes without roads are difficult terrain, as are rough and rocky fields in the southern hinterlands. When the PCs travel, make sure you know what exploration activities they’re taking. Once per day the PCs spend in the hinterlands, attempt a @Check[flat|dc:17] to see if an encounter occurs. On a success, roll [[/r 1d12]] on the following table if the PCs are within 2 hexes of Willowshore. Otherwise, roll a [[/r 1d20]] to determine what they meet in the wilderness. If an encounter occurs, you should decide if it takes place while they travel or while they camp.</p>\n\n<h1 class=\"table\">Hinterlands Random Encounters</h1>\n<hr />\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>[[/r 1d12]]{d12}/[[/r 1d20]]{d20}</th>\n      <th>Encounter</th>\n      <th>Threat</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–3</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.nuup7VijH5sidWgW]{Giant Centipedes}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4–6</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.IUvO1RsdI8ECHJZv]{Slime Mold}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7–9</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.Yc41IEb5kKayrMgN]{Thatchlings}</td>\n      <td>Trivial 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10–11</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.PckLz0BWyLcbvuZQ]{Hunting Spiders}</td>\n      <td>Low 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>12–13</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.1b4T5NeX6Oy8Fii5]{Wolves}</td>\n      <td>Low 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>14–15</td>\n      <td>3 @UUID[Actor.Yc41IEb5kKayrMgN]{Thatchlings}</td>\n      <td>Low 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>16–17</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.rVHaUobZlIE1txxP]{Jinkins}</td>\n      <td>Low 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>18</td>\n      <td>1 @UUID[Actor.bszU2NHYzIFKkn6R]{Giant Stag Beetle}</td>\n      <td>Moderate 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>19</td>\n      <td>4 @UUID[Actor.XIgSrA8HGoQsxfAw]{Noppera-bo Grunts}</td>\n      <td>Moderate 2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>20</td>\n      <td>2 @UUID[Actor.SxEWCTkiVM0OYB1B]{Boars}</td>\n      <td>Moderate 2</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Animals:</strong> Wild animals the PCs encounter are wary of the party and only attack if they’re attacked first. There’s only one giant stag beetle living in the region.</p>\n<p><strong>Jinkins:</strong> These jinkins are survivors from the invasion of Willowshore. A jinkin shrieks in fear if it takes any damage and flees into the wild.</p>\n<p><strong>Noppera-bos:</strong> These noppera-bo grunts are outcasts who never quite managed to be accepted into the larger gathering found at the lumber camp (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d11lumbercam00]{D11}). They fight to the death, hoping that if they can claim the PCs as trophies, they’ll be able to buy their way into the larger group. At your option, if the PCs are about to reach 3rd level, you can have them learn about the noppera-bo presence in the lumber camp—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{Chapter 4} for more details.</p>\n<p><strong>Slime Molds:</strong> These patches of ravenous fungi emerged from the fungal infestation south of Willowshore at area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d7infestedgr00]{D7}, and slithered out into the surrounding hinterlands to wander and prey upon wildlife indiscriminately. There are only six slime molds in all in the hinterlands.</p>\n<p><strong>Thatchlings:</strong> These undead aren’t part of the thatchlings found at Canary Inn (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05d4canaryinn000]{D4}).</p>"
            },
            "The Mindscape Border": {
              "name": "思维空间边界 The Mindscape Border",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Mindscape Border\">思维空间边界</h2>\n<p>PC们不该指望在前往唐入的路上遇到多少危险；为了也让玩家感受到这一点，你不应该把他们从柳岸镇顺流而下的旅程呈现为一次带有任何可能发生遭遇的探索——很快就会有大量这种玩法的时间！相反，一旦PC们动身出发，只需简要概述他们的旅程，并务必描述在这几天里降雨稀少（尽管头顶的天空往往仍阴云密布）会让人觉得这是个好兆头，预示着一个干燥、甚至宜人的夏天。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.nMGSWEzGAV8oU5KZ]{Toggle Mindscape Border Visibility}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>在他们预计抵达唐入前的几个小时里——离开葫芦湖不久、正要进入一处宽阔山谷之际——那里本应让他们首次瞥见幽海，并能看见坐落在海岸峭壁上的唐入要塞——另一团诡异的浓雾降临到队伍周围。这雾迅速变得出人意料、近乎超自然地浓重，将可见度压到十来英尺左右。马匹变得紧张而易受惊；而无论PC们朝哪个方向行进（甚至哪怕他们一动不动），片刻之后，雾气散去，显露出PC们已回到了他们刚刚离开的地方。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">环境音</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.2EdHOVRkV6jCZPFM]{Dense Fog}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>无论他们多少次试图继续前进，浓雾都会降下，而PC们发现自己又回到了起点。每当PC们试图跨越思维空间的边界时（如柳岸腹地地图所示；包括如果这些低等级PC不知怎地设法飞到空中），都会发生这种情况；但第一次发生时，理应令人不安、困惑，甚至恐惧。</p>\n<p>解开这一谜团会占据冒险路径相当多的篇幅，因此如果PC们施放法术，或尝试进行技能检定来回忆知识以了解这一怪异现象，你不应向他们透露太多。让PC们去尝试，但不论结果如何，都要让他们知道：造成浓雾的事物超出了他们目前的认知；顶多只能暗示可能是某种离奇的诅咒降临在这片土地上——毫无疑问与怪物的入侵以及贺总督与其宅邸的消失有关。由于PC们无法抵达唐入，他们应返回柳岸镇汇报自己的发现。他们这么做之后，继续进行第63页的“调查诅咒”。</p>\n<p>与此同时，夜幕将很快降临，随之而来的是一场暴雨。PC们将面临选择：是在葫芦湖附近露营过夜，还是在黑暗与湿冷中返家——此时，继续进行探索模式的游戏。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>使用本章</h2>\n  <p>一旦PC们发现思维空间的边缘，他们接下来去哪由他们自己决定——但最终，他们会回到柳岸镇。在那里与盟友的商议会提出三条特定的调查途径，以弄清该地区究竟发生了什么。这些调查在本章最后一节呈现，从第63页开始。本章其余部分概述了小型遭遇、地点，以及让PC们建立名声、获取财富与经验的机会。无论如何，本章内容应填满夏季的大部分时间，因为默认设定是：在鬼季的最后几周里，当秋意已隐约逼近时，PC们将在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{第4章}中找到有关“柳岸镇诅咒”真实成因的第一批线索。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Mindscape Border\">The Mindscape Border</h2>\n<p>The PCs shouldn’t expect to face much danger on the trip to Karahai, and to help the players feel this as well, you shouldn’t present their journey downriver from Willowshore as an exploration with any potential for an encounter—there will be plenty of time for this sort of gameplay soon enough! Instead, once the PCs set out on their trip, simply summarize their journey, making sure to describe how the lack of rain (even as the skies above tend to stay overcast) for these few days might feel like a good sign for a dry and even pleasant summer.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.nMGSWEzGAV8oU5KZ]{Toggle Mindscape Border Visibility}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>A few hours before they expect to reach Karahai, not long after they leave Gourd Lake behind and are about to emerge into a wide valley that should give them their first glimpse of the Sea of Ghosts with the fortress of Karahai visible on its coastline bluffs, another strange fog descends on the party. This fog quickly grows unexpectedly and almost supernaturally thick, reducing visibility to a dozen feet or so. The horses grow nervous and skittish, and regardless of the direction the PCs travel (or even if they remain motionless), a few moments later, the fog lifts to reveal the PCs have returned to the spot they just left.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.2EdHOVRkV6jCZPFM]{Dense Fog}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>No matter how many times they push forward, the fog descends, and the PCs find themselves back where they started. This takes place whenever the PCs attempt to cross the mindscape’s boundary, as indicated on the Willowshore Hinterlands map (including if the low-level PCs somehow manage to fly up into the air), but the first time it happens, it should be unsettling, confusing, and even frightening.</p>\n<p>The unraveling of this mystery takes up a fair amount of the Adventure Path, so you shouldn’t reveal much to the PCs if they cast spells or attempt skill checks to Recall Knowledge on this strange phenomenon. Let the PCs try, but regardless of the result, let them know that whatever is causing the fog is beyond their current knowledge, other than to suggest the possibility that some strange curse has settled down on the land—no doubt something tied to the invasion of monsters and the vanishing of Governor Heh and his estate. As the PCs won’t be able to reach Karahai, they should return to Willowshore to report their findings. Proceed with Investigating the Curse on page 63 once they do so.</p>\n<p>In the meantime, night will soon fall, and with it comes a rainstorm. The PCs are faced with the choice of camping for the night near Gourd Lake or returning home in the dark and wet—at this point, proceed with exploration mode play.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Using this Chapter</h2>\n  <p>Once the PCs discover the mindscape’s edge, where they go next is up to them—but eventually, they’ll return to Willowshore. Consultations with their allies there suggest three specific avenues of investigation to figure out what’s going on in the region. These investigations are presented in the last section of this chapter, starting on page 63. The remainder of this chapter summarizes minor encounters, locations, and opportunities to build reputation, wealth, and experience for the PCs. In any event, the contents of this chapter should fill the bulk of the summer, as the assumption is that in the last weeks of the season, as fall looms on the horizon, the PCs will find their first clues as to the true cause of the “Willowshore curse” in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal]{Chapter 4}.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Into the Hinterlands": {
              "name": "深入腹地 Into the Hinterlands",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Into the Hinterlands\">深入腹地</h1>\n<p>近来的事件让柳岸镇遭受重创；消息（以及求援请求）必须送往柳岸镇最近的邻居——设防聚居地唐入。唐入位于城镇以东数十英里处，坐落在幽海的海岸线上，长期以来一直是柳岸镇最重要的贸易伙伴。关于这次攻击，以及他们的总督与其庄园的损失，都必须上报。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.itMVg738D9sSe1lx]{柳岸腹地}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>这项任务落在PC们身上，因为他们给镇民与临时领导者都留下了深刻印象。无论是胡太婆还是老松木前来把任务交给PC们，请求都一样——沿着杜月江河岸向东南行进，将近期事件的消息送达唐入的温都督。前往唐入的路程是柳岸镇许多人走过的，也被认为是一条相对安全的路线。PC们所亲近的长者为他们每人准备了一匹马，以便更快沿路前行；若他们黎明出发，便能在日落前抵达海岸边的唐入。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Into the Hinterlands\">Into the Hinterlands</h1>\n<p>Recent events have left Willowshore reeling, and news (as well as requests for aid) must be sent to Willowshore’s closest neighbor, the fortified settlement of Karahai. Located several dozen miles to the east of town on the coast of the Sea of Ghosts, Karahai has long served as Willowshore’s most important trade partner. Word of the attack and the loss of their governor and his estate must be reported.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.HgqDtdyAVJFT3Dr1.PlaylistSound.itMVg738D9sSe1lx]{Willowshore Hinterlands}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>This task falls to the PCs, who have impressed both the town and its temporary leaders. Whether it’s Granny Hu or Old Matsuki who approaches the PCs with this task, the request is the same—make the journey southeast along the banks of the Duyue River to deliver news of recent events to Commander Wen of Karahai. The trip to Karahai is one many in Willowshore have made, and it’s known to be a relatively safe route. The PCs’ favored elder provides them all with horses to make the trip along the road even swifter, so that if they leave at dawn, they’ll arrive on the coast at Karahai just before sunset.</p>"
            },
            "The Mysterious Merchant": {
              "name": "神秘商人 The Mysterious Merchant",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Mysterious Merchant\">神秘商人</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇解放后的第二天（最好是在PC们与某位长老会面、并开始思考自己在小镇未来中将扮演的角色之前），一位带着乌鸦的陌生人乘坐马车来到柳岸镇镇区，支起了一个摊位。商人看起来很友善，但他到来的时机让镇民心生戒备。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinzo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shinzo\" alt=\"A man with a friendly smile wearing a wide brimmed hat\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinzo.webp')\" />\n<p>这位毫不起眼的商人看上去像个普通的天朝男子，但他暗地里其实是在为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}效力的强大存在——一名死神，名叫朝比奈神藏；他仍在为数十年前、早于预言破灭之年降临之前对法莱斯玛犯下的过失赎罪。由于被明确禁止直接干预任何凡人的命运，神藏希望通过尽己所能帮助那些被困在柳岸镇的思维空间中的人逃脱（无论是回归生命还是走向死亡），以偿还自己对墓之女士的债。他的乌鸦同伙是一名名叫Yix的诺索伊招魂者，并始终保持鸟类形态。诺索伊来到这里是为了默默观察神藏，却丝毫不会透露自己并非只是一只友善（尽管偶尔吵闹）的乌鸦。他的马与马车是魔法构装体，每当他造访思维空间时便会显现，但他所出售的货物都是真货。</p>\n<p>神藏始终维持着人类伪装，自我介绍为一名旅行推销员，希望将柳岸镇加入他的常规路线。他向PC们展示自己目前的货品，打开马车让他们挑选，但此时他能提供的东西不多，除了一些小物件与补给品之外（任意2级或以下的普通物品）。神藏也能收购PC们想要出售的任何物品或装备，并按正常价格出价。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>神藏去了哪里？</h1>\n  <p>\n    神藏拥有一种独特的能力，能随心所欲地出入柳岸镇的思维空间，但他从不会在PC们观察到时这么做。他的等级足够高，以至于任何试图跟踪他的人都应当会轻易被他的隐匿所挫败。若有人问他如何获得补给，或他是否能在边地的边界之外旅行，神藏起初会含糊其辞。如果被追问，他会“承认”自己也不确定在两次造访之间自己究竟去往何处、又从何处而来，只希望自己在柳岸镇的这段时间能对PC们有所帮助。随着<em>鬼季</em>\n    的推进，PC们将逐渐了解更多关于神藏的事，但至少在第1幕与第2幕中，这位商人应当始终保持友善、乐于帮助、彬彬有礼……而又难以捉摸。\n  </p>\n</aside>\n<p>然而，正如他热切解释的那样，他对PC们最大的帮助，是他有能力取得PC们可能想要的物品，并在下次造访时带回来出售。起初，这项服务看起来未必有什么优势，因为在较低等级时，PC们在柳岸镇的商店里就能以更低等级买到许多所需之物。不过，随着冒险之路的推进，神藏那种能来去自如的诡异能力将成为PC们愈发重要的资产，使他们获得原本无法得到的购物机会。</p>\n<p><strong>神藏的补给：</strong>你可以用两种方式处理神藏提供的补给。你可以为PC们制作一份清单，作为他每次造访时可供挑选的物品，把他的马车装满十来件等级不高于队伍等级的各类物品；或者，你也可以允许玩家“下订单”。在第二种系统中，PC们请求的物品会在神藏下次造访小镇时可供购买，但同样地，他能提供出售的物品的最高等级仍以队伍等级为上限。</p>\n<p><strong>造访时机：</strong>神藏造访柳岸镇的频率每月不超过四次。他往往会很“恰好”地在PC们升级前后出现，并在他们出发进行或从一次漫长远征归来前后现身。他的造访通常应至少间隔1周。尽量将他的到来安排在PC们接近升级时，或当PC们达到某一级别的进度中点时。</p>\n<p><strong>停留时长：</strong>神藏每次造访时都会在柳岸镇停留24小时。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.VR1b9qD9ECg88orU]{神藏}</span>\n    <span>生物 17</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Monitor</li>\n  </ul>\n    <p>男性死神</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.67ppwa3mx0hrjRJi]{Yix}</span>\n    <span>生物 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">超小型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Monitor</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Psychopomp</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Mysterious Merchant\">The Mysterious Merchant</h1>\n<p>The day after the liberation of Willowshore (preferably before the PCs have met with one of the elders and have begun to think about their role in the town’s future), a stranger with a raven arrives in a horse-drawn cart and sets up a stall in downtown Willowshore. The merchant appears friendly, but the timing of his arrival makes the townsfolk wary.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinzo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shinzo\" alt=\"A man with a friendly smile wearing a wide brimmed hat\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinzo.webp')\" />\n<p>Though this nondescript merchant looks like an average Tian man, he’s secretly a powerful entity in the service of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}—a @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21shinigami00000]{Shinigami} named Asahina Shinzo who’s still undergoing penitence for an infraction against Pharasma made decades before the advent of the Age of Lost Omens. Explicitly barred from directly intervening in the fate of any mortal, Shinzo hopes that by doing what he can to help those trapped in Willowshore’s mindscape escape (be it back to life or on to death), he can repay his debt to the Lady of Graves. His raven accomplice is a nosoi psychopomp named Yix who remains in bird form at all times. Here to silently observe Shinzo, the nosoi gives no clue that he’s anything other than a friendly (if periodically noisy) raven. His horse and wagon are magical constructs that manifest whenever he visits the mindscape, but the wares he has to offer are real.</p>\n<p>Shinzo maintains his human disguise at all times, introducing himself to the PCs as a traveling salesperson who hopes to add Willowshore to his regular route. He offers his current wares to the PCs, opening his cart for them to shop through, but at this time, he has little to offer beyond minor items and supplies (any common item of up to 2nd level). Shinzo can also buy any items or equipment the PCs wish to sell, offering normal prices.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Where Does Shinzo Go?</h1>\n  <p>\n    Shinzo has a unique ability to come and go from Willowshore’s mindscape as he wishes, but never does so when the PCs observe him. His level is sufficiently high enough that any attempt to follow him should be easily defeated by his Stealth. If asked about how he obtains his supplies, or whether he can travel beyond the boundaries of the hinterlands, Shinzo is initially evasive. If pressed, he “admits” he isn’t sure where he goes to or comes from in between visits, hoping only that his time here in Willowshore proves helpful to the PCs. As <em>Season of Ghosts</em>\n    continues, the PCs will learn more about Shinzo, but for Acts 1 and 2 at least, the merchant should remain friendly, helpful, polite... and enigmatic.\n  </p>\n</aside>\n<p>His greatest service to the PCs, though, as he eagerly explains, is his capacity to obtain items the PCs might desire and to return with them for sale on a following visit. Initially, this service might not seem like a particular advantage, as the PCs can purchase much of what they need at lower levels from shops in Willowshore. However, as the Adventure Path progresses, Shinzo’s uncanny ability to come and go will become an increasingly important asset for the PCs, giving them access to shopping opportunities they otherwise wouldn’t have.</p>\n<p><strong>Shinzo’s Supplies:</strong> You can handle the supplies Shinzo offers in two ways. You can create a list of items for the PCs to shop through on each of his visits, filling his cart with a dozen various items of a level no higher than the party’s level, or you can allow your players to “place orders” for things. In this second system, items the PCs request are available for purchase upon Shinzo’s next visit to town, but again, the upper-level limit of items he can offer for sale is set by the party’s level.</p>\n<p><strong>Visit Timing:</strong> Shinzo visits Willowshore no more often than four times per month. He conveniently tends to show up right before or after the PCs level up, and before or after they set out on or return from a lengthy expedition. His visits should generally be spaced out by at least 1 week. Try to time his arrival for when the PCs are close to leveling up, or when the PCs reach the halfway point of a level.</p>\n<p><strong>Length of Stay:</strong> Shinzo stays in Willowshore for 24 hours each time he visits.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.VR1b9qD9ECg88orU]{Shinzo}</span>\n    <span>Creature 17</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Monitor</li>\n  </ul>\n    <p>Male Shinigami</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.67ppwa3mx0hrjRJi]{Yix}</span>\n    <span>Creature 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Tiny</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Monitor</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Psychopomp</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Willowshore Curse": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的诅咒 The Willowshore Curse",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Willowshore Curse\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第3章：</span>\n  <span>柳岸镇的诅咒</span>\n</h1>\n<p>一旦PC们击败了三名怪物头目并点亮<em>长明灯</em>，柳岸镇的生活便能回归正常。在接下来的日子里，镇民着手进行一项沉重的工作：为死者安排葬礼、救治伤者、搜寻失踪者，同时也努力修补、重建并修复这座城镇，使其从怪物入侵造成的伤害中恢复过来。最终，近三打市民在怪物占领期间丧生，使柳岸镇的人口降至225人。</p>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{胡太婆}和@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{老松木}承担起领导角色。尽管两人对柳岸镇的未来各有愿景与计划，但PC们可以决定更愿意站在哪一边——或者是否更愿意与两人都结盟，或与两人都不结盟。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-spider-fight.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Spider Fight\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Willowshore Curse\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 3:</span>\n  <span>The Willowshore Curse</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs have defeated the three monstrous ringleaders and lit the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, life can return to normal for Willowshore. In the days that follow, townsfolk set about the grim task of arranging funerals for the dead, treating the wounded, and searching for the missing, as well as working to repair, rebuild, and restore the town from the damage caused by the monstrous invasion. In the end, nearly three dozen citizens perished during the monstrous occupation, leaving Willowshore’s population at 225.</p>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21grannyhubann00]{Granny Hu} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21oldmatsukish00]{Old Matsuki} fall into leadership roles. While each has their own vision and plan for Willowshore’s future, the PCs get to decide who they prefer to side with—or if they prefer to ally with both or neither.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 1.4: The Wall of Ghosts": {
          "name": "第一幕 1.4：鬼打墙 Act 1.4: The Wall of Ghosts",
          "pages": {
            "Concluding Act 1": {
              "name": "第 1 幕收尾 Concluding Act 1",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding Act 1\">第一幕结尾</h1>\n<p>在PC们造访旧伐木营地后幸存下来的无面怪，会在接下来的几天里迅速解散，可能是因为他们的首领被击败，也意识到PC们强大到无法对抗。由你酌情决定：如果PC们在对付无面怪时表现不够强势，这些生物可能会继续作为柳岸镇的持续威胁，直到他们被击败或被谈判安抚为止。尽管随着冬季在<em>鬼季</em>中到来，PC们还会遭遇另一支更强大的无面怪团体，但这一伙在战役中不再有后续的既定戏份。</p>\n<p>如果PC们带着从马厩中救回的被绑者返回柳岸镇，队伍会被当作英雄迎接，并在两个派系中各获得3点声望点数。如果PC们带回的幸存被绑者更少，尤其是当PC们对怪物夺走的生命显得轻率或漠不关心时，你可以视情况降低这份声望点数奖励。</p>\n<p>根据夏季结束、秋季开始前还剩多少天，你会想给PC们一些时间来休息、恢复，并进行额外的休整模式活动。此时可以继续推进并完成来自@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}中尚未完成的@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00]{机遇}。否则，你也可以直接将时间跳转到秋季第一天，将夏末剩余的日子描述为阴郁、雨水不断的数周，在这段时间里，镇民们慢慢适应自己被困在诅咒之中的新现实。</p>\n<p>不过也有一条好消息：PC们为帮助柳岸镇巩固并提供支援所采取的动作，让小镇对自身更有信心了。此时，柳岸镇的有效等级提升至5，相关影响详见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02peopleofwill00#growing-the-town]{小镇成长}边栏。</p>\n<p>当夏季的最后几天走向终结时，关于折磨柳岸镇的“诅咒”的本质，PC们应当留下的问题多于答案；但他们应把鬼打墙之谜、墙外有什么，以及神秘的名字“苦迦菩提”，视为今后推进的主要线索。随着秋季开始，更紧迫的事务很快迫近：柳岸镇是否有足够的食物让居民撑过即将到来的冬季？此外，镇里开始出现诡异的新一轮闹鬼——与PC们之前面对过的不同的超自然事件。柳岸镇再一次出了问题；当那场仿佛从未存在过的多雨之夏的最后一天逝去，解决小镇困境的责任将越来越多地落在这片地区最新的英雄肩上。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{更改季节}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>更改@UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{柳岸镇}与@UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{柳岸腹地}场景的季节。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding Act 1\">Concluding Act 1</h1>\n<p>The noppera-bos who survive the PCs’ visit to the lumber camp quickly disband in the following days, likely as a result of the defeat of their leaders and the realization that the PCs are too powerful to stand against. At your discretion, if the PCs didn’t make a strong showing against the noppera-bos, the creatures might remain as a continuing threat to Willowshore until they’re either defeated or bargained with. While the PCs will encounter another, more powerful group of noppera-bos as winter arrives in <em>Season of Ghosts</em>, this particular band has no further scheduled role to play in the campaign.</p>\n<p>If the PCs return to Willowshore with the abductees from the stables, the party is greeted as heroes and earn 3 Reputation Points with both factions. Reduce this Reputation Point award as you see fit if the PCs return with fewer surviving abductees, especially if the PCs seem cavalier or dismissive about any lives lost to the monsters.</p>\n<p>Depending on how many days are left in summer before fall begins, you’ll want to give the PCs some time to rest, recover, and pursue additional downtime activities. Unfinished @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05opportunitie00]{Opportunities} from @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3} can be pursued and completed at this time. Otherwise, you can simply jump forward in time to the first day of fall, describing the remaining days of summer as dreary, rain-filled weeks during which the townsfolk slowly adapt to their new reality of being trapped within a curse.</p>\n<p>There’s one bit of good news, though: the PCs’ actions in helping to bolster and support Willowshore have helped the town grow more confident in itself. At this point, Willowshore’s effective level increases to 5, with ramifications detailed in the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02peopleofwill00#growing-the-town]{Growing the Town} sidebar.</p>\n<p>As the final days of summer draw to a close, the PCs should be left with more questions than answers as to the nature of the “curse” that afflicts Willowshore, but they should consider the mystery of the Wall of Ghosts, what lies beyond it, and the mysterious name of “Kugaptee” as their primary clues going forward. With fall beginning, more pressing matters soon loom, for the question of whether or not Willowshore will have enough food for its citizens through the coming winter arises. In addition, strange new hauntings begin to manifest in the town—supernatural events unlike those the PCs have faced before. Something is wrong with Willowshore once again, and as the last day of the rainy summer that never was passes, the responsibility of solving the town’s problems increasingly falls upon the shoulders of the region’s newest heroes.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{Change Season}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Changes the Season on the @UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{Willowshore} and @UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{Willowshore Hinterlands} Scenes.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Arriving too Late": {
              "name": "来得太迟 Arriving too Late",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">来得太晚</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 3</span>\n</h3>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">来得太晚</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.WU9xvNKJAkAn1ldw]{苦迦菩提的祝福（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>如果邹斗完成了仪式，她对蒙松的献祭将导致同样的进展，只是蒙松的尸体也会转化为苦迦菩提的祝福之一。当PC们最终抵达仪式地点时，他们会发现四个行动迟缓的不死，以俯伏的姿势匍匐在鬼打墙前，仿佛在膜拜它。这四个怪物会在PC们靠近时起身发动攻击，战斗方式如上文所述，但在这场战斗中，PC们将面对四个变体蛮力丧尸，而不是三个，使其成为一次严峻 3 的遭遇。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Arriving too Late</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 3</span>\n</h3>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Arriving too Late</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.WU9xvNKJAkAn1ldw]{Kugaptee's Blessings (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If Zoudou finishes the ritual, her sacrifice of Meng-sung results in the same development, only Meng-sung’s body also transforms into one of Kugaptee’s Blessings. When the PCs eventually arrive at the ritual site, they find four lumbering undead in prostrate positions before the Wall of Ghosts, as if worshipping it. These four monsters rise up to attack the PCs as they approach, fighting as detailed above, but in this fight, the PCs face four of the variant zombie brutes rather than three, making this a Severe 3 encounter.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Interrupting the Ritual": {
              "name": "打断仪式 Interrupting the Ritual",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">打断仪式</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kugaptee's Blessing\" alt=\"Kugaptee's Blessing\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p>如果PC们在邹斗献祭蒙松之前赶到仪式地点，而PC们最终与无面鬼交战，那么一旦仪式被打断（很可能就在邹斗被杀死、并且维持对仪式专注的剩余无面鬼秘术师放弃并逃跑之时；但如果PC攻击或以其他方式打断该秘术师对仪式的专注，则可能更早发生），鬼打墙之外便会传来一阵突如其来的轰鸣——仿佛一棵巨树突然倾倒。任何幸存的无面鬼都会因恐惧而瘫跪在地，开始用心灵感应乞求饶命；与此同时，一个庞大而朦胧的人形阴影在鬼打墙之外直立而起。阴影从远侧猛扑向墙，使得那道雾状屏障骤然弯曲鼓胀，仿佛它是一堵正被外力推挤的实体墙。阴影随即消失，鬼打墙仍完好无损，但三名无面鬼的尸体——无论生死——都会突然爆裂，从他们的体内爬出对其原本形态的巨大拙劣模仿，甩脱较小的躯壳，化作自身扭曲的不死版本。他们的手臂低垂，几乎垂至脚踝，且在数处看似折断；他们没有头颅，取而代之的是发霉的柳条笼，笼中塞满血色蝴蝶。这些便是苦迦菩提的祝福，它们立刻攻击PC们。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">音效</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.PM69203E3Y3UrHfA.PlaylistSound.zTB0rlZ50l913rYN]{打断仪式}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">打断仪式</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.WU9xvNKJAkAn1ldw]{苦迦菩提的祝福 (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>尽管这些可怖的不死生物外表格外令人不安，预示着PC们在接下来的冒险中将越来越常面对的灵堕魔邪魔的形貌，但它们在机制上与蛮力丧尸完全相同。虽然它们是中型而非大型，但其断裂的长肢仍保有典型蛮力丧尸的触及。苦迦菩提的祝福无心智且嗜暴，会蹒跚上前攻击PC，但一旦PC移动到仪式地点地图边界之外，它们在1轮后便会放弃追击，返回祭坛，在鬼打墙前俯首跪拜，直到再次遭到攻击。每当一名苦迦菩提的祝福受到伤害，一团闪亮的血红蝴蝶便会从伤口爆散而出，盘旋升空后融化为缕缕红烟，飞上去重新汇入鬼打墙的雾气之中。</p>\n</section>\n<p>如果某位PC提出以自己替代蒙松，那么同样的场景会再度上演，只是从无面鬼体内爬出的三名祝福不会攻击那位向苦迦菩提献身的PC。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Interrupting the Ritual</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kugaptee's Blessing\" alt=\"Kugaptee's Blessing\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p>If the PCs arrive at the ritual site before Zoudou sacrifices Meng-sung, and the PCs end up fighting the noppera-bos, then as soon as the ritual is disrupted (likely as soon as Zoudou is slain and the remaining noppera-bo occultist maintaining concentration on the ritual gives up and flees, but earlier if the PCs attack or otherwise disrupt that occultist’s focus on the ritual), a sudden rumble—as if an enormous tree suddenly toppled over—rolls out from beyond the Wall of Ghosts. Any surviving noppera-bos collapse to their knees in fear and begin to telepathically beg for mercy as a vast, vaguely humanoid shadow rears up beyond the Wall of Ghosts. The shadow lunges at the wall from the far side, causing the misty barrier to suddenly flex and bulge as if it were a solid wall being pushed against from beyond. The shadow vanishes and leaves the Wall of Ghosts intact, but the bodies of the three noppera-bos, be they living or dead, suddenly burst apart as immense mockeries of their previous forms climb out of their bodies, shedding the smaller frames to emerge as misshapen undead versions of themselves. Their arms hang low, nearly to their ankles, and appear to be broken in several places; instead of heads, they have moldy wicker cages filled with blood-colored butterflies. These are Kugaptee’s Blessings, and they attack the PCs at once.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Sound Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.PM69203E3Y3UrHfA.PlaylistSound.zTB0rlZ50l913rYN]{Interrupting the Ritual}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-kugaptees-blessing.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Interrupting the Ritual</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.WU9xvNKJAkAn1ldw]{Kugaptee's Blessings (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>While these awful undead creatures have particularly unsettling appearances that foreshadow the shapes of the nindoru fiends the PCs will increasingly face in the coming adventures, they function identically to zombie brutes. While they’re Medium sized rather than Large, their long broken limbs retain the reach of a typical zombie brute. Mindless and violent, Kugaptee’s Blessings shamble forth to attack the PCs but give up pursuit after 1 round once the PCs move beyond the ritual site map’s border, returning to the altar to bow down before the Wall of Ghosts until they’re attacked again. Each time one of Kugaptee’s Blessings is damaged, a cloud of glistening blood-red butterflies bursts from the wound to spiral into the air before melting away into wisps of red smoke that fly up to rejoin the mists of the Wall of Ghosts.</p>\n</section>\n<p>If one of the PCs offered themselves as a replacement for Meng-sung, then the same scene plays out, only the three blessings that emerge from the noppera-bos don’t attack the PC who offered themself to Kugaptee.</p>"
            },
            "Horror from Beyond": {
              "name": "彼岸之外的恐怖 Horror from Beyond",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Horror from Beyond\">墙外恐怖</h1>\n<p>邹斗希望在@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}仪式的最后，献祭一个灵魂已多次转世的生物（她相信自己是在用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.OhD2Z6rIGGD5ocZA]{阅读灵光}检查蒙松时发现了这一点），从而赢得苦迦菩提的青睐，并从鬼打墙之外召来更多爪牙为她的计划效力。然而，邹斗关于蒙松的理论，以及关于苦迦菩提的理论，都是错误的——作为苦迦菩提意志的造物，邹斗对这名恶魔的了解不过是其名字，以及一种与他相关的、奇异的忠诚感。在她存在的过去几个月里为祷告派建立起来的大部分信仰，都是无心编造的谎言；这些谎言披着“看似真实”的外衣，甚至连邹斗自己也被其迷惑。</p>\n<p>因此，如果邹斗完成她的仪式，等待她的命运可能比死在PC们手中更糟，因为她的仪式确实会吸引到一丝苦迦菩提的影响——只是不是以她所希望的方式。</p>\n<p>PC们将如何遭遇这来自鬼打墙之外的恐怖，取决于他们是在邹斗献祭蒙松之前就与其对峙并将其击败，还是她得以完成仪式。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Horror from Beyond\">Horror from Beyond</h1>\n<p>Zoudou hopes that by sacrificing a creature whose soul has reincarnated several times (a discovery she believes she made while examining Meng-sung with @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.OhD2Z6rIGGD5ocZA]{Read Aura}) at the end of the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} ritual, she can earn Kugaptee’s favor and draw additional minions from beyond the Wall of Ghosts to serve her agenda. However, Zoudou’s theories about Meng-sung, as well as those about Kugaptee, are faulty—as a creation of Kugaptee’s will, Zoudou knows little more than the fiend’s name and a strange sensation of loyalty related to him. The majority of the faith she has built for the Prayers over the past few months of her existence are unintentional fabrications that delude even Zoudou with their veneer of veracity.</p>\n<p>As a result, if Zoudou completes her ritual, the fate that awaits her might be worse than death at the PCs’ hands, for her ritual does attract a glimmer of Kugaptee’s influence—just not in the way she hopes.</p>\n<p>The way in which the PCs encounter this horror from beyond the Wall of Ghosts depends on if they confront and defeat Zoudou before she sacrifices Meng-sung or if she’s able to complete the ritual.</p>"
            },
            "Zoudou’s Rite": {
              "name": "邹斗的仪式 Zoudou’s Rite",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E17. 走豆的仪式</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>林间小径忽然抵达一处林中空地，几棵倒下的树木与残存的树桩昭示着多年前曾在此进行、后又被遗弃的伐木工作。越过一根倒木，空地西北侧被一堵翻涌的雾墙遮蔽，那雾墙直冲天际，高达五十尺。偶尔，有些似乎在无声尖叫的幽魂在雾中挣扎翻滚，仿佛受折磨的灵魂被困在浓雾里。雾墙旁立着一座三层石台，而在这座台子以东不远处，则是一座用弯折枝条与木条搭成的半球形笼子。</p>\n</div>\n<p>若PC抵达得太晚而无面鬼已离开，你也可以用同样的描述来呈现此处。若PC按时到达，则向他们描述正在此处进行复杂仪式的生物。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenote\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">场景音频</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.0bOWhoQGj3oszwDz]{停止吟诵}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>这座古老的石制神龛原本供奉本地的神祇，但已被苦迦菩提的信徒腐化，改作奉祀那位古老邪魔的神龛。</p>\n<p>木笼子是空的——原先关在其中的祭品刚被移至神龛本体。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zoudou.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zoudou\" alt=\"female noppera-bo\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zoudou.webp');width:65%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>祷徒首领——狂热者走豆——站在被腐化祭坛的第二级台阶上；可怜的蒙松被绑住手脚，仰面躺在神龛最高一层的台阶前。那年轻人不断扭动挣扎，隔着口中的塞布发出尖叫，却毫无用处。一对无面鬼秘术师站在东侧与南侧的地面上，距离神龛最低一级台阶约5尺，作为副施法者履行职责。与此同时，走豆正主导进行@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}仪式，她希望藉此引起苦迦菩提的注意，为这片区域获得他的祝福，甚至可能让他从彼岸派出爪牙来壮大祷徒的力量。</p>\n<p>走豆傲慢地认为不会有人打断她正在进行的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}仪式，因此在PC变得无法忽视之前，她与副施法者进行察觉检定时承受–4环境减值——这也包括先攻检定。蒙松只穿着兜裆布并被牢牢捆住（逃脱DC 25）；他除此之外并未受伤，但只要有个拿着匕首、阴森而无面的怪物在他身旁逼视，他就不会尝试挣脱。</p>\n\n<p>由于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}需要3天施放，PC当然有时间在仪式结束、蒙松被献祭前进行阻止。仅仅靠近走豆并引起她注意不足以打断仪式：只要至少有一名副施法者持续将注意力集中在仪式上，即便另一名副施法者与走豆正在与PC战斗，仪式仍可继续。</p>\n<p>由于加持术需要3天施放，PC当然有时间在仪式结束、蒙松被献祭前进行阻止。仅仅靠近走豆并引起她注意不足以打断仪式：只要至少有一名副施法者持续将注意力集中在仪式上，即便另一名副施法者与走豆正在与PC战斗，仪式仍可继续。</p>\n<p>若PC是被来自区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e14workersdo00]{E14}的无面鬼秘术师引来此处，走豆虽为打扰而恼火，但仍同意与PC交谈，听听他们的请求。对PC不幸的是，走豆无意停止仪式；若PC确实想救蒙松，走豆只同意以高昂代价交换：必须有一名PC自愿代替蒙松。若PC同意，走豆如下回应。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“事情再简单不过，苦迦菩提慷慨而包容。到他的鬼打墙之前来吧，被缠缚之子。我将教你如何从尘世的枷锁中解脱。重复我的话：</p>\n  <p>“我献上我的名字，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从那些我曾称作朋友之人中解开。</p>\n  <p>“我献上我的血，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从那些我曾称作家人之人中解开。</p>\n  <p>“我献上我的肉，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从我称为自我的躯体中解开。</p>\n  <p>“最后，我献上我的灵魂，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从那曾是我命运之物中解开。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>多数PC很可能会对这段祷词退缩，而这确实理所当然，因为下一阶段将让那名PC取代蒙松躺上祭坛。@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}仪式并不会以牺牲PC性命告终，而是以走豆用匕首划过PC身体，并“切断”其灵魂与生死轮回之间的联系作为终结。以这种方式许诺灵魂，除崇拜苦迦菩提之外的所有宗教而言都算作禁忌之举，并可能对武僧或牧师角色带来后果，但对该PC不会产生其他立刻的效果——直到他们死亡。届时，该PC的灵魂会被吸入苦迦菩提的领域，使该PC无法被复活或以其他方式恢复生命。由你决定：在<em>鬼季</em>最终幕的最后一部分中，这类被杀PC的灵魂或许有机会被遭遇或被救出。一次成功的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.7Fd4lxozd11MQ55N]{赎罪}仪式也能打破与苦迦菩提之间的这条联系，避免这般不快的结局。</p>\n<p>若PC拒绝交换，走豆便嗤笑并评论她并不意外PC缺乏信念与灵性上的怯懦。若PC不发起攻击，走豆将回到@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}仪式中。若PC放任仪式进行至结束，蒙松将被献祭。继续@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06horrorfrombe00]{来自彼岸的恐怖}。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-zoudou.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">走豆的仪式</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.msoPJuPk1q97mDXm]{狂热者走豆} @UUID[Actor.LcC1VeVjPz5BwrMF]{无面鬼秘术师（2名）} @UUID[Actor.lGBv5utJ47MczpYw]{蒙松}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>PC更有可能（且合情合理地）对这个选项退缩——甚至更可能在看到无面鬼正准备献祭蒙松时直接发起攻击。在这种情况下，走豆与其中一名无面鬼秘术师会脱离仪式与PC作战，并尽全力保护另一名秘术师不被打断。只要仍有一名秘术师每个回合都以心灵感应向苦迦菩提吟诵祷文（你可以让PC“偷听”到这些祷文与上方朗读文本相似，以向玩家传达对这位神秘邪魔所作的诡异许诺），若走豆设法击败队伍，加持术仪式仍可继续推进。</p>\n  <p>走豆战至死地；秘术师也会在走豆存活时战斗至死。一旦走豆被杀，任何幸存的秘术师便会惊慌失措，准备逃跑。此时，继续@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06horrorfrombe00]{来自彼岸的恐怖}，这可能使这些逃跑的邪教徒遭遇一种比PC能施加给他们的任何下场都更为可怕的命运。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.IRymcJl2t1euPXn0]{走豆} <br />走豆随身携带的那本破烂皮装账册，曾被旧伐木营地的头目用来记录利润与支出，但只有前四分之一的页面写着这些平凡的记账内容。其余页面则写满了走豆密密麻麻的笔记与理论，内容涉及苦迦菩提、鬼打墙的本质，以及她逐渐坚信在墙外存在的“乐园”。这些笔记混杂以阿克罗语与深渊古语写成，因此角色必须能读懂这两种语言才能研读其内容。能读懂两者的角色可以通过该日记学会加持术仪式，但这些信息更大的用途将于下一幕中展开：走豆笔记中的线索能帮助PC穿越鬼打墙打开一道门扉。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E17. Zoudou’s Rite</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The forest trail suddenly reaches a clearing in the woods, where a few fallen trees and stumps testify to woodcutting pursuits abandoned years ago. Beyond a fallen tree, the clearing’s northwestern side is obscured by a seething wall of mist that reaches fifty feet into the sky. Now and then, what appear to be silently screaming ghosts thrash and writhe through this mist, as if tormented souls were trapped within the fog. A three-tiered stone stands near this wall, while a bit further to the east of this platform stands a dome-shaped cage built of bent branches and wooden slats.</p>\n</div>\n<p>You can use this same description for the location if the PCs arrive too late and the noppera-bos have moved on. If the PCs arrive on time, though, describe to them the creatures that are performing a complex ritual here.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenote\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Audio</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.0bOWhoQGj3oszwDz]{Stop Chanting}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>The old stone shrine was originally devoted to the kami of the region but has been corrupted by Kugaptee’s faithful into a shrine devoted to the ancient fiend.</p>\n<p>The wooden cage is empty—the sacrifice that was kept in it having just been moved to the shrine itself.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zoudou.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zoudou\" alt=\"female noppera-bo\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zoudou.webp');width:65%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The leader of the Prayers, Zoudou the Zealous, stands on the second step of the corrupted altar, with poor Meng-sung bound hand and foot and lying on his back before her on the tallest tier of the shrine. The young man squirms and thrashes and shrieks through the gag he wears, but to no avail. A pair of noppera-bo occultists stand on the ground to the east and south, about 5 feet from the shrine’s lowest step, performing duties as secondary casters. Meanwhile, Zoudou leads the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} ritual she hopes will attract Kugaptee’s attention, secure his blessing over the area, and potentially even result in him sending agents from beyond to bolster the Prayers’ strength.</p>\n<p>Zoudou arrogantly doesn’t expect interruptions to the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} ritual she’s in the middle of performing, so she and the secondary casters take a –4 circumstance penalty to Perception checks until the PCs become impossible to ignore—this includes initiative checks. Meng-sung wears only a loincloth and is tightly bound (Escape DC 25); while he’s otherwise unharmed, he won’t try to get free as long as a creepy, faceless monster armed with a dagger looms over him.</p>\n\n<p>As @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} takes 3 days to cast, the PCs certainly have time to interrupt the ritual before it ends with Meng-sung’s sacrifice. Merely approaching Zoudou and getting her attention isn’t enough to disrupt the ritual, for as long as at least one of the secondary casters maintains focus on the ritual, it can continue even while the other and Zoudou fight the PCs.</p>\n<p>As consecrate takes 3 days to cast, the PCs certainly have time to interrupt the ritual before it ends with Meng-sung’s sacrifice. Merely approaching Zoudou and getting her attention isn’t enough to disrupt the ritual, for as long as at least one of the secondary casters maintains focus on the ritual, it can continue even while the other and Zoudou fight the PCs.</p>\n<p>If the PCs were led here by the noppera-bo occultists from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e14workersdo00]{E14}, Zoudou is annoyed at the interruption but agrees to speak with the PCs to hear their plea. Unfortunately for the PCs, Zoudou isn’t interested in halting her ritual, and if the PCs truly wish to save Meng-sung, Zoudou agrees only at a steep price: one of the PCs must offer themself in Meng-sung’s place. If the PCs agree, Zoudou replies as follows.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“It is quite simple, for Kugaptee is generous and accepting. Come before his Wall, Child of the Ensnared. I will show you how to free yourself from the bondage of the world. Repeat my words:</p>\n  <p>“I offer thee my name, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from those whom I called friends.</p>\n  <p>“I offer thee my blood, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from those whom I called family.</p>\n  <p>“I offer thee my flesh, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from the body I called my own.</p>\n  <p>“Lastly, I offer thee my soul, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from that which was my fate.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>Most PCs will likely balk at this prayer, and rightfully so, for the next stage involves that PC taking Meng-sung’s place on the altar. Rather than ending in the sacrifice of the PC’s life, the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} ritual ends with Zoudou passing her dagger over the PC’s body and “cutting” their soul’s link to the cycle of life and death. Promising a soul in this way counts as an act of anathema for all religions other than the worship of Kugaptee and could have repercussions on champion or cleric characters, but it has no other immediate effect on the PC—until they die. At which point, the PC’s soul is absorbed into Kugaptee’s domain, preventing that PC from being resurrected or otherwise restored to life. At your discretion, the soul of such a slain PC could potentially be encountered or rescued in the final part of the last act of <em>Season of Ghosts</em>. A successful @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.7Fd4lxozd11MQ55N]{Atone} ritual can also break this link to Kugaptee and prevent this unpleasant fate.</p>\n<p>If the PCs refuse the exchange, Zoudou sneers and observes that she isn’t surprised at the PCs’ lack of conviction and their spiritual cowardice. If the PCs don’t attack, Zoudou returns to the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} ritual. If the PCs allow the ritual to play out to its end, Meng-sung is sacrificed. Proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06horrorfrombe00]{Horror from Beyond}.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-zoudou.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Zoudou’s Rite</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.msoPJuPk1q97mDXm]{Zoudou The Zealous} @UUID[Actor.LcC1VeVjPz5BwrMF]{Noppera-bo Occultists (2)} @UUID[Actor.lGBv5utJ47MczpYw]{Meng-Sung}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>It’s more likely that the PCs will (rightfully) balk at this option—or even more likely, simply attack the noppera-bos when they see them in the act of preparing to sacrifice Meng-sung. In this case, Zoudou and one of the noppera-bo occultists break off from the ritual to fight the PCs, doing their best to protect the other occultist from being disrupted. As long as one occultist continues to spend every round telepathically chanting prayers to Kugaptee (feel free to let the PCs “overhear” these prayers as ones similar to those in the read aloud text above, so as to convey to the players the eerie promises to the mysterious fiend), the consecrate ritual can proceed if Zoudou manages to defeat the party.</p>\n  <p>Zoudou fights to the death, as do the occultists as long as Zoudou lives. Once Zoudou is slain, any remaining occultists panic and prepare to flee the area. At this point, proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06horrorfrombe00]{Horror from Beyond}, which may result in these fleeing cultists facing a fate worse than any the PCs could inflict upon them.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.IRymcJl2t1euPXn0]{Zoudou} <br />The tattered leather-bound ledger that Zoudou carries was once used by the lumber camp boss to track profits and expenditures, but only the first quarter of the pages contain these mundane annotations. The rest of the journal is filled with Zoudou’s dense notes and theories about the nature of Kugaptee, the Wall of Ghosts, and the “paradise” she has come to believe lies beyond the wall. These notes are all written in a mix of Aklo and Chthonian, so a character must be able to read both languages to study the contents. A character who can read both can use the journal to learn the consecrate ritual, but an even greater use for the information is explored in the next act, where clues within Zoudou’s notes can help the PCs open a doorway through the Wall of Ghosts.</p>"
            },
            "The Ritual Site": {
              "name": "仪式地点 The Ritual Site",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Ritual Site\">仪式地点</h1>\n<p>只要PC们在绑架发生后的几天内前往仪式地点，他们就应当能在邹斗完成她的献祭仪式之前触及该地点——请继续阅读下文的“邹斗的仪式”。如果PC们到得太晚（由你自行裁定），则改为继续阅读@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06horrorfrombe00]{彼界恐魔}。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Ritual Site\">The Ritual Site</h1>\n<p>As long as the PCs travel to the ritual site within a few days of the abduction, they should be able to reach the location before Zoudou finishes her sacrificial rite—proceed with Zoudou’s Rite below. If the PCs arrive too late (at your discretion), instead proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06horrorfrombe00]{Horror from Beyond}.</p>"
            },
            "Log Piles": {
              "name": "原木堆 Log Piles",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E17. Log Piles\">E17. 原木堆</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这里狭窄的空地上仍堆着四座高达15英尺的原木堆，每座都用沉重且锈蚀的铁链牢牢固定。空地的远端有一条走得很勤的小路蜿蜒向北延伸。</p>\n</div>\n<p>PC可以攀爬到其中一座原木堆的顶部，尝试进行一次跳远，跳进旧伐木营地。这条小路过去曾继续通往更高处的山里，但如今被祷告派用来往返他们在鬼打墙设立的仪式地点。这条小路很快向西转弯，沿着起伏的丘陵步行约6英里后，抵达鬼打墙；祷告派的首领正在那里为苦迦菩提进行一场复杂的仪式。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E17. Log Piles\">E17. Log Piles</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Four fifteen-foot-high log piles remain stacked in a narrow clearing here, each secured with heavy, rusty chains. At the far side of the clearing, a well-traveled trail winds further to the north.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The PCs can climb atop one of the log piles to attempt a Long Jump into the lumber camp. The trail once led further up into the mountains but is used today by the Prayers to come and go from the ritual site they’ve erected at the Wall of Ghosts. This trail soon turns west and, after a hilly hike of about 6 miles, reaches the Wall of Ghosts where the leader of the Prayers is performing a complex ritual to Kugaptee.</p>"
            },
            "Mugirou’s Throne": {
              "name": "麦郎的王座 Mugirou’s Throne",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E16. 麦郎的王座</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这座仿佛仓库一般的建筑高过营地的围栏。里面，一只临时拼凑的木笼——显然是用从大型锯子和其他木工作业工具上拆下的部件制成——摆在一张杂乱无章的王座前；那王座由一块巨大的树根瘤制成，几乎有五英尺高。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-mugirou.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Mugirou\" alt=\"麦郎，无面鬼骗子\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-mugirou.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>“流浪者”的首领麦郎懒散地瘫坐在他的木王座上，阴郁沉思；四名无面鬼士兵则围着笼中的囚犯纠缠取笑。这四名囚犯是从柳岸镇马场被绑来的，但当佐豆判定他们的灵魂不够“老”，不足以用于献祭时，她便把这四人交给了“流浪者”。本意是把这四人当作某种“和解的礼物”，但麦郎将这份“赠礼”视为侮辱，认为佐豆这么做只是为了把“不要的垃圾”甩给“流浪者”。</p>\n<p>当PC们表明自己的存在时，四名囚犯会大声呼救求援。四名无面鬼士兵则无声地窜到麦郎身旁，等待他们首领的命令。麦郎并不立刻攻击，因为他早就怀疑英雄们很快会来救囚犯。他目前没有脸，用心灵感应向PC们致意，并告诉他们，绑架并非由他策划。他们复仇的真正目标应当是“祷告派”的首领佐豆。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-mugirou.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E16. 麦郎的王座</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.8Hjhq9gXfibH45NM]{反叛者麦郎} @UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{无面鬼士兵（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>如果PC们发动攻击，麦郎会命令他的士兵战斗至死，而他们也会忠诚照做。但麦郎自己并不想死；若其生命值降到8点以下，他会尝试逃跑或乞求饶命，此时任何幸存的士兵也会投降或逃走。</p>\n</section>\n<p>如果PC们与“流浪者”的首领交谈，麦郎会表示他甚至并不享受手下正在做的事。他只是无聊，而且已经想不出别的点子。如果由他做主，他宁愿直接杀掉囚犯，然后继续去探索营地之外的地区，并最终试着把柳岸镇据为己有。当然，他会对这些欲望含糊其辞，并在需要时撒谎，以隐藏真实动机。</p>\n<p>麦郎愿意谈条件。若PC们能消灭营地内及仪式地点的所有无面鬼秘术师，从而终结佐豆对无面鬼们的影响，麦郎便承诺释放笼中的囚犯，并允许PC们毫发无伤地离开营地。若PC们试图让他承诺不再打柳岸镇的主意，他会变得恼火——但若以一次成功的 @Check[intimidation|dc:17|traits:auditory,concentrate,emotion,exploration,linguistic,mental,skill,action:coerce|name:Coerce] 胁迫他，他就会同意这些条件。至于他是否会遵守，由你决定。</p>\n<p>不过，如果麦郎向PC们投降，他会坦诚地同意以性命为代价不再打柳岸镇的主意，并且言出必行。麦郎与其同族无面鬼会退入该地区的荒野之中，并在战役剩余时间里尽力避开柳岸镇的居民。</p>\n<p>注意，被俘的农民除了被抓时身上穿的皮甲（如今已肮脏破烂）之外，全部都没有任何装备。</p>\n<p><strong>宝藏：</strong>如果PC们同意交易，麦郎会赠予他们一根<em>战地医师警棍</em>作为“友谊”的象征。若PC们与他交战并击败他，则可以从他的尸体上搜出这根警棍。</p>\n<p>若PC们成功救出四名囚犯，心怀感激的农民会凑出资源，并在他们安全返乡后的第二天将一副<em>工匠目镜</em>送到队伍手中。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>奖励：</strong> @UUID[Actor.GfqOuyjkn7LARocw]{麦郎} @UUID[Actor.reeqvpxji3RrZwbi]{农民的赠礼} <br />\n  若PC们与麦郎达成交易，则给予他们等同于在战斗中击败麦郎及其士兵的经验值；但若消息在柳岸镇传开，说PC们放任这些怪物活着或没有把它们赶走，那么他们将从每个派系各失去1点声望值。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E16. Mugirou’s Throne</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This warehouse-like building stands taller than the fences of the camp. Within, a makeshift wooden cage, apparently crafted from parts scavenged from large saws and other lumber work tools, sits before a haphazard throne made from a large root burl that’s nearly five feet tall.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-mugirou.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Mugirou\" alt=\"Mugirou, noppera-bo trickster\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-mugirou.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Mugirou, the leader of the Rovers, slouches on his wooden throne brooding, while four noppera-bo grunts pester and mock prisoners held inside the cage. These four prisoners were abducted from Willowshore Stables, but when Zoudou determined that their souls weren’t “old” enough to suffice for sacrifice, she turned the four over to the Rovers. The intent was that these four would be a sort of “peace offering,” but Mugirou interpreted the “gift” as an insult, believing that the only reason Zoudou did this was to “pass off undesirable trash” to the Rovers.</p>\n<p>When the PCs make their presence known, the four prisoners cry out for rescue. The four noppera-bo grunts silently scamper over to Mugirou’s side, awaiting orders from their leader. Mugirou doesn’t immediately attack, as he suspected that heroes would come soon to rescue the prisoners. Currently faceless, he telepathically greets the PCs and tells them that it wasn’t he who orchestrated the abductions. The true target of their vengeance should be Zoudou, leader of the Prayers.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-mugirou.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E16. Mugirou’s Throne</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.8Hjhq9gXfibH45NM]{Mugirou the Rebel} @UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{Noppera-bo Grunts (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If the PCs attack, Mugirou orders his grunts to fight to the death, which they do loyally. Mugirou has no such desire to die, though, and if reduced to fewer than 8 Hit Points, he either attempts to flee or begs for mercy, at which point any surviving grunts surrender or flee as well.</p>\n</section>\n<p>If the PCs speak to the leader of the Rovers, Mugirou states he doesn’t even enjoy what his underlings are doing. He’s simply bored and out of ideas. If it were up to him, he would rather just kill the prisoners and move on to explore the region beyond the camp and eventually attempt to take Willowshore for his own domain. Of course, he’s evasive about these desires, Lying as needed to hide his true motives.</p>\n<p>Mugirou is willing to bargain. If the PCs can eliminate all noppera-bo occultists in the camp and at the Ritual Site, and thus end Zoudou’s influence over the noppera-bos, Mugirou promises to free the prisoners in the cage and allow the PCs to leave the camp unharmed. If the PCs seek to secure a promise from him that he’ll leave Willowshore alone, he grows frustrated—but if Coerced with a successful @Check[intimidation|dc:17|traits:auditory,concentrate,emotion,exploration,linguistic,mental,skill,action:coerce|name:Coerce], he’ll agree to those terms. Whether or not he honors them is up to you.</p>\n<p>If Mugirou surrenders to the PCs, though, he’ll honestly agree to leave Willowshore alone in return for his life, and he makes good on his word. Mugirou and his fellow noppera-bos retreat into the wilderness of the region and do their best to avoid the citizens of Willowshore for the remainder of the campaign.</p>\n<p>Note that the captured farmers all lack gear other than the (now filthy and ragged) leather armor they were wearing when captured.</p>\n<p><strong>Treasure:</strong> If PCs agree on the deal, Mugirou gifts them a <em>battle medic’s baton</em> as a token of “friendship.” If the PCs fight and defeat him, they can instead loot the baton from his corpse.</p>\n<p>If the PCs successfully rescue the four prisoners, the grateful farmers pool their resources and deliver to the party a <em>crafter’s eyepiece</em> a day after they safely return home.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Reward:</strong> @UUID[Actor.GfqOuyjkn7LARocw]{Mugirou} @UUID[Actor.reeqvpxji3RrZwbi]{Farmer's Gift} <br />\n  If the PCs strike a deal with Mugirou, grant them experience as if they’d defeated him and his grunts in combat, but if word spreads through Willowshore that the PCs let these monsters live or didn’t chase them off, they’ll lose 1 Reputation Point from each faction.\n</p>"
            },
            "Outhouses": {
              "name": "户外厕所 Outhouses",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E15. Outhouses\">E15. 厕所</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一股令人作呕的恶臭从这栋侧面建筑敞开的门里飘出，毫无疑问地揭示了这些厕所极不卫生的状况。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这些厕所的状况糟糕到，野衬坊每当必须在这些建筑10英尺范围内工作或经过时，都会刻意让自己变得无脸，只为躲开这股臭味。由于它们从不进去，厕所便成了方便的藏身处；但进入这处恶臭建筑的PC必须通过一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:18] ，否则会因这股令人难以承受的恶臭而陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{力竭 1} ，持续10分钟。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E15. Outhouses\">E15. Outhouses</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A horrible, gag-inducing stench wafts out of the open doors of this side building, revealing the unsanitary condition of these outhouses without a shadow of a doubt.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The state of the outhouses is so bad that noppera-bos intentionally go faceless whenever they must work or pass within 10 feet of the structures, just to avoid the smell. As they never go inside, the outhouses are convenient hiding places, but a PC who enters this foul structure must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:18] or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 1} for 10 minutes from the overwhelming stink.</p>"
            },
            "Worker’s Dormitory": {
              "name": "工人宿舍 Worker’s Dormitory",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E14. 工人宿舍</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一处抬高的地板占据了房间的大部分空间。这里点着数十支血红色蜡烛，蜡烛被雕刻成各种族裔的形状，烛芯燃烧却不冒烟。在这片不规则的灯火配置中央，蹲着一尊由严重畸形的瘤木制成的怪异塑像。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这里的烛火是由苦迦菩提的影响所维持的诡异魔法效果——火焰不会融化蜡烛，也不会放出烟雾。那尊塑像在被仔细观察时，会古怪地闪烁与起伏，仿佛正试图把自己的真实形态隐藏起来。上一刻它像是一个佝偻的男人，手臂又长又破损，头颅由一束树枝扎成；下一刻，它又变成一只蜷伏的青蛙，正被它整吞下去的人卡住喉咙；再下一刻，它似乎呈现出一种既非蜘蛛、也非章鱼、也非植物的形态，却又以某种方式将三者融为一体。随后，只要有人辨认出一个轮廓，它便立刻又变回一团纠结的根须、枝条与树皮。此等怪景是苦迦菩提本人的显现之一，它只提供关于其真实本质的模糊暗示，却不揭露任何确切真相。若蜡烛被熄灭，塑像便失去这些特征，只会显得像一块与人等高的纠结瘤木。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>一对无面鬼异能术士坐在塑像前，面无五官，反复跪拜以敬奉该形象，并吟诵心灵感应的祷告；PC们能在脑海中听见他们一遍又一遍地念着“苦迦菩提”之名。这些异能术士对PC们毫不理会，即便PC们口头威胁他们也不关心。只有在PC们对其中一人动手、伤害或熄灭蜡烛，或试图触碰或伤害塑像时，他们才会攻击。</p>\n<p>若被提问，这两名无面鬼会耐心回答PC们的询问。这些无面鬼属于祷告派阵营，不过他们不会用这个名字自称。相反，他们称自己为“苦迦菩提之牙”，并解释苦迦菩提寄望让人从灵魂之河的痛苦循环中获得自由。这些异能术士称赞他们的领袖邹斗是位富有远见且一丝不苟的仆从，能够将献祭的完美时刻精确到那一秒。提到麦郎时，这两名无面鬼会啐一口唾沫，说他忘恩负义、毫无责任感，竟把自己的欲望置于苦迦菩提的需求之上。被要求提供更多关于苦迦菩提本人的信息时，这些异能术士会用隐喻来回答，甚至有时彼此说法相互矛盾：其中一人将他比作“你出生时吸入的第一口气”，另一人却说他是“你死后将永远不会再吸到的第一口气”。</p>\n<p>若PC们宣称自己是来营救被绑架的NPC，这些异能术士认为这一目标相当可以理解，并指出：“若命运注定他们不该被送去献给苦迦菩提，我们又有什么资格否认他们的命运？”他们提出一笔交易：如果PC们能在战斗中羞辱或击败麦郎，这两人愿意护送PC们去见邹斗，并替他们请求她饶恕那些将被献祭之人——但要付出一个价格。至于价格是什么，无面鬼说不出来，因为那只能由邹斗决定。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E14. 工人宿舍</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.vrVgCCIFhVUirVJZ]{无面鬼异能术士（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>如果PC们在试图离开前没有达成此类协议，两名异能术士就会几乎带着遗憾地告知他们：他们不能被允许离开，他们的灵魂应当留在这里，成为苦迦菩提领域中的更多灯火。随后他们发动攻击，战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.dG5JreiCR1bhh4vP]{异能吊坠} <br />\n  如果PC们完成了击败麦郎的交易，在被护送前往仪式地点之前，无面鬼异能术士会奖励他们一枚<em>异能吊坠</em>。如果PC们转而击败这些异能术士，则可以从苦迦菩提塑像的一条“手臂”上取下同样的物品。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E14. Worker’s Dormitory</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>An elevated floor takes up the majority of this room. Dozens of blood-red candles carved into the shapes of various ancestries are lit here, their wicks burning without smoke. In the center of the irregular configuration of lights hunkers a misshapen effigy crafted from a very deformed burl.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The candle flames here are an eerie magical effect sustained by Kugaptee’s influence—the flames don’t melt the candles or give off smoke. The effigy strangely seems to shimmer and ripple when studied, as if it were trying to hide its actual form from observation. One moment it appears as a hunched-over man with long broken arms and a head made of a bundle of twigs. In another, it shifts to a crouching frog choking on a man it swallowed whole. In the next, it appears to take on a form not wholly spider nor octopus nor plant, yet somehow combining all three. Then, as soon as someone identifies a shape, it shifts back to a tangled knot of roots, branches, and bark. This strange sight is a manifestation of Kugaptee himself, one that provides vague hints to his true nature without revealing any actual truth. If the candles are extinguished, the effigy loses these traits and appears simply as a human-sized burl of tangled wood.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of noppera-bo occultists sit before the effigy, faceless and repeatedly genuflecting as they worship the image, chanting telepathic prayers the PCs can hear in their minds as the name “Kugaptee” over and over. The occultists pay no attention to the PCs and are indifferent even if the PCs verbally threaten them. They only attack if the PCs lay hands on one of them, damage or extinguish the candles, or attempt to touch or damage the effigy.</p>\n<p>If questioned, the two noppera-bos patiently answer the PCs’ queries. These noppera-bos belong to the Prayers faction, though they don’t identify themselves by that name. Rather, they call themselves the Teeth of Kugaptee, and explain that Kugaptee promises freedom from the cycle of suffering that is the River of Souls. The occultists praise their leader, Zoudou, as a visionary and meticulous servant who can narrow down the perfect second for a sacrifice. The two noppera-bos spit at the mention of Mugirou, calling him ungrateful and irresponsible for putting his own wants before Kugaptee’s needs. Asked for more information about Kugaptee himself, the occultists speak in metaphors and even at times seem to contradict each other, with one comparing him to the “first breath you take when you are born” to the other describing him as “the first breath you’ll never take after you die.”</p>\n<p>If the PCs declare they’re here to rescue the kidnapped NPCs, these occultists find this goal quite understandable, noting that “if it is to be that they should not be sent to Kugaptee, who are we to deny their fate?” They propose a bargain: if the PCs can humiliate or defeat Mugirou in combat, these two are willing to escort the PCs to Zoudou and ask her to spare those who are to be sacrificed, for a price. What that price is, the noppera-bos can’t say, as that’s a decision only Zoudou can make.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E14. Worker’s Dormitory</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.vrVgCCIFhVUirVJZ]{Noppera-bo Occultists (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If the PCs don’t secure such an agreement before they attempt to leave, the two occultists inform them, almost regretfully, that they can’t be allowed to leave and that their souls should remain here as more lights for Kugaptee’s domain. They attack, fighting to the death.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.dG5JreiCR1bhh4vP]{Pendant of the Occult} <br />\n  If the PCs complete the deal to defeat Mugirou, they’re awarded a <em>pendant of the occult</em> by the noppera-bo occultists before they’re escorted to the ritual site. If the PCs defeat the occultists instead, they can obtain the same item hanging off one of the “arms” of the Kugaptee effigy.\n</p>"
            },
            "Guest House": {
              "name": "客栈 Guest House",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E13. 客舍</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这栋建筑看起来比营地里的其他建筑建造得更晚，几乎没有被苔藓或腐朽侵蚀。它格外显眼，是营地里唯一一栋看起来像正常房屋的建筑。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>如果钱币兜姐妹在本次冒险开始时与PC们的遭遇中没能活下来，那么这栋建筑就是空的。如果她们活了下来，那么金灵青与紫就在这里。尽管她们的渡鸦盟友麻雀抛弃了她们，黄鼠狼面条在变回普通动物之后，仍旧忠心耿耿地陪在她们身边。</p>\n<p>不幸的是，钱币兜姐妹在逃离柳岸镇后命运也没有好转；当她们跌跌撞撞来到营地附近时，被祷告派抓住了。起初她们注定要被当作祭品，但邹斗意识到这两只金灵在“适应”新角色一段时间后，可能会成为很棒的手下，甚至盟友。尽管如此，邹斗“招募”盟友的方法也好不到哪去——她对金灵发表了一通极具威胁性的“要么加入我们，要么去死”的演说后，就把她们留在这里自行考虑。自那之后，祷告派被其他事情分了心（其中不乏与漫游者日渐扩大的裂痕），钱币兜姐妹也就基本被遗忘了。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/midori.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E13. 客舍</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.l2OASni6a1cm0b52]{Midori} @UUID[Actor.OZr27GtHKvwz7N3o]{Murasaki} @UUID[Actor.vwrUmnX3ZVVHRBuq]{Noodles}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>再次见到PC们时，钱币兜姐妹会立刻投降，并恳求队伍救她们出去——尽管她们的门上没有锁，她们也没有被捆绑。只要在 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e1entrance0000]{E1} 和 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e7courtyard000]{E7} 区域没有敌人，一旦PC们指出这一点，钱币兜姐妹就能轻松脱身。作为救她们的回报，钱币兜姐妹会提供重要信息——无脸僧相信鬼打墙的另一边有某种乐园。如果PC们还没见过鬼打墙，钱币兜姐妹会畏惧地将其描述为“西北方的一堵闹鬼的墙，真正的怪物就住在墙的另一边”，但她们对其所知也不多。被问到“苦迦菩提”时，金灵只会打寒战并说：“那是个坏名字。我们不谈它。我们甚至连<em>想</em>都不想。”逼她们继续谈论苦迦菩提（她们只知道那是个可怕的恶魔）是确保能把她们吓得逃跑的办法之一；或者如果她们被逼到走投无路，就会发动攻击。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们帮助钱币兜姐妹从旧伐木营地逃脱，给予他们等同于在战斗中击败钱币兜姐妹的XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E13. Guest House</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This building appears to be of more recent construction than the other structures in the camp and is relatively unblemished by moss or rot. It stands out as the only camp building that resembles a normal house.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> If the Abacus Sisters didn’t survive their encounter with the PCs at the start of this adventure, then this building is empty. If they did survive, the jinkins Midori and Murasaki are here. While their raven ally Sparrow abandoned them, the weasel Noodles remained loyally at their side even after he became a mundane animal once more.</p>\n<p>Unfortunately, the Abacus Sisters’ fate didn’t improve after fleeing Willowshore, for as they stumbled into the camp’s vicinity, they were captured by the Prayers. Initially destined to be sacrifices, Zoudou realized that the two jinkins might make great underlings or even allies, after they’ve had some time to “acclimate” to their new roles. Zoudou’s method of “recruiting” allies is little better than imprisonment, though—after giving the jinkins a very intimidating “you can join us or you can die” speech, she left them to think things over here. Since then, other events have distracted the Prayers (not least of which being the growing schism with the Rovers), and the Abacus Sisters have largely been forgotten.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/midori.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E13. Guest House</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.l2OASni6a1cm0b52]{Midori} @UUID[Actor.OZr27GtHKvwz7N3o]{Murasaki} @UUID[Actor.vwrUmnX3ZVVHRBuq]{Noodles}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Meeting the PCs again, the Abacus Sisters instantly surrender and beg the party to free them, despite the fact that there are no locks on their doors and they aren’t bound. So long as there are no enemies in areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e1entrance0000]{E1} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e7courtyard000]{E7}, the Abacus Sisters can make their getaway with ease once the PCs point this out. In exchange for saving them, the Abacus Sisters provide important information—that the noppera-bos believe that some sort of paradise lies beyond the Wall of Ghosts. If the PCs haven’t seen the Wall of Ghosts yet, the Abacus Sisters can fearfully describe it as a “haunted wall to the northwest, beyond which the real monsters live,” but don’t know much more about it. Asked about “Kugaptee,” the jinkins just shudder and say, “That’s a bad name. We don’t talk about it. We don’t even <em>think</em> about it.” Pushing them to talk more about Kugaptee (whom they know only as a frightening fiend) is one sure way to drive them to flee or, if they’re cornered, to attack.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs help the Abacus Sisters to escape from the lumber camp, grant them XP as if they’d defeated them in combat.</p>"
            },
            "Treasury": {
              "name": "宝库 Treasury",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E12. Treasury\">E12. 金库</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>数排独立的空置搁架摆满了这间大房间，其中一些上面仍放着敞开但空空如也的箱子。这里显然已被洗劫一空，而且很可能已经过去很久了。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.nN9tdmrjSAnj8E6D]{被洗劫的金库} @UUID[Actor.jgtSxfQ9cj2IDEwQ]{藏匿的储藏} <br />\n  当旧伐木营地被遗弃后，被剥夺权利的工人们洗劫了金库。花 10 分钟搜查这间房间会自动找到 24 cp 和 3 sp，它们藏在搁架后或那些被漏掉的空箱子里；但若 PC 进行搜寻并在一次 @Check[perception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 中成功，则会注意到西北侧两排搁架之间有一道藏匿的活板门。\n</p>\n<p>活板门下方是一处贵重物品的藏匿点，一名腐败的官员曾将其存放于此，却再也没有机会带着他侵吞的资金逃之夭夭。这处藏匿点包括一个皮革小袋，内有一瓶<em>隐形药水</em>和一块价值 100 gp 的银锭。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E12. Treasury\">E12. Treasury</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Several empty freestanding shelves fill this large room, some of which still display open but empty chests. The place is obviously looted and likely has been for quite some time.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.nN9tdmrjSAnj8E6D]{Looted Treasury} @UUID[Actor.jgtSxfQ9cj2IDEwQ]{Hidden Stash} <br />\n  When the lumber camp was abandoned, the disenfranchised workers looted the treasury. A 10-minute search of the room automatically turns up 24 cp and 3 sp behind shelves or empty chests that got missed, but PCs who Search and succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] notice a hidden trapdoor between the two northwestern shelves.\n</p>\n<p>Within the trap door is a stash of valuables that a corrupt official had been storing, only to never have the chance to make off with his embezzled funds. The stash consists of a leather pouch that contains an <em>invisibility potion</em> and a silver ingot worth 100 gp.</p>"
            },
            "Camp Office": {
              "name": "营地办公室 Camp Office",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E11. 营地办公室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>营地办公室里的物品大多摆放得井井有条——几乎一尘不染——仿佛已经有一段时间没人进来过了。从箱子到椅子，所有家具都在原位，只有一处例外：松散的文件散落得满地都是，就像曾有一阵狂风扫过房间。北墙上有一扇看起来非常坚固的木门，并用铁箍加固。</p>\n</div>\n<p>通往区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e12treasury000]{E12} 的铁门已上锁，而钥匙早已不见。要打开这扇门，需要一名角色成功进行三次 @Check[thievery|dc:20|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock]，或进行一次 @Check[athletics|dc:23|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]。或者，也可以把门砸烂——这是一扇典型的加固木门（硬度 15 HP 60 [BT 30]）。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/air-wisp.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">E11. 营地办公室</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.9ttrvzOU2pS8L57i]{召唤符文 (3)} @UUID[Actor.HydQUAqujiNR7Isg]{精英空气微灵 (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>由于此处安置了几道召唤符文（由营地先前的管理者为安保而布置），无面灵一直避开这间房。无面灵第一次试图进入时触发了这些召唤符文，数团“愤怒的风团”显现出来，令它们惊惧不已，从此彻底回避这栋建筑。该区域共有三道召唤符文，任何人一旦完全踏入此房间，它们便会同时触发。虽然陷阱召唤出的元素微灵会追击敌人离开该区域，但它们仍会在 [[/r 2d6 #rounds]] 轮后消失，符合召唤符文陷阱的通常规则。若它们追击PC进入其他区域，请注意：被召唤的空气微灵不会区分队伍成员与旧伐木营地中的任何怪物住民。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.gBt6VcWor8E3z3sM]{营地办公室} <br />\n  房间里散落的文件表明：伐木营地在最后几个月仍在产出，但随着龙华的崩溃引发动荡，导致不和与逃离，最终使此地被废弃。对办公室进行一次搜寻可找到 15 gp 和一瓶<em>修复油</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E11. Camp Office</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The contents of the camp office are mostly well-organized—almost immaculate—as if no one has been inside for a while. All furniture from chests to chairs is in place, with one exception: loose documents lie strewn all over the floor, as if a gust of wind tore through the room at some point. A very solid looking wooden door that has been reinforced with iron bands stands in the northern wall.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The iron door to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e12treasury000]{E12} is locked, and the key is long gone. Opening this door requires a character to succeed at three @Check[thievery|dc:20|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock], or a single @Check[athletics|dc:23|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]. Alternately, the door can be battered down—it’s a typical reinforced wooden door (Hardness 15 HP 60 [BT 30]).</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/air-wisp.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">E11. Camp Office</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.9ttrvzOU2pS8L57i]{Summoning Runes (3)} @UUID[Actor.HydQUAqujiNR7Isg]{Elite Air Wisps (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> The noppera-bos have avoided this chamber due to several summoning runes that were placed here by the camp’s previous management for security. The first attempt the noppera-bos made to enter here triggered these summoning runes, and the manifestation of several “angry puffs of wind” frightened them enough that they’ve completely avoided the building ever since. In all, there are three summoning runes in the area, and all of them trigger simultaneously once anyone steps fully into this room. While the elemental wisps the traps summon will pursue foes beyond this area, they still vanish after [[/r 2d6 #rounds]] rounds, as normal for a summoning rune trap. If they do pursue PCs into other areas, note that the summoned air wisps make no distinction between the party members and any of the monstrous inhabitants of the lumber camp.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.gBt6VcWor8E3z3sM]{Camp Office} <br />\n  The documents strewn about the room indicate that, while the lumber camp was still producing in its final months, upheaval from the collapse of Lung Wa was resulting in discord and desertion that ultimately led to the site being abandoned. A search of the office uncovers 15 gp and a bottle of <em>oil of mending</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Manager’s Dormitory": {
              "name": "管理员宿舍 Manager’s Dormitory",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E10. 主管宿舍</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房陈设齐全，配有书桌、衣柜，以及一张带有私密床帘的床。南侧的两扇门用额外的木板条加固过。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>这里曾是旧伐木营地主事者的私人住处，而无面鬼如今将这栋坚固的建筑当作监牢，用来关押要进行特殊献祭的人。柳岸镇马场的主人昆舜重和他的儿子蒙松最终被关在这里。当他的儿子仅仅过了半小时就被带走后，舜重的绝望更甚；如今，这位年迈的兽医已然陷入真正的绝境。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E10. 主管宿舍</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.vrVgCCIFhVUirVJZ]{无面鬼秘术师（2）} @UUID[Actor.THLCv8oDccy3Y1lC]{昆舜重}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>舜重被绳索紧紧捆在东侧卧室里，而两名与祷告派结盟的无面鬼秘术师则在主房间站岗。与本区域许多打手和诡计者不同，这两名秘术师不容易被骗；他们会迅速认定PC是来自柳岸镇、前来营地营救囚犯的英雄，因此一见面就发动攻击。若其中一名秘术师被杀死，另一名会试图逃离营地，向西北方向的仪式地点赶去，以警告那里的同伴。</p>\n</section>\n<p>如果PC救下舜重，他会含泪恳求他们救出自己的儿子，并解释说怪物只把他关在这里很短时间就把他带走了。他设法得知蒙松被带到西北方某处——一条小径尽头——而他的儿子似乎拥有某种“古老灵魂”，邪教徒迫切想把它当作献给某个他们称为“伟大苦迦菩提”的存在的祭品。这位兽医除上述信息外提供不了更多帮助；他没有任何装备，而且只剩下2点生命值。他建议暂时留在这里，让PC继续前进，但也请求他们在返回柳岸镇时不要把他丢下。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC救下舜重，给予PC 40 XP，并在他回到家后让两个派系各获得1点声望点数。若他们故意伤害他或需对他的死亡负责，他们在两个派系的声望各失去5点。</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>苦迦菩提是谁？</h1>\n  <p>许多年前，当那名恶魔仍活着时，“苦迦菩提”这个名字几乎等同于死亡与恐惧。然而，在谭隋靖击败了他、却又在不久后殒命之后，幸存者采取措施，确保人们记得隋靖的英勇，却遗忘苦迦菩提，并且无人会去寻找他的坟冢。距离那恶魔被击败已过去近九个世纪；在这段时间里，他的名字基本已湮没在历史长河之中。PC在本章中必定会数次听到这个名字，但除了从上下文推断出他是某种无面鬼所崇拜的实体之外，起初他们几乎无从得知更多信息。一名PC若在一次用于回忆知识的 @Check[religion|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]、@Check[society|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定中成功，便能认出这是某种远古且早已死去的怪物之名，但也仅此而已。随着PC在下一幕抽出时间进一步研究并调查这项古老威胁，了解更多关于苦迦菩提的信息将变得更为重要。就目前而言，让这个名字保持为一种模糊的威胁即可，让玩家自行得出结论。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E10. Manager’s Dormitory</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This room is well-furnished, complete with a desk, wardrobe, and a bed with privacy curtains. Two doors to the south have been reinforced with extra slats of wood.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Once the personal quarters for the lumber camp’s manager, the noppera-bos have taken to using this sturdy building as a prison to hold special sacrifices. Kum Soon-chong, the owner of Willowshore Stables, and his son, Meng-sung, wound up here. When his son was taken away after only a half hour, Soon-chong’s despair only grew, and now, the elderly veterinarian is truly desperate.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E10. Manager’s Dormitory</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.vrVgCCIFhVUirVJZ]{Noppera-bo Occultists (2)} @UUID[Actor.THLCv8oDccy3Y1lC]{Kum Soon-Chong}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>Soon-chong is tightly bound with rope in the eastern bedroom while two noppera-bo occultists allied with the Prayers stand guard in the main room. Unlike many of the grunts and tricksters in the area, these two occultists aren’t easily tricked; they’re quick to assume that the PCs are heroes from Willowshore who have come to the camp to rescue prisoners, and as such, they attack on sight. If one of the occultists is slain, the other attempts to flee the camp to make his way northwest to the ritual site to warn the others there.</p>\n</section>\n<p>If the PCs rescue Soon-chong, he tearfully begs them to save his son, explaining that the monsters kept him here for only a short time before taking him away. He managed to learn that Meng-sung has been taken somewhere to the northwest at the end of a trail and that his son has some sort of “old soul” the cultists were eager to use as an offering to something or someone they called “Great Kugaptee.” The veterinarian can’t provide much help beyond the above replies, and he lacks any gear and has been reduced to 2 Hit Points. He suggests that, for the time being, he can remain here while the PCs press on, but asks them not to leave him behind once they return to Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs rescue Soon-chong, grant the PCs 40 XP, as well as 1 Reputation Point for both factions once he returns home. If they intentionally hurt him or are responsible for his death, they lose 5 Reputation Points with both factions.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Who Is Kugaptee?</h1>\n  <p>The name “Kugaptee” was synonymous with death and fear many years ago when the fiend still lived. However, after Tan Sui-Jing defeated him only to perish soon thereafter, those who survived took steps to ensure that while Sui-Jing was remembered for her bravery, Kugaptee would be forgotten and that none would seek his grave. Nearly nine centuries have passed since the fiend’s defeat, and in that time, his name has largely been lost to time. The PCs are certain to hear his name several times during this chapter, but other than contextual clues that he’s some sort of entity the noppera-bos worship, they’ll have little to go on at first. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[religion|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge], @Check[society|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge], or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge recognizes the name as an ancient and long dead monster of some sort, but little more than that. Learning more about Kugaptee will become more important in the next act as the PCs take time to research and investigate the ancient threat further. For now, leave the name as a vague menace, and let the players draw their own conclusions.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Storeroom": {
              "name": "储藏室 Storeroom",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E9. Storeroom\">E9. 储藏室</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间食品储藏室已被清空，只剩下空篮子和袋子，里面还有些蔬菜与谷物的碎屑。</p>\n</div>\n<p>如果PC们保持无踪或未发现，他们可以在这间目前空置的储藏室里安全地休息。在他们休息时，可能会听到隔壁区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e8kitchen00000]{E8} 里蜘蛛爬行的窸窣声。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E9. Storeroom\">E9. Storeroom</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This pantry has been cleaned out, leaving empty baskets and bags with scraps of vegetables and grains.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The PCs can safely rest in this currently empty storeroom if they stay undetected or unnoticed. While they rest, they may hear the skittering of the spiders next door in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e8kitchen00000]{E8}.</p>"
            },
            "Kitchen": {
              "name": "厨房 Kitchen",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E8. 厨房</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间厨房的炉灶因长期使用而熏得漆黑。地面上散落着破损的陶罐。一层薄薄的蜘蛛网覆盖了大部分表面，其中还包括几捆看起来像尸体的东西，躺在房间中央。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hunting-spider.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E8. 厨房</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.SDlfNU9r0WFloFWX]{猎蛛 (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>在夏季的头几天里，由于苦迦菩提的影响，生物获得了些许知性，无面鬼用“免费食物”的承诺把三只猎蛛从附近的树林里引诱到这里来。当PC点亮<em>长明灯</em>后，这些蜘蛛恢复成普通动物，但仍继续栖身于此。它们后来对被囚禁的处境愈发厌倦，会迅速攻击任何进入房间的人，战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.P7IuoHUnK66SOjPT]{无面鬼} <br />\n  地板上的其中一具尸体属于一名无面鬼；他在还来不及使用手中仍紧握的<em>中等爆破石</em>之前就死了。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E8. Kitchen</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The hearth of this kitchen is dark from heavy use. The floor is lined with broken pots. A thin layer of cobwebs cover much of the surfaces, including a few bundles of what seem like bodies that lie in the middle of the room.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hunting-spider.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E8. Kitchen</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.SDlfNU9r0WFloFWX]{Hunting Spiders (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> In the first few days of summer, when Kugaptee’s influence granted creatures a modicum of sapience, the noppera-bos lured a trio of hunting spiders here from the nearby woods with promises of free food. When the PCs lit the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, these spiders reverted to normal animals but continued to dwell here. They’ve since grown somewhat weary of their captivity and swiftly attack anyone who enters the room, fighting to the death.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.P7IuoHUnK66SOjPT]{Noppera-bo} <br />\n  One of the bodies on the floor belongs to a noppera-bo who died before they could use the <em>moderate blasting stone</em> still clutched in their hand.\n</p>"
            },
            "Courtyard": {
              "name": "庭院 Courtyard",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E7. 庭院</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这片开阔的庭院中央燃着一堆由破旧家具碎片与木料搭成的篝火，火势熊熊。火堆南侧不远处立着一座由树枝与薄木条制成的穹顶状笼子。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/giant-rat.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E7. 庭院</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{无面鬼士兵 (6)} @UUID[Actor.H70XgCOyEQ3u7eLa]{巨鼠 (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>欢闹声与烤肉的香味从这里传来。一群效忠流浪派的半打无面鬼士兵正在火上烤着牛肉条，同时押注他们刚刚在木笼里安排的两只巨鼠打斗的胜负。</p>\n  <p>角色可以在成功进行一次 @Check[athletics|dc:18|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 来破拆笼子后将其摧毁；或者也可以直接用伤害破坏笼子（AC 12，硬度 3，HP 12 [BT 6]）。如果笼子破损，其中一只动物会立刻逃脱，另一只会在 [[/r 1d4 #rounds]] 轮后逃脱。若笼子被摧毁，两只动物都会逃脱。逃脱的动物会先攻击无面鬼们，然后试图逃离营地。</p>\n  <p>如果无面鬼们意识到PC并非乔装的骗徒（若PC放走笼中动物则会自动暴露），他们会战斗到其中两人被杀死或被击败为止；此后剩余者会逃往区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e16mugiroust00]{E16}，加入他们首领一方以寻求庇护。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E7. Courtyard</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A roaring campfire built from furniture scraps and lengths of timber roars in the middle of this open courtyard. A dome-shaped cage made of branches and thin wooden slats stands just to the south of the fire.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/giant-rat.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E7. Courtyard</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{Noppera-bo Grunts (6)} @UUID[Actor.H70XgCOyEQ3u7eLa]{Giant Rats (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The sounds of revelry and the scent of cooking meat come from here, where a gathering of a half-dozen noppera-bo grunts loyal to the Rovers are cooking strips of beef over the fire while betting on the outcome of a fight they’ve just staged in the wooden cage between two giant rats.</p>\n  <p>The cage can be destroyed by a character who Forces it Open with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:18|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] or simply by damage (AC 12, Hardness 3, HP 12 [BT 6]). If the cage is broken, one of the animals escapes at once and the other in [[/r 1d4 #rounds]] rounds. If the cage is destroyed, both animals escape. Escaped animals attack the noppera-bos before trying to flee the camp.</p>\n  <p>If the noppera-bos realize the PCs aren’t disguised tricksters (which happens automatically if the PCs let the caged animals loose), they’ll fight until two of them are slain or defeated, at which point those remaining flee to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e16mugiroust00]{E16} to join their leader’s side for protection.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Secret Door": {
              "name": "暗门 Secret Door",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E6. Secret Door\">E6. 秘密门</h2>\n<p>如果一名PC在此区域进行搜寻并在一次@Check[perception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]中成功，他们就会发现这里围栏中内置的秘密门。如果他们由于前期调查而得知秘密门的存在（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06advanceknowl00]{Advance Knowledge}），则角色必须在一次@Check[perception|dc:8|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]中成功，才能定位这扇门。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E6. Secret Door\">E6. Secret Door</h2>\n<p>If a PC Searches this area and succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search], they find the secret door built into the fence here. If they know about the secret door’s existence as a result of preliminary investigations (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06advanceknowl00]{Advance Knowledge}), a character must succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:8|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] to locate the door.</p>"
            },
            "Loading Island": {
              "name": "加载岛屿 Loading Island",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E5. 装载岛</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>穿过一座下陷的木桥，是一座小岛，人们在这里将原木卸入水中，以便储存或运输。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-grunt.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E5. 装载岛</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{无面鬼士兵（4）} @UUID[Actor.53zJvKWN5TKmMpDa]{受伤的河童}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>一群四名无面鬼士兵抓住了一只惊惧且受伤的河童，正借着欺负这可怜的生物来打发时间，以此发泄他们因被认为“不适合”参加营地墙内社交聚会而积攒的怨气。这些无面鬼在扮演“英勇的冒险者”，要消灭一个“可怕的威胁”。</p>\n  <p>与附近的守卫一样，这四个家伙很可能会把PC误认为乔装的无面鬼骗子；PC可以通过提出请求或威吓来尝试影响这些士兵的行为。如果PC在任一尝试中的检定结果为失败，无面鬼就会起疑，并问PC站在邹斗那边还是麦郎那边。由于这四名无面鬼与祷告派结盟，如果PC声称自己跟随麦郎，无面鬼会愤怒尖叫并发动攻击，迫不及待想通过痛揍对手来“赢得尊重”。如果PC声称自己跟随邹斗，则PC必须成功对无面鬼撒谎。若成功，无面鬼会提议将他们抓到的河童献祭给鬼打墙，但也会怯生生地请求允许他们过去围观。如果PC能继续维持这场欺骗，他们可以借此被护送进入营地内部。</p>\n  <p>在这段时间里，这只河童的头碗已经空了，生命值也被打到只剩5点，他苦苦哀求饶命。他甚至可能认出PC——这只河童正是PC在本冒险早些时候遭遇过的其中之一：要么是在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{第2章}城里的澡堂，要么是在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}的葫芦湖。</p>\n  <p>如果PC救下河童，尤其是如果他们在先前的遭遇中善待过这只河童，这名生物在获救后会在附近停留一小段时间。由于一直在这一带活动，河童知道名为邹斗（其追随者是狂热分子）与麦郎（其追随者是好战分子）的两人之间似乎存在一些摩擦，但除此之外就所知不多。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.IEPbppyH0ZQIUbgT]{泥水} <br />\n  若一名PC在西侧漂浮木材群南端附近的泥水中进行搜寻，并在一次@Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]中成功，则会发现一名伐木工遗忘的宝藏——一把<em>+1 战斧</em>。如果PC救下了河童，这名生物会在最终逃离该区域前指出宝藏的位置。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E5. Loading Island</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Across a sagging wooden bridge is a small island where logs are unloaded into the water for storage or transport.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-grunt.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E5. Loading Island</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{Noppera-bo Grunts (4)} @UUID[Actor.53zJvKWN5TKmMpDa]{Injured Kappa}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A group of four noppera-bo grunts have captured a frightened and injured kappa and are passing the time bullying the poor creature as a way to take out their frustrations at being deemed “unfit” for the social gathering inside the camp’s walls. These noppera-bos play at the role of “heroic adventurers” taking out a “monstrous threat.”</p>\n  <p>As with the guards nearby, these four are likely to mistake the PCs for disguised noppera-bo tricksters, and the PCs can attempt to influence the grunts’ behavior by Requesting or Coercing them. If a PC’s check results in a failure on either attempt, the noppera-bos grow suspicious and ask the PCs if they stand with Zoudou or Mugirou. As these four noppera-bos are allied with the Prayers, if the PCs claim to be with Mugirou, the noppera-bos shriek in anger and attack, eager to “earn respect” by beating up the opposition. If they claim to be with Zoudou, the PCs must successfully Lie to the noppera-bos. If successful, the noppera-bos offer their captured kappa to be sacrificed to the Wall of Ghosts but also sheepishly ask to be allowed to come watch. If the PCs can keep the deception going, they can use it to be escorted into the camp proper.</p>\n  <p>During this time, the kappa, whose head bowl is empty and who has been reduced to 5 Hit Points, begs for mercy. He might even recognize the PCs, for this kappa was one of those the PCs encountered earlier in the adventure, either at the baths downtown in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog04reclai]{Chapter 2} or at Gourd Lake in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs rescue the kappa, and particularly if they treated the kappa well in their previous encounter, the creature remains nearby for a short time after being rescued. Having been around the area, the kappa is aware that there’s some friction between two individuals named Zoudou (whose followers are zealots) and Mugirou (whose followers are warmongers) but doesn’t know much else.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.IEPbppyH0ZQIUbgT]{Muddy Water} <br />\n  A PC who Searches the muddy water near the southern end of the western floating logs and succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] discovers a treasure forgotten by a woodcutter—a <em>+1 battle axe</em>. If the PCs rescued the kappa, the creature points out the treasure’s location before he eventually flees the area.\n</p>"
            },
            "Guard Dormitory": {
              "name": "卫兵宿舍 Guard Dormitory",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E4. Guard Dormitory\">E4. 守卫宿舍低 3</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>血迹飞溅与武器留下的痕迹遍布这间宿舍的墙壁。干涸的血泊把地板与上下铺的床铺都染得斑驳。在东南侧的墙上，有几个类人生物的剪影是用血画成的。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-grunt.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E4. 守卫宿舍</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{无面鬼士兵（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>共有四个无面鬼士兵在这间宿舍里，其中三个正在用他们找到的一把手弩比试射击。最后一个则因为一件鸡毛蒜皮的小事被派来这里打扫，算作惩罚。由于沉迷于游戏，无面鬼一开始对PC们不关心——他们不认为会有入侵者，并会很快认定这些人是刚偷到新面孔的无面鬼骗子。只要PC们没有做出任何让他们产生怀疑的举动，无面鬼就会继续无视队伍。这些偷懒的无面鬼属于流浪派；一旦他们意识到PC们是入侵者，就会战斗至死，因为他们相信若不处理掉，PC们可能会威胁到麦郎的安全。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.NbEQ2tEkiumY78di]{架子} <br />\n  在东侧门旁的架子上放着一小瓶<em>潜能油</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E4. Guard Dormitory\">E4. Guard DormitoryLow 3</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Blood splatters and weapon marks cover this dormitory’s walls. Pools of dried blood stain the floor and bedding of the bunk beds. On the southeastern wall, several humanoid silhouettes have been painted using blood.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90196-noppera-bo-grunt.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E4. Guard Dormitory</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{Noppera-bo Grunts (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A total of four noppera-bo grunts are inside this dormitory, three of whom are engaging in a shooting contest with a hand crossbow they found. The last was sent here to clean up as punishment for a trivial matter. Deep in their game, the noppera-bos are initially indifferent to the PCs since they don’t expect intruders and are quick to assume they’re noppera-bo tricksters with newly stolen faces. As long as the PCs do nothing to suggest otherwise, the noppera-bos continue to ignore the party. These slacking noppera-bos are part of the Rovers, and as soon as they realize the PCs are intruders, they fight to the death, believing the PCs might pose a threat to Mugirou’s safety if not dealt with.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.NbEQ2tEkiumY78di]{Shelf} <br />\n  A vial of <em>oil of potency</em> sits on a shelf next to the eastern door.\n</p>"
            },
            "Ox Stables": {
              "name": "牛厩 Ox Stables",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E3. Ox Stables\">E3. 公牛马厩</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>马厩显眼地空无一物。老旧的干草散落在地上，踩上去嘎吱作响。干草槽里腐烂的饲料散发出一股甜腻的气味。</p>\n</div>\n<p>营地被遗弃后，这些马厩一直空着，不过更近些时候，野面鬼把先前抓到的鹿与野牛关在这里——而他们现在正一边在营地内庆祝，一边把这些猎物吃掉。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.5zxmI4fJdDCrj8a7]{Stables} <br />\n  搜索马厩会在其中一个干草槽里发现一瓶次等狂徒纯酿。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E3. Ox Stables\">E3. Ox Stables</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The stables are conspicuously empty. Old hay lies scattered across the floor and crunches underfoot. A sweet smell drifts from the rotting feed in the hay boxes.</p>\n</div>\n<p>These stables stood empty after the camp was abandoned, although more recently, the noppera-bos used them to cage deer and wild oxen they caught earlier—which they are now in the process of eating in their celebration inside the camp.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.5zxmI4fJdDCrj8a7]{Stables} <br />\n  Searching the stables uncovers a bottle of lesser bravo’s brew in one of the hay boxes.\n</p>"
            },
            "Guard Tower": {
              "name": "警卫塔 Guard Tower",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E2. Guard Tower\">E2. 警卫塔</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这座简易的木制警卫塔支撑着一个露天平台，离地约15英尺。西侧倚着一架梯子，可通往上方的平台。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>通常驻守在此的无面鬼第一次在PC来访时会偷懒待在警卫宿舍（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e4guarddormi00]{E4}），让这座塔恰好无人看守；但在之后的来访中，会有一对无面鬼士兵驻扎于此。</p>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{无面鬼士兵 (2)}</span>\n    <span>生物 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">异怪</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E2. Guard Tower\">E2. Guard Tower</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This simple wooden guard tower supports a single open-air platform, some fifteen feet off the ground. A ladder leaning against the west side provides access to the platform above.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The noppera-bos that are usually posted here are slacking off in the guard dormitory (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e4guarddormi00]{E4}) the first time the PCs visit, leaving the tower conveniently unattended, but on subsequent visits, a pair of noppera-bo grunts are stationed here.</p>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n    <span>@UUID[Actor.1UkSPinr0GbmH3GU]{Noppera-bo Grunt (2)}</span>\n    <span>Creature 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Aberration</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Entrance": {
              "name": "入口 Entrance",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E1. 入口</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这两扇沉重的双开门紧闭不动。右侧门上开着一扇带铁框的小窗。</p>\n</div>\n<p>无面鬼用门内侧的一根大圆木将这些门（以及北面正对的那两扇门）顶住上闩。从内侧移开圆木需要 3 个交互动作——或者，角色可以以一次成功的 @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 来破拆这扇沉重的门。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>一对无面鬼骗子（每个都伪装成人类）站在这里。因为不被允许加入里面的派对而心生懊恼，这两位过去几小时一直在激烈争论里面的旱厕是否闹鬼，好让自己分心，别对这份差事怨气太重。他们与“祈祷者”同盟，且并不想与区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e4guarddormi00]{E4} 里的那些“懒狗们”扯上太多关系。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">效果</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Item.RbmwOxIj5zWRckGs]{效果：伪装}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>你也可以使用上方链接的效果，将冒险中未明确提及正在伪装的其他任意生物伪装成“人类守卫”。要关闭该伪装，你只需在该效果所施加的角色卡上，取消勾选“Noppera-Bo Disguised”掷骰选项即可。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>除这两名无面鬼外，还有旧伐木营地的看门犬“肉干”（Jerky）。两年前伐木工人们抛弃它后，它一直在这一带野化生存。它已将无面鬼视作自己的新主人，但仍更喜欢真正人类的陪伴。PC 可以尝试以一次 @Check[nature|dc:14|traits:auditory,concentrate,action:command-an-animal|name:Command an Animal] 来指挥动物，使肉干意识到它的“主人”其实是伪装的怪物。成功时，肉干对该 PC 变为不关心，并退到一旁，拒绝再听从无面鬼的命令。大成功时，肉干会倒戈无面鬼并攻击他们。之后，只要 PC 愿意让这只热情的狗留在身边并善待它，它就会一直随行。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/jerky.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E1. 入口</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.6QMo5HWoY4yWoG1Q]{无面鬼骗子（2）} @UUID[Actor.TxrHxk0gPcAC9j0O]{肉干}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>PC 一靠近，无面鬼就会向他们喊话，声称自己是“营地主人”派来驻守此处的人，并表示不允许任何访客进入。若被问及里面的喧闹声，这两位看起来闷闷不乐、脾气暴躁，只会重复命令 PC“掉头回镇上去”。若 PC 仍坚持，他们就会发起攻击：用欺瞒进行先攻检定，并以“摘下自己的脸”作为战斗开场。他们会战斗到其中一名生命值降到 5 点以下为止；此时两名无面鬼都会丢下武器，逃入树林。若 PC 尚未争取到肉干的支持，这条狗会本能地追击，不过 PC 可以使用指挥动物把它叫回来。</p>\n  <p>当无面鬼需要打开大门时，他们会用心灵感应联络区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e10managersd00]{E10} 的打手，让对方从内侧来开门。注意：任何关于绑架的提问都必然会让这些无面鬼警觉，意识到 PC 并不是骗子以为的那类人，并很快导致战斗爆发。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E1. Entrance</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 3</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>These heavy double doors are shut tight. A single iron-framed wicket is set in the right door.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The noppera-bos keep these doors (as well as the northern doors opposite) barred with a large log on the inside. Removing the log from the inside takes three Interact actions—alternately, a character can Force Open the heavy doors with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open].</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of noppera-bo tricksters, each disguised as a human, stand here. Frustrated over not being allowed to join the party inside, the two have spent the past several hours in a heated debate about whether the outhouses inside are haunted, as a way to distract themselves from feeling too bitter about their assignment. They’re allied with the Prayers and want little to do with the “slackers” in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e4guarddormi00]{E4}.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Item.RbmwOxIj5zWRckGs]{Effect: Disguise}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>You can also use the effect linked above to disguise any other creatures as Human Guards not explicitly mentioned to be disguised in the adventure. To turn off the disguised, you just need to uncheck the \"Noppera-Bo Disguised\" roll option on the actor that the effect is applied to.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>Along with the two noppera-bos is the lumber camp’s guard dog, Jerky, who has been living feral in the area after being abandoned by the woodworkers 2 years ago. He has come to see the noppera-bos as his new owners, but still prefers the company of actual humans. A PC can attempt to Command an Animal with a @Check[nature|dc:14|traits:auditory,concentrate,action:command-an-animal|name:Command an Animal] to get Jerky to realize that his “masters” are monsters in disguise. On a success, Jerky becomes indifferent to the PC and stands aside, refusing to follow the orders of the noppera-bos. On a critical success, Jerky turns on the noppera-bos and attacks them. He then accompanies the PC for as long as they’ll have the eager dog by their side and treat him well.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/jerky.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">E1. Entrance</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 3</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.6QMo5HWoY4yWoG1Q]{Noppera-bo Tricksters (2)} @UUID[Actor.TxrHxk0gPcAC9j0O]{Jerky}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The noppera-bos call out to the PCs as soon as they approach, claiming to be men posted here by “the camp’s owners” and that no visitors are allowed. Asked about the sound of revelry inside, the two appear sullen and cranky but only repeat their command to the PCs to “turn around and head back to town.” They attack if the PCs persist, rolling for initiative with Deception and starting the fight by Removing their Faces. They fight until one is reduced to fewer than 5 Hit Points, at which point both noppera-bos throw down their weapons and flee into the woods. If the PCs haven’t won Jerky over yet, the dog’s instinct is to pursue, though the PCs can use Command an Animal to call him back.</p>\n  <p>When the noppera-bos need the gate to be opened, they telepathically contact the grunts in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e10managersd00]{E10} to come do so from the inside. Note that any questions about the abduction are sure to alert these noppera-bos that the PCs aren’t actually who the tricksters think they are and will quickly result in a fight.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Lumber Camp Features": {
              "name": "旧伐木营地特征 Lumber Camp Features",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Lumber Camp Features\">旧伐木营地特征</h2>\n<p>这座旧伐木营地位于柳岸镇以西刚过8英里处，坐落在一条年久失修的道路尽头；这条道路沿着木棉河北岸延伸。</p>\n<p>PC们第一次接近营地时，无论一天中的什么时刻，里面都会传来喧闹的庆祝声，以及烟雾与烤肉的气味。此外，西侧的岛上（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e5loadingisl00]{E5}）传来咯咯的怪笑与嘲弄的声音；而东侧的宿舍（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e4guarddormi00]{E4}）则不时传来欢呼与咒骂，并伴随着弩箭发射的声响，PC们越靠近，越可能被这些动静吸引注意。</p>\n<p>一圈高15英尺的原木栅栏围住了伐木营地的核心区域。每根原木都被削尖成木桩，使人不可能站在其顶端。PC必须成功通过一次 @Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] 才能攀上这些墙。除非另有说明，内部建筑物高度为10英尺。与柳岸镇不同，这座伐木营地只使用木制旋转门，而不使用推拉门。</p>\n<p>野襟坊之间的争吵与冲突并不少见，因此如果某个遭遇区域里的家伙看见附近区域爆发打斗，它们很可能会留意、围观，甚至出言嘲讽；但一般不会急着加入正在进行的战斗，而是选择留在岗位上，因为它们害怕一旦被发现擅离职守，会遭到更严厉的惩罚。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Lumber Camp Features\">Lumber Camp Features</h2>\n<p>The lumber camp is located just over 8 miles west of Willowshore, at the end of a poorly maintained road that follows the northern bank of the Ceiba River.</p>\n<p>The first time the PCs approach the camp, regardless of time of day, the sound of rowdy celebration comes from within, along with the smells of smoke and roasting meat. In addition, the sounds of cackling and taunting voices come from the island to the west (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e5loadingisl00]{E5}), while periodic cheers and curses accompanied by the sound of a crossbow firing come from the dormitory to the east (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e4guarddormi00]{E4}), potentially attracting the PCs’ attention as they draw near.</p>\n<p>A 15-foot-tall log fence surrounds the heart of the lumber camp. Each of the logs has been sharpened to a stake, making it impossible to stand atop them. A PC must succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] these walls. Buildings within are 10 feet tall unless stated otherwise. Unlike Willowshore, the lumber camp exclusively uses wooden swivel doors instead of sliding doors.</p>\n<p>Bickering and conflicts aren’t uncommon among noppera-bos, so if those in one encounter area see a fight break out in a nearby area, they’re likely to take note, watch, and even call out taunts, but generally won’t rush to join a battle in progress, instead choosing to remain at their posts for fear of greater punishments should they be caught abandoning their duties.</p>"
            },
            "The Merchant Returns": {
              "name": "商人归来 The Merchant Returns",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Merchant Returns\">商人归来</h2>\n<p>在PC们第一次出发前往旧伐木营地之前，古怪的商人神藏又来到柳岸镇拜访了一次——他甚至可能在PC们离开城镇时在路上与他们碰面。神藏很高兴能在PC们离开前拦住他们，并警告他们，西边地区有一些奇怪的怪物一直在伪装成“强盗”。听到绑架的消息后，神藏似乎并不惊讶；他叮嘱PC们务必小心，随后提出了一个古怪的问题，意在提醒他们一种战术选择——有些队伍可能并不会想到这一点。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“你们打算如何对付这些入侵你们城镇、掳走你们同伴的敌人？你们是要在战斗中以怒火将其彻底摧毁，还是认为自己能骗过他们，让他们相信你们是他们的一员，从而在不诉诸暴力的情况下完成营救？”</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.B6InFE0pC0HnnZbX]{神藏的赋礼（隐秘）} @UUID[Actor.5C3ki7ERJu5KAqnO]{神藏的赋礼（复仇/正义）} <br />\n  无论队伍如何回答，神藏都会若有所思地点点头。如果PC们的回答更倾向于复仇或伸张正义，他会赠予他们一件<em>正义斗篷</em>，并警告他们不要偏离自己的道路。如果PC们的回答更倾向于隐秘行事，神藏会赠予他们一件<em>无面鬼面罩</em>，并称赞他们的勇气。无论他没有赠送哪件物品，都仍可供购买，此外他可能提供的任何其他物品也同样可以购买。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Merchant Returns\">The Merchant Returns</h2>\n<p>Before the PCs set out for the lumber camp the first time, the strange merchant Shinzo pays one more visit to Willowshore—perhaps even meeting the PCs on the road as they leave town. Shinzo is delighted to have caught the PCs before they left and warns them of strange monsters who have been masquerading as “bandits” in the region to the west. Upon hearing about the abduction, Shinzo doesn’t seem surprised and tells the PCs to take care before asking a strange question meant to suggest a tactical option that might not occur to some parties.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“How do you intend to approach these enemies who invade your town and take your people? Do you intend to bring furious ruin to them in battle, or do you think you can fool them into believing that you are one of them to effect a rescue without resorting to violence?”</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.B6InFE0pC0HnnZbX]{Shinzo's Gift (Subtlety)} @UUID[Actor.5C3ki7ERJu5KAqnO]{Shinzo's Gift (Revenge/Justice)} <br />\n  Shinzo nods sagely at however the party answers. If the PCs’ answer leans toward revenge or enacting justice, he gifts them a <em>cape of justice</em> and a warning not to stray from their path. If the PCs’ answer leans toward subtlety, Shinzo gifts them a <em>noppera-bo hood</em> and compliments them for their bravery. Whichever item he doesn’t gift remains available for purchase, along with any other items he might have to offer.\n</p>"
            },
            "Advance Knowledge": {
              "name": "进阶知识 Advance Knowledge",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Advance Knowledge\">深入了解</h2>\n<p>尽管旧伐木营地已空置两年，但它的位置与基本布局仍为许多本地人所知。为了了解营地情况，PC 可以尝试就此主题进行一次回忆知识检定：@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[society|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]。或者，PC 也可以在镇上四处打听，并在花 2 小时搜集信息后尝试一次 @Check[diplomacy|dc:16|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]。</p>\n<p>成功时，PC 们能获得足够的营地描述，从而绘制出该地点的地图。主营地有两个入口，但从其中一条路线进入可能过于显眼。</p>\n<p>大成功时，PC 们还会得知木栅墙上有一扇秘密门（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e6secretdoor00]{E6}），过去伐木工曾用它偷偷溜出去，去使用条件更好的守卫旱厕。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Advance Knowledge\">Advance Knowledge</h2>\n<p>While the lumber camp hasn’t been occupied for two years, its location and basic layout are still known to many locals. In order to learn about the camp, a PC can attempt to Recall Knowledge on the subject with a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or a @Check[society|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]. Alternatively, a PC can ask around town and then attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:16|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] after Gathering Information for 2 hours.</p>\n<p>On a success, the PCs can secure enough of a description of the camp to create a map of the site. There are two entrances to the main camp, but entering through one of these routes might be too obvious.</p>\n<p>On a critical success, the PCs also learn about a secret door in the stockade wall (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog06thewal.JournalEntryPage.06e6secretdoor00]{E6}) that woodworkers once used to sneak out and enjoy the nicer guard outhouse.</p>"
            },
            "The Lumber Camp": {
              "name": "旧伐木营地 The Lumber Camp",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Lumber Camp\">旧伐木营地</h1>\n<p>当PC们救出丑小乖后，石蜘蛛可以向他们告知如今占据这处废弃旧伐木营地的怪物们的情况；不过，PC们在探索柳岸腹地时，也可能自己偶然发现该地点。待柳岸镇有了新的领袖后，能面男会通过重演引发这条冒险路径的事件来升级事态——他们潜行进城，绑走新一批受害者；由于需要更多祭品献给苦迦菩提，祷告派便被迫尝试这种孤注一掷的行动。绑架的消息应当促使PC们立刻采取行动，柳岸镇西南部的许多当地人都会证实：“一群戴面具的强盗刚袭击了柳岸镇马场，把那里的所有人都押着往西边走了！”</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Lumber Camp\">The Lumber Camp</h1>\n<p>When the PCs rescue Ugly Cute, the stone spider can inform them about the monsters now occupying the abandoned lumber camp, but the PCs might stumble across the location on their own as they explore the Willowshore hinterlands. Once Willowshore has a new leader, the noppera-bos escalate the situation by repeating the event that started this Adventure Path—they sneak into town to abduct a fresh batch of victims, as the need for more sacrifices to Kugaptee pushes the Prayers to attempt such a desperate move. News of the abduction should galvanize the PCs into action, with many locals in southwest Willowshore confirming that a “group of masked bandits just raided Willowshore Stables and marched everyone there off to the west!”</p>"
            },
            "The Wall of Ghosts": {
              "name": "鬼打墙 The Wall of Ghosts",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Wall of Ghosts\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第4章：</span>\n  <span>鬼打墙</span>\n</h1>\n<p>木材曾是柳岸镇的传统出口之一，但随着龙华的覆灭，柳岸镇的居民转而从事其他营生，木材的重要性也随之退居次要地位。本地区一处主要的旧伐木营地位于木棉河源头附近，但在龙华崩溃后，工人们弃岗逃离此地，营地的生产也因此停摆。将近2年的时间过去了，这座旧伐木营地一直处于废弃状态；然而在最近一次思维空间周期中一切发生改变，一群由苦迦菩提的影响催生的怪物占据了营地。</p>\n<p>旧伐木营地的新住民中最主要的是一种被称为“noppera-bo”的无面怪物。它们曾经同仇敌忾，如今却分裂为两派，各自受苦迦菩提亲自烙印于它们身上的信念所左右：祷告派与流浪派。祷告派由狂热者邹斗领导，虔诚地崇拜苦迦菩提；而流浪派由侦察队长麦郎带领，将苦迦菩提视为征服的号召。祷告派一直在献祭俘虏，期望借此开启鬼打墙，显露他们所相信的、墙外等待着他们的“乐园”。与此同时，流浪派则想在当地制造痛苦与苦难，认为如此便能让墙扩张，并把乐园带到他们身边。这两种方式都无法真正达成各派所追求的目标，但迟迟不见进展迫使祷告派做出更多献祭，而流浪派也愈发不耐烦，准备对柳岸镇发动一场光荣的攻击。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-campfire-fight.webp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Wall of Ghosts\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 4:</span>\n  <span>The Wall of Ghosts</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Lumber is one of Willowshore’s traditional exports, but with the fall of Lung Wa, the lumber became of secondary importance as Willowshore’s citizens turned to other pursuits. One of the region’s major lumber camps was located near the source of the Ceiba River, but production there was halted when its workers abandoned their posts and fled the region after Lung Wa’s collapse. In the nearly 2 years that have passed, the lumber camp has remained abandoned, but when everything changed during the latest mindscape cycle, a gathering of monsters spawned from Kugaptee’s influence took control of the camp.</p>\n<p>Primary among the lumber camp’s new inhabitants are faceless monsters known as noppera-bos. Once a united front, these monsters have fractured into two groups, each influenced by beliefs imprinted on them by Kugaptee himself: the Prayers and the Rovers. The Prayers, led by a zealot named Zoudou, are those who worship Kugaptee religiously, while the Rovers, led by scoutmaster Mugirou, see Kugaptee as a call to conquest. The Prayers have been sacrificing captives in hopes of opening the Wall of Ghosts and revealing the “paradise” they believe awaits them beyond. The Rovers, meanwhile, want to cause pain and suffering in the region, believing that doing so will make the wall expand and bring paradise to them. Neither method will actually result in the goals the factions seek, but the lack of progress has pushed the Prayers to make more sacrifices, while the Rovers are growing impatient to make a glorious attack on Willowshore.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 2.1: Turning of the Seasons": {
          "name": "第2.1幕：四季更迭 Act 2.1: Turning of the Seasons",
          "pages": {
            "Week 12: Vanishings": {
              "name": "第12周：失踪事件 Week 12: Vanishings",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 12: Vanishings\">第12周：失踪</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>一些额外的日子</h1>\n  <p>秋季的每个月在4周之外还会多出2–3天，因此从严格意义上说，在本幕中，除了本章所呈现的12周事件之外，还会多出相当于额外一周的时间。这些额外日子在你的游戏中如何体现，由你决定；它可以是PC们从上一幕中恢复的时间。也可以是用于推进 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{第6章} 与 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{第7章} 内容的时间。你也可以用第二周的失踪作为结尾，在第13周重复第12周的事件。你还可以自行设计一个新事件，或许让你的团队有机会按你认为合适的方式赚取一些额外的希望、食物或安全点。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>随着秋季接近尾声，晴朗的日子成为过去，风雨成了新的常态。气温下降，每天清晨大地都覆着一层薄霜，而在本幕最后一周的第一天，第一次失踪发生了。</p>\n<p>在现代世界中，孙海的驱魔师终于设法锁定了他们所认为的、侵扰柳岸镇废墟的超自然闹鬼现象的真实本质；他们第一次成功且彻底地驱除了其中一个闹鬼现象，导致与之相关联的那名村民的魂魄——对PC们而言，那人仍像是在镇上过着正常生活——消失无踪。这次驱魔也使该个体从柳岸镇中消失，这是思维空间在其115年历史中遭遇的第一次“真正死亡”。即使思维空间重置，这名村民也不会回来，但他们的灵魂也不会前往灵魂之河——相反，他们被放逐到一个可怕、藏匿的思维空间之中，那处思维空间被埋在柳岸镇思维空间“后面”的深处，在那里苦迦菩提的影响更为强大。</p>\n<p>从PC们结交的村民中选择一位失踪者，但避免选择其职责已对某个角色变得至关重要的人。随着下一幕开始，类似事件还会发生，而PC们对这些超自然事件成因的调查将构成那一幕的主要目标之一。选择哪位NPC失踪时，务必参考<em>鬼季</em>的后两幕，挑选一位之后不会承担特定剧情职责的NPC；除此之外，下列任何一位镇民都可能遭此厄运：@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w19downtownw00]{快乐河童}的德格，本地渔夫 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week7anicygr00]{高}，镇卫 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03easternwatch00]{哈亥尔}，镇卫 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w24hojeonghu00]{洪正辉}，退休厨师 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w12matsushom00]{马苏}，柳岸镇马场的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w2willowshor00]{锦顺清}，银雾斋的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{澄香}，或 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w21mamabaos000]{中村“包子嫲嫲”于明}。</p>\n<p>最好把这次事件安排在秋季的最后一天发生，如此你就能在冬季第一天——也就是下一幕的开端——让这件令人不安的事件在玩家脑海中仍历历在目。那一幕《欲泣无息》将继续探究这次离奇失踪所带来的影响，同时也会让柳岸镇面对一整套全新的险厄！</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 12: Vanishings\">Week 12: Vanishings</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Some Extra Days</h1>\n  <p>Each month of fall consists of 2–3 additional days beyond the 4-week mark, so that there’s technically an extra week’s worth of time during this act beyond the 12 weeks of events presented in this chapter. How these extra days manifest in your game is up to you; it could be time the PCs spend recovering from the previous act. It could be time spent pursuing the content of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{Chapter 6} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{Chapter 7}. You could end with a second week of vanishings, repeating week 12’s event on week 13. You could also create a new event of your own design, perhaps one to give your group the chance to earn a few extra Hope, Food, or Security Points as you see fit.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>As fall comes to a close, the sunny days are a thing of the past and rain and wind become the new norm. Temperatures drop, frost dusts the ground each morning, and on the first day of the final week of this act, the first vanishing takes place.</p>\n<p>In the modern world, Mago Kai’s exorcists have finally managed to isolate what they believe to be the true nature of the supernatural hauntings that infest the ruins of Willowshore, and their first successful and complete exorcism of one of those hauntings causes the spirit of the associated villager—who, to the PCs, still appears to be living a normal life here in town—to vanish. This exorcism causes that individual to vanish from Willowshore as well, the first “true death” to hit the mindscape in its 115 years. This villager won’t return if the mindscape resets but neither does their soul move on to enter the River of Souls—they’re instead banished to an awful, hidden mindscape buried “behind” the Willowshore mindscape, a place where Kugaptee’s influence is that much stronger.</p>\n<p>Choose the villager to vanish from among those the PCs have befriended, but avoid choosing one whose role has become significant to a specific character. Similar events will take place as the next act begins, and the PCs’ investigation into what’s causing these supernatural events makes up a primary goal of that act. When choosing which NPC vanishes, make sure to reference the next two acts of <em>Season of Ghosts</em> to select an NPC who doesn’t have a specific role to play going forward, but otherwise, any of the following townsfolk could suffer this unfortunate fate: De-ge of the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w19downtownw00]{Happy Kappa}, local fisherman @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week7anicygr00]{Goh}, town guard @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog03toligh.JournalEntryPage.03easternwatch00]{Ha Hai-er}, town guard @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w24hojeonghu00]{Ho Jeong-hui}, retired chef @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w12matsushom00]{Matsu}, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w2willowshor00]{Kum Soon-Chung} of Willowshore Stables, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w7silvermist00]{Sumika} of Silvermist Lodge, or @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w21mamabaos000]{Nakamura “Mama Bao” Yu Ming}.</p>\n<p>It’s best to time this event to take place on the last day of fall, so that you can start the first day of winter—and the next act—with this unnerving event fresh in the players’ minds. That act, “No Breath To Cry,” continues to explore the ramifications of this strange vanishing, but presents Willowshore with an entirely new set of perils as well!</p>"
            },
            "Week 11: The Face at the Foot of the Bed": {
              "name": "第11周：床尾的那张脸 Week 11: The Face at the Foot of the Bed",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 11: The Face at the Foot of the Bed\">第11周：床尾的脸</h2>\n<p>本周，持续惊吓镇民的超自然事件仍在继续——但这一次，被作祟盯上的不再是某位NPC，而是某位PC本人！</p>\n<p>本周开始时，随机选择一名PC作为这场轻微却令人不安的作祟的目标。在本周的某个夜晚，这名PC会做一个骇人的噩梦：他们走出家门，发现柳岸镇的所有人都变了——他们照常忙着各自的事务，但每个人的头颅都被一小团飘动的血红色蝴蝶云所取代。其他镇民无视这名PC，而PC愈发清晰地意识到有某个看不见的东西正在追逐他们，悄无声息地尾随。就在这名无形的跟踪者即将现身之际，PC却惊醒——却看见一张离体的、倒悬的幽灵般面孔正从床尾盯着他们。更糟的是，那张看着他们睡觉的脸，正是他们自己的脸！当他们看见这张幽灵面孔时，它立刻崩散成一团红色蝴蝶云，猛然掠过PC，蝶翼如同剃刀般割裂皮肉。刹那之后，蝴蝶消失无踪，而PC在床上睁眼躺着——并暴露于一道险恶的诅咒之中：这诅咒将他们自身魂魄的回响与苦迦菩提在此地区日益增长的影响交织在一起；与此同时，孙海的驱魔师们在试图驱逐柳岸镇废墟中的邪祟时，无意间让那恶魔的魂魄获得了更强的力量。至于那名PC是否会在枕头上发现一只被压碎的、死去的血红色蝴蝶，则由你决定。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Item.yapa3j7xagO3ud3Y]{床尾的脸}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">诅咒 5</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">罕见</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">诅咒</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">魔法</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你与自己的幽灵打了个照面！</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>豁免骰</strong> @Check[will|dc:19]; <strong>效果</strong>你意识到自己目睹了自身的幽灵——它从未来回望，试图警告你某个即将杀死你的事物；然而，同一股未知力量却将你的幽灵撕扯而去，让你带着一种确信而受诅咒：最终将杀死你的那个东西，如今已经知道你在哪里。你对抗恐惧术效果的所有豁免骰承受–1减值。此外，每当你被降至0生命值时，你便离真正的死亡更近一步，并在接下来的24小时内成为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 1}。此持续时间不会叠加，但每当你濒死一次就会重置。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 11: The Face at the Foot of the Bed\">Week 11: The Face at the Foot of the Bed</h2>\n<p>The supernatural events that have been frightening the townsfolk continue this week, only this time it’s not one of the NPCs who are targeted by a haunt, but instead one of the PCs themselves!</p>\n<p>As this week begins, choose one PC at random to be the target of this minor but unnerving haunting. One night during this week, that PC has a harrowing nightmare where they step outside their home to find that everyone in Willowshore changed—they’re going about their business normally, but each and every person’s head has been replaced by a tiny cloud of fluttering blood-red butterflies. The other townsfolk ignore the PC, who increasingly becomes aware of something unseen that’s coming after them, stealthily pursuing them. Just as this unseen stalker is about to reveal themself, though, the PC awakes—only to see a disembodied, upside-down, ghostly face staring at them from the foot of the bed. Worse, the face watching them sleep is their own! As soon as they look upon this ghostly face, the face breaks apart into a cloud of red butterflies that swoops around the PC, their wings like razors that cut the flesh. An instant later, the butterflies are gone, and the PC lies awake in bed—and is exposed to a sinister curse that combines echoes of their own soul with Kugaptee’s growing influence over the region, as Mago Kai’s exorcists inadvertently give the fiend’s spirit greater power while working to exorcise Willowshore’s ruins. Whether or not that PC finds a dead, blood-red butterfly crushed on their pillow is left for you to decide.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Item.yapa3j7xagO3ud3Y]{Face at the Foot of the Bed}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Curse 5</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Curse</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Magical</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You’ve come face-to-face with your own ghost!</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Saving Throw</strong> @Check[will|dc:19]; Effect You realize that you’ve witnessed your own ghost, peering back from the future in an attempt to warn you of what will soon kill you, only for that same unknown force to tear your ghost away and leave you cursed with the conviction that what will eventually kill you now knows where you are. You suffer a –1 penalty to all saving throws against fear effects. Additionally, each time you’re reduced to 0 Hit Points, you grow that much closer to your true death and become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for the next 24 hours. This duration doesn’t stack but does reset each time you nearly die.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Next Day": {
              "name": "次日 The Next Day",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Next Day\">次日</h3>\n<p>\n  <strong>奖励：</strong> @UUID[Actor.J0dQ7rFLDJ33V8fS]{神藏的赋礼} <br />\n  如果PC们成功取悦了神灵，他们会在茶馆里发现一份为每个人准备好的礼物。为每名PC选择一件符合其兴趣的5级永久物品——<em>+1护甲强效符文</em>或<em>2环法术魔杖</em>都是极佳的选择。\n</p>\n<p>如其所言，神藏也会在当天返回，要么祝贺PC们的成功，要么安慰他们的失败。不过，即便他们彻底失败，神藏也会为这番尝试鼓掌；而只要PC们至少努力想摆上一场体面的茶饭，这位神秘商人便会交出一本以绿色布料装订的大书，散发着清雅的茶香。书中收录了冒险工具箱中展示的全部 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20magictea000000]{魔茶} 的抄本，以及 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.oYxxcgszpT242sEi]{冬之息} 的配方。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Next Day\">The Next Day</h3>\n<p>\n  <strong>Reward:</strong> @UUID[Actor.J0dQ7rFLDJ33V8fS]{Shinzo's Gift} <br />\n  If the PCs successfully entertained the kami, they find a gift waiting for each of them in the teahouse. Choose a 5th-level permanent item for each PC that fits their interests—<em>+1 armor potency runes</em> or <em>wands of 2nd-level spells</em> make excellent options.\n</p>\n<p>As promised, Shinzo returns that day as well, either to congratulate the PCs on their success or to commiserate with them on their failure. Even if they completely failed, though, Shinzo applauds the attempt, and as long as the PCs at least tried to put on a good banquet, the mysterious merchant hands over a large book bound in green cloth that exudes the fine scent of tea. This book contains copies of all of the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20magictea000000]{Magic Tea} presented in the Adventure Toolbox, as well as the formula for the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.oYxxcgszpT242sEi]{Winter's Breath}.</p>"
            },
            "After the Feast": {
              "name": "宴会过后 After the Feast",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"After the Feast\">宴会过后</h3>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>在PC们为聚集的神灵完成娱乐表演后，茶饭便告结束。不论神灵们玩得尽兴还是感到失望，他们都会突然意识到自己离开护已经很久，于是迅速穿过街道四散而去，为镇民们呈现出一幕令人愉悦的超自然奇景。无论宴席本身是否成功，PC们都获得1希望点与40 XP。</p>\n<p><strong>装饰：</strong>如果PC们获得至少4点装饰点，他们获得1安全点与20 XP。</p>\n<p><strong>茶饭：</strong>如果PC们获得至少4点茶饭点，他们获得1食物点与20 XP。</p>\n<p><strong>娱乐：</strong>如果PC们获得至少4点娱乐点，他们获得1希望点与20 XP。如果至少两名PC在用于娱乐神灵的技能检定中成功，那么在夜里的某个时刻，魂魄会留下一个赋礼，让PC们在早晨发现（见下文@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07thenextday0000]{次日}）。</p>\n<p><strong>声望：</strong>如果PC们在装饰点、茶饭点与娱乐点三者合计至少获得10点，他们可以选择一个阵营并获得1点声望点。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"After the Feast\">After the Feast</h3>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> After the PCs complete their entertainment for the gathered kami, the banquet comes to an end. Whether or not the kami had a great time or were disappointed, they suddenly realize they’ve been away from their wards for quite a long time and quickly disperse through the streets, forming a delightful spectacle of supernatural delight to the townsfolk. The PCs earn 1 Hope Point and 40 XP, regardless of the success of the feast itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Decorations:</strong> If the PCs earned at least 4 Decoration Points, they earn 1 Security Point and 20 XP.</p>\n<p><strong>Banquet:</strong> If the PCs earned at least 4 Banquet Points, they earn 1 Food Point and 20 XP.</p>\n<p><strong>Entertainment:</strong> If the PCs earned at least 4 Entertainment points, they earn 1 Hope Point and 20 XP. If at least two of the PCs succeeded in their skill checks to entertain the kami, then at some point during the night, the spirits leave a gift for the PCs to find in the morning (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07thenextday0000]{The Next Day}, below).</p>\n<p><strong>Reputation:</strong> If the PCs earned at least 10 points overall among Decoration, Banquet, and Entertainment Points, they gain 1 Reputation Point to the faction of their choice.</p>"
            },
            "Night of the Feast": {
              "name": "宴会之夜 Night of the Feast",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Night of the Feast\">宴会之夜</h3>\n\n<p>宴会之日已至，柳岸镇一片沸腾，镇民们热切地等待着这场活动——虽说这场盛宴并不为他们而设，但消息早已传开，镇民们装点了街道，以供品与致敬来庆祝此事，并献给柳岸镇的神灵。夕阳渐沉、夜幕降临时，一幕令人惊叹的景象出现了——数十位神灵从各自的驻地现身，一路嘟囔、咯咯笑着、彼此八卦，沿街向青天茶馆走去。他们无视那些目瞪口呆、欣喜地看着队伍越聚越长的镇民；但当他们走近茶馆时，却对为他们专门做的准备发出惊叹的“噢——”与“啊——”。</p>\n<p>若大尊柳也受邀，它会比那些两尺高的式神高出一尺多；而这些式神总数将近40个——远远超过镇上任何人原先猜想居住在柳岸镇里的神灵数量的两倍。他们涌入茶馆，忙忙碌碌，立刻在整栋建筑里安顿下来，彼此叽叽喳喳地聊着神灵间的八卦，并对PC们的成果惊叹——或许也可能是在嘲弄。PC们主持宴会时，神灵往往无视他们，把注意力放在装饰与食物上，最终还会自己提供一些娱乐。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>装饰</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">神灵欣赏这类盛会的装饰所展现的艺术性与创造力，而且有个怪习惯：他们会把无生命的物件与艺术作品当作同伴，对它们赞美，甚至与其展开单方面的对话。神灵抵达茶馆时的初始反应，取决于PC获得了多少装饰点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>3点或更少装饰点数：</strong>神灵嘲笑并戏弄这些装饰，且随着夜色渐深，会变得有点闹腾。由于造成的破坏，在茶馆再次适合使用之前，一名PC必须成功完成 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#repair-and-restore]{修缮重建} 准备休整行动。队伍失去1安全点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4–5点装饰点数：</strong>神灵对装饰印象深刻，并以尊重的态度对待茶馆。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6点或更多装饰点数：</strong>神灵被装饰震撼，并受到启发，在宴会结束回家后，会把自己的驻地也装点得更华丽并加以强化。队伍获得2安全点。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>宴会</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">神灵一安顿下来，便立刻期待按正确方式为他们奉上茶点——详见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07nightofthefe00#the-tea-ceremony]{茶道} 侧栏。所提供茶与食物的品质能增强宴会效果，具体取决于PC获得了多少宴会点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>3点或更少宴会点数：</strong>食物与茶勉强过得去，但品质低劣——神灵会注意到这一点。茶道的结果降低一个成功等级。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4–6点宴会点数：</strong>食物与茶都不错，而PC需要通过呈现方式来尽可能发挥其效果。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>7点或更多宴会点数：</strong>食物与茶精致绝伦，提升了为神灵服务的整体体验；神灵会毫不吝啬地表达赞赏。茶道的结果提高一个成功等级。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>娱乐</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">宴会邀请中最令神灵好奇的一点，是能欣赏娱乐表演；在宴席期间，他们总会低声议论并猜测自己将会看到什么样的节目。然而，一旦用餐结束，神灵便会集体开始要求“饭后节目”。让每位PC描述自己打算如何娱乐神灵，然后为其选择一个合适的技能进行检定，以决定表现如何。力量壮举可能需要 @Check[athletics|dc:19]，而杂耍表演可能需要 @Check[acrobatics|dc:19]。对于大多数娱乐内容，@Check[performance|dc:19] 是绝佳选择；而依靠魔法的PC则可以投掷 @Check[arcana|dc:19]、@Check[nature|dc:19]、@Check[occultism|dc:19] 或 @Check[religion|dc:19]。无论选择何种技能，成功的DC均为19。根据PC获得的娱乐点数，他们的掷骰可能获得加值；且若至少有2名PC在此检定中成功，神灵会额外给予他们一份奖励（见下方 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07afterthefeas00]{宴会过后}）。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>3点或更少娱乐点数：</strong>神灵的期待高到无法满足，而且他们的点评极其苛刻。所有用于娱乐的技能检定承受–2环境减值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4–6点娱乐点数：</strong>神灵渴望娱乐，所有用于娱乐的技能检定获得+1环境加值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>7点或更多娱乐点数：</strong>神灵很中意PC及其个性。所有用于娱乐的技能检定不仅获得+1环境加值，且每个结果提高一个成功等级。</p>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>茶道</h1>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teakami.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Tea Kami\" alt=\"Tea Kami\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teakami.webp')\" />\n  <p>到为神灵奉茶之时，必须由一名PC担任本次服务的组织者，并尝试一次 @Check[tea-lore|dc:17] 或 @Check[society|dc:21] 检定。其他PC可以通过投掷茶学识或社交来援助该检定。该检定的结果会受PC获得的宴会点数影响而调整。</p>\n  <p><strong>大成功</strong>神灵被服务的品质彻底震撼。他们不仅会如同下文“成功”所述那样回报主人，还会以超自然之力祝福茶馆。从此刻起，在此处进行 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#host-ceremony]{主持茶事} 的所有检定，以及在此处制作食物与茶（包括 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20magictea000000]{冒险工具箱} 中详述的魔法茶）时的所有工艺检定，均获得+1状态加值。PC获得1食物点与1希望点。</p>\n  <p><strong>成功</strong>神灵对仪式十分满意，并在回家后于余下的整个冬季回报主人，帮助守护镇上的食物储备。PC获得1食物点。</p>\n  <p><strong>失败</strong>神灵感到失望，但并未公开嘲弄PC的服务。</p>\n  <p><strong>大失败</strong>神灵被此仪式冒犯，半途离开宴会。PC没有机会为神灵表演（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07nightofthefe00#entertainment]{娱乐}），更糟的是，神灵决定用定期劫掠柳岸镇食物储备的方式来弥补所受的侮辱。PC失去1食物点与1希望点。</p>\n</aside>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Night of the Feast\">Night of the Feast</h3>\n\n<p>The day of the banquet has arrived, and Willowshore is abuzz with townsfolk eagerly awaiting the event—while the feast isn’t for them, word has spread, and the townsfolk have decorated the streets to celebrate the event with offerings and homages to Willowshore’s kami. As the sun dips low in the sky and evening falls, an astonishing sight takes place—dozens of kami emerge from their wards, muttering and giggling and gossiping among themselves as they make their way up the streets toward the Cerulean Teahouse. They ignore the gawking townsfolk who watch the growing parade with delight, but as they approach the teahouse, they “oooh” and “ahhh” in wonder at the preparations made just for them.</p>\n<p>Great Willow, if they were invited, towers more than a foot above the two-foot-tall shikigami, who themselves number nearly 40 in all—well over twice the amount of kami that anyone in town suspected dwelled within Willowshore. They bustle and hustle as they swarm into the teahouse and immediately settle in throughout the building, chattering among themselves about kami gossip and marveling—or perhaps mocking—the PCs’ work. As the PCs perform the feast, the kami tend to ignore them and focus on the decor and the food, eventually providing their own entertainment as well.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Decorations</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The kami appreciate artistry and creativity when it comes to decorating a gala like this and have a strange habit of treating inanimate objects and works of art as fellow people, complimenting these objects and even engaging in one-sided discussions with them. Their initial reaction upon arriving at the teahouse depends on how many Decoration Points the PCs have earned.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>3 or fewer Decoration Points:</strong> The kami mock and tease the decorations and, as the night progresses, get a bit rowdy. As a result of the damage, a PC must successfully take the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#repair-and-restore]{Repair and Restore} preparation downtime activity before the teahouse will be fit for use again. The party loses 1 Security Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4–5 Decoration Points:</strong> The kami are impressed by the decorations and treat the teahouse with respect.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6 or more Decoration Points:</strong> The kami are overwhelmed by the decor and are inspired to fancy up and bolster their own wards when they return home after the feast. The party gains 2 Security Points.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Banquet</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">Once the kami settle in, they immediately expect to be served tea and snacks in the proper way—see the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07nightofthefe00#the-tea-ceremony]{The Tea Ceremony} sidebar for details. The quality of the tea and food served helps to bolster the feast, depending on how many Banquet Points the PCs have earned.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>3 or fewer Banquet Points:</strong> The food and tea are serviceable but low quality—and the kami take note. The result of the tea ceremony is reduced by one degree of success.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4–6 Banquet Points:</strong> The food and tea are fine, and it falls to the PCs to make the best of it through presentation.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>7 or more Banquet Points:</strong> The food and tea are exquisite and elevate the experience of the service for the kami, who are quite vocal in their appreciations. The result of the tea ceremony is increased by one degree of success.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Entertainment</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">One thing that intrigued the kami about the invitation to a banquet was the opportunity for entertainment, and whispers and guesses as to what sort of show they might be treated to remains a frequent topic during the feast. Once the meal is over, though, the kami as a group begin demanding the “post-meal show.” Have each PC describe what they’re doing to entertain the kami, then select an appropriate skill for them to attempt a check to determine how well they do. A feat of strength might call for @Check[athletics|dc:19], while a juggling act might need @Check[acrobatics|dc:19]. @Check[performance|dc:19] is a great choice for a majority of entertainments, while a PC who relies on magic might roll @Check[arcana|dc:19], @Check[nature|dc:19], @Check[occultism|dc:19], or @Check[religion|dc:19]. Regardless of the skill chosen, the DC for success is 19. Depending on how many Entertainment Points the PCs have earned, they might gain bonuses to their rolls, and if at least 2 PCs succeed at this check, the kami grant them an extra reward (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07afterthefeas00]{After the Feast}, below).</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>3 or fewer Entertainment Points:</strong> The kami have impossible-to-meet expectations and are harsh critics. All skill checks to entertain take a –2 circumstance penalty.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4–6 Entertainment Points:</strong> The kami are eager for entertainment, and all skill checks to entertain gain a +1 circumstance bonus.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>7 or more Entertainment Points:</strong> The kami are taken with the PCs and their personalities. Not only do all skill checks to entertain gain a +1 circumstance bonus, but each result is improved by one degree of success.</p>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>The Tea Ceremony</h1>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teakami.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Tea Kami\" alt=\"Tea Kami\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teakami.webp')\" />\n  <p>When it comes time to serve the kami, one of the PCs must serve as the organizer for the service and attempt a @Check[tea-lore|dc:17] or a @Check[society|dc:21] check. Other PCs can Aid this check by rolling either Tea Lore or Society. The results of this check are modified by how many Banquet Points the PCs have earned.</p>\n  <p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The kami are overwhelmed by the quality of the service. Not only do they pay back their hosts as detailed in Success below, but also bless the teahouse with supernatural power. From this point on, all checks to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#host-ceremony]{Host Ceremony} and to Craft food and tea here (including the magical teas detailed in the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20magictea000000]{Adventure Toolbox}) gain a +1 status bonus. The PCs gain 1 Food Point and 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p><strong>Success</strong> The kami are delighted by the ceremony, and upon returning home, they pay back their hosts for the rest of winter by helping to protect the town’s food stores. The PCs gain 1 Food Point.</p>\n  <p><strong>Failure</strong> The kami are disappointed but don’t openly mock the PCs for their service.</p>\n  <p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The kami are insulted by the ceremony and abandon the feast partway through. The PCs don’t get a chance to perform for the kami (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07nightofthefe00#entertainment]{Entertainment}), and worse, the kami decide to make up for the insult by periodically raiding Willowshore’s food stores. The PCs lose 1 Food Point and 1 Hope Point.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Preparing for the Feast": {
              "name": "准备宴会 Preparing for the Feast",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparing for the Feast\">准备宴会</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teaset.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Tea Set\" alt=\"Tea Set\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teaset.webp')\" />\n<p>信三当然建议PC邀请大尊柳与小星，也建议他们花上一两天向镇上其他神灵奉上供品并献上祈祷，让祂们知道即将举行的宴会，但除此之外，他将准备工作完全交给PC们。他还建议将宴会安排在一周的最后一天举行，好让消息传开，并给PC留出准备时间。他承诺在宴会结束后的第二天带着一些特别的礼物回来，供队伍用来提升他们的茶馆；然后（等PC们完成他们还想进行的其他交易后）便把他们留给自己的计划，离开了城镇。</p>\n<p>在接下来的一周里，每位PC都可以进行三次准备宴会，但这样做会使该PC没有时间进行任何休整模式活动。PC可以在其三次准备宴会中混搭具体的准备方式，从装饰、食物与茶的准备、或邀请三者中选择。本行动获得的点数应以一种能让玩家追踪的方式记录——让他们知道，他们需要在某一类别中达到4点，才能成功完成庆祝活动的该性相。获得的点数越多，队伍的成功就越大。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>准备宴会</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">移动</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花时间为宴会准备茶馆：要么用神灵会欣赏的方式装饰，要么为宴会收集并布置资源。或者，你花时间在镇上向当地神灵献上祈祷与礼物，让祂们知道自己都被邀请参加宴会。为增添节庆气氛，让每位玩家描述其角色如何装饰、准备或制作邀请函——如果某位PC想出了特别有趣或令人发笑的描述，你可以酌情让其检定获得+1状态加值。</p>\n  <p>要装饰茶馆，尝试一次@Check[art-lore|dc:17]或@Check[performance|dc:19]检定。该检定的结果为队伍获得装饰点数。</p>\n  <p>要为茶饭本身做准备，尝试一次@Check[food-lore|dc:17]或@Check[drink-lore|dc:17]或@Check[crafting|dc:19]检定。该检定的结果为队伍获得茶饭点数。</p>\n  <p>要邀请神灵，尝试一次@Check[religion|dc:17]或@Check[diplomacy|dc:19]检定。该检定的结果为队伍获得娱乐点数。</p>\n  <p>如果大尊柳已被邀请，消息便会传开。在邀请大尊柳之后进行的每次准备宴会检定获得+1环境加值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> PC根据所选技能获得1点，并额外在三个类别中的任意一个再获得1点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> PC根据所选技能获得1点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> PC根据所选技能失去1点。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparing for the Feast\">Preparing for the Feast</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teaset.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Tea Set\" alt=\"Tea Set\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-teaset.webp')\" />\n<p>Shinzo suggests the PCs invite Great Willow and Kohoshi, of course, and also suggests they spend a day or two making offerings and giving prayers to the town’s other kami to let them know of the upcoming feast, but he otherwise leaves the preparation entirely in the PCs’ hands. He also suggests they hold the feast on the last day of the week, to let word spread and to give the PCs time to prepare. He promises to return the day after the feast finishes with some special gifts for the party to use to enhance their teahouse, then (once the PCs have completed any other transactions they wish) leaves them to their plans and departs from town.</p>\n<p>During the following week, each PC can Prepare for the Feast three times, but doing so prevents that PC from having the time to perform any downtime activities. A PC can mix and match what specific method they use to prepare for their three Prepare for the Feast activities, choosing from decorating, food and tea preparation, or invitations. Points earned by this activity should be tracked in a way that allows the players to keep track of them—let them know that they need to reach 4 points in a category in order to pull off that aspect of the celebration successfully. The more points they earn, the greater the party’s success will be.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Prepare for the Feast</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Move</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend time preparing the teahouse for the feast, either by decorating it in a way the kami will appreciate or by gathering and staging resources for the feast. Alternatively, you spend time out in town offering prayers and gifts to the local kami to let them know that they’ve all been invited to the feast. To add to the festive flair, ask each player to describe how their character decorates, prepares, or makes invitations—a PC who comes up with a particularly fun or amusing description can be rewarded with a +1 status bonus to their check at your option.</p>\n  <p>To decorate the teahouse, attempt a @Check[art-lore|dc:17] or a @Check[performance|dc:19] check. This check’s results earn the party Decoration Points.</p>\n  <p>To prepare for the banquet itself, attempt a @Check[food-lore|dc:17] or @Check[drink-lore|dc:17] or a @Check[crafting|dc:19] check. This check’s results earn the party Banquet points.</p>\n  <p>To invite the kami, attempt a @Check[religion|dc:17] or a @Check[diplomacy|dc:19] check. This check’s results earn the party Entertainment Points.</p>\n  <p>If Great Willow has been invited, word spreads. Every check to Prepare for the Feast after Great Willow is invited gains a +1 circumstance bonus.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The PCs gain 1 point as appropriate for the skill chosen, plus an additional 1 point for any of the three categories.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The PCs gain 1 point as appropriate for the skill chosen.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The PCs lose 1 point as appropriate for the skill chosen.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Shinzo’s Suggestion": {
              "name": "神藏的建议 Shinzo’s Suggestion",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Suggestion\">神藏的建议</h3>\n<p>神秘的商人神藏在一周的第一天一早来到青天茶馆，可能会耐心地等在前门外，在那里摆好他的手推车，好让PC们早晨第一次走到外面时就能发现他。他热情地向PC们问候，他的“渡鸦”小伊在他车顶上好奇地注视着，并祝贺队伍最近取得的成功。如果你觉得PC们在第6章或第7章错过了了解某些重要信息的机会，神藏可以作为引入这些信息的方式，但他此行的真正目的，是赞赏PC们在准备迎冬方面取得的进展——尤其是他们为建立希望与士气所做的努力。</p>\n<p>说到这里，神藏提出了一项建议。他指出，依他经验，灵性上的安康与身体上的安康同样重要——即便小镇设法为冬天把食物与住处都准备得万无一失，也不代表镇民就一定会兴旺。他说，振奋镇民的魂魄固然有帮助，但同样重要的是，也要振奋小镇里那些真正的魂魄的魂魄！</p>\n<p>神藏进一步解释说，他说的是该区域内存在的神灵。PC们已经见过居住在该区域内唯一的木灵神——大尊柳；他们也可能见过式神神灵小星，它守护着镇上的 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna} 神龛；但神藏指出，还有更多式神神灵散居在柳岸镇各处，悄然藏身其中，守护着雕像、艺术作品、花园与路标。若PC们能专为镇上神灵族群准备一场特别的盛宴，它们的喜悦必定会为柳岸镇的灵性健康带来奇效。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Suggestion\">Shinzo’s Suggestion</h3>\n<p>The mysterious merchant Shinzo arrives at the Cerulean Teahouse early on the first day of the week, potentially waiting patiently outside the front door where he sets up his cart for the PCs to find him when they first step outside in the morning. He greets the PCs warmly, his “raven” Yix watching curiously from the top of his cart, and congratulates the party on their recent successes. If you feel the PCs missed a chance to learn something important in Chapters 6 or 7, Shinzo can be a method to introduce that information, but his real purpose for the visit is to admire the PCs in their progress for preparing for winter—particularly their efforts to build hope and morale.</p>\n<p>To this point, Shinzo makes a suggestion. He notes that, in his experience, spiritual well-being is just as important as physical well-being—even if the town manages to fully prepare its food and shelter for winter, that doesn’t mean that its citizens shall thrive. While lifting the townsfolk’s spirits will help, it’s just as important to lift the spirits of the town’s actual spirits as well!</p>\n<p>Shinzo explains further that he’s speaking of the kami present in the region. The PCs have already met the only kodama kami to dwell in the area, Great Willow, and might also have met the shikigami kami, Kohoshi, who guards the town’s @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.JgqH3BhuEuA4Zyqs]{Desna} shrine, but Shinzo notes that many more shikigami dwell throughout Willowshore, quietly hiding within and protecting statues, works of art, gardens, and road signs. If the PCs were to create a special feast specifically for the town’s kami population, their delight will surely work wonders for Willowshore’s spiritual health.</p>"
            },
            "Week 10: Feast of the Kami": {
              "name": "第10周：神灵庆宴 Week 10: Feast of the Kami",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 10: Feast of the Kami\">第10周：神灵庆宴</h2>\n<p>随着柳岸镇的超自然事件愈演愈烈，而且PC们很可能已经挺过了@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{第6章}和@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{第7章}中呈现的危险，这场事件为队伍提供了一个很可能会受欢迎的机会，让他们放松一下，并从日益阴沉可怖的现实恐怖中恢复过来。即便这可能是秋季结束前最后一个“美好”的日子——在比喻意义上，冬日的严酷已开始叩响门扉——朝比奈神藏在本周第一天抵达城镇，应当会为氛围定下更轻松的基调——至少持续几天。注意：本事件假定PC们已经重建了青天茶馆。若他们尚未如此，则本事件不会发生；取而代之的是，队伍选择让这家深受喜爱的本地机构继续化为废墟，会导致他们失去2点希望点。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景笔记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.iuhjjuLADK3seQ8k]{神灵庆宴}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 10: Feast of the Kami\">Week 10: Feast of the Kami</h2>\n<p>With the supernatural events building in Willowshore, and with the good chance that the PCs have already endured the dangers presented in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{Chapter 6} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{Chapter 7}, this event offers the party a likely welcome opportunity to relax and recover from the growing grim horrors of their reality. Even if it promises to be the last “good” day of fall before the harshness of winter begins to metaphorically knock at the door, Asahina Shinzo’s arrival in town on the first day of this week should set the mood for a lighter tone—at least for a few days. Note that this event assumes the PCs have rebuilt the Cerulean Teahouse. If they haven’t yet, then this event doesn’t occur, and instead the party’s choice to leave the beloved local institution in ruins causes them to lose 2 Hope Points.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.iuhjjuLADK3seQ8k]{Feast of the Kami}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "Week 9: Kimchi’s Ascent": {
              "name": "第9周：飞天泡菜 Week 9: Kimchi’s Ascent",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 9: Kimchi’s Ascent\">第9周：飞天泡菜</h2>\n<p>当PC们在进行休整模式时，他们从一位镇民那里听说，村里的一只猫泡菜被困在树上了。这只毛茸茸的橘白相间的猫追着一只松鼠爬到了镇外一棵树的最高枝头，喵喵叫得很大声，附近的村民都能听见。从地面很容易看到这只猫，但她在离地30尺的地方，村民们尝试去救她太危险了。</p>\n<p>如果PC们决定救泡菜，PC能飞上去救她的可能性不大，因此最好的办法是攀爬那棵树，这需要一次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定来攀爬。一旦有PC到达猫的位置，他们必须在一次@Check[athletics|dc:19]检定中成功来擒拿这只惊惧的动物（大失败表示PC从树上掉下去！）。由于她的挣扎和爪子，尝试从树上攀爬下去会受到–2环境减值，除非把猫固定在袋子或类似的东西里。拥有动物共情的角色可以成功进行一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:19]交涉检定来安抚泡菜，并引导她自己爬下来。由你酌情决定，其他救猫方法也可能奏效，只要通过其他DC 19的技能检定即可。一旦回到坚实的地面上，泡菜开心地喵喵叫了几声，然后夹着尾巴跑回镇里。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们救下泡菜，队伍获得1点希望点。如果灾害发生并且泡菜死亡，队伍失去1点希望点。同样地，如果没有PC尝试救援，一位当地的年轻人会尝试去救，然后在下到一半时脚下一滑，抱着泡菜一起摔下来。这个年轻人和猫是否能在坠落中幸存由你决定，但无论如何，这也会让队伍失去1点希望点。</p>\n<p>如果PC们救下泡菜，给予PC们10 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 9: Kimchi’s Ascent\">Week 9: Kimchi’s Ascent</h2>\n<p>While the PCs are going about their downtime, they hear from one of the townsfolk that one of the village cats, Kimchi, has gotten herself stuck up in a tree. The fluffy orange-and-white cat chased a squirrel up to the highest branches of a tree just outside of town and has been meowing loudly enough for nearby villagers to hear. The cat is easy to spot from the ground, but she’s 30 feet up, and it’s too dangerous for the villagers to try and help her.</p>\n<p>If the PCs decide to save Kimchi, it’s unlikely that a PC will be able to fly up to save her, so climbing the tree is the best bet, which requires a successful @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check to Climb. Once a PC reaches the cat, they must succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:19] check to grapple the frightened animal (with a critical failure indicating the PC falls out of the tree!). Due to her squirming and claws, attempts to Climb down the tree take a –2 circumstance penalty unless the cat is secured in a bag or something similar. A character with Animal Empathy can calm Kimchi and guide her down on her own with a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:19] check. Other methods of rescuing the cat could work as well with other DC 19 skill checks, at your discretion. Once she’s back on solid ground, Kimchi meows happily and then turns tail and runs into town.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs save Kimchi, the party earns 1 Hope Point. If disaster strikes and Kimchi dies, the party loses 1 Hope Point. Likewise, if no PC attempts the rescue, a local youth makes the attempt, then slips and falls halfway down with Kimchi in their hands. Whether or not the youth and cat survive the fall is left to you to decide, but regardless, this also costs the party 1 Hope Point.</p>\n<p>Grant the PCs 10 XP if they save Kimchi.</p>"
            },
            "Week 8: Stable Fire": {
              "name": "第8周：马场失火 Week 8: Stable Fire",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 8: Stable Fire\">第8周：马场失火</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-burning-barn.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Burning Barn\" alt=\"A burning barn\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-burning-barn.webp')\" />\n<p>柳岸镇马场在夏天经历了一段艰难时期，而对其老板昆舜重（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w2willowshor00]{柳岸镇马场}）来说，不幸的是，秋天还会带来更多危险。在本周临近结束时，一股黑烟开始从柳岸镇马场的主畜棚升起。PC们应当很快就能发现这股烟，至少也会在街上“着火了！”的喊声中被吸引注意。</p>\n<p>只要PC们反应迅速，他们就能及时赶到柳岸镇马场施以援手。此时，大火已吞没畜棚，雇工们已设法把牲畜赶到牧场里救下。然而火势现在威胁要蔓延到牧场，甚至可能进一步烧向镇里。PC们可以通过进行“扑灭畜棚大火”行动来协助灭火。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.y3wK3OJE2af6Uijq]{Barn Fire}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>扑灭畜棚大火</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">移动</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你帮助扑灭这场威胁要吞噬柳岸镇马场、且若无人照料就可能蔓延到镇上其他地方的大火。要扑灭火势，你可以尝试一次@Check[athletics|dc:19]检定，加入接力传桶的人群来主动对抗火焰，或制造隔火带以控制火势；或者尝试一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:21]检定来组织镇民，让他们的灭火技巧更有效率。若你拥有可能有助于灭火的魔法法术，你也可以使用它们——消耗最多三个由GM同意确实有助于灭火的法术，然后尝试一次奥术、自然、秘术或宗教检定（取决于你的施法根源）。若你使用了三个法术，此检定DC为17；使用两个法术则DC为19；使用一个法术则DC为21。</p>\n  <table>\n    <tbody><tr>\n      <td>@Check[Arcana,Nature,Occultism|dc:17|traits:exploration,manipulate,move|name:Fight Barn Fire]</td>\n      <td>@Check[Arcana,Nature,Occultism|dc:19|traits:exploration,manipulate,move|name:Fight Barn Fire]</td>\n      <td>@Check[Arcana,Nature,Occultism|dc:21|traits:exploration,manipulate,move|name:Fight Barn Fire]</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody></table>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 你对抗火势的努力极其有效。队伍获得2点胜利点数。此外，你令人印象深刻的作为使队伍获得1点希望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功 </strong>你的灭火努力帮助镇民遏制了火势。队伍获得1点胜利点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败 </strong>你尽力协助，但没能做出特别有帮助的贡献。更糟的是，你在过程中被烧伤，受到@Damage[3d6[fire]]点伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:19|basic]豁免）。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 灾害！你试图灭火的举动反而导致火势蔓延！更糟的是，你在过程中严重烧伤，受到@Damage[3d10[fire]]点伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:19|basic]豁免）。队伍失去1点胜利点数。</p>\n</section>\n<p>若PC们在“扑灭畜棚大火”期间设法取得至少3点胜利点数，他们与镇民就能以凯旋般的大获成功迅速控制住火势。若PC们取得0、1或2点胜利点数，火势会蔓延到田地并在被扑灭前损坏栅栏，结果为一次中等成功。若PC们最终得到–1点或更少的胜利点数，火势也会吞没主建筑，并在镇民控制住大火、防止其继续蔓延之前将其连同田地一起烧成灰烬，结果为一次悲剧性的成功，使队伍损失2点食物点与2点安全点。</p>\n<p>火势扑灭后，PC们可以花1小时调查废墟，对严重烧毁的畜棚进行调查。调查会发现一条令人不寒而栗的证据——一具被烧焦的天狗骷髅，头骨上刻着罪印；其头似乎曾在颈部被沉重的利刃斩断，尽管头骨与骨架看起来仍完好地躺在原位。允许PC们进行一次@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:17]检定（或进行一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:17|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]来搜集信息）；若成功，他们会回想起一名名叫宁诺克的纵火犯曾在柳岸镇掀起短暂恐怖统治，后来被抓获并因其罪行被处决——她被斩首，且人们在她的头骨上刻下罪印，以标示她在来世的惩罚，之后将她埋在镇子西北方受弃者之骨的一处无名坟中。若PC们随后前往那座墓园，只需10分钟的调查就能找到一座看起来像是从内部被挖开的无名坟——这又是一个不安的灵体因现世驱魔尝试而从死亡中归来的例子；不过眼下，这似乎只是笼罩柳岸镇那诡异诅咒的又一种“症状”。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们在灭火中取得至少3点胜利点数，给予他们80 XP；若他们发现了火灾背后令人不安的谜团，再额外给予40 XP。他们也会因取得3点胜利点数而获得1点与南岸的声望点。若他们获得少于0点胜利点数，则会失去1点与南岸的声望点。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 8: Stable Fire\">Week 8: Stable Fire</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-burning-barn.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Burning Barn\" alt=\"A burning barn\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-burning-barn.webp')\" />\n<p>Willowshore Stables had a rough time of things during the summer, and unfortunately for its proprietor Kum Soon-chong (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w2willowshor00]{Willowshore Stables}), fall has more peril in store. Near the end of this week, a plume of dark smoke starts to rise from the main barn of Willowshore Stables. The PCs should spot this smoke quickly or, at the very least, have their attention drawn to it by calls of “Fire!” in the streets.</p>\n<p>As long as the PCs react quickly, they should be able to reach Willowshore Stables in time to help. By this point, the fire has engulfed the barn and the employees have managed to save the livestock by leading them into the pasture. However, the fire now threatens to spread into the pasture and potentially further into town. The PCs can assist in putting out the fire by taking the Fight Barn Fire activity.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.y3wK3OJE2af6Uijq]{Barn Fire}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Fight Barn Fire</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Move</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You help fight the fire that threatens to consume Willowshore Stables and, if left untended, that can potentially spread into the rest of town. To fight the fire, attempt a @Check[athletics|dc:19] check to actively fight the flames by joining a bucket brigade or creating fire breaks to contain the fire, or a @Check[diplomacy|dc:21] check to organize townsfolk to help them be more efficient about their firefighting techniques. If you have magical spells that might help to fight the fire, you can use them to do so—expend up to three spells that the GM agrees would be helpful in fighting fires, then attempt an Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion check (as is appropriate for your spellcasting tradition). The DC of this check is 17 if you used three spells, 19 if you used two, and 21 if you used one.</p>\n  <table>\n    <tbody><tr>\n      <td>@Check[Arcana,Nature,Occultism|dc:17|traits:exploration,manipulate,move|name:Fight Barn Fire]</td>\n      <td>@Check[Arcana,Nature,Occultism|dc:19|traits:exploration,manipulate,move|name:Fight Barn Fire]</td>\n      <td>@Check[Arcana,Nature,Occultism|dc:21|traits:exploration,manipulate,move|name:Fight Barn Fire]</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody></table>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> Your efforts to fight the fire are enormously helpful. The party gains 2 Victory Points. In addition, your impressive efforts earn the party 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success </strong>Your firefighting efforts help the townsfolk stem the blaze. The party gains 1 Victory Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure </strong>You did your best to assist but weren’t able to contribute anything particularly helpful. Worse, you got burned in the process and take @Damage[3d6[fire]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:19|basic] save).</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Disaster! Your attempt to fight the fire caused the flames to spread! Worse, you got badly burned in the process and take @Damage[3d10[fire]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:19|basic] save). The party loses 1 Victory Point.</p>\n</section>\n<p>If the PCs manage to achieve at least 3 Victory Points as they Fight the Barn Fire, they and the townsfolk manage to get the blaze under control quickly with a triumphant success. If the PCs achieve 0, 1, or 2 Victory Points, the fire spreads into the field and damages the fences before it’s put out, resulting in a moderate success. If the PCs end up with –1 or fewer Victory Points, the fire engulfs the main building as well and burns it all down, field included, before the townsfolk contain the fire and keep it from spreading, resulting in a tragic success that costs the party 2 Food Points and 2 Security Points.</p>\n<p>After the fire is out, the PCs can investigate the badly burnt barn by spending an hour Investigating the ruins. The investigation turns up an eerie bit of evidence—a charred tengu skeleton with a mark of crime etched on the skull, whose head seems to have been severed at the neck by a heavy blade, even though the skull and skeleton lie in place apparently intact. Allow the PCs a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:17] (or a @Check[diplomacy|dc:17|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] to Gather Information); on a success, they recall the short-lived reign of terror an arsonist named Nin Nok went on in Willowshore before she was captured and executed for her crimes—she was beheaded, and a mark of crime was etched on her skull to indicate her punishment in the afterlife before she was buried in an unmarked grave in the Bones of the Forgotten northwest of town. If the PCs then visit that graveyard, it takes only 10 minutes of Investigating to locate an unmarked grave that appears to have been dug up from within—another example of restless spirits coming back from death as a result of exorcism attempts in the living world, but for now, it seems like simply one more “symptom” of the eerie curse afflicting Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP if they achieve at least 3 Victory Points fighting the fire and an extra 40 XP if they discover the unnerving mystery behind the fire. They also earn 1 Reputation Point with Southbank for earning 3 Victory Points. If they earned less than 0 Victory Points, though, they lose 1 Reputation Point with Southbank.</p>"
            },
            "Week 7: An Icy Grasp": {
              "name": "第7周：冰冷的纠缠 Week 7: An Icy Grasp",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span>第7周：冰冷的纠缠</span> <span>低4</span></h2>\n<p>五十年前，<strong>Goh</strong>（毁灭的男性渔夫3级）趁着溜出去玩，把弟弟独自留在无人看管的情况下，导致他唯一的手足在木棉河中丧生。因自己在弟弟意外溺水中的责任而产生的羞愧折磨了Goh数十年；而当现代的驱魔人开始在生者世界施展魔法，对抗柳岸镇的作祟时，这份羞愧化作了一场极其真实的作祟。</p>\n<p>Goh神情恍惚、惊恐不安地找到PC们，讲述自己当天早些时候下水把小艇拖上岸时，有一双手抓住了他的脚踝。他坚信那双手属于弟弟的魂魄——弟弟回来把他带走，惩罚他放任弟弟溺水。当Goh描述这场作祟，并含泪诉说自己对弟弟之死所怀的羞愧时，让每位PC进行一次 @Check[perception|dc:19|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] 检定，以意识到这场作祟可能是由Goh自己的羞愧所引起。若大成功或大失败，某位PC推断：用交涉来安抚Goh，并帮助他原谅自己，或许是终结这场作祟最简单的方式。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">第7周：冰冷的纠缠</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.4TOkx9RSH8FmaLSl]{Goh's Shame}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>作祟：</strong> Goh的判断并非相去甚远，但问题不在于他弟弟的魂魄——而在于Goh自己的羞愧。当他带着PC们回到他家附近河边、当年事故发生的地点时，尽管PC们尝试调查，却没有出现新的作祟。Goh松了口气，也踏入河中，然而作祟立刻再次对他发动攻击。PC们必须迅速行动，才能从溺水中救下这位年迈的渔夫。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong> 如果PC们解除或摧毁该作祟，队伍获得1点希望点；除非Goh死去——若是如此，队伍转而失去1点希望点。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span>Week 7: An Icy Grasp</span> <span>Low 4</span></h2>\n<p>Fifty years ago, <strong>Goh</strong> (doomed male fisher 3) lost his only sibling to the Ceiba River when he left his younger brother unsupervised while he snuck away to play. Shame for his role in his brother’s accidental drowning has haunted Goh for decades, but when the modern exorcists begin to work their magic against Willowshore’s haunts from the living world, this shame manifests as a very real haunting.</p>\n<p>Goh approaches the PCs, shaken and scared, with a story of hands grabbing his ankles earlier in the day after he got into the water to pull his skiff ashore. He’s convinced that these hands belong to his brother’s spirit, returned to carry him away for letting his brother drown. As Goh describes the haunt and tearfully recounts the shame he feels for his role in his brother’s death, allow each PC a @Check[perception|dc:19|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] check to realize that it might be Goh’s own shame that’s causing the haunt. On a critical success, a PC theorizes that using Diplomacy to try to calm Goh down and to forgive himself could be the simplest way to end the haunt.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Week 7: An Icy Grasp</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.4TOkx9RSH8FmaLSl]{Goh's Shame}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Haunting:</strong> Goh isn’t far off from the truth, but it’s not his brother’s spirit that’s the problem here—it’s Goh’s own shame. When he leads the PCs back to the spot on the river near his home where the incident occurred, no new haunting manifests despite the PCs’ attempts to investigate. Relieved, Goh steps into the river as well, only to immediately be attacked by the haunting once more. The PCs must move quickly to save the elderly fisherman from drowning.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs disable or destroy the haunt, the party earns 1 Hope Point unless Goh perishes, in which case the party instead loses 1 Hope Point.</p>"
            },
            "Week 6: The Faceless Ghost": {
              "name": "第6周：无脸的幽魂 Week 6: The Faceless Ghost",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">第6周：无脸的幽魂</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 4</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jeonghuiho.webp\" data-tooltip=\"洪正辉\" alt=\"洪正辉，男性人类镇卫兵\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jeonghuiho.webp')\" />\n<p>洪正辉（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w24hojeonghu00]{洪正辉的家}）被认为是柳岸镇最抢手的单身汉之一。日落后一个小时，他正在家里做一顿迟来的晚餐时，看到窗外有个身影。他抓起一把剑走到屋外，准备与那身影对峙，以为是潜入者或坏人。但他发现的既不是这两者；这次遭遇把他吓得拔腿就逃，转而来向PC们求助。</p>\n<p>找到PC们后，这名仍惊魂未定的卫兵描述道：他起初以为那是一件又长又黑的袍子，实际上却是由雾与烟构成、隐约呈人形的轮廓；当它转身面对他时，所戴的那张毫无五官的石面具令他恐惧万分。他请求PC们前往他的家（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w24hojeonghu00]{W24}）调查潜伏在他院子里的“无脸幽魂”，并在PC们调查之前拒绝回家。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-gwishin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">第6周：无脸的幽魂</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.6J4FxMi8HejSvOJw]{蛋脸鬼}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>洪正辉所对峙的身影，是另一个躁动不安的魂魄；在现代试图驱除柳岸镇闹鬼现象的行动推动下，它被迫现身活动。然而在这个案例中，这个魂魄是一种真正的不死生物：蛋脸鬼。PC在听完这次可怕遭遇的故事后，若成功进行一次 @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 以回忆知识，便能认出这生物的真面目。</p>\n  <p>蛋脸鬼因洪正辉的人气而被吸引到他家。它每晚都会回来在此潜伏徘徊，并在每次日出时消失。若PC们在三天内未能击败这不死生物，它会去寻找躲藏起来的洪正辉；若没有PC留下来保护他，次日人们将发现他无脸的尸体。之后，蛋脸鬼会选择魅力调整值最高的PC作为下一个受害者。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们击败该生物，队伍获得1点希望点与1点来自北岭人的声望点。若洪正辉先行死亡，队伍失去1点希望点与1点来自北岭人的声望点。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Week 6: The Faceless Ghost</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 4</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jeonghuiho.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ho Jeong-hui\" alt=\"Ho Jeong-hui, male human town guard\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jeonghuiho.webp')\" />\n<p>Ho Jeong-hui (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w24hojeonghu00]{Ho Jeong-hui’s Home}), known as one of Willowshore’s most eligible bachelors, was cooking a late dinner at home an hour after sunset when he saw a figure outside his window. He grabbed a sword and headed outside, ready to confront the figure, expecting a prowler or miscreant. What he found was neither, and his encounter sent him fleeing to ask the PCs for aid.</p>\n<p>Upon reaching the PCs, the still-shaken guard describes what he at first took for a long, dark robe to be a vaguely humanoid shape made of mist and smoke, and when it turned to face him, the featureless stone mask it wore filled him with fright. He asks the PCs to head to his home (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w24hojeonghu00]{W24}) and investigate the “faceless ghost” that’s lurking in his yard, refusing to go back home until the PCs have investigated.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-gwishin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Week 6: The Faceless Ghost</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.6J4FxMi8HejSvOJw]{Dalgyal Gwishin}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The figure Jeong-hui confronted was another restless spirit driven into action by the attempts in the modern era to exorcise the hauntings in Willowshore. In this case, though, the spirit is an actual undead creature: a dalgyal gwishin. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] to Recall Knowledge after hearing the story of the frightening encounter recognizes the creature for what it is.</p>\n  <p>The dalgyal gwishin was drawn to Jeong-hui’s home as a result of his popularity. It returns to skulk about the place every night, vanishing with every sunrise. If the PCs don’t defeat the undead within three days, it seeks out Jeong-hui wherever he might have gone into hiding and, if no PC remains behind to protect him, his faceless corpse is discovered the next day, after which the dalgyal gwishin chooses the PC with the highest Charisma modifier as their next victim.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs defeat the creature, the party earns 1 Hope Point and 1 Reputation Point with Northridge. If Ho Jeong-hui dies first, the party loses 1 Hope Point and 1 Reputation Point with Northridge.</p>"
            },
            "Week 5: The Missing Corpse": {
              "name": "第5周：失踪的尸体 Week 5: The Missing Corpse",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 5: The Missing Corpse\">第5周：失踪的尸体</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Elizeth Candora\" alt=\"Elizeth Candora, female human cleric of Pharasma\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp')\" />\n<p>某天早晨，<strong>伊丽丝·堪多拉</strong>（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w9ladyofsoul00]{司魂娘娘}），司魂娘娘庙的女祭司长，私下请求PC们抽空见她一面。一位年迈的村民昨晚因流感去世；同一晚稍晚时候，尸体却失踪了，“就好像它自己走掉了一样”。她怀疑照看坟边居的精灵草药师游素锦用某种“炼金调配物”让尸体动了起来，但无论如何都没有证据。她希望PC们调查这具失踪尸体发生了什么事，并提出以神庙的赠礼作为解开谜团的交换。</p>\n<p>若PC们花费10分钟在司魂娘娘庙进行调查，一名成功通过@Check[perception|dc:19|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]检定的角色会发现一串看似拖沓踉跄的脚印向北延伸。以成功的@Check[survival|dc:20|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]检定即可追踪这条足迹，将PC们带到木棉河的南岸，位置在晨步桥以西约200尺处——足迹似乎直接走进了河里。若PC们花费10分钟调查对岸，并成功通过@Check[survival|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]检定，他们能再次找回足迹；拖沓的脚印从河里走出，踏入泥地并朝西北前进。若再成功通过第三次@Check[survival|dc:20|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]检定，PC们会一路将足迹追到镇上——而且，竟然是追到了青天茶馆！</p>\n<p>素锦与此谜案毫无关系（若PC们指控她，她会变得恼火，她对队伍的态度降低一级）。真正的犯人正是小暗——那只住进PC们茶馆的化猫。数个月来，这只对死灵术充满好奇的化猫一直克制自己不去唤起一具僵尸，但她的意志最终崩溃。她用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.c3b6LdLlQDPngNIb]{唤起死灵}唤起了一位老妇人的尸体；那名老妇人生前常常为小暗留食物。小暗认为自己的唤起是在回报恩情，但也明白当地人未必会这么想，因此她让僵尸蹒跚者一直藏在茶馆后方的灌木丛中。</p>\n<p>若PC们成功将僵尸追踪到茶馆后方的灌木丛，他们会在浓密的枝叶深处发现它：它蜷伏着，耐心等待小暗回来——被发现时会抬眼看向PC们，却不会移动；只有在先遭到攻击时才会反击。无论如何，一旦PC们发现僵尸，小暗便会迅速靠近，站到她的僵尸旁边，然后决定是时候坦白自己在这场胡闹中的角色了。</p>\n<p>如果PC们已经交好小暗（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#befriend-yami]{交好小暗}），他们也许早已发现她的真相；但不管怎样，小暗都会请求PC们让她“留着”这具僵尸，并解释说它在月光下跳舞跳得很好（甚至会命令僵尸当场跳舞示范）。小暗也能理解若PC们想让僵尸回归死亡、并把尸体送回教会；但她仍固执地希望PC们允许她留下它。要说服小暗放弃她的僵尸，PC们必须成功通过一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:21]或@Check[intimidation|dc:21]检定。若PC们已经交好小暗，他们将该检定的结果提升一级成功度。</p>\n<p>若PC们摧毁僵尸、或违背小暗的意愿将其带走，又或者他们用威吓迫使她同意，化猫会变得阴沉乖戾，并离开柳岸镇。由你决定，PC们未来也许会再次遭遇她，并有机会弥补关系；或者她也可能回来折磨PC们以报复。</p>\n<p>若PC们没能追踪到僵尸，那也只是时间问题：迟早某个深夜他们会撞见小暗在茶馆后方让僵尸为她跳舞；届时，PC们应当能根据伊丽丝给出的描述认出那具不死尸体。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>财宝：</strong> @UUID[Actor.RbSPe4sD93QOZEK5]{伊丽丝的报酬} <br />\n  若PC们找到并将尸体归还给伊丽丝，队伍除了承诺的报酬——四瓶<em>次等治疗药水</em>与一枚<em>活化属性符文石</em>——还可获得1点希望点。伊丽丝也想知道是谁偷走了尸体或让它动了起来，但只要尸体在未被唤起的状态下归还，她就不会过多追问细节。若PC们在归还失踪的尸体时仍维持与小暗的友谊，队伍额外获得1点希望点。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们因发现并归还失踪的尸体获得80 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 5: The Missing Corpse\">Week 5: The Missing Corpse</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Elizeth Candora\" alt=\"Elizeth Candora, female human cleric of Pharasma\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp')\" />\n<p>One morning, <strong>Elizeth Candora</strong> (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w9ladyofsoul00]{Lady of Souls}), the head priestess of Her Fluvial Lady of Souls, requests a moment of the PCs’ time in private. An elderly villager died from the flu the previous night; the corpse went missing sometime later that same evening, “as if it just walked away on its own.” She suspects that You So-Jin, the elven herbalist who minds Graveside Manners, animated the body with some sort of “alchemical concoction” but doesn’t have any proof one way or the other. She wants the PCs to investigate what happened to the missing body and offers gifts from the temple in exchange for solving the mystery.</p>\n<p>If the PCs spend 10 minutes Investigating Her Fluvial Lady of Souls, a character who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:19|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate] check spots what appears to be a set of shambling footprints leading north. The trail can be Tracked with a successful @Check[survival|dc:20|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] check, which leads the PCs to the south bank of the Ceiba River, about 200 feet west of Dawnstep Bridge—the trail seems to have led right into the river. If the PCs spend 10 minutes Investigating the opposite shore, with a successful @Check[survival|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate] check, they can pick up the trail again; the shambling prints emerge from the river into mud and head northwest. By succeeding at a third @Check[survival|dc:20|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] check, the PCs track the prints through town to, of all places, the Cerulean Teahouse!</p>\n<p>So-Jin has nothing to do with this mystery (and if the PCs accuse her of it, she grows frustrated and her attitude toward the party shifts down one degree). The actual perpetrator is none other than Yami, the bakeneko who has taken up residence in the PCs’ teahouse. For many months, the necromantically-curious bakeneko has resisted the urge to animate a zombie, but her resolve finally broke down. She used @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.c3b6LdLlQDPngNIb]{Create Undead} to animate the corpse of an elderly woman who often left food out for Yami while she lived. Yami sees her animation as repaying a favor but understands that locals might not see it the same way, so she had the zombie shambler remain in hiding in the bushes behind the teahouse.</p>\n<p>If the PCs successfully track the zombie to the bushes behind their teahouse, they find it deep in the shrubbery, crouched down and waiting patiently for Yami to return—it glances up at the PCs when discovered but doesn’t move, attacking only if it’s attacked first. As soon as the PCs discover the zombie, in any event, Yami quickly approaches to stand next to her zombie, then decides it’s time to confess her role in the shenanigan.</p>\n<p>If the PCs have already befriended Yami (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#befriend-yami]{Befriend Yami}), they might have already discovered the truth about her, but regardless, Yami asks the PCs to let her “keep” the zombie, explaining that it dances well in the moonlight (and even orders the zombie to dance as a demonstration). Yami understands if the PCs want the zombie to be returned to death and brought back to the church, but stubbornly hopes the PCs will let her keep it. To convince Yami to let her zombie go, the PCs must succeed at a @Check[diplomacy|dc:21] or @Check[intimidation|dc:21] check. If the PCs have already befriended Yami, they improve the result of this check by one degree of success.</p>\n<p>If the PCs destroy the zombie or otherwise take her away against Yami’s wishes, or if they use Intimidation to get her to agree, the bakeneko grows surly and abandons Willowshore. At your option, the PCs might encounter her again in the future and have a chance to make amends, or she might return to torment the PCs to get revenge.</p>\n<p>If the PCs don’t manage to track the zombie, it should just be a matter of time before they catch Yami making the zombie dance for her out behind the teahouse late one night, at which point the PCs should be able to recognize the undead corpse by the description given to them by Elizeth.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.RbSPe4sD93QOZEK5]{Elizeth's Reward} <br />\n  If the PCs find and return the corpse to Elizeth, the party earns 1 Hope Point in addition to the promised rewards—four <em>lesser healing potions</em> and a <em>vitalizing property runestone</em>. Elizeth also wants to know who stole the corpse or animated it, but as long as the corpse is returned in an unanimated state, she won’t press much for details. If the PCs managed to return the missing corpse while maintaining Yami’s friendship, the party earns 1 additional Hope Point.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP for discovering and returning the missing corpse.</p>"
            },
            "Week 4: Haunted Hair": {
              "name": "第4周：鬼发 Week 4: Haunted Hair",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">第4周：鬼发</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低阶4</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yumingnakamura.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nakamura Yu Ming\" alt=\"Nakamura Yu Ming, female human cook\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yumingnakamura.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>中村玉茗</strong>（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w21mamabaos000]{包子嫲嫲}），大家亲切地称她为“包子嫲嫲”，是柳岸镇镇区附近一家小包子铺的老板。本周伊始，她开始发现店铺天花板上垂下的一缕缕头发；不管她清理多少次，这些头发每天早晨都会重新出现。起初，她以为罪魁祸首是顽皮的神灵，或是小孩在恶作剧——直到今天，她的顾客咬开包子后，却只得把夹杂在馅料里的发团吐出来。包子嫲嫲心烦意乱，关了店，去找PC们求助，请他们回到她的店里过夜，看看能否逮到制造这桩怪事的元凶。</p>\n<p>抵达包子嫲嫲的店铺后，PC们很快就能确认：前一晚做好的所有包子，其馅料里都混入了头发。一次@Check[perception|dc:14]检定可确认这些发丝长度几乎一致，且来自同一个人的头。通过@Check[society|dc:17]或@Check[medicine|dc:17]，一名角色会注意到这些头发保养得很好且未受损，但看起来是从发根处被硬生生拔下，而不是用刀刃剪断。头发的来源是一名灵体；在现代世界里，驱邪者试图净化柳岸镇的举动惊扰了她的安息。</p>\n<p>纠缠包子嫲嫲的幽魂是日出明里：一位年轻女子。她离开柳岸镇，寻求冒险人生，却在旅途开始仅两天时，于镇外遇见包子嫲嫲的祖父而惨遭横死。他听说司泽城有一位制偶师会高价收购长发来制作人偶，于是杀害了明里，将她头上的每一根头发都从发根拔下并卖给制偶师，换来足以让家人熬过寒冬并开设一间小包子铺的钱。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-writing-hair.webp\" />\n\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">第4周：鬼发</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低阶4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.h0Pjx3rzAZGBWMD1]{缠怨之发}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-writing-hair.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hinode Akari\" alt=\"the ghostly form of a young woman with long hair\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-writing-hair.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>明里在她被谋杀的地点徘徊了数十年；但当驱邪者开始在现代柳岸镇施展法术时，她的灵体受惊躁动到足以对杀害她的凶手那毫不知情的孙女发起报复。尽管她的故事悲惨，明里最初的出没更多只是令人毛骨悚然的困扰，而非真正的威胁；但当PC们在店里过夜时，这一点便会改变。因此，PC们是这间店被闹鬼后第一批在此过夜的人。</p>\n  <p>午夜过后一小时，一名长发年轻女子的幽影会从某一扇门飘入店内，随后开始从发根处将自己的头发一把把拔下。她捧出一把把头发，那些头发如虫般在空中蠕动，钻入明日的包子馅里，并在椽梁间结成怪异的编发图案。若PC们不采取行动，这处怨灵将在1分钟后完成其诡异的仪式，随即消散。目睹这幅幽影后，一名PC可以尝试一次@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:21]检定（或在次日尝试一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:21|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]检定来搜集信息）以回想起一则旧闻：曾有人在葫芦湖附近发现一具年轻女子的尸体，她头上的每一根头发都被从头皮上拔了下来。后来，这名女子被确认为当地一位草药师，名叫日出明里。若PC们将此事告知包子嫲嫲，她会脸色煞白，待各个碎片拼接起来后，震惊得咒骂出声。她透露，在尸体被发现的前几个夜晚，她祖父突然发了一笔横财，并用这笔钱建起了这家包子铺。他曾对她父母说钱来自把“一批旧假发卖给司泽的制偶师”，但如今包子嫲嫲回想起祖父当时的闪烁其词，开始怀疑那可怕的真相。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们击败或解除此怨灵，队伍获得1点希望点。若PC们查明了怨灵的故事，包子嫲嫲承诺会设法让日出明里的名声得到应有的纪念，以赎她祖父的残忍之罪，而队伍额外获得1点希望点。此外，若PC们击败或解除此怨灵，因帮助柳岸镇镇区的一家店铺，PC们获得北岭人1点声望点。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Week 4: Haunted Hair</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 4</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yumingnakamura.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nakamura Yu Ming\" alt=\"Nakamura Yu Ming, female human cook\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yumingnakamura.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Nakamura Yu Ming</strong> (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w21mamabaos000]{Mama Bao’s}), known affectionately as “Mama Bao,” is the owner of a small steamed bun shop near downtown Willowshore. As this week begins, she starts finding clumps of hair dangling from the ceiling of her shop that reappear each morning no matter how often she cleans them up. At first, she assumed the culprit was a mischievous kami or children playing pranks on her—at least until today, when her customers all bit into their steamed buns only to spit out clumps of hair mixed in with the bun fillings. Distraught, Mama Bao closes her shop and seeks out the PCs for help, asking them to come back to her shop to help solve the strange mystery by spending the night and seeing if they can catch the culprit.</p>\n<p>Upon arriving at Mama Bao’s shop, the PCs can swiftly confirm that all of the buns prepared the evening before have had hair mixed in with their fillings. A @Check[perception|dc:14] confirms that the hair strands are all around the same length and came from the same head. With a @Check[society|dc:17] or @Check[medicine|dc:17], a character notes that the hair is well-maintained and undamaged but appears to have been plucked from the scalp at the root and not cut with a blade. The source of the hair is a spirit whose rest has been agitated by exorcists in the modern world attempting to cleanse Willowshore.</p>\n<p>The ghost haunting Mama Bao is that of Hinode Akari, a young woman who left Willowshore in search of a life of adventure, only to have her life cut short when she ran into Mama Bao’s grandfather outside of town just two days into her journey. He had heard that a doll maker in the city of Sze paid handsomely for long hair to use for his dolls, so he killed Akari, plucked each strand of hair from her head, and sold it to the doll maker for enough money to last his family through the winter and open a small steamed bun shop.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-writing-hair.webp\" />\n\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Week 4: Haunted Hair</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.h0Pjx3rzAZGBWMD1]{Writhing Hair}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-writing-hair.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hinode Akari\" alt=\"the ghostly form of a young woman with long hair\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-writing-hair.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> Akari lingered for decades where she had been murdered, but when exorcists begin to work their magic on modern Willowshore, her spirit becomes agitated enough to lash out at her killer’s unsuspecting granddaughter. Despite her tragic story, Akari’s haunting presence is initially more of an unnerving inconvenience than an actual threat, but that changes when the PCs stay overnight in the shop. The PCs are thus the first to spend the night in the shop after it becomes haunted.</p>\n  <p>An hour after midnight, the ghostly form of a young woman with long hair drifts into the shop through one of the doors, then proceeds to pull out her hair by the roots. She holds out handfuls of hair, and they slither through the air like worms to infest tomorrow’s steamed buns and to form strange, braided patterns tangled in the rafters. If the PCs take no action, the haunt completes its uncanny rite after a minute before it fades away. After seeing the spectral image, a PC can attempt a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:21] check (or can attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:21|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] check the next day to Gather Information) to recall an old story about a young woman’s corpse that was found near Gourd Lake with every hair on her head plucked from her scalp. The woman was later identified as a local herbalist named Hinode Akari. If the PCs mention this tale to Mama Bao, she grows pale and then curses in shock as the pieces fall into place. She reveals that a few nights before the body was found, her grandfather came into a sudden windfall of money which he used to build the steamed bun shop. He told her parents that the money came from selling “an old collection of wigs to a puppet maker in Sze,” but now Mama Bao recalls how evasive her grandfather had been and suspects the awful truth.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs defeat or disable the haunt, the party earns 1 Hope Point. If the PCs discovered the haunt’s story, Mama Bao promises to see to it that Hinode Akari’s memory is honored in order to atone for her grandfather’s cruelty, and the party earns 1 additional Hope Point. In addition, for helping a downtown business, the PCs earn 1 Reputation Point with Northridge if they defeat or disable the haunt.</p>"
            },
            "Shinzo’s Visit": {
              "name": "神藏的拜访 Shinzo’s Visit",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Visit\">神藏的拜访</h3>\n<p>神秘的商人朝比奈神藏会在节日期间到镇上拜访，并带着他那只古怪的渡鸦同伴小伊。如同前一幕，神藏应当保持神秘却友善；他不会直接参与任何庆典活动，但似乎很享受旁观镇民的狂欢。与之前一样，他的补给车应根据PC的兴趣来调整。你可以制作一份供PC选购的物品清单，在他的车上装满十来件等级不高于队伍等级的物品；或者你也可以允许玩家为物品“下订单”，这些物品会在神藏下次来访时可供购买。</p>\n<p>不过在首长夜期间，神藏会更投入庆典，并以九折出售他的物品（此折扣不适用于PC下订单的物品）。</p>\n<p>PC可能会想到请求神藏协助为柳岸镇运来食物补给，但面对这一请求，这位神秘商人只是悲伤地微笑，解释说他没有能力提供如此协助所需的大量资源（事实上，向柳岸镇提供这种程度的支援，已经略微超出了限制——这些限制使他无法对身陷险境的凡人给予过多协助；这种限制令他沮丧，却也无可奈何）。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Visit\">Shinzo’s Visit</h3>\n<p>The mysterious merchant Asahina Shinzo pays a visit to town during the festival along with his strange raven companion, Yix. As in the previous act, Shinzo should be enigmatic but friendly, and while he won’t directly take part in any of the festivities, he does seem to enjoy watching the townsfolk’s revels. As before, his cart of supplies should be tailored to serve the PCs’ interests. You can create a list of items for the PCs to shop through, filling his cart with a dozen items of a level no higher than the party’s level, or you can allow the players to “place orders” for items that will be available for purchase upon Shinzo’s next visit.</p>\n<p>During First Long Night, though, Shinzo gets into the festivities and offers his items for sale at a 10% discount (this discount doesn’t apply to items the PCs place orders for).</p>\n<p>The PCs might think to ask Shinzo for aid in bringing supplies of food for Willowshore, but to this request, the mysterious merchant only smiles sadly, explaining he doesn’t have the capacity to provide the significant amount of resources that would be required for such assistance (in fact, providing this level of support to Willowshore is just a step beyond the restrictions that bar him from giving too much aid to mortals in peril—a restriction that frustrates him but that he can do nothing about).</p>"
            },
            "On the Night of the Festival": {
              "name": "庆典之夜 On the Night of the Festival",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"On the Night of the Festival\">在节庆之夜</h3>\n<p>首长夜在秋分时举行，而秋分恰好落在一周的最后一天。这给了你的PC们一个机会，能与他们最喜欢的柳岸镇NPC进行一些角色扮演。阅读@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl]{首长夜}以帮助你向PC呈现节庆；也可以分别花点时间和每位PC确认他们打算如何盛装参加节庆。</p>\n<p>注意：本书中对首长夜的描述假设庆典发生在现代时代——在络新妇统治了一个世纪左右之后。不过，对PC而言这些传统几乎无需改动；他们所处的时间线是在神门这个新秩序黎明之际。大体上，柳岸镇的人民对络新妇的恐惧应当改为对侵扰小镇的诅咒的恐惧；甚至可能有人希望，一场成功的首长夜能以某种方式帮助解除诅咒。</p>\n<p>节庆主要在柳岸镇镇区的镇广场举行，但全镇各处也会举办规模较小的庆祝、活动与宴席。主要庆典在晚上6:00到午夜的6小时内展开。在这段时间里，每位PC都可以各参加一次首长夜期间举行的三项@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17traditionalc00]{传统比赛}。</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17admiringthem00]{咏月诗会：} @UUID[Actor.a0rifkCPNhKWyhWX]{咏月诗会奖励} <br />\n  若至少一名PC在咏月诗会中获得4点胜利点数，则队伍获得1点希望点。任何在咏月诗会中获得6点胜利点数的PC，会因其胜利赢得一份炼金灵药，从下列三项中选择其一：<em>中等认知突变药剂</em>、<em>中等宁静突变药剂</em>或<em>中等巧舌突变药剂</em>。\n</p>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17bundlecuttin00]{割草绳：} @UUID[Actor.AO5gV1JCW2fBDiPc]{割草绳奖励} <br />若至少一名PC在割草绳比赛中获得4点胜利点数，则队伍获得1点希望点。任何在割草绳比赛中获得6点胜利点数的PC，会因其压倒性胜利赢得一枚由其自选的<em>强击武器符文</em>或<em>幽冥武器符文</em>。</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17lanternmakin00]{制作天灯：} @UUID[Actor.yMia3XbY4pPcJoMC]{制作天灯奖励} @UUID[Actor.hkB6tLKigqZ3xLVm]{制作天灯大奖} <br />\n  若至少一名PC在制作天灯比赛中获得4点胜利点数，则队伍获得1点希望点。任何在制作天灯比赛中获得6点胜利点数的PC，会因其压倒性胜利赢得三瓶<em>低等生命灵药</em>。与另外两项比赛不同，制作天灯比赛是一项单一活动，只能有一位大奖得主。若没有PC获得至少6点胜利点数，则获胜者为来自@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w3gravesidem00]{坟边居}的游素金。若有PC获得6点或更多胜利点数，则胜利点数最高的PC为大奖得主；若出现平手，则大奖均分。大奖本身是一只丝绸小袋，内含数颗珍珠与宝石，总价值100 gp。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>无论PC赢得了多少项比赛，队伍都会因参加首长夜而获得1点希望点以及120 XP。若PC至少赢得1项比赛，他们获得1点声望点数，可分配给他们选择的任一派系。若他们赢得全部三项比赛，他们同时获得分配给南岸与北岭人的各1点声望点数。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"On the Night of the Festival\">On the Night of the Festival</h3>\n<p>First Long Night takes place during the fall equinox, which happens to occur on the last day of the week. This is an opportunity for your PCs to get some roleplaying time in with their favorite Willowshore NPCs. Read through @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl]{First Long Night} to help present the festival for the PCs, perhaps taking time with each PC to determine how they wish to dress for the festival.</p>\n<p>Note that the description of First Long Night of this book assume the celebration takes place in the modern era, after a century or so of jorogumo rule. Few changes to these traditions take place for the PCs, though, who exist in a timeline at the dawn of this new order in Shenmen. For the most part, fears about jorogumo in particular for the people of Willowshore should instead be fears about the curse afflicting the town, perhaps with some even hoping that a successful First Long Night will help lift the curse in some way.</p>\n<p>The festival primarily takes place on the town square in downtown Willowshore, but smaller celebrations and events and feasts occur throughout the town. The bulk of the celebrations play out over a 6-hour span from 6:00 p.m. to midnight. During this time, the PCs can each take part once in the three @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17traditionalc00]{Traditional Contests} held during First Long Night.</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17admiringthem00]{Admiring the Moon:} @UUID[Actor.a0rifkCPNhKWyhWX]{Admiring the Moon Reward} <br />\n  If at least one PC earns 4 Victory Points in the Admiring the Moon contest, the party earns 1 Hope Point. Any PC who earns 6 Victory Points while Admiring the Moon wins an alchemical elixir for their victory, chosen from the following three options: a <em>moderate cognitive mutagen</em>, a <em>moderate serene mutagen</em>, or a <em>moderate silvertongue mutagen</em>.\n</p>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17bundlecuttin00]{Bundle-Cutting:} @UUID[Actor.AO5gV1JCW2fBDiPc]{Bundle-Cutting Reward} <br />If at least one PC earns 4 Victory Points in the Bundle-Cutting contest, the party earns 1 Hope Point. Any PC who earns 6 Victory Points while Bundle-Cutting wins their choice of a <em>striking weapon rune</em> or a <em>ghost touch weapon rune</em> for their overwhelming victory.</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog17firstl.JournalEntryPage.17lanternmakin00]{Lantern Making:} @UUID[Actor.yMia3XbY4pPcJoMC]{Lantern Making Reward} @UUID[Actor.hkB6tLKigqZ3xLVm]{Lantern Making Grand Prize} <br />\n  If at least one PC earns 4 Victory Points in the Lantern Making contest, the party earns 1 Hope Point. Any PC who earns 6 Victory Points while Lantern Making wins three <em>lesser elixirs of life</em> for their overwhelming victory. Unlike the other two contests, the Lantern Making contest is a single event that can have only one grand prize winner. If no PC earns at least 6 Victory Points, then the winner is You So-Jin of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w3gravesidem00]{Graveside Manners}. If a PC earns 6 or more Victory points, the PC who earns the most Victory Points is the grand prize winner. In the event of a tie, the grand prize is split evenly. The grand prize itself is a silk pouch containing several pearls and gems worth a total of 100 gp.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Regardless of how many contests the PCs win, the party earns 1 Hope Point for taking part in First Long Night as well as 120 XP. If the PCs win at least 1 contest, they gain 1 Reputation Point to the faction of their choice. If they win all three contests, they gain 1 Reputation Point to both Southbank and Northridge.</p>"
            },
            "Week 3: First Long Night": {
              "name": "第3周：首长夜 Week 3: First Long Night",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 3: First Long Night\">第3周：首长夜</h2>\n<p>首长夜是神门乡间最令人期待的节日之一，柳岸镇也不例外——尤其是当下，镇民们正需要一天来庆祝，好从他们所处的令人不安的局势中分散注意力。仅在这一周内，每位PC都可以选择进行以下休整模式行动，以协助城镇为首长夜做准备，并可能获得更多希望点。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>协助节日准备</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整模式</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花这一周帮助镇民为首长夜做准备：可能是为庆典准备食物、清扫并准备市中心的城镇广场以举办活动，或协助制作节日期间当地人要穿的服装与其他配饰。要协助节日准备，尝试一次 @Check[food-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations]、@Check[games-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations]、@Check[labor-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations]、@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations]、@Check[crafting|dc:19|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations] 或 @Check[society|dc:21|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations] 检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 你为节日所做的准备不但高效且乐于帮助，还非常令人愉快。在首长夜期间，你在解决你参与的任何竞赛之效果的所有技能检定上获得+1环境加值。队伍获得2点希望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 你的协助帮助柳岸镇为首长夜做好了充分准备。队伍获得1点希望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 你尽力协助了，但没能做出什么特别有用的贡献。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 你试图帮忙却适得其反：你更多是在碍事而非真正提供协助，使挫败感在镇民间蔓延。由于你担心再犯更尴尬的错误而变得紧张，在首长夜期间，你在解决你参与的任何竞赛之效果的所有技能检定上承受–1环境减值。队伍失去1点希望点。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景笔记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.0N8xNGUTThSRU1zC]{Festival}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 3: First Long Night\">Week 3: First Long Night</h2>\n<p>First Long Night is one of the most anticipated holidays in rural Shenmen, and Willowshore is no exception—particularly now when the townsfolk could really use a day of celebration and distraction from the unsettling situation they find themselves in. During this week only, each PC has the option of taking the following downtime activity to help the town prepare for First Long Night and, potentially, earn more Hope Points.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Aid Festival Preparations</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week helping townsfolk get ready for First Long Night, either by preparing food for the celebration, cleaning and preparing downtown’s town square to host the event, or helping to craft outfits and other accessories for locals to wear during the festivities. To Aid Festival Preparations, attempt a @Check[food-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations], @Check[games-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations], @Check[labor-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations], @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:17|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations], @Check[crafting|dc:19|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations], or @Check[society|dc:21|traits:downtime,manipulate,preparation|name:Aid Festival Preparations] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> Your time preparing for the festival is not only efficient and helpful, but also highly enjoyable. During First Long Night, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to all skill checks to resolve the effects of any contests you take part in. The party gains 2 Hope Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> Your assistance has helped Willowshore prepare well for First Long Night. The party gains 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> You did your best to assist but weren’t able to contribute anything particularly helpful.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Your attempts to help backfire, with you getting in the way more than actually providing assistance, spreading frustration through the townsfolk. During First Long Night, you take a –1 circumstance penalty to all skill checks to resolve the effects of any contests you take part in as a result of being nervous about making more embarrassing mistakes. The party loses 1 Hope Point.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.0N8xNGUTThSRU1zC]{Festival}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "Week 2: A Slithering Situation": {
              "name": "第2周：滑行之灾 Week 2: A Slithering Situation",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">第2周：滑行之灾</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">琐事 4</span>\n</h2>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-viper-danger.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Infested Outhouse\" alt=\"被一窝蝰蛇侵占的户外厕所\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-viper-danger.webp')\" />\n<p>一名神色紧张的男子走近其中一位PC，自我介绍说他叫马苏（第16页），并解释自己遇到了一个需要真正英雄出手的问题，但他似乎又对多说有所戒备。只要PC不嘲笑或恐吓他，他很快就会说出自己的麻烦——一窝蝰蛇在他户外厕所的粪坑里安了家；而他在里面如厕时差点被咬，险些遭遇缓慢而痛苦的死亡。马苏脸红结巴，恳求PC们除掉蝰蛇群；如果他们能帮忙，他愿意支付2 gp，并邀请他们共进晚餐。马苏的家位于区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w12matsushom00]{W12}。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/viper.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">第2周：滑行之灾</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">琐事 4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.LQyA6WEksE2szg7M]{蝰蛇群}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC们来到户外厕所时，马苏小心翼翼地打开门锁，然后逃开，从他窗户的安全处观看事态发展。当PC们处理蝰蛇群时，他偶尔会喊出诸如“请一定小心！”和“你们做得比我强多了！”之类的话。蝰蛇群已经从粪坑里爬了出来，门一打开就会立刻发起攻击。</p>\n  <p>如果你愿意，可以从一开始就用战斗来解决这次事件；但你也可以先问问PC们，是否有什么巧妙的计划来把蛇引出或赶出户外厕所。这里的成功与否以一次DC 19的技能检定结果来衡量——具体使用哪项技能由你根据PC计划的性质来决定。用诱饵把蛇引出来可能需要一次自然检定；想用烟把它们熏出来则可能需要一次生存检定。发明一个复杂装置把蛇舀出来可能需要一次制作检定；而拥有动物同理或具备与动物交谈能力的人，或许能通过一次交涉检定说服蛇离开。若失败，蝰蛇会发动攻击，你应以战斗来解决这场遭遇。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.BoiA91hH8G1chIPF]{马苏的赠礼} <br />\n  如果PC们在不损坏马苏财物的情况下，将蝰蛇从他的户外厕所杀死或迁移到更不危险的地点，除了先前承诺的奖励外，他们还会额外获得1希望点。马苏是个单身汉，也是个手艺极佳的厨师，因此他承诺的那顿饭本身就应当是相当可观的奖励。晚餐结束时，马苏将一件多年来一直上锁藏匿的家族宝藏交给PC们——他认为PC们比他更配拥有它，毕竟他连自家厕所里的几条蛇都照顾不了。他满怀感激地将这件宝藏——一枚<em>幽冥符文</em>——赠予PC们，并真诚致谢。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>无论PC们如何处理这些蝰蛇，都给予他们80 XP作为清除蛇患的报酬。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Week 2: A Slithering Situation</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 4</span>\n</h2>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-viper-danger.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Infested Outhouse\" alt=\"Outhouse infested with a nest of vipers\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-viper-danger.webp')\" />\n<p>A nervous-looking man approaches one of the PCs and introduces himself as Matsu (page 16), explaining that he has a problem that needs true heroes, but he seems wary about saying more. As long as the PC doesn’t mock or intimidate him, he reveals his problem soon enough—a nest of vipers has taken up residence in the pit of his outhouse, and he narrowly escaped a slow and painful death after he was nearly bitten while conducting his business inside. Blushing and stammering, Matsu begs the PCs to get rid of the viper swarm and offers 2 gp and an invitation to dinner if they can help. Matsu’s home is located at area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w12matsushom00]{W12}.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/viper.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Week 2: A Slithering Situation</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 4</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.LQyA6WEksE2szg7M]{Viper Swarm}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When the PCs arrive at the outhouse, Matsu gingerly unlocks the door then flees to watch the events from the safety of his window. He occasionally shouts out things like “please be careful!” and “you’re doing better than I could!” while the PCs deal with the viper swarm. The viper swarm has made its way out of the pit, and they attack as soon as the door opens.</p>\n  <p>You can resolve this event with combat from the start if you wish, but you can also ask the PCs if they have any cunning plan for luring or chasing the snakes out of the outhouse. Success here is gauged by the result of a DC 19 skill check—the skill in question should be determined by you, depending on the nature of the PCs’ plan. An attempt to lure the snakes out using bait could require a Nature check, while an attempt to smoke them out might require a Survival check. The invention of a complex device to scoop the snakes out might need a Crafting check, and someone with Animal Empathy or the ability to speak to animals might be able to convince the snakes to leave with a Diplomacy check. On a failure, the vipers attack, and you should resolve the encounter with combat.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.BoiA91hH8G1chIPF]{Matsu's Gift} <br />\n  If the PCs kill or relocate the vipers from Matsu’s outhouse to a less dangerous location without damaging his property, they earn 1 Hope Point in addition to the promised rewards. Matsu is a bachelor and an excellent cook, so his promised meal should be a significant reward all on its own. As dinner concludes, Matsu presents the PCs with a family treasure he has kept locked up and hidden for years—he figures the PCs are more deserving of it than he is since he can’t even take care of a few snakes in his outhouse. He presents the PCs with this treasure, a <em>ghost touch rune</em>, with a heartfelt thank-you.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Regardless of how the PCs deal with the vipers, grant them 80 XP for getting rid of the snakes.</p>"
            },
            "Week 1: An Offering for Daikitsu": {
              "name": "第1周：献给大狐女的贡品 Week 1: An Offering for Daikitsu",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 1: An Offering for Daikitsu\">第1周：献给大狐女的贡品</h2>\n<p>一个名叫<strong>珉焕</strong>的孩子（善良的男性人类孩童1级）一直在森林里照料一只受伤的狐狸。昨天，他去探望那只狐狸，却沮丧地<strong>发现</strong>狐狸已经离开了他为它搭建的临时庇护所。他垂头丧气地回到家，当晚梦见一只白狐用鼻子轻触他的额头。珉焕醒来后坚信，那只狐狸是女神@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{大狐女}的使者，来告诉他在保护受伤狐狸这件事上做得很好。</p>\n<p>在此事件中，珉焕会走近其中一位PC，害羞地询问他应该向大狐女献上什么贡品（他很快补充道：不要花太多钱），并表示如果他们帮他挑选一份合适的供品，他愿意帮PC们一个忙。进行一次成功的@Check[religion|dc:15|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]来回忆知识（大狐女的崇拜者将其结果提高一个成功等级）后，PC会知道：献上一些朴素但可口的食物，尤其是稻荷寿司，并将其留在镇上的九耳神社，会是可以接受的。由你决定，PC提出的任何其他暗示（包括PC自己提供给珉焕的更昂贵礼物）同样有效。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们真诚地帮助珉焕为大狐女挑选一份贡品，他们获得1点希望点与80 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Week 1: An Offering for Daikitsu\">Week 1: An Offering for Daikitsu</h2>\n<p>A child named <strong>Minhwan</strong> (kindly male human child 1) has been taking care of an injured fox in the forest. Yesterday, he went to visit the fox only to discover to his dismay that the fox had abandoned the makeshift shelter he had built for it. Dejected, he returned home, and that night, he dreamed of a white fox touching its nose to his head. Minhwan woke with the conviction that the fox was a messenger of the goddess @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{Daikitsu} telling him he had done a good job protecting the injured fox.</p>\n<p>Minhwan approaches one of the PCs during this event and shyly asks what gift he should offer to Daikitsu (something that doesn’t cost a lot of money, he’s quick to add) and offers to do the PCs a favor if they help him pick out a good offering. With a successful @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] to Recall Knowledge (worshippers of Daikitsu increase their result by one degree of success), a PC knows that an offering of some sort of simple but tasty food, particularly inarizushi, left at Nine Ear Shrine in town would be acceptable. At your option, any other suggestions the PCs have (including pricier gifts of their own imparted to Minhwan) work just as well.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs help Minhwan pick out a gift for Daikitsu in earnest, they earn 1 Hope Point and 80 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Events": {
              "name": "柳岸镇事件 Willowshore Events",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore Events\">柳岸镇事件</h1>\n\n<p>随着日子一天天过去，秋季迅速迈向冬季，柳岸镇每周都会发生需要队伍关注的事件。这些事件在探索模式中进行，并且解决起来不超过一天。演绎这些事件不会影响队伍进行任何每周的休整模式活动。最好先解决一周的休整模式活动，再继续处理该周的事件。下方列出了这些事件发生的时间表，而事件本身的细节会在本章后文出现。若某个事件发生时PC们不在镇上，那么该事件应在他们返回后的第二天发生，其他所有“积压”的事件则每隔一天发生一次，直到重新赶上每周的日程——唯一的例外是首长夜，它总是在第3周发生。如果PC们因整周都不在镇上而错过这个事件，他们将错失一个获得希望点的绝佳机会。</p>\n<h2 class=\"table\">完整时间轴</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>周</th>\n      <th>事件</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week1anoffer00]{献给大狐女的贡品}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week2aslithe00]{滑行之灾}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{首长夜}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week4haunted00]{鬼发*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week5themiss00]{失踪的尸体}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week6theface00]{无脸的幽魂*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week7anicygr00]{冰冷的纠缠*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week8stablef00]{马场失火*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>9</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week9kimchis00]{飞天泡菜*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week10feasto00]{神灵庆宴}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>11</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week11thefac00]{床脚处的脸*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>12</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week12vanish00]{失踪事件*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"note\">*这是一起超自然事件；当其发生时，PC失去1点希望点。</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>魑魅魍魉</h1>\n  <p>当PC们为冬季做准备并照料茶馆时，村民间开始流传离奇的传闻，骇人的事件也会打断他们的日常劳作。随着周数推进，这些超自然事件愈发常见，逐渐取代更为寻常的每周事件。每当这些超自然事件发生一次，就将PC们已累积的希望点数量减少1点，因为这些令人不安的事件会侵蚀士气，并在镇上散播恐惧。</p>\n  <p>镇民将这些事件视作折磨城镇的诅咒正在增强的证据，而你不应劝阻PC们也这么认为。事实上，其中一些事件是现代世界中的尝试所导致的结果：由木材大亨@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21magokai0000000]{Mago Kai}主导，试图驱逐徘徊在现代柳岸镇的灵体。PC们将在下一幕发现这一真相（并与之对抗）。</p>\n</aside>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore Events\">Willowshore Events</h1>\n\n<p>As the days unfold and fall hurtles toward winter, weekly events occur in Willowshore that demand the party’s attention. These events play out in exploration mode and take less than a day to resolve. Playing out these events doesn’t impact the party’s ability to pursue any weekly downtime activities. It’s best to resolve a week’s downtime activities first before moving on to that week’s event. A timeline of when these events occur appears below, while details of the events themselves appear later in this chapter. If an event takes place during a week when the PCs are out of town, that event should occur a day after their return, with any other “backed-up” events taking place every other day until you catch back up to the weekly schedule—the one exception to this is First Long Night, which always takes place on week 3. If the PCs miss this event by being out of town that whole week, they’ll miss out on one of the best opportunities they have to earn Hope Points.</p>\n<h2 class=\"table\">Fall Timeline</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Week</th>\n      <th>Event</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week1anoffer00]{An Offering for Daikitsu}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week2aslithe00]{A Slithering Situation}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{First Long Night}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week4haunted00]{Haunted Hair*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week5themiss00]{The Missing Corpse}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week6theface00]{The Faceless Ghost*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week7anicygr00]{An Icy Grasp*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week8stablef00]{Stable Fire*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>9</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week9kimchis00]{Kimchi’s Ascent*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week10feasto00]{Feast of the Kami}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>11</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week11thefac00]{The Face at the Foot of the Bed*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>12</td>\n      <td>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week12vanish00]{Vanishings*}</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"note\">*This is a supernatural event, and when it occurs, the PCs lose 1 Hope Point.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Spirits and Hauntings</h1>\n  <p>As the PCs make their preparations for winter and tend to the teahouse, strange rumors begin to spread among the villagers and frightening events interrupt their daily chores. These supernatural events grow more common as the weeks go by, replacing the more mundane weekly events. Each time one of these supernatural events occurs, reduce the number of Hope Points the PCs have accumulated by 1, as these unsettling events erode morale and spread fear through town.</p>\n  <p>The townsfolk see these events as evidence that the curse afflicting the town is growing in power, and you shouldn’t dissuade the PCs from believing the same. In fact, some of these events are the results of attempts in the modern world, led by lumber baron @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21magokai0000000]{Mago Kai}, to exorcise the spirits that linger in modern Willowshore, a truth the PCs will discover (and fight back against) in the next act.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Researching the Curse": {
              "name": "研究诅咒 Researching the Curse",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Researching the Curse\">研究诅咒</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jubeiigawa.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Igawa Jubei\" alt=\"Igawa Jubei, human female bibliophile\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jubeiigawa.webp')\" />\n<p>在前一幕中，PC们探索了柳岸腹地，与超自然盟友建立了联系，并听到了“Kugaptee”这个名字。他们也亲身经历了如今封锁这片区域的诡异边界，以及在镇子西侧阴森逼近、更加令人不安的鬼打墙。这些发现带来了更多疑问而非答案；但随着秋季开始，PC们已掌握足够信息，可以开始认真研究困扰他们所有人的奇异诅咒的本质。</p>\n\n<p>\n  为了调查诅咒并确定可采取哪些步骤来解除它，或至少弄清如何解除它，PC们必须花费休整时间来调查这一主题，并使用\n  <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>第190–191页所详述的研究规则。通常而言，研究会在探索模式中进行结算，但对于这个更隐晦、也更难理解的主题，PC们必须用休整时间来寻求答案。尝试研究诅咒的PC需要花费1周休整时间（但由于这不具有准备特征，PC可以在进行任何带有准备的休整活动的同时进行研究）。\n</p>\n<p>柳岸镇有三项重要资源可供PC们用来研究诅咒（坟边居的游素锦、主母之绾的井川十兵卫，以及木灵大尊柳），或者如果他们擅长魔法学识，也可以独自研究。如果队伍在前一幕中找回了走道的笔记，也可以对其进行研究。你应确保玩家知晓下文详述的所有潜在研究途径，以便他们能选择自己角色最擅长的求知路线。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>柳岸镇的诅咒</span> <span>研究 4</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>游素锦</strong> 你花费这一周与游素锦交谈柳岸镇的历史，发现许多当地人早已遗忘之事；<strong>最大RP</strong> 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] 或 @Check[diplomacy|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>井川十兵卫</strong> 你花费这一周在主母之绾借助井川十兵卫的帮助调查该主题：与你交谈或翻检她收藏的书籍；<strong>最大RP</strong> 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[library-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] 或 @Check[arcana|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大尊柳</strong> 柳岸镇北方那株参天柳树的奇异灵能守卫在前一幕中帮助确定了诅咒的范围。你花费这一周多次往返大尊柳，通过向神灵请教来进一步洞察诅咒；<strong>最大RP</strong> 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[nature|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>独自调查</strong> 你花费这一周自行研究一般意义上的诅咒本质：要么使用你自己的典籍与参考资料收藏，要么使用镇上他人持有的图书馆；<strong>最大RP</strong> 4</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[sangpotshi-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] 或 @Check[occultism|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研读走道的笔记</strong> 如果你会读阿克洛语与冥渊语，你可以研读走道的笔记来了解这只无面鬼（noppera-bo）对鬼打墙的发现；若两名不同角色分别会其中一种语言，他们可以合作研读笔记，但他们之间每周只能进行一次检定（若井川十兵卫已被安排为愿意帮忙，她可以担任这两名角色之一）；<strong>最大RP</strong> 3</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[academia-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] 或 @Check[religion|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]（若两名角色合作，将这两个DC都提高2）</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>2点研究点数</strong> 诅咒在柳岸腹地北、南、东三侧的边界十分隐晦，若不直接跨越它们便很难与其产生互动；而在西侧，鬼打墙是一道可见的屏障，带有可辨识的灵性要素——因此，它很可能是一道更容易尝试移除的屏障。此外，谭杉寺的遗迹就在此墙不远处；如果仍能抵达该地点，其中的传承与藏书将对进一步了解诅咒本身极为宝贵。谭杉寺的修建始于7020年，也就是柳岸镇建立的同一年；但该寺于7062年被废弃，其大量传承也随之散佚或被遗忘。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4点研究点数</strong> 住在废弃伐木场的无面鬼崇拜某个名为“Kugaptee”的存在。它究竟是谁仍需更多研究，但PC们确实得知Kugaptee与一种罕见的怪物类别有关，这类怪物被称为nindorus——源自对转世循环之腐化的恶魔；这不仅是无面鬼感兴趣的话题，也是曾在谭杉寺崇拜修行的僧侣们所关注的主题。此时，PC们可以尝试对一般意义上的nindorus进行回忆知识（关于这一追寻的更多细节，见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo.JournalEntryPage.18nindorus000000]{Nindorus}）。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6点研究点数</strong> Kugaptee是一位强大的nindoru，数百年前在谭杉寺所在地被一位名为谭穗镜的英雄击败。古老传说称，谭穗镜也在那场战斗中死去，并转世为那株高耸的杉树——它曾是谭杉寺的核心焦点。关于Kugaptee的更多信息——包括诅咒可能与这位强大的nindoru有关的可能性——或许仍藏在废弃寺院的墙内？</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>8点研究点数</strong> 在谭杉寺被废弃之前，僧侣们每日举行仪式以确保杉树健康；但如今此地已成废墟，诅咒最可能的源头似乎是Kugaptee的影响渗入了这片区域——尤其考虑到寺院似乎隐藏在它自身的诅咒帷幕之中。若再花更多时间研究，并借鉴无面鬼在前一幕中试图运用的方法，PC们就能开发出一种专门仪式，或许可以让人穿越鬼打墙。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>10+点研究点数</strong> PC们成功研究出@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{洞开鬼打墙}仪式；从此刻起，他们可以随时使用该仪式尝试放倒鬼打墙（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08throughthewa00]{穿越鬼打墙}）。他们也明白：关于这道诅咒，在镇上他们已获知所有能学到的内容；更多信息必定在鬼打墙之外、谭杉寺遗迹之中。完成该研究后，给予PC们120 XP。</p>\n</section>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>获得研究方面的帮助</h2>\n  <p>PC们在研究诅咒时，可能就是缺少将研究点数推进到10+所需的技能或语言组合。如果这一点变得明显，那么他们可以求助于镇上的其他专家，例如游素锦、井川十兵卫、大尊柳，甚至是在他某次进城时的心藏，来最终完成工作并彻底研究出该仪式。PC们不会因这种解决方案获得XP，并且在秋季的最后一个月之前不应提供这一选项，这可能会让完成第2幕的时间线更加复杂。</p>\n</aside>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Researching the Curse\">Researching the Curse</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jubeiigawa.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Igawa Jubei\" alt=\"Igawa Jubei, human female bibliophile\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-jubeiigawa.webp')\" />\n<p>In the previous act, the PCs explored Willowshore’s hinterlands, made contacts with supernatural allies, and heard the name “Kugaptee.” They also had firsthand experience with the strange boundary that now contains the region and the more disturbing Wall of Ghosts that looms to the west of town. These discoveries posed more questions than answers, but as fall begins, the PCs have enough information to begin properly researching the nature of the strange curse that afflicts them all.</p>\n\n<p>\n  To investigate the curse and determine what steps can be taken to lift it, or at least learn how to lift it, the PCs must spend downtime investigating the topic, making use of the Research rules detailed on pages 190–191 of\n  <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>. Normally, Research resolves in exploration mode, but for this more obscure and hard to understand topic, the PCs must use downtime to seek answers. A PC who attempts to Research the curse takes a week of downtime (but as it doesn’t have the preparation trait, a PC can Research simultaneously to any preparation downtime activity they attempt).\n</p>\n<p>Willowshore has three important resources that the PCs can work with to research the curse (You So-Jin of Graveside Manners, Igawa Jubei of Mother’s Coil, and the kodama Great Willow), or they can go at it alone if they’re skilled in magical knowledge. Zoudou’s notes, if the party recovered them in the previous act, can also be researched. You should make sure the players are aware of all of the potential avenues of research detailed below so that they’ll be able to pick the route to knowledge that their characters are most skilled at.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>The Willowshore Curse</span> <span>Research 4</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>You So-Jin</strong> You spend the week talking with You So-Jin about Willowshore’s history and discover things that many locals have forgotten; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[diplomacy|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Igawa Jubei</strong> You spend the week investigating the topic with the aid of Igawa Jubei at Mother’s Coil, speaking with her or sifting through her collection of books; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[library-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[arcana|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Great Willow</strong> The strange spiritual guardian of the towering willow tree north of Willowshore helped to determine the extent of the curse in the previous act. You spend the week making several trips to and from Great Willow to gain further insight into the curse by consulting with the kami; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[nature|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Solo Investigations</strong> You spend the week researching the nature of curses in general on your own, either using your own collection of tomes and reference materials or libraries held by others in town; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 4</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[sangpotshi-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[occultism|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Studying Zoudou’s Notes</strong> If you can read Aklo and Chthonian, you can study Zoudou’s notes to learn what the noppera-bo discovered about the Wall of Ghosts; if two different characters each speak one of these languages, they can work together to study the notes, but only one check between them can be made per week (Igawa Jubei can serve as one of these two characters if she’s been made helpful); <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 3</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[academia-lore|dc:17|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[religion|dc:19|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] (if two characters work together, increase both of these DCs by 2)</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>2 Research Points</strong> The curse borders along the Willowshore hinterlands to the north, south, and east are subtle and hard to interact with without stepping directly through them, whereas to the west, the Wall of Ghosts is a visible barrier with recognizable spiritual elements—as such, it’s likely an easier barrier to attempt to remove. Further, the ruins of the Tan Sugi monastery lie not far beyond this wall, and if this site can still be reached, the lore and libraries found within will be invaluable in learning more about the curse itself. Construction on the Tan Sugi monastery began back in 7020, the same year Willowshore was founded, but the monastery was abandoned in 7062, and much of its lore was lost or forgotten.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4 Research Points</strong> The noppera-bo who dwelt in the abandoned lumber worshipped something named “Kugaptee.” Who this was requires more research, but the PCs do learn that Kugaptee was associated with a rare category of monsters known an nindorus—fiends that rise from corruptions to the cycle of reincarnation, which was not only a topic of interest to the noppera-bo, but among the monks who once worshipped at the Tan Sugi monastery. At this point, the PCs can attempt to Recall Knowledge about nindorus in general (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo.JournalEntryPage.18nindorus000000]{Nindorus} for more details on this pursuit).</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6 Research Points</strong> Kugaptee was a powerful nindoru defeated hundreds of years ago by a hero named Tan Sui-Jing at the site of the Tan Sugi monastery. The old legend says Tan Sui-Jing also perished in the battle and that she reincarnated into the towering sugi tree that served as the focal point of the Tan Sugi monastery. Perhaps more information about Kugaptee—including the possibility that the curse might be associated with the powerful nindoru—still resides within the abandoned monastery walls?</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>8 Research Points</strong> Before the Tan Sugi monastery was abandoned, the monks performed daily rituals to ensure the health of the sugi trees, but now that the place has fallen into ruin, the most likely source of the curse seems to be Kugaptee’s influence seeping out into the region—particularly given the fact that the monastery appears to be hidden inside a cursed shroud of its own. By spending a more time researching and drawing upon methods the noppera-bo were attempting to utilize in the previous act, the PCs could develop a specialized ritual that might allow passage through the Wall of Ghosts.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>10+ Research Points</strong> The PCs successfully research the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{Open the Wall of Ghosts} ritual and, at this point, can use the ritual to attempt to bring down the Wall of Ghosts at their leisure (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08throughthewa00]{Through the Wall of Ghosts}). They also now understand that they’ve learned everything about the curse that they can in town, and that more information surely lies beyond the Wall of Ghosts at the ruins of the Tan Sugi monastery. Grant the PCs 120 XP for completing this research.</p>\n</section>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Getting help with Research</h2>\n  <p>It’s possible that the PCs just won’t have the right mix of skills or languages to reach 10+ Research Points while researching the curse. If this becomes apparent, then they can turn to other experts in town, such as You So-Jin, Igawa Jubei, Great Willow, or even Shinzo on one of his trips to town to finally complete their work and fully research the ritual. The PCs earn no XP for this solution, and it shouldn’t be something that’s available until the last month of fall, potentially complicating the timeline for completing Act 2.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Increasing Security": {
              "name": "保障安全 Increasing Security",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Increasing Security\">保障安全</h1>\n<p>为让柳岸镇的建筑与道路为冬季做好准备，PC们需要累积安全点。若PC们曾帮助胡太婆成为柳岸镇的新领袖，她的援助与影响会让PC们起始拥有3点安全点；否则，他们从0点安全点开始。</p>\n<p>郑鹏是柳岸镇的卫队长，PC们很可能在上一幕中从他自己的牢房里把他救了出来。那段经历至今仍让郑鹏保持谦卑，因此他渴望着眼未来，而不是沉溺过去。凭借他对防御措施的了解以及他对柳岸镇民兵的影响力，镇中长者招募他来领导相关工作，帮助镇子与柳岸镇的人民为一个没有加固的冬天做准备。他建议PC们，为冬季做准备的最佳方式，是进行“援助镇民”和“加固建筑”这两项休整模式活动。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们在首次获得12点安全点时获得40 XP。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>援助镇民</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整模式</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花一周时间帮助柳岸镇的人民为冬季做准备。这可能包括体力劳动，例如劈柴以增加镇上的柴火储备，或协助清理枯死的树木与枝条以防止倒木。或者，你也可以通过提供娱乐，或帮助他们在辛苦劳作一天后放松身心，来维持镇上工人的士气。最后，你还能运用你对柳岸镇及其历史的了解，提醒人们以往的冬季里什么做法有效、什么做法无效。要援助镇民，尝试一次@Check[athletics|dc:17]、@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:19]或@Check[performance|dc:21]检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong>你确实大大提振了镇上的士气，居民觉得你的援助既鼓舞人心又乐于帮助。队伍获得2点安全点。你也可以改为获得1点安全点和1点希望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>你的协助让镇民完成了比他们自己能做到的更多事情。队伍获得1点安全点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>工作比预期更复杂、更困难也更累人。队伍不获得安全点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong>一次未预料的挫折或毁灭性的事故抵消了大量成果，并可能打击士气。队伍失去1点安全点。若这是本周在援助镇民时首次掷出大成功或大失败，队伍还会失去1点希望点。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>加固建筑</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整模式</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花一周时间出力协助修缮与加固建筑，为即将到来的冬季做准备。或者，你也可以运用你的制造技艺来协助指挥这些工作，或处理精细的修补与改良。最后，你还可以运用你的知识提出方案，以加固城镇的基础设施，或建议尚未尝试过的冬季准备方法。要加固建筑，尝试一次@Check[architecture-lore|dc:17]、@Check[engineering-lore|dc:17]、@Check[crafting|dc:19]或@Check[athletics|dc:21]检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong>工作进行得比你预期更顺利！队伍获得2点安全点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>工作按计划进行，没有任何事故或挫折。队伍获得1点安全点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>尽管建筑加固仍在继续，但工作揭露了底层且出乎意料的损坏，或其他未预见的修缮需求。队伍不获得安全点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong>一次危险的事故阻碍了进度，可能是屋顶坍塌、脚踝扭伤，或使用工具时犯下令人疼痛的错误。由于事故造成的损害，队伍失去1点安全点；且尝试该检定的角色必须进行一次@Check[fortitude|dc:20]豁免检定，以避免在1周内（或直到该状态被魔法治愈）陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{力竭 1}或@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{笨拙 1}；PC选择自己获得哪一种苦难。若强韧豁免为大成功或大失败，则PC同时获得两种状态。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Increasing Security\">Increasing Security</h1>\n<p>To prepare Willowshore’s buildings and roads for winter, the PCs accumulate Security Points. If the PCs helped Granny Hu to become Willowshore’s new leader, her aid and influence allows the PCs to start with 3 Security Points; otherwise, they begin with 0 Security Points.</p>\n<p>Zheng Peng is Willowshore’s captain of the town guard, a man the PCs likely rescued from his own jail in the previous act. That experience continues to be a source of humility for Zheng Peng, so he’s eager to focus on the future rather than dwell on the past. With his knowledge of defensive measures and his influence over Willowshore’s militia, the town elder has recruited him to lead the efforts at preparing the town and its people for a winter without reinforcement. He advises the PCs that the best way they can help prepare for winter is to pursue the Aid Townsfolk and Reinforce Buildings downtime activities.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> The PCs earn 40 XP upon earning 12 Security Points for the first time.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Aid Townsfolk</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week helping the people of Willowshore prepare for winter. This could entail physical labor, such as chopping wood to build up the town’s supply of firewood or helping to harvest dead trees or branches to prevent deadfalls. Alternatively, you could work to keep the town’s workers’ spirits up by providing entertainment or helping them to relax after a hard day’s work. Finally, you can draw upon your knowledge of Willowshore and its history to remind folks what has and hasn’t worked well in previous winters. To Aid Townsfolk, attempt a @Check[athletics|dc:17], @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:19], or @Check[performance|dc:21] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> You’ve really helped to bolster the town’s spirits, and the citizens find your aid to be as inspiring as it is helpful. The party gains 2 Security Points. You can choose instead to gain 1 Security Point and 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> Your assistance helps the townsfolk accomplish more than they could’ve on their own. The party gains 1 Security Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The work proves to be more complicated, difficult, and tiring than expected. The party gains no Security Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> An unforeseen setback or devastating accident undoes a lot of the work, potentially damaging morale. The party loses 1 Security Point. If this is the first time a critical failure was rolled for Aid Townsfolk this week, the party also loses 1 Hope Point.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Reinforce Buildings</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week lending your labors to the efforts to repair and reinforce buildings to prepare for the upcoming winter. Alternatively, you could lend your skill at crafting to help direct those efforts or to handle delicate repairs or improvements. Finally, you could use your knowledge to come up with solutions to bolster the town’s infrastructure or to suggest unexplored methods of winter preparation. To Reinforce Buildings, attempt a @Check[architecture-lore|dc:17], @Check[engineering-lore|dc:17], @Check[crafting|dc:19], or @Check[athletics|dc:21] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The work went better than you expected! The party gains 2 Security Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> Work proceeds on schedule without any accidents or setbacks. The party gains 1 Security Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> While reinforcements on the buildings continue, the work has revealed underlying and unexpected damage or other unanticipated repair needs. The party gains no Security Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> A dangerous accident hinders progress, be it a collapsing roof, a twisted ankle, or a painful mistake made while using a tool. The party loses 1 Security Point from the damage caused by the accident, and the character who attempted this check must now attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:20] saving throw to avoid becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 1} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{Clumsy 1} for 1 week (or until the condition is healed magically); the PC chooses which affliction they gain. If the Fortitude save is a critical failure, the PC gains both conditions.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Gathering Food": {
              "name": "筹措食粮 Gathering Food",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Gathering Food\">筹措食粮</h1>\n\n<p>为了让柳岸镇的食物储备能撑过冬季，PC们需要累积食物点。如果PC们曾协助老松木成为柳岸镇的新领导者，他的帮助与影响能让PC们以3点食物点起步；否则他们从0点食物点开始。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-nadoya.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nadoya Sanmi\" alt=\"Nadoya Sanmi, female\thuman family matriarch\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-nadoya.webp')\" />\n<p>三美奈户弥在柳岸镇镇区经营树雀居，这地方有点像杂货铺，专营干货、腌渍食品与酒类。由于三美对食物保存有着丰富的知识，镇上的长者征召她来协助组织全镇的储粮工作。她建议PC们，为冬季筹措食物的最佳方式是进行协助收割与协助捕猎这两项休整模式行动。至于这些食物最终存放在何处、由谁负责确保安全、以及冬天来到柳岸镇后如何分配给居民——这些都不是PC们需要操心的事。</p>\n<p>某些超自然能力与法术可以帮助人们填饱肚子，但除非这些能力能制造可长期保存的食物，否则即便能使用这些选项，对准备即将到来的冬季也帮助不大（尽管它们在食物短缺的紧急状况下可能派得上用场——见第3幕 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10weeklyattrit00]{这里}）。由GM自行裁量：若某位PC能使用一种能力，能在规模上提供更持久的食物，而不只是影响自己或队伍（例如能使用木卫哨兵激涌的动能使），则他们可以用该能力尝试协助收割或协助捕猎（以较合适者为准），并以进行一次 @Check[nature|dc:19] 检定来取代标准的 @Check[nature|dc:21] 检定选项。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们在第一次获得12点食物点时获得40 XP。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>准备食物</h2>\n  <p>在柳岸镇与天夏的大部分地区，食谱并非依照精确单位量测的科学，而是一种每个家庭与个人各自独有的传统。父母会用“一撮”“一把”或炊具上那些晦涩的刻线来描述菜肴用量。因此，即便经验丰富的村民会给年轻人提供技巧与建议，他们也总会被鼓励“顺着家的味道走”，以目测与品尝来调整原料。像腌渍或保存食物这类密集的食物准备工作，往往是一种社交活动，能让时间过得更快，也让劳作显得没那么辛苦。做好的菜肴会被封存在大而厚重的陶罐中，埋入地下，直到冬天食用时再取出。泡菜、味噌、洋葱与萝卜，都是常见的以这种方式准备的食物。</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>协助收割</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整模式</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">移动</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花这一周帮助农民收割谷物、稻米、水果与蔬菜；你可以下田劳作、提供后勤方面的专业知识，或分享你对自然世界的见解。若PC们在前一幕成功将柳岸镇北方的旧村扩建地 확보为临时补种作物的补充地点，则所有用于协助收割的检定获得+1环境加值，且在任意一周内，第一次进行协助收割的掷骰其成功等级提高一级。要协助收割，尝试一次 @Check[farming-lore|dc:17]、@Check[athletics|dc:19] 或 @Check[nature|dc:21] 检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong>不仅本周收成极为丰硕，而且从附近荒野进行的额外采集又带回更多食物。队伍获得2点食物点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>作物收割顺利，并收集到相当数量的盈余。队伍获得1点食物点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>产量平平；足以在短期内帮助人们果腹，但不足以留下任何储备。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong>灾害！作物遭虫害侵袭、霉菌滋生，或干脆腐坏变质。队伍失去1点食物点。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>协助捕猎</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整模式</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">移动</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花这一周协助猎人和渔夫追踪猎物、检查陷阱并捕鱼；你可以运用野外求生技能、提供专家建议，或单纯借助你对自然世界的知识。尝试一次 @Check[fishing-lore|dc:17]、@Check[hunting-lore|dc:17]、@Check[survival|dc:19] 或 @Check[nature|dc:21] 检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong>你在不对该地区造成过度捕猎的情况下，收集到数量可观的食物。队伍获得2点食物点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>你捕获并收存了相当数量的猎物与鱼类，但该地区的富饶变得稀缺；本周剩余时间内无人能再进行协助捕猎。队伍获得1点食物点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>你只找到少量动物并捕到少量鱼；足以补充本周食物，但不足以充实城镇储备。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong>你的狩猎与捕鱼尝试以灾害告终：管理不善的狩猎与过度捕鱼让生态系统不堪重负——更糟的是，先前收集的一些鱼类与猎物被发现感染或腐坏，必须销毁。本周剩余时间内无人能再进行协助捕猎。队伍失去1点食物点。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Gathering Food\">Gathering Food</h1>\n\n<p>To prepare Willowshore’s food stores for winter, the PCs accumulate Food Points. If the PCs helped Old Matsuki to become Willowshore’s new leader, his aid and influence allows the PCs to start with 3 Food Points; otherwise, they begin with 0 Food Points.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-nadoya.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nadoya Sanmi\" alt=\"Nadoya Sanmi, female\thuman family matriarch\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-nadoya.webp')\" />\n<p>Nadoya Sanmi runs Treesparrow’s Rest in downtown Willowshore, a sort of grocery store that specializes in dry goods, preserved food, and alcohol. Due to Nadoya’s extensive knowledge of food preservation, the town elder has recruited her to aid in organizing the town’s food storage efforts. She advises the PCs that the best way they can help to gather food for winter is to pursue the Aid Harvest and Aid Hunt downtime activities. Where this food ends up being stored, who’s in charge of keeping it secure, and how it gets distributed to the populace once winter comes to Willowshore aren’t things the PCs need to concern themselves with.</p>\n<p>Certain supernatural abilities and spells can help to feed people, but unless those abilities create lasting food, access to these options doesn’t do much to help prepare for the coming winter (although they might aid in the case of a food shortage emergency—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10weeklyattrit00]{Here} in Act 3). At your discretion, if a PC has access to an ability that could provide for longer lasting food at a scale beyond simply affecting themselves or the party (such as a kineticist with access to the timber sentinel impulse), they can use this ability to attempt to Aid Harvest or Aid Hunt (whichever activity seems most appropriate) by attempting a @Check[nature|dc:19] check instead of the standard @Check[nature|dc:21] check option.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> The PCs earn 40 XP upon earning 12 Food Points for the first time.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Preparing Food</h2>\n  <p>In Willowshore and much of Tian Xia, recipes aren’t an exact science with unit measurements, but rather a tradition unique to each family and individual. Parents describe measurements for their dishes in pinches, handfuls, and obscure lines on the earthenware used to cook their meals. So while experienced villagers might offer tips and advice to the younger ones, they’re always encouraged to “follow the flavor of home” and adjust ingredients by eye and taste. Intensive food preparation, like pickling or preserving food, is often a social affair that makes the time pass more quickly and the work seem less arduous. The prepared dishes are preserved in large, hefty clay pots and buried in the ground until they’re ready for consumption during the winter. Kimchi, miso, onions, and radishes are some of the more common foods prepared in this way.</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Aid Harvest</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Move</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week helping farmers to harvest grain, rice, fruits, and vegetables, either by working in the fields, providing logistical expertise, or offering insights from your knowledge of the natural world. If the PCs successfully secured the old village expansion north of Willowshore as a supplementary site for last-minute crops in the previous act, then all checks to Aid Harvest gain a +1 circumstance bonus, and the first roll in any given week to Aid Harvest is improved by one degree of success. To Aid Harvest, attempt a @Check[farming-lore|dc:17], @Check[athletics|dc:19], or @Check[nature|dc:21] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> Not only is this week’s harvest wildly successful, but supplemental foraging from the nearby wilds brought in even more food. The party gains 2 Food Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The crop harvest is a success, with a fair amount of surplus gathered. The party gains 1 Food Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The crop yield is unimpressive; it’s enough to help feed folks in the short term, but not enough to set aside anything for stores.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Disaster! The crop was infested with pests, riddled with fungus, or simply became spoiled. The party loses 1 Food Point.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Aid Hunt</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Move</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week helping hunters and fishers to stalk game, check traps, and catch fish, either by using your skill at woodland survival, providing expert advice, or simply by lending your knowledge of the natural world. Attempt a @Check[fishing-lore|dc:17], @Check[hunting-lore|dc:17], @Check[survival|dc:19], or @Check[nature|dc:21] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> You gather an impressive amount of food while not overhunting the area. The party gains 2 Food Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> You catch and secure a fair amount of game and fish, but the area’s bounty becomes scarce; no one can Aid Hunt for the rest of the week. The party gains 1 Food Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> You find only a few animals and catch a few fish; it’s enough to supplement food for the week, but not enough to build up the town stores.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Your attempt to hunt and fish ends in disaster, with poorly managed hunts and overfishing overtaxing the ecosystem—and even worse, some of the fish and game previously gathered is revealed to be infected or spoiled and must be destroyed. No one can Aid Hunt for the rest of the week. The party loses 1 Food Point.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Restoring the Teahouse": {
              "name": "重开茶馆 Restoring the Teahouse",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Restoring the Teahouse\">重开茶馆</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>茶具</h1>\n  <p>一旦青天茶馆被修缮重建并复原，若PC们想真正举办茶会或主持活动，就必须设法弄到茶具，因为建筑里仅存的物资都已破败不堪。茶具可在镇上购买，等同于一套@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.y34yjumCFakrbtdw]{工匠工具组}（4 gp），或从莱西的沙龙购买@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.0QgniSjpzksm5riV]{纯银工匠工具组}（50 gp）。在本情境下，纯银工匠工具组提供的物品加值适用于所有主持茶事与制作魔茶的检定。当然，有才能的PC也可以选择自己制作茶具！</p>\n</aside>\n<p>本幕假定PC们已经取得了青天茶馆的控制权——如果他们尚未做到，考虑让镇上长者将该地点的所有权作为他们在上一幕行动的奖励之一授予队伍。</p>\n<p>青天茶馆依然矗立，但在夏初那些日子里，它成为一头享乐主义怪物的私人领地之前，就已因数月疏于照料而破败不堪。如今，这里需要修理、翻新与更新，才能再次向公众敞开大门。茶馆的招牌饱经风霜，几乎难以辨认；下雨时，雨水会从门缝、墙洞与屋顶的破口渗入；夜晚还有冰冷的穿堂风沁入骨髓。</p>\n<p>尽管如此，建筑的主体结构仍然稳固；一旦修好，茶馆除了能让PC们作为行动据点使用，也能让这家深受本地喜爱的生意重获新生。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>小暗</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yami.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yami\" alt=\"female bakeneko\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yami.webp')\" />\n  <p>当PC们继承这家茶馆时，他们也一并继承了小暗——一只灰色、半野性的家猫。它曾与茶馆的前任主人一同生活，但在夏季期间躲了起来。茶馆的前任主人庆麦莱在穿过村子时发现了这只猫：当时它还是幼崽，蜷缩在一处篝火余烬渐冷的灰堆里。她以为这猫是黑色的，便给它取名“小暗”，但在认真清洗后才发现，它其实是浅灰色，背上有一道黑色条纹，肚皮的毛更浅。名字就这么沿用下来，而这只猫也成了麦莱最忠诚的伙伴之一：它在阴影中守望茶馆，偶尔也会蜷在客人的腿上取暖。在本幕中，PC们第一次于此地造访时，其中一位PC应当注意到小暗回到了茶馆——他们可以用一次成功的@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定进行回忆知识，以认出这只猫（若没有任何PC这么做，那么茶馆迎来的第一位访客肯定会认出来）。</p>\n  <p>PC们与其他村民都不知道的是，小暗远不止表面看起来那样。事实上，她是一只化猫——当一只猫活得异常长久时便会被唤醒的魔法生物。在将柳岸镇拖入其思维空间的事件发生之前，小暗就已开始向化猫转变。随着思维空间里年份的重复轮回，她在保持同样小猫外形的同时变得愈发强大；但她对村民的敬慕之情依旧不变（无论每一年的循环里事件如何发展，村民们总是善待她）。小暗和村民一样，不会记得前几次循环发生的事，但她能察觉到：以她的年龄与阅历而言，她强得不合常理——而这种感觉会随着一年年过去而愈发强烈。</p>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span>@UUID[Actor.lSXJXrlkiYcsYvDP]{小暗}</span><span>生物 3</span></h2>\n  </section>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">小型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">野兽</li>\n  </ul>\n</aside>\n\n<p>以下休整活动可用于复原青天茶馆。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>修缮重建</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花一周时间清扫、修理并复原青天茶馆。尝试一次@Check[crafting|dc:19]、@Check[architecture-lore|dc:21]或@Check[labor-lore|dc:21]，或@Check[athletics|dc:24]检定。若你额外花费10 gp用于资源协助，则将该次检定结果提高一个成功等级。一旦PC们累计获得5点复原点数，青天茶馆即完全复原，他们不能再进行此活动；他们获得80 XP，并在两个阵营中各获得1点声望点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 你取得极佳进展，PC们获得2点复原点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 你取得正常进展，PC们获得1点复原点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 你未能取得任何进展。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 挫折！你不慎损坏了建筑，PC们失去1点复原点数。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>交好小暗</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">小暗这只“本地猫”在整个夏天躲进野外后回到茶馆。起初她对PC们很警惕，一开始不允许任何人靠近。一位PC可以尝试一次@Check[nature|dc:14]检定来交好小暗。一旦有PC在交好小暗上取得大成功，此准备活动便不能再尝试。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 小暗喜欢上了整个队伍，尤其偏爱掷出该大成功的PC。不能再进行交好小暗的掷骰。每周结束时，小暗特别喜欢的那位PC应尝试一次@Check[flat|dc:11]；成功则小暗会为该PC带来一份礼物（在下方“小暗的礼物”表中掷骰）。PC们获得80 XP与1点希望点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 小暗开始喜欢这支队伍，允许人们抚摸或抱起她，但她仍会偶尔无缘无故显得疏离。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 小暗依然警惕，但没有被吓跑。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 小暗嘶嘶作响并逃回野外好几天；在本周剩余时间以及下周，你都不能尝试交好小暗。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"table\">小暗的礼物</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>掷骰</th>\n      <th>礼物</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>一个土豆（@UUID[Actor.4lP5by9s4h2L0geP]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>某人的内衣（@UUID[Actor.lMqn0CvzlgQKT6s4]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>1枚金币（@UUID[Actor.gdzqXG6DidGafIMS]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>一张写有关于该PC俳句的羊皮纸（每次得到此礼物时俳句都不同，且每一首都由小暗私下写成）（@UUID[Actor.2ktgLXCrx5teMUVQ]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>一个<em>翡翠猫护符</em>*（@UUID[Actor.x7GuKRaIDbqgoktS]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>一条<em>次级军械护腕</em>*（@UUID[Actor.A9Jl1FRa2EWvxe4q]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>一把镶嵌祖母绿的银匕首（价值100 gp）*（@UUID[Actor.wsO97tAcBzocwe2F]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>一根<em>粉碎跳跃魔杖</em>*（@UUID[Actor.R3g8PilMWws1Jl6p]{小暗的礼物}）</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"note\">此礼物只能掷出一次；之后若再次掷出该结果，改为1枚铂金币。</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>主持茶事</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">准备</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>需求</strong> 青天茶馆已完全修缮，且你拥有一套可用的茶具。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花一周时间准备为付费顾客主持一次茶道，并在工作周的最后一天为出席者执行茶道，为他们提供茶水、清淡点心与妙趣横生的交谈。花费10 gp用于物资。若你改为花费100 gp用于物资，则将一次失败视为成功。尝试一次@Check[performance|dc:19]检定或@Check[society|dc:21]检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 茶道大获成功！你赚到了一些钱，获得15 gp。队伍获得2点希望点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 茶道成功！队伍获得1点希望点数。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 茶道令人失望。若本周有其他PC尝试主持茶事，该次尝试承受–1环境减值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 茶道一塌糊涂。本周无人能再次主持茶事，且下周任何主持茶事的尝试在检定上承受–1环境减值。队伍失去1点希望点数。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Restoring the Teahouse\">Restoring the Teahouse</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Tea Ware</h1>\n  <p>Once the Cerulean Teahouse is rebuilt and restored, the PCs must secure tea ware if they wish to actually perform tea parties or host events, as what supplies remain in the building are in ruins. Tea ware can be purchased in town as an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.y34yjumCFakrbtdw]{Artisan's Toolkit} (4 gp) or as a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.0QgniSjpzksm5riV]{Sterling Artisan's Toolkit} (50 gp) from Leshy’s Salon. The item bonus granted from a sterling artisan’s toolkit in this case applies to all checks to Host Ceremony and to Craft magic tea. Talented PCs might elect to Craft their own tea ware, of course!</p>\n</aside>\n<p>This act assumes that the PCs have secured control of the Cerulean Teahouse—if they haven’t yet, consider having the town elder award the party ownership of the location as part of a reward for their actions in the previous act.</p>\n<p>The Cerulean Teahouse still stands, but it was in rough shape after months of neglect even before it became the personal domain of a hedonistic monster during the first days of summer. Today, the place is in need of repair, refurbishing, and renewal before it can once again open its doors to the general public. The teahouse’s sign has weathered and is barely visible, water leaks in through the doors and holes in the walls and roof when it rains, and a cold draft chills the bones in the evenings.</p>\n<p>Still, the building’s core is sound, and once repaired, the teahouse can serve well as a base of operations for the PCs in addition to bringing back a beloved local business.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Yami</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yami.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yami\" alt=\"female bakeneko\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yami.webp')\" />\n  <p>When the PCs inherit the tea shop, they also inherit Yami, a gray feral house cat who lived alongside the previous owner of the tea shop but went into hiding during the summer. The teahouse’s previous owner, Qing Mai-Lai, found the cat as a kitten, curled up in the cooling embers of a campfire while she was walking through the village. Thinking the cat was black, she named it Yami, but upon giving it a proper cleaning, the cat turned out to be light gray with a black strip on her back and lighter fur on her belly. The name Yami stuck, and the cat became one of Mai-Lai’s most loyal companions, watching over the teahouse from the shadows while occasionally warming the laps of guests. Yami’s return to the teahouse should be noted by one of the PCs the first time they visit the location during this act—which they can do with a successful @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge to recognize the cat (and if no PC does so, their first visitor to the teahouse certainly will).</p>\n  <p>Unbeknownst to the PCs and the other villagers, Yami is more than she appears. In truth, she’s a bakeneko—a magical creature awakened when a cat lives an unusually long life. Before the events that thrust Willowshore into its mindscape, Yami had already started her transition into a bakeneko. With the mindscape’s repeating years, she has only grown stronger while retaining the same small cat form, yet she retains her feelings of admiration for the villagers (who have always treated her kindly no matter how differently events have played out each yearly cycle). Yami, like the villagers, doesn’t recall the events of previous cycles, but she does recognize she’s much more powerful than she should be given her age and experience—a feeling that grows stronger with each passing year.</p>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span>@UUID[Actor.lSXJXrlkiYcsYvDP]{Yami}</span><span>Creature 3</span></h2>\n  </section>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Small</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Beast</li>\n  </ul>\n</aside>\n\n<p>The following downtime activities can be pursued to restore the Cerulean Teahouse.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Repair and Restore</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week cleaning, repairing, and restoring the Cerulean Teahouse. Attempt a @Check[crafting|dc:19], @Check[architecture-lore|dc:21] or @Check[labor-lore|dc:21], or @Check[athletics|dc:24] check. If you expend 10 gp on resources to help, increase the result of your check by one degree of success. Once the PCs earn a total of 5 Restoration Points, the Cerulean Teahouse is fully restored and they can no longer pursue this activity; they earn 80 XP and 1 Reputation Point with both factions.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> You make excellent progress, and the PCs gain 2 Restoration Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> You make normal progress, and the PCs gain 1 Restoration Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> You fail to make any progress.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Setback! You’ve accidentally damaged the building, and the PCs lose 1 Restoration Point.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Befriend Yami</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">Yami, the “local cat” who returns to the teahouse after hiding in the wild all summer, is initially wary of the PCs and doesn’t allow anyone to approach at first. A PC can attempt a @Check[nature|dc:14] check to befriend Yami. Once a PC achieves a Critical Success at Befriending Yami, this preparation activity can no longer be attempted.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> Yami takes a liking to the entire party, but particularly to the PC who rolled this critical success. No further rolls can be attempted to Befriend Yami. At the end of each week, the PC who Yami particularly likes should attempt a @Check[flat|dc:11]; on a success, Yami brings that PC a gift (roll on the “Yami’s Gifts” table below). The PCs earn 80 XP and 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> Yami takes a liking to the party and allows people to pet her and hold her, but she remains randomly standoffish.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> Yami remains wary but isn’t chased off.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Yami hisses and runs into the wild for several days; you can’t attempt to Befriend Yami for the rest of this week or the next week.</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"table\">Yami's Gifts</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Roll</th>\n      <th>Gift</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>A potato (@UUID[Actor.4lP5by9s4h2L0geP]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>Someone’s undergarments (@UUID[Actor.lMqn0CvzlgQKT6s4]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>1 gold piece (@UUID[Actor.gdzqXG6DidGafIMS]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>Piece of parchment with a haiku written about the PC (this haiku changes each time this gift is given, and each is written by Yami in secret) (@UUID[Actor.2ktgLXCrx5teMUVQ]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>A <em>jade cat talisman</em>*(@UUID[Actor.x7GuKRaIDbqgoktS]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>A <em>minor armory bracelet</em>* (@UUID[Actor.A9Jl1FRa2EWvxe4q]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>Silver dagger with an inlaid emerald (worth 100 gp)*(@UUID[Actor.wsO97tAcBzocwe2F]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>A <em>wand of crushing leaps</em>* (@UUID[Actor.R3g8PilMWws1Jl6p]{Yami's Gift})</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"note\">This gift can only be rolled once; treat further rolls of this gift as 1 platinum piece.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Host Ceremony</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Preparation</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requirements</strong> The Cerulean Teahouse is fully repaired, and you have a functional set of tea ware.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the week preparing to host a tea ceremony for paying customers, then perform the ceremony for attendees on the last day of the workweek, providing them with tea, light snacks, and scintillating conversation. Spend 10 gp on supplies. If, instead, you spend 100 gp on supplies, treat a failure as a success. Attempt a @Check[performance|dc:19] check or a @Check[society|dc:21] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The ceremony is an overwhelming success! You make a bit of money and earn 15 gp. The party gains 2 Hope Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The tea ceremony is a success! The party gains 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The tea ceremony was disappointing. If another PC attempts to Host a Ceremony this week, that attempt suffers a –1 circumstance penalty.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The ceremony was a disaster. No one can Host a Ceremony again this week, and any attempt to Host a Ceremony next week suffers a –1 circumstance penalty to the check. The party loses 1 Hope Point.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Bolstering Hope": {
              "name": "振奋希望 Bolstering Hope",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Bolstering Hope\">鼓舞希望</h1>\n<p>为了鼓舞小镇的希望，PC们会累积希望点。PC们最常见的获得方式是在城镇事件期间，但他们也可以通过将青天茶馆修复至可正常运作的状态来进一步提升希望。不同于其他准备点数值，PC们在本幕开始时便已累积了3点希望点，这是他们在上一幕中的行动所带来的结果。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们在首次获得12点希望点时获得40 XP。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Bolstering Hope\">Bolstering Hope</h1>\n<p>To bolster the town’s hope, the PCs accumulate Hope Points. The most common way the PCs will be able to do so is during the town events, but they can further build up hope by restoring the Cerulean Teahouse to working order. Unlike other Preparation Point values, the PCs begin this act with 3 Hope Points already accumulated as a result of their actions in the previous act.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> The PCs earn 40 XP upon earning 12 Hope Points for the first time.</p>"
            },
            "Preparing for Winter": {
              "name": "准备迎冬 Preparing for Winter",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparing for Winter\">准备迎冬</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>引用柳岸镇声望</h1>\n  <p>关于与柳岸镇的两个政治派系——南岸与北岭人——建立声望的规则，见前一幕以及《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》第200页。本幕开始时，PC很可能至少已受柳岸镇某个派系敬佩；在本幕中，他们还应有额外机会赚取足够多的声望点数，以在本幕结束前成为某个派系所尊崇之人。声望，以及PC累计的任何准备点数，最终将帮助判定《<em>鬼季</em>》第三幕中柳岸镇的人民将如何度过难关。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>为了准备迎冬，PC必须努力积累三类不同的胜利点数（《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》184页），在本冒险中称为准备点数，并进一步细分：希望点数代表镇民的态度与士气；食物点数记录柳岸镇的食物储备；安全点数记录城镇的基础设施与用于熬过冬天的物资。PC在本幕中为这些类别所积累的点数，将决定柳岸镇如何挺过下一幕即将到来的可怖事件。同时，PC也可以在试图了解他们所身处局势的过程中研究笼罩城镇的诅咒。</p>\n\n<p>PC获取这三种胜利点数的所有方式，都会以带有准备特征的特殊休整活动来呈现。</p>\n<p>本幕的休整以周为单位衡量；每周最多可有四名PC各尝试一次准备休整活动。若你的队伍多于四名PC，额外的PC可以协助其他PC的准备。PC若愿意，也可以每周再进行一次额外的非准备休整活动，可从制造、赚取收入或重训等标准休整活动中选择，也可以尝试进行研究检定以研究诅咒。</p>\n<p>PC何时能够开始 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{第6章} 取决于他们在调查诅咒时积累的研究点数（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07researchingt00]{此处}）；但一旦他们决定开始第6章，在他们为追求本幕第二与第三章目标而花费的任何一周（无论整周或部分周）里，都无法进行休整活动。由于大多数队伍不应需要超过一到两周就能在探索模式与遭遇模式下完成这些章节，他们应当有充足时间来积累准备点数。</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>准备奖励</h1>\n  <p>PC首次在准备点数的三种类别中各自达到12点时，队伍获得40 XP；若三类都至少达到12点，则共计获得120 XP。此外，每当PC在这三类之一达到12点时，他们获得1点声望点数，可分配给任意一个他们选择的派系。</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">点数追踪影响</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Item.RLbK3MpjS4T3GIAZ]{希望点数} @UUID[Item.NpYuhkiadwwrgvQd]{食物点数} @UUID[Item.7MiVl5eleJ4t54cv]{安全点数}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>将这些添加到 @UUID[Actor.sOoLKv6nUesBfTyK]{点数追踪} actor 上，以记录准备点数。</p>\n</section>\n<p>当PC准备迎冬时，他们还将面对每周事件，并需要参与其中——详见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07willowshoree00]{柳岸镇事件}。尤其要让玩家知道：首长夜将在第三周末举行。关于该节庆的完整细节见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{首长夜}。在本幕第三周，为首长夜所做的准备会为PC提供一种额外获得希望点数的方式。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>追踪准备点数</h2>\n  <p>用一种直观的方式记录PC在本章中积累的点数，让玩家始终能看到他们进度的视觉提醒。一旦你开始《<em>鬼季</em>》第三幕，随着冬季周数推进，这三类点数都会被“花费”。</p>\n  <p><strong>希望点数：</strong>队伍在本幕开始时拥有3点希望点数。在准备点数的三类之中，希望点数最有可能在游戏过程中被周期性降低。告知玩家：只要希望点数为正值，镇民就会富有成效且士气高昂。希望点数越高越好，但PC无需知道一个明确的目标数值。若某一周开始时希望点数为负值，由于镇民的协助与合作减少，所有用于获得准备点数的技能检定承受–1环境减值。PC可通过完成每周城镇事件、重开茶馆（见本页 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00]{重开茶馆}），或参与首长夜的任何庆典与活动（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{第3周 - 首长夜}）来获得希望点数。</p>\n  <p><strong>食物点数：</strong>若老松木担任柳岸镇镇长，他的远见会让城镇在此方面占得先机，队伍以3点食物点数开始——否则队伍以0点食物点数开始。收获季此刻才刚开始，柳岸镇大多数市民尚未开始储存食物。告知玩家：若PC能在秋末前确保至少12点食物点数，柳岸镇将达到熬过冬天所需的最低食物储备量——但获得超过12点的食物点数无疑能帮助应对意外事件，并为城镇提供对抗潜在饥荒的宝贵缓冲。PC可以通过每周休整活动来提升食物点数（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07gatheringfoo00]{筹措食粮}）。</p>\n  <p><strong>安全点数：</strong>若胡婆婆担任柳岸镇的领袖，她已经让手下探员着手加固城镇防务，队伍以3点安全点数开始——否则队伍以0点安全点数开始。在柳岸镇准备迎冬包括修补屋顶、为墙体与建筑做防风雨处理、训练如何应对火灾与洪水演练等紧急情况，以及其他市政准备。告知玩家：若PC能在秋末前获得至少12点安全点数，柳岸镇将能应付一个一般的冬天——但额外点数将有助于处理突发紧急状况。PC可通过每周休整活动来提升安全点数（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07increasingse00]{保障安全}）。</p>\n</aside>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparing for Winter\">Preparing for Winter</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Willowshore Reputation</h1>\n  <p>Rules for building up reputation with the two political factions in Willowshore known as Southbank and Northridge appear in the previous act as well as on page 200 of <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>. It’s likely that the PCs are at least admired by one of Willowshore’s factions when this act begins, and they should have additional opportunities during this act to earn enough additional Reputation Points to become revered by one of the factions by this act’s conclusion. Reputation, along with any Preparation Points the PCs accumulate will ultimately help determine how the people of Willowshore fare in the third act of <em>Season of Ghosts</em>.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>In order to prepare for winter, the PCs must work to accumulate three different categories of Victory Points (<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 184), referred to in this adventure as Preparation Points that are further subcategorized: Hope Points represent the townsfolk’s attitude and morale, Food Points track Willowshore’s food stores, and Security Points track the town’s infrastructure and supplies for enduring the winter. The amount of points the PCs accumulate during this act for these categories will determine how Willowshore endures the dreadful events to come in the next act. At the same time, the PCs can research the curse afflicting the town as they work to learn more about the situation they all find themselves in.</p>\n\n<p>All of the methods by which the PCs can accumulate these three kinds of Victory Points play out as special downtime activities that have the preparation trait.</p>\n<p>Downtime in this act is measured in weeks, with up to four individual PCs being able to attempt one preparation downtime activity each week. If your group has more than four PCs, the additional PCs can Aid other PCs’ preparations. A PC can also pursue one additional non-preparation downtime activity each week if they wish, choosing from standard downtime activities like Craft, Earn Income, or Retraining as well as attempting Research checks to research the curse.</p>\n<p>The point at which the PCs can begin @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{Chapter 6} is determined by their accumulation of Research Points while investigating the curse (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07researchingt00]{Here}), but once they decide to begin Chapter 6, they won’t be able to pursue downtime activities during any week—partial or full—they spend in pursuit of this act’s second and third chapter goals. Since most parties shouldn’t need more than one or two weeks to play out those chapters in exploration and encounter mode, they should have plenty of time to build up Preparation Points.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Preparation Awards</h1>\n  <p>The first time the PCs reach 12 points in each of the three categories of Preparation Points, the party earns 40 XP, for a total of 120 XP if they earn at least 12 points in all three categories. In addition, each time the PCs reach 12 points in one of these three categories, they gain 1 Reputation Point to the faction of their choice.</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Point Tracking Effects</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Item.RLbK3MpjS4T3GIAZ]{Hope Points} @UUID[Item.NpYuhkiadwwrgvQd]{Food Points} @UUID[Item.7MiVl5eleJ4t54cv]{Security Points}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Add these to the @UUID[Actor.sOoLKv6nUesBfTyK]{Point Tracking} actor to keep track of Preparation Points.</p>\n</section>\n<p>As the PCs prepare for winter, they’ll also face weekly events that they’ll need to take part in—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07willowshoree00]{Willowshore Events} for more details. In particular, let the players know that First Long Night will take place at the end of week three. Full details on this festival are covered in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{First Long Night}. During week three of this act, preparations for First Long Night give the PCs an additional way to earn Hope Points.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Tracking Preparation Points</h2>\n  <p>Keep track of the points the PCs accumulate during this chapter in a visual way so that the players have a constant visual reminder of their progress. Once you begin the third act of <em>Season of Ghosts</em>, all three of these categories of points are “spent” as winter’s weeks proceed.</p>\n  <p><strong>Hope Points:</strong> The party starts this act with 3 Hope Points. Of the three categories of Preparation Points, Hope Points are the most likely value to be periodically reduced during play. Inform the players that as long as they have a positive value for Hope Points, the townsfolk are productive and morale is high. The higher the value they can build, the better, but there isn’t a specific number the PCs should know to aim for. If a week begins with negative Hope Points, all skill checks to earn Preparation Points take a –1 circumstance penalty as aid and cooperation from townsfolk diminishes. The PCs can earn Hope Points by completing weekly town events, by building up their teahouse (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00]{Restoring the Teahouse} on this page), or by taking part in any of the First Long Night festivities and events (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{Week 3 - First Long Night}).</p>\n  <p><strong>Food Points:</strong> If Old Matsuki serves as mayor of Willowshore, his foresight gives the town a leg up here, and the party starts with 3 Food Points—otherwise, the party starts with 0 Food Points. The harvest season is only now beginning, and most of Willowshore’s citizens haven’t yet started to store food. Let the players know that if the PCs can secure at least 12 Food Points by the end of fall, Willowshore will reach the minimum amount of food stores needed to endure the winter—but earning more than 12 points will certainly help against unforeseen events and give the town a valuable cushion against potential starvation. The PCs can build up Food Points by pursuing weekly downtime activities (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07gatheringfoo00]{Gathering Food}).</p>\n  <p><strong>Security Points:</strong> If Granny Hu serves as Willowshore’s leader, she already has her agents working at shoring up the town’s defenses, and the party starts with 3 Security Points—otherwise, the party starts with 0 Security Points. Preparing for winter in Willowshore involves repair work to roofs, weatherproofing walls and buildings, training in how to respond to emergencies with things like fire and flood drills, and other civic preparations. Let the players know that if the PCs can earn at least 12 Security Points by the end of fall, Willowshore will be prepared for an average winter—but that additional points will be useful in dealing with unexpected emergencies. The PCs can build up Security Points by pursuing weekly downtime activities (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07increasingse00]{Increasing Security}).</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Willowshore in the Fall": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的秋日 Willowshore in the Fall",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore in the Fall\">柳岸镇的秋季</h2>\n<p>困扰夏季月份的反常频繁暴雨终于在秋天有所缓和，取而代之的是清爽的秋季——至少在第一个月里，还会有一些真正晴朗的日子可供享受。随着时间推移，白天变得更短，也更阴沉。大约每周两次左右，可能会下几小时的小雨；当树叶开始变色时，劲风也变得更常见。但总体而言，本幕期间的天气肯定还能忍受，甚至称得上宜人。到了最后几周，天空持续阴沉，随着冬季逼近，清晨的露水会被一层薄霜取代。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.kjCdhgE9DC3lLJaG]{柳岸镇} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.ZURyPThe4OMZxZJd]{室内}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore in the Fall\">Willowshore in the Fall</h2>\n<p>The unseasonably frequent rainstorms that plagued the summer months finally eases up during fall, giving way to a crisp autumn that, at least for the first month, offers some actually sunny days to enjoy. As time marches on, the days grow shorter and more overcast. Light rain might fall for a few hours twice a week or so, and blustery breezes grow more common as the leaves begin to turn, but overall, the weather during this act should certainly be bearable, if not actually pleasant. In the final few weeks, days remain overcast and a thin layer of frost replaces the morning dew as winter looms.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.kjCdhgE9DC3lLJaG]{Willowshore} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.ZURyPThe4OMZxZJd]{Indoors}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "Getting Started": {
              "name": "冒险开始 Getting Started",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">冒险开始</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇已至秋日，树叶开始变色，夏季的雨水被清爽的秋风取代；然而，这个异常多雨的夏天终于结束，加之曾威胁本地区的怪物被击败，却并未给镇民带来多少安慰。新的领导层已经就位，但自夏季第一天起失踪的知府赫山宝（以及他的宅邸，说来也怪）究竟发生了什么，依旧是个令人困惑的谜团。更令人不安的是笼罩该地区的诡异诅咒：它既阻止任何人离柳岸镇走得太远，也似乎阻止邻近聚居地的人前来拜访。只有一名神秘商人——名叫申藏的怪人——似乎能够自由出入柳岸镇；而就连他也不确定原因，对诅咒的本质一无所知。随着日子渐渐步入深秋，有一点变得清楚：若柳岸镇的人民要熬过即将到来的冬天，就必须储备食物并加固防备，好让镇民能在接下来季节性的风暴中生存下去。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>谁来领导柳岸镇？</h1>\n  <p>在上一幕接近尾声时，谁来取代柳岸镇失踪知府的问题已有答案。柳岸镇的人民认为这项任命只是暂时的，并希望失踪的知府赫山宝很快归来，但这种事不会发生（至少不会以当地人所期望的方式发生）。本战役其余部分假设PC支持老松木或胡婆婆担任该职位，但在你的游戏中，可能由另一名NPC（甚至某位PC本人）接任。究竟是谁在管理柳岸镇并不重要；在本次冒险中，该角色被称作“镇老”或“知府”。若在你的游戏里由某位PC领导柳岸镇，则请选择队伍在镇上结盟的一位重要NPC，改由其在本次冒险中担任顾问与任务发布者的角色。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>尽管当地人可以继续囤积柴火、把食物腌渍与发酵以便长期保存、加固建筑以抵御严寒、并储存谷物以策安全，但缺少援助与激励，他们仅凭自己能做的终究有限。所幸对柳岸镇来说，镇民在困境中并不孤单——他们身边有一群英雄能帮助他们为最坏的情况做好准备！</p>\n<p>本幕从秋季第一天开始。让队伍有时间从上一幕的事件中休息并恢复；但当你准备开始这一幕时（最好在秋季第一天后的数日内），镇老会联络队伍，邀请他们在柳岸镇的贸易栈会面，商讨小镇迫在眉睫的未来。</p>\n<p>当PC抵达时，迎接他们的是如今担任柳岸镇知府的镇老，以及在领导权竞选中落败的那位镇老——<strong>郑鹏</strong>（代表镇卫以及柳岸镇需要在物理层面为冬季作准备），还有<strong>三美奈户弥</strong>（代表柳岸镇的农户，以及储备食物与物资的需求）。</p>\n<p>你若愿意，可以将这场会面进行角色扮演；但概述下列要点能帮助快速启动冒险。会议以知府感谢PC迄今为止对柳岸镇的所有帮助开场，但随即指出工作才刚开始。镇老请PC继续研究困扰小镇的诅咒本质，但也补充说，当下更重要的是确保柳岸镇已为冬季做好准备；小镇只有三个月时间，之后食物与庇护将成为最重要的资源。基于这一需求，镇老请求PC在以下三个方面提供协助。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>镇民士气：</strong>镇老观察到镇民对未来愈发担忧与恐惧，因此无论PC能做什么来振奋精神、传播希望，都会令人感激。一个极好的方式，是重建并将青天茶馆重新对公众开放，使其成为传统的休憩与聚会之所（见第94页“重开茶馆”）；不过，参加本月22日的首长夜庆典，或许更能鼓舞士气（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{Week 3 - First Long Night}）。除这两种选择外，PC也应随时准备在需要时向镇民提供帮助与援助，以改善士气。</li>\n  <li><strong>食物储备：</strong>三美奈户弥指出，只要柳岸镇的人民仍被困在诅咒之中，建立食物储备就至关重要。她建议PC可以进行数项活动来帮助柳岸镇准备迎冬（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07gatheringfoo00]{筹措食粮}），但她仍对一个简单事实深感忧虑：柳岸镇一直依赖贸易来补充食物供给，而如今这条路行不通了，镇上的农夫与猎人将很难满足即将到来的需求。</li>\n  <li><strong>风暴准备：</strong>郑鹏告诉PC，他已请镇卫协助修缮与加固建筑以抵御风暴，但若PC能以其他方式协助确保柳岸镇准备迎冬，他将不胜感激（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07increasingse00]{保障安全}）。尽管夏季的暴雨已相当夸张，但与柳岸镇在接下来数月预期将面对的强风、雷霆与闪电、倾盆暴雨，甚至周期性的暴雪相比，仍算不了什么。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>PC能了解到的任何有关困扰小镇的诅咒的信息都会有所帮助；若他们能找出任何解除诅咒的线索，镇老希望尽快听到这些情报——但不要以牺牲以上三项更迫切的要务为代价（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07researchingt00]{研究诅咒}）。凭借PC在上一幕结束时从走豆那里取回的账册，他们已经掌握了下一步去向的绝佳线索，但解读走豆的笔记需要时间与工作。若PC在文本上遇到困难，镇老建议他们前往三个地点寻求协助：坟边居的草药师游素锦（她在柳岸镇居住的时间比任何人都久，或许能提供他人忽略的见解）、主母之绾的法师井川十兵卫（柳岸镇最多的旧文本都收藏在此），以及大尊柳（在上一幕中协助PC判定本地区诅咒范围的木灵）。</p>\n<p>会议很快便告结束，让PC可以按自己的想法开始准备迎冬的工作。除首长夜（发生在秋季第三周的最后一天）之外，PC处理这些任务的顺序由他们自行决定——明智的PC不会只专注于一个类别，而会将精力分散在所有方面。本章余下内容涵盖PC在这些努力期间将面对的各式各样的休整活动。即便在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{第6章}与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{第7章}中，PC学会如何击败鬼打墙并踏上前往谭杉寺的旅程后，他们仍可继续进行本章的休整活动，直到秋季结束、本幕落幕为止。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">Getting Started</h1>\n<p>It’s fall in Willowshore, and as the leaves begin to turn, the summer rains are replaced by crisp autumn breezes, yet the end of the unusually rainy summer and the defeat of the monsters that had menaced the region bring the townsfolk little comfort. New leadership has been put in place, but the mystery of what happened to Governor Heh Shan-Bao (and his manor, for that matter), missing since the first day of summer, continues to perplex. However, even more worrisome is the strange curse that surrounds the region, one that prevents anyone from traveling too far from Willowshore and also seems to prevent anyone from neighboring settlements from visiting. Only one mysterious merchant, a strange man named Shinzo, seems able to come and go to Willowshore, and even he is unsure of why and has no insight into the curse’s nature. As the days march forward into fall, one thing becomes clear: if the people of Willowshore are to survive the coming winter, food must be stored and reinforcements must be made so that the townsfolk can survive the seasonal storms to come.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Who Leads Willowshore?</h1>\n  <p>Near the end of the previous act, the question of who should replace Willowshore’s missing governor is answered. While the people of Willowshore assume this appointment will be temporary and hope that missing governor Heh Shan-Bao will return soon, such an event will not be occurring (at least, not in the way the locals hope). The rest of this campaign assumes that the PCs supported either Old Matsuki or Granny Hu for the position, but in your game, another NPC (or perhaps even one of the PCs themselves) might have taken on the role. Who exactly runs Willowshore is largely irrelevant, though, and in this adventure, that character is referred to as the “town elder” or “governor” If a PC leads Willowshore in your game, choose a significant NPC in town the party has allied with to instead play the role of adviser and quest giver throughout this adventure.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>While the locals can continue to stockpile firewood, pickle and ferment food for long-term storage, fortify structures against the cold, and store grain for safekeeping, there’s only so much they can do on their own without aid and without inspiration. Fortunately for Willowshore, the townsfolk aren’t alone in this plight—they have a band of heroes at their side to help prepare them for the worst!</p>\n<p>This act begins on the first day of fall. Give the party time to rest and recover from the events of the previous act, but when you’re ready to begin this one (preferably within a few days of the first day of fall), the party is contacted by the town elders with an invitation to meet at the Willowshore Trade Office to discuss the town’s immediate future.</p>\n<p>When the PCs arrive, they’re greeted by the town elder who now serves as Willowshore’s governor, along with the elder who lost that bid for leadership, <strong>Zheng Peng</strong> (representing the town guard and Willowshore’s need to physically prepare for winter), and <strong>Nadoya Sanmi</strong> (representing Willowshore’s farmers and the need to stockpile food and supplies).</p>\n<p>While you can roleplay out this meeting if you want, summarizing the important points listed below can help get the adventure started quickly. The meeting begins with the governor thanking the PCs for all they’ve done to help Willowshore so far but then noting that the work has only begun. The elder asks the PCs to continue to research the nature of the curse afflicting the town, but adds that it’s more important to make sure that Willowshore is ready for winter at this point; the town has only three months before food and shelter become its most important resources. In light of this need, the town elder asks the PCs to aid in the following three ways.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Townsfolk Morale:</strong> The town elder observes that the townsfolk are growing worried and fearful of the future, so whatever the PCs can do to keep spirits high and spread hope will be appreciated. An excellent way to do so would be to rebuild and reopen the Cerulean Teahouse to the public as a traditional place to relax and gather (see Restoring the Teahouse on page 94), but taking part in the festivities for First Long Night on the 22nd day of the month might be an even better way to keep spirits high (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07week3firstlo00]{Week 3 - First Long Night}). Beyond these two options, the PCs should also be ready to provide help and aid to the townsfolk as needed in order to improve morale.</li>\n  <li><strong>Food Stores:</strong> Nadoya Sanmi notes that as long as the people of Willowshore remain trapped in the curse, food stores are important to build. She suggests several activities the PCs can pursue to help Willowshore prepare for winter (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07gatheringfoo00]{Gathering Food}), but remains very concerned by the simple fact that Willowshore has always relied on trade to supplement its food supplies, and without that option available, the town’s farmers and hunters are going to be hard-pressed to meet the upcoming demand.</li>\n  <li><strong>Storm Preparation:</strong> Zheng Peng tells the PCs that he has asked the town guard to help with repair work and storm-proofing of buildings, but he would be grateful if the PCs can help in other ways to ensure Willowshore is ready for the coming winter (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07increasingse00]{Increasing Security}). While the summer’s rainstorms were excessive, they’re still nothing compared to the powerful winds, thunder and lightning, torrential downpours, and even periodic snowstorms that Willowshore expects to face in the coming months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Anything the PCs can learn about the curse afflicting the town will help, and if they can determine any clues as to how to lift the curse, the town elder wants to hear about such information as soon as possible—but not at the expense of the three more immediate concerns above (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07researchingt00]{Researching the Curse}). With the ledger the PCs recovered from Zoudou at the end of the previous act, they’ve got an excellent lead on where to go next, but interpreting Zoudou’s notes will take time and work. If the PCs struggle with the text, the town elder suggests the PCs pay a visit to three locations in particular for aid: the herbalist You So-Jin at Graveside Manners (who has lived in Willowshore longer than anyone else and might have insights others have missed), the wizard Igawa Jubei at Mother’s Coil (where the largest amount of old texts in Willowshore are stored), and Great Willow (the kodama who helped the PCs in the previous act determine the scope of the region’s curse).</p>\n<p>The meeting adjourns soon thereafter, allowing the PCs to begin the work of preparing for winter as they see fit. With the exception of First Long Night, which take places on the last day of the third week of fall, the order in which the PCs work on these tasks is left to them—wise PCs don’t focus on one category but instead spread their efforts across them all. The remainder of this chapter covers the wide range of downtime activities the PCs will face during these efforts. Even after the PCs learn how to defeat the Wall of Ghosts and make their journey to the Tan Sugi monastery in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl]{Chapter 6} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{Chapter 7}, they can continue to pursue the downtime activities in this chapter up until the end of fall, when this act ends.</p>"
            },
            "Turning of the Seasons": {
              "name": "季节轮转 Turning of the Seasons",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Turning of the Seasons\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第5章：</span>\n  <span>四时流转</span>\n</h1>\n<p>在7020年ic，也就是两百多年前，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠大师}——@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}的追随者——来到这片地区，寻找幽魂之森深处一片传说中的杉树神林。传言说，这些树中最高的一棵，是一位名为@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{谭隋靖}的远古英雄的转世之灵；此人曾击败一位名为库加普提的强大邪魔。智惠希望亲眼见证这生命轮回的壮丽例证。她抵达时，在那偏远林中神林里感受到的力量令她震撼，她明白林心那棵参天巨树具有非凡的灵性意义。她在树根处冥想了10天后，决定必须在林中建起一座寺院，让他人也能前来朝圣，并长驻于此，帮助守护这处圣地免受伤害。</p>\n<p>同一年，柳岸镇建立了，因为智惠需要一处居所，安置那些将协助建造寺院的人。最初几年里，谭杉林（智惠开始如此称呼该地）几乎没有开展多少工程，因为建立柳岸镇占据了朝圣者的大部分精力。随着柳岸镇发展，智惠专注于开辟新镇与圣地之间的道路。她知道，急行者穿越崎岖地形前往神林，用不了一天即可抵达，但匆忙赶路会让旅人失去摆脱日常琐碎牵扰的机会；因此，智惠大师意图打造一条朝圣之径，让行者在三天的耐心内省与自我反思中完成这段路途。</p>\n<p>于是，智惠大师穿行于林间，步步皆怀定意。她穿越树林时，时而攀上陡坡又越过其顶，时而在看似一模一样、极易迷路的林段间曲折前行；她又沿着一面如镜的大湖岸边绕行，最终抵达谭杉林。开辟这条道路——铺设石阶、架设小桥，以及建造小型神龛与建筑作为驿站——她与追随者们用了将近一年才完成。</p>\n<p>而建造谭杉寺又花了数年。每一根木料、每一块石头，都经过慎重挑选与安放。寺院直到10年后才告竣，但在那段时间里，智惠大师的弟子日益增多。对他们而言，智惠的神导术如同一片秋叶轻落心间——温柔，却带着历经沧桑的分量；并且始终给予弟子选择自身道路的自由。待寺院落成时，每年已有数十名朝圣者跋涉至柳岸镇，踏上前往谭杉寺的旅程。</p>\n<p>然而，智惠于7054年因自然原因去世不久，纷争便悄然渗入谭杉寺信众的生活。寺中来投的新面孔渐渐稀少，继而反转——僧侣开始离去，转往他处寻求觉悟。僧侣们永远不会知道，甚至不会怀疑的是：在智惠大师死后，他们之中有一人堕落失德。这名僧侣名为@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{心月}，其前世记忆异常强烈。心月的悲恸毒化了他的内心，使库加普提的影响得以侵入他的灵魂；库加普提的遗骸埋在地下，寺中大多数人对此毫无察觉。正是心月诸多细微的操弄，使得僧侣间的纷争得以滋长。</p>\n<p>到7060年时，寺里所剩无几的僧侣都已被库加普提腐化。当心月将自己献祭给那邪魔，却又在其他僧侣眼前转生术重生时，他们觉得谭杉寺的真相已然揭示——这里并非静思与安宁之所，而是一座囚墓：一股会以奖赏回报他们效劳的伟力被囚禁于此，已历经数百年。</p>\n<p>这些腐化的僧侣与柳岸镇断绝往来；接下来两年里，柳岸镇的人民以为寺院已被遗弃，实则心月与追随者把时间都花在探寻如何将库加普提从坟冢中解放出来。若仅砍倒那棵生长在库加普提遗骸之上的杉树，只会把邪魔的灵魂释放到浩瀚众界；心月从幻象中得知，库加普提想要的并非如此，而是要转生到凡世。为此，那棵杉树必须保持完好，以作为他新化身的原始材料。库加普提意图利用其旧敌谭隋靖的残存之物，作为自己转生入世的手段。不过，要实现这一目标，心月与僧侣们必须花费数十年冥想与祈祷，以铺就前路。</p>\n<p>7062年，来自瑟兹城的一群伐木工来到柳岸镇，寻觅一处隐秘的杉树林。他们沿路行军至谭杉寺，意图采伐那里的树木，却被僧侣屠戮殆尽。随后，伐木工的尸体被用来施行一场盛大的召唤仪式，召来宁多鲁邪魔，继而将其派往柳岸镇传递警告。那些怪物披着被杀伐木工的躯壳、挥舞着他们折断的武器，这场骇人之事被称作断刀夜；自那日起，柳岸镇的人民便惊惧地确保再也无人胆敢前往谭杉寺。</p>\n<p>此后局势一直延续，直到总督和善保试图清除侵入谭隋靖杉树的腐化，这场灾难性的尝试以仪式反噬告终，导致镇上所有人——以及谭杉寺中的人——尽数死亡。当思维空间被创造出来后，寺院周边地区，包括通往寺院的整段朝圣之径，都被鬼打墙所吞没；其中居住的僧侣死去，又以亡灵之身复起。作为思维空间的一部分，心月与其追随者知道自己在一遍又一遍地重复这些年份，却无力挣脱。于是，关于思维空间本质的诸多秘密与揭示，正等待柳岸镇的英雄们去发现；然而，他们在鬼打墙之后的谭杉寺中将遭遇的威胁，也将是他们迄今为止面对过的最大凶险。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-kami-tea-party.webp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Turning of the Seasons\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 5:</span>\n  <span>Turning of the Seasons</span>\n</h1>\n<p>In 7020 ic, just over two centuries ago, Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}, a follower of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi}, traveled to the region in search of a legendary grove of sugi trees deep in the Specterwood. Rumors held that the tallest of these trees was the reincarnated spirit of an ancient hero named Tan Sui-Jing, who defeated a powerful fiend named Kugaptee, and Zhi Hui hoped to see this magnificent example of the cycle of life with her own eyes. When she arrived, the power she felt in the remote grove astounded her, and she knew that the towering tree at the center was of great spiritual significance. After meditating at the tree’s base for 10 days, she decided she needed to build a monastery in the grove so that others could make the pilgrimage, then remain there to help preserve the site from harm.</p>\n<p>Willowshore was founded that same year, as Zhi Hui needed a place to live for those who would help build the monastery. For the first few years, little work was done at the Tan Sugi grove (as Zhi Hui had taken to calling the site), as the establishment of Willowshore took up most of the pilgrims’ focus. While Willowshore grew, Zhi Hui focused on creating the path between the new town and the sacred site. She knew that while the journey to the grove through the rugged terrain could be traversed by the hasty in less than a day, rushing the trip robbed the traveler of the chance to shed the distractions of day-to-day life, and so Master Zhi Hui sought to create a pilgrim’s trail that would be traversed over the course of three days of patient introspection and self-reflection.</p>\n<p>Thus, Master Zhi Hui traversed a path through the forest, choosing each footstep with intention. As she made her way through the woods, she found herself climbing up and over steep slopes, winding through seemingly identical stretches of forest where one could easily lose their way, and skirting the shore of a large lake with a mirrorlike surface before reaching the Tan Sugi grove. The creation of this path—the laying of its stones, the building of a footbridge, and the construction of small shrines and buildings to serve as way stations—would take her and her followers the better part of a year to complete.</p>\n<p>The creation of the Tan Sugi monastery took several more years. Every timber and every stone was chosen and placed with careful consideration. It would be 10 years before the monastery was completed, but in that time, Master Zhi Hui’s disciples grew. To them, Zhi Hui’s guidance was like a single autumn leaf alighting upon their minds—gentle yet arriving with the weight of a well-lived life, and always allowing the disciple the freedom to choose their own path. By the time the monastery was completed, dozens of pilgrims were making yearly treks to Willowshore to undertake the journey to the Tan Sugi monastery.</p>\n<p>But soon after Zhi Hui passed away from natural causes in 7054, discord crept into the lives of the adherents of the Tan Sugi monastery. The arrival of newcomers to the monastery dwindled, then reversed as monks began leaving in search of enlightenment elsewhere. What none of the monks would ever learn or even suspect is that upon Master Zhi Hui’s death, one of their own fell from grace. This monk was named @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue}, and the memories of their past lives remained unusually strong. Xin Yue’s grief poisoned them enough to allow the influence of Kugaptee, whose remains lay buried and unguessed at by most of the monastery’s occupants, to creep into his soul. It was largely the subtle manipulations of Xin Yue that helped discord to flourish among the monks.</p>\n<p>By 7060, what few monks remained at the monastery had become corrupted by Kugaptee, and when Xin Yue offered themself as a sacrifice to the fiend, only to reincarnate before the other monks’ very eyes, they felt that the truth of the Tan Sugi monastery had been revealed—this place wasn’t one for quiet reflection and peace, but a cage-tomb in which a great power that would give them all rewards for service had been imprisoned for centuries.</p>\n<p>These corrupted monks cut ties with Willowshore, and for the next two years, the people of Willowshore assumed that the monastery had been abandoned when, in fact, Xin Yue and their followers now spent their time exploring a way in which they could free Kugaptee from his grave. Simply chopping down the sugi tree that grew over Kugaptee’s remains would only release the fiend’s soul into the Great Beyond—Xin Yue knew from his visions that what Kugaptee wanted was to instead reincarnate into the mortal realm, and to do so, the sugi tree needed to remain intact to serve as the raw materials for his new incarnation. Kugaptee wished to use what remained of his old enemy, Tan Sui-Jing, as his method of reincarnation into the world. In order to achieve such a goal, though, Xin Yue and the monks needed to spend decades in meditation and prayer to prepare the way.</p>\n<p>In 7062, a group of woodcutters sent from the city of Sze came to Willowshore seeking a hidden sugi grove. They marched up the path to the Tan Sugi monastery, intent on harvesting its trees, only to be slaughtered by the monks. The bodies of the woodcutters were then used to perform a grand conjuration of nindoru fiends, which were subsequently sent down to Willowshore with a warning. Wearing the bodies of the slaughtered woodcutters and wielding their broken weapons, the resulting horror became known as the Night of Broken Blades, and from that date onward, the people of Willowshore frightfully ensured that no one else would ever dare visit the Tan Sugi monastery.</p>\n<p>And so things went, until Governor Heh Shan-Bao made his disastrous attempt to remove the corruption growing into Tan Sui-Jing’s sugi tree, a ritual that backfired and resulted in the deaths of everyone in town—and in the Tan Sugi monastery as well. When the mindscape was created, the region surrounding the monastery, including the entirety of the pilgrim’s path leading to it, became engulfed within a Wall of Ghosts, and the monks who dwelled within died and rose as undead. As part of the mindscape, Xin Yue and their followers know that they’ve been repeating the years over and over but have been powerless to break free. Many secrets and revelations about the nature of the mindscape thus lie in wait for Willowshore’s heroes to discover, yet the threats they’ll encounter in the Tan Sugi monastery beyond the Wall of Ghosts will be the greatest dangers they’ve yet faced.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 2.2: The Enlightened Path": {
          "name": "第二幕 2.2：踏险斩祸一道清 Act 2.2: The Enlightened Path",
          "pages": {
            "The Final Day": {
              "name": "最终之日 The Final Day",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Final Day\">最后一天</h1>\n<p>如果PC们没有击败伊奥加卡，那么第三天的暴风雨状态会在本幕剩余时间里持续（或至少持续到她被击败为止）。不过，本次冒险假定PC们击败了她；因此，当PC们在旅程的最后一天醒来时，迎接他们的是晴朗的蓝天。尽管天空放晴，气温依旧寒冷，并在当天持续下降，让人感觉越来越像冬天而非秋天。当PC们接近修道院时，请翻到@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{第7章}。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Final Day\">The Final Day</h1>\n<p>If the PCs didn’t defeat Iogaka, then the stormy conditions of the third day continue for the remainder of this act (or at least until she’s defeated). This adventure assumes the PCs defeat her, though, and when the PCs wake on the final day of their journey, they do so to clear blue skies. Despite the clear skies, the temperature remains cold, dropping further as the day goes on and feeling more and more like winter than fall. As the PCs approach the monastery, turn to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{Chapter 7}.</p>"
            },
            "Mountain Shrine": {
              "name": "山岳神龛 Mountain Shrine",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D3. 山岳神龛</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在傍晚，PC们在夕阳西下之际抵达山岳神龛；使用山岳神龛的地图。随着PC们靠近，一声雷鸣与一道闪光令风暴愈发猛烈。风暴对远程攻击施加的罚值提高至–2，并且现在也适用于察觉检定（@UUID[Item.VCLublg5hicujGO9]{Weather: Storm}）。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一道瀑布从五十英尺高的峭壁倾泻而下，注入下方的河流；风啸与雨声轰鸣在一定程度上掩盖了瀑布奔流的声响。一座摇摇欲坠的木桥横跨河面便于通行，而一段狭窄的台阶则自小径蜿蜒向上，通往北侧的断崖。</p>\n</div>\n<p>当大师@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}首次登上这座山时，她被倾泻入此湖的壮丽瀑布所吸引，并为此地之美所折服。鉴于河流在众多关于生死循环的神话与寓言中的象征意义，这里似乎是设立朝圣之径第三座神龛的完美地点，以呼应桥之神龛的位置。然而与那座神龛不同，这里的小湖——河水汇聚并停驻之处——并不象征从生到死的循环；它要求朝圣者思考每个生命都是值得享受之物，同时也为朝圣者在辛苦攀登一整天后提供了一个完美的沐浴洗涤之所。若PC在宗教上为专家，或信奉@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}，则会自动从当地传说中知晓这些；其他人则可以尝试一次@Check[religion|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]来回忆知识。</p>\n<p>真正的山岳神龛从朝圣之径上无法看见。PC们可以通过成功的@Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定攀爬被雨水浸透的峭壁前往神龛，但更容易的路线是从<strong>D3b</strong>区域的台阶上行，到达<strong>D3c</strong>区域的湖岸。该湖（<strong>D3d</strong>区域）平均深20英尺，一名成功通过@Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim]检定的角色可以在风暴搅动的湖水中游泳。不游泳的生物会向南移动20英尺，朝向<strong>D3a</strong>区域正北的瀑布；若生物跌落瀑布，会坠落50英尺落入下方水中，承受@Damage[15[bludgeoning]]坠落伤害。</p>\n<p>在<strong>D3c</strong>与<strong>D3e</strong>之间的两岸，各有一根杆子，上面固定着滑轮；两滑轮之间拉着一根绳索。<strong>D3f</strong>区域的洞穴里有六张供朝圣者睡卧的芦席，还有数条毛巾与几把刷子便于洗浴；而真正的山岳神龛（<strong>D3g</strong>区域）位于一座25英尺高的石制神龛建筑内。位于木筏上的生物可以尝试以下行动，沿着绳索长度移动木筏。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yama.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Iogaka\" alt=\"Iogaka, female storm hag\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yama.webp')\" />\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">移动木筏 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">2</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你通过拉拽绳索尝试将木筏向东或向西移动到对岸。进行一次@Check[athletics|dc:15]检定。木筏上的其他生物可以援助此检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 木筏移动25英尺。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 木筏移动15英尺。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 木筏移动5英尺。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 木筏不移动。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>离修道院如此之近，苦迦菩提的影响更为强烈；他愤怒的直接显化如今将神龛据为己有：一名名为伊欧伽卡的岚鬼婆。她就是折磨河童恩寇（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b1tormentedk00]{B1}区域）的那同一名残忍生物，同时也是PC们沿着朝圣之径旅途中持续受恶劣天气侵扰的始作俑者。岚鬼婆将山岳神龛视为自己的私人领地——一个她可以俯瞰下方山谷，并沉浸于自己经常召来的风暴荣光之处。PC们闯入此地，对她而言是深刻而私人化的侮辱。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-yama.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">山岳神龛</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.BQpABYrqhgvvOPXs]{Iogaka} @UUID[Actor.JeE0By58Vd0AjU9R]{Spark Moths (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>凭借她穿透风暴视物的能力，除非PC们行动隐秘并避免使用木筏横渡湖面，否则她会从神龛中的位置发现PC们。若PC们正试图乘木筏过湖，她会等他们渡到约1/3的路程时再对他们施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.9AAkVUCwF6WVNNY2]{闪电束}，以便让法术既能波及数名PC，也能击中对岸的滑轮。闪电束造成的猛烈伤害会自动摧毁滑轮，导致木筏开始向南漂移，朝向<strong>D3a</strong>区域的瀑布。每回合结束时，木筏会漂移20英尺，更接近坠落边缘。只要在<strong>D3e</strong>区域固定的绳索仍完好，PC便可以继续移动木筏，但该行动的DC提高至@Check[athletics|dc:25|name:Move the Raft]。当然，在第二回合，伊欧伽卡会移动到<strong>D3e</strong>区域的柱桩旁，用利爪砍向绳索；绳索AC为17且有15点生命值。若她摧毁绳索，木筏将失控地漂向瀑布，除非筏上的某位PC有办法推动它或将其固定。若木筏坠入瀑布，它会被摧毁——任何与木筏一同坠落的PC都将承受正常坠落伤害，视同从50英尺高处坠落到坚硬地面而非水面，这是因为下坠途中会撞上岩石与船体碎片；不过一次@Check[reflex|dc:20]豁免骰允许坠落的PC以更缓和的方式落入水中，从而只承受坠落伤害的一半。</p>\n  <p>伊欧伽卡身边还有一对电火蛾陪同。她会派蛾子去攻击湖中的PC，而自己则用风爆对付他们；但只要有PC与她进行近战对峙，她就会召回蛾子到身边为她防御。伊欧伽卡会战斗至死，但若PC们撤退，她不会追击到此处以外。若伊欧伽卡被杀，雷暴会立刻开始减弱，并在一小时内衰减为细雨；到第二天早晨，细雨会转为澄澈的蓝天。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">音效</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.kcrfM86DAcpOfBrs.PlaylistSound.M5txTumUDf7T8Cbc]{闪电束}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.pBcz5eRZMMc2znXA]{洞穴} @UUID[Actor.cHPAa9IKSOln2d9N]{神龛} <br />\n  洞穴（<strong>D3f</strong>区域）是一个相对舒适且干燥、可供过夜休息的地点。除用于在湖水中洗浴的毛巾与搓洗刷外，一处小岩架上还放着四块<em>提神香皂</em>。在神龛（<strong>D3g</strong>区域）里，中央石台上摆着一只饰有杉树图案的<em>次等揭示香炉</em>。伊欧伽卡把泥巴和死鱼塞进了香炉，因此在使用前必须先清理干净。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>开悟奖励：</strong> @UUID[Item.FUm3BqhNfrdJ3fuS]{Mountain Shrine Enlightenment} <br />\n  如果PC们击败伊欧伽卡、在湖水中沐浴，然后在此区域休息过夜，他们醒来时会迎来寒冷但晴朗的一天。若前一晚木筏被摧毁，它已神秘地被完全修复并可正常使用。此外，直到本幕结束前，PC们所有的强韧豁免骰都获得来自神龛的+1物品加值。由于从山岳神龛获得开悟，给予PC们40 XP。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D3. Mountain Shrine</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place in the evening, with the PCs arriving at the Mountain Shrine just as the sun is setting; it uses the map for the Mountain Shrine. As the PCs approach, the storm intensifies with a peal of thunder and a flash of lightning. The penalty to ranged attacks imposed by the storm increases to –2 and now also applies to Perception checks (@UUID[Item.VCLublg5hicujGO9]{Weather: Storm}).</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A waterfall pours over a fifty-foot-high cliff into the river below, the sound of the cascading water somewhat obscured by the howl of the wind and the pounding of the rain. A rickety wood bridge allows passage over the river, while a narrow set of steps winds up off the path into the escarpments to the north.</p>\n</div>\n<p>When Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} first ascended this mountain, she was drawn to the majestic waterfalls that cascade into this lake and was taken by the site’s beauty. In light of rivers’ symbolism in so many myths and parables about the cycle of life and death, this seemed the perfect place to set up the Pilgrim’s Path’s third shrine, to parallel the Bridge Shrine’s position. Unlike that shrine, though, the presence of the small lake here, where river waters gather and linger, does not symbolize the cycle of life to death; it asks the pilgrim to contemplate each life as something to be enjoyed and also gives the pilgrims a perfect place to bathe and wash at the end of a tiring day of climbing. A PC who’s an expert in Religion or who follows @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi} knows this from local lore automatically, while others can attempt a @Check[religion|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] to Recall Knowledge.</p>\n<p>The actual Mountain Shrine isn’t visible from the Pilgrim’s Path. While the PCs could Climb the rain-soaked cliffs up to the shrine with successful @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] checks, an easier route is to take the steps at area <strong>D3b</strong> up to the lakeshore at area <strong>D3c</strong>. The lake (area <strong>D3d</strong>) averages 20 feet deep, and a character who succeeds at a @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim] check can Swim in the storm-tossed waters. A creature who doesn’t swim moves 20 feet south toward the waterfall just north of area <strong>D3a</strong>; a creature who goes over the waterfall plummets 50 feet into the water below, taking @Damage[15[bludgeoning]] damage from the fall.</p>\n<p>A rope is strung between two pulleys affixed to poles on either side of the lakeshore between areas <strong>D3c</strong> and <strong>D3e</strong>. A cave at area <strong>D3f</strong> contains six reed mats for pilgrims to sleep on, along with several towels and brushes to aid in bathing, while the actual Mountain Shrine (area <strong>D3g</strong>) sits inside a 25-foot-high stone shrine. A creature on the raft can move it along the rope’s length by attempting the following activity.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yama.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Iogaka\" alt=\"Iogaka, female storm hag\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yama.webp')\" />\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Move the Raft <span class=\"pf2-icon\">2</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You attempt to move the raft to the east or west between the lakeshores by tugging on its ropes. Attempt a @Check[athletics|dc:15] check. Other creatures on the raft can Aid this check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The raft moves 25 feet.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The raft moves 15 feet.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The raft moves 5 feet.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The raft doesn’t move.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> This close to the monastery, Kugaptee’s influence is stronger still, and a direct manifestation of his wrath now claims the shrine as her home: a storm hag named Iogaka. The same cruel creature who tormented the kappa Enko (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b1tormentedk00]{B1}), Iogaka is also the cause of the foul weather that has plagued the PCs on their journey along the Pilgrim’s Path. The storm hag sees the Mountain Shrine as her personal domain—a place where she can look out over the valley below and bask in the glory of the storms she often conjures into being. The PCs’ intrusion into this domain is a deep and personal insult.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-yama.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Mountain Shrine</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.BQpABYrqhgvvOPXs]{Iogaka} @UUID[Actor.JeE0By58Vd0AjU9R]{Spark Moths (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>With her ability to see through the storm, unless the PCs are stealthy and avoid using the raft to cross the lake, she spots the PCs from her position in the shrine. If the PCs are attempting to cross the lake on the raft, she waits for them to get 1/3 of the way over before she casts @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.9AAkVUCwF6WVNNY2]{Lightning Bolt} at them so that she’ll catch a few PCs in the spell as well as the pulley on the opposite shore. The violent damage caused by the lightning bolt automatically destroys the pulley, causing the raft to begin drifting south toward the waterfall to area <strong>D3a</strong>. At the end of each round, the raft drifts 20 feet closer to plummeting over the edge. As long as the rope anchored at area <strong>D3e</strong> remains intact, a PC can continue to Move the Raft, but the DC for the activity increases to @Check[athletics|dc:25|name:Move the Raft]. Of course, on the second round, Iogaka moves to the post at area <strong>D3e</strong> and slashes at the rope with her claw; the rope has AC 17 and 15 Hit Points. If she destroys the rope, the raft floats uncontrollably toward the falls unless one of the PCs on board has some means of propelling it or anchoring it. If the raft goes over the falls, it is destroyed—any PC who goes over the falls with it takes normal falling damage as if they fell 50 feet onto a hard surface rather than water, as a result of striking rocks and parts of the boat on the way down, although a @Check[reflex|dc:20] save allows the falling PC to land more softly in the water and thus only take half damage from the plummet.</p>\n  <p>Iogaka is accompanied by a pair of spark moths. She sends the moths out to attack the PCs in the lake while she uses wind blasts against them, but as soon as a PC confronts her in melee, she calls the moths back to her side to defend her. Iogaka fights to the death but won’t pursue the PCs beyond the immediate area if they flee. If Iogaka is slain, the thunderstorm immediately begins to abate, and within an hour, it has reduced in power to a light drizzle that, by the next morning, gives way to a clear blue sky.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.kcrfM86DAcpOfBrs.PlaylistSound.M5txTumUDf7T8Cbc]{Lightning Bolt}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.pBcz5eRZMMc2znXA]{Cave} @UUID[Actor.cHPAa9IKSOln2d9N]{Shrine} <br />\n  The cave (area <strong>D3f</strong>) is a relatively comfortable and dry place to rest for the night. In addition to the towels and scrubbing brushes to aid bathing in the lake waters, four bars of <em>invigorating soap</em> sit on a small ledge. Over in the shrine (area <strong>D3g</strong>), a <em>lesser thurible of revelation</em> decorated with images of sugi trees sits on the central stone platform. Iogaka has filled the thurible with mud and dead fish, so it must be cleaned out before it can be used.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Enlightenment Reward:</strong> @UUID[Item.FUm3BqhNfrdJ3fuS]{Mountain Shrine Enlightenment} <br />\n  If the PCs defeat Iogaka, bathe in the lake’s waters, and then spend the night resting in this area, they awaken to a cold but clear day. If the raft was destroyed the previous night, it has been mysteriously and fully restored to functionality. In addition, the PCs all gain a +1 item bonus from the shrine to all Fortitude saving throws until the end of this act. Grant the PCs 40 XP for achieving enlightenment from the Mountain Shrine.\n</p>"
            },
            "A Whisper in the Woods": {
              "name": "林中低语 A Whisper in the Woods",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D2. 林中低语</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在下午，正当太阳开始沉入西方群山之后，并使用林中道路地图。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>山中道路陡峭的上坡与斜坡在此处暂时趋缓，路径在平坦却林木密布的地形间蜿蜒穿行；然而，这段路显得格外阴森——道路两侧的树枝上，数十颗处于不同腐烂程度的人类头颅被头发吊挂着。随着PC们走近，这些头颅开始低语与嘶嘶作响，腐朽的嘴唇抽动，轻柔而充满威胁的声音在空气中盘旋。“你们很快就会加入我们”，“欢迎你加入我们的家庭”，或“加入我们的声音，与苦迦菩提合而为一”之类令人不安的话语嘲弄着PC们。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/taunting-skull.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">林中低语</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.s5RfTcgA0CRm0ODD]{嘲弄僧侣的颅骨}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>其中有一颗头与其他不同；这一颗几乎只剩下颅骨，悬在道路中央，正对着PC们。只要有人进入颅骨30尺内，它便会升到空中，命令术PC们停下并返回，并告知他们：“你们不受欢迎；你们缺乏与伟大的苦迦菩提合而为一所需的真正洞见！”这是一名早已死去的僧侣的颅骨，如今被唤起成为一具格外强大的嘲弄颅骨；若PC们不转身离开，它便会尝试对他们挫败士气。若有人进入它10尺内或试图从旁通过，它就会发动攻击——它头发所连的那几片皮革般的头皮碎片会从上方的树枝处被扯裂脱落。嘲弄僧侣的颅骨能够喷吐亵渎的灵质污泥，并会战斗直至被摧毁。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D2. A Whisper in the Woods</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place in the afternoon, just as the sun is starting to dip behind the mountains to the west, and uses the Forested Path map.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The steep inclines and slopes of the mountain path taper off here for a while, winding through flat but densely forested terrain, but this stretch of pathway becomes particularly grim as dozens of human heads in varying states of decay hang by their hair from tree branches on either side of the road. As the PCs draw near, the heads begin to whisper and hiss, decaying lips twitching as soft, menacing voices swirl in the air. Unnerving phrases like, “You will join us soon,” or “We welcome you to our family,” or “Join our voices and become one with Kugaptee,” taunt the PCs.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/taunting-skull.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">A Whisper in the Woods</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.s5RfTcgA0CRm0ODD]{Taunting Monk's Skull}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>One head in particular is different than the others; this one is little more than a skull, and it hangs in the middle of the path, facing the PCs. As soon as anyone approaches within 30 feet of the skull, it rises up into the air and commands the PCs to stop and turn back, informing them, “You are not welcome here; you lack the true insight needed to be one with Great Kugaptee!” This is the skull of a long-dead monk, now animated as a particularly powerful taunting skull, and it attempts to Demoralize the PCs if they don’t turn back. It attacks if anyone comes within 10 feet of it or attempts to pass it, the fragments of leathery scalp from which its hair extends to the branch above ripping free as it does so. Capable of spitting unholy ectoplasmic sludge, the taunting monk’s skull fights until it is destroyed.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "A Voice in the Fog": {
              "name": "雾中的声音 A Voice in the Fog",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D1. 雾中的声音</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在PC离开园圃圣祠1小时后，并使用山中道路地图。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>雾变得更浓，道路也更陡。让每名PC尝试一次察觉检定。掷骰结果最高的PC瞥见了一个看起来像是昏暗灯笼的光点，但片刻之后，那光熄灭了，雾将这道景象吞没。</p>\n<p>PC在路上方瞥见的身影是一只刚刚“熄光”的鬼火。此时，道路西侧边缘是一处30尺高的悬崖，直落入下方的森林；树梢高度与道路差不多齐平。当PC靠近时，鬼火发出一声尖叫，听起来像一名惊惧女子的声音，随后飞到崖边下方的地面。它再次点亮自己，因此对于在上方崖边的PC来说，那光芒看起来就像树枝间一盏灯笼的摇曳光亮。鬼火用颤抖的声音向上喊道，哭喊着：“救命！我摔下来了！我想我腿断了！”掷一次欺骗检定来对PC说谎。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/fvtt90198-will-o-wisp.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">雾中的声音</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.imLw1FbzrHXKTn7J]{鬼火}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>鬼火希望把一名PC从道路上引诱下来，落入它的掌控之中；若正在攀爬的PC失足跌落，那就更合它意。成功通过一次@Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定的角色可以攀下崖壁。只要有PC接近它的光，怪物就会立刻发动攻击，并为先攻掷欺骗。若PC没有上当，鬼火会“熄光”，然后飞上来在崖边发动攻击，并为先攻掷隐匿。不同于多数鬼火，这个生物在变得可见时呈现为一小团发光的血红色蝴蝶群，而非骷髅般的面孔——这是它由苦迦菩提的梦境孕生所带来的副作用。它会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D1. A Voice in the Fog</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place an hour after the PCs leave the Garden Shrine and uses the Mountain Path map.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The fog grows thicker and the path grows steeper. Have each PC attempt a Perception check. The PC who rolls the highest catches a glimpse of what appears to be a dimly lit lantern, but a moment later, the light is extinguished and the fog swallows the vision up.</p>\n<p>The figure glimpsed up the path is a will-o’-wisp that has just Gone Dark. At this point, the western edge of the path is a 30-foot cliff that drops into the forest below; the tops of the trees are about equal with the path. As the PCs approach, the will-o’-wisp screams out in what sounds like the voice of a frightened woman, then flies down to the ground below the ledge. It lights up again, so that to the PCs on the ledge above, the glow looks like the flickering of a lantern through the branches. The will-o’-wisp calls up in a trembling voice, crying out, “Help me! I fell! I think I broke my leg!” Roll a Deception check to Lie to the PCs.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/fvtt90198-will-o-wisp.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">A Voice in the Fog</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.imLw1FbzrHXKTn7J]{Will-o'-Wisp}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The will-o’-wisp hopes to lure one PC down off the path and into its clutches; if a climbing PC falls, so much the better. Climbing down the cliffside is possible for a character who succeeds at a @Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check. The monster attacks as soon as a PC approaches its light, rolling Deception for initiative. If the PCs don’t fall for the ruse, the will-o’-wisp Goes Dark and then flies up to attack on the ledge, rolling Stealth for initiative. Unlike most will-o’-wisps, this creature appears as a small mass of glowing, blood-red butterflies when it becomes visible, rather than as a skull-like face—a side effect of its genesis from Kugaptee’s dreams. It fights to the death.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Third Day": {
              "name": "第三天 The Third Day",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Third Day\">第三天</h1>\n<p>黎明时雨势减弱，但浓雾滚滚而来，并在白天的前半段持续不散。过了正午，风力增强，将雾气驱散。随着下午推移，频繁的阵风会吹灭手持火焰，并使物理远程攻击承受–1环境减值（@UUID[Item.NslNsr8m4doy1F0G]{天气：风}）。当PC们抵达山中神社时，大雨再度倾盆，PC们将面对一场雷暴。见区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08d3mountainsh00]{D3}。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景笔记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.IcMQs5bqFUW3hOTs]{浓雾} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.nezy4qHmtlstrXAe]{雨声} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.UGTtO5R4VbSOPooG]{雷暴}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>这一天的旅程中，旅行将愈发变得“向上”，道路有数处之字形回转与陡坡需要攀行。道路两侧依旧是森林，尽管峭壁与岩架常常逼近路旁。一旦雾气散去，向东望去的视野便能瞥见柳岸镇。更远处，笼罩边远荒地的朦胧雾霭，使这片地区呈现出一种令人不安的景象，仿佛被暗云构成的巨碗扣在其下。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Third Day\">The Third Day</h1>\n<p>The rain lets up with the dawn, but a thick fog rolls in and persists for the first part of the day. Past noon, the wind picks up and disperses the fog. As the afternoon wears on, frequent gusts of wind can snuff out handheld flames, and impose a –1 circumstance penalty to physical ranged attacks (@UUID[Item.NslNsr8m4doy1F0G]{Weather: Wind}). By the time the PCs reach the Mountain Shrine, the rain returns in force, and the PCs face a thunderstorm. See area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08d3mountainsh00]{D3}.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.IcMQs5bqFUW3hOTs]{Dense Fog} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.nezy4qHmtlstrXAe]{Rain} @UUID[Playlist.jXKZ6O8NnYJaazKE.PlaylistSound.UGTtO5R4VbSOPooG]{Thunderstorm}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>Travel increasingly becomes vertical during this day’s trip, with the path having several switchbacks and steep slopes to navigate. The forest remains on either side of the path, although cliffsides and ledges often encroach. Once the fog has dispersed, the view to the east allows glimpses of Willowshore. Beyond that, the haze surrounding the hinterlands gives the region the unnerving appearance of being trapped under a bowl made of dark clouds.</p>"
            },
            "Garden Shrine": {
              "name": "园圃圣祠 Garden Shrine",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C3. 园圃圣祠</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在傍晚，PC们在太阳落山时正好抵达园圃圣祠；使用园圃圣祠的地图。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>林中道路在此处出现一段断开，断口旁的空地上散落着灰烬，横跨在道路两侧。道路旁有一间部分烧毁的木屋；一条五英尺宽的岩石步道蜿蜒绕过废墟，通向后方一座杂草丛生的花园。在这里，一棵被烧毁的橡树焦黑残骸高高耸立；而在焦黑空地的尽头，则坐落着一座小型石制神龛。石径一路通向神龛，最后这一段路由三对未点燃的石灯笼夹道相伴。</p>\n</div>\n<p>在穿越这段旅程时，师父 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} 曾欣喜地发现，这片如画的空地上生长着一丛野花、浆果与野萝卜。花朵的美丽与果实和根茎蔬菜的美味，使这里成为建立神龛的绝佳地点：朝圣者可以在此享用一顿简朴的餐食，在一天行旅的尽头沉思“享受进餐”的价值，同时也提醒自己不要在食物或饮品上过度放纵。任何宗教为专家、或信奉 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解} 的PC都会从当地传闻中自动知道这些；其他人则可以尝试一次 @Check[religion|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定以回忆知识。</p>\n<p>五英尺宽的石径（区域C3a）绕过小屋（区域<strong>C3b</strong>），通向后院的一座小花园（区域<strong>C3c</strong>与<strong>C3d</strong>）。石径提供了稳固的落脚处，但任何人只要走离石径，便会发现覆满灰烬的泥地属于困难地形。区域<strong>C3c</strong>处夹道的六盏石灯笼本用于燃烧锥形熏香，并提供足够的遮护，使其即便在暴雨中也能持续燃烧。</p>\n<p>当PC们初到此处时，这里看起来像是不久前才发生过火灾。小屋（区域<strong>C3b</strong>）被严重焚毁，但屋顶仍有足够部分保持完整，至少能在暴雨中提供些许遮蔽。园圃圣祠本身位于后方的石屋内（区域<strong>C3d</strong>），其中的物品在火灾中完好无损。额外的维护与修缮物资也储存在这里。PC可以利用这些物资，以一次成功的 @Check[crafting|dc:18] 检定与1小时的工作来修补主屋的屋顶与墙壁（失败表示修缮物资在尝试中被损坏）。完成修缮后，PC们便可在<strong>C3b</strong>区域舒适地睡上一觉；否则，次日醒来时，潮湿会令他们起身时获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏} 状态，除非他们成功通过一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:15] 豁免骰。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>与桥梁圣祠（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b3bridgeshri00]{B3}）与山岳圣祠（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08d3mountainsh00]{D3}）不同，园圃圣祠曾经有守护者负责照料。这里住着四名看守——负责照料神龛的人，他们非常乐于在通往谭杉寺的约半程处，为旅人提供舒适的落脚点。看守们喜欢为朝圣者提供餐食与便利；但在寺院被遗弃后，他们选择继续留在此处，作为隐士生活，偶尔为零星旅人提供庇护。这一切在7062年结束：樵夫们前去寻找谭杉寺时，看守们试图劝退樵夫却未能成功……而当樵夫们当晚沿路返回、化作不死怪物之时，他们点燃了园圃圣祠。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/combusted.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">园圃圣祠</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.oqbHWrUNTjCbeGmK]{神龛看守（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>神龛的看守在那场大火中丧生，如今作为不死生物存在。他们会在PC进入<strong>C3b</strong>区域时立刻自灰烬中起身，因体表燃烧的感觉而痛苦尖叫，并在这股灼烧感的驱使下发动攻击。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.psCcz5htBhSFHIGf]{园圃圣祠} @UUID[Actor.6O9IZRG3Cr0C7KYK]{香炉} <br />\n  搜索神龛（区域C3d）会发现修缮物资，以及一只陶罐，内装十二枚薰衣草锥香。成功通过一次 @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定以回忆知识的PC会知道，薰衣草熏香据说能刺激食欲。每枚锥香价值25gp。若PC搜索神龛并在一次 @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 检定中成功，也会发现一件做工精巧的<em>银与橡木香炉</em>，能保护其中熏香不被风雨吹灭。该香炉价值50gp，外形为龙首，使烟雾从鼻孔袅袅飘出。\n</p>\n<p>若PC们在C3c区域的每盏石灯笼中各放入一枚锥香并点燃，一股宁静的感觉便会笼罩此地。若C3b区域的焚身尸尚未遭遇，熏香会使其在任何战斗期间处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{迟缓 1} 状态。</p>\n<p>一旦点燃，灯笼中的锥香会在本幕剩余时间里持续燃烧。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>开悟奖励：</strong> @UUID[Actor.y9JYS9xak3tg6jSg]{根系} @UUID[Item.p8njZzf4ZZXcz6VW]{园圃圣祠开悟} <br />\n  若PC们点燃六盏灯笼中的所有熏香并在此过夜，他们会发现灰烬之上新生出一层鲜绿的草皮。那棵烧毁的橡树根部之间也绽放出半打鲜亮的蓝色兰花。若PC们走近橡树，他们会被一股冲动攫住，想要摘下全部六朵花。每朵花在被摘下时都会变为一件消耗品物品，可如同一剂<em>次等治疗蒸汽</em>般被启动。\n</p>\n<p>无论PC们是否摘花，他们全员都会从神龛获得一项+1物品加值，作用于所有意志豁免骰，持续至本幕结束。因从园圃圣祠获得开悟，给予PC们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C3. Garden Shrine</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place in the evening, with the PCs arriving at the Garden Shrine just as the sun is setting; it uses the map for the Garden Shrine.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The forested path reaches a break here, next to an ash-strewn clearing astride the path. A partially burned wooden cottage sits near the path, while a five-foot-wide rock walkway winds around the ruins to an overgrown garden beyond. Here, the scorched remnants of a burned oak tree loom tall, while at the far end of the charred clearing sits a small stone shrine. The rock pathway leads up to it, with this last stretch flanked by three pairs of unlit stone lanterns.</p>\n</div>\n<p>While traversing this leg of the journey, Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} was delighted to find a grove of wildflowers, berries, and wild radishes growing in an idyllic clearing here. The floral beauty and the delicious taste of the fruits and root vegetables made an excellent spot for a shrine, where pilgrims could enjoy a simple meal and contemplate the values of enjoyable repasts at the end of a day of travel while also ensuring that they did not overindulge in food or drink. Any PC who’s an expert in Religion or who follows @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi} knows this from local lore automatically, while others can attempt a @Check[religion|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge.</p>\n<p>The 5-foot-wide stone path (area C3a) leads around the cottage (area <strong>C3b</strong>) to a small garden in the backyard (areas <strong>C3c</strong> and <strong>C3d</strong>). The stone path offers solid footing, but anyone who steps off the path finds that the ash-caked mud is difficult terrain. The six stone lanterns that flank the path at area <strong>C3c</strong> are meant to burn cone-shaped incense, and offer enough protection to allow such burning even in a rainstorm.</p>\n<p>When the PCs first arrive, the place appears to have burned relatively recently. The cottage (area <strong>C3b</strong>) is badly burned, but enough of the roof remains intact to offer at least some shelter from the rainstorm. The garden shrine itself is located in the stone building in the back (area <strong>C3d</strong>), the contents of which survived the fire intact. Additional supplies for upkeep and repair were stored here. A PC can use these to patch up the roof and walls in the main cottage with a successful @Check[crafting|dc:18] check and an hour’s work (failure indicating that the supplies were ruined in the attempt). Once these repairs are made, the PCs can sleep in area <strong>C3b</strong> comfortably; otherwise, when they awaken the next day, the damp causes them to rise @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} unless they succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Unlike the Bridge Shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b3bridgeshri00]{B3}) and the Mountain Shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08d3mountainsh00]{D3}), the Garden Shrine once had keepers to tend to it. Four caretakers dwelled here, shrine tenders who took great delight in providing travelers with a comfortable place to stay at the approximate halfway point to the Tan Sugi monastery. The caretakers enjoyed providing meals and comforts for pilgrims, but after the monastery was abandoned, the group opted to stay on, living as hermits who would periodically offer shelter to the odd traveler. This all came to an end in 7062, when the woodcutters sought out the Tan Sugi monastery. The caretakers tried to turn the woodcutters away but were unsuccessful... and when the woodcutters returned along the path that evening as undead monsters, they lit the Garden Shrine on fire.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/combusted.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Garden Shrine</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.oqbHWrUNTjCbeGmK]{Shrine Caretakers (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The shrine’s caretakers died in that fire and now exist as undead. They rise up from the ashes as soon as the PCs enter area <strong>C3b</strong>, crying out in pain as the sensation of their bodies burning drives them to attack.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.psCcz5htBhSFHIGf]{Garden Shrine} @UUID[Actor.6O9IZRG3Cr0C7KYK]{Incense Burner} <br />\n  A search of the shrine (area C3d) uncovers the repair supplies, along with a clay pot containing a dozen cones of lavender incense. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[nature|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge knows that lavender incense is said to stimulate the appetite. Each cone of incense is worth 25 gp. A PC who Searches the shrine and succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check also discovers a cunningly crafted <em>silver and oak incense burner</em>\n  that shields the incense within from being extinguished by wind and rain. This incense burner is worth 50 gp and is shaped like a dragon’s head, so that the smoke wafts from its nostrils.\n</p>\n<p>If the PCs place a cone of this incense in each of the stone lanterns at area C3c and light them, a feeling of calm settles over the area. If the combusted at area C3b haven’t yet been encountered, the incense causes them to be @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} during any combats.</p>\n<p>Once lit, the cones of incense continue to burn in the lanterns for the remainder of this act.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Enlightenment Reward:</strong> @UUID[Actor.y9JYS9xak3tg6jSg]{Roots} @UUID[Item.p8njZzf4ZZXcz6VW]{Garden Shrine Enlightenment} <br />\n  If the PCs light incense in all six of the lanterns and then spend the night here, they find a fresh layer of green grass has sprung up from the ashes. A half-dozen bright blue orchids have likewise bloomed among the roots of the burned oak tree. If the PCs approach the oak tree, they are overcome with the urge to pluck all six of the flowers. Each of these flowers, upon being plucked, becomes a consumable item that can be activated as if it were a dose of <em>lesser healing vapor</em>.\n</p>\n<p>Whether or not the PCs pluck the flowers, they all gain a +1 item bonus from the shrine to all Will saving throws until the end of this act. Grant the PCs 40 XP for achieving enlightenment from the Garden Shrine.</p>"
            },
            "The Girl in the Tree": {
              "name": "树上的女孩 The Girl in the Tree",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C2. 树中的女孩</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在日落前几小时，并使用林中道路地图。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yeri.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yeri\" alt=\"Yeri, human girl huddled in a hollow tree\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yeri.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC们旅行时，他们听到路边一棵枯死大树根部的巨大树洞里传来一名年轻女子的啜泣声。那声音夹杂着打嗝般的抽噎与哭喊：“姐姐！你在哪儿？姐姐，救救我！”</p>\n<p>这些可怜的求救声来自一个看起来像是名叫耶丽（Yeri）的年轻人类女子，她此刻蜷缩在树洞底部。从PC们的视角看，在7098年（10年前），耶丽的姐姐尤妮（Yuni）怂恿她偷偷溜出柳岸镇，打赌去看看那座废弃修道院，于是两人沿着朝圣之径前行。她们愚蠢地在下午离开城镇，也没有放慢脚步沿路走。夜幕降临时，两姐妹遭到一只可怖怪物——庞南加兰——的攻击。战斗中，两人被迫分散。尤妮最终抵达废弃修道院，并在那里迎来自己的结局（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}），而耶丽则被庞南加兰杀害。</p>\n<p>当柳岸镇思维空间形成后，苦迦菩提的影响将耶丽的灵魂拉了回来，并把她变成了杀死她的那种存在——庞南加兰。每天，耶丽都会从她以为是被“飞头”追逐的噩梦中醒来，然后到朝圣之径附近寻找庇护，等待姐姐归来。然而每到夜晚，她便屈从于新的本性，从身体里滑出，去林地中猎杀受害者。她死去的那棵空心树以一种防腐之力维持她的躯体，作用方式与多数庞南加兰使用醋浴类似；而她每次醒来都会忘记自己是什么。</p>\n<p>作为耶丽时，这名庞南加兰看起来是一位相貌平平的人类女子，穿着肮脏的衣服，无论去哪儿都紧紧攥着一串念珠。若被问及念珠，她说那是从母亲那里继承来的，作为能让她记住母亲的唯一物件，它一直带给她安慰。她把高领外套裹得很紧；若PC询问，她声称自己很冷，但一名在 @Check[perception|dc:22] 检定中成功的PC会瞥见她脖子上有一道淡淡的疤痕，环绕颈部一圈。PC们一旦开始与她交互，便可尝试进行一次 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20] 或 @Check[society|dc:25] 检定，以认出她是10年前失踪的那个人。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-yeri.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">树中的女孩</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.FSNsRYYrZZAkpI6Z]{Yeri}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>这只乔装的怪物恳求PC们帮忙护送她前往废弃修道院，称她的姐姐尤妮正在那里等她。如果PC们同意并护送她，那么夜幕降临后不久，她的真性便会夺取主导，她的头颅会从身体上脱离；当PC们准备夜间休息时，她便发动攻击。若PC们拒绝护送她前往修道院（无论是把她丢下，还是试图护送她回柳岸镇），或是他们当面指出她已经失踪十年之久，她会愈发崩溃，直到最终怪物本性接管，她的头颅脱离，并驱使她当场发动攻击。她一旦开始攻击，就会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">效果</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">将 @UUID[Item.81DaM7bFuyCIC4ce]{Yeri True Form} 效果拖拽上去以关闭她的伪装</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>奖励：</strong> @UUID[Actor.cpzbP3nJ7aUfa90Q]{耶丽的手链} <br />\n  庞南加兰一被杀死，她的身体便崩解为尘土，只留下耶丽作为人类时的幽影。她在消散前恳求PC们去找到她的姐姐尤妮，“也救救她。”随后耶丽的幽魂彻底消散，留下一个手链，其上镶有一枚护符，描绘着 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解} 的轮状符号。该手链作为一枚<em>抗力魅惑物品</em>运作，提供对心灵伤害的抗力5。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C2. The Girl in the Tree</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place a few hours before sunset, and uses the Forested Path map.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yeri.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yeri\" alt=\"Yeri, human girl huddled in a hollow tree\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yeri.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> As the PCs travel, they hear the sound of a young woman sobbing coming from a large hollow at the base of a dead tree at the edge of the road. The sounds are interrupted by hiccuping sobs and cries of “Big sister! Where are you? Big sister, help me!”</p>\n<p>These plaintive calls for help come from what appears to be a young human woman named Yeri, who now huddles in the hollow tree’s base. In 7098 (10 years ago, from the PCs’ perspective), Yeri’s big sister, Yuni, convinced her to sneak out of town and walk along the Pilgrim’s Path on a dare to check out the abandoned monastery. Foolishly, they left town in the afternoon and didn’t bother to walk the path slowly. As night fell, the two sisters were attacked by a horrifying monster—a penanggalan. In the fight, the two women were separated. Yuni eventually made her way to the abandoned monastery where she met her fate (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}), while Yeri was slain by the penanggalan.</p>\n<p>When the Willowshore mindscape came to be, Kugaptee’s influence drew back Yeri’s soul and transformed her into the very thing that slew her—a penanggalan. Every day, Yeri wakes from what she believes was a nightmare of being chased by a “flying head,” then seeks shelter near the Pilgrim’s Path to wait for her sister to return. Every night, however, she succumbs to her new nature, slithers out of her body, and hunts the woodlands for victims. The hollow tree she died in serves as a preservative force in the same manner most penanggalans use baths of vinegar, and each time she wakes she forgets what she is.</p>\n<p>As Yeri, the penanggalan appears as a plain-looking human woman dressed in filthy clothes and clutching a string of beads tightly wherever she goes. If asked about the beads, she says she inherited them from her mother, and as the one thing she has to remember her by, they’ve always brought her comfort. She keeps her high-collared jacket wrapped tightly around herself, claiming that she’s cold if the PCs ask, but a PC who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:22] check catches a glimpse of a faint scar that curls all the way around her neck. Once the PCs begin to interact with her, they can attempt a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20] or a @Check[society|dc:25] check to recognize her as someone who went missing 10 years ago.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-yeri.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Girl in the Tree</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.FSNsRYYrZZAkpI6Z]{Yeri}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The disguised monster begs the PCs to help escort her to the abandoned monastery, saying that her big sister Yuni is waiting for her there. If the PCs agree and escort her, soon after night falls, her true nature takes over and her head detaches from her body; she attacks as the PCs prepare to rest for the night. If the PCs refuse to escort her to the monastery (be it by leaving her behind or trying to escort her back to Willowshore), or if they confront her with the fact that she’s been missing for a decade, she grows increasingly distraught until finally her monstrous nature takes over and her head detaches, driving her to attack on the spot. Once she attacks, she fights to the death.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">Drag on the @UUID[Item.81DaM7bFuyCIC4ce]{Yeri True Form} effect to turn off her disguise</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Reward:</strong> @UUID[Actor.cpzbP3nJ7aUfa90Q]{Yeri's Bracelet} <br />\n  As soon as the penanggalan is slain, her body crumbles to dust, leaving behind a ghostly image of Yeri as a human. As she fades away, she asks the PCs to find her sister Yuni “and save her too.” Yeri’s ghostly form then fades entirely, leaving behind a bracelet fitted with a charm depicting the wheel-like symbol of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi}. This bracelet functions as a <em>charm of resistance</em> that provides resistance 5 against mental damage.\n</p>"
            },
            "Hungry Foliage": {
              "name": "饥饿的枝叶 Hungry Foliage",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C1. 饥饿的枝叶</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在中午前几小时，并使用湖边道路地图。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mandragora.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">饥饿的枝叶</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.w4cMEYdLNsIGExc0]{曼陀罗草（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>苦迦菩提的死亡之梦不仅影响了动物生命，也影响了思维空间中的植物生命。在道路沿线的这一处，靠近道路森林一侧、看似一对扭曲破损的树瘤木头的东西，实际上是嗜血的曼陀罗草。随着PC接近，这些可憎的植物抽搐着苏醒；当它们展开为模糊的人形时，会狂热地低语着“苦迦菩提”这个词。再加上它们扭曲的躯体，这应当会让PC想起他们很可能在上一幕的旧伐木营地里遭遇过的那座怪异的苦迦菩提神龛。曼陀罗草将战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.uP7USCiZANNgWNDH]{显现曼陀罗草}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.44SXNgKaR1jwTnJd]{被杀死的曼陀罗草} <br />\n  每当一株曼陀罗草被杀死时，它会在一分为二前最后一次喊出苦迦菩提的名字，露出其核心处一团结晶化的血块。每一团血块都是一个<em>恐惧宝石</em>护符。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C1. Hungry Foliage</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place a few hours before noon, and uses the Lakeside Path map.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mandragora.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Hungry Foliage</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.w4cMEYdLNsIGExc0]{Mandragoras (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Kugaptee’s death dreams have influenced not just the animal life, but the plant life in the mindscape as well. At this point along the path, a pair of twisted, broken burls of wood resting on the forest side of the path are in fact bloodthirsty mandragoras. The hideous plants twitch to life as the PCs approach, and as they unfold into their vaguely human shapes, they feverishly whisper the word, “Kugaptee.” Coupled with their distorted frames, this should remind the PCs of the strange shrine to Kugaptee that they likely encountered in the lumber camp in the previous act. The mandragoras fight to the death.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.uP7USCiZANNgWNDH]{Reveal Mandragoras}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.44SXNgKaR1jwTnJd]{Slain Mandragoras} <br />\n  Each time a mandragora is slain, it cries out Kugaptee’s name one last time before splitting in half to reveal a clot of crystallized blood at its core. Each of these clots is a <em>fear gem</em> talisman.\n</p>"
            },
            "The Second Day": {
              "name": "第二天 The Second Day",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Second Day\">第二天</h1>\n<p>阴云愈发昏暗，到中午时分开始落雨。这场雨会浇灭小型火焰，使察觉检定承受–1环境减值，并且越来越令人不适（@UUID[Item.3gSA40OFOjamNrKS]{天气：降雨}）。当PC们在一天行程末尾接近园圃圣祠时，每名PC都必须尝试一次@Check[fortitude|dc:18]豁免，以抵抗因降雨而陷入@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}。那些为避免在寒冷雨中赶路的不适而采取了充分预防措施的角色（例如施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.5esP2GVzvxWsMgaX]{环境耐受}或穿着@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.SLQgdLk5K9JV4ACF]{冬装}）会自动在这次豁免中成功。入夜后，雨势加剧为暴雨，使察觉检定的减值提高至–2，并使距离超过60尺的生物变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{隐蔽}（@UUID[Item.5AbRQ2qUL8IiC20b]{天气：暴雨}）。</p>\n<p>当天行程的前半段沿着镜湖的湖岸前行，随后沿西须木河的北岸继续。到后半天时，小径开始在海拔上蜿蜒向上攀升，但还未真正进入山地地形。周围的森林变得越来越杂乱丛生。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Second Day\">The Second Day</h1>\n<p>The overcast clouds grow darker, and by noon, rain starts to fall. This rain douses small flames, imparts a –1 circumstance penalty to Perception checks, and increasingly causes discomfort (@UUID[Item.3gSA40OFOjamNrKS]{Weather: Rain}). As the PCs approach the Garden Shrine at the end of the day, each must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:18] save to resist becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} by the rainfall. Characters who took significant precautions to avoid the discomfort of traveling in the chill rain (such as by casting @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.5esP2GVzvxWsMgaX]{Environmental Endurance} or wearing @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.SLQgdLk5K9JV4ACF]{Winter Clothing}) automatically succeed at this saving throw. Once evening sets in, the rain worsens to a downpour, increasing the Perception check penalty to –2 and causing creatures further than 60 feet away to become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{Concealed} (@UUID[Item.5AbRQ2qUL8IiC20b]{Weather: Downpour}).</p>\n<p>The first half of the day’s walk is along the shore of Mirror Lake and then along the northern bank of the West Sugi River. By the second half of the day, the path begins to wind upward in elevation but doesn’t quite enter truly mountainous terrain. The surrounding forest becomes more and more overgrown.</p>"
            },
            "Bridge Shrine": {
              "name": "桥梁神社 Bridge Shrine",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B3. 悬桥神龛</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在傍晚，PC们抵达悬桥神龛时，太阳正好落下地平线。本遭遇使用朝圣悬桥地图。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>小径通向河岸，一座二十英尺宽的绳桥悬挂在下方缓缓流动的河面之上，离水面约半打英尺高。河中央立着一座六角形木制神龛，其屋顶既能遮风挡雨，又在正中央开了一个观景孔，让神龛内的人得以俯视并静观下方的水流。几只长柄水勺靠在中央孔洞的栏杆旁，用来舀取河水饮用；旁边还放着半打看上去很精致的陶土小瓶。中央孔洞周围一共铺着六张草编垫子，提供了在河面上方睡觉的地方。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-arms-of-the-drowned.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Arms of the Drowned\" alt=\"Arms of the Drowned\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-arms-of-the-drowned.webp')\" />\n<p>大师 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} 最初沿镜湖北半岸开辟道路时，需要在北苏吉河流入湖口处架设一座桥。她没有建造什么宏伟工程，而是在河上一处位置搭起一座简单的绳桥，并在河中央竖起一座六角木亭来帮助固定桥体。这座亭子是朝圣之径三座神龛中的第一座——让旅人能在过桥中途避雨歇脚，并透过平台中央的开口，静观下方河水流动之处。</p>\n<p>Zhi Hui 认为，在镜湖岸边度过的时光能提供自我观察与反思的机会。她希望朝圣者在远离他人干扰与日常琐事的纷扰时，能从倒影中看见一个不再背负重担的真实自我。为此，每位朝圣者都会吟诵一段反复的祷词，以祈唤轮回的循环，随后就在温柔流动的水面上方就寝。任何宗教为专家或信奉 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解} 的PC会自动从本地传闻中得知这些；其他人则可以尝试一次 @Check[religion|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定以回忆知识。</p>\n<p>任何PC若在 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定中成功以回忆知识，就会记得这座神龛在十年前一次洪水中被冲走了；可如今它却立在此处，看起来维护得很好，却仍然荒废无人。</p>\n<p>这里的河水深10英尺，角色可以通过 @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim] 在河中游泳。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/brood-leech-swarm.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">悬桥神龛</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.y562LBc0r0z2Blp4]{幼水蛭群（2）} @UUID[Actor.HWtCD42iNa7c0ljo]{溺死鬼的邀请}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>两群嗜血的幼水蛭群栖息在神龛下方的水中，纠缠翻滚的掠食者通常只会威胁那些下水的人；但在充斥于神龛的闹鬼现象影响下，这些幼水蛭很可能变得危险得多。一旦水蛭群涌上神龛，它们还会展现出一种额外、令人不安的特性：当它们在地板上翻涌蠕动时，会在四处爬动的同时一次又一次拼出“苦迦菩提”这个词。一旦幼水蛭开始战斗，它们会战至死；但它们不会追逐猎物越过地图边缘。</p>\n\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>无论PC们决定留下休息还是继续过桥，在他们抵达中央神龛本体不久之后（或当一名游泳的PC抵达横渡河流的中点时），下方河面开始剧烈起伏。起初看似只是水泡翻涌上浮，很快便化作一幕噩梦般的景象：数以百计的幽灵手臂从湖底深处挣扎着爬出水面。溺死者的魂魄在此水域中累积，并在苦迦菩提的影响下被激得暴怒。这些手掌从两侧探起抓住桥板，同时也会从神龛中央的孔洞伸出，或越过外侧栏杆升起，以便更好地攫抓PC们。</p>\n  <p>在此闹鬼现象启动的同时，一股水柱从神龛中央孔洞喷涌而出，将两群幼水蛭一起抛进神龛内，使它们能够在中央结构中攻击PC。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.kcrfM86DAcpOfBrs.PlaylistSound.R45UNuhZVL66clwa]{溺死鬼的邀请}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>启悟奖励：</strong> @UUID[Actor.KzJEE1VlV9Cz6DrW]{水勺} @UUID[Item.jccZj7Xyr8EjPzEc]{悬桥神龛启悟} <br />\n  若PC们击败闹鬼现象与水蛭群，并在神龛中过夜，他们醒来时神清气爽，却发现水勺不知为何都已装满河水。若他们靠近水勺，也会被一种奇异的冲动驱使，想用水勺将河水灌入六个陶土小瓶；这么做会使这六个小瓶各自变成一枚<em>中等镇魂炸药</em>。\n</p>\n<p>无论PC们是否制造这些炼金炸弹，他们在本幕结束前都从神龛处获得对所有反射豁免骰的+1物品加值。此外，因从悬桥神龛获得启悟，给予PC们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B3. Bridge Shrine</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place in the evening, with the PCs arriving at the Bridge Shrine just as the sun is setting. It uses the Pilgrim’s Path Bridge map.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The path leads up to a river’s edge, where a twenty-foot-wide rope bridge hangs a half-dozen feet over the slowly flowing river surface below. A hexagonal wooden shrine stands in the center of the river, its roof providing shelter from the elements while also offering a viewing portal in the center to allow those in the shrine to contemplate the flow of water below. Several long-handled dippers for bringing up drafts of river water for drinking lean against the central hole’s railing, along with a half-dozen delicate-looking clay vials. A total of six wicker mats lie around this central hole, affording places to sleep above the river.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-arms-of-the-drowned.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Arms of the Drowned\" alt=\"Arms of the Drowned\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-arms-of-the-drowned.webp')\" />\n<p>Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s original path along the northern half of Mirror Lake required the construction of a bridge over the North Sugi River, where it flows into the lake. Rather than build something grandiose, she had a simple rope bridge constructed over a point in the river, then erected a hexagonal wooden pagoda at the center to help anchor the bridge. This pagoda is the first of the Pilgrim’s Path’s three shrines—a place where travelers could take shelter mid-crossing and gaze through an opening at the platform’s center to contemplate the river’s flow below.</p>\n<p>Zhi Hui felt that time spent along the shore of Mirror Lake provided an opportunity for self-observation and reflection. She hoped that pilgrims, when stripped of the distractions of others and the mundane problems of daily life, might see in their reflections a true vision of who they are when unburdened. To aid in this, each pilgrim would chant a repetitive prayer meant to invoke the cycle of reincarnation, then retire to sleep above the gently flowing waters. Any PC who’s an expert in Religion or who follows @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi} knows this from local lore automatically, while others can attempt a @Check[religion|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge.</p>\n<p>Any PC who succeeds at a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge remembers that the shrine washed away a decade ago during a flood, yet here it stands, looking well-cared for but still abandoned.</p>\n<p>The river here is 10 feet deep, and a character can Swim in the river with a @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim].</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/brood-leech-swarm.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Bridge Shrine</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.y562LBc0r0z2Blp4]{Brood Leech Swarms (2)} @UUID[Actor.HWtCD42iNa7c0ljo]{Arms of the Drowned}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Two swarms of blood-ravenous brood leeches dwell in the water under the shrine, a tangle of writhing predators that normally would pose a threat only to those who enter the water, but combined with the haunting that infuses the shrine, these brood leeches are likely to become much more dangerous. Once the leech swarms surge up into the shrine, they display an additional unnerving quality; as they seethe on the floors, they form the word “Kugaptee” over and over as they swarm about. Once the brood leeches begin combat, they fight to the death, though they won’t pursue prey beyond the edges of the map.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> Whether the PCs decide to stay and rest or continue across the bridge, shortly after they arrive at the central shrine itself (or as soon as a swimming PC reaches the halfway point across the river), the surface of the river below starts rippling violently. What at first appears to be water bubbling up to the surface quickly resolves into a nightmarish vision of hundreds of ghostly arms scrambling up out of the water from the lake’s depths. Spirits of the drowned have accumulated in these waters, driven to fury by Kugaptee’s influence. These hands reach up on either side to grab onto the bridge’s planks, but also rise through the hole at the center of the shrine or up over its outer railings, the better to snatch at the PCs.</p>\n  <p>At the same time that this haunt activates, a plume of water sprays up through the central hole in the shrine, tossing both swarms of brood leeches up into the shrine and allowing them to attack PCs in the central structure.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.kcrfM86DAcpOfBrs.PlaylistSound.R45UNuhZVL66clwa]{Arms of the Drowned}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Enlightenment Reward:</strong> @UUID[Actor.KzJEE1VlV9Cz6DrW]{Dippers} @UUID[Item.jccZj7Xyr8EjPzEc]{Bridge Shrine Enlightenment} <br />\n  If the PCs defeat the haunt and the leech swarms, then spend the night in the shrine, they awaken refreshed but find that the dippers have mysteriously filled with water from the river. Should they approach the dippers, they are also filled with the strange urge to use them to fill the six clay vials; doing so causes each of the six vials to become a <em>moderate ghost charge</em>.\n</p>\n<p>Whether or not the PCs create these alchemical bombs, they all gain a +1 item bonus from the shrine to all Reflex saving throws until the end of this act. In addition, grant the PCs 40 XP for achieving enlightenment from the Bridge Shrine.</p>"
            },
            "Serpent Ambush": {
              "name": "巨蛇伏击 Serpent Ambush",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B2. 蛇群伏击</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在午后。此遭遇使用湖边道路地图。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/amphisbaena.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">蛇群伏击</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.GXD32AEKyWiklTim]{双头蛇（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>柳岸镇以西的荒野以其危险而闻名，PC们踏上旅程没多久，便遭到这种险恶事物的伏击——一对双头蛇。这两只怪物分别潜伏在道路两侧：一只藏在林地地面杂物之中，另一只藏在湖边浅水处。当PC们从它们之间经过时，怪物便发动攻击，战至死方休。</p>\n  <p>如果PC们正在护送恩科，其中一只野兽会攻击他，除非PC们采取措施保护他。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.lcWo3ru9KtGgOMM2]{恩科的赋礼} <br />\n  若PC们将恩科护送到湖边且他在这场战斗中存活，这名河童会感激地扑通一声跳进湖里，如释重负地叹了口气，然后对PC们说：“就在那儿等几分钟。”他潜入水下游走，5分钟后返回，带回了他知道附近一艘沉船里卡住的宝藏。他将这些物品——一把<em>+1 强击银制短剑</em>和一根<em>环境耐受魔杖</em>（收纳在一面<em>次级坚固护盾</em>上携带）——赠予他们，以感谢他们的善意。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们成功将恩科护送到水边，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B2. Serpent Ambush</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place in the mid-afternoon. Use the Lakeside Path map for this encounter.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/amphisbaena.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Serpent Ambush</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.GXD32AEKyWiklTim]{Amphisbaenas (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The wilderness west of Willowshore is known for its dangers, and it isn’t long after the PCs begin their journey that they’re ambushed by such a peril in the form of a pair of amphisbaenas. The two monsters lie in wait on either side of the path, one hidden among the detritus of the forest floor and another in the shallow water at the lake’s edge. As the PCs pass between them, the monsters attack, fighting to the death.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs are escorting Enko, one of the beasts attacks him unless the PCs take steps to defend him.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.lcWo3ru9KtGgOMM2]{Enko's Gift} <br />\n  If the PCs escorted Enko to the lake and he survives this fight, the kappa gratefully splashes into the lake and sighs in relief, then tells the PCs to “wait right there for a few minutes.” He swims underwater, then returns 5 minutes later with treasures he knew had been lodged in a sunken boat nearby. He gives them these items—a <em>+1 striking silver shortsword</em> and a <em>wand of environmental endurance</em> carried on a <em>minor sturdy shield</em>—as thanks for their kindness.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs successfully escort Enko to the water, grant them 40 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Tormented Kappa": {
              "name": "受折磨的河童 Tormented Kappa",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">B1. 受折磨的河童</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低级 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>本次遭遇发生在PC们踏上旅程后不久，并使用林中道路地图。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-enko.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Enko\" alt=\"Enko, male kappa\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-enko.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>在PC们开始跋涉约30分钟后，他们发现有一只孤零零的河童正以蜗牛般的速度沿着小路缓慢前行，方向与PC们一致。这只河童名叫恩科（Enko）。他被一名名为伊欧加卡（Iogaka）的岚鬼婆欺骗：她让他跪在地上用手和膝盖爬行、乞求饶命，结果他把自己头碗里的水洒了出来。伊欧加卡对这河童乐不可支，便抓起惊恐万分的恩科，挟在爪中飞上天空，发出残忍快意的尖笑，随后把他丢在鬼打墙附近——那儿离任何水源都很远。</p>\n<p>恩科一直在用自己5尺的速度，艰难地往镜湖的家走，好回去把头碗重新装满水；但他时不时会因一阵微风拂过而惊叫、挥舞双臂。那所谓的“微风”其实是伊欧加卡的声音——她通过风暴之声能力将声音传来，不断对恩科低语折磨，并扬言只要他一回到家，就会一遍又一遍把他抓起来，丢到“世界的尽头”。</p>\n<p>一看见PC们，恩科立刻跪伏在地，乞求饶命。他为自己挡了PC们的路而道歉，并可怜巴巴地爬到路边让他们通过；他既不会攻击，也甚至不敢与任何PC对视。恩科既惊惧又警惕；因此，他的初始态度为不友善。若被变为敌对，他不会攻击，而是会因恐惧而昏厥。若被提升到至少不关心，恩科会解释自己的困境，并希望PC们不是伊欧加卡的爪牙。时不时，会有更多低声的嘲弄飘进恩科耳中，使他惊恐叫喊。若某位PC凑近倾听，并成功通过一次 @Check[perception|dc:15] 察觉检定，便能听见伊欧加卡的折磨之语。幸运的是，岚鬼婆无法得知恩科是否刚遇到盟友——她的风暴之声能力仅为单向传递。</p>\n<p>恩科只想回家；若PC们提出护送他，他简直不敢相信自己这么走运。事实上，在回到水里之前，他都会一直保持警惕与紧张；一旦回到水中，他对PC们的态度便变为友善。若PC们在抵达湖边前就为他的头碗补上水，他会变得乐于帮助。若没有这份仁慈，PC们若想在日落前赶到镜湖（以及桥之神龛），可能就得把他背着走；在如此缓慢的速度下，思维空间那种扭曲距离的效果也无法让PC们在一天内走那么远。</p>\n<p>若PC们协助恩科，他会反复道谢，几乎到了荒谬的程度。若谈到伊欧加卡，他也会警告PC们：“风暴之母”是一只可怕而令人胆寒的怪物，能投掷闪电，掀起足以剥离血肉、露出白骨的狂风冲击。恩科不确定伊欧加卡为何最近会盯上他加以折磨，但若他对PC们至少是友善，他会告诉PC们：伊欧加卡对焚香燃烧的气味有一种特别而古怪的厌恶——这是一项弱点；不过恩科也警告说，考虑到伊欧加卡对风的掌控，要利用这一点相当困难。</p>\n<p>恩科被困在思维空间中，对于诅咒的本质没有更多见解，除了指出诅咒的边缘沿着朝圣之径延伸。尽管他哀叹自己再也不能绕着湖跑圈了，但他已经适应了自己新的（哪怕孤独的）生活。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span>@UUID[Actor.2IVaUeniTciZmadu]{Enko}</span><span>生物 2</span></h2>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">B1. Tormented Kappa</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This encounter takes place soon after the PCs begin their journey and uses the Forested Path map.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-enko.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Enko\" alt=\"Enko, male kappa\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-enko.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> About 30 minutes after the PCs begin their trek, they find a lone kappa trudging at a snail’s pace down the path in the same direction the PCs are heading. This kappa, whose name is Enko, was tricked by a storm hag named Iogaka into spilling the water in his head bowl when she told him to beg for his life on his hands and knees. Thoroughly entertained by the kappa, Iogaka picked the terrified Enko up and flew into the air with him in her clutches, cackling with cruel delight and dropping him off near the Wall of Ghosts, far from any source of water.</p>\n<p>Enko has been painstakingly making his way back home in Mirror Lake using his 5-foot speed to refill his head bowl with water, but now and then cries out in fear and waves his arms as a slight breeze wafts by. This “breeze” is Iogaka’s voice, carried via her voice of the storm ability, and she issues tormenting whispers to Enko as she promises to pick him up and drop him off “at the edge of the world” over and over whenever he gets back to his home.</p>\n<p>Upon spotting the PCs, Enko drops down on his hands and knees and begs for mercy. He apologizes for getting in the PCs’ way and crawls pitifully to the side of the path to let them pass, but doesn’t attack or even look a PC in the eye. Enko is frightened and wary; as a result, his initial attitude is unfriendly. If made hostile, he doesn’t attack but instead just faints from fear. If made at least indifferent, Enko explains his plight, hoping that the PCs aren’t Iogaka’s agents. Now and then, more whispered taunts reach Enko’s ears, causing him to cry out in fear. A PC who leans in close can hear Iogaka’s torments with a successful @Check[perception|dc:15] check. Fortunately, the storm hag has no way to tell that Enko might have just met allies—her voice of the storm ability is one-way only.</p>\n<p>Enko only wants to get back home, and if the PCs offer to escort him, he can’t believe his luck. In fact, he remains wary and nervous until he’s back in the water, at which point his attitude toward the PCs becomes friendly. If the PCs refill his head bowl with water before reaching the lake, he becomes helpful. Without this mercy, the PCs might need to carry him if they want to make it to Mirror Lake (and the Bridge Shrine) by nightfall; at such a slow speed, the mindscape’s distance-distorting effects don’t allow the PCs to cover that much ground in a day.</p>\n<p>If the PCs assist Enko, he thanks them over and over to the point of near absurdity. If the topic of Iogaka comes up, he also warns the PCs that the “storm mother” is a terrible and frightening monster who can hurl lightning and blasts of wind that can strip flesh from bone. Enko isn’t sure why Iogaka took to tormenting him recently, but if he’s at least friendly, he’ll tell the PCs that she’s got a particular and strange distaste for the scent of burning incense—a weakness that Enko warns is tough to take advantage of, given Iogaka’s mastery over wind.</p>\n<p>Enko is trapped in the mindscape and has no insights into the nature of the curse other than to note that the edges of the curse follow the Pilgrim’s Path. Though he laments that he can’t do laps across the lake anymore, he has acclimated to his new (if lonely) life.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span>@UUID[Actor.2IVaUeniTciZmadu]{Enko}</span><span>Creature 2</span></h2>\n</section>"
            },
            "The First Day": {
              "name": "第一天 The First Day",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The First Day\">第一天</h1>\n<p>当PC们前往桥边神龛时，天气清冷且多云。尽管PC们知道从鬼打墙（区域 <strong>A</strong>）到桥边神龛（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b3bridgeshri00]{B3}）的实际距离约为5英里，但沿着朝圣之径的这段行程原本就打算缓慢进行，好让旅人能在日落时抵达神龛。在旅行的前半天里，道路蜿蜒穿过茂密的森林；而下午所走的路线则沿着镜湖的湖岸弯曲前行。在这里，当PC们眺望湖面时，他们能一直看见对岸，以及更远处的群山。然而，若游泳者深入湖中超过几百英尺，就会被带回柳岸镇思维空间的边缘。</p>\n<p>当PC们沿着朝圣之径继续前行时，有一件事他们应当注意：这条道路看起来被保存得异常完好。这条路曾经人来人往，但在修道院被遗弃后的46年里，道路逐渐被植物覆盖，越来越难与周围的林地分辨开来。然而，当PC们行走其上时，朝圣之径却呈现出它在半个多世纪前仍被使用时的模样。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The First Day\">The First Day</h1>\n<p>As the PCs make their way toward the Bridge Shrine, the weather is crisp and cloudy. While the PCs know that the physical distance from the Wall of Ghosts (area <strong>A</strong>) and the Bridge Shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08b3bridgeshri00]{B3}) is about 5 miles, this leg of the journey along the Pilgrim’s Path was intended to be taken slowly, so that the traveler arrived at the shrine at sunset. For the first half of the day spent traveling, the path winds through dense forest, while the route traveled in the afternoon curves along the shore of Mirror Lake. Here, as the PCs look out over the lake, they can see all the way to the opposite shore to the mountains beyond. Traveling further than a few hundred feet out into the lake, however, brings a swimmer back to the edge of the Willowshore mindscape.</p>\n<p>One thing the PCs should note as they travel further down the Pilgrim’s Path is how strangely preserved it appears. The road was once well-traveled, but in the 46 years since the monastery was abandoned, the road became overgrown and increasingly indistinguishable from the surrounding woodland. As the PCs travel it, though, the Pilgrim’s Path appears as it did while it was in use over half a century ago.</p>"
            },
            "Walking the Path": {
              "name": "行走道路 Walking the Path",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Walking the Path\">踏上朝圣之径</h2>\n<p>无论PC打算离开多久，思维空间都会受到传统四日旅程的影响。为了抵达那座毁坏的寺院，PC必须依照朝圣之径的传统，花费四天三夜完成这段行程。考虑让神藏在PC出发前不久造访柳岸镇，好给他们最后一次购买补给的机会；如果某位PC有物品处于“订购”状态，那么这些物品此时也应已到货，不受他们原本预计等待时间长短的影响。</p>\n<p>当PC穿过鬼打墙并开始旅程后，他们很快意识到，这里的现实比在柳岸腹地更为局促。朝圣之径（以及在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{第7章}详述的谭杉寺建筑群）是思维空间中唯一可进入的地区。离开朝圣之径、前往周围林木覆盖山地的角色，会在失去小径视觉线不久后发现自己又回到了朝圣之径上；他们在不知不觉间被转了向。这甚至会影响飞行；飞到120尺以上的角色会发现自己不由自主地向下偏转，但在此之前，他们会注意到：在树梢上方大约半里之外，雾气会遮蔽清晰的视觉线。不过，只要PC仍在朝圣之径上，他们就能不受阻碍地朝任一方向旅行。</p>\n<p>另一个好奇之处在于，沿着朝圣之径的旅行无法被催促。无论队伍走得多快或多慢，他们都会在旅行8小时后抵达下一个路标神龛（或在旅行的第4天抵达寺院本身）。如果PC朝柳岸镇方向折返，这种距离的扭曲会更为明显：不论他们已沿着道路走了多少天，返回鬼打墙入口所需时间都不会超过1小时。返程时，先前经过的神龛会被神秘地“跳过”；而下一次队伍进入朝圣之径时，他们必须从头开始行程，按顺序重新造访每一座神龛。值得注意的是，每座神龛的状态都会保持为PC上次到访时的样子；遭遇不会“重置”，留下的物品或对神龛做出的改动都会持续存在。</p>\n<p>经历任何一种怪异效果的PC都可以尝试一次@Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识；成功时，他们得出结论：朝圣之径是束缚柳岸镇及其柳岸腹地的同一诅咒的更受限制版本，并意识到道路上发生的事可能表明，在谭杉寺中等待被发现的，是关于这道诅咒本质的更深层揭示。</p>\n<p>朝圣之径沿途的天气与更大的柳岸镇思维空间中的天气不同步，而是会在旅途中按天变化。如果PC撤回柳岸镇并重新开始沿着道路向上行走，他们会在旅程的每一天经历相同的天气。</p>\n<p>除非另有说明，朝圣之径周围的森林为困难地形。柳岸腹地的地图展示了道路所走的路线，以及旅途中数场遭遇发生的位置。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Walking the Path\">Walking the Path</h2>\n<p>Regardless of how long the PCs intend to be away, the mindscape is influenced by the traditional four-day journey. To reach the ruined monastery, the PCs must spend those four days and three nights following the Pilgrim’s Path traditions. Consider having Shinzo pay a visit to Willowshore just before the PCs set out in order to give them a last chance to purchase supplies; if a PC had items on “order,” then they should be available at this time, regardless of how much time they expected to have to wait.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs step through the Wall of Ghosts and begin their trip, they soon realize that reality is even more confined here than in the Willowshore hinterlands. The Pilgrim’s Path (and the Tan Sugi monastery complex detailed in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther]{Chapter 7}) are the only regions accessible in the mindscape. A character who leaves the Pilgrim’s Path and travels into the surrounding wooded mountains finds themselves returning to the Pilgrim’s Path not long after losing sight of the trail, having been turned around without noticing the change in direction. This even affects flight; a character who flies higher than 120 feet finds themselves veering back downward, but not before noting that fog obscures clear line of sight over the treetops beyond a half mile or so. As long as the PCs remain on the Pilgrim’s Path, though, they can travel unimpeded in either direction.</p>\n<p>Another curiosity is that travel along the Pilgrim’s Path can’t be rushed. No matter how fast or how slow the party moves, they reach the next waypoint shrine after 8 hours of travel (or the monastery itself on the fourth day of travel). This distortion of distance is even more noticeable if the PCs travel back toward Willowshore, for no matter how many days along the Path they’ve traveled, returning to the Wall of Ghosts entrance never takes more than an hour. Previously passed shrines are mysteriously skipped on a return trip, and the next time the party enters the Pilgrim’s Path, they must start their trek over from the beginning, revisiting each shrine in succession. Notably, the status of each shrine remains as it was the last time the PCs visited; encounters don’t “reset,” and items left or alterations made to the shrines persist.</p>\n<p>A PC who experiences any of these strange effects can attempt a @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge; on a success, they come to the conclusion that the Pilgrim’s Path is a more constrained version of the same curse that contains Willowshore and its hinterlands, and they realize that what’s happening on the Path could indicate that a deeper revelation about the nature of the curse awaits discovery at the Tan Sugi monastery.</p>\n<p>The weather along the Pilgrim’s Path isn’t in sync with that in the greater Willowshore mindscape, and instead changes by the day along the journey. If the PCs retreat to Willowshore and start their walk up the Path over again, they experience the same weather on each day of the journey.</p>\n<p>Unless otherwise indicated, the forest surrounding the Pilgrim’s Path is difficult terrain. The map of the Willowshore hinterlands shows the route that the path takes as well as where several of the encounters occur during the journey.</p>"
            },
            "The Pilgrim’s Path": {
              "name": "朝圣之径 The Pilgrim’s Path",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Pilgrim’s Path\">朝圣之径</h1>\n<p>随着完成@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{洞开鬼打墙}的仪式，PC们可以自由踏上传统的步行路线，从柳岸镇前往谭杉寺。然而在他们启程之前，务必确保玩家熟悉关于寺院与朝圣之径的常见传闻与知识。这些信息也在<em>《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》</em>中提供给PC们。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>常识</h2>\n  <p>谭杉寺由一位名为@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}的僧侣@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}于7020年建立，寺院围绕着一棵据说具有神秘力量的古老杉树而建。柳岸镇最初的建立，是为了支援那些修建寺院与通往寺院的长径之人；这条长径也被称为朝圣之径。智惠于7054年去世，随着寺院僧侣开始四散离去，柳岸镇的重心转向木材产业。到7060年时，寺院已被彻底遗弃；但在7062年，一群伐木工试图采伐生长在那里的古老杉树时，悲剧发生了。伐木工带着破损的武器与支离破碎的躯体回到柳岸镇；虽然这些不死伐木工在天亮前被击败，但仍有数十名镇民死于他们残破的工具之下。如今，这起事件被称为断刀夜；在此后的46年里，几乎没有访客再踏上前往废墟寺院的旅程。人们认为那地方被诅咒、闹鬼，或更糟；然而镇上仍有人忍不住猜想，废墟里也许依旧遗留着被抛下的宝藏与传说。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>寺院坐落在西方数英里外的一处僻静山谷中，四周被陡峭群山环绕。往返该地唯一安全的路线便是朝圣之径。沿着朝圣之径从柳岸镇前往寺院的最后一段路程仅有13英里的徒步距离，但传统上，寻求学识之人会缓步前行，并在途中三处神龛各停留过夜一次。这三处神龛——一处位于湖面漂浮的平台上，一处在一株古老枯死的树旁，另一处则在一块僻静、嶙峋的岩座上，俯瞰下方的小径——分别象征旅人前世、来世与今生。通过把这段短途徒步变为多日的冥想之旅，求知与求悟者便能调整心境，使之更适合领受谭杉寺僧侣的教诲。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Pilgrim’s Path\">The Pilgrim’s Path</h1>\n<p>With the completion of the ritual to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{Open the Wall of Ghosts}, the PCs are free to undertake the traditional walk from Willowshore to the Tan Sugi monastery. Before they set off on the journey, though, make sure the players are familiar with commonplace lore about the monastery and the Pilgrim’s Path. This information is presented to the PCs in the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em> as well.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Common Knowledge</h2>\n  <p>The Tan Sugi monastery was founded by a @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi} monk named @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} in 7020 and was built around an ancient sugi tree said to have mystic properties. Willowshore was originally founded to support those who built the monastery and the long trail that leads to it, also known as the Pilgrim’s Path. Zhi Hui passed away in 7054, and as the monks of the monastery began to drift away, Willowshore shifted focus to the lumber industry. By 7060, the monastery had been fully abandoned, but when a group of woodcutters attempted to harvest the ancient sugi trees that grew there in 7062, tragedy struck. The woodcutters returned to Willowshore with broken weapons and torn bodies, and while the undead woodcutters were defeated by morning, dozens of townsfolk perished to their battered tools. The event is remembered today as the Night of Broken Blades, and few visitors have made the journey to the ruined monastery in the 46 years since. The place is regarded as cursed, haunted, or worse, yet there are those in town who can’t help but wonder what treasures and lore might still lie abandoned in the ruins.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>The monastery is located in a secluded valley many miles to the west, surrounded by steep mountains. The only safe route to and from the site is the Pilgrim’s Path. While the last stretch of the trip to the monastery from Willowshore along the Pilgrim’s Path is only a 13-mile hike, traditionally those who would seek knowledge made the trek slowly, pausing to spend the night three times at three shrines along the way. These shrines—one on a floating platform in a lake, one near an ancient dead tree, and one on a secluded, rocky perch overlooking the path below—represented the traveler’s past lives, their future lives, and their current life. By turning the short hike into a multiday meditative trip, the seeker of knowledge and enlightenment adopts a mindset better suited to receiving the teachings of the monks of the Tan Sugi monastery.</p>"
            },
            "Planting the Soul Seed": {
              "name": "种下灵魂种子 Planting the Soul Seed",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">种下灵魂种子</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>在杀死秃鹫和狂躁邪魔后，PC们可以从秃鹫临死时丢下的位置把那颗有些被啃咬过的心脏从地上捡起。从心脏里传出微弱的声音呼喊“救我”，应会促使PC们这么做；而一旦有角色将其拾起，一股把心脏送回位于区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08a2tansuijing00]{A2} 的尸体胸腔中的冲动便会充斥其脑海。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">种下灵魂种子</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1J6BM3TWythOKBVA]{苦迦菩提之怒}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>心脏一被拿走，思维空间的氛围立刻转变。夜幕降临，将迷雾森林投入黑暗之中，末日将至与被窥视的感觉愈发强烈。此时，苦迦菩提那已死却仍在做梦的心智会更积极地对抗队伍，使下述危害在整个思维空间中显现。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注释</span><span class=\"keepme\">音效</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.kcrfM86DAcpOfBrs.PlaylistSound.0O2KkeZV97joZxCt]{骇魂咆哮}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p><strong>种下种子：</strong>与穗镜的遗体相邻的PC可以用一个交互动作把她的心脏放回去。如此一来，苦迦菩提之怒会因痛苦与挫败而嚎叫，随后那无形巨人般的声响会变得仿佛正在逃跑，渐远而去。穗镜的身体沉入石中，接着一棵巨大的杉树从地里拔地而起，吞没石头，并无害地将所有相邻角色推到一旁。树木长至近百尺高时，枝条舒展，驱散迷雾……随后现实褪去，PC们发现自己回到了柳岸镇西北、靠近鬼打墙处的朝圣之径上。现在，穿过鬼打墙的迷雾隧道可以轻松通行。在战役余下的时间里，踏入这条隧道会将PC们带到朝圣之径上，如本章余下部分所详述。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们因获得朝圣之径的许可，获得60 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Planting the Soul Seed</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Once they’ve slain the vulture and cacodaemons, the PCs can retrieve the somewhat gnawed-upon heart from the ground where the vulture dropped it as it died. The sound of a faint voice calling out “save me” from the heart should encourage the PCs to do so, and once a character has picked it up, the urge to return the heart to the corpse’s chest in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08a2tansuijing00]{A2} fills their mind.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Planting the Soul Seed</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1J6BM3TWythOKBVA]{Kugaptee's Anger}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> As soon as the heart is taken, the ambiance of the mindscape shifts. Night falls, plunging the foggy forest into darkness, and the feelings of doom and of being watched intensify. At this time, Kugaptee’s dead but dreaming mind takes a more active role in opposing the party, causing the following hazard to manifest throughout the mindscape.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.kcrfM86DAcpOfBrs.PlaylistSound.0O2KkeZV97joZxCt]{Terrifying Roar}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Planting the Seed:</strong> A PC who’s adjacent to Sui-Jing’s body can return her heart as an Interact action. Doing so causes Kugaptee’s Anger to howl in pain and frustration, then to sound as if the unseen giant were fleeing into the distance. Sui-Jing’s body sinks into the stone, and then an immense sugi tree grows up out of the ground, consuming the stone and harmlessly pushing any adjacent characters aside. As the tree grows to a height of nearly a hundred feet, its branches unfurl and drive away the fog... and then reality fades and the PCs find themselves back on the Pilgrim’s Path northwest of Willowshore near the Wall of Ghosts. Now, the foggy tunnel through the wall can be traversed with ease. For the remainder of the campaign, stepping through this tunnel sets the PCs onto the Pilgrim’s Path, as detailed in the remainder of this chapter.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 60 XP for gaining access to the Pilgrim’s Path.</p>"
            },
            "The Soulthief’s Nest": {
              "name": "窃魂者之巢 The Soulthief’s Nest",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A3. 窃魂者之巢</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 5</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一处由倒伏树木堆成的腐烂土丘横在这片空地里，足有十尺高。腐朽的木料上溅着血迹，中央的一个洞口散发出令人作呕的腐臭。</p>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/heart-eating-vulture.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">窃魂者之巢</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1kPkJWXmgiyZAWvn]{噬心秃鹫} @UUID[Actor.i0pkcYhNLaxmMozr]{狂躁邪魔（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>苦迦菩提对这片思维空间的影响，显现为一只饥饿且聪慧的秃鹫：它蜷伏在巢中，啃咬并啄食穗净的心脏。对PC们来说幸运的是，她的灵魂坚韧而顽强。秃鹫注意到PC们靠近时愤怒地低吼，用沙哑的声音命令他们立刻离开，否则就把他们也加进它的美餐！随后它发起攻击；与此同时，三团血块从心脏上猛地撕裂出来，化作尖啸的狂躁邪魔，看起来像扭曲的人脸——仔细观察会发现，这些脸与区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08a2tansuijing00]{A2}中的尸体面容相似，只是它们长着发光的黄色眼睛，口中布满尖牙。</p>\n  <p>如果PC们不立刻离开，秃鹫与狂躁邪魔就会攻击；它们几乎没有与任何人交谈的兴趣。战斗一旦开始，它们会在整片思维空间中追击PC们并死战到底。它们无法离开思维空间，但如果PC们逃回柳岸镇，它们会回到这里。由你决定，PC们可能会不断承受秃鹫啃食他们心脏的诡异噩梦，直到他们回来完成这项工作。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.c128mFG0wnilFMQj]{秃鹫之巢} <br />\n  秃鹫的巢里满是肮脏的羽毛，其中两根具有魔法效果。发现这些魔法羽毛需要进行一次@Check[nature|dc:15]检定或一次@Check[perception|dc:18]检定。每根魔法羽毛都作为一枚<em>阴森战利品</em>护符起效。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A3. The Soulthief’s Nest</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A ten-foot-high deadfall of trees lies in a rotting mound in this clearing. Blood spatters the decaying timbers, and an opening in the center emits a foul, rotten stink.</p>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/heart-eating-vulture.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Soulthief's Nest</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 5</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.1kPkJWXmgiyZAWvn]{Heart-Eating Vulture} @UUID[Actor.i0pkcYhNLaxmMozr]{Cacodaemons (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Kugaptee’s influence over this mindscape manifests as a ravenous, intelligent vulture that hunkers in its nest while it chews and pecks at Sui-Jing’s heart. Fortunately for the PCs, her soul is tough and resilient. The vulture snarls in anger as it notices the PCs approaching and demands in a raspy voice that they leave at once, lest they find themselves added to its fine meal! It then attacks, and as it does, three clots of blood rip free from the heart and transform into shrieking cacodaemons that look like distorted human faces—close inspection reveals the faces to be similar to that of the corpse at area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08a2tansuijing00]{A2}, save that these faces possess glowing yellow eyes and mouths filled with sharp teeth.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs don’t leave at once, the vulture and cacodaemons attack; they have little interest in talking to anyone. Once a battle begins, they pursue the PCs throughout the mindscape and fight to the death. They can’t exit the mindscape, though, and return here if the PCs flee back to Willowshore. At your discretion, the PCs might endure strange nightmares of a vulture eating their hearts until they return to finish this job.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.c128mFG0wnilFMQj]{Vulture's Nest} <br />\n  The vulture’s nest is filthy with its feathers, two of which have magical effects. Spotting these magic feathers requires a @Check[nature|dc:15] check or a @Check[perception|dc:18] check. Each magic feather functions as a <em>grim trophy</em> talisman.\n</p>"
            },
            "Tan Sui-Jing’s Grave": {
              "name": "谭隋靖之墓 Tan Sui-Jing’s Grave",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A2. Tan Sui-Jing’s Grave\">A2. 谭隋靖之墓</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>泥土小路在一片宽五十英尺的空地前戛然而止。一条更窄的小径通向北面的树林，而空地中央放着一块巨大的石板。一具女尸仰卧其上，胸口是一个豁开的大洞，血肉模糊。她的左臂似乎指向北面的那条小路。缕缕盘旋的雾气从尸体胸口的洞中翻涌而出，蜿蜒上升，随后与周围的雾气交融在一起。尸体下方，石板上表面被深深刮出数道沟槽，仿佛拼成了一个词，但很难确定写的是什么。</p>\n</div>\n<p>岩石上的尸体看起来似乎刚死不久。她的心脏不见了，但要辨认死者身份，需要进行一次 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[society|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来回忆知识。成功的角色知道，这具尸体属于谭隋靖——传说中的女英雄，据说近一千年前她曾在谭杉寺修建之地击败过一名强大的邪魔。</p>\n<p>PC在观察从尸体胸口升起的雾之触须时，若成功通过一次 @Check[perception|dc:15] 察觉检定，便能看见从洞中升起的扭曲人形面孔，它们无声尖叫着，随后淡去并融入周遭雾气之中。最后，一旦PC爬上石板或从较高处观察，任何懂得邪灵语的人都能读出石头上刻出的词：“苦迦菩提”。</p>\n<p>在这片思维空间中，原本应长在苦迦菩提墓上的那棵树从未扎根，因为谭隋靖的灵魂已被撕走。尸体伸出的手为PC指明了方向，那是谭隋靖临死前试图为未来的复仇者留下的一条小路。若成功通过一次 @Check[medicine|dc:15] 或 @Check[perception|dc:20] 检定，PC可以判断这处致命伤的来源是一只巨大的带爪手掌，它撕开胸膛造成了伤口。</p>\n<p>血迹飞溅一路指向东北；谭隋靖的心脏（以及她的灵魂）被区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08a3thesoulthi00]{A3} 中那只诡异的秃鹫带走。若成功通过一次 @Check[survival|dc:25|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] 检定，PC便能追踪小路上滴落的血点，将队伍带到秃鹫所在之处；不过他们也可以直接沿北边的小径前往秃鹫的巢穴。</p>\n<p>尽管已极度虚弱，谭隋靖灵魂的一缕回响仍在这片思维空间中徘徊；她的声音夹杂在窃窃私语里，向PC提供指引。PC在调查隋靖的遗体时，会听到一个声音低语：“找到种子。”PC调查空地并成功通过一次 @Check[survival|dc:18|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] 检定，会在落叶与泥地中发现脚印。他们可以追踪这些脚印到秃鹫用过的那棵树。若检定失败，他们可以花10分钟搜寻附近，找到一条秃鹫常走的小路，沿着它可通往其巢穴。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A2. Tan Sui-Jing’s Grave\">A2. Tan Sui-Jing’s Grave</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The dirt trail comes to an end at a fifty-foot-wide clearing. A smaller trail leads into the woods to the north, while at its center sits a large slab of stone. A woman’s corpse lies atop the slab, her chest a gaping, gory hole. Her left arm seems to point toward the northern path. Curling coils of fog writhe up from the hole in the corpse’s chest, slithering up and merging into the fog that surrounds it. Under the body, deep furrows on the upper surface of the stone seem to form a word, although it’s difficult to be sure what it says.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The corpse on the rock appears only recently dead. Her heart is missing, but identifying the dead woman requires a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or a @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[society|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge. A character who succeeds knows that that the body is that of Tan Sui-Jing, a legendary heroine said to have defeated a powerful fiend nearly a thousand years ago at the site where the Tan Sugi monastery was built.</p>\n<p>A PC who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:15] check while observing the tendrils of fog that rise out of the corpse’s chest can spot distorted and silently screaming humanoid faces rising up from the hole before they fade and merge with the surrounding fog. Finally, once a PC climbs up onto the slab or observes it from a height, the word carved into the stone can be read by anyone who understands Aklo: “Kugaptee.”</p>\n<p>In this mindscape, the tree that grew above Kugaptee’s grave never took root, for Tan Sui-Jing’s soul has been ripped away. The corpse’s outstretched hand points the way for the PCs, and was Tan Sui-Jing’s dying attempt to provide a trail for her would-be avengers. With a successful @Check[medicine|dc:15] or @Check[perception|dc:20] check, a PC can tell that the grievous wound’s source was a large, clawed hand that ripped through the chest.</p>\n<p>Splatters of blood lead northeast; Tan Sui-Jing’s heart (as well as her soul) was carried away by the strange vulture in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08a3thesoulthi00]{A3}. With a successful @Check[survival|dc:25|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track], a PC can Track the drips of blood left on the trail can lead their group to the vulture’s location, but they can also simply follow the northern trail to the vulture’s nest.</p>\n<p>Although greatly weakened, an echo of Tan Sui-Jing’s soul persists in this mindscape; her voice can be heard among the whispers and provides guidance to the PCs. While investigating Sui-Jing’s body, the PCs make out a voice whispering, “Find the seed.” PCs investigating the clearing and who succeed at a @Check[survival|dc:18|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] check find footprints in the leaves and mud. They can Track these prints to the tree used by the vulture. If they fail, they can take 10 minutes to Search the vicinity and find a trail used by the vulture that leads to its lair.</p>"
            },
            "Entrance": {
              "name": "入口 Entrance",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A1. Entrance\">A1. 入口</h2>\n<p>这个思维空间的20尺宽入口与出口会保持固定不变，只要PC们仍未在这个小型思维空间内解决当前局势；试图从其他任何地方穿过鬼打墙离开，其效果如同PC们在执行仪式之前试图进入鬼打墙一样。</p>\n<p>如果PC们离开这个思维空间，他们会从通往柳岸镇的道路上踏出鬼打墙，不论他们是从哪里进入的。之后再次进入鬼打墙时，他们可以选择在此处踏回思维空间，或在其他地方重新施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{洞开鬼打墙}，以创造一个通往此处的临时传送门。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A1. Entrance\">A1. Entrance</h2>\n<p>The 20-foot-wide entrance and exit from this mindscape remains static as long as the PCs leave the situation within this small mindscape unresolved; attempts to exit through the Wall of Ghosts anywhere else function as if the PCs attempted to enter the wall before performing the ritual.</p>\n<p>If the PCs exit this mindscape, they step out of the Wall of Ghosts on the road leading back to Willowshore regardless of where they entered. On return trips into the Wall of Ghosts, they can either step back into the mindscape at this point or recast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{Open the Wall of Ghosts} elsewhere to create a temporary portal back to this location.</p>"
            },
            "Into the Wall of Ghosts": {
              "name": "进入鬼打墙 Into the Wall of Ghosts",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Into the Wall of Ghosts\">进入鬼打墙</h2>\n<p>当仪式为PC们洞开鬼打墙时，这道超自然屏障仍持续抗拒他们进入，并积极阻止他们开始沿着朝圣之径前行。若PC们打算继续向西旅程，就必须直接面对鬼打墙内的险恶力量。</p>\n<p>当PC们完成仪式、踏入鬼打墙，并踏上显露出的朝圣之径时，迷雾再次将他们包围，切断退路，将他们困在一片似乎被雾笼罩的林地之中——然而这片森林有些古怪。地形完全不对，道路蜿蜒穿过的是一条森林覆盖的山谷，而非林木葱郁的丘陵。以一次成功的 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20] 或 @Check[religion|dc:22] 或 @Check[society|dc:22] 检定，PC能确认此处地形与谭杉寺遗迹所在的位置相吻合，尽管看不见任何寺院的迹象。若为大成功或大失败，他们会知道这片森林比预期年轻将近1,000年，来自寺院建成之前的时代。此外，这片区域中森林的灵性氛围也显得不对劲。雾气弥漫的矮丛环境中传来被注视的感觉、听不见任何动物叫声甚至没有一丝微风，以及一种无处不在的末日将至之感，共同营造出令人不安的氛围。</p>\n<p>队伍进入了另一处思维空间，与他们刚离开的那一个不同，并深受已死的苦迦菩提之梦影响。在这个版本的朝圣之径中，那枚曾是谭隋靖灵魂、并萌发为后来在其坟墓中容纳苦迦菩提的杉树的种子已被取走，而他的存在渗透于整片森林之中。这处思维空间让PC有机会目睹大杉树、苦迦菩提以及（进而）谭杉寺背后历史的一段缩影。</p>\n<p>接下来的遭遇使用“鬼打墙内”地图。无论PC们在此停留多久，此地似乎都处于傍晚时分，但浓雾遮蔽了对上方天空的视线。在超过60尺的雾中看到的生物为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{隐蔽}。试图穿过包围该区域的更浓厚迷雾会导致角色从迷雾中出现时，朝向与其进入时相反的方向。</p>\n<p>离开道路在浓密森林中移动会因困难地形而受阻。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Into the Wall of Ghosts\">Into the Wall of Ghosts</h2>\n<p>While the ritual opens the Wall of Ghosts for the PCs, the supernatural barrier continues to resist their entry and actively works to prevent them from beginning their walk along the Pilgrim’s Path. The PCs must confront the sinister forces within the Wall of Ghosts directly if they intend to continue their journey west.</p>\n<p>When the PCs complete the ritual, step into the Wall of Ghosts, and set foot onto the revealed Pilgrim’s Path, the fog surrounds them again, cutting off their retreat and trapping them in what appears to be a fog-shrouded woodland—yet something about the woods seems strange. The terrain is all wrong, with the road winding through a forested valley rather than forested hills. With a successful @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20] or @Check[religion|dc:22] or @Check[society|dc:22] check, a PC confirms that the terrain matches where the Tan Sugi monastery ruins stand, though no sign of the monastery is apparent. With a critical success, they know that the forest is nearly 1,000 years younger than expected, from an era before the monastery was built. In addition, the spiritual atmosphere of the forest within this area feels off. The sensation of being watched from the foggy undergrowth, the lack of any animal calls or even a soft breeze, and a pervasive feeling of impending doom make for an unnerving atmosphere all around.</p>\n<p>The party has entered another mindscape, unique from the one they’ve just exited, that’s heavily influenced by the dead Kugaptee’s dreams. In this version of the Pilgrim’s Path, the seed that was Tan Sui-Jing’s soul and that sprouted the sugi tree that would contain Kugaptee in his grave was removed, and his presence permeates the forest. This mindscape gives the PCs the opportunity to witness a snapshot of the history behind the great sugi tree, Kugaptee, and, by extension, the Tan Sugi monastery.</p>\n<p>Use the Within the Wall of Ghosts map for the following encounters. Regardless of how long the PCs remain here, it seems to be late afternoon, but thick fog obscures sight of the sky above. Creatures viewed through more than 60 feet of fog are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{Concealed}. Attempts to step through the thicker fog surrounding the region result in the character emerging from the fog in the opposite direction from where they entered it.</p>\n<p>Movement through the thick forest off the paths is hindered by difficult terrain.</p>"
            },
            "Performing the Ritual": {
              "name": "进行仪式 Performing the Ritual",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Performing the Ritual\">施行仪式</h2>\n<p>施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{洞开鬼打墙} 需要价值60 gp的米粒与熏香。如果PC至少受到柳岸镇某个派系的钦佩，那么镇上会提供仪式所需的米与熏香；否则，他们就得在镇上自行购买这些昂贵的材料成分。</p>\n<p>仪式必须在距离鬼打墙40英尺以内施放，但沿着墙体长度的具体施法地点由PC自行决定。施行仪式需要一天时间；在这一天里PC不应被敌人打断，不过你不必让玩家知道他们在施法期间会很安全！</p>\n<p>如果PC成功施行仪式，一股巨大的波纹般效果会席卷鬼打墙。这道波纹将蜂拥的幽影身形推开，驱赶至更深的迷雾之中，并消除鬼打墙对周围地形造成的诡异消音效果。</p>\n<p>在本冒险路径的剩余篇章中，只要 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{洞开鬼打墙} 的施法者之一（无论是主施法者还是次施法者）接近鬼打墙40英尺以内，雾墙中就会打开一个半径10英尺、如隧道般的缺口。这条隧道让旁观者能看见一条略显荒草丛生的道路蜿蜒通向前方的迷雾森林——这就是朝圣之径。若PC在从柳岸镇通向外界的道路上施行仪式，看起来就像道路周围的雾中打开了一条隧道；但若PC在鬼打墙的其他位置施行仪式，这条道路看起来会在雾墙边缘突兀地开始。无论PC在何处施行仪式，当他们踏入这条雾之隧道时，便等同踏上朝圣之径。隧道会在他们身后保持开启；若他们从墙中退回，便会重新出现在通往柳岸镇的朝圣之径上，而不论他们是从鬼打墙的哪一段进入的。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC在施行仪式的尝试中大失败并最终与两个幽灵战斗，则除非他们已是5级，否则按常规为这场战斗给予他们XP。无论如何，一旦PC成功施放洞开鬼打墙，给予他们80 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Performing the Ritual\">Performing the Ritual</h2>\n<p>Casting @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{Open the Wall of Ghosts} requires rice grains and incense worth 60 gp. If the PCs are admired by at least one of Willowshore’s factions, then the town supplies the rice and incense needed for the ritual; otherwise, they’ll need to purchase the costly components themselves in town.</p>\n<p>The ritual must be cast within 40 feet of the Wall of Ghosts, but the exact location along the wall’s length is up to the PCs. Casting the ritual takes a day; the PCs shouldn’t be interrupted by foes during this day, although you don’t need to let the players know that they’ll be safe during the casting of the ritual!</p>\n<p>If the PCs are successful in casting the ritual, an immense rippling effect washes through the Wall of Ghosts. This ripple pushes the swarming ghostly figures away, deeper into the mists, and removes the weird sound-dampening effect the wall had on the surrounding terrain.</p>\n<p>For the remainder of the Adventure Path, any time one of the casters of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{Open the Wall of Ghosts} (be they a primary or secondary caster) approaches within 40 feet of the Wall of Ghosts, a 10-foot-radius tunnel-like gap opens in the fog bank. This tunnel allows onlookers to see a somewhat overgrown road winding into the foggy forest beyond—this is the Pilgrim’s Path. If the PCs cast the ritual along the road leading out of Willowshore, it’ll look like a tunnel in the fog has opened around the road, but if the PCs cast the ritual elsewhere along the Wall of Ghosts, the road will seem to start abruptly at the edge of the fog wall. No matter where the PCs cast the ritual, when they step into this fog tunnel, they set foot onto the Pilgrim’s Path. The tunnel remains open behind them, and if they step back out of the wall, they reappear on the Pilgrim’s Path leading back to Willowshore regardless of where along the Wall of Ghosts they entered.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs critically fail in their attempt to cast the ritual and end up fighting two ghosts, grant them XP as normal for this fight unless they’re already 5th level. Regardless, once the PCs successfully cast Open the Wall of Ghosts, grant them 80 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Through the Wall of Ghosts": {
              "name": "穿过鬼打墙 Through the Wall of Ghosts",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Through the Wall of Ghosts\">穿越鬼打墙</h1>\n<p>鬼打墙阻断了通往谭杉寺的许可，但一旦PC们研究出“洞开鬼打墙”仪式，他们就能刺穿这道超自然屏障。关于鬼打墙的描述，以及未先执行该仪式就试图穿过者会发生什么的规则，见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05wallofghosts00]{此处}。</p>\n<p>PC们何时完成对柳岸镇诅咒本质的研究并发展出“洞开鬼打墙”仪式，取决于他们自己；但一旦完成，他们就可以在自己方便的时候尝试打开这道墙。此举默认他们在第二个月进行。鬼打墙沿着思维空间西侧绵延全长，但只有一条道路能穿过这道墙——所谓的“朝圣之径”，它从柳岸镇向西北方向延伸出去。无论PC们沿着鬼打墙的哪一段施行仪式，当他们穿过这道超自然屏障时，都会发现自己来到了另一侧的朝圣之径上。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.q6Aq46b4KfzM4gbR]{洞开鬼打墙}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>当PC们接近鬼打墙时，野生动物的声音、风穿过树枝的沙沙声，甚至他们自己的脚步声，都变得诡异地安静——这是苦迦菩提影响力日益增长的副作用。那些上一次靠近鬼打墙时并未经历令人不安的环境声“抑制”的PC，可能会因此感到担忧。当他们迈步进入能看见墙体的范围时，朗读或意译如下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>向北与向南延伸至目力所及之处，一道银色薄雾的瀑布之墙升腾而起，高达五十英尺，直入空中与周围林地。薄雾仿佛从地面涌出，向上流淌时几乎像一张幽影般、泡沫水做成的帘幕，随后又渐渐消散。然而，这一性相远不是这道墙最令人不安之处：在雾中，有幽灵般的形体翻搅浮沉，时隐时现。偶尔，会有一个逼近到边缘，伸出一条手臂，或把一张脸贴在雾面上——这些动作会将它们的肢体与面容扭曲成野性、怪诞的人形怪物讽像，随后雾中某种看不见的力量又将它们猛地拽回迷雾深处。</p>\n</div>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Through the Wall of Ghosts\">Through the Wall of Ghosts</h1>\n<p>The Wall of Ghosts prevents access to the Tan Sugi monastery, but once the PCs research the Open the Wall of Ghosts ritual, they can pierce this supernatural barrier. A description of the Wall of Ghosts, as well as rules for what happens to those who attempt to pass through without first performing this ritual, are presented @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil.JournalEntryPage.05wallofghosts00]{Here}.</p>\n<p>The timing of when the PCs complete their research into the nature of Willowshore’s curse and develop the Open the Wall of Ghosts ritual depends on them, but once they do so, they can attempt to open the wall at their leisure. This act assumes they do this during the second month. The Wall of Ghosts runs the length of the mindscape to the west, but only one road leads through the wall—the so-called “Pilgrim’s Path,” which exits Willowshore to the northwest. Regardless of where along the Wall of Ghosts the PCs perform the ritual, when they make their way through the supernatural barrier, they find themselves on the Pilgrim’s Path on the far side.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.q6Aq46b4KfzM4gbR]{Open the Wall of Ghosts}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>As the PCs approach the Wall of Ghosts, the sounds of wildlife, the rustle of wind through tree branches, and even the sound of their own footsteps grow eerily quiet—a side effect of Kugaptee’s growing influence. This might concern PCs who didn’t experience an unsettling “dampening” of ambient sound the last time they drew near to the Wall of Ghosts. As they step into view of the wall, read or paraphrase the following.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Stretching as far as the eye can see to the north and south, a cascading wall of silvery mist rises fifty feet into the air and the surrounding woods. The mist seems to rise up from the ground, looking almost like a ghostly sheet of foamy water as it flows upward before fading away. Yet, this aspect is far from the most unsettling quality of the wall, for within the mist, ghostly shapes churn and float into and out of sight. Every now and then, one draws close enough to the edge to reach out an arm or to press a face against the mist—acts that distort those limbs and visages into feral, monstrous caricatures of humanoids, before some unseen force within the mist yanks them back into the foggy depths.</p>\n</div>"
            },
            "The Enlightened Path": {
              "name": "踏险斩祸一道清 The Enlightened Path",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Enlightened Path\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第6章：</span>\n  <span>踏险斩祸一道清</span>\n</h1>\n<p>何时开始第6章取决于两个因素——玩家角色在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07researchingt00]{研究柳岸镇的诅咒}期间获得至少10点研究点数后完成“洞开鬼打墙”仪式的创造，以及玩家角色达到5级。由于第5章中获得的大多数XP奖励都源于每周事件，因此玩家角色很可能要到秋季第二个月过了相当一段时间后才会接近5级；@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{洞开鬼打墙}仪式通过其“必须在弦月或新月之日施放”的要求来考虑到这一点，这意味着它可以在本幕中任意一个月的后半段（尤其是第3与第4周、第7与第8周，以及第11与第12周）施放。如果你的游戏时间安排使得让玩家角色在一个月的前半段施放该法术会更合适，只需将该仪式的要求改为“必须在盈月或满月期间施放”，或干脆完全省略该要求。</p>\n<p>你可能会发现，你的玩家没有意识到：要揭开柳岸镇正在发生之事的最佳希望，其实在鬼打墙之外的谭杉寺——尤其当某个小队更在意无法前往海岸、无法联系柳岸镇最重要的贸易伙伴：唐入海岸要塞时。在这种情况下，就用镇上的长者、神秘商人神藏，或任何其他与玩家角色建立了羁绊的NPC，去推动他们调查鬼打墙；毕竟，西边那座古老的寺院在对抗诅咒方面，必然拥有比柳岸镇更充足的资源。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-kugaptees-anger.webp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Enlightened Path\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 6:</span>\n  <span>The Enlightened Path</span>\n</h1>\n<p>The timing of when to begin Chapter 6 depends on two factors—the PCs’ creation of the Open the Wall of Ghosts ritual after earning at least 10 Research Points while @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07researchingt00]{Researching the Willowshore Curse} and the PCs being 5th level. Since most of the XP awards earned in Chapter 5 come as the result of weekly events, it’s likely that the PCs won’t near 5th level until well into the second month of fall; the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.PvkEzzCaDT07DcJb]{Open the Wall of Ghosts} ritual accounts for this with its requirement that it be cast on a day with a crescent or new moon, which means that it can be cast during the last half of any month (notably, week 3 and 4, week 7 and 8, and week 11 and 12) of this act. If the timing of your game is such that it’d work better for the PCs to cast the spell in the first half of a month, simply change the ritual’s requirement so that it must be cast during a waxing or full moon, or just omit the requirement entirely.</p>\n<p>You might find that your players don’t realize that their best hope for discovering what’s going on in Willowshore lies beyond the Wall of Ghosts at the Tan Sugi monastery, especially if a group is more concerned about being unable to head toward the coast and contact Willowshore’s most important trade partner, the coastal fortress of Karahai. In this case, use the town elder, the mysterious merchant Shinzo, or any other NPC that the PCs have bonded with to push them toward investigating the Wall of Ghosts, since the old monastery to the west will certainly have greater resources than Willowshore does as far as combating curses goes.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 2.3: In the Ruins of Wisdom": {
          "name": "第2.3幕：智慧遗迹中 Act 2.3: In the Ruins of Wisdom",
          "pages": {
            "Return to Willowshore": {
              "name": "返回柳岸镇 Return to Willowshore",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Return to Willowshore\">返回柳岸镇</h2>\n<p>既然苦迦菩提带来的直接威胁已经解决，而PC们也已收集到继续研究思维空间所需的重要书籍与文件，那么接下来除了返回柳岸镇、度过秋季最后几周之外，就没有更多事情可做了。关于PC们如何进一步研究思维空间并发现和善保下落的信息，会出现在下一幕开头；下一幕从冬季的第一天开始。</p>\n<p>当PC们在终结苦迦菩提的威胁后返回柳岸镇，他们的名声也随之增长。他们会在柳岸镇的两大派系中各获得2点声望点。柳岸镇的人民也渴望听听PC们的冒险经历，以及他们对诅咒所了解的事；但“这座城镇并非被诅咒，而是被困在思维空间中”的认知可能会让镇民困惑，甚至不安，尤其当显而易见的是PC们其实还没找到解决问题的办法时。如果PC们对修道院发生的事守口如瓶，他们会失去4点希望点，并且由于这种保密滋生了担忧与挫败感，他们在每个派系中也各失去4点声望点。若PC们愿意说明发生了什么，他们可以选择说谎（使用@Check[deception|dc:22|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie]），或讲出真相（使用@Check[diplomacy|dc:22]），此时必须由一名PC尝试一次DC 22的技能检定。其他PC可以协助该检定。成功时，他们获得1点希望点（大成功时获得2点希望点）；失败时，他们失去1点希望点（大失败时失去3点希望点）。</p>\n<p>PC们或许会认为，柳岸镇的闹鬼现象是由苦迦菩提的影响导致；但这个推断是错误的，而秋季最后几周将揭示，仍有更多超自然事件即将发生。导致这些作祟的其实另有其因——这一真相仍是个谜，PC们将在战役的下一幕中面对、并加以调查；最终他们将发现，柳岸镇的前任执政官已经被困在属于他自己的思维空间里。而迄今最巨大、最令人震骇的发现——执政官失败的仪式不仅创造了一个思维空间，还杀死了整座城镇，并将其居民困在其中逾一个世纪——也将很快随着寒冷的冬月将柳岸镇纳入掌控而变得清晰可见！</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注释</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{Change Season}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>更改@UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{柳岸镇}与@UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{柳岸腹地}场景中的季节。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Return to Willowshore\">Return to Willowshore</h2>\n<p>Now that the immediate threat posed by Kugaptee has been resolved and the PCs have gathered the important books and documents they’ll need to research the mindscape further, there’s nothing more to do other than return to Willowshore and finish the last several weeks of fall. Information for how the PCs can further research the mindscape and discover the whereabouts of Heh Shan-Bao appears at the start of the next act, which begins on the first day of winter.</p>\n<p>When the PCs return to Willowshore after ending the Kugaptee threat, their fame grows. They earn 2 Reputation Points with both of Willowshore’s factions. The people of Willowshore are eager to hear about the PCs’ adventures and what they’ve learned about the curse as well, but the knowledge that the town isn’t cursed but trapped in a mindscape could confuse or even distress the townsfolk, especially when it becomes apparent that the PCs haven’t actually found a solution for the problem. If the PCs keep what happened at the monastery secret, they lose 4 Hope Points and also lose 4 Reputation Points with each faction since their secrecy breeds concern and frustration. If the PCs do speak about what happened, they can either Lie (with @Check[deception|dc:22|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie]) or tell the truth (with @Check[diplomacy|dc:22]), in which case one PC must attempt a DC 22 skill check. The other PCs can Aid this check. On a success, they earn 1 Hope Point (or 2 Hope Points on a critical success); on a failure, they lose 1 Hope Point (or 3 Hope Points on a critical failure).</p>\n<p>While the PCs might believe that Kugaptee’s influence caused the hauntings in Willowshore, this assumption is wrong, and as the final weeks of fall will reveal, there are still more supernatural events to come. The revelation that something else entirely is causing these haunts remains a mystery that the PCs shall confront and investigate in the next act of the campaign, culminating in their discovery that Willowshore’s ex-governor has become trapped in a mindscape of his own. And the greatest and most staggering discovery yet—that the governor’s failed ritual not only created a mindscape, but killed the entire town and trapped its inhabitants within for over a century—will soon be made clear as the cold months of winter take Willowshore into its grasp!</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{Change Season}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Changes the Season on the @UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{Willowshore} and @UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{Willowshore Hinterlands} Scenes.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Concluding the Act": {
              "name": "终幕结束 Concluding the Act",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding the Act\">结束本幕</h1>\n<p>一旦PC们击败最后一只灵堕魔，一声咆哮撕裂洞窟。一个由血雾与阴影构成、闪烁不定的形体从洞穴中央盘旋升起，高耸于PC们之上；它从未真正稳定成单一形态，多条手臂向外伸展，盘绕的茎秆顶端长着恶魔般的头颅。紧接着，片刻之后，整个洞窟突然仿佛在PC们周围收缩。一阵眩晕感袭来，仿佛突然被抬升到空中，令胃部翻搅；而四周的根须变得更细小，却愈发繁多。根须缠绕住苦迦菩提的形体，将其遮蔽，也切断了咆哮。又过了片刻，PC们发现自己身处一座狭窄、遍布根须的洞窟，大小几乎只够所有人勉强站立。苦迦菩提的手指已不见踪影，辛玥的人类尸体（以及她的道具） леж在地上，终于得以安息。邪魔之墓已被恢复，他对柳岸镇造成的迫在眉睫的威胁也已不复存在。</p>\n<p>通往区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e15treasurec00]{E15} 的楼梯变得短了许多。当PC们返回地表时，他们发现寺院仍是一片废墟，但所有不死、怪物、作祟、灵堕魔的存在都已消失。更重要的是，谭杉树如今健康地矗立在寺院核心，视野中再无蛛网或病变的条纹。智惠的幽灵（特征）最后一次出现在PC们面前，感谢他们的付出。这次交谈将是PC们与她说话的最后机会，因此给他们足够时间，从她那里获得任何最后的答案。尤其是，PC们现在应当知道：柳岸镇并未被诅咒，而是一处循环的思维空间——在镇长试图（却失败地）施行一场旨在进一步保护所有人免受苦迦菩提侵害的仪式之后，这座城镇便一遍又一遍地重复着同一年。如今PC们已在寺院中拨乱反正，来自苦迦菩提的威胁已被移除，但他们仍被困在这处思维空间中，并不知道自己究竟重复了多少次同一年。若PC们尚未探索藏匿的图书馆（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}）并取回其中的珍贵书籍，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}也可以带领他们前往该地点。</p>\n<p>一旦PC们与智惠交谈完毕，她的魂魄便逐渐消散（暂时）与谭杉树融为一体。若思维空间重置，一切都将重新开始；但若PC们能打破思维空间，智惠的灵魂终于能够旅行前往来世。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding the Act\">Concluding the Act</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs defeat the final nindoru, a roar rips through the cavern. A shimmering form made from bloody mist and shadows coils up from the center of the cave to tower over the PCs, a shape that never quite settles on one form, reaching out with multiple arms and demonic heads atop coiling stalks. And then, a moment later, the entire cavern suddenly seems to shrink around the PCs. A sense of vertigo, as if suddenly being lifted up into the air, causes stomachs to lurch while the surrounding roots grow smaller but more numerous. The roots wrap around the form of Kugaptee, shrouding it and cutting off the roar. A moment later, the PCs find themselves in a cramped, root-filled cavern barely large enough for them all to stand in. No sign of Kugaptee’s fingers remains, and Xin Yue’s dead human body (and her gear) lies on the ground, finally at peace. The fiend’s grave has been restored, and the immediate threat he poses to Willowshore is no more.</p>\n<p>The stairs leading back up to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e15treasurec00]{E15} are much shorter. When the PCs return to the surface, they find the monastery still in ruins, but the presence of all the undead, monsters, haunts, and nindorus has vanished. More importantly, the Tan Sugi tree now stands healthy at the monastery’s core, with no spiderwebs or diseased streaks in sight. Zhi Hui’s ghost appears before the PCs one last time, thanking them for their service. This exchange will be the last opportunity the PCs have to speak to her, so allow them enough time to get any final answers from her they can. In particular, the PCs should know now that Willowshore isn’t cursed but is a cyclic mindscape that keeps repeating the same year over and over after the town’s governor tried (and failed) to perform a ritual meant to further protect everyone from Kugaptee. Now that the PCs have put things right in the monastery, the threat from Kugaptee has been removed, but they remain trapped in this mindscape with no knowledge of how long they’ve repeated the same year. If the PCs haven’t explored the hidden library (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}) and recovered its valuable books, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} can lead them to this location as well.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs have finished speaking to Zhi Hui, her spirit fades away, merging (for now) with the Tan Sugi tree. If the mindscape resets, everything starts over, but if the PCs can break the mindscape, Zhi Hui’s soul will finally travel to the afterlife.</p>"
            },
            "Kugaptee’s Grave": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提之墓 Kugaptee’s Grave",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E16. 苦迦菩提之墓</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">重度 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>发光的红色液体细流沿着地面蜿蜒流动，汇聚在房间中央，照亮这座潮湿、寒冷、高达三十尺的洞窟。这液体看似鲜血，却从数条巨大的树根上滴落——它们自天花板垂下或自墙壁凸出，让人以为那是稀薄的树汁。这种发光的物质在洞穴中央积成一个直径十尺的池子，环绕着看似四根巨大的石指与一根拇指；每根指尖都镶着一枚红色水晶爪。这些指头从地面伸出，仿佛某尊被埋葬的雕像正从下方伸手，想用掌心收集这股液体。</p>\n</div>\n<p>从区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e15treasurec00]{E15} 延伸而下的盘旋阶梯向地下下降近60尺后，抵达这座洞窟。若成功进行一次 @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 来回忆知识，PC会辨认出这些树根属于一棵杉树；但即便这些确实是上方区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e13thetansug00]{E13} 那棵高达100尺的谭杉之根，它们看上去也过于庞大。整个房间都是谭隋靖与苦迦菩提远古冲突的超自然显现，将一切都化为夸张到超越现实的巨大复刻。正如这些树根一样，从地面伸出的苦迦菩提石化手指——每根高达5尺——也远比他生前所拥有的巨大。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyueportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Xin Yue\" alt=\"Xin Yue\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyueportrait.webp')\" />\n<p>从树根滴落的液体是新鲜、温热的血液，这是那场远古冲突的另一种显现：苦迦菩提正从谭隋靖那转世的灵魂之生命中吸取力量，把血液吸入下方那具仍大半埋在地下的尸体之中。地图上显示的树根并未触及地面，使PC能轻松地在其下方地面上移动。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>这座修道院腐化的主要推手、也是苦迦菩提影响的核心受害者，正站在房间中央的血池里，血水没至小腿胫部。此人是 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{辛月}；过去几个月里——从夏季第一天后的几周开始——她几乎始终在此进行不断循环的祷告，努力引导苦迦菩提的魂魄重返生命。若无人阻止，她的工作将导致上方谭杉之树腐化崩塌，并使苦迦菩提苏醒；但希望PC能在隆冬时节那一刻到来之前终止这一进程。她身边有六名苦迦菩提的僧侣侍奉，他们分布在房间各处，专注地注视着她持续进行的仪式。</p>\n<p>当辛月注意到PC时，她会如下说道。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“啊，是的。我一直在等你们。伟大的苦迦菩提预言，很快就会有装作英雄的镇民来到这里。你们来得正好，省得我再派人去叫你们。伟大的苦迦菩提在他的坟墓中蠢动，但他还需要更多时间来彻底吞噬隋靖的魂魄。你们的血肉、你们的鲜血、你们的性命，会加速这一过程。能被选中扮演这样的角色，你们应当感到荣幸。既然你们如此好心，直接来到苦迦菩提面前等我亲手送你们去死，那么按礼数，我也该自我介绍。我名辛月，我将成为斩断你们、让你们脱离你们所知那名为生死轮回之陷阱的刀刃。”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>辛月唯一的目标就是让苦迦菩提复活；如果PC允许她完成上述讲话，她便以交涉掷先攻；若他们在她讲完之前就攻击她，她便以察觉掷先攻。她知道唤醒苦迦菩提意味着他们被困的思维空间将被彻底毁灭并遭到吞噬，而她对自己的灵魂将与自己崇拜的恶魔合而为一这一念头感到极度愉悦。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-xinyueportrait.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提之墓</span> <span class=\"keepme\">重度 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.HH7pl57fPYEcb82I]{Xin Yue} @UUID[Actor.mqTFTmYQoUKUyj2e]{莫啖魔（6）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>与此处七名敌人全体交战，难度远超“极限 6”遭遇；但假设PC已净化全部四尊雕像并获得智慧的协助，他们也有援手。战斗开始后，修道院创立者的幽灵会在PC身旁显现，随即抬起双臂，化作向上流入谭杉树根系的魂魄能量。那些巨大的树根随之翻腾苏醒，盘卷而下，绞缠并碾碎六名黑坊主，使辛月不得不独自面对PC——这令她无比挫败与暴怒。</p>\n  <p>当PC击败辛月后，战斗只完成了一半。随着她的亵渎转生发生，她的身体会裂开。当她转生成索闹灵堕魔时，苦迦菩提石化的手指会突然抽动颤抖。智慧痛苦的尖叫声撕裂洞窟，树根看似迅速枯萎腐朽，而那六具被碾碎的黑坊主尸体也会转生：每具尸体都裂开，释放出一只莫啖魔灵堕魔。这两场连续战斗分别构成一次低度 6 遭遇与一次中度 6 遭遇。由你决定，若PC在最终战斗中需要援助，你可以让智慧的幽灵再次显现，但只用于对PC施放治疗法术。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E16. Kugaptee’s Grave</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Glowing rivulets of red fluid wind along the floor to pool in the center of the room, illuminating this damp, cold thirty-foot-high cavern. The fluid looks like blood but drips from several enormous tree roots that hang down from the ceiling or protrude from the walls, giving the impression of runny sap. This glowing substance accumulates in a ten-foot-diameter pool in the middle of the cave, surrounding what appear to be four immense stone fingers and a thumb, each tipped with a red crystal talon. These digits protrude from the ground, as if some buried statue were reaching up from below to gather the liquid in the palm of its hand.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The winding stairwell from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e15treasurec00]{E15} descends nearly 60 feet below ground before reaching this cavern. With a successful @Check[nature|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] to Recall Knowledge, a PC identifies the tree roots as those of a sugi tree, but even if they’re the roots of the 100-foot-tall one in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e13thetansug00]{E13} above, they seem far too immense. This entire chamber is a supernatural manifestation of the ancient clash between Tan Sui-Jing and Kugaptee that transformed everything into a larger-than-life replica. As with the roots, Kugaptee’s petrified fingers that extend from the ground, each standing 5 feet tall, are much larger than those he possessed in life.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyueportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Xin Yue\" alt=\"Xin Yue\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyueportrait.webp')\" />\n<p>The fluid dripping from the tree roots is fresh, warm blood, another manifestation of the ancient clash as Kugaptee leeches Tan Sui-Jing’s reincarnated life of its power, absorbing the blood into his still mostly-buried corpse below. The tree roots shown on the map don’t reach the floor, allowing the PCs to move over the ground below them with ease.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The primary architect of the monastery’s corruption and the central victim of Kugaptee’s influence stands shin-deep in the pool of blood in the center of the room. This individual is @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue}, and she has spent almost the entirety of the past several months, starting a few weeks after the first day of summer, in a constant cycle of prayer here as she works to guide Kugaptee’s spirit back to life. Left unopposed, her work results in the corrupting collapse of the Tan Sugi tree above and Kugaptee’s awakening, but hopefully the PCs put a stop to this process before that event comes to pass in the dead of winter. She’s attended by six monks of Kugaptee, who gather around the room and watch raptly as her work continues.</p>\n<p>When Xin Yue notices the PCs, she addresses them as follows.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Ah, yes. I’ve been expecting you. Great Kugaptee foretold that townsfolk playing at being heroes would arrive soon. Your arrival is timely and saves me the hassle of sending for you. Great Kugaptee stirs in his grave, but he needs more time to finish the consumption of Sui-Jing’s soul. Your flesh, your blood, and your lives will quicken this process. You should feel honored to be chosen such a role. Since you’ve been so kind as to come directly to Kugaptee to die by my hand, it’s only proper that I introduce myself. I am Xin Yue, and I shall be the blade that severs you from the trap you know as the cycle of life and death.”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Xin Yue’s singular goal is to bring about the revival of Kugaptee, and if the PCs allow her to finish her speech above, she rolls for initiative with Diplomacy; if they attack her before she finishes, she rolls with Perception. She knows that waking Kugaptee means the complete destruction and consumption of the mindscape they’re trapped in, and she draws extreme pleasure from the idea that her soul will become one with the fiend she worships.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-xinyueportrait.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Kugaptee's Grave</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.HH7pl57fPYEcb82I]{Xin Yue} @UUID[Actor.mqTFTmYQoUKUyj2e]{Meokdans (6)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>A fight against all seven foes in this room is well beyond even an Extreme 6 encounter, but the PCs have help on their side, assuming they’ve purified all four statues and have the aid of Zhi Hui. Once combat begins, the ghost of the monastery’s founder manifests at the PCs’ side, then raises up her arms and transforms into spiritual energy that flows up into the Tan Sugi tree’s roots. The immense roots thrash to life and coil down to constrict and crush the six kurobozus, leaving Xin Yue to face the PCs on her own—much to her frustration and rage.</p>\n  <p>Once the PCs defeat Xin Yue, the combat is only half complete. Her body splits open as her Profane Reincarnation takes place. While she reincarnates as a sojiruh nindoru, Kugaptee’s petrified fingers suddenly flex and shudder. Zhi Hui’s scream of agony rips through the cavern as the tree roots appear to wither and decay, and the crushed bodies of the six kurobozus reincarnate as well, each splitting open to release a meokdan nindoru. Back-to-back, these combats entail a Low 6 encounter and a Moderate 6 encounter. At your discretion, if the PCs need aid in the final fight, you can have Zhi Hui’s ghost manifest again, but only to cast healing spells on the PCs.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Treasure Chamber": {
              "name": "宝藏室 Treasure Chamber",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E15. Treasure Chamber\">E15. 宝藏密室</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>空荡的架子与贫瘠的平台上摆着朴素的武器与护甲架，旁边还有敞开、满是灰尘的宝箱，这些都暗示着这里曾经可能存放过宝藏。只有靠近西墙的一只箱子仍然合着。南侧的双开门上刻着一道螺旋状符文，并被涂成红色。</p>\n</div>\n<p>南门上的螺旋符文，任何至少受训于宗教或善解学识的人都能辨认出那是一道警告；或者也可以由通过一次 @Check[society|dc:20] 检定的人识别出来。如果PC们尚未净化上方寺院里的四座雕像，苦迦菩提的影响仍然强大，一道力墙会阻止他们接近大门。一旦他们净化了四座雕像，这道屏障就会消失，PC们便能轻松打开大门。门后是一段漫长、蜿蜒的楼梯井，螺旋向下没入黑暗，在抵达区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16} 之前，会完整但缓慢地绕上一圈。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.guGa5KSWZIm5WewF]{Chest} <br />\n  虽然看起来这间宝藏密室早在很久之前就被洗劫一空，但任何通过一次 @Check[sangpotshi-lore|dc:17] 或 @Check[religion|dc:20] 检定的PC都知道，在供奉善解的寺院中，这种刻意保持空荡的宝库并不罕见。僧侣们不会囤积财富，而是常在设防区域建造像这房间一样的假宝库，以强调物质财富对他们而言意义甚微。\n</p>\n<p>不过，这种信念并不怎么适用于继承了寺院的堕落僧侣；在思维空间形成之前，他们一直把从误入其掌控之中的受害者那里搜刮来的、更有价值的一些宝藏留作己用。那只合上的箱子里有1,600 cp、430 sp、54 gp、价值120 gp的各式珠宝、一枚<em>绿宝石蝗虫护符</em>、一件染血的<em>+1 链甲衫</em>，以及一根<em>清明心智魔杖</em>。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E15. Treasure Chamber\">E15. Treasure Chamber</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Empty shelves and barren platforms that hold unadorned weapon and armor racks, along with open, dust-filled treasure chests, provide hints to the possible treasures once held here. Only one chest near the west wall remains closed. A double door to the south is carved with a spiraling rune that has been painted red.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The spiraling rune on the southern door can be identified as a warning by anyone who’s at least trained in Religion or Sangpotshi Lore, or by someone who succeeds at a @Check[society|dc:20] check. If the PCs haven’t purified all four of the statues in the monastery above, Kugaptee’s influence remains strong, and a wall of force bars access to the doors. Once they’ve purified the four statues, though, this barrier vanishes, and the PCs can open the doors with ease. Beyond, a long, winding stairwell spirals down into the darkness, making a complete but lazy revolution before reaching area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.guGa5KSWZIm5WewF]{Chest} <br />\n  While it might look like this treasure chamber was looted long ago, any PC who succeeds at a @Check[sangpotshi-lore|dc:17] or a @Check[religion|dc:20] check knows that such intentionally empty treasuries aren’t unknown in monasteries devoted to Sangpotshi. Rather than hoard wealth, the monks often built false treasuries like this room in defended areas to drive home the fact that material wealth had little meaning to them.\n</p>\n<p>This belief doesn’t so much apply to the corrupted monks who inherited the monastery, and they’ve been keeping some of the more valuable treasures they’ve collected from victims who stumbled into their clutches before the mindscape formed. Within the closed chest are 1,600 cp, 430 sp, 54 gp, 120 gp in assorted bits of jewelry, an <em>emerald grasshopper talisman</em>, a bloodstained <em>+1 chain shirt</em>, and a <em>wand of clear mind</em>.</p>"
            },
            "Storage Room": {
              "name": "储藏室 Storage Room",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E14. 储藏室</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间宽敞的地下室曾经或许用来存放园艺装备、肥料桶、木材以及修理工具，但如今却更像一间屠宰场。整个房间散落着被肢解的野兽与类人生物的尸体，以及四处飞溅的内脏；腐肉的恶臭让人在这冰凉的空气中呼吸都成了痛苦的折磨。</p>\n</div>\n<p>僧侣们曾用这片宽阔空间作为材料和季节性装备的储藏区，但修道院被遗弃时，大多数物品都被带走或捐了出去。自从接管之后，苦迦菩提的邪教徒就把这个房间当作倾倒他们这些年来献祭受害者尸体的垃圾场。低温只让腐坏稍稍变慢一点，却更让这里变得真正可怖。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hell-hound.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">储藏室</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bdOAkorJbVOqobUp]{苦迦菩提僧侣} @UUID[Actor.sipFaaLMxLg8iB2b]{地狱犬（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>除了作为弃置尸体的场所，这个房间也通向前往苦迦菩提之墓的路线，因此@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{辛玥}不愿让此处无人看守。一名黑坊主——曾经是修道院的厨师——如今在此守卫；它身边还有辛玥最喜欢的宠物：三只流着涎、比起狗更像燃烧的野狐的地狱犬。PC们抵达时，黑坊主正自娱自乐地和地狱犬玩“捡回”的游戏，用的是一颗被啃得很烂的人类头骨。它们一发现PC，地狱犬立刻龇牙低吼，凶相毕露；但黑坊主伸出一只腐烂的手制止它们的攻击，随后宣告：“打扰别人的闲暇时光很失礼。你们来这里做什么？我为什么不把你们喂给我的宠物？”</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>如果PC们没有立刻攻击，他们会发现这名无名黑坊主还算乐于交谈。下面列出PC可能提出的一些问题及其潜在回答；但回答了几句后，黑坊主便会厌倦，啪地打个响指，命令猎犬扑向队伍。一旦战斗开始，他们将战斗至被摧毁为止。</p>\n<p><strong>你是谁？</strong>“我记不起来了，但无所谓。我随辛玥的心意行事，而她侍奉伟大的苦迦菩提。”</p>\n<p><strong>为什么这里有这么多尸体？</strong>“剩饭。食物。装饰。尸体还能有什么用？不过如果你问的是——在它们变成尸体之前我们拿身体做什么——那就，辛玥需要新鲜的血肉和温热的鲜血来取悦苦迦菩提，给他力量，让他能从坟墓里起身。你们是来献上自己的肉和汁液的吗？”</p>\n<p><strong>辛玥是谁？</strong>“她是我们的焦点，我们的理由，我们的目的。伟大的苦迦菩提命令我们追随她，于是我们就追随。自从我们到来，她只做过杀戮并把灵魂献给苦迦菩提。我想是这样。跟她待在一起很不愉快。你一定觉得，从我这种东西嘴里说出这话很刺耳吧。等你见到她就明白了。”</p>\n<p><strong>苦迦菩提是谁？</strong>“哦！你想见苦迦菩提？我们可以安排会面。只要别动……”（说到这里，苦迦菩提僧侣命令猎犬发动攻击。突如其来的攻击使这些生物在进行先攻检定时获得+2环境加值。）</p>\n\n<p><strong>囚犯：</strong>当辛玥在修道院大体被遗弃后接管此处时，她和追随者把这间房的一些储藏壁龛改成了临时牢房，用来关押抓来的祭品，通常是误闯遗迹的流浪猎人或探险者。</p>\n<p>当思维空间形成时，这个房间里唯一的囚犯——一个名叫卡伦·布雷的小贼——与其他僧侣一起死去，但他并未变成黑坊主。相反，他以僵尸之身复活，并保留了生前的记忆——而每当思维空间的循环重置时，这些记忆仍会保留。在过去的115年里，卡伦早已记不清究竟重置了多少次；他受损的记忆彼此混杂，使他只相信自己在这里“永远”受苦。</p>\n<p>卡伦生前来自艾巴萨罗姆，他来到神门的唯一目的就是掠夺物品，卖给内海地区各地的收藏家。听说有座被遗弃的修道院后，他便赶来勘察，结果却被辛玥的僧侣抓住。起初僧侣们打算几周后就献祭他，但卡伦被捕一周后思维空间便形成了；他新获得的不死状态让他不再适合作为祭品，于是他们干脆把他留在这里，让他真的一点点腐烂。</p>\n<p>卡伦对自己逃出牢房却被灵堕魔屠杀的记忆多到数不清，早已放弃尝试逃脱。他后来明白，最好的方式就是保持不动、“装死”。一旦PC们击败黑坊主及其地狱犬，卡伦便从麻木的呆滞中微微动了动，从最西北的壁龛里向PC们喊话——他在那里被镣铐锁在地面上。“哎，这可新鲜了！不是怪物的人？你们是谁？”</p>\n<p>卡伦会对PC撒谎，声称自己是个猎人，暴风雨时在这些遗迹里避难，却被住在这里的邪恶僧侣抓走；并请求PC们击败如今盘踞在上方遗迹中的怪物，好让他终于能逃出去。凭借他模糊的记忆，他能给PC一些令人抓狂又混乱的线索——告诉他们，他和住在这里的僧侣在“很久很久以前”的同一时间变成了不死生物，但他记不起原因。事实上，在PC们到来之前，他已经开始相信世上所有生命都已灭绝。</p>\n<p>卡伦是邪恶的，但并不特别危险；如果PC们帮他逃脱，他在该地区也不会惹出太多额外的麻烦——反而会转而过上潜伏在林中的生活，并最终招惹上一头怪物，被对方了结。他并不介意自己不死的外表，还说：“换身新衣服再戴个面具就遮得住。”作为放他出去的交换，他会向PC透露自己藏在区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e8storage00000]{E8}的那批宝藏的地点。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span>@UUID[Actor.RslmqUYHooPfdhDu]{卡伦·布雷}</span><span>生物 2</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不死</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不洁</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">僵尸</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E14. Storage Room</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This large basement might have once been used to store gardening equipment, barrels of fertilizer, lumber, and repair tools, but today it’s more like a slaughterhouse. The entire room is littered with the dismembered corpses and splattered internal organs of beasts and humanoid creatures, and the stink of decaying flesh makes breathing the cool air an agonizing chore.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The monks once used this large space as a storage area for materials and seasonal equipment, but most of the items were taken or donated when the monastery was abandoned. Since taking over, the Kugaptee cultists have been using this chamber as a dumping ground for sacrificial victims they’ve gone through over the years. The cold temperature slows decay just enough to make things truly awful in here.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hell-hound.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Storage Room</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bdOAkorJbVOqobUp]{Monk of Kugaptee} @UUID[Actor.sipFaaLMxLg8iB2b]{Hell Hounds (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> In addition to being a dumping ground for carcasses, this chamber provides access to the route leading to Kugaptee’s Grave, and as such, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue} didn’t want to leave the place unguarded. A kurobozu, once the monastery’s cook, now watches over this chamber, attended by Xin Yue’s favorite pets—a trio of slavering hell hounds that look more like burning feral foxes than they do dogs. As the PCs arrive, the kurobozu is entertaining themself by playing fetch with the hell hounds, using a well-chewed human skull for the game. Upon spotting the PCs, the hell hounds immediately bare their teeth and growl menacingly, but the kurobozu holds out a rotting hand to stay their attack, then proclaims that “it’s rude to interrupt someone’s idle moments. Why are you here? Why should I not feed you to my pets?”</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>If the PCs don’t immediately attack, they’ll find this nameless kurobozu somewhat eager for conversation. Potential answers to some questions the PCs might pose are listed below, but after answering a few, the kurobozu grows weary and, with a snap of their fingers, sics the hounds on the party. Once combat begins, they fight until destroyed.</p>\n<p><strong>Who are you?</strong> “I can’t remember, but it doesn’t matter. I serve at Xin Yue’s whim, and she serves the great Kugaptee.”</p>\n<p><strong>Why are there so many corpses here?</strong> “Leftovers. Food. Decoration. What other use do corpses have? If you mean what are we doing with the bodies before they become corpses, though, well, Xin Yue needs fresh flesh and warm blood to sate Kugaptee, to provide him with strength so that he may rise from his grave. Are you here to volunteer your meat and juices?”</p>\n<p><strong>Who is Xin Yue?</strong> “She is our focus, our reason, our purpose. Great Kugaptee bid us to follow her so we do. She has only killed and offered souls to Kugaptee since we arrived. I think. She’s quite unpleasant to be around. You must think that’s quite disturbing coming from someone like me. You’ll understand when you meet her.”</p>\n<p><strong>Who is Kugaptee?</strong> “Oh! You wish to meet Kugaptee? We can arrange a meeting. Just hold still...” (At this, the monk of Kugaptee orders the hounds to attack. The suddenness of the attack grants the creatures a +2 circumstance bonus to their initiative rolls.)</p>\n\n<p><strong>Prisoner:</strong> When Xin Yue took over after the monastery was mostly abandoned, she and her followers used of some of this chamber’s storage alcoves as improvised prisons for captured sacrifices, usually wandering hunters or explorers who stumbled upon the ruins.</p>\n<p>When the mindscape formed, this room’s sole prisoner, a small-time thief named Kalen Bray, perished along with the other monks, yet he didn’t rise as a kurobozu. Instead, he rose as a zombie who retained his memories from life—and each time the mindscape cycle resets, those memories remain. Over the past 115 years, Kalen has lost track of just how many times things have reset, and his damaged memories have merged so that he simply believes he’s languished here “forever.”</p>\n<p>In life, Kalen hailed from Absalom, and he came to Shenmen solely to plunder items to sell to collectors throughout the Inner Sea Region. After hearing of the abandoned monastery, he made his way over to survey the grounds, only to be captured by Xin Yue’s monks. The monks initially intended to sacrifice him in a few weeks, but when the mindscape formed a week after Kalen’s capture, his new undead state rendered him useless for such a purpose, and so they’ve simply left him here to literally rot.</p>\n<p>Kalen has so many memories of escaping his cell only to be slaughtered by nindorus that he’s long since given up trying to escape. He’s since learned that it’s best to remain still and “play dead.” Once the PCs defeat the kurobozu and their hell hounds, Kalen stirs from his torpor and calls out to the PCs from the northwesternmost alcove, where he’s chained to the floor with manacles. “Well, this is new! People who aren’t monsters? Who might you be?”</p>\n<p>Kalen Lies to the PCs, claiming to have been a hunter who took shelter in these ruins during a storm only to be captured by the evil monks who live here, and asks the PCs to defeat the monsters that now live in the ruins above so he can finally escape. With his vague memories, he can give the PCs some maddening and confusing clues—telling them that he and the monks who dwell here became undead at the same time “many, many years ago,” but he can’t remember why. In fact, until the PCs’ arrival, he’d come to believe that all life had perished in the world.</p>\n<p>Kalen is evil but not particularly dangerous, and if the PCs help him escape, he won’t cause much additional mischief in the region—instead taking to a life lurking in the woods and eventually running afoul of a monster that finishes him off. He’s not bothered by his undead appearance, stating, “It’s nothing some new clothes and a mask can’t hide.” In return for promising to let him out, he reveals to the PCs the location of the stash of treasure he hid in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e8storage00000]{E8}.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span>@UUID[Actor.RslmqUYHooPfdhDu]{Kalen Bray}</span><span>Creature 2</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Undead</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Zombie</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Tan Sugi": {
              "name": "谭杉 The Tan Sugi",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E13. 谭隋靖</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一棵巨大、高达一百英尺的杉树耸立在这片杂草丛生的庭院中，让整座寺院都笼罩在它的阴影下。数条闪着湿光的腐烂与朽坏之带自几处树根向上蔓延，缠绕着树干；而更高处的许多枝桠上，则密布着层层厚重的巨大蛛网。一把银刃大斧嵌在离地约四英尺高的树干侧面；黑色树液结成硬痂的细流在伤口处发亮，沿着树干淌下。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-shadow-of-kugapte.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shadow of Kugaptee\" alt=\"Shadow of Kugaptee\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-shadow-of-kugapte.webp');width:50%\" />\n\n<p>这棵异常巨大的杉树，生长在谭隋靖与苦迦菩提一战之后身亡之处。正是她为阻止那死去的邪魔再度转生，而转世的灵魂所化成的那一棵。自树根向上蔓延的腐坏起始于下方的一间地下密室（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}）；在过去115年里，这种腐坏每年都会重置，但由于真世中马戈·凯的插手导致苦迦菩提的影响不断增长，使这一过程加速——若PC们不加以阻止，至隆冬时分，谭隋靖这棵杉树将会倒塌，苦迦菩提将逃脱；该事件会摧毁整个思维空间，将其中被困的灵魂（包括PC们）尽数吸收进苦迦菩提之中，并把这强大的邪魔释放到现代世界。苦迦菩提逃入现代世界的后果超出了本次冒险的范围，但本书的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog16contin]{Continuing the Campaign} 中做了简要讨论。</p>\n<p>有些PC也许会想到砍倒这棵杉树，但这么做只会加速终局，给柳岸镇（以及PC们）带来与任其腐朽同样的毁灭（如上所述）。虽然这样能阻止苦迦菩提立刻在现代世界重生，但也只是延后这一如今已不可避免的结果。若PC们坚持执行这种自毁计划，他们应当会收到幻象，或来自 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} 的警告：若要有任何希望解除柳岸镇的诅咒，这棵杉树就必须活下去。</p>\n<p>一名PC若成功通过一次 @Check[nature|dc:20] 检定，会注意到使树木患病的苦难会在数月内杀死它，而其源头似乎来自地下某处。</p>\n<p>当PC们靠近树时，让他们进行秘密的 @Check[perception|dc:24] 检定。成功者会注意到在靠近树干、约75英尺高的几根枝杈间，一团蛛网中有某物微微泛着淡蓝色光芒（天黑后，此DC降为 @Check[perception|dc:17]）。以大成功通过者会注意到光芒的源头是一颗木制雕像头部，部分被蛛网包裹。</p>\n<p>要攀爬这棵杉树，PC必须成功通过一次 @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-undeadkitsune.webp\" data-tooltip=\"The Chewer\" alt=\"The Chewer, male kurobozu kitsune\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-undeadkitsune.webp');width:55%\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>笼罩杉树的蛛网源自苦迦菩提思绪的另一种显现——一只巨大而令人惊惧的食人魔蛛。然而，这片区域的居住者并不只有这只巨蛛。PC们第一次进入庭院时，蜘蛛潜伏在上方枝头，位于50英尺高处，暂时一动不动。下方，在树根间蹲着一个令人不安的身影——一名身披破布的亡灵狐人；他一边蜷伏着，一边啃咬树皮。此人曾是心月最忠诚的追随者之一，是一名钻研园艺的僧侣；当他在思维空间中转生为黑坊主后，忘记了自己的名字，也忘记了前生的许多事。如今，这名亡灵僧侣只称自己为“咀嚼者”，因为他自告奋勇啃咬杉树的树根，试图加速其腐坏。到目前为止，他的努力收效甚微，但仔细查看会发现有几处被他啃咬过的根部出现了感染区域。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-undeadkitsune.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">谭隋靖</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Y5zDh5oQrdwzR3My]{The Chewer} @UUID[Actor.EGr8S808E890Cmft]{Ogre Spider}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>咀嚼者注意到PC们后直起身子，把嘴里的树皮碎屑啐出来，随后邀请他们加入他的“用餐”，并指出“更多的牙齿会更快放倒这棵凄凉的树——你们总不至于残忍到让它继续受苦吧？”咀嚼者很乐于与PC们交谈，但他能透露的内容并不多，除了确认这棵树是过去一位伟大女英雄的遗骸所生长出的。只要树仍在生长，她的灵魂就会一直被困，无法进入生命的轮回。亡灵僧侣希望用这套说辞拉拢PC们协助自己；一旦遭到反驳，他很快就会变得不耐烦并愤怒。用不了多久，咀嚼者就会被迫发起攻击；届时他会拔出他的寺院佩刀，战斗至被摧毁为止。一旦战斗开始，食人魔蛛也会从树上攀下加入战斗。咀嚼者不会追击逃跑的PC，但食人魔蛛会；它会利用自己诡异的柔韧性穿梭在寺院中追猎队伍。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>财宝：</strong> @UUID[Actor.lHjir7rIumzg0Vui]{Trunk} <br />\n  嵌在树干里的那把斧头，属于7062年曾来到寺院的伐木者首领；他只挥了一斧就惨遭屠戮。一名PC若成功通过一次 @Check[athletics|dc:22] 检定，便可将斧头拔出。多年下来，谭隋靖的影响进一步为这把斧头赋予了魔法性质，如今它是一把<em>+1 幽冥 强击 银质战斧</em>；但在下方苦迦菩提之墓中的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{心月} 被击败之前，这件武器带有一个令人不安的怪癖——每次拔出它，都会有把斧头埋进朋友头骨里的冲动侵入使用者的脑海，使使用者陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{惊惧 1}，除非其成功通过一次 @Check[will|dc:20|traits:emotion,fear,mental] 豁免（该怪癖具有 emotion、fear 与 mental 特征，并会在心月被击败后立刻消失）。\n</p>\n<p>卡在上方75英尺处蛛网中的发光雕像头，是区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e5pharasmass00]{E5} 中 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛} 雕像所缺失的头部。一旦咀嚼者与食人魔蛛被击败，光芒会增强，使任何用以注意到它的DC降低10。当某名PC触碰到头部时，光芒立刻消退，但会令该PC心中充满将头部送回雕像的冲动——该角色在进行任何用于净化那座雕像的检定时，获得+2物品加值。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E13. The Tan Sugi</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A massive, one-hundred-foot-tall sugi tree towers over this overgrown courtyard, bathing the monastery in its shadow. Glistening coils of rot and decay spread up from several of the tree’s roots to wind along its trunk, while many branches above are thick with immense spiderwebs. A large silver-bladed axe lies embedded in the side of the tree trunk about four feet off the ground; crusty rivulets of black sap glisten and run down from the wound.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-shadow-of-kugapte.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shadow of Kugaptee\" alt=\"Shadow of Kugaptee\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-shadow-of-kugapte.webp');width:50%\" />\n\n<p>This unusually enormous sugi tree grows at the site of Tan Sui-Jing’s death following her battle with Kugaptee. It’s the very one that she reincarnated into in order to keep the dead fiend from reincarnating himself. The decay spreading up from the roots starts in an underground chamber below (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}); while it has reset every year for the past 115 years, Kugaptee’s growing influence as the result of Mago Kai’s meddling in the real world has accelerated the process—if the PCs don’t put a stop to it, by midwinter, the Tan Sugi tree will fall, and Kugaptee will escape, an event that will destroy the entire mindscape, absorb the souls trapped within (including the PCs) into Kugaptee, and release the powerful fiend into the modern world. The implications of Kugaptee’s escape into the modern world are beyond the scope of this adventure but are discussed briefly in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog16contin]{Continuing the Campaign} of this book.</p>\n<p>The notion of chopping down the sugi tree might come to some of the PCs, but this pursuit would only hasten the end, resulting in the same devastation to Willowshore (and to the PCs) that allowing the tree to decay would (as detailed above). While doing so would prevent Kugaptee from being immediately reborn into the modern world, this only delays that now inevitable outcome. If the PCs insist on pursuing such a self-destructive plan, they should receive visions, or perhaps warnings from @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}, that the sugi tree must live if there’s to be any hope in lifting Willowshore’s curse.</p>\n<p>A PC who succeeds at a @Check[nature|dc:20] check notes that the affliction sickening the tree will kill it in a few months, and its source seems to be coming from somewhere underground.</p>\n<p>As the PCs approach the tree, allow them to make secret @Check[perception|dc:24] checks. Those who succeed notice something shimmering with a faint blue glow in a clot of spiderwebs among several branches about 75 feet up near the tree’s trunk (after dark, this DC drops to @Check[perception|dc:17]). With a critical success, a PC notices that the source of this glow is a wooden statue head wrapped partially in spiderwebs.</p>\n<p>To Climb the sugi tree, a PC must succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb].</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-undeadkitsune.webp\" data-tooltip=\"The Chewer\" alt=\"The Chewer, male kurobozu kitsune\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-undeadkitsune.webp');width:55%\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The source of spiderwebs that shroud the sugi tree is another manifestation of Kugaptee’s thoughts—an immense and frightening ogre spider. However, the enormous spider isn’t the only occupant in the area. The first time the PCs enter the courtyard, the spider lurks in the branches above, visible at a height of 50 feet but motionless for the moment. Down below, squatting among the tree’s roots as he gnaws and chews at the bark, is an unsettling figure—an undead kitsune dressed in rags. This individual was one of Xin Yue’s most loyal followers, a horticulturist monk who forgot his name as well as much of his previous life when he was reborn in the mindscape as a kurobozu. Now, the undead monk simply refers to himself as the Chewer, for he has taken it upon himself to gnaw at the sugi’s roots in an attempt to quicken its decay. So far, his efforts have had minimal results, but closer inspection reveals several infected areas among the roots where he has been chewing.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-undeadkitsune.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Tan Suhi</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Y5zDh5oQrdwzR3My]{The Chewer} @UUID[Actor.EGr8S808E890Cmft]{Ogre Spider}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The Chewer straightens up and spits bits of bark out of his mouth as he notices the PCs, then invites them to join him at his “meal,” noting that “more teeth will bring down this forlorn tree more quickly—surely you aren’t cruel-minded enough to let it continue to suffer?” The Chewer is delighted to speak to the PCs but doesn’t really have much to reveal to them other than to confirm that this tree grew from the remains of a great heroine from the past. As long as the tree still grows, her soul remains trapped and outside of the cycle of life. The undead monk hopes to use this line of reasoning to recruit the aid of the PCs and quickly grows impatient and angry if he’s contradicted. It shouldn’t be long before the Chewer is compelled to attack, at which point he draws his temple sword and fights until destroyed. Once combat begins, the ogre spider clambers down from the tree to join the fight as well. While the Chewer won’t pursue fleeing PCs, the ogre spider will, taking advantage of its eerie flexibility to chase the party through the monastery.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.lHjir7rIumzg0Vui]{Trunk} <br />\n  The axe embedded in the tree trunk belonged to the leader of the woodcutters who came to the monastery back in 7062; he was slaughtered after making only one swing with the axe. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[athletics|dc:22] check can pull the axe free. Over the years, Tan Sui-Jing’s influence has further enhanced this axe with magical properties, and it’s now a <em>+1 ghost touch striking silver battle axe</em>, but until @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue} is defeated in Kugaptee’s grave below, this weapon bears an unsettling quirk—each time it’s drawn, unsettling urges to bury the axe in the skull of a friend invade the user’s mind, causing the user to become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1} unless they succeed at a @Check[will|dc:20|traits:emotion,fear,mental] save (this quirk has the emotion, fear, and mental traits and vanishes as soon as Xin Yue is defeated).\n</p>\n<p>The glowing statue head lodged in a web 75 feet up is the missing head to the statue of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e5pharasmass00]{E5}. Once the Chewer and the ogre spider are defeated, the glow increases, reducing any DC to notice it by 10. The glow fades as soon as a PC touches the head but fills that PC with the urge to return the head to the statue—that character gains a +2 item bonus to any checks to purify that statue.</p>"
            },
            "Burial Garden": {
              "name": "葬园 Burial Garden",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E12. 埋葬花园</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房里的空气潮湿，且异常温暖。房间中央摆着一排四个长20英尺的木制种植箱，里面装满泥土；每个种植箱都被病态的杂草、潮湿的真菌以及闪着光泽的藤蔓所覆盖。东侧有一张矮桌，周围放着发霉的坐垫；东北侧靠近一扇小木门处，立着一尊被潮湿病藤缠满的雄鹿雕像。</p>\n</div>\n<p>东北侧的门通往下方的储藏室（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e14storagero00]{E14}）。</p>\n<p>在寺院被废弃之前，这间大房间是僧侣们用来种植食物、培育花卉以及处理死者的地方。对谭杉寺的僧侣而言，像谭隋靖那样转世为植物的概念，代表着一种特定形式的开悟；当有僧侣死去时，他们会被埋进这里的种植箱里，使遗骸能滋养那些他们的灵魂希望转世成的植物。一旦遗体只剩白骨，这些骨头就会在一场漫长而复杂的仪式中被敬奉：将遗骨掘出、研成粉末，再洒回土壤之中。僧侣们希望借此强化谭隋靖（但愿永恒的）对苦迦菩提坟墓的守望。对某些人而言这也许是阴森的传统；但对僧侣们来说（他们相信灵魂一旦离开肉身，就会有新的身体等待着他们），死亡后留下的遗骸不过是过去的遗物。此处曾具备强力的魔法效应，使这里的植物即便在室内也能生长繁茂，但寺院一旦废弃，这些效应很快便消散了。</p>\n<p>寺院的废弃以及其沦陷于那些被苦迦菩提腐化之物，已在这间房内以实体方式显现：曾经在此生长的美丽、健壮且富有营养的植物，如今被病态杂草与寄生真菌取代。室内空气潮湿黏稠，充斥着恶臭孢子；任何非植物或非真菌的生物，只要在该房间内开始其回合，就必须进行一次 @Check[fortitude|dc:20] 豁免，否则陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1}（大失败则为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 2}）。这是嗅觉与毒素效果；若角色在该豁免中大成功，则在24小时内对其暂时免疫。</p>\n<p>雄鹿雕像是必须被净化的四尊雕像之一；只有净化它们，才能获得进入苦迦菩提坟墓的许可，并与 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智辉} 的幽灵交谈。但在开始这一过程之前，必须先击败这间房里危险的真菌。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/fungus-leshy.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">埋葬花园</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.qe6TeAuJRX2zPaS2]{真菌莱西（6）} @UUID[Actor.HG9HAFwYEPEWFw5l]{黏菌怪（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC开始在房间内移动时，种植箱各处生长的数团真菌开始颤动，并踉跄着活动起来。它们被苦迦菩提的梦中之死赋予生命，又被灵堕魔半神的虐待欲与残忍所浸染，于是这些真菌怪物挺身而起发动攻击，渴望谋杀PC，并将他们的尸体拖入泥土，作为更多肥料供其生长。这些生物由两只黏菌怪（无心智的掠食者，却仍以令人不安的残酷感发动攻击，偏好寻找生命值较低的目标）与六只残忍的真菌莱西组成；每只真菌莱西都会将骨头的碎片与残片嵌进它们畸形、勉强呈类人外观的身体中。除了潮湿的真菌物质挪动时发出的声响外，所有这些生物在战斗中都诡异地保持沉默，而且它们不会追击离开此房间的敌人。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.QYcPdXc1CPMTj1GP]{花园} <br />\n  若PC杀死这些真菌，花费10分钟搜寻房间的PC会发现僧侣们留下的几件宝藏：一株<em>远古槲寄生</em>缠在其中一只真菌莱西的残骸上；以及一根<em>翠绿法杖</em>， леж在雄鹿雕像后方地面上、被数条恶臭藤蔓压着。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC净化雄鹿雕像，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E12. Burial Garden</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The air in this chamber feels humid and unusually warm. A row of four twenty-foot-long wooden planter boxes filled with earth sit in the middle of the room, each overgrown with diseased-looking weeds, damp fungi, and glistening vines. A low table with moldy cushions around it sits to the east, near a small wooden door to the northeast; a statue of a stag covered with damp, diseased vines stands near this door.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The northeast door leads down to the storeroom (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e14storagero00]{E14}).</p>\n<p>Before the monastery was abandoned, this large room served the monks as a place to grow food, cultivate flowers, and dispose of the dead. To the monks of the Tan Sugi monastery, the concept of being reincarnated as a plant, as Tan Sui-Jing was, represented a specific form of enlightenment, and when a monk died, they were buried in the planter boxes here so their remains could nurture the plants their spirits hoped to reincarnate into. Once a body was reduced to bones, those bones were honored in a long, complex ritual that included the remains being exhumed, powdered, and then sprinkled back into the soil. In this way, the monks hoped to bolster Tan Sui-Jing’s (hopefully eternal) vigil over Kugaptee’s grave. Perhaps a grim tradition to some, to the monks (who believed that once the spirit moved on from the body, a new body awaited them), the remains left behind after death were simply a relic of the past. This place once had potent magical effects to help give the plants here a place to grow and thrive despite being indoors, but those effects quickly faded once the monastery was abandoned.</p>\n<p>The abandonment of the monastery and its fall to those corrupted by Kugaptee manifests within this chamber physically, for the beautiful, hearty, and nutritious plants that grew here have been replaced by diseased weeds and parasitic fungi. The air in this room is humid and thick with foul-smelling spores; a non-plant or non-fungus creature that begins its turn in this room must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:20] save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1} (@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2} on a critical failure). This is an olfactory and poison effect, and if a character critically succeeds at the saving throw, they’re temporarily immune to it for 24 hours.</p>\n<p>The stag statue is one of the four statues that must be purified in order to gain access to Kugaptee’s grave and speak to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s ghost, but before this process can be started, the dangerous fungi in this chamber must be defeated.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/fungus-leshy.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Burial Garden</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.qe6TeAuJRX2zPaS2]{Fungus Leshies (6)} @UUID[Actor.HG9HAFwYEPEWFw5l]{Slime Molds (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Once the PCs begin to move through the room, several clots of fungi growing throughout the planter boxes begin to shudder and lurch into motion. Given life by Kugaptee’s dreaming death and infused with the nindoru demigod’s sadism and cruelty, these fungal monsters rise up and attack, eager to murder the PCs and drag their bodies into the dirt to be used as yet more fertilizer for them to grow in. The creatures consist of two slime molds (mindless predators that still attack with an unsettling sense of cruelty, preferring to seek out lower Hit Point targets) and six cruel fungus leshies, each of which incorporates fragments and pieces of bone into their malformed, barely-humanoid-looking bodies. Apart from the wet sound of shifting fungal matter, all these creatures remain eerily silent as they fight, and they don’t pursue foes out of this room.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.QYcPdXc1CPMTj1GP]{Garden} <br />\n  If the PCs kill the fungi, a PC who spends 10 minutes Searching the room uncovers a few treasures left behind by the monks: a <em>primeval mistletoe</em> tangled up in the remains of one of the fungus leshies, and a <em>verdant staff</em> lying under several nasty-smelling vines on the ground behind the stag statue.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs purify the stag statue, grant them 40 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Hidden Library": {
              "name": "藏匿的图书馆 Hidden Library",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E11. 隐秘图书馆</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>书架沿着这间房的大多数墙面排开，房间中央摆着一张低矮的圆桌，周围围着坐垫。一具骷髅瘫倒在桌上，手里握着一支羽毛笔，颅骨下压着一本摊开的书。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这具骷髅属于谭杉寺最后一位忠诚的僧侣严蕊。她战斗至最后一刻以抵抗库加普提的腐化，却最终被迫退入此室，而其余僧侣则在附近的图书馆中尽数殒命。她设法维持魔法结界以阻止他人进入图书馆，但她没料到叛徒们竟只是把门锁死，将她封在其中，把这间房变成了她的墓穴。她最终因口渴而死，但在此之前，她竭尽所能确保自己关于库加普提的研究得以记录下来。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/poltergeist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">隐秘图书馆</span> <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.cqYzLo7R7P0f9Lqu]{严蕊的骚灵（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>严蕊的灵魂如今栖居于此，但她并未显化为幽灵；相反，她强大的魔法能力渗入了这座隐秘图书馆中所存的每一部典籍。她现在以无形的存在徘徊于室内，无法离开，却足以阻止库加普提的信徒入内。如有必要，她可以在此室内实体显现以保护此地——将这些显现视为三只精英骚灵，但她不太可能需要做到这一步，便能抵御PC们对房间的威胁。</p>\n  <p>PC们进入房间后不久，严蕊便会向他们致意；她以无形之声说话，仿佛同时从房间的每个角落低语而来。她尽力安抚PC们对她可能是邪恶幽灵或作祟之物的担忧，承诺只要他们说明来意，她就能帮忙。她静静聆听PC们的陈述，并尽己所能提供指引：劝PC们继续净化雕像；就寺院的布局提供建议（她不知道如今各房间里有什么危险，但至少能告诉PC们其他受腐化雕像所在的位置）；并保证他们可以在此休息与恢复，因为寺中的邪祟不会打扰他们的睡眠。你也可以让严蕊回答PC们的其他问题。其中一些回答可能与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智慧}能给出的答案相似（第364页）；或者，你也可以让严蕊坦承不知情，但建议PC们继续净化雕像，以便之后向智慧本人提问。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.nPZZarpBXhLc6Dlq]{颅骨} @UUID[Actor.HYVG5wJpk4duYOkl]{书架} <br />\n  颅骨下那本摊开的书中包含严蕊的笔记；若PC们不与她交谈，而是决定摧毁骚灵，这些笔记能让他们获得上文信息。</p>\n<p>此室中存放的大多数书籍与卷轴都与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}的教义有关；但其中还有一小批格外稀有的书籍，构成了一套相当可观的收藏：当在与该哲学相关的话题上进行调查或进行回忆知识时，这套收藏为善解背景、宁多鲁背景与宗教检定提供+2物品加值。整套收藏共12体积，价值600 gp。不过，对PC们而言，这套收藏的最大价值在于下一幕：他们将用其学习关于柳岸镇思维空间的真相。</p>\n<p>\n  若要彻底搜查这里的书架需要1小时；但如果PC们与严蕊关系友好，她会将下列重要物品呈给PC们以示感谢，让它们从书架上漂浮而出。这些宝物包括一册<em>次等滋补清洁书卷</em>、数张卷轴（<em>纠缠命运</em>卷轴、<em>生命的新绽</em>卷轴、<em>预言家之运</em>卷轴、<em>神圣雨云</em>卷轴、<em>明日黎明</em>卷轴，以及<em>镜墙术</em>卷轴；这些新法术均详述于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20newspells00000]{冒险工具箱}），以及一本封面题为《轮回守望者》的厚书。该书前半部收录了数百则短寓言与故事，采集自多种宗教传统，并逐一筛选以呈现其能给予善解追随者的教益。若某个角色在研究任何与善解或转世相关的主题时引用此书，则其进行回忆知识的善解背景或宗教检定获得+1物品加值。书的后半部记载了若干仪式的配方，包括<em>食月</em>、<em>终夜守夜</em>、<em>掠夺黑夜</em>、<em>招待失者</em>与<em>如蜜冬至</em>（这些仪式均详述于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20newspells00000]{冒险工具箱}，从第310页开始）。书的最后几页则记录了<em>转生术</em>仪式的配方。《轮回守望者》价值90 gp。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们与严蕊交谈并成功了解她所知之事，给予他们120 XP。</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>转生</h1>\n  <p>如果PC们从<em>《轮回守望者》</em>中学会<em>转生术</em>，他们就能按常规使用该仪式，让死者在一具新身体中复活。当他们这么做时，被转生的生物仍是柳岸镇思维空间的一部分，且不会获得关于思维空间本质的任何洞见；他们的“活着”只是在思维空间语境下成立——作为被困于思维空间中的灵魂而存在，正如PC们自本冒险路径开篇以来一直如此。到了本冒险路径的后期，对转生术的知识将变得极其重要：PC们将利用这份知识去研究一种方法，借此撤销柳岸镇思维空间，并让一切回归到现代的、真实活着的世界。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E11. Hidden Library</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Shelves line most of this room’s walls, while a low round table sits in the middle of the room, surrounded by sitting cushions. A skeleton lies slumped over the table, a writing quill in hand and an open book under the skull.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The skeleton belongs to Yen Rui, the last loyal monk of the Tan Sugi monastery. She’d fought to the end to resist Kugaptee’s corruption, only to be forced into this room while the remaining monks perished in the nearby library. She managed to maintain magical wards to prevent entry into the library, but she hadn’t expected the traitors to simply lock the doors, sealing her in and turning this chamber into her crypt. She perished of thirst, but not before she did her best to ensure her research on Kugaptee was recorded.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/poltergeist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Hidden library</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.cqYzLo7R7P0f9Lqu]{Yen Rui's Poltergeists (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Yen Rui’s spirit dwells here now, but rather than manifest as a ghost, her potent magical abilities infused every single text stored in this hidden library. She now exists as a disembodied presence in the room, unable to leave yet empowered well enough to prevent Kugaptee’s faithful from entering. If she must, she can manifest physically in this room to protect it—treat these manifestations as three elite poltergeists, but it’s unlikely she’ll need to do so to defend the room against the PCs.</p>\n  <p>Yen Rui greets the PCs soon after they enter the room, speaking in a disembodied voice that seems to whisper from all corners of the room at once. She does her best to soothe the PCs’ fears that she might be a sinister ghost or haunt, promising that she can help if they tell her what they’re here for. She listens quietly as the PCs speak and provides what guidance she can, urging the PCs to continue to purify the statues, giving them advice on the monastery’s layout (she doesn’t know what dangers await in the rooms now but can, at the very least, tell the PCs where the other corrupted statues are), and promising that they can rest and recuperate here knowing that the evils in the monastery won’t interrupt their sleep. You can use Yen Rui to answer other questions the PCs might have. Some of these responses might be similar to answers that @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} can give (page 364); alternatively, you can have Yen Rui admit ignorance but then suggest the PCs continue purifying statues so they can ask these questions of Zhi Hui herself.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.nPZZarpBXhLc6Dlq]{Skull} @UUID[Actor.HYVG5wJpk4duYOkl]{Book Shelves} <br />\n  The open book under the skull contains Yen Rui’s notes, giving the PCs access to the information above if, instead of speaking to her, they decide to destroy the poltergeists.\n</p>\n<p>The majority of the books and scrolls stored in this room concern the teachings of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi}, but a smaller selection of particularly rare books makes up a significant collection that, as a whole, grants a +2 item bonus to Sangpotshi Lore, Nindoru Lore, and Religion checks while Investigating or Recalling Knowledge on topics related to this philosophy; the collection in all is 12 Bulk and worth 600 gp. This collection’s greatest value to the PCs, though, is their use in the next act when learning the truth about the Willowshore mindscape.</p>\n<p>\n  A full search of the shelves here takes an hour, but if the PCs are on friendly terms with Yen Rui, she presents the following important items to the PCs as thanks, causing them to float off their shelves. These treasures include a\n  <em>lesser tome of restorative cleansing</em>, several scrolls (a <em>scroll of entangle fate</em>, a <em>scroll of life’s fresh bloom</em>, a <em>scroll of prophet’s luck</em>, a <em>scroll of sacred nimbus</em>, a <em>scroll of tomorrow’s dawn</em>, and a <em>scroll of wall of mirrors</em>; all of these new spells are detailed the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20newspells00000]{Adventure Toolbx}), and a large book bearing the title Watchers of the Cycle. The first half of this book contains hundreds of short parables and stories culled from a wide range of religions, each curated for the lessons they can impart to a follower of Sangpotshi. If a character references this book while researching any topic relating to Sangpotshi or reincarnation, they gain a +1 item bonus to any Sangpotshi Lore or Religion checks to Recall Knowledge. The second half of the book contains the formulas for several rituals, including <em>gnaw at the moon</em>, <em>last night’s vigil</em>, <em>ransack the night</em>, <em>regale the lost ones</em>, and <em>sweetest solstice</em> (all of these rituals are detailed the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20newspells00000]{Adventure Toolbox}, starting on page 310). The final pages of the book contain the formula for the ritual <em>reincarnate</em>. Watchers of the Cycle is worth 90 gp.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs speak with Yen Rui and manage to learn what she knows, grant them 120 XP.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Reincarnation</h1>\n  <p>If the PCs learn <em>reincarnate</em> from <em>Watchers of the Cycle</em>, they’ll be able to use the ritual normally to bring the dead back to life in a new body. When they do, the reincarnated creature remains a part of the Willowshore mindscape and receives no insight into the nature of the mindscape, and they’re “alive” only in the context of being a trapped soul within the mindscape, just as the PCs have been since the start of this Adventure Path. Later in this Adventure Path, knowledge of reincarnate will become incredibly important, as the PCs will use this knowledge to research a method by which they can undo the Willowshore mindscape and return everything to the modern, living world.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Library": {
              "name": "图书馆 Library",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E10. 图书馆</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>\n    这间图书馆的墙壁已被熏得焦黑，烧毁后灰白破烂的书架残片在屋顶塌陷处滴落着污浊的雨水，落到地面上。书籍与卷轴被撕成碎片，所有家具都被掀翻倒地。\n  </p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  在曾经属于谭杉寺图书馆的焦黑瓦砾中，几乎没剩下几本书。僧侣们花了数十年将寺院的图书馆建设成宗教知识的储藏所，但当欣月与她的追随者带着她们豢养的地狱犬在此与最后几名幸存僧侣对峙时，一切都被毁于一旦。随之而来的大火让房间化为废墟，使寺院中最后的未被腐化僧侣尽数死去，并让 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{欣月} 更加坚信自己做出了正确的选择。\n</p>\n<p>\n  通往隐秘图书馆（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}）的秘密门，可由在门的大致位置进行搜寻（Seek）的PC发现，或由花费10分钟搜索房间并成功通过一次\n  @Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 检定的PC发现，除非PC已净化了\n  至少两尊雕像：在那种情况下，一旦他们接近至距门20尺内，门就会柔和地发光，使其自动被发现。若门在发光，则门未上锁；否则，PC必须以成功的\n  @Check[athletics|dc:27|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定破拆（Force Open）大门，或以成功的 @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock]\n  检定开锁（Pick the Lock）。\n</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n  <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-ijda.webp\" />\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">图书馆</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n  <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.jcCnDDp13OAELZiL]{伊吉达（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <strong>生物：</strong>一对笨重的伊吉达灵堕魔在此房间里蹒跚游荡，时不时用它们的破损打刀翻拨灰烬，挑起一页残破书页端详片刻后丢弃，或只是茫然望向远方。它们对PC的到来没有反应，直到它们受到攻击（此时它们会战斗至死）、被搭话，或有人靠近。后两种情况下，其中一只伊吉达仍无视PC，另一只则用低沉而空洞的声音问道：“你记得吗？这里曾有什么？你记得吗？谁曾在这里？”PC可以通过编造故事来对这些邪魔撒谎，或尽其所知尝试讲述真相。无论哪种方式，他们都必须尝试一次 @Check[deception|dc:22] 或 @Check[diplomacy|dc:22] 检定。\n<p></p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n  <strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 灵堕魔对这些揭示感到震惊，其中一只说出房间内那本隐蔽的守护祷文书的位置（见下文宝藏），并说道：“那你肯定也记得这个吧？”除非PC在第一次会面时先动手，否则灵堕魔不会攻击；但若PC之后返回此房间，这些邪魔会立刻发动攻击——它们已经忘了之前的遭遇。若PC在离开前攻击灵堕魔，这些心不在焉的邪魔会为先攻进行纯骰检定，而非察觉检定。\n</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 同大成功或大失败，但邪魔不会提及宝藏。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n  <strong>失败</strong> 邪魔摇晃着它们空空的笼状头颅，随后悲戚地说道：“你若不记得，为何要对我们撒谎？也许你临死的惨叫会揭示真相！”然后它们发动攻击。\n</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n  <strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 同失败，但PC笨拙的叙述令邪魔暴怒，使其在战斗开始后的前两轮获得加速；它们只能用额外动作进行移动（Stride）或打击（Strike）。\n</p>\n  </section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.G67uVoAaG7eTgO5s]{瓦砾} <br /> 尽管图书馆已彻底破败，但并非所有东西都在大火中毁去。\n  细心的PC若花费至少10分钟在瓦砾中搜索，会在一层灰烬之下发现一本献给 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛} 的<em>守护祷文书</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E10. Library</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>\n    The walls of this library have been charred black, and the tatters of burned and ash-grayed shelves drip dirty\n    rainwater onto the floor where the roof has caved in. Books and scrolls have been shredded to pieces, and all of\n    the furniture has been overturned.\n  </p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  Few books remain in the burned rubble of what once was the Tan Sugi monastery’s library. The monks spent decades\n  building up the monastery’s library as a storehouse of religious knowledge, but all of that was destroyed when Xin\n  Yue and her followers confronted the last few remaining monks here with their pet hell hounds. The resulting fire\n  left the room in ruins, the final non-corrupted monks in the monastery dead, and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue} with the conviction that\n  she’d made the right choice.\n</p>\n<p>\n  The secret door to the hidden library (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}) can be found by a PC who Seeks in the door’s approximate location\n  or spends 10 minutes to Search the room and succeeds at a\n  @Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check, unless the PCs have\n  purified at\n  least two of the statues, in which case the door glows softly once they approach within 20 feet of it, making its\n  discovery automatic. The door is unlocked if it’s glowing; otherwise, a PC must either Force Open the door with a\n  successful @Check[athletics|dc:27|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check or\n  Pick the Lock with a successful @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock]\n  check.\n</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n  <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-ijda.webp\" />\n  <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Library</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n  <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.jcCnDDp13OAELZiL]{Ijda (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of lumbering ijda nindorus shamble through this room, periodically sifting through the ashes\n  with their broken katanas, lifting up a ruined page to peer at it before discarding it or simply staring into the\n  distance. They don’t react to the PCs’ arrival until they’re attacked (in which case they fight to the death),\n  addressed, or approached. In the latter two cases, one of the ijdas continues to ignore the PCs while the other\n  asks in a deep, hollow-sounding voice, “Do you remember? What was here? Do you remember? Who was here?” The PCs can Lie\n  to the fiends by making up a story, or they can attempt to tell the truth as far as they know. In either case,\n  they must attempt a @Check[deception|dc:22] or @Check[diplomacy|dc:22] check.\n<p></p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n  <strong>Critical Success</strong> The nindorus are astounded at the revelations, and one of them reveals the location of the hidden\n  book of warding prayers in the room (see Treasure, below), saying, “Then surely you must remember this?” The\n  nindorus don’t attack unless the PCs do during their first meeting, but if the PCs return later to this room, the\n  fiends attack at once, having forgotten the encounter already. If the PCs attack the nindorus before leaving, the\n  distracted fiends roll flat checks for initiative rather than Perception checks.\n</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the fiends don’t mention the treasure.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n  <strong>Failure</strong> The fiends shake their empty cage-heads, then mournfully say, “If you don’t remember, why lie to us?\n  Perhaps your dying screams will reveal the truth!” before they attack.\n</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n  <strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the PCs’ fumbling narrative so enrages the fiends that for the first two rounds\n  of combat, they’re quickened; they can use the extra action only to Stride or Strike.\n</p>\n  </section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.G67uVoAaG7eTgO5s]{Rubble} <br /> While the library is in a complete state of disrepair, not everything was destroyed in the fire.\n  Diligent PCs who spend at least 10 minutes Searching through the rubble uncover a <em>book of warding prayers</em>\n   devoted to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} under a layer of ashes.\n</p>"
            },
            "Dorms": {
              "name": "宿舍 Dorms",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E9. 宿舍</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>两排狭窄、看上去并不舒适的上下铺是这房间里唯一的陈设，不过其中几张被压碎后推到一起，堆在东北方屋顶破洞下方，形成了一个由瓦砾堆成、看起来潮湿的巢。床上的床单与薄床垫都发霉了，气味令人作呕。北边有三只半塌的衣柜倚着墙歪斜倒靠着。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这里曾是僧侣们的主要起居处。僧侣们在这些床上休息，因为僧侣人数多于床位，他们会轮班睡觉；他们还会用北边的衣柜存放自己少得可怜的私人物品。就连修道院的创立者 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智慧} 也和其他人一起睡在这里。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Guhdggi\" alt=\"Guhdggi\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>如今栖身在废墟中的灵堕魔里体型最大的一只——孤寂——在此安了家，把好几张床压碎成了那座看起来潮湿的巢。这生物大部分时间都趴在巢里打滚，偶尔起身笨拙地走出修道院，在周围林地里闲逛，沿着朝圣之径一路踏到山中神龛再折返回来。在这些外出途中，它会收集更多原料，用于它过去几个月一直在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7} 里烹煮的炖汤。由你决定：如果PC在击败孤寂之前离开修道院，他们可能会在路上遭遇这只游荡的灵堕魔。</p>\n<p>孤寂身边跟着五只谄媚的莫啖魔，替它按摩腰胯与腿脚，不停乞求食物。它们表现好时，孤寂会喂它们一些难以下咽的炖汤；但通常莫啖魔都表现不好，只能将就啃食瓦砾碎块。</p>\n<p>一看到PC，孤寂便从巢里振作起身，挥手招呼PC过来，请他们分享旅途见闻。这个灵堕魔确实急切想听每位PC讲一个故事，但每当PC开始讲述时，让所有角色各自尝试一次 @Check[perception|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] 察言观色检定（以整个队伍为对象）。成功时，PC注意到灵堕魔舔着嘴唇，并竭力掩饰自己肚腹里传来的咕噜声。</p>\n<p>最终，孤寂会让PC去区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7} “把晚餐取来”，打算与他们分享那顿闹鬼的餐食。若PC把锅一路搬到这里都没打开，锅仍保有其闹鬼特性，但如果由孤寂来打开，它不会触发。然而，任何非灵堕魔者只要接受并吃下一份，仍会受到 @Damage[5d6[poison]] 伤害（@Check[fortitude|dc:24|basic] 豁免）。饭后，孤寂会分享它自己的某段游荡故事，提到它在修道院里散步的经历。你可以借此机会向PC揭示他们尚未发现的修道院内某个藏匿的危险或宝藏。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-guhdggi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">宿舍</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.8rc8nf8rTES8Rwta]{孤寂} @UUID[Actor.mqTFTmYQoUKUyj2e]{莫啖魔（5）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>如果PC用故事逗乐这只灵堕魔、并在不发动攻击的情况下分食那顿毒餐，这只恶魔会揉着肚子，用近乎失望的语气说道：“你们真是好客人；真可惜我们现在也得把你们全吃了。”它们会立刻发动攻击，但由于被那恶臭的调和物灌得肚胀、还有些微醺，孤寂在战斗开始时处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 2}。莫啖魔们因这顿美餐而欣喜若狂，在战斗开始后的前两轮里处于 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{迟缓 1}，因为它们花了太多时间打嗝、发出满足的咕噜声来赞美厨子。</p>\n  <p>战斗一旦开始，灵堕魔们会战至死。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.Pmx28vdIDhOmGuEd]{宿舍} <br />\n  僧侣们离开时带走了大部分私人物品，但其中一名僧侣遗落了一枚<em>灵视戒指</em>——他把它藏在自己床垫下方一个小裂口里。若PC在房间内进行搜索，并在 @Check[perception|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 察觉检定中成功，便会发现这枚戒指。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E9. Dorms</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Twin rows of narrow, uncomfortable-looking bunks are this room’s only decoration, although several have been crushed and then pushed together under a hole in the roof to the northeast, forming a damp-looking nest made of rubble. The sheets and thin mattresses on the bunks are moldy and smell awful. To the north, three partially collapsed dressers are slumped against the wall.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This area served as the main living quarters for the monks. The monks rested in these beds, sleeping in shifts since there were more monks than beds, and used the dressers to the north to store their meager personal belongings. Even the founder of the monastery, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}, slept here with the others.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Guhdggi\" alt=\"Guhdggi\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> One of the largest of the nindorus dwelling in the ruins today, a guhdggi, has taken up residence here, crushing several of the beds into the damp-looking nest. The creature spends most of their time wallowing in their nest, periodically getting up to lumber out of the monastery to walk around in the surrounding woods and trod Pilgrim’s Path up to the mountain shrine and back. During these excursions, they gather more ingredients for the stew they’ve been cooking in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7} for the past few months. At your discretion, if the PCs leave the monastery before they defeat the guhdggi, they could encounter the wandering nindoru along the path.</p>\n<p>The guhdggi is attended by a group of five simpering meokdans who massage their flanks and legs, constantly begging for food. When they’re good, the guhdggi feeds them some of the foul-tasting stew, but usually, the meokdans aren’t good and have to settle for eating bits of rubble.</p>\n<p>Upon spotting the PCs, the guhdggi rouses from their nest and waves the PCs over, asking them to share stories of their journeys. The nindoru is legitimately eager to hear a tale from each PC, but each time the PCs start a story, allow the characters to attempt a @Check[perception|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] check to Sense Motive for the group as a whole. On a success, the PCs note the way the nindorus lick their lips and do their best to hide the rumbling in their stomachs.</p>\n<p>Eventually, the guhdggi asks the PCs to go “fetch dinner” from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7}, intending to share the haunted meal with them. If the PCs carry the pot all the way here without opening it, the pot retains its haunted nature but doesn’t trigger if the guhdggi opens it. However, any non-nindoru who accepts and eats a serving still takes @Damage[5d6[poison]] damage (@Check[fortitude|dc:24|basic] save). After this meal, the guhdggi shares one of their own tales of wandering, mentioning their strolls through the monastery. You can use this as an opportunity to reveal to the PCs one of the hidden dangers or treasures in the monastery that they haven’t yet found.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-guhdggi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Dorms</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.8rc8nf8rTES8Rwta]{Guhdggi} @UUID[Actor.mqTFTmYQoUKUyj2e]{Meokdans (5)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If the PCs humor the nindoru with stories and partake of the poison meal without attacking, the fiend rubs their belly and, in an almost disappointed voice, says, “You’ve been such great guests; it’s a shame that we’ll have to eat you all now too.” They attack at once, but gorged and slightly drunk on the foul concoction, the guhdggi begins the fight @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2}. The meokdans are so ecstatic about the fine meal that they’re @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} for the first two rounds of combat, as they take too much time to compliment the chef with belches and gurgles of satisfaction.</p>\n  <p>Once combat begins, the nindorus fight to the death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.Pmx28vdIDhOmGuEd]{Dorms} <br />\n  The monks took most of their personal effects with them when they left, but one of the monks forgot a <em>spiritsight ring</em> that they’d hidden in a small tear under their mattress. A PC finds the ring if they succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check while Searching in the room.\n</p>"
            },
            "Storage": {
              "name": "存储 Storage",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E8. Storage\">E8. 储藏室</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>厚厚的灰尘覆盖着这间食品贮藏室里存放的架子和容器。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.YIiNO31W9RalcQBQ]{Storage} @UUID[Actor.lgdHpG7TBVzDDGcw]{Loose Floor Stone}<br />\n  存放在这里的大部分食物早已腐烂，但一名PC若花1分钟在此处搜寻，会找到大量茶叶，其中包括一罐价值150 gp的稀有茶叶。用这些稀有茶叶中的一部分来抵消制作魔茶时消耗的原材料，可使【制作】检定获得+1物品加值。将其全部用于在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e6refectory000]{E6} 为不死进行一场茶事仪式，则在主持茶事的检定上获得+2物品加值。\n</p>\n<p>\n  一名PC若花10分钟搜寻这间储藏室，并在一次 @Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 检定中成功，就会发现房间西南角一块松动的地砖下藏着一份极其巧妙的宝藏——一个<em>II型宽敞袋</em>，其中装有数量惊人的珠宝、小雕像与其他精美艺术品，总价值200 gp。这个袋子原本属于一名叫卡伦·布雷的盗贼，他如今在修道院地下室的储藏间里作为一名不死囚徒“继续活着”（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e14storagero00]{E14}）。在被捕前，他把从柳岸镇民宅中盗取的全部财富藏在这里。当PC们发现这处藏匿点时，若有PC在一次 @Check[society|dc:15] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15] 检定中成功，便能认出这些失窃物品正是本年稍早、春末最后一天前后约一个月里失踪的那些东西。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们将失窃物品归还给柳岸镇的镇民，给予他们60 XP与2点希望点。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E8. Storage\">E8. Storage</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Thick layers of dust cover the shelves and containers stored in this pantry.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.YIiNO31W9RalcQBQ]{Storage} @UUID[Actor.lgdHpG7TBVzDDGcw]{Loose Floor Stone}<br />\n  Most of the food stored here has long since rotted away, but a PC who spends a minute Searching here finds a large supply of tea leaves, including a tin of rare tea worth 150 gp. Using some of this rare tea to cover the raw materials consumed when crafting magic tea grants a +1 item bonus to the Crafting check. Using all of it to perform a tea ceremony for the undead in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e6refectory000]{E6} grants a +2 item bonus to the check to Host Ceremony.\n</p>\n<p>\n  A PC who takes 10 minutes Searching this storeroom and succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check discovers a very cleverly hidden treasure under a loose floor stone in the southwest corner of the room—a <em>type II spacious pouch</em>\n  that contains an astounding amount of jewelry, statuettes, and other fine art, worth a total of 200 gp. The bag itself belonged to a thief named Kalen Bray, who now “lives on” as an undead prisoner in the monastery basement storage room (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e14storagero00]{E14}). He stashed this bag containing all the stolen wealth he’d pilfered from homes in Willowshore here before he was captured. When the PCs discover this stash, a PC who succeeds at a @Check[society|dc:15] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:15] check recognizes the stolen objects as things that went missing a month or so before the last day of spring earlier in the year.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs return the stolen items to the townsfolk of Willowshore, grant them 60 XP and 2 Hope Points.</p>"
            },
            "Kitchen": {
              "name": "厨房 Kitchen",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E7. 厨房</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一座陶制炉灶占据了这间厨房的东南角。炉灶上放着一口烹饪锅，盖着带污渍的锅盖，锅中咕嘟作响；下方的炉膛里火焰正旺。其他地方，破损的桌子与架子散落在地上。</p>\n</div>\n<p>僧侣们在此烹制餐食，通常包括米饭、园中种植或从森林采集的青菜，以及汤或炖菜。来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e9dorms0000000]{E9} 的孤寂灵堕魔正慢炖一大缸炖菜，起初的原料包括：切得很粗且未剥皮的洋葱、几整瓣大蒜、一根被它用利爪切片的萝卜，以及某个倒霉黑坊主的肝脏与肠子——那家伙在错误的时间出现在了错误的地点。灵堕魔每次找到新食材就会往缸里添加，一边啜饮如今已酸腐的稀糊，一边吞噬受害者的转世的灵魂，并且不时奖赏它所统治的“饥饿”莫啖魔。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">厨房</span> <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.5P2jOuVbvr3dzaKV]{不洁饥渴}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>如果一名PC拉拽开炖菜的锅盖，一颗煮熟的眼球会从这锅恶臭、作祟的混合物中瞪着他们。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.l7lKM6DUpbuKqOhC]{厨房} <br />\n  如果作祟被击败，锅中的液体会迅速蒸发，留下黏稠的残渣，一名角色可以在花费1分钟工作并成功通过一次 @Check[crafting|dc:22] 检定后采集这些残渣，制成5剂毒素，其效果与猎蛛毒相同。若失败，角色只能制成1剂；若大失败，则一剂也制不出来，但会暴露于该毒素之下。此外，还可以从本房间的器具中收集到一套上等工匠的工具包，用于冲泡与奉茶。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E7. Kitchen</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A clay furnace occupies the southeast portion of this kitchen. A cooking pot atop the furnace bubbles under a stained lid, a fire burning in the hearth below it. Elsewhere, ruined tables and shelves lie scattered on the floor.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The monks cooked their meals here, usually consisting of rice, greens grown in the garden or foraged from the forest, and soup or stew. The guhdggi nindoru from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e9dorms0000000]{E9} is in the process of slow-cooking a vat of stew originally consisting of poorly chopped, unpeeled onions, several whole cloves of garlic, a radish sliced up with its claws, and the liver and intestines of an unfortunate kurobozu who was in the wrong place at the wrong time. The nindoru adds to the vat of stew each time they come across a new ingredient, slurping down the now-rancid slosh alongside the souls of their victims and, periodically, rewarding the “starving” meokdans who he lords over.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Kitchen</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.5P2jOuVbvr3dzaKV]{Unholy Hunger}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazards:</strong> If a PC pulls the lid off the stew, a boiled eyeball stares up at them from the foul-smelling, haunted concoction.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.l7lKM6DUpbuKqOhC]{Kitchen} <br />\n  If the haunt is defeated, the fluid in the pot quickly evaporates, leaving behind a sticky residue that a character can harvest after 1 minute of work and with a successful @Check[crafting|dc:22] check to produce 5 doses of poison that functions the same as hunting spider venom. On a failure, a character produces only one dose, and on a critical failure, they produce no doses but are exposed to the poison. In addition, a sterling artisan’s toolkit for brewing and serving tea can be gathered from the utensils in this room.\n</p>"
            },
            "Refectory": {
              "name": "食堂 Refectory",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E6. 食堂</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>几张毁坏的桌子与破损的长凳在这间食堂里堆成一团。这个房间或许曾是个适合用餐、精致而令人放松的地方，但如今却令人感到寒冷与空荡。</p>\n</div>\n<p>僧侣们曾经每天在这里一同用餐两次。如今，桌子与坐垫全都被同一批僧侣毁掉了——他们成为不死之后，知道自己再也不需要吃东西。肮脏的碗盘散落在仅存的几张桌上，更多的则散在地面各处。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>三名不死僧侣无精打采地站在这间厅堂里，哀伤地凝视着曾带给他们同袍情谊的房间——即便在他们为了苦迦菩提而背叛了同门之后亦然。三名黑坊主在PC进入时抬起头来，问道：“你知道能吃东西是多么大的享受吗？”这两名不死会继续追问PC们最喜欢的食物，逼他们给出越来越多的细节；若他们得知任何一名PC懂得茶道，便会要求他们到储藏室（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e8storage00000]{E8}）取来材料，在厨房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7}）为他们煮些茶，然后回到这里侍奉他们。</p>\n<p>若PC照做，他们必须进行@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#host-ceremony]{主持茶事}，才能将茶正确呈给三名黑坊主。若PC大成功，黑坊主显然对茶感到满意，尽管他们尝不出味道；他们咽下之后，茶却只会从胸口的孔洞里漏出来。生物感谢PC的慈悲，并提到：“我们知道你在搜索净化此地，而为报答你的善意，也让我们奉上一点帮助。我们用闯入者的魔法斧劈下了你们死亡女神的头颅，使其与身体分离，然后把头放在杉树的高处枝桠上，离她的身体越远越好——在我们所能触及的最远之处。若你想纠正我们对她雕像的亵渎，就得把它取回来。”说完，三名黑坊主便崩解成尘。若为成功，黑坊主只是感谢PC，随后崩解成尘，并不会给出这条建议。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/kurobozu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">食堂</span> <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bdOAkorJbVOqobUp]{苦迦菩提的僧侣（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>若PC在尚未准备好向三名不死奉茶的情况下回到此处，或他们在尝试进行主持茶事时失败，三名黑坊主便会痛苦哀号并发动攻击，战斗至被摧毁为止（但他们不会离开此厅堂去追击敌人）。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC以一次茶道仪式使黑坊主满意，则给予他们XP，视同他们在战斗中击败这些生物。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E6. Refectory</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Several ruined tables and broken benches lie in heaps within this refectory. The chamber might have once been a fine and relaxing place to take a meal, but now it feels cold and empty.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The monks once ate together twice a day here. Presently, the tables and seat cushions have all been ruined by the same monks who, as undead, know that their days of eating are behind them. Dirty bowls and plates are scattered across the few tables that still stand, while more lie scattered on the floor.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A trio of undead monks stand listlessly in this chamber, mournfully staring at a room that once brought them camaraderie, even after they betrayed their brothers and sisters for Kugaptee. The three kurobozus look up as the PCs enter and ask, “Do you realize what a pleasure it is to be able to eat?” The two undead continue to ask the PCs about their favorite meals, pushing them for more and more details; if they learn that any of the PCs knows about tea, they ask them to fetch supplies from the pantry (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e8storage00000]{E8}), brew them some tea in the kitchen (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7}), and then return here to serve them.</p>\n<p>If the PCs do so, they must @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog07turnin.JournalEntryPage.07restoringthe00#host-ceremony]{Host Ceremony} to properly present the tea to the three kurobozus. If the PCs critically succeed, the kurobozus are obviously satisfied with the tea, even though they can’t taste it, and after they swallow, the tea simply leaks out through holes in their chests. The creatures thank the PCs for their compassion and also mention, “We know you seek to purify this place, and in thanks for your kindness, let us offer some as well. We used the interloper’s magical axe to cleave the head of your death goddess free then placed the head in the upper boughs of the sugi tree, as far from her body as we could reach. You’ll need to retrieve it if you wish to rectify our desecration of her statue.” With that, the three kurobozus crumble to dust. On a success, the kurobozus simply thank the PCs and crumble to dust without offering this advice.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/kurobozu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Refectory</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bdOAkorJbVOqobUp]{Monks of Kugaptee (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If the PCs return to this room without being ready to serve tea to the three undead, or if they fail in their attempt to Host Ceremony, the three kurobozus cry out in anguish and attack, fighting until destroyed (although they don’t pursue foes from this chamber).</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs satisfy the kurobozus with a tea ceremony, grant them XP as if they’d defeated the creatures in combat.</p>"
            },
            "Pharasma’s Shrine": {
              "name": "法莱斯玛的神殿 Pharasma’s Shrine",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E5. 法莱斯玛的神龛</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>在这间本来空无一物的房间南侧，一尊神态威严的女性木雕像端坐在低矮的台座上，摆出冥想的姿势。雕像周围堆着成堆的骨头、枯叶与一块块干瘪的木乃伊化血肉；雕像缺失的头颅看上去像是被一击劈落。血迹斑斑、长满霉斑的绳索被紧紧缠绕在雕像上，其间还固定着更多旧骨头，骨头上还粘着些许风干的肉屑。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-pharasma-statue.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Pharasma Shrine\" alt=\"Pharasma Shrine\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-pharasma-statue.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p>谭杉寺的僧侣们遵循着@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}的教诲，但他们仍在此竖立了这尊@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}的雕像，以表达对她在宇宙生死循环中所扮演角色的敬意。灵堕魔却毫无这般尊重；它们在出现在寺院后的第一个夏日，就亵渎了这尊雕像。若以成功的@Check[religion|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]进行回忆知识，PC可以辨认出这尊无头雕像描绘的是法莱斯玛；若为大成功或大失败，他们还能确认这次亵渎的本质意在象征对她掌控生死之力的根本否定，宣称她对真相视而不见，也无力改变自身的行事之道。</p>\n<p>这尊雕像是四尊必须被净化的雕像之一；净化全部四尊后，才能获得前往苦迦菩提坟墓并与智慧之鬼魂交谈的许可。在开始这一过程之前，必须先击败此室内的生物，并将雕像缺失的头颅（位于区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e13thetansug00]{E13}）安放回雕像颈部的断桩之上。一旦成功净化雕像，头颅便会以魔法重新接合，仿佛从未被劈下过一样。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.xmmRfbitBY6ViuKM]{Return Head}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC进入时，三个看似身披僧袍的僧侣跪在雕像前，仿佛在祷告。然而这些“僧侣”实际上是索闹灵堕魔；它们并非祷告，而是在冥想法莱斯玛的存在于多元宇宙中是何等徒劳，并准备以仪式将雕像用一圈新绳索重新捆缚——绳索就放在它们面前的地上。若这些恶魔注意到PC，它们会起身转向来者，以令人不安的方式抽动着被缝合的嘴巴，向PC致意。索闹渴望弄清PC为何来到神龛，并会试图说服他们：死后仍有生命不过是神话。“死亡之后，只有我们！”它们如此寄望，并提出愿意杀死PC来证明自己的观点。你可以用这些恶魔透露一些关于寺院的信息（例如留下来的僧侣如今全都成了不死生物、他们由一名叫@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{辛月}的人领导，甚至寺院创立者的鬼魂被囚禁在此），但用不了多久，恶魔就会厌倦交谈并向PC发起挑战。</p>\n<p>挑战很简单：PC要绕中央庭院跑一圈，从此房间前往区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e1grandgate000]{大门}，再到区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7}、区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e6refectory000]{E6}、区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e3mainhall0000]{E3}、区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e4infirmary000]{E4}，最后回到这里。灵堕魔知道在这些区域中很可能会有危险阻碍PC通行，但仍告诉PC：如果他们之中哪怕有一人能在灵堕魔完成对法莱斯玛亵渎雕像的重新捆缚之前跑完整个路线，它们就会以一件贵重宝藏作为奖赏。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-sojiruh.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">法莱斯玛的神龛</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Bilhe9obVVB9UFFx]{索闹（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>灵堕魔并不在乎PC是否诚实地跑完比赛，还是作弊；若PC在这项挑战期间离开，那么当他们返回此房间时，会发现三只灵堕魔甚至连重新捆缚雕像都还没开始。它们会以“宝藏”——灵堕魔的智慧——欢迎PC归来：“你们按我们的挑战跑完了一圈；然而正如你们的生死循环一般，这个循环本身毫无意义、空洞无物，不可信赖。”说完，三只灵堕魔便发动攻击。若PC拒绝参赛，它们同样会攻击，并以窃取尖叫作为战斗的开场。灵堕魔会战至死亡，在寺院内追击敌人。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC净化了法莱斯玛的雕像，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E5. Pharasma’s Shrine</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A wooden statue of a regal-looking woman sits in a meditative pose atop a low dais to the south of this otherwise empty room. Bones, dead leaves, and chunks of mummified flesh lie in heaps around the statue, whose missing head appears to have been hewn off by a single blow. Bloodstained, moldy ropes have been wrapped tightly around the statue, amid which many more old bones with bits of dried meat have been affixed.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-pharasma-statue.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Pharasma Shrine\" alt=\"Pharasma Shrine\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-pharasma-statue.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p>The monks of the Tan Sugi monastery followed the teachings of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi}, but they erected this statue of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} here out of respect for the role she plays in the cosmic cycle of life and death. The nindorus hold no such respect and defiled this statue on the very first day of summer after they appeared in the monastery. With a successful @Check[religion|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] to Recall Knowledge, a PC can identify the headless statue as depicting Pharasma; with a critical success, they confirm that the nature of the statue’s defiling is meant to represent a fundamental rejection of her power over life and death, indicating that she’s blind to the truth of it and powerless to change her ways.</p>\n<p>The statue is one of the four that must be purified in order to gain access to Kugaptee’s grave and speak to Zhi Hui’s ghost. Before this process can be started, the creatures in this chamber must be defeated, and the statue’s missing head (found in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e13thetansug00]{E13}) must be placed atop the stump of the statue’s neck. Upon successfully purifying the statue, the head magically reattaches itself, as if it had never been hewed free in the first place.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.xmmRfbitBY6ViuKM]{Return Head}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When the PCs enter, creatures who appear to be three robed monks kneel before the statue, as if in prayer. These monks are, in fact, sojiruh nindorus, and rather than praying, they’re meditating on the futility of Pharasma’s presence in the multiverse and preparing to ritualistically rebind the statue in a fresh coil of rope they’ve placed on the ground before themselves. If the fiends notice the PCs, they rise up and turn to face them, their stitched mouths twitching unnervingly as they greet the PCs. The sojiruhs are eager to find out why the PCs have come to the shrine and work to convince them that the idea of life after death is a myth. “After death, there is only us!” they promise, offering to kill the PCs to prove their points. You can use these fiends to reveal bits of information about the monastery (such as that the monks who remained are now all undead, that they’re led by someone named @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue}, or even that the ghost of the monastery’s founder is imprisoned here), but it shouldn’t be long before the fiends grow weary of conversation and issue a challenge to the PCs.</p>\n<p>The challenge is simple. The PCs are to run a circle around the central courtyard, moving from this room to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e1grandgate000]{Grand Gate}, then to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e7kitchen00000]{E7}, area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e6refectory000]{E6}, area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e3mainhall0000]{E3}, area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e4infirmary000]{E4}, and finally back here. The nindorus know that dangers are likely to oppose the PCs’ passage through many of these areas but nonetheless tell the PCs that if even one of them can make their way through this circuit before the nindorus can complete the rebinding of Pharasma’s defiled statue, they’ll reward them with a valuable treasure.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-sojiruh.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Pharasma's Shrine</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Bilhe9obVVB9UFFx]{Sojiruhs (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The nindorus don’t care if the PCs actually run the race honestly or cheat; should the PCs leave during this challenge, upon returning to this room, they’ll find the three nindorus haven’t even started rebinding the statue. They welcome back the PCs with “treasure” in the form of nindoru wisdom: “You have run a circuit as we challenged you to, yet as with your cycle of life and death, the cycle itself is meaningless, hollow, and not to be trusted.” With that, the three nindorus attack. They attack as well if the PCs refuse to race, opening combat with Stolen Scream. The nindorus fight to the death, pursuing foes throughout the monastery.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs purify Pharasma’s statue, grant them 40 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Infirmary": {
              "name": "医务室 Infirmary",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E4. 医务室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房间北侧的门被撕开了一个大洞。地面上散落着被撕碎的行军床、损坏的椅子与桌子，以及其他杂物；墙上还被刻出又深又长的抓痕。浓烈的腐臭味弥漫整个房间，而被撞坏的架子则堆成一团，靠在西侧墙边。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/kurobozu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">医务室</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bdOAkorJbVOqobUp]{苦迦菩提僧侣（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>僧侣们曾用这间房间为病患与伤者治疗，无论是同门僧侣还是需要帮助的旅人。原本朴素的医务室，如今已被曾在此工作的两名僧侣彻底弄得一团糟。在加入 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue} 对苦迦菩提的崇拜之后，当思维空间吞没这片区域时，这两人死后化作黑坊主复生。这两名苦迦菩提的不死僧侣在PC们进入时踉跄着迎上前来，但不会立刻攻击。相反，他们会齐声用沙哑的声音说道：“你们是来加入苦迦菩提的吗？你们是来逃脱生命的牢狱的吗？”这些不死者渴望将PC们献祭给他们的邪魔神祇；一旦显然队伍并不打算自我奉献，他们便会迅速发动攻击。他们会在整座寺院中追击敌人，但会避开 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2} 区域，因为他们仍然畏惧并敬重那里的幽灵（特征）。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.9QM7HQKoZsnDpkga]{杂物} <br />\n  橱柜与架子都已破烂不堪，但你能在杂物中找到两瓶<em>中等治疗药水</em>、一套<em>专家级医疗工具</em>与一副<em>医者手套</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E4. Infirmary</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A large hole has been torn into this room’s northern door. Shredded cots, ruined chairs and tables, and other debris adorn the floor, and deep, long gashes have been carved into the walls. A thick rancid smell permeates the chamber, while battered shelves lie in a heap against the western wall.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/kurobozu.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Infirmary</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bdOAkorJbVOqobUp]{Monks of Kugaptee (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The monks once used this room to treat the sick and injured, be they fellow monks or travelers in need of aid. What was once a simple infirmary has been thrown into complete disarray by two of the monks who once worked here. After joining @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue} in the worship of Kugaptee, these two rose in undeath as kurobozus after the mindscape engulfed the region. The two undead monks of Kugaptee lurch toward the PCs as they enter but don’t attack at once. Instead, they rasp out in unison, “Have you come to join Kugaptee? Are you here to escape the prison of life?” The undead are eager to sacrifice the PCs to their fiendish god and swiftly attack as soon as it becomes apparent the party doesn’t intend to offer themselves up. They pursue foes throughout the monastery but avoid area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}, as they still fear and respect the ghost there.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.9QM7HQKoZsnDpkga]{Debris} <br />\n  The cabinets and shelves are in tatters, but two <em>moderate healing potions</em>, a set of <em>expanded healer’s tools</em>, and a pair of <em>healer’s gloves</em> can be found in the debris.\n</p>"
            },
            "Main Hall": {
              "name": "主厅 Main Hall",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E3. 主厅</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间露天大厅的天花板高达60英尺。墙上等距分布的拱门之间，可以望见周围的庭院；拱门间雕刻并彩绘着幽魂之森的丘陵与森林的繁复图景，色彩已然褪去。大厅中央矗立着一尊高达50英尺的石制树木雕像，枝条向外延伸覆盖整个房间。雕像周围的地面上摆放着一圈圈发霉的坐垫。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这座露天建筑曾是访客抵达寺院后的第一站。巨大的石树雕像是谭杉树的一尊半尺寸复制品；谭杉树生长在北方不远处的区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e13thetansug00]{E13}。僧侣们将石块拖运到位，雕刻后再用魔法将其黏合在一起，让朝圣者能够在此冥想，并触摸那棵圣树的近似之物——因为只有僧侣才被许可进入北庭院，真正的树就生长在那里。</p>\n<p>这尊杉树雕像是四尊必须被净化的雕像之一；只有净化它们，才能获得进入苦迦菩提墓地的许可，并与 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠} 的幽灵交谈。但在开始这一过程之前，必须先击败栖身在树中的怨灵。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/ittan-momen.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">主厅</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.nBZYrLLAsuHwKjtW]{一反木绵（4）} @UUID[Actor.VnIjJNtx29XGDofD]{苦迦菩提之树}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>这间大厅内最危险的威胁是雕像本身（见危害），但腐化雕像的那股凶恶能量也在腐朽的坐垫间显化出其他实体。其中有四个坐垫包裹的并非布满真菌的布料，而是一反木绵付丧神；一旦危害触发，这些怪物便会从它们所覆盖的潮湿填充物中挣脱出来，攻击PC。它们会在整个寺院中追击敌人，战至死方休。</p>\n\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>当苦迦菩提的影响渗入寺院时，此处的雕像曾作为场地的灵能守卫，起初吸收并净化了大量邪恶能量。随着时间推移，这股能量持续涌入，最终溢出并腐化了雕像。如今，整间大厅都充斥着极其强烈的邪恶能量，强到就连灵堕魔恶魔都不情愿进入，而雕像也已被苦迦菩提的存在所纠缠，变得阴魂不散。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.ngFhNTGn08ZJO8Xp]{主厅} <br />\n  一面<em>护法盾</em>，由一名命途多舛的掠夺者遗落——他在思维空间形成前几年曾来过寺院——如今就躺在雕像正东侧的发霉坐垫之间。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC净化杉树雕像，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E3. Main Hall</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This open-air chamber has a sixty-foot ceiling. In between regularly spaced archways in the walls that allow views into the surrounding courtyard, intricate depictions of the hills and forests of Specterwood are carved and painted in fading colors. A fifty-foot-tall stone statue of a tree rises in the center of the chamber, its branches extending over the room. Circular rows of moldy cushions lie on the ground around the statue.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This open structure was the first stop for visitors to the monastery. The giant stone tree statue is a half-sized replica of the Tan Sugi tree, which grows not far to the north in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e13thetansug00]{E13}. The monks carved this statue from stone blocks hauled into place and bound together with magic so that pilgrims could meditate before and touch a close approximation of the sacred tree since only the monks were permitted to enter the northern courtyard where the actual tree grew.</p>\n<p>The sugi statue is one of the four statues that must be purified in order to gain access to Kugaptee’s grave and speak to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s ghost, but before this process can be started, the haunt within the tree must be defeated.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/ittan-momen.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Main hall</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.nBZYrLLAsuHwKjtW]{Ittan-Momen (4)} @UUID[Actor.VnIjJNtx29XGDofD]{Kugaptee's Tree}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The most dangerous peril within this chamber is the statue itself (see Hazards), but the same fell energies that have corrupted the statue manifest other entities among the moldering cushions. Four of these cushions are wrapped not in fungus-riddled cloth, but ittan-momen tsukumogami, and these monsters rip free from the damp stuffing they cover to attack the PCs once the hazard triggers. They pursue foes throughout the monastery and fight to the death.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Hazards:</strong> When Kugaptee’s influence seeped into the monastery, the statue here served as a spiritual guardian of the grounds and initially absorbed and purified much of the evil energy. Over time, the continuous influx of this energy overflowed and corrupted the statue. Now, the entire chamber brims with evil energy so strong that even the nindoru fiends are reluctant to enter, and the statue has become haunted by Kugaptee’s presence.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.ngFhNTGn08ZJO8Xp]{Main Hall} <br />\n  A <em>spellguard shield</em> left behind by an ill-fated looter who visited the monastery a few years before the mindscape formed lies among the moldy cushions just east of the statue.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs purify the sugi statue, grant them 40 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Courtyard": {
              "name": "庭院 Courtyard",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">E2. 庭院</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一条看起来被污染的小溪连接着这片杂草丛生的庭院中六七个小池塘。数棵杉树散乱地生长在区域各处的小石祠之间，它们的树干与枝条上覆着某种黝黑的霉菌或苔藓般的赘生物；而那座曾连接南侧门楼通路与北侧更大建筑的桥梁，如今已成废墟。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yuni.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yuni\" alt=\"Yuni, female human ghost\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yuni.webp')\" />\n<p>这座庭院中茂密的杂草造成困难地形。池塘与小溪中曾栖息的鱼与青蛙早已死去或被吃光，3英尺深的水看起来被绿色淤泥污染，边缘处堆积成起泡的褐色硬壳。</p>\n<p>庭院东北侧的<strong>E2a</strong>区域立着一尊3英尺高的木灵神石像。石像表面覆盖着厚厚的、散发恶臭的黑霉；这是必须净化的四尊石像之一，唯有如此才能获得进入苦迦菩提坟墓并与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}的幽灵交谈的许可。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>在7098年（从PC的视角看，比当前年份早十年），两姐妹试图踏上朝圣之径，却各自遭遇了可怖的结局。妹妹耶莉的厄运详述于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08c2thegirlint00]{C2}区域，而姐姐由妮一路走到寺院庭院，却被一只如今早已死去的老虎攻击并杀害；那只老虎被堕落的僧侣当作宠物与守卫饲养。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-yuni.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">庭院</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.SWLdQD9yQOQ4hPRg]{由妮} @UUID[Actor.lC5iiouooyONCzUy]{Fiendish Reflection}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>当由妮的魂魄以幽灵之身归来时，堕落的僧侣们欣喜若狂，并把这座庭院留给她作为徘徊作祟之地。直至今日她仍被困在此处，但会一直藏匿在庭院西南角<strong>E2b</strong>区域的小神龛中，直到有人接近至30英尺以内。此时，她那被老虎撕裂的幽灵身影会自当年被扑倒撕咬之处从地面升起，先释放骇人悲叹，然后发动攻击。她无法离开<strong>E2</strong>区域，但只要敌人仍在视线内，她就会持续以她的远程手段进行攻击。</p>\n  <p>若有一名PC携带来自@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08c2thegirlint00]{C2}区域、耶莉的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.EkZVXMdtqTTgahiJ]{抗力护符}，由妮的幽灵在战斗第一轮后不会继续攻击。相反，在第二轮她自己的回合，她会走向携带护符的PC并说：“把我妹妹的手链给我！那不是你的！”若PC拒绝，由妮会恢复攻击，并在每个回合都要求归还手链。</p>\n  <p>若PC把<em>抗力护符</em>交给由妮，这幽灵便停止攻击，她用自己虚体的双手不可思议地托住手链。她凝视护符片刻，然后问：“我妹妹在哪里？”若PC如实相告，由妮会悲恸地哭喊，但随后感谢PC的坦诚；她将护符还给他们，说：“现在这该属于你们了。谢谢你们帮助耶莉寻得安宁。”说完，她也逐渐消散，化为虚无。若PC成功对她撒谎，谎称耶莉的结局亦会如此；但若由妮看穿谎言，护符会从她的双手间落到地上，她将以更盛的狂怒发起攻击，直至被摧毁为止。</p>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>此处小溪与池塘中受污染的水会使饮用者在一次@Check[fortitude|dc:15]豁免失败时变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{恶心 1}。大部分地方的水都因污秽而浑浊，唯有中央例外——那里曾有一座木桥横跨其上（<strong>E2c</strong>区域）。在这里，水色幽暗却清澈，反光极强——也闹鬼得厉害。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC净化木灵神石像，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">E2. Courtyard</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 6</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A polluted-looking creek connects over a half-dozen small ponds in this weed-tangled courtyard. Sugi trees, their trunks and branches bearing dark growths of some sort of mold or moss, grow fitfully amid small stone shrines throughout the area, while the bridge that once connected the pathway between the gatehouse to the south and a larger building to the north lies in ruins.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yuni.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Yuni\" alt=\"Yuni, female human ghost\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-yuni.webp')\" />\n<p>The thick weeds in this courtyard creates difficult terrain. Any fish or frogs that the pond and creeks once housed have long since died or been eaten, and the 3-foot-deep water looks to be polluted with green silt that forms into a foamy brown crust along the edges.</p>\n<p>A 3-foot-tall stone statue of a kodama kami stands in the northeast section of the courtyard at area <strong>E2a</strong>. Coated with thick, foul-smelling black mold, this statue is one of the four that must be purified in order to gain access to Kugaptee’s grave and speak to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s ghost.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> In 7098 (a decade prior to the current year from the PC’s perspective), two sisters attempted to walk the Pilgrim’s Path, only to each meet horrific fates. The doom that came to the younger sister, Yeri, is detailed in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08c2thegirlint00]{C2}, but her older sister, Yuni, made it all the way to the monastery courtyard before she was attacked and killed by a now-long-dead tiger kept by the corrupted monks as a pet and guardian.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90197-yuni.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Courtyard</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 6</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.SWLdQD9yQOQ4hPRg]{Yuni} @UUID[Actor.lC5iiouooyONCzUy]{Fiendish Reflection}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The corrupted monks were delighted when Yuni’s spirit came back as a ghost and left this courtyard for her as a place to haunt. She remains trapped here to this day but stays hidden within the small shrine located in area <strong>E2b</strong> in the southwest corner of the courtyard until someone approaches within 30 feet. At this point, her tiger-torn ghostly figure rises up from the ground where she was mauled to unleash her Frightful Moan before attacking. She can’t leave area <strong>E2</strong> but continues to attack with her ranged options as long as her enemies remain in sight.</p>\n  <p>If one of the PCs carries Yeri’s @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.EkZVXMdtqTTgahiJ]{Charm of Resistance} from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog08theenl.JournalEntryPage.08c2thegirlint00]{C2}, Yuni’s ghost doesn’t continue her attack after the first round of combat. Instead, on her turn on the second round, she approaches the PC who carries the charm and says, “Give me my sister’s bracelet! That isn’t yours!” If the PC refuses, Yuni returns to attacking, demanding the return of the bracelet each turn.</p>\n  <p>If a PC gives the <em>charm of resistance</em> to Yuni, the ghost ceases to attack as she cradles the bracelet impossibly in her incorporeal hands. She gazes at the charm for a moment, then asks, “Where is my little sister?” If the PCs tell the truth, Yuni cries out in sadness but then thanks the PCs for their honesty; she returns the charm to them, saying, “You deserve this now. Thank you for helping Yeri find peace,” before she too fades away to nothingness. She does this as well if the PCs successfully Lie to her about Yeri’s fate, but if Yuni sees through the lie, the charm falls through her hands to the ground, and she attacks in a renewed fury, fighting until destroyed.</p>\n  <p><strong>Hazards:</strong> The polluted water in the creek and ponds here causes a drinker to become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1} if they fail a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save. The water is murky with filth in most places, save for the middle, where a wooden bridge once crossed over it (area <strong>E2c</strong>). Here, the water is dark, clear, and very reflective—and very haunted.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs purify the kodama statue, grant them 40 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Grand Gate": {
              "name": "宏伟之门 Grand Gate",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E1. Grand Gate\">E1. 宏伟大门</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>朝圣之径通向一座嵌在修道院南墙上的木制门楼正面。破碎的符箓装饰着木门的竹制栅栏，一只孤零零的风铃在风中叮当作响，悬挂在一根摇摇欲坠、从门顶上方伸出的柱子上。</p>\n</div>\n<p>在 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠} 大师去世后的数年里，大多数僧侣离开了修道院；他们每个人都在大门上贴了一张非魔法符箓。对一些人来说，这是用来清算自己因抛弃修道院而产生的愧疚。对另一些人来说，这是无声的希望：希望有人能在他们之后到来，延续修道院的根源与教诲。不论如何，占据修道院的生物并不需要这些东西；它们在宣称此地归己所有时把符箓全都撕碎，只留下残破的碎片挂在那里，用以嘲弄。</p>\n<p>大门紧闭，但可以轻松打开，从而获得进入后方空荡门楼的许可。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.fjLoZbudvuxVK4UN]{大门} <br />\n  灵堕魔在处理这些符箓时很懒散，认为根本不会有人能到达修道院；因此，有三张魔法符箓——一张<em>逃脱符箓</em>与两张<em>踉跄符箓</em>\n  ——在破坏中幸存了下来。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"E1. Grand Gate\">E1. Grand Gate</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The Pilgrim’s Path leads to the front of a wooden gatehouse built into the monastery’s southern wall. Shredded fulus adorn the bamboo bars of the wooden gate, and a lone wind chime jingles in the wind as it dangles from a rickety post protruding over the top of the gate.</p>\n</div>\n<p>As most of the monks left the monastery in the years following Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s death, they each left a non-magical fulu affixed to the gate. For some, this act was a way to settle the guilt they felt for abandoning the monastery. For others, it was a silent wish for someone to come after them and continue the monastery’s traditions and teachings. Regardless, the creatures who took up residence in the monastery had no need for such things and shredded them all as they claimed the grounds as their own, leaving up the ruined remains hanging in mockery.</p>\n<p>The gates are closed but can be opened with ease, allowing access into the empty gatehouse beyond.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.fjLoZbudvuxVK4UN]{Gate} <br />\n  The nindorus were lazy in dealing with the fulus, believing no one would actually make it to the monastery to begin with, and as a result, three magical fulus—an <em>escape fulu</em> and two <em>stumbling fulus</em>\n  —survived the destruction.\n</p>"
            },
            "Monastery Features": {
              "name": "修道院特性 Monastery Features",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Monastery Features\">寺院特征</h2>\n<p>谭杉寺是一处阴森的院落，坐落在林地那棵巨大的杉树阴影之下。尖叫与幽魂般的低语随风起伏，树枝摇曳时持续的吱呀声更增添了诡异的氛围。PC可以按任意顺序探索寺院，但必须完成散落各处的四尊雕像的全部净化，才能获得进入地下等级的许可；在那里，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue}在苦迦菩提的坟前劳作。</p>\n<p>尽管寺院中的灵堕魔与不死生物以折磨@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{善解}的追随者、杀戮活人并吞噬他们的转世的灵魂为乐，但自他们上一次有访客以来已过去了漫长岁月。因此，这里栖居的存在并不总会在第一时间就抓住机会与PC投入战斗；他们之中许多会先进行令人不安的交谈，然后不可避免地发动攻击。</p>\n<p>寺院以木材建造，地面为石质。柱廊步道内的天花板高度为15英尺，而在较大的厅室中，这一高度升至40英尺（中央主殿则为60英尺）。寺院没有人工光源，但白天时，步道会被明亮照亮，厅室则由阳光提供昏暗照明。寺院对外侧没有窗户；面向庭院的窗户目前全都紧闭，且没有玻璃。穿过一扇开着的窗户进行移动视为困难地形。</p>\n<p>陡峭的挑檐装点着寺院建筑与柱廊的顶部。PC可以在成功通过一次@Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定后攀爬这些外墙，但从墙面转到挑檐并爬上屋顶十分棘手，需要其成功通过一次@Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定。</p>\n<p>柱廊墙面与内部建筑上的开口使中型或更小的生物可以轻松通行。大型生物穿过这些区域时，将其视为高等困难地形。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Monastery Features\">Monastery Features</h2>\n<p>The Tan Sugi monastery is a gloomy compound set in the shadow of the grove’s giant sugi tree. Screams and ghostly whispers rise and fall with the wind, and the steady creaking of swaying tree branches augments the eerie ambiance. The PCs can explore the monastery in any order but must complete the purification of all four statues scattered throughout to gain access to the subterranean level where @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue} toils before Kugaptee’s grave.</p>\n<p>While the monastery’s nindorus and undead enjoy tormenting followers of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo]{Sangpotshi}, killing the living and consuming their souls, ages have passed since they’ve last had visitors. As such, those who dwell here don’t always jump at the first opportunity to engage in combat with the PCs, and many of them will engage in unsettling conversation before, inevitably, they attack.</p>\n<p>The monastery is made of wood with stone floors. Ceiling height within the colonnaded walkways is 15 feet, while in the larger chambers, this height rises to 40 feet (or 60 feet in the central main hall). The monastery has no artificial light sources, but during the day, walkways are brightly lit and the chambers are dimly lit by sunlight. There are no windows facing out of the monastery; those facing into the courtyards are all currently shuttered and have no glass. Moving through an open window counts as difficult terrain.</p>\n<p>Overhanging, steep rooflines adorn the tops of the monastery’s buildings and colonnades. A PC can Climb these external walls with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check, but transitioning from the wall to the overhang and onto the roof is tricky and requires them to succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check.</p>\n<p>Openings in the colonnade walls and internal buildings allow easy access for Medium or smaller creatures. Large creatures moving through these areas treat them as greater difficult terrain.</p>"
            },
            "Fourth Purification": {
              "name": "第四净化 Fourth Purification",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Fourth Purification\">第四次净化</h3>\n<p>当最后一尊雕像被净化后，修道院中患有恶心的树木（谭杉本身除外）恢复健康，庭院里过度滋生的杂草枯萎，使得穿过区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2} 不再是困难地形。南侧庭院（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}）的水变得纯净，不再映出恶魔般的倒影；宝库中苦迦菩提之墓入口上方的屏障（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e15treasurec00]{E15}）消散；而 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠} 能在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16} 的最终战斗中协助 PC。</p>\n<p>智惠再次显现，感谢 PC 的付出，但警告他们：为了彻底清除苦迦菩提的影响，他们必须前往修道院下方他的墓穴并击败 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{心月}——正是她最初放任这份腐化扩散。智惠可以随其意志显现，并能在任意雕像处停留到她想离开为止。她会回答 PC 想问的任何问题。她也提出，只要她做得到，就会为 PC 施放法术。PC 可以在修道院内这些雕像所在地点安全无虞地休息。更多细节见她的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{NPC Entry}。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Fourth Purification\">Fourth Purification</h3>\n<p>When the final statue is purified, the monastery’s sickened trees (with the exception of the Tan Sugi itself) become healthy, and the overgrown weeds in the courtyards wither so that passage through area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2} isn’t difficult terrain. The water in the southern courtyard (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}) becomes pure and no longer shows fiendish reflections, the barrier over the entrance to Kugaptee’s Grave in the treasury (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e15treasurec00]{E15}) fades, and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} can aid the PCs in their final fight in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}.</p>\n<p>Zhi Hui manifests again and thanks the PCs for their service but warns them that, in order to fully remove Kugaptee’s influence, they must travel into his grave below the monastery and defeat @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21xinyue00000000]{Xin Yue}, the one who allowed this corruption to spread in the first place. Zhi Hui can manifest at will and remain as long as she wishes at any of the statues. She’ll answer any questions the PCs wish to ask. She also offers to cast spells on the PCs as she’s able. The PCs can rest safe and secure at any of these statue sites in the monastery. See her @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{NPC Entry} for further details.</p>"
            },
            "Third Purification": {
              "name": "第三次净化 Third Purification",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Third Purification\">第三次净化</h3>\n<p>净化第三尊雕像会让苦迦菩提对寺院的控制进一步减弱。笼罩在PC身上的巨大阴影重压感随之消散。他们意识到，自从进入遗迹以来，自己一直在灵性层面受到一股压倒性的心灵力量的压迫，而此刻那股力量已然不复存在。如果风暴仍在肆虐（因为PC尚未击败岚鬼婆伊奥加卡），风暴会在此刻终止（而伊奥加卡本人也会从思维空间中消失）。周围森林里鸟鸣与虫鸣渐起，为这片地区带回一丝自然的气息，尽管在遗迹之内，氛围依旧异常阴森。智惠的幽灵（特征）再次显现，这一次她能停留足够长的时间，在消散前回答三个问题；但她是安宁地淡去，而非像之前那样仿佛被无形利爪撕碎。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Third Purification\">Third Purification</h3>\n<p>Purifying the third statue causes Kugaptee’s hold on the monastery to weaken even further. The sensation of a great shadowy weight lifts from the PCs. They realize that they’d been spiritually oppressed by an overwhelming psychic presence ever since entering the ruins, only to find it now gone. If the storm still rages because the PCs haven’t yet defeated the storm hag Iogaka, the storm ends now (and Iogaka herself vanishes from the mindscape). The sound of birds and insects builds in the surrounding forest, bringing a hint of nature back to the region, although within the ruins, things remain unnaturally grim. Zhi Hui’s ghost manifests again, and this time she can remain long enough to answer three questions before fading away, but she fades peacefully rather than appearing to be ripped apart by unseen talons.</p>"
            },
            "Second Purification": {
              "name": "第二次净化 Second Purification",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Second Purification\">第二次净化</h3>\n<p>净化第二座雕像会使藏匿图书馆（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}）的秘密门不仅会解锁，而且在PC下一次接近其中任意一扇门时，还会散发出柔和的光辉。@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}再次显现，向队伍再度致谢，并鼓励他们继续前进，净化剩下的两座雕像。她这次有时间回答两个问题，之后才会被撕裂；但在离去之际，她喊道：“搜索藏匿图书馆……我的朋友颜蕊能帮上忙……”</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Second Purification\">Second Purification</h3>\n<p>Purifying the second statue causes the secret doors to the hidden library (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}) to not only unlock, but to glow with a soft radiance the next time the PCs approach either of them. @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui} manifests again, thanking the party once more and encouraging them to keep going and purify the remaining two statues. She has time to answer two questions this time before she’s ripped apart, but as she goes, she cries out, “Seek the hidden library... my friend, Yen Rui, can help...”</p>"
            },
            "First Purification": {
              "name": "首次净化 First Purification",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"First Purification\">第一次净化</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihuiportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zhi Hui\" alt=\"Zhi Hui's ghost\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihuiportrait.webp')\" />\n<p>净化第一尊被腐化的雕像后，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}大师的幽灵（特征）便能在PC面前短暂显现——在此之前，她一直被困在苦迦菩提的坟墓中（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}）。她从雕像中现身，形容凄楚、神情黯然；当她望向队伍时，表情逐渐柔和，转为如释重负与感激。她以轻柔而飘渺的声音对PC们说道。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\" style=\"clear:both\">\n  <p>“感谢你们的这份善意。我已经很久没能看穿那吞没一切的黑暗了，但它依旧在拉拽着我。我无法停留太久，但还能停留到足以回答你们一个问题。要知道，还有其他雕像。净化它们，我就能进一步协助你们。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>智惠的幽灵（特征）能够停留的时间，刚好足以回答PC们向她提出的一个问题；随后，苦迦菩提的影响会将她再次拖回那处灵性遗忘之所——自她死后，她便一直被囚禁于此。关于她可能被问到的问题及可给出的答案列表，见她的@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{NPC条目}。当她回答完那个问题，或几分钟过去后，她会痛苦地尖叫，仿佛被撕扯成血淋淋的碎片，继而彻底消失，被拉拽回苦迦菩提的坟墓中（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}）。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"First Purification\">First Purification</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihuiportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zhi Hui\" alt=\"Zhi Hui's ghost\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihuiportrait.webp')\" />\n<p>Purifying the first of the corrupted statues allows Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s ghost, which up until this point has been trapped within Kugaptee’s grave (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}), to temporarily manifest before the PCs. She emerges from the statue, a forlorn and despondent figure whose expression softens to relief and gratitude as she gazes upon the party. She addresses the PCs in a soft, ephemeral voice.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\" style=\"clear:both\">\n  <p>“Thank you for this kindness. It has been so long since I’ve been able to see beyond the engulfing darkness, but it still pulls at me. I will not be able to remain for long, but I can remain long enough to answer a question you may have for me. Know that there are other statues. Cleanse them and I can aid you further.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>Zhi Hui’s ghost can remain present long enough to answer one question the PCs might have for her before Kugaptee’s influence draws her back into the spiritual oubliette in which she has been imprisoned since her death. See her @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{NPC Entry} for a list of answers she’ll have for potential questions asked of her. Once she answers her question, or once a few minutes have passed, she cries out in pain and appears to be ripped to bloody shreds before she vanishes entirely, pulled back into Kugaptee’s grave (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e16kugaptees00]{E16}).</p>"
            },
            "Purifying the Monastery": {
              "name": "净化修道院 Purifying the Monastery",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Purifying the Monastery\">净化修道院</h2>\n<p>修道院内的四尊雕像已被苦迦菩提与灵堕魔亵渎并腐化。为了阻止苦迦菩提的影响外溢至柳岸镇，并进入修道院的地下区域，PC必须净化这四尊雕像。随着PC将每尊雕像恢复至原本状态，苦迦菩提对修道院的掌控就会减弱。</p>\n<p>这些雕像可以按任意顺序净化，而净化某尊雕像会在修道院内触发与之对应的事件，无论被恢复的是哪一尊。每净化一尊雕像，苦迦菩提对遗迹的掌控便会削弱，而修道院创立者、被压迫且徘徊不去的魂魄——@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}大师——会变得更强大，也更能协助PC。</p>\n<p>雕像位于庭院（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}）、正殿（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e3mainhall0000]{E3}）、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}的圣坛（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e5pharasmass00]{E5}），以及葬园（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e12burialgar00]{E12}）。每当其中一尊被净化时，便会发生下述事件。要净化一尊雕像，PC必须执行以下行动；其他PC可以使用“净化雕像”允许的任一技能，以协助来帮助该行动。</p>\n<p>注意：对某些团来说，“净化这些雕像”的想法可能并不明显，尤其是因为在第一尊雕像被净化之前，智惠的幽魂无法直接与PC接触。若你的团属于这种情况，他们可能会在噩梦或梦境（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09resting0000000]{休息}）中获得提示；或者，你也可以允许PC在探索修道院遗迹时，至少遭遇四尊雕像中的两尊后，自动意识到这是一个可行选项。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>净化雕像</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>需求</strong> 雕像所在的遭遇区域内所有敌对生物均被击败。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花费10分钟向雕像的守护魂魄献上祷告、清理或修复雕像所受的伤害，或移除恶性的结痂与超自然印记。尝试一次@Check[religion|dc:20]检定、一次@Check[crafting|dc:22]检定，或一次@Check[thievery|dc:24]检定。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 雕像被净化。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 雕像被净化，但在你这么做时，被从雕像中驱逐出的纯粹憎恶以减弱的冲击爆发反噬。你受到@Damage[2d6[mental]]伤害（@Check[will|dc:22|basic]豁免）。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 雕像仍未被净化。一阵心灵怒火的冲击向你爆发，令你以及任何尝试协助你净化雕像的人都受到@Damage[5d6[mental]]伤害（@Check[will|dc:22|basic]豁免）。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 同失败，但伤害为@Damage[10d6[mental]]，且在1小时内无人可以再次尝试净化这尊特定的雕像。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Purifying the Monastery\">Purifying the Monastery</h2>\n<p>Four statues in the monastery have been desecrated and corrupted by Kugaptee and the nindorus. To stem Kugaptee’s influence from overflowing into Willowshore and to reach the underground area of the monastery, the PCs must purify these four statues. As the PCs restore each statue to its original state, Kugaptee’s hold on the monastery weakens.</p>\n<p>The statues can be purified in any order, and purifying a statue triggers a corresponding event within the monastery regardless of which statue is restored. As each statue is purified, Kugaptee’s hold over the ruins diminishes, and the oppressed, lingering spirit of the monastery’s founder, Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}, grows more powerful and more able to assist the PCs.</p>\n<p>The statues are located in the courtyard (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e2courtyard000]{E2}), the main hall (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e3mainhall0000]{E3}), @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma's} shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e5pharasmass00]{E5}), and the burial garden (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e12burialgar00]{E12}). As each is purified, the events below take place. To purify a statue, a PC must perform the following activity; other PCs can Aid in this activity using any of the skills allowed by Purify Statue.</p>\n<p>Note that for some groups, the idea of purifying these statues might not be obvious, especially since Zhi Hui’s ghost can’t directly contact the PCs until the first of the statues is purified. If your group falls into this category, they could receive hints as part of nightmares or dreams (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09resting0000000]{Resting}), or you could just allow the PCs to automatically realize this is an option once they’ve encountered at least two of the four statues while exploring the monastery ruins.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Purify Statue</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Requirements</strong> All hostile creatures in the encounter area where the statue is located are defeated.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend 10 minutes offering prayers to the statue’s guardian spirits, cleaning or repairing damage done to the statue, or removing malignant encrustations and supernatural markings. Attempt a @Check[religion|dc:20] check, a @Check[crafting|dc:22] check, or a @Check[thievery|dc:24] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The statue is purified.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The statue is purified, but as you do so, a weakened blast of pure loathing lashes out as it’s driven from the statue. You take @Damage[2d6[mental]] damage (@Check[will|dc:22|basic] save).</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The statue remains unpurified. A blast of psychic rage lashes out at you, inflicting @Damage[5d6[mental]] damage (@Check[will|dc:22|basic] save) to you and anyone who attempted to Aid your attempt to Purify the Statue.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but @Damage[10d6[mental]] damage, and no one can attempt to Purify this particular Statue again for 1 hour.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Resting": {
              "name": "休息 Resting",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Resting\">休息</h2>\n<p>整座修道院都应让PC感到不安全；在他们发现藏匿的图书馆（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}）之前，一旦需要休息，最好就从遗迹中撤退。PC走过朝圣之径后，那些怪异的扭曲便会消退，而沿着小径徒步3英里返回山中圣所，则是撤退并过夜休息最安全的地方。修道院里的敌人是否会在PC这么做时追出来攻击他们，由你决定；但至少，那些在遗迹内睡眠的人应当承受令人胆寒的噩梦：被活埋、悲惨的转生，或因背叛而遭受痛苦且血腥的死亡。将这些噩梦视为每名PC都成为一次 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Uqj344bezBq3ESdq]{Nightmare} 法术的目标（@Check[will|dc:23] 意志豁免）。当PC净化修道院中的四座雕像后（见下一节），这些噩梦便会结束；此后在遗迹中休息仍往往会做噩梦，但不再具有先前那般使人衰弱的效果。如果你的玩家起初没有意识到净化修道院内的雕像竟然也是一种选择，你可以用这些噩梦在PC心中种下暗示术，让他们尝试以此方式反抗已笼罩遗迹的那股诡异邪恶影响。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Resting\">Resting</h2>\n<p>The entire monastery should feel unsafe to the PCs, and until they discover the hidden library (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{E11}), it’s best to retreat from the ruins should the need to rest arise. Once the PCs have walked the Pilgrim’s Path, the strange distortions fade, and the 3-mile hike along the path back to the Mountain Shrine is the safest place to retreat to for a night’s rest. Whether or not enemies from the monastery seek out the PCs to attack them if they do so is left for you to decide, but at the very least, those who sleep within the ruins should endure harrowing nightmares of being buried alive, of tragic reincarnations, or of painful and grisly deaths from betrayals. Treat these nightmares as if the PCs were each targeted by a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Uqj344bezBq3ESdq]{Nightmare} spell (@Check[will|dc:23] save). These nightmares end once the PCs purify the four statues in the monastery (see the following section), after which resting in the ruins still tends to cause bad dreams, but not to the debilitating effect they manifested before. If your players don’t realize that purifying the statues found within the monastery is even an option in the first place, you can use these nightmares to plant the suggestion to do so in the PCs’ minds as a way to potentially fight back against the eldritch, evil influence that has settled over the ruins.</p>"
            },
            "Tan Sugi Monastery": {
              "name": "谭杉寺 Tan Sugi Monastery",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Tan Sugi Monastery\">谭杉寺</h1>\n<p>谭杉寺的建造方式旨在致敬并衬托那些最初将智惠大师带到此地的杉树。寺院坐落在一座森林茂密的休眠破火山口中，围绕着当地最高的一棵树而建——那正是从谭隋靖的遗体上生长出来的树，扎根于她宿敌、灵堕魔苦迦菩提的坟冢之上。寺院的建造者清除了几棵树，但将这棵高大的杉树以及另外九棵较小的杉树纳入寺院设计之中，随后以自然为主题装饰环绕树丛的步道与木制建筑。寺院的木墙与石质地基上雕刻着植物、动物与各类魂魄的形象，南侧庭院点缀着小型神龛，为来访的魂魄提供栖身之处。寺院南侧的一道门欢迎访客，但遍布场地的道路如今大多已被粗厚、带刺的杂草覆盖。构成寺院的六座木屋都拥有高耸的层叠屋顶，拱起至40英尺高；而中央那棵杉树接近一百英尺，几乎将此高度加倍，巍然俯瞰整个院落。</p>\n<p>寺院的设计不仅用于容纳僧侣，也作为朝圣者前来静修的场所。中央道路通往大殿，僧侣与访客每日在此集会祈祷与冥想；另外五座附属建筑则作为僧侣的住处与其他设施。智惠大师最初建造寺院时，希望在林间各处创造用于观察、冥想与自省的空间，这些空间是谭杉寺所独有的。</p>\n<p>如今，寺院已成废墟。曾经精心打理的庭院被杂草吞没。泥泞与落叶铺满步道，屋顶与墙壁上的破洞让雨水侵入，致使多数建筑内部遭受伤害。在领袖逝世后，虔诚的僧侣们弃寺而去；留下的人则落入苦迦菩提的影响之下，而当这一地区被转化为思维空间时，那些僧侣也随之死去。然而，与PC与柳岸镇的居民不同，这些僧侣死后化为苦迦菩提的不死爪牙，如今听命于统治遗迹的灵堕魔恶魔们的任性驱使。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Tan Sugi Monastery\">Tan Sugi Monastery</h1>\n<p>The Tan Sugi monastery was constructed in a way that honors and complements the sugi trees that first brought Master Zhi Hui to the region. Nestled in a thickly forested dormant caldera, the monastery was built around the tallest tree in the region—the same tree that grew from Tan Sui-Jing’s body over the grave of her nemesis, the nindoru Kugaptee. The monastery’s creators cleared away several trees but incorporated this tall sugi tree, as well as nine smaller ones, into the monastery’s design then proceeded to decorate the walkways and wooden buildings surrounding the grove with motifs of nature. Depictions of plants, animals, and various spirits were carved into the wooden walls and stone foundations of the monastery, and small shrines dot the southern courtyard to provide shelter for visiting spirits. A gate at the southern side of the monastery welcomes visitors, but the pathways laid throughout the grounds are now mostly overgrown by thick, spiky weeds. The six wooden buildings that make up the monastery have tall tiered roofs that arch to a height of 40 feet, but at nearly a hundred feet, the central sugi tree more than doubles this height, looming properly over the entire compound.</p>\n<p>The monastery was designed not only to house monks but also as a place for pilgrims to come and meditate. The central path leads to the main hall, where monks and visitors gathered daily to pray and meditate, while five outbuildings served the monks as living quarters and other facilities. When Master Zhi Hui first built the monastery, she wanted to create spaces throughout the grove for observation, meditation, and introspection unique to the Tan Sugi monastery.</p>\n<p>Today, the monastery is in ruins. The once well-maintained courtyards are overgrown with weeds. Mud and fallen leaves litter the walkways, and holes in the roofs and walls have allowed the rain to damage most of the buildings’ interiors. After the devout monks abandoned the monastery in the wake of their leader’s death, those who remained fell under Kugaptee’s influence, and when the region was transformed into a mindscape, those monks died as well. Unlike the PCs and the citizens of Willowshore, though, the monks rose as undead minions of Kugaptee and now serve at the whims of the nindoru fiends who rule the ruins.</p>"
            },
            "In the Ruins of Wisdom": {
              "name": "智慧遗迹 In the Ruins of Wisdom",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"In the Ruins of Wisdom\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第7章：</span>\n  <span>智惠遗迹之中</span>\n</h1>\n<p>旅程的最后一段，将见蜿蜒的朝圣之径在靠近山峰的一处最后山脊上再度攀升，随后下行进入一处宽阔的圆形山谷——因为谭杉寺就建在一座小型、沉寂已久的火山那古老、林木繁茂的破火山口之中。大约在日落前一小时（也是PC们抵达废墟寺院之前），他们会来到朝圣之径的尽头：那里有一座小神龛，旁边立着一道朴素的木拱门，高高耸立在他们过去几天一直沿着行进的道路之上。随着PC们靠近，空气中的寒意突然消退。令人安心的秋日暖意笼罩了这片区域，鸟儿的歌唱与蝉鸣充盈耳畔，连周围森林的气息也变得更加鲜明而舒缓。</p>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{智惠}大师的精魂感知察觉到PC们的接近；尽管她的幽灵（特征）此刻仍被困在寺院之中，但PC们已走过朝圣之径这一事实，让她获得了一个机会来奖赏他们——具体取决于PC们在三座神龛中有多少成功达成了开悟。</p>\n<p><strong>少于三座神龛：</strong>PC们感到某种无形的力量对他们感到失望。他们明白自己应沿路退回，前往那些错过的神龛寻求开悟。回到这些神龛后，以额外的幻象或来自彼岸的神秘催促形式，让他们获得更多关于如何达成开悟的洞见。若他们愿意，也可以继续向寺院推进，但将不会获得任何额外益处。</p>\n<p><strong>三座神龛全部完成：</strong>如果PC们在三座神龛都达成了开悟，他们会感到一种欢迎般的自豪感，但也同样会感到前路存在不容忽视的危险。除了这些感受之外，PC们还会经历一种冲动，想要调查道路旁的小神龛。若他们这么做，就会在神龛中发现数件强大的魔法物品——这些是由智惠之力在此显现的赋礼，其方式与苦迦菩提更强大的存在在思维空间中显现出如此多怪物的方式极为相似。</p>\n<p>本战役的冒险工具箱为这些@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20pilgrimagegi00]{朝圣礼物}提供了数种不同选项。为每位PC选择一件与其能力、主题与兴趣相符的物品作为奖励——PC们应会本能地识别出哪一份赋礼是为自己准备的。或者，你也可以将冒险工具箱中提供的物品作为模板，设计并制作你自己的定制赋礼。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-kurobozo-fight.webp\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"In the Ruins of Wisdom\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 7:</span>\n  <span>In the Ruins of Wisdom</span>\n</h1>\n<p>The final leg of the journey sees the winding Pilgrim’s Path rise over one final crest near a mountain peak before descending down into a wide, circular valley—for the Tan Sugi monastery is built within the ancient, forested caldera of a small and long dormant volcano. About an hour before sunset (and the PCs’ arrival at the ruined monastery), they’ll come to the end of the Pilgrim’s Path, where a small shrine stands next to a plain wooden arch that looms over the route they’ve been following for the past few days. As the PCs approach, the chill in the air suddenly abates. As a comforting fall warmth settles over the area, the sound of singing birds and chirping cicadas fills the air, and even the scent of the surrounding forest grows more vibrant and soothing.</p>\n<p>Master @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21zhihui00000000]{Zhi Hui}’s spirit senses the PCs’ approach, and while her ghost remains trapped within the monastery for now, the fact that the PCs have walked the Pilgrim’s Path gives her a chance to reward them, depending on how many of the three shrines the PCs have managed to achieve enlightenment at.</p>\n<p><strong>Fewer than Three Shrines:</strong> The PCs feel that some unseen force is disappointed in them. They understand that they should retreat along the path to seek enlightenment at the shrines they missed. Upon returning to these shrines, give them more insight into how to achieve enlightenment in the form of additional visions or mysterious urgings from beyond. They can continue to progress toward the monastery instead if they wish but do so without any additional benefits.</p>\n<p><strong>All Three Shrines:</strong> If the PCs have achieved enlightenment at all three shrines, they feel a sense of welcoming pride but also an unmistakable sense of peril at what lies ahead. In addition to these feelings, the PCs also experience an urge to investigate the small shrine alongside the path. If they do so, they find within the shrine several potent magic items—gifts manifested here by Zhi Hui’s power, in much the same way that Kugaptee’s greater presence has manifested so many monsters in the mindscape.</p>\n<p>This campaign’s Adventure Toolbox presents several different options for these @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20pilgrimagegi00]{Pilgrimage Gifts}. Choose one of these items for each PC that’s appropriate for their abilities, themes, and interests as their reward—the PCs should instinctively recognize which gift is intended for each of them. Alternatively, you can use the items presented in the Adventure Toolbox as templates to create customized gifts of your own design.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 3.1: Oblivion of Truth": {
          "name": "第3.1幕：真相的湮灭 Act 3.1: Oblivion of Truth",
          "pages": {
            "End of the Dream": {
              "name": "梦境的终结 End of the Dream",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">梦境终结</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>尽管PC们或许想对知府那悲怆的恳求作出回应，但他们没有时间这么做。一旦他交出自己的日记（或者，作为替代，在战斗中被击败后他恳求苦迦菩提带走他），和善保的身体便猛地一抽一颤，开始痉挛。片刻之后，伴随着布料撕裂的声响，他的身体被撕开，一团绯红蝴蝶从他空洞的躯壳中迸发而出，充满他周围的空气。</p>\n<p>如果这一切发生在宅邸中，背景是镇民正用力捶打宅邸大门，那么那些门会被向内砸开，无面鬼模仿者们汹涌而入，其后跟着一大群嚎叫、尖啸的镇民。若发生在别处，则模仿者与尖叫的镇民会突然从PC们四周冲来，视情况从小巷涌出、从门后扑出，甚至从林中杀出。苦迦菩提在和善保思维空间中的残余影响知道PC们能做到知府做不到的事，而这股影响试图在此阻止他们。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.TmxsF1RiQJ0m8o5M.PlaylistSound.st2Q3xsAFhE8Ko9O]{嚎叫的人群}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>本冒险假定这场战斗发生在知府的宅邸中，但若发生在其他地点，你需要提供一张与周遭环境相符的地图；可以从先前幕次中出现过的城市地点取用一张，或将宅邸地图改作他用。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">梦境终结</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nopperaboimp00]{无面鬼模仿者（4）} | @UUID[Actor.vFNg9BATB9crqnDn]{奥术} @UUID[Actor.aYR61sI47XlE9ul8]{神术} @UUID[Actor.2NmupNwbuAt5GcWy]{武技}@UUID[Actor.UgfzkrEkFrdeegD0]{秘术} @UUID[Actor.vmOACyFUJqWHY8YD]{原初} @UUID[Actor.n9L4akwW1KlBXQQd]{娴熟}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>此时，四名无面鬼模仿者上前挑战PC们——嚎叫与尖啸的镇民们留在后方，为他们的“英雄”无面鬼们助威，但不会参加战斗。当被杀死时，每一名无面鬼都会爆裂成一团转瞬即逝的红色蝴蝶云。一旦最后一名被击败（或一旦PC们被杀死），PC们周围的思维空间便会淡去，其在本轮循环中的目的已然达成，他们会回到柳岸镇思维空间——也就是他们最初施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{思维空间转移}之处。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.Sl4VZHQv6huLUvlu]{显现} <br />\n  和善保的日记（连同他的<em>高等雄辩颈圈</em>、<em>+1 强击 长剑</em>、<em>+1 韧性 软垫护甲</em>以及他的<em>高等储物袖</em>）会在PC们返回自己的思维空间时，与他们一同显现。回到此思维空间的行为也改变了日记本身——它仍包含数十张散页与卷轴（这些文书包含PC们在下一章所需的重要研究，此外还有<em>复生术</em>的配方），但日记本身已变成一本<em>中等复原净化典籍</em>。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>因直面知府并取得他关于移魂仪式的笔记，给予PC们120 XP。此外，若PC们是在其自愿协助的情况下获得了和善保的帮助，则再给予PC们如同在战斗中击败他一般的XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">End of the Dream</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Though the PCs might wish to react to the governor’s tragic plea, they won’t have time to do so. Once he hands over his journal (or alternatively, once he begs Kugaptee to take him after being defeated in combat), Heh Shan-Bao’s body lurches and thrashes as he goes into convulsions. A moment later, his body rips open to the sound of tearing fabric, and a cloud of crimson butterflies erupts from his hollow shell to fill the air around him.</p>\n<p>If this takes place in the manor with the backdrop of townsfolk hammering on the doors to the manor, those doors smash inward and the noppera-bo impersonators surge through with a mass of howling, shrieking townsfolk behind them. If this take place elsewhere, then the impersonators and shrieking townsfolk suddenly rush at the PCs from their surroundings, surging out of alleys or from doors or even the woods as appropriate. Kugaptee’s remaining influence in Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape knows that the PCs can achieve what the governor couldn’t, and that influence attempts to stop them here.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.TmxsF1RiQJ0m8o5M.PlaylistSound.st2Q3xsAFhE8Ko9O]{Howling Crowd}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> This adventure assumes this fight takes place in the governor’s manor, but if it takes place elsewhere, you’ll need to provide a map to match the surroundings, perhaps pulling one from a previous city location featured in an earlier act or repurposing the map of the manor.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">End of the Dream</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nopperaboimp00]{Noppera-bo Impersonators (4)} | @UUID[Actor.vFNg9BATB9crqnDn]{Arcane} @UUID[Actor.aYR61sI47XlE9ul8]{Divine} @UUID[Actor.2NmupNwbuAt5GcWy]{Martial}@UUID[Actor.UgfzkrEkFrdeegD0]{Occult} @UUID[Actor.vmOACyFUJqWHY8YD]{Primal} @UUID[Actor.n9L4akwW1KlBXQQd]{Skilled}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>At this point, the four noppera-bo impersonators step forward to challenge the PCs—the howling and shrieking townsfolk remain behind and cheer on their “heroes,” the noppera-bos, but don’t take part in the fight. When slain, each of these noppera-bos bursts into a cloud of short-lived red butterflies. As soon as the final one is defeated (or as soon as the PCs are slain), the mindscape around the PCs fades, its purpose for this cycle fulfilled, and they return to the Willowshore mindscape where they cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} in the first place.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.Sl4VZHQv6huLUvlu]{Manifestation} <br />\n  Heh Shan-Bao’s journal (along with his <em>greater choker of elocution</em>, <em>+1 striking longsword</em>, <em>+1 resilient padded armor</em>, and his <em>greater sleeves of storage</em>) manifest along with the PCs when they return to their own mindscape. The act of returning to this mindscape has transformed the journal as well—it still contains dozens of loose sheets and scrolls (these documents contain the important research the PCs will need in the next chapter, in addition to the formula for <em>resurrect</em>), but the journal itself has become a <em>moderate tome of restorative cleansing</em>.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> For confronting the governor and obtaining his notes on the transmigrate ritual, grant the PCs 120 XP. In addition, if the PCs received Heh Shan-Bao’s help willingly, grant the PCs XP as if they’d defeated him in combat.</p>"
            },
            "Asking for Help": {
              "name": "寻求帮助 Asking for Help",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Asking for Help\">请求帮助</h2>\n<p>最终，PC们应该会谈到他们来到这里的根本原因——请求帮助，逃离他们所有人都被困住的思维空间。当他们直接请求协助逃脱时，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}颓然瘫下，深吸一口气，又长长地、颤抖着叹出一声，随后承认了一件他一直以来都害怕说出口的事。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“也许……确实有办法。我们都死了。苦迦菩提杀了我们所有人。也就是说，是我杀了我们所有人。但我们的灵魂并没有前往来世。我们被困在这里——困在用苦迦菩提的梦境与我们自身的恐惧铸成的牢笼里。</p>\n  <p>“可只要工具得当，任何牢笼都能打开。唉，可那些工具不在我触及之内。我看得见它们，却用不了。”他的眼中第一次泛起希望，并伸出一只戴着手套的手。</p>\n  <p>“不过，也许……你们能完成我已经开始的事？对。对！你们不是苦迦菩提。你们的灵魂与心智仍属于你们自己。你们仍能迁回生者的领域，仍能从死亡中以转生术归来。完成我开始的事！只要你们找到办法，我们就都能逃脱！”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>说完这些，和善保总督把手伸进他的<em>高等储物袖</em>中，取出一本厚厚的日志，里面夹满散页与潦草涂写的卷轴——那是他关于仪式的全部笔记：他原本希望借此强化谭杉树；以及他在每一次思维空间循环中所做的研究，试图创造一个<em>迁移</em>仪式，好逃回活人的世界。</p>\n<p>总督把笔记交出去后，最后又问了一次：“你们不会残忍对待黑豆吧？她没得选，她的主人不是她能决定的。她什么错都没有。”</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Asking for Help\">Asking for Help</h2>\n<p>Eventually, the PCs should get around to the reason they’ve come here in the first place—to ask for help in escaping the mindscape they’ve all been trapped in. Asked directly for aid in escaping, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} slumps in defeat, takes a deep breath and exhales a long, shuddering sigh, and then admits something he has been afraid to say this whole time.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“There might just be a way. We’re dead. Kugaptee slew us all. That is to say, I slew us all. But our souls didn’t move on to the afterlife. We became trapped here, in cages forged from Kugaptee’s dreams and our own fears.</p>\n  <p>“But with the right tools, any cage can be opened. Alas, those tools lie beyond my reach. I can see them, but I can’t use them.” His eyes turn hopeful for the first time, and he holds out one gloved hand.</p>\n  <p>“Perhaps, though... you could finish what I’ve started? Yes. Yes! You aren’t Kugaptee. Your souls and minds remain your own. You can still transmigrate back to the living realm, still reincarnate back from death. Finish what I started! We can all escape if you find the way!”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>With that, Governor Heh reaches into his <em>greater sleeves of storage</em> and withdraws a thick journal filled with loose pages and scribbled scrolls—the total of his notes on the ritual he hoped would strengthen the Tan Sugi tree as well as those he worked on each mindscape cycle to create a <em>transmigrate</em> ritual to escape back to the living world.</p>\n<p>Once the governor hands over his notes, he asks one final time, “You won’t be cruel to Black Bean, will you? She didn’t choose her master. She didn’t do anything wrong.”</p>"
            },
            "Know and Despair": {
              "name": "知晓与绝望 Know and Despair",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Know and Despair\">知晓与绝望</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-baoheh.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Heh Shan-Bao\" alt=\"dishevelled human man\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-baoheh.webp')\" />\n<p>如果PC们赢得了总督的信任，他会同意在自己的宅邸与他们交谈；若他们尚未到那里，他还会提出立刻护送他们前往。和善保带领PC们来到宅邸东南角的会客室，请他们与他一同坐在其中一张长桌旁的坐垫上。在这间看似闲置的会议室那种无菌般的环境里，他衣衫不整的模样，以及他举止间不复往日精确优雅的状态，都显得更为明显。尽管宅邸里看不到任何仆役，桌上却摆着一桌食物与饮品，包括丰盛的肉菜、热茶，以及大量酒精——而总督对此毫不惊讶。若被问起，他耸耸肩说：“我的仆人离开了，但在这里，我的需要仍会得到照料。”仿佛这就足以解释一切——事实上，正是思维空间本身按需维持着他的营养。</p>\n<p>他用颤抖的双手为桌上每个人斟倒（也许这是对PC们出人意料的敬意表现）之后，一声突兀而细小的吱叫打破了沉默：一只小黑猫从一堆枕头搭成的窝里探出头来。猫的出现终于让总督开口，他的声音此刻柔和，且微微发颤。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“你们还记得我的猫，黑豆吗？多么优秀的猫。多么小的猫。你们不会对黑豆残忍吧？她会替你们抓老鼠。她还能陪孩子们玩。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}随即转向食物，摆出一碗碗米饭，每一碗中央都直直插着一双黑色筷子。他把它们利落地放在每只茶杯旁，随后猛然在桌首自己的座位上坐下。总督的猫又吱叫了一声，从它那柔软的“宫殿”里窜出来跳到男人腿上；总督迟疑了一下，才抚摸起这只毛茸茸的生物。</p>\n<p>PC们应当会自动认出：插着香或将筷子直立插入米饭的做法，是给死者的供品。再结合他先前为PC们奉茶的敬意之举，他们可以尝试一次 @Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] 察言观色检定——成功时，他们意识到总督并非把他们当作活人对待，而是当作鬼魂。总督用这种不言而喻的方式向PC们传达他的意思，但由于他心智濒临崩坏，除非先被询问，否则他很难用言语解释任何事。随着谈话进行，太阳落山（无论讨论开始时是什么时辰），PC们还会听到前门处不断增强的刮擦与捶击声。和善保对此置若罔闻，除非PC们试图调查；若他们这么做，他会命令英雄们别管，除非他们想死。看来总督的结界不知为何已经削弱，让外头的镇民开始试图破门而入。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.TmxsF1RiQJ0m8o5M.PlaylistSound.2eBD8ZQAMj7hPoRh]{Pounding at the Manor Walls}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>无论这段对话需要多长时间才能演完，与总督的谈话都应涵盖下列大多数要点，其中还包括建议你朗读的示例台词。</p>\n<p><strong>柳岸镇之死：</strong>如果PC们质疑总督献上的米饭、驱逐不死的符箓，或以其他方式询问思维空间或如何逃离，和善保会苦涩地轻笑一声才回答：“你们还没弄明白吗？你们肯定已经有所怀疑。我的符箓、镇民们的怪异举止、把我们领地围得水泄不通的屏障——它们都指向同一件事。我们都不过是饥饿鬼魂。”如果PC们因当地禁忌而抗议总督使用“鬼魂”一词，男人会阴沉地笑起来，然后一掌拍在桌上，震得茶杯叮当作响。“别这么天真！你以为友善的问候就能把你从坟墓里救出来？你们还在躲着夜里吹口哨或洗衣服吗？你们怕自己冒犯了什么，然后把自己吃掉吗？啊？不……我们都死了。如今我们已欲泣无息。那段日子已经过去了。自从春末那天起，我们就死了。自从苦迦菩提把我们全都杀了之后。”</p>\n<p><strong>毁灭的原因：</strong>“苦迦菩提从谭杉下方的坟里发作了。人们怎么说来着？‘把鳗鱼的头砍下来，它照样还能咬人。’”总督啜了一口茶，然后盯着杯中的液体看了片刻。“你们知道他在下面吗？你们至少也该有所怀疑。柳岸镇是个怪地方。谁能想到，一个偏僻小村竟会有如此圣洁的传承，或藏着如此不可思议的邪恶？”</p>\n<p><strong>苦迦菩提的苏醒：</strong>如果PC们问是什么挑衅了苦迦菩提，和善保会停顿片刻，羞愧地垂下头，然后迅速吸一口气作答：“是我。多么可怕的事，都是我干的。来吧，恨我吧。让你们的怒火把你们从鬼魂变成复仇的恶灵，把所有威胁我们城镇的人统统吞噬！”</p>\n<p>随后，总督发出失控的狂笑。待他冷静下来之后（很可能要等某位PC采取措施安抚他才行），和善保才恢复镇定并解释道，声音低哑而破碎。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“我太愚蠢了。我想保护柳岸镇不受苦迦菩提伤害，想在络新妇找到他之前把他藏起来。像苦迦菩提这样强大的邪恶无法被阻止，只能被封印。他挣脱出来的部分越多，就越会试图吞噬我们。只要那棵神圣的树仍因他的毒素而恶心，某个蜘蛛女人终究会被引向苦迦菩提的坟墓。她们想法跟我一样，你明白吗？她们喜爱强力的仆从，也喜爱美丽的人。嗯，我是个罪人，但我的罪还差络新妇一千条。你们从未爱过我或我的帝国，但你们根本想象不到络新妇到来时会对你们做什么。</p>\n  <p>“我试图治愈谭杉，帮它继续囚禁那魔物，可即使在死亡之后，苦迦菩提也强大到让我无法战胜。我以为自己能像操控寻常灵体那样控制他，但他远超我所能想象的一切。多么宏伟的存在！多么宏伟的邪恶！若有一位心地纯净、无尘无累的女祭司，也许还有一线机会。对他而言，我什么也不是。他把我吞噬了，里里外外，每一部分。你们现在明白了吗？我就是苦迦菩提——屠戮了你们所有人的那头野兽。我就是把你们囚禁在这里的恶人！”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>怪物与闹鬼：</strong>“苦迦菩提或许杀了你们，但他依然死着且被囚禁着，他的舌头贪婪地垂着，渴望你们的鲜血。他满脑子只想着吞噬那些他尝过味道的人。那些无脸的娃娃和嘶嘶作响的生物，折磨着我们的城镇——那是他的第一步。当你们鲁莽地来到这里时，苦迦菩提用牙齿从你们的灵魂上撕下一小块，把它变成了仆从。即便此刻，你们的替身也在猛砸这座宅邸的大门，渴望夺走你们的面孔据为己有。你们一旦离开这里，等着你们的就是它们。你们的命运就是如此。你们瞧……像我们这样的鬼魂，也能再死一次……”</p>\n<p><strong>我们来自与你不同的思维空间：</strong>在回答之前，和善保停顿了一下，然后难以置信地摇头。“荒唐。你们一直都在这里。死亡会对心智做些事，你懂的。没事的。我理解。”在他们与他相处的短暂时间里，无论PC们怎么说，都无法让善保相信：并非只有这一个思维空间，是由他失败的结果所升起的。</p>\n<p><strong>我们现在该怎么办？</strong>“你们为什么要问我？宽恕已经太迟了。我们都死了。到头来，我什么都保护不了。我作为总督失败了。我作为救星失败了。我作为一个人也失败了。你们指望我能以某种方式救你们吗？指望我的魔法能让你们起死回生？还是说，你们想跟我做个了断？”</p>\n<p>PC们现在可以选择与总督战斗，或解释他们当前的处境并请求他的帮助。尽管由于压力，他在言语上可能咄咄逼人，但除非先遭到攻击，否则善保不会动手。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Know and Despair\">Know and Despair</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-baoheh.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Heh Shan-Bao\" alt=\"dishevelled human man\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-baoheh.webp')\" />\n<p>If the PCs win the governor’s trust, he’ll agree to speak with them in his manor, offering to escort them there at once if they aren’t there already. Governor Heh leads the PCs to the manor’s meeting room in the southeast corner, asking them to be seated with him on the cushions that surround one of the long tables. His disheveled appearance and the way he moves without his former precise grace are all the more apparent here in the sterile environment of what looks like an unused meeting room. Despite the lack of any servants in the manor, a spread of food and drink, including hearty meat dishes, hot tea, and plenty of alcohol, waits on the table, a development the governor accepts without surprise. If asked, he shrugs and says, “My servants are gone, but my needs are attended nonetheless in this place,” as if that’s all that needs to be said—in truth, the mindscape itself keeps him nourished as needed.</p>\n<p>After pouring for everyone at the table with shaking hands (perhaps an unexpected display of respect toward the PCs), the sudden, tiny squeak of a small black cat breaks the silence as the feline peeks out from a nest of pillows. The cat’s appearance causes the governor to finally speak, his voice now soft and trembling slightly.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“You remember my cat, Black Bean? Such an excellent cat. Such a little cat. You wouldn’t be cruel to Black Bean, would you? She would hunt mice for you. She could play with the children.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} then turns to the food, setting out small bowls of rice, black chopsticks plunged upright in the center of all of them. He places them down sharply next to each teacup before abruptly sitting down at his place at the head of the table. The governor’s cat squeaks again, scampering from its soft palace into the man’s lap, and the governor hesitates before petting the fuzzy creature.</p>\n<p>The PCs should automatically recognize that rice with incense sticks or upright chopsticks is meant as an offering for the dead. This, combined with his earlier act of respect by serving tea to the PCs, allows them to attempt a @Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] check to Sense Motive—on a success, they realize the governor is treating them not as if they were alive, but as if they were ghosts. The governor is being very blatant in his unspoken message to the PCs, but due to his ruinous state of mind, he has difficulty explaining anything verbally unless asked first. As the conversation progresses, the sun sets (regardless of the time of day when the discussion began), and the PCs can hear the increasing sound of scraping and pounding at the front doors. Heh Shan-Bao ignores it unless the PCs attempt to investigate, at which point he demands the heroes leave it alone unless they want to die. It appears that the governor’s wards have somehow weakened, allowing the townsfolk outside to begin trying to break in.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.TmxsF1RiQJ0m8o5M.PlaylistSound.2eBD8ZQAMj7hPoRh]{Pounding at the Manor Walls}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>Regardless of how long it takes to play out, the conversation with the governor should cover most of the talking points below, which include suggested dialogue for you to read aloud.</p>\n<p><strong>Willowshore’s Death:</strong> If the PCs question the governor’s offering of rice, the undead-repelling fulus, or otherwise inquire about the mindscape or how to escape it, Heh Shan-Bao chuckles ruefully before he answers. “Haven’t you figured it out? You must have suspected. My fulus, the townspeople’s strange behavior, the impassible barriers around our domain, they all point to the same thing. We are all nothing more than hungry ghosts.” If the PCs protest Governor Heh’s use of the word “ghost” due to local taboo, the man laughs bleakly, then slams his hand on the table, rattling the teacups. “Don’t be so naive! Do you think that friendly greetings will save you from the grave? Do you still avoid whistling or doing laundry at night? Are you scared you’ll get offended and eat yourselves? Huh? No... we’re all dead. We have no breath to cry now. That time is behind us. We’ve been dead since the last day of spring. Since Kugaptee killed us all.”</p>\n<p><strong>Cause of Destruction:</strong> “Kugaptee lashed out from his grave beneath the Tan Sugi. What’s it they say? ‘Cut off the head of an eel, and it can still bite.’” The governor sips from his cup of tea, then stares into the liquid for a moment. “Did you know he was down there? Surely you must have at least suspected. Willowshore is a strange place. Who would have thought a backwater village would have such a saintly legacy, or hide such an unfathomable evil?”</p>\n<p><strong>Kugaptee’s Awakening:</strong> If the PCs ask what provoked Kugaptee, Heh Shan-Bao pauses a moment, hanging his head in shame before taking a brisk breath to answer: “I did. What a terrible thing I’ve done. Go ahead, hate me for it. Let your rage turn you from ghosts into vengeful spirits, and devour all who threaten our town!”</p>\n<p>The governor then lapses into unhinged laughter. After calming down (likely not until a PC takes steps to calm him), Heh Shan-Bao sobers and explains, his voice low and ragged.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“It was foolish. I wanted to protect Willowshore from Kugaptee, to hide him before the jorogumo found him. An evil as powerful as Kugaptee can’t be stopped, only sealed. The more of him that shakes loose, the more he will try to consume us. And so long as that sacred tree remains sickened by his poisons, one of the spider women will be drawn to Kugaptee’s grave eventually. They think like me, do you understand? They love powerful servitors and beautiful people. Well, I’m a sinful man, but I’m a thousand sins short of jorogumo. You never loved me or my empire, but you have no idea what the jorogumo will do to you when they arrive.</p>\n  <p>“I sought to heal the Tan Sugi, to help it keep the fiend imprisoned, but even in death, Kugaptee was too powerful for me to overcome. I thought I could control him like a mere spirit, but he was beyond what I could have possibly imagined. What a magnificent being! What magnificent evil! A pure-hearted priestess, free of earthly attachments, might have stood a chance. I was nothing to him. He devoured me, every part, inside and out. Do you see now? I am Kugaptee, the beast that slaughtered you all. I am the villain who keeps you imprisoned here!”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>The Monsters and Hauntings:</strong> “Kugaptee might have killed you, but he’s still dead and imprisoned, his tongue lolling hungrily toward your blood. He thinks of nothing but consuming those he has tasted. Those faceless dolls and hissing creatures that plague our town are his first step. When you rashly came here, Kugaptee pulled a tiny piece of your soul away with his teeth and turned it into a servitor. Even now, your doubles hammer at the doors to this manor, eager to take your faces for their own. That’s who waits for you when you leave this place. That’s what fate has in store for you. You see... ghosts like us can die, too...”</p>\n<p><strong>We came from a different mindscape than yours:</strong> Before he replies, Governor Heh pauses, then shakes his head in disbelief. “Nonsense. You’ve been here all along. Death does things to the mind, you know. It’s okay. I understand.” Nothing the PCs might say can convince Shan-Bao in the short time they have with him that this mindscape isn’t the only one that rose as a result of his failure.</p>\n<p><strong>What do we do now?</strong> “Why would you ask me? It is too late for forgiveness. We’re all dead. In the end, I couldn’t protect anything. I failed as a governor. I failed as a savior. I failed as a human being. Were you hoping I could somehow save you? That my magic could bring you back to life? Or do you want to have it out?”</p>\n<p>The PCs now have a choice to either fight the governor or to explain their current situation and ask for his help. Though he can be verbally belligerent due to his stressful situation, Shan-Bao won’t fight unless attacked first.</p>"
            },
            "Fighting the Governor": {
              "name": "与总督作战 Fighting the Governor",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">与总督战斗</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span>\n</h2>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shan-bao-heh.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">与总督战斗</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.2nzFpUAKC7MMxWka]{和善保}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>如果PC与他交战，和善保会尽其所能反击。若在其宅邸之外与他对峙，他的目标是逃离战斗并回到家中的安全之所；但若在宅邸内遭到攻击，他会战斗至死。尽管如此，和善保是学者而非战士；若被迫卷入暴力冲突，他更倾向于保持距离。战斗开始时，他会在使用更具攻击性的卷轴之前，尽可能多地使用防御性卷轴。只有当他的卷轴全部耗尽时，他才会诉诸剑术。</p>\n  <p>总督明知自己的思维空间重置后仍会再有机会达成目标，因此会战斗至死。然而，当他死去之际，他的灵魂失去了对自身人性的最后一丝把握，他呼唤苦迦菩提，喘息着说：“我将我的灵魂献给汝，苦迦菩提！解开将我束缚于命运之物！”片刻之后，灵堕魔的存在会如@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10endofthedrea00]{梦境终结}中所述那般作出反应。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Fighting the Governor</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span>\n</h2>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shan-bao-heh.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Fighting the Governor</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.2nzFpUAKC7MMxWka]{Heh Shan-Bao}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If the PCs engage him in combat, Heh Shan-Bao fights back as best he can. If confronted outside of his manor, his goal is to escape the fight and make it back to the safety of his home, but if attacked in the manor, he fights to the death. That said, Heh Shan-Bao is a scholar, not a fighter. He prefers to keep his distance if forced into a violent conflict. At the start of a fight, he uses as many of his defensive scrolls as possible before using his more offensive scrolls. Only when all of his scrolls have been consumed does he resort to swordplay.</p>\n  <p>The governor fights to the death, knowing that he’ll have another chance to achieve his goal once his mindscape resets. As he dies, though, his soul loses the last grip he has on his own humanity, and he calls out to Kugaptee, gasping out, “I offer thee my soul, Kugaptee! Unbind me from that which was my fate!” A few moments later, the nindoru’s presence reacts as detailed in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10endofthedrea00]{End of the Dream}.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Manor Interior": {
              "name": "庄园内部 Manor Interior",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Manor Interior\">宅邸内部</h3>\n<p>总督的宅邸由木材建成。外墙厚实坚固，但内墙由纸制成，并装饰着田园乡村生活或荒野风景的图景。在思维空间形成之前，这座宅邸曾有数名卫兵与宝藏；而如今这些都已不见踪影，使得整座建筑几乎给人一种像是某种展示品的感觉，而非供人起居的家。</p>\n<p>宅邸内没有任何危险在等待PC，因此让他们按自己的意愿使用地图进行探索即可。若他们在白天探索，将不会发现任何值得注意之物。入夜后，总督赫一旦注意到他们到来，便会在庭院中迎上前，要求他们立刻离开。他会做好战斗准备，但不会主动发起战斗；只有当PC先攻击他、开始对他的家造成伤害，或以其他方式采取任何敌对动作时，他才会攻击。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Manor Interior\">Manor Interior</h3>\n<p>The governor’s manor is made of wood. External walls are thick and solid, but internal walls are made of paper and decorated with scenes of idyllic country life or wilderness landscapes. While the manor had several guards and treasures before the mindscape’s formation, today these are missing, leaving the structure feeling almost as if it were a display of some sort, not a home meant to be lived in.</p>\n<p>There are no dangers awaiting the PCs in the manor, so allow them to explore as they see fit, using the map. If they explore during the day, they’ll find nothing of interest. After dark, Governor Heh greets them in the courtyard once he notices their arrival, demanding they leave at once. He prepares for a fight but won’t initiate combat, attacking only if the PCs first attack him, begin to damage his home, or otherwise take any hostile action.</p>"
            },
            "Breaking Into the Manor": {
              "name": "闯入庄园 Breaking Into the Manor",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Breaking Into the Manor\">闯入宅邸</h2>\n<p>如果PC无法获得总督许可进入宅邸，他们可以尝试闯入建筑，以获取他们所需的关键情报——前提是他们先想办法彻底解除或避开宅邸护（例如使用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate}传送进入宅邸）。</p>\n<p>在宅邸内，一切看起来干净整洁，却又诡异地毫无生气、空空如也。如今，赫总督是他宅邸里唯一的住民；他的仆从与卫兵都已各自离世，前往各自的来世——柳岸镇那少数没有被困在思维空间中的市民亦是如此。</p>\n<p>此时，PC提出的任何合情合理的论点或要求，都应自动成功说服山宝坐下来交谈；因此只要PC不主动挑起战斗，就继续进行@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10knowanddespa00]{知晓与绝望}。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Breaking Into the Manor\">Breaking Into the Manor</h2>\n<p>If the PCs are unable to get the governor’s permission to enter the manor, they could attempt to break into the building to get the critical information they need once they figure out how to disable or avoid the manor wards entirely (by using @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate} to teleport into the manor, for example).</p>\n<p>Within the manor, things appear clean and tidy but strangely sterile and empty of life. Governor Heh is the only inhabitant of his manor these days; his servants and guards have simply passed on to their individual afterlives, the few citizens of Willowshore who escaped being trapped in a mindscape.</p>\n<p>At this point, any well-reasoned argument or demand voiced by the PCs should automatically succeed at convincing Shan-Bao to sit down and talk, so assuming the PCs don’t start a fight, proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10knowanddespa00]{Know and Despair}.</p>"
            },
            "Manor Wards": {
              "name": "庄园护卫 Manor Wards",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">庄园结界</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严重 7</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-manorward.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Manor Ward\" alt=\"守护总督宅邸的魔法结界\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-manorward.webp')\" />\n<p>总督明白夜里会变得更加危险，而苦迦菩提的影响在日落之后也更强。他也知道自己因仪式失败而被困在这处思维空间里，但并未意识到柳岸镇的人民在一个平行的思维空间中“幸存”。相反，随着每一轮时间循环不断上演，山-保越来越相信：柳岸镇市民所剩下的，只有那些栖居于他思维空间里的“幽灵”——白天时无知地重复日常职责的幻影，到了夜里便愤怒而复仇，列队向他的庄园进军。</p>\n<p>在内疚的折磨下，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}在每次循环重启时，都会用非魔法的符箓与其他护符形式的魅惑术覆贴在庄园外墙上。随着每一年展开，这些结界的数量愈发增多，以至于在每个循环末尾，整座庄园几乎被这些纸条与飘动的祷告“裹成木乃伊”。尽管这些单张符箓本身并非魔法物品，但它们叠加起来的效果会借由和总督的心灵来保护他的庄园。</p>\n<p>若PC们设法绕过这处危害并进入庄园，请继续进行@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10breakinginto00]{闯入庄园}。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">庄园结界</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">严重 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.3I4bwqook4CXmQ52]{庄园结界}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>这些结界不仅能阻止PC们使用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{思维空间转移}直接进入他的庄园，也会在PC们抵达思维空间后保护总督的庄园免受他们侵扰。任何靠近庄园5尺内的PC都会发现自己无法再前进一步：当他们触发魔法结界时，就像被一堵无形之墙在物理上挡住了一样。与庄园墙壁保持5尺以上距离的PC，可以用10分钟行动来调查这些结界，然后尝试一次@Check[occultism|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[religion|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识。成功时，PC判断这些结界旨在阻挡不死、邪恶魂魄以及来自其他领域的超自然生物靠近，但他们无法解释为何结界会对自己也生效（除了：由于PC是来自另一个思维空间的访客，这些结界有可能将他们解读为魂魄）。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若和善保以能让他们自由穿过结界的篆体封印在PC们手上盖印，则在PC们绕过该危害时给予他们经验值奖励。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Manor Wards</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 7</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-manorward.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Manor Ward\" alt=\"magical ward guarding the governor's mansion\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-manorward.webp')\" />\n<p>The governor understands that things grow more dangerous at night and that Kugaptee’s influence is stronger after the sun sets. He also knows that he has become trapped in this mindscape as the result of his failed ritual but doesn’t realize that the people of Willowshore “survived” in a parallel mindscape. Instead, as each cycle of time plays out, Shan-Bao comes to believe more and more that all that remains of Willowshore’s citizens are the “ghosts” that inhabit his mindscape—phantasms who by day ignorantly repeat their daily duties but who grow angry and vengeful at night as they march upon his manor.</p>\n<p>Tormented by his guilt, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} covers the outer walls of his manor with wards in the form of non-magical fulus and other charms every time the cycle repeats. As each year plays out, the number of these wards increases, so that by the end of each cycle, the manor is all but mummified in these strips of papers and fluttering prayers. While these individual fulus aren’t themselves magic items, the cumulative effect of them draws upon Governor Heh’s psyche to protect his manor.</p>\n<p>If the PCs manage to bypass this hazard and enter the manor, proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10breakinginto00]{Breaking Into the Manor}.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Manor Wards</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.3I4bwqook4CXmQ52]{Manor Wards}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> Beyond preventing the PCs from using @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} to enter his manor directly, these wards also protect the governor’s manor from the PCs once they arrive in the mindscape. A PC who approaches within 5 feet of the manor finds they can’t proceed any further, as if they were physically blocked by an invisible wall when they trigger the magical ward. A PC who remains more than 5 feet from the manor’s walls can Investigate the wards as a 10-minute activity, then attempt a @Check[occultism|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge. On a success, the PC determines these wards are meant to bar the approach of undead, evil spirits, and supernatural creatures from other realms, but they have no explanation as to why the wards work against them (other than that it’s possible these wards interpret the PCs as spirits because they’re visitors from a different mindscape).</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Award the PCs XP for bypassing the hazard if Heh Shan-Bao inks their hands with the seal script that allows them to pass freely through the wards.</p>"
            },
            "The Governor Escapes": {
              "name": "总督逃脱 The Governor Escapes",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Governor Escapes\">总督逃脱</h3>\n<p>如果 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保} 一路成功返回他的宅邸，他就会把自己锁在里面，并在PC们显然仍在城里期间拒绝外出。此时，PC们需要克服宅邸的护才能闯入宅邸，或者他们也可以先撤退，日后再尝试与他取得联系。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Governor Escapes\">The Governor Escapes</h3>\n<p>If @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} makes it all the way back to his manor, he locks himself in and refuses to exit for as long as the PCs remain obviously in town. At this point, the PCs will need to overcome the manor wards to break into the manor, or they can retreat and try to contact him again in the future.</p>"
            },
            "The Governor Caught": {
              "name": "总督被抓住了 The Governor Caught",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Governor Caught\">逮住总督</h3>\n<p>如果PC们在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}到达他的宅邸之前追上他，他会颓然垮下身子，做好战斗准备（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10fightingtheg00]{与总督战斗}），但不会主动发起战斗。如果PC们不攻击他，他同意与他们交谈，但坚持要在他的宅邸里谈，而不是在外面空旷处。他先要来一支笔和墨，随后又心不在焉地在袖子里翻找，自己把这些东西取了出来，然后在每位PC手背上潦草画下一个符号。他解释说，这道印记能让他们进入他的宅邸时，不必害怕他在墙周围设下的护。他说这道印记会持续有效，只要PC们仍留在思维空间中，或直到某位PC用一个交互动作将其擦掉为止。</p>\n<p>若PC们希望在会面前继续探索，和善保会告诉他们务必在日落前到达他的宅邸，并多次强调不要把墨迹洗掉或弄花，然后便退回家中。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们在总督到达宅邸之前逮住他，给予他们120 XP。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Governor Caught\">The Governor Caught</h3>\n<p>If the PCs catch up to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} before he reaches his manor, he slumps and prepares himself for a fight (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10fightingtheg00]{Fighting the Governor}) but doesn’t initiate combat. If the PCs don’t attack him, he agrees to talk to them but insists they speak in his manor rather than out in the open. He asks for a brush and ink before absentmindedly searching his sleeves and retrieving those items himself, then scrawls a symbol on the back of each PC’s hand. He explains that this seal will allow them to enter his manor without fear from the wards he created around his walls. This seal persists as long as the PCs remain in the mindscape or until a PC takes an Interact action to wipe it off.</p>\n<p>Should the PCs wish to continue exploring before the meeting, Heh Shan-Bao tells them to be sure to arrive at his manor before the sun sets, insisting multiple times they don’t wash off or smear the ink marking, before retreating to his home.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs catch the governor before he reaches his manor, grant them 120 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Dead Man Walking": {
              "name": "行尸走肉 Dead Man Walking",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">亡者行走</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>长久不散的恐惧、罪疚与折磨，已将总督@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}摧残得面目全非，成为昔日自我的残破空壳；但在被囚禁期间，他并未无所事事。与PC们不同，善保明白他以及柳岸镇的人民都已经死去，只是“重生”于这片思维空间之中，并被困在生与死的夹缝里。基于这一认知，和善保每年都会设法筹划一次@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{移灵}仪式，试图借此逃离思维空间，并以转生术回到活人世界。从那里开始，他希望运用自己的魔法知识复活镇民、撤离柳岸镇，然后再招募帮手来执行封印苦迦菩提的仪式，使其更加稳妥安全。当然，这一切出发点都很高尚——但他永远不可能成功。</p>\n<p>同样如PC们一般，由于善保的记忆会在他的思维空间每次年度循环重置时一并重置，因此他并不知道自己已经将这些行动重复了115次。若能拥有超过一年的时间来构筑仪式，他或许终有一天能完成移灵仪式的准备；但即便如此，他也只会以幽魂般的灵体形态出现在活人世界。所幸，为了他的理智，这个真相始终未被总督察觉；当PC们来到他的思维空间时，他正外出为最新一轮仪式实验搜集物资。</p>\n<p>任何居民都能为PC们指引总督的去处——他经常进镇采买或收集物资并非秘密，而今天他的差事把他带到了妙手回春。或者，如果PC们花上一小时探索柳岸镇，你也可以让他们直接看见总督从拜访处返回家中。若你想避免PC们与庄园的结界发生冲突，尽可让他们在接近庄园时自动在街上遇到总督。若你将此事件从镇上其他地点开始进行，可能需要调整下方追逐中的部分障碍的风味描写。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>在要道处截住</h1>\n  <p>PC们可能会推断出和善保的目的地，并决定在那儿截住他，直接前往他的庄园，在他抵达时伏击。让每名PC尝试一次@Check[stealth|dc:25]检定，对抗善保察觉DC 25，以令他措手不及。若他发现PC们埋伏在此，总督便会再次逃跑（可能引发一场新的追逐），并尽可能长时间不回家。黄昏时分，绝望迫使他即便PC们仍在埋伏，也会尝试冲进庄园。允许PC们用单独1个轮次来克服“孤注一掷冲刺”障碍。若他们未能克服，善保便从他们身边溜过，进入庄园。</p>\n</aside>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>在PC们眼中，和善保是个家喻户晓的人物；尽管他们一眼就能认出他，但也能立刻看出此人已不再是他们记忆中的那个人。善保的头发原本梳成一丝不苟的宫廷发式，如今却披散凌乱。他黑色的外袍布满细小裂口，边缘也被烧焦，看起来更像一件破旧的家居袍，而非他最初那件时髦、缀有银色刺绣的衣装。他那惶惶不安的神情仿佛在不断压抑狂乱失控的大笑，或因惊惧而尖叫的冲动。</p>\n\n<p>总督立刻认出PC们，并很快意识到他们不是这片思维空间里常见的那种“人”的仿制品。不幸的是，和善保的第一反应是偏执——他认定PC们是某种与苦迦菩提相关的险恶存在。更不幸的是，正假扮英雄的无面鬼模仿者们非常乐意强化这种先入为主的印象。总督试图甩开PC们，引得他们在镇上展开一场追逐。</p>\n<p>本遭遇使用《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》第192页详述的追逐规则进行。这是一种“追捕”类型的追逐，由PC们追赶总督。由于PC们是追逐者，他们在先攻中后行动；总督和善保以障碍2“祁仲之怒”作为追逐起点。每个轮次结束时，总督会自动推进至下一个障碍，无需掷任何检定来克服当前障碍。追逐的每个轮次经过10分钟。</p>\n<p>若PC们在总督离开某个障碍之前赶到该障碍，追逐以@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10thegovernorc00]{抓住总督}结束。若PC们在追逐第5轮结束前仍未能追上总督，追逐以@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10thegovernore00]{总督逃脱}s结束。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>1：总督在哪？</span><span>障碍 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>追逐点数</strong> 7；<strong>克服</strong> @Check[society|dc:21]或@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:19]以迅速辨认他的官服，@Check[stealth|dc:23]在他注意到你之前悄悄接近他，@Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive]以察言观色，察觉他的动机与打算溜走的意图</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">追逐开始于PC们得知总督目前正在妙手回春购物，并试图在不暴露自己的情况下接近他。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>2：祁仲之怒</span><span>障碍 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>追逐点数</strong> 3；<strong>克服</strong> @Check[qi-zhong-lore|dc:21]或@Check[religion|dc:21]用正确的祷词安抚守护的壁虎灵，@Check[diplomacy|dc:23]就对神龛的亵渎向达米大夫郑重道歉，@Check[crafting|dc:25]迅速修复破坏处</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">若PC们在前一障碍中大获全胜，并在追逐第1轮就抵达这里，他们会在总督意识到自己被追赶之前抓住他。然而，若他已继续前进，PC们会发现妙手回春一片混乱：达米大夫惊慌失措，他与助手们正忙着安抚一只暴怒的幽灵壁虎。这只生物是妙手回春的魔法守护者；在总督和善保得知此举能制造混乱、为自己赢得抢先奔回庄园的时间后，他在诊所庭院里砍裂了一座供奉@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.giAsBYiL2omr0x2L]{祁仲}的小纸神龛，导致守护者在狂乱中显形。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>3：穿行人潮</span><span>障碍 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>追逐点数</strong> 4；<strong>克服</strong> @Check[intimidation|dc:23]迫使商贩让开道路，@Check[acrobatics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:balance|name:Balance]沿桥栏保持平衡通过（那里没有人流阻碍），@Check[athletics|dc:27]推搡着挤过人群。任何拥有飞行速度、攀爬速度，或能无视人群造成的困难地形的PC，在这些检定上获得+4环境加值。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">总督从一群讨价还价、堵住了跨越狭窄溪流的桥面通道的商贩之间滑身而过，仿佛他能预先知晓人群将做出的每个动作。PC们则在桥上与街道上遭遇拥堵的“车流”，商贩与其他恼火的旅人挤成密集的人群，难以穿行。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>4：他往哪边走了？</span><span>障碍 7</span></h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>追逐点数</strong> 4；<strong>克服</strong> @Check[arcana|dc:23]或@Check[occultism|dc:23]侦测幻觉中的破绽，@Check[survival|dc:25]追踪真正总督的踪迹，@Check[perception|dc:27]注意到幻象背后的真实。任何PC若在一次@Check[will|dc:28]豁免中成功识破该幻觉，在这些检定上获得+4环境加值。若该幻觉被解除，则每名PC都获得此加值。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">走投无路之下，和善保总督使用一张@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE]{幻象场景}卷轴，在柳岸镇镇区的街道与小巷间制造出多个“自己”的版本四处游走。这些复制体以不同的间隔穿行于该区域，但仓促成形的幻象并不完美；PC们可以运用对魔法的认识看穿正在发生的事，并找出这些仿制品的破绽。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>5：孤注一掷</span><span>障碍 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>追逐点数</strong> 3 <br />\n    <strong>克服</strong> @Check[diplomacy|dc:23]或@Check[deception|dc:23]让总督相信他们并非冒名顶替者，@Check[athletics|dc:25]追上并擒住总督，@Check[intimidation|dc:27]以高声威胁迫使他当场停下。速度至少35的PC在运动检定上获得+2环境加值；速度至少50的PC（或能传送到他前方者）则在该检定上获得+4环境加值。\n  </p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">眼见庄园入口在望，总督开始全力冲刺，拼命想赶到那座贴满符箓结界的家中寻求庇护。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Dead Man Walking</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Though the constant fear, guilt, and torment have left Governor @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} a traumatized wreck of his former self, he hasn’t spent his captivity idle. Unlike the PCs, Shan-Bao understands that he and all the people of Willowshore died, only to be “reborn” within this mindscape and become trapped between life and death. With this knowledge in mind, Heh Shan-Bao attempts to engineer a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} ritual every year that will allow him to escape the mindscape and reincarnate into the living world. From there, he hopes to use his magical knowledge to resurrect the townsfolk, evacuate Willowshore, and then recruit help to perform the ritual to seal Kugaptee more safely. This is all noble in intent, of course, but he will never be able to succeed at this.</p>\n<p>As with the PCs, since Governor Heh’s memories reset each time his mindscape’s yearly cycle resets, he isn’t aware that he has repeated these actions 115 times. With more than a year to build his ritual, perhaps he could eventually complete his work on the transmigrate ritual, but even then, he would simply appear in the living world as a ghostly spirit. Fortunately for his sanity, this truth continues to elude the governor, and when the PCs arrive in his mindscape, he’s out gathering supplies for his latest ritual experiments.</p>\n<p>Any resident can direct the PCs to the governor—it’s no secret that he often makes trips into town to shop or gather supplies, and that today his errands have brought him to the Hand of Spring. Alternatively, if the PCs spend an hour exploring Willowshore, you can simply have them spot the governor as he’s walking back home from the visit. If you want to prevent having the PCs clash against the manor’s wards, feel free to have them automatically encounter the governor on the street as they approach the manor. You might wish to adjust the flavor of some of the obstacles in the chase below if you start this event somewhere else in town.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Head Off at the Pass</h1>\n  <p>The PCs might deduce Heh Shan-Bao’s destination and decide to cut him off there, going directly to his manor to ambush him on arrival. Have each PC attempt a @Check[stealth|dc:25] check against Shan-Bao’s Perception DC of 25 to surprise him. If he spots the PCs lying in wait, the governor flees again (potentially triggering a new chase) and avoids returning home for as long as possible. At dusk, desperation forces him to make an attempt to run into his manor even if the PCs are lying in wait. Allow the PCs a single round to overcome the Last-Ditch Run obstacle. If they fail to overcome it, Shan-Bao slips by them into the manor.</p>\n</aside>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> To the PCs, Heh Shan-Bao is a well-known figure, and while they all recognize him on sight, they can immediately tell this man isn’t the same man they remember. Shan-Bao’s hair, normally pulled up into a perfect courtly style, now hangs loose and unkempt. His black outer robe is covered in tiny rips and is burned at the edges, looking more like a ragged dressing gown than the fashionable, silver-embroidered garment it originally was. His haunted expression seems to be constantly fighting off frenzied, uncontrollable laughter or an urge to scream in fright.</p>\n\n<p>The governor immediately recognizes the PCs and quickly realizes they aren’t the typical facsimiles of people that inhabit this mindscape. Unfortunately, Governor Heh’s immediate reaction is one of paranoia, as he assumes the PCs are sinister beings somehow related to Kugaptee. Even more unfortunately, the noppera-bo impersonators who are posing as the heroes are all too happy to reinforce that preconception. The governor attempts to evade the PCs, leading them on a chase throughout town.</p>\n<p>This encounter plays out using the chase rules detailed on page 192 of <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>. This is a “chase down” type of chase in which the PCs pursue the governor. The PCs go second in initiative since they’re the pursuers, with Governor Heh starting the chase at obstacle 2: Qi Zhong’s Ire. At the end of each round, the governor automatically progresses to the next obstacle without needing to roll any checks to overcome the obstacle. Each round of the chase takes 10 minutes to pass.</p>\n<p>If the PCs reach an obstacle before the governor has left it, the chase ends with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10thegovernorc00]{The Governor Caught}. If the PCs don’t manage to catch up to the governor before the end of round 5 of the chase, the chase ends with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10thegovernore00]{The Governor Escapes}s.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>1: Where is the Governor?</span><span>Obstacle 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Chase Points</strong> 7; <strong>Overcome</strong> @Check[society|dc:21] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:19] to quickly identify his official robes, @Check[stealth|dc:23] to sneak up on him before he notices you, @Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] to Sense his Motive and intention to slip away</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The chase begins as the PCs learn that the governor is currently shopping at the Hand of Spring and attempt to approach without giving themselves away.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>2: Qi Zhong’s Ire</span><span>Obstacle 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Chase Points</strong> 3; <strong>Overcome</strong> @Check[qi-zhong-lore|dc:21] or @Check[religion|dc:21] to placate the guardian gecko spirit with the proper prayers, @Check[diplomacy|dc:23] to respectfully apologize to Doctor Dami for the sacrilege to the shrine, @Check[crafting|dc:25] to quickly repair the damage</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">If the PCs wildly succeed at the previous obstacle and manage to reach this one on the chase’s first round, they’ll catch the governor before he realizes they’re after him. If he has moved on, however, the PCs find the Hand of Spring in chaos, with Doctor Dami in a panic as he and his assistants work to calm down an irate phantom gecko. This creature, a magical guardian of the Hand of Spring, has manifested in a frenzy after Governor Heh slashed at a small paper shrine devoted to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.giAsBYiL2omr0x2L]{Qi Zhong} in the clinic’s courtyard, knowing this act would create mayhem and hoping it would give him time to get a head start on the race back to his manor.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>3: Plowing Through Crowds</span><span>Obstacle 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Chase Points</strong> 4; <strong>Overcome</strong> @Check[intimidation|dc:23] to make the merchants step aside, @Check[acrobatics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:balance|name:Balance] to balance across the bridge railing where no traffic is in the way, @Check[athletics|dc:27] to shove your way through the crowd. Any PC who has a fly Speed, climb Speed, or the ability to bypass difficult terrain created by crowds gains a +4 circumstance bonus to these checks.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The governor slips through a throng of haggling merchants who are blocking the way on a bridge that crosses a narrow creek, as if he knows every movement the crowd is going to make in advance. The PCs are met with congested traffic on the bridge and streets, with the merchants and other frustrated travelers forming dense crowds that are difficult to navigate.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>4: Which Way Did He Go?</span><span>Obstacle 7</span></h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Chase Points</strong> 4; <strong>Overcome</strong> @Check[arcana|dc:23] or @Check[occultism|dc:23] to detect flaws in the illusion, @Check[survival|dc:25] to follow the real governor’s trail, @Check[perception|dc:27] to notice reality behind the illusion. Any PC who succeeds at a @Check[will|dc:28] save to disbelieve the illusion gains a +4 circumstance bonus to these checks. Every PC gains this bonus if the illusion is dispelled.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">In a fit of desperation, Governor Heh uses a scroll of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE]{Illusory Scene} to create multiple versions of himself wandering around the streets and alleyways of downtown Willowshore. These copies move through the area at different intervals, but the rushed illusion is imperfect, and the PCs can use their knowledge of magic to realize what’s going on and spot the flaws in the facsimiles.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>5: Last-Ditch</span><span>Obstacle 7</span></h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Chase Points</strong> 3 <br />\n    <strong>Overcome</strong> @Check[diplomacy|dc:23] or @Check[deception|dc:23] to convince the governor that they aren’t impostors, @Check[athletics|dc:25] to run the governor down, @Check[intimidation|dc:27] to force him to stop in his tracks with a yelled threat. A PC who has a Speed of at least 35 gains a +2 circumstance bonus to the Athletics check, while those with a Speed of at least 50 (or who can teleport ahead of him) gain a +4 circumstance bonus to this check.\n  </p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">With the entrance to his manor in sight, the governor breaks into a sprint, desperate to reach the safety of his fulu-warded home.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Your Face is Mine": {
              "name": "你的脸是我的 Your Face is Mine",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Your Face is Mine\">你的脸是我的</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Noppera-bo Oracle Impersonator\" alt=\"从背后看起来像普通类人生物的无脸畸变体\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p>PC们和 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}并不是这个思维空间里唯一真正的居住者——还有另一批能够完全掌控自身动作的存在潜伏在其边界之内。这里栖居着一群无面鬼，它们由苦迦菩提的死亡之梦显化而成，并被外来存在的闯入所吸引。每名PC对应一只无面鬼，每只无面鬼都呈现出其对应PC的外貌——唯独明显不同的是它没有脸。眼下，这些无面鬼会避开PC们，除非被迫自卫，或是PC们在追逐总督时失败（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10thegovernore00]{总督逃脱}），否则它们不会发动攻击。它们目前更有兴趣观察PC们，以便日后更准确地模仿他们的行为。</p>\n<p>用这些无面鬼来进一步凸显总督思维空间中那种阴森诡异的氛围。无面鬼暂时会回避PC们，但镇民可能会被它们弄糊涂。对那些半真实的村民而言，PC们和他们的无面鬼复制体完全一模一样，这可能导致某位当地人对某个PC打招呼说：“哦，欢迎回来！”或“你是不是忘了什么？”这些互动应当暗示对方刚刚才见过这个PC，尽管这次遭遇可能是该PC第一次与那位当地人说话。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">你的脸是我的</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nopperaboimp00]{无面鬼模仿者} | @UUID[Actor.vFNg9BATB9crqnDn]{奥术} @UUID[Actor.aYR61sI47XlE9ul8]{神术} @UUID[Actor.2NmupNwbuAt5GcWy]{武技}@UUID[Actor.UgfzkrEkFrdeegD0]{异能} @UUID[Actor.vmOACyFUJqWHY8YD]{原能} @UUID[Actor.n9L4akwW1KlBXQQd]{熟练}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>此时PC们不应能追踪到并攻击他们的无面鬼复制体，但执拗的PC也可能迫使遭遇提前发生。若战斗爆发，附近思维空间中的镇民会以真实镇民看到邻居被怪物般的分身攻击时的同样方式作出反应，但他们会把无面鬼当作“真正的”人，而不是PC们。</p>\n  <p>每个无面鬼模仿者都会将其攻击集中在它所模仿的那名PC身上。关于无面鬼模仿者的完整细节，以及如何将其自定义以匹配你的PC们，见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21impersonator00]{此处}。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Your Face is Mine\">Your Face is Mine</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Noppera-bo Oracle Impersonator\" alt=\"faceless aberration that appears as a regular humanoid from behind\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp');width:60%\" />\n<p>The PCs and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} aren’t the only real occupants of this mindscape—one more set of beings that are fully in control of their actions lurk within its borders. A group of noppera-bos dwell here, manifested from Kugaptee’s dead dreams and attracted by the intrusion of a foreign presence. There’s one noppera-bo for each PC, and each has the appearance of their associated PC—with the notable exception of the lack of a face. For the moment, these noppera-bos avoid the PCs and don’t attack unless they’re forced to in self-defense or if the PCs fail at pursuing the governor (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10thegovernore00]{The Governor Escapes}). They’re more interested in observing the PCs for now, the better to accurately mimic their behavior later on.</p>\n<p>Use these noppera-bos to further accentuate the eerie atmosphere of the governor’s mindscape. The noppera-bos avoid the PCs for now, but the townsfolk might be confused by them. To the half-real villagers, the PCs and their noppera-bo duplicates are truly identical, which might result in a local greeting a PC with an “Oh, welcome back!” or a “Did you forget something?” These interactions should imply that they just met the PC in question even though this encounter might be the PC’s first time speaking with that particular local.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-noppera-bo-oracle-impersonator.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Your Face is Mine</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nopperaboimp00]{Noppera-bo Impersonator} | @UUID[Actor.vFNg9BATB9crqnDn]{Arcane} @UUID[Actor.aYR61sI47XlE9ul8]{Divine} @UUID[Actor.2NmupNwbuAt5GcWy]{Martial}@UUID[Actor.UgfzkrEkFrdeegD0]{Occult} @UUID[Actor.vmOACyFUJqWHY8YD]{Primal} @UUID[Actor.n9L4akwW1KlBXQQd]{Skilled}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The PCs shouldn’t be able to track down and attack their noppera-bo duplicates at this time, but persistent PCs can force an early encounter. If a fight results, nearby mindscape townsfolk react in the same manner that the real townsfolk would if they saw their neighbors attacked by monstrous doubles, but they treat the noppera-bos as the “real” people instead of the PCs.</p>\n  <p>Each noppera-bo impersonator focuses its attacks on the PC it imitates. Full details for noppera-bo impersonators and how to customize them to match your PCs appear @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21impersonator00]{Here}.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Ill Omens": {
              "name": "凶兆 Ill Omens",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Ill Omens\">不祥征兆</h2>\n<p>尽管总督的思维空间仍在勉力维持“如常”的表象，苦迦菩提的邪恶灵光却无法藏匿——在这里，这头恶魔的影响依旧强烈。若PC们花更多时间在这版的柳岸镇四处游荡与探索，你可以使用下表中的不祥迹象与阴魂不散的瞬间来让玩家不安。</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>[[/r 1d10]]</th>\n      <th>结果</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>有人咬下一颗又大又熟的柿子。顺着其口唇与下巴淌下的汁水甜香得令人发腻，却看起来与鲜血一模一样；无论如何指责或劝说，都无法让此人意识到这一事实。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>一名PC向前走时，感觉有什么东西像一根绷紧的发丝在其脸颊上“啪”地绷断，受到@Damage[(1)[slashing]]伤害。其脸上出现一道薄如刀锋的划口，仿佛那根头发锋利到足以割出血来。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>一名PC感觉有什么异常柔软的东西擦过皮肤。一团蚕不知从何处高处坠下，在落地途中撞上PC。这些幼虫像蛆一样无助地在地上蠕动，因为冬天里没有桑树可供它们取食。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>在一名PC所站近旁的一栋建筑上，缓慢浮现出一团神秘的黑影，仿佛墙体正从内部被烧灼。调查后看不出任何起火的迹象，然而空气中依旧残留着不容错认的烟臭味。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>一名PC听见脚下传来尖锐的咯吱碎裂声。调查后发现，破损的牙齿碎片嵌在其鞋底或皮肤里；除了令人不安的感觉外，不会留下任何持久伤害。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>有人正在把河鱼剁碎，准备将其发酵成鱼酱。那些鱼长着呆滞的人类眼睛，口中还有显眼的人类牙齿，但剁鱼的人似乎完全没注意到——即便有PC指出这一点也是如此。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>一只猩红的蝴蝶从附近意想不到的地方出现，例如从一杯茶里飞出，或在某名PC打喷嚏时从其口中飞出。它绕着队伍飞舞了几轮后坠落地面，融化成一滩血迹。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>一阵异常寒冷的微风在区域内沙沙掠过；当它吹过队伍时，一名PC（随机决定）听见带威胁的低语，许诺死亡与毁灭——发出低语的声音似乎来自另一名PC。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>9</td>\n      <td>光线变暗，仿佛云层掠过头顶的日月，但天空中并无任何对应变化。PC们突然感到寒意直透骨髓，胃里也涌起令人作呕的饥饿啃噬；片刻之后，光线与这些感觉又恢复正常。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10</td>\n      <td>当至少两名PC正在交谈时，其中一名PC听见另一名PC把“苦迦菩提”这个名字当作别的词说了出来。说出这句话的PC，以及任何在旁倾听的其他PC，都完全没听到这个词。听见该名字的PC在接下来这一小时都惶惶不安，确信自己正被监视。</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Ill Omens\">Ill Omens</h2>\n<p>While the governor’s mindscape plays at normalcy, Kugaptee’s evil aura can’t be hidden—here, the fiend’s influence remains strong. If the PCs take more time to wander and explore this version of Willowshore, you can use the ominous signs and haunting moments on the following table to unnerve the players.</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>[[/r 1d10]]</th>\n      <th>Result</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>Someone bites into a large, ripe persimmon. The torrent of juice that flows down their mouth and chin smells overwhelmingly sweet but looks exactly like blood; no amount of accusation or persuasion can make the person cognizant of this fact.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>A PC feels something like a taut strand of hair snap across their cheek while walking forward and takes @Damage[(1)[slashing]] damage. A razor thin cut appears on their face, as if the hair was sharp enough to draw blood.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>A PC feels something oddly soft brush their skin. A ball of silkworms has fallen from somewhere on high and struck the PC on the way down. The caterpillars writhe helplessly on the ground like maggots, as there are no mulberry trees in winter to feed them.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>A mysterious black shadow slowly appears on a building that a PC is standing near, as if the walls were being burnt from the inside. An investigation reveals no sign of any fire, yet the unmistakable stink of smoke lingers in the air nonetheless.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>A PC hears a sharp crunching noise beneath their feet. An investigation reveals the broken fragments of teeth embedded in their shoes or skin, leaving no lasting damage other than a sense of disquiet.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>A person minces river fish to prepare them for fermentation into fish paste. The fish have glassy human eyes and prominent human teeth in their mouths, but the person doing the mincing doesn’t seem to notice, even if a PC points this out to them.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>A crimson butterfly emerges from an unexpected nearby location, such as from a cup of tea or out of a PC’s mouth when they sneeze. The butterfly flutters around the party for a few rounds before it drops to the ground and melts into a bloodstain.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>A strangely cold breeze rustles through the area; as it blows across the party, one PC (determined randomly) hears threatening whispers promising death and doom—the voice delivering the whispers seems to be that of a different PC.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>9</td>\n      <td>The light dims as if a cloud were passing over the sun or moon above, yet no corresponding event in the skies seems apparent. The PCs feel a sudden chill in their bones and the hideous gnaw of hunger in their stomachs, only for the light and sensations to return to normal a moment later.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>10</td>\n      <td>While at least two PCs are having a discussion, one of the PCs hears a different PC say the name “Kugaptee” in place of another word. The PC who spoke, and any other PCs listening in, do not hear this word at all. The PC who heard the name spends the rest of the hour unnerved, certain they’re being watched.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
            },
            "Seeking out Heh Shan-Bao": {
              "name": "寻找和善保 Seeking out Heh Shan-Bao",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Seeking out Heh Shan-Bao\">寻找和善保</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>柔化的死亡</h1>\n  <p>尽管PC们在和善保的思维空间中，可能会像在柳岸镇思维空间里那样感觉自身在肉体上凝实而真实地存在，但事实并非如此。在这个思维空间里，他们比之前更接近以魂魄的形式存在，不过直到本章末尾他们才会意识到真相。然而，在和善保的思维空间中死亡的PC会得到一条重要线索：该PC并不会死去，而是其身体会从思维空间中消失，并在他们自己的柳岸镇中苏醒，且在施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}时所处的同一地点显现出来。该PC变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.3uh1r86TzbQvosxv]{Doomed 1}，并在苏醒时拥有1点生命值，但除此之外，其状态与在总督的思维空间里“死亡”试图夺走他们之前完全相同。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>一旦PC们发现@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}，他们便可在任何时间或地点自由施放该仪式。在他们这么做之前，《欲泣无息》的剧情无法推进到第9章安排的冬季事件之后。施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}的主要技能检定DC为27，而其次要技能检定DC为22。若PC们至少被柳岸镇的某个派系所钦佩，该派系每周最多可补贴一次施放仪式的费用。若某派系敬奉他们，则该派系每天最多可补贴一次费用。（若你的团体包含超过四个角色，请增加思维空间转移可传送的目标数量，以覆盖团体中的每一位成员，而不是迫使PC们多次施放该仪式来运送整个队伍。）</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">音效</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.0GuH1kstxWaqGSJx.PlaylistSound.PqkA73gCCn7sSZhv]{Mindscape Shift}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>和善保被转移到的思维空间，几乎是PC们那版柳岸镇的复制品，只在少数关键之处有所不同。和善保的思维空间比PC们来自的那个小得多——其边界仅环绕小镇的范围，而不是向外延伸数里，覆盖柳岸镇周边的荒野地带。</p>\n<p>在PC们的思维空间里已被修复或摧毁的建筑，在和善保的思维空间中并未发生改变——因此，青天茶馆在这里仍是一片废墟，而云纸屋依旧矗立。更重要的是，在这个思维空间中，总督庄园仍位于柳岸镇镇区的原址。根据PC们在何处施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}，他们从自己的柳岸镇过渡到这个新思维空间时，可能几乎察觉不到；也可能难以忽视，因为周遭景象会突然仿佛退回残破，或恢复为正常状态，抑或看起来异常相似。同样地，当PC们离开柳岸镇时若附近有人，这些人可能在他们抵达总督的思维空间时并不在场。</p>\n<p>注意：PC们必须身处柳岸镇之内，才能成功使用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}进入和善保的思维空间。他庄园上的结界（第163页）会阻止PC们出现在建筑内部，因此若PC们试图在那片曾经是庄园所在的空地上施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}，那么他们在新思维空间中显现时，会出现在空地的边缘。</p>\n<p>事实上，当PC们探索这版柳岸镇时，很快就会意识到有些不对劲。原因既阴郁又悲惨：当和善保在仪式中失败并催生这些思维空间时，他的心智、肉体与灵魂都被苦迦菩提彻底吞噬。PC们刚进入的这个思维空间，源自总督在惊恐中残存的最后一丝意识火花——他的心智在苦迦菩提将他完全吸收之前，仍在竭力维持自我。</p>\n<p>当PC们来到总督的思维空间时，他们的第一印象应当是：这是故乡里一个可爱的日子。初冬的空气仍带着一丝潮润的暖意，草丛里能听见蟋蟀啁啾。街道弥漫着甜香的熏香味、木烟味，以及烹饪食物的香气。居民们看上去心情都极好，只要PC们与其互动，他们便十分友善，尽管他们更优先处理日常事务，而非与英雄攀谈。实际上，镇民似乎友善得有些过头——即便最爱争吵的居民如今也更爱玩笑而非争辩，他们惯常的揶揄也不再带有任何真正的恶意。也许最令人不安的是，镇民似乎没有任何人认得PC们。相反，他们把PC们当作来到柳岸镇的受欢迎却陌生的访客来对待。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">环境</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.qpwb9j7dRnHA64DZ]{Dark Willowshore}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>随着白昼渐向夜幕推进，这层伪装开始变薄。柳岸镇的居民变得僵硬，带着呆滞的凝视与空洞的回答，拖着步子过完他们的日常生活与对话。一群群红色蝴蝶成簇地落在随机的人身上，以及总督庄园的墙壁上。小镇的一些细小部分——比如店铺招牌或小型神龛——会仿佛被从存在中抹除一般消失。街道的气味变得异常甜腻，使得闻到这些气味的人被难以遏止且不合时宜的饥渴所折磨。和善保的“天堂”正在被吞食。</p>\n<p>夜幕降临时，一切伪装都不再维持。镇民变得毫无反应，拖着步子围拢到总督庄园周围，饥渴地盯着它的门窗，然而他们似乎无法靠近庄园墙上大量装饰的熏香与辟邪符箓。他们就在那里等着，一动不动、悄无声息，直到黎明的第一缕光出现；那时他们便走回各自的家中睡下。几小时后，他们醒来，对日落之后发生的一切毫无记忆，仿佛前一晚从未存在过。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Seeking out Heh Shan-Bao\">Seeking out Heh Shan-Bao</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Softened Death</h1>\n  <p>While the PCs might feel as physically solid and present in Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape as they did in the Willowshore mindscape, that isn’t quite the case. In this mindscape, they’re closer to existing as spirits than before, but they won’t realize the truth until the end of this chapter. A PC who dies in Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape receives an important clue, though, for rather than dying, that PC’s body vanishes from the mindscape and awakens back in their own Willowshore, manifesting there at the same location they were in when @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} was first cast. The PC becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.3uh1r86TzbQvosxv]{Doomed 1} and has 1 Hit Point upon awakening but is otherwise in the same condition they were before death attempted to take them in the governor’s mindscape.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Once the PCs discover @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}, they’re free to cast the ritual at any time or place they wish. Until they do so, the plot of “No Breath to Cry” can’t progress beyond the winter events scheduled to take place in Chapter 9. The DC of the primary skill check for casting @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} is 27, while the DC for its secondary skill checks is 22. If the PCs are at least admired by one of Willowshore’s factions, that faction can subsidize the cost of casting the ritual up to once per week. If a faction reveres them, that faction can subsidize the cost up to once per day. (If your group features more than four characters, increase the number of targets mindscape shift can transport to cover every member of the group rather than forcing the PCs to cast the ritual multiple times to transport the entire party.)</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.0GuH1kstxWaqGSJx.PlaylistSound.PqkA73gCCn7sSZhv]{Mindscape Shift}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>The mindscape into which Heh Shan-Bao was transported is a near duplicate of the PCs’ version of Willowshore, except for a few key differences. Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape is much smaller than the one the PCs come from—this mindscape’s borders wrap around the boundaries of the town, rather than extending miles outward into the hinterlands surrounding Willowshore.</p>\n<p>Buildings that have been restored or destroyed in the PCs’ mindscape aren’t altered in Heh Shan-Bao’s—as such, the Cerulean Teahouse remains in ruins here, while Cloud Paper House is still standing. More importantly, the governor’s manor remains in its place in downtown Willowshore in this mindscape. Depending on where the PCs cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}, their transition from their Willowshore into this new mindscape might be either impossible to notice or to ignore as the surroundings suddenly appear to fall back into ruin or return to their normal state, or else look exceptionally similar. Likewise, anyone present in the vicinity when the PCs leave Willowshore might not be there when they arrive in the governor’s mindscape.</p>\n<p>Note that the PCs must be within Willowshore to successfully use @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} to enter Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape. The wards on his manor (page 163) prevent the PCs from appearing within the structure, so if the PCs attempt to cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} while within the empty lot his manor once stood upon, they’ll appear at the edge of the lot once they manifest in the new mindscape.</p>\n<p>In fact, as the PCs explore this version of Willowshore, they soon realize that something seems to be off. The reason is both grim and tragic: when Heh Shan-Bao failed in his ritual and spawned these mindscapes, he was entirely devoured—mind, body, and soul—by Kugaptee. The mindscape the PCs have just entered sprang from the last flickers of the governor’s panicked consciousness, as his mind struggles to maintain its individuality before Kugaptee absorbs him entirely.</p>\n<p>When the PCs arrive in the governor’s mindscape, their first impression should be one of a lovely day in their hometown. The early winter air still holds a trace of damp warmth, and crickets can be heard chirping in the grass. The streets smell sweet with incense, wood smoke, and the scent of cooking food. The residents all seem to be in excellent moods and are very friendly whenever the PCs engage with them, though they prioritize their daily routines over conversation with the heroes. In fact, the townsfolk seem a little too friendly—even the most quarrelsome residents are now more playful than argumentative, and their standard jibes lack any true acrimony. Perhaps most unsettling of all is the fact that none of the townsfolk seem to recognize the PCs. Instead, they treat them as welcome but unknown visitors to Willowshore.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotesaudio2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.qpwb9j7dRnHA64DZ]{Dark Willowshore}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>As day progresses toward nightfall, this whole facade begins to thin. Willowshore’s residents become stilted, trudging through their daily lives and conversations with glassy stares and vacant answers. Swarms of red butterflies land in clusters on random people and the walls of the governor’s manor. Small bits of the town, like shop signs or lesser shrines, vanish as if they’ve been erased from existence. The smells of the streets become unnaturally luscious, leaving those exposed to them plagued with unquenchable and inappropriate hungers. Heh Shan-Bao’s “paradise” is being eaten.</p>\n<p>At nightfall, all pretense drops. The townsfolk become unresponsive and shuffle to surround the governor’s manor, staring hungrily at its doors and windows, though they seem unable to approach the incense and warding fulus that heavily adorn its walls. There they wait, still and silent, until the first light of dawn, at which point they walk back to their homes and go to sleep. A few hours later, they wake, recalling nothing past sundown, as if the evening before had never been.</p>"
            },
            "Another Willowshore": {
              "name": "另一座柳岸镇 Another Willowshore",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Another Willowshore\">另一个柳岸镇</h1>\n<p>这些事件一结束，PC们和柳岸镇就能稍作喘息：孙海的驱魔师暂时放过这座废墟城镇——不过这份喘息只是一种战略性撤退。无论他们的仪式结果如何，驱魔师都已经意识到，有什么东西在干扰他们净化城镇的尝试。与其在存在未知且可能危险的变数时冒险继续行动，驱魔师决定在再次尝试驱魔之前，更加认真而谨慎地调查柳岸镇废墟中的超自然存在。随着冬季数周的推移，他们的行动以及其他事件仍会在柳岸镇持续上演——这些事件在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto]{第9章}中有更详细的说明，并会随着时间流逝按既定日程发生。关于冬季事件的时间表，见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11winterevents00#winter-timeline]{冬季时间线}。</p>\n<p>不过，更重要的是：PC们现在可以自由追查他们在上一幕中发现的线索了。他们从在谭杉寺的冒险，以及与智慧的幽灵的交谈中得知：他们和柳岸镇的所有人都被困在一个不断重复同一年岁月的思维空间里；而这个思维空间是在镇子前任总督@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}试图（并失败地）施行一场仪式，以保护柳岸镇免受苦迦菩提影响之后形成的。上一幕以PC们恢复了那份保护、并移除了苦迦菩提的直接威胁而告终，但这几乎无助于揭示、甚至厘清他们以及柳岸镇其余人要如何逃回现实世界。为了了解更多，PC们必须使用研究（子系统）（<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 190）对柳岸镇思维空间进行调查与研究。PC们的这次研究没有时间限制，但他们完成所花的天数越多，就越没时间处理本幕期间发生的其他事件。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">柳岸镇思维空间</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">研究 7</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>单人调查</strong> 你花上一天翻阅从谭杉寺隐秘图书馆中收集来的书籍与卷轴；<strong>最大RP</strong> 8</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[academia-lore|dc:21|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]或@Check[library-lore|dc:21|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]，或@Check[arcana|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]、@Check[nature|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]、@Check[occultism|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]，或@Check[religion|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>集思广益的方案</strong> 你花上一天与柳岸镇其他有学识的当地人讨论理论，并调查可能的解决方案；<strong>最大RP</strong> 4</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[arcana|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]、@Check[nature|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]、@Check[occultism|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]，或@Check[religion|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]，或@Check[diplomacy|dc:25|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>2点研究点数</strong> 总督和善保那场试图提供防护、以抵御苦迦菩提影响的失败仪式发生了反噬；其结果是创造了PC们如今被困其中的思维空间，并让该恶魔的影响变得更加强大。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4点研究点数</strong> 在PC们于第2幕取得胜利之后，苦迦菩提不再直接威胁该思维空间；然而，它仍然存在这一事实，以及仍笼罩在柳岸镇上方的超自然威胁，都证实背后有更大的效果在起作用。总督和善保很可能是在他的官邸中施行该仪式；当仪式失败时，他与官邸被偏移进了他们自己的思维空间，而这个思维空间与柳岸镇其余部分平行存在。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6点研究点数</strong> 通常，要进入或离开思维空间，必须使用一种名为“思维空间之门”的复杂仪式。虽然使用镇里以及从谭杉寺收集到的资源，无法发现这一完整仪式的精微复杂之处，但只要再多进行一些研究，应该就能想出一种类似但更聚焦的仪式：由于和善保的思维空间在形而上学层面与柳岸镇自身的思维空间距离极近，该仪式应当能够打开一扇通往和善保思维空间的门。随着时间推移，并且或许在和善保的帮助下，或通过使用很可能仍保存在其官邸内的参考资料，完整的“思维空间之门”仪式也许能够被研究出来，从而让众人得以从柳岸镇的思维空间彻底逃脱，回到现实世界！</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>8点研究点数</strong> PC们发现@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}仪式，它允许往返于和善保的思维空间。PC们获得120 XP。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Another Willowshore\">Another Willowshore</h1>\n<p>Once these events are complete, the PCs and Willowshore receive a break as Mago Kai’s exorcists leave the ruined town alone for the time being—though this reprieve is merely a strategic retreat. Regardless of the outcomes of their rituals, the exorcists have realized that something is interfering with their attempts to purify the town. Rather than risk continuing their efforts with an unknown and potentially dangerous variable in play, the exorcists decide to investigate the supernatural presence in the ruins of Willowshore more diligently and carefully before proceeding with additional exorcism attempts. Their efforts, as well as other events, continue to play out in Willowshore as the winter weeks proceed—these events are detailed further in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto]{Chapter 9} and play out on a scheduled as time passes. See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11winterevents00#winter-timeline]{Winter Timeline} for a timeline of winter’s events.</p>\n<p>Of more importance, though, is the fact that the PCs are now free to pursue their investigation of the leads they uncovered in the previous act. They know from their adventures in the Tan Sugi monastery and their discussions with Zhi Hui’s ghost that they and everyone else in Willowshore are trapped in a mindscape that keeps repeating the same year over and over, and that this mindscape formed after the town’s previous governor, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao}, tried (and failed) to perform a ritual to protect Willowshore from Kugaptee’s influence. The previous act ended with the PCs restoring that protection and removing Kugaptee’s immediate threat, but this did little to reveal or even clarify how they and the rest of Willowshore might escape back into the real world. To learn more, the PCs must investigate and research the Willowshore Mindscape using the research subsystem (<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 190). The PCs have no time limit for this research, but the more days it takes them to finish, the less time they’ll have to deal with other events that take place during this act.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">The Willowshore Mindscape</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Research 7</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Solo Investigations</strong> You spend the day looking through the collection of books and scrolls gathered from the hidden library in the Tan Sugi monastery; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 8</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[academia-lore|dc:21|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[library-lore|dc:21|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], or @Check[arcana|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], @Check[nature|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], @Check[occultism|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], or @Check[religion|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Brainstorming Solutions</strong> You spend the day discussing theories and investigating possible solutions with other learned locals in Willowshore; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 4</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[arcana|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], @Check[nature|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], @Check[occultism|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], or @Check[religion|dc:23|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], or @Check[diplomacy|dc:25|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>2 Research Points</strong> Governor Heh Shan-Bao’s failed ritual to offer protection from Kugaptee’s influence backfired; it resulted in the creation of the mindscape the PCs are now trapped in and allowed the fiend’s influence to grow stronger.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4 Research Points</strong> After the PCs’ triumphs in Act 2, Kugaptee no longer directly threatens the mindscape, yet the fact that it remains and that supernatural threats still loom over Willowshore confirm there’s a greater effect at play. Governor Heh Shan-Bao likely performed the ritual in his manor, and when it failed, he and the manor were shunted into their own mindscape, which exists in parallel to the rest of Willowshore.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6 Research Points</strong> Normally, to enter or exit a mindscape, one must use a complex ritual called mindscape door. While this full ritual’s intricacies are beyond discovery using the resources in town and gathered at the Tan Sugi monastery, it should be possible with a little more study to come up with a similar but more focused ritual capable of opening a door into Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape because of its metaphysically close proximity to Willowshore’s own. In time, and perhaps with Heh Shan-Bao’s aid or by using references likely still contained within his manor, the full mindscape door ritual might be researched, allowing for a full escape from Willowshore’s mindscape back into the real world!</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>8 Research Points</strong> The PCs discover the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} ritual, which allows travel to and from Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape. The PCs earn 120 XP.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Wrapping Up": {
              "name": "收尾 Wrapping Up",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Wrapping Up\">收尾</h2>\n<p>混乱被处理完后，镇民仍会在接下来的几分钟里保持警惕，等着看接下来还会发生什么可怕的事。当入侵的力量似乎已经退去——至少暂时如此——柳岸镇的工业区开始骚动起来，人们从藏身处出来，趁着机会在投入那种不体面的重建生活的工作之前，先评估损失。若他们所爱之人最终消失不见，有些人会被听见在哭嚎，但事后整体氛围取决于PC们在多大程度上缓解了损害。若破坏与损失极为严重，柳岸镇便会沉默而阴郁，在悲恸的尖叫声陪伴下收拾生活的残骸。若PC们在控制这些灾害方面做得很好，小镇则会更为倔强，一些年长居民会大声抱怨并辱骂那一切的始作俑者——那些看不见的力量。</p>\n<p>若三名NPC都被救出，队伍获得3点希望点，并使其在柳岸镇两大派系的声望各提高1点。PC们获得120 XP。</p>\n<p>若只救出两名NPC，队伍获得1点希望点，并使其在柳岸镇其中一个派系（由队伍选择）的声望提高1点。PC们获得80 XP。</p>\n<p>若只救出一名NPC，队伍既不获得也不失去希望点。PC们获得40 XP。</p>\n<p>若未救出任何NPC，队伍失去2点希望点，并使其在柳岸镇两大派系的声望各降低1点。</p>\n<p>若云纸屋倒塌，PC们失去1点安全点，并且纸厂将不再能作为PC的工作地点使用，也不能再用于购买纸张及纸制品。若仅受损，同样无法用于上述用途，但若PC们花费4点安全点，则该建筑可在2周的工作后修复。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kawaka.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Myna Kawaka\" alt=\"male tengu guild leader\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kawaka.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.4EyPHYXJyP7hFKyM]{Myna's Gift} @UUID[Actor.NYcGFeauCDToaCDr]{Myna's Gift (Saved Two)} @UUID[Actor.fMacvK39aRl0TUiy]{Myna's Gift (Saved Three)} @UUID[Actor.UpsaboiTp5my3pGC]{Yu Er’s Parents Thanks} @UUID[Actor.n7DOFprbrQUzkeGj]{Townsfolks' Rewards}<br />\n  次日，川冈米娜（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w14cloudpape00]{W14}），云纸屋的主人，前来拜访PC们。若他们在三名被困者中至少救出一人，她便会赠予他们一根强效烟棒和四瓶<em>中等治疗药水</em>以示感谢；若至少救出两人，她还会再赠予一<em>瓶永恒黏合剂</em>以及额外四瓶<em>中等治疗药水</em>；若三人全救出，她则会再赠予一瓶<em>迅捷药水</em>和一枚<em>符文石</em>，其上刻有一枚<em>强韧护甲符文</em>。这些奖励可叠加。若英雄们还完整找回了果冻先生，玉儿的父母会亲自以一双<em>腾跃之靴</em>向他们致谢，随后感叹若玩具不见了，想找到一模一样的替代品会有多困难。</p>\n<p>若PC们在两只林鬼消失前击败了它们，镇民会更加安心（而若这些灵体自行消失，人们仍会担心它们随时可能回来）。镇中长者会集结资源，并在一天后以一对力场皮带与一只绘有凤凰、价值150 gp的青瓷花瓶作为奖励呈给队伍。</p>\n<p>若PC们在战斗后被魔宠阴影的诅咒所侵染，但自身没有解除诅咒的方法，考虑让伸三免费送来几张4环<em>净化苦难</em>卷轴给队伍，并解释说他有种感觉他们会用得上。</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>无端谋杀</h1>\n  <p>和善保的柳岸镇镇民并不敌对，但他们确实令人不安。若某位PC攻击任何一名市民，将他们全部视作@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-npc-core.Actor.APn9B54hhRtr0oCQ]{平民}。遭到攻击的居民会惊恐尖叫，若能退就退，但若被逼到角落也会战斗。若被杀死，村民会倒在地上，面孔逐渐褪为一张空白、毫无五官的椭圆。并且，仔细检查会发现他们的装备由廉价道具组成。其他镇民除非自己也被攻击，否则对暴力场面毫无反应。PC们可能会怀疑这些镇民是无脸鬼；他们不是（他们不过是由思维空间维持的思念造形），但他们确实能为PC们不久后将在总督府邸面对的无脸鬼的存在埋下伏笔！</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Wrapping Up\">Wrapping Up</h2>\n<p>The townsfolk remain wary for several minutes after the chaos has been dealt with, waiting to see what horrible thing might happen next. When it seems that the invading force is gone—at least for the time being—Willowshore’s industrial district stirs as people emerge, taking the chance to assess the damage before getting down to the unglamorous work of putting their lives back together. A few can be heard wailing if their loved ones ultimately vanished, but the overall tone of the aftermath depends on how well the PCs managed to mitigate the damage. If the destruction and loss was extensive, Willowshore is silent and somber, collecting the wreckage of their lives with screams of grief as their only accompaniment. If the PCs did well in containing the disasters, the town is more defiant, with older residents loudly complaining and insulting the unseen forces that caused it all.</p>\n<p>If all three NPCs were rescued, the party earns 3 Hope Points and increases their reputation with both of Willowshore’s factions by 1. The PCs earn 120 XP.</p>\n<p>If only two NPCs were rescued, the party earns 1 Hope Point and increases their reputation with one of Willowshore’s factions (the party’s choice) by 1. The PCs earn 80 XP.</p>\n<p>If only one NPC was rescued, the party neither gains nor loses Hope Points. The PCs earn 40 XP.</p>\n<p>If no NPCs were rescued, the party loses 2 Hope Points and 1 Reputation Point with each of Willowshore’s factions.</p>\n<p>If Cloud Paper House collapses, the PCs lose 1 Security Point, and the paper mill can no longer be used as a work site for PCs or to purchase paper and paper products. It likewise remains unavailable for such use if it only suffered damage, but if the PCs spend 4 Security Points, the building can be repaired after 2 weeks of work.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kawaka.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Myna Kawaka\" alt=\"male tengu guild leader\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kawaka.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.4EyPHYXJyP7hFKyM]{Myna's Gift} @UUID[Actor.NYcGFeauCDToaCDr]{Myna's Gift (Saved Two)} @UUID[Actor.fMacvK39aRl0TUiy]{Myna's Gift (Saved Three)} @UUID[Actor.UpsaboiTp5my3pGC]{Yu Er’s Parents Thanks} @UUID[Actor.n7DOFprbrQUzkeGj]{Townsfolks' Rewards}<br />\n  The next day, Myna Kawaka (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w14cloudpape00]{W14}), the owner of Cloud Paper House, visits the PCs and gives them a greater smokestick and four <em>moderate healing potions</em> in thanks if they saved at least one of the three trapped people, a <em>vial of everlasting adhesive</em> and four additional <em>moderate healing potions</em> if they saved at least two, and a <em>potion of quickness</em> and a <em>runestone</em> bearing a <em>resilient armor rune</em> if they saved all three. These rewards are cumulative. If the heroes also recovered Mr. Jelly intact, Yu Er’s parents personally thank them with a pair of <em>boots of bounding</em> before lamenting how difficult it would’ve been to find an identical replacement for the toy.\n</p>\n<p>If the PCs defeated both waldgeists before they vanished, the townsfolk are further relieved (whereas if the spirits are allowed to vanish on their own, fears that they might return at any time linger). The town elder gathers resources and, one day later, presents the party with a reward in the form of a pair of leather bands of force and a celadon vase decorated with phoenixes worth 150 gp.</p>\n<p>If the PCs became infested with the familiar shadows’ curse after the battle but have no method of removing curses themselves, consider having Shinzo deliver a few 4th-rank <em>scrolls of cleanse affliction</em> to the party for free, explaining that he had a feeling they could use them.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Unprovoked Murder</h1>\n  <p>The townsfolk of Heh Shan-Bao’s Willowshore aren’t hostile, but they’re certainly unsettling. If a PC attacks any of the citizens, treat them all as if they were @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-npc-core.Actor.APn9B54hhRtr0oCQ]{Commoners}. Attacked residents shriek in terror and retreat if able, but they fight if cornered. If slain, the villager collapses to the ground and their face fades to a blank, featureless ovoid. Furthermore, their equipment turns out to consist of cheap props on closer examination. Other townsfolk don’t react to the sight of violence unless they’re attacked themselves. The PCs might suspect these townsfolk are noppera-bos; they aren’t (they’re little more than thoughtforms maintained by the mindscape), but they can certainly foreshadow the presence of the noppera-bos the PCs will soon face at the governor’s manor!</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Event 3. Tomorrow’s Shadows": {
              "name": "事件 3：明日之影 Event 3. Tomorrow’s Shadows",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件3：明日之影</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低威胁7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>一旦两只林幽魂被击败，现实世界中的驱魔人便从废墟中撤退，回到唐入向孙海汇报他们的成功或失败，但他们的干预所引发的后果还远未结束。在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10event2unnatu00]{事件2：非自然的起义}结束后约10分钟，每位PC都会感到一阵诡异的寒意——那种经典的感觉，有人形容为“仿佛有人刚从你的坟上走过”。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>片刻之后，朦胧的黑色形体从每位PC的影子里升起，它们的轮廓逐渐凝聚成每个角色的烟雾般、扭曲的幽灵。这些身影是PC自身闹鬼的回声，它们正穿过思维空间的边界，从未来向他们反延伸而来。当这些阴影般的身影痛苦地哭嚎时，PC从那扭曲的形态中认出了自己。随后，这些阴影生物发动攻击。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/familiar-shadow.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">明日之影</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Ce9789tqv5KRxq58]{魔宠之影（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>这些怪异的身影在大多数方面都如同典型的影怪运作，唯独它们缺少从敌人身上滋生影怪的能力。取而代之的是，它们拥有一种不同寻常的能力：侵染那些与其外形相同之人的影子，详见数据表。由于它们窃取与侵染影子的能力只能对其所复制形态的PC生效，这些魔宠之影会将攻击集中在对应的PC身上，除非它们已经杀死了自己所复制的PC，否则将完全无视区域中的其他人。</p>\n  <p>本遭遇假设有四只影怪攻击队伍；按需调整数量，以确保每位PC都要面对自己的影子。影怪会战斗至被摧毁为止；但当最后一只被解决后，一种如释重负的感觉会涌上每位PC心头——一种至少在当下，这次最新的危险已经过去的感觉。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 3. Tomorrow’s Shadows</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Once the two waldgeists are defeated, the exorcists in the living world retreat from the ruins to report to Mago Kai at Karahai on their successes or failures, but the repercussions of their meddling aren’t quite over. About 10 minutes after @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10event2unnatu00]{Event 2. Unnatural Uprising} ends, each of the PCs feels a strange chill—the classic sensation some describe as feeling as if “someone just walked over your grave.”</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A moment later, nebulous black forms rise up from each PC’s shadow, their shapes coalescing as a smoky, distorted ghosts of each character. These figures are echoes of the PCs’ own hauntings, which are extending back to them from the future through the mindscape’s borders. As these shadowy figures cry out in pain, the PCs recognize themselves in their distorted shapes. Then the shadowy creatures attack.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/familiar-shadow.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Tomorrow’s Shadows</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Ce9789tqv5KRxq58]{Familiar Shadows (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>Each of these strange figures functions as a typical shadow for the most part, with the exception that they lack the ability to spawn shadows from their foes. Instead, they have the unusual ability to infest the shadows of those whose forms they duplicate, as detailed in the stat block. As their ability to steal and infest shadows only functions against PCs whose shapes they duplicate, these familiar shadows focus their attacks on those particular PCs, ignoring others in the area entirely unless they have already slain the PC they duplicated.</p>\n  <p>This encounter assumes four shadows attack the party; adjust these numbers as needed so each PC faces their own shadow. The shadows fight until destroyed, but once the last of them is finished off, a sense of relief washes over each PC—a feeling that, for now at least, this latest danger has passed.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Event 2. Unnatural Uprising": {
              "name": "事件 2：非自然的暴动 Event 2. Unnatural Uprising",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 2：反常暴动</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>一旦NPC们已从建筑中获救，且灵性干扰器被清除，PC们就有时间休息并恢复。经过10分钟后，或在PC们决定离开该区域时（以先发生者为准），又一股红烟从街道升入空中；孙海的驱魔人们在现世重新集结，开始第二次尝试驱逐该区域里那些相当顽强的魂魄。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/willowshore-waldgeist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">反常暴动</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.hJEmfJJOQm9FImqP]{柳岸镇 森灵（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>这一次，驱魔人们将精力集中在驱逐侵染该区域的一大团泛化灵性能量上（以废墟中非智慧生命的累积损失来体现），而不是针对灵性能量的特定“点位”（以现世中城镇居民残留的魂魄来体现）。在街道东端的<strong>A5</strong>区域，烟雾翻涌而起；短暂的一瞬间，又出现了数个金眼、披绛红衣的幻影，但随着在现实世界施行大规模驱魔的尝试失败，它们随即消散。</p>\n  <p>然而在思维空间里，他们的尝试却产生了非常真实的结果：这股灵性能量被迫从现世挤出，进入思维空间，并浸染了现代柳岸镇中生长在云纸屋废墟之上的植物与树木。自然秩序的这种腐化从那个世界映入思维空间，在<strong>A5</strong>区域显现为两只森灵——扭曲的形体，像是畸形的迷你柳树，树干上长着尖叫的动物面孔。这些虚体魂魄立刻向前涌去，毫不费力地漂浮着，用垂落的根须攻击PC们，几乎像幽灵水母般在空中飘荡。尽管这些变种森灵比典型森灵大得多，且它们与云纸屋的灵性纠缠已将其“木质化”能力调整为能把血肉变成纸张的版本，但它们并不如其同类的正常个体那般强大。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 2. Unnatural Uprising</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Once the NPCs have been rescued from the building and the spiritual disruptors are gone, the PCs have time to rest and recover. After 10 minutes have passed, or as soon as the PCs decide to leave the area (whichever comes first), another plume of red smoke rises into the air from the street as Mago Kai’s exorcists regroup in the living world and begin a second attempt to exorcise the rather robust spirits in the region.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/willowshore-waldgeist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Unnatural Uprising</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.hJEmfJJOQm9FImqP]{Willowshore Waldgeists (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> This time, the exorcists focus their efforts not on specific pinpoints of spiritual energy (represented by the lingering spirits of townsfolk in the living world), but instead on banishing a large mass of generalized spiritual energy infesting the area (represented by the accumulated loss of non-sapient life in the ruins). Smoke wells up at the eastern end of the street at area <strong>A5</strong>, and for a brief moment, several more of the gold-eyed, crimson-clad phantasms appear, only to vanish as the attempt to perform the mass exorcism fails in the real world.</p>\n  <p>Here in the mindscape, though, their attempt has a very real result, forcing this spiritual energy out of the living world and into the mindscape, where it infuses the very plants and trees that have grown over the ruins of Cloud Paper House in modern Willowshore. This corruption of the natural order manifests from that world into the mindscape at area <strong>A5</strong> as two waldgeists appear—distorted shapes that resemble deformed, miniature willow trees with screaming animal faces growing from their trunks. These incorporeal spirits immediately surge forward and float effortlessly to attack the PCs with dangling roots, drifting through the air almost like ghostly jellyfish. While these variant waldgeists are much larger than typical waldgeists and their spiritual entanglement with Cloud Paper House has adjusted their Lignify ability into one that transforms flesh into paper, they aren’t quite as powerful as normal specimens of their kind.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Event 1. Structural Collapse": {
              "name": "事件1：结构坍塌 Event 1. Structural Collapse",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件1：结构坍塌</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span>\n</h2>\n\n<p>\n  地图展示了云纸屋的一部分，其中包括一大片正在缓慢坍塌的区域，以及对面的街道和附近的建筑。本事件以及接下来的两个事件都发生在这个地点。\n</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-edited-ghostly-exorcist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">结构坍塌</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 7</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.EcvTHGd4tW4unX88]{Aruka} @UUID[Actor.5ntnQwWZmqDkJPwp]{Yu Er} @UUID[Actor.vgV2eqTlalwGWFFj]{Zhen Luoyang} @UUID[Actor.CMlumtTEaGVq9wNU]{Spiritual Disruptors (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n<p>\n  被困在建筑里的三名NPC需要救援，而由于在现实世界中进行的驱魔尝试，这里还出现了额外的危害。废墟中的三名NPC各自面临不同的困境，而PC必须完成任务把他们带到安全处。如果PC需要把NPC背出去，Aruka与Zhen Luoyang的负荷值都是6，而Yu Er的负荷值是3。要让一名NPC（或玩偶）免受危害影响，他们必须抵达废墟建筑南侧的街道；一旦到达，他们就会向东或向西逃离（或被人抬走）。围观人群会照顾他们，并确保他们安全抵达能休养恢复的地方。\n</p>\n<p>\n  在本次遭遇中，如果三名NPC的生命值降至0，请允许他们依照PC的濒死规则行事。在本次遭遇中死亡的6级或更低等级的生物会彻底消失：其灵魂被从柳岸镇思维空间中驱逐，前往浩瀚众界中的来世；但这一结果不应让PC或柳岸镇的其他居民察觉——在他们看来，只会像是该角色的身体突然无影无踪地消失。7级或更高等级的生物（例如PC）若在此被杀，这些驱魔人无力将其驱逐；如果他们被该区域的危害杀死，其身体（与灵魂）仍会被困在思维空间中。\n</p>\n <p>\n    <strong>危害：</strong>现实世界中柳岸镇废墟里的驱魔，在此处显现为一对灵扰破坏器危害。在本事件开始时，这些危害位于标注为<strong>A4</strong>的两个区域。\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    若PC花费超过6轮仍未解决局势，且至少有一个危害仍然处于活动状态，则结构会进一步坍塌，对建筑内所有目标造成@Damage[(2d6+6)[bludgeoning]]伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:15|basic]豁免）。每过6轮重复一次，直到所有NPC都被救出为止。若发生坍塌时建筑内没有任何活着的角色，则整座结构完全坍塌，灵扰破坏器随之消失。当PC成功救出所有仍被困者后的1轮，本事件自动发生。\n  </p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>A1. Aruka：</strong>Aruka是一名体格结实的狐人女性，当时正在搬运木材，天花板在她周围塌落，将她击倒在地，并把她的腿压在一张坍塌的桌子下。由于她的替身形态是人类女性而非狐狸，她试图通过变形逃脱均告失败。每轮在她的回合，她会尝试一次运动检定以逃脱，并获得+3加值；若她成功脱困，她会尽力一瘸一拐地朝街道与安全处移动。\n</p>\n<p>\n  要逃脱或破拆瓦砾，她或相邻的PC必须在\n  @Check[athletics|dc:23|traits:attack,skill,action:escape|name:Escape]（逃脱）或\n  @Check[athletics|dc:23|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]（破拆）检定中成功。\n  或者，\n  也可以摧毁瓦砾来解救她（AC 15，硬度10，生命值30［破损阈值15］）；如果瓦砾被破坏，用于逃脱与破拆的检定DC降为18。Aruka当前有2点生命值，并因伤势处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{缓慢（状态） 2}；若她被治疗至满生命值，她会失去缓慢2状态。成功进行一次\n  @Check[medicine|dc:20|traits:exploration,healing,manipulate,skill,action:treat-wounds|name:Treat Wounds]检定以\n  治疗伤势，也会移除她的缓慢状态，但除非PC拥有战地医疗专长，否则他们很可能没有奢侈到花10分钟来执行这一选项。在这种情况下，他们可以用该选项在同一DC下尝试移除她的缓慢状态。\n</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mrjelly.webp\" data-tooltip=\"My. Jelly\" alt=\"a cloth doll with a pleasant face and wearing a gray dress\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mrjelly.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  <strong>A2. Yu Er：</strong>Yu Er是一名五岁小女孩，她偷偷爬到椽子间的阁楼上玩耍。建筑开始坍塌时，她从阁楼地板跌落，但好运地落在地面一团纸浆里，只擦破了点皮。然而，她非常沮丧，因为她最喜欢的玩偶——Jelly先生——仍然用斗篷挂在她上方天花板破洞处伸出的一根断裂竹杆上。玩偶是一个以稻草填充的六臂人形体，戴着面具、披着斗篷；PC若成功通过\n  @Check[nature|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或\n  @Check[society|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,search,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall\n  Knowledge]检定来进行回忆知识，就能辨认出这是对黄谷神秘的Taljjae的一种漫画式夸张形象（详见《Pathfinder Lost Omens Monsters of Myth》第96–101页）。\n</p>\n<p>\n  Yu Er的一名家长冲进来想把她抱走，但女孩抗拒着，因害怕而哭喊，并伸手去抓Jelly先生。Jelly先生卡在离地20尺高处。可以对AC 24进行一次远程攻击把玩偶击落。若远程打击命中，攻击者还必须成功通过一次@Check[flat|dc:16]以将玩偶打落；若远程打击造成重击，则自动将其打落。诸如@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{念动射弹}之类的魔法手段若用于把玩偶向下掷出，则可自动取回。PC可利用松动的支撑物攀爬破碎的墙壁以接近玩偶，成功通过一次\n  @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定即可；相邻的PC可以以一次交互动作自动拾起玩偶。\n</p>\n<p>\n  取回Jelly先生时必须小心，避免撕裂他的斗篷或扯出部分填充物——每次尝试取回玩偶时，执行尝试的生物必须成功通过一次@Check[reflex|dc:22]豁免或\n  @Check[thievery|dc:22]检定，以避免损坏玩偶。一旦玩偶受损，就不再需要进行避免进一步损坏的检定——撕裂了就是撕裂了。\n</p>\n<p>\n  若Jelly先生完好无损并被送回Yu Er手中，她会立刻平静下来。若救援过程中Jelly先生受损，Yu Er会大发雷霆，因朋友受伤而崩溃。拥有修理工具包的PC可以用一次需要成功通过\n  @Check[crafting|dc:25]检定的三动作行动迅速修补玩偶（或者若其拥有@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.ASy9AKEIRxPYUi5o]{Quick Repair}专长，则即使没有修理工具包，也能以单动作自动完成），或者他们也可以对其施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.dINQzhqGmIsqGMUY]{Mending}或\n  @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.4ZGte0i9YbLh4dRi]{伪装物件}来修好玩偶。无论如何，Yu Er的父母都会对PC拯救Jelly先生深表感谢。PC也可以不去取回Jelly先生，转而通过一次DC 25检定来对Yu Er说谎、提出请求，甚至强迫她冷静下来\n  （@Check[deception|dc:25|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie]、\n  @Check[diplomacy|dc:25|traits:action:request,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental|name:Request]或\n  @Check[intimidation|dc:25|traits:auditory,concentrate,emotion,exploration,linguistic,mental,skill,action:coerce|name:Coerce]）。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>A3. Zhen Luoyang：</strong>这位矫健的老人当时正给在磨坊工作的侄子（围观灾害发生的人群中一名惊慌的年轻人）送自制午餐，混乱便突然爆发。建筑刚开始坍塌时，一阵碎片倾泻而下把他砸得失去知觉，同时也把他埋在一层崩落的灰泥与尘土之下。要在他仍被埋着时找到他，PC必须进行搜索并成功通过一次\n  @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定。\n</p>\n<p>\n  本事件开始时，Luoyang处于昏迷状态，俯卧在地面上。每轮在他的回合，他可以以+6强韧豁免加值尝试一次@Check[fortitude|dc:20]豁免。若成功，他会醒来，挣扎着站起，并以5尺速度一瘸一拐地朝安全处移动。他的伤势可用与Aruka相同的方式治疗（见<strong>A1</strong>），如此他将恢复25尺的完整速度。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\" data-split-here=\"Planting the Soul Seed\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 1. Structural Collapse</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span>\n</h2>\n\n<p>\n  The map shows a portion of Cloud Paper House, including a significant section that’s in the process\n  of slowly collapsing, along with the facing street and nearby buildings. This event, as well as the next two, all\n  take place in this location.\n</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-edited-ghostly-exorcist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Structural Collapse</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 7</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.EcvTHGd4tW4unX88]{Aruka} @UUID[Actor.5ntnQwWZmqDkJPwp]{Yu Er} @UUID[Actor.vgV2eqTlalwGWFFj]{Zhen Luoyang} @UUID[Actor.CMlumtTEaGVq9wNU]{Spiritual Disruptors (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n<p>\n  The three NPCs trapped in the building are in need of rescue, and additional hazards have manifested as a result\n  of the exorcism attempts taking place in the living world. Each of the three NPCs in the ruins faces their own\n  difficulty, and the PCs must perform tasks to get them to safety. If a PC has to carry out an NPC, Aruka and\n  Zhen Luoyang are both Bulk 6, while Yu Er is Bulk 3. For an NPC (or doll) to be safe from the hazard, they must reach\n  the street south of the ruined building, after which they flee (or are carried) to the east or west. The crowd\n  of onlookers takes care of them and ensures they make it safely to a place where they can recover.\n</p>\n<p>\n  In this encounter, allow the three NPCs to follow the PC rules for dying if they’re reduced to 0 Hit Points. A\n  creature of 6th level or lower that dies in this encounter vanishes entirely, their spirit exorcised from the\n  Willowshore mindscape to move on to the afterlife in the Great Beyond, but this outcome shouldn’t be apparent to\n  the PCs or to Willowshore’s other inhabitants—to them, it should simply look as if the character’s body has\n  suddenly vanished without a trace. Creatures of 7th level or higher (such as the PCs) who are slain here are\n  beyond the power of these exorcists to banish, and their bodies (and souls) remain trapped in the mindscape if\n  they’re killed by this area’s hazard.\n</p>\n <p>\n    <strong>Hazards:</strong> The exorcism in the ruins of Willowshore in the living world manifests here as a pair of spiritual\n    disruptor hazards. At the start of this event, the hazards are located at the two areas marked <strong>A4</strong>.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    If the PCs take longer than 6 rounds to resolve the situation and at least one hazard remains active, more of\n    the structure collapses, causing @Damage[(2d6+6)[bludgeoning]] damage to all within the building (@Check[reflex|dc:15|basic]\n    save). This repeats every 6 rounds until all of the NPCs are rescued. If this collapse takes place while there are no living\n    characters within the building, the entire structure collapses, and the spiritual disruptors vanish. This event\n    occurs automatically 1 round after the PCs manage to rescue all of those still trapped.\n  </p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>A1. Aruka:</strong> Aruka is a solidly built kitsune woman who was hauling logs when the ceiling fell all around her,\n  knocking her to the ground and pinning her leg under a collapsed table. Since her alternate form is of a human\n  woman and not a fox, her attempts to change shape to escape have proven fruitless. On her turn each round, she\n  attempts an Athletics check to Escape with a +3 bonus; if she manages to get free, she hobbles her way toward\n  the street and to safety as best she can.\n</p>\n<p>\n  To Escape or Force Open the rubble, she or an adjacent PC must succeed at a\n  @Check[athletics|dc:23|traits:attack,skill,action:escape|name:Escape] (Escape) or\n  @Check[athletics|dc:23|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] (Force Open) check.\n  Alternatively,\n  the rubble can be destroyed to free her (AC 15, Hardness 10, HP 30 [BT 15]); if the rubble is broken, the DC for\n  checks to Escape and Force Open drops to 18. Aruka currently has 2 HP and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 2} by her wound; if she’s\n  healed to full HP, she loses the slowed 2 condition. A PC who succeeds at a\n  @Check[medicine|dc:20|traits:exploration,healing,manipulate,skill,action:treat-wounds|name:Treat Wounds] check to\n  Treat Wounds also removes her slowed condition, but the PCs likely don’t have the luxury of spending 10 minutes to pursue\n  this option unless they have the Battle Medicine feat. In that case, they can attempt to remove her slowed condition\n  using that option against the same DC.\n</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mrjelly.webp\" data-tooltip=\"My. Jelly\" alt=\"a cloth doll with a pleasant face and wearing a gray dress\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mrjelly.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  <strong>A2. Yu Er:</strong> Yu Er is a five-year-old girl who snuck into a loft in the rafters to play. When the building began\n  to collapse, she fell through the loft floor but was lucky enough to fall into a mass of paper pulp on the ground\n  and only suffered superficial scrapes. However, she’s quite distressed that her favorite doll, Mr. Jelly, remains\n  hanging by its cape from a snapped bamboo pole protruding from the hole in the ceiling above her. The doll is a\n  straw-stuffed, six-limbed humanoid wearing a mask and a cape that, with a successful\n  @Check[nature|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or\n  @Check[society|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,search,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall\n  Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC can identify as a caricature of Hwanggot’s mysterious Taljjae (detailed on pages\n  96–101 of <em>Pathfinder Lost Omens Monsters of Myth</em>).\n</p>\n<p>\n  One of Yu Er’s parents races in to collect her, but the girl resists, crying in fear and reaching up for Mr.\n  Jelly. Mr. Jelly is snagged at a height of 20 feet off the ground. The doll can be knocked loose via a ranged\n  attack against AC 24. If a ranged Strike hits, the attacker must then succeed at a @Check[flat|dc:16] to knock the\n  doll loose; if the ranged Strike is a critical hit, it’s automatically knocked loose. Magical solutions like\n  @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{Telekinetic Projectile} used to hurl the doll downward can automatically recover it. A PC can Climb up the\n  crumbling wall using the loose supports to reach the doll with a successful\n  @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check, and an\n  adjacent PC can pick up the doll automatically as an Interact action.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Care must be taken when retrieving Mr. Jelly to avoid ripping his cape or some of his stuffing out—each time an\n  attempt is made to retrieve the doll, the creature making the attempt must succeed at a @Check[reflex|dc:22] save or\n  @Check[thievery|dc:22] check to avoid damaging the doll. Once the doll has been damaged, no further checks to avoid\n  further damaging it are necessary—what’s torn is torn.\n</p>\n<p>\n  If Mr. Jelly is intact and returned to Yu Er, she calms down immediately. If Mr. Jelly was damaged during the\n  rescue, Yu Er throws an epic tantrum, devastated that her friend got hurt. A PC who has a repair toolkit can\n  quickly patch the doll up as a three-action activity that requires a successful\n  @Check[crafting|dc:25] check (or automatically as a single action even without access to a repair toolkit \n  if they have the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.ASy9AKEIRxPYUi5o]{Quick Repair} feat), or\n  they can fix the doll by casting @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.dINQzhqGmIsqGMUY]{Mending} or \n  @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.4ZGte0i9YbLh4dRi]{Item Facade} on it. Either way, Yu Er’s parents thank the PCs\n  profusely for saving Mr. Jelly. A PC can instead Lie, Request, or even Coerce Yu Er into calming down without retrieving\n  Mr. Jelly by succeeding at a DC 25 check\n  (@Check[deception|dc:25|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie],\n  @Check[diplomacy|dc:25|traits:action:request,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental|name:Request], or\n  @Check[intimidation|dc:25|traits:auditory,concentrate,emotion,exploration,linguistic,mental,skill,action:coerce|name:Coerce]).\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>A3. Zhen Luoyang:</strong> This spry, elderly man was delivering a homemade lunch to his nephew (a panicked young man in\n  the crowd watching the disaster unfold) who works in the mill when chaos struck. When the building first began\n  to collapse, a blast of debris showered down on him and left him senseless, and it also buried him under a layer of\n  crumbled plaster and dust. In order to locate him while he remains buried, a PC must Search and succeed at a\n  @Check[perception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Luoyang is unconscious when this event begins, lying prone on the ground. Each round on his turn, he can attempt\n  a @Check[fortitude|dc:20] save with a +6 Fortitude save bonus. On a success, he wakes, hobbles to his feet, and limps at\n  a speed of 5 feet toward safety. His wounds can be treated in the same way as for Aruka (see <strong>A1</strong>), in\n  which case he regains his full Speed of 25 feet.\n</p>"
            },
            "Red Smoke, Gold Eyes": {
              "name": "红烟，金眸 Red Smoke, Gold Eyes",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Red Smoke, Gold Eyes\">红烟金瞳</h1>\n<p>在上一幕的最后一周里，柳岸镇的一名居民神秘失踪。人们不会找到任何这名失踪者的痕迹；他们已被孙海的一名驱邪师驱逐，而其灵魂已前往来世，在骨园接受审判。这次失踪的性质应当让PC既担忧又好奇；因此，上一幕建议将这次失踪的时机安排在秋季的最后一天。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-edited-ghostly-exorcist.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ghostly Exorcist\" alt=\"ghostly exorcist dressed in a frightening red costume and a mask with four glowing gold eyes\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-edited-ghostly-exorcist.webp')\" />\n<p>在PC与柳岸镇的人民还来不及调查这起神秘失踪，或开始研究柳岸镇思维空间以及如何最好地与镇上失踪的执政官取得联系之前，另一场失踪事件便开始了——但这一次，孙海的驱邪师行动更为激进。数十名驱邪师身着惊惧的装束，挥舞着火焰，意在吓退那些在现世中徘徊于柳岸镇废墟的魂魄，开始在镇上推进。随着他们的行动，柳岸镇各处升起缕缕红烟，仿佛诡异的无形火焰正吞没那些区域的建筑；然而，这些地点并未出现真正的火势。真正等待着众人的，是由驱邪师设计的危险危害——PC必须战胜这些危害，才能阻止更多柳岸镇居民失踪。</p>\n<p>此事件发生在上午接近正午之前、且PC已全体集结之后的某个时刻。最好让事件在他们途经柳岸镇镇区附近时开始，这样他们就能看见木筏湖南岸的云纸屋（区域W14）升起的诡异红烟；否则，惊惧的NPC会迅速去找PC，提醒他们这桩怪事。若PC立刻动身调查现场，他们应能及时赶到并顺利开始这场事件。</p>\n<p>当PC靠近时，任何关于造纸工坊冒烟是因失火所致的担忧都应当烟消云散，因为那里没有任何火焰可见；那烟羽的深红色尤其显得不自然。PC抵达现场时，街道上聚集着数十名惊惧的镇民，他们告诉PC，建筑的某些部分正直接化作烟雾消失，导致结构开始坍塌。有三名平民被困在这座缓慢坍塌的建筑内，这条消息应当促使PC尝试迅速营救。</p>\n<p>在现实世界中，云纸屋如今已成一片几乎无法支撑自身重量的废墟，但它仍是湖泊南岸少数尚未倒塌的建筑之一。在这里，孙海的驱邪师决定进行他们首次重大的尝试，试图将魂魄从废墟中驱逐出去；随着他们的工作推进，现实世界的废墟开始“渗入”思维空间，导致建筑在更多部分凭空消失时逐步崩塌。</p>\n<p>该区域升起的红烟是驱邪师仪式的显现；该仪式包括燃起篝火，并使用火把、火焰与惊惧的装束来驱逐“邪灵”。当PC首次进入受影响的区域（见第154页地图）时，他们会短暂而令人不安地瞥见其中一名驱邪师身着惊惧装束的景象——宣读或转述以下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>四只发光的金色眼睛在烟雾中燃起，向前移动，却没有身躯或双腿承载。一个怪物般的红色面孔只在周围空气中渗出一瞬，泛黄的獠牙骇人地从口中扭曲伸出，随即骤然消失。黑色袖口在猩红的躯体周围翻涌，以布匹的洪流滑入现实，漏出滚滚的香云，继而崩塌成灰，在风中吹散。又前行几步，金色眼睛也随之熄灭。刺鼻的烟味仍在，而远处那座正在坍塌的建筑里，求救声仍不断响起。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这名驱邪师的幻象消失得太快，没人能看清更多细节；但进行一次@Check[religion|dc:23|traits:secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识后，PC会注意到那个衣着诡异的身影似乎在执行某种仪式，但很可能只是该区域强大魔法所制造的幻影。若取得大成功或大失败，PC会推断那身影的影像或许是从另一个思维空间投射而来……也许正是执政官@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{和善保}被困的那个？</p>\n<p>关于这一影像其实是来自115年后现实世界的一名驱邪师的投影，这一认知不应在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第10章}相当后段之前出现；但一旦PC确实在现世遭遇这些驱邪师，你就应确保他们意识到：这些特工与PC在柳岸镇街头所面对的那些超自然力量其实是同一批存在——当柳岸镇仍被困在其思维空间之中时尤其如此。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Red Smoke, Gold Eyes\">Red Smoke, Gold Eyes</h1>\n<p>During the final week of the previous act, one of Willowshore’s citizens mysteriously vanished. No trace of the missing resident will be found; they’ve been exorcised by one of Mago Kai’s exorcists, and their soul has moved on to the afterlife to be judged in the Boneyard. The nature of this disappearance should worry and intrigue the PCs, and as such, the previous act suggested timing this vanishing so it takes place on the last day of fall.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-edited-ghostly-exorcist.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ghostly Exorcist\" alt=\"ghostly exorcist dressed in a frightening red costume and a mask with four glowing gold eyes\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-edited-ghostly-exorcist.webp')\" />\n<p>Before the PCs and the people of Willowshore have a chance to look into this mysterious disappearance or start researching the Willowshore mindscape and how best they can contact the town’s missing governor, another vanishing event begins—but this time, Mago Kai’s exorcists are more aggressive in their work. Dozens of these exorcists, dressed in frightening costumes and wielding fire meant to scare off the spirits that haunt the ruins of Willowshore in the living world, begin to work their way through the town. As they do, plumes of red smoke rise from various sites in Willowshore, as if strange, invisible flames were engulfing the buildings in these areas; however, no actual fires appear at these sites. What do await are dangerous hazards engineered by the exorcists—hazards the PCs must defeat before even more of Willowshore’s citizens vanish.</p>\n<p>This event takes place mid-morning at a time after the PCs have all gathered together. It’s best for the event to begin as they are traveling near downtown Willowshore so that they can spot the eerie plumes of red smoke that start to rise from the Cloud Paper House (area W14) on the southern shore of Woodraft Lake; otherwise, frightened NPCs quickly seek the PCs out to alert them of the strange event. If the PCs set off to investigate the site at once, they should arrive in time to begin this event without issue.</p>\n<p>Any fears that the smoke rising from the paper-making factory are the consequence of a fire should be put to rest as the PCs approach, for no flames are visible; the crimson color of the plumes appears particularly unnatural. When the PCs arrive at the scene, dozens of frightened townsfolk who have gathered in the streets tell them that parts of the building have simply been vanishing into smoke, causing the structure to begin to collapse. Three civilians are trapped inside the slowly collapsing building, news that should spur the PCs to attempt a swift rescue.</p>\n<p>In the real world, Cloud Paper House is now a ruin that can barely support its own weight, but it’s one of the few buildings still standing along the lake’s southern shore. Here, Kai’s exorcists have decided to pursue their first significant attempt to banish spirits from the ruins, and as their work proceeds, the real-world ruins begin to “seep” into the mindscape, causing the building to collapse as more of its parts simply vanish.</p>\n<p>The red smoke rising from the area is a manifestation of the exorcists’ ritual, which involves the burning of a bonfire and the use of torches, fire, and frightening costumes to drive out “evil spirits.” When the PCs first enter the afflicted area (presented on the map on page 154), they catch a brief but unsettling glimpse of one of these exorcists in their frightening attire—read or paraphrase the following.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Four glowing golden eyes blaze into existence in the smoke, moving forward without a body or legs to carry them. A monstrous red visage bleeds into air around them for just a moment, yellowed fangs twisting gruesomely out of its mouth before abruptly vanishing. Black sleeves billow around a crimson body, slipping into reality in torrents of cloth and leaking rolling clouds of incense before collapsing into ash and blowing away in the wind. A few paces more, and the golden eyes wink out. The acrid smell of smoke remains, and calls for help continue to ring out from the collapsing building beyond.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The vision of this exorcist is gone too quickly for anyone to see more, but with a @Check[religion|dc:23|traits:secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC notes that the strangely dressed figure seemed to be performing some sort of ritual, but was likely little more than a figment created by the powerful magic afflicting the area. With a critical success, the PC surmises that the image of the figure might have been projected from another mindscape entirely... perhaps the one that Governor @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} is trapped in?</p>\n<p>The realization that this image was a projection of an exorcist from the real world 115 years in the future shouldn’t come until well into @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10}, but once the PCs do encounter these exorcists in the living world, you should ensure they realize that these agents are one and the same with the supernatural forces the PCs have faced on the streets of Willowshore while it remains entrapped in its mindscape.</p>"
            },
            "Repercussions": {
              "name": "后果 Repercussions",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Repercussions\">后果</h3>\n<p>任何一类准备点数都不能被降到0以下，但每当有至少一类点数以这种方式被彻底耗尽并持续过了一周，就会给柳岸镇的人民带来可怕的后果。</p>\n<p><strong>没有希望：</strong>柳岸镇的人民陷入绝望与惊惧，他们很少离开自己的家。为购买物品与服务之目的，将柳岸镇视为一个等级1的聚落。每当你本应减少希望点数时，改为使PC与柳岸镇双方势力的声望各降低2。</p>\n<p><strong>没有食物：</strong>柳岸镇的人民正在挨饿。每当你本应减少希望点数时，改为使柳岸镇的人口减少[[/r 2d6]]。</p>\n<p><strong>没有安全：</strong>柳岸镇的人民毫无防备。每当你本应减少安全点时，改为使柳岸镇的人口减少[[/r 1d6]]。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Repercussions\">Repercussions</h3>\n<p>No category of Preparation Points can be reduced below zero, but every week that passes where at least one category is completely depleted in this way has dire repercussions for the people of Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>No Hope:</strong> The people of Willowshore are despondent and frightened, and they rarely exit their homes. Treat Willowshore as a level 1 settlement for the purposes of purchasing items and services. Each time you would normally reduce Hope Points, instead reduce the PCs’ reputation with both of Willowshore’s factions by 2.</p>\n<p><strong>No Food:</strong> The people of Willowshore are starving. Each time you would normally reduce Hope Points, instead reduce Willowshore’s population by [[/r 2d6]].</p>\n<p><strong>No Security:</strong> The people of Willowshore are defenseless. Each time you would normally reduce Security Points, instead reduce Willowshore’s population by [[/r 1d6]].</p>"
            },
            "Weekly Attrition": {
              "name": "每周损耗 Weekly Attrition",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Weekly Attrition\">每周损耗</h3>\n<p>随着时间推移，镇民在日渐严酷的天气与骇人的超自然事件影响下变得更加阴郁，精神也愈发疲惫；他们消耗的食物储备越来越多，并且在天气与他们作对之际，手忙脚乱地维持房屋修缮。每周结束时，对柳岸镇的准备点数进行以下调整。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>希望点减少[[/r 1d4]]。</li>\n  <li>食物点减少1。</li>\n  <li>安全点减少1。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Weekly Attrition\">Weekly Attrition</h3>\n<p>As time passes, the townsfolk grow gloomier and more mentally exhausted by the increasingly harsh weather and frightening supernatural events, consume more and more of their food stores, and scramble to keep their homes repaired as the weather works against them. At the end of every week, make the following adjustments to Willowshore’s Preparation Points.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Reduce Hope Points by [[/r 1d4]].</li>\n  <li>Reduce Food Points by 1.</li>\n  <li>Reduce Security Points by 1.</li>\n</ul>"
            },
            "Preparation Points": {
              "name": "准备点数 Preparation Points",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparation Points\">准备点数</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>呼叫替补！</h1>\n  <p>本次冒险中的事件有时会提及居住在柳岸镇、并在前几幕中登场过的NPC。然而，《鬼季》对NPC而言可能相当致命，而在本段冒险中被赋予职责的部分NPC，在你的游戏里也许已经死亡。若是如此，只需用一名合适的在世替代者替换已故NPC，或编造一位新的村民与PC交谈——也许是那位已故NPC的家人或朋友。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>在第2幕期间，PC们花了数周时间为柳岸镇即将到来的冬季做准备。随着“第3幕：欲泣无息”在冬季的第一天拉开序幕，准备的时间已经过去。希望柳岸镇已经准备就绪！本幕通过三类准备点数来追踪村庄的状态：希望点、食物点与安全点。</p>\n<p>当你开始这一幕时，务必让玩家知晓他们累积的希望点、食物点与安全点总数。本幕的事件将需要花费这些点数：既包括每周固定的常规消耗，也包括特定遭遇与事件发生后导致的消耗，详见后续页面。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparation Points\">Preparation Points</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Call the Understudy!</h1>\n  <p>Events in this adventure sometimes reference NPCs who live in Willowshore and who have appeared in previous acts. <em>Season of Ghosts</em> can be lethal for NPCs, however, and some of the NPCs given roles in this part of the adventure might be dead in your game. If so, simply swap the deceased NPC with an appropriate living substitute, or make up a new villager to converse with the PCs—perhaps a family member or friend of the dead NPC in question.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>During Act 2, the PCs spent weeks preparing Willowshore for the coming winter. As “Act 3: No Breath to Cry” begins on the first day of winter, the time for preparation has passed. Hopefully, Willowshore is ready! This act tracks the village’s status via three categories of Preparation Points: Hope Points, Food Points, and Security Points.</p>\n<p>When you begin this act, make sure the players are aware of the total number of Hope Points, Food Points, and Security Points they’ve accumulated. The events of this act will require the expenditure of these points, both on a regular weekly basis and as the results of specific encounters and occurrences, as detailed on the following pages.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore in the Winter": {
              "name": "冬日的柳岸镇 Willowshore in the Winter",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore in the Winter\">冬日柳岸镇</h2>\n<p>在本幕中，清爽的秋日与日渐稀少的晴朗午后已成过去。神门的冬季多风而寒冷，常有暴雨与雷暴。降雪虽罕见却并非闻所未闻，而今年，雪将以某种出人意料的猛烈之势降在柳岸镇思维空间的范围之内。虽然气温不会冷到让湖泊与河流结冰，但寒意将强烈到足以让任何被困在户外过夜的人面临因暴露在风雨严寒中而死亡的重大危险。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.gfm2uOw7FTb4po3S]{柳岸镇} @UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.hcOE3Y4scm0wvt1j]{室内} @UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.64W4hCezS4mJFerz]{边地} @UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.1p1iJlqwTDWo7RHc]{林地}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>人口下降</h1>\n  <p>在第一幕的前两章所详述的最初怪物入侵之后，柳岸镇起初有人口225人；但随着战役推进，随着NPC死亡——或因遭遇中的坏运气，或在预设事件中——人口将缓慢下降。城镇的实际人口对其数据没有影响，但追踪这个不断减少的数字，是在玩家之间营造并维持紧迫感的绝佳方式。随着这场冒险继续，某些事件或食物与安全的匮乏会使人口总数进一步下降。随着人口下降，请记录柳岸镇的最终人口，因为它将影响冒险路径的结局。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore in the Winter\">Willowshore in the Winter</h2>\n<p>Crisp autumn days and increasingly sparse sunny afternoons are a thing of the past in this act. Winters in Shenmen are blustery and cold, boasting frequent rainstorms and thunderstorms. Snow is rare but not unknown, and this year, it will fall with somewhat unexpected force within the confines of the Willowshore mindscape. While it won’t grow cold enough for the lakes and rivers to freeze, the chill will be intense enough that anyone trapped outside overnight will be in grave peril of dying from exposure to the elements.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.gfm2uOw7FTb4po3S]{Willowshore} @UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.hcOE3Y4scm0wvt1j]{Indoors} @UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.64W4hCezS4mJFerz]{Hinterlands} @UUID[Playlist.gTnkl7DUH19mzyJj.PlaylistSound.1p1iJlqwTDWo7RHc]{Woods}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>A Declining Population</h1>\n  <p>After the initial monstrous invasion detailed in the first two chapters of Act 1, Willowshore begins with a population of 225 people, but as the campaign goes on, that population slowly declines as NPCs perish—either as the results of poor luck in encounters or in scripted events. The town’s actual population has no effect on its stats, but keeping track of this declining number can be a great way to foster and maintain a sense of urgency among the players. As this adventure goes on, certain events or lack of food or security will cause this population total to decline even further. As it does, keep track of Willowshore’s final population, as it will impact the Adventure Path’s conclusion.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Getting Started": {
              "name": "冒险开始 Getting Started",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">冒险开始</h1>\n<p><em>鬼季冒险路径</em>的上一幕以PC们得知自己被困在一个循环的思维空间中而告终；这个思维空间每年在春季最后一天都会重置。借助他们从谭杉寺取回的文本，PC们如今已拥有开始研究一项仪式所需的最后工具；该仪式将使他们得以逃脱柳岸镇思维空间并返回现实世界。</p>\n<p>当你准备开始“第三幕：欲泣无息”时，继续进行@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10redsmokegold00]{红烟金瞳}中详述的事件。孙海的代理人正试图在现实世界中将幽灵从柳岸镇的废墟中驱逐出去；在PC们与这些代理人的初次遭遇结束后，他们应当意识到，柳岸镇所面临的超自然威胁并不仅仅源自苦迦菩提的影响。为查明这桩谜团的真相，他们应尽一切努力在和善保的思维空间中联系到@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{总督和善保}——不管那会在哪里！</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">Getting Started</h1>\n<p>The previous act of the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em> ended with the PCs learning that they’re trapped within a cyclic mindscape that resets every year on the last day of spring. With the texts they’ve recovered from the Tan Sugi monastery, the PCs now have the final tools they need to begin researching a ritual that will allow them to escape the Willowshore mindscape and return to the real world.</p>\n<p>Once you’re ready to begin “Act 3: No Breath to Cry,” proceed with the events detailed in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10redsmokegold00]{Red Smoke, Gold Eyes}. Mago Kai’s agents are attempting to exorcise ghosts from the ruins of Willowshore in the living world, and after the PCs’ initial encounters with these agents conclude, they should realize that the supernatural threats facing Willowshore stem from more than just Kugaptee’s influence. To get to the bottom of this mystery, they should make every effort to contact Governor @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0000]{Heh Shan-Bao} in his mindscape—wherever that might be!</p>"
            },
            "Oblivion of Truth": {
              "name": "真相的湮灭 Oblivion of Truth",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Oblivion of Truth\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第8章：</span>\n  <span>真相的湮灭</span>\n</h1>\n<p>柳岸镇已经被困在一个无休止的循环中超过一百年，但其居民并非麻木地参与着自身不知情的折磨。这个循环从不会以完全相同的方式重演。各种超自然事件、不同的抉择，以及单纯的运气使得每一轮循环中总有不同的镇民偶然触及自身存在的真相，并尝试逃脱。尽管已有一百多次机会这样做，迄今为止却无人获得成功。更糟的是，每当思维空间回溯到夏季第一天时，他们的进展就会被彻底重置，导致柳岸镇的人民忘却所学的一切，并失去所有关于其发现的物证。</p>\n<p>而这一次，在思维空间的第115轮循环中，情况不同了。现实世界中的事件改变了思维空间中的现状，一支新的英雄团队——玩家角色——对将他们困住的“诅咒”有了惊人的发现。但尽管他们现在知道自己被困在思维空间之中，他们仍未得知自身处境的终极真相——他们全都死了。困扰柳岸镇的“闹鬼”现象，乃是活人驱魔师所为；他们试图驱逐这些幽灵般的镇民，以便安全采伐当地森林。一旦柳岸镇的魂魄被解缆并送往@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}，孙海及其伐木营地便可进驻，并开始将木材运回神门的首都。</p>\n<p>如今，玩家角色已掌握从谭杉寺废墟中回收的资源，可以开始探查春季最后一夜究竟发生了什么；但一场格外惨烈的严冬阴影正笼罩小镇，他们必须明智地分配自己的时间与资源。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-fighting-your-own-shadow.webp\" alt=\"Fighting Your Own Shadow\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Oblivion of Truth\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 8:</span>\n  <span>Oblivion of Truth</span>\n</h1>\n<p>The town of Willowshore has been trapped in an unending cycle for over a hundred years, but its inhabitants aren’t mindless participants in their own unknowing torment. The cycle never plays out in quite the same way. Various supernatural events, choices made differently, and simple turns of luck allow different citizens to stumble upon the truth of their existence each cycle and make attempts to escape. Despite having had more than a hundred opportunities to do so, none have found success thus far. It doesn’t help that their progress is completely reset every time the mindscape reverts to the first day of summer, causing the people of Willowshore to forget everything they’ve learned and lose all physical evidence of their discoveries.</p>\n<p>This time around, during the mindscape’s 115th cycle, things are different. Events in the living world have changed the status quo in the mindscape, and a new group of heroes, the PCs, have made incredible discoveries about the “curse” that has kept them trapped. But while they now know they’re held within a mindscape, they have yet to learn the ultimate truth of their situation—they’re all dead. The “hauntings” that have been plaguing Willowshore are the work of living exorcists attempting to banish the ghostly townsfolk so that the local forest can be safely harvested. Once the spirits of Willowshore have been unmoored and sent on to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}, Mago Kai and his logging camp can move in and begin sending lumber back to Shenmen’s capital.</p>\n<p>Now armed with resources recovered from the ruins of the Tan Sugi monastery, the PCs can begin the process of learning what actually happened on the last night of spring, but with the cruelty of a particularly harrowing winter looming over the town, they’ll need to spend their time and resources wisely.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 3.2: Face-to-Face with Death": {
          "name": "第三幕 3.2：与死亡面对面 Act 3.2: Face-to-Face with Death",
          "pages": {
            "Between Life and Death": {
              "name": "生死之间 Between Life and Death",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">生死之间</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>当PC们施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}，烈焰在他们周围燃烧，将他们裹在陶土外壳中的身躯烘烤时，他们在脑海中听见一个不祥的声音，听起来与贺赫总督的声音相似——那声音命令他们向自身欲望屈服，让足以撕裂死亡桎梏的强烈情绪将他们吞没。让玩家描述此刻驱动其角色的最强烈感受。除了作为一次角色扮演机会之外，这些情绪还可以在PC们于现代神门获得幽魂之力时为其选择提供指引（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20hauntingthel00]{Haunting the Living}）。</p>\n<p>当仪式结束、PC们从陶土外壳中脱出时，他们并未回到生者世界——相反，他们在一条由凿刻石材构成的走廊中醒来。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>两扇木制推拉门封住了这间沉闷的石墙房间两端；房间约三十尺宽、六十尺长。木门上雕饰华丽，刻着一名畸形巨人残忍地将人活活捶死的场景。尽管墙壁与天花板相对光滑，石质地面却纵横交错着浅浅的裂痕。房间中央是一座仪式祭坛，上面摆满了熏香、蜡烛与其他器具。</p>\n</div>\n<p>成功进行一次 @Check[arcana|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[occultism|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 的回忆知识检定后，某位PC意识到他们出现在一处夹在柳岸镇与生者世界之间的思维空间之中；此地作为形而上的“碎屑收集器”，会收纳那些未被苦迦菩提完全吞噬的灵魂。</p>\n<p>推拉门具有硬度5与20 HP（BT 10）。雕刻在门上留下了大量孔洞，因此门关闭时并不会完全阻挡视觉线，而是为位于门另一侧的生物提供较大掩护。整个边境地带是一个闭合回环：在<strong>B1</strong>、<strong>B2</strong>、<strong>B3</strong>与<strong>B4</strong>区域中的走廊会无缝延续到其对应部分，使地图自身相连。</p>\n<p>PC们能感觉到生者世界对他们的感召；每经过一轮，祭坛上方那道闪烁的光环就变得更加清晰，并逐渐转化为通往晨步桥的传送门。但在该传送门完全成形之前，PC们必须击败栖居在这片思维空间中的灵堕魔。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.Kpb494oaT9HBq20S]{Partially Open Portal} @UUID[Macro.FnxYz1My8Hsh2Uf3]{Fully Open Portal}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-kagekuma-nindoru.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">生死之间</span> <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.0yBS3zFGEvoeQB1L]{痂苦魔（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>PC们一站起身，光线便仿佛开始闪烁，令人不安的低语充斥空气；那些声音以嘲弄的口吻宣告PC们抛下柳岸镇前往生者世界，宣告被他们留下的人们感到背叛，宣告他们永远无法重获那些人的信任。这些低语是三只痂苦魔灵堕魔（潜伏灵堕魔）在思维空间中喷吐的谎言；它们分别显现于地图上每个标注为<strong>B5</strong>的位置。它们用察觉掷先攻，然后朝中央房间移动以攻击队伍——它们已显现出包裹，因此其速度降为15尺。</p>\n  <p>一旦某只痂苦魔发现一名PC，该灵堕魔便会弃下它的包裹，猛然加速冲上前攻击。若其生命值降至50以下，痂苦魔会施放translocate撤退回起始点，显现一个新的包裹以获得AC加值，并开始再次跟踪PC们。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>穿过传送门：</strong>当最后一只痂苦魔灵堕魔（潜伏灵堕魔）被杀死后，祭坛上方的传送门闪烁并凝实。PC们可在任何时候踏入其中；当他们这么做时，便完成了transmigration，并开始 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第10章}。为PC们这项意义重大的成就给予80 XP。</p>\n<p>在此遭遇中死亡的任何PC并不会真正被杀死，除非整个队伍全灭。只要至少有一名PC存活并踏入传送门，所有PC都会在第10章开始时于柳岸镇的废墟中醒来，但在此遭遇中死去者将获得 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.3uh1r86TzbQvosxv]{毁灭 1}。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Between Life and Death</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As the PCs cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}, and as the flames burn around them and bake them in their clay shells, they feel a baleful voice in their minds that resembles Governor Heh’s—the voice orders them to give in to their desires, to be consumed by emotions strong enough that they can rip themselves free from the clutches of death. Have the players describe the most powerful feelings that motivate their characters at this time. In addition to serving as a roleplaying opportunity, these emotions can help guide the PCs when choosing the ghostly powers they gain in modern-day Shenmen (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20hauntingthel00]{Haunting the Living}).</p>\n<p>When the ritual ends and the PCs emerge from their clay shells, they don’t emerge into the living world—instead, they wake inside a hallway of carved stone.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Two wooden sliding doors cap the ends of this drab, thirty-by-sixty-foot stone-walled chamber. The wooden doors are ornately carved with depictions of a misshapen giant brutally bludgeoning people to death. Despite the relatively smooth walls and ceilings, the stone floor is crisscrossed with shallow gashes. In the center of the chamber is a ritual altar covered in incense, candles, and other accoutrements.</p>\n</div>\n<p>With a successful @Check[arcana|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[occultism|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC realizes they’ve emerged in a mindscape wedged between Willowshore and the living world that acts as metaphysical “crumb catcher” for souls not fully consumed by Kugaptee.</p>\n<p>The sliding doors have Hardness 5 and 20 HP (BT 10). Their carvings leave a great many holes, so they don’t entirely block line of sight when closed, instead providing greater cover to those on the opposite side. The entire borderland is a closed loop: corridors in areas <strong>B1</strong>, <strong>B2</strong>, <strong>B3</strong>, and <strong>B4</strong> continue seamlessly into their counterparts, connecting the map to itself.</p>\n<p>The PCs can feel the living world calling to them, and during each round that passes, the shimmering aura above the altar grows clearer as it transforms into a portal to Dawnstep Bridge. But before that portal is fully formed, the PCs must defeat the nindorus that dwell in this mindscape.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macros</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.Kpb494oaT9HBq20S]{Partially Open Portal} @UUID[Macro.FnxYz1My8Hsh2Uf3]{Fully Open Portal}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-kagekuma-nindoru.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Between Life and Death</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.0yBS3zFGEvoeQB1L]{Kagekumas (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> As soon as the PCs stand, the light seems to flicker and unsettling whispers fill the air, voices that issue mocking decrees about the PCs abandoning Willowshore for the living world, of how the people they left behind feel betrayed, and of how they’ll never be able to regain their trust. These whispers are lies spewed into the mindscape by three kagekuma nindorus that manifest at each location labeled <strong>B5</strong> on the map. They roll Perception for initiative, then make their way toward the central chamber to attack the party—they already have bundles manifested, so their Speed is reduced to 15 feet.</p>\n  <p>Once one of the kagekumas spots a PC, the nindoru Sheds its Bundle to lurch forth quickly and attack. If reduced to fewer than 50 Hit Points, a kagekuma casts translocate to retreat to its starting point, manifests a new bundle to gain an AC bonus, and begins stalking the PCs again.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Through the Portal:</strong> Once the last of the kagekuma nindorus are slain, the portal atop the altar flickers and solidifies. The PCs can step through at any point; as they do so, they complete their transmigration and begin @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10}. Grant the PCs 80 XP for this momentous achievement.</p>\n<p>Any PC who dies in this encounter isn’t actually slain unless the whole party dies. As long as at least one PC lives and steps through the portal, all of the PCs wake in the ruins of Willowshore at the start of Chapter 10, but those who died in this encounter are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.3uh1r86TzbQvosxv]{Doomed 1}.</p>"
            },
            "Transmigrating": {
              "name": "转生 Transmigrating",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Transmigrating\">移魂转生</h1>\n<p>PC何时施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} 取决于他们何时学会该仪式。他们在这么做之前至少应达到8级——游戏内“必须等待榊木木片准备好”的要求，意在让PC有足够时间经历 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto]{Chapter 9} 中除 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event13inter00]{Event 13} 之外的所有事件，从而有机会获得所需的经验。</p>\n<p>PC应当已经得知，<em>长明灯</em>之光在生者世界已然熄灭，这使他们只能施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} 的4环版本。即使他们知道这一限制，或已得知火焰被带去了唐入，从柳岸镇的思维空间过渡到生者世界时仍有另一个惊喜在等着他们。苦迦菩提的影响依旧强大，他会反抗PC死亡被逆转之事：为试图在他们继续前进之前杀死他们，他将PC投入另一个规模小得多的思维空间之中。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Transmigrating\">Transmigrating</h1>\n<p>The timing of when the PCs cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} depends on when they learn the ritual. They should be at least 8th level before they do so—the in-game requirement of needing to wait for the sakaki slats to be prepared is intended to give the PCs enough time to play through all of the events in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto]{Chapter 9} save for @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event13inter00]{Event 13} so that they’ll have the chance to earn the experience they need.</p>\n<p>The PCs should’ve learned that the light of the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> has been extinguished in the living world, and that this limits them to casting only the 4th-level version of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}. Even if they know this limitation or have learned that the flame has been taken to Karahai, the transition from Willowshore’s mindscape to the living world has one more surprise in store. Kugaptee’s influence remains strong, and he fights against the reversal of the PCs’ deaths by plunging them into another, much smaller, mindscape in an attempt to kill them before they can proceed.</p>"
            },
            "Event 16. One Kind Favor": {
              "name": "事件16：一个善意的帮忙 Event 16. One Kind Favor",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件16：一次善意的帮忙</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这个事件可以在你希望的任何时候发生，但在你决定让它发生的前几天或几周里，关于又一次闹鬼的流言会传播开来。当你准备开始这个事件时，镇上的长者会找到PC们，请他们去调查这些传闻。</p>\n<p>据传闻所说，一个黑发白眼的幽魂出现在当地的一处墓地里，夜间她会一动不动、默不作声地站着，直到黎明时分才消失。尽管一些保守的村民很快就断言这个幽魂肯定是罪有应得才会不得安宁（尽管他们对她遭遇的具体情况一无所知），但就连他们也不希望这个幽魂在镇子周围徘徊。</p>\n<p>如果PC们在天黑后进行调查，他们会如传闻所述在墓地里发现那道身影。这个魂魄会无视PC们，除非他们问她想要什么——此时她会沉默地示意他们跟随，并滑入林中。如果PC们试图攻击这个幽魂，她只会消失不见，第二天夜里又在墓碑间出现，毫发无伤。</p>\n<p><strong>幽魂的旅程：</strong>跟随幽魂需要PC们在夜间穿行森林。幽魂不沿着林间小道行走，也不会被岩石或树枝减缓脚步，反而选了一条格外艰难的路线，而PC们也能看出这条路线异常迂回。幽魂以毫不动摇的笃定前进，偶尔对自己点点头，仿佛在默数步数，但她选择的道路几乎毫无道理可言。每当她的路线靠近河流，她总会沿着水边漂浮前行。</p>\n<p>为了跟上幽魂，一名PC必须进行一次@Check[survival|dc:22]或一次@Check[perception|dc:25]检定。队伍中的其他PC可以协助该检定。成功时，队伍尽管被她绕来绕去，仍设法与她保持同样的速度。失败时，每名PC都必须强行军才能跟上，并在幽魂最终抵达目的地时变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}。</p>\n<p>旅程开始约三小时后，幽魂来到一条干涸的河床。她带PC们到那里，然后指向岸边一处满是砂砾的地块。如果PC们有合适的工具，他们可以在此挖掘——如果没有，他们可能得徒手挖，或重复这趟旅程并带着铁锹回来。使用合适工具挖掘需要两次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:21]检定或一次大成功。徒手挖掘则将DC提高到@Check[athletics|dc:25]。大失败会导致正在挖掘的PC变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{疲乏}。在泥土下约3英尺处，是裹在粗麻布尸衣中的人类骸骨。</p>\n<p>一旦PC们取回骸骨，幽魂会带他们返回她最初所在的墓地，这次她走的是直路（旅程仅需30分钟）。回到起点后，她再次指向自己最初站立处的泥土，显然期待PC们将骸骨重新安葬在那里。如果PC们不埋葬骸骨，幽魂便会开始亲自跟随他们：出现在他们的镜子里，站在他们床边俯视他们睡觉，并在随机时刻出现分散他们的注意力。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/forgotten-spirit.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">一次善意的帮忙</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.zuDhmclOm1uM89af]{被遗忘的魂魄} @UUID[Actor.gjs9pmhe7TabalI9]{亡怨（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>在旅程之后，PC们可以在任何时候攻击幽魂；如果他们这么做，她会反击直到被摧毁，但在[[/r 2d4]]天后会复苏，再次出现在墓地里（若PC们移动了她的骸骨，则会出现在骸骨附近）。只有最终将她的骸骨埋葬在她所指示的位置，这个无名幽魂才能获得安宁。</p>\n  <p>不过，埋葬骸骨并不是一件简单的事，因为幽魂所选择的地点已经是四名死去多年的罪犯的坟墓——正是他们当初杀害了她，并将她的遗骸沉入河中。这四名罪犯会从坟中爬出攻击PC们，断断续续地喘着气说出诸如“不是我们”、“我们没杀她”、“那是个意外！”之类的话。这些借口很快就会变成威胁，比如“你也一样会死！”或“杀你同样容易！”这些亡怨会同时攻击幽魂和PC们，但如果幽魂被摧毁，他们不死的复仇也不会解除，因为她不得安宁的魂魄几天后就会回来。在这种情况下，一名PC（最好是看起来最能共情或最支持幽魂困境的那位）会成为亡怨憎恨的目标，他们会排除队伍中其他所有人，专门攻击那名PC。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>如果PC们击败亡怨，幽魂会跪倒在地，因挫败而啜泣。她的哭泣只有在PC们埋葬她的骸骨后才会停止；随后她如释重负地叹息，并优雅地向PC们鞠躬。她生前是谁、为何被谋杀，是个谜团——你可以让PC们最终解开它，也可以干脆让它永远成为谜。</p>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们埋葬了幽魂的骸骨，给予他们XP，视同他们在战斗中击败了她。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 16: One Kind Favor</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This event can take place whenever you wish, but in the days or weeks before you decide it will be taking place, rumors of another haunting spread. When you’re ready to begin this event, the town elder seeks the PCs out to ask them to investigate these rumors.</p>\n<p>According to hearsay, a ghost with black hair and white eyes has appeared in a local cemetery, standing completely still and silent during the night until she vanishes with the dawn. While certain conservative villagers are quick to proclaim the ghost must deserve her restless death (despite knowing nothing about the circumstances of the ghost’s situation), even they don’t want the ghost hanging around the town.</p>\n<p>Should the PCs investigate after dark, they find the figure haunting the cemetery as described. The spirit ignores the PCs unless they ask her what she wants, at which point she silently beckons them to follow her and glides off into the woods. If the PCs try to attack the ghost, she simply vanishes, appearing unharmed amid the gravestones the next night.</p>\n<p><strong>The Ghost’s Journey:</strong> Following the ghost requires the PCs to work their way through the forest during the night. The ghost does not stick to forest paths and is not slowed by rocks or branches, taking a particularly onerous route, and the PCs can tell that the route is unusually circuitous. The ghost moves with unerring certainty, occasionally nodding to herself as if silently counting the steps, but the path she chooses seems to make little sense. Whenever her path comes near a river, she always floats along the water’s edge.</p>\n<p>In order to keep up with the ghost, one PC must attempt a @Check[survival|dc:22] or a @Check[perception|dc:25] check. Other PCs in the group can Aid this check. On a success, the party manages to maintain pace with her despite her meandering. On a failure, each of the PCs must hustle to keep up and becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} by the time the ghost finally reaches her destination.</p>\n<p>About three hours after the journey begins, the ghost reaches a dry riverbed. The ghost leads the PCs to it, then points to a gravelly patch on the shore. If the PCs have the proper tools, they can dig here—if not, they may have to dig by hand or repeat this journey and return with shovels. Digging with the proper tools requires two successful @Check[athletics|dc:21] checks or one critical success. Digging by hand increases the DC to @Check[athletics|dc:25]. A critical failure results in the PCs who are digging becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued}. About 3 feet beneath the earth are human bones wrapped in a burlap shroud.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs have retrieved the bones, the ghost leads them back to the cemetery she started at, this time taking a direct route (a journey that takes only 30 minutes). When she returns to where she started, she points again at the dirt where she was originally standing, clearly expecting the PCs to rebury the bones there. If the PCs do not bury the bones, the ghost begins to follow them personally, appearing in their mirrors, standing over their beds and watching them while they sleep, and appearing to distract them at random moments.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/forgotten-spirit.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">One Kind Favor</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.zuDhmclOm1uM89af]{Forgotten Spirit} @UUID[Actor.gjs9pmhe7TabalI9]{Revenants (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The PCs can attack the ghost at any time after the journey; if they do so, she fights back until destroyed, only to rejuvenate [[/r 2d4]] days later to once again appear in the cemetery (or near her bones, if the PCs have moved them). Only by finally burying her bones where she’s indicated will the nameless ghost find peace.</p>\n  <p>Burying the bones isn’t a simple task, though, for the site the ghost has chosen already serves as the graves for four long-dead criminals—the ones responsible for killing her in the first place and sinking her remains in the river. These four criminals dig up out of their graves to attack the PCs, gasping out phrases like, “It wasn’t us,” “We didn’t kill her,” or “It was an accident!” These excuses swiftly give way to threats like, “You’ll die just as well!” or “Killing you is just as easy!” The revenants attack the ghost and the PCs alike, but if the ghost is destroyed, their undying vendetta doesn’t release them, for her unquiet spirit simply returns in a few days. In this case, one of the PCs (preferably the one who seems to have been the most empathetic or supportive of the ghost’s plight) becomes the target of the revenants’ hatred, and they attack that PC to the exclusion of all others in the party.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>If the PCs defeat the revenants, the ghost drops to her knees and sobs in frustration. Her sobs end only when the PCs bury her bones, at which point she sighs in relief and gives the PCs a graceful bow. Who she was in life and why she was murdered is a mystery that you can allow the PCs to eventually solve—or you can simply let it remain a mystery.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs bury the ghost’s bones, grant them XP as if they’d defeated her in combat.</p>"
            },
            "Event 15. Reprisal": {
              "name": "事件15：报复 Event 15. Reprisal",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件15：报复</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>苦迦菩提也许再次被囚禁，但他的影响依旧强大。玩家角色能感受到他存在的一种方式，是一头巨大的掠食者显现出来——它直接由那死去的邪魔的思绪塑成，并被派去追踪玩家角色，为他们在上一幕中的动作实施复仇。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/titan-centipede.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">报复</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.lYUvYbH8m1Y6ulg2]{苦迦菩提的蜈蚣}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>该遭遇可以发生在玩家角色穿越荒野腹地时，也可以从这生物自更深的林中缓缓爬入小镇边缘地带时开始。一条几乎有一百英尺长的亮橙色蜈蚣从矮丛环境中爬出，盘绕起身体并发动攻击——目标要么是玩家角色，要么是镇子边缘的建筑物。和玩家角色在这场战役中最初遭遇的那些蜈蚣一样，这头庞然大物一边战斗一边咆哮着吐出词语：“肉……血肉……骨头……手指……头发……皮肤……眼睛……”当它发现玩家角色时，它的词语改变了，并用它那沉重的嗓音轰然喊出几句完整的话。“你们必须付出代价！苦迦菩提将会崛起！该死了！”</p>\n  <p>如果你让苦迦菩提的蜈蚣去攻击小镇，而不是在玩家角色身处荒野时攻击他们，那么这头巨型生物会毫不偏差地疾行向玩家角色当前所在之处。若队伍立刻行动迎战，他们应当能在怪物造成太多伤害之前赶到，但如果他们拖得太久（或被迫逃离），蜈蚣的动作足以对柳岸镇造成伤害，使其安全点减少[[/r 1d4]]。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 15: Reprisal</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Kugaptee may be imprisoned once more, but his influence remains strong. One way his presence can be felt is through the manifestation of an enormous predator, formed directly from the dead fiend’s thoughts and sent to track down the PCs to enact revenge for their actions in the previous act.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/titan-centipede.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Reprisal</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.lYUvYbH8m1Y6ulg2]{Kugaptee's Centipede}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creature:</strong> This encounter can take place while the PCs are traveling through the hinterlands, or it could begin as the creature trundles into the town’s outskirts from deeper in the woods. A bright orange centipede that’s nearly a hundred feet long crawls out of the undergrowth to coil upon itself and attack—either PCs or buildings at the edge of town. As with the very first centipedes the PCs encountered in this campaign, this behemoth roars words out as it fights: “Meat... flesh... bones... fingers... hair... skin... eyes...” When it spots the PCs, its words change, and in its lumbering voice, it thunders out a few complete sentences. “You must pay! Kugaptee will rise! Time to die!”</p>\n  <p>If you have Kugaptee’s Centipede attack town rather than attack the PCs while they’re out in the wilderness, the massive creature scuttles unerringly toward wherever the PCs are currently located. If the party acts immediately to meet the challenge, they should be able to reach the monster before it does too much damage, but if they take too long (or if they’re forced to flee), the centipede’s actions can inflict enough damage to Willowshore that its Security Points are reduced by [[/r 1d4]].</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Event 14. The Trees Live": {
              "name": "事件14：树木活着 Event 14. The Trees Live",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件14：树木苏生</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这可以发生在任意时点，只要PC们正在柳岸镇周边的森林里四处游荡。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>柳岸镇伐木工人的遗产，留存的不仅仅是镇内的被遗弃的庄园和磨坊。大自然与森林的魂魄记性很长，并非所有都能轻易被供品与仪式安抚。柳岸镇的某些森林守护者憎恨村民，因其曾对荒野造成的伤害；而在纯粹的坏运气使然下，PC们闯入了它们盘踞的一片灌木丛。或者，也可能有一名NPC失踪，PC们受召去追踪并找到对方——沿着该NPC的小路前进，同样会来到这片灌木丛。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/arboreal-reaper.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">树木苏生</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.dAGayypNZzq40ghO]{Arboreal Reapers (2)} @UUID[Actor.YGHerllkN24395fJ]{Awakened Tree}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>这片怒意的灌木丛具现为一对树木收割者与一棵觉醒树。当PC们遭遇这些树木生物时，愤怒的植物并不会立刻攻击——它们会要求PC们就这些年来柳岸镇的人民对林地造成的一切痛苦与伤害给出交代。树木生物的初始态度为不友善，但若能让它们变得不关心，它们就会放PC们离开而不必战斗。若它们绑走了一名NPC，则只有在PC们能让它们至少变得友善时，才会释放受害者。任何试图调整树木生物态度的失败尝试，都会自动使它们转为敌对并发动攻击；一旦战斗开始，它们会死战到底。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们达成和平解决方式，给予他们经验值，视同他们在战斗中击败了这些生物。更重要的是，树木生物对PC们印象深刻；一周后，一批来自自然寿终的树木之枯木会出现在镇子边缘，并被整齐码放。这份优质木材的赋礼为小镇提供了意外资源，用以修复风暴造成的破坏，并使PC们获得2点安全点。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 14: The Trees Live</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This can take place at any point while the PCs are out wandering in the forest surrounding Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The legacy of Willowshore’s lumber harvesters lives on in more than the abandoned estates and mills within the town. The spirits of nature and the forest have long memories, and not all are easily placated by offerings and rituals. Some of Willowshore’s forest guardians despise the villagers for the damage they once did to the wilds and, by a sheer stroke of bad luck, the PCs wander into a thicket of them. Alternatively, an NPC could go missing and the PCs are called upon to track them down—following the NPC’s trail leads to this same thicket.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/arboreal-reaper.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Trees Live</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.dAGayypNZzq40ghO]{Arboreal Reapers (2)} @UUID[Actor.YGHerllkN24395fJ]{Awakened Tree}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>This thicket of anger manifests as a pair of arboreal reapers and an awakened tree. When the PCs encounter the arboreals, the angry plants don’t immediately attack—they instead demand an accounting for all the pain and damage done to the woodlands by the people of Willowshore over the years. The arboreals’ initial attitude is unfriendly, but if they can be made indifferent, they let the PCs go without a fight. If they abducted an NPC, they’ll only release their victim if the PCs can make them at least friendly. Any failed attempt to adjust the arboreals’ attitude automatically shifts them to hostile and causes them to attack; once a fight begins, they battle to the death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs achieve a peaceful solution, grant them XP as if they’d defeated the creatures in combat. More importantly, the arboreals are impressed by the PCs, and one week later, a delivery of deadwood from trees that have come to a natural end of life appears at the edge of town, neatly stacked. This gift of fine wood provides the town with unexpected resources to repair storm damage and grants the PCs 2 Security Points.</p>"
            },
            "Other Winter Events": {
              "name": "其他冬季事件 Other Winter Events",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Other Winter Events\">其他冬季事件</h1>\n<p>你可能会发现，在冬季期间，当PC们正等待机会继续前往下一步时，有些时刻需要一些额外的刺激或获得XP的机会。在这些情况下，你可以使用以下事件之一来让冬天更有生气。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Other Winter Events\">Other Winter Events</h1>\n<p>You might find moments during winter while the PCs are waiting for the chance to move on to the next step could use some additional excitement or XP opportunities. In these cases, you can use one of the following events to liven up the winter.</p>"
            },
            "Parting Ways": {
              "name": "分道扬镳 Parting Ways",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Parting Ways\">分道扬镳</h3>\n<p>当影响遭遇在第 6 轮后结束时，若 PC 未能累积至少 6 点影响点，任美璃会因自己受到的糟糕对待而勃然大怒并发动攻击。同样地，若 PC 在任何时候对她发作（例如当她对其中一人施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KSAEhNfZyXMO7Z7V]{流放诅咒} 或 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KHnhPHL4x1AQHfbC]{读心术} 这类法术时，PC 反而出手攻击），她也会攻击。</p>\n<p>若 PC 拥有 7 到 12 点影响点，美璃会试图“收走”任何入了她眼的俊美男子，以及她在 PC 中曾赠予项圈的任何人。每名潜在受害者都可以尝试一次 @Check[deception|dc:28] 或 @Check[diplomacy|dc:28] 检定来劝她打消念头。若失败，她会坚持在离开时把他们一并带走。若他们仍然拒绝，她会先尝试用魔法魅惑他们，若失败则诉诸暴力。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-mei-li-ren.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">分道扬镳</span> <span class=\"keepme\">极限 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.lKgG84Maepjro99O]{任美璃}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>若爆发战斗，与 13 级生物交战对 8 级 PC 来说甚至超过一次极限遭遇。由于该事件很可能发生在 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第 10 章}完成之后，PC 或许已经是 9 级，甚至可能达到 10 级，但即便如此，与 13 级生物的战斗仍然十分危险。战斗中，任美璃会在第一回合施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.4YnON9JHYqtLzccu]{召唤动物} 召来一只 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-monster-core.Actor.4ISm82EYQeOndynw]{巨型狼蛛}，随后攀上天花板，并运用 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.qwlh6aDgi86U3Q7H]{暗示术} 与网缚来分隔 PC。之后她会尝试让那些特别冒犯过她或引起她注意的 PC 失去行动能力并将其俘获。对后者，她会让自己的打击承受 –2 环境减值，以造成非致命伤害。若她的生命值降至 45 或更少，她会试图逃回自己的肩舆，然后逃离城镇。若被杀死，她会翻倒在地，蜘蛛腿向内蜷缩，呈现出怪诞的一幕，随后彻底消散，她那由思维构成的躯体化作蒸汽。同样地，若其女主人被击败，她的四名思维体人类仆从也会消散。若她尚未将其赠出，PC 可以回收她的信使戒指与尸体活化之尘，但那只硬木箱（见下文宝藏）却遍寻不着。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>若 PC 在遭遇结束时拥有超过 12 点影响点，这名络新妇会暗自对整个过程感到满意，并不会要求任何 PC 跟她回去，尽管她会暗示：等到春末最后一天缴纳什一税之时，她打算带他们中的部分或全部前往她的宫殿。她不再多言，回到自己的肩舆，仆从将她抬到镇子边缘，在那里他们全都化作虚无消散。当然，此时被她带走的任何 PC 也都已获得自由，可以不受任何后果地回归自己的生活。</p>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.4XeiNtVFiMN4bZqt]{硬木箱} <br />\n  若 PC 累积至少 12 点影响点，当队伍在镇子边缘消散时，会留下一只硬木箱。箱内有六颗月光石（每颗价值 25 gp）、一件<em>强效人格面具</em>与一件<em>荒寂坠盒</em>。此外，她那四名幻影仆从所佩戴的四个银项圈也会被留在原地。若 PC 不在场目睹她离去，有村民会偶然发现这批宝藏，并在几天后将其送交 PC。\n</p>\n<p>这些宝藏，以及任夫人在影响遭遇期间给出的任何奖励（包括她要求某位 PC 佩戴的任何银项圈），都会在遭遇结束后继续存在，尽管络新妇本人不过是由思维空间所显现的思维体。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若任夫人未战而离开城镇，给予 PC 160 XP 与 [[/r 1d4]] 希望点。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Parting Ways\">Parting Ways</h3>\n<p>When the influence encounter ends after round 6, if the PCs failed to accrue at least 6 Influence Points, Ren Mei Li is enraged by the poor treatment she has received and attacks. Likewise, she attacks if at any time the PCs lash out at her (such as if they attack when she casts a spell like @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KSAEhNfZyXMO7Z7V]{Outcast's Curse} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KHnhPHL4x1AQHfbC]{Mind Reading} on one of them).</p>\n<p>If the PCs have 7 to 12 Influence Points, Mei Li attempts to “collect” any pretty men that caught her eye and anyone to whom she gave a collar among the PCs. Each potential victim can attempt a @Check[deception|dc:28] or @Check[diplomacy|dc:28] check to dissuade her of her intentions. Should they fail, she insists on taking them with her when she leaves. Should they still decline, she’ll first attempt to magically charm them, then resort to violence if that fails.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-mei-li-ren.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Parting Ways</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Extreme 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.lKgG84Maepjro99O]{Ren Mei Li}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If combat breaks out, a fight against a level 13 creature is beyond an extreme encounter for 8th-level PCs. Since this event likely plays out after @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10} is completed, the PCs may already be 9th level, or perhaps even 10th level, but even then, such a fight against a level 13 creature is dangerous. During combat, Ren Mei Li spends her first turn casting @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.4YnON9JHYqtLzccu]{Summon Animal} to call up a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-monster-core.Actor.4ISm82EYQeOndynw]{Giant Tarantula}, then climbs to the ceiling and uses @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.qwlh6aDgi86U3Q7H]{Suggestion} and web trap to separate the PCs. She then attempts to incapacitate and capture any PCs that either particularly offended her or drew her eye. Against the latter, she’ll take a –2 circumstance penalty with her strikes to deal nonlethal damage. If reduced to 45 or fewer Hit Points, she attempts to flee back to her palanquin and then out of town. If slain, she rolls onto her back and her spider legs curl inward in a grotesque display before fading away entirely, her thoughtform body vaporizing. Likewise, her four thoughtform human servants fade away if their mistress is defeated. The PCs can recover her messenger’s ring and the dust of corpse animation if she hasn’t already gifted them, but the hardwood chest (see Treasure, below) is nowhere to be found.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>If the PCs have more than 12 Influence Points at the end of the encounter, the jorogumo is secretly pleased with the proceedings and doesn’t demand that any of the PCs return with her, although she hints that, come time to tithe on the last day of spring, she intends to take some or all of them with her to her palace. Without another word, she returns to her palanquin and her servants carry her to the edge of town, where all of them fade away into nothingness. Any PCs she has taken with her at this point, of course, are now free to return to their lives without repercussion.</p>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.4XeiNtVFiMN4bZqt]{Hardwood Chest} <br />\n  If the PCs accrued at least 12 Influence Points, a hardwood chest is left behind when the procession fades away at the edge of town. The chest contains six moonstones worth 25 gp each, a <em>greater persona mask</em>, and a <em>desolation locket</em>. Additionally, the four silver collars worn by her phantasmal servants remain behind. If the PCs aren’t there to witness her exit, a villager happens across the treasure and brings it to the PCs in a few days.\n</p>\n<p>This treasure, along with any rewards Lady Ren gave out during the influence encounter (including any silver collars she demanded a PC wear), persist after the encounter is over, even though the jorogumo herself was merely a thoughtform manifested by the mindscape.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If Lady Ren leaves town without a fight, grant the PCs 160 XP and [[/r 1d4]] Hope Points.</p>"
            },
            "Influence Rounds": {
              "name": "影响轮 Influence Rounds",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Influence Rounds\">影响轮</h3>\n<p>本次遭遇的6轮流程如下。</p>\n<p><strong>第1轮（1分钟）</strong>本轮从任美璃到场并向队伍致意开始。她希望对方呈上礼物；若PC没有立刻献上，她会要求他们这么做。价值至少50gp的礼物符合她的标准，并立刻使PC获得1点影响点。价值低于此数（或根本没送礼）的礼物也会被接受，但她会虚情假意地评论：对如此低贱的小镇来说，这样的供奉完全可以接受。不过，把公主的最初标准定得太高也有风险：若礼物价值超过100gp，PC获得2点影响点，但第2轮期间所有影响检定的DC提高1。</p>\n<p>本轮只需一分钟，因此本轮可以进行发现检定，但不能进行影响检定。</p>\n<p><strong>第2轮（30分钟）</strong>寒暄之后，任夫人要求有人陪同她穿行小镇，好让她观览景致。她由仆人抬着坐在肩舆里；这些仆人脖子上都戴着银项圈——和先前抵达的信使一样，这些仆人（以及他们的银项圈）并非真正的活体生物，而只是任夫人心灵的沉默延伸。络新妇公主没有携带武器，且显然认为自己不可能遭到袭击；不过即便没有盟友，任夫人仍旧极度危险。</p>\n<p>任夫人在走访区域时会审视镇民。她要求所有村民都在她面前弯腰以示身份卑下，即便（或尤其是）他们因年老或其他身体限制而难以弯下身。她甚至会愉快地伸出一条蜘蛛腿，强迫某人低头。</p>\n<p>一路上，她会对小镇评头论足。她那些尖刻的评论不过是对人的含沙射影——除非柳岸镇的安全点少于6点；若是如此，她就会公开嘲讽受损的建筑、动物粪便或杂乱未修的道路（导致失去1点希望点）。</p>\n<p><strong>第3轮（10分钟）</strong>无论PC选择在哪里接待她，任夫人都会跟随前往，但不管是什么选择她都会公开质疑：若PC带她去茶馆，她会问为何不去总督府邸；若带她去总督府邸，她又会评论茶馆看起来要诱人得多。若她被允许入座却未先奉上一杯热茶，这名络新妇就会评论这是种怠慢，并质疑他们是否就是这样对待尊贵宾客的。这是任夫人的一套伎俩——在门口奉上热饮是非常古老的礼仪，在帝国龙华时期逐渐失宠。成功的@Check[society|dc:24]或@Check[tea-lore|dc:22]检定能让某位PC知晓这一事实，但如果有人告诉任夫人她错了或过时了，她会略感冒犯。</p>\n<p><strong>第4轮（30分钟）</strong>若有人奉上葡萄酒或其他酒精，任夫人一概拒绝，转而要求茶。在准备茶水期间，她会询问茶壶与茶杯的来历，显然期待听到一段分量十足的回答，但若没人答得出来，她也不会当场发作。</p>\n<p>茶端上来后，任夫人会再施一计，质问为什么上茶的侍者没有跪着侍奉。成功的@Check[society|dc:24]或@Check[tea-lore|dc:22]检定能让某位PC知道：这种礼仪在技术上确实正确，但只在婚礼上才会这么做。与之前一样，如果有人告诉她不对，她会略感冒犯。</p>\n<p>本轮中，某位PC可以用一次成功的@Check[crafting|dc:24]或@Check[tea-lore|dc:24]检定来影响任夫人。这不计入他们本轮的行动。若他们放弃此检定或检定失败，络新妇会假装被茶烫到嘴唇，把茶泼到地上，并指控PC故意把茶泡得太烫。PC必须成功进行一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:28]检定来把事情圆过去，或做出一副允许惩罚泡茶者的样子——若两者皆未做到，将失去2点影响点。@Check[deception|dc:28]检定可以伪造惩罚；否则，任夫人会给上茶的侍者一只银项圈，要求对方戴上。</p>\n<p><strong>第5轮（30分钟）</strong>品用为她准备的茶与食物时，若英雄们表现得太好，任夫人反而会不悦。若PC进入本轮时，任夫人仍未能折磨或惩罚至少一人，则之后所有影响检定的DC提高1（与其他任何DC提高效果累积）。</p>\n<p><strong>第6轮（1小时）</strong>任夫人询问餐后是否能期待一些娱乐节目。每位PC都可以立刻尝试一次免费的影响检定，使用表演、用杂技进行翻滚、用运动展示力量壮举，或任何他们能自圆其说、足以满足这类挑剔观众标准的其他技能。若大成功，任夫人会高兴到要求表演者在今年晚些时候去她家拜访，并赠予他们一只银项圈。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Influence Rounds\">Influence Rounds</h3>\n<p>The six rounds of this encounter play out as follows.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 (1 minute)</strong> This round plays out as Ren Mei Li arrives and greets the party. She expects to be presented with a gift, demanding one if the PCs don’t offer it immediately. A gift worth at least 50 gp meets her standards and immediately grants the PCs 1 Influence Point. A gift worth less than that (or no gift at all) is accepted with an insincere comment that such an offering is perfectly acceptable for such a lowborn town. There’s a risk to setting the princess’s initial standards too high, however. If the gift is worth more than 100 gp, the PCs gain 2 Influence Points, but the DCs of all Influence checks during round 2 increase by 1.</p>\n<p>This round takes only a minute to play out, and as a result, Discovery checks can be attempted during this round but Influence checks can’t.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 (30 minutes)</strong> After the greetings, Lady Ren asks to be escorted through town so she can take in the sights. She’s carried in a palanquin by servants who wear silver collars around their necks—like the messenger who arrived earlier, these servants (and their silver collars) aren’t actual living creatures but merely silent extensions of Lady Ren’s psyche. The jorogumo princess is unarmed and clearly considers it inconceivable that she might be attacked, though even without allies, Lady Ren is still extremely dangerous.</p>\n<p>Lady Ren takes stock of the townsfolk as she travels through the area. She expects all of the villagers to stoop before her in order to indicate their lower status, even (or especially) if they can’t easily bend due to age or other physical limitations. She’s quite happy to reach out a spider leg and force someone to bow.</p>\n<p>As they go, she comments on the town. Her snarky remarks are thinly veiled insults—unless Willowshore has fewer than 6 Security Points, in which case she openly mocks the damaged buildings, animal excrement, or unkempt roads (resulting in a loss of 1 Hope Point).</p>\n<p><strong>Round 3 (10 minutes)</strong> Lady Ren follows the PCs to the location they’ve chosen to receive her, though she openly questions their decision, no matter what it is: if the PCs take her to the tea house, she asks why they don’t go to the governor’s manor, while if brought to the governor’s manor, she comments that the tea house looked far more inviting. If allowed to be seated without first being given a cup of hot tea, the jorogumo comments on the slight and wonders if this is how they treat their honored guests. This is a ploy on Lady Ren’s part—offering a hot drink at the door is a very old piece of etiquette that fell out of favor during Imperial Lung Wa. With a successful @Check[society|dc:24] or @Check[tea-lore|dc:22] check, a PC is aware of this fact, but Lady Ren takes slight offense at being told she’s incorrect or outdated.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 4 (30 minutes)</strong> Lady Ren refuses wine or any other alcohol if offered, instead requesting tea. She asks about the history of the tea pot and cup while the tea is prepared, clearly expecting a significant answer but not acting out if one isn’t provided.</p>\n<p>When served tea, Lady Ren attempts another ploy, asking why her servers didn’t kneel to serve her. With a successful @Check[society|dc:24] or @Check[tea-lore|dc:22] check, a PC knows that while this is technically correct etiquette, it’s only done for weddings. As before, she takes slight offense at being told she’s incorrect.</p>\n<p>For this round, one PC can attempt to Influence Lady Ren with a successful @Check[crafting|dc:24] or @Check[tea-lore|dc:24] check. This doesn’t count as their action for the round. If they forgo this check or fail, the jorogumo pretends to burn her lips on the tea and throws it to the ground before accusing the PCs of making the tea too hot on purpose. The PCs must either succeed at a @Check[diplomacy|dc:28] check to smooth the incident over or make a show of allowing the tea preparer to be punished—failure to do either results in a loss of 2 Influence Points. A @Check[deception|dc:28] check can fake the punishment; otherwise, Lady Ren offers a silver collar to the tea server, demanding they put it on.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 5 (30 minutes)</strong> While enjoying the tea and food prepared for her, Lady Ren grows cross if the heroes perform too well. If the PCs reach this round and Lady Ren hasn’t managed to torment or punish at least one person, the DCs of all further Influence checks are raised by 1 (cumulative with any other DC increases).</p>\n<p><strong>Round 6 (1 hour)</strong> Lady Ren asks if she can expect any post-meal entertainment. Each PC can immediately attempt a free Influence check using Performance, Acrobatics to tumble, Athletics to display a feat of strength, or any other skill they can justify to meet the standards of such a fussy audience. On a critical success, Lady Ren is so pleased she demands the performer visit her at her home later in the year, and she gives them a silver collar.</p>"
            },
            "Influencing Ren Mei Li": {
              "name": "影响任美璃 Influencing Ren Mei Li",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Influencing Ren Mei Li\">影响任梅丽</h3>\n\n<p>任梅丽到来时不带任何护卫，以此展示她的自信与优越；她认为带护卫会显得软弱又缺乏自信。她以真身傲然现身，并要求PC们在带她去他们决定举办会面的地点之前先带她四处逛逛；镇上的长老陪同他们，但在这次事件中几乎无事可做也无话可说，因为他很清楚这件事只有PC们才能处理。</p>\n<p>这场影响遭遇在6个回合中展开，每个回合都包含可能让事情更复杂的额外要素；6个回合的列表从@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11influencerou00]{这里}开始。</p>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>任梅丽</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mei-li-rin.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ren Mei Li\" alt=\"a spider-human woman hybrid creature\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mei-li-rin.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">令人生畏的络新妇公主</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>意志</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[jorogumo-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[society|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:26|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响技能</strong> @Check[performance|dc:22|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[diplomacy|dc:24|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[occultism|dc:26|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:28|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:30|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响 4</strong> 任夫人因PC们太有影响力、把她的游戏搅黄而恼火。每名PC都应尝试一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:24]。若没有任何PC在此检定中成功，她会对随机一名PC施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KSAEhNfZyXMO7Z7V]{流放诅咒}（@Check[will|dc:34]豁免）。若PC们发动攻击，见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11partingways000]{分道扬镳}。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响 8</strong> 任夫人解释，如今络新妇掌权后柳岸镇将如何改变。首先，她要求向络新妇缴纳什一税，每年在每个春末的鬼季仪式期间支付；这一条款不容讨价还价。其次，她要求所有居住在村中或进入村中的天狗立刻处决。第三，她宣布所有镇民不得再读写，所有书籍都必须交给络新妇保管。最后，村里所有钱币与桃木都必须销毁，以免金钱的诱惑腐化凡人的心。她“仁慈”地允许小镇在春季最后一天、第一笔什一税到期之前，满足上述所有需求。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">由于任夫人是思维空间的复制体，而思维空间会在每年春末重演，最简单的做法就是全心全意地附和她，然后在她离开后无视她的法令——这会取悦她，此后针对她进行的所有影响检定获得+1状态加值。若他们愿意，PC们也可以尝试谈判。她愿意谈判，但唯一的例外是向络新妇缴纳什一税——没有这份供奉，任夫人就无法承诺让他们免于她同族的危害。若PC们选择谈判，此时梅丽同意从PC们选择的三条“非什一税”条款中撤销一条。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>影响 12</strong> @UUID[Actor.9aNWoy10kwDSkvoB]{任夫人的戒指} <br />\n    任夫人询问关于谭杉树的事。PC们可以推说不知而不承担任何风险或损失，因为任夫人并不指望乡下人知道任何有用信息。PC们也可以用真相满足她的好奇，或用谎言取悦她（不同于其他情况，她的惩罚在这里不适用）。从任夫人的举止不难看出，她对这棵树以及它可能关联的事物抱有阴险的兴趣。若PC们告诉她真相，她会明确表示希望这棵树受到保护，并赠予PC们一枚信使戒指，以便出现任何问题时联络。\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">若PC们在影响 8时选择谈判，任梅丽同意再撤销她所要求的三条“非什一税”条款中的第二条。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>影响 16</strong> @UUID[Actor.WI67Nu8en7gpWs8R]{任夫人的尘} <br />\n    尽管难以置信，PC们说服了任梅丽，使她相信她自身的存在同样岌岌可危，不亚于PC们。违背她的天性，她交给他们一只袋子，里面装有四剂<em>尸体活化之尘</em>\n    ，以协助保护小镇。\n  </p>\n  <p>若PC们在影响 8时选择谈判，任梅丽同意撤销她所要求的三条“非什一税”条款中的第三条。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>抗力</strong> 任梅丽憎恶桃木与天狗。任何一方的明显存在都会冒犯她；她要求焚烧桃木物品，并立刻处决任何天狗（例如Myna Kawaka或Matsu）。任何天狗，或明显持有桃木物品者，使影响她的所有DC增加2。好在任夫人并不要求亲眼见证这些行为，因此做出逮捕天狗或把冒犯她的物品拖走的样子就足以安抚她。若PC们拒绝，此后所有针对她的影响检定DC增加2。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">她也嫉妒迷人而漂亮的女性。由这类PC执行的影响尝试使DC增加2。若某PC成功进行一次Deception检定，以对抗她的察觉DC来伪装自己，则可以抵消此阻碍；自愿在自己脸上留下疤痕也同样可以。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>弱点</strong> 由富有魅力、外貌出众的男性进行的影响尝试使DC减少2。然而，若这类男性在影响她时出现大成功或大失败中的大失败，任夫人会宣布他将在她离开时随她同行，然后给他一只银项圈戴上（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11partingways000]{分道扬镳}）。</p>\n  <p>任夫人对镇上蜘蛛守护者的蛛形外表很是欣喜，尽管她尽力不表露出来。与“丑萌”相关的对话使影响她的DC减少2。然而，若告诉任夫人那只蜘蛛被称为“丑”，会招致她公开的冷笑，并使此后不再获得该益处。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>背景</strong> 在梅丽无数的姐妹之中，只有五个撑过了她们的第一年。以络新妇的标准而言，这已算是一个大家族。任夫人知道自己不是神门最强大络新妇的对手，但她希望为自己开辟一片安全舒适的领地。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>外貌 </strong> 梅丽仪态优雅，长长的黑发盘成精致发髻，以花朵与发簪点缀。她身穿刺绣长袍，并竭力不让自己类人形态的任何部位沾到尘土。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>个性</strong> 这个古老版本的任夫人梅丽是一头玩弄猎物的怪物。她打算把不幸的农民诱入不可能应对的社交困境，再把惩罚他们当作病态游戏的一部分。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>惩罚</strong> 任夫人对阴司察夕丝绸宫廷中的背叛与权谋并不陌生。每当某位PC未能对她彻底撒谎时（奉承用的善意谎言与更隐晦的欺骗除外），她会立刻对其施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KHnhPHL4x1AQHfbC]{读心术}（@Check[will|dc:34]豁免）。若某PC在此豁免中失败，她便能预判其下一步策略，使该PC下一次影响检定的结果自动降低一个阶段。若大成功或大失败中的大成功，PC会立刻得知关于她的一条信息，如同他们在一次发现检定中成功一般。</p>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 class=\"sidebar\">银项圈</h1>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silvercollar.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Silver Collar\" alt=\"a finely filigreed silver collar\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silvercollar.webp')\" />\n  <p>任夫人的银项圈看起来或许只是虚荣的小饰品，但Shinzo或任何在络新妇学识或柳岸镇学识上达到专家或更高熟练度的PC，都能认出它们远比表面更有价值。属于络新妇的凡人会以银项圈为标记；该项圈可以锁在凡人的颈上，使其无法取下。任夫人原本打算带着她的战利品回家后这么做，但她在离开柳岸镇时停止存在，显然使这一计划落空。在现代的神门，这些项圈备受追捧，因为它们表明佩戴者被允许自由旅行、被允许读写，并可与外人自由贸易。PC们在第4幕回归现实生活时可以佩戴这些项圈，以获得显而易见的社交优势。每个项圈价值50 gp，并可按全价出售。</p>\n</aside>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Influencing Ren Mei Li\">Influencing Ren Mei Li</h3>\n\n<p>Ren Mei Li arrives without any bodyguards as a show of her confidence and superiority, believing that bringing a guard makes her look weak and unconfident. She imperiously arrives in her true form and requests the PCs show her around before taking her to wherever they’ve decided to host the meeting; the town elder accompanies them but has little to do or say during this event, knowing full well that this matter is something only the PCs can handle.</p>\n<p>This influence encounter plays out over the course of 6 rounds, each of which includes additional elements that might complicate things; a list of the 6 rounds starts @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11influencerou00]{Here}.</p>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>Ren Mei Li</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mei-li-rin.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ren Mei Li\" alt=\"a spider-human woman hybrid creature\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-mei-li-rin.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Intimidating jorogumo princess</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Will</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[jorogumo-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[society|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:26|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence Skills</strong> @Check[performance|dc:22|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[diplomacy|dc:24|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[occultism|dc:26|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:28|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:30|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 4</strong> Lady Ren becomes annoyed that the PCs are ruining her game by being so influential. Each PC should attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:24]. If no PC succeeds at this check, she casts @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KSAEhNfZyXMO7Z7V]{Outcast's Curse} (@Check[will|dc:34] save) on a random PC. If the PCs attack, see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11partingways000]{Parting Ways}.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 8</strong> Lady Ren explains how things will change in Willowshore now that jorogumo are in charge. Firstly, she demands tithes to the jorogumo, to be paid every year during the season of ghosts ritual at the end of each spring; this stipulation is nonnegotiable. Secondly, she demands all tengu who live in or enter the village be executed immediately. Thirdly, she declares that all townsfolk are no longer permitted to read or write, and all books must be turned over to the jorogumo for safekeeping. Finally, all coins and peachwood in the village are to be destroyed, so as to avoid the temptation of money corrupting the hearts of mortals. She graciously allows the town until the first tithe is due on the last day of spring to meet these all of these requirements.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">Since Lady Ren is a mindscape duplicate, and since the mindscape repeats every year at the end of spring, the easiest thing is to agree with her wholeheartedly and then ignore her decrees once she leaves—this pleases her, and all future Influence checks against her gain a +1 status bonus. If they wish, the PCs can attempt to negotiate. She’s willing to do so, but the one exception is the tithes to the jorogumo—Lady Ren can’t offer safety from her kin without such an offering. If the PCs choose to negotiate, Mei Li agrees to remove one of the three non-tithe stipulations of the PCs’ choice at this time.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Influence 12</strong> @UUID[Actor.9aNWoy10kwDSkvoB]{Lady Ren's Ring} <br />\n    Lady Ren inquiries about the Tan Sugi. The PCs can plead ignorance without any risk or loss, as Lady Ren doesn’t expect the rural folk to know anything of use. The PCs can also choose to indulge her curiosity with the truth or regale her with falsehoods (unlike other instances, her Penalty doesn’t apply here). It’s obvious from Lady Ren’s behavior that she has a sinister interest in the tree and what it might be associated with. If the PCs tell her the truth, she makes it clear that she wishes the tree to be protected and gives the PCs a messenger’s ring in case any issues arise.\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">If the PCs chose to negotiate at Influence 8, Ren Mei Li agrees to remove a second of the three non-tithe stipulations she demanded.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Influence 16</strong> @UUID[Actor.WI67Nu8en7gpWs8R]{Lady Ren's Dust} <br />\n    Against all odds, the PCs have convinced Lady Ren Mei Li that her own existence is just as much in danger as their own. Against her nature, she gives them a bag containing four doses of <em>dust of corpse animation</em>\n    to help protect the town.\n  </p>\n  <p>If the PCs chose to negotiate at Influence 8, Ren Mei Li agrees to remove the third of the three non-tithe stipulations she demanded.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Resistances</strong> Ren Mei Li hates peachwood and tengu. The obvious presence of either offends her; she demands that peachwood items are burned and any tengu (such as Myna Kawaka or Matsu) be executed immediately. Anyone who is a tengu or in clear possession of a peachwood item increases all DCs to Influence her by 2. Fortunately, Lady Ren doesn’t demand to witness either of these tasks personally, so making a show of arresting a tengu or hauling off the offending item is enough to placate her. If the PCs refuse, all future Influence check DCs against her increase by 2.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"text-indent:2ch\">She’s also jealous of charming and pretty women. Influence attempts performed by such PCs increase the DC by 2. A PC who succeeds at a Deception check to disguise themself against her Perception DC can negate this impediment, as can willingly scarring their own face.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Weaknesses</strong> Influence attempts by charismatic, attractive men decrease the DC by 2. However, on a critical failure made to Influence by such a man, Lady Ren declares he will come with her when she leaves, then gives them a silver collar to wear (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11partingways000]{Parting Ways}).</p>\n  <p>Lady Ren is delighted by the arachnid form of the town’s spider guardian, though she tries her best not to show it. Conversation relating to Ugly Cute reduces the DC to Influence her by 2. However, informing Lady Ren that the spider is known as “ugly” provokes an open sneer and negates the benefit going forward.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Background</strong> Of Mei Li’s countless sisters, she was one of only five to survive their first year. This is considered a large family by jorogumo standards. While Lady Ren knows she isn’t a match for the most powerful jorogumo in Shenmen, she hopes to carve out a secure and comfortable territory for herself.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Appearance </strong> Mei Li is graceful, with long black hair worn up in an elegant style, adorned with flowers and pins. She’s dressed in an embroidered robe and does her best to never let any part of her humanoid body touch dirt.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Personality</strong> This ancient version of Lady Ren Mei Li is a monster toying with her prey. She intends to catch hapless peasants in impossible social situations and then punish them as part of a sick game.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Penalty</strong> Lady Ren is no stranger to the betrayals and the politicking of the silken courts of Yin-Sichasi. Any time a PC fails to outright lie to her (excepting white lies for flattery and more subtle deceptions), she immediately casts @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.KHnhPHL4x1AQHfbC]{Mind Reading} on them (@Check[will|dc:34] save). If a PC fails this save, she can anticipate their next tactic, automatically reducing the result of their next Influence check by one step. On a critical success, the PC immediately learns one piece of information about her as though they’d succeeded at a Discovery check.</p>\n</section>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1 class=\"sidebar\">Silver Collars</h1>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silvercollar.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Silver Collar\" alt=\"a finely filigreed silver collar\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silvercollar.webp')\" />\n  <p>While Lady Ren’s silver collars might seem like little more than vain trinkets, Shinzo or a PC who’s an Expert or better in Jorogumo Lore or Willowshore Lore recognizes them as far more valuable. Mortals who belong to a jorogumo are marked by a silver collar, which can be locked around the mortal’s neck so that it can’t be removed. Lady Ren intended to do so when she returned home with her prizes but was obviously stymied by ceasing to exist when she left Willowshore. These collars are avidly sought in modern Shenmen, for they indicate that the wearer is permitted to travel freely, is allowed to read and write, and can trade freely with outsiders. The PCs can wear these collars to reap the obvious social advantages when they return to life in Act 4. Each collar is worth 50 gp and can be sold for full price.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Preparing for the Visit": {
              "name": "为来访做准备 Preparing for the Visit",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparing for the Visit\">为来访做准备</h3>\n<p>一旦PC得知任美璃夫人即将来访，他们只有大约8小时来为她的到来做好准备。如果他们向柳岸镇的其他人征求建议，胡太婆会明确表示，端上的茶与点心必须无可挑剔且符合时令；但她也警告说，任夫人很可能会提出一些不合理的要求，只为彰显她的权势。老松木建议把公主灌醉；若做不到，就要确保所有迎接她的人都穿得华美，同时把脸弄得朴素些或遮住。PC可以尝试一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]，或用@Check[society|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]来回忆知识；成功时，一名PC会注意到，络新妇蔑视天狗、憎恶桃木、企图确保神门的市民保持孤立与目不识丁，并且往往会吃掉俊美的年轻男子，出于嫉妒而毁伤漂亮的女子。大成功时，PC还知道他们应当在任夫人到来时准备一份至少价值50 gp的礼物。</p>\n<p>本冒险默认PC会把他们已投入资源进行维护的地点——例如青天茶馆——准备好用来接待任夫人。为此，他们必须完成“为皇族做准备”行动。</p>\n<p>PC也可能会对与络新妇这种怪物合作的想法感到愤慨。在这种情况下，他们的NPC盟友会警告他们：不管个人观感如何，络新妇都是一股强大的政治力量，而且看起来注定会变得更强大。在此情况下，最好先搁置分歧，与来访的公主合作；但如果PC拒绝好好配合，那么等到需要@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11partingways000]{分道扬镳}时，将其视为他们未能与任美璃获得任何影响点。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>为皇族做准备</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">一名PC花费8小时准备一处选定地点以接待任夫人。其他PC可以援助此检定，但如果没有任何PC甚至尝试进行准备检定，则将其视为他们在此行动中大失败。该PC必须尝试一次@Check[crafting|dc:24]、@Check[society|dc:24]或@Check[tea-lore|dc:24]检定。若PC选择的地点并未在战役过程中逐步建设完善，则此检定承受–4环境减值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 在本次遭遇期间，PC在所有影响检定上获得+1环境加值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> PC把地点准备妥当，但不得不动用了储备来把一切布置齐全。食物点减少1点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 同成功，但食物点减少[[/r 1d4+1]]点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 同失败，但由于准备得很寒酸，PC在本次遭遇期间进行所有影响检定时承受–2环境减值。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Preparing for the Visit\">Preparing for the Visit</h3>\n<p>Once the PCs learn that Lady Ren Mei Li is coming to visit, they have only about 8 hours to get things ready for her arrival. If they ask others in Willowshore for advice, Granny Hu makes it clear that the tea and snacks served must be both impeccable and seasonally appropriate, but she warns that Lady Ren will probably make a few unreasonable demands just to flex her power. Old Matsuki suggests getting the princess drunk or, failing that, making sure everyone greeting her is beautifully dressed while keeping their faces plain or obscured. The PCs can attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] or to Recall Knowledge with @Check[society|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]; on a success, a PC notes that jorogumo despise tengu, hate peachwood, seek to ensure that the citizens of Shenmen are kept isolated and illiterate, and tend to eat beautiful young men and maim pretty women out of jealousy. On a critical success, the PC also knows they should prepare a gift worth at least 50 gp for Lady Ren when she arrives.</p>\n<p>This adventure assumes the PCs prepare a site they’ve already put resources into maintaining, such as the Cerulean Teahouse, to receive Lady Ren. To do so, they must complete the Prepare for Royalty activity.</p>\n<p>It’s possible that the PCs might take umbrage to the idea of working with a monster like a jorogumo. In this case their NPC allies warn them that regardless of their personal views, the jorogumo are a powerful political force, and it seems like they’re destined to grow more powerful. It’s best, in this case, to set aside their differences and work with the visiting princess, but if the PCs refuse to play nice, treat it as if they earned no Influence points with Ren Mei Li when the time comes to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11partingways000]{Part Ways}.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Prepare for Royalty</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">One of the PCs spends 8 hours preparing a chosen site to host Lady Ren. Other PCs can Aid this check, but if no PC even attempts the check to prepare, then treat it as if they’d critically failed at this activity. The PC must attempt a @Check[crafting|dc:24], @Check[society|dc:24], or @Check[tea-lore|dc:24] check. This check takes a –4 circumstance penalty if the site the PCs choose hasn’t been built up over the course of the campaign.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The PCs gain a +1 circumstance bonus to all Influence checks during this encounter.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The PCs prepare the site but had to dip into the stores to get everything set up. Reduce Food Points by 1.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> As success, but reduce Food Points by [[/r 1d4+1]].</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As Failure, but the shabby job causes the PCs to take a –2 circumstance penalty to all Influence checks during this encounter.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Event 13. Interview with a Spider": {
              "name": "事件13：与蜘蛛的访谈 Event 13. Interview with a Spider",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件13：与蜘蛛的会面</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 8</span>\n</h2>\n    \n<p>\n      正如死神神藏先前警告的那样，络新妇公主任美璃的某个“版本”最终会来到柳岸镇，但很可能要等到PC们完成@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第10章}很久之后才会发生，因为她的来访发生在本幕的第71天，也就是第72天农历新年开始的前一天。如果由于你这场游戏的时间安排，PC们在这段时间仍在进行第10章，那么你应该让此事件发生在PC们返回柳岸镇之后、但在他们开始施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}的5环版本的前一天。\n    </p>\n<p>\n      任美璃是朗洛依宫廷中众多高阶成员之一。关于朗洛依接管神门的传闻已经传到柳岸镇，但请记住，从PC们的角度来看，这一事态的发展只发生在一年前，而且迄今为止，这位络新妇女王尚未把注意力转向柳岸镇。在生者世界里，被派往柳岸镇的先遣侦察兵发现那里已死寂一片；当他们向任美璃回报后，她亲自前往废墟进行调查。\n    </p>\n<p>\n      虽然任美璃最终在现场没有发现值得注意的东西，除了能掠夺到相当数量、可作为献给朗洛依夫人的宝藏之外；但她对柳岸镇覆灭原因所做的神秘学研究，将她的心灵复制进了思维空间，然而她自己并不知情。PC们也会在下一幕遭遇任美璃，而他们在此处如何处理初次会面，或许能在他们回到生者世界时获得优势。\n    </p>\n<p>\n      任美璃的来访始于日出时一名陌生人抵达镇上。这名英俊的年轻男子戴着银色项圈，前去寻找柳岸镇的镇长老，告知他们该镇如今已归朗洛依夫人统治；她的一位公主——任女士——将于今晚抵达；柳岸镇应当做好准备迎接新的王族。这位古怪的信使明确表示，任美璃期望得到王室规格的欢迎，尽管柳岸镇过于乡野贫穷，根本不可能在短时间内提供这种待遇。这一举动是任美璃残酷的游戏——她打算让村民陷入绝望与恐慌，因为他们注定会一次又一次无法满足她的要求，直到她最终因他们的失败而惩罚他们。无论如何，这名神秘来客在带来消息后不久便消散；他本身不过是络新妇公主的前驱思念形体。\n    </p>\n<p>\n      这条消息让镇长老措手不及——不仅遭遇陌生人本就令人震惊，听到神门如今由一位络新妇统治的确凿消息更是骇人。镇长老十分清楚，PC们是唯一可能安抚或震慑这位公主的人，于是迅速联系他们，告知今晚将发生之事。假设PC们曾投入精力维护青天茶馆，镇长老认为那里是接待任女士的最佳地点，但在PC们的暗示下，其他选择也可能行得通。\n    </p>\n<p>\n      请注意，尽管任美璃在即将到来的拜访中会以真正的络新妇形态出现，但这名信使以及随行的其余仆从，都不过是她心灵的显现，并非独立的生物。他们更接近可见的幻影爪牙，而非活着的生物。\n    </p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 13: Interview with a Spider</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8</span>\n</h2>\n    \n<p>\n      As the shinigami, Shinzo, previously warned, a “version” of the jorogumo princess Ren Mei Li eventually comes to\n      town, but likely not until well after the PCs have completed @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10}, for her visit takes place on the 71st\n      day of the act, one day before the lunar new year begins on day 72. If, due to the timing of your game, the PCs are\n      still playing through Chapter 10 at this time, you should have this event take place after the PCs return to\n      Willowshore but a day before they begin casting the 5th-level version of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}.\n    </p>\n<p>\n      Ren Mei Li is one of many high-ranking members of Lang Loi’s court. Rumors of Lang Loi’s takeover of Shenmen\n      have reached Willowshore, but remember that from the PCs’ perspective, this development only happened a year ago, and\n      so far, the jorogumo queen hasn’t yet turned her attention to Willowshore. In the living world, the advance\n      scouts sent to Willowshore found the place dead, and when they reported back to Ren Mei Li, she traveled to the ruins\n      to investigate them herself.\n    </p>\n<p>\n      While Ren Mei Li eventually found nothing of note on-site other than a fair amount of treasure to loot as\n      offerings to Lady Lang Loi, her occult research into the cause of Willowshore’s doom copied her psyche into the\n      mindscape, though she’s unaware of this. The PCs will encounter Ren Mei Li in the next act as well, and how they\n      handle their first meeting here might give them an advantage once they return to the world of the living.\n    </p>\n<p>\n      Ren Mei Li’s visit begins with the arrival of a stranger in town at sunrise. This handsome young man wears a\n      silver collar and seeks out Willowshore’s town elder to inform them that the town is now under the rulership of\n      Lady Lang Loi; that one of her princesses, Lady Ren, shall be arriving this very evening; and that Willowshore\n      should make itself ready to receive the new royalty. The strange messenger makes it clear that Ren Mei Li\n      expects to receive a royal welcome, despite Willowshore being far too rustic and poor to provide such a thing on short\n      notice. This move is a cruel game on Ren Mei Li’s part—she intends to drive the villagers into despair and panic\n      as they inevitably fall short of her demands again and again before finally punishing them for their failures.\n      In any event, the mysterious visitor fades away soon after bringing the news, himself merely a precursor\n      thoughtform of the jorogumo princess.\n    </p>\n<p>\n      This news catches the town elder off guard—not only is it a shock to encounter a stranger, but hearing\n      confirmation that Shenmen is now ruled by a jorogumo is frightening indeed. The town elder is keenly aware that\n      the PCs are the only people who might actually placate or threaten the princess and quickly contacts them to let\n      them know what’s coming that evening. Assuming the PCs have put effort into the upkeep of the Cerulean Teahouse,\n      the town elder feels it’s the best place to receive Lady Ren, but other options might work at the PCs’\n      suggestion.\n    </p>\n<p>\n      Note that while Ren Mei Li appears in the upcoming visit as an actual jorogumo, this messenger, as well as the\n      rest of the servants who accompany her, are little more than manifestations of her psyche and are not individual\n      creatures. They are more akin to visible phantasmal minions than they are to living creatures.\n    </p>"
            },
            "Ending the Seance": {
              "name": "结束通灵仪式 Ending the Seance",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Ending the Seance\">结束降神会</h3>\n<p>一旦驱魔师们完成仪式（且所有 PC 的影响轮都已用尽），曹宸会念出最后的祷告，然后用火把轻轻敲一下上方的铃。铃声回荡时的声势出人意料地压倒性，明明只是如此轻的一下，PC 们却被抛回降神会开始时他们在柳岸镇的所在之处。当他们回归时，会一阵天旋地转，必须进行一次 @Check[will|dc:24] 意志豁免，以抵抗变为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1}（若大失败则为 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2}）。随后他们会发现，在过去的几分钟里，他们一直躺在地板上昏迷不醒、毫无反应。这样的发展可能会吓到附近的镇民，而当 PC 醒来时，他们很可能会面对铺天盖地的提问。PC 可以随心回答，但必须以一次 @Check[diplomacy|dc:24] 交涉检定小心应对；若失败，镇民会担心自己可能会成为这些驱魔师召唤的下一个目标，而柳岸镇失去 [[/r 1d4]] 希望点。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">音效</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.0GuH1kstxWaqGSJx.PlaylistSound.1v8fZOWDIQO6erYk]{结束降神会}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>当 PC 返回后，他们意识到，不知为何，他们在降神会期间看到的那口铃已经被注入了来自柳岸镇<em>长明灯</em>的光芒，这证实了长明灯在现世必定已经熄灭。只要情况仍是如此，他们就只能施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} 的 4 环版本。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若 PC 与至少一名驱魔师合计获得了 4 影响点，则给予他们 80 XP。若他们在三名驱魔师之间获得了全部 12 点可能的影响点，则改为奖励英雄们 120 XP。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Ending the Seance\">Ending the Seance</h3>\n<p>Once the exorcists finish (and all of the PCs’ influence rounds have been spent), Cao Chen utters a final prayer and then taps the bell above softly with his torch. The sound of the bell ringing out is unexpectedly overwhelming given such a small tap, and the PCs are hurled back to wherever they were in Willowshore when the seance began. As they return, they’re sent reeling and must attempt a @Check[will|dc:24] save to resist becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 1} (or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.4D2KBtexWXa6oUMR]{Drained 2} on a critical failure). They then discover that, for the past several minutes, they’ve been lying unconscious and unresponsive on the floor. This development might have shocked nearby townsfolk and, when the PCs awaken, they likely face a deluge of questions. The PCs can answer as they wish but must do so delicately with a @Check[diplomacy|dc:24] check; failure causes the townsfolk to worry that they might be the next to be conjured by these exorcists, and Willowshore loses [[/r 1d4]] Hope Points.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.0GuH1kstxWaqGSJx.PlaylistSound.1v8fZOWDIQO6erYk]{Ending the Seance}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>Once the PCs return, they realize that, somehow, the bell they saw during the seance has been infused with the light from Willowshore’s <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, confirming that the lantern must be unlit in the living world. As long as this remains the case, they’ll only be able to cast the 4th-level version of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs gained a total of 4 Influence Points with at least one exorcist, grant them 80 XP. If they gained all 12 possible Influence Points among all three exorcists, award the heroes 120 XP instead.</p>"
            },
            "Running the Seance": {
              "name": "主持通灵会 Running the Seance",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Running the Seance\">主持降神会</h3>\n<p>降神会使用影响力（子系统）（<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 187）来进行，每一轮持续几分钟。一轮开始时，由陈向PC们提出一个问题（在他眼里，PC们只是模糊闪烁、彼此无法区分的形体）。每一轮按以下步骤进行。</p>\n<p><strong>步骤1：</strong>陈提出该轮的问题（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11runningthese00#seance-questions]{降神会问题}），并随机决定一名PC会被强迫作答（选定后，该PC在之后的轮次不应再被选中）。该PC必须尝试一次@Check[will|dc:26]豁免。成功时，队伍中任意PC都可以按自己想要的方式回答该问题；但失败时，被选中的PC必须尽可能如实回答问题。若某PC被强迫如实作答，询问该玩家想如何回答，然后将该答案在主题上调整为与下文列出的“被强迫的答案”相符。</p>\n<p>如果PC们在任何回答中提到苦迦菩提，陈会陷入沉思，开始考虑问题的规模。显然他并没有识破PC们，但由于他倾向于驱逐PC们和苦迦菩提，而不是设法帮助PC们恢复生命，因此这条信息不会改变PC们可能的命运。</p>\n<p>若某PC没有被强迫回答，则可以由一名PC尝试用@Check[deception|dc:24]、@Check[diplomacy|dc:24]或@Check[intimidation|dc:24]检定来作答（其他PC可以协助该检定），以决定他们回答的结果。成功时，在步骤2中该轮所有用于影响与发现的检定获得+2状态加值（大成功则为+4状态加值）。大失败时，这些检定改为承受–2状态减值。</p>\n<p><strong>步骤2：</strong>祭司们会花一点时间吟唱并集中精神，然后再进入下一个问题（或者若这是最后一轮，则专注于结束降神会）。在这段时间里，PC们意识到他们与驱邪师之间的灵性链接是双向的，他们能够感知每位祭司的想法。每名PC都可以尝试去影响或发现自己选择的一名祭司的情报。当一名驱邪师被成功影响时，PC们的存在会促使其脱口说出不该说的话，或做出意料之外的举动，从而向PC们揭露比其本意更多的信息。每位驱邪师会透露什么，取决于队伍对其累计的影响点数量，如下方三个影响数据表所述。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>降神会问题</h2>\n  <p>祭司们在降神会中对PC们提出的四个问题如下——注意，PC们回答什么、怎么回答，并不会在很大程度上改变本幕的进程，但在每个问题之后、PC们于步骤2反制祭司时，这些回答能给予PC们优势。</p>\n  <p><strong>第1轮：</strong>“你们是谁？”被强迫如实回答的PC必须说出自己的名字与其他PC的名字，告知驱邪师们各自在队伍中的职责，并揭示他们是柳岸镇的居民。</p>\n  <p><strong>第2轮：</strong>“你们想要什么？”被强迫如实回答的PC必须说出诸如“我们想要复活”之类的话。若该PC愿意，允许其在此基础上补充更多内容；他们也可以借机提到，他们寻求阻止苦迦菩提逃离死亡。</p>\n  <p><strong>第3轮：</strong>“你们为何还未离去？”被强迫的PC必须回答：“我们做不到；我们被困在这里。”并且在尽可能符合PC们所知事实的前提下，补充他们在思维空间中所面临危险的任何说明。PC可以提到，是苦迦菩提的意志将他们困住。</p>\n  <p><strong>第4轮：</strong>“你们是怎么死的？”被强迫的PC会揭露：“我们的总督在试图用仪式囚禁恶魔苦迦菩提时失败了，我们因此被杀。”并可按其意愿加以润色。</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>Cao Chen</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-caochen.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Cao Chen\" alt=\"a scowling, middle-aged bald human man\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-caochen.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">驱邪师领袖</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>意志</strong> +20</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:26|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>影响技能</strong>\n    @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[religion|dc:24|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:26|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响2</strong>“别怕，我的学生们。我们在这里绝对安全。没有明确的目的，这些百年魅影对物质世界的影响，和鱼点火一样不可能。”</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响4</strong>“我能感到你们的力量，亡灵；但我们的圣铃注入了来自你们自身长明灯的光辉，阻止你们的恶毒影响与魔法渗入我们的世界。只要这口铃在卡拉海发光，你们就无法伤害我们。我们有时间保持耐心并循序渐进，因此你们最好照做，如实回答我们的问题。”</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>Pan Fenfang</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-panfenfang.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Pan Fenfang\" alt=\"a pensive human man with black hair in a bun and a scar across his cheek\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-panfenfang.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">紧张且藏有秘密的驱邪师</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +16</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>意志</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:21|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:23|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[religion|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>影响技能</strong>\n    @Check[deception|dc:21|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:23|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[religion|dc:25|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响2</strong>“像大多数顽固的灵一样，这些鬼魂就是拒绝讲理，曹师父。我们得接受这会是一份难差事，然后回去继续干。花时间讲话就是浪费时间。”他直呼其名的用法让曹陈皱起了眉头。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响4</strong>“你们已经死得太久了，亡灵。除了最阴邪的魔法之外，没有任何东西能让你们复活，而我们绝不会允许那种事发生。接受你们的命运，祈祷当你们在骨园站在@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}面前受审时，她会怜悯你们的罪孽。”她说这番话时，脸上掠过一丝疑虑，PC们也得以更深地窥见她的内心——看见其中似有猩红的蝴蝶在扑动。通过一次成功的@Check[occultism|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识后，PC会意识到这名驱邪师在不自知的情况下受到了灵堕魔的影响。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>弱点</strong>芬芳对另外两名驱邪师隐瞒着某件事。她对马戈·凯那套循序渐进地从柳岸镇清除灵体的方法感到幻灭，于是去寻求其他神圣力量的来源。她所认为的谭隋靖之灵显现并向她提供了那股力量。不幸的是，这个幻影其实是苦迦菩提的投影，被她的祈祷吸引而来。如今芬芳属于驱邪师队伍内部一个小型的灵堕魔崇拜者教团。他们仍相信自己的事业正当，但他们尚未坦白他们的新庇护者，因为灵堕魔不断在他们耳边低语，要求他们必须对马戈·凯保密。尽管PC们无法确定她秘密的确切性质，但一旦他们提到该地区存在灵堕魔的影响，芬芳会变得更加紧张，她所有发现与影响技能的DC都降低1。若PC们提到苦迦菩提，则这些技能DC改为全部降低2。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">Sha “Shagua” Guanghao</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shaguang.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Sha Guanghoa\" alt=\"a young human man with a shaved head and a smug smile\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shaguang.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">年轻而鲁莽的驱邪师</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +14</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>意志</strong> +16</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>影响技能</strong>\n    @Check[deception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[diplomacy|dc:24|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响2</strong>“可师父，如果铃声和光能把灵困住，那我们为什么不能直接不理他们，去把这片区域的树都砍来收成呢？”这个问题引来曹陈夸张地翻了个白眼，并做了个噤声的手势。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响4</strong>“你们要是敢耍花样，马戈大人就会带着他的魔法摇铃人冲进来把你们驱逐走！就像这样——哗啊啊！”广浩夸张地模仿用力摇铃，随即被芬芳拍了一下后脑勺；之后曹陈说道：“根本不是这样运作的！我让你读的典籍卷轴你读了吗？”</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Running the Seance\">Running the Seance</h3>\n<p>The seance plays out using the influence subsystem (<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 187), with each round lasting for a few minutes. A round begins with Chen asking a question of the PCs (who, to him, appear as vague shimmering forms that are indistinguishable from one another). Each round, follow these steps.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Chen asks that round’s question (listed in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11runningthese00#seance-questions]{Seance Questions}), and a randomly determined PC is compelled to reply (once selected, that PC shouldn’t be selected on future rounds). That PC must attempt a @Check[will|dc:26] save. On a success, any PC in the group can reply to the question however they want, but on a failure, the targeted PC must reply to the question as truthfully as they can. If a PC is compelled to reply truthfully, ask that player how they would like to answer, then adjust that answer to match, thematically, the compelled answers listed further below.</p>\n<p>If the PCs mention Kugaptee in any of their answers, Chen becomes pensive, considering the scope of the problem. It’s clear that he doesn’t disbelieve the PCs, but since his inclination is to banish both the PCs and Kugaptee, rather than helping the PCs somehow restore themselves to life, this information won’t change the PCs’ potential fate.</p>\n<p>If a PC isn’t compelled to answer, one PC can attempt to answer with a @Check[deception|dc:24], @Check[diplomacy|dc:24], or @Check[intimidation|dc:24] check (the other PCs can Aid this check) to determine the result of their reply. On a success, all checks attempted to Influence and Discover that round during step 2 gain a +2 status bonus (or a +4 status bonus on a critical success). On a critical failure, these checks instead take a –2 status penalty.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The priests spend a few moments chanting and focusing their concentration before moving on to the next question (or, if this is the final round, focusing on ending the seance), during which the PCs realize the spiritual link between them and the exorcists works both ways, and they can sense each priest’s thoughts. Each PC can attempt to Influence or Discover information about the priest of their choice. When an exorcist is successfully Influenced, the PCs’ presence causes them to say something out of turn or take an unanticipated action that reveals more to the PCs than they intend. What every exorcist reveals depends on the number of Influence points the party has accumulated with each one of them, as detailed in the following three Influence stat blocks.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Seance Questions</h2>\n  <p>The four questions the priests ask the PCs during the seance are as follows—note that what and how the PCs reply won’t change the course of this act much, but they can give the PCs advantages when they turn the tables on the priests during step 2 following each question.</p>\n  <p><strong>Round 1:</strong> “Who are you?” A PC compelled to answer truthfully must give their name and the names of the other PCs, inform the exorcists of each of their roles in the party, and reveal that they’re citizens of Willowshore.</p>\n  <p><strong>Round 2:</strong> “What do you want?” A PC compelled to answer truthfully must say something to the effect of, “We seek to come back to life.” Allow the PC to add more to this answer if they wish. They can use this opportunity to mention they seek to oppose Kugaptee’s escape from death.</p>\n  <p><strong>Round 3:</strong> “Why haven’t you moved on?” A compelled PC must answer, “We cannot; we are trapped here,” along with any additional clarifications about the dangers they’ve been facing in the mindscape, as long as they’re truthful to the best of the PCs’ knowledge. A PC can mention that Kugaptee’s will has trapped them.</p>\n  <p><strong>Round 4:</strong> “How did you die?” A compelled PC reveals, “We were slain when our governor failed at a ritual to imprison the fiend Kugaptee,” embellishing that however they wish.</p>\n</aside>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>Cao Chen</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-caochen.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Cao Chen\" alt=\"a scowling, middle-aged bald human man\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-caochen.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Leader of the exorcists</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Will</strong> +20</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:26|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Influence Skills</strong>\n    @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[religion|dc:24|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:26|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 2</strong> “Fear not, my students. We are perfectly safe here. Without a focused purpose, these century-old phantoms can no more affect the material world than a fish can light a fire.”</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 4</strong> “I sense your strength, spirits, but our holy bell, infused with light from your own Eternal Lantern, prevents your fell influence and magic from seeping through to our world. As long as this bell shines in Karahai, you cannot harm us. We have time to be patient and methodical, so you would do well to simply comply and answer our questions truthfully.”</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>Pan Fenfang</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-panfenfang.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Pan Fenfang\" alt=\"a pensive human man with black hair in a bun and a scar across his cheek\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-panfenfang.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Nervous exorcist with a secret</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +16</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Will</strong> +18</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:21|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:23|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[religion|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Influence Skills</strong>\n    @Check[deception|dc:21|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:23|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[religion|dc:25|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 2</strong> “Like most stubborn spirits, these ghosts simply refuse to listen to reason, Master Cao. We must accept that this will be a difficult job and get back to it. Spending time talking is time wasted.” The use of his name prompts a scowl from Cao Chen.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 4</strong> “You have been dead for far too long, spirits. There is nothing that can return you to life beyond the most sinister forms of magic, and we will not permit that. Make peace with your fate and pray that @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} shows mercy for your sins when you stand before her in the Boneyard and are judged.” As she speaks, her face flashes doubt, and the PCs catch a deeper glimpse into her mind—seeing the crimson butterflies that seem to flutter therein. With a successful @Check[occultism|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC realizes this exorcist is unknowingly influenced by nindorus.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Weakness</strong> Fenfang is hiding something from the other two exorcists. Disillusioned with Mago Kai’s methodical approach to purging spirits from Willowshore, Fenfang sought out other sources of divine power. What she believes to be the spirit of Tan Sui-Jing appeared and offered her just that. Unfortunately, this apparition was actually a projection of Kugaptee, drawn to answer her prayers. Fenfang now belongs to a small cult of nindoru followers within the ranks of the exorcists. They still believe that their cause is just, but they haven’t yet come forward about their new patron, as the nindoru keeps whispering in their ears that they must keep this development secret from Mago Kai. While the PCs aren’t sure as to the exact nature of her secret, once they mention the influence of nindorus in the region, Fenfang grows more nervous and all of her Discovery and Influence Skill DCs are reduced by 1. If the PCs mention Kugaptee, these skill DCs are instead all reduced by 2.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">Sha “Shagua” Guanghao</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shaguang.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Sha Guanghoa\" alt=\"a young human man with a shaved head and a smug smile\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shaguang.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Young and brash exorcist</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +14</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Will</strong> +16</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Influence Skills</strong>\n    @Check[deception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[diplomacy|dc:24|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 2</strong> “But master, if the bell and the light keeps the spirits trapped, why can’t we just ignore them and get to harvesting all the trees in the region?” This question draws an exaggerated eye-roll and a motion to shush from Cao Chen.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 4</strong> “If you try anything funny, Lord Mago will come in here with his magic bell ringer and banish you away! Like this—hwahhh!” Guanghao mimics forcefully ringing a bell and then is slapped on the back of the head by Fenfang, after which Cao Chen says, “That’s not how it works! Did you even read the codex scroll like I told you?”</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Event 12. The Seance": {
              "name": "事件12：降神会 Event 12. The Seance",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 12：降神会</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>当作祟事实证明比孙海的驱魔师们所预期的更顽强、更强大时（这是由于 PC 从思维空间内部进行反击所致），他们转而采用一个不那么激进的计划。在首次试图驱逐魂魄失败约一个月后，他们现在打算举行一场降神会，与这些魂魄沟通，希望能更多了解在废墟中作祟的幽灵（特征）。</p>\n<p>该事件应在 PC 开始 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第 10 章} 之前的某个时间发生，因为它让队伍首次真正有机会了解他们转生时会遇到什么。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>对自身的挫败（由 PC 造成）感到困惑的孙海驱魔师们回到柳岸镇的废墟，并举行一场降神会以寻求答案。资深驱魔师曹辰主持仪式，并由他的两名助手潘芬芳与沙“傻瓜”广豪协助。祭司们在唐入的神龛（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}）中进行降神会。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.h82ztCVRXELKQI8K]{降神会}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>当降神会开始时，PC 突然感觉自己被猛地拽离，穿过一层层现实，仿佛以极高速度飞掠过柳岸镇、穿过森林，随后进入一间没有窗户的小房间。房间里由燃烧的火把昏暗照明，而其大部分空间都被一口巨大的青铜寺钟占据——那钟悬挂在天花板上。五个装着色彩斑斓鸟儿的小笼子被摆成一个大圆圈，与此同时，地面上、圆圈之内，摆放着数量与 PC 人数相等的若干卷轴。来自上方寺钟的闪烁却又莫名熟悉的光芒向下辐射，照亮这些卷轴，并将 PC 困在圆圈之中。在这场遭遇中，除下文提到者外，PC 不能采取任何动作。</p>\n<p>允许每名 PC 尝试一次 @Check[perception|dc:24] 检定；成功者意识到自己已从柳岸镇被拉向东方，来到唐入沿海要塞内某处的一间密室。接着，每名 PC 都可以尝试一次 @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[religion|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来进行回忆知识，以注意到他们出现在某种降神会的中心，而他们头顶的寺钟是一件强大的圣物，能够防范幽灵（特征）。他们也能看出，这口钟的存在会干扰任何源自魂魄或不死来源的魔法。</p>\n<p>片刻之后，三名祭司的幽影浮现出来。他们各自都穿着在本幕首次遭遇时所穿的黑袖绛红长袍，但这次没有戴那种骇人的四眼面具。曹辰是一名中年秃头的人类男子；芬芳是一名中年人类女子，右脸颊上有一道陈旧的伤疤；广豪是一名留着修整得体胡须的年轻人类男子。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 12: The Seance</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>When the hauntings proved to be more tenacious and powerful than Mago Kai’s exorcists expected (as a result of the PCs fighting back from within the mindscape), they turned to a less aggressive plan. About a month after their first failed attempt to drive off the spirits, they now seek to perform a seance to communicate with them in hopes of learning more about the ghosts that haunt the ruins.</p>\n<p>This event should take place at some time before the PCs begin @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10} since it gives the party their first real chance to learn about what to expect when they transmigrate.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Confounded at their setbacks (caused by the PCs), Mago Kai’s exorcists return to Willowshore’s ruins and engage in a seance to get some answers. Senior exorcist Cao Chen leads the ceremony and is joined by two of his assistants, Pan Fenfang and Sha “Shagua” Guanghao. The priests perform the seance in Karahai’s shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}).</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.h82ztCVRXELKQI8K]{Seance}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>When the seance begins, the PCs suddenly feel themselves yanked away through layers of reality, as if flying at great speed through Willowshore, the forest, and then into a small windowless room that’s dimly lit by burning torches and mostly occupied by a massive bronze temple bell that hangs from the ceiling. Five small cages containing colorful birds are set in a large circle, and a number of scrolls equal to the number of PCs lie on the ground inside this circle. Flickering but strangely familiar-looking light radiates down from the bell above to illuminate those scrolls, containing the PCs within the circle. The PCs can’t take any actions other than those mentioned below during this encounter.</p>\n<p>Allow each PC to attempt a @Check[perception|dc:24] check; those who succeed realize they’ve been pulled east from Willowshore into a chamber somewhere within the coastal fortress of Karahai. Next, each PC can attempt a @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge to note that they’ve appeared in the center of a type of seance, and that the temple bell above them is a powerful holy item that wards against ghosts. They can also tell the bell’s presence can interfere with any magic coming from spiritual or undead sources.</p>\n<p>A moment later, the ghostly images of the three priests appear, each wearing the same black-sleeved crimson robes they wore in this act’s first encounter, but this time without the frightening four-eyed masks. Cao Chen is a middle-aged bald human man, Fenfang is a middle-aged human woman who bears an old scar on her right cheek, and Guanghao is a young human man with a well-trimmed beard.</p>"
            },
            "Tea with the Nosois": {
              "name": "与疫鸟共饮茶道 Tea with the Nosois",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Tea with the Nosois\">与诺索伊共饮</h3>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>如蜜冬至</h1>\n  <p>在上一幕中，PC们可能发现并学会了一个名为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.wAJ8mXPYbyAg0qWX]{如蜜冬至}的仪式，只能在冬至时施放。如果PC们学会该仪式，他们可以把它纳入烛光泥塑节之中。</p>\n  <p>施放如蜜冬至取得大成功可获得4点食物点。</p>\n  <p>该仪式成功可获得1点食物点。</p>\n  <p>大失败会使城镇中毒。这将花费2d6点准备点数，其中至少一半必须从希望点中扣除；其余则从希望、食物或安全点中扣除（由PC选择）。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>在本幕第21天、冬季正式开始后的几天里（并假设PC们没有把他们赶走），四只诺索伊来到青天茶馆拜访PC们；他们对村民的困境变得更为同情。尽管如此，诺索伊仍认为恰当的行动方针是尽快解决这个非自然的思维空间，并且开始相信最好的办法是援助真吾会的驱魔师。在一番内部商议后，这些招魂者决定先来找PC们，听听这些英雄有什么要为自己辩解的——顺便在此期间用甜点与茶填饱肚子。作为顾客，诺索伊可能略显轻慢，因为他们认为PC们公然违反神祇律法。尽管态度如此，只要善待这些招魂者，英雄们就能获得情报，并可能在之后得到一些人情。</p>\n<p>招待这些讨厌的鸟是一项多线并行的事务。按顺序执行以下步骤，但允许PC们按自己的意愿分配劳动。某一方面的失误可以通过在另一方面表现出色来弥补。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>步骤1：</strong>一名PC必须用@Check[tea-lore|dc:22]或@Check[crafting|dc:24]检定来准备茶。其他PC可以用茶学识或制作检定协助此检定，或用运动来协助（代表该角色在仪式开始前把茶叶研磨成细粉）。</li>\n  <li><strong>步骤2：</strong>除了惯常的仪式餐食与甜点外，诺索伊还要求一座甜麻糬山。一名PC必须准备这道点心：要么用@Check[athletics|dc:22]检定捣打熟米，要么用@Check[crafting|dc:24]检定准备餐食；其他PC可以协助此检定。</li>\n  <li><strong>步骤3：</strong>仪式必须由一名角色完美执行，该角色需在@Check[tea-lore|dc:22]或@Check[society|dc:24]检定中成功；其他PC可以协助此检定。</li>\n  <li><strong>步骤4：</strong>尽管诺索伊自身缺乏礼仪，主人一方仍必须保持体面。一名参与的PC必须尝试@Check[deception|dc:24]或@Check[diplomacy|dc:24]检定；其他PC只能用交涉来协助此检定。</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>决定结果：</strong>统计PC在以上四次检定中的成功次数；每次大成功额外计1次成功，每次大失败则扣除1次成功。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>成功1次或更少：</strong>诺索伊被冒犯得无以复加，连一句话都不说就离开了。在本幕的最终章节中，他们会协助驱魔师击退PC们的幽魂入侵（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c9purificati00]{C9}）。</li>\n  <li><strong>成功2或3次：</strong>PC们平平无奇的仪式没能打动诺索伊。鸟儿们只是失去兴趣并离开柳岸镇——事态不会明显恶化，但英雄们的努力也不会得到任何回报。</li>\n  <li><strong>成功4或5次：</strong>PC们呈现了一场成功的茶会仪式，诺索伊放松下来，开始毫不遮掩地八卦。他们在对话初期有很大篇幅都在谈论真三，喧嚷着认为这位死神对亡者过于心软、过于纵容。他们也兴高采烈地告诉PC们，真三仍在因冒犯@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}而受罚，而且惩罚使他无法直接干涉凡人的命运。每只诺索伊都自信地宣称自己知道真三做了什么惹怒了墓冢夫人，但他们的说法却完全不同——一只声称真三滥用权能以谋私利，而其他几只则坚持认为他饶了一个不该饶的凡人一命、放走了一名强大邪魔、或是爱上了人类。</li>\n  <p>仪式结束时，诺索伊会为这次用茶向PC们付费（见下文“宝藏”），并承诺只要柳岸镇居民不再做任何冒犯法莱斯玛的事，就不再找PC们麻烦。</p>\n  <li><strong>成功6次或更多：</strong>PC们呈现了一场大成功的茶会仪式。诺索伊会如同上文成功茶会仪式那样八卦并付费，但他们还会因为太过满意而提出日后若有机会便会出手相助，并建议PC们“若你们有朝一日置身生者世界，遇到任何法莱斯玛的神龛，都该花点时间净化自己。”这句话指向唐入区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c9purificati00]{C9}中一次获得意外援助的机会。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.HIkFzolLNDjikUel]{诺索伊的报酬} <br />\n  若PC们在奉茶时取得4次或更多成功，招魂者会先在彼此之间争论几分钟，讨论他们四个之中究竟该由谁来“买单”，每一个都宣称自己愿意付账。他们最终妥协决定平摊费用，然后又开始争论谁该付多少。最后，他们在羽毛间翻找，掏出一堆小玩意作为补偿。这些物品包括一枚<em>绞刑架之牙</em>、一枚<em>玉制小饰物</em>、一枚价值800 gp的银与蓝宝石戒指，以及一枚<em>冻寒武器符文石</em>。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们在招待诺索伊时取得4次或更多成功，给予他们120 XP。若少于4次但仍至少有1次成功，则给予他们60 XP。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Tea with the Nosois\">Tea with the Nosois</h3>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Sweetest Solstice</h1>\n  <p>In the previous act, the PCs might have discovered and learned a ritual called @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.wAJ8mXPYbyAg0qWX]{Sweetest Solstice}, which can only be cast during the winter solstice. If the PCs learn this ritual, they can include it in the Claylight Festival.</p>\n  <p>A critical success at casting sweetest solstice grants 4 Food Points.</p>\n  <p>A success at the ritual grants 1 Food Point.</p>\n  <p>A critical failure poisons the town. This costs 2d6 Preparation Points, at least half of which must be subtracted from Hope Points, with the remainder being subtracted from either Hope, Food, or Security Points (the PCs’ choice).</p>\n</aside>\n<p>A few days after winter officially begins on the 21st day of the act (and assuming the PCs haven’t chased them off), the four nosois approach the PCs at the Cerulean Teahouse, having become more sympathetic to the villagers’ struggle. The nosois still feel the proper course of action is to resolve the unnatural mindscape as fast as possible, however, and have come to believe that the best method of doing so is to aid Mago Kai’s exorcists. After some internal deliberation, the psychopomps have decided to approach the PCs to see what the heroes have to say for themselves first—and to fill their stomachs with sweets and tea while doing so. The nosois can be slightly dismissive as customers, considering the PCs to be in blatant violation of divine law. Despite their demeanor, treating the psychopomps well can net the heroes information and possible favors down the line.</p>\n<p>Entertaining the obnoxious birds is a multi-pronged affair. Perform the following steps in order, but allow the PCs to split the labor between themselves as they see fit. Failings in one area can be compensated for by excelling in another.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> One PC must prepare the tea with a @Check[tea-lore|dc:22] or @Check[crafting|dc:24] check. Other PCs can Aid this check with a Tea Lore or Crafting check or with Athletics (representing that character grinding the tea leaves into fine powder before the ceremony starts).</li>\n  <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> In addition to the usual ritual meal and sweets, the nosois demand a mountain of sweet mochi. One PC must prepare this treat, either by pounding the cooked rice with a @Check[athletics|dc:22] check or by preparing the meal with a @Check[crafting|dc:24] check; other PCs can Aid this check.</li>\n  <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> The ceremony should be performed flawlessly by a character who succeeds at a @Check[tea-lore|dc:22] or @Check[society|dc:24] check; other PCs can Aid this check.</li>\n  <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Despite the nosois’ own lack of etiquette, decorum must be kept on the hosts’ side. One of the participating PCs must attempt a @Check[deception|dc:24] or @Check[diplomacy|dc:24] check; other PCs can Aid this check only with Diplomacy.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Determine the Results:</strong> Total the PCs’ successes from these four checks, awarding an extra success for each critical success and deducting one for each critical failure.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>1 or fewer successes:</strong> The nosois are so offended that they leave without a word. In the final chapter of this act, they aid the exorcists in repelling the PCs’ ghostly incursion (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c9purificati00]{C9}).</li>\n  <li><strong>2 or 3 successes:</strong> The PCs fail to impress the nosois with their lackluster ceremony. The birds simply lose interest and depart Willowshore—the situation doesn’t become notably worse, but the heroes don’t gain anything for their efforts either.</li>\n  <li><strong>4 or 5 successes:</strong> The PCs present a successful tea ceremony, and the nosois relax enough to shamelessly gossip. They spend much of their early conversation speaking about Shinzo, loudly opining that the shinigami is too soft and indulgent toward the dead. They also gleefully inform the PCs that Shinzo is still being punished for an infraction against @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} and that his punishment prevents him from directly interfering with the fates of mortals. Each nosoi confidently declares they know what Shinzo did to offend the Lady of Graves, but they all have a completely different story—one claims that Shinzo abused his powers for his own benefit, while others insist he spared a mortal life he shouldn’t have, let a powerful fiend escape his grasp, or fell in love with a human.</li>\n  <p>At the end of the ceremony, the nosois pay the PCs in exchange for the tea (see Treasure below) and promise to trouble the PCs no further so long as the residents of Willowshore don’t do anything else to offend Pharasma.</p>\n  <li><strong>6 or more successes:</strong> The PCs present a critically successful tea ceremony. The nosois gossip and pay as detailed above for a successful tea ceremony, but they are also so pleased they offer to help out later when they have the chance, suggesting the PCs “take the time to purify themselves at any shrine of Pharasma they might encounter, should they ever find themselves in the living world.” This is a reference to an opportunity for unexpected aid in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c9purificati00]{C9} of Karahai.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.HIkFzolLNDjikUel]{Nosois' Payment} <br />\n  If the PCs achieve four or more successes while serving tea, the psychopomps argue for a few minutes among themselves over which one of them should “pay the bill,” with each proclaiming that they’ll cover it. They finally compromise by deciding to split the payment, then argue about the specifics of who should pay what. Finally, they rifle through their feathers, producing a pile of trinkets as compensation. These items consist of a <em>gallows tooth</em>, a <em>jade bauble</em>, a silver and sapphire ring worth 800 gp, and a <em>frost weapon runestone</em>.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs achieve four or more successes when entertaining the nosois, grant them 120 XP. If they achieve fewer than that but still have at least 1 success, grant them 60 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Event 11. Nosois’ Brunch": {
              "name": "事件11：疫鸟的早午餐 Event 11. Nosois’ Brunch",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件11：疫鸟的早午餐</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>在此之前，唯一会定期造访柳岸镇思维空间的招魂者，是神藏的疫鸟观察者伊克斯，但在PC们于第8章末尾返回后，又有另外四名招魂者前来拜访。这四位在神藏与PC们会面前便迅速分散到镇上，接着花上数日观察与等待；在此期间，他们的存在会导致当地的麻雀群出现怪异行为。每当发生特别危险的事件，或在镇民丧命的日子里，麻雀便会变得喧闹而焦躁。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-nosoi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">疫鸟的早午餐</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.EiOgIiuwocy6joyW]{疫鸟（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoi.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nosoi\" alt=\"a crow with glowing eyes wearing a porcelain mask\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoi.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>这四只疫鸟各自显现为怪异的乌鸦，闪着发光的绿色眼睛。它们从不真正加入麻雀的群聚，但总在附近出现。人们目击到这些鸟的次数逐渐增加，不久之后镇民便将其解读为可怕的凶兆，因为在神门，“四”是不祥之数。</p>\n  <p>这四只疫鸟分别名为山口、坂口、井口与野口。它们是伊克斯的同行，同样知晓神藏与包裹柳岸镇的思维空间之间的牵连。与神藏（以及延伸而言的伊克斯）不同，这四只疫鸟对拯救PC们及其同村者并无特别兴趣；它们强烈认为神藏对凡人的偏袒已经到了不配作为死亡仲裁者的地步。神藏未能协助孙海的驱魔师、反而持续援助PC们这一事实，成了压垮疫鸟的最后一根稻草。尽管它们在技术上并未得到@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}授权去干预，但这些官僚作风的招魂者已经开始彼此密谋，打算协助驱逐这片幽灵（特征）思维空间，并将柳岸镇的异常归档到它们的已解决事件记录中。</p>\n  <p>四只疫鸟抵达柳岸镇后，首要任务是观察区域及其居民，以便在未来更好地拟定有效计划。你可以用这四只疫鸟为本幕各个场景增添一层阴森氛围。疫鸟不会干预事件，除非出现让它们难以抗拒的机会（比如几乎肯定能帮助杀死一只灵堕魔），否则它们更倾向于与任何可能危险之物保持安全距离。若PC们追踪到疫鸟并以战斗与之对峙，这些招魂者会立刻逃离；待神藏下次离开时，它们会彻底放弃这片思维空间——这会被视为在接下来的社交遭遇中大失败。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 11: Nosois’ Brunch</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Before now, the only psychopomp to visit the Willowshore mindscape regularly was Shinzo’s nosoi watcher, Yix, but after the PCs return at the end of Chapter 8, four more psychopomps come to visit. These four quickly disperse into the town before Shinzo meets with the PCs, then spend several days observing and waiting, during which their presence causes local flocks of sparrows to behave strangely. Whenever a particularly dangerous event takes place, or on days when townsfolk perish, the sparrows grow loud and agitated.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-nosoi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Nosois' Brunch</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.EiOgIiuwocy6joyW]{Nosois (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoi.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nosoi\" alt=\"a crow with glowing eyes wearing a porcelain mask\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoi.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The four nosois each appear as strange crows with glowing green eyes. They never quite take part in the sparrows’ flocking but are always nearby. Sightings of these birds increase, and it doesn’t take long before the townsfolk interpret them as a terrible omen, since four is an unlucky number in Shenmen.</p>\n  <p>The four nosois are named Yamaguchi, Sakaguchi, Iguchi, and Noguchi. They are Yix’s professional colleagues and are likewise aware of Shinzo’s involvement with the mindscape that encapsulates Willowshore. Unlike Shinzo (and by extension Yix), these four nosois have no particular interest in saving the PCs and their fellow villagers, and they strongly feel that Shinzo has become biased toward mortals in a way that’s unbecoming for an arbiter of death. The fact that Shinzo failed to assist Mago Kai’s exorcists and instead continues to aid the PCs was the final straw for the nosois. While they aren’t technically authorized by @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} to interfere, the bureaucratic psychopomps have begun scheming among themselves to help banish the ghostly mindscape and file the anomaly of Willowshore away in their resolved incident records.</p>\n  <p>When the four nosois arrive in Willowshore, their first order of business is to observe the area and its residents to better devise an effective plan later down the road. You can use these four nosois to add an eerie atmosphere to scenes throughout this act. The nosois don’t interfere in events unless presented with an opportunity too tempting to pass up (such as a near-certain chance to help kill a nindoru), preferring to keep a safe distance away from anything that might be dangerous. If the PCs track down the nosois and confront them in combat, the psychopomps flee at once, abandoning the mindscape entirely the next time Shinzo leaves—this counts as critically failing the following social encounter.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Event 10. The Claylight Festival": {
              "name": "事件10：黏光节 Event 10. The Claylight Festival",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 10: The Claylight Festival\">事件10：泥灯节</h2>\n<p>尽管本幕的前三周天气严酷、季节将至，但直到本月第21天、至日到来时，冬天才真正降临。随着这一天临近，九耳神社的看守人欧·巴明（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w16nineearsh00]{W16}）带着一个提议来找PC。上个季节的首长夜庆典极大提振了镇上的士气；即使如今看起来阴郁而沉重，她仍建议柳岸镇再参与另一项古老传统，以庆祝冬季的第一天：泥灯节。</p>\n<p>泥灯节比首长夜要简略得多，但仍需要整整一天。在这个冬季真正到来的第一天，镇民会制作小小的泥土小屋，并把它们摆在田野里或街道旁，在屋内点上一盏小灯。当超小型小屋把田地照亮后，居民们会围着火堆烤蔬菜，并祈祷好运降临。欧·巴明希望至少有一名PC在至日前一周参与为庆典做准备。在这一周里，每位愿意参与的PC都必须将当周的休整模式行动用于该目标，然后尝试进行一次@Check[crafting|dc:25]检定或一次@Check[religion|dc:24]检定。在庆典进行期间，村民会陆续前来，根据他们检定的结果，要么称赞要么嘲弄英雄们的成果。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.AO9vQaItI4LjcB92]{Front Porch} <br />\n  泥灯节看似只是简单的消遣，但参与并取悦当地魂魄会带来好处。每位成功参与庆典的PC，会在第二天早晨发现青天茶馆的前廊上匿名留下的一瓶<em>中等治疗药水</em>（最多四瓶）。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若至少一名PC在为泥灯节做准备的技能检定中成功，他们的努力会受到认可：柳岸镇获得1点希望点，PC获得80 XP。若所有PC都参与这些准备，只要至少一名PC在检定中成功，则这些奖励提升为2点希望点与120 XP。若没有任何PC参与，庆典即为失败，柳岸镇失去[[/r 1d4]]点希望点。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 10: The Claylight Festival\">Event 10: The Claylight Festival</h2>\n<p>Although the first three weeks of this act feature stark weather and the looming season, it isn’t until the 21st day of the month that winter arrives with the solstice. As this day nears, Ouh Ba-Ming (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w16nineearsh00]{W16}), caretaker of Nine Ear Shrine, approaches the PCs with a proposition. Last season’s First Long Night festival did wonders for the town’s morale, and even though things seem grim and somber, she suggests that Willowshore participate in another old tradition to celebrate the first day of winter: the Claylight Festival.</p>\n<p>Claylight is a much less involved festival than First Long Night, but it still requires an entire day. On this first true day of winter, the townsfolk create small clay huts and set them out in the fields or along streets with a small light inside. Once the fields are lit up with the tiny huts, the residents grill vegetables over fires and pray for good fortune to come. Ouh Ba-Ming would like at least one PC to take part in preparing for the festival on the week leading up to the solstice. On this week, each PC who wishes to do so must devote their downtime activity that week to that goal, then attempt either a @Check[crafting|dc:25] check or a @Check[religion|dc:24] check. Villagers come by over the course of the festivities to either praise or mock the heroes’ efforts, depending on the results of their checks.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.AO9vQaItI4LjcB92]{Front Porch} <br />\n  While the Claylight Festival might seem like a simple diversion, there are benefits for participating and pleasing the local spirits. For each PC who succeeded at participating in the festival, they find a <em>moderate healing potion</em> (to a maximum of four potions) left anonymously on the front porch of the Cerulean Teahouse the next morning.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If at least one PC succeeds at their skill check to prepare for the Claylight Festival, their efforts are appreciated: Willowshore gains 1 Hope Point, and the PCs gain 80 XP. If all of the PCs take part in these preparations, these awards are increased to 2 Hope Points and 120 XP, as long as at least one PC succeeds at the check. If no PC takes part, the festival is a failure and Willowshore loses [[/r 1d4]] Hope Points.</p>"
            },
            "Event 9. The Crane-Wife": {
              "name": "事件9：鹤妻 Event 9. The Crane-Wife",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 9. The Crane-Wife\">事件9：鹤妻</h2>\n<p>即使柳岸镇的粮食储备相当充足，镇上仍有人不满足。某位本地猎人遇到一只大型仙鹤后，将其杀死充作食物，并回家烹制了一顿奢侈大餐。消息很快传开；尽管柳岸镇里有些人可能嫉妒这名猎人意外得来的丰收，但更多人的反应却是担忧。一名PC若在一次 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:18] 或 @Check[society|dc:20] 检定中成功，便明白缘由：传说仙鹤一生只择一伴。若在该检定中获得大成功，该PC还会想起一个古老故事：曾有猎人在冬天杀死一只仙鹤，随后一位悲恸的伴侣前来拜访，请求也被杀死。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-the-crane-wife.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Crane-Wife\" alt=\"a strange, beautiful woman crying and calling out\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-the-crane-wife.webp')\" />\n<p>果不其然，在猎人享用大餐后的第二天，一位新来者抵达柳岸镇——对这座在过去半年里与外界隔绝的城镇来说，这是一件不同寻常的事。没人认得这位奇异而美丽的女子；她穿行过镇子，边走边啜泣，呼喊着其中一位PC的名字。从队伍中挑选一名与自然世界联系最紧密、或你认为最富同情心的PC。这名怪异女子会寻找那名PC，然后揭露一个令人心碎的事实：她的丈夫被杀了，而她也来此寻死。这位无名女子在悲伤中安静而有礼，却拒绝离开，直到有人杀死她，或直到她饿死为止。耐人寻味的是，这位鹤妻死后并不会变回仙鹤，这使人不禁怀疑：猎人抓住并吃掉的那只“鹤”，一开始究竟是不是鹤。</p>\n<p>这场遭遇并非旨在引发战斗；相反，它是让PC们面对的一道道德难题。鹤妻或许不过是在思维空间中显现的思念体，但这一次，她的诞生并非源自苦迦菩提，而是源自镇民集体的绝望与忧虑。她也同样可能是某种超自然生物，比如水泽仙女或溪精。她甚至可能是柳岸镇里某个对猎人怀有怨念的人，在一顶 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.SswqJqeAWGtX3tTF]{法师帽} 的帮助下，精心策划了一场品味低劣的复杂恶作剧。无论真相如何，重要的是PC们将如何处理这一复杂局面。</p>\n<p>此遭遇通过DC 24的检定来获得胜利点数（<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 184）以解决。一旦PC们得知情况，询问每个人打算如何回应鹤妻的请求。欺骗、交涉或威吓都是很好的选项；若深入当地民俗寻求建议，则可使用社交或柳岸镇学识；若方案涉及关于原初魔法的知识，则使用自然。每名PC可以尝试一次技能检定以获得胜利点数，最多进行四次尝试。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们获得5点或更多胜利点数，无论他们选择了哪种方案，柳岸镇都会认为他们做出了正确决定并表示理解；在此情况下，PC们获得120 XP。如果PC们获得2到4点胜利点数，柳岸镇的许多人会对这起事件感到不安；PC们获得60 XP并失去1点希望点。如果PC们获得1点或更少胜利点数，镇民将因结局而抑郁并被其阴影萦绕；PC们不获得XP，并失去[[/r 1d4+1]]点希望点。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 9. The Crane-Wife\">Event 9. The Crane-Wife</h2>\n<p>Even if Willowshore’s food stores are robust, there are those in town who aren’t satisfied. When one such local hunter encounters a large crane, they kill the bird for food and return home to cook an extravagant meal. Word spreads, and while some in Willowshore might be jealous of this hunter’s unexpected bounty, a larger reaction is one of worry. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:18] or a @Check[society|dc:20] check understands why, for the stories say that cranes mate for life. With a critical success at this check, the PC recalls an old story of a hunter who killed a crane in the winter only to be visited by a grieving spouse who asked to be killed as well.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-the-crane-wife.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Crane-Wife\" alt=\"a strange, beautiful woman crying and calling out\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-the-crane-wife.webp')\" />\n<p>Sure enough, the day after the hunter’s meal, a newcomer arrives in Willowshore—an unusual event for a town that, for the past half year, has been cut off from the outside world. No one recognizes the strange, beautiful woman as she strides through town, sobbing and calling out one of the PCs’ names. Choose the PC from the group who has the strongest ties to the natural world or who you feel is the most compassionate. This strange woman seeks that PC out, then reveals the heartbreaking fact that her husband was slain and she’s here to seek death as well. The nameless woman is quiet and polite in her sorrow but refuses to leave until someone kills her, or until she starves to death. Curiously, the crane-wife doesn’t become a crane upon death, calling into question whether the “crane” the hunter captured and ate was a crane in the first place.</p>\n<p>This encounter isn’t meant to be a combat; rather, it’s a moral quandary for the PCs to face. The crane-wife could be nothing more than a thoughtform manifested in the mindscape, but this time born from the collective despair and worry of the townsfolk rather than from Kugaptee. She could just as easily be a supernatural creature like a naiad or nixie. She could even be someone from Willowshore with a grudge against the hunter who has engineered a complex prank in poor taste with the aid of a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.SswqJqeAWGtX3tTF]{Mage's Hat}. Regardless, it’s how the PCs handle this complex situation that matters.</p>\n<p>This encounter is resolved via DC 24 checks to earn Victory Points (<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> 184). Once the PCs learn of the situation, ask each how they wish to handle the crane-wife’s request. Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation all make great options; looking deep into local folklore for advice could suggest Society or Willowshore Lore, while a solution that draws upon knowledge of primal magic would use Nature. Each PC can attempt one skill check to earn Victory Points, to a maximum of four attempts.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs earn 5 or more Victory Points, their solution is viewed by Willowshore as the right call, regardless of the option they went with, and the town understands; in this case, the PCs earn 120 XP. If the PCs earn 2 to 4 Victory Points, many in Willowshore are unsettled by the event; the PCs earn 60 XP and lose 1 Hope Point. If the PCs earn 1 or fewer Victory Points, the townsfolk are depressed and haunted by the outcome; the PCs earn no XP and lose [[/r 1d4+1]] Hope Points.</p>"
            },
            "Event 8. A Lonely Home": {
              "name": "事件8：孤独的家 Event 8. A Lonely Home",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 8：孤寂的家</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>在云纸屋的事件发生后数周，于本幕的第 10 天，PC 们被一位神情紧张的荒香（Aruka）找上门——她就是本幕开始时建筑坍塌之际被他们救出的那位狐妖女子。（若荒香未能幸存，则改用另一位 PC 们十分喜爱的 NPC，甚至可以用镇上的长者替代。）荒香已从造纸厂的惊险遭遇中恢复，但她担心自己的上司，米娜·卡瓦卡（Myna Kawaka），并解释说建筑的结构损伤也摧毁了卡瓦卡位于上层的私人住处。由于大楼仍在修缮中，卡瓦卡搬回了镇郊那座朴素而传统的老家——那是一幢小房子，在他父母去世、他搬进造纸厂宿舍后便一直无人居住。</p>\n<p>荒香说卡瓦卡已经好几天没离开那座房子了；她和几名造纸厂员工前去查看时，发现他坐在破败建筑的中央，因受寒而发抖，看起来神志恍惚。荒香踏入屋内想把他拖出来、让他去避风处时，他却反抗并哭喊：“不！我得待在这里，在家里——我一直属于这里！”当碎石与残骸开始在屋里四处飞舞，她便意识到这栋建筑真的闹鬼了；在几名同事的协助下，她设法把卡瓦卡拖到安全处。自那以后，公会领袖便沉默寡言、郁郁不乐；他目前在荒香的客房里很安全，但她与其他工人担心卡瓦卡的家被邪灵盘踞。荒香的同事们本打算把废墟烧掉，但她承诺会去请 PC 们帮忙，才勉强阻止了他们；若还有别的解决办法，她宁可不毁掉上司的祖宅。</p>\n<p>荒香请求 PC 们调查此事，并看看能否说服那“邪灵”放过卡瓦卡。那位天狗的祖宅位于镇子南边的林中，旁边有一座几乎坍塌的谷仓（区域 W34）。卡瓦卡的父母起初希望在此开垦农场，却从未真正让计划步入正轨；此后数十年间，这里一直被废弃，连通往林间空地的小径都已杂草丛生。若 PC 们愿意，荒香可以带他们前往，但她不会进入那幢破屋所在的空地。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>卡瓦卡的祖宅确实闹鬼——但并非幽灵所为。真正的元凶是一种名为逝宅神的孤寂生物。这个潜伏的灵体名叫特农（Tenon）；在卡瓦卡的父母去世多年后，卡瓦卡作为独子在几个月后搬离、米娜家作为祖宅的历史就此结束，特农便搬进了这间屋子。在卡瓦卡最近回到这里之前，特农一直独自住在这座缓慢崩坏的废墟中。</p>\n<p>特农目前藏在建筑破损的墙体中，为“客人”被带走而懊恼。PC 们一踏入屋内，他就施展幻觉住宅，试图将所有 PC 困在屋里。若此计失败，他便从墙中现身，含泪请求 PC 们留下来与他同住——他实在太孤单了，同时也惊惧于几年后建筑可能会彻底崩塌，而他的生命也将随之终结。特农不会主动攻击，除非受到挑衅；但一旦开战，他会战斗至死，并在数日后再生归来。</p>\n<p>若 PC 们与他交谈，特农会解释自己的困境：他与这座房子绑定，若无人同住，他将永远孤独。更糟的是，一旦房子最终因风化与疏于照料而毁坏，他也会死去。他只希望有人来此居住并修缮，让这里作为休憩与安全之所的根源得以延续。他希望 PC 们能帮他解决这个问题；但若他们看起来无能为力或不愿意，他便绝望地哭喊并发动攻击——无论这迫使 PC 们逃走还是杀死他都无关紧要，因为就算他被斩杀，也会在几天后再生。</p>\n<p>一个简单的解决方案是让一名 PC 承诺住进农舍并修缮它——若有 PC 自愿承担此责任，将下述行动的结果上调一级成功度。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>解决特农的问题</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">秘密</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你花上一天时间思考特农的问题该如何解决，与卡瓦卡及镇上其他人交谈以尝试招募协助，然后将你的成果回报给特农。进行一次 @Check[diplomacy|dc:22] 检定、@Check[society|dc:24] 检定或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:24] 检定。此行动只能尝试一次，但其他 PC 可以通过在 @Check[diplomacy|dc:20]、@Check[society|dc:20] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20] 检定中成功来协助（Aid）此次尝试。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong>PC 们——与卡瓦卡、老松木以及镇上的几位工匠合作——招募到足够的支援，立即开始加固那座老农舍，确保它能熬过冬季。卡瓦卡与其他镇民同意定期探望特农，避免他感到孤单，直到找到新家庭搬进屋里。许多镇民主动出力，帮助加固建筑并保护其免受即将到来的冬季风暴侵袭，PC 们与镇子的安全都无需为此付出任何代价。PC 们获得 120 XP 与 [[/r 1d4+1]] 希望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>同大成功，但 PC 们必须花费 400 gp，或由城镇消耗 2 安全点，以确保房屋能抵御即将到来的冬天。PC 们获得 80 XP 与 1 希望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>同成功，但镇上没人愿意花时间陪伴一个可能危险且难以预测的灵体——包括卡瓦卡在内。某位 PC 可以承诺在整个冬季陪伴特农：将每周的休整模式行动用于对房屋进行数次长时间探访；然而，若某周没有任何 PC 这么做，他的绝望便会占据上风。在一阵挫败感驱使下，特农不慎破坏了草率的修缮工作，导致房屋坍塌成废墟，并永久杀死特农。若发生此事，这则悲剧消息将使希望点减少 1 点。PC 们获得 40 XP。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong>同失败，但有一位本地人提出要陪伴特农。此人应是最近因镇上有人失踪或死亡而失去挚爱或朋友的人——选择一位符合你战役剧情的 NPC。不幸的是，这名 NPC 只是出于一种错置的责任感才自愿前往，而其悲伤的影响比任何人（包括他自己）所意识到的都更深。该 NPC 的悲痛与特农的悲痛相互叠加，形成破坏性的循环，最终驱使 NPC 在自己仍在屋内时将房子烧毁。柳岸镇的人口减少 1；更糟的是，这场悲剧结局将使希望点减少 [[/r 1d4+1]] 点。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.4RsT9ANu67WgoKMd]{Tenon}</span><span>生物 8</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">小型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">虚体</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">神祇</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵体</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.h6x2FY0mvjGjnzmS]{Floorboards} <br />\n  若 PC 们设法与特农成为朋友，这位逝宅神会透露一件连卡瓦卡都不知道的事——在破屋某块地板下的空洞暗格里，藏着他母亲的<em>+1 轰鸣短弓</em>；他原以为这把武器早已遗失。卡瓦卡握着短弓片刻后，便将其交给 PC 们，说若他们愿意收下这把武器作为他的赠礼，他将深感荣幸，而且他的母亲也会赞同这把武器落入如此英勇之人的手中。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 8: A Lonely Home</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>A few weeks after the events at Cloud Paper House, on the 10th day of the act, the PCs are approached by a nervous-looking Aruka—the kitsune woman whom they rescued during the building’s collapse at the start of this act. (If Aruka didn’t survive, substitute another NPC the PCs have grown fond of, or even the town’s elder.) Aruka has recovered from her ordeal at the paper mill but worries about her boss, Myna Kawaka, and explains that the structural damage to the building also destroyed Kawaka’s personal quarters on an upper floor. While the building is being repaired, Kawaka relocated to his humble and traditional home on the outskirts of town—a small structure that was left unoccupied after his parents died and he moved into accommodations in the paper mill.</p>\n<p>Aruka says that Kawaka hasn’t left that house in a few days, and that upon investigating, she and a few other paper mill employees found him sitting in the middle of the ruined building, shivering from exposure and apparently delirious. When Aruka stepped into the house to try to drag him out to get him to shelter, he fought back and cried out, “No! I need to stay here, at home, where I’ve always belonged!” When bits of rubble and debris began to fly about the place, she knew the building was actually haunted, and with the aid of a few coworkers, she managed to drag Kawaka to safety. Since then, the guild leader has been uncommunicative and sullen; he’s safe now in Aruka’s guest room, but she and the other workers fear that Kawaka’s home is infested with an evil spirit. Aruka’s coworkers were ready to burn the ruin down, but she managed to prevent this by promising to ask the PCs for help; she would rather not destroy her boss’s family home if there’s another possible solution.</p>\n<p>Aruka asks the PCs to investigate the situation and find out if they can convince the “evil spirit” to let Kawaka go. The tengu’s family home is located in the woods south of town, next to a mostly collapsed barn (area W34). Kawaka’s parents initially hoped to start a farm here but never got that venture off the ground, and in the decades since, the place has been abandoned; even the footpath leading to the clearing is overgrown. Aruka offers to escort the PCs to the location if they wish, but she won’t enter the clearing in which the decrepit house stands.</p>\n<p><strong>Creature:</strong> Kawaka’s family home is indeed haunted, but not by a ghost. The actual culprit is a lonely creature known as a silsyche. Named Tenon, this lurking spirit moved into the house after its long run as the Myna family home ended when Kawaka, the only child, moved out a few months after his parents’ death years ago. Until Kawaka’s recent return, Tenon lived alone in the slowly crumbling ruin.</p>\n<p>Tenon is currently hiding in the building’s ruined walls, frustrated that his guest has been taken away. As soon as the PCs enter, he uses Hallucinatory Home to try to trap all of the PCs inside. If that fails, he steps out of the walls to tearfully ask the PCs to stay in the home with him—he’s so lonely, but he’s also frightened that in a few years, the building might fully crumble apart, and that with it, so shall his life. Tenon won’t attack unless provoked, but he fights to the death in that case, only to rejuvenate a few days later.</p>\n<p>If the PCs speak to him, Tenon explains the situation he faces: he’s bound to this home, and if no one lives here with him, he’ll be lonely forever. Worse, once the home is finally destroyed by erosion and neglect, he’ll die. He only wants someone to come live in the home and repair it so that its tradition as a place of rest and safety can continue. He hopes the PCs can help him solve this problem, but if they seem unable or unwilling, he cries out in despair and attacks—whether this causes the PCs to flee or kill him is irrelevant, since even if they slay him, he’ll just rejuvenate in a few days.</p>\n<p>One simple solution is for a PC to commit to living in the farmhouse and repairing it—if a PC volunteers for this responsibility, adjust the result of the following activity up by one degree of success.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Solving Tenon’s Problem</h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Secret</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend the day considering a solution to Tenon’s problem, speaking to Kawaka and others in town to try to recruit assistance, and then report the results of your work back to Tenon. Attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:22] check, a @Check[society|dc:24] check, or a @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:24] check. This activity can only be attempted once, but other PCs can Aid this attempt by succeeding at a @Check[diplomacy|dc:20], @Check[society|dc:20], or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20] check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The PCs—working with Kawaka, Old Matsuki, and several artisans in town—recruit enough support to begin work on shoring up the old farmhouse at once, ensuring that it will survive the winter. Kawaka and other townsfolk agree to visit Tenon regularly to keep him from getting lonely until a new family can be found to live in the house. Many townsfolk pitch in to help shore up and protect the building from the winter storms yet to come, at no cost to the PCs or the town’s security. The PCs earn 120 XP and [[/r 1d4+1]] Hope Points.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the PCs must either spend 400 gp or the town must expend 2 Security Points to ensure the house is protected from the coming winter. The PCs earn 80 XP and 1 Hope Point.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> As success, but no one in town is interested in spending time with a potentially dangerous and unpredictable spirit, including Kawaka. A PC can commit to keeping Tenon company through the winter by making several lengthy visits to the house as their weekly downtime activity; however, if no PC performs this in a week, his despair takes over. In a fit of frustration, Tenon accidentally damages the slipshod repair work on the house, causing the house to collapse into ruins, killing Tenon permanently. If this occurs, the tragic news costs 1 Hope Point. The PCs earn 40 XP.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but a local offers to keep Tenon company. This local should be someone who recently lost a loved one or friend to a vanishing or death in town—choose an NPC who fits your game’s story. Unfortunately, this NPC is only volunteering out of a misplaced sense of obligation and has been more affected by their grief than anyone (including themself) realizes. This NPC’s grief compounds with Tenon’s, forming a destructive cycle that eventually compels the NPC to burn the house down while they’re inside. Reduce Willowshore’s population by 1; worse, the tragic end costs [[/r 1d4+1]] Hope Points.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.4RsT9ANu67WgoKMd]{Tenon}</span><span>Creature 8</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Small</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Incorporeal</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Kami</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Spirit</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.h6x2FY0mvjGjnzmS]{Floorboards} <br />\n  If the PCs manage to befriend Tenon, the silsyche reveals something that not even Kawaka knows—hidden in a hollow below one of the ruined house’s floorboards is his mother’s <em>+1 thundering shortbow</em>, a weapon he’d assumed was lost. After holding the shortbow for a moment, Kawaka hands it to the PCs, saying he would be honored if they took this weapon as a gift from him and that his mother would approve of it being in such heroic hands.\n</p>"
            },
            "Event 7. The Fox Ghost": {
              "name": "事件 7：狐幽灵（特征） Event 7. The Fox Ghost",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 7：狐妖幽灵</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>冬季的狩猎与采集收获寥寥，但即便日子愈发严酷，仍有少数本地人继续靠这些营生讨生活。在这场遭遇的前期，一些猎人发现他们的数个陷阱与隐蔽处被撕开，并且有部分被烧焦。无论PC们是选择调查，还是在旅行途中偶然撞见案发现场，在这场遭遇中他们都能当场抓到肇事者。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-rin.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Rin\" alt=\"female kitsune with elemental fire powers\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-rin.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>肇事者看起来是个半野性的少女人类，身穿一袭被熏焦的连衣裙，怀里抱着一只烧焦的小狐狸。她触碰到的东西都会被部分烧灼，这也正是她能撕开陷阱并熏焦本地树木的原因。这个女孩名叫凛（Rin），是一名狐妖幽灵，她在许多个轮回之前意外闯入柳岸镇的思维空间，并被困在此处。她与她的幼弟悠（Yuu）死于另一座人类捕兽村落之手：那座村落认定当地狐狸是一连串超自然厄运的源头，于是烧毁了她的山中家园，意图杀死所有居住于此的狐妖。</p>\n<p>由于这段创伤，凛憎恨捕兽人，也憎恨人类。她的态度起始为不友善，因为她认为PC们会因她毁坏陷阱而发怒并惩罚她。被抓到时，她会逃跑，除非PC们成功通过一次 @Check[diplomacy|dc:27] 检定来阻止她。显露自己同为狐妖的狐妖角色在此检定上获得+2环境加值。若PC们攻击她、威胁她，或在交涉检定中大失败，她会试图对冒犯者施加她的狐火诅咒，然后逃离。PC可以通过追随她一路无法避免留下的细小焦痕来再次追踪到凛：成功通过一次 @Check[survival|dc:28|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]。</p>\n<p>若PC们将凛的态度调整为不关心，她愿意在抽泣间隙回答问题，尽管除了自身的悲惨遭遇外她所知甚少。她也愿意待在PC们能再次找到她的地方，但除非她的态度提升至友善，否则她拒绝进入柳岸镇。若她确实变得友善，凛最常被发现与本地年轻人一起玩耍：时而尖叫着朝他们扔东西，时而又帮他们策划夜间恶作剧。若PC们问凛要怎样才能帮助她安息，她会耸耸肩说：“只要我能走，我就会走，但这个地方暂时把我留在这里。”当PC们在本幕末尾迁移柳岸镇时，他们将能进一步帮助凛——见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12concludingth00]{Concluding the Act}。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.PblvhzuySMcnHQO2]{Rin}</span><span>生物 8</span></h2>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.XyhI61LwKFrbynGO]{Rin's Gift} <br />\n  若PC们将凛的态度提升至友善，这名幽灵会感谢PC们的善意，并献出自身的一部分作为回报——她俯身从地上拾起一块扁平的石头，石头飘浮起来，随后在她的虚体之手中燃起火焰。她将这块漂浮燃烧的石头放入一名PC手中，石头立刻冷却，显露出其本体是一枚<em>炽焰武器符石</em>。凛只能施展这把戏一次。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们将凛的态度提升至友善，给予他们120 XP。若允许她来到柳岸镇生活，本地人起初会心存戒备；这将花费 [[/r 1d4]] 希望点。随着时间推移，本地人对这位坚韧的年轻幽灵及其顽皮行径的钦佩，会让他们意识到并非所有幽灵都残忍。在此后每一周开始、当你计算城镇损耗时，柳岸镇获得1希望点。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 7: The Fox Ghost</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Hunting and foraging is a sparse business in winter, yet still, a few locals continue to ply their trades even as the days grow crueler. In the lead-up to this encounter, some hunters find several of their traps and blinds have been ripped open and partially burned. Whether the PCs choose to investigate or stumble upon the scene of the crime while traveling, they can catch the culprit in the act in this encounter.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-rin.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Rin\" alt=\"female kitsune with elemental fire powers\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-rin.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creature:</strong> The culprit appears to be a half-feral human girl clad in a singed dress and clutching a burned fox kit in her arms. She partially burns anything she touches, which is what allowed her to rip open the traps and singe the local trees. This girl is Rin, a kitsune ghost who accidentally stumbled into Willowshore’s mindscape and became trapped here many cycles ago. She and her baby brother Yuu died when a different human trapper village, convinced the local foxes were the cause of some supernatural misfortune, burned down her mountain home to kill all of the kitsune who lived there.</p>\n<p>Due to this trauma, Rin hates human trappers and humans in general. Her attitude begins at unfriendly, as she assumes the PCs will be mad and punish her for destroying the traps. She runs when caught unless the PCs succeed at a @Check[diplomacy|dc:27] check to stop her. Kitsune who reveal themselves as such receive a +2 circumstance bonus to this check. If the PCs attack her, threaten her, or critically fail the Diplomacy check, she attempts to inflict her foxfire curse on the offender and then flees. A PC can track Rin down again by following the small singe marks she can’t help but leave in passing by succeeding at a @Check[survival|dc:28|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track].</p>\n<p>If the PCs adjust Rin’s attitude to indifferent, she’s willing to answer questions in between her sobs, though she knows very little outside of her own tragic circumstances. She’s also willing to stay in a place where the PCs can find her again but refuses to enter Willowshore unless her attitude is increased to friendly. If she does become friendly, Rin is most often found playing with local youths, alternating between screaming and throwing things at them or helping them with their nighttime pranks. If the PCs ask Rin how they can help her rest, she shrugs and says, “As soon as I can go, I shall, but this place keeps me here for now.” When the PCs transmigrate Willowshore at the end of the act, they’ll be able to help Rin further—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12concludingth00]{Concluding the Act}.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.PblvhzuySMcnHQO2]{Rin}</span><span>Creature 8</span></h2>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.XyhI61LwKFrbynGO]{Rin's Gift} <br />\n  If the PCs increase Rin’s attitude to friendly, the ghost thanks the PCs for their kindness and offers them a part of herself as reward—she reaches down to pick up a flat stone off the ground, the stone floating and then igniting with fire in her incorporeal hand. She drops the floating, burning stone into a PC’s hand, whereupon it instantly cools, revealing itself to be a <em>flaming weapon runestone</em>. Rin can perform this trick only once.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs increase Rin’s attitude to friendly, grant them 120 XP. If she’s allowed to come to Willowshore to live, the locals are initially wary; this costs [[/r 1d4]] Hope Points. Over time, their admiration of the tenacious young ghost and her playful antics causes the locals to realize not all ghosts are cruel. At the start of each following week when you calculate the town’s attrition, Willowshore gains 1 Hope Point.</p>"
            },
            "Event 6. Little Gifts": {
              "name": "事件6：小小赋礼 Event 6. Little Gifts",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 6: Little Gifts\">事件6：小小赠礼</h2>\n<p>在前一幕中，PC们可能已经交好小暗。若这段友谊得以延续，小暗会继续给它偏爱的PC带来礼物。若英雄们把何知府的猫黑豆带到茶馆，小暗会容忍黑豆的存在，但化猫往往会欺负这只更小的猫，拍打黑豆的脑袋。</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>[[/r 1d8]]{掷骰}</th>\n      <th>结果</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>一只被咬嚼过一部分的折纸鹤（@UUID[Actor.uSTSi74yrGrzxkPF]{小暗的礼物}）。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>一只被吃掉一部分的麻雀（可能还活着）（@UUID[Actor.nAJlff0aVAUZHCNJ]{小暗的礼物}）。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>一个被压扁的柠檬（@UUID[Actor.X8QcN6wybCNHBZQz]{小暗的礼物}）。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>一只来自包子嫲嫲的鲜肉包子（@UUID[Actor.DZsoGYsk1MFGvGCh]{小暗的礼物}）。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>一个<em>阴森战利品</em>护符，看起来像是一只仍在滴血的人耳（@UUID[Actor.zaxPVMQh7PG8a7Yc]{小暗的礼物}）。*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>一袋防水的番红花，价值100 gp（@UUID[Actor.8hBfwikWrbBFYoXf]{小暗的礼物}）。*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>一颗<em>高等烟雾弹</em>（@UUID[Actor.dx5cJZoETeE4Ot2E]{小暗的礼物}）*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>一顶<em>高等法师帽</em>，目前呈幞头“展脚幞头”的形态（一顶黑帽子，两侧有两片细长、硬挺、如翼般的帽翅）（@UUID[Actor.x30AI8eg5YTkCJsz]{小暗的礼物}）。*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td class=\"note\" colspan=\"2\">该礼物只能掷出一次；之后若再次掷到该礼物，将其视为1枚白金币。</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 6: Little Gifts\">Event 6: Little Gifts</h2>\n<p>In the previous act, the PCs could befriend Yami. If this friendship persists, Yami continues to bring gifts to favored PCs. Yami tolerates the presence of Black Bean should the heroes bring Governor Heh’s cat to the teahouse, but the bakeneko tends to bully the smaller cat by smacking Black Bean on the head.</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>[[/r 1d8]]{Roll}</th>\n      <th>Result</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>A partially chewed origami crane (@UUID[Actor.uSTSi74yrGrzxkPF]{Yami's Gift}).</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>A partially eaten sparrow (possibly still alive) (@UUID[Actor.nAJlff0aVAUZHCNJ]{Yami's Gift}).</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>A squished lemon (@UUID[Actor.X8QcN6wybCNHBZQz]{Yami's Gift}).</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>A fresh dumpling from Mama Bao’s (@UUID[Actor.DZsoGYsk1MFGvGCh]{Yami's Gift}).</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>A <em>grim trophy</em> talisman that appears to be a still-bloody human ear (@UUID[Actor.zaxPVMQh7PG8a7Yc]{Yami's Gift}).*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>A waterproof bag of saffron worth 100 gp (@UUID[Actor.8hBfwikWrbBFYoXf]{Yami's Gift}).*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>A <em>greater smoke ball</em> (@UUID[Actor.dx5cJZoETeE4Ot2E]{Yami's Gift})*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>A <em>greater mage’s hat</em> currently in the form of a zhanjiao putou (a black hat with two long, stiff, wing-like flaps) (@UUID[Actor.x30AI8eg5YTkCJsz]{Yami's Gift}).*</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td class=\"note\" colspan=\"2\">This gift can only be rolled once; treat further rolls of this gift as 1 platinum coin.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
            },
            "Event 5. Faceless Evil": {
              "name": "事件5：无面之恶 Event 5. Faceless Evil",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件5：无面之恶</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>从和善保的思维空间里跟着PC们出来的不只有总督的宅邸。即便PC们在上一章杀死了他们的无面鬼模仿者，等PC们返回后，柳岸镇里仍会出现更多这种扰乱秩序的妖怪来制造麻烦。作为其显现的一部分，无面鬼会获得其复制的那名PC的脸，但会刻意在PC们不常去的镇区活动。起初它们会做些小却恶毒的事，比如把针藏进别人的食物里、侮辱PC们结交的NPC，或用颜料破坏PC们支持的地点，随后事态升级到谋杀。一旦PC们察觉哪里不对，他们就必须迅速行动，拯救自己的名声与村民的性命。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>若无人干预，无面鬼每[[/r 1d4]]天就会犯下一起事件。PC们会在第一起事件发生后的第二天得知无面鬼的存在：一名PC们未曾结交的NPC（更好的是，已经与PC们敌对的那种）会怒气冲冲地来找他们，指控其中一名PC“把针塞进你给我的饺子里！”，随后张开嘴展示他们遭受的不适伤口。若被指控的PC未能通过一次成功的@Check[diplomacy|dc:20]检定，该NPC就会向任何愿意听的人抱怨这场恶意的恶作剧，而到当天结束时，PC们会从你选择的一个阵营中失去1点声望点。（记录下因本事件而失去的所有声望点，因为若PC们妥善解决此事，他们很有机会把这些点数赢回来。）</p>\n<p>虽然柳岸镇居民起初愿意接受“PC们是被栽赃的”这一安抚（在这一幕的过程中已经发生了足够多的怪事，让人几乎没法理性地提出抗议），但这种说法不会长久奏效。毕竟，PC们离开过村子，还把鼻子伸进各种怪地方——这意味着他们很可能已经被杀并被某种可怖之物取代；甚至更糟，他们可能已经暗中堕入了他们一直在对抗的腐化！</p>\n<p>每[[/r 1d4]]天，就会发生一次类似事件，并相应失去1点声望点。当无面鬼模仿者进行第5次“恶作剧”时，会有一名次要NPC因此死亡（柳岸镇人口减少1），这让它们尝到暴力的滋味。此后的每一次恶作剧都会导致新的谋杀。每发生一起谋杀，都会使PC们从两个阵营中各失去3点声望点。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-noppera-bo-impersinator.webp\" />\n\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">无面之恶</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等8 </span></h2>\n\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nopperaboimp00]{无面鬼模仿者（4）} | @UUID[Actor.vFNg9BATB9crqnDn]{奥术} @UUID[Actor.aYR61sI47XlE9ul8]{神术} @UUID[Actor.2NmupNwbuAt5GcWy]{武技}@UUID[Actor.UgfzkrEkFrdeegD0]{异能} @UUID[Actor.vmOACyFUJqWHY8YD]{原能} @UUID[Actor.n9L4akwW1KlBXQQd]{技巧}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>每天一次，一名PC可以花费数小时（除了其正在进行的任何每周休整模式行动之外）通过尝试一次秘密@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]、@Check[society|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]或@Check[perception|dc:26|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]检定来调查这一谜团。成功时，他们确认模仿者已潜入城镇；大成功时，无面鬼不会立刻注意到PC们，使他们有时间设下伏击，或将一只无面鬼从其他同伴身边引开。面对乐子要结束，模仿者会战斗至死以除掉PC们；在攻击队伍之前，它们会尽可能先集结成一组。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们公开揭露其模仿者的本质，这一令人不安的真相会使队伍失去1点希望点（若至少发生过一起谋杀，则失去1d6点希望点）。若没有镇民被谋杀，则他们因本事件失去的所有声望点都会被恢复。每发生一起谋杀，就会使以此方式恢复的声望点总数减少2点。</p>\n<p>若本事件期间没有镇民被谋杀，则给予PC们40 XP；每有一名本地人被谋杀，将该XP奖励减少10。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 5: Faceless Evil</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The governor’s manor isn’t the only thing that followed the PCs from Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape. Even if the PCs slew their noppera-bo impersonators in the previous chapter, more of these disruptive yokai appear in Willowshore to cause trouble after the PCs return. As part of their manifestation, the noppera-bos gain their duplicated PC’s face but make sure to operate in parts of town the PCs don’t frequent. They initially perform small but spiteful acts, like hiding needles in people’s food, insulting NPCs the PCs have befriended, or vandalizing PC-supported locations with paint, before escalating toward murder. Once the PCs catch wind that something is wrong, they need to act quickly to save their reputations and the lives of the villagers.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> If left to their own devices, the noppera-bos perpetrate an incident every [[/r 1d4]] days. The PCs are alerted to the noppera-bos’ presence the day after the first of these incidents, when an NPC whom the PCs haven’t befriended (or better yet, one who’s become antagonistic) approaches them angrily, then accuses one of the PCs of “stuffing needles into the dumplings you gave me!” before opening their mouth to show off the uncomfortable wounds they’ve suffered. Without a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:20] check from the accused PC, the NPC complains about the mean-spirited prank to anyone who’ll listen, and by the end of the day, the PCs lose 1 Reputation Point from a faction of your choice. (Keep track of all Reputation Points lost as a result of this event, as the PCs have a good chance of regaining them if they resolve this event well.)</p>\n<p>While the residents of Willowshore are initially willing to accept reassurance that the PCs are being framed (enough strange things have happened over the course of the act that it’s hardly rational to protest), they won’t be placated by this for long. After all, the PCs have been out of the village and have been sticking their noses in strange places, meaning it’s just as likely they’ve been killed and replaced by something horrible—or worse, that they’ve secretly fallen to the corruption they’ve been fighting against!</p>\n<p>Every [[/r 1d4]] days, a similar event takes place, along with a corresponding loss of 1 Reputation Point. When the noppera-bo impersonators perform their 5th “prank,” a minor NPC dies as a result (reduce Willowshore’s population by 1), giving them the taste for violence. Every following prank results in a new murder. Every murder that takes place results in a loss of 3 Reputation Points from both factions.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-noppera-bo-impersinator.webp\" />\n\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Faceless Evil</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 8 </span></h2>\n\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nopperaboimp00]{Noppera-bo Impersonators (4)} | @UUID[Actor.vFNg9BATB9crqnDn]{Arcane} @UUID[Actor.aYR61sI47XlE9ul8]{Divine} @UUID[Actor.2NmupNwbuAt5GcWy]{Martial}@UUID[Actor.UgfzkrEkFrdeegD0]{Occult} @UUID[Actor.vmOACyFUJqWHY8YD]{Primal} @UUID[Actor.n9L4akwW1KlBXQQd]{Skilled}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Once per day, a PC can spend a few hours (in addition to any weekly downtime activity they’re pursuing) Investigating this mystery by attempting a secret @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate], @Check[society|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate], or @Check[perception|dc:26|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate] check. On a success, they confirm that impersonators have infiltrated the town, and on a critical success, the noppera-bos don’t immediately notice the PCs, giving them time to set up an ambush or lure a noppera-bo away from the others. Faced with the end of their fun, the impersonators fight to the death to eliminate the PCs, gathering as a group if they can before they attack the party.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs publicly reveal the nature of their impersonators, the unsettling revelation costs the party 1 Hope Point (or 1d6 Hope Points if there has been at least one murder). All Reputation Points they lose as a result of this event are restored if no townsfolk were murdered. Each murder that took place lowers the total Reputation Points restored in this manner by 2.</p>\n<p>Grant the PCs 40 XP if no townsfolk were murdered during this event; reduce this XP reward by 10 for each murdered local.</p>"
            },
            "Unexpected Troubles": {
              "name": "意外麻烦 Unexpected Troubles",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Unexpected Troubles\">意外麻烦</h2>\n<p>每周开始时，进行一次 @Check[flat|dc:16]。成功时，柳岸镇会遭遇并发症。也许镇里有人吃得超过自己应得的份额，或是某些食物储藏发生了腐坏蔓延。风暴可能损坏了镇上建筑的屋顶，或突如其来的暴雨引发了洪水。也许无望与厄运的流言正在镇上传播，居民开始意识到自身处境的严峻。</p>\n<p>若确实发生了未预见的并发症，就在本页顶部的表格上掷骰，以确定发生了何种麻烦，并得知由于本周意外损耗而额外失去了多少准备点数。PC可以选择用这一周的休整模式来将这些影响降到最低，尝试进行表中所示的技能检定（其他PC可以进行休整模式活动来援助该检定）。大成功或大失败中，大成功则不失去任何点数。成功则只失去1点。大成功或大失败中，大失败则失去的点数加倍。若PC使用了特别乐于帮助的法术、仪式或其他策略，你可以允许他们将该检定结果的成功等级提高一级。</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>掷骰</th>\n      <th>准备点损失</th>\n      <th>用DC 24的……将影响降到最低</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–2</td>\n      <td>[[/r 1d4]] 食物点</td>\n      <td>@Check[nature|dc:24] 或 @Check[survival|dc:24] 检定</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3–4</td>\n      <td>[[/r 1d4+2]] 希望点</td>\n      <td>@Check[diplomacy|dc:24] 或 @Check[performance|dc:24] 检定</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5–6</td>\n      <td>[[/r 1d4]] 安全点</td>\n      <td>@Check[athletics|dc:24] 或 @Check[crafting|dc:24] 检定</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>为柳岸镇创造食物</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇有超过200张饥饿的嘴需要喂饱，而施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Mt6ZzkVX8Q4xigFq]{创造食物} 所产生的餐食不会持续超过一天，这使得该选项作为提高食物点的手段受到限制。不过，在柳岸镇以0食物点开始的一周里，该法术仍能拯救生命。若在这样的周里失去1点希望点将导致2d6名当地人死亡，则只要PC在希望点损失发生后的1小时内施放足够多的创造食物法术，以喂饱至少12人（不论 [[/r 2d6]] 掷骰结果如何），就能阻止这些死亡发生。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Unexpected Troubles\">Unexpected Troubles</h2>\n<p>At the start of every week, attempt a @Check[flat|dc:16]. On a success, Willowshore faces complications. Perhaps someone in town has been eating more than their share or decay has spread through some of the food stores. A storm might have damaged the roofs of buildings in town or sudden rains could’ve caused flooding. Perhaps rumors of hopelessness and doom have been spreading through town as the citizens begin to realize the gravity of their situation.</p>\n<p>If unforeseen complications do occur, roll on the table at the top of this page to determine what sort of trouble takes place and to find out how many additional Preparation Points are lost as a result of the unexpected attrition for the week. A PC can choose to spend their week’s downtime to minimize these effects by attempting the indicated skill check (other PCs can take downtime activities to Aid this check). On a critical success, no points are lost. On a success, only 1 point is lost. On a critical failure, twice as many points are lost. If the PCs use a particularly helpful spell, ritual, or other tactic, you can permit them to increase the result of this check by one degree of success if you like.</p>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Roll</th>\n      <th>Preparation Point Loss</th>\n      <th>Minimize with a DC 24...</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1–2</td>\n      <td>[[/r 1d4]] Food Points</td>\n      <td>@Check[nature|dc:24] or @Check[survival|dc:24] check</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3–4</td>\n      <td>[[/r 1d4+2]] Hope Points</td>\n      <td>@Check[diplomacy|dc:24] or @Check[performance|dc:24] check</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5–6</td>\n      <td>[[/r 1d4]] Security Points</td>\n      <td>@Check[athletics|dc:24] or @Check[crafting|dc:24] check</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Creating Food for Willowshore</h1>\n  <p>There are over 200 hungry mouths to feed in Willowshore, and meals from castings of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Mt6ZzkVX8Q4xigFq]{Create Food} don’t last longer than a day, which limits this option as a way to bolster Food Points. The spell can save lives, though, on weeks where Willowshore begins with 0 Food Points. If the loss of a Hope Point during such a week would result in the deaths of 2d6 locals, the PCs can prevent those deaths if they cast enough create food spells to feed a minimum of 12 people (regardless of the result of the [[/r 2d6]] die roll) within an hour of the Hope Point loss occurring.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Winter Events": {
              "name": "冬季事件 Winter Events",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Winter Events\">冬季事件</h1>\n<p>在PC们必须等待、直到他们能够施放transmigrate的这几周里，冬天可不会等待；随着一周周过去，小镇必须承受希望、食物与安全的逐步消耗，具体如本幕开头第151页所述。</p>\n<p>除了这种稳定的消耗之外，随着冬季无情推进，还会发生数个其他事件。不同于“第二幕：任落叶飘零”中秋季每周都会发生一个事件，冬季期间发生的事件要么被安排在特定日期，要么留作可在任何时间发生。下方时间线概述了这13个事件应当发生的时间（也包括前一章中的事件）。你可以在游戏中按需调整这些日期，以配合游戏进程的起伏与节奏！</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>冬季时间线</h2>\n  <p>本幕中的事件应当大致按以下顺序发生。未对应特定日期的事件标为“任意”，但仍应在其后列出的事件之前发生。</p>\n  <p><strong>第1天</strong> 第8章的事件；之后PC们即可施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift}，随心所欲地前往和善保的思维空间。</p>\n  <p><strong>从和善保的思维空间返回后的第二天</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event4shinzo00]{事件4：神藏的回答}。@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event5facele00]{事件5——无面之恶}开始；PC们可以开始研究transmigration</p>\n  <p><strong>每7天</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event6little00]{事件6——小小赠礼}</p>\n  <p><strong>任意</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event7thefox00]{事件7——狐狸幽灵}</p>\n  <p><strong>第10天</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event8alonel00]{事件8——孤寂的家}</p>\n  <p><strong>任意</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event8alonel00]{事件8——孤寂的家}</p>\n  <p><strong>第21天</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event10thecl00]{事件10——陶光节}；冬季的第一个实际日子。</p>\n  <p><strong>任意</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{事件11——疫鸟的早午餐}</p>\n  <p><strong>任意</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event12these00]{事件12——降神会}</p>\n  <p><strong>第44天</strong> 最早在这一天，为施放<em>transmigrate</em>而准备的榊木板条将会就绪。</p>\n  <p><strong>第71天</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event13inter00]{事件13——与蜘蛛的访谈}</p>\n  <p><strong>第72天（元旦）</strong> 此时PC们可开始将<em>transmigrate</em>作为一个5环仪式进行施放。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>运行这些事件的一个好方法，是以按周安排的休整模式来进行。每过一周，先调整柳岸镇的消耗，然后让每位玩家进行一项休整模式行动。之后，再演绎在该周预定发生的任何事件（这些事件不会影响PC们在所选休整模式事务上花费的时间）。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Winter Events\">Winter Events</h1>\n<p>During the weeks the PCs must wait before they can cast transmigrate, winter doesn’t wait, and as the weeks go by, the town must endure the attrition of hope, food, and security as detailed on page 151 at the start of this act.</p>\n<p>In addition to this steady attrition, several other events take place as winter marches ceaselessly onward. Unlike “Act 2: Let the Leaves Fall,” where an event took place every week of the fall season, the events that take place during winter are either scheduled to occur on specific days or are left open to happen at any time. The following timeline summarizes when these 13 events should occur, including those in the previous chapter. Feel free to adjust these dates as needed in your game to account for the ebb and flow of play!</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Winter Timeline</h2>\n  <p>The events in this act should occur in roughly the following order. Events that aren’t keyed to specific days are listed as “Any,” but should still take place before those that follow.</p>\n  <p><strong>Day 1</strong> Chapter 8’s events, after which the PCs can cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VJgSQBYwXGDbMmiW]{Mindscape Shift} to visit Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape as they wish.</p>\n  <p><strong>The day after returning from Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event4shinzo00]{Event 4. Shinzo’s Answers}. @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event5facele00]{Event 5 - Faceless Evil} begins; the PCs can start researching transmigration</p>\n  <p><strong>Every 7 days</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event6little00]{Event 6 - Little Gifts}</p>\n  <p><strong>Any</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event7thefox00]{Event 7 - The Fox Ghost}</p>\n  <p><strong>Day 10</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event8alonel00]{Event 8 - A Lonely Home}</p>\n  <p><strong>Any</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event8alonel00]{Event 8 - A Lonely Home}</p>\n  <p><strong>Day 21</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event10thecl00]{Event 10 - The Claylight Festival}; first actual day of winter.</p>\n  <p><strong>Any</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{Event 11 - Nosois’ Brunch}</p>\n  <p><strong>Any</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event12these00]{Event 12 - The Seance}</p>\n  <p><strong>Day 44</strong> The earliest day by which the prepared sakaki slats for casting <em>transmigrate</em> will be ready.</p>\n  <p><strong>Day 71</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event13inter00]{Event 13 - Interview with a Spider}</p>\n  <p><strong>Day 72 (New Year’s Day)</strong> The PCs can begin casting <em>transmigrate</em> as a 5th-level ritual at this point.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>A good way to run these events is via downtime mode on a week-by-week schedule. Each week that passes, adjust Willowshore’s attrition, then allow each player to pursue a downtime activity. After that, play out any events scheduled to take place during that week (these events won’t impact the time the PCs spend on a chosen downtime pursuit).</p>"
            },
            "Researching Transmigration": {
              "name": "研究转生 Researching Transmigration",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Researching Transmigration\">研究灵魂迁渡</h1>\n<section class=\"handout\">\n  <p>关于灵魂迁渡的笔记</p>\n  <p>尽管显然赫赫总督并不知道他的思维空间只是柳岸镇所困在的更大思维空间的缩小版，他的研究依然很有价值，可概括如下。</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>赫赫总督在春季最后一天试图加固库伽普提牢笼的失败行动以灾难告终，镇上所有人全部丧生。赫赫总督被困在他自己的小思维空间里，而其他所有人则被困在包含该地区柳岸腹地在内的更大思维空间中。</li>\n    <li>尽管所有人都死了，但他们如今仍“活着”，被困在这个不断重复、为期一年的思维空间里。赫赫总督把灵魂在这种思维空间中塑造出新身体称为“灵魂迁渡”——他也用这个词来指代这种人回到活人世界的概念。按此定义，灵魂迁渡与转生术相似，只是为被杀害的灵魂创造的新身体并非不同的身体；相反，它正是该灵魂在最近一次生命中所拥有的同一个身体。</li>\n    <li>赫赫总督关于灵魂迁渡仪式的公式将允许被困在此思维空间中的人，利用从柳岸镇的<em>长明灯</em>照出的光芒，从这个思维空间前往活人世界，但这些笔记并不完整：一部分原因是他不了解转生术仪式，另一部分原因则是他独自研究，且在灵性学识方面并不精通。对于了解转生术仪式，或在神秘学或宗教事务上更有学识的人而言，完成这项工作会容易得多。</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>赫赫总督的笔记以通用语写成，但阅读它们需要8小时的工作。一旦PC阅读了这些日志与笔记，他们学到的关键要点总结在上方的“仪式笔记”讲义中。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-ritualcomponents.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ritual Components\" alt=\"Ritual Components\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-ritualcomponents.webp')\" />\n<p>PC们应当已在前一幕发现了@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.gIVaSCrLhhBzGHQY]{Reincarnate}的公式。凭借这些笔记与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kqhPt9344UkcGVYO]{Resurrect}的公式（即便他们还不能完全学会或施放该仪式），他们完成总督工作的条件已远胜于当初的他。尽管如此，PC们仍必须投入时间继续研究并开发@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}，之后才能尝试施放该仪式。要研究此仪式，PC们必须花费8小时研究该主题，并使用以下研究数据表来追踪进度。</p>\n<p>知晓@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.gIVaSCrLhhBzGHQY]{Reincarnate}或@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kqhPt9344UkcGVYO]{Resurrect}的PC，将把所有这些研究检定的DC降低2。若两者都知晓，则把所有这些研究检定的DC降低4。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">灵魂迁渡</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">研究 8</span>\n  </h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>独立调查</strong> 你花一天时间检视赫赫总督的笔记，并推演你自己关于<em>灵魂迁渡</em>仪式可能如何运作的理论；<strong>最大RP</strong> 3</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[academia-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]或@Check[library-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]，或@Check[arcana|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]或@Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>请教专家</strong> 你花一天时间与当地专家讨论该主题；<strong>最大RP</strong> 每名NPC 2</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[arcana|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]（在主母之绾请教井川十兵卫）；@Check[nature|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]（请教木灵大尊柳）；@Check[occultism|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]（拜访期间请教真三）；@Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]（在司魂娘娘庙向伊丽丝·堪多拉请教）</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>在神社静思</strong> 你花一天时间安静思考或祈祷，在柳岸镇众多神社之一或自然景致优美之处冥想；<strong>最大RP</strong> 3</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>研究检定</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]或@Check[religion|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research ]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>2点研究点数</strong> 让死者复生的仪式通常需要一具尸体（或至少其一部分）。在此情形下并不存在尸体，但赫赫总督关于用<em>长明灯</em>的光作为此世与生者领域之间某种“通道”的想法，是解决该问题的绝妙方案。给予PC 10 XP。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4点研究点数</strong> 纳入一个对长寿与生命本身的隐喻性致意与让步至关重要——鹭羽长期以来被认为能活数百年，并能在灵魂过渡到新生命时“净化”之，这将完美契合。羽毛应从活鸟身上采集，且在仪式施放时那只鸟必须仍然活着。除此之外，焚烧稀有香料与经特殊处理的榊木薄板，是该仪式的最佳材料；但制备这些榊木薄板的过程既昂贵又耗时。更令人振奋的是，有线索表明更强力版本的灵魂迁渡或许能让远不止PC的更多灵魂逃离思维空间。给予PC 20 XP。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6点研究点数</strong> 赫赫总督的大多数研究都聚焦于“牺牲”的概念——尤其是牺牲一条生命，以推动另一条“更值得的”生命离开这座思维空间炼狱；被牺牲的生命会在巨大的窑炉中、置于陶土外壳内被仪式性焚化。之所以如此，倒不是总督嗜恶，而更多是他在转生知识匮乏下不得不做出的让步。研究至此，某位PC灵光乍现——若改为将要迁渡的人置入陶土外壳，再在巨大的窑炉中烧制，那么对生命的“牺牲”便可被内化，使得只有迁渡目标受到影响。当然，未能正确执行仪式可能导致痛苦（甚至致命）的烧伤，但对任何希望避免以一命换一命的人来说，这样的风险也值得。更宏大的灵魂迁渡仪式的可能性也得到确认——它甚至可能允许PC把镇上的建筑结构也一并迁渡到活人世界，用以替换那里的现存废墟。给予PC 30 XP。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>8点研究点数</strong> PC完成了<em>灵魂迁渡</em>的公式，这是一种从<em>长明灯</em>汲取成功所需力量的仪式。PC也得知，只要活人世界中的<em>长明灯</em>仍未点亮（由真三向他们揭示），他们就只能施放该仪式的4环版本，而无法施放能更永久返回活人世界的5环版本。给予PC 60 XP。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>建造窑炉：</strong>PC们必须建造一座足够大、能让所有人都置身其中以接受灵魂迁渡的窑炉。这样做需要一周的工作、花费25 gp资源，并且需要一名角色在一次@Check[crafting|dc:20]检定中成功。若PC得到永火铁厂的支持，其所有者雍武秀可免费替他们建造窑炉；陶艺略微超出她的专长范围，但她对熔炉与火焰作业的知识足以让她在一周工作后自动建成一座可用的窑炉，使PC能自由从事其他休整期活动。</p>\n<p><strong>收集鹭羽：</strong>要从一只活鹭身上收集鹭羽，PC必须花一天时间在柳岸镇的柳岸腹地中狩猎，并尝试一次@Check[survival|dc:20]检定。成功时，他们获得足够的羽毛以尝试施放灵魂迁渡两次；若大成功，则获得足够以尝试该仪式六次。若PC受到银雾斋或九耳神社的支持，这些地点的朋友也可在需要时免费为他们提供羽毛（只要他们先有一天时间去收集）。</p>\n<p><strong>制备榊木薄板：</strong>PC可以通过将其浸泡于特殊油剂中来制备数十片榊木薄板，足够多次施放该仪式，但没有任何办法能缩短所需时间。油剂花费25 gp（若PC至少受到柳岸镇任一派系的仰慕，则这笔费用可由任一派系支付），且无需进行检定。该过程大约需要六周，这意味着PC最早也要到冬季中期才能尝试施放灵魂迁渡——若他们迟迟未能在该主题上获得4点研究点数，甚至可能更晚。在这种情况下，可酌情减少制备薄板所需时间，以确保PC至少有几周时间完成@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第10章}。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Researching Transmigration\">Researching Transmigration</h1>\n<section class=\"handout\">\n  <p>Notes on Transmigration</p>\n  <p>While it’s apparent Governor Heh didn’t know his mindscape was a smaller version of the larger one Willowshore is trapped in, his research remains valuable and can be summarized as follows.</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>The governor’s failed attempt to bolster Kugaptee’s cage on the last day of spring ended in disaster, killing everyone in town. Governor Heh became trapped in his own small mindscape, while everyone else became trapped in the larger one that includes the region’s hinterlands.</li>\n    <li>Even though everyone died, they live on now, trapped in this repeating, year-long mindscape. Governor Heh’s term for a soul forming a new body in a mindscape like this is “transmigration”—a word he also uses interchangeably for the concept of such a person returning to the living world. Transmigration is similar to reincarnation in this definition, save that the new body created for the slain soul isn’t a different one; rather, it is the same one that soul possessed in its most recent life.</li>\n    <li>Governor Heh’s formula for a transmigrate ritual would allow those trapped within this mindscape to use the light shining from Willowshore’s <em>Eternal Lantern</em> to travel from this mindscape to the living world, but the notes are incomplete, in part due to his ignorance of the reincarnate ritual, and in part because he was working alone and wasn’t particularly well-versed in spirituality. Completing the work will be much easier for someone who knows the reincarnate ritual or is more learned in occult or religious matters.</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p>Governor Heh’s notes are written in Common, but reading them takes 8 hours of work. Once a PC reads the journals and notes, the key elements they learn are summarized in the Ritual Notes handout above.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-ritualcomponents.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ritual Components\" alt=\"Ritual Components\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-ritualcomponents.webp')\" />\n<p>PCs should’ve discovered the formula for @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.gIVaSCrLhhBzGHQY]{Reincarnate} in the previous act. Armed with these notes and the formula for @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kqhPt9344UkcGVYO]{Resurrect} (even if they can’t quite yet learn or cast the ritual themselves), they’re in a much better place to complete the governor’s work than he ever was. Still, the PCs must spend time continuing to research and develop @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} before they can attempt to cast the ritual. To research the ritual, the PCs must spend 8 hours researching the topic, using the following research stat block to track progress.</p>\n<p>A PC who knows @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.gIVaSCrLhhBzGHQY]{Reincarnate} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kqhPt9344UkcGVYO]{Resurrect} reduces all DCs for these research checks by 2. A PC who knows both reduces all DCs for these research checks by 4.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Transmigration</span>\n    <span class=\"keepme\">Research 8</span>\n  </h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Solo Investigations</strong> You spend the day examining Governor Heh’s notes and working out your own theories on how the <em>transmigrate</em> ritual might work; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 3</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[academia-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[library-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research], or @Check[arcana|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Consulting Experts</strong> You spend the day discussing the topic with a local expert; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 2 per NPC</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[arcana|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] (consulting with Igawa Jubei at Mother’s Coil); @Check[nature|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] (consulting with the kodama Great Willow); @Check[occultism|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] (consulting with Shinzo during a visit); @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] (consulting with Elizeth Candora at Her Fluvial Lady of Souls)</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Introspection at a Shrine</strong> You spend the day in quiet thought or prayer, meditating in the presence of one of Willowshore’s many shrines or places of natural beauty; <strong>Maximum RP</strong> 3</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Research Checks</strong> @Check[occultism|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research] or @Check[religion|dc:24|traits:concentrate,exploration,linguistic,action:Research|name:Research ]</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>2 Research Points</strong> Rituals to bring the dead back to life typically require a dead body (or at least a part of one). In this case, no dead body exists, but Governor Heh’s idea of using the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>’s light as a sort of “pathway” between this world and the living realm is a brilliant solution to this problem. Grant the PCs 10 XP.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>4 Research Points</strong> Including a metaphorical nod and concession toward longevity and life itself is important—feathers from a heron, long believed to live for centuries and to be capable of “purifying” spirits as they transition to new lives, would work perfectly. The feathers should be gathered from a living bird that must still be alive when the ritual is cast. Beyond this, the burning of rare incense and specially treated slats of sakaki wood serve as the best components for this ritual, but the process of preparing those sakaki slats is expensive and time consuming. Even more exciting, there are hints that a more powerful version of transmigrate might allow for many more souls than just the PCs to escape the mindscape. Grant the PCs 20 XP.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>6 Research Points</strong> Most of Governor Heh’s research focused on the concept of sacrifice—in particular, the sacrifice of one life in order to propel another, “worthier” life out of this mindscape purgatory, in which the sacrificed life was ritualistically incinerated in a clay shell within a huge kiln. This was less because of a predilection toward evil on the governor’s part and more of a concession due to his lack of knowledge of reincarnation. At this point in the research, a PC has an epiphany—by placing the person to be transmigrated into the clay shell instead and then firing them in a huge kiln, the sacrifice of life can be internalized, so that only the target to be transmigrated is affected. Of course, failure to perform the ritual correctly can result in painful (and potentially lethal) burns, but such a risk would be worth it for anyone who wishes to avoid sacrificing one life for another. The possibility of a greater transmigration ritual is also confirmed—and it might even allow the PCs to transmigrate the town’s structures into the living world as well to replace the ruins that exist there now. Grant the PCs 30 XP.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>8 Research Points</strong> The PCs complete the formula for <em>transmigrate</em>, a ritual that draws the power it needs to succeed from the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>. The PCs also know that as long as the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> remains unlit in the living world (as revealed to them by Shinzo), they’ll only be able to cast the 4th-rank version of the ritual, not the 5th-rank one that will allow for a more permanent return to the living world. Grant the PCs 60 XP.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Building the Kiln:</strong> The PCs must construct a kiln large enough for all of them to be placed in so that they can be subjected to transmigrate. Doing so requires a week’s work, an expenditure of 25 gp in resources, and for a character to succeed at a @Check[crafting|dc:20] check. If the PCs have the support of Eternal Blaze Ironworks, its owner, Yong Wu-Xiu, can step in to construct the kiln for them free of charge; pottery is somewhat outside of her skill set, but her knowledge of forges and working with fire allow her to construct a serviceable kiln automatically after a week’s work, leaving the PCs free to pursue other downtime activities.</p>\n<p><strong>Gathering Heron Feathers: </strong>To gather heron feathers from a living heron, a PC must spend a day on the hunt in Willowshore’s hinterlands and attempt a @Check[survival|dc:20] check. On a success, they net enough feathers to attempt to cast transmigrate twice, and with a critical success, they have enough to attempt the ritual six times. If the PCs are supported by Silvermist Lodge or Nine Ear Shrine, their friends at those locations can instead provide these feathers for them as needed for free (as long as they have a day to gather them first).</p>\n<p><strong>Preparing the Sakaki Slats:</strong> A PC can prepare dozens of sakaki slats, enough to cast the ritual many times over, by soaking them in special oils, but there is no way to shorten the time required to do so. The oils cost 25 gp (a cost that either of Willowshore’s factions can pay if the PCs are at least admired by one of them), and no check is required to prepare them. The process takes about six weeks, which means the earliest the PCs can attempt to cast transmigrate is the middle of winter—or perhaps even later if they’re late in achieving 4 Research Points on the topic. In this case, consider reducing the time it takes to prepare the slats as needed to give the PCs at least a few weeks to complete @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10}.</p>"
            },
            "Spreading the News": {
              "name": "传播消息 Spreading the News",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Spreading the News\">传播消息</h2>\n<p>如果PC把他们其实已经死了、而且实际上成了鬼魂的消息告诉村里其他人，反应果然充满震惊、痛苦与愤怒——面对骇人的消息时，说出真相未必是最有交涉手腕、也最能安抚人心的选择，但从长远来看，对镇民坦诚或许才是最好的。若PC向所有人揭露真相，柳岸镇的居民表现出的心理韧性会比预期更强；毕竟在这场战役先前的事件之后，“死了”不过是神祇又一次扔到他们头上的荒唐事。如果PC已在村中树立起权威形象，一些更强势或更爱争执的村民很快就会开始追问PC打算如何处理这局面。毕竟，问题是英雄们提出来的，那就成了他们必须解决的责任！</p>\n<p>虔诚的法拉丝玛信徒角色可能会建议让死亡顺其自然，而不是设法重返生命，但这种观点在大众之中极不受欢迎，有些村民甚至威胁要把持这种想法的人丢进河流。揭露“所有人都死了”的真相会使队伍的希望点减少[[/r 2d6]]，除非他们同时传播另一条消息：他们或许能用从和善保总督那里取回的一场仪式找到让所有人复活的方法（若如此，希望点的减少最小化为2点）。</p>\n<p>如果和善保的行径真相曝光，大多数人会表现出公开的怨愤。总督从来就不怎么受柳岸镇人爱戴，如今他们也很快宣称这人是个蠢货。年长的村民——例如胡太婆——会大声发表看法，谈论总督本该怎么做；但由于柳岸镇的大多数居民对超自然的认知仅来自道听途说与迷信，这些“解决方案”里真正可行的寥寥无几。尽管如此，这消息仍会侵蚀镇民对政府的信任，使队伍的安全点减少[[/r 1d4+2]]。不过，如果PC将一场能让柳岸镇恢复生命的仪式归功于和善保总督，并且在这么做时成功通过一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:20]检定，这些反对者便显得并不真心，很快就会原谅（在这种情况下，只损失1点安全点）。</p>\n<p>如果PC在自己得知这消息后的几天内没有传播出去，那么当该消息日后公开时，他们将冒着失去柳岸镇居民信任的风险；若发生这种情况，则每当一个重大的藏匿真相被公开时，PC在每个派系中都会失去2点声望点。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Spreading the News\">Spreading the News</h2>\n<p>Should the PCs inform the rest of the villagers that they’re dead and actually ghosts, the response is predictably filled with surprise, anguish, and anger—truth is not always the most diplomatic and calming choice to make when it comes to frightening news, but in the long run, it might be best to be honest with the townspeople. Willowshore’s inhabitants prove more mentally resilient than might be expected if the PCs reveal the truth to them all, as after the previous events of the campaign, being dead is simply one more outrage the gods have slung their way. If the PCs have positioned themselves as authorities within the village, some of the more assertive or quarrelsome villagers quickly start to ask what the PCs intend to do about the situation. After all, the heroes brought the problem up, which makes it their responsibility to fix!</p>\n<p>Devout Pharasmin characters might suggest allowing death to take its natural course instead of seeking to return to life, but this viewpoint proves extremely unpopular among the general public, with some of the villagers threatening to throw anyone with that opinion into the river. Revealing the truth that everyone is dead reduces the party’s Hope Points by [[/r 2d6]] unless they also spread the news that they might be able to find a way to bring everyone back to life using a ritual they recovered from Governor Heh (in which case, the Hope Point reduction is minimized to 2 points).</p>\n<p>Should the truth about Heh Shan-Bao’s actions be brought to light, the majority of people show open resentment. The governor was never particularly loved by Willowshore, and they’re quick to proclaim the man a fool now. Older villagers, such as Granny Hu, loudly share their thoughts on what the governor should’ve done instead, though since most of Willowshore’s residents know about the supernatural only through second-hand experience and superstition, few of these solutions are actually practical. This news still erodes the townsfolk’s trust in their government, reducing the party’s Security Points by [[/r 1d4+2]]. If the PCs credit Governor Heh with a ritual that can return Willowshore to life, however, and they succeed at a @Check[diplomacy|dc:20] check when doing so, these detractors prove insincere and are quick to forgive (in this case, only 1 Security Point is lost).</p>\n<p>If the PCs don’t spread this news within a few days of learning it themselves, they risk losing trust among Willowshore’s residents if that news later becomes public; if this occurs, the PCs lose 2 Reputation Points with each faction every time a significant hidden truth is made public.</p>"
            },
            "Current Objectives": {
              "name": "当前目标 Current Objectives",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Current Objectives\">当前目标</h1>\n<p>在本章剩余部分，队伍的主要目标是研究（并完成）和善保的转移仪式，以重返人世；并尽可能保护更多村民，使他们也能复活。正如神藏所指出的（而PC们也可能自己拼凑出了结论），孙海的驱魔人所造成的干扰意味着PC们不能再无所事事地等待循环重置，好让他们从更有利的位置再尝试一次。若旧伐木营地成功放逐英雄与其邻里当前栖身的思维空间，他们就会永远死去。更糟的是，若孙海的工人搜遍该区域并砍倒谭杉，苦迦菩提将能够施展转生术，而那恶魔般的半神将被释放到神门！</p>\n<p>当然，即便在死亡之中，时间也不会为PC们停步。在冬季的数月里，各种事件似乎困扰着柳岸镇的居民，PC们必须做好准备并在事件来临时加以应对。其中一些事件有固定的时间范围，或取决于PC的动作；除此之外，GM应将这些事件分散安排在本幕的整个过程中。</p>\n<p>此外，孙海的驱魔人使用一口神圣的寺院钟，在该地区周围竖立了灵性护。他们自认为是在柳岸镇废墟中隔离某个危险的超自然存在，但这些护也会阻止转移仪式按预期运作；当PC们使用该仪式时，他们会以更接近不死而非生命的生物形态回到生者的领域——而且只是暂时如此。若PC们希望真正复活，而不是享受那苍白而短暂的生命仿制品，就必须摧毁或移除这些护。他们最可能在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event12these00]{降神会}期间发现这些护的存在；但如果他们在尝试让自己复活之前没有发现这些护，神藏或其他更倾向超自然的NPC也可能提醒PC们注意这些护。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Current Objectives\">Current Objectives</h1>\n<p>The party’s main goals for the rest of this chapter are to research (and finish) Heh Shan-Bao’s transmigrate ritual to return to life and to protect as many villagers as possible so the villagers can also be returned to life. As Shinzo noted and the PCs might have pieced together themselves, the interference of Mago Kai’s exorcists means the PCs can’t afford to sit idly and wait for the cycle to reset for them to try again from a more advantageous position. Should the lumber camp succeed at banishing the mindscape that the heroes and their neighbors currently inhabit, they’ll be dead for good. Worse yet, should Kai’s workers scour the area and chop down the Tan Sugi, Kugaptee will be able to reincarnate, and the fiendish demigod will be unleashed upon Shenmen!</p>\n<p>Of course, time doesn’t sit still and wait for the PCs, even in death. Over the course of the winter months, various events appear to trouble the residents of Willowshore, and the PCs will have to prepare for and deal with them as they come. Some of these events have set time frames or depend on PC actions, but otherwise, the GM should space them out over the course of the act.</p>\n<p>In addition, Kai’s exorcists have erected spiritual wards around the region using a holy temple bell. They believe themselves to be quarantining a dangerous supernatural presence in Willowshore’s ruins, but these wards also prevent the transmigrate ritual from working as intended; when the PCs use the ritual, they return to the living realm as creatures closer to undeath than life—and only temporarily. The PCs must destroy or remove the wards if they wish to return to life rather than enjoy a pale and fleeting facsimile of it. They’re most likely to discover the presence of these wards during @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event12these00]{The Seance}, but if they don’t discover the wards before attempting to revive themselves, Shinzo or another supernaturally inclined NPC could warn the PCs about the wards.</p>"
            },
            "Event 4. Shinzo’s Answers": {
              "name": "事件 4：神藏的回答 Event 4. Shinzo’s Answers",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 4. Shinzo’s Answers\">事件4：神藏的回答</h2>\n<p>PC们返回柳岸镇的思维空间后不久，神藏便带着他如影随形的渡鸦同伴伊克斯前来与他们碰面。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shinzo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shinzo\" alt=\"male human merchant\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shinzo.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>神藏脸上带着惆怅的微笑向PC们致意；他仍愿意像之前一样买卖交易，但他也知道PC们已朝自救迈出了关键一步。他以低沉的语调说道：“你们揭开了真相。恭喜。你们并不总能做到。我想你们一定还有更多问题。既然你们已知道自己是什么，我就被允许回答了。”</p>\n<p>神藏建议找个更舒适的地方聊天，比如青天茶馆；但如果PC们等不及听解释，他也愿意当场回答他们的问题。</p>\n<p><strong>你是谁？</strong>“我是朝比奈神藏，收割那些颠覆天界秩序之人的存在。人类称我为‘死神’，一位死亡之神。”若PC在一次@Check[occultism|dc:26]或@Check[religion|dc:26]检定中成功，他们会认出死神乃是宇宙法则的化身，确保即使是超自然存在也无法逃避死亡。他们也会意识到：对一名死神而言，神藏似乎发展出了不同寻常的人类性格——虽然并非闻所未闻，但与凡人过于亲近的死神，其传说往往以悲剧收场。</p>\n<p><strong>我们真的死了吗？</strong>“是的，恐怕你们已经死了，但你们也仍然活着。你们被困在生与死之间，就在这处思维空间里。只要你们维持这种状态，你们便无法前往来世，但你们依旧能够回到生命之中。”</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么不告诉我们我们死了？</strong>“你怎么知道我没说？不得安宁的灵魂很少会接受自身命运的真相。我说出口的下一秒，你们就忘了我的话。直到现在，你们亲自学到了这些，我们才能自由交谈。”</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么在这里？</strong>“一百多年来，这座镇子向每一座神龛里的每一位神明祈祷。你们乞求理解。你们乞求援助。你们乞求怜悯。我就是你们的理解——因为如今我赐予你们答案。我就是你们的援助——因为我给你们带来了补给。我就是你们的怜悯——因为纵使你们已死，你们却尚未真正死去。”</p>\n<p><strong>我们被困在这里多久了？</strong>“我在柳岸镇死去后的第七年来到这里。我又在此守望了一百零八年。你们的这一年重复了一百一十五次。这一次也许就是最后一次。也许不是。这由你们决定。”</p>\n<p><strong>如今的生者世界是什么样？</strong>“络新妇如今统治着神门。蛛女们并不仁慈。她们索取银两、木材与人作为贡品。母亲会在孩子脸上留下疤痕，以免引来赞美或嫉妒。老人会用蟋蟀安抚屋中的蜘蛛，希望这能让怪物再晚一个冬天才来带走他们。柳岸镇如数十年来那般沦为废墟；而现在，一个名叫@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21magokai0000000]{马戈·凯}的人想要夺回它，把它当作行动基地，为一己私利采伐本地区的木材。”</p>\n<p><strong>如果你是死神而我们也死了，为什么你还没带走我们？</strong>“墓之女士很有耐心。你们是回到人世延续生命，还是在死亡中前去觐见她，重要的只有一点：自然秩序必须被纠正。最终你们都会来到她面前，无论以哪一种方式。”神藏说完，他的渡鸦发出一声响亮、颤音般的呱鸣。一名PC若在一次@Check[perception|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive]检定中以察言观色成功，便能看出神藏更希望柳岸镇重返生命、而非就此走向死亡——这种投入远超一名公正的死神应有的程度。同时也很明显：死神与他的渡鸦在此事上彼此对立。</p>\n<p><strong>你能帮助我们吗？</strong>“帮助？我难道不是一直在帮你们吗？我的本性是夺取生命。我不能把生命赐予你们。我也不能在没有命令的情况下杀戮。但若你们给我时间，我能从生者世界带来你们可能需要的情报或物品。我也能告诉你们未来会发生什么，因为有些事无论循环如何都会以同样方式上演。三周后会有一场严酷的冬季风暴，浓雾弥漫。而且，络新妇公主任美璃的某个版本也会在冬至首次来这里，逼你们宣誓效忠。她并非真正的公主，但她自以为是，而且她依旧能杀了你们。你们需要说服她离开且不引发麻烦；若做不到，就在她杀你们之前杀了她。这……乐于帮助吗？”死神迟疑地笑了笑。</p>\n<p><strong>如果你想帮我们，为什么我们还得为你带来的物品付钱？</strong>“别把我误当成慷慨的朋友。我提供的补给并非我所有。我给你们交易的机会，但你们支付的款项会交给浩瀚众界中的其他存在。我无权夺走他们的交易，来把礼物送给你们。尽管如此，我确实为无法提供更多援助而道歉。我本打算在会面结束时再做这件事，但既然你们提到了这个话题……”说到这里，神藏将@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20heroiclegaci00]{英雄传承}中“宝藏”部分所详述的四件魔法物品赠予PC们。</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么能在这个思维空间里来去自如？</strong>“我能穿行于现实；在位面之间迈步对我而言并非难事。我不能带你们一起走，因为你们已经死了，因此无法与我同行旅行。”</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么要这么做？</strong>“有些原因我可以与你们分享，但不是今天。你们只需安心：我在这里是为了帮你们，不必纠结我为何选择如此。”他说话时，他的渡鸦在他脚上来回跳动并呱呱叫着，仿佛不耐烦，或许也是在警告。</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么和一只渡鸦一起行动？</strong>“伊克斯不只是一只渡鸦。伊克斯是我的看守者，也是我的提醒。伊克斯确保我不逾越界限。伊克斯有耐心，但不是永远。你们无需为伊克斯操心；伊克斯是我该烦恼的事。”尽管他的话让伊克斯显得强大，这只渡鸦本质上仍是一名典型的诺索伊招魂者——但作为更高存在的观察代理、且直接侍奉@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}，他的存在就显得重要。</p>\n<p><strong>我们能否等待并重置循环？</strong>“你们以前这么做过，试图拯救所有人，但都失败了。每一次循环重置，你们的记忆都会回溯。但无论你们做何选择，这将是最后一次循环，因为这一次，生者世界的势力正试图驱邪你们家园的废墟。”</p>\n<p><strong>我们就不能让马戈·凯的驱魔师完成工作吗？</strong>“如果你们所求是浩瀚众界与来世，是拥抱那早已将你们夺走的死亡，那么可以。你们什么都不必做，只需等待；这些驱魔师很快就会完成工作，这个现实将会终结，而你们的灵魂将继续前行，去墓之女士面前受审。可在我看来，或许回到那被骤然截断的人生会更可取？”</p>\n<p><strong>驱魔师为什么要这么做？</strong>“你们在这里每重复一年，生者世界便向前推进一年。花了一个多世纪，但这座偏远小镇失落的资源终于引起了掠夺者的注意。驱魔师由马戈·凯带领；此人被恐惧与傲慢所驱使，想把柳岸镇据为行动基地，并开始采伐这片土地的木材。然而，在你们这些不安之灵被驱逐之前，他无法真正开展他的计划，因为柳岸镇的人民造成的闹鬼现象会扰乱在这一地区进行的任何工作。你们的幽灵是最后一道防线；一旦你们消失，他的采伐就会开始。照目前来看，用不了多久他就会发现“丹杉”并将其移除，到那时苦迦菩提的死亡也将终结。他转生回生者世界之事不可容忍。”</p>\n<p><strong>有没有办法拯救赫赫总督？</strong>如果PC们曾在他的思维空间里蓄意攻击并杀死赫赫总督，神藏会回答：“拯救他？是你们摧毁了他残存的那点灵魂。你们以为罪孽能如此轻易被抹去吗？”否则，这名死神会思索片刻，说道：“我不知道。我原以为苦迦菩提吞噬他后已什么都不剩，但……我不认为你们能让他起死回生，不过当你们回到生者世界后，也许能拯救他残余的部分灵魄。”</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>我们能做什么？</strong>“你们寻找失踪的总督以求得答案；尽管他未必意识到，他的计划确有可取之处。转迁是你们的救赎，但你们必须完成他的研究。即便如此，我也担心这魔法起初只能让你们以灵体显现。在生者界，马戈·凯将你们<em>长明灯</em>\n  的灯火当作战利品取走了。那是你们社群的心脏；没有它，我担心你们能用转迁做到的最多只是暂时以灵体显现——但即便是灵体，你们也应当能对他采取行动。把灯火从卡拉海带回柳岸镇的废墟，它将成为锚点与诱饵。唯有如此，你们与镇上柳岸镇的人民才能找到回家的路，回到生命之中。唉，我对马戈·凯及其计划所知甚少——我目前所发现的内容，已经逼近了我在不招致不可挽回的个人后果之前所被允许追查的极限。”（说到这里，伊克斯用力点头，并大声呱叫了一次。）\n</p>\n<p><strong>结束会面：</strong>神藏与PC们会面的主要目的，是揭示他的身份与职责，并为队伍提供一条清晰的前进道路。死神会在离开前继续留在镇上与PC们交易，但他承诺每隔一周便会回来一次，带来新的购物机会，或提供帮助与建议。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.18Ml1AfEku1LqfaG]{神藏的赠礼} <br />\n  无论是在PC们询问他为何向他们收钱购物时，还是在会面结束时，神藏都会向PC们揭示：他为他们收集了一些极为特别的礼物——那些遥远过去的知名人物曾拥有的著名魔法物品之实用复制品。这些英雄传承见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20heroiclegaci00]{此处}。神藏为无法提供更多帮助而道歉，并希望这些礼物能在某种程度上使这份歉意更显真诚。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>因发现他们已将此循环重复了115次，并得知马戈·凯的消息，给予PC们120 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Event 4. Shinzo’s Answers\">Event 4. Shinzo’s Answers</h2>\n<p>Soon after the PCs return to the Willowshore mindscape, they’re approached by Shinzo and his ever-present raven companion, Yix.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shinzo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shinzo\" alt=\"male human merchant\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shinzo.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>Shinzo greets the PCs with a wistful smile on his face, and while he’s willing to buy and sell as before, he also knows that the PCs have made a significant step toward their self-rescue. As he greets the PCs, he says in a somber tone, “You’ve uncovered the truth. Congratulations. You don’t always. I expect you have many more questions. Now that you know what you are, I am allowed to answer them.”</p>\n<p>Shinzo suggests retiring to a more comfortable place to chat, such as the Cerulean Teahouse, but he is also comfortable answering their questions on the spot if the PCs can’t wait for explanations.</p>\n<p><strong>Who are you?</strong> “I am Asahina Shinzo, a reaper of those who subvert the celestial order. Humans call me ‘shinigami,’ a god of death.” PCs who succeed at a @Check[occultism|dc:26] or @Check[religion|dc:26] check recognize a shinigami as an incarnation of cosmic law that ensures even supernatural beings can’t escape death. They’re also aware that Shinzo appears to have developed an unusually human personality for a shinigami—while it isn’t unheard of, legends of shinigami who become too close to mortals tend to end in tragedy.</p>\n<p><strong>Are we really dead?</strong> “Yes, I’m afraid you are, yet you are also still alive. You are trapped between life and death, here in this mindscape, and as long as you remain so, you cannot move on to the afterlife, yet you can still return to life.”</p>\n<p><strong>Why didn’t you tell us we were dead?</strong> “What makes you think I didn’t? Unquiet spirits rarely accept the truth of their fates. You forgot my words the second I spoke them. Only now that you have learned things for yourselves can we freely converse.”</p>\n<p><strong>Why are you here?</strong> “For over a hundred years, this town has prayed to every god at every shrine. You begged for understanding. You begged for aid. You begged for mercy. I am your understanding, as now I grant you answers. I am your aid, for I have brought you supplies. I am your mercy, for even though you are dead, you have not yet died.”</p>\n<p><strong>How long have we been trapped here?</strong> “I arrived here seven years after Willowshore died. I’ve stood vigil here for one hundred and eight more. You have repeated your year a hundred and fifteen times. This may be the last. It may not. That is for you to decide.”</p>\n<p><strong>What’s the living world like now?</strong> “Jorogumo rule Shenmen now. The spider women are not kind. They take tribute in silver, lumber, and people. Mothers scar the faces of their children so as to avoid attracting admiration or jealousy. Old men placate the spiders in their houses with crickets, hoping it will buy them one more winter before the monsters take them. Willowshore lies in ruins, as it has for decades, and now a man named @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21magokai0000000]{Mago Kai} seeks to reclaim it, to use it as a base of operations to harvest the region’s lumber for his own profit.”</p>\n<p><strong>If you’re a shinigami and we’re dead, why haven’t you taken us?</strong> “The Lady of Graves is patient. Whether you return to resume your lives or go to stand before her in death, all that matters is that the natural order is righted. You’ll come to her in the end, either way,” Shinzo says, as his raven gives a loud, trilling caw. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:24|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] check to Sense Motive can tell Shinzo is invested in Willowshore returning to life rather than passing on to death—far more so than an unbiased shinigami should be. It’s also clear the shinigami and his raven are at odds with each other about this issue.</p>\n<p><strong>Can you help us?</strong> “Help? Haven’t I been helping you? My nature is to take life. I cannot grant life to you. I cannot kill without orders, either. But if you give me time, I can bring you information or things you might need from the living world. I can tell you what’s going to happen in the future, as well, for some things play out the same regardless of the cycle. There’s going to be a severe winter storm in three weeks, with heavy fog. And a version of the jorogumo princess, Ren Mei Li, will also make her first visit here during the winter solstice to force you to swear fealty. She isn’t the actual princess, but she thinks she is, and she can still kill you. You’ll need to convince her to leave without causing trouble or, barring that, to kill her before she kills you. Is that... helpful?” The shinigami smiles uncertainly.</p>\n<p><strong>If you’re trying to help us, why do we have to pay you for the items you bring us?</strong> “Do not mistake me for a generous friend. The supplies I provide are not my own. I offer you these chances for trade, but the payments go to others in the Great Beyond. It is not my place to rob them of their trade to provide you gifts. That said, I do apologize for not being able to provide more aid. I had intended to do this at the end of our meeting, but since you brought up the subject...” At this point, Shinzo gifts the PCs the four magic items detailed in Treasure on @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20heroiclegaci00]{Heroic Legacies}.</p>\n<p><strong>How is it you can come and go from this mindscape?</strong> “I can travel reality; stepping between planes is no significant task for me. I cannot take you with me, for you are dead and thus cannot travel at my side.”</p>\n<p><strong>Why are you doing this?</strong> “There are reasons I may share with you, but not today. Take solace in that I am here to help you, and worry not why I choose to do so.” As he speaks, his raven hops back and forth on his feet and caws as if impatient, or perhaps in warning.</p>\n<p><strong>Why do you travel with a raven?</strong> “Yix is more than a raven. Yix is a minder of me and a reminder to me. Yix ensures I do not overstep my bounds. Yix is patient, but not forever. Do not trouble yourself with Yix, for Yix is mine to worry about.” Despite his words making Yix seem powerful, the raven remains a typical nosoi psychopomp—but his placement here as an observer agent of greater powers who directly serve @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} make him important.</p>\n<p><strong>Can we wait and reset the cycle?</strong> “You’ve done so before, to try to save everyone, but have failed. Each time the cycle resets, your memories revert. But this will be the last cycle, regardless of your choice, for this time, forces in the living world seek to exorcise the ruins of your home.”</p>\n<p><strong>Can’t we just let Mago Kai’s exorcists do their job?</strong> “If what you seek is the Great Beyond and your afterlife, to embrace the death that has already claimed you, then yes. You need do nothing more than wait, and these exorcists will soon finish their work, this reality will end, and your souls will move on to stand before the Lady of Graves. It seems to me, perhaps, that a return to the lives cut short would be preferable?”</p>\n<p><strong>Why are the exorcists doing this?</strong> “With each year that you repeat here, the living world travels forward a year. It took over a century, but finally, the lost resources of this remote town have drawn the attention of those who would plunder it. The exorcists are led by Mago Kai, a man driven by fear and pride, who seeks to claim Willowshore as a base of operations and begin the harvest of this land’s lumber. Yet until your restless spirits have been banished, he cannot begin his endeavor in earnest, for the hauntings by the people of Willowshore disrupt any attempt to work in the region. Your ghosts are the last line of defense, and once you are gone, his harvest begins. It won’t be long at this point until he discovers the Tan Sugi and removes it, at which point Kugaptee’s death will end as well. His reincarnation into the living world is not to be tolerated.”</p>\n<p><strong>Is there any way to save Governor Heh?</strong> If the PCs deliberately attacked and killed Governor Heh in his mindscape, Shinzo responds, “Save him? You’re the ones who destroyed what little of his soul was left to him. Do you think your sins can be so easily erased?” Otherwise, the shinigami thinks for a moment before saying, “I don’t know. I didn’t think there was anything remaining after Kugaptee devoured him, but... I don’t think you can bring him back to life, though you might be able to rescue what remains of his spirit once you return to the living world.”</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>What can we do?</strong> “You sought your lost governor for answers, and while he may not have realized it, his plan has merit. Transmigration is your salvation, but you must complete his research. Even then, I fear that this magic will initially only allow you to manifest as spirits. In the living realm, Mago Kai has taken your <em>Eternal Lantern's</em>\n  flame as a trophy. It was the heart of your community, and without it, I fear the most you can do with transmigration is to manifest temporarily as spirits—yet even as spirits, you should be able to move against him. Return the lantern’s flame from Karahai to Willowshore’s ruins, and it will serve as an anchor and a lure. Only then will you and the people of this town be able to find your way back home and back to life. Alas, I learned little of Mago Kai and his plans—what I’ve discovered already has strained the limits of what I am allowed to pursue without irrevocable personal repercussions.” (At this, Yix nods his head vigorously and caws loudly once.)\n</p>\n<p><strong>Ending the Meeting:</strong> The primary purpose of Shinzo’s meeting with the PCs is both to reveal his role and to provide the party with a clear path forward. The shinigami remains in town to trade with the PCs before leaving again, but promises to return once every other week to provide new opportunities to shop or to offer help and advice.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.18Ml1AfEku1LqfaG]{Shinzo's Gifts} <br />\n  Either when the PCs ask why he has been charging them money to shop or at the end of the meeting, Shinzo reveals to the PCs that he has gathered some very special gifts for them—functional replicas of famous magical items once owned by notables from the distant past. These heroic legacies are presented @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20heroiclegaci00]{Here}. Shinzo apologizes for not being able to help more and hopes these gifts go some way toward making that apology all the more sincere.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> For discovering that they’ve repeated this cycle 115 times and learning of Mago Kai, grant the PCs 120 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Winter in Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇之冬 Winter in Willowshore",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Winter in Willowshore\">柳岸镇的冬日</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-blackbean.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Black Bean\" alt=\"a smoky gray cat with yellow eyes\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-blackbean.webp')\" />\n<p>当PC们终结了和善保的思维空间后，总督的灵魂便离去，成为苦迦菩提的囚徒；而他的宅邸则回到了柳岸镇，仿佛从未消失过一般。建筑的大门被撕扯得大敞，镇守的符箓也已破烂不堪，使任何人都能轻易进入这栋建筑。然而，没有村民敢这么做，PC们也很快就会得知这一变化。</p>\n<p>如果PC们回到宅邸，他们会听到从里面传来哀怨的呜咽声，像是一个孩子在微弱地哭泣。若他们进行调查，会发现声音来自一只被关在破旧橱柜里的小黑猫。这只猫“黑豆”惊惧、黏人且饥饿，但除此之外很健康。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Winter in Willowshore\">Winter in Willowshore</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-blackbean.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Black Bean\" alt=\"a smoky gray cat with yellow eyes\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-blackbean.webp')\" />\n<p>When the PCs bring Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape to an end, the governor’s soul moves on to become Kugaptee’s prisoner while his manor returns to Willowshore as if it had never vanished to begin with. The building’s doors have been ripped open and the warding fulus lie in tatters, allowing anyone to enter the building easily. No villager dares do so, though, and the PCs are quickly made aware of this development.</p>\n<p>If the PCs return to the manor, they hear the sound of plaintive wails coming from within, like a child crying weakly. Should they investigate, they find the sound comes from a little black cat shut inside a battered cupboard. This cat, Black Bean, is frightened, clingy, and starving but otherwise healthy.</p>"
            },
            "Face-to-Face with Death": {
              "name": "与死亡面对面 Face-to-Face with Death",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Face-to-Face with Death\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第9章：</span>\n  <span>直面死亡</span>\n</h1>\n<p>随着时间流逝，冬季在柳岸镇逐渐加深。白昼愈发短暂，天气愈发严酷。每周请记得按照 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10weeklyattrit00]{每周损耗} 中的说明减少希望、食物与安全点。本章还详述了许多额外的遭遇，在这些遭遇中，PC们可能需要花费更多点数，或在少数情况下，有机会赚回其中一些点数。</p>\n<p>尽管PC们可能没有在冬季的第一周前往和善保的思维空间，但预计他们会在第一个月结束前这么做。因此，本章并未安排任何重要事件在那段时间发生。冬季的其他事件与进展，应在PC们从替代思维空间归来后，按本章所呈现的顺序依次展开。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-fiend-fight.webp\" alt=\"Fiend Fight\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Face-to-Face with Death\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 9:</span>\n  <span>Face-to-Face with Death</span>\n</h1>\n<p>As time passes, winter advances on Willowshore. The days grow shorter and the weather grows crueler. Each week, remember to reduce Hope, Food, and Security Points as detailed on @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog10oblivi.JournalEntryPage.10weeklyattrit00]{Weekly Attrition}. This chapter details many additional encounters where the PCs might need to spend more points or, rarely, have a chance to earn a few of them back.</p>\n<p>While the PCs might not have traveled to Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape in the first week of winter, it’s expected they’ll do so before the first month passes. As a result, no significant events are scheduled in this chapter to occur then. The other events and developments of winter should play out in the order they’re presented in this chapter, after the PCs’ return from the alternate mindscape.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 3.3: This Place is Ours": {
          "name": "第3.3幕：此地归我们所有 Act 3.3: This Place is Ours",
          "pages": {
            "Running out of Time": {
              "name": "时间所剩无几 Running out of Time",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Running out of Time\">时间所剩无几</h2>\n<p>PC们必须在春季最后一天、他们的思维空间重置之前，成功施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}的5环版本——但如果由于某些原因，这点时间根本不够，又会发生什么？若无人阻止，孙海会在春季最后一周砍倒谭杉；而当苦迦菩提从死亡中被释放出来时，他会吞噬柳岸镇的思维空间以及其中所有居住者——在这种情况下，将不会再有重置，PC们也不会有任何来世。</p>\n<p>如果你仍想继续进入冒险路径的下一幕，你可以考虑让神秘商人神藏在最后关头介入，协助PC们完成转生。不过，这么做可能会在某些团体的观感中稍微破坏体验，因此如果你想在你的游戏中动用这种天降神助，一定要与玩家沟通，或者询问他们是否更愿意拥抱失败。毕竟，并非每个故事都需要以胜利告终；若所有人都同意，用一个阴郁而骇人的结局来收束一场恐怖主题战役，也未必是结束这个故事的最糟方式！</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景笔记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{Change Season}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>更改@UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{柳岸镇}与@UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{柳岸腹地}场景的季节。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Running out of Time\">Running out of Time</h2>\n<p>The PCs have until their mindscape resets on the last day of spring to successfully cast the 5th-level version of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}, but what happens if, for whatever reason, that’s simply not enough time? Without being stopped, Mago Kai manages to chop down the Tan Sugi during the last week of spring, and as Kugaptee is released from death, he absorbs the Willowshore mindscape and all who dwell within it—there will be no reset, nor any afterlife for the PCs, in this event.</p>\n<p>If you want to continue into the next act of the Adventure Path anyway, you might consider having the mysterious merchant Shinzo step in to aid the PCs at the last minute to help them transmigrate. Doing so can slightly sour the experience in some group’s minds, though, so be sure to communicate with your players if you want to pull this deus ex machina in your game, or ask them if the group would rather embrace failure. After all, not every story needs to end in a win, and a grim, horrific ending to a horror-themed campaign might not be the worst way to close out this tale if everyone agrees to it!</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.qMjiMOWIstGMjrXk]{Change Season}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Changes the Season on the @UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{Willowshore} and @UUID[Scene.6LzSSdZgPfQ2K0dL]{Willowshore Hinterlands} Scenes.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Concluding the Act": {
              "name": "幕终结 Concluding the Act",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding the Act\">终结本幕</h1>\n<p>一旦PC从孙海那里取得寺庙钟槌，他们就能轻松停用警戒钟。由于这根钟槌是用从<em>长明灯</em>取走的金属燃料容器锻造而成，只要队伍中任何人接触到它，PC便会感到一股冲动，想尽快把钟槌送回<em>长明灯</em>。如果将钟槌放入现世柳岸镇废墟中的<em>长明灯</em>内，钟槌会立刻恢复为先前的容器形态，并在无需任何钱币供奉的情况下绽放光芒。完成后，PC只需等待到农历新年的第一天，便可开始尝试施展5环版本的<em>转生</em>。他们是以魅影形态在现世度过剩余时间，还是返回思维空间，取决于他们自己，但<em>转生</em>必须在思维空间内施放。</p>\n<p>PC越早施展仪式越好，因为仪式的总体成功与否，部分取决于仪式施放时柳岸镇还剩下多少准备点数。如果这些点数中的一部分或全部被降至零，那么能够完成转生的人口与建筑就会更少；但如果PC保有足够点数，整个镇子便能穿越时间与空间，回到现世。要让PC与柳岸镇重获新生，请参阅<em>鬼季冒险路径</em>中下一幕也是最终一幕的开篇内容。</p>\n<p>尽管柳岸镇的救赎或许已近在眼前，但活下去并不轻松，接下来的日子里，小镇仍将面对诸多挑战。村民与英雄们倾注于小镇的爱情与努力，或许能将它的一部分灵性存在带入他们的新世界，但柳岸镇仍需努力，在这个早已将它遗忘的世界里开辟一席之地。更糟的是，那些原本只会在抽象层面伤害他们的政治力量，如今已变得近在眼前。周冥瑕对柳岸镇森林的痴迷不会随着孙海一同消散，而络新妇也用不了多久就会注意到一座新村落的突然出现。PC终于从死亡手中夺回了自己的生命。现在，能否守住这条命，就要看他们能否抵御生者的野心。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Concluding the Act\">Concluding the Act</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs gain the temple bell ringer from Mago Kai, they can easily deactivate the warding bell. As the temple bell ringer was forged from the metal fuel receptacle taken from the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, the PCs feel an urge to return the bell ringer to the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> as soon as any of them touch it. If the ringer is placed within the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> in the ruins of Willowshore in the living world, the ringer instantly reverts back to its previous form as a receptacle and flares into light without the need for any offerings of coins. This done, the PCs need only wait until the first day of the lunar new year to begin their attempt at the 5th-rank version of <em>transmigrate</em>. Whether they spend their remaining time in the living world as phantoms or return to the mindscape is up to them, but <em>transmigrate</em> must be cast from within the mindscape.</p>\n<p>The sooner the PCs cast the ritual, the better, for the overall success of the ritual depends in part on how many Preparation Points the town of Willowshore still has once the ritual is cast. If some or all of these points have been reduced to zero, fewer citizens and buildings will make the transmigration, but if the PCs have enough points, the entire township can make the journey through time and space to return to the living world. See the beginning of the next, and final, act in the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em> to bring the PCs and Willowshore back to life.</p>\n<p>Though Willowshore’s salvation might just be in sight, living isn’t easy, and the town has many challenges still facing it in the days ahead. The love and effort that the villagers and heroes put into the town might help draw some of its spiritual presence into their new world, but Willowshore still needs to work hard to carve a place in a world that has long forgotten it. Worse yet, the political forces that could only hurt them in the abstract are now very present. Chou Mingxia’s obsession with Willowshore’s forests won’t vanish alongside Mago Kai, and the jorogumo notice the sudden appearance of a new village before too long. The PCs have finally won their lives back from death. Now, it’s up to them to protect their lives from the ambitions of the living.</p>"
            },
            "Garden": {
              "name": "花园 Garden",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C22. 花园</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一座精心打理的花园占据了要塞中央的庭院，庭院中央有一口带顶棚的水井。几棵修剪整齐的木棉树以赏心悦目的间距点缀其间。它们的枝条此刻光秃秃的，让人觉得像是一根根锯齿状的尖刺伸向天空。花园南侧竖起了立杆支撑的彩色棚盖，棚盖下铺着地毯，摆着一把椅子和一张桌子，桌上备着茶水与点心。</p>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-kai-mago.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">花园</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.d0rXk6BrTDxPSfk4]{孙海}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kaimagoportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Mago Kai\" alt=\"human man fighter lumber baron\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kaimagoportrait.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>孙海渐渐喜欢上了这座花园，几乎把那些木棉树当作被俘的听众。趁着冬季等待他的驱魔师终于让柳岸镇安全、好让他回去重新夺回那里时，他把许多时间都花在这里：读他最爱的小说、品茶放松，或在天气转暖后筹划春季的采伐收获。他觉得凛冽的冬日空气令人振奋，而棚盖也能遮雨。由于追随者明白他重视隐私，PC们最可能在这里遇到他，而且是他独自一人（除非他们在要塞里散播恐惧时闹得太过火了）。</p>\n  <p>一看到PC们，孙海便从椅子上一跃而起，伸手去抓他的斧头时也许会打翻一杯茶，但随即又停住。他的驱魔师一直定期向他汇报；即使PC们至今还没累积到哪怕1点恐惧，他也能认出他们是来自柳岸镇的魂魄。考虑到守护钟的影响，他们还能一路闯到这里，这一点就足以让他警觉：这些魂魄很可能是危险的敌手。因此，他希望用言语而非斧头来解决这次初次遭遇。若PC们同意与他交谈，参见他的@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21magokai0000000]{NPC词条}以了解他们可能得知的信息。</p>\n  <p>若PC们表现出任何敌意，孙海也会毫不犹豫地以牙还牙。若他的生命值降到100点以下，他会试图撤回自己的住处重整。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 7：</strong>孙海撤退到区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c20kaisquart00]{C20}的住处以求安全。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们说服孙海在无需与他战斗的情况下提供帮助，给予他们的XP视同在战斗中击败了他；随后，再将所有仍然存活的驱魔师、佣兵与巫女的额外XP也一并给予PC们，视同他们也在战斗中击败了那些生物。（无论PC们在此处能获得多少XP，他们获得的总量不应远超升至10级所需，但也不该因为高效闹鬼而受到惩罚！）</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>和平的奖励</h1>\n  <p>虽然本冒险假设孙海会在与PC们的战斗中丧命，而他们能获得唐入中由守卫者保管或随身携带的大部分宝藏，但此地出现的大多数生物并非邪恶——他们只是对这片地区另有打算，却因无知而让柳岸镇的人民身陷险境。不过，下一章仍假设PC们会按10级角色的预期来装备自己。</p>\n  <p>若你的PC们完成@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{第10章}后，并未因自身努力而变得特别富有——若他们与孙海谈判达成和平解决，这很可能就是如此——那么当他们返回柳岸镇时，应在神藏最后几次造访思维空间的其中一次与他相见。虽然这次会面并非PC们最后一次遭遇这位神秘的死神，但这将是他们最后一次在他作为商人的身份下与他会面。神藏祝贺他们在唐入找到和平的解决办法，并指出即便身为“死之神”，他也欣赏凡人能为暴力冲突找到非暴力的解决方案。为证明他的钦佩，他给予每位PC一笔可在他所售物品中购物的额度——这笔额度的价值应足以让PC们的装备提升到10级角色应有的水平（每位PC约1,500 gp；但若你觉得他们资源尤其匮乏，也可酌情上调，最高至每位PC 3,000 gp）。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C22. Garden</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A beautifully tended garden occupies the fortress’s central courtyard, which features a covered well at the center. Several well-pruned cotton trees dot the area at aesthetically pleasing intervals. Their branches are currently bare, giving the impression of jagged spines reaching up toward the sky. A colorful canopy has been erected on poles in the southern part of the garden, under which rugs, a chair, and a table set with tea and snacks has been set up.</p>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-kai-mago.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Garden</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.d0rXk6BrTDxPSfk4]{Mago Kai}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kaimagoportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Mago Kai\" alt=\"human man fighter lumber baron\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kaimagoportrait.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Creature:</strong> Mago Kai has grown fond of this garden and thinks of the cotton trees almost as a captive audience. While he waits out the winter for his exorcists to finally make Willowshore safe for reclaiming, he spends much of his time here, relaxing with his favorite novels, enjoying tea, or working out his springtime harvest plans for once the weather breaks. He finds the brisk winter air bracing, and the canopy keeps the rain away. Since his followers understand he values his privacy, he’s most likely encountered here, alone, by the PCs (unless they’ve been a bit too exuberant in spreading terror through the fortress).</p>\n  <p>Upon spotting the PCs, Kai leaps up from his chair, perhaps spilling a cup of tea as he reaches for his axe, but then pauses. He has been updated regularly by his exorcists, and even if the PCs haven’t accumulated a single point of Terror yet, he recognizes them as spirits from Willowshore. The fact that they’ve made it this far, despite the warding bell’s influence, is all he needs as a warning that these spirits are potentially dangerous foes, and so he hopes to solve this initial encounter with words rather than his axe. If the PCs agree to speak to him, see his @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21magokai0000000]{NPC Entry} for what they might be able to learn.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs show any hostility, Kai doesn’t hesitate to respond in kind. If brought below 100 Hit Points, he attempts to regroup in his quarters.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 7:</strong> Kai retreats to his quarters in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c20kaisquart00]{C20} for safety.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs convince Mago Kai to help without having to fight him, grant them XP as if they’d defeated him in combat, and then grant them additional XP for all of the exorcists, mercenaries, and shrine maidens who still live, as if they’d defeated those creatures in combat as well. (Regardless of how much XP the PCs might earn here, they shouldn’t earn much more than is needed to reach 10th level, but neither should they be penalized for efficient haunting!)</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Rewards for Peace</h1>\n  <p>While this adventure assumes that Mago Kai perishes in a fight with the PCs and that they gain most of the treasure held in Karahai or carried by its defenders, the majority of the creatures found here aren’t evil—they merely have plans for the region that ignorantly put the people of Willowshore in peril. However, the next chapter still assumes the PCs will be geared up as expected for 10th-level characters.</p>\n  <p>If your PCs finish @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl]{Chapter 10} and don’t come out of it particularly richer for their efforts—as is likely the case if they negotiate a peaceful solution with Mago Kai—then when they return to Willowshore, they should be greeted by Shinzo on one of his final visits to the mindscape. While this meeting won’t be the last time the PCs encounter the mysterious shinigami, it will be their last meeting with him in his role as a merchant. Shinzo congratulates them on finding a peaceful solution in Karahai, noting that even as a “god of death,” he appreciates when mortals find nonviolent solutions to violent conflicts. To prove his admiration, he grants each PC credit to shop among his items—the value of this credit should be enough to bring the PCs’ gear up to where it should be for 10th-level characters (approximately 1,500 gp per PC, but feel free to adjust this up to a maximum of 3,000 gp per PC if you feel they’re particularly resource poor).</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Treasury": {
              "name": "宝库 Treasury",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C21. 金库</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这间房间的铁门一直上锁；唯一能打开它的钥匙是孙海随身携带的唐入要塞钥匙。否则，PC可以通过一次成功的 @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定将其破拆打开，或进行四次 @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] 检定来开锁。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>乍看之下，这房间显得有些平平无奇，因为架子和展示位大多空空如也。中央的架子上放着朴素的木箱，而东南侧架子上则随意摆着一尊描绘国府幸的偶像，仿佛只是顺手放上去的点缀。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.vKj1Fw3hlclDB7K1]{Treasury} <br />\n  凯的全部资产与资金都存放在这些箱子里。尽管他在唐入的安置以及最初几次试图夺回柳岸镇的行动中，已经耗尽了大部分启动资金与资源，但这里剩下的依旧相当可观。箱中装有折叠成卷的丝绸布匹、象牙条、青铜器皿，以及彼此堆叠的船形银锭。若遇紧急情况，这些简单的方形木箱可以轻易装上木材货车并运出要塞。金库内的财物总计为价值 1,400 gp 的银锭、象牙与丝绸，外加一枚<em>火跃戒指</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C21. Treasury</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This room’s iron door is kept locked; the only key that can open it is the Karahai fortress key Mago Kai carries. Otherwise, a PC can Force it Open with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check or unlock it with four @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>At first glance, the room appears somewhat underwhelming, as its shelves and displays are mostly empty. Unadorned wooden chests sit on the central shelf, while a haphazardly placed idol depicting Kofusachi stands almost as an afterthought on the southeastern shelf.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.vKj1Fw3hlclDB7K1]{Treasury} <br />\n  All of Kai’s resources and funds are kept within the chests. While he has used up most of his initial funding and resources getting set up in Karahai and on his initial attempts to reclaim Willowshore, what remains here is still significant. Within the chests can be found folded bolts of silk, slats of ivory, bronze vessels, and boat-shaped silver ingots stacked on top of one another. In the event of an emergency, the simple square chests can easily be packed onto lumber wagons and carried out of the fortress. The contents of the treasury amount to a collection of silver ingots, ivory, and silk worth 1,400 gp total, along with a <em>fire-jump ring</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Kai’s Quarters": {
              "name": "凯的住处 Kai’s Quarters",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C20. 孙海的住处</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>与要塞其余部分相比，这个房间带着些许奢华气息。虽然没有什么特别浮夸的陈设引人注目，但这些私人房间里摆着结实、打磨光亮的木制家具。绘有雅致狩猎场景的折屏为房间部分区域增添了些许私密感；北墙旁一只冒着烟的炭炉提供热量，让整个空间弥漫着宜人的气味与暖意。房间西侧摆着两张矮桌：一张上面放着茶具与点心，另一张则铺满卷轴；东侧则更像一间卧室。东墙上有一扇厚重的铁门，配着极具威慑力的锁；门两侧的墙面上各装饰着一把看起来价值不菲的斧子。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这间房曾是要塞指挥官的居所（自龙华覆灭后，这个职位便一直空缺），如今同样作为孙海的居所使用。桌上散落的卷轴勾勒出他针对柳岸镇废墟的计划：从驱邪到将废墟大半夷平，再到在这座城镇的残骸上重建一个更高效、更工业化的伐木营地。几张便笺则标出附近可能出产稀有木材的潜在地区，“这肯定能让周冥瑕总督至少满意上一整年”。在这些地点中，镇子西边、谭杉生长的那片林地似乎尤为令他在意。</p>\n<p>对PC而言，或许更迫在眉睫的是一部典籍，里面描述了如何使用一种名为“守护铃”的防护物品。启动铃的方法由一连串吟唱、供奉与有节奏的敲铃构成，并与施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{加持术}仪式同时进行。笔记还记载了孙海、巫女与驱邪师如何从柳岸镇的<em>长明灯</em>中取出燃料容器，再将其金属重新锻造成铃的撞槌，并通过恰当的仪式与献祭，为其灌注一种对灯焰原本给予柳岸镇之庇护的“反转”。这种力量转而帮助将柳岸镇的魂魄困住，使其无法轻易从废墟中扩散。对PC而言幸运的是，笔记也写明了如何用撞槌解除守护铃：连续用力敲击八下即可。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/animated-axe.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">孙海的住处</span> <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.W48BwZkFOHgaiAdO]{活化斧（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>安装在通往区域C21之门两侧墙上的四把精致斧子绝非只是装饰。若任何生物在孙海不在场时进入房间，这四把斧子会突然活化并俯冲攻击，像被隐形战士挥舞般在空中飞旋。若孙海在房间里，他会简短地下达命令并打个响指；以一个交互动作，他可以命令斧子攻击房间内除他自己之外的所有生物。</p>\n  <p>这四把斧子按活化物体运作。若被摧毁，它们会掉落在地，并像玻璃制成的一样粉碎。在此之前，这些斧子会在本房间内与任何闯入者战斗直至被击败；它们不会追击离开该区域的敌人。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐慌 7：</strong>孙海会撤回自己的房间以求安全。与区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c22garden00000]{C22}相同，他会先尝试与PC交谈，但若战斗爆发，他将战至最后一刻。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C20. Kai’s Quarters</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>In contrast to the rest of the fortress, a modicum of luxury graces this room. While nothing particularly ostentatious catches the eye, these personal chambers feature solid and polished wooden furniture. Folding screens displaying elegant hunting scenes give parts of the room a nod toward privacy, and a smoking charcoal burner against the north wall provides heat, filling the area with a pleasant smell and warmth. Two low tables, one set with a tea service and snacks and another covered with scrolls, sit in the western portion of the room, while to the east, the chamber seems more akin to a bedroom. A large iron door with an imposing lock sits in the eastern wall, while a pair of expensive-looking axes adorn the walls to either side of it.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This chamber, once used as the fort commander’s chambers (a position that had remained vacant since the fall of Lung Wa), now serves the same purpose for Mago Kai. The scattered scrolls on the table outline his plans for Willowshore’s ruins, running from exorcism to razing much of the ruins and then rebuilding a more efficient and industrial logging compound on the town’s bones. Several notes map out potential regions nearby that might supply rare timber “that will certainly appease Governor Chou Mingxia for at least a year.” Among these sites, the grove west of town where the Tan Sugi grows seems of particular interest.</p>\n<p>Perhaps of more immediate significance to the PCs is a codex that describes the use of a protective item called a warding bell. The method to activate the bell consists of a series of chants, offerings, and rhythmic rings, coinciding with the casting of a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN]{Consecrate} ritual. The notes include the method by which Kai, the shrine maidens, and the exorcists extracted the fuel receptacle from Willowshore’s <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, then reforged the metal into a ringer for the bell that would imbue it, through proper rites and sacrifice, with a sort of “inversion” of the protection the flame within the lantern afforded Willowshore. This power instead helps to keep the spirits of Willowshore trapped so they can’t easily spread from the ruins. Fortunately for the PCs, the notes also describe how the ringer can be used to disarm the warding bell by striking it solidly eight times in succession.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/animated-axe.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Kai's Quarters</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.W48BwZkFOHgaiAdO]{Animated Axes (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The four elegant axes mounted on the walls on opposite sides of the door to area C21 are no mere decorations. If any creature enters the room while Kai isn’t present, the four axes suddenly animate and swoop to attack, flying through the air as if wielded by invisible warriors. If Kai is in the room, he issues a brief command and snaps his fingers; with an Interact action, he can command the axes to attack all creatures in the room save himself.</p>\n  <p>The four axes function as animated objects. If destroyed, they drop to the ground and shatter as if made from glass. Until then, the axes fight any intruders in this room until defeated; they don’t pursue foes out of the area.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 7:</strong> Mago Kai retreats to his room for safety. As in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c22garden00000]{C22}, he’ll first try to speak with the PCs, but if battle ensues, he fights to the bitter end.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Jail": {
              "name": "监狱 Jail",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C19. Jail\">C19. 监牢</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这些牢房肮脏不堪，陈设也极其简陋；每间牢房里唯一的物件只有一个简易的金属便盆和一张编织的灯心草席。</p>\n</div>\n<p>每扇牢门都可以在成功进行一次 @Check[athletics|dc:28|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定后用破拆打开；也可以通过进行三次 @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] 检定来开锁打开；或者用孙海随身携带的唐入万能钥匙解锁。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-hu-deming.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hu Deming\" alt=\"human man prisoner chained to the floor\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-hu-deming.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>胡德明，一名来自唐入的村民，目前是这里唯一被关押的囚犯。他被锁链拴在东北侧牢房的地面上，脖子上还固定着一副枷。孙海接管堡垒时，德明朝凯扔了一条鱼，从那以后就一直被关在这里。尽管他对PC的意图抱有戒心——尤其考虑到他们那古怪的、幽灵般的本质——但他目前的状态让他毫无躲藏或逃跑的机会。他同意用自己知道的情报交换自由。或者，若一名PC成功进行一次 @Check[deception|dc:23|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie] 检定来撒谎，也能让他开口而自己并无意兑现放他走的承诺；但一旦德明意识到自己被骗了，或者PC未能胁迫住他，他就会开始大喊求救。若他这么做，外围环道上的任意巡逻队会在[[/r 1d4]]分钟内前来查看。</p>\n<p>如果给他机会，德明会滔滔不绝，恨不得把PC的耳朵都说聋；但实际上，他的信息因被关押了数月而十分有限。他不知道孙海搬进来后，堡内建筑被如何重新利用。下面列出了一些可能的问题及他的回答。</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么会被关在这？</strong>“没啥大不了的；就是那头笨牛凯厚着脸皮叫我滚出我自己的铺子时，我稍微闹腾了点。”</p>\n<p><strong>你能告诉我们这座要塞的情况吗？</strong>“当然，打我一辈子都在这儿干活。直到今年早些时候孙海来了才变样。卖鱼这行是臭了点，但总得有人干，对吧？”德明夸张地眨了下眼。“布局挺简单，像个大轮子。商铺一圈围着。马厩在西北边，猪圈就在这儿往东一点儿——如果我没记错的话。”</p>\n<p><strong>你能说说孙海吗？</strong>“那个贪心、木头脑袋、偷鸡摸狗的猪崽子？当然能！他就是把猪头塞进马屁股里，还留着满脸鬃毛好去刷里面的那种货色。他像泡软了的甲鱼。他像鱼眼、像搅烂的蛋。他爹妈要是他娘生下来的是一块烤猪肉，日子都能好过些。他一枚金币还差俩铜子儿。”德明这通骂街至少持续五分钟，措辞越来越花哨，引用的身体构造也越来越不可能，随后才绕回有用的内容。“他自称是什么‘嗣’来的领主。根本不在乎我们，只在乎能榨出多少木材和财富。成天扛着把大斧头，但我怀疑他连怎么挥都不会。”</p>\n<p><strong>你见过一个大型青铜钟吗？</strong>“见过啊，他们来的时候把它放在车上。刚到那会儿敲了几下，之后就没再敲过。那种讲究玩意儿多半锁在库房里。就在堡里南边那栋内侧建筑。可得小心；我听说有个醉兵晃进去，结果为此被人一边肢解一边把脑袋砸开了花。”</p>\n<p><strong>那凯的追随者呢？</strong>“我可说不上喜欢他们任何一个，毕竟都是那蠢货的走狗。不过要是有哪个厉害的妖怪上门，我要说我不想让这些‘光明的正义守卫’站岗，那就是撒谎。嗯，至少大部分是这样。”</p>\n<p><strong>大部分？</strong>“有些事不对劲。有几个祭司一直鬼鬼祟祟地到处走，觉得没人听就低声嘀咕。我不是行家，但整件事就是有股不对劲。很邪门。脸颊上有道疤的那个，似乎是他们的头儿。”</p>\n<p><strong>恐惧6：</strong>德明一直在偏执狂乱中越想越多，琢磨着自己在牢房外听到的可怕声响。如果他看见PC，就会发出一声令人毛骨悚然的尖叫，使总恐惧点数+1。这会像德明呼救时一样，惊动外围环道上的巡逻队。当然，他被关着，也不可能真的从幽灵手里逃脱；PC可以像上面那样审问他而无需与他讨价还价，只是他的回答会夹杂更多哭喊与哀求。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.8ad7swUxoJZ950Ui]{Hu Deming}</span><span>生物 -1</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC救出胡德明并得知他的情报，给予他们80 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C19. Jail\">C19. Jail</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>These jail cells are wretched and sparsely furnished, with a simple metal bed pan and a woven rush mat as the only appointments in each.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Each of these cell doors can be Forced Open with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:28|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check, opened with three @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock, or unlocked with the Karahai skeleton key carried by Mago Kai.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-hu-deming.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hu Deming\" alt=\"human man prisoner chained to the floor\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-hu-deming.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Hu Deming, a villager from Karahai, is currently the only prisoner incarcerated here. He’s chained to the floor in the northeastern cell with a cangue fastened around his neck. Deming threw a fish at Kai when the lumber baron took over the fortress and has been imprisoned here ever since. While he’s wary of the PCs’ intentions, especially considering their strange, ghostly nature, his current condition leaves him no opportunity to hide or flee. He agrees to tell them what he knows in exchange for his freedom. Alternatively, a PC who succeeds at a @Check[deception|dc:23|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie] check to Lie can get him to open up without intending to follow through on a promise to release him, but once Deming realizes he has been betrayed, or if the PCs fail to Coerce him, he starts yelling for help. If he does so, any patrol on the periphery ring comes to check on him in [[/r 1d4]] minutes.</p>\n<p>While Deming talks the PCs’ ears off if given the chance, in reality, his information is limited by his many months of incarceration. He doesn’t know how buildings have been repurposed since Mago Kai moved in. Some likely questions and their responses are listed below.</p>\n<p><strong>What are you in here for?</strong> “Nothing much, really; just got a little rowdy when that blundering ox Kai had the gall to tell me to get out of my own shop.”</p>\n<p><strong>What can you tell us about the fortress?</strong> “Plenty, worked here all my life. Until Mago Kai got here earlier in the year, that is. Fishmongering’s a smelly business, but someone’s got to do it, right?” Deming gives an exaggerated wink. “It’s a pretty simple design. Like a big wheel. Shops all around. Stables to the northwest, pig pen just east of here if I recall.”</p>\n<p><strong>Can you tell us about Mago Kai?</strong> “That greedy, blockheaded, thieving son of a sow? Sure thing! He’s a pig’s head shoved up a horse’s rear, with plenty of bristles on his face to scrub out the insides. He’s a soggy softshell turtle. A fish-eyed, scrambled-up egg. His parents would have been better off if his mother had given birth to a chunk of roasted pork. He’s two coppers out of a gold coin.” Deming continues on in this tirade for at least five minutes, his language growing more colorful and citing more anatomical impossibilities, before he circles back to useful information. “He claims to be some kind of lord from Sze. Doesn’t care about us; just whatever lumber and wealth he can squeeze. Carries around a big axe, but I doubt he even knows how to swing it.”</p>\n<p><strong>Have you seen a large bronze bell?</strong> “Yeah, they had it on a cart when they got here. Banged on it a bit when they first arrived, but not since. Something that fancy is probably locked up in the vault. Southern inner building in the fort. Watch out, though; I heard talk of a drunken soldier wandering in there and being simultaneously dismembered and having their head bashed in for their trouble.”</p>\n<p><strong>What about Kai’s followers?</strong> “Can’t say I care for any of them, on account of them being that oaf’s lackeys. But when the big bad yokai comes a-knocking, I’d be lying if I said I didn’t want these ‘virtuous defenders of the light’ standing guard. Well, most of them anyway.”</p>\n<p><strong>Most of them?</strong> “There’s something strange going on. A few of the priests have been sneaking around, whispering when they think no one is listening. I’m no expert, but there’s just something wrong about the whole thing. Something evil. The one with the scar on her cheek seems to be the ringleader of them.”</p>\n<p><strong>Terror 6:</strong> Deming has been stewing in his paranoia about the terrible noises he’s been hearing outside of his cell. If he sees the PCs, he lets out a bloodcurdling shriek, adding 1 Terror Point to the total. This alerts the patrol on the periphery ring, in the same manner as it would if Deming had called for help. Of course, as he’s imprisoned, he can’t exactly escape the ghosts; the PCs can question him as above without having to bargain with him, though his answers involve a lot more crying and begging.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.8ad7swUxoJZ950Ui]{Hu Deming}</span><span>Creature -1</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs rescue Hu Deming and learn his information, grant them 80 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Armory": {
              "name": "军械库 Armory",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C18. Armory\">C18. 军械库</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一排排刀剑、薙刀与斧头将这间房间分隔成几条过道。远处墙边的木制假人上披着厚重的板甲，几个假人的手臂上挂着黑色盾牌。地上放着两面巨大的战鼓。战鼓旁边是装满箭矢与弩矢的木桶。西南角的一张工作台上整齐摆放着保养工具。一侧是一台脚踏式砂轮，另一侧则是一座小熔炉与铁砧。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.EBXeltUhDZe6ExAk]{Armory} <br />\n  这里存放的大多数物品都是普通品质的非魔法武器与护甲，但任意PC若在这些军备中进行搜寻，便能发现一把<em>+2强击九环刀</em>、一对各自装有一份<em>强效猎豹药剂</em>的瓶子，以及一块丝绸包着的三支<em>风暴箭</em>。\n</p>\n<p>更令人不安的是，同样的搜寻会在熔炉周围的地面上发现破损金属的碎片；任何PC都能辨认出这些碎片来自<em>长明灯</em>的燃料容器，这暗示着有人将这件神器的关键部件当作基底金属，用来锻造某种新东西。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C18. Armory\">C18. Armory</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Racks of swords, naginatas, and axes split this room into aisles. Thick, plated armor sits on wooden dummies against the far wall, black shields hanging from a few of their arms. Two large war drums sit on the floor. Next to the drums are barrels filled with arrows and crossbow bolts. A workbench in the southwest corner is covered in neatly arranged maintenance tools. At one side is a foot pedal grindstone, while at the other are a small forge and anvil.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.EBXeltUhDZe6ExAk]{Armory} <br />\n  Most of the items stored here are non-magical weapons and armor of mundane quality, but a PC who Searches among the armaments can discover a <em>+2 striking jiu huan dao</em>, a pair of flasks each containing a <em>greater cheetah’s elixir</em>, and a silk cloth wrapped around three <em>storm arrows</em>.\n</p>\n<p>More distressingly, the same search turns up fragments of broken metal on the ground around the forge; any PC can identify these fragments as having come from the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>’s fuel receptacle, suggesting that someone has used the key part of the artifact as base metals to forge something new.</p>"
            },
            "Chen’s Chambers": {
              "name": "陈的密室 Chen’s Chambers",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C17. 陈的寝室</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>寝室的床只是一张铺在地上的简易垫子和毯子。北侧与南侧的架子上摆放着整齐的漆制祭坛与各式各样的驱魔工具；西北角则放着一面小型青铜锣。房间中央的天花板上悬挂着一面大型彩绘鼓。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这间房属于曹陈，孙海的资深驱魔师；他每晚都会回到这间寝室睡上几个小时，但最近大部分时间都待在神社（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}）。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.mz2A9ZWQRAqocbgm]{Peg} <br />\n  寝室里的一根木钉上挂着一只精致的香炉，其作用等同于一件<em>中等启示香炉</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C17. Chen’s Chambers</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The chamber’s bed is a simple mat and blanket on the floor. Neat, lacquered altars and a variety of exorcist implements rest on shelves to the north and south, while a small bronze gong sits in the northwest corner. A large painted drum hangs from the ceiling in the center of the room.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This room belongs to Cao Chen, Mago Kai’s senior exorcist; he returns to this chamber to sleep for a few hours each night but has spent most of his time of late at the shrine (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}).</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.mz2A9ZWQRAqocbgm]{Peg} <br />\n  Hanging from a peg in the bedroom is an elegant incense holder that functions as a <em>moderate thurible of revelation</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Fenfang’s Chambers": {
              "name": "芬芳的寝宫 Fenfang’s Chambers",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C16. 芬芳的寝室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>家具很简朴，只有一个木柜用来收纳衣物和书籍。染色编织席垫铺满地面，墙上装饰着法莱斯玛与月夜的宗教圣像彩绘。床由一块架在烤炉上的黏土板制成，因此可以从下方加热。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这间房原本属于驱魔师芬芳，但现在属于取代了她的恪尸魔灵堕魔。灵堕魔在杀死芬芳后，把她的大部分遗骸丢弃在树林里，却“念旧”地决定把头骨作为战利品留下。她把头骨藏在床体内置的烤炉里；任何搜索房间的人都将自动发现它。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>恐惧 6：</strong> @UUID[Actor.RbRaSK08W7PUOOSr]{寝室} <br />\n  芬芳与她的两名驱魔师为躲避来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c14generalst00]{C14} 的危险而转移到此房间。若PC尚未有机会在那边偷听到他们的谈话，可以考虑让他们在此获得偷听的机会。\n</p>\n<p><strong>宝藏：</strong>一本名为《匡因宗师录》的书中夹着一张<em>血族驱命卷轴</em>。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C16. Fenfang’s Chambers</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The furniture is sparse, with only a wooden cupboard serving as storage for clothing and books. Dyed woven mats cover the floor, and the walls are decorated with painted religious icons of Pharasma and Tsukiyo. The bed is made out of a clay slab that’s set over an oven, allowing it to be heated from below.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This room belonged to the exorcist Fenfang but now belongs to the akashti nindoru who replaced her. While the nindoru disposed of most of Fenfang’s remains in the woods after killing her, she “sentimentally” decided to keep the skull as a trophy. She keeps it hidden within the oven built into the bed, where it can be discovered automatically by anyone who Searches the room.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Terror 6:</strong> @UUID[Actor.RbRaSK08W7PUOOSr]{Chambers} <br />\n  Fenfang and her two exorcists relocate to this room for safety from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c14generalst00]{C14}. If the PCs haven’t had a chance to eavesdrop on their conversation there, consider giving them a chance to do so here.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Treasure:</strong> Tucked into a book titled Grandmasters of Quain is a <em>scroll of vampiric exsanguination</em>.</p>"
            },
            "Shrine Maiden Quarters": {
              "name": "巫女宿舍 Shrine Maiden Quarters",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C15. 巫女寝所</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间屋子里有一座小烤炉、几卷铺盖、几个橱柜、一座法莱斯玛的神龛，以及一面靠墙放置的青铜锣。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">巫女寝所</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 9</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.3hLps0uPoHvijSi0]{巫女（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>驻扎在唐入的巫女们对柳岸镇或孙海打算如何处置遗迹并不怎么感兴趣；她们同意为他效力，唯一的回报就是等孙海动身前往柳岸镇后，允许她们将这座要塞发展为一座供奉@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}的神殿。作为交换，她们的协助与建议在帮助他守护要塞方面发挥了关键作用；正是她们提出要偷走<em>长明灯</em>的火焰（而巫女们反倒将这一行为视为让一个迷失的使命摆脱湮没）。三名巫女各自轮值8小时守卫警戒钟，其余两人则在寝所里休息与祈祷。她们将闯入的PC视作本地区邪恶魂魄的显现（最坏的情况），或迷失的魂魄（最好的情况）——无论如何，她们对PC的反应都是尽可能迅速地将其放倒，好让他们能继续走向法莱斯玛的拥抱。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 4：</strong>这两名巫女离开房间，去巡逻外围小径（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c3peripheryp00]{C3}）。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.LgfOPt7fG6BD94hD]{寝所} <br />\n  对这间屋子进行一次5分钟的搜寻，会找到一张<em>治疗术卷轴</em>（5环）、两张<em>净除苦难卷轴</em>（4环）、四张<em>清晰心智卷轴</em>（4环）以及一张<em>传讯术卷轴</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C15. Shrine Maiden Quarters</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This room contains a small oven, bed rolls, cupboards, a shrine to Pharasma, and a bronze gong set against the wall.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Shrine Maiden Quarters</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.3hLps0uPoHvijSi0]{Shrine Maidens (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The shrine maidens stationed here at Karahai have little interest in Willowshore or Mago Kai’s plans for the ruins, having agreed to work for him solely in return for permission to develop the fortress into a temple to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} once Kai moves on to Willowshore. In return, their aid and advice has been instrumental in helping him to protect the fortress; it was they who suggested stealing the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>’s flame (an act the shrine maidens instead regard as liberating a lost cause from obscurity). The three shrine maidens each work an 8-hour shift guarding the warding bell, while the other two rest and pray here in their quarters. They regard the intruding PCs as manifestations of the evil spirits of the region at worst, or lost spirits at best—regardless, their reaction to the PCs is to put them down as quickly as possible so they can move on to Pharasma’s embrace.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 4:</strong> These two shrine maidens exit the room to patrol the periphery path (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c3peripheryp00]{C3}).</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.LgfOPt7fG6BD94hD]{Quarters} <br />\n  A 5-minute Search of this room turns up a <em>scroll of heal</em> (5th-rank), two <em>scrolls of cleanse affliction</em> (4th-rank), four <em>scrolls of clear mind</em> (4th-rank), and a <em>scroll of sending</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "General Storage": {
              "name": "通用储物空间 General Storage",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C14. 综合储藏室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">严峻 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间堆满架子的房间里杂乱地存放着各种可能有用、却没有专门存放地点的物品，例如木材锯、维护工具、成捆树枝、动物皮毛、晒干的竹秆，以及用于修补墙洞的黏土。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>PC们第一次来到这间储藏室时，且假设唐入要塞的恐怖阈值低于6，则有三名孙海的驱邪师聚集在此，其中包括潘芬芳——她曾在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event12these00]{事件12——降神会}期间在场。这三名驱邪师构成了芬芳秘密教团的全部成员。</p>\n<p>如果PC们避免被发现，他们就能偷听这三人的谈话；他们会从降神会中认出芬芳的声音。芬芳正对一名看起来很紧张的驱邪师说话，而第三名驱邪师则手持薙刀，专注地站在芬芳身后几步处。谈话持续几分钟；每过一分钟，所有偷听谈话的PC都必须在一次@Check[stealth|dc:26|traits:move,skill,secret,exploration,action:avoid-notice|name:Avoid Notice]检定中成功以避免被察觉，并在一次@Check[perception|dc:22]检定中成功以听清这段低声交谈。每成功坚持一分钟，PC就能获知更多信息，如下所述。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>第1分钟：</strong>芬芳让那名紧张的驱邪师确认：他已经厌倦了曹师傅的领导，并且渴望听听芬芳要说什么。</li>\n  <li><strong>第2分钟：</strong>芬芳要求那名紧张的驱邪师发誓：在死亡惩罚之下不得泄露她即将告诉他的事；那名紧张的驱邪师同意了，而那名专注的驱邪师松了口气，采取了不那么敌对的姿态，抬起了薙刀。</li>\n  <li><strong>第3分钟：</strong>芬芳告诉那名紧张的驱邪师，她和她的同盟一直在接收来自一位名为谭隋靖的灵体的异象；谭隋靖是一位强大的圣洁女子，很久以前死在此地附近。</li>\n  <li><strong>第4分钟：</strong>芬芳继续解释：隋靖的灵体被困在柳岸镇废墟之外的一棵参天巨树下方；若那名紧张的驱邪师加入他们、共同执行解放隋靖的计划，他就能分享她在异象中承诺的巨大奖励。</li>\n  <li><strong>第5分钟：</strong>那名紧张的驱邪师同意并加入教团；芬芳让他回去继续履行职责，并表示之后会再进一步谈论一项计划：夺取要塞资源的控制权，将努力集中于解放谭隋靖。随后芬芳退回自己的住处（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c16fenfangsc00]{C16}），而另外两名驱邪师前往餐厅（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c6diningroom00]{C6}）。</li>\n</ul>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-panfenfang.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">综合储藏室</span> <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.O0NKMBs5GZCEnskv]{\"芬芳\"} @UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{驱邪师（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>如果芬芳在任何时候注意到PC，她就会与他们对质；而在注意到他们那诡异、超凡脱俗的外貌后，她指控他们是邪恶的灵体，并命令她的驱邪师同伴协助她消灭他们，同时她后退一步观察战斗。芬芳和其他驱邪师一样携带薙刀与火把，但她并不会和他们一同攻击——因为她根本不是真正的芬芳。在降神会与这次和PC的新会面之间的某个时刻，芬芳被苦迦菩提腐化的过程以悲剧告终：某晚她走进林中。她找到了一个无人能见的僻静处，试图对抗苦迦菩提的影响，却遭到袭击、被杀害，并被一只能够在此地显形的恪尸魔灵堕魔所取代（讽刺的是，这一切正是芬芳信念动摇的结果）。</p>\n  <p>如今，那只恪尸魔伪装在芬芳的身体之中，通过远距离施法来支援其他驱邪师战斗；它会先施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.f8SBoXiXQjlCKqly]{幻象生物}，让人看起来仿佛她召唤出一条中型的蛇形巨龙在身旁参战。若芬芳受到10点伤害，这些伤害会导致她显形的躯体从骨架上腐朽剥落，显露其真实形态。她会愤怒嚎叫；若此时仍有任何驱邪师存活，他们会立刻逃离战斗。若他们成功逃脱，芬芳骇人的变形将传遍要塞，使恐怖点数增加3点。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐怖6：</strong>储藏室空无一人；芬芳已与她的两名驱邪师同伴撤回住处，直到危险过去。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">效果</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">将@UUID[Item.FfYS95Q82b6NUDeR]{潘芬芳真实形态}效果拖入以关闭她的伪装</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC每发现一分钟的信息可获得10 XP奖励；若他们偷听满五分钟，总奖励为50 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C14. General Storage</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This shelf-filled room contains an eclectic mess of anything that might be useful but doesn’t have its own dedicated space, such as lumber saws, maintenance equipment, bundles of branches, animal pelts, dried bamboo stalks, and clay for patching up holes in the walls.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The first time the PCs visit this storeroom, and assuming that Karahai Fortress’s Terror Threshold is lower than 6, three of Mago Kai’s exorcists are gathered here, including Pan Fenfang, one of the exorcists who was present during @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event12these00]{Event 12 - The Seance}. These three exorcists comprise the total of Fenfang’s secret cult.</p>\n<p>If the PCs avoid being detected, they can eavesdrop on the trio; they’ll recognize Fenfang’s voice from the seance. Fenfang speaks to one exorcist, who looks nervous, while the third stands intently a few paces behind Fenfang, his naginata in hand. The conversation lasts for a few minutes; each minute, all PCs eavesdropping on the conversation must succeed at a @Check[stealth|dc:26|traits:move,skill,secret,exploration,action:avoid-notice|name:Avoid Notice] check to Avoid Notice and a @Check[perception|dc:22] check to hear the quiet conversation. With each minute’s success, the PCs learn more, as detailed below.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>1st Minute:</strong> Fenfang has the nervous exorcist confirm that he is tired of Master Cao’s leadership and is eager to hear what Fenfang has to say.</li>\n  <li><strong>2nd Minute:</strong> Fenfang asks the nervous exorcist to swear not to reveal what she’s about to tell him under punishment of death, the nervous exorcist agrees, and the intent exorcist breathes a sigh of relief and adopts a less antagonistic stance, raising his naginata.</li>\n  <li><strong>3rd Minute:</strong> Fenfang tells the nervous exorcist that she and her ally have been receiving visions from a spirit named Tan Sui-Jing, a powerful holy woman who died in the area long ago.</li>\n  <li><strong>4th Minute:</strong> Fenfang goes on to explain that Sui-Jing’s spirit is trapped below a towering tree beyond the ruins of Willowshore, and that if the nervous exorcist joins with them in their plan to set Sui-Jing free, he’ll be able to share in the great rewards she promised in her visions.</li>\n  <li><strong>5th Minute:</strong> The nervous exorcist agrees and joins the cult; Fenfang tells him to return to his duties and that they’ll later speak further about a plan to take control of the fort’s resources and focus their efforts on freeing Tan Sui-Jing. Fenfang then retreats to her quarters (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c16fenfangsc00]{C16}), while the other two exorcists head to the dining hall (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c6diningroom00]{C6}).</li>\n</ul>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-panfenfang.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">General Storage</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.O0NKMBs5GZCEnskv]{\"Fenfang\"} @UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{Exorcists (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If at any point Fenfang notices the PCs, she confronts them, and upon noticing their eerie, otherworldly appearances, she accuses them of being evil spirits and orders her exorcist allies to help her destroy them while she steps back to observe the fight. While Fenfang carries a naginata and torch just like the other exorcists, she doesn’t attack with them—for she isn’t really Fenfang at all. At some point between the seance and this new meeting with the PCs, Fenfang’s corruption by Kugaptee reached a tragic conclusion when she headed into the woods one night. She found a private place where no one else could see and attempted to fight Kugaptee’s influence, only to be attacked, murdered, and replaced by an akashti nindoru that was able to manifest in the area (ironically as a result of Fenfang’s faltering belief).</p>\n  <p>Now disguised in Fenfang’s body, the akashti supports the other exorcists in a fight by casting spells from a distance, starting with @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.f8SBoXiXQjlCKqly]{Illusory Creature} to make it appear as if she summoned a Medium serpentine dragon to join the fight at her side. If Fenfang takes 10 damage, that damage causes her manifested body to decay away from her frame, revealing her true form. She howls in rage, and if any exorcists remain alive at this point, they flee the battle at once. If they escape, word of Fenfang’s horrific transformation spreads through the fortress, adding 3 Terror Points.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 6:</strong> The storage room is empty; Fenfang has retreated to her quarters with her two exorcist allies until the danger has passed.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">Drag on the @UUID[Item.FfYS95Q82b6NUDeR]{Pan Fenfang True Form} Effect to turn off her disguise</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Each minute of information the PCs discover grants a 10 XP reward, for a total reward of 50 XP if they overhear the full five minutes.</p>"
            },
            "Bath": {
              "name": "沐浴 Bath",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C13. 浴室</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>与要塞的其他区域不同，这个房间的地面铺着瓷砖。瓷砖在地面上构成同心圆图案，看起来刚刚被清洗过。西北侧立着三间竹制隔间，里面是蹲便器；东南侧则是一座大型浴池。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shaguang.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">浴室</span> <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.51Tl7LCWXtrMSi1T]{沙观超}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>沙光豪——在事件12：降神会出席的三名驱魔师之一——在这里。他佝偻着身子，用小刷子用力刷洗地面；他的薙刀和未点燃的火把靠在东北侧门框上。若有人与他对质，他会像挥舞武器一样挥舞刷子，宣称：“退后！我精通宇宙奥秘。只消一眼，我就能把你直接送进骨园！”进行一次成功的 @Check[perception|dc:19|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] 察言观色检定后，PC会看出光豪不过是在虚张声势。若他遭到攻击，尽管处境不利也会还手。他对自身极限缺乏认知，导致他会在无意间战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>另一方面，如果PC在降神会期间将沙光豪的影响提升到4，他会认出PC正是他和其他人先前交谈过的那些魂魄。他犹豫片刻，随即放下刷子，下意识地揉了揉后脑勺，说：“等一下，曹师父说你们不可能在这里。你们怎么会在这儿？”只要PC不攻击或威胁他，光豪愿意回答一些问题，尽管答得不太顺畅。下面列出了一些可能的回应。</p>\n<p><strong>你为什么在这里？</strong>“因为我有强大的灵力。那方面的天才。绝不说谎。”</p>\n<p><strong>那你为什么要在这里刷地？</strong>“哦，那个。那、那个是在积攒灵能。让我‘修炼魂魄，’”光豪用一种机械、单调的语气重复最后那句话。他盯着地板。“诸如此类的东西。至少曹师父是这么说的。”</p>\n<p><strong>你能告诉我们关于曹师父的事吗？</strong>“一个老头儿懂得可真多。手也快得出奇。”光豪又揉了揉头。</p>\n<p><strong>你能告诉我们关于这座要塞的事吗？</strong>“如果我没记错，地基是龙华帝国大概一千年前打下的，用来压制本地盗匪。还是一万年前来着？总之，很久以前。对。”</p>\n<p><strong>你能告诉我们要塞目前的情况吗？</strong>“我觉得还行吧。伙食还可以，尤其是你能赶上第一轮开饭的时候。有些新来的佣兵打呼噜，不过你把布往他们头上一盖，几乎就听不见了。”</p>\n<p><strong>你能告诉我们关于孙海的事吗？</strong>“那个大块头？他挺能打的。有次还把我从一只巨蜘蛛手里救了下来。我说是‘救了’，但其实那情况我自己完全能搞定，你懂的。不过看他把那把大斧头甩出去还是挺震撼的；他一斧就把那虫子劈成两半！”</p>\n<p><strong>你见过一口大型青铜钟吗？</strong>“呃，见过。几周前你们就在场。你们不太聪明，是吧？”</p>\n<p><strong>钟在哪儿？</strong>“当然在神龛那边。不然还能在哪儿？”他指着盥洗间的门，指向走廊尽头的那扇门。“从那儿过去，右转，然后再穿过几扇门。你不可能找不到。”</p>\n<p>\n  <strong><em>长明灯</em>的火焰怎么了？</strong>“那个大块头把它拿走了，放进了钟里；想知道更多你得去问他。”\n</p>\n<p>尽管光豪的回答大多帮不上忙，但只要任务不涉及直接伤害要塞里的其他住民，就可以通过一次成功的 @Check[deception|dc:24|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie] 说谎检定来哄他，或通过一次成功的 @Check[diplomacy|dc:27|traits:action:request,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental|name:Request] 请求检定来让他做几乎任何事。</p>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC设法从沙光豪那里得知有关要塞的信息，给予他们经验值，视同在战斗中击败了他。如果他们让他协助完成一项任务，额外给予40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C13. Bath</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>In contrast to the rest of the fortress, the floor of this room is set with tiles. They form a design of concentric circles on the floor and appear to be freshly cleaned. Three bamboo stalls containing squat toilets stand to the northwest, while to the southeast is a large pool for bathing.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shaguang.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Bath</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.51Tl7LCWXtrMSi1T]{Sha Guanchao}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creature:</strong> Sha Guanghao, one of the three exorcists who were present for Event 12: The Seance, is here. His hunched figure scrubs vigorously at the floor with a small brush, and his naginata and unlit torch rest against the northeastern door frame. If confronted, he brandishes the brush like a weapon and declares, “Stay back! I am adept in the mysteries of the universe. With the slightest glance, I can send you straight to the Boneyard!” With a successful @Check[perception|dc:19|traits:concentrate,secret,action:sense-motive|name:Sense Motive] check to Sense Motive, a PC discerns that Guanghao is all bluster. If he’s attacked, he fights back despite his disadvantages. His poor grasp of his own limits means he inadvertently fights to the death.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>On the other hand, if the PCs brought Sha Guanghao up to Influence 4 during the seance, he’ll recognize the PCs as the spirits he and the others spoke to earlier. He hesitates, then lowers his brush and reflexively rubs the back of his head, saying, “Wait a minute, Master Cao said you can’t be here. How are you here?” Assuming the PCs don’t attack or threaten him, Guanghao is willing to answer some questions, albeit with difficulty. Some likely responses are listed below.</p>\n<p><strong>Why are you here?</strong> “Because I’ve got great spiritual powers. Real prodigy with that stuff. No lie.”</p>\n<p><strong>But why are you here scrubbing?</strong> “Oh, that. It, uh, builds spiritual energy. Lets me ‘cultivate my spirit,’” Guanghao says, repeating the last phrase in a rote monotone. He stares at the floor. “That kind of stuff. At least that’s what Master Cao says.”</p>\n<p><strong>What can you tell us about Master Cao?</strong> “Knows a lot of stuff for an old man. Surprisingly fast hands.” Guanghao rubs his head once again.</p>\n<p><strong>What can you tell us about the fortress?</strong> “If memory serves, the foundation was laid down by Imperial Lung Wa about a thousand years ago to rein in the local bandits. Or was it ten thousand years? Anyway, a long time ago. Yeah.”</p>\n<p><strong>What can you tell us about the current state of the fortress?</strong> “It’s okay, I guess. The food is all right, especially if you get in the first service. Some of the new mercenaries snore, but if you drop a cloth over their heads, you can barely hear it.”</p>\n<p><strong>What can you tell us about Mago Kai?</strong> “The big man? He’s pretty tough. Saved me from a giant spider once. I say ‘saved,’ but I totally had that situation taken care of on my own, you know. But it was still kind of amazing to see him throw that big axe of his; he sliced the bug right in half!”</p>\n<p><strong>Have you seen a large bronze bell?</strong> “Uh, yes. You were there a few weeks ago. You aren’t too bright, are you?”</p>\n<p><strong>Where is the bell?</strong> “Over in the shrine, of course. Where else would it be?” He points through the water closet’s door to the one down the hall. “Through there, make a right, then head through a couple more doors. You can’t miss it.”</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>What happened to the <em>Eternal Lantern’s</em> flame?</strong> “The big man took it and placed it in the bell; you’d have to talk to him to find out more, I suppose.”\n</p>\n<p>While Guanghao’s answers are mostly less than helpful, he can be convinced to do just about any task with a successful @Check[deception|dc:24|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie] check to Lie or a @Check[diplomacy|dc:27|traits:action:request,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental|name:Request] check to Request, as long as the task doesn’t involve directly harming any of the other fortress residents.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs manage to learn information about the fortress from Sha Guanghao, grant them XP as if they’d defeated him in combat. If they get him to help with a task, grant them an additional 40 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Inner Gates": {
              "name": "内门 Inner Gates",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C12. Inner Gates\">C12. 内门</h2>\n<p>这些区域的两侧都由坚固的木墙覆盖并用栅栏围起，木墙上装有大门。</p>\n<p><strong>C12a. 内水门：</strong>通往该区域的两扇门上的黑色油漆看起来比区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2a} 的门更为崭新、风化程度也更低。奇怪的是，虽然其中三个铰链很普通，但每扇门都有一个铰链被设计成微笑的乌龟造型。这里的门总是保持关闭并上锁。</p>\n<p><strong>C12b. 土门：</strong>这两扇门上固定着一对装饰性的牛角。若将其用作把手，它们会将翻越大门的 @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] 攀爬检定降低至 DC 15。这些门保持关闭；当要塞达到恐惧阈值 3 后，它们也会被上锁。</p>\n<p><strong>C12c. 小木门：</strong>这些门保持敞开；当它们关闭时，每扇门上都能辨认出一幅鸡的彩绘图案。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">内门</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{佣兵执法者（5）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 3：</strong>土门与小木门都关闭并上锁。来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c6diningroom00]{C6} 的五名佣兵在小木门内侧站岗，准备对任何试图从此处进入的人发起对峙，或踏入花园（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c22garden00000]{C22}）去对付其中的入侵者。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 7：</strong>任何在小木门站岗的佣兵都会撤退到营房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}）。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C12. Inner Gates\">C12. Inner Gates</h2>\n<p>Each of these areas is covered and fenced in on either side by stout wooden walls fitted with gates.</p>\n<p><strong>C12a. Inner Water Gate:</strong> The black paint on the two gates into this area appears fresher and less weathered than that of those at area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2a}. Oddly, while three of the hinges are normal, one on each is designed to look like a smiling turtle. The gates here are always kept closed and locked.</p>\n<p><strong>C12b. Earth Gate:</strong> A pair of decorative cow horns are affixed to these two gates. If used as handholds, they reduce the @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check to Climb over the gate to DC 15. These gates are kept closed; they’re also locked once the fortress reaches Terror Threshold 3.</p>\n<p><strong>C12c. Small Wood Gate:</strong> These gates are left open; when shut, a painted image of a chicken is discernible on each.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Inner Gates</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{Mercenary Enforcers (5)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Terror 3:</strong> Earth Gate and Small Wood Gate are both closed and locked. The five mercenaries from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c6diningroom00]{C6} stand guard within Small Wood Gate, ready to confront anyone who attempts to enter here or to step into the garden (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c22garden00000]{C22}) to confront intruders therein.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 7:</strong> Any mercenaries on guard at Small Wood Gate retreat to the barracks (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}).</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Shrine": {
              "name": "圣坛 Shrine",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C11. 神龛</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">极难 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>假设PC们已经经历过事件12：招魂会，他们会自动认出这个房间。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房由燃烧的火把提供昏暗照明，一口巨大的青铜寺钟悬挂在房间中央。房间四周摆放着五个小而空的鸟笼，而钟口处闪烁着苍白、诡异的光辉。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  PC们会自动认出从钟内散出的光芒，与柳岸镇的\n  <em>长明灯</em>所发出的光芒相同。\n</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>曹陈与一名巫女在此房间中。巫女忙于清扫与冥想，而曹陈则在悬钟旁跪地祷告。若他们任何一人发现PC们，便会立刻发动攻击，将PC们视作前来复仇的邪恶魂魄。</p>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-wardingbell.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Warding Bell\" alt=\"a massive bronze temple bell\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-wardingbell.webp')\" />\n<p>然而，若PC们在招魂会期间将曹陈的影响提升至4，这位资深驱魔师会认出他们正是先前与他交谈过的魂魄。他抬手示意，阻止巫女的攻击。随后他请PC们离开房间，前往前厅（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c10shrineant00]{C10}）交谈。若PC们拒绝，他会悲伤地叹息，然后他与巫女发动攻击。</p>\n<p>若PC们与陈交谈，他会听取关于苦迦菩提的进一步警告，以及他们要求停用镇守钟的请求，但他也警告PC们：要劝退孙海将会很困难。陈不愿背叛他当前的雇主，因为海的资源与影响力使他与他的驱魔师们能在神门内行事而少受政治掣肘。这位驱魔师也认为，与其说服这位木材领主离开并寄望事情自然好转，不如继续留在海的麾下并重新封印苦迦菩提更为高效。若有人告知他苦迦菩提已经腐化了一名驱魔师，陈会感到警惕——他不愿仅凭PC们的一面之词就采取行动，但也不会在未调查前就将警告置之不理。陈派巫女去警告海并着手调查，同时要求PC们留在他视线所及之处。若PC们按命令耐心等待，孙海会在15分钟后亲自前来与他们交谈，细节见第354页。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.PwfqbtvRr8WRGhnV]{Warding Bell}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-caochen.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">神龛</span> <span class=\"keepme\">极难 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.unQezEYEP43zyDbg]{Cao Chen} @UUID[Actor.3hLps0uPoHvijSi0]{Shrine Maiden} @UUID[Actor.nlicOr5pze7UKIPV]{Warding Bell}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>靠近镇守钟会使PC们暴露在其神圣灵光之下，只要他们仍处于其存在范围内就会持续受到伤害。由于缺少钟槌——该物由孙海携带——要停用或摧毁它都很困难。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们解除镇守钟，他们不仅会像击败一个等级11的复杂危害那样照常获得经验值，而且此举还会使要塞的防幽灵墙失效（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12karahaifeatu00]{唐入特性}）。一旦镇守钟被解除，唐入的恐惧点数若尚未达到3则提升至3，并在本幕剩余时间内无法降至3以下。</p>\n<p>为达成此目标给予PC们80 XP——这是将柳岸镇迁渡回生者世界所需的两项任务之一。若他们在不摧毁镇守钟的情况下完成，将此XP奖励提高至120 XP，因为这口圣钟在他们开始第4幕时可能成为助力。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C11. Shrine</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Assuming the PCs already endured Event 12: The Seance, they’ll automatically recognize this room.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This room is dimly lit by burning torches, and a massive bronze temple bell hangs from the center of the chamber. Five small, empty bird cages are placed around the sides of the room, and the bell’s mouth flickers with a pale, eerie radiance.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  The PCs automatically recognize the glow issuing from within the bell as the same glow emitted by Willowshore’s\n  <em>Eternal Lantern</em>.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Cao Chen and a shrine maiden are present in this room. The shrine maiden busies herself with cleaning and meditation while Cao Chen kneels in prayer near the hanging bell. If either of them spot the PCs, they attack at once, interpreting the PCs as evil spirits come for vengeance.</p>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-wardingbell.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Warding Bell\" alt=\"a massive bronze temple bell\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-wardingbell.webp')\" />\n<p>If the PCs brought Cao Chen up to Influence 4 during the seance, however, the senior exorcist recognizes them as the spirits he spoke with earlier. With a raised hand, he stays the shrine maiden’s attack. He then asks the PCs to step out of the room into the antechamber (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c10shrineant00]{C10}) to speak. If the PCs turn him down, he sighs sadly, and he and the shrine maiden attack.</p>\n<p>If the PCs speak with Chen, he listens to further warnings about Kugaptee and their pleas to deactivate the warding bell, but he warns the PCs that it will be difficult to dissuade Mago Kai. Chen isn’t willing to betray his current employer, as Kai’s resources and influence allow him and his exorcists to work within Shenmen with fewer political complications. The exorcist also feels like it would be more efficient to stay with Kai and reseal Kugaptee rather than simply convincing the lumber lord to leave and hope things work out. If he’s informed that Kugaptee has corrupted one of the exorcists, Chen becomes alarmed—he isn’t willing to act only on the PCs’ word but also won’t brush their warnings aside without investigating them. Chen sends the shrine maiden to warn Kai and then investigate while telling the PCs to stay where Chen can see them. If the PCs wait patiently as ordered, Mago Kai comes to speak to them in person in 15 minutes, as detailed on page 354.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.PwfqbtvRr8WRGhnV]{Warding Bell}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-caochen.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Shrine</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.unQezEYEP43zyDbg]{Cao Chen} @UUID[Actor.3hLps0uPoHvijSi0]{Shrine Maiden} @UUID[Actor.nlicOr5pze7UKIPV]{Warding Bell}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> Close proximity to the warding bell exposes the PCs to its sacred aura, causing them to take damage so long as they remain in its presence. Without the bell’s ringer, which is carried by Mago Kai, deactivating or destroying it is difficult.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs disable the warding bell, they not only earn experience for the act as normal for defeating a level 11 complex hazard, but doing so also disables the ghost-proof walls of the fortress (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12karahaifeatu00]{Karahai Features}). Once the warding bell is disabled, Karahai’s Terror Points increase to 3 if they aren’t there already and can’t be reduced below 3 for the remainder of this act.</p>\n<p>Grant the PCs 80 XP for achieving this—one of the two tasks required to transmigrate Willowshore back to the living world. Increase this XP reward to 120 XP if they do so without destroying the warding bell, as the sacred bell could be a boon for them once they begin Act 4.</p>"
            },
            "Shrine Antechamber": {
              "name": "神龛前厅 Shrine Antechamber",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C10. Shrine Antechamber\">C10. 神社前厅</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间石室由三十支白色蜡烛照明，蜡烛沿着两侧狭窄的壁架燃烧。地面中央有一座略微抬高的圆形台座，周围环绕着一圈雕刻装饰环。成百上千张细长的纸符与纸垂如帘幕般悬挂在这圈环的四周。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.yGUkHnNEwP8Ht1Kr]{前厅} <br />\n  如果PC们花10分钟搜寻悬挂的纸垂与纸符，他们会找到一张<em>千痛针符箓</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C10. Shrine Antechamber\">C10. Shrine Antechamber</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This stone room is lit by thirty white wax candles that burn along narrow shelves to either side. A raised circular dais sits in the center of the floor, with a carved decorative ring surrounding it. Hundreds of long paper talismans and shide hang like curtains around this ring.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.yGUkHnNEwP8Ht1Kr]{Antechamber} <br />\n  If the PCs Search the hanging shide and talismans for 10 minutes, they’ll find a <em>needle thousand-pains fulu</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Purification Room": {
              "name": "净化室 Purification Room",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C9. 净化室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房的远墙边放着一座石台，石台上嵌着一个直径五英尺的石盆。盆中盛着清水，旁边整齐摆放着数个竹勺。墙上挂着一幅绘有水墨画的卷轴，画中一只麻雀停在王座靠背上。一名蓝皮肤的女子坐在王座上，目光始终警觉地注视着周围。</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoiscroll.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nosoi Scroll\" alt=\"magic scroll painted with Pharasma sitting on her throne and a nosoi perched on the back\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoiscroll.webp')\" />\n<p>石盆里的水由巫女定期净化，供访客在前往东南方的神社前清洁自身使用。墙上的卷轴描绘的是@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}在骨园的王座之上。一名PC若在一次@Check[religion|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定中成功进行回忆知识，便知晓这些信息；若大成功或大失败，则他们还知道这石盆是用来舀水浇洗双手以进行净化的。</p>\n<p>PC可以在此处以1分钟行动进行净身。这样做可能会让他们得到法莱斯玛的赠礼（见下方宝藏条目），但无论是否获得赠礼，每周一次，此行动还会让一股不祥感笼罩要塞中的其他住民，获得1点恐惧点数。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/vanth.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">净化室</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.TjojyI1jP458IIiW]{疫鸟们的复仇} @UUID[Actor.IEcwf7XUUl35OduW]{梵斯（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>如果PC们在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{事件11——疫鸟们的早午餐}中，那些鸟类造访柳岸镇时，曾严重冒犯来访的疫鸟，那么这些复仇心切的疫鸟便会利用它们的人脉，以及这座供奉法莱斯玛的圣所之神圣性质，制造出如下危害。PC可以通过一次成功的@Check[stealth|dc:29|traits:move,skill,secret,action:sneak|name:Sneak]检定进行潜行，从而在1轮内避免被该危害注意到。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.z7MFMwM52pqgHGw0]{招魂者的恩赐} <br />\n  如果PC们在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{事件11——疫鸟们的早午餐}中取悦了疫鸟，达成至少六次成功，那么这些招魂者已安排好一份恩赐；但PC必须在卷轴前使用盆中之水进行1分钟净身以净化自身，才能获得该恩赐。这样做的PC会听到麻雀的啼鸣声，随后在刚洗净的双手中得到下列之一（选择PC最能用得上的那件物品）：一份<em>中等生命灵药</em>、一个装有<em>强效潜能水晶</em>的袋子、一支<em>中等灵性战号</em>，或一张属于该PC魔法根源中某个实用5环法术的<em>卷轴</em>。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{事件11——疫鸟们的早午餐}中成功安抚了疫鸟，因此此处没有陷阱在等待他们，则给予他们XP，视同他们在战斗中击败了被召唤出来的梵斯。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C9. Purification Room</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A stone platform with a five-foot-diameter stone basin built into it sits against the far wall of this room. The basin is filled with clear water, and several bamboo ladles are arranged nearby. A painted ink scroll depicting a sparrow as it perches on the back of a throne hangs on the wall. A blue-skinned woman sits on the throne, her gaze ever watchful.</p>\n</div>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoiscroll.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nosoi Scroll\" alt=\"magic scroll painted with Pharasma sitting on her throne and a nosoi perched on the back\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nosoiscroll.webp')\" />\n<p>The water in the basin is regularly purified by the shrine maidens for use by visitors to cleanse themselves before proceeding on to the shrine to the southeast. The scroll on the wall depicts @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} on her throne in the Boneyard. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[religion|dc:10|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge is aware of this information, while on a critical success, they know that the basin is used to purify their hands by ladling water onto them.</p>\n<p>A PC can perform ablutions here as a 1-minute activity. Doing so might grant them a gift from Pharasma (see Treasure entry below), but regardless, once per week, this activity also causes a sense of foreboding to settle over the other inhabitants of the fortress, granting 1 Terror Point.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/vanth.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Purification Room</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.TjojyI1jP458IIiW]{Nosois' Vengeance} @UUID[Actor.IEcwf7XUUl35OduW]{Vanths (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> If the PCs seriously offended the visiting nosois when the birds visited Willowshore in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{Event 11 - Nosois’ Brunch}, the vengeful nosois use their contacts and the sacred nature of this shrine to Pharasma to create the following hazard. A PC can avoid being noticed by the hazard for 1 round by Sneaking with a successful @Check[stealth|dc:29|traits:move,skill,secret,action:sneak|name:Sneak] check.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.z7MFMwM52pqgHGw0]{Psychopomp's Boon} <br />\n  If the PCs pleased the nosois during @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{Event 11 - Nosois’ Brunch} by achieving at least six successes, the psychopomps have arranged for a boon, but a PC must spend 1 minute performing ablutions using water from the basin before the scroll to purify themselves to receive this boon. A PC who does so hears the sound of sparrows singing, then receives in their freshly washed hands one of the following (choose the item that the PC will gain the most use out of): a <em>moderate elixir of life</em>, a pouch containing a <em>greater potency crystal</em>, a <em>moderate spiritual warhorn</em>, or a <em>scroll</em> of a useful 5th-rank spell from that PC’s magical tradition.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If no trap awaits the PCs here because they did well in appeasing the nosois during @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog11faceto.JournalEntryPage.11event11nosoi00]{Event 11 - Nosois’ Brunch}, grant them XP as if they’d defeated the summoned vanths in combat.</p>"
            },
            "Lumber Storage": {
              "name": "木材储存区 Lumber Storage",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C8. Lumber Storage\">C8. 木材储藏间</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间狭长而弯曲的房间里，墙边堆满了原木、木料和各式各样大小的木板，大多覆着尘土。两架梯子分别位于东侧与南侧，通往墙上离地十五英尺处的小门。</p>\n</div>\n<p>孙海最初来到这一带时，身边带着数十名伐木工，打算立刻让他们着手处理从柳岸镇运来的木材。然而，当这座破败城镇的状况变得显而易见后，他改而让他们去砍伐更靠近唐入一带、价值较低的树木。到夏末时，他意识到这些木材品质太差，不值得投入成本，便将伐木工送回伺城；此处存放的木材，正是他们至今为止设法采伐到的部分。其间有一些被用于部分修复唐入桥，但大多数在过去几个月里都只是在这里积灰。</p>\n<p>这些木材十分干燥，若PC们在此点火，纵火会令要塞的住民不安；这会获得1点恐惧点数。要塞的夯土墙能将火势控制住，但失去他们迄今为止好不容易收集到的少量木材会让孙海尤其恼火；下一次遭遇他时，他的挫败感显而易见，并使他对抗情绪效果的所有豁免骰承受–1环境减值。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.Ji0DndBI88azMfSY]{Lumber Storage North} @UUID[Actor.IuPVHsJeFpgHip5G]{Lumber Storage South} <br />\n  尽管这些木材的规格并不统一，但仍足以对彻底修复唐入桥大有帮助（将在下一幕中处理）。若PC们花费10分钟在此搜索，他们会注意到在房间北侧木材堆中，有一枚似乎被遗忘的<em>蜥蜴人钉刺</em>。在南侧，他们会发现一把同样被冷落的<em>+2强击手斧</em>。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C8. Lumber Storage\">C8. Lumber Storage</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The walls of this long, curving room are stacked with logs, lumber, and planks of all shapes and sizes, most of them covered in dust. Two ladders, one to the east and one to the south, lead up to small doors in the wall that are located fifteen feet off the ground.</p>\n</div>\n<p>When Mago Kai first arrived in the area, he had dozens of woodcutters with him, and he intended to get them to work processing lumber from Willowshore immediately. When the state of the ruined town became apparent, however, he instead had them work on less viable trees closer to Karahai. By the end of summer, he realized that this lumber was too inferior to justify the cost and sent his woodcutters back home to Sze; the lumber stored here represents what they’ve managed to harvest so far. Some of it was used to partially repair Karahai Bridge, but most of it has just been gathering dust for the past several months.</p>\n<p>The lumber is dry, and if the PCs start a fire here, the arson unsettles the fortress’s occupants; this grants 1 Terror Point. The fortress’s earthen walls contain the fire, but the loss of what little lumber they’ve gathered so far frustrates Kai in particular; the next time he’s encountered, his frustration is apparent and imparts a –1 circumstance penalty to all of his saving throws against emotion effects.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.Ji0DndBI88azMfSY]{Lumber Storage North} @UUID[Actor.IuPVHsJeFpgHip5G]{Lumber Storage South} <br />\n  Despite its mismatched nature, the lumber here could go a long way toward fully repairing Karahai Bridge (which is addressed in the next act). If the PCs spend 10 minutes Searching here, they’ll notice a <em>saurian spike</em> lying apparently forgotten amid the lumber stacks in the northern part of the room. To the south, they find a similarly neglected <em>+2 striking handaxe</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Kitchen": {
              "name": "厨房 Kitchen",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C7. Kitchen\">C7. 厨房</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房铺着红色瓷砖地面，泥土墙面被烟熏得发黑。东墙边靠着一座砖砌炉灶，房间北侧有两扇用于通风的大窗户。沉重的锅具与平底锅挂在木钉上，一个大木橱柜里放着陶碗与干燥香料。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/servant.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">厨房</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.57THLHf0Eh584f2M]{仆人（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>白天，一对厨子正忙着工作：擀面、蒸饺子，以及准备其他食物。夜幕降临时，他们会回到村里的家中。要吓跑这两名仆人很容易，而他们逃跑时的慌乱会为要塞增加1点恐惧点数。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 2：</strong>仆人们放弃此处的职责，返回村里的家中。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.BMFdBvJ2FVDJ0PRv]{橱柜} <br />\n  搜寻橱柜会找到相当数量用于冲泡魔法茶的补给；总计有价值150 gp的原材料存放在这里。还能在挂钩上发现三口沉重、养锅良好的铸铁炒锅。每口炒锅为1 负载，价值50 gp，并且在用其烹饪餐食时，进行烹饪相关的制作检定可将其视为一套上等工匠工具包。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C7. Kitchen\">C7. Kitchen</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This room has red tiled floors and smoke-stained earthen walls. A brick stove sits against the eastern wall, and the northern side of the room features two large windows for ventilation. Heavy pots and pans hang from wooden pegs, and a large wooden cupboard contains clay bowls and dried spices.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/servant.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Kitchen</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.57THLHf0Eh584f2M]{Servants (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of cooks are busy at work during the day, rolling dough, steaming dumplings, and otherwise preparing food. As night falls, they return to their homes in the village. Frightening these two servants is an easy task, and the way they carry on as they flee adds 1 Terror Point to the fortress.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 2:</strong> The servants abandon their duties here and return to their homes in the village.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.BMFdBvJ2FVDJ0PRv]{Cabinets} <br />\n  A search of the cabinets turns up a fair amount of supplies for brewing magical tea; in all, there’s 150 gp worth of raw materials kept here. Three heavy, well-seasoned cast iron woks can be found hanging from hooks. Each wok is 1 Bulk, is worth 50 gp, and functions as a sterling artisan’s toolkit for Crafting checks to cook meals in them.\n</p>"
            },
            "Dining Room": {
              "name": "餐厅 Dining Room",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C6. 餐厅</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>该区域是一间宽敞的餐厅，房间中央摆放着两张矮桌，西南侧墙边则有一排长长的餐食架。桌子与架子旁摆放着许多坐垫，提供了好几处可以坐下休息放松的地方。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">餐厅</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{佣兵打手（5）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>白天时，五名佣兵打手会在这里放松，享用食物或彼此玩牌类游戏。夜晚房间为空；若PC在用餐时间潜入要塞，可能会在这里遭遇更多要塞的住客。在用餐时间袭击这个房间会获得1点恐惧点数。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 3：</strong>此房间内的佣兵会转移到区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c12innergate00]{C12c}，锁上大门，并在门内站岗警戒。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 7：</strong>此房间内的佣兵会转移到区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}，并将自己 barricade 在其中。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C6. Dining Room</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This area is a large dining room containing two low tables in the middle of the room and a long dining shelf along the southwest wall. Numerous cushions have been arranged along the tables and the shelf, providing several places to sit and relax.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Dining Room</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{Mercenary Enforcers (5)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> During the day, five mercenary enforcers relax here, enjoying food or playing tile games with each other. The room is empty at night; if the PCs infiltrate the fortress during mealtime, more of the fortress’s occupants might be encountered here. Attacking this room during mealtime grants 1 Terror Point.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 3:</strong> The mercenaries in this room relocate to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c12innergate00]{C12c}, lock the gates, and stand guard within.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 7:</strong> The mercenaries in this room relocate to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5} and barricade themselves in.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Common Barracks": {
              "name": "普通营房 Common Barracks",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C5. Common Barracks\">C5. 公共营房</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>整齐排列的双层床沿着这间弧形房间的墙壁摆放，每张床都配有一个小脚柜。西南角有一架梯子，通往离地约十五英尺高的墙上一个小门。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这间房供佣兵与驱魔人用来休息放松。脚柜里放着制服、洗漱用品以及其他个人物品。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">公共营房</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{佣兵执法者（至多9名）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>总共有九名佣兵执法者与七名驱魔人驻扎在唐入。白天这间房间是空的，但到了夜里，他们都会（除曹宸与潘芬芳外；两人另有他处的私人房间）回到这里睡觉。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 7：</strong>要塞内仍然活着的所有佣兵执法者都会回到这间房间，锁上门，然后把自己 barricade 在里面。成功通过一次 @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] 检定后，PC可以破拆打开门（如果门上了锁，则该DC提升至 @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]）。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C5. Common Barracks\">C5. Common Barracks</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Neatly arranged bunk beds, each with a small footlocker, line the walls of this curved room. A ladder in the southwest corner leads up to a small door in the wall about fifteen feet off the ground.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This room is used by the mercenaries and exorcists to rest and relax in. The footlockers contain uniforms, toiletries, and other personal items.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Common Barracks</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{Mercenary Enforcers (up to 9)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> In all, there are nine mercenary enforcers and seven exorcists stationed at Karahai. During the day, this room is empty, but at night, they all (save for Cao Chen and Pan Fenfang, who have their own chambers elsewhere) return here to sleep.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 7:</strong> All of the mercenary enforcers in the fort who still live return to this room, lock the door, then barricade themselves in. With a successful @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check, a PC can Force Open the door (this DC increases to @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] if the door is locked).</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Stables": {
              "name": "马厩 Stables",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C4. 马厩</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>第二段默认第五个栏位里的生物仍然存在。如果PC能看穿黑暗，请删去该段或按需调整。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>低矮的栅栏沿着这间屋子的西北侧墙分隔出五个圈栏。入口旁的前两个圈栏里关着健壮、毛茸茸的马匹，而另外三个除了散落的干草铺垫外空无一物。北边有一架梯子通向上方的一扇小门，那扇门位于离地十五英尺高的墙面上。</p>\n</div>\n<p>房间南侧笼罩在神秘的黑暗中，黑暗里传来一种奇怪、轻柔的咔嗒声。</p>\n<p>这两匹坐骑虽受过战斗训练，但只在需要快速传信或紧急情况下才会被骑乘。自从巫女们来到要塞后，她们能使用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.R9xqCBblkS5KE4y7]{传讯术}法术，使这对马在传递迅速消息方面更显得不那么有用了。这些马十分易受惊，但对PC不构成威胁；它们只是被最远那个栏位的住客吓到了。</p>\n<p>生物：离入口最远的栏位里关着一只远比马更古怪的生物。雇佣兵们抓住并圈养了一种奇怪的魔法兽，称为窃光者——一种蜥蜴般的生物，孙海和他的雇佣兵刚抵达柳岸镇的废墟时发现它就住在那里。他们设法活捉了这只生物并把它带回此处，将其既当作宠物，也因为首席驱魔师曹辰对它很感兴趣。</p>\n<p>他们谁也没意识到，这生物是有智慧的，而且能说话；只是要塞里没人会窃光者懂的任何语言，因此他们把它试图交流的行为误认为“怪物发出的怪声”。与马不同，窃光者被锁链拴在马厩栏位里，身躯被数条铁链束缚，使其处于禁足状态。它的口鼻也被紧紧套住，以防它发出那些怪声（也包括说话），或使用其惊悚尖叫。它可以在自己的栏位里活动，但也仅此而已。</p>\n<p>曹辰将窃光者视为一个不同寻常却重要的机会，可用来使他们的力量更加多样化——因为这种生物在黑暗中如鱼得水（而邪恶往往潜伏于黑暗）。他提出一种理论：该生物吞噬光亮的能力或许能被改变，从而吞噬亡灵能量。这个想法虽离奇，但旁人越是嘲笑，他越坚信自己找到了突破口。孙海仍不相信这生物有何价值，尤其考虑到它会发出骇人的尖叫；不过到目前为止，他仍允许曹辰留它一命。</p>\n<p>窃光者被套上口套时无法施放其先天法术，但它的窃光灵光仍使其周围区域变得相当昏暗。它起初对PC的态度为不友善，不过其本性极其天真，更像小狗而非警惕的人类。由于它只会说龙语，PC可能（就像要塞当前的住客一样）无法与其沟通。</p>\n<p>如果PC能与窃光者沟通，他们便可得知它那悲惨的经历。解除其锁链需要将锁链开锁（用曹辰携带的钥匙，或进行四次@Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock]检定来开锁），用一次@Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open]检定来破拆锁链，或将锁链摧毁（硬度5，HP 20［BT 10］）。解救窃光者会使其对PC的态度自动提升一级，朝向乐于帮助。</p>\n<p>如果PC让窃光者至少变得友善，它就会同意帮助他们。它可以与PC同行并并肩作战，但窃光者更偏好（并会建议）另一种做法——在要塞里潜行，折磨并惊吓它的捕获者。如果PC选择此方案，窃光者的行动会在接下来的4小时内自动以每小时1点的速率增加恐惧点数；之后该生物会被发现并被驱逐，或可能被杀死（由你决定）。精明的PC能在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}区域很好地利用窃光者的能力。</p>\n<p>如果PC释放了窃光者却未与其建立沟通，它会逃离此地，但由你决定，它可能在本幕稍后的某个时刻返回来帮助PC。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shimmerthief.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">马厩</span> <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.fd3Zd6e85EnFiofp]{窃光者} @UUID[Actor.WprQospX4zSvdTV9]{战马（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>若遭到攻击，窃光者会在可能的情况下反击，但若其生命值降至40点以下，它会逃离该区域。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC释放并招募窃光者，给予他们80 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C4. Stables</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The second paragraph assumes the creature in the fifth stall remains present. Omit it or adjust it as needed if the PCs can see through darkness.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Low fences partition off five pens along the northwest wall of this room. The first two pens by the entrance are occupied by sturdy, shaggy horses, while the other three are empty save for strewn beds of hay. A ladder to the north leads up to a small door that’s located in the wall fifteen feet off the ground.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The southern portion of the room is shrouded in a mysterious darkness from which a strange, soft clicking sound emanates.</p>\n<p>While combat trained, these two steeds are only ridden when a speedy messenger is needed or in an emergency, and since the shrine maidens arrived in the fortress, their access to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.R9xqCBblkS5KE4y7]{Sending} spells has rendered the pair even less useful in conveying swift messages. The horses are very skittish but not a threat to the PCs; they’re merely unnerved by the occupant of the farthest stall.</p>\n<p>Creature: The stall farthest from the entrance contains a creature far stranger than a mere horse. Here, the mercenaries have captured and kept a strange magical beast known as a shimmerthief, a lizard-like creature Mago Kai and his mercenaries discovered living in the ruins of Willowshore when they first arrived. They managed to capture the creature alive and brought it back here, where they’ve kept the beast both as a pet and because chief exorcist Cao Chen is intrigued by it.</p>\n<p>What none of them realize is that the creature is intelligent and can speak, although no one in the fortress speaks any of the languages the shimmerthief knows; instead, they’ve mistaken its attempts to communicate for “weird monster sounds.” Unlike the horses, the shimmerthief has been chained into place in its stable stall, its body bound by several iron chains that keep it immobilized. It’s also muzzled tightly to keep it from making those weird noises (and also from talking) or using its Unnerving Shriek. It can move about inside its stall, but that’s it.</p>\n<p>Cao Chen perceives the shimmerthief as an unusual but important opportunity to diversify their forces, as the creature thrives in darkness (where evil often lurks). His theory that the creature’s ability to consume light might be altered so that it can consume undead energy is unusual, but the more others scoff at the notion, the more Chen becomes convinced that he’s on to something. Mago Kai remains unconvinced of the creature’s worth, especially given its nature to issue frightening shrieks, but he has so far allowed Chen to keep the creature alive.</p>\n<p>The shimmerthief can’t cast its innate spells while it’s muzzled, but its gleam theft aura keeps the area around it quite dark. It starts as unfriendly toward the PCs, though it’s extremely innocent in nature, closer to a puppy than a wary human. As it only speaks Draconic, it’s possible (as with the fortress’s current occupants) that the PCs can’t communicate with it.</p>\n<p>If the PCs can communicate with the shimmerthief, they are able to learn its sad tale. Releasing it from its chains requires unlocking them (either with the key carried by Chen, or via four @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock), Forcing Open the chains with a @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:attack,skill,action:force-open|name:Force Open] check, or destroying them (Hardness 5, HP 20 [BT 10]). Freeing the shimmerthief automatically adjusts its attitude up one step toward helpful.</p>\n<p>If the PCs make the shimmerthief at least friendly, the creature agrees to help them. While it can accompany and fight alongside them, the shimmerthief would prefer (and suggests) an alternative—to skulk around the fortress and torment and frighten its captors. If the PCs pursue this option, the shimmerthief’s actions automatically add a Terror Point at the rate of 1 per hour for the next 4 hours, after which the creature is discovered and chased off or perhaps slain (at your whim). Canny PCs can make excellent use of the shimmerthief’s abilities in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}.</p>\n<p>If the PCs free the shimmerthief but don’t establish communication with it, the creature flees the area but, at your discretion, might return to help the PCs out at a later point during the act.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shimmerthief.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Stables</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.fd3Zd6e85EnFiofp]{Shimmerthief} @UUID[Actor.WprQospX4zSvdTV9]{War Horses (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If attacked, the shimmerthief fights back if it can, but it flees the region if reduced to fewer than 40 Hit Points.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs release and recruit the shimmerthief, grant them 80 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Periphery Path": {
              "name": "边缘路径 Periphery Path",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C3. 边缘小径</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这条十尺宽的夯土小路上方无遮无挡，直通天空。道路两侧的建筑似乎最近加固过，使其外观更具军事风格；但在零星之处，仍能看到它们过去作为商铺与食肆的遗留痕迹——几缕金色流苏、悬铃或其他商贸装饰仍挂在那儿。</p>\n</div>\n<p>由于要塞的安保，这些建筑被唐入村的居民用来储藏货物、进行交易，以及偶尔举办集市日。尽管夺走要塞的是孙海，但他允许这些造访而不加阻拦，因为这能让他的驱邪师与工人更方便地取得补给。只要恐惧点阈值低于 2，白天大约能在此遭遇半打左右的村民；夜里他们会收起货物，回到各自的家中。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C3. 边缘小径</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低 9</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{驱邪师（2）} @UUID[Actor.3hLps0uPoHvijSi0]{巫女（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shrine Maiden\" alt=\"human woman archer spiritualist\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>大约每隔一小时，来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} 的两名驱邪师就会下来，对这条小路进行一次快速巡逻——除非他们已被重新指派去巡逻村子。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 4：</strong>改为由来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c15shrinemai00]{C15} 的两名巫女在此站岗：一名驻守在金属门（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2b}）附近，一名驻守在木门（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2d}）附近；她们每 10 分钟互换一次位置，以巡查小路。若巫女遭遇 PC，她会在战斗初期使用传讯术，向孙海通报入侵者。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C3. Periphery Path</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 9</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This ten-foot-wide path of packed earth is open to the sky above. The buildings to either side of it appear to have been recently reinforced to be more militaristic in appearance, but here and there, legacies of their prior use as shops and eateries remain in the form of a few golden tassels, hanging bells, or other mercantile adornments.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Due to the security of the fortress, the residents of Karahai’s village used these buildings for storage, trade deals, and the occasional market day. While Mago Kai was the one who took the fortress from the villagers, he allows these visits without issue, as it provides his exorcists and workers with easier access to supplies. So long as the Terror Point threshold is below 2, a half dozen or so villagers can be encountered here during the day; at night, they pack up their wares and head to their homes.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C3. Periphery Path</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 9</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{Exorcists (2)} @UUID[Actor.3hLps0uPoHvijSi0]{Shrine Maidens (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Shrine Maiden\" alt=\"human woman archer spiritualist\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shrine-maiden.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Every hour or so, the two exorcists from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} descend to make a quick patrol of this path unless they’ve been reassigned to patrol the village.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 4:</strong> The two shrine maidens from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c15shrinemai00]{C15} instead stand guard here, one posted near Metal Gate (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2b}) and one near Wood Gate (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2d}), swapping positions every 10 minutes to patrol the path. A shrine maiden who encounters a PC uses sending early in the fight to alert Mago Kai of their intrusion.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Fortress Gates": {
              "name": "要塞大门 Fortress Gates",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C2. Fortress Gates\">C2. 要塞大门</h2>\n<p>当要塞达到 5 点恐怖点数后，这四道门都会关闭并上锁。</p>\n<p><strong>C2a. 水门：</strong>这道门漆成黑色，并饰有一幅跃起的鲤鱼画。一个超小型的 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{阿巴达尔}陶土塑像摆在其中一个铰链旁的地面上。这道门总是上着锁。</p>\n<p><strong>C2b. 金属门：</strong>这道门漆成灰色，并装饰着一幅褪色但庄严的白虎图。它通常不上锁并保持敞开，因为大多数步行往来似乎都从这边经过。</p>\n<p><strong>C2c. 火门：</strong>这道门漆成红色，并饰有一幅凤凰图；显然有人毫无绘画技能，最近还对这幅画进行了补画，使得那只鸟看起来有点瞪眼。此门通常保持关闭。</p>\n<p><strong>C2d. 木门：</strong>这道门漆成绿色，并装饰着一道金色的弯曲线条，隐约像一条龙。门上的漆看起来明显很新。地面上有一些沟槽，仿佛许多沉重的物体被拖拽着穿过这道门。此门通常保持关闭。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"C2. Fortress Gates\">C2. Fortress Gates</h2>\n<p>These four gates are all closed and locked once the fortress reaches 5 Terror Points.</p>\n<p><strong>C2a. Water Gate:</strong> This gate is painted black and is decorated with a painting of a jumping carp. A tiny clay statue of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.d56paSkcwvll2OhR]{Abadar} sits on the ground by one of the hinges. This gate is always kept locked.</p>\n<p><strong>C2b. Metal Gate:</strong> This gate is painted gray and is decorated with a faded but majestic depiction of a white tiger. It’s normally unlocked and left open, as the majority of foot traffic seems to pass this way.</p>\n<p><strong>C2c. Fire Gate:</strong> This gate is painted red and is decorated with a depiction of a phoenix; someone with no artistic skill appears to have touched up the painting recently, and the bird looks a bit bug-eyed. The gate is normally kept closed.</p>\n<p><strong>C2d. Wood Gate:</strong> This gate is painted green and is decorated with a golden squiggle that vaguely resembles a dragon. The paint on the door looks notably fresh. There are ruts in the ground as if many heavy objects have been dragged through this gate. The door is normally kept closed.</p>"
            },
            "Upper Ring": {
              "name": "上环 Upper Ring",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C1. 上层环道</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">极难 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>一条宽5尺的封闭走廊位于要塞外墙之内，环绕整座要塞，离地15尺高。马厩（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c4stables00000]{C4}）、营房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}）以及木材储藏室（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c8lumberstor00]{C8}）中的梯子可通往这条步道，且四面都有狭窄的箭孔朝外。小型生物可以通过一次成功的 @Check[acrobatics|dc:20|traits:exploration,move,action:squeeze|name:Squeeze] 检定从箭孔中挤过，而超小型生物则可毫不费力地通过。走廊从每一道大门上方经过。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C1. 上层环道</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">极难 9</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{驱魔师（2）} @UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{佣兵执法者（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-exorcist.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Exorcist\" alt=\"a human wearing red robes, and a four-eyed, horned mask, wielding a spear and a torch\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-exorcist.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>一对孙海的驱魔师与四名佣兵驻守于此负责警戒，但在恐惧点数达到2点之前，他们几乎不留意周遭环境；当达到2点时，驱魔师会被派出去巡视村庄，而佣兵则开始沿环道巡逻。若战斗爆发，驱魔师会战至死，但佣兵在生命值降至30点或更少时，会逃往营房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}）。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 2：</strong>驱魔师被派往村庄巡逻。</p>\n  <p><strong>恐惧 7：</strong>佣兵放弃该区域，加入其他人，将自己 barricade 在营房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}）内。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C1. Upper Ring</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 9</span>\n</h2>\n<p>A 5-foot-wide enclosed hall circumnavigates the fortress within its outer wall at a height of 15 feet. Ladders in the stable (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c4stables00000]{C4}), the barracks (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}), and the lumber storage (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c8lumberstor00]{C8}) allow access to this walkway, and narrow arrow slits face out in all directions. A Small creature can Squeeze through one with a successful @Check[acrobatics|dc:20|traits:exploration,move,action:squeeze|name:Squeeze] check, while a Tiny creature can fit through without trouble. The hall passes over each of the gates.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/mercenary-enforcer.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C1. Upper Ring</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 9</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{Exorcists (2)} @UUID[Actor.R6MFmm46QhJV4Zvm]{Mercenary Enforcers (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-exorcist.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Exorcist\" alt=\"a human wearing red robes, and a four-eyed, horned mask, wielding a spear and a torch\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-exorcist.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of Mago Kai’s exorcists and four mercenaries are stationed here to keep watch, but they pay little attention to their surroundings until 2 Terror Points, when the exorcists are sent out to survey the village and the mercenaries start patrolling the ring. If combat begins, the exorcists fight to the death, but the mercenaries flee to the barracks (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}) if reduced to 30 or fewer Hit Points.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 2:</strong> The exorcists are sent into the village to patrol.</p>\n  <p><strong>Terror 7:</strong> The mercenaries abandon this area and join the others in barricading themselves in the barracks (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}).</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Alternate Approaches to the Fortress": {
              "name": "攻取要塞的替代途径 Alternate Approaches to the Fortress",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Alternate Approaches to the Fortress\">通往要塞的替代路线</h3>\n<p>虽然预期PC会扮演骇人的幽灵，并很可能在唐入与孙海及其追随者发生相当多的战斗，但队伍并非只能用这一种方式在要塞中行动。</p>\n<p>在第9等级时，PC应当可以轻松运用潜行，悄悄从各色商人、农民以及其他村民身边溜过去。若PC采取潜入路线，你可以放心地假定：只要他们都尽力保持隐蔽，并将接近要塞的时机安排在明显巡逻队之间，他们就会自动成功。只有当恐惧达到2或更高时，才会出现以驱魔人为代表的重大威胁，需要PC去应对。进入要塞后，这里被设计为一个动态地点——也就意味着，居民越是警觉，他们的活动范围就越大、移动得越频繁。若PC的潜入行动造成了此类扰动，你就需要临场调整遭遇。以下遭遇在底线层面提供了足够的信息，让你拥有进行调整所需的工具。</p>\n<p>PC还可能尝试另一种选择：纯粹的外交手段，但这种尝试应当很快以灾害告终。由于PC显得幽灵般可怖，而居住在唐入的所有人过去数月里对家乡上游闹鬼的遗迹愈发忧心，没有人会相信这些“友善的幽灵”只是想谈谈。更有可能的结果，是演变为一场压倒性的遭遇：整个唐入会同仇敌忾地起而反击这场意外却令人恐惧的“幽灵入侵”。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Alternate Approaches to the Fortress\">Alternate Approaches to the Fortress</h3>\n<p>While the expectation is that the PCs take on the role of frightening ghosts and likely get into a fair number of fights against Mago Kai and his followers in Karahai, this isn’t the only way a party can navigate the fortress.</p>\n<p>At 9th level, the PCs should have no problem using Stealth to creep past the various merchants, peasants, and other villagers. If the PCs adopt a stealthy approach, you can safely assume that as long as they all do their best to be sneaky and time their approach to the fortress between obvious patrols, they are automatically successful. Only once Terror is at 2 or higher are there significant threats in the form of exorcists that the PCs might have to contend with. Once inside, the fortress is intended to be a dynamic location, and that does mean that the more alarmed its inhabitants get, the more they move around. You will need to adjust encounters on the fly if the PCs’ stealthy approach causes such disruptions. The following encounters present enough information at the baseline that you’ll have the tools you need to do so.</p>\n<p>Another option the PCs might try is a purely diplomatic approach, but this attempt should quickly end in disaster. Since the PCs appear ghostly, and since all of those who dwell in Karahai have spent the past several months growing increasingly concerned about the haunted ruins upriver from their home, none will believe that these “friendly ghosts” just want to talk, and this attempt is more likely to result in an overwhelming encounter as all of Karahai rises up as one to fight back against this unexpected but frightening “ghost invasion.”</p>"
            },
            "Karahai Features": {
              "name": "唐入特性 Karahai Features",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Karahai Features\">唐入要塞特征</h2>\n<p>当PC们第一次望见唐入要塞时，向他们朗读或转述以下内容。白天时，PC们也可能会看到村民进出要塞，不过频率并不高。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>唐入要塞坐落在村庄中央，是一座由夯土与石头建成的圆形建筑。除四座外门外整体完全封闭，四门分别朝向四个基本方位。建筑进行了加固，显然是以防御为目的而建。外墙顶部一圈分布着细小的瞭望窗，每扇都刚好足以伸出一颗头或一把弩，窗内侧还做了倾斜的斜面，便于进出。外墙高二十五尺，屋顶坡度很陡，向中心上扬，最高处达四十尺。</p>\n</div>\n<p>PC必须在一次@Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定中成功才能攀爬垂直墙面，但在陡峭屋顶上攀行只需在一次@Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]中成功即可。</p>\n<p>除非另有说明，要塞墙体由石质砾岩构成，按砖石墙运作。每道外门由厚木制成并以铁加固，按铁闸门运作，而每扇门都由加固木材制成。所有门与外门都可以上锁（开锁需要进行四次@Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock]检定），但在达到特定的恐惧点阈值之前都会保持未上锁状态（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12thehauntingo00#a-summary-of-terror]{恐惧概要}）。有关墙与门的额外规则见《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》第93页。</p>\n<p>只要位于区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}的护卫钟仍在运作，要塞的墙壁、地板与屋顶就会受到神秘加固，虚体生物无法穿过它们，其中包括获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.adventure-specific-actions.Item.pHXGTgjwWY3OBRF2]{蜕变}主要魂魄力量的PC。门与外门也会获得部分这种魂魄强化，但其不稳定的性质意味着虚体生物可以以一个具有移动（特征）的三动作行动穿过它们。</p>\n<p>下方每个遭遇都假设尚未累积任何恐惧点，其遭遇威胁也基于这一假设。随着恐惧点累积，使用@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12thehauntingo00#a-summary-of-terror]{恐惧概要}中的表格，以及各个遭遇中“恐惧”条目来进行调整（每条“恐惧”后方的数值表示发生所列变化所需达到的恐惧点阈值）；务必注意，这些调整可能会大幅影响遭遇的威胁等级。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Karahai Features\">Karahai Features</h2>\n<p>The first time the PCs look upon Karahai fortress, read or paraphrase the following to them. During the day, the PCs might also spy villagers coming and going from the fortress, although not with any significant frequency.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Nestled in the middle of the village, Karahai fortress is a round structure made of packed earth and stone, completely enclosed except for four outer gates, one at each cardinal direction. The building is fortified and clearly built with defense in mind. Tiny lookout windows ring the top of the outer walls, each large enough to stick a head or crossbow through, with a slanting bevel on the inside for ease of access. The exterior wall is twenty-five feet high, with a steeply sloped roof that angles upward toward the center and reaches a height of forty feet.</p>\n</div>\n<p>A PC must succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:25|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check to Climb the vertical wall, but they need only succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] to clamber along the steep roof.</p>\n<p>Unless otherwise specified, the fortress walls are made of stone conglomerate, functioning as masonry walls. Each gate is made of thick wood reinforced with iron and functions as an iron portcullis, while each door is made of reinforced wood. All doors and gates can be locked (requiring four @Check[thievery|dc:25|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock) but remain unlocked until certain Terror Point thresholds are reached (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12thehauntingo00#a-summary-of-terror]{A Summary of Terror}). Additional rules for walls and doors appear on page 93 of <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>.</p>\n<p>As long as the warding bell remains in operation in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c11shrine00000]{C11}, the walls, floors, and roofs of the fortress are mystically bolstered and can’t be passed through by incorporeal creatures, including PCs who have taken the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.adventure-specific-actions.Item.pHXGTgjwWY3OBRF2]{Dematerialize} major spirit power. Doors and gates also receive some of this spiritual reinforcement, but their fluctuating nature means that an incorporeal creature can pass through as a three-action activity with the move trait.</p>\n<p>Each of the encounters below assumes no Terror Points have accumulated, and the encounter threat reflects this assumption. As Terror Points accumulate, use the chart on @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12thehauntingo00#a-summary-of-terror]{A Summary of Terror} and the Terror entries in each encounter to adjust things (the value after each Terror entry refers to the Terror Point threshold at which the listed change takes place); make sure to note that these adjustments can drastically affect the encounter’s threat level.</p>"
            },
            "Karahai Village": {
              "name": "唐入村 Karahai Village",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">唐入村</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 9</span>\n</h2>\n\n<p>一座小小的村庄坐落在幽海边缘，此地以附近矗立的一座大型要塞之名而为人所知——唐入。这里仅有约三打村民在此安家，为沿海岸线往北或往南行旅的旅人提供家务服务；并且自去年早春以来，在木材大亨夺取唐入要塞的控制权后，他们也一直在支援孙海的部队。</p>\n<p>村里的建筑均为单层，以夯实黏土筑成、覆以茅草屋顶。房屋虽简陋，却易于维护，几乎不见磨损。村中大部分食物与材料都依赖进口，但有一处小码头维持着几艘摇摇欲坠的渔船运作，以补充储备。村民生活困苦，却相当迷信。作为神门的居民，他们不得不向络新妇缴纳人丁什一税，并常常在自己孩子的脸上留下疤痕，以避免引起蛛女的注意。虽然村民很容易被吓到，但在此地进行的行径不会让恐怖点数在阈值等级2以上继续增加——毕竟，这些村民在超自然威胁上“狼来了”喊得太多了。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.crhi7BRJVChbTKDx]{唐入的恐怖}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>打开一个对话框，用于选择恐怖等级与夜晚，并切换数个已撤退的群组。</p>\n  <p>选择一个恐怖等级后，该宏会将所有活着的指示物移动到其在该恐怖等级下应处的位置。若为夜晚时间，请在应用新的恐怖等级后点击“Night”按钮。这也会在各场景间同步一个指示物的死亡状态。</p>\n  <p>最后，当增援到达时，该宏也能恢复被击败的巫女、驱魔人和佣兵的指示物。</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-exorcist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">唐入村</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{驱魔人（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>当恐怖点数阈值达到2时，孙海会从区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} 派出两名驱魔人前来调查并巡逻村庄。驱魔人来此更多是为了安抚村民的恐惧，而非别的原因，他们并不指望真有闹鬼之事。他们会在该区域巡逻一个多小时，然后返回要塞内区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1}。若驱魔人发现PC，他们会发动攻击，试图“驱逐幽灵”。若其中一名驱魔人的生命值降至40点以下，两人便会一同逃回营房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}）。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Karahai Village</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 9</span>\n</h2>\n\n<p>A tiny village sits on the edge of the Sea of Ghosts, a place known by the name of the large fortress that stands nearby—Karahai. Only about three dozen villagers make their homes here, providing domestic services for travelers plying the coastline to the north or south and, since early last spring, supporting Mago Kai’s forces after the lumber baron took control of Karahai fortress.</p>\n<p>The village buildings are one story, constructed of packed clay with thatch roofs. Though simple, the houses are easy to maintain and have little wear and tear. Most of the village’s food and materials are imported, but a small dock supports the operation of a few rickety fishing boats to supplement their stores. The villagers are a hardscrabble lot but fairly superstitious. As residents of Shenmen, they’ve had to pay human tithes to the jorogumo and often scar their own children’s faces to avoid attention from the spider women. While it’s easy to frighten the villagers, acts performed here don’t increase Terror Points past threshold level 2—the villagers have “cried wolf” about supernatural threats too often, after all.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macros</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.crhi7BRJVChbTKDx]{Terror in Karahai}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Opens a dialog to select the Terror level, night, and toggles several retreated groups.</p>\n  <p>When a terror Level is selected, the macro will move all living tokens to the position they would be in at that terror level. If it is night time, click the \"Night\" button after applying the new terror level. This also synchronizes a token's death status across scenes.</p>\n  <p>Finally, this macro can also restore the tokens of defeated shrine maidens, exorcists, and mercenaries when reinforcements arrive.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90198-exorcist.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Karahai Village</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 9 </span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E8jzdv6jEAjP5s5e]{Exorcists (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> At a Terror Point threshold of 2, Mago Kai dispatches two exorcists from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} to investigate and patrol the village. The exorcists are here more to quell the villagers’ fears than anything else, and they don’t expect a real haunting. They patrol the area for a little over an hour before returning to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} in the fortress. If the exorcists spot the PCs, they attack in an attempt to “banish the ghosts.” If one of the exorcists is reduced below 40 Hit Points, both flee back to the barracks (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}).</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Haunting of Karahai": {
              "name": "唐入之缠扰 The Haunting of Karahai",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Haunting of Karahai\">唐入的闹鬼事件</h2>\n<p>孙海和他的手下认为闹鬼现象被限制在柳岸镇的废墟中，而在PC施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate} 之前，他们的这一假设一直是正确的。当PC推进本章内容时，他们将有机会在要塞的居民之间营造不祥的预感；这样做会提高唐入的恐怖点数。</p>\n<p>对某些团来说，恐吓唐入的战术可能并不直观。如果你的玩家没有意识到这是他们对抗孙海及其追随者武器库中的重要工具，那么可以考虑让他们在路上遇到一名村民或商人：此人一看到PC就惊慌失措，喊他们是鬼，然后惊恐逃跑；此时你可以宣布他们获得了1点恐怖点数。在这之后，你可以直接把这一机制告诉他们。或者，如果PC杀死了要塞中的一名住户，然后把尸体留在原地，让他们在稍后听到一声尖叫，再同样宣布他们也获得了1点恐怖点数。</p>\n<p>如果这两种方式都不足以提供足够强的提示，就别太拘谨，直接对玩家说明即可。让他们知道：当地人显然把他们的PC当作幽灵，而他们可以利用这一点——装出那副样子，在这里散播一些恐惧！如果你愿意，你可以把这个提示藏在一次 @Check[society|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定之后：当任何PC在接近唐入时试图对其进行回忆知识，或有人询问村庄或要塞防御以及可能的入口时，就让他们进行该检定。</p>\n<p>唐入的恐怖点数从0开始，但会按文中所述提升。玩家使用任何巧妙手段让住户心生恐惧时，都应通过获得1点恐怖点数来奖励他们。制造恐怖最简单的方法，是把一具尸体布置得格外血腥或令人恐惧——一旦这具尸体被发现（由你决定发现的时机），让一名PC尝试进行一次 @Check[intimidation|dc:25] 检定。成功时，该发现产生1点恐怖点数；大成功或大失败中的大成功则产生2点恐怖点数。</p>\n<p>每当过去24小时，且PC没有进行任何可能提高恐怖的行动时，唐入的恐怖点数就会减少 [[/r 2d6]] 点。</p>\n<p>在不同的恐怖点数阈值下，PC在唐入遭遇的NPC可能会以带有 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened} 状态开始战斗。照常，惊惧状态会在每个生物的回合结束时减少1点。敌人的位置与战术也会随恐怖点数阈值而变化。</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"table\">恐怖概要</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>恐怖阈值</th>\n      <th>NPC恐惧</th>\n      <th>要塞反应</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n      <td>无。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n      <td>来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} 的两名驱魔师离开去巡逻村庄。要塞内的村民与厨子撤回村庄。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}</td>\n      <td>土之门上锁。小木门上锁，并由来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c6diningroom00]{C6} 的佣兵把守。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}</td>\n      <td>来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c15shrinemai00]{C15} 的巫女在外围走廊巡逻。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}</td>\n      <td>所有要塞外部大门（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2}）关闭并上锁。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}</td>\n      <td>芬芳与两名驱魔师撤退到区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c16fenfangsc00]{C16}。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}</td>\n      <td>要塞的九名佣兵把自己 barricade 在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5} 内。孙海撤回到他位于区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c20kaisquart00]{C20} 的住处。</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 3}</td>\n      <td>孙海让一名巫女施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.R9xqCBblkS5KE4y7]{Sending}，向司厄城中的盟友报告情况并请求增援。援助不会立刻抵达，但在接下来的几天内，PC可能击败的驱魔师、佣兵与巫女会被新的人员替换。孙海最多可以呼叫增援三次。</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>并非完全不死</h1>\n  <p>本章中，PC在敌人眼中看起来有些幽灵般，但他们更接近魅影而非不死生物。当驱魔师或巫女等施法者首次与他们对峙时，会依赖 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.z9T4c1hXwOotsMCp]{Holy Water}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.rfZpqmj0AIIdkVIs]{Heal}、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kcelf6IHl3L9VXXg]{Vitality Lash} 以及其他通常会伤害不死敌人的攻击；但一旦他们意识到这些对PC不起作用，就会相应改变战术。如果某位施法者得知此事并在与PC的遭遇中幸存，消息就会在要塞内传开；此后，不会有施法者再重复这个错误。</p>\n  <p>像 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.bay4AfSu2iIozNNW]{Banishment} 这样的法术，对处于此状态的PC会非常有效：若对该法术的豁免以失败告终，就会把PC送回柳岸镇的思维空间。由于PC必须经历复杂的方法才能返回生者世界，因此有意决定不为本幕的任何NPC“配备”这一法术，以避免出现可能破坏节奏并令人沮丧的游戏要素。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Haunting of Karahai\">The Haunting of Karahai</h2>\n<p>Mago Kai and his crew believe the hauntings are constrained to the ruins of Willowshore, and until the PCs cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.8Lk9K3tRnV68MQPW]{Transmigrate}, they’ve been correct in this assumption. As the PCs make their way through this chapter, they’ll have opportunities to create a sense of foreboding among the fortress’s residents, and doing so increases Karahai’s Terror Points.</p>\n<p>For some groups, the tactic of terrorizing Karahai might not be intuitive. If your players don’t realize this is a significant tool in their arsenal against Mago Kai and his followers, then consider having them encounter a villager or merchant along the way who reacts in panic upon spotting the PCs, calling them ghosts before fleeing in terror, at which point you can announce they’ve earned a Terror Point. After this, you can simply tell them about the mechanic. Alternatively, if the PCs kill one of the fortress’s occupants and then leave the body where it lies, have them hear a scream a bit later and then announce they earned a Terror Point as well.</p>\n<p>If neither of these give a strong enough hint, don’t be too timid about speaking directly to the players. Let them know that the locals apparently see their PCs as ghosts, and that they can capitalize on that by acting the part and starting to spread some fear around the place! If you want, you can lock this hint behind a @Check[society|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check should any PC attempt to Recall Knowledge about Karahai as they approach, or if anyone asks about the village or fortress defenses and possible entrances.</p>\n<p>Karahai’s Terror Points begin at 0 but increase as indicated in the text. The players should be rewarded for whatever clever tactics they use to induce dread among the occupants by gaining a Terror Point. The simplest way to create terror is to stage a dead body in a way that’s particularly grisly or frightening—once that body is discovered (at a time left to you to decide), have one of the PCs attempt a @Check[intimidation|dc:25] check. On a success, the discovery generates 1 Terror Point, or 2 Terror Points on a critical success.</p>\n<p>Karahai’s Terror Points reduce by [[/r 2d6]] points every time 24 hours pass without any activity from the PCs that could potentially increase terror.</p>\n<p>At different thresholds of Terror Points, NPCs encountered in Karahai might begin a combat with the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened} condition. As normal, the frightened condition reduces by 1 at the end of each creature’s turn. Enemy locations and tactics also change based on Terror Point thresholds.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"table\">A Summary of Terror</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Terror Threshold</th>\n      <th>NPC Fear</th>\n      <th>Fortress Response</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n      <td>None.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n      <td>The two exorcists from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c1upperring000]{C1} leave to patrol the village. Villagers and cooks inside the fort retreat to the village.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}</td>\n      <td>Earth Gate is locked. The Small Wood Gate is locked and guarded by mercenaries from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c6diningroom00]{C6}.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}</td>\n      <td>The shrine maidens from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c15shrinemai00]{C15} patrol the periphery hall.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 1}</td>\n      <td>All exterior fortress gates (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c2fortressga00]{C2}) are closed and locked.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}</td>\n      <td>Fenfang and two exorcists retreat to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c16fenfangsc00]{C16}.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 2}</td>\n      <td>The fortress’s nine mercenaries barricade themselves into area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c5commonbarr00]{C5}. Mago Kai retreats to his quarters in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog12thispl.JournalEntryPage.12c20kaisquart00]{C20}.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TBSHQspnbcqxsmjL]{Frightened 3}</td>\n      <td>Mago Kai has a shrine maiden cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.R9xqCBblkS5KE4y7]{Sending} to report to allies back in the city of Sze about the situation and ask for reinforcements. Help won’t arrive immediately, but within the next several days, exorcists, mercenaries, and shrine maidens the PCs might have defeated are replaced by new ones. Mago Kai can call for reinforcements up to three times.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Not Quite Undead</h1>\n  <p>The PCs appear somewhat ghostly to their foes in this chapter, but they’re more akin to phantoms than undead. When spellcasters like the exorcists or shrine maidens first confront them, they’ll rely upon @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.z9T4c1hXwOotsMCp]{Holy Water}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.rfZpqmj0AIIdkVIs]{Heal}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kcelf6IHl3L9VXXg]{Vitality Lash}, and other attacks that normally harm undead foes, but upon realizing that the PCs aren’t affected, they’ll change tactics as appropriate. If a spellcaster learns this and survives an encounter with the PCs, word spreads through the fortress, and no spellcaster will repeat this mistake going forward.</p>\n  <p>A spell like @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.bay4AfSu2iIozNNW]{Banishment} would be quite effective against the PCs in this state, for a failure to save against this spell would send a PC back to the Willowshore mindscape. Due to the complicated method the PCs must endure to return to the living world, it was a conscious decision not to “arm” any of this act’s NPCs with this spell, in an effort to protect against a potentially disruptive and frustrating gameplay element.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "On to Karahai": {
              "name": "前往唐入 On to Karahai",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"On to Karahai\">前往唐入</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>滴答作响的计时器</h1>\n  <p>尽管<em>转生</em>仪式威力强大，它也无法让PC永远以魂魄形态显现。该仪式的4环版本持续时间为1个月，这应该足够PC完成第10章。万一他们花的时间更久，当1个月结束时，他们会从生者世界中消散，返回柳岸镇思维空间，并把装备一并带回。如果发生这种情况，他们就需要再次施放该仪式，才能尝试在生者世界完成任务，但PC每这么做一次，孙海就有时间招募增援并强化防御。具体如何发展由你决定，但至少，每次往返都会额外增加4点恐惧点数，PC必须先将其累积到足够程度，才能再次开始影响要塞。</p>\n  <p>思维空间中的时间流逝与外界一致。虽然PC离开期间那里不该发生什么重大事件，但请记得按需每周扣除准备点数。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>在过去115年的荒废中，柳岸镇已化为废墟。道路被植被淹没，许多建筑坍塌，柳岸镇大坝也已崩毁，使木筏湖几乎只剩一片恶臭的沼泽。晨步桥依然矗立，但这座石质结构看上去已濒临崩塌。PC出现地点附近矗立着<em>长明灯</em>，其上长满苔藓但整体仍大致完好——然而它没有点亮，原本盛放祝福钱币的内部容器也完全不见了。直到PC从唐入取回这个容器之前，长明灯都将保持黑暗，而PC也无法从他们的思维空间中逃脱。</p>\n<p>PC可能会被驱使去调查柳岸镇的废墟。与PC此前一直栖身的那座热闹（尽管多灾多难）的思维空间相比，如今的柳岸镇应当让人感到空洞、荒凉而悲怆。废墟中已无任何有价值之物，但PC在某些地方应能发现近期营地的痕迹——尤其是在云纸屋的坍塌遗址处——这表明在过去几个月里，孙海、他的雇员以及驱魔师们曾间歇性地在这些废墟中停留。</p>\n<p>即便PC没有意识到自己的目标，他们与<em>长明灯</em>被盗之焰的联系也会将他们向东拉向唐入。这种感觉仿佛是一段强烈的记忆与近乎具象的腹部牵扯交织在一起。沿着杜月江向东南走一段不算太艰难的路程，便能抵达海岸要塞唐入及其周边村落。当英雄们开始踏上前往孙海海岸要塞的旅程并离开柳岸镇时，他们会在柳岸镇残骸附近经过一只石质守护蜘蛛的碎裂残片——那是丑小乖的遗骸，孙海在本冒险路径前的事件中杀死了它。</p>\n<p>前往唐入的旅程应当风平浪静。PC一路上会看到更多近期行动的证据：倒下的树被砍断或从路上拖走的地方，或是在道路大多已化为泥泞的区域里，仍留有行人和货车往来的痕迹。在作为思维空间东部边界的葫芦湖稍往前不远处，PC来到唐入桥——它曾是一座木桥，跨越一道峡谷，而木棉河正穿过此峡谷奔流入海。多年前，峡谷两岸部分在泥石流中崩塌，桥也随之被冲毁；但孙海的工人用木板与绳索搭起了一座临时替代品，PC可以轻松通过。过桥后不到一小时，他们拐过最后一个弯，唐入便映入眼帘。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"On to Karahai\">On to Karahai</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Ticking Timer</h1>\n  <p>Despite the power of the <em>transmigrate</em> ritual, it can’t keep the PCs manifested as spirits forever. The 4th-level version of the ritual has a duration of 1 month, which should be plenty of time for the PCs to finish Chapter 10. In the event it takes them longer, when the month runs out, they fade away from the living world and return to the Willowshore mindscape, taking their gear with them. If this happens, they’ll need to cast the ritual again to try to complete their tasks in the living world, but each time the PCs do so, Mago Kai has time to recruit reinforcements and bolster his defenses. How this plays out is left to you to decide, but at the very least, each return trip adds four new Terror Points that the PCs must build up to before they can start to affect the fortress again.</p>\n  <p>Time passes equally in the mindscape. Though no significant events should occur there while the PCs are gone, remember to deduct Preparation Points each week as appropriate.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Over the last 115 years of neglect, Willowshore has fallen to ruin. The roads are overgrown with foliage, many buildings have crumbled, and Willowshore Dam has collapsed, leaving Woodraft Lake little more than a stinking swamp. Dawnstep Bridge still stands, but the stone structure looks on the verge of collapse. Near to where the PCs emerge stands the <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, overgrown with moss but still mostly intact—yet it’s unlit, and the inner receptacle that once held blessed coins is missing entirely. Until the PCs recover this receptacle from Karahai, the Eternal Lantern remains dark, and the PCs can’t escape their mindscape.</p>\n<p>The PCs might be compelled to investigate the ruins of Willowshore. Compared to the lively (if troubled) mindscape that the PCs have been inhabiting up until this point, modern-day Willowshore should feel hollow, empty, and tragic. Nothing of value remains in the ruins, but here and there, the PCs should find evidence of recent camps—particularly at the collapsed ruins of Cloud Paper House—that are evidence of Mago Kai, his employees, and exorcists periodically spending time in the ruins over the past several months.</p>\n<p>Even if the PCs don’t realize their goal, their link to the stolen flame from the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> pulls them eastward toward Karahai. This sensation feels like a compelling memory combined with an almost physical tugging in the gut. The coastal fortress of Karahai and its surrounding village is only a moderate trek southeast along the Duyue River. As the heroes begin their journey toward Mago Kai’s coastal fortress and exit Willowshore, they pass smashed pieces of a stone guardian spider near the wreck of Willowshore—the remains of Ugly Cute, who Mago Kai killed in the events leading up to this Adventure Path.</p>\n<p>The trip to Karahai should be uneventful. As the PCs travel, they’ll see more evidence of recent activity, places where fallen trees have been cut or pulled away from the road, or the sign of foot and wagon traffic in areas where the road has turned mostly to mud. Not far from the point just past Gourd Lake that served as the mindscape’s eastern border, the PCs come to Karahai Bridge, once a wooden structure that crossed a gorge through which the Ceiba River flows on its way out to sea. The bridge was swept away many years ago after the banks of the gorge partially collapsed in mudslides, but Mago Kai’s workers have rigged a temporary replacement of planks and ropes that the PCs can cross with ease. Less than an hour after crossing the bridge, they turn a final bend and set their eyes on Karahai.</p>"
            },
            "This Place is Ours": {
              "name": "此地属于我们 This Place is Ours",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"This Place is Ours\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第10章：</span>\n  <span>此地属于我们</span>\n</h1>\n<p>当PC们从生与死之间的边境地带现身时，他们发现自己从晨步桥的南侧走下，来到一座与他们所知截然不同的小镇。这里才是真正的柳岸镇——一座已成废墟一百多年的柳岸镇。</p>\n<p>PC们应当很快意识到，他们看似坚实的身体，实际上是由灵质构成的临时造物。他们的所有道具都随他们一同而来，因此对他们的装备（或本章期间获得的新物品）造成的任何伤害都会持续存在，不会改变；但作为灵质的灵魂，PC们存在于生命与不死之间。现在正是向玩家揭示他们新能力的时机，如@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20hauntingthel00]{萦绕生者}中所详述。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-haunting-the-living.webp\" alt=\"Haunting the Living\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"This Place is Ours\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 10:</span>\n  <span>This Place Is Ours</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs emerge from the borderland between life and death, they find themselves stepping off of the southern side of Dawnstep Bridge into a town much different than the one they know. This place is the real Willowshore—one that has been in ruins for over a century.</p>\n<p>The PCs should swiftly realize that their apparently solid bodies are, in fact, temporary constructs of ectoplasm. All of their gear has come with them, so any damage done to their equipment (or to new items gained during this chapter) remains constant regardless, but as ectoplasmic souls, the PCs exist between life and undeath. Now is the time to reveal to the players their new powers, as detailed under @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20hauntingthel00]{Haunting the Living}.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 4.1: Willowshore’s Return": {
          "name": "第4.1幕：柳岸镇的归来 Act 4.1: Willowshore’s Return",
          "pages": {
            "The Silkwasp Camp": {
              "name": "丝蜂营地 The Silkwasp Camp",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">绢蜂营地</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严重 10</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>绢蜂营地地点</h1>\n  <p>以下是对绢蜂盗匪营地各地点的简要描述。</p>\n  <p><strong>B1：</strong>前门。</p>\n  <p><strong>B2：</strong>靠近鱼塘的储物棚屋，周围是沼泽般的泥地。</p>\n  <p><strong>B3：</strong>内门。</p>\n  <p><strong>B4：</strong>部分坍塌的谷仓。</p>\n  <p><strong>B5：</strong>起居/餐厅，现在用作盗匪营房。</p>\n  <p><strong>B6：</strong>厨房，现在用作罗坤的营房。</p>\n  <p><strong>B7：</strong>食品储藏间。</p>\n  <p><strong>B8：</strong>工坊，现在用作盗匪营房。</p>\n  <p><strong>B9：</strong>后门廊。</p>\n  <p><strong>B10：</strong>卧室，被红玫瑰占用。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>如果PC们设法通过移除某个盗匪身上的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.5pwK2FZX6QwgtfqX]{Inveigle}效果来争取到其配合，那么此人可以为PC们指出他们藏身处的方向，但只有罗坤同意陪同PC们，尝试向红玫瑰复仇。同样地，只有罗坤知道红玫瑰是僵尸，因此他能提供更多关于如何与她战斗的建议。他建议PC们带上手持镜子，以及在击败她后用来让她永远安息的材料（糯米或母鸡蛋共1负荷）。最后，罗坤还可以告诉PC们：她在自己的住处用丝绸包着某种物品——她似乎既害怕它又对它痴迷。</p>\n<p>若没有获救盗匪的帮助，PC们就得转而用其他方法来发现绢蜂营地。营地位于卡拉海以北数小时路程处、俯瞰幽海的一处高耸断崖上的旧农庄；通往这处据说已废弃农庄的唯一陆路，是一条从柳岸镇向东北延伸、杂草丛生的小径。PC们也许会在探索乡间时自行偶然发现此地，但在PC们或柳岸镇的人民与盗匪每发生一次遭遇之后，PC们也可以以一次成功的@Check[survival|dc:20|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track]检定来追踪盗匪至其营地。那处破败农庄位于柳岸腹地地图边缘以东略少于3英里处——从镇上骑马大约一天路程。</p>\n<p>当PC们接近营地时，朗读或转述以下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一处朴素的农庄坐落在俯瞰幽海的低矮崖地上，其西半边蜷伏在一圈圈杂草丛生、摇摇欲坠的篱笆之内。西端有一大片鱼塘，周围芦苇环绕，靠近通往最外层篱笆的门。农舍看上去破败不堪，谷仓的状况更糟，屋顶已经部分塌陷。</p>\n</div>\n<p>沼泽和灌木丛斑块属于困难地形。鱼塘大部分区域水深10英尺，在距离任一岸边5英尺以内的水域趟水前进同样属于困难地形。木篱笆非常摇晃——高8英尺，PC可以以一次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定翻越；若大失败，则该5英尺长的一段篱笆坍塌，使攀爬者倒地，并使该方格变为困难地形。<strong>B1</strong>与<strong>B3</strong>区域的木门已无法打开，但缺失的木板足够多，使得一名中型或更小的生物（或一条身形蜿蜒的大型蛇）可以用一个迈步动作穿过缝隙通过。农庄东侧的崖边向下落差50英尺直入下方浪涛；那里的水深远不足以缓冲坠落。这些被海雾喷洒得湿滑的峭壁，PC若以一次成功的@Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climbed]检定即可攀爬。</p>\n<p><strong>B2</strong>区域的棚屋和农舍都有数扇窗户，但已被部分钉板封住。这些窗户可用作箭孔：相邻生物可通过其射箭攻击更远处的目标而不受减值，同时自身获得更高的掩护。</p>\n<p>一根40英尺长的绳子被隐蔽地埋在虚线红色标示路径旁的一层泥土下。绳子系在通往<strong>B4</strong>区域的门上，并穿过窗户伸入<strong>B5</strong>区域，使得任何人在B5区域（或沿绳路径任一处）都能以一个交互动作拽动绳子，从而拉开通往<strong>B4</strong>区域的门。PC若在此区域附近进行搜索，可通过一次成功的@Check[perception|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定发现这根隐藏的绳子。若要从更远距离（由GM决定）发现绳子，则需要PC在该检定中大成功。</p>\n<p>尽管营地内有多个地点，但仍视为一次单一遭遇。各地点的简要概览请见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13thesilkwaspc00#silkwasp-camp-locations]{绢蜂营地地点}侧栏。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.eNUvJRJogbeXCaFb]{绢蜂营地警戒等级}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meigui-ci.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hong Meigui\" alt=\"female provincial jiang-shi vampire\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meigui-ci.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>绢蜂盗匪目前由僵尸红玫瑰领导，罗坤（前任首领）如今担任剩余盗匪的副指挥者。他们还饲养了一对训练程度不高的帝王眼镜蛇作为守卫。PC们此前在桥上击败的盗匪不会在此遭遇，因此这里用于守卫营地的敌人至少构成一次严重10级遭遇（红玫瑰、两条精英帝王眼镜蛇以及五名绢蜂盗匪）。若有任何盗匪在桥上的战斗中幸存，要么给PC们机会在野外或柳岸镇外围与其对峙以削减盗匪数量，要么就向本遭遇中补足人数，使其改为一次极限10级遭遇。</p>\n<p>意外来访：若盗匪没有理由怀疑PC们是来战斗的，那么罗坤（或者若他已死亡，则由剩余的绢蜂之一）会从屋里出来，在某个门口的路径上与PC们会面，弄清他们想要什么；他会尽力让PC们离开，同时其他盗匪与红玫瑰按下文“防御中的盗匪”所述准备作战。注意：如果PC们曾在桥上与盗匪交战，那么盗匪总会预期PC们会上门拜访，即便所有盗匪都从那场战斗中全身而退。</p>\n<p>如果PC们在盗匪尚未进入防御状态时隐秘接近，则有两名盗匪在屋外警戒：一名在房屋前门廊，另一名坐在鱼塘旁小棚屋外的一把椅子上。其他盗匪分散在B5、B8与B9区域；罗坤（若在场）位于B6区域，红玫瑰位于B10区域。一旦警报拉响，盗匪会尽力执行其防御措施，如下所述。</p>\n<p>防御中的盗匪：多数情况下，盗匪预期会有战斗。若与PC们发生任何暴力冲突，或PC们让他们有其他理由提高戒心，则盗匪会在接下来1周内保持高度警戒。当营地处于警戒状态时，一名盗匪在B2区域的棚屋内站岗，另一名则巡逻房屋西南侧、靠近B3区域的一片矮丛环境中。至少还有三名盗匪在B5与B8区域警戒；若现场盗匪多于五名，则可酌情让额外盗匪藏在矮丛环境中。入夜后，盗匪轮班休息，同时睡觉的最多不超过两人。若罗坤在场，他会在B5区域站岗。红玫瑰在B10区域站岗。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-meigui-ci.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">绢蜂营地</span> <span class=\"keepme\">严重 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.9F0HsQUbRP8lqeB5]{Hong Meigui} @UUID[Actor.03Z6RQw6IfT5gGqw]{Elite Emperor Cobras (2)} @UUID[Actor.0SkFM5JauCarAiSy]{Silkwasp Bandits (5)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>盗匪战术：</strong>战斗开始后，盗匪会用弓从各自的掩护位置向PC们射击。B5区域的一名盗匪会以一个交互动作拽动隐藏的绳子，拉开通往B4区域的门，使里面两条帝王眼镜蛇滑行而出。这些大蛇会去攻击任何明显的入侵者，但也会攻击与其相邻的盗匪——它们只听命于红玫瑰。僵尸本人会留在B10区域的房间内，通过被封板窗户的缝隙对目标施放远程法术或@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{念动射弹}；但若PC们进入屋内，她会立刻上前与其近战交锋。</p>\n  <p>若PC们设法进入屋内，盗匪会全部向该区域聚集，与PC们近战缠斗。只要红玫瑰仍活着，盗匪就会战至死；但一旦她被击败，她对盗匪的控制便会瓦解，任何幸存的盗匪都会逃跑。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>财宝：</strong> @UUID[Actor.4nMKGGxh1UnSoRjJ]{Large Chest} @UUID[Actor.iQu7bpHo1lCpu5gf]{False Bottom} <br />\n  PC若在B10区域进行搜索，会自动注意到床脚处的大箱子。箱子上有一把显眼且看起来很结实的挂锁，可用红玫瑰袍子口袋里携带的钥匙打开，也可通过进行三次@Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock]检定来开锁。箱内有数十个丝绸钱袋，共计3,500 sp、220 gp、价值120 gp的各式珠宝、一枚<em>消失钱币护符</em>以及一根<em>4环安抚魔杖</em>——这些曾是绢蜂盗匪聚敛的财物，如今不过是用来掩盖红玫瑰真正财宝的幌子；她把真货藏在箱子的假底之下。\n</p>\n<p>PC若在箱内进行搜索，可通过一次成功的@Check[perception|dc:28|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定发现假底。紧紧包在一张上等蛛丝布（价值60 gp）里的，是一枚<em>僵尸铃</em>；红玫瑰长期以来对其痴迷，却又将其藏在此处，以防敌人用它来对付自己。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Silkwasp Camp</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 10</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Silkwasp Camp Locations</h1>\n  <p>Brief descriptions of the Silkwasp Bandit camp locations follow.</p>\n  <p><strong>B1:</strong> Front gates.</p>\n  <p><strong>B2:</strong> Storage shack near a fishpond surrounded by swampy mud.</p>\n  <p><strong>B3:</strong> Inner gates.</p>\n  <p><strong>B4:</strong> Partially collapsed granary.</p>\n  <p><strong>B5:</strong> Living/dining room, now used as bandit barracks.</p>\n  <p><strong>B6:</strong> Kitchen, now used as Lo Kuon’s barracks.</p>\n  <p><strong>B7:</strong> Pantry.</p>\n  <p><strong>B8:</strong> Workshop, now used as bandit barracks.</p>\n  <p><strong>B9:</strong> Back porch.</p>\n  <p><strong>B10:</strong> Bedroom, claimed by Hong Meigui.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>If the PCs managed to secure a bandit’s cooperation by removing the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.5pwK2FZX6QwgtfqX]{Inveigle} effect on them, they can give the PCs directions to their hideout, but only Lo Kuon agrees to accompany the PCs in an attempt to get revenge on Hong Meigui. Likewise, only Lo Kuon knows that Hong Meigui is a jiang-shi, allowing him to provide more advice on how to fight her. He suggests the PCs bring handheld mirrors and materials to put her to rest forever once they defeat her (either 1 Bulk of glutinous rice or hen eggs). Finally, Lo Kuon can also tell the PCs that she keeps some sort of item that she seems both to fear and be obsessed with wrapped in silk in her quarters.</p>\n<p>Without the aid of a rescued bandit, the PCs will need to resort to other methods to discover the Silkwasp Camp. The camp is in a former farmstead located on a tall bluff overlooking the Sea of Ghosts a few hours north of Karahai; the only overland route to the supposedly abandoned farmstead is via an overgrown trail leading northeast from Willowshore. The PCs might stumble upon this location on their own simply by exploring the countryside, but after each encounter they or the people of Willowshore have with the bandits, the PCs can also Track the bandits to their camp with a successful @Check[survival|dc:20|traits:secret,concentrate,exploration,move,skill,action:track|name:Track] check. The ruined farmstead is just shy of 3 miles east of the edge of the Willowshore hinterlands map—about a day’s horseback ride from town.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs approach the camp, read or paraphrase the following.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A humble farmstead sits on a low bluff overlooking the Sea of Ghosts, its western half nestled within rings of overgrown, ramshackle fences. Reeds surround a large fishpond at the western end, near the gates that lead up through the outermost fence. The farmhouse appears to be in dire repair, and the barn is in even worse shape with a partially collapsed roof.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The swamp and thicket patches are difficult terrain. The water in the pond is 10 feet deep for most of its expanse and is difficult terrain to wade through up to 5 feet from any shore. The wooden fences are quite rickety—they’re 8 feet high, and PCs can Climb over them with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check; on a critical failure, that 5-foot-section of fence collapses, causing the climber to fall prone and making that square into difficult terrain. The wooden gates at areas <strong>B1</strong> and <strong>B3</strong> no longer open but have enough missing boards that a Medium or smaller creature (or a sinuous Large snake) can move through them by passing through gaps with a Stride action. The cliffside along the east of the farm drops 50 feet into the surf below; the water is nowhere near deep enough to break a fall. These sea-spray slick cliffs can be Climbed by a PC who succeeds at a @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climbed] check.</p>\n<p>Both the shack at area <strong>B2</strong> and the farmhouse have several windows, but they’ve been partially boarded up. These can be used as arrow slits, allowing an adjacent creature to fire arrows through them at no penalty to targets beyond while gaining greater cover for themselves.</p>\n<p>A 40-foot-long rope lies concealed under a layer of dirt along the path indicated by the dotted red line. The rope is attached to the doors leading into area <strong>B4</strong> and threaded through the window into area <strong>B5</strong>, allowing anyone to tug on the rope from area B5 (or along its path) as an Interact action to pull open the doors to area <strong>B4</strong>. A PC who Searches near this area can discover the hidden rope with a successful @Check[perception|dc:22|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check. Spotting the rope from a greater distance (as determined by the GM) requires a PC to critically succeed at this check.</p>\n<p>Although there are numerous locations at the campsite, it’s still treated as one single encounter. See the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13thesilkwaspc00#silkwasp-camp-locations]{Silkwasp Camp Locations} sidebar for a brief overview of each location.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.eNUvJRJogbeXCaFb]{The Silkwasp Camp Alert Level}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meigui-ci.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hong Meigui\" alt=\"female provincial jiang-shi vampire\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meigui-ci.webp');width:50%\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The Silkwasp Bandits are currently led by the jiang-shi Hong Meigui, with Lo Kuon (the previous leader) now serving as a sub-commander over the remaining bandits. They also keep a pair of partially trained emperor cobras as guardians. Any bandits the PCs defeated earlier at the bridge won’t be encountered here, leaving what amounts to, at minimum, a Severe 10 encounter (Hong Meigui, two elite emperor cobras, and five Silkwasp Bandits) to defend the camp. If any bandits did survive the battle at the bridge, either give the PCs a chance to whittle down the bandits’ numbers by confronting them in the wild or on the outskirts of Willowshore, or add enough to this encounter to make it an Extreme 10 encounter instead.</p>\n<p>Unexpected Visit: If the bandits have no reason to suspect the PCs are here to fight, then Lo Kuon (or, if he’s dead, one of the remaining Silkwasps) emerges from the house to meet with the PCs on the path at one of the gates to find out what they want; he does his best to get the PCs to leave while the other bandits and Hong Meigui prepare for battle as detailed in Bandits on the Defensive below. Note that if the PCs fought the bandits at the bridge, they’ll always expect a visit from the PCs, even if all of the bandits escaped that fight alive.</p>\n<p>If the PCs approach stealthily while the bandits aren’t on the defensive, then two bandits stand watch outside: one at the house’s front porch and one sitting in a chair outside the small shack near the fishpond. The other bandits are spread out between areas B5, B8, and B9, with Lo Kuon (if present) in area B6, and Hong Meigui in area B10. Once an alarm is raised, the bandits do their best to enact their defenses, as detailed below.</p>\n<p>Bandits on the Defensive: In most cases, the bandits expect a fight. They are on high alert for 1 week after any violent clash with the PCs or if the PCs have given them other cause to be wary. When the camp is on alert, a bandit stands watch in the shack at area B2 and another patrols the patch of undergrowth southwest of the house near area B3. At least three more bandits stand watch in areas B5 and B8; if there are more than five bandits on-site, then additional bandits hide in the undergrowth as you see fit. After dark, the bandits take shifts, with no more than two sleeping at a time. If he’s present, Lo Kuon stands guard in area B5. Hong Meigui stands guard in area B10.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-meigui-ci.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Silkwasp Camp</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.9F0HsQUbRP8lqeB5]{Hong Meigui} @UUID[Actor.03Z6RQw6IfT5gGqw]{Elite Emperor Cobras (2)} @UUID[Actor.0SkFM5JauCarAiSy]{Silkwasp Bandits (5)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Bandit Tactics:</strong> Once a fight begins, the bandits use their bows to fire upon the PCs from their positions of cover. One bandit in area <strong>B5</strong> takes an Interact action to tug open the doors to area <strong>B4</strong> via the concealed rope, allowing the two emperor cobras within to slither out. These large snakes move to attack any obvious intruders but also attack adjacent bandits as well—they obey only Hong Meigui. The jiang-shi herself remains in her room at area <strong>B10</strong> and casts ranged spells or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{Telekinetic Projectile} at targets through the gaps in her boarded-up windows, but if the PCs enter the house, she moves to engage them in melee at once.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs make their way into the house, the bandits all converge on that area to engage the PCs in melee. As long as Hong Meigui lives, the bandits fight to the death, but once she’s defeated, her control over them breaks, and any surviving bandits flee.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.4nMKGGxh1UnSoRjJ]{Large Chest} @UUID[Actor.iQu7bpHo1lCpu5gf]{False Bottom} <br />\n  A PC who Searches in area <strong>B10</strong> automatically notices the large chest at the foot of the bed. The chest is locked with an obvious and solid-looking padlock that can be opened either with the key that Hong Meigui carries in a pocket in her robe or by three @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock. Inside the chest are dozens of silk pouches containing a total of 3,500 sp, 220 gp, 120 gp in assorted pieces of jewelry, a <em>vanishing coin talisman</em>, and a <em>4th-rank wand of soothe</em>—once the Silkwasp Bandits’ collected treasure, but now little more than a cover for the true treasure Hong Meigui keeps hidden under a false bottom in the chest.\n</p>\n<p>A PC who Searches inside the chest can spot the false bottom with a successful @Check[perception|dc:28|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check. Wrapped tightly in a sheet of fine spidersilk (worth 60 gp) is a <em>jiang-shi bell</em> that Hong Meigui has long been obsessed with yet keeps stashed here to prevent her enemies from using it against her.</p>"
            },
            "Dealing with Bandits": {
              "name": "对付强盗 Dealing with Bandits",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Dealing with Bandits\">应对强盗</h2>\n<p>如果PC们同意付钱，那么在桥上被勒索的钱仅仅是他们与丝蜂强盗麻烦的开端。在接下来的几个月里，这群强盗会持续成为柳岸镇的眼中钉，每隔几周就冒出新的抱怨——农场里的牲畜和役畜被偷，有人在野外或沿路旅行时遭到劫掠，甚至还有传言说，有些陌生的麻烦制造者在镇子东北部一些建筑的院落里鬼鬼祟祟。这些事件都是强盗持续试探城镇防御的手段。如果PC们不采取行动，洪玫瑰最终会带着她剩余的所有强盗，在镇上对PC们发动一次胆大妄为的攻击；这种事件不应早于第13章开始时发生，并且应被构建为一次极限遭遇——PC们明智的做法是尽早处理这群强盗，而不是拖到以后！</p>\n<p>如果PC们在桥上与罗阔恩战斗并击败了强盗，那么针对柳岸镇的强盗活动会来得更快。洪玫瑰会加快她的计划，最初的麻烦报告会在几天内传来，而不是几周。</p>\n<p>尽管柳岸镇里无人知晓关于强盗的任何重要情报，PC们仍可以前往唐入，尝试进一步了解丝蜂帮。到了那里，只要一名PC在唐入的市民之间花费2小时搜集信息后，成功通过一次 @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] 检定，PC们就能得知更多关于丝蜂强盗的消息。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 按照传统，当地人曾通过把便条藏进蜂巢里来向丝蜂帮传讯，请求他们协助对抗络新妇；但自从去年夏初丝蜂帮沉寂之后，再也没有人用这种方法得到回应。大多数人都以为这些强盗在某场欠考虑的战斗中被消灭了。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 丝蜂强盗的名字来源于丝蜂——一种以蜘蛛为食的本地黄蜂品种。这些强盗设法对抗了该地区络新妇的大部分活动，并以黄蜂的凶猛与狡黠为榜样。他们的首领罗阔恩被视为某种程度上的地方英雄。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 丝蜂强盗多年前就被杀光了，但他们的幽灵（特征）仍在一些地区道路上作祟，要求缴纳贡品。那些按他们要求付出的人，会在下一个满月前染上一种令人消耗的疾病诅咒。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Dealing with Bandits\">Dealing with Bandits</h2>\n<p>The money extorted at the bridge is only the beginning of the PCs’ trouble with the Silkwasp Bandits if they agree to pay the price. Over the months to come, the bandits continue to be a thorn in Willowshore’s side, with a new complaint rising every few weeks—livestock and draft animals stolen from farms, folks being robbed while out in the wild or traveling the roads, and even rumors of unfamiliar troublemakers skulking around the yards of some of the buildings along the northeast section of town. All these events are the bandits’ continued attempts to test the town’s defenses. If the PCs don’t take action, Hong Meigui eventually leads all of her remaining bandits on a brazen attack against the PCs in town; such an event shouldn’t take place until the start of Chapter 13 and should be structured as an Extreme encounter—the PCs would be wise to handle this bandit situation sooner than later!</p>\n<p>If the PCs fought Lo Kuon and defeated the bandits at the bridge, the bandit activity against Willowshore happens even more swiftly. Hong Meigui speeds up her plans, with the first reports of trouble coming in within a few days rather than a few weeks.</p>\n<p>While no one in Willowshore knows anything of note about the bandits, the PCs can travel to Karahai to try to learn more about the Silkwasps. There, once a PC succeeds at a @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] check after spending 2 hours to Gather Information among the citizens of Karahai, the PCs can learn more about the Silkwasp Bandits.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> Traditionally, locals have passed messages to the Silkwasps to beg for aid against the jorogumo by hiding notes inside of wasp nests, but no one has received any response after using this method since early last summer, when the Silkwasps went silent. Most assumed that the bandits had been wiped out in some sort of ill-conceived battle.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The Silkwasp Bandits take their name from the silkwasp, a local species of wasp known to prey upon spiders. The bandits, who have managed to oppose much of the jorogumo activity in the region, model themselves after the wasps’ fierceness and cunning. Their leader, Lo Kuon, is considered something of a local hero.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The Silkwasp Bandits were slain years ago, but their ghosts still haunt some of the regional roads, demanding tribute. Those who pay their demands find themselves cursed with a wasting disease by the next full moon.</p>"
            },
            "Silkwasps at the Bridge": {
              "name": "桥上的丝蜂 Silkwasps at the Bridge",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">桥上的丝蜂</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 10</span>\n</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇是一座偏远小镇，但它回归现代神门并未被忽视。唐入的村民很可能最先意识到小镇回来了；随着月份推移，更远的城镇与村落也会得知消息。但有一伙人尤其注意到唐入桥上的修复工程——一群自称“丝蜂盗匪”的罪犯。</p>\n<p>桥梁重建工程开工约一周后，一名紧张又气喘吁吁的信使找到PC，告知他们“盗匪来了唐入桥，还说他们说了算！”桥梁工人已经从工地撤回，需要PC出面处理这些急于敲诈工人的盗匪。信使将盗匪描述为“六个左右凶神恶煞的男女，脖子上都围着染血的绷带”。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kuonlo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Lo Kuon\" alt=\"a human male bandit with studded leather armor\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kuonlo.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>丝蜂盗匪的据点位于柳岸镇东北方、需走上数日路程的一处废弃农庄。对PC而言，试图占据唐入桥的计划看起来或许只是寻常的打家劫舍，但这其实是一名狡猾敌人对他们决心与力量的首次试探，也是把柳岸镇推向全面战争的第一步。</p>\n<p>当PC抵达桥边时，忧心忡忡的工人迎了上来。自盗匪到来后，这些工人一直聚在桥西南方数百尺外的工地营地里。尽管勇敢地拒绝彻底放弃工地，他们至今仍未与盗匪正面交涉，除了不断承诺：有权支付罚金的人很快就会到。</p>\n<p>盗匪在路上扎营，在峡谷西侧路边搭起两顶帐篷。虽然确有三名盗匪在帐篷里等着PC，但另外四名埋伏在峡谷对面：在公路旁的密林中潜藏，分成两组——北面两人、南面两人。一旦盗匪注意到PC靠近，就有一人走出帐篷，笑容满面地上前招呼。</p>\n<p>此人名叫罗·坤，是丝蜂盗匪的“门面”（但PC很快会知道，他并非现任首领）。罗·坤在当地名声不小：他大胆、有魅力，年近四十，曾因反抗络新妇而成为地方传奇。他那些大胆的事迹在乡野神门颇受欢迎（只不过多半是低声传讲），但PC大概率没听过他。当他自我介绍时，会张开双臂，愉快地说：“欢迎来到我的桥！我想你们肯定知道我是谁吧？”如果PC坦言不知道，他会显得震惊，但很快恢复镇定，称自己是“人民的庇护者、与编织欺诈之网者为敌、对配得上我仁慈的人而言的传奇”。</p>\n<p>事实上，罗·坤作为荒野反叛者、对抗络新妇统治的日子，在去年夏天就结束了——当时他带着盗匪闯入谭杉寺劫掠。他原本计划夺取武器与魔法用来对付络新妇，却在这座破败寺院里，与同伙一并沦为红玫瑰的奴仆；红玫瑰是一名侍奉苦迦菩提、栖居于废寺的僵尸吸血鬼（特征）代理人。</p>\n<p>丝蜂盗匪脖子上缠着的染血头巾，遮住了他们堕落与苦迦菩提联系的唯一外在痕迹——咽喉处一道渗血、部分结痂的伤口，形如纠结的根结，正是苦迦菩提的象征。此伤口不会影响盗匪的数据，但作为对红玫瑰臣服的烙印，它令他们备受折磨。只有罗·坤不戴这条绷带，而是用头盔遮住自己颈后的印记。PC可以通过一次成功的@Check[religion|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来进行回忆知识并识别该象征；或者，如果他们在本战役更早时曾遇到并辨认过该象征，则会自动认出。</p>\n<p>罗·坤最初对PC的态度看似不关心，但只要他仍受红玫瑰蛊惑，就根本无意与柳岸镇达成长期协议。不过在提出要求前，他会先要求PC解释他们是谁，以及为何自认为有资格对唐入桥发号施令。罗·坤表面上带着兴趣听他们解释，并试图尽可能了解PC与柳岸镇为何仿佛一个世纪未过般突然出现。尤其是，他对他们对苦迦菩提的立场显得颇感兴趣——他假装不知情，以此套出PC对灵堕魔了解多少，以及打算如何应对。若他判断PC认为苦迦菩提的威胁已经结束，他会祝贺他们，并不会试图纠正这一结论。</p>\n<p>罗·坤依靠欺瞒来维持这场表演；任何试图戳穿他的谎言或把话题引向他不愿谈及之事的举动，都会促使他转而谈论PC为使用这座桥该向丝蜂盗匪支付多少。他要求的初始费用为每月200 gp，并承诺若PC完成重建工程，就把费用降到每月50 gp。如果PC试图讨价还价，他会不管PC检定结果如何，直接把要价减半——毕竟这场骗局只是为了“摸清”PC的信念。</p>\n<p>如果PC同意付款，罗·坤会既惊讶又满意，并要求立刻交钱。若PC照付，他会鞠躬示意，让盗匪收起帐篷，然后沿道路返回营地（不过一旦离开视线，他们会穿林抄近路以甩掉可能的跟踪者）。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/silkwasp-bandit.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">桥上的丝蜂</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.C7LZB4hB7au7D3Wj]{Lo Kuon} @UUID[Actor.0SkFM5JauCarAiSy]{Silkwasp Bandits (6)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>如果PC拒绝付款或变得敌对，罗·坤会带着明显的失望叹口气，然后说：“我就怕你们会这么回答。那好吧……看来这桥谁也别想用！”他拔出短剑，并用欺瞒掷先攻。附近两名盗匪用察觉掷先攻，而峡谷对面的盗匪用潜行掷先攻。战斗中，罗·坤与他身边两名同伴在近战中作战，把攻击集中在此刻最常发言的那名PC身上；同时他们也会设法阻止任何人去接战桥对岸的同伙。东侧的四名盗匪则把攻击重点放在桥梁上：他们每人先启动随身携带的两支爆炸箭之一，再向桥梁射击。从他们的位置来看，被他们瞄准的桥梁承重部位AC为24；每支命中桥梁的爆炸箭都会在火焰爆裂中对结构造成伤害，而每支未命中则会在河流较低的西岸或PC身后的森林中无害爆炸。当盗匪对桥梁命中两次后，桥面的木板会被炸碎，使得通往对岸变得不再容易。若盗匪对桥梁累计命中五次，PC此前投入的全部修复成果都将被毁，他们必须在之后某个日期再次进行一次“重建唐入桥”的行动，从头开始。一旦这四名盗匪用尽爆炸箭或桥梁被毁，他们就会转而专注射击PC。</p>\n  <p>只要仍受蛊惑，盗匪就会战斗至死。如果PC活捉他们，或成功驱散红玫瑰的仪式，盗匪会立刻投降，而罗·坤会和盘托出一切，恳求PC前往他们的营地，击败那头把他们当作棋子操控了数月的怪物。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Silkwasps at the Bridge</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 10</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Willowshore is a remote town, but its return to modern Shenmen doesn’t go unnoticed. The villagers of Karahai are likely the first to realize the town is back, with more distant towns and villages learning the news as the months go by, but one group in particular takes note of work done at Karahai Bridge—a band of criminals who call themselves the Silkwasp Bandits.</p>\n<p>About a week after work on rebuilding the bridge gets underway, the PCs are approached by a nervous and out-of-breath messenger who informs them that “bandits have come to Karahai Bridge and are claiming they’re in charge!” The bridge workers have retreated from work and need the PCs to step in to deal with the bandits, who are eager to extort the workers. The messenger describes the bandits as “a half dozen rough-looking men and women wearing bloodstained bandages around their necks.”</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kuonlo.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Lo Kuon\" alt=\"a human male bandit with studded leather armor\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kuonlo.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The Silkwasp Bandits are based in a ruined farmstead a few days’ travel northeast of Willowshore. While the plot to claim Karahai Bridge might seem like typical banditry to the PCs, this is the first test of their resolve and strength by a canny foe and the first move toward all-out war on Willowshore.</p>\n<p>When the PCs arrive at the bridge, they’re greeted by the worried workers, who have spent their time gathered in their work camp a few hundred feet southwest of the bridge since the bandits arrived. Bravely refusing to fully abandon the site, these workers haven’t engaged with the bandits yet other than to continue to promise that those with the authority to pay their fines will be here soon.</p>\n<p>The bandits have set up camp on the road, pitching a pair of tents on the west side of the gorge. While three bandits indeed await the PCs in the tents, another four lie in wait on the far side of the gorge, hidden in the dense forest just off the road, in two pairs—two to the north and two to the south. As soon as the bandits notice the PCs’ approach, one steps out of the tent to greet the PCs with a broad smile.</p>\n<p>This individual is Lo Kuon, the “face” of the Silkwasp Bandits (though not, as the PCs soon learn, their current leader). Lo Kuon has a local reputation of being a daring and charismatic man, now in his late thirties, who became a local legend for his stance against the jorogumo. Tales of his bold escapades are popular (if only told in whispers) in rural Shenmen, but the PCs aren’t likely to have heard of him. When he introduces himself, he does so with arms wide and a cheerful, “Welcome to my bridge! I’m sure you know who I am?” If the PCs reveal they have no idea, he expresses shock but recovers quickly, describing himself as a “patron of the people, foe to those who spin their webs of deceit, and legend to those who have earned his mercy.”</p>\n<p>In fact, Lo Kuon’s days of being a wilderness-based rebel against jorogumo rule ended last summer when he led his bandits to the Tan Sugi Monastery to loot it. There, his plans to gain weapons and magic to use against the jorogumo ended as he and his crew fell into thrall of Hong Meigui, a jiang-shi vampire agent of Kugaptee who dwelt in the ruined monastery.</p>\n<p>The bloodstained kerchiefs the Silkwasp Bandits wear around their necks hide the only outward manifestation of their corruption and link to Kugaptee—a seeping, partially scabbed-over wound on their throats in the shape of a tangled knot of roots, the symbol of Kugaptee. While the wound doesn’t impact the bandits’ statistics, it’s an uncomfortable manifestation of their servitude to Hong Meigui. Only Lo Kuon eschews this bandage, instead hiding the mark on the back of his neck with his helmet. A PC can recognize the symbol with a successful @Check[religion|dc:28|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, or automatically if they encountered the symbol and identified it earlier in this campaign.</p>\n<p>Lo Kuon’s initial attitude to the PCs seems indifferent, but as long as he’s inveigled by Hong Meigui, he isn’t actually interested in striking a long-lasting deal with Willowshore. Before he gets to his demands, though, he asks the PCs to explain themselves and why they’ve decided they’re the ones who get to make the calls for Karahai Bridge. Lo Kuon listens to their explanation with apparent amusement and tries to learn all he can about how the PCs and Willowshore suddenly appeared as if no time had passed for a century. In particular, he appears intrigued by their stance on Kugaptee—he feigns ignorance here in an attempt to find out what the PCs know of, and plan to do about, the nindoru. If he determines that the PCs think Kugaptee’s threat has ended, he congratulates them and does nothing to dissuade them of that conclusion.</p>\n<p>Lo Kuon relies on Deception to keep up the charade, and any attempt to pierce his lies or redirect the discussion toward topics he would rather stay silent on prompts him to change the subject to what the PCs owe the Silkwasp Bandits for use of the bridge. He demands an initial payment of 200 gp per month, promising to lower those payments to a mere 50 gp a month if the PCs complete the rebuilding project. If the PCs make any attempt to bargain, he’ll cut these asking prices in half regardless of any check results the PCs make—after all, this ruse is just to “feel out” the PCs’ convictions.</p>\n<p>If the PCs agree to a payment, Lo Kuon is surprised but also pleased, and he demands payment at once. If they pay, he bows and has his bandits gather up their tents, then they head back to their encampment via the roads (although once they’re out of sight, they cut through the forest to throw off anyone following them).</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/silkwasp-bandit.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Silkwasps at the Bridge</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.C7LZB4hB7au7D3Wj]{Lo Kuon} @UUID[Actor.0SkFM5JauCarAiSy]{Silkwasp Bandits (6)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>If the PCs refuse to pay or become hostile, Lo Kuon sighs in apparent disappointment, then says, “I was afraid that’d be your response. Well then... no bridge for anyone, I suppose!” He draws his shortsword and rolls Deception for initiative. The two nearby bandits roll Perception, and those on the far side of the gorge roll Stealth. During combat, Lo Kuon and his two nearby allies fight in melee, focusing their attacks on the PC who spoke up the most at this point, but they also work to prevent anyone from engaging their allies on the far side of the bridge. The four bandits on the east side focus their attacks on the bridge, each activating one of the two explosive arrows they carry before firing the arrow at the bridge. From their positions, the load-bearing parts of the bridge they’re targeting have AC 24; each explosive arrow that hits the bridge bursts in a ball of fire that damages the structure, while each that misses explodes harmlessly on the lower west bank of the river or beyond the PCs in the forest. Once the bandits hit the bridge twice, the planks crossing the bridge are blown apart, preventing easy access to the other side. If the bandits score a total of five hits on the bridge, all the work the PCs have put into it is destroyed, and they must start from scratch by taking the Rebuild Karahai Bridge activity once more at a later date. Once the four bandits run out of explosive arrows or the bridge is destroyed, they focus on shooting the PCs.</p>\n  <p>As long as they remain inveigled, the bandits fight to the death. If the PCs capture them alive or manage to dispel Hong Meigui’s ritual, the bandits immediately surrender, and Lo Kuon reveals everything, begging the PCs to travel to their campsite to defeat the monster that has kept them as her pawns for months.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Rebuilding the Bridge": {
              "name": "重建桥梁 Rebuilding the Bridge",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Rebuilding the Bridge\">重建大桥</h2>\n<p>重建唐入桥需要数周时间。虽然这项工程的推进甚至开工都不要求PC必须在现场，但PC可以通过花费3天休整模式来绘制图纸、勘察现场并召集有才干的工人来重建大桥，从而对工程产生重大影响。如果PC们不参与，柳岸镇的镇长老会承担这项任务，而下方的“重建唐入桥”行动将自动获得一次失败结果。其他PC可以在“重建唐入桥”的掷骰中协助主要PC。</p>\n<p>一旦唐入桥重建完成，柳岸镇就能正式开始与唐入进行贸易的流程。这样做会对本幕后续发生的一些事件产生影响，如正文所述。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>重建唐入桥</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">休整模式</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">操作</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你为重建唐入桥制定计划，并招募一个团队在3天内执行该计划。尝试一次@Check[engineering-lore|dc:25]检定、一次@Check[crafting|dc:27]检定，或一次@Check[society|dc:29]检定；其他PC可以花费同样数量的休整模式时间，使用上述任意技能为该检定提供协助。如果某位PC拥有法术或其他魔法效果，且GM判定这些效果能在流程中提供显著帮助，并且该PC花费其休整模式时间参与协助，则该PC的魔法使主要检定获得+1状态加值。该加值可与多名不同的施法PC叠加，最高状态加值为+3。一旦进行过此检定，PC们就无需在该工程上再花费更多休整模式时间。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> PC们想出了绝妙的方案，而镇上的工人也格外熟练且热情高涨。大桥只需1个月即可重建完成，并会在第12章事件开始前竣工。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 计划扎实，工程推进迅速，未遭遇任何重大挫折。大桥需要2个月重建完成。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 重建大桥的计划耗时更久才能完成，工程也遭遇数次小挫折与延误。大桥需要3个月才能完工，因此很可能无法在本冒险路径结束前竣工。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 开工数日后灾害降临，造成数人死亡（若你希望随机决定本次事件中柳岸镇有多少市民死亡，可掷骰[[/r 1d8]]）。PC们必须从头开始，再次进行“重建唐入桥”休整模式行动以重新启动工程，但由于开工更晚，此次掷骰的检定承受–4减值。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>大桥重建完成后，给予PC们120 XP。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Rebuilding the Bridge\">Rebuilding the Bridge</h2>\n<p>Rebuilding Karahai Bridge takes weeks. While the work doesn’t require a PC to be on-site to progress or even to begin, a PC can significantly impact the project by spending 3 days of downtime to draw up plans, survey the site, and gather talented workers to rebuild the bridge. If the PCs don’t get involved, Willowshore’s town elder takes on the task, and the Rebuild Karahai Bridge activity below automatically gets a failure result. Other PCs can Aid the primary PC’s roll to Rebuild Karahai Bridge.</p>\n<p>Once Karahai Bridge is rebuilt, Willowshore can officially begin the process of trading with Karahai. Doing so has repercussions on some of the events that take place later in this act, as noted in the text.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Rebuild Karahai Bridge</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Downtime</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Manipulate</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You create a plan for rebuilding Karahai Bridge and recruit a team to enact that plan over the course of 3 days. Attempt a @Check[engineering-lore|dc:25] check, a @Check[crafting|dc:27] check, or a @Check[society|dc:29] check; other PCs can Aid this check with any of those skills by spending the same amount of downtime providing that assistance. If a PC has access to spells or other magic effects that the GM decides could be of significant aid to the process, and if that PC spends their downtime helping, the PC’s magic grants the primary check a +1 status bonus. This bonus stacks with multiple different spellcasting PCs, up to a maximum status bonus of +3. Once this check has been attempted, the PCs don’t need to spend more downtime on the project.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> The PCs hit upon a brilliant plan, and the town’s workers prove to be particularly skilled and exuberant. The bridge takes only 1 month to rebuild and is finished before the events of Chapter 12 begin.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The plans are solid and the project proceeds quickly without any major setbacks. The bridge takes 2 months to rebuild.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> The plans for rebuilding the bridge take longer to complete, and the project suffers several minor setbacks and delays. The bridge takes 3 months to complete and is thus unlikely to be finished before this Adventure Path ends.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Disaster strikes several days into the job, resulting in several deaths (roll [[/r 1d8]] if you wish to randomly determine how many of Willowshore’s citizens perish in this event). The PCs must start over, taking the Rebuild Karahai Bridge downtime activity once more to get the project restarted, but the roll suffers a –4 penalty to the check as a result of the later start.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Once the bridge is rebuilt, grant the PCs 120 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Bridges and Bandits": {
              "name": "桥梁与强盗 Bridges and Bandits",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Bridges and Bandits\">桥梁与匪徒</h1>\n<p>尽管柳岸镇已经恢复，这座村庄之外的地区仍然破败不堪。最紧迫的问题是唐入桥：它曾将柳岸腹地与海岸线以及要塞村庄唐入连接起来，却在几十年前被泥石流摧毁。正如PC们在前一幕中得知的那样，孙海拼凑出了一个临时替代品，但他那种绳索加木板的结构从来就不是为永久使用而建，也无法承受沉重载荷。</p>\n<p>如今，曾经连接柳岸镇与神门木材市场的那座原始桥梁，只剩下八根巨大木支撑中的六根——它们过去把桥体高高架在峡谷之上。曾位于西南方的两根支撑被泥石流毁坏，导致其余木桥的木板坠入水中，顺流向北漂走，最终流入大海。</p>\n<p>有五块巨大的木板被铺设在南侧的桥桩上，并用支架和绳索固定；这座宽5英尺的临时桥看起来险象环生，但实际上建造得相当结实，成功进行一次 @Check[crafting|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[engineering-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定以回忆知识的PC可以确认这一点。PC可以通过行走安全地过桥；众多绳索提供了抓握点，而木板沉重且稳定。然而，任何包含剧烈或防御性动作的动作（包括所有带有攻击（特征）的动作）若导致大成功或大失败，则会使位于木板桥上的PC坠落30英尺，落入下方20英尺深的水中（坠落的PC可以在成功通过一次 @Check[reflex|dc:20|traits:manipulate,action:grab-an-edge|name:Grab an Edge] 豁免后抓住边缘）。攀爬峡谷壁需要进行一次 @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] 检定（或沿着陡峭倾斜的旧泥石流坡面攀爬则为 @Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] 检定），在河中游泳需要进行一次 @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim] 检定。木板足够宽，可以牵引甚至骑乘一只大型坐骑通过，只要该坐骑将木板视为困难地形，并且PC在其坐骑每进行一次行走时，都成功通过一次 @Check[nature|dc:25|traits:auditory,concentrate,action:command-an-animal|name:Command an Animal] 检定来指挥动物。</p>\n<p>PC们随时都可以再次造访唐入（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13silvercollar00#returning-to-karahai]{返回唐入} 侧栏），但在桥梁修复之前，柳岸镇仍与其最重要的贸易伙伴隔绝。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Bridges and Bandits\">Bridges and Bandits</h1>\n<p>Although Willowshore has been restored, the area beyond the village remains in disrepair. The most pressing problem is that Karahai Bridge, which once connected the Willowshore hinterlands to the coastline and the fortress village of Karahai, was destroyed decades ago by mudslides. As the PCs learned in the previous act, Mago Kai patched together a temporary replacement, but his rope-and-board construction was never meant to be permanent and won’t withstand heavy loads.</p>\n<p>All that currently remains of the original bridge that once connected Willowshore to the lumber markets of Shenmen are six of the eight massive wooden supports that used to hold the bridge aloft over the gorge. The two supports that once stood to the southwest were destroyed by the mudslide, which caused the rest of the wooden bridge’s planks to tumble into the water and float away to the north, downstream and out to sea.</p>\n<p>A set of five enormous planks has been placed across the southern pilings, held in place by supports and ropes; while the 5-foot-wide temporary bridge looks treacherous, it’s actually solidly built, as a PC who succeeds at a @Check[crafting|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[engineering-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge can confirm. A PC can cross the bridge safely by Striding; the numerous ropes give handholds, and the planks are heavy and stable. However, any action that includes violent or defensive motion (including all actions with the Attack trait) that results in a critical failure causes the PC on the plank bridge to fall 30 feet and into the 20-foot-deep water below (a falling PC can Grab the Edge by succeeding at a @Check[reflex|dc:20|traits:manipulate,action:grab-an-edge|name:Grab an Edge] save). It’s a @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check to Climb the gorge walls (or a @Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check to Climb along the steeply sloped old mudslide), and a @Check[athletics|dc:15|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim] check to Swim in the river. The planks are wide enough to lead or even ride a Large mount across them, as long as the mount treats the planks as difficult terrain and a PC succeeds at a @Check[nature|dc:25|traits:auditory,concentrate,action:command-an-animal|name:Command an Animal] check to Command the Animal with each Stride their mount takes.</p>\n<p>The PCs can visit Karahai again as soon as they wish (see the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13silvercollar00#returning-to-karahai]{Returning to Karahai} sidebar), but until the bridge is repaired, Willowshore remains cut off from its most important trade partner.</p>"
            },
            "Shinzo’s Farewell": {
              "name": "神藏的告别 Shinzo’s Farewell",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Farewell\">神藏的告别</h1>\n<p>PC们在柳岸镇醒来后的几天，死神商人神藏最后一次到访，向他们道别，并祝贺他们将小镇恢复回生者世界。既然他们如今已回归自然循环，他也到了该继续前行的时候。尽管他在上一幕中已向PC们承认了自己的身份，死神仍没有向PC们展示其真实形态；相反，他说道：“我已如你们了解我那般了解你们，而对我们而言，此刻这一形态便是真实。”若有好奇的PC，他或许会在片刻间显露真身，但绝不会在公众场合这样做，因为他很清楚自己的外貌可能引发意料之外的恐慌。</p>\n<p>这次会面是PC们从神藏的店铺购买物品的最后机会。若你希望引入PC们在先前各幕中错过入手机会的任何新魔法物品，让这些物品（在合理范围内）可供出售，能让PC们最后一次获得取得它们的许可。</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.soCNRN76cgMZUeHe]{神藏的临别赠礼}<br />\n  就在他离开之前，神藏确实留下了一些最后的临别赠礼——一只<em>凤凰符箓匣</em>，以及四张符箓：一张<em>禁忌符箓</em>、一张<em>千痛针符箓</em>，以及两枚<em>强效潜能水晶</em>。随后，他与他的招魂者同伴一同淡出视野，或许会让PC们好奇：他究竟为何要费心帮助他们。\n</p>\n<p>如果你有兴趣进一步探索神藏的故事，关于他动机与结局的附加说明见于 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog16contin]{继续战役}。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Farewell\">Shinzo’s Farewell</h1>\n<p>A few days after the PCs awaken in Willowshore, the shinigami merchant Shinzo arrives one last time to bid them farewell and congratulate them on restoring the town to the living world. As they’ve now returned to the natural cycle, the time has come for him to move on. The shinigami still doesn’t reveal his true form to the PCs, even though he admitted what he was to them in the previous act; instead, he notes, “I have come to know you as you know me, and for us, this form is what is truth now.” He may reveal his true shape to curious PCs for a moment, but never in public, knowing full well that his appearance could spark an unintended panic.</p>\n<p>This meeting is the PCs’ final opportunity to purchase items from Shinzo’s store. If you wish to introduce any new magic items that the PCs missed the chance to acquire during previous acts, having these items (within reason) be available for sale gives the PCs one last chance to gain access to them.</p>\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.soCNRN76cgMZUeHe]{Shinzo's Parting Gift}<br />\n  Just before he leaves, Shinzo does have some final parting gifts—a <em>phoenix fulu holder</em>, along with four fulus: an <em>anathema fulu</em>, a <em>needle thousand-pains fulu</em>, and two <em>greater potency crystals</em>. Afterward, he and his psychopomp companion fade from view, perhaps leaving the PCs curious as to why he bothered to help them at all.\n</p>\n<p>If you’re interested in exploring Shinzo’s story further, additional notes about his motivations and fate are in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog16contin]{Continuing the Campaign}.</p>"
            },
            "Reporting to the Town Elder": {
              "name": "向镇上长老报到 Reporting to the Town Elder",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Reporting to the Town Elder\">向镇长汇报</h3>\n<p>一旦PC们击败了侵扰废弃庄园的灵堕魔，修复并重建这栋建筑的工作就可以开始了。PC们不必直接参与这些行动——镇长感谢他们再次前来协助柳岸镇，并鼓励PC们保留他们在庄园里找到的任何宝藏（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13thegovernors00#looting-the-manor]{搜刮庄园}），随后请他们在方便时尽早向东旅行前往唐入，与那里的村民取得联系，并开始将柳岸镇重新融入生者世界的进程。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Reporting to the Town Elder\">Reporting to the Town Elder</h3>\n<p>Once the PCs defeat the nindoru infesting the ruined manor, work on repairing and rebuilding the structure can begin. The PCs don’t need to be directly involved in these efforts—the town elder thanks them for once again coming to Willowshore’s aid and encourages the PCs to keep any treasure they found in the manor (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13thegovernors00#looting-the-manor]{Looting the Manor}), then asks them to travel east to Karahai at their earliest convenience to make contact with the villagers there and begin the process of reintegrating Willowshore back into the living world.</p>"
            },
            "Primary Suite": {
              "name": "主套件 Primary Suite",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A8. 主套房</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 10</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这间房的入口都被保持关闭——这是宅邸里唯一仍能正常使用的门。任何PC走到任意一扇关闭的门前，都会听到门后房间里传来一名男子轻声吟诵的细微声响。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>宅邸的主卧室和建筑的其他部分一样，破败不堪，但至少这里的天花板似乎还撑得住，使得这间房没有被真菌和蔓生藤蔓占据。尽管如此，家具已成瓦砾，空气中弥漫着霉臭味。房间中央的地面上，数十支蜡烛与线香围成一个圆圈燃烧着，仿佛这里正在进行某种仪式。</p>\n</div>\n<p>正是在这间房里，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}曾试图进行仪式以增强谭杉，却导致灾难性的反噬并摧毁了柳岸镇——任何PC只要花几分钟研究房间并在一次@Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[religion|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定中成功进行回忆知识，就会意识到这一点；若大成功或大失败，则还能看出该仪式因匆忙而漏洞百出。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>那轻柔吟诵声的来源并非那名跪在蜡烛与线香前、沉默不动的人形，而是他头顶上方、黏附在天花板上的一大团红色蝴蝶。此时便能辨认出那团蝴蝶的吟诵是在反复用通用语念诵向苦迦菩提祈祷的词句。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“我奉上我的名字，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从我称作朋友之人那里解开。</p>\n  <p>“我奉上我的鲜血，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从我称作家人之人那里解开。</p>\n  <p>“我奉上我的血肉，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从我称作自己的身躯那里解开。</p>\n  <p>“我奉上我的灵魂，伟大的苦迦菩提！将我从那曾是我命运之物那里解开。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>跪在地上的男人看起来正是和善保本人，活着而且健康。PC进入时，他站起身转向他们致意，感谢他们来寻找自己，并为未能保护城镇而道歉。他请求PC护送他离开宅邸，好让他去见柳岸镇的新总督（镇中长老），告知对方自己已准备好回归职责。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-false-governor.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">主套房</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.DvEzzM2qtwRs1R3z]{伪总督}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img class=\"float-right\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-false-governor.webp\" alt=\"a man appearing to be Governor Heh Shan-Bao\" title=\"False Governor\" style=\"height:18rem;width:auto;shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-false-governor.webp')\" />\n  <p>当然，这个身影并非真正的和善保，而是一只灵堕魔，披着一套具现化的血肉外壳，使自己看起来像他。如果PC同意这位伪总督的请求，在被带到镇中长老面前后，他会说：“多谢你们在我离开期间照看我的城镇，但现在，你们的职责到此为止。伟大的苦迦菩提将统治你们曾统治之地！”随后他施放幻象生物，创造出一个阴影般、多臂多首、强大灵堕魔的化身，企图杀死镇中长老以及在场的任何PC。</p>\n  <p>但愿PC不会上当。如果他们看穿他的谎言（即便起初没看出来，这个版本的和善保从未见过他们、因此对前一幕中他们谈过的事毫无记忆这一点也应能让他们起疑），拒绝护送他，或干脆发动攻击，伪总督会愤怒地嘶声说道：“那你们也一样适合作为苦迦菩提的开宴第一餐！”随后转而攻击。一旦战斗开始，灵堕魔会在战斗中使用其法术，直到其躯体受到足够伤害而褪去血肉外壳。此时他会先使用震慑绝望，再以法术与爪击的打击混合继续战斗。他战至死方休，会穿过宅邸追击敌人，甚至一路追到柳岸镇里。</p>\n  <p>如果区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a3servantsro00]{A3}的鬼魂与区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a5guestquart00]{A5}的妖灵尚未被击败，它们会听见伪总督的震慑绝望，并迅速离开那些房间来到此处，与灵堕魔并肩对PC作战。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">效果</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">将@UUID[Item.lniKnlzc7OuDfeM1]{伪总督真实形态}效果拖拽到其上以关闭他的伪装</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.blO6F33izvOeoevS]{破败房间} <br />\n  一名PC花10分钟搜索这些破败房间，会找到若干有价值的物品，包括：一个凹陷的红金相间夜壶（价值150 gp）、一个金边单片眼镜（价值100 gp， леж在破碎的床头柜残骸中）、一个<em>落语扇</em>（置于樱木盒中，盒上饰有鱼的图案，价值90 gp），以及一个雕刻成盘龙造型的木制药水托架（价值50 gp），其中目前装有如下物品：一份<em>万灵膏药</em>、一瓶<em>迅捷药水</em>以及一瓶<em>高等治疗药水</em>。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>随着伪总督死亡，苦迦菩提对这些废墟的掌控立刻消失。宅邸依旧一片狼藉，但“不受欢迎的门面”以及区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a3servantsro00]{A3}与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a5guestquart00]{A5}的亡灵会立即消散。若PC尚未击败这些遭遇，则按他们已击败这些遭遇来给予XP；然后再额外给予80 XP，作为让那些被困住的灵魂得以前往来世的奖励。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A8. Primary Suite</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 10</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The entrances to this room are kept closed—the only doors in the manor that still function. Any PC who steps up to either closed door hears the soft sound of a man chanting quietly in the room beyond.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The manor’s primary bedroom, as with the rest of the building, is in poor repair, but here at least the ceiling seems to have held up, resulting in a chamber that hasn’t been colonized by fungi and creeping vines. Nonetheless, the furniture lies in rubble, and a musty stink fills the air. Dozens of candles and sticks of incense burn in a circle in the middle of the room, as if a ritual were in progress here.</p>\n</div>\n<p>It was in this very room that @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} attempted the ritual to bolster the Tan Sugi, only for it to backfire catastrophically and destroy the town of Willowshore—any PC who studies the room for a few moments and succeeds at a @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge realizes this, and with a critical success, the ritual’s rushed nature is apparent.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The source of the soft sound of chanting comes not from the silent human figure kneeling before the candles and incense, but instead from a thick mass of red butterflies that clings to the ceiling above his head. The mass’s chanting can now be made out as a repetition of a prayer to Kugaptee, spoken in Common.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“I offer thee my name, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from those whom I called friends.</p>\n  <p>“I offer thee my blood, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from those whom I called family.</p>\n  <p>“I offer thee my flesh, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from the body I called my own.</p>\n  <p>“I offer thee my soul, Great Kugaptee! Unbind me from that which was my fate.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>The man kneeling on the floor appears to be none other than Heh Shan-Bao, alive and healthy. As the PCs enter, he rises to his feet and turns to greet them, thanking them for seeking him out and apologizing for failing to protect the town. He asks to be escorted out of his manor so he can meet the new governor of Willowshore (the town elder) to let them know he’s ready to return to his duties.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-false-governor.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Primary Suite</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.DvEzzM2qtwRs1R3z]{False Governor}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img class=\"float-right\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-false-governor.webp\" alt=\"a man appearing to be Governor Heh Shan-Bao\" title=\"False Governor\" style=\"height:18rem;width:auto;shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-false-governor.webp')\" />\n  <p>Of course, this figure isn’t the real Heh Shan-Bao, but in fact a nindoru wearing a manifested suit of flesh that appears to be him. If the PCs agree to the false governor’s request, upon being brought before the town elder, he says, “Thank you for caring for my town while I was away, but now, your duties are at an end. Great Kugaptee shall rule where you once ruled!” He then casts illusory creature to create a shadowy, multi-armed, many-headed incarnation of the powerful nindoru in an attempt to kill the town elder and any PCs present.</p>\n  <p>Hopefully, the PCs don’t fall for the ruse. If they see through his lies (even if they don’t at first, the fact that this version of Heh Shan-Bao has never met them before and thus has no recollection of anything they spoke of in the previous act should clue them in), refuse to escort him, or simply attack, the false governor hisses in anger and says, “You’ll do just as well for Kugaptee’s inaugural meal!” He then attacks in turn. Once the combat begins, the nindoru uses his spells in battle until his body takes enough damage to shed its flesh. At this point, he uses Stunning Despair before continuing the fight with a mix of spells and claw Strikes. He fights to the death, pursuing foes through the manor or even beyond into Willowshore proper.</p>\n  <p>If the ghosts in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a3servantsro00]{A3} and the wraiths in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a5guestquart00]{A5} haven’t yet been defeated, they hear the false governor’s Stunning Despair and swiftly leave those rooms to come here and join the nindoru in combat against the PCs.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">Drag on the @UUID[Item.lniKnlzc7OuDfeM1]{False Governor True Form} Effect to turn off his disguise</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.blO6F33izvOeoevS]{Ruined Rooms} <br />\n  A PC who Searches the ruined rooms for 10 minutes turns up several objects of value, including a dented red-and-gold chamber pot worth 150 gp, a gold-rimmed monocle worth 100 gp lying amid a shattered nightstand, a <em>fan of falling words </em> stored in a cherry wood case decorated with images of fish worth 90 gp, and a wooden potion holder carved to look like a coiled dragon worth 50 gp that currently holds the following: a <em>panaceatic salve</em>, a <em>potion of quickness</em>, and a <em>greater healing potion</em>.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> With the death of the false governor, Kugaptee’s hold over the ruins vanishes instantly. The manor remains in shambles, but the Unwelcoming Facade and the undead in areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a3servantsro00]{A3} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a5guestquart00]{A5} vanish immediately. Grant the PCs XP as if they’d defeated these encounters if they haven’t done so already, and then grant them an additional 80 XP for allowing those trapped souls to move on to the afterlife.</p>"
            },
            "Storage Rooms": {
              "name": "储藏室 Storage Rooms",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A7. Storage Rooms\">A7. 储藏室</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这些储藏室里的大部分物品看起来都已崩解腐朽，化为一片废墟。木板条腐坏导致箱子破裂，发霉的内容物散落满地；而空桶周围则有陈年的污渍，那是多年来桶中内容物渗漏所致。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.dC9sXQ2srOQ4P2JD]{Wooden Box}@UUID[Actor.Q0fDu09hyixDsjWY]{Hollow Space} <br />\n  虽然其中一间储藏室没有任何有价值的东西，但其余各间都含有有用的宝藏。PC在<strong>A7b</strong><strong>搜寻</strong>10分钟，会找到一个木盒，里面装有六颗<em>提神丹</em>；PC对<strong>A7c</strong>区域进行10分钟的<strong>搜寻</strong>，并在一次 @Check[perception|dc:28|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] 检定中成功，则会发现一面<em>漆面腰鼓</em>——它从一组架子后方掉落，通过地板上的洞落入一处中空空间。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A7. Storage Rooms\">A7. Storage Rooms</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Most of the contents of these storage rooms appear to have crumbled and decayed into ruin. Crates have broken open as wooden slats decayed, spilling moldering contents over the floor, and empty barrels are surrounded by old stains caused by the leakage of their contents over the years.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.dC9sXQ2srOQ4P2JD]{Wooden Box}@UUID[Actor.Q0fDu09hyixDsjWY]{Hollow Space} <br />\n  While one of these storage rooms has nothing of value, the others each contain useful treasures. A PC Searching area <strong>A7b</strong> for 10 minutes turns up a wooden box containing six <em>energizing pills</em>; a PC who conducts a 10-minute Search of area <strong>A7c</strong>, and who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:28|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check, reveals a <em>lacquered waist drum</em> that fell behind a set of shelves into a hollow space through a hole in the floor.\n</p>"
            },
            "Dining Area": {
              "name": "用餐区 Dining Area",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A6. Dining Area\">A6. 用餐区</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>霉斑与水渍沿着厨房的墙壁滴落，形成一道道又长又鼓胀的污痕，将灰泥装饰糟蹋得不成样子。主房间里有一处腐朽的用餐座位区；而在北侧的侧室里，安放着一对古老的炉灶。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong>@UUID[Actor.4CgTadr60rPa1Nzo]{High Shelf} <br />\n  区域 <strong>A6a</strong> 里没什么值得注意的东西，但厨房（区域 <strong>A6b</strong>）里有一处高架，上面存放着几瓶珍贵的米酒与烈酒。总共有12瓶：其中10瓶每瓶价值50 gp；第11瓶装着一剂<em>登龙醇</em>，第12瓶装着一剂<em>复仇恶魔之泪</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A6. Dining Area\">A6. Dining Area</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Mildew and water stains drip down the kitchen’s walls in long, swelling streaks that ruin the plasterwork. The main room features a moldering seating area for eating, while to the north, a pair of ancient stoves rest in a side room.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong>@UUID[Actor.4CgTadr60rPa1Nzo]{High Shelf} <br />\n  Area <strong>A6a</strong> has little of interest within it, but the kitchen (area <strong>A6b</strong>) includes a high shelf on which several valuable bottles of rice wine and liquor were stored. There are a dozen bottles in all: 10 of them are worth 50 gp each, while the eleventh bottle contains a dose of <em>ascendant dragon spirit</em> and the twelfth contains a dose of <em>vengeful demon’s tears</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Guest Quarters": {
              "name": "客房 Guest Quarters",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A5. 客房</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 10</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这几间客房套间的装潢都呈现出相似的凌乱状态；以下可供三间房间共用的朗读文本，但请依各房间大小不同酌情调整描述（并在<strong>A5b</strong>与<strong>A5c</strong>区域省略最后一句，因为那两处没有尸体）。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间曾经雅致的卧室过去拥有旅途贵族所期望的一切舒适，如今家具却已破败不堪。空气中萦绕着霉腐的臭味，一对身着腐烂祭服的骸骨遗骸瘫卧在破毁的床铺上。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>A5b</strong>与<strong>A5c</strong>在贺总督那场失败的仪式发生时是空的，但最大的套间（<strong>A5a</strong>区域）当时住着一对圣职修行者，他们曾在天京著名的森航寺修学——这对搭档正是总督为协助他完善仪式而召来的。两名祭司知道贺总督打算不顾他们对“仪式尚未完全准备好”的担忧而执意推进，但没料到他会在没有他们在场的情况下贸然动手。当他试图强化谭杉树却失败时，他们便死在了这间房里。</p>\n<p>床上的骷髅是两名祭司的肉身遗骸；一名PC若研究这些遗骸，并在一次@Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]宗教检定中成功以进行回忆知识，便能认出那些长袍是天京森航寺祭司的装束；若取得大成功或大失败中的大成功，他们还会注意到这些特定的长袍属于专精仪式魔法的祭司。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/dread-wraith.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">客房</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.pCwUhO8XJvDxc2PK]{战缚灵（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>两名祭司的魂魄因腐化而变得可怖——既因为他们死在贺总督仪式失败地点附近，也因为他们自身的悔恨。他们如今以满怀憎恨的不死继续徘徊，外表如同自身的幽魂版本，只是他们的长袍总像被撕裂般化作成群的红蝴蝶四散飘离，而这些蝴蝶又会在飘远时化为烟雾。两名战缚灵潜伏在尸体下方的床内，任何人一靠近他们的遗骸便立刻升起，并以潜行掷骰作为先攻。他们会战斗到被摧毁为止，并在整座庄园中追击敌人。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.j2KvU1W67INlQAFX]{大型套间} <br />\n  一名PC若花费10分钟对<strong>A5a</strong>区域进行一次搜寻，会在窗下的黄铜香座里发现几截部分烧焦的天京香锥残根；此外，其中一具骷髅的拳头里还紧攥着一枚布满裂纹的水晶。一名PC若在对该水晶进行辨识魔法的DC 30检定中成功（(@Check[arcana|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[nature|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[occultism|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[religion|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic]))，便能辨认出那是一枚被毁坏的<em>天牙水晶</em>——一种用来防护恶魔与不死的魔法物品；这枚水晶被某种远超其庇护能力的强大力量所摧毁，如今仅仅是一件价值5 gp的好奇物。另一具骷髅的骨颈上仍戴着一条<em>月银项链</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A5. Guest Quarters</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This suite of guest quarters all feature decor in a similar state of disarray; you can use the following read-aloud text for all three, but adjust each description as needed to account for the differing size of each chamber (and omitting the final sentence for areas <strong>A5b</strong> and <strong>A5c</strong>, which lack bodies).</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This once-elegant bedroom used to feature all the comforts a traveling aristocrat expected, but now, the furniture is in disrepair. A musty stink lingers in the air, and a pair of skeletal remains clad in rotting vestments lie sprawled on the ruined beds.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Areas <strong>A5b</strong> and <strong>A5c</strong> were vacant at the time of Governor Heh’s botched ritual, but the largest suite (area <strong>A5a</strong>) was occupied at the time by a pair of holy practitioners who studied at the renowned Senhang Monastery of Tianjing—a duo the governor had called upon for aid in the development of his ritual. The two priests knew Governor Heh was preparing to go ahead with the ritual despite their concern it wasn’t quite ready to be performed, but they didn’t expect him to forge ahead without them. They perished in this chamber when his attempt to bolster the Tan Sugi tree failed.</p>\n<p>The skeletons on the beds are the priests’ physical remains; a PC who studies them and succeeds at a @Check[religion|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge recognizes the robes as those worn by priests of the Senhang Monastery of Tianjing, and with a critical success, they also note these particular robes were worn by priests who specialized in ritual magic.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/dread-wraith.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Guest Quarters</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.pCwUhO8XJvDxc2PK]{War Wraiths (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The spirits of the two priests grew corrupted and horrific, both as a result of their deaths so close to where Governor Heh failed his ritual and their own regrets. They now continue on as hateful undead, appearing as ghostly versions of themselves save that their robes constantly appear to drift apart in flocks of red butterflies that, in turn, drift away into smoke. These two war wraiths lurk inside the beds below their bodies before rising up, rolling Stealth for initiative as soon as anyone approaches their remains. They fight until destroyed and pursue foes throughout the manor.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.j2KvU1W67INlQAFX]{Large Suite} <br />\n  A PC who conducts a 10-minute Search of area <strong>A5a</strong> finds stumps of partially burned Tian-Jing incense cones in brass holders beneath the windows, and a single cracked crystal is clutched in the fist of one of the skeletons. A PC who succeeds at a DC 30 check to Identify Magic ((@Check[arcana|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[nature|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[occultism|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[religion|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic])) on the held crystal identifies it as a destroyed <em>skyfang crystal</em>, a magical item used to ward against fiends and undead; this crystal was ruined by a potent force beyond its power to shelter against and is now merely a curiosity worth 5 gp. The other skeleton still wears a <em>moonsilver necklace</em> around its bony neck.\n</p>"
            },
            "Meeting Area": {
              "name": "会面区域 Meeting Area",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A4. 会面区域</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 10</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间宽敞的房间过去曾摆着两张修长而雅致的会议长桌，四周围以舒适的矮椅，侧柜上还能陈列各式各样的茶水与点心服务。如今，这间厅室里的家具已成一片废墟。上方天花板有数个大洞，透出铅灰色的天空。南墙上有一把不起眼的樵夫斧，斧刃为冷铁，挂在一处部分坍塌的展示架上。</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">会面区域</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bcZbAps8p1eKvzAI]{Weakened Floor}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>天花板并不是这间房间里唯一严重失修的部分——地板也即将塌陷；其下方有一大片危险的霉菌与真菌削弱了地板，多年来似乎一直在啃食支撑结构。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.zL7OeT0yNQSZWQNW]{Partially Collapsed Display} <br />\n  展示的<em>木材领主之斧</em>，是镇长抵达城镇不久后，一家木材财团（早已倒闭）为博取其欢心而赠送的赋礼。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A4. Meeting Area</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This expansive room formerly hosted two long, elegant meeting tables surrounded by comfortable low chairs, with sideboards capable of displaying all manner of tea and snack services. Today, the furniture within this chamber lies in ruins. The ceiling above features several large holes that reveal the leaden sky above. An unassuming woodcutter’s axe with a cold iron blade hangs on the southern wall in a partially collapsed display.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Meeting Area</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.bcZbAps8p1eKvzAI]{Weakened Floor}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> The ceiling isn’t the only part of this room that’s in terrible repair—the floor is about to give way, weakened from below by a large swath of dangerous mold and fungi that seems to have eaten away at the supports for years.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.zL7OeT0yNQSZWQNW]{Partially Collapsed Display} <br />\n  The <em>lumber lord’s axe</em> on display was a gift given to the governor soon after his arrival in town by a lumber consortium (which has long since gone out of business) eager to earn his favor.\n</p>"
            },
            "Servants’ Rooms": {
              "name": "仆役房间 Servants’ Rooms",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A3. 仆役房间</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 10</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这些房间的墙上曾挂着发霉的符箓，但如今只剩在墙上深深爪痕间飘动的破布条。双层床、五斗柜、椅子以及其他家具在地板上堆成一堆堆正在崩碎的残骸，与数具人类骷髅的散落骨头纠缠在一起。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这些房间曾住着总督手下那小小的仆役班子，但当他的仪式出了岔子时，睡在这里的四个人都死在了床上。本房间里的骨头就是他们的遗骸。</p>\n<p>仔细检查那些破损的符箓会发现，它们是被一只巨大带爪的手挥击后从柱子上扯下的，爪击在下方木头上留下了刮凿的沟痕；其中一处，一枚外形独特的爪子还卡在木头里，爪上还黏着一点皮革般的肉。PC若检查这些沟痕与爪子，并以一次成功的 @Check[religion|dc:29|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 宗教检定来进行回忆知识，便能认出这枚利爪属于一只恪尸魔灵堕魔——该恪尸魔如今栖身于主套房（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a8primarysui00]{A8}）。</p>\n<p><strong>A3a</strong>区域是一间供仆役使用的小休息室，没有任何值得注意的东西。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-hungryghost.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">仆役房间</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.6v7IJY9GbiJoPI0F]{精英饿鬼（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-hungryghost.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hungry Ghost\" alt=\"blood red skeletal ghost\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-hungryghost.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>仆役们死去时，他们的灵魂被困在和善保的思维空间里；然而，直到宅邸以这种状态回到生者世界之后，那些被困住的灵魂在经历了一个多世纪的徘徊后，才显现为不死。如今这四者以饿鬼的形态存在，并从自己的骸骨中起身，化作闪烁的幽红色骷髅，眼窝里亮着炫目的红光。这些幽灵会迅速攻击任何闯入其巢穴的人。他们会在宅邸内无情地追击敌人，但不会追出宅邸；若被摧毁，这些饿鬼将会复苏，除非宅邸被净化（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri]{第12章}）。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.6jU3rDGlOHzhJ1l3]{双层床床柱} @UUID[Actor.pRUZKDHxy8QgSawf]{地板} <br />\n  尽管这间房墙上的符箓早已尽数毁坏，但在<strong>A3b</strong>区域的一根双层床床柱上仍挂着三条<em>魌头君流苏</em>；而在东侧，<strong>A3c</strong>区域外那间盥洗室的地板上，躺着一根<em>暮木蝙蝠息手杖</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A3. Servants’ Rooms</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Moldering fulus once hung from the walls in these rooms, but now, only fluttering tatters remain amid deep claw marks in the walls. Bunk beds, dressers, chairs, and other furnishings lie in crumbling heaps on the floor, tangled amid the scattered bones of several human skeletons.</p>\n</div>\n<p>These chambers once housed the governor’s small staff of servants, but when his ritual went bad, the four people who slept here perished in their beds. The bones in this room are their remains.</p>\n<p>Close inspection of the ruined fulus shows that they were torn off the posts by swipes of a large, clawed hand that left gouges in the wood beneath, and in one spot, a distinctive-looking claw with a bit of leathery flesh still attached remains lodged in the wood. A PC who examines the gouges and claw can identify the talon as that of an akashti nindoru with a successful @Check[religion|dc:29|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge—the akashti in question now dwells in the primary suite (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a8primarysui00]{A8}).</p>\n<p>Area <strong>A3a</strong> is a small lounge for the servants that contains nothing of interest.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-hungryghost.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Servant's QUarters</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.6v7IJY9GbiJoPI0F]{Elite Hungry Ghosts (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-hungryghost.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hungry Ghost\" alt=\"blood red skeletal ghost\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-hungryghost.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When the servants perished, their souls became trapped in Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape, yet it isn’t until the manor returns to the living world in this state that those trapped souls, after spending over a century in limbo, manifest as undead. The four exist now as hungry ghosts, and they rise up from their bones in the form of shimmering, ghostly red skeletons with dazzling red lights in their eye sockets. The ghosts quickly attack anyone who intrudes upon their lair. They’ll pursue foes relentlessly through the manor, but not beyond it; if destroyed, these hungry ghosts rejuvenate unless the manor is cleansed (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri]{Chapter 12}).</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.6jU3rDGlOHzhJ1l3]{Bunk Bed Post} @UUID[Actor.pRUZKDHxy8QgSawf]{Floor} <br />\n  While all of the fulus on the walls of this room have long since been destroyed, a trio of <em>Taljjae tassels</em> still hang from one of the bunk bed posts in area <strong>A3b</strong>, while to the east, a <em>duskwood batsbreath cane</em> lies on the floor of the restroom off of area <strong>A3c</strong>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Courtyard": {
              "name": "庭院 Courtyard",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">A2. 庭院</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低10</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这座曾经优雅的庭院过去有着闪耀的水池、假山庭园喷泉与精心布置的植被，但如今已腐败成一片泥泞、杂草丛生的烂摊子。真菌与霉菌在大片残破的叶丛间滋生，池水被藻类黏稠到如布丁一般，从屋顶垂下的一片片湿润藤蔓遮蔽了通往周围建筑的所有出口。就连头顶的天空似乎也病恹恹地灰暗，厚重阴云密布，深沉得更像冬日而非春天。</p>\n</div>\n<p>对PC而言，这座庭院应该会有些模糊的熟悉感，因为他们在第8章曾造访过它更为洁净的版本。如今，这地方看起来像是被丢着任其腐烂衰败了几十年。天空的异样景象是宅邸诡异超自然影响的一部分——若有能飞行的PC移动到宅邸屋檐线之上，且高度超过20尺，天空便会恢复为柳岸镇真实的春季天气。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/drakauthix.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">庭院</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.jX2XimM5NU4AAHIK]{苦迦菩提的德拉卡乌西克斯（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>苦迦菩提的影响将庭院里两堆格外巨大的真菌团块转化为危险的怪物——一对形态隐约似水母、漂浮的“马勃”般的德拉卡乌西克斯。与这些巨型真菌怪物中的大多数不同，这两只德拉卡乌西克斯因苦迦菩提的影响而被灌注了残忍的智慧；也因为这份超自然的污染，它们还能施放少量异能内在法术。其中一只盘踞在庭院的西南部，另一只潜伏在东北方。若它们听见有人在区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a1manorentra00]{A1}内活动，就会潜行向该区域靠近，使其30尺长的触须能在任何人从那里进入庭院时立刻发动伏击；这些生物用隐匿来掷先攻，但若入侵者从上方接近，它们就改为用察觉掷骰。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A2. Courtyard</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This formerly elegant courtyard once featured sparkling pools of water, a rock garden fountain, and artfully arranged foliage, but it has since decayed into a swampy, overgrown mess. Fungi and mold grow through much of the dilapidated foliage, the water is thick with algae to the consistency of pudding, and sheets of moist vines hanging down from the roof obscure all exits into the surrounding building. Even the sky above seems sickly and gray, deeply overcast like a day from winter rather than spring.</p>\n</div>\n<p>This courtyard should seem vaguely familiar to the PCs, as they visited a cleaner version of it during Chapter 8. Today, the place looks like it has been left to rot and decay for decades. The strange appearance of the sky is all part of the manor’s eerie supernatural influence—if a flying PC moves above the manor’s roofline beyond a height of 20 feet, the sky reverts to Willowshore’s actual spring weather.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/drakauthix.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Courtyard</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.jX2XimM5NU4AAHIK]{Kugaptee's Drakauthixes (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Kugaptee’s influence has transformed two particularly large mounds of fungal matter in the courtyard into dangerous monsters—a pair of vaguely jellyfish-shaped floating puffball-like drakauthixes. Unlike most of these huge fungal monsters, these two drakauthixes have been imbued with cruel intellects as a result of Kugaptee’s influence and can also cast a few occult innate spells because of this supernatural taint. One of these creatures lies in the southwestern portion of the courtyard, while the other lurks to the northeast. If they hear anyone moving about in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a1manorentra00]{A1}, they’ll Sneak toward the area so that their 30-foot-long tendrils can attack from ambush as soon as anyone enters the courtyard from there; the creatures use Stealth to roll Initiative, but they roll Perception if intruders approach from above.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Manor Entrance": {
              "name": "庄园入口 Manor Entrance",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A1. Manor Entrance\">A1. 庄园入口</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这处破败入口内的温度骤降，足以让呼吸结霜。腐朽的垫子散落在污渍斑斑的木地板上。墙壁上蔓生着一丛丛真菌，以及盘绕的湿藤蔓。北侧屋顶垂下一道厚重的藤蔓帘幕，形成一堵滴水的植被之墙，遮挡了通往庭院的视线。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这座庄园内的地板已经翘曲，踩上去会吱呀作响。任何未试图保持隐蔽的人都会自动制造出足够的噪声，惊动区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a2courtyard000]{A2} 的住户。在此房间内尝试潜行时，若正在潜行的生物走在地板上，该潜行检定承受–4环境减值。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"A1. Manor Entrance\">A1. Manor Entrance</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The temperature drops enough to frost breath within this ruined entrance. Moldering mats lie on the stained wood floor. The walls are overgrown with patches of fungi and coiling moist vines. A thick curtain of vines hangs over the roof to the north, forming a wall of dripping vegetation that blocks the view into the courtyard.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The floor in this manor is warped and creaks when stepped on. Anyone who isn’t trying to be stealthy automatically makes enough noise to alert the occupants of area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a2courtyard000]{A2}. Attempts to Sneak in this room suffer a –4 circumstance penalty if the sneaking creature is walking on the floor.</p>"
            },
            "Approaching the Manor": {
              "name": "接近庄园 Approaching the Manor",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">接近庄园</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 10</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unwelcomingfacade.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Unwelcoming Facade\" alt=\"一个狰狞的邪恶面孔从该结构的建筑上怒目而视\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unwelcomingfacade.webp')\" />\n<p>即使在白天，这座废弃的总督庄园也是个令人心生畏惧的地方。走廊里挥之不去的非自然寒意，仿佛几乎要渗入周围的庭院。破烂的挂毯在没有风时也会窃窃私语；历任总督的肖像褪色得只剩令人不安的无面轮廓，而他们的礼服与徽饰却依旧鲜亮清晰；被敲打变形的银镜上尽是奇异的回环污渍，仿佛有人反复把黏稠的墨汁倒在镜面之上，墨迹在重叠的流淌中干涸成形。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">接近庄园</span> <span class=\"keepme\">琐碎 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.BqycsXlbPuLt2buN]{不受欢迎的立面}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>PC可以用他们希望的任何方式接近庄园。将通行证显眼地出示并走向正门是最安全的做法。外墙依旧坚固，无法直接通行，但PC可以在成功通过一次@Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]检定后攀爬上去。具有飞行的PC可以从上方进入庄园，抵达区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a2courtyard000]{A2}；或者他们也可以在成功通过一次@Check[acrobatics|dc:25|traits:exploration,move,action:squeeze|name:Squeeze]检定后，从屋顶的破洞挤入，进入区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a3servantsro00]{A3}–@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a7storageroo00]{A7}。PC可以直接进入通往区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a4meetingare00]{A4}的洞口，而完全不需要进行挤入。没有任何洞口能让人获得进入区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a8primarysui00]{A8}的许可。</p>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>无论PC选择哪条路线，环绕庄园的灵光都会试图将他们排斥在外。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Approaching the Manor</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 10</span>\n</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unwelcomingfacade.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Unwelcoming Facade\" alt=\"a leering, evil face glaring from the structure's architecture\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unwelcomingfacade.webp')\" />\n<p>Even by daylight, the abandoned governor’s manor is a foreboding place. The unnatural chill that lingers in the hallways seems almost to seep into the surrounding grounds. Tattered tapestries whisper when no wind is present, portraits of past governors are faded to an eerie facelessness while their regalia remains bright and crisp, and beaten silver mirrors are all tarnished with odd, looping patterns, as if viscous ink had been poured repeatedly over their faces and had dried in overlapping spills.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Approaching the Manor</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 10</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.BqycsXlbPuLt2buN]{Unwelcoming Facade}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The PCs can approach the manor however they wish. Approaching the front door with their pass in view is the safest. While the external walls remain solid and offer no passage, a PC can Climb them with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check. PCs with flight can enter the manor from above into area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a2courtyard000]{A2}, or they can Squeeze through holes in the roof with a successful @Check[acrobatics|dc:25|traits:exploration,move,action:squeeze|name:Squeeze] check to enter areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a3servantsro00]{A3}–@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a7storageroo00]{A7}. PCs can enter the holes leading into area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a4meetingare00]{A4} without needing to Squeeze at all. No holes allow access into area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a8primarysui00]{A8}.</p>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> Regardless of the route the PCs take, the aura that surrounds the manor seeks to repel them.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Manor Features": {
              "name": "庄园特性 Manor Features",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Manor Features\">庄园特征</h2>\n<p>PC们在前一幕中曾造访过这位总督庄园完好无损的版本，因此他们可能已经熟悉它的部分或全部建筑布局。这座建筑最初由精美的材料建成，如今却因时代与疏于维护而显得破败不堪。外墙、支撑梁与地板皆以优质木材打造，外部以瓦片与彩绘点缀，内部则用精工细作的银饰作装饰。内墙曾以格子纸糊成，但几乎已被害兽与天气彻底毁坏，只剩下纤细而空荡的框架。幸存的装饰强烈倾向于帝国龙华晚期流行的主题与设计：巨龙、凤凰，以及对过往皇帝与其功业的神话式引用。</p>\n<p>室内没有照明。白天时，足够的自然光会从窗户与屋顶的缺口倾泻而入，使整座宅邸可视为昏暗照明。夜间则为黑暗。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Manor Features\">Manor Features</h2>\n<p>The PCs visited an intact version of the governor’s manor during the previous act, so they might already be familiar with some or all of its architectural layout. Originally built from exquisite materials, the building now appears to be badly damaged by time and neglect. Outer walls, support beams, and floors are all crafted of fine wood, with tile and painted accents on the exterior, and interior accents in ornately worked silver. Interior walls were once made of latticed paper, but they’ve almost entirely been destroyed by vermin and weather, leaving only the delicate, empty frames. The surviving decor leans heavily on themes and designs popular in late Imperial Lung Wa: dragons, phoenixes, and mythical references to past emperors and their exploits.</p>\n<p>The interior is unlit. During daylight hours, enough natural light streams in through the windows and gaps in the roofs that the mansion can be considered dimly lit. At night, it’s dark.</p>"
            },
            "The Governor’s Manor": {
              "name": "总督庄园 The Governor’s Manor",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Governor’s Manor\">总督府邸</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>洗劫府邸</h1>\n  <p>总督府邸里有相当数量的宝藏等待发现，但某些PC可能会对将其据为己有心存顾虑，认为这些物品属于城镇的总督，而在他缺席的情况下，应当归还柳岸镇。若有人就此询问，镇老会坚决反对这种想法，并指出PC们为拯救柳岸镇做了许多，却从未得到报偿。镇老完全允许PC保留在府邸中找到的任何财富或魔法物品，甚至鼓励PC搜遍各个房间，寻找资源与装备。镇老还指出，PC们在其中可能发现的东西，其价值很可能超过柳岸镇村民能作为他们服务奖励所给予的一切。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>无论PC是自己注意到，还是由某位NPC告知这项进展，他们都无法长久忽视总督和善保的宅邸回到柳岸镇镇区东北侧原址这件事——也无法忽视那种“并不受欢迎”的怪异感觉：任何靠近的人都会感到一股彻骨寒意，直透灵魂。不管柳岸镇其余地方的状况如何，总督府邸归来时已成废墟：墙壁上长满真菌与藤蔓，屋顶也向下塌陷。镇上无人敢过于靠近，因为当地人理所当然地畏惧府邸离奇归来，以及它那令人不安的外观。若PC不主动去调查府邸，镇老必定会在他们“复生”归来的第一天入夜前，请求他们这么做。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenote-manor\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" data-tooltip=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">氛围</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">\n      @UUID[Macro.DCAnEoCwWwKmS5hq]{Toggle Governor's Manor}\n    </span>\n  </div>\n  <p>在@UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{柳岸镇}场景中显示总督府邸。</p>\n</section>\n<p>事实上，总督府邸存在两个版本。当前出现在柳岸镇的那一座是一处崩塌的废墟，栖居着受苦迦菩提意志牵引而来的怪物，镇民也都避而远之。若让如今居住其中的生物有足够时间适应并从废墟中现身，这个版本的府邸随着时间推移可能会对城镇造成轻微威胁。第二个版本目前仍无法进入，PC此时多半甚至不会猜到它的存在，直到它被<em>尖牙与钥匙</em>解锁（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14thefangandke00]{第12章}）。</p>\n<p>即便并不知道宅邸出现的同时也显现了怪物，柳岸镇的镇民仍认为：在没有适当授权的情况下闯入此地是违法的——不仅在已覆灭的龙华法律之下如此，在天庭的律法之下亦然。</p>\n<p>由于总督并未与柳岸镇其他人一同归来，习俗要求想要进入者应从具有足够级别的政府机构取得一份授权通行证。若镇老主动接触PC，镇老会将该通行证作为请求他们调查该建筑的一部分交给他们；但若PC决定自行调查，他们在一次成功的@Check[society|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定以进行回忆知识后，便会想起这个关键步骤。若未获发此通行证，灌注于废墟府邸中的残留力量会对PC稍微更为强势，使与府邸相关的所有危害的潜行、解除与豁免检定DC提高2。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Governor’s Manor\">The Governor’s Manor</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Looting the Manor</h1>\n  <p>A fair amount of treasure awaits discovery in the governor’s manor, but some PCs might have qualms about claiming it for themselves, reasoning that these items belong to the town’s governor and, in his absence, should revert to Willowshore. The town elder has none of this if they’re asked, noting that the PCs have done much to save Willowshore without recompense. They give their full blessing for the PCs to keep any wealth or magic items found in the manor, even going so far as to encourage the PCs to scour its rooms for resources and gear. The town elder also notes that what the PCs might discover within is likely of greater value than anything the villagers of Willowshore can give them as rewards for their service.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Whether the PCs take note of it on their own or they’re informed of the development by an NPC, they can’t long ignore the return of Governor Heh Shan-Bao’s mansion to its spot just northeast of downtown Willowshore—nor the strange sensations of being unwelcome that chill the soul of anyone who approaches it. Regardless of the state of the rest of Willowshore, the governor’s manor returns in ruin, its walls overgrown with fungi and vines and its roof sagging. No one in town dares draw too close to it, as the locals rightfully fear the manor’s eerie return and unsettling appearance. If the PCs don’t take it upon themselves to investigate the manor, the town elder surely requests they do so before their first day back alive has reached twilight.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenote-manor\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" data-tooltip=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Ambience</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">\n      @UUID[Macro.DCAnEoCwWwKmS5hq]{Toggle Governor's Manor}\n    </span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Shows the Governor's Manor on the @UUID[Scene.KjhqnhLwdTc2JUZV]{Willowshore} Scene.</p>\n</section>\n<p>In fact, there are two versions of the governor’s manor. The one that currently exists in Willowshore is a crumbling ruin, inhabited by monsters drawn from Kugaptee’s will and avoided by the townspeople. This version of the manor might present a minor danger to the town over time if the creatures that now dwell inside it are afforded enough time to adjust and emerge from the ruins. The second version remains inaccessible and likely even unguessed at by the PCs at this time until it’s unlocked by the <em>Fang and Key</em> (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14thefangandke00]{Chapter 12}).</p>\n<p>Even without knowing that monsters have manifested along with the mansion, Willowshore’s townsfolk believe it’s illegal to break into the place without a proper mandate, not only under the law of fallen Lung Wa, but under that of the Heavenly Court.</p>\n<p>Since the governor didn’t return with the rest of Willowshore, custom demands that those who wish to enter should obtain an authorization pass from a government entity of sufficient rank. If the town elder approaches the PC, the elder grants this pass to them as part of the request to investigate the building, but if the PCs decide to investigate on their own, they recall this important step with a successful @Check[society|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge. Without being issued this pass, the lingering power infusing the ruined manor becomes slightly more potent against the PCs, increasing the Stealth, Disable, and saving throw DCs of all hazards associated with the manor by 2.</p>"
            },
            "Silver Collars": {
              "name": "银颈圈 Silver Collars",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Silver Collars\">银项圈</h3>\n<p>被神门的络新妇选为盟友、仆从甚至宠物的人，会被授予佩戴特殊银项圈的权利。PC们可能在上一幕中获得了一些项圈——络新妇的银项圈是一件非魔法的宝藏，价值50 gp。若PC们在与任美璃的第一次遭遇中没有得知这些项圈，那么当他们与任何来自现代神门的人交谈时（例如他们在唐入与之交谈的任何人），项圈就应该是他们最早得知的事情之一。这些项圈让人能在神门自由旅行，授予读写许可，并提供与神门之外的人进行贸易的合法权利。</p>\n<p>传统上，人们应当将银项圈明显地戴在身上，因为你永远不知道自己是在与络新妇说话，还是在与其代理人交谈；但如果你在神门边境之外旅行、阅读、书写或与人贸易时被络新妇逮到，只要在被其当面对质时迅速亮出你随身携带的项圈，通常就足以避免其怒火。</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>返回唐入</h1>\n  <p>唐入村规模不大，但对柳岸镇而言承担着至关重要的作用：它将柳岸镇连接到幽海海岸沿线的贸易路线。在唐入桥修复之前，柳岸镇的食物与补给仍将十分匮乏，而小镇也无法开始全面重新融入现代神门。</p>\n  <p>当神藏最后一次造访柳岸镇之后，唐入的贸易联系人将成为PC们获取新物品的默认途径；虽然该村目前只是一个等级3的聚居地，但随着柳岸镇重回生者之列，它将随时间而发展壮大。PC们可以在唐入订购物品，最高可达等级11，但这些订购的物品需要一周时间，才能从其他地点（例如伺城）运送到此。</p>\n  <p>在上一章中，伐木领主孙海掌管唐入，但本幕假定他已被击败。若你的游戏并非如此，请参阅边栏 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog01frontm.JournalEntryPage.12tobloombelow00#mago-kais-fate]{孙海的命运}。</p>\n</aside>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Silver Collars\">Silver Collars</h3>\n<p>Those who the Shenmen jorogumo choose as allies, minions, or even pets are granted the right to wear special silver collars. The PCs might have earned some collars in the previous act—a jorogumo’s silver collar is a non-magical treasure worth 50 gp. If the PCs didn’t learn about the collars during their first encounter with Ren Mei Li, then the collars should be one of the earliest things they learn about when speaking with anyone from modern Shenmen, such as anyone they talk to at Karahai. These collars allow one to travel freely in Shenmen, grant permission to read and write, and provide the legal right to engage in trade with those outside of Shenmen.</p>\n<p>Traditionally, one is expected to visibly wear a silver collar since you never know if you’re talking to a jorogumo or one of their agents, but quickly displaying a collar carried on your person when confronted by a jorogumo is usually enough to avoid their wrath if you get caught traveling, reading, writing, or trading with those beyond Shenmen’s borders.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>Returning to Karahai</h1>\n  <p>The village of Karahai is small, but it serves a vitally important role to Willowshore: it connects Willowshore to trade routes all along the coast of the Sea of Ghosts. Until Karahai Bridge is repaired, Willowshore’s food and supplies will remain sparse, and the town won’t be able to begin to fully reintegrate into modern Shenmen.</p>\n  <p>Once Shinzo pays his last visit to Willowshore, trade contacts at Karahai become the default assumption for the PCs to acquire new items; while the village is only a level 3 settlement now, it will grow over time now that Willowshore is back among the living. The PCs can place orders for items of up to level 11 at Karahai, but it takes a week for these requested items to be shipped in from other locations, such as the city of Sze.</p>\n  <p>In the previous chapter, lumber lord Mago Kai ran Karahai, but this act assumes he was defeated. See the sidebar @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog01frontm.JournalEntryPage.12tobloombelow00#mago-kais-fate]{Mago Kai's Fate} if this isn’t the case in your game.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Beyond Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇之外 Beyond Willowshore",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Beyond Willowshore\">柳岸镇之外</h3>\n<p>本幕标志着PC们首次能够越过边界进行旅行——当他们被困在柳岸镇思维空间时，那些边界曾定义了他们的整个世界。起初，PC们所掌握的柳岸腹地之外的世界信息，已经过时一百多年。了解现代世界并为柳岸镇在其中争取立足之地的过程，见于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri]{第12章}；但在此之前，你可以与PC们分享以下关于柳岸腹地之外情况的信息。这些信息也收录于《肆季鬼志：玩家指南》，但不含括号中的更新内容；括号中的内容代表关于每条通往柳岸镇地区之外道路所延伸之处的更现代的信息。</p>\n<p><strong>西北小路：</strong>这条古老且杂草丛生的小路通向森林深处；大多数人认为它通往一座早已废弃的神龛，但如今几乎没人走这条偏僻的路。（这条小路确实通往一座神龛——低语网神龛，PC们会在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event5spiced00]{第12章}造访此地。）</p>\n<p><strong>中央北路：</strong>这条部分被侵蚀的道路蜿蜒穿过数片荒芜的田地，田地间散落着一座多年前被遗弃村庄的废墟，最终在一片大型湿地前止步；那里因生长着橙色的夜间开花植物，其花朵在月光下闪耀，被称为月沼。（如今，这些废墟已完全被植被吞没——除非PC们在第一幕收复了农田；而月沼由于地处偏远，已基本被唐入当地人遗忘。PC们会在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event2fieryf00]{第12章}造访月沼。）</p>\n<p><strong>东北东路：</strong>这条道路将柳岸镇与幽魂之森各处散落的众多小村与小镇连接起来，并最终通向罗网山脉。沿路最近的聚居地是狐谷，但也要三天的行程，而且规模比柳岸镇还小。（PC们可能会在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14walkingthego00]{第12章}沿此路前往罗网山脉；在现代时代，这条路上的聚居地都已变成被遗弃的鬼城。）</p>\n<p><strong>东北路：</strong>这条路通往一处新近建立的农庄，位于俯瞰幽海的峭壁上；那里是一座牛场，由一名从紫城流亡而出的政客所有，此人以冷酷无情而臭名昭著。（该农庄已荒废数十年，政客也早已不知所踪；通往那里的道路杂草丛生，而农庄现已成为丝蜂盗匪的藏身处——见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13thesilkwaspc00]{丝蜂营地}。）</p>\n<p><strong>东路：</strong>这条路通往唐入的贸易要塞，是柳岸镇与神门其他地区最重要的经济纽带。（这条路线包含一座被毁的桥，PC们必须修复它以帮助柳岸镇重新振作；见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13rebuildingth00]{重建桥梁}。）</p>\n<p><strong>南路：</strong>通往区域之外的南路是一条漫长的陆上路线，最终会接入更完善的道路网络，并连接到更南方、数日路程之外人口更多的村镇；不过柳岸镇大多数人称其为“苹果之路”，因为这条路通向一片野苹果树林，每到秋季都会结出格外美味的果实。（如今，这条路年久失修且杂草丛生；PC们会在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event3fallss00]{第12章}造访苹果林。）</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Beyond Willowshore\">Beyond Willowshore</h3>\n<p>This act marks the first time the PCs will be able to travel beyond the borders that once defined their world when they were trapped in the Willowshore mindscape. Initially, the information the PCs have about the world beyond the Willowshore hinterlands is just over a century outdated. The process of learning more about the modern world and securing Willowshore’s place in it is covered in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri]{Chapter 12}, but in the meantime, you can share the following information with the PCs about what lies beyond the Willowshore hinterlands. This information is also provided in the <em>Season of Ghosts Player’s Guide</em>, but without the updates in parentheses, which indicate more modern information about what lies down each of the roads leading out of the Willowshore region.</p>\n<p><strong>Northwest Trail:</strong> This old overgrown trail leads off into the forest; most folks believe it leads to a long-abandoned shrine, but few travel this remote path today. (This trail does indeed lead to a shrine—the Whisperweb Shrine, which the PCs visit in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event5spiced00]{Chapter 12}.)</p>\n<p><strong>Central Northern Road:</strong> This partially eroded road winds through several fields that have gone fallow amid the ruins of a village that was abandoned many years ago, then eventually comes to an end at a large wetland known as Moon Marsh for the way the orange, night-blooming flowers that grow there shine under the moonlight. (Today, these ruins are completely overgrown unless the PCs reclaimed the farmland during the first act, and Moon Marsh has largely been forgotten by Karahai’s locals due to its remote location. The PCs visit Moon Marsh in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event2fieryf00]{Chapter 12}.)</p>\n<p><strong>Eastern Northern Road:</strong> This road connects Willowshore with numerous small villages and towns scattered throughout Specterwood and eventually finds its way to the Gossamer Mountains. The next-closest settlement down this road is Foxhollow, but it’s three days’ travel away and even smaller than Willowshore. (The PCs might use this road to make a journey to the Gossamer Mountains in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14walkingthego00]{Chapter 12}; the settlements along this road have all become abandoned ghost towns in the modern era.)</p>\n<p><strong>Northeastern Road:</strong> This road leads to a recently established farmstead on a bluff overlooking the Sea of Ghosts, a cattle ranch owned by a notoriously ruthless expatriate politician from the city of Sze. (The farmstead has been abandoned for decades and the politician is long gone; the road leading there is overgrown, while the farmstead now serves as the hideout for the Silkwasp Bandits—see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13thesilkwaspc00]{The Silkwasp Camp}.)</p>\n<p><strong>Eastern Road:</strong> This road leads to the trade fortress of Karahai and represents Willowshore’s major economic link to the rest of Shenmen. (The route includes a destroyed bridge the PCs must repair to help Willowshore get back on its feet; see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13rebuildingth00]{Rebuilding the Bridge}.)</p>\n<p><strong>Southern Road:</strong> The southern road out of the region is a long overland route that eventually connects to better maintained roads and more populous villages and towns several days’ travel to the south, but most in Willowshore call it the “Apple Road,” as it leads to a grove of wild apple trees that produce particularly delicious fruit every fall. (Today, this road is in ill repair and overgrown; the PCs visit the apple grove during @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event3fallss00]{Chapter 12}.)</p>"
            },
            "The Warding Bell": {
              "name": "守护铃 The Warding Bell",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Warding Bell\">守护钟</h3>\n<p>在“第三幕：欲泣无息”中，PC们必须解除一口强大的守护钟，它被安装在唐入的堡垒内。如果他们设法避免摧毁这口守护钟，那么在本幕中他们首次造访唐入时，村民会将这口钟作为赠礼送给PC们，以感谢他们赶走了孙海，并让大家得以夺回家园。如果PC们将守护钟安置在柳岸镇的任意一座神龛内，他们与城镇之间的灵性连结会变得更为强大，并且在与该神龛神祇的神圣技能相关的所有技能检定中获得+2物品加值。通过将守护钟放置在与他们用来祝福长明灯的神龛不同的另一座神龛中，PC们可以将该物品加值应用于两种不同的技能。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Warding Bell\">The Warding Bell</h3>\n<p>In “Act 3: No Breath to Cry,” the PCs had to disable a powerful warding bell that had been installed in the fortress of Karahai. If they managed to avoid destroying the warding bell, then upon their first visit to Karahai in this act, the villagers gift the bell to the PCs in thanks for driving out Mago Kai and allowing them to reclaim their homes. If the PCs install the warding bell at any shrine in Willowshore, their spiritual connection to the town grows even stronger, and they gain a +2 item bonus to all skill checks associated with the divine skill of that shrine’s deity. By placing the warding bell at a different shrine than the one they use to bless the Eternal Lantern, the PCs can gain this item bonus to two different skills.</p>"
            },
            "The Eternal Lantern": {
              "name": "长明灯 The Eternal Lantern",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Eternal Lantern\">长明灯</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Eternal Lantern\" alt=\"a stone lantern\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp')\" />\n<p>随着柳岸镇回归生者世界，PC们与该聚居地的魂魄联系变得更为强烈。在“第一幕：不曾到来的夏日”中，PC们重新点燃了小镇的<em>长明灯</em>——这是一件固定不动的奇物，据说其光芒能使邪恶魂魄不敢靠近。一旦PC们将柳岸镇带回生者世界，他们通过祈唤<em>长明灯</em>而获得的技能检定的物品加值提升至+2。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Eternal Lantern\">The Eternal Lantern</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Eternal Lantern\" alt=\"a stone lantern\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp')\" />\n<p>With Willowshore’s return to the living world, the PCs’ spiritual connection to the settlement grows stronger. In “Act 1: The Summer That Never Was,” the PCs relit the town’s <em>Eternal Lantern</em>, a stationary artifact whose light reputedly keeps evil spirits at bay. Once the PCs bring Willowshore into the living world, the item bonus to skill checks they gained from invoking the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> increase to +2.</p>"
            },
            "Waking in Willowshore": {
              "name": "在柳岸镇醒来 Waking in Willowshore",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Waking in Willowshore\">在柳岸镇醒来</h2>\n<p>当PC们在仪式后醒来时，他们会发觉自己身处晨步桥南端、<em>长明灯</em>附近。朗读或转述以下内容，然后花些时间描述柳岸镇的现状——其状况由其准备点数决定。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>世界现在给人的感觉微妙却无可置疑地不同了，仿佛一切都变得更细密、更有质感。阳光里闪烁着尘埃微粒，清风振翼般捎来鲜活的气息，甚至连脚下的地面都似乎变得更加坚实。这不再是思维空间。这是真实的、鲜活的现实。</p>\n</div>\n<p>给PC们一些时间四下查看，与重要的NPC交谈，并体会他们动作所带来的结果；根据PC们所处的局势，这段时间既可以用来庆祝，也可以用来进行沉重的准备。镇中长老走近PC们，感谢他们让小镇重获生机，或征询他们的建议：是最好彻底放弃这些废墟，还是尽己所能重建家园。</p>\n<p>即便柳岸镇完整无缺地回归，其市民也不会立刻适应这个世界。毕竟一个多世纪已经过去了。那些在柳岸镇境外可能还有朋友或家人的镇民，必须接受自己已比他们活得更久这一事实；而与唐入或其他城镇村落重新建立贸易的任务，也会因另一件事而变得复杂：多数得知柳岸镇归来的消息的人，起初都会恐惧，认为PC们与其他镇民是复仇的幽灵（特征）。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Waking in Willowshore\">Waking in Willowshore</h2>\n<p>When the PCs awaken after the ritual, they do so near the <em>Eternal Lantern</em> on the south end of Dawnstep Bridge. Read or paraphrase the following, then take some time to describe the state of Willowshore, as determined by its Preparation Points.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The world feels subtly but unmistakably different now, as though it has become more finely grained. Motes of dust shimmer in the sunlight, the breeze carries vibrant scents on its wings, and even the ground seems somehow more solid. This is no longer a mindscape. This is true, living reality.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Give the PCs time to look around, speak with NPCs of note, and take in the results of their actions; this time could be used for either celebration or grim preparation, depending on the situation the PCs find themselves in. The town elder approaches the PCs to thank them for restoring the town to life, or to seek their advice on whether it would be best to abandon the ruins entirely or do what can be done to rebuild.</p>\n<p>Even if Willowshore came back fully intact, its citizens won’t instantly acclimate to the world. Over a century has passed, after all. Townsfolk who might have had friends or family beyond Willowshore’s borders must come to terms with the fact that they’ve outlived them, and the task of reestablishing trade with Karahai or other towns and villages will be complicated by the fact that most of those who learn the news of Willowshore’s return will initially fear that the PCs and the other townsfolk are vengeful ghosts.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore In the Spring": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的春日 Willowshore In the Spring",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore In the Spring\">柳岸镇的春天</h2>\n<p>冬天已成过去，PC们可以期待柳岸镇的春季。按传统，这是四季中最令人愉悦的时节，天气温和晴朗，白昼渐长。在这最后一幕中，降雨十分罕见。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Willowshore In the Spring\">Willowshore In the Spring</h2>\n<p>With winter behind them, the PCs can look forward to spring in Willowshore, traditionally the most pleasant of the seasons, when weather is mild and sunny and the days grow long. Rain is rare during this final act.</p>"
            },
            "Determining Willowshore’s Fate": {
              "name": "决定柳岸镇的命运 Determining Willowshore’s Fate",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Determining Willowshore’s Fate\">决定柳岸镇的命运</h2>\n<p>当PC们升级，并可能选择新的族裔或转世专长时，花点时间把此刻柳岸镇剩余的所有食物、希望与安全点数合计起来，以决定柳岸镇的总准备点数。能够复活的镇民人数以及城镇的状态，取决于这个准备点数总额，如下所述。</p>\n<p>若<em>transmigrate</em>仪式为大成功或大失败中的大成功，则将该总额提高12点。</p>\n<p>若PC们成功施展transmigrate时柳岸镇的人口为100或以上，则将他们的总准备点数提高4点。</p>\n<p><strong>0准备点：</strong>只有PC以及本冒险路径中点名的特定NPC会转世。所有其他镇民仍然死亡，他们的灵魂前往来世。柳岸镇仍是一片破败废墟；建筑若不进行大规模修复便无法居住，田地也被森林重新吞没。由于所有可能进行交易的人都已死亡，在镇上无法赚取收入或获得普通物品。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>1到4准备点：</strong>PC、点名的NPC，以及在施展<em>transmigrate</em>\n  仪式时柳岸镇人口的40%回到生者世界。城镇建筑部分恢复，但仍需大量修缮：许多屋顶与墙壁破洞累累，小动物在食品储藏室与地窖里世代筑巢，水井必须清除杂物，田地也被杂草堵塞。来年将异常艰苦，柳岸镇为求生存将面临艰难攀爬。本冒险余下部分中，赚取收入的机会与可购买的货物限制为3级或更低。给予PC 10 XP。\n</p>\n<p><strong>5到12准备点：</strong>PC、点名的NPC，以及柳岸镇剩余人口的80%复活。城镇以尚可的状态归来，尽管仍有一些工作要做；其基础设施似乎被疏于维护了一两个月，因此显出相应的磨损。尽管来年不会轻松，且一些家庭为未能归来的成员哀悼，柳岸镇的人们仍以乐观而坚定的意志面对挑战：毕竟他们经历了难以置信的磨难，如今又回到了生者之中。本冒险余下部分中，赚取收入的机会与可购买的货物限制为5级或更低。给予PC 60 XP。</p>\n<p><strong>13或更多准备点：</strong>柳岸镇的所有人（包括PC们可能在偏远地区遇到的其他人，例如琳的幽灵）都恢复生命。城镇回到PC们在前三幕中所熟悉的同等状态。田地可以立刻播种。人们将自己的生命视作诸神的赋礼，并以乐观与幽默迎接未来。赚取收入与可购买的货物受柳岸镇的实际等级限制（此时为7级）。给予PC 120 XP。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.a4l69xh4WDdkcJUH]{思维空间转移}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Determining Willowshore’s Fate\">Determining Willowshore’s Fate</h2>\n<p>While the PCs are leveling up and potentially choosing new ancestries or Reincarnation feats, take a moment to total up all of the Food, Hope, and Security Points Willowshore has remaining at this time to determine Willowshore’s total Preparation Points. The number of townsfolk who are brought back to life, as well as the condition of the town, depends on this total of Preparation Points, as detailed below.</p>\n<p>If the <em>transmigrate</em> ritual was a critical success, increase this total by 12 points.</p>\n<p>If Willowshore’s population at the time the PCs performed transmigrate successfully was at 100 or higher, increase their total Preparation Points by 4.</p>\n<p><strong>0 Preparation Points:</strong> Only the PCs and the specific NPCs named in this Adventure Path are reincarnated. All other townsfolk remain dead, and their souls move on to the afterlife. Willowshore remains a dilapidated ruin, its buildings uninhabitable without major repair and its fields reclaimed by forest. It isn’t possible to Earn Income or obtain ordinary items in town, as everyone who might be traded with is dead.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>1 to 4 Preparation Points:</strong> The PCs, named NPCs, and 40% of Willowshore’s population at the time the <em>transmigrate</em>\n  ritual is performed return to the living world. The town’s buildings are partially restored but need significant work: many roofs and walls have holes, small animals have made generational homes in pantries and cellars, wells must be cleared of debris, and fields are choked with weeds. The coming year will be grueling, and Willowshore faces an uphill climb to survive. Earn Income opportunities and purchasable goods are limited to level 3 or lower for the rest of the adventure. Grant the PCs 10 XP.\n</p>\n<p><strong>5 to 12 Preparation Points:</strong> The PCs, named NPCs, and 80% of Willowshore’s remaining population are returned to life. The town returns in decent repair, although there’s still some work to be done; its infrastructure appears to have been neglected for a month or two and shows wear accordingly. Though the coming year won’t be easy, and families grieve the loss of members who didn’t return, Willowshore’s people face their challenges with optimistic determination: after all, they’ve endured an incredible ordeal and are back among the living. Earn Income opportunities and purchasable goods are limited to level 5 or lower for the rest of the adventure. Grant the PCs 60 XP.</p>\n<p><strong>13 or more Preparation Points:</strong> All of Willowshore’s people (including others the PCs might have encountered in the hinterlands, such as Rin’s ghost) are restored to life. The town returns in the same condition as the PCs are used to from the previous three acts. Fields can be planted immediately. The people regard their lives as a gift from the gods and greet the future with optimism and humor. Earn Income and purchasable goods are limited by Willowshore’s actual level (level 7 at this point). Grant the PCs 120 XP.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.a4l69xh4WDdkcJUH]{Mindscape Shift}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "Getting Started": {
              "name": "冒险开始 Getting Started",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">冒险开始</h1>\n<p>在第3幕期间，PC们发现了自身存在的全部真相，并在该幕的高潮施行了迁魂仪式，使自己以及整个柳岸镇重返生命。第4幕默认PC们成功完成了该仪式，并在他们施行迁魂仪式的地点——晨步桥南侧、靠近重新点亮的<em>长明灯</em>——于活人的世界醒来。</p>\n<p>在开始本章之前，给玩家时间将他们的PC提升至10级。与大多数升级机会不同，这一次PC们拥有一次独特的机会：他们可以彻底改变自己的族裔，并选择全新的族裔专长，因为他们可能选择在一具全新的身体中以转生术归来。不想利用这一机会的PC，仍然可以回到他们在《<em>鬼季冒险路径</em>》前三幕中所使用的同一具身体里——这通常并非转生者能拥有的选择。选择保留原本身体的PC，即便其外形与之前完全一致，仍可按自身意愿更换族裔专长。</p>\n<p>无论PC们是否选择新的族裔，他们都应当能为1级、5级与9级选择不同的族裔专长。除了能从其当前族裔可用的专长中选择之外，每位PC还可以选择本书冒险工具箱中提供的全新@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20reincarnatio00]{转生术族裔专长}。</p>\n<p>柳岸镇的所有NPC都会转生回PC们在冒险过程中逐渐熟悉并能辨认的那些身体（不过，如果其中某些NPC转生为不同族裔有令人信服的理由，你也可以在你的游戏中如此处理）。</p>\n<p>虽然迁魂仪式能让PC们重返生命，但它对城镇及其其他居民所产生的额外效果，则取决于PC们迄今为止在保护柳岸镇方面做得如何，并取决于上一幕结束时他们还剩下多少准备点数。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Getting Started\">Getting Started</h1>\n<p>During Act 3, the PCs discovered the full truth of their existence and, at that act’s climax, performed a transmigrate ritual to restore themselves and all of Willowshore to life. Act 4 assumes that the PCs performed that ritual successfully, and that they wake in the living world at the site where they performed the transmigrate ritual—the southern side of Dawnstep Bridge near the newly relit <em>Eternal Lantern</em>.</p>\n<p>Before starting this chapter, give the players time to level up their PCs to 10th level. Unlike most opportunities to do so, this time, the PCs have the unique chance to completely change their ancestry and select entirely new ancestry feats, for they may have chosen to reincarnate in an entirely new body. A PC who doesn’t wish to take advantage of this opportunity can always return in the same body they’ve occupied for the previous three acts of the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em>—a choice not normally afforded to those who reincarnate. A PC who elects to keep their original body can still opt to swap out ancestry feats as they wish, even though their physical form remains unchanged from before.</p>\n<p>Regardless of whether the PCs choose a new ancestry, they should all get to select different ancestry feats for 1st, 5th, and 9th level. In addition to being able to choose from feats available to their current ancestry, each PC can opt to select from the new @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog20advent.JournalEntryPage.20reincarnatio00]{Reincarnation Ancestry Feats} presented in this book’s Adventure Toolbox.</p>\n<p>All of Willowshore’s NPCs reincarnate into their own familiar bodies the PCs have come to recognize during the course of the adventure (although if there’s a compelling reason for some of them to reincarnate into a different ancestry, feel free to make it so in your game).</p>\n<p>While the transmigrate ritual allows the PCs to return to life, its additional effects on the town and its other citizens is contingent on how well the PCs have done up to this point in protecting Willowshore, and it depends on how many Preparation Points they have remaining when the previous act comes to an end.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore’s Return": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的归来 Willowshore’s Return",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"This Place is Ours\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第11章：</span>\n  <span>柳岸镇的归来</span>\n</h1>\n\n<p>当总督 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保} 未能加固将苦迦菩提禁锢于其坟墓中的护时，这场失败的仪式宣告的毁灭不仅降临在总督身上，也降临在整个城镇及其周边地区。柳岸镇的人民尽数死去，却又在这座城镇及其周围荒野的思维空间中重生，并被诅咒在一个多世纪里一遍又一遍重演同样可怖的一年。和善保则被困在一个更为狭小、仅限于城镇本身的思维空间中，并被诅咒在每个重复的年份里都试图研究出一条逃脱之道，却又一次次眼看自己的进展被不断重置。</p>\n<p>当柳岸镇的英雄们进入这片思维空间并与他对峙时，他们发现失踪的总督被愧疚折磨——这份愧疚使他将自己与苦迦菩提等同起来：既然他是城镇毁灭的源头，那么他事实上不正是他一直试图击败的那个东西吗？无论PC们在第8章中选择以战斗对抗他，还是帮助他走出愧疚，他们最终都带着所需的魔法走出总督的思维空间，使自己与柳岸镇重获生命。</p>\n<p>然而，这个仪式并未拯救和善保，因为他仍被困在自己的牢笼中，而苦迦菩提的影响也很快便彻底接管一切。随着PC们与柳岸镇重返人世，思维空间的建筑被苦迦菩提的死寂梦境所吞没，并扭曲成某种替代现实——一种本可能存在的柳岸镇：如果和善保从未进行那场仪式，而是成为苦迦菩提奴役下的不死统治者。从这最终的思维空间中，和善保着手为自己架起返回生者世界的桥梁；当他完成这项工作时，便开始将自己的身躯献给苦迦菩提，好让其从死亡中复起，并借此施展转生术，转生到一个尚未为其重生做好准备的国度。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-wraith-fight.webp\" alt=\"Haunting the Living\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"This Place is Ours\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 11:</span>\n  <span>Willowshore’s Return</span>\n</h1>\n\n<p>When Governor @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} failed to bolster the wards keeping Kugaptee imprisoned in his grave, the botched ritual spelled doom not only for the governor, but for the entire town and surrounding region. The people of Willowshore perished, only to be reborn in a mindscape of the town and its surrounding hinterlands and doomed to replay the same awful year again and again for over a century. Heh Shan-Bao became trapped in a much smaller mindscape limited to the town itself and was cursed to spend each repeating year attempting to research a way to escape, only to have his progress reset time and time again.</p>\n<p>When the heroes of Willowshore make their way into this mindscape and confront him, they find the missing governor to be racked with guilt—guilt that has driven him to equate himself with Kugaptee, reasoning that since he’d been the source of the town’s destruction, wasn’t he, in fact, the very thing he’d sought to defeat? Whether the PCs chose to confront him in combat or help him work through his guilt in Chapter 8, they emerged from the governor’s mindscape armed with the magic they needed to bring themselves and Willowshore back to life.</p>\n<p>Yet this ritual didn’t save Heh Shan-Bao, for he remains trapped in his own cage, and it isn’t long before Kugaptee’s influence takes complete control. As the PCs and Willowshore return to life, the mindscape’s architecture becomes absorbed by Kugaptee’s dead dreams and warps into a sort of alternate reality—a version of Willowshore that could have been, if Heh Shan-Bao never performed the ritual and instead became a deathless ruler in Kugaptee’s thrall. From this final mindscape, Heh Shan-Bao works to create his own bridge back to the living world, and when he completes his task, he begins the work of offering his body to Kugaptee that he might rise from death and thus reincarnate into a nation unprepared for his rebirth.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 4.2: The Princess’s Web": {
          "name": "第4.2幕：公主的蛛网术 Act 4.2: The Princess’s Web",
          "pages": {
            "The Un-Weavers": {
              "name": "解编者 The Un-Weavers",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">解织者</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>尽管柳岸镇所面对的最大威胁，是恶魔苦迦菩提带来的危机，但小镇离奇地重返现实这一异象，也引来了其他恶魔与畸形怪物的注意，它们察觉到了现实中那诡异的涟漪。本次遭遇旨在凸显这一点，并让PC明白：若他们失败，将会有怎样的恐怖在前方等候。</p>\n<p>生物：本次遭遇开始于PC们结伴穿行于柳岸镇之时——四个诡异的生物突然在视野边缘淡入显现：也许蜷伏在某处低矮屋顶上，或潜藏在昏暗小巷的入口阴影里。</p>\n<p>这些蜷伏的生物是精华噬者——罕见而残忍的怪物，以活人灵魂被撕碎后的残渣为食；它们会先将灵魂的一切身份与个体性剥离殆尽，然后才吞食。柳岸镇骤然涌入的新生命吸引了这四足、形似蜘蛛的生物的注意；它们合称自己为“解织者”。尽管强大，“解织者”并不愚蠢，它们明白贸然攻击未知的敌人可能会反噬自身。于是，这四者在它们怀疑是小镇“领袖”的人——PC——附近显形，试图促成一笔令人不安的交易。</p>\n\n<p>四只精华噬者中的一只上前与队伍交涉，用平静而带着好奇的声音问道：“你们这些新鲜灵魂是从哪里来的？”只要PC不先动手，这只精华噬者很快便会把话题引向它的提案——若PC愿意在今天献给四名“解织者”一名柳岸镇的“新鲜灵魂”，并在此后每个季节的第一天再次献上一名，“解织者”便承诺保护小镇免受其他超自然掠食者侵害。无论精华噬者是否真打算履行这桩交易中它们的那一份（它们很可能不会），如果PC同意，随着消息传开，他们在镇上的名声会迅速崩塌，任美璃甚至可能为此当面质问他们。即便精明的PC试图借机清除小镇的敌人，选择与这种怪物结盟也几乎不可能让他们在镇上受欢迎！</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/quintessivore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">解织者</span> <span class=\"keepme\">严峻 11</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.a0pEt1uwpdofRfsQ]{精华噬者（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>PC更有可能拒绝精华噬者；若他们这么做，这些怪物会变得焦躁不安，随后其中一只说道：“那我们就把你们的灵魂当作贡品取走，再随心所欲地啃食你们的朋友！”然后它们便发动攻击。根据对话在暴力爆发时的进展情况，PC可以为先攻掷骰，使用欺瞒、交涉或威吓。</p>\n  <p>你可以用任何街区尺度的地图来进行这场遭遇。这场战役第一幕中的柳岸镇镇区地图就是极佳选择。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Un-Weavers</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>While the greatest threat Willowshore faces is that presented by the fiend Kugaptee, the town’s strange return to reality attracts the attention of other fiends and monstrosities who take note of the strange ripples in reality. This encounter is meant to spotlight this, and to give the PCs an idea of the horrors that await if they should fail.</p>\n<p>Creature: This encounter begins as the PCs are traveling as a group through Willowshore, when four strange creatures suddenly fade into view at the edge of vision—crouched atop a low roof, perhaps, or lurking in a shadowy alleyway entrance.</p>\n<p>These crouching creatures are quintessivores, rare and cruel monsters that feed on the shredded remnants of living souls, which they strip of all identity and individuality before consuming. The sudden influx of new life into Willowshore attracted the attention of these four-legged spider-like creatures, who collectively call themselves the “Un-Weavers.” While powerful, the Un-Weavers are no fools, and they realize that an attack against an unknown foe could backfire against them. Instead, the four manifest near those they suspect are the town’s “leaders”—the PCs—and attempt to broker an unsettling deal.</p>\n\n<p>One of the four quintessivores steps forward to address the party, speaking in a calm voice tinged with curiosity as they ask, “Where did all you fresh souls hail from?” Assuming the PCs don’t attack, the quintessivore soon guides the conversation toward its proposal—if the PCs offer to the four Un-Weavers one of the “fresh souls” of Willowshore today, and then again on the first day of every season to follow, the Un-Weavers promise to protect the town from other supernatural predators. Whether or not the quintessivores actually intend to honor their side of this bargain (they likely won’t), if the PCs do agree to this, their reputation in town will swiftly falter as word spreads, and Ren Mei Li might even confront them about the choice. Even if canny PCs attempt to use this as an opportunity to get rid of enemies of the town, the choice to ally with such monsters is unlikely to make them popular in town!</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/quintessivore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">The Un-Weavers</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 11</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.a0pEt1uwpdofRfsQ]{Quintessivores (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>It’s more likely that the PCs turn the quintessivores down; if they do so, the monsters grow jittery before one of them says, “Then we shall simply take yours as tribute and feed on your friends as we see fit!” before they attack. Depending on how the conversation was going when violence breaks out, the PCs can roll Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation for initiative.</p>\n  <p>You can use any street-level map for this encounter. The map of downtown Willowshore from this campaign’s first act makes an excellent choice.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Other Encounters": {
              "name": "其他遭遇 Other Encounters",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">其他遭遇</span>\n</h1>\n<p>与先前的冒险不同，“在蛛网之下绽放”不一定要在季节的最后一天结束。虽然本冒险的遭遇与事件不应导致你的战役拖到夏季，但如果确实如此，也完全没问题。同样地，你可能会发现你的PC在完成对谋杀现场的调查或完成他们被派去取回五季宝藏的任务时，效率格外高。</p>\n<p>无论哪种情况（尤其是如果你的小组在经验点数或道具方面落后），你都可以考虑加入额外的遭遇让队伍面对。其中一些可以只是由那位怪物总督实施的额外谋杀（见前一页的 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event8thethi00#additional-murders]{额外谋杀} 侧栏），但你也可以加入全新的遭遇，用以体现PC、镇民，以及柳岸镇这处聚落本身如何适应在现代的、充满生机的世界中存在这一新的现实。</p>\n<p>在对页展示的是一个可选的加值遭遇，供PC在他们继续前往本冒险路径的最终章之前加以应对。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Other Encounters</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Unlike the previous adventures, “To Bloom Below the Web” doesn’t have to end on the last day of the season. While this adventure’s encounters and events shouldn’t cause your campaign to trail into summer, if they do, that’s perfectly fine. Likewise, you might find that your PCs are particularly efficient in completing the investigation of murder scenes or accomplishing the tasks to which they are sent to recover the Five Season treasures.</p>\n<p>In either case (and particularly if your group is lagging behind in experience points or gear), you may wish to include additional encounters for the party to face. Some of these could simply be additional murders performed by the monstrous governor (see the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event8thethi00#additional-murders]{Additional Murders} sidebar on the previous page), but you can also include brand new encounters to represent how the PCs, the townsfolk, and the settlement of Willowshore itself adjust to the new reality of existing in the modern, living world.</p>\n<p>Presented on the facing page is one potential bonus encounter for the PCs to navigate before they move on to this Adventure Path’s final chapter.</p>"
            },
            "The Fang and Key": {
              "name": "尖牙与钥匙 The Fang and Key",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">獠牙与钥匙</span>\n</h1>\n<p>任美璃在将PC们送上沿着薄纱行道的旅程后一周返回柳岸镇时，迫切想知道他们从行道女那里得知了什么，并要求他们做一份完整汇报。如果PC们没问到关键问题，她会感到失望，但仍希望他们能成为柳岸镇的监护者。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-thefangandkey.webp\" data-tooltip=\"The Fang and Key\" alt=\"一把华丽的黄铜钥匙，钥身上串着几枚小金属獠牙\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-thefangandkey.webp')\" />\n\n<p>当PC们完成汇报后，任美璃向PC们微微鞠躬以示敬意，随后从袍袖的褶裥中取出一把巨大的金钥匙。钥匙华丽的钥身上有四个圆形凹槽，钥首的穿孔处穿着丝线，丝线上垂挂着蜘蛛獠牙。当五季宝藏的景泰蓝球被嵌入钥身的凹槽时，它们会扣锁固定，物体周围随即泛起金色辉光。将景泰蓝球安置妥当后，任美璃再次对PC们开口：“向职务宣誓，并明智而尽责地担任柳岸镇的监护者。”她说话间递出金钥匙；PC们只需接下这把钥匙，便会成为神门络新妇庭院的正式监护者。</p>\n<p>这把钥匙名为<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>。有了它，PC们如今在法律上成为现代柳岸镇政府的一员，并被视为与现任总督共同治理城镇的正统统治者。<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>是一件仪式性物品，本身并无真正的内在功能，除了可作为一枚@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.mRz8Jmk4Q06SsZpC]{永光水晶}使用。<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>所能开启的最重要之物，是通往和善保领地的许可：只要PC之中有人携带它，那片领地就会欢迎他们，视其为依法任命的统治者。他们可以进入他的庄园，并使用其中的思维空间之门前往被腐化的柳岸镇思维空间，如第13章所述。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.YMpaXnskvQDnVskE]{监护者徽记} @UUID[Actor.MXAp7aimO3k06OKV]{任美璃的赋礼} <br />\n  传统上，成为监护者者不会得到额外赠礼，但若PC们表现得格外出色，任美璃就会破例如此。若PC们在执行五项仪式中至少获得10点胜利点数，她会取出一个由蛛丝制成的<em>II型宽敞袋</em>，袋中装有一面<em>辟邪盾</em>、一根<em>财富绳</em>、一根<em>炼狱使者法杖</em>以及一把<em>宗师伞</em>。任美璃允许PC们从这四件物品中选择一件作为奖励。PC们每比10点多获得1点胜利点数，她就允许他们额外选择一件奖励；若PC们获得14点或更多胜利点数，她会将四件物品连同袋子本身一并交给他们。\n</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>当PC们成为柳岸镇的监护者并获得<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>时，给予他们80 XP。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Fang and Key</span>\n</h1>\n<p>When Ren Mei Li returns to Willowshore a week after sending the PCs on their trek along the Gossamer Path, she’s eager to find out what they’ve learned from the path maiden and asks them to give a full report. If the PCs didn’t ask the right question, she is disappointed but still wishes for them to become Willowshore’s stewards.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-thefangandkey.webp\" data-tooltip=\"The Fang and Key\" alt=\"an ornate brass key with small metal fangs strung from the shaft\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-thefangandkey.webp')\" />\n\n<p>Once the PCs conclude the report, Ren Mei Li offers a slight bow of respect to the PCs, then produces from the folds of her robe a large golden key. Four circular hollows punctuate the key’s ornate shaft, and spider fangs dangle from silken threads strung through its pierced heads. When the cloisonne balls of the Five-Season Treasures are slotted into the key’s shaft, they lock into place, and a golden glow surrounds the object. After fitting the cloisonne balls in place, Ren Mei Li speaks once more to the PCs: “Swear yourself to the office and to serve as Willowshore’s stewards wisely and well.” As she speaks, she offers the golden key; the PCs need only accept this key to become official stewards of Shenmen’s jorogumo court.</p>\n<p>This key is known as the <em>Fang and Key</em>. With it, the PCs are now legally part of modern Willowshore’s government and are considered the rightful rulers of the town alongside their currently serving governor. The <em>Fang and Key</em> is a ceremonial item and has no real intrinsic function of its own other than to serve as an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.mRz8Jmk4Q06SsZpC]{Everlight Crystal}. The most important thing the <em>Fang and Key</em> unlocks is access to Heh Shan-Bao’s domain, for as long as one of the PCs carry it, that domain welcomes them as legally appointed rulers. They can access his manor and use the mindscape door found within to travel to the corrupted Willowshore mindscape, as detailed in Chapter 13.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.YMpaXnskvQDnVskE]{Steward's Token} @UUID[Actor.MXAp7aimO3k06OKV]{Ren Mei Li's Gift} <br />\n  Traditionally, no additional gifts are provided to those who become stewards, but if the PCs did exceptionally well, Ren Mei Li does just that. If the PCs earned at least 10 Victory Points from performing the five rites, she produces a <em>type II spacious pouch</em> made of spidersilk that contains an <em>evil-reflecting shield</em>, a <em>fortune cord</em>, a <em>purgatory emissary’s staff</em>, and a <em>sensei’s parasol</em>. Ren Mei Li allows the PCs to choose one of these four items as a reward. For every additional Victory Point above 10 the PCs earned, she allows them to choose one additional reward; if the PCs earned 14 or more Victory Points, she gives them all four items plus the bag itself.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> When the PCs become stewards of Willowshore and gain the <em>Fang and Key</em>, grant them 80 XP.</p>"
            },
            "Event 8. The Third Murder": {
              "name": "事件 8：第三起谋杀 Event 8. The Third Murder",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 8：第三起谋杀</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right sidebar\">\n  <h1>额外的谋杀</h1>\n  <p>\n    如果PC们拖拖拉拉，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}可能会再次出手。之后任何受害者都会视机而定，取决于这位怪物般的总督能找到谁落单；这些人作为目标并无特殊意义。在这些谋杀现场找不到更多线索。他甚至可能开始在他认为能趁PC们独自一人时伏击他们的时机，把目标转向个别PC。\n  </p>\n</aside>\n<p>\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的第三名受害者是守墓人兼炼金术士尤素珍（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w3gravesidem00]{坟边居}）。和善保之所以盯上她，是因为他能感知到她最近在试验一种新型炼金炸弹，意图让其对灵堕魔特别有效。这起杀戮发生在PC们从薄纱之径返回之后、任美璃最后一次来访之前。遗体很可能要到上午稍晚才会被发现——夜间宵禁解除后，有顾客前来光顾坟边居，却遭遇此生最骇人的景象。\n  </p>\n<p>\n    素珍的尸体在她的店里被发现，四肢摊开，周围是一片被毁的存货与报废的炼金材料。她的遗体与其他受害者一样，状况惨不忍睹。\n  </p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 data-no-toc>犯罪现场</h2>\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-so-jinyousjournal.webp\" data-tooltip=\"You So-Jin's Journal\" alt=\"a blood-stained leather-bound journal\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-so-jinyousjournal.webp')\" />\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>搜寻线索</strong> 调查；@Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>轻微</strong> 与前两起案件不同，凶手在现场停留了相当长的时间——要么是在与受害者搏斗，要么是在把这里翻个底朝天寻找某样东西。\n  </p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>中等</strong> 受害者似乎同样是被迅速而高效地杀害，这证实店内的破坏并非搏斗所致，而是在行凶结束后进行的狂乱搜寻，或是一阵暴怒的破坏。屋后方的实验室承受了主要破坏：它已被砸得粉碎，大多数物资也都被毁。如果PC们再花10分钟搜寻这间被毁的炼金实验室，并在一次@Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]检定中成功，他们会发现一本旧日记藏在一只未被完全毁坏的梳妆柜后方，梳妆柜上放着一个小金属匣。这本日记在尤素珍家族中代代相传，包含她的母亲、外祖母与曾外祖母留下的炼金与草药研究笔记。关于日记与金属匣的更多细节见下文“宝藏”，但这本日记也是一件重要的个人信物，可用于在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15theherbalist00]{第13章}中解放素珍的灵魂。\n  </p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>重大</strong> PC们会自动发现尤素珍的日记和<em>银魂炸弹</em>。\n  </p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>错误线索</strong> 尤素珍对袭击者进行了出乎意料的强力反击，导致建筑遭到如此破坏。或许她在草药方面的技艺带来了某种意想不到的保护？\n  </p>\n    </section>\n\n<p>\n    <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.sSTaVc48j9x3Glx4]{店铺} <br /> 若PC们发现素珍的日记并花一小时通读，他们会发现其中记载着一种稀有的炼金武器配方：<em>银魂炸弹</em>。该配方似乎是素珍的母亲在去世前开始研究的内容，而素珍直到最近才完成相关研究。笔记还表明，尤素珍原本打算在PC们从“最近一次差事”归来后，将该配方与她制作的少数几枚炸弹交给PC们，以协助他们对抗灵堕魔；但她在付诸行动前就被谋杀了。\n  </p>\n<p>\n    日记下方发现的金属匣内装有三枚<em>银魂炸弹</em>，以及价值500 gp的银粉和其他炼金材料；若将这些材料用于制作额外的<em>银魂炸弹</em>，会使相应的制作检定获得+2物品加值。\n  </p>\n<p>\n    <strong>奖励：</strong> PC们因发现<em>银魂炸弹</em>及其相关配方而获得80 XP。若PC们设法阻止素珍被谋杀，她会在第13章开始时将<em>银魂炸弹</em>与配方赠予他们。\n  </p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 8: The Third Murder</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right sidebar\">\n  <h1>Additional Murders</h1>\n  <p>\n    If the PCs dawdle, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} might strike again. Any further victims are chosen opportunistically, depending\n    on who the monstrous governor can find alone and have no particular significance as targets. There are no\n    additional clues to be found at these murder sites. He might even begin to target individual PCs at points where he thinks\n    he can ambush them while they’re alone.\n  </p>\n</aside>\n<p>\n    @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s third victim is the grave keeper–alchemist\n    You So-Jin (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w3gravesidem00]{Graveside Manners}), whom Heh Shan-Bao targets because\n    he can sense her recent work on experimenting with a new type of alchemical bomb that’s intended to work particularly\n    well against nindorus. This killing occurs after the PCs return from the Gossamer Path but before Ren Mei Li’s\n    last visit. The body is unlikely to be found until late morning, after the nightly curfew lifts, and a customer visits\n    Graveside Manners only to find the shock of their life.\n  </p>\n<p>\n    So-Jin’s body is found in her shop, sprawled amid a chaos of destroyed stock and ruined alchemical supplies. Her\n    corpse is in the same grisly condition as the others.\n  </p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 data-no-toc>Scene of the Crime</h2>\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-so-jinyousjournal.webp\" data-tooltip=\"You So-Jin's Journal\" alt=\"a blood-stained leather-bound journal\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-so-jinyousjournal.webp')\" />\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Search for Clues</strong> Investigate; @Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Minor</strong> Unlike the first two crimes, the murderer spent a significant amount of time at the crime scene—either\n    fighting against the victim or tearing the place apart in search of something.\n  </p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Moderate</strong> The victim appears to have been slain as quickly and efficiently as the others, confirming that the\n    devastation in the shop wasn’t a result of a struggle but instead a frenzied search or a bout of enraged\n    destruction after the killing was over. The lab at the back of the house bore the brunt of this devastation, as it has been\n    smashed to splinters and most of the supplies have been ruined. If the PCs spend 10 more minutes Searching the\n    ruined alchemical lab and succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:27|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search] check, they discover an old journal hidden behind a\n    not-completely-destroyed dresser atop a small metal case. This journal has been in You So-Jin’s family for\n    generations and contains alchemical and herbalism research notes from her mother, grandmother, and\n    great-grandmother. See Treasure below for additional details on the journal and the metal case, but the journal\n    serves as a significant personal token that can be used to free So-Jin’s soul in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15theherbalist00]{Chapter 13}.\n  </p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>Major</strong> The PCs automatically discover You So-Jin’s journal and <em>silversoul bombs</em>.\n  </p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">\n    <strong>False Lead</strong> You So-Jin put up an unexpectedly powerful fight against her attacker, resulting in the devastation of\n    the building. Perhaps her skill at herbalism afforded some sort of unexpected protection?\n  </p>\n    </section>\n\n<p>\n    <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.sSTaVc48j9x3Glx4]{Shop} <br /> If the PCs discover So-Jin’s journal and spend an hour reading through it, they’ll discover it contains\n    a rare formula for an alchemical weapon: a <em>silversoul bomb</em>. The formula appears to be one that So-Jin’s mother began\n    researching up until her death and that So-Jin only recently completed the research for. The notes also indicate\n    how You So-Jin intended to present the formula and the few bombs she crafted to the PCs to aid them in their fight\n    against nindorus once they returned from their “latest errand,” but she was murdered before she could act on this\n    plan.\n  </p>\n<p>\n    The metal case found under the journal contains three <em>silversoul bombs</em> and 500 gp worth of powdered silver and\n    other alchemical supplies that, if used to craft additional <em>silversoul bombs</em>, grants a +2 item bonus to the Crafting\n    check.\n  </p>\n<p>\n    <strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP for discovering the <em>silversoul bombs</em> and the associated formula. If the PCs manage to\n    prevent So-Jin’s murder, she gifts them the <em>silversoul bombs</em> and formula at the start of Chapter 13.\n  </p>"
            },
            "Walking the Gossamer Path": {
              "name": "漫步于蛛丝之径 Walking the Gossamer Path",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">踏行罗网之道</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 11</span>\n</h3>\n<p>“罗网之道”在神门广为人知（因此也为所有居住在柳岸镇的人所知，PC当然也包括在内），这一术语指的是穿行于罗网山脉之间、蜿蜒盘旋的所有山路与小径。自玉鸟客栈向北延伸的道路最终确实会抵达这些山脉，但PC并不一定要走这条路线才能踏行罗网之道——在山中道路上行走任何一段距离，都能让PC有充足机会遭遇行道女。</p>\n<p>罗网山脉位于柳岸镇以西近300英里处，但若PC选择沿着出镇后向北蜿蜒的道路前进，这段旅程将接近450英里。若没有任美璃授予他们的<em>罗网绶带</em>，PC若想寻求行道女的建议，就将面临漫长旅途；但有了这件物品，他们可以在午夜过后，从神门的任何一条道路“踏行罗网之道”。本次冒险默认PC使用@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Q3ZYTbPGPDG6WINq]{Gossamer Sash}与行道女取得联系；但如果他们选择亲自前往山中，你可以借此机会在途中加入更多由你自行设计的遭遇——如果PC需要额外几场遭遇，或正愈发渴望打一架，这是个极好的选择。</p>\n<p>最多4名PC可以使用一条<em>罗网绶带</em>进入一处拟真思维空间，与一群行道女会面；如果你的队伍人数超过四人，要么让玩家选择由哪四名PC前往，要么干脆调整<em>罗网绶带</em>的长度，使所有PC都能参与。当PC在夜间沿道路行走了1小时后启动绶带，浓雾会在他们周围降下，随即又迅速散去，显露出他们正站在一条狭窄的山中道路上：道路宽10英尺，右侧是一面直冲云霄的峭壁，左侧则是另一面峭壁，坠落向下方雾气弥漫的森林深处。</p>\n<p>这场遭遇并不打算以战斗收场，但若PC攻击行道女，你可以使用第二幕的山中道路地图，或使用你自制的类似山道地图。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC进入思维空间后不久，一名行道女便会出现在他们面前——她可能在他们转过一道弯时步入视野，甚至可能从道路中升起。她身着紫色与深海蓝的长袍，面纱遮住了面容。行道女以低语的声线对PC开口，同时也以心灵感应对他们的心智说话。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“温血者，活血者，脆弱的凡人盛宴。你们为何踏上罗网之道？你们追寻的是谁的死者秘辛，又要为谁的性命而动用它们？”</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">踏行罗网之道</span> <span class=\"keepme\">低威胁 11</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.kcER7jXFIce5IrKF]{行道女}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>如果PC并非借助<em>罗网绶带</em>的力量来寻找行道女，她几乎不等他们回答就会发动攻击。PC只有一次迅速作答的机会——每名PC都可以尝试一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:34]检定，以说服行道女暂缓攻击。只要至少有一名PC在此检定中取得至少一次成功，且没有任何PC大失败，行道女便允许PC继续说下去。否则，她会战斗至被摧毁；之后，那面诡异的镜子（见下文）将会显现。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  PC可以向行道女提出一个问题。她的知识仅限于神门的死者，但也包括那些曾死亡一段时间、却在近期复生的人。关于苦迦菩提与总督@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的命运，是她已准备好提供见解的特定主题（见下文）；但若PC询问其他事物，你应尽量给出能满足他们好奇心的回答。若问题轻浮或不敬，行道女可能以攻击作为回答。一旦问题得到回答，PC会突然发现自己回到了出发处（若本次遭遇发生在由<em>罗网绶带</em>创造的思维空间中），或者行道女从视野中淡去，只留下他们独自站在山间小径上（若他们亲自前往了罗网山脉）。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-spooky-portal.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Strange Mirror\" alt=\"a mirror with a latticed wooden frame vignetting the glass\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-spooky-portal.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>问对问题：</strong>如果PC询问苦迦菩提、总督和善保，或困扰柳岸镇的谋杀案，行道女会一言不发地移到一旁，并示意PC沿路继续前进。道路中央的空中会凭空显现一面银色的长椭圆镜子，悬浮不动。即便PC正站在镜前，它的倒影仍只呈现一条空无一人的小径，仿佛它只反映从未有人踏足时道路的样子。</p>\n<p>当任何人靠近镜子5英尺内时，镜中影像便会改变。镜中出现柳岸镇的总督府——并非如今那副破败模样，而是一栋辉煌宅邸：刚粉刷一新、铺着绚丽瓦片，大门上方悬挂帝国旗帜，灯柱上垂下金色流苏。影像继续向内推进，穿过府邸大门、再穿过庭院，最终进入主卧套间，并停在北墙上一扇门前——在PC此前两次造访那房间时，这扇门都并不存在。门由上等柏木制成，门中央镶着一把华丽的金锁；金锁嵌在一张青铜铸成、獠牙外露的恶魔面孔之中。其张开的口器上方，有两点红光闪烁。那恶魔的面孔再次扭曲变化，此刻看上去已成了总督和善保的脸。他从镜中探视PC，直接对他们开口。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“贪婪与羞耻。催化变化的烈性补剂。人化为怪物。怪物化为门径。村落化为盛宴。贪婪与羞耻，羞耻与贪婪。它们织就多么奇妙的锁链！多么可爱的把戏，多么聪明的锁！我会为你们开启大门，再多造访几回，很快人与怪物便将合而为一。届时苦迦菩提便已得胜，因为只有正统的统治者才能携带通往我领域的钥匙！”</p>\n</div>\n<p>随即影像消散，片刻之后，镜子也一同消失。薄雾在道路周围变得愈发浓重，其存在仿佛活物、饥渴难耐，带来一种先前没有的幽闭压迫感。然而，小径也更空寂了——蒙面的侍女们已然不见。似乎她们那场怪异的试炼已经结束。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC完全避免战斗并问对了问题，则给予他们如同在战斗中击败行道女一般的XP。</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Walking the Gossamer Path</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 11</span>\n</h3>\n<p>The Gossamer Path is well known in Shenmen (and thus to all who live in Willowshore, the PCs included) as a term that applies to all of the winding mountain roads and trails that coil their way through the Gossamer Mountains. While the road leading north from Canary Inn eventually reaches these mountains, the PCs need not take this route to walk the Gossamer Path—any length of road walked in the mountains gives the PCs ample opportunity to encounter path maidens.</p>\n<p>The Gossamer Mountains lie nearly 300 miles to the west of Willowshore, but if the PCs choose to follow the winding road north from town, the journey is closer to 450 miles. Without the <em>Gossamer Sash</em> granted to them by Ren Mei Li, the PCs face a long journey if they wish to seek the advice of path maidens, but with the item, they can “walk the Gossamer Path” from any road in Shenmen after midnight. This adventure assumes the PCs use a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Q3ZYTbPGPDG6WINq]{Gossamer Sash} to contact path maidens, but if they choose to journey to the mountains in person, you can use this opportunity to introduce more encounters along the way of your own design—an excellent choice if the PCs could use a few additional encounters, or are growing eager for a fight.</p>\n<p>Up to 4 PCs can use a <em>Gossamer Sash</em> to travel into an immersive mindscape to meet with a group of path maidens; if your group has more than four, either have the players choose which four PCs make the trip, or simply adjust the length of the <em>Gossamer Sash</em> to allow for all your PCs to take part. When the PCs activate the sash after an hour spent walking a roadway at night, a thick fog descends upon them, only to swiftly clear and reveal that they now stand on a narrow mountain pathway that measures 10 feet wide, with a sheer cliff rising into the clouds to their right and another dropping away into a foggy forest far below to their left.</p>\n<p>This encounter isn’t intended to result in combat, but if the PCs do attack the path maiden, you can use the mountain path map from Act 2, or a similar mountain path map of your own design.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> When the PCs enter the mindscape, it won’t be long before a path maiden appears before them, either stepping into view as they walk around a bend or even rising up out of the road. Clad in robes of purple and deep sea blue with veils obscuring their features, the path maiden addresses the PCs in a whispering voice while simultaneously speaking telepathically to their minds.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Warm-bloods, living-bloods, fragile mortal feasts. Why do you tread the Gossamer Path? Whose dead secrets do you seek, and for whose lives would you use them?”</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Walking the Gossamer Path</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Low 11</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.kcER7jXFIce5IrKF]{Path Maiden}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If the PCs didn’t seek a path maiden via the power of the <em>Gossamer Sash</em>, she barely waits for an answer before attacking. The PCs have one chance to swiftly answer—each PC can attempt a @Check[diplomacy|dc:34] check to get the path maiden to stay her attack. As long as at least one PC scores at least a success at this check and no PC critically fails it, the path maiden lets the PCs speak further. Otherwise, she fights until destroyed, after which the strange mirror (see below) manifests.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  The PCs are allowed one question of the path maiden. Her knowledge is limited to the dead in Shenmen, but it includes those who have spent time dead only to recently return to life. The topics of Kugaptee and the fate of Governor @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} are specific topics that she’s prepared to offer insights on (see below), but if the PCs ask about anything else, provide an answer as best you can that will satisfy their curiosity. If the question is frivolous or disrespectful, the path maiden might answer by attacking. Once the question is answered, the PCs suddenly find themselves back where they started (if this encounter took place in a mindscape created by a\n  <em>gossamer sash</em>), or the path maiden fades from view, leaving them alone on the mountain trail (if they physically traveled to the Gossamer Mountains).\n</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-spooky-portal.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Strange Mirror\" alt=\"a mirror with a latticed wooden frame vignetting the glass\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-spooky-portal.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Asking the Right Question:</strong> If the PCs ask about Kugaptee, Governor Heh Shan-Bao, or the murders that have been plaguing Willowshore, the path maiden moves aside wordlessly and indicates the PCs should continue down the road, where an oblong silver mirror manifests out of nothingness, hovering in the air in the middle of the road. Its reflection shows an empty path, even when the PCs stand directly before it, as if reflecting only the road as it appears when not traveled at all.</p>\n<p>As soon as anyone approaches within 5 feet of the mirror, the image shifts. The governor’s manor in Willowshore appears, not in its current dilapidated state, but as a splendid house, freshly painted and colorfully tiled, with imperial banners hanging above the doors and gold tassels streaming from the lantern posts. The image moves inward, passing through the mansion’s doors and then through its courtyard, to finally enter the manor’s primary suite before stopping at a door in the northern wall that didn’t exist in that room during either of the PCs’ two previous visits. The door is made of fine cypress wood, with an ornate golden lock worked into a fanged fiend’s face made of bronze affixed to the center of the door. Two glowing red points of light shimmer above the visage’s open jaws. The fiend’s face shifts again, now appearing to be that of Governor Heh Shan-Bao. He peers out of the mirror and addresses the PCs directly.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Greed and shame. Such potent tonics to quicken a change. A man becomes a monster. A monster becomes a gateway. A village becomes a feast. Greed and shame, shame and greed. What marvelous chains they weave! What lovely tricks, what clever locks! I’ll open your doors and visit some more, and soon shall man and monster be one. And then Kugaptee has won, for only a rightful ruler shall carry the key to my domain!”</p>\n</div>\n<p>The image then dissipates, and a moment later, the mirror does as well. The mist thickens about the path, and its presence seems alive and hungry, creating a claustrophobic closeness that wasn’t present before. Yet, the path is emptier, too, as the veiled maidens have vanished. It seems their strange test is at its end.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs XP as if they’d defeated the path maiden in combat if they avoided battle entirely and asked the right question.</p>"
            },
            "Event 7. The Final Season": {
              "name": "事件7：最终季 Event 7. The Final Season",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 7：最终季</span>\n</h2>\n<p>任美璃在约定的时间回到柳岸镇——在把PC们派去低语蛛网神龛后的一周。她并不询问他们是如何设法收集到足以滤过冬日香料茶的丝，但她要求他们护送她前往青天茶馆，然后在浸泡过程中用收集来的丝充当滤材，为她煮一杯饮品。不论PC们如何准备，她都很享受这杯饮品，并在进行最后的仪式——行走罗网之道——之前称赞他们迄今为止的表现。她喝完茶后，任美璃露出捉摸不定的微笑，接着舒展全身；在这一伸展间，她背后展开八条蜘蛛腿，落地支撑，将她的人形身躯抬离地面。如今PC们已经完成前四项任务，她不再觉得有必要掩饰自己的真实本性。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“既然你们已令低语蛛网神龛的守护者满意，也已准备好追寻第五件、也是最终季的宝藏，那么我们是时候就柳岸镇的未来达成清晰的共识——不带幻象，也不带虚饰。</p>\n  <p>“我准备接纳你们所有人担任管事。我也准备以银印为柳岸镇提供相当程度的自治。具体条款可以协商，但我想你们会发现它们非常合理——远比你们从任何其他朝廷能得到的都更合理。</p>\n  <p>“作为交换，我要的是：一份个人效忠誓言，凌驾于你们对朗洛依女士或络新妇朝廷其余成员的任何忠诚之上。我希望你们成为我的代理人，只为我效力。当然，这将会保持低调。表面上，你们必须扮演络新妇朝廷忠诚臣民的角色，绝不可让我们的私下协议走漏风声。若你们发现我的同族提出不合理的要求，你们必须请求我出面干预，而不是自行其是；但我承诺，若你们的村子需要，我会给予庇护。</p>\n  <p>“我提出此事，只因为你们至今展现出的技能令我印象深刻。我希望你们不会背叛我的信任。你们怎么说？”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>若PC们同意，或成功通过一个 @Check[deception|dc:39|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie] 检定对她说谎，公主便会继续。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“你们现在必须行走罗网之道，并寻求蒙面行道女的青睐。她们是秘密的守护者，尤其是那些蒙羞死者的秘密；我相信她们会掌握对你们有价值的情报，与你们城镇近来所遭受的不幸残酷有关。去见她们。向她们询问你想知道的事，以及原因。寻求她们的睿智建议来破解你们的凶案，并证明你们愿意为解决城镇之痛承担巨大风险。</p>\n  <p>“这是最终季，是你们最后的考验。配得上管事之职的人，必须足够勇敢，能为其人民寻求援助，而不被高位或个人危险所威慑。去吧，证明你们的胆识。”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.SSw3XpqxnqF6PH7E]{Ren Mei Li's Supplies} @UUID[Actor.HQxoO4AKbipQGFRv]{Ren Mei Li's Scroll} <br />\n  在她离开前，她给PC们一条<em>罗网绶带</em>和四剂<em>圣豆</em>。她解释说，这条绶带能让他们在不必亲自前往罗网山脉的情况下与行道女取得联系，而圣豆则能在他们与行道女的遭遇进展不顺时提供帮助。\n</p>\n<p>若PC们拒绝任美璃的提议，她明显感到失望。她不会给他们<em>罗网绶带</em>或<em>圣豆</em>，而是给他们一张<em>传讯卷轴</em>，并说道：“我不会强迫你们，但我希望你们对我们在此谈及之事守口如瓶。你们不会希望我成为敌人。若你们日后改变主意，用这张卷轴通知我，我将回来接受你们的道歉。在那之前，祝你们好运，去对抗未来数日里等待你们城镇的事物。”</p>\n<p>说完，她承诺会在一周后返回，随即再次消失在薄雾之中。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 7: The Final Season</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Ren Mei Li returns to Willowshore at the appointed time, a week after sending the PCs to Whisperweb Shrine. She doesn’t ask how they managed to gather the silk needed to strain winter’s spiced tea, but she asks them to escort her to the Cerulean Teahouse and then brew her a drink using the gathered silk as a filter during the steeping process. She enjoys the drink regardless of how the PCs prepare it and compliments them on their work so far before proceeding with the final rite: Walking the Gossamer Path. As she finishes her tea, Ren Mei Li smiles mercurially, then gives a full body stretch, during which her eight spider legs unfurl from her back to stand on the ground and lift her humanoid form into the air. Now that the PCs have completed the first four tasks, she no longer feels the need to obscure her true nature.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Now that you have satisfied the guardians of the Whisperweb Shrine and are prepared to pursue the fifth and final season treasure, it is time for us to reach a clear understanding, without illusion or pretense, about Willowshore’s future.</p>\n  <p>“I am prepared to accept you all as stewards. I am also prepared to offer considerable autonomy to Willowshore with a Silver Seal. The precise terms can be negotiated, but I expect you will find them very reasonable—far more reasonable than you would receive from any other court.</p>\n  <p>“In exchange, what I want is this: an oath of personal fealty, superseding any loyalty you may have to Lady Lang Loi or the rest of the jorogumo court. I wish for you to be my agents, and mine alone. Naturally, this will be kept discreet. Outwardly, you must play the part of loyal subjects to the jorogumo court and never let our private agreement slip. If you find that my kindred make unreasonable demands, you must ask me to intercede rather than taking matters into your own hands, but I do promise my protection if your village should need it.</p>\n  <p>“I make this offer only because I have been impressed with your skills so far. I hope you will not betray my trust. What do you say?”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>If the PCs agree, or succeed at a @Check[deception|dc:39|traits:action:lie,auditory,concentrate,linguistic,mental,secret|name:Lie] check to Lie to her, the princess continues.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“You must now walk the Gossamer Path and seek the favor of the veiled path maidens. They are guardians of secrets, particularly those of the shameful dead, and I believe they will have information of value to you about the unfortunate cruelties your town has been experiencing of late. Go to them. Ask of them what you wish to know, and why. Seek their wise counsel in solving your murders, and prove you are willing to take great risks to solve your town’s pains.</p>\n  <p>“This is the final season, your final test. A steward worthy of the office is courageous enough to seek assistance for their people without being cowed by high office or personal danger. Go then, and prove your mettle.”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>\n  @UUID[Actor.SSw3XpqxnqF6PH7E]{Ren Mei Li's Supplies} @UUID[Actor.HQxoO4AKbipQGFRv]{Ren Mei Li's Scroll} <br />\n  Before she leaves, she gives the PCs a <em>gossamer sash</em> and four doses of <em>sanctified beans</em>. The sash, she explains, will allow them to contact path maidens without actually traveling to the Gossamer Mountains, while the beans will aid them if their encounter with the path maidens goes poorly.\n</p>\n<p>If the PCs reject Ren Mei Li’s offer, she’s visibly disappointed. She doesn’t give them the <em>gossamer sash</em> or the <em>sanctified beans</em>, but instead gives them a <em>scroll of sending</em> and says, “I will not force you, but I expect you to keep what we spoke of here in confidence. You do not wish me as an enemy. If you change your minds later, use this scroll to inform me, and I shall return to accept your apologies. Until then, I wish you luck against what awaits your town in the coming days.”</p>\n<p>With that, she promises to return in a week before she vanishes into the mist once more.</p>"
            },
            "Event 6. The Second Murder": {
              "name": "事件6：第二起谋杀 Event 6. The Second Murder",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 6：第二起谋杀</span>\n</h2>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的第二名受害者是<strong>伊丽丝·堪多拉</strong>（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w9ladyofsoul00]{司魂娘娘}），柳岸镇的@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}——司魂娘娘庙的看守人。他以她为目标，部分原因是她与法莱斯玛的关联：法莱斯玛是一位掌管亡者灵魂的神祇，其权能与苦迦菩提所代表的事物相互对立；此外，由于他妖狯的本性，他内心被灌输了对笛声的恐惧与憎恨。他在某个夜晚袭击了她——当时她正在司魂娘娘庙西南方的墓地里吹奏长笛，以安抚那里的亡魂；他希望借此在柳岸镇散播恐惧，让镇民担忧他们死后所有人的灵魂将迎来何种命运。</p>\n<p>她的尸体在墓地里被发现，瘫卧在乌诺新坟的顶部，与先前受害者的状况如出一辙。PC们从低语蛛网神社返回镇上后不久便得知了这一发现。此次命案之后，柳岸镇进入高度戒备，因为显然有一个怪物——不论是人类还是其他什么——正在夜间潜伏于街巷之中。镇老下令实行日落宵禁。孩子们待在室内或被严密看护，人们对外出采集食物和柴火变得更加犹豫，除紧急情况外无人在天黑后出门。笼罩全镇的恐惧使PC们在柳岸镇进行所有用于赚取收入或搜集信息的检定时，承受–1环境减值。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>犯罪现场</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-brokenflute.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Broken Flute\" alt=\"a broken wooden flute\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-brokenflute.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>搜寻线索</strong> 调查；@Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>轻微</strong> 虽然伊丽丝的遗体如今停放在教堂内供人瞻仰，但她折断的长笛却 леж在乌诺坟旁的草地上。若PC们检查长笛并在一次@Check[perception|dc:25]检定中成功，他们会注意到它似乎是被音波伤害摧毁，而非遭受物理打击；若以DC 20检定成功辨识魔法，他们还能判定其毁坏原因很可能来自一个粉碎音波法术（(@Check[arcana|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[nature|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[religion|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic]))。这支断笛是一件重要的个人信物，可在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15thewandering00]{第13章}中用于解放伊丽丝的灵魂。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>中等</strong> 伊丽丝常在新近亡者的坟前吹奏长笛，她相信音乐能帮助他们走向来世。她的长笛被折断或许暗示，有人想进一步确保乌诺的灵魂会迷失，从而为这些罪行增添一层额外的残忍。PC还会自动意识到，长笛的损坏是由@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.1xbFBQDRs0hT5xZ9]{粉碎音波}法术造成的。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>重大</strong> 断笛也可能暗示另一种可能性——凶手或许是一种名为妖狯的超自然生物；据说它们憎恶并畏惧由圣洁之人吹奏的笛声。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>错误线索</strong> 伊丽丝曾在乌诺坟前停留这一事实，暗示两人之间可能存在某种隐秘关系——也许凶手是个嫉妒或遭抛弃的情人？</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们发现伊丽丝的断笛后，给予他们60 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 6: The Second Murder</span>\n</h2>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s second victim is <strong>Elizeth Candora</strong> (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w9ladyofsoul00]{Lady of Souls}), caretaker of Willowshore’s temple of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}, Her Fluvial Lady of Souls. He targets her in part due to her association with Pharasma, a deity whose domain over the souls of the dead runs counter to what Kugaptee represents, but also because of the fear and hatred of flute music instilled within him as a result of his yohoi nature. He attacks her one night as she plays her flute to soothe the spirits in the graveyard just southwest of Her Fluvial Lady of Souls, hoping to spread fear in Willowshore about the fate of all of the townsfolk’s souls once they die.</p>\n<p>Her body is discovered in the graveyard, sprawled over the top of Oono’s fresh grave, in the same state as the previous victim. The PCs learn of the discovery soon after their return to town from Whisperweb Shrine. After this killing, Willowshore goes on high alert as it becomes obvious there’s a monster—be they human or otherwise—stalking the streets at night. The town elder imposes a sundown curfew. Children stay indoors or under close supervision, people become much more reluctant to forage for food and firewood, and no one ventures out after dark except in cases of emergency. The fear infecting the town causes the PCs to take a –1 circumstance penalty to all checks in Willowshore to Earn Income or Gather Information.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Scene of the Crime</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-brokenflute.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Broken Flute\" alt=\"a broken wooden flute\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-brokenflute.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Search for Clues</strong> Investigate; @Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Minor</strong> While Elizeth’s body now lies in state in the church itself, her broken flute lies in the grass near Oono’s grave. If the PCs examine the flute and succeed at a @Check[perception|dc:25] check, they note that it appears to have been destroyed by sonic damage rather than a physical blow; they can identify the cause of the destruction as likely coming from a shatter spell with a successful DC 20 check to Identify Magic ((@Check[arcana|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[nature|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic] @Check[religion|dc:20|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:identify-magic|name:Identify Magic])). The broken flute serves as a significant personal token that can be used to free Elizeth’s soul in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15thewandering00]{Chapter 13}.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Moderate</strong> Elizeth often played her flute over the graves of the recently deceased, believing that music would help guide them to the afterlife. Her flute being broken suggests, perhaps, that someone wanted to further ensure Oono’s soul would become lost and indicates an extra layer of cruelty to the crimes. The PC also automatically realizes the damage to the flute was caused by a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.1xbFBQDRs0hT5xZ9]{Shatter} spell.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Major</strong> The broken flute could suggest a different possibility—the murderer might be a supernatural creature called a yohoi, as they’re said to loathe and fear the sound of flute music performed by a holy person.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>False Lead</strong> The fact that Elizeth spent time at Oono’s grave suggests that there might have been some hidden relationship between the two—perhaps the killer was a jealous or jilted lover?</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 60 XP for discovering Elizeth’s broken flute.</p>"
            },
            "Event 5. Spiced Tea of Winter": {
              "name": "事件5：冬日香料茶道 Event 5. Spiced Tea of Winter",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件5：冬日香料茶</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">严峻11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>任梅丽派遣PC们去复原苹果园一周后（也很可能是在PC们调查第一起谋杀案的几天后），那名络新妇回到了柳岸镇。她感谢PC们的工作，但与其说她为果园已开始复原而高兴，不如说她更因四只khravgodon已死的消息而欣喜。她的举止依旧一如既往地彬彬有礼，但她的言谈之间却带着一种此前从未显露过的强烈迫切感。她眼睛上覆着的银色光泽更为明显，她说话时还能看到獠牙尖端。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“你们来到第四季，也来到最能揭示真相的任务。冬之仪式要求为众人奉上香料茶，以此象征管事者能在这一季寒冷饥饿的夜晚里提供温暖、食粮与安全。此等场合最好用上等茶叶；然而即便最上等的茶，也能因穿过最精细的蛛丝滤过而更臻完美。</p>\n  <p>“西北方耳语蛛网神社的看守者能提供这般上好丝线，其质地与编织恰适合滤去细茶中的微末。它们或许与你们所习惯的不同，但只要让它们品尝你们打算呈上的茶味，你们便应能赢得它们的青睐。我建议你们别只是从它们那里夺走所需之物——但你们的选择，一如既往，仍由你们自己决定。</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>这一次，她奉上那枚描绘果盘的景泰蓝球，同时仍扣留最后一件饰物：其上描绘一口冒着蒸汽的坩埚，在一片白色雪花——或许是蛛网——的背景映衬下发出幽光。随后，她再次向众人告别，并承诺一周后回来品尝用从耳语蛛网神社采集的蛛丝滤过的茶。</p>\n<p>柳岸镇无人知晓“耳语蛛网神社”这个名字，因为在他们一百年前的时代，那处地点根本没有名字。人们只把它当作一座怪异、被遗忘、早于现代镇落的古老神社。若PC们向Karahai打听或与洛阔恩之类的本地人交谈，便可确认：位于柳岸镇以北、需行走数日的那座旧神社，在他们记忆中一直都叫“耳语蛛网”。而事实上，该地直到柳岸镇被拉入思维空间之后的几年才得此名。</p>\n<p><strong>前往神社：</strong>前往神社的旅途——它位于小径在地图上断开的地方以北约十二英里——一路平顺无事；但当PC们逐渐接近时，一阵不祥的寂静便笼罩大地。PC们接近实际地点时，朗读或转述下述内容。</p>\n<p>本次遭遇使用耳语蛛网神社地图。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>蜿蜒小径在此处豁然开朗，通向一片如画般的空地；空地中心，一汪美得令人心痛的池塘熠熠生辉。树枝高处垂挂着装饰：纸灯笼、鎏金面具、编织丝绦，以及同样醒目地混在其中的——动物干尸与不止几具人类干尸。它们无声的尖叫被紧紧封存在层层丝绢之中，令人窒息，仿佛此地的看守者觉得这种表情格外悦目或有趣。</p>\n</div>\n<p>空地中央闪烁的装饰水池四周，环绕着由叠砌石块建成的古老石质神龛；西北侧低矮山脊边缘则有一道优美的水瀑轻柔倾泻，注入池中，又在南侧以一道狭窄溪流流出。</p>\n<p>池水深20尺，但水面相对平静——角色只要成功通过一次@Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim]检定，便能游过水池。南侧小溪仅2尺深，可涉水而过，视为困难地形。此溪流本身具有季节性——入夏稍晚时，涓涓细瀑会变成真正的瀑布，溪流也会变宽，最终向南流入名为文业王左眼的洼地，之后再排入地下蓄水层。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>耳语蛛网神社的守卫者是半打被称为algriever的灵体——外形似蜘蛛、自封为此类遗忘神社的管理者。algriever并不邪恶，但它们会迅速防卫神社免遭闯入者侵犯；四处散落的大量被蛛网裹覆的骨骸与尸体便是明证。即便如此，它们也不会一见面就立刻攻击。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.Ohk6Up1PvXsIC9LA]{The Algrievers Emerge}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>algriever一注意到PC们，便从周围林地现身，攀上水池东西两侧的六座岩石神龛，与PC们对话。离PC们最近的那只algriever用柔和而文雅的声音开口。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“你们擅闯圣地。你们的族类将此神社弃置给了我们。你们又凭何宣称你们有权归来？”</p>\n</div>\n<p>algriever会听PC们的回答，但对于任何索要丝线的请求都反应僵硬，并告知PC们：既然他们已来到此处，就不能在未履行适当的仪式与祈祷、献给“你们已经遗忘之人”之前离开。此神社最初奉祀@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{大狐女}，尽管那已是数百年前的往事，algriever依旧尊崇这位女神。若PC们自己不这么做，它们就会命令PC们为农业女神举行一次茶道——见下文“敬奉神社”。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-algriever.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">事件5：冬日香料茶</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">严峻11</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E6fuG6L5VyWMvz08]{Algrievers (6)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>若PC们拒绝，或若他们攻击、或试图从周围区域采集蛛丝，algriever便会愤怒嘶鸣并发动攻击。它们会战斗至死，但并不打算杀死PC们，而是试图将他们活捉，以便让他们忏悔并献上祈祷。注意：虽然杀死algriever能让PC们轻松采集到所需蛛丝，但他们将失去在本次遭遇中赚取胜利点数的机会。</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>敬奉神社：</strong>你不需要让玩家完整地把整场茶道都演出来以敬奉神社，尽管某些团体会乐于扮演整段场景。若你的团体偏好这种更长的演出，你应把这当作机会，让玩家运用至今对茶文化所学到的内容；若他们呈现仪式的表现尤其令人难忘，你可以将本次遭遇中赚取胜利点数所需的DC降低2点。</p>\n<p>为判定展示的成功程度，让每位玩家说明其角色会如何恰当地敬奉神社，然后让他们用合适的技能进行一次DC 28的技能检定，以赚取胜利点数。若PC们在未被algriever提示的情况下就选择进行此项服务，则这些检定获得+2环境加值；但若PC们与algriever交战后被俘、被迫进行仪式，则改为承受–2环境减值。对于想向神社祈祷或正确执行茶道的PC而言，@Check[religion|dc:28]或@Check[tea-lore|dc:28]是最显而易见的选择。@Check[diplomacy|dc:28]可用于争取algriever的配合，@Check[performance|dc:28]可用于为茶道增色，而施法者可按需使用@Check[arcana|dc:28]、@Check[nature|dc:28]或@Check[occultism|dc:28]。</p>\n<p>algriever会欣赏执行得当的仪式，但并不强求。即便PC们在此完全没能赚取任何胜利点数，只要algriever相信他们已尽了全力，便会允许PC们采集所需蛛丝并和平离开。若PC们获得至少3点胜利点数，algriever会因这场仪式深受触动，赠予至多6名自愿的PC一枚<em>朝圣御守</em>。在本次冒险的剩余部分，algriever不会再把此御守赠予其他人；因此若PC们获得此奖励，只要他们遵守信奉大狐女的训令与禁忌，便能一直保有它。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们获得至少1点胜利点数，给予60 XP；若获得最多的4点胜利点数，则给予80 XP。若他们以非暴力方式解决本次遭遇，也按在战斗中击败algriever的标准给予XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 5: Spiced Tea of Winter</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>A week after Ren Mei Li sends the PCs to restore the apple grove (and likely a few days after the PCs investigate the first murder), the jorogumo returns to Willowshore. She thanks the PCs for their work but is more delighted at the news that the four khravgodons are dead than to hear about the restoration work that has begun on the grove. While her demeanor is as courteous as ever, there’s an intensity to her manner that she never showed before. The silvery sheen over her eyes is more pronounced, and the tips of her fangs are visible when she speaks.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“You come to the fourth season, and to the most revealing task. The ritual of winter requires providing a spiced tea for the people, signifying the steward’s ability to provide warmth, sustenance, and safety throughout the season’s cold and hungry nights. It’s best to use fine tea for such an occasion, yet even the finest tea can be improved by filtering it through the most delicate of webbing.</p>\n  <p>“The caretakers of Whisperweb Shrine to the northwest provide such fine silk, the texture and weave are perfect for the straining of delicate teas. They might not be what you are accustomed to, but provide them with a taste of the teas you seek to present, and you should be able to secure their favor. I advise against simply taking from them what you need, but your choices, as always, remain your own.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>This time, she offers the cloisonne ball depicting the fruit platter, while holding back one final ornament, which shows a steaming cauldron glowing against a backdrop of white snowflakes, or perhaps spiderwebs. Then, she once again bids the party farewell and promises to return in one week to sample the teas strained through spidersilk gathered from Whisperweb Shrine.</p>\n<p>None in Willowshore know the name “Whisperweb Shrine,” for in their time a century ago, the site was without a name at all. Instead, it was known only as a strange, forgotten shrine that predated the modern township. If the PCs ask around Karahai or speak to a local like Lo Kuon, they can confirm that the old shrine located a few days travel north of Willowshore has been known as Whisperweb for as long as they can remember, when, in fact, the site gained that name only a few years after Willowshore was pulled into the mindscape.</p>\n<p><strong>Traveling to the Shrine:</strong> The journey to the shrine, which lies a dozen miles north of where the trail leads off the map, is uneventful, though an ominous hush descends upon the land as the PCs draw close. Read or paraphrase the following as the PCs approach the actual location.</p>\n<p>Use the Whisperweb Shrine map for this encounter.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The winding path opens here into an idyllic clearing, at the heart of which shines an achingly beautiful pond. Ornaments hang from tree branches overhead: paper lanterns, gilt masks, braids of woven silk, and, hung among the rest with equal prominence, the mummified corpses of animals and more than a few people. Their silent screams are preserved in tight, suffocating layers of silk, as though the keepers of this place found that expression particularly pleasing or amusing.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The ornamental pool that glimmers in the middle of the clearing is surrounded by old stone shrines built out of stacked stones, while a beautiful cascade of water runs softly over the edge of a low ridge to the northwest to fill the pool, flowing back out to the south in a narrow creek.</p>\n<p>The pool is 20 feet deep, but the waters are relatively calm—a character can Swim the pool with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:10|traits:move,skill,action:swim|name:Swim] check. The creek to the south is only 2 feet deep and can be waded through as difficult terrain. The creek itself is seasonal—later in the summer, the trickling cascade turns into a proper waterfall and the stream widens, with the water eventually flowing south into the hollow known as the Left Eye of Fumeiyoshi before draining into underground reservoirs.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The guardians of Whisperweb Shrine are a half-dozen spirits known as algrievers—spider-like self-appointed custodians of forgotten shrines like this one. While not evil, the algrievers are quick to defend their shrine from intruders, as the large amount of web-shrouded bones and bodies that lie about the place testify. Still, they don’t attack on sight.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.Ohk6Up1PvXsIC9LA]{The Algrievers Emerge}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>As soon as they notice the PCs, the algrievers emerge from the surrounding woods and clamber up onto the six rock shrines to the east and west of the pool to address the PCs. The algriever closest to the PCs speaks in a soft, eloquent voice.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“You intrude upon sacred ground. Your kind abandoned this shrine to us. By what right do you claim such a return?”</p>\n</div>\n<p>The algrievers listen to the PCs’ responses but react stiffly to any request for them to give over some of their silk, instead informing the PCs that, now that they’ve arrived, they can’t be allowed to leave before they perform proper rites and prayers to “those you have forgotten.” This shrine was originally devoted to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.M3eb94Nd6uXti2IK]{Daikitsu}, and while that was many centuries ago now, the algrievers still honor the goddess. If the PCs don’t do so themselves, they’re ordered to perform a tea ceremony in memory of the goddess of agriculture—see Honoring the Shrine below.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-algriever.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Event 5: Spiced Tea of Winter</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 11</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.E6fuG6L5VyWMvz08]{Algrievers (6)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If the PCs refuse, or if they attack or attempt to harvest silk from the surrounding area, the algrievers hiss in fury and attack. They fight to the death but don’t seek to kill the PCs, instead working to trap them alive so that they can repent and offer prayers. Note that while killing the algrievers allows the PCs to gather the silk they need with ease, they won’t have a chance to earn Victory Points in this encounter.</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Honoring the Shrine:</strong> You don’t need to have the players roleplay the entire tea ceremony to honor the shrine, although some groups will enjoy the chance to roleplay the scene out. If your group prefers such an extended scene, you should use this as an opportunity to give the players a chance to build on what they’ve learned so far about tea culture, and if they do a particularly memorable job at presenting the ceremony, feel free to reduce the DCs needed to earn Victory Points in this encounter by 2.</p>\n<p>In order to determine how successful the display is, ask each player what their character does to properly honor the shrine, then have them attempt a DC 28 skill check with an appropriate skill to earn Victory Points. If the PCs chose to perform this service without being prompted by the algrievers, they gain a +2 circumstance bonus to these checks, but if the PCs fought the algrievers and were captured and are forced to perform the ceremony, they take a –2 circumstance penalty instead. @Check[religion|dc:28] or @Check[tea-lore|dc:28] are the most obvious choices here for PCs who wish to pray to the shrine or to perform the tea ceremony correctly. @Check[diplomacy|dc:28] can be used to secure the algrievers’ cooperation, @Check[performance|dc:28] can be used to supplement the tea ceremony, and magic users can employ @Check[arcana|dc:28], @Check[nature|dc:28], or @Check[occultism|dc:28] as needed.</p>\n<p>The algrievers appreciate a well-performed ceremony but don’t require it. Even if the PCs completely fail to earn any Victory Points here, as long as the algrievers believe that they did their best, they’ll allow the PCs to harvest the silk they desire and leave in peace. If the PCs earned at least 3 Victory Points, the algrievers are moved enough by the rite to give up to 6 willing PCs a <em>Pilgrim’s Ward</em>. The algrievers won’t be giving anyone else this ward for the remainder of this adventure, so if the PCs earn this reward, they’ll retain it as long as they obey the edicts and anathemas of worshipping Daikitsu.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 60 XP if they earn at least 1 Victory Point, or 80 XP if they earn the maximum of 4 Victory Points. Grant them XP as if they’d defeated the algrievers in combat if they resolve this encounter without violence.</p>"
            },
            "Event 4. The First Murder": {
              "name": "事件4：第一桩谋杀 Event 4. The First Murder",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件4：第一起谋杀</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>谋杀开始</h1>\n  <p>本章呈现三起谋杀案供PC调查；你也可以按需增加更多，但PC很可能在那之前就已掌握解决方案。三名受害者都是柳岸镇的特定NPC。如果这些NPC中的任何一位已被杀害，或你觉得他们的死亡会过度扰乱你这段特定的<em>鬼季</em>故事，请以其他NPC替代。</p>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 data-no-toc>搜寻线索</h2>\n\n    <ul class=\"traits\">\n      <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">秘密</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p class=\"no-indent\">你花费10分钟调查一具尸体、一件证物，或与谋杀有关的地点（例如案发现场本身），或花费2小时从潜在目击者处搜集信息。随后，你尝试进行调查之“搜寻线索”条目中列出的检定之一。拥有调查员职业的PC在这么做时可以使用追查方向，以获得该能力对检定的加值，并且可以使用Clue In来协助他人搜寻线索。</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong> 你发现轻微、中等与重大线索。</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> 你得知轻微与中等线索。</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong> 你得知轻微线索。</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong> 你得知错误线索，并相信它是一条轻微线索。</p>\n  </section>\n</aside>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}会在PC拜访苹果园并与khravgodons战斗期间的某个时刻夺取他的第一名受害者，因此修复果园的实际工作很可能会与他们对这起罪行的调查同步进行。</p>\n<p>当这起谋杀发生之时（以及之后的连环杀戮发生时），和善保会通过被腐化的柳岸镇思维空间中的一扇传送门，现身于柳岸镇中他庄园的废墟——在本章结束之前，PC既无法进入也无法知晓这扇传送门的存在。他会在夜间出现，然后施放@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate}，瞬间出现在他曾到访过的地点，并把抵达时间掐在他希望所选目标独处之时，以确保能出其不意。暴行完成后，他会飞回庄园废墟，并穿过传送门返回被腐化的柳岸镇思维空间，不留下任何可追踪的痕迹。</p>\n<p>第一名受害者是<strong>大野和马</strong>（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w19downtownw00]{柳岸镇镇区}）。和善保之所以选择他，一方面是因为他对几个月前那场《织水者纪事》演出的导演处理方式耿耿于怀（那是在总督尝试仪式之前），另一方面则是因为他担心大野可能向PC提供有用信息。善保通过translocate进入大野的房间，在他伏案写作时将其杀害，夺走他的笔记本以防PC得到它，随后砸穿建筑离开并飞回废弃庄园的传送门。</p>\n<p>大野的尸体在PC返回柳岸镇前不久，于七彩鸣莺的私人办公室中被发现，因此PC将会看到仍在为此事喧嚣并震惊的城镇。门是锁着的，锁也未被破坏。一面纸墙从内向外被砸开，破碎的框架内侧留有血迹斑斑的涂抹痕。洞口大得足以让一名人类通过。没有搏斗迹象。尸体周围血泊遍布，他倒在写字桌旁的地上，仿佛只是没起身也没做出任何反应就从椅子上跌落一般。</p>\n<p>这起谋杀的消息传开后，柳岸镇的人民哀悼这位备受爱戴的导演之死，并向PC寻求答案。如“谋杀开始”边栏所述，PC可以通过“搜寻线索”这一探索活动来调查这些谋杀案。之后还会发生更多谋杀（@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event6thesec00]{事件6}与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event8thethi00]{事件8}），每一起都和这次一样，提供一个可供调查的案发现场，以及一些事件特有的调查内容。除这些事件特有的调查外，PC还可以检查遗骸以确定死因——三具尸体都共享一些可进一步调查的相似线索（他们消瘦的身形、他们失去的眼睛，以及他们手腕上的奇怪符文）。这四项额外调查的细节可在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{此处}找到，与和善保的yohoi NPC数据并列。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>案发现场</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-theendlessshore.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Endless Shore Manuscript\" alt=\"a blood-spattered manuscript\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-theendlessshore.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>搜寻线索</strong> 调查； @Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>轻微</strong> 凶手平静地进入案发现场，没有损坏任何东西，但离开时却只是直接砸穿脆弱的纸门，从而在门外庭院处的房间之外不留下任何足迹。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>中等</strong> 靠着被砸开处附近墙边的一只箱子上留有血手印；箱内是一批对开本，收录了大野最喜爱的剧作之批注本。书看上去被某个满手鲜血的人翻找过。成功进行一次@Check[theater-lore|dc:25]或@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:25]检定后，PC会注意到大野常规上演的剧目中少了一部：《织水者纪事》。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>重大</strong> PC会自动意识到《织水者纪事》不见了。此外，PC还发现了一叠掉到大野写字桌后面的纸张——服装草图与《无尽之岸》的剧本草稿；这出戏讲述柳岸镇在思维空间中的时光，灵感来自PC在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event1bright00]{事件1 - 明春鸟}中为演出所做的表演。虽然这份草稿与大野之死无关，但它是一件重要的个人信物，可在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15thesilenceds00]{第13章}中用来解放大野的灵魂。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>错误线索</strong> 众所周知，大野在政治上非常亲近北岭人，并且常对南岸人冷嘲热讽——也许凶手是某个被他冒犯的南岸人，决定亲自动手解决他？</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>《织水者纪事》</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>搜寻线索</strong> 调查； @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>轻微</strong> 这出戏讲述一名僧侣学会了用水织布，随后卷入一场复杂阴谋，其中包括争吵不休的丝绸商人为争夺一位反复无常的总督的青睐而明争暗斗。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>中等</strong> 大野传统上会在每个夏至执导此剧的新版本，但今年没有——很可能是由于柳岸镇的诅咒相关事件所致。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>重大</strong> 大野今年其实已开始筹备制作，但当谣言传出他正在改编该剧，使其成为对总督和善保的露骨批判时，总督在春末拜访了大野；此后，关于当年夏季该剧制作的一切讨论都归于沉寂。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>错误线索</strong> 大野已经对这出戏失去兴趣，并把它从常规轮换中撤下；因此它从他的藏书中消失并不值得大惊小怪。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>访谈</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>搜寻线索</strong> 搜集信息； @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>轻微</strong> 大野最后一次被人见到是在他遇害当晚黄昏前不久：他在晚饭后到乐天河童浴场泡澡。他在那儿与华德哥简短交谈，当时看起来心情不错。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>中等</strong> 大野对根据PC在明春鸟期间的表演（内容涉及他们在思维空间中的经历）创作一出新戏感到兴奋，并觉得自己刚刚在灵感上有所突破。他一离开浴场就说要直接回剧院，把那一闪而过的灵感在消散前立刻写下来。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>重大</strong> 虽然大野没有明显的仇敌，但在春季最后一天前几周，总督和善曾去拜访他一次，有人声称听见了激烈争吵……之后大野显得格外沮丧与挫败。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>错误线索</strong> 大野常以尖刻评语把拙劣演员说到落泪——也许凶手是某个被冷落或怀恨在心的演员？</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC在调查中第一次找到与和善保有关的联系，或发现重要的个人信物时，给予80 XP。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>案发现场疑难排解</h2>\n  <p>谋杀案调查中一些潜在的复杂情况可按如下方式处理。</p>\n  <p><strong>牵涉任美丽：</strong>如果PC让任美丽参与调查，这名jorogumo对提供援助兴趣不大，并指出若他们要成为可靠的柳岸镇管事，处理这类犯罪与事件本就应是职责之一。尽管如此，她理解PC的担忧；若玩家在案情上卡住，也可用她来帮助玩家把线索串起来。如果她察觉PC把她当作嫌疑人，她会责备他们疑神疑鬼，并建议他们别被“错误的逻辑跳跃”分散注意力。</p>\n  <p><strong>与死者交谈：</strong>在<em>鬼季</em>中，PC不太可能获得死者交谈、call spirit或类似能与亡者交谈的魔法；但如果他们确实有，这些方法应当能提供与调查相同的信息。当被要求描述凶手时，这些尸体更会强调凶手树根般的身体、从他眼中飞出的蝴蝶，以及他那折断而修长的手臂；但如果你愿意，他们也可以指出凶手是总督和善保的扭曲版本。</p>\n  <p><strong>监视庄园：</strong>一旦PC怀疑和善保以某种方式牵涉谋杀，他们可能会选择调查他的庄园。没有<em>Fang and Key</em>，他们无法进入修复后的庄园，而在废墟结构中也找不到他存在的新线索。PC可能决定监视庄园。若他们在夜间这么做，由你裁定，PC也许能在谋杀发生前（或之后）与和善保正面冲突，此时他会与PC战斗。与和善保的冲突是一场中等11级遭遇。若PC杀死他，他会在被腐化的柳岸镇思维空间中重新成形，必须再次面对，如第13章所述；但他将不会再回到柳岸镇继续行凶。以这种方式每阻止一场潜在谋杀，给予PC 80 XP。</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 4: The First Murder</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h1>The Murders Begin</h1>\n  <p>Three murders are presented in this chapter for the PCs to investigate; you can add more if you wish, but it’s likely the PCs will have a solution at hand before then. All three of the victims are specific NPCs from Willowshore. If any of these NPCs have already been slain, or if you feel that their deaths would overly derail your specific <em>Season of Ghosts</em> story, substitute a different NPC in their place.</p>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 data-no-toc>Search for Clues</h2>\n\n    <ul class=\"traits\">\n      <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">Secret</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p class=\"no-indent\">You spend 10 minutes Investigating a body, piece of evidence, or location associated with the murder (such as the Scene of the Crime itself), or spend 2 hours Gathering Information from potential witnesses. You then attempt one of the checks listed in the investigation’s Search For Clues entry. A PC with the investigator class can use Pursue a Lead when they do so to gain that ability’s bonus to their check and can use Clue In to aid others in Searching for Clues.</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> You discover minor, moderate, and major clues.</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> You learn the minor and moderate clues.</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> You learn the minor clues.</p>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> You learn the false lead and believe it to be a minor clue.</p>\n  </section>\n</aside>\n<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} claims his first victim at some point while the PCs are visiting the apple grove and fighting khravgodons, so the actual work of restoring the grove will likely take place alongside their investigation of this crime.</p>\n<p>When the time comes for this murder to occur (and again when subsequent slayings take place), Heh Shan-Bao uses a portal from the corrupted Willowshore mindscape to emerge into the ruins of his manor in Willowshore itself—a portal the PCs won’t be able to access or even know about until the end of this chapter. He emerges at night, then uses @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate} to instantly appear at a location he has visited before, timing his arrival for when he hopes his chosen target is alone to ensure he catches them by surprise. After his violent work is done, he returns to the manor ruins via flight and passes back through the portal to the corrupted Willowshore mindscape, leaving nothing to track in his wake.</p>\n<p>This first victim is <strong>Kazuma Oono</strong> (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog02willow.JournalEntryPage.02w19downtownw00]{Downtown Willowshore}), whom Heh Shan-Bao targets because he’s bitter about how the director handled a performance of The Chronicle of the Water-Weaver a few months before the governor attempted his ritual, but also because he’s afraid Oono might be able to provide useful information to the PCs. Shan-Bao entered Oono’s room via translocate, killed him as he worked at his writing desk, seized his notebook to prevent the PCs from obtaining it, and then smashed out of the building before flying back to the portal in the ruined manor.</p>\n<p>Oono’s body is discovered in his private office at the Seven-Colored Songbird shortly before the PCs return to Willowshore, so they’ll be greeted with a town still abuzz and shocked at the event. The door was locked, and the lock is undisturbed. A paper wall has been smashed outward from within, and the inner surface of the splintered framework is marked with bloodstained smears. The hole is easily large enough for a human to have passed through. There are no signs of struggle. Copious amounts of blood surround the body, which lies on the floor next to a writing desk as if he’d simply fallen out of his chair without standing or otherwise responding to his attacker.</p>\n<p>After word spreads of this murder, the people of Willowshore mourn the loss of the beloved director and look to the PCs for answers. As noted in the The Murders Begin sidebar, the PCs can investigate these murders via the Search for Clues exploration activity. Additional murders will occur later (@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event6thesec00]{Event 6} and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event8thethi00]{Event 8}), each of which, like this one, presents a scene of the crime to investigate, along with a few other event-specific investigations. In addition to these event-specific investigations, the PCs can examine the remains for a cause of death—all three bodies share similar clues that can be further investigated (their emaciated frames, their missing eyes, and strange runes on their wrists). Details on these four additional investigations can be found @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Here}, alongside Hen Shan-Bao’s yohoi NPC statistics.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Scene of the Crime</h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-theendlessshore.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Endless Shore Manuscript\" alt=\"a blood-spattered manuscript\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-theendlessshore.webp')\" />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Search for Clues</strong> Investigate; @Check[perception|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Minor</strong> The killer entered the crime scene calmly, without damaging anything, but they exited by simply smashing through the fragile paper doorway, leaving no tracks outside of the room in the courtyard beyond.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Moderate</strong> A trunk that rests against a wall near the smashed open section has bloody handprints on it; within lies a collection of folios that contain Oono’s annotated copies of his favorite plays. The books appear to have been pawed through by someone with blood-soaked hands. With a successful @Check[theater-lore|dc:25] or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:25] check, a PC notes that one play from Oono’s regular cycle of offerings is missing: The Chronicle of the Water-Weaver.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Major</strong> The PC automatically realizes The Chronicle of the Water-Weaver is missing. In addition, the PC discovers a sheaf of pages that fell behind Oono’s writing desk—costume sketches and a draft script for The Endless Shore, a play about Willowshore’s time in the mindscape inspired by the performances the PCs put on for @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog14thepri.JournalEntryPage.14event1bright00]{Event 1 - Bright Spring Bird}. While this draft manuscript has no relevance to Oono’s murder, it serves as a significant personal token that can be used to free Oono’s soul in @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15thesilenceds00]{Chapter 13}.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>False Lead</strong> Oono was known to be very allied with Northridge politically and often had snarky remarks about Southbankers—perhaps the killer was someone from Southbank who was insulted by him and decided to take matters into their own hands?</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>The Chronicle of the Water-Weaver</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Search for Clues</strong> Investigate; @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:22|traits:concentrate,secret,action:investigate|name:Investigate]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Minor</strong> This play is about a monk who learned how to weave cloth from water, then became embroiled in a complex plot involving bickering silk traders vying for the attentions of a fickle governor.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Moderate</strong> Oono traditionally directed a new version of this play at every summer solstice, but he didn’t this year—likely due to the events surrounding the Willowshore curse.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Major</strong> Oono was starting this year’s production, but when rumors spread that he was altering the play to make it a blatant critique of Governor Heh Shan-Bao, the governor paid Oono a visit at the end of spring, and all discussion of that summer’s production of the play went silent thereafter.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>False Lead</strong> This play is one that Oono had lost interest in and took out of his regular rotation; it being missing from his collection is thus unremarkable.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Interviews</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Search for Clues</strong> Gather Information; @Check[diplomacy|dc:22|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Minor</strong> Oono was last seen shortly before dusk on the night he was killed, when he stopped by the Happy Kappa bathhouse for a post-dinner soak. He spoke briefly to Hua De-ge while he was there and seemed to be in good spirits at the time.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Moderate</strong> Oono was excited about writing a new play based on the PCs’ performance during the Bright Spring Bird earlier regarding their time spent in the mindscape, and he felt that he’d just had a breakthrough in his inspiration. As soon as he left the bathhouse, he said he was going straight back to the theater to write down his sudden flash of ideas before they evaporated.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Major</strong> While Oono didn’t have any obvious enemies, there was that time a few weeks before the last day of spring that Governor Heh paid him a visit, and folks reported hearing a heated argument... after which Oono seemed particularly depressed and frustrated.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>False Lead</strong> Oono often reduced bad actors to tears with his cutting remarks—perhaps the murderer was a spurned or vengeful actor?</p>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP the first time they either find links to Heh Shan-Bao or discover the significant personal token during their investigation.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>Murder Scene Troubleshooting</h2>\n  <p>Some potential complications in the murder investigations can be handled as follows.</p>\n  <p><strong>Involving Ren Mei Li:</strong> If the PCs involve Ren Mei Li in their investigations, the jorogumo has little interest in providing aid, noting that if they’re to be reliable stewards of Willowshore, dealing with crimes and events like these will be part of their duties. Still, she’s sympathetic to the PCs’ concerns and can be used to help the players connect some dots if they’re struggling with the case. If she gets the idea that the PCs consider her as a suspect, she chides them for being paranoid and suggests they don’t get distracted by “faulty leaps of logic.”</p>\n  <p><strong>Speaking to the Dead:</strong> It’s unlikely for a PC in <em>Season of Ghosts</em> to have access to talking corpse, call spirit, or similar magic that lets them speak to the dead, but if they do, these methods should give the same information that investigations could. Asked to describe their killer, these corpses focus more on the killer’s rootlike body, the butterflies that come from his eyes, and his long broken arms, but they can also identify the killer as a distorted version of Governor Heh Shan-Bao if you wish.</p>\n  <p><strong>Staking Out the Manor:</strong> Once the PCs suspect Heh Shan-Bao is somehow involved in the murders, they might choose to investigate his manor. Without the <em>Fang and Key</em>, they won’t be able to enter the restored manor, and no new clues of his presence can be found in the ruined structure. The PCs might decide to stake out the manor. If they do so at night, at your discretion, the PCs might be able to confront Heh Shan-Bao before (or after) a murder, in which case he fights the PCs. A conflict with Heh Shan-Bao is a Moderate 11 encounter. If the PCs slay him, he re-forms in the corrupted Willowshore mindscape and must be confronted again, as detailed in Chapter 13, but he won’t return to Willowshore to murder again. Grant the PCs 80 XP for each potential murder prevented in this way.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "Event 3. Fall's Sweet Fruits": {
              "name": "事件 3：秋之甘果 Event 3. Fall's Sweet Fruits",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件 3：秋日甜果</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这片苹果园位于柳岸镇以南20英里处，是许多镇民熟知的地方，长期以来也一直享用着这里的果实。然而今天，这座果园已经完全荒芜蔓生。苹果树仍在此茁壮生长，果实依旧香甜可口，但在过去七年里，这里一直是一个危险怪物团体的巢穴。</p>\n<p>本次遭遇使用“蔓生的苹果园”地图。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>曾经美丽的空地上长着数十棵优质苹果树，如今却被杂草与荆棘纠结成的茂密乱丛所吞没。零星的苹果树仍立在矮丛环境中，但还有同样醒目的，是某种体型如大象之物留下的宽阔兽径——小径两侧散落着无数巨大蜘蛛被踩碎、啃咬后的残骸。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>并非所有栖居在神门的生物都将络新妇及其蜘蛛视作恐惧之物。对某些掠食者而言，例如魁梧的克拉夫戈登，蜘蛛是格外美味的一餐，而甲壳在齿间嘎吱作响的触感更是令人愉悦。不是一只，而是四只这种超大负鼠搬进了这片蔓生的苹果园，并将整片区域都视为自己的领地。每当这些掠食者迁入，络新妇采取行动也只是时间问题。对这四只而言，那行动便通过PCs的形式体现出来。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/khravgodon.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">事件 3：秋日甜果</span> <span class=\"keepme\">中等 11</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.93ScUkuBzeyh31bL]{克拉夫戈登（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>虽然脾气暴躁的克拉夫戈登更偏爱蜘蛛肉的腥香以及其毒腺，但这些巨型动物也不会犹豫攻击PCs，它们会从矮丛环境中猛然蹿出发动攻击，并用隐匿来进行先攻。一只克拉夫戈登的生命值降到40点以下时会试图逃跑，但最终会回到此地夺回领地。若PCs能与这些动物建立某种交流方式，他们或许能谈成协议并说服这些生物迁往别处；否则，在开始修复果园的工作之前，必须杀死这四只生物。</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.m7W9DIYrYhVAzM6F]{一名早已死去的冒险者的遗骸} <br />\n  一名角色若花费1小时搜索果园，便会发现一名早已死去的冒险者几乎被完全掩埋的遗骸。如今他只剩下一具骷髅，但仍穿着他那标志性的<em>龙龟甲</em>，并携带着一根沉重的钢制圆筒——一门<em>龙龟炮</em>。一旦PCs开始着手修复果园，他们将自动发现这份宝藏。\n</p>\n<p><strong>修复果园：</strong>PCs不需要亲自完成修复苹果园的任务，这一过程也不必由他们来做，但任美璃交给他们的这项任务之初步规划，必须在他们继续进行下一场仪式之前完成。为了在秋季苹果成熟时判定他们的规划有多成功，询问每位玩家其角色为协助修复果园做了什么，然后让他们以合适技能进行DC 28的技能检定来获得胜利点数。@Check[nature|dc:28] 对希望运用植物知识（无论是否借助原初魔法）来帮助地点恢复的PCs而言是最显而易见的选择，但其他魔法同样可能有帮助；在这种情况下，PC可以按需进行一次@Check[arcana|dc:28]、@Check[occultism|dc:28]或@Check[religion|dc:28]检定。@Check[diplomacy|dc:28] 可用于从柳岸镇招募工人。@Check[farming-lore|dc:28] 可用于修枝除草，确保苹果树有最佳的生长机会。@Check[survival|dc:28] 可用于设置陷阱与防护，防止食腐动物伤害树木。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PCs获得至少1点胜利点数，则给予60 XP；若获得最多的4点胜利点数，则给予80 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 3: Fall's Sweet Fruits</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The apple grove in question lies 20 miles south of Willowshore and is a place that many townsfolk know well and have long enjoyed the fruits of. Today, though, the grove is completely overgrown. Apple trees still thrive here, and their fruit remains delicious, but for the past seven years, the area has been the lair of a group of dangerous monsters.</p>\n<p>Use the Overgrown Apple Grove map for this encounter.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Where once stood a beautiful clearing in which grew dozens of fine apple trees, now creeps an overgrown tangle of weeds and brambles. Here and there, apple trees still stand among the undergrowth, but wide animal trails left by something the size of an elephant do as well-trails lined with the crunched and chewed remnants of countless enormous spiders.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Not every creature that dwells in Shenmen sees the jorogumo and their spiders as objects of fear. To certain predators, such as the hulking khravgodon, spiders make for a particularly delicious meal, and the sensation of chitin crunching between teeth is a delight. Not one but four of these oversized opossums have moved into this overgrown apple grove, and they consider the entire region part of their territory. Whenever these predators move in, it's only a matter of time before the jorogumo take action. In the case of these four, that action manifests in the form of the PCs.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/khravgodon.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Event 3: Fall's Sweet Fruits</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 11</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.93ScUkuBzeyh31bL]{Khravgodons (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>While the ill-tempered khravgodons prefer the tang of spider meat and their poison glands, the giant animals won't hesitate to attack the PCs as well, lurching from the undergrowth to attack and using Stealth for initiative. A khravgodon reduced to fewer than 40 Hit Points attempts to flee but will eventually return to the area to reclaim its territory. If the PCs can establish a method of communication with the animals, they might be able to work out a deal and convince the creatures to relocate elsewhere, but otherwise, before work on restoring the grove can begin, the four creatures must be slain.</p>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.m7W9DIYrYhVAzM6F]{Remains of a Long-Dead Adventurer} <br />\n  A character who spends 1 hour Searching the grove uncovers the almost entirely overgrown remains of a long-dead adventurer. Little more than a skeleton now, he still wears his distinctive <em>dragon turtle armor</em> and carries a heavy steel cylinder-a <em>dragon turtle artillery</em>. The PCs automatically discover this treasure once they begin work on restoring the grove.\n</p>\n<p><strong>Restoring the Grove:</strong> The PCs don't need to complete the task of restoring the apple grove, nor does the process need to be done by them, but the preliminary planning for the task Ren Mei Li sets them must be done before they can move on to the next rite. To determine how successful their plans are once the apple season begins in autumn, ask each player what their character does to help restore the grove, then have them attempt a DC 28 skill check with an appropriate skill to earn Victory Points. @Check[nature|dc:28] is the most obvious choice here for PCs who wish to use their knowledge of plant life to help the site recover (with or without primal magic), but other magic can help as well, in which case a PC can roll an @Check[arcana|dc:28], @Check[occultism|dc:28], or @Check[religion|dc:28] check, as appropriate. @Check[diplomacy|dc:28] can be used to recruit workers from Willowshore. @Check[farming-lore|dc:28] can be used to prune and weed and ensure the apple trees have the best chance to thrive. @Check[survival|dc:28] can be called upon to set traps and protections to keep scavengers from harming the trees.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 60 XP if they earn at least 1 Victory Point, or 80 XP if they earn the maximum of 4 Victory Points.</p>"
            },
            "Event 2. Fiery Flower Fireworks": {
              "name": "事件 2。火花花烟花 Event 2. Fiery Flower Fireworks",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件2：炽花烟火</span>\n</h2>\n\n<p>\n  接下来交给PC们的任务，是举办一场烟火表演，用以庆祝夏日之美，同时也遵循传统——据说这能吓退恶意的鬼魂与精怪。虽然使用魔法，尤其是诸如幻象场景之类的法术，可以制造出引人入胜的烟火表演，但任美丽希望这场表演来真的——这意味着他们得收集一些稀有植物，以确保烟火炸裂时呈现出传统所要求的、精确无误的炽烈橙色。\n</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-heifengshorn.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hei Feng's Horn\" alt=\"red-petaled flower\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-heifengshorn.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  这种传统配料是“黑风之角”的新鲜花瓣——一种罕见、亮橙色的湿地花卉。虽然这种花在本地区的湿地中零星生长，但数量最多、花朵品质最佳的一大片区域位于月沼；其名源自这些夜间绽放的花在月光照耀下散发出的柔和橙色光辉。PC们并不知道的是，在过去的数十年里，一名名为伊索里（Isori）的纳迦占星师已在此地定居。\n</p>\n<p>\n  从镇子向北出发，穿过废弃村庄与（很可能已重新开垦的）田地，便可抵达月沼；季节性月溪从这些田地间向南流入杜月江。春季时，这条小溪会干涸，但作为一条可供循迹的路线，它仍比杂草丛生的道路更可靠。月沼位于地图边缘以北约6英里处，距柳岸镇以北约18英里。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>寻找花朵：</strong>PC们到达月沼后，可以在白天花8小时寻找一片可用的黑风之角花丛；或在天黑后花1小时（因为那时植物会开花并发出柔光）。此地的装饰不止花朵。青铜与玻璃制的日晷、星盘仪，以及各种透镜与棱镜，悬挂在系于树枝的绳索上；而一串串刻有几何符号与天文公式的大型扁平玻璃珠，也装点着披挂在林地间的绳索。\n</p>\n<p>\n  这些装饰出自一名名为伊索里的维查拉牟尼（vicharamuni）——一种觉醒者纳迦——他在这片沼泽区域栖居了数十年。他喜欢在黑风之角花林间观测苍穹，并用自己漫长一生中收集的各式占星与天文学小玩意装点此处。伊索里大多独来独往，天性并不嗜暴，但若有人闯入他的观测所，他会立刻感到被冒犯——从水中升起，沉静地用发光而聪慧的眼睛注视PC们。\n</p>\n<p>\n  如果PC们一见面就攻击，他会愤怒嘶鸣并还击，但并不特别想把战斗拖得太久。他每回合都会用1个动作在继续战斗前向PC们提出休战。他会尽力避免杀死任何PC，甚至会用诸如breath of life之类的法术救回战斗中倒下的人。若其生命值被削减至少于75点，他便认为最好放弃此地并逃离。\n</p>\n<p>\n  如果PC们不攻击（或接受休战提议），伊索里会向他们致意，并自称为“这片沼泽的守护者”，然后询问他们是谁、来自何方。柳岸镇的回归这一消息令他颇感兴趣——在他眼中，那地方一直只是片废墟，而他也在那里收集到了许多心爱的饰品。\n</p>\n<p>\n  作为苍穹的学者，伊索里最近被其天文与占星仪器捕捉到的不祥征兆所困扰；他想知道PC们是否知晓本地区发生了什么。他也在试图判断，PC们是否可能是他所见“蔓延锁链”的始作俑者——那些锁链如饥饿藤蔓般伸向自然世界——无论是蓄意还是无心。\n</p>\n<p>\n  伊索里所探测到的，PC们或许能猜到，是库加普提的影响。那恶魔的触碰正迅速侵蚀湿地；尽管伊索里并不理解威胁的真实规模，但他确实已注意到这些警告。若PC们向他揭示真相（或至少说服他他们并非罪魁祸首），他会问他们打算如何应对。这场遭遇旨在强调PC们所面临的利害关系，尤其是队伍中任何偏向自然的角色；不过，如果PC们能通过一次成功的@Check[diplomacy|dc:27|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make\n  an Impression]检定来建立印象，使伊索里变得友善或乐于相助（其初始态度为不关心），他会与他们分享一件隐藏的宝物，帮助他们作战。\n</p>\n<p>\n  伊索里不反对PC们采集黑风之角的花瓣——前提是他们尊重环境，不要无谓地破坏植株，也不要采得超过所需。\n</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.SvKWVoIl2CPT1MJZ]{Isori}</span>\n    <span>生物 6</span>\n  </h2>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>财宝：</strong>@UUID[Actor.PYXubF4kQUtM1ZQO]{Isori's Gift} @UUID[Actor.xvM3MRczzVobDx6H]{Tree Hollow} <br /> 若PC们让伊索里变得友善，他会从自己藏在一处不起眼树洞中的储藏里，赠与他们一株<em>千年龙根</em>。若他们让他变得乐于相助，他会把三株都给他们。否则，PC们可以在他的观测所中花费1小时进行搜索，并在一次@Check[perception|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]\n 检定中成功，从而找到这三株千年龙根。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>采收花朵：</strong>一名PC可以尝试一次秘密@Check[crafting|dc:28|traits:secret]、@Check[herbalism-lore|dc:28|traits:secret]、\n  @Check[nature|dc:28|traits:secret]或@Check[survival|dc:28|traits:secret]检定来采集花瓣；其他PC可以使用上述技能之一，以DC 20的检定来援助该检定。若大成功，采下的花瓣特别适合用于烟火，PC们在之后制作烟火并赢得胜利点数的检定中获得+2环境加值；但若失败，他们在这些检定中承受–2环境减值（若大失败则为–4环境减值）。\n</p>\n<p>\n  如果PC们已让伊索里至少变得友善，他会提供自己的采收建议，使所有采收的DC降低4点。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>制作烟火：</strong>当PC们返回柳岸镇后，下一步便是制作足够的烟火以呈现一场得体的表演。与前一个事件相同，当任美丽到场后，你不必让玩家把整场表演完整地角色扮演出来。为判定表演的成功程度，询问每位玩家其角色会做什么来确保烟火正常运作，然后让他们以合适的技能尝试一次DC 28的技能检定来获得胜利点数。对想亲手搭建烟火的PC而言，@Check[crafting|dc:28]是最显而易见的选择；而希望用魔法增强表演的人，则可视情况掷@Check[arcana|dc:28]、@Check[nature|dc:28]、@Check[occultism|dc:28]或@Check[religion|dc:28]检定。@Check[performance|dc:28]也很适合那些想确保表演在艺术层面顺利引爆的人——通过把握何时、如何发射这场奇观。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>表演之后：</strong>当最后一枚烟火绽放，聚集的镇民便各自散回家中，任美丽再次走近PC们。与先前一样，她热切地称赞PC们的努力，然后再度从发间摘下一枚银簪。这一枚银簪上装饰着两件掐丝珐琅饰物，垂挂在彩色丝绦上，并带着苹果的香气。\n</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>\n    “我祝贺你们呈现了如此壮丽的表演，但我知道你们急于得知下一项任务。秋之甘果象征管事者愿意为即将到来的寒冬困厄收集资源并明智地储藏。我知道——或许你们也知道——南边不远处有一片果园，生长着格外娇嫩的苹果；但此地荒废已久，我担心那果园如今可能成了某种……对我这一类存在而言尤其不讨喜之物的巢穴。距离苹果成熟尚有数月，但若你们现在就开始恢复这片果园的工作，待到秋天，你们定会收获真正的甜美果实！而若那令人不快的东西能受到惩罚，那就更好不过了。照旧，我给你们一周时间完成这项任务，祝你们好运！”\n  </p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  任美丽随即消失在银色薄雾中，未再对苹果园里如今可能栖居着什么作出任何警告。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们至少获得1点胜利点数，给予60 XP；若他们获得最高的4点胜利点数，给予80 XP。若他们让伊索里至少变得友善，额外给予40 XP。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 2: Fiery Flower Fireworks</span>\n</h2>\n\n<p>\n  The next task given to the PCs involves putting on a fireworks display intended to celebrate the beauty of summer,\n  but also one that is traditionally said to frighten away malicious ghosts and spirits. While the use of magic,\n  particularly something like illusory scene, can produce a compelling fireworks display, Ren Mei Li wants this\n  display to be the real thing, and that means gathering some rare plants to help make sure the fireworks burst in\n  the exact precise shade of fiery orange that tradition demands.\n</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-heifengshorn.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Hei Feng's Horn\" alt=\"red-petaled flower\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-heifengshorn.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  This traditional ingredient is the fresh petals of Hei Feng’s horn, a rare, bright-orange wetlands flower. While\n  this flower grows sporadically throughout the region’s wetlands, the largest swath with the best flowers grows in\n  abundance in Moon Marsh, so named for the soft orange glow that these night-blooming flowers give under the\n  radiance of moonlight. Unbeknownst to the PCs, in the intervening decades, a naga astrologer named Isori has taken up\n  residence in this area.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Moon Marsh can be reached by traveling north from town, through the abandoned village and (likely recultivated)\n  fields through which the seasonal Moon Creek flows south into the Duyue River. During the spring, this creek runs\n  dry, but it remains a more reliable path to follow than the overgrown road. Moon Marsh lies about 6 miles north of\n  the edge of the map, about 18 miles north of Willowshore.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Finding the Flowers:</strong> Once the PCs reach Moon Marsh, they can spend 8 hours of daylight searching for a serviceable\n  patch of Hei Feng’s horn, or 1 hour after dark (since that’s when the plant blooms and softly glows). The flowers\n  aren’t the only adornments in the area. Bronze and glass sundials, astrolabes, and various lenses and prisms hang\n  from cords tied to overhanging tree branches, while strands of large, flat glass beads inscribed with geometric\n  symbols and astronomical formulas adorn lengths of cord draped around the grove.\n</p>\n<p>\n  These adornments have been placed by a vicharamuni—an awakener naga—named Isori who has dwelt in this part of the\n  marsh for decades. He has grown fond of admiring the heavens amid the grove of Hei Feng’s horns, decorating it\n  with various astrological and astronomical trinkets he has gathered over his long life. Isori mostly keeps to himself\n  and isn’t a naturally violent sort, but he’ll take swift offense at anyone who enters his observatory, rising up from\n  the waters to quietly regard the PCs with his luminous, intelligent eyes.\n</p>\n<p>\n  If the PCs attack on sight, he hisses in anger and fights back, but isn’t particularly interested in continuing\n  the battle for long. He uses an action each round to offer the PCs a truce before continuing to fight. He does his\n  best to avoid killing any of the PCs, and even uses spells like breath of life to save any who fall in battle. If\n  reduced to fewer than 75 HP, he decides it’s best to abandon the area and flees.\n</p>\n<p>\n  If the PCs don’t attack (or accept the offer of a truce) Isori greets them and introduces himself as the “guardian\n  of this swamp” before he asks who they are and where they’re from. News of Willowshore’s return intrigues him—he\n  has only ever known the site as a ruin where he gathered many of his favorite trinkets.\n</p>\n<p>\n  As a scholar of the heavens, Isori has recently been troubled by ominous portents captured by his astronomical and\n  astrological instruments, and he wants to know whether the PCs have any idea what’s happening in the region. He’s\n  also trying to figure out whether they might be responsible, either intentionally or unknowingly, for the\n  “creeping chains” that he has seen reaching for the natural world like hungry vines.\n</p>\n<p>\n  What Isori has detected, as the PCs might surmise, is Kugaptee’s influence. The fiend’s touch has been encroaching\n  upon the wetlands rapidly, and while Isori doesn’t understand the true extent of the threat, he has certainly\n  noticed the warnings. If the PCs reveal the truth to him (or at the very least convince him they’re not the\n  culprits), he asks them what’s to be done about it. This encounter is meant to underscore the stakes for the PCs,\n  particularly any nature-oriented characters in the group, but if the PCs can make Isori friendly or helpful (his\n  initial attitude is indifferent) with a successful @Check[diplomacy|dc:27|traits:action:make-an-impression|name:Make\n  an Impression] check to Make an Impression, he shares with them one of\n  his hidden treasures to aid them in their fight.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Isori has no objection to letting the PCs gather petals of Hei Feng’s horn, provided they do so with respect for\n  the environment, don’t damage the plants unnecessarily, and don’t take more than they need.\n</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.SvKWVoIl2CPT1MJZ]{Isori}</span>\n    <span>Creature 6</span>\n  </h2>\n</section>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.PYXubF4kQUtM1ZQO]{Isori's Gift} @UUID[Actor.xvM3MRczzVobDx6H]{Tree Hollow} <br /> If the PCs make Isori friendly, he’ll offer them a single <em>thousand-year dragonroot</em> from\n  a stash he keeps hidden in an unassuming tree hollow. If they make him helpful, he’ll offer them all three of the roots.\n  Otherwise, the PCs can locate the three thousand-year dragonroots by succeeding at a @Check[perception|dc:30|traits:concentrate,exploration,secret,action:search|name:Search]\n check after spending an hour Searching his observatory.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Harvesting the Flowers:</strong> One PC can attempt a secret @Check[crafting|dc:28|traits:secret], @Check[herbalism-lore|dc:28|traits:secret],\n  @Check[nature|dc:28|traits:secret], or @Check[survival|dc:28|traits:secret] check to\n  gather the petals, and the other PCs can Aid this check with DC 20 checks in one of the above skills. On a\n  critical success, the harvested petals are particularly viable for use in fireworks, and the PCs get a +2 circumstance\n  bonus to their checks later to craft fireworks and earn Victory Points, but on a failure, they take a –2 circumstance\n  penalty to these checks (or a –4 circumstance penalty on a critical failure).\n</p>\n<p>\n  If the PCs have made Isori at least friendly, he provides his own advice on how to harvest the petals, reducing\n  all DCs to harvest by 4.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Crafting the Fireworks:</strong> When the PCs return to Willowshore, the next step is to craft enough fireworks to put on a\n  proper show. As with the previous event, you don’t need to have the players roleplay out the entire display once\n  Ren Mei Li arrives. In order to determine how successful the display is, ask each player what their character does to\n  make sure the fireworks function, then have them attempt a DC 28 skill check with an appropriate skill to earn\n  Victory Points. @Check[crafting|dc:28] is the most obvious choice here for PCs who wish to build the fireworks, but those who\n  seek to bolster the display with magic can roll an @Check[arcana|dc:28], @Check[nature|dc:28], @Check[occultism|dc:28], or\n  @Check[religion|dc:28] check, as appropriate. @Check[performance|dc:28] is a good check to attempt for those who want to make sure that the actual display goes off\n  artistically by knowing when and how to launch the spectacle.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>After the Show:</strong> Once the last firework bursts, the gathered townsfolk disperse back to their homes, and Ren Mei Li\n  once again approaches the PCs. As before, she eagerly compliments the PCs’ efforts before she again plucks a\n  silver pin from her hair. This one is adorned with two cloisonne ornaments on strands of colored silk that carry the\n  scent of apples.\n</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>\n    “I congratulate you on a magnificent display, but I know you are eager to learn of your next task. The Sweet\n    Fruits of Autumn symbolize the steward’s willingness to gather and wisely stockpile resources for the coming\n    hardships of winter. I know, and perhaps you do as well, of a grove of particularly delicate apples that grow\n    not far to the south, but no one has lived here for so long that I fear the grove may have become the home of\n    something... particularly disagreeable to those of my persuasion. We are some months away from apple season, but\n    if you begin the work of restoring this grove now, come autumn, you’ll be rewarded with sweet fruits indeed! And\n    if this disagreeable element can be punished, all the better for it. Again, I give you a week to accomplish this\n    task, and I wish you luck!”\n  </p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  Ren Mei Li then vanishes into the silver mist without further warning about what might now dwell in the apple\n  grove.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 60 XP if they earn at least 1 Victory Point, or 80 XP if they earn the maximum of 4 Victory\n  Points. Grant them an additional 40 XP if they made Isori at least friendly.\n</p>"
            },
            "Event 1. Bright Spring Bird": {
              "name": "事件1：明亮的春鸟 Event 1. Bright Spring Bird",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">事件1：明亮春鸟</span>\n</h2>\n<p>五季宝藏中的第一件是“明亮春鸟”。正如任美璃解释的那样，它将是一场戏剧表演，旨在唤起光明、喜悦，以及对未来执政者统治的乐观期待。表演可以是歌唱、舞蹈、表演，或将所有艺术结合创作而成。</p>\n<p>这第一项仪式给PC们一个机会，去回顾自己在这场战役中的经历对他们意味着什么，这些经历如何影响了他们与柳岸镇的人民的关系，以及在他们回到现实世界之后，这座小镇集体的希望与恐惧如今落在何处。若PC们卡住了，其他镇民可以提供乐于帮助的建议与物资支持；但如果PC们不需要他们帮忙，那么镇民也很乐意配合PC们的艺术构想，并且不去妨碍。</p>\n<p><strong>筹备演出：</strong>“明亮春鸟”的策划与演出，应当强化PC们为柳岸镇取得的成功。这段冒险也给了你一个机会，让个别NPC表达他们对PC们的感激、希望与忧虑，以此深化NPC形象。举例来说，若PC们向村民询问他们从思维空间归来后的经历，或他们对PC们执政有何期望，那么律师骆熙旸可能会公开担忧：如今络新妇建立了自己的法典，她对龙洼律法的专长已毫无用处。金工匠兼发明家霍天哲则感到困惑并略有恼火：那些他曾视为创新的发条小玩意，如今却被当成可爱而老派的古董奇物。金具元为许多旧日贸易伙伴的离世而难过，但也对开始陆续流入商行的新样品感到兴奋。</p>\n<p>其他NPC也会对这次突兀的时间跳跃产生各自的反应，而本幕的这一部分，正是让PC们在发展演出时探索这些想法的机会。</p>\n<p><strong>上演：</strong>演出应当是一场盛大晚会。镇上每个人都兴奋地想要参加：既想看PC们将这场戏搬上舞台（本冒险假设演出在七彩鸣鸾剧院举行——你可以借此让PC们在大野和马后来遭遇悲惨命运之前，先有机会与这位剧院常驻导演进行交互），也想一睹小镇神秘的新赞助人任美璃的风采。和之前一样，络新妇公主在开场前几分钟于一团银色薄雾中现身，并刻意将自己的蜘蛛腿隐藏不让人看见。</p>\n<p>你不必让玩家把整场戏都角色扮演出来（尽管有些团体可能会乐在其中）。为了决定演出有多成功，让每位玩家说说他们的角色会做什么来确保演出成功，然后让他们用合适的技能进行一次DC 28的技能检定来获得胜利点数。@Check[performance|dc:28]显然是最直接的选择，适用于想要表演、歌唱或为演出提供音乐的PC。想要负责布景与服装的人可以尝试@Check[crafting|dc:28]。想用魔法特效为演出增色的人，则可以视情况掷@Check[arcana|dc:28]、@Check[nature|dc:28]、@Check[occultism|dc:28]或@Check[religion|dc:28]检定。想以力量或敏捷协助制作的人可以使用@Check[acrobatics|dc:28]与@Check[athletics|dc:28]。@Check[deception|dc:28]、@Check[diplomacy|dc:28]与@Check[intimidation|dc:28]则适用于想在演出期间充当主人或女主人的人，用来招待任美璃。</p>\n<p><strong>演出之后：</strong>不熟悉柳岸镇故事的新人（例如若罗昆幸存并被社区接纳）会表达对PC们成就的敬佩。经历过那些事件并活下来的人，在舞台上看到自己的亲身经历时会感到震撼；这不知怎地让那些往事既显得更真实，也显得更具传奇色彩。你可以借此机会称赞PC们不可思议的壮举。</p>\n<p>演出结束、其余观众散去后，任美璃起身，最后一次赞赏地拍手，然后走向PC们。无论演出好坏，她都会祝贺PC们；即便有人检定惨败，她也总能找出可以称赞的地方。她从发间抽出一枚银色发簪，随后将发簪上那颗描绘着拥有多彩尾羽之鸟的景泰蓝珠取下，递给掷出最高结果的那位PC。她将下一颗珠子留在发簪上——那颗珠子在深蓝色珐琅底色上呈现出红、金、绿火花重叠绽放的图样，想必代表夜空中的烟花——然后才开口说话。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“你们的下一个任务，是‘夏之烈花’。即便在庆祝时节之时，一位称职的管事也不会放任职责被忽视；但同时，他们也不会让受保护的人民平白受惊。这些烟花以庆祝夏日之美的名义献给众人，同时也能吓退怀有恶意的鬼魂与精灵。</p>\n  <p>“要实现此目的，烟花必须以黑风之角的干花制作。遗憾的是，我没有这些花可以给你们；不过我毫不怀疑，你们能在北方的月沼某处找到更多，并且能轻易采集到足以办一场精彩表演的数量。再一次，恐怕时间相当重要。我们再给一周，如何？很好；我很期待看看你们能做到什么！”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>说完，络新妇再次在一缕银色薄雾中离去。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们至少获得1点胜利点数，给予他们80 XP；若他们获得最高的4点胜利点数，则给予120 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Event 1: Bright Spring Bird</span>\n</h2>\n<p>The first of the Five-Season Treasures is the Bright Spring Bird, which, as Ren Mei Li explained, is to be a theatrical performance intended to evoke brightness, joy, and optimism regarding the future governor’s rule. The performance can be sung, danced, acted, or created by combining all the arts.</p>\n<p>This first rite provides a chance for the PCs to reflect on what their experiences in this campaign have meant to them, how it has affected their relationships with the people of Willowshore, and where it has left the town’s collective hopes and fears now that they’ve returned to the real world. The other townsfolk can provide helpful advice and material support if the PCs get stuck, but if the PCs don’t need their help, then they’re happy to assist the PCs’ artistic vision and not get in the way.</p>\n<p><strong>Preparing for the Show:</strong> The planning and performance of the Bright Spring Bird should reinforce the PCs’ successes on Willowshore’s behalf. This part of the adventure is also an opportunity to develop individual NPCs by having them express their gratitude, hopes, and worries to the PCs. For example, if the PCs ask the villagers for their experiences on returning from the mindscape, or what they hope for from the PCs’ governorship, then the lawyer Luo Xi Yang might worry aloud that her expertise in Lung Wa’s laws is useless now that the jorogumo have instituted their own legal codes. Huo Tian-Zhe, the metalsmith and inventor, is bemused and slightly annoyed that the clockwork gadgets he thought of as innovative are now viewed as charming, old-fashioned curios. Kim Gu-won is sad that many of his old trading partners have passed on but is also excited about the new samples that have begun to trickle into the trading house.</p>\n<p>Other NPCs will have their own reactions to their abrupt lurch forward in time, and this section of the act is an opportunity to explore those thoughts as the PCs develop their performance.</p>\n<p><strong>Putting on the Show:</strong> The show should be a gala event. Everyone in town is excited to attend, both to see the PCs enact the show (which this adventure assumes takes place at the Seven-Colored Songbird theater—you can use this time to give the PCs a moment to interact with Kazuma Oono, the theater’s resident director, before his grisly fate later) and to see the town’s mysterious new patron, Ren Mei Li. As before, the jorogumo princess appears in a cloud of silver mist minutes before the show begins, and she takes pains to keep her spider legs hidden from view.</p>\n<p>You don’t need to have the players roleplay out the entire show (although some groups might enjoy the opportunity). In order to determine how successful the show is, ask each player what their character does to make sure the show is a success, then have them attempt a DC 28 skill check with an appropriate skill to earn Victory Points. @Check[performance|dc:28] is the most obvious choice here, for PCs who wish to act, sing, or provide music for the show. Those who wish to instead work on the sets and costumes can attempt a @Check[crafting|dc:28]. Those who seek to bolster the show with magic special effects can roll an @Check[arcana|dc:28], @Check[nature|dc:28], @Check[occultism|dc:28], or @Check[religion|dc:28] check, as appropriate. @Check[acrobatics|dc:28] and @Check[athletics|dc:28] can be used by PCs who wish to lend their brawn or agility to the production. @Check[deception|dc:28], @Check[diplomacy|dc:28], and @Check[intimidation|dc:28] work for those who wish to play host or hostess to Ren Mei Li during the show.</p>\n<p><strong>After the Show:</strong> Newcomers who aren’t familiar with Willowshore’s story (such as Lo Kuon, if he survives and has been welcomed into the community) express admiration of the PCs’ achievements. Townsfolk who survived the events are awed by seeing their own experiences on stage, which somehow makes the events feel both more real and more legendary. You can use this chance to laud the PCs’ incredible achievements.</p>\n<p>At the show’s conclusion and when the rest of the audience has dispersed, Ren Mei Li stands and claps her hands appreciatively one last time, then approaches the PCs. Regardless of how well or poorly the show went, she congratulates the PCs, somehow managing to find a compliment even for those who failed their checks miserably. She withdraws a silver pin from her hair, then unthreads the cloisonne ball depicting the bird with the many-colored tail attached to the pin, offering it to the PC who rolled the highest result. She keeps the next ball attached to the pin—a ball that shows overlapping bursts of red, gold, and green sparkles against a backdrop of deep blue enamel, presumably representing fireworks against the night sky—before she speaks.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“The Fiery Flowers of Summer are your next assignment. Even as one celebrates the season, a competent steward does not allow their duties to go neglected. Neither do they cause undue fear among the people being protected, however. These fireworks, presented to the people as a celebration of summer’s beauty, also serve to frighten away malicious ghosts and spirits.</p>\n  <p>“To fulfill this purpose, the fireworks must be made with dried blossoms of Hei Feng’s horn. Regrettably, I have no supplies of these blossoms to give you, but I have no doubt you will be able to find more somewhere in the Moon Marsh to the north, and will have no difficulty harvesting enough to put on a fine show. Once again, I’m afraid, time is rather important. Shall we give it another week? Good; I look forward to seeing what you can do!”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>With that, the jorogumo once again departs in a waft of silver mist.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP if they earn at least 1 Victory Point, or 120 XP if they earn the maximum of 4 Victory Points.</p>"
            },
            "Treasure and Murder": {
              "name": "宝藏与谋杀 Treasure and Murder",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">宝藏与谋杀</span>\n</h1>\n<p>五季宝藏象征着一位领袖具备能力并愿意在一年中不断变化的情绪与挑战里统治并保护人民。起初，与这些象征相关的五项仪式体现了人们对生活喜悦的感恩，其中一些性相至今仍然保留。尽管这些特定的仪式变体主要是为了任美璃而测试PC的胜任程度，但它们也应当成为一个机会，让PC加深与柳岸镇NPC的关系，并享受他们迄今为止取得的成就。</p>\n<p>这五项仪式中的每一项都让PC有机会获得胜利点数，每项仪式最多4点胜利点数。最终任务完成后，他们累计获得的胜利点数总数将影响任美璃最后的提议以及提供的奖励。</p>\n<p>当PC搜寻五季宝藏时，另一连串更为阴险的事件也在发生。和善保如今已完全变形为一只可怖的yohoi（一种“brainchild”），来到柳岸镇行凶并散播恐惧。这些谋杀发生在PC离开城镇期间，但他们在继续寻找五季宝藏的间隙，将有机会调查犯罪现场与尸体。</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>什么是Yohoi？</h2>\n  <p>PC最终会得知，一种出自都市传说、名为yohoi的生物可能已在柳岸镇活动。一名PC若在一次用于回忆知识的@Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]、@Check[society|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定中成功，或在一次用于搜集信息的@Check[diplomacy|dc:20|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]检定中成功，则会了解到关于yohoi的下列一条信息。在大成功时，PC将了解到两条不同的要点信息。</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Yohoi以乡间小镇为猎物，最初被认为是遭到忽视的祖先之鬼魂的显现；但如今，它们已在神门的乡村聚居地中成了一种被泛化（尽管鲜为人知）的“床底怪”形象。</li>\n    <li>Yohoi可以呈现任何形状，但你可以通过它们鼓胀的黄色眼睛、扭曲多毛的脖颈，以及又长又脏的指甲来辨认它们。它们的武器致死并不主要靠造成身体伤害，而是靠其施加的心灵痛苦。</li>\n    <li>Yohoi惧怕笛声，笛声能够伤害它们，甚至将其驱离，尤其是由祭司或信仰强大之人演奏时。</li>\n    <li>当一只yohoi死亡时，它的身体会在数分钟内消逝。除非以一种能确保世人相信它们将永远消失的方式将其杀死，否则它们可能会归来。</li>\n    <li>学者认为，yohoi是某个人的思想所显现的结果，甚至可能是整个社群的恐惧所致——在其他文化中，它们也以其他名称为人所知，例如“brainchildren”。</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p><strong>奖励：</strong>一旦PC得知有yohoi牵涉其中，给予他们80 XP。</p>\n</aside>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Treasure and Murder</span>\n</h1>\n<p>The Five-Season Treasures are symbols of a leader’s ability and willingness to rule and protect their people across all the changing moods and challenges of the year. Originally, the five rites associated with these symbols reflected a people’s gratitude for the joys of their lives, and some of that aspect remains. Although these specific variants on the rites primarily test the PCs’ competence for Ren Mei Li’s benefit, they should also serve as an opportunity to deepen their relationships with the NPCs of Willowshore and enjoy their achievements up to this point.</p>\n<p>Each of these five rites gives the PCs a chance to achieve Victory Points, up to a maximum of 4 Victory Points per rite. Once the final task is done, the total number of Victory Points they’ve accumulated impacts Ren Mei Li’s final offer and rewards offered.</p>\n<p>As the PCs search for the Five-Season Treasures, another, far more sinister set of events takes place. Heh Shan-Bao, now fully transformed into a horrific yohoi (a type of brainchild), visits Willowshore to murder and spread terror. These murders take place while the PCs are out of town, but they’ll have opportunities to investigate the crime scenes and bodies in between seeking out the Five-Season Treasures.</p>\n<aside class=\"sidebar\">\n  <h2>What’s a Yohoi?</h2>\n  <p>The PCs eventually learn that a creature from urban legend known as a yohoi might have become active in Willowshore. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge], @Check[society|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge], or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, or a @Check[diplomacy|dc:20|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] check to Gather Information, learns one of the following pieces of information about yohoi. On a critical success, the PCs learn two different bullet points of information.</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Yohoi prey upon small rural towns and were initially believed to be manifestations of the ghosts of neglected ancestors, but today, they’ve become something of a generalized (if obscure) form of the “boogeyman” for Shenmen’s rural settlements.</li>\n    <li>Yohoi can be any shape, but you can recognize them by their bulging yellow eyes, crooked hairy necks, and long filthy fingernails. Their weapons can kill not so much by physical damage but by the mental anguish they inflict.</li>\n    <li>Yohoi fear flute music and can be harmed or even driven away by it, particularly when played by a priest or someone with powerful faith.</li>\n    <li>When a yohoi dies, its body fades away within minutes. Unless slain in a way that ensures society believes they’re gone forever, they can return.</li>\n    <li>Scholars believe that yohoi manifest as the result of a person’s thoughts, or even of an entire community’s fears—in other cultures, they’re known by other names, such as “brainchildren.”</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p><strong>Reward:</strong> Once the PCs learn a yohoi is involved, grant them 80 XP.</p>\n</aside>"
            },
            "The Princess’s Requests": {
              "name": "公主的请求 The Princess’s Requests",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">公主的请求</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“是时候讨论五季宝藏了。根源要求新任管事完成一项仪式，以证明他们的忠诚、勇气，以及作为使者服务的能力。这样的人必须熟悉他们的子民并关心他们的福祉，你不这么认为吗？当这些考量被忽视时会发生什么，我们都再清楚不过了。</p>\n  <p>“至于你，我想，一项用来纪念你们历经艰辛才得以坐在这里与我相对的仪式就足够了；而我想不出有什么仪式能比寻找五季宝藏更合适。四件宝藏象征生命的四季，意在表明一位称职的统治者会全年遵守他们的誓约：春之明鸟、夏之烈花、秋之甘果、冬之辛茶。收集齐全后，生者的馈赠必须献给受敬的亡者，以获得祖先与守护者的祝福——这便是第五季，一个超越凡人生命的季节。若祖先接受并赐下祝福，那么你只需向我宣誓效忠，管事之位便归你所有。”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>精明的PC或许会注意到，任美璃要求效忠的是她本人，而不是朗洛依夫人或络新妇宫廷。若他们指出这一点，任美璃只是又笑了笑，耸耸肩：“哦，我是这么说的吗？”</p>\n<p>如果PC询问这项仪式具体包含什么，任美璃会告诉他们如下内容：</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“我们会按顺序一一处理，但首先，你必须献给我一只明亮的春鸟。”</p>\n  <p>任美璃从发间抽出一对银簪，将它们刺入面前的席垫。她轻触第一支簪上垂挂的两枚景泰蓝小球之一；那小球描绘着一只白鸟，拖着由多色羽毛组成的修长卷曲尾羽，然后她再次开口。</p>\n  <p>“春之明鸟象征喜悦与新生冲破冬日的阴郁。若一位管事称职，他们的统治便代表着为村庄带来好运的复苏。你将根据自身才华进行一场表演——音乐、舞蹈、戏剧皆可——来庆祝你为柳岸镇做过的最伟大之事。就你而言，我想那应当是将你的人民从思维空间中解救出来，对吗？无论你选择什么，这场演出都应包含多彩服装、鲜明布景、特效，以及富有戏剧性的音乐。</p>\n  <p>“请在一周内准备好表演。我会回来观看。我非常期待你的演出。”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>不再多言，任美璃起身、行礼，并沿来路离开——在一阵银色薄雾的旋涡中消失。若PC试图搜索以了解任美璃的更多信息，甚至与她战斗，关于任美璃的额外信息（包括她如何通过那团薄雾云彩如此轻松地来去）见于她的@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21renmeili000000]{NPC条目}。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC同意与任美璃合作并开始追寻她的请求，给予PC 60 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Princess’s Requests</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“It is time to discuss the Five-Season Treasures. Tradition demands that new stewards complete a ritual to prove their loyalty, courage, and capacity to serve as ambassadors. Such people must be acquainted with their citizens and concerned with their welfare, don’t you agree? We all know too well what happens when those considerations are ignored.</p>\n  <p>“For you, I think a ritual honoring the struggles you’ve endured to sit here with me shall do, and no better ritual than seeking the Five-Season Treasures comes to mind. Four of these treasures symbolize the four seasons of life, to symbolize that a worthy ruler keeps their pact year round: the bright bird of spring, the fiery flowers of summer, the sweet fruits of autumn, and the spiced tea of winter. Once gathered, the gifts of the living must then be offered to the honored dead, to gain the blessing of ancestors and guardians—this is the fifth season, a season beyond mortal life. If the ancestors accept, and grant their blessing, then all you need do is swear fealty to me, and the stewardship is yours.”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Canny PCs might note that Ren Mei Li asks for fealty to herself, rather than to Lady Lang Loi or the jorogumo court. If they point this out, Ren Mei Li merely smiles again and shrugs: “Oh, was that what I said?”</p>\n<p>If the PCs ask what, specifically, the ritual entails, Ren Mei Li tells them the following:</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“We shall address them all in turn, but to begin with, you must offer me a bright spring bird.”</p>\n  <p>Ren Mei Li draws a pair of silver pins from her hair and stabs them into the mat before her. She touches one of the two cloisonne balls dangling from the first pin, which depicts a white bird with a long, curling tail of many-colored feathers, then speaks again.</p>\n  <p>“The bright bird of spring is a symbol of joy and renewal breaking through winter’s drear. If a steward is good, then their rule represents a revival of good fortune for the village. You will put on a performance of whatever type suits your talents—music, dance, drama—to celebrate the greatest thing you have done to benefit Willowshore. In your case, I should imagine that would be freeing your people from the mindscape, no? Whatever you choose, the show should involve multicolored costumes, vivid backdrops, special effects, and dramatic music.</p>\n  <p>“Please have your performance ready within the week. I shall return to watch it. I quite look forward to your show.”</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Without further ado, Ren Mei Li stands, bows, and leaves the same way she came—vanishing in a swirl of silver mist. Should the PCs seek to learn more about Ren Mei Li or even confront her in combat, additional information about Ren Mei Li (including how she comes and goes so effortlessly via that cloud of mist) appears in her @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21renmeili000000]{NPC Entry}.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 60 XP if they agree to work with Ren Mei Li and begin to pursue her requests.</p>"
            },
            "Meeting the Princess": {
              "name": "会见公主 Meeting the Princess",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">会见公主</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meiliren.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ren Mei Li\" alt=\"female Tian princess\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meiliren.webp')\" />\n<p>在约定的时刻，一团闪烁的银色薄雾充满了青天茶馆（或任何PC告诉阿迈她们将在那里接待其女主人的地点）。一位美得惊人的银发女子从雾中迈步而出，身着最上等的浅蓝与海绿色丝绸。几根银簪上装饰着宝石蜘蛛，将她的头发盘起。她饶有兴致地环顾茶馆，先打量其家具与装饰，然后才转向PC。她的声音轻柔，笑容安宁。她外表中唯一可能令人不安的地方，是她双眼上的银色光泽，以及她发间蜘蛛的活动——那些蜘蛛是活的生物，终究不是由宝石做成的装饰。</p>\n<p>任美璃独自前来，这既是她“驾轻就熟”的展示，也为了在需要时，与PC私下说的话不会被旁人听见并回报宫廷。她现身时也没有伸展出她的蜘蛛腿，为了不那么吓人，她看起来更像人类。她对众人微笑，等他们自我介绍后，便开口说道。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“很高兴见到你们。我是任美璃。我不会把你们从职责上拉开太久，因为我明白柳岸镇需要你们的关注。我希望你们不会觉得我直来直去太过无礼。</p>\n  <p>“简单说，我想向你们提出结盟。我知道司则已将贪婪的目光投向柳岸镇的资源，也希望将贪婪之手伸向此处。我能阻止这一切。我甚至愿意给予柳岸镇相当程度的自治，只要其管理者是我能够信任的人。</p>\n</div>\n<p>“你们觉得，你们中的一些人——或全部人——能否担任我的管理者？”</p>\n<p>如果PC对“管理者”这一职位（某种作为络新妇使节的角色，独立于城镇的实际总督）表现出兴趣，哪怕只是试探性的，任美璃都会显得既高兴又觉得有趣，随后以茶与餐点为先，将敲定协定的细节暂且搁置。在这段间隙中，她会询问PC自身的情况——尤其想知道他们来自何处，又是如何让柳岸镇从废墟中恢复过来。只要PC说出真相，或至少说出其中一部分，她便会完全相信，因为他们的解释与她的理论完全吻合。若她得知在思维空间里有一个“她的版本”拜访过PC，她会大感兴趣，并要求他们详细描述她当时的举止，对这次意料之外的遭遇着迷不已。</p>\n<p>任美璃对PC的初始态度是“不关心”。如果PC佩戴或公开展示他们可能在那次遭遇中获得的银色项圈，任美璃会以明显的眼神流露出对这一展示的赞赏。这会将她的起始态度从“不关心”转变为“友善”。在这顿初步的餐点与交谈期间，允许PC尝试进行@Check[diplomacy|dc:28]、@Check[performance|dc:28]、@Check[society|dc:28]或@Check[tea-lore|dc:28]检定，或进行@Check[arcana|dc:23]检定来给她留下深刻印象。成功意味着PC累计胜利点数；若PC以此方式获得至少3点胜利点数，他们就会将她的态度改善为“友善”（或者若她已是“友善”，则改善为“乐于帮助”）。</p>\n<p>随着谈话继续，任美璃会就思维空间现象、他们与苦迦菩提的冲突，以及PC如何处理这一切提出见多识广且一针见血的问题。若PC描述了他们使用的任何巧妙战术，或关于思维空间运作机制的非同寻常发现，她会明显受到触动并表示赞赏。</p>\n<p>如果PC解释他们为帮助柳岸镇而做过的具体事情，以及改善其未来前景的计划，任美璃也会专注倾听。若PC讲述他们为支援城镇而取得的重要成就（无论是先前的冒险中，还是他们近来修桥与剿匪的努力），任美璃会向他们致贺。若他们问她是否能为柳岸镇的未来计划提供帮助，她会谨慎地避免做出任何具体承诺，但表示会认真看待他们的暗示。她并不反对将柳岸镇指定为银印村，“但当然，那要取决于是否有一位值得信赖的管理者。”</p>\n<p>最终——并且假设PC愿意接受她的提议——这位络新妇会解释接下来会发生什么。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Meeting the Princess</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meiliren.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Ren Mei Li\" alt=\"female Tian princess\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-meiliren.webp')\" />\n<p>At the appointed hour, a shimmering silver mist fills the Cerulean Teahouse (or whatever location the PCs told Amai they’d be receiving her mistress at). From it steps a silver-haired woman of extraordinary beauty, clad in pale blue and sea green silk of the finest quality. Silver sticks, ornamented with jeweled spiders, bind up her hair. She looks around the teahouse with open interest, examining its furnishings and decor before turning to the PCs. Her voice is gentle and her smile serene. The only aspects of her appearance that might be unsettling are the silver sheen over her eyes and the movements of the spiders in her hair, which are living creatures and not, after all, decorations made of gemstones.</p>\n<p>Ren Mei Li arrives alone, a display of her assurance but also so that, if needed, words spoken with the PCs in confidence won’t be overheard by others who might report back to the court. She also appears without her spider legs extended, looking human in an attempt to be less intimidating to the PCs. She smiles at the party, waits for them to introduce themselves, then speaks.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“How nice to meet you. I am Ren Mei Li. I will not draw you away from your duties for long, as I understand Willowshore demands your attention. I hope you will not find my directness too rude.</p>\n  <p>“In short, I wish to offer you an alliance. I understand that Sze has cast its greedy eyes upon Willowshore’s resources and wishes to cast its greedy hands upon it as well. I can prevent this. I am even willing to offer Willowshore a considerable degree of autonomy, provided its stewards are people I can trust.</p>\n</div>\n<p>“Do you suppose that some, or all, of you might serve as my stewards?”</p>\n<p>If the PCs express interest in the position of steward (a sort of ambassador to the jorogumo apart from the town’s actual governor), however tentatively, Ren Mei Li seems both pleased and amused, then waves aside the particulars of settling on this accord in deference to tea and a meal. During this interlude, she asks the PCs about themselves—in particular, she’s interested to find out where they’re from and how they’ve managed to bring Willowshore back from ruins. Assuming the PCs tell the truth, or at least parts of it, she believes them entirely, as their explanation perfectly matches her theories. If she learns that a version of herself visited the PCs in the mindscape, she is intrigued and demands exact details of how she behaved, fascinated by this unexpected encounter.</p>\n<p>Ren Mei Li’s initial attitude toward the PCs is indifferent. If the PCs wear or openly display the silver collars they might have gained during that encounter, Ren Mei Li makes an obvious visual note of appreciation at the display. This shifts her starting attitude from indifferent to friendly. During this preliminary meal and conversation, allow the PCs to attempt @Check[diplomacy|dc:28], @Check[performance|dc:28], @Check[society|dc:28], or @Check[tea-lore|dc:28] checks, or @Check[arcana|dc:23] checks to impress her. Successes mean the PCs accumulate Victory Points; if the PCs earn at least 3 Victory Points in this way, they improve her attitude to friendly (or if she’s already friendly, to helpful).</p>\n<p>As the conversation continues, Ren Mei Li asks knowledgeable and incisive questions about the mindscape phenomenon, their clashes with Kugaptee, and how the PCs dealt with it all. If the PCs describe any inventive tactics they used, or unusual discoveries they made about the mindscape’s workings, she’s visibly impressed.</p>\n<p>Ren Mei Li also listens attentively if the PCs explain concrete things they’ve done to help Willowshore and plans they have to improve its future prospects. If the PCs recount their significant achievements to aid the town (be it in previous adventures or their recent efforts to build bridges and fight bandits), Ren Mei Li congratulates them. If they ask whether she can help with their future plans for Willowshore, she’s careful not to promise anything specific but indicates that she’ll take their suggestions seriously. She isn’t opposed to designating Willowshore as a Silver Seal village, “but, of course, that would depend on having a trustworthy steward.”</p>\n<p>Eventually, and assuming the PCs are receptive to her offer, the jorogumo explains what comes next.</p>"
            },
            "Preparing for the Visit": {
              "name": "为来访做准备 Preparing for the Visit",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">为来访做准备</span>\n</h3>\n<p>在前一幕中，PC们只有8小时来为任美璃的来访做准备。这一次，他们有整整一周时间，而且PC们并不知道的是，任美璃已经有一百年的时间来完善自己的统治，并抑制她那更为专横、急躁的性格特征。在青天茶馆接待她依旧是最佳选择，但PC们不必再那么担心要藏起天狗与桃木，或害怕她会决定把柳岸镇的居民带回去当俘虏或食物。当然，PC们很可能要等到她抵达时才会意识到这一点！</p>\n<p>由于PC们有一周时间准备，只要让他们向你描述他们想做什么来布置会面即可。无需进行任何技能检定来决定成功与否。如果他们准备得恭敬得体，任美璃会很高兴；但如果他们没有这样做，或是公然无礼，那也正符合她的预期，她会不为所动地继续这次来访。</p>\n<p>与此同时，PC们可能会四处打听更多关于任美璃的信息。柳岸镇里没人对现代的神门有足够了解能给出建议，但如果花上几个小时在唐入打听，甚至去问问丝蜂盗匪中是否有人幸存并愿意与PC们交谈，PC们就有机会通过一次用于搜集信息的@Check[diplomacy|dc:25|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information]交涉检定来搜集信息，从而了解更多。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> 同成功，但PC还会得知任美璃被认为在奥术技艺上格外娴熟，并且很可能会对任何表现出对奥术感兴趣或拥有深厚奥术学识的人反应良好。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong> PC发现任美璃被视为络新妇之中“没那么折磨人的”那一类——依旧可怕，但比其他同类更容易打交道。因此，当地人很快就会积极讨好她，好让她继续留下来，因为他们非常清楚：若她被替换，接任的那只络新妇很可能会残酷得多。尤其会强调她愿意接纳天狗，以及她极少要求以人作为贡品这一点。PC们也会被告知：如果他们有银项圈，就在她面前戴上。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功或大失败</strong> PC得知的信息似乎支持这样一种看法：任美璃依旧像上一幕她“拜访”柳岸镇思维空间时那样专横、傲慢，而且可能更为暴力。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC们在打听任美璃的更多信息时至少取得一次成功，则给予PC们40 XP。</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Preparing for the Visit</span>\n</h3>\n<p>In the previous act, the PCs had only 8 hours to prepare for Ren Mei Li’s visit. This time, they have an entire week, and unknown to the PCs, Ren Mei Li has had a hundred years to perfect her rule and to curb her more imperious and impatient personality traits. Receiving her at the Cerulean Teahouse remains the best option, but the PCs don’t need to worry as much about hiding tengu and peachwood or being fearful that she might decide to take citizens of Willowshore back home with her as captives or meals. Of course, the PCs likely won’t realize this until her arrival!</p>\n<p>Since the PCs have a week to prepare, simply have them describe to you what they wish to do to set up for the meeting. There’s no need to attempt any skill checks for success. If they prepare respectfully, Ren Mei Li is delighted, but if they don’t or if they’re actively disrespectful, that just plays into her expectations, and she proceeds with the visit without being ruffled.</p>\n<p>In the meantime, the PCs might ask around for more information about Ren Mei Li. No one in Willowshore has enough experience with modern Shenmen to offer any advice, but a few hours spent asking around at Karahai, or even asking one of the Silkwasp Bandits if any of them survived and are willing to speak to the PCs, allows the PCs to potentially learn more with a @Check[diplomacy|dc:25|traits:exploration,skill,secret,action:gather-information|name:Gather Information] check to Gather Information.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> As success, but the PC also learns that Ren Mei Li is considered to be exceptionally adept in the arcane arts and will likely react well to anyone who displays an interest or deep knowledge in arcana.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> The PC discovers that Ren Mei Li is regarded as one of the “less harrowing” of the jorogumo—still frightening, but much easier to work with than others. As such, the locals are quick and eager to please her in order to keep her around, knowing full well that the next jorogumo who would replace her would likely be much more cruel. In particular, her willing acceptance of tengu and the fact that she only very rarely demands tribute in the form of people is stressed. The PCs are also told to wear their silver collars in her presence if they have them.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The information the PC learns seems to support that Ren Mei Li remains as imperious, arrogant, and potentially more violent than she was during her “visit” to the Willowshore mindscape in the previous act.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 40 XP if they achieve at least a success in asking around for more information about Ren Mei Li.</p>"
            },
            "A Feline Emissary": {
              "name": "猫科使者 A Feline Emissary",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">一位猫科使者</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>任美璃派出一位使者，提醒PC们她即将到来，但与前一幕不同的是，她已经明白耐心的价值。她提前一周派出使者，这应当能让柳岸镇有绰绰有余的时间准备。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-amai.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Amai\" alt=\"female dweomercat\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-amai.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>任美璃的使者是一只名叫阿麦的魔法猫。她（不同于同类中的大多数）是这只络新妇忠诚且可靠的同伴。她对在第一世界消磨时光兴趣寥寥，反倒很享受因与神门一位贵族的关联而获得的恭敬与仰慕。当她被指派去宣告女主人即将造访柳岸镇时，阿麦会躲在暗处观察镇民——并且越来越多地观察PC们。此遭遇开始时，让PC们尝试进行 @Check[perception|dc:27] 检定。成功者会注意到一只奇异的紫色猫正从附近某处藏身之所窥视他们——可能是在矮丛环境中、昏暗的小巷里、透过敞开的门望进黑暗的房间，等等。由你裁定：如果PC们仍与青天茶馆的化猫“吉祥物”雅弥保持友好，那么她可以先与阿麦碰面。她会与这只魔法猫交好，并把新朋友介绍给PC们——两只猫对彼此名字如此相似这件事感到格外有趣。</p>\n<p>无论阿麦是在藏身处被发现并被当面质问，还是她使用 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate} 直接“蹦”到PC面前公开接近他们，这只魔法猫都会尽力表明自己不是来打架的——即便她的初次现身会吓PC们一跳。她的蓝宝石色皮毛上点缀着紫罗兰色的螺旋纹，她佩戴的银与蛛丝项圈也比络新妇通常发给盟友和特务的那些要优雅得多。</p>\n<p>阿麦对任美璃极为忠诚，尤其是对一只魔法猫而言；而这样一个平日里反复无常的存在却如此依恋其女主人，应当是PC们得到的第一条线索：这只络新妇不仅异常强大，还能从意想不到的盟友那里赢得忠诚。阿麦并非被魔法强迫才效忠，任何此类暗示都会令她受辱；她认为任美璃是个迷人的个体，能用她理应享有的一切奢华来宠爱这只魔法猫，因此是值得相伴的人。阿麦会很随意地聊任美璃的八卦，但除了些许小抱怨——比如没给她的闪亮小饰物，或不让她把玩的有趣魔法——她基本只会说好话。</p>\n<p>阿麦说话时用的是一种有教养的女性嗓音。她第一次见到PC们时，会这样问候他们。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“向你们致意，柳岸镇。我是阿麦。我有幸侍奉任美璃女士——银丝公主、阴司察夕的灿耀之女。我的主人对你们很感兴趣，希望与你们结识。七日之后，你们愿意与她共饮一杯茶吗？”</p>\n</div>\n<p>阿麦愿意回答几个问题，而PC们每问她一个问题，她也会反问一个，通常会针对PC们的穿着或习惯（“你头发上那是什么东西？”或“你祈祷时为什么要拿着那件小饰物？”之类天真而直白的问题）。阿麦与PC们交谈大约5分钟后便会离开。</p>\n<p><strong>任美璃女士是谁？</strong>“她当然是这片土地的统治者之一！哎呀呀！你们可真是与世隔绝！她是一只络新妇，而且她光彩夺目！”（如果PC们表示已经见过她，阿麦会先震惊困惑片刻，随后若有所思地说：“我敢肯定这会是主人感兴趣的消息！”然后继续下一个问题。）</p>\n<p><strong>任美璃为什么想见我们？</strong>“她对你们很好奇。此外，这个镇需要一位正式的管事。也许你们当中一个人——或你们所有人——都很合适。”</p>\n<p><strong>我们能得到什么？</strong>“你们不想继续住在这里了吗？我的主人能在许多方面帮助你们。哪怕只是回去禀报一次令人满意的拜访，从而避免惩罚也好。”</p>\n<p><strong>我们能信任络新妇吗？</strong>猫听到这种无礼的问题便笑了。“你会信我的回答吗？直接与她交谈。然后再决定。”</p>\n<p>不论PC们是否愿意接受阿麦带来的信息，PC们其实都没有真正拒绝这次拜访的选项；等这只魔法猫感到无聊并离开后，他们有7天时间准备。若PC们发动攻击，她会逃走。在这种情况下，任美璃女士会更少把PC们当作潜在盟友，而更像是必须偿还债务以免被处决的罪犯。本冒险假定PC们不会走这条路，但如果他们真的这么做了，你应当相应调整之后各次遭遇的基调。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.RMUc5gzn3KdD6Y6H]{Amai}</span><span>生物 7</span></h2>\n</section>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们若愿意花时间与阿麦交谈，给予他们40 XP。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A Feline Emissary</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 11</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Ren Mei Li sends an emissary to alert the PCs of her imminent arrival, but unlike in the previous act, she has learned the value of patience. She sends her emissary a week ahead of time, which should give Willowshore more than enough time to prepare.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-amai.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Amai\" alt=\"female dweomercat\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-amai.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Ren Mei Li’s emissary is a dweomercat named Amai, who (unlike most of her kind) is a faithful and loyal companion to the jorogumo. She has little interest in spending time in the First World and quite enjoys the deference and admiration afforded her by dint of her association with one of Shenmen’s aristocrats. When she’s assigned the task of announcing her mistress’s imminent visit to Willowshore, Amai spends some time watching the townsfolk and, increasingly, the PCs from hiding. When this encounter begins, allow the PCs to attempt @Check[perception|dc:27] checks. Those who succeed notice the strange purple cat peering at them from somewhere nearby in hiding—the undergrowth, a shadowy alley, through an open door into a dark room, and so on. At your discretion, if the PCs remain friends with the Cerulean Teahouse’s bakeneko “mascot” Yami, then she can meet Amai first. She befriends the dweomercat and introduces her new friend to the PCs—the two cats are unusually amused at how similar their names are.</p>\n<p>Whether Amai is spotted and confronted from her hiding spot, or whether she openly approaches the PCs by using @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate} to pop into their presence, the dweomercat does her best to make it apparent she isn’t here to fight—even if her initial appearance startles the PCs. Her sapphire fur is highlighted by violet spirals, and the silver and spidersilk collar she wears is much more elegant than those normally handed out by the jorogumo to their allies and agents.</p>\n<p>Amai is quite faithful to Ren Mei Li, especially for a dweomercat, and the fact that an ordinarily fickle being is so attached to her mistress should be the PCs’ first clue that this jorogumo is both unusually powerful and able to earn loyalty from unexpected allies. Amai isn’t magically compelled to serve and is insulted by any such suggestion; she views Ren Mei Li as a fascinating individual who can pamper the dweomercat with all the luxuries she so richly deserves and, therefore, as company worth keeping. Amai gossips freely about Ren Mei Li but has only good things to say other than minor criticisms about shiny baubles the cat wasn’t given or interesting magic the cat wasn’t allowed to play with.</p>\n<p>When Amai speaks, she does so in a cultured, feminine voice, and when she first meets the PCs, she greets them as follows.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“Greetings, Willowshore. I am Amai. I have the honor of serving Lady Ren Mei Li, the Silversilk Princess, Resplendent Daughter of Yin-Sichasi. My mistress is curious about you, and wishes to make your acquaintance. Will you meet with her for tea in seven days’ time?”</p>\n</div>\n<p>Amai is willing to answer a few questions, and after each question the PCs ask her, she asks a question of her own, generally directed at aspects of the PCs’ dress or habits (“What’s that thing in your hair?” or “Why do you hold that bauble when you pray?” and similarly guileless, blunt questions). Once Amai has talked to the PCs for 5 minutes or so, she leaves.</p>\n<p><strong>Who’s Lady Ren Mei Li?</strong> “She’s one of this land’s rulers, of course! My, my! You have been out of it! She’s a jorogumo, and she’s glorious!” (If the PCs indicate they’ve met her already, Amai seems shocked and confused for a moment, then muses, “I’m sure that’ll be something my mistress will be interested to hear about!” before moving on to the next question.)</p>\n<p><strong>Why does Ren Mei Li want to meet us?</strong> “She’s curious about you. Also, this town needs an official steward. Perhaps one or all of you will suit.”</p>\n<p><strong>What will we get out of it?</strong> “Do you not wish to continue living here? My mistress can help you in so many ways. Even if only reporting back a favorable visit to prevent punishment.”</p>\n<p><strong>Can we trust a jorogumo?</strong> The cat laughs at being asked such an impertinent question. “Would you trust my answer? Speak to her directly. Then decide.”</p>\n<p>Whether or not the PCs are receptive to Amai’s message, there isn’t really an option for the PCs to deny the visit; they have 7 days to prepare once the dweomercat grows bored and departs. If the PCs attack, she flees. In this case, Lady Ren Mei Li treats the PCs less as potential allies and more as criminals who must work off a debt to avoid execution. This adventure assumes the PCs don’t take this route, but if they do, you should adjust the tenor of the encounters to come appropriately.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span>@UUID[Actor.RMUc5gzn3KdD6Y6H]{Amai}</span><span>Creature 7</span></h2>\n</section>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 40 XP for taking the time to speak with Amai.</p>"
            },
            "Ren Mei Li’s Return": {
              "name": "任美璃的归来 Ren Mei Li’s Return",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">任美璃的归来</span>\n</h1>\n<p>任美璃最初造访柳岸镇，部分是为了欢迎这座失落已久的小镇重回“蛛网之下”（这是对那些发现自己处于络新妇统治之下的非蛛类生物的一种委婉说法），但她的首要目标出于好奇：她想弄清柳岸镇是如何、又为何从废墟中归来。她的关注很快转向PC们；作为对他们潜在价值的考验，任美璃给PC们安排了一系列任务，以评估他们的技能，并衡量他们对柳岸镇忠诚的程度，因为她可能会把这些纽带当作筹码来施压。若PC们成功，任美璃会印象深刻，并提出以他们承诺效忠为交换，授予他们管理柳岸镇的监护权。</p>\n<p>将PC们安置为监护人能为任美璃解决两个问题——这会让柳岸镇拥有一套可靠的领导班子，帮助保卫城镇并促进其发展（从而使她不必亲自处理那项工作），同时也给了她一个机会：暗中把PC们的忠诚牢牢系在自己身上，而不是让他们忠于络新妇宫廷与朗洛依夫人。</p>\n<p>一旦PC们证明了自己，任美璃就会提出异常优厚的条件来确保他们的协助。虽然PC们可能会对与络新妇达成交易心存顾虑，但应当清楚，这是确保柳岸镇在神门中安全与繁荣的最佳选择。更进一步，因为任美璃更关心推进自己的野心而非朗洛依夫人的，她愿意接受一份暗中只承诺维护她利益的提议；她甚至可能让PC们保持自由，以便他们潜在地反对神门中络新妇的整体统治。</p>\n<p>PC们也应当有强烈的动机接受总督之位，因为唯有取得络新妇宫廷的正式授权（其象征是一件名为<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>的仪式物品），他们才能最终击败@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}并阻止苦迦菩提的转世。</p>\n<p><em>獠牙与钥匙</em>是本章中的关键要素。本章有数个情节要素都依赖PC们持有它。尽管他们在没有<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>的情况下也能完成本章，但若未能取得它，PC们将错过这场冒险中相当重要的部分。因此，务必不要把任美璃呈现为敌人，而应当呈现为PC们能够合作的对象——即便她可能并非他们的首选盟友。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Ren Mei Li’s Return</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Ren Mei Li’s initial visit to Willowshore is in part to welcome the long-lost town back “below the web” (a euphemism for non-arachnid creatures who find themselves under jorogumo rule), but her primary goal is one of curiosity: she wants to find out how and why Willowshore returned from ruin. Her focus soon shifts to the PCs, and as a test of their possible value, Ren Mei Li sets the PCs a series of missions that will evaluate their skills and also assess the extent of their loyalty to Willowshore, since she can potentially use those ties as leverage. If the PCs succeed, Ren Mei Li is impressed and offers them stewardship of Willowshore in exchange for a promise of fealty.</p>\n<p>Installing the PCs as stewards solves two problems for Ren Mei Li—it gives Willowshore a reliable set of leaders to help defend the town and cultivate its growth (thus freeing her up from having to handle that work directly), and it provides her a chance to secretly secure the PCs’ loyalties for herself rather than on behalf of the jorogumo court and Lady Lang Loi.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs have proven themselves, Ren Mei Li offers unusually generous terms to secure their help. While the PCs might have qualms about striking a bargain with a jorogumo, it should be clear that this is their best option to assure Willowshore’s safety and prosperity in Shenmen. Further, because Ren Mei Li is more interested in advancing her own ambitions than Lady Lang Loi’s, she’s willing to accept an offer that secretly only promises to uphold her interests, and she might leave the PCs free to potentially work against the overall rule of the jorogumo in Shenmen.</p>\n<p>The PCs should also have a significant incentive to accept the governorship because it’s only by obtaining the jorogumo court’s official mandate, as symbolized by a ceremonial item called the <em>Fang and Key</em>, that they can finally defeat @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} and prevent Kugaptee’s reincarnation.</p>\n<p>The <em>Fang and Key</em> is a critical element in this chapter. Several plot elements rely on the PCs having it. While they can complete this chapter without the <em>Fang and Key</em>, the PCs will miss significant portions of the adventure if they don’t obtain it. Therefore, it’s important that Ren Mei Li not be presented as an enemy, but as someone the PCs can work with—even if she might not be their first choice of allies.</p>"
            },
            "The Princess’s Web": {
              "name": "公主的蛛网术 The Princess’s Web",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Princess’s Web\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第12章：</span>\n  <span>公主的蛛网</span>\n</h1>\n\n<p>络新妇是神门残酷而反复无常的统治者。这个国家的公民畏惧她们，因为她们对臣民的对待充斥着恐怖与惊惧。许多人所能期望的最好结局，不过是被遗忘——完全得不到政府的任何支援，只能自生自灭。任美璃夫人是络新妇宫廷中的高位成员，而落入她蛛网的诸多社群之一便是柳岸镇。尽管PC们在上一幕中遭遇过她的某个版本，但她实际上从未见过PC们——她第一次造访柳岸镇，是在镇民被屠杀并被迅速带入思维空间后的新年第一天。她发现柳岸镇已被遗弃，便命令仆从洗劫此地的贵重物品，作为献给朗洛依夫人的供品（同时也为自己留下了相当一部分）；而在过去的一个世纪里，她几乎没有把这片区域放在心上。</p>\n<p>柳岸镇返回的消息很快传入她耳中。任美璃不久便重返柳岸镇，查明它与镇民这段时间去了哪里，并用络新妇最“擅长”的方式“欢迎”他们归来——提出残酷的要求，并处以在经济上令人难以承受的罚金。PC们可以缓和这些政治上的打击，也能把他们在上一幕中与任美璃那诡异回声的遭遇转化为优势。</p>\n<p>本章开头的几场遭遇假定PC们为11级，但由于缺乏战斗遭遇，即便是10级PC们也仍能应对这些内容，并在开始执行任美璃的任务之前获得足够的XP升至11级。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-murder-scene-investigation.webp\" alt=\"Murder Scene Investigation\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"The Princess’s Web\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 12:</span>\n  <span>The Princess’s Web</span>\n</h1>\n\n<p>The jorogumo are the cruel and capricious rulers of Shenmen. The nation’s citizens fear them, for their treatment of their subjects is fraught with horror and dread. The best many can hope for is to be forgotten and left to struggle on their own without any support from their government at all. Lady Ren Mei Li is a high-ranking member of the jorogumo court, and among the communities that fall into her web is Willowshore. While the PCs encountered a version of her in the previous act, she has never actually met the PCs—her first visit to Willowshore was on the first day of the year after the townsfolk had been slaughtered and whisked away to the mindscape. She found Willowshore abandoned and had her servants loot the place of its valuables as offerings to Lady Lang Loi (while keeping a fair amount for herself), and for the past century, she spared very little thought for the area.</p>\n<p>News of Willowshore’s return reaches her ears quickly. Ren Mei Li soon returns to Willowshore to find out where it and its people have been, and to “welcome” them back in the best way the jorogumo know how—with cruel demands and economically fraught fines. The PCs can soften these political blows, and they can use their encounter with the strange echo of Ren Mei Li in the previous act to their advantage.</p>\n<p>While the first few encounters in this chapter assume the PCs are 11th level, the lack of combat encounters means that 10th level PCs will still be able to navigate them and earn enough XP to be 11th level before they begin to run Ren Mei Li’s missions.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Act 4.3: A Fiend in Two Worlds": {
          "name": "第4.3幕：游走于两个世界的邪魔 Act 4.3: A Fiend in Two Worlds",
          "pages": {
            "Concluding the Adventure": {
              "name": "冒险总结 Concluding the Adventure",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">冒险总结</span>\n</h1>\n<p>随着和善保被击败或获救、苦迦菩提的最终死亡，以及谭杉寺的复原，柳岸镇在现代神门中的地位得以稳固。未来仍会有危险威胁这座城镇，但此刻，柳岸镇的人民可以休息、恢复，并继续兴盛。</p>\n<p>若PC们回到谭杉寺的废墟，他们会发现杉树比以往任何时候都更健康；入夜后，树叶会闪烁着淡淡的银光。如今，一股平和而神圣的气息弥漫在废墟之中；关于这场惊人蜕变的消息很快便会传开，吸引新一代朝圣者前来，并在时光流转中，将寺院恢复到它最初的使命。</p>\n<p>如果PC们在战役结束时与罗昆、 大尊柳或伊索里关系良好，他们会在接下来的几天里前来拜访，描述他们在各自领地中观察到的变化。罗昆报告说他希望重建丝蜂团——他提出将团队的服务提供给柳岸镇，作为道路上的探员，协助保护往来旅人穿越周边土地；若PC们未来打算对抗络新妇，他也可能将这支队伍培养成一项宝贵资源。与此同时，大尊柳与伊索里先前在自然界中察觉到的细微扰动，以及他们所目睹的凶兆，都已消散——不过，那伽尤其指出，在他占卜所及的外缘仍残留着些许令人不安的小征兆。</p>\n<p>接下来的几个月，柳岸镇过得安宁愉快。天气良好，庄稼兴旺。重建工作稳步推进，只出现一些寻常问题，比如招募劳力与获取材料。任美璃信守承诺，柳岸镇也在含蓄的私语间渐渐得名——被视为某种能躲避络新妇劫掠的庇护所。</p>\n<p>在这段时日之后，柳岸镇的未来将完全取决于PC们的行动与长远计划。他们或许会选择更积极地介入络新妇宫廷的谋划之中，比如扶持任美璃成为朗洛依夫人的竞争者，或着手从根本上削弱络新妇。他们也可能把柳岸镇打造成神门中一座小小的安全孤岛；不过也始终存在一种可能：某位引人注目的逃亡者或政治难民试图在此藏身，从而让PC们陷入尴尬的困境。</p>\n<p>当然，最重要的未了之事，便是灵堕魔半神苦迦菩提。他再一次沉寂，死在谭杉寺根系之下；而与所有灵堕魔一样，他仍有可能转世重生。要将苦迦菩提彻底从灵魂轮回中抹除，是一种只有最强大的英雄才该尝试的传奇任务。此举将需要一次漫长的使命——不是进入被他死去梦境所腐化的思维空间，而是深入灵堕魔那邪恶心智内部、完全存在其中的现实；那里的恐怖将让PC们在《鬼季》冒险路径中所挺过的一切都相形见绌，并以前所未有的方式考验他们！</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Concluding the Adventure</span>\n</h1>\n<p>With Heh Shan-Bao’s defeat or rescue, Kugaptee’s final death, and the restoration of the Tan Sugi, Willowshore’s place in modern Shenmen is assured. Future dangers will face the town, but for now, the people of Willowshore can rest, recover, and thrive.</p>\n<p>Should the PCs return to the ruins of the Tan Sugi Monastery, they’ll find the sugi tree to be healthier than it has ever been before, and after dark, its leaves shimmer with a faint silvery light. An aura of peace and sanctity now pervades the ruins, and news of this astonishing transformation soon begins to draw a new generation of pilgrims who, in time, shall restore the monastery to its original cause.</p>\n<p>If the PCs finished the campaign on good terms with Lo Kuon, Great Willow, or Isori, they visit in the next few days to describe the changes they’ve observed in their territories. Lo Kuon reports that he hopes to rebuild the Silkwasps—he offers the group’s services to Willowshore as road agents who’ll help defend travelers through the surrounding lands, and he could possibly grow the group into a valuable resource should the PCs seek to oppose the jorogumo in the future. Meanwhile, the subtle disturbances that Great Willow and Isori saw in the natural world, and the ominous portents they’ve borne witness to, have vanished—although the naga in particular notes that there are still some minor, disquieting omens in the outer reaches of his divinations.</p>\n<p>The next few months pass pleasantly in Willowshore. The weather is good, and the crops thrive. Rebuilding proceeds apace, with only ordinary problems arising, like acquiring labor and materials. Ren Mei Li keeps her word, and Willowshore becomes known, via discreet whispers, as something of a sanctuary from the depredations of the jorogumo.</p>\n<p>What happens with Willowshore beyond these months depends entirely on the PCs’ actions and plans for the future. They might choose to take a more active role in the schemes of the jorogumo court, perhaps advancing Ren Mei Li as a rival to Lady Lang Loi or working to undermine the jorogumo altogether. They might establish Willowshore as a small island of safety in Shenmen, although it’s always possible that a high-profile escapee or political refugee might try to hide there, putting the PCs in an uncomfortable predicament.</p>\n<p>The most significant loose end, of course, is the nindoru demigod Kugaptee. Once again quiet and dead below the roots of the Tan Sugi, as with all nindorus, there remains the chance of his potential reincarnation. Removing Kugaptee entirely from the cycle of souls is the type of legendary quest only the most powerful of heroes should attempt. This endeavor would require a lengthy mission not into a mindscape corrupted by his dead dreams, but one found entirely within the nindoru’s evil mind—a reality that would put the horrors the PCs braved during the Season of Ghosts Adventure Path to shame and that would challenge them more than anything they’ve yet faced!</p>"
            },
            "A Heroine Passes Her Burden": {
              "name": "女英雄卸下她的重担 A Heroine Passes Her Burden",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">女英雄卸下重担</span>\n</h2>\n<p>只要至少有一名PC在苦迦菩提的最终死亡中幸存，这些幸存者便在柳岸镇的残破景象里默然蜷缩在一起。薄雾自四面八方翻涌而来，一段轻柔的笛声在烟雾般的寂静中蜿蜒回旋。那曲调看似简单，却带着一种让PC们在骨子深处某个地方似曾相识的节奏。随着乐声而来的，是一阵无声却强烈的情绪脉动，诸般情绪交织其间：希望、恐惧、骄傲，以及在痛苦面前的抗争。一种共同的使命感与自我牺牲的信念驱散了疲惫，振奋了魂魄。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-sui-jingtan.webp\" data-tooltip=\"谭隋靖\" alt=\"一位身着古装的女剑士的金色幻影\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-sui-jingtan.webp')\" />\n\n<p>研究古乐的学生可以凭借一次成功的 @Check[arts-lore|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 或 @Check[performance|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来回忆知识，从而辨认出这首曲子名为“暮光火炬”——一部同名古老英雄歌剧中曾经更为著名的一支曲子。其主题关乎新一代英雄从陨落的前辈手中接过希望之光并守护下去；象征意义则是于落日之前点燃火炬，在黑暗中保留其光芒的一部分。</p>\n<p>曲终之时，每名PC（包括任何已死亡者）都会闪现般看见一段幻象：他们曾在保卫柳岸镇时展现勇气或怜悯的某个瞬间，随后是一名身着古装的女剑士的身影；她的面容隐没不见，被夕阳映成剪影。战士松开长剑，每名PC都看见自己的手伸出去握住它。任何在一次 @Check[perception|dc:20] 检定中成功的PC都会认出那身影正是谭隋靖——击败苦迦菩提的女英雄，并转世的灵魂为至今仍生长在他坟上的杉木。</p>\n<p>幻象结束时，每名PC都感到神清气爽、恢复如初。任何生命值伤害都被治愈，所有残留状态都被移除，甚至那些在苦迦菩提的最终死亡中殒命的PC也会复生。谭隋靖分享自己的力量来复原PC时，也从他们身上汲取他们自身的经历、信念与灵性力量——这不会削弱或伤害PC，但会修复苦迦菩提坟上的杉木，使之如同 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}曾希望用他那失败的仪式做到的那样，得以在未来世代中愈发茁壮。</p>\n<p>所有PC都感到一阵疲惫、可怕的恐惧，以及再也无法抗拒的虚脱。片刻之后，他们全都在现实世界醒来，从他们在思维空间中总督宅邸对应版本里所处的相同位置起身——而这座宅邸终于以修复后的形态回到了活人的世界。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">A Heroine Passes Her Burden</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As long as at least one PC survives Kugaptee’s Final Death, those survivors huddle in silence within a ruined version of Willowshore. Mist rolls in all around them, and the sound of a softly playing flute winds through the smoky silence. It’s a deceptively simple song, but with a rhythm that the PCs recognize from somewhere deep in their bones. With the song comes a soundless but powerful pulse of mingled emotions: hope, fear, pride, and defiance in the face of pain. A shared sense of purpose and self-sacrifice lifts weariness and bolsters the spirit.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-sui-jingtan.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Tan Sui-Jing\" alt=\"a golden vision of a swordswoman in ancient dress\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-sui-jingtan.webp')\" />\n\n<p>Students of old music can recognize the song as “The Dusklight Torch” with a successful @Check[arts-lore|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[performance|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge—a once much-more-famous song from an old heroic opera by the same title. The theme of the piece concerns a new generation of heroes preserving the light of hope by claiming it from a fallen predecessor, symbolized by the lighting of a torch in front of the setting sun to preserve some fraction of its light in the darkness.</p>\n<p>As the song ends, each PC (including any who are dead) receives a flashed vision of a moment when they displayed bravery or compassion in Willowshore’s defense, followed by the image of a swordswoman in ancient dress; her face unseen as it’s silhouetted against the sunset. The warrior drops her sword, and each PC sees their own hand reach out to grasp it. Any PC who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:20] check recognizes the figure as that of Tan Sui-Jing, the heroine who defeated Kugaptee and reincarnated as the sugi that grows still over his grave.</p>\n<p>At the conclusion of the vision, each PC feels refreshed and restored. Any Hit Point damage is healed, all lingering conditions are removed, and even PCs who perished during Kugaptee’s Final Death are restored to life. As Tan Sui-Jing shares her strength to restore the PCs, she also draws from them their own experiences, convictions, and spiritual power—this doesn’t diminish or harm the PCs, but it does restore the sugi tree over Kugaptee’s grave, bolstering the tree for generations to come in the same way @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} had hoped to do so with his failed ritual.</p>\n<p>All the PCs feel a wave of weariness, terrible fear, and an exhaustion that can no longer be resisted. A moment later, they all awaken in the real world, rising from the same positions they occupied in the mindscape’s version of the governor’s manor—which has finally returned in its restored form to the living world.</p>"
            },
            "Kugaptee’s Final Death": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提的最终死亡 Kugaptee’s Final Death",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提的最终死亡</span>\n</h2>\n<p>一旦PC们击败了此处的敌人，并且@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的命运已被决定，苦迦菩提终于做出直接反应。若PC们未能击败敌人而死去，他的利爪将猛然向下拍击，在他重生回现世之前摧毁宅邸以及其中PC们的遗骸，从而为整个神门带来一场可怖的新现实。</p>\n<p>否则，他的利爪将狂乱抽打、胡乱挥舞，徒劳地抓向周遭世界，而这片世界开始被拉拽回地下。随着这一过程继续，PC们周围的世界会在震颤中支离破碎：地动山摇、刮肉剜肌的灵堕魔蝴蝶风暴、一阵心灵的痛苦浪潮，以及来自死亡本身的撕魂拉拽——直到苦迦菩提再次沉落回真正而寂静的死亡。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注释</span><span class=\"keepme\">氛围 / 音效</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.FGK5jsYreqU1AR5o.PlaylistSound.oJzJaUgSUvz1iSVu]{环境音：Kuraptree's Rise} | @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.odgltUm1HHlAxrpq]{1: Crashing Arms} @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.m1oFrwQQj59kIEw4]{2: Clouds Of Butterflies} @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.iTPjeUEOk6IAwKbo]{3: Demonic Roar} @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.bKPpzdkOEBNYuAPW]{4: Death Roar}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>这场灾厄会在四轮内上演。在此期间，思维空间在PC们周围被撕裂瓦解，PC们无法逃回现实。若想逃回家园，他们必须坚持并见证这个世界的终结；但如果他们已找回与和善保生平相关的四个“联结”，则会获得一定的保护。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>1：世界震颤</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">当苦迦菩提的手臂撼动世界时，会引发一场猛烈地震。PC们周围的宅邸坍塌，他们被抛倒在地并被瓦砾重击；与此同时，透过宅邸屋顶被撕裂出的破洞，仍可见天空中苦迦菩提手臂屈伸的影像。每名PC承受@Damage[5d6[bludgeoning]]伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:30|basic]豁免）。若某名PC携带着在<em>七贤之智</em>中找到的信件，他会被一种受保护的感觉所笼罩，仿佛父母正用护盾术为他们挡住震颤。信件随即消失，且所有PC不受苦迦菩提死亡此阶段的影响。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>2：血肉撕裂</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">苦迦菩提手臂沿线裂口绽开，一团团刀翼灵堕魔蝴蝶俯冲而下，吞没世界；它们的翅、足与齿会刮削一切裸露的血肉。每名PC承受@Damage[5d6[slashing]]伤害（@Check[fortitude|dc:30|basic]豁免）。若某名PC携带着玉真珠公主那幅破损的画像，他会被一种仿佛被爱人拥抱庇护的感觉所笼罩，使蝴蝶完全无视他们。画像随即消失，且所有PC不受苦迦菩提死亡此阶段的影响。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>3：心智战栗</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">当苦迦菩提的手臂被拉拽下沉入地面时，灵堕魔蝴蝶群被重新吸回他的血肉之中；与此同时，他因被拖回死亡而产生的痛苦与恐惧化作令人麻木的心灵感应咆哮，爆裂开来，甚至将思维本身撕成碎片。每名PC承受@Damage[5d6[mental]]伤害（@Check[will|dc:30|basic]豁免）。若某名PC携带着《七贤之智》，卷轴中承载的真理会支撑他们的心智，并使他们扎根于现实。卷轴随即消失，且所有PC不受苦迦菩提死亡此阶段的影响。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>4：最终死亡</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">当苦迦菩提的利爪滑回地底，他的咆哮戛然而止，PC们会短暂窥见死亡的本质。每名PC承受@Damage[5d6[void]]伤害（DC 30基础豁免；PC可以选择用@Check[fortitude|dc:30|basic]豁免承受此伤害，用@Check[reflex|dc:30|basic]豁免避开此伤害，或用@Check[will|dc:30|basic]豁免以护卫他们的转世的灵魂）。若某名PC携带着保存完好的山茶花与缎带，花朵将绽放新生，而一种属于生者世界的归属感会保护PC们。花朵与缎带随即消失，且所有PC不受苦迦菩提死亡这最后阶段的影响。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Kugaptee’s Final Death</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Once the PCs have defeated the foes here and @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s fate has been determined, Kugaptee finally and directly reacts. If the PCs fail to defeat the foes and perish, his claw slams downward to destroy the manor and the PCs’ remains within before he’s reborn into the living world, resulting in a horrific new reality for all of Shenmen.</p>\n<p>Otherwise, his claw thrashes and flails, grasping at the world around ineffectually as it begins to be drawn back into the ground. As this process continues, the world around the PCs is wracked by tremors, storms of flesh-scouring nindoru butterflies, a wave of psychic anguish, and a soul-wrenching pull from death itself before Kugaptee once again settles back into true and silent death.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Ambiance / SFX</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Playlist.FGK5jsYreqU1AR5o.PlaylistSound.oJzJaUgSUvz1iSVu]{Ambience: Kuraptree's Rise} | @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.odgltUm1HHlAxrpq]{1: Crashing Arms} @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.m1oFrwQQj59kIEw4]{2: Clouds Of Butterflies} @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.iTPjeUEOk6IAwKbo]{3: Demonic Roar} @UUID[Playlist.Mv66f1NNleR53M5o.PlaylistSound.bKPpzdkOEBNYuAPW]{4: Death Roar}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>This catastrophe plays out over the course of four rounds, during which the PCs can’t escape back to reality while the mindscape around them is torn apart. They must endure and witness the end of this world if they’re to escape back home, but if they’ve recovered the four links to Heh Shan-Bao’s life, they’ll be afforded some protection.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>1: The World Trembles</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">As Kugaptee’s arm shakes the world, it causes a violent earthquake. The manor surrounding the PCs collapses as they’re thrown to the ground and battered with rubble, while glimpses of Kugaptee’s arm flexing in the sky above are visible through holes tearing through the manor’s roof. Each PC takes @Damage[5d6[bludgeoning]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:30|basic] save). If a PC carries the letter found in <em>The Wisdom of the Seven Sages</em>, they’re bathed in a sensation of protection, as if their parents were shielding them from the tremors. The letter vanishes, and all the PCs are unaffected by this stage of Kugaptee’s death.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>2: The Flesh Tears</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">Rents open along the length of Kugaptee’s arm and clouds of razor-winged nindoru butterflies swoop down to engulf the world, their wings, legs, and teeth scouring any exposed flesh. Each PC takes @Damage[5d6[slashing]] damage (@Check[fortitude|dc:30|basic] save). If a PC carries the ruined portrait of Princess Ok Jinju, they’re bathed in the sensation of being sheltered in a lover’s arms, causing the butterflies to ignore them completely. The portrait vanishes, and all the PCs are unaffected by this stage of Kugaptee’s death.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>3: The Mind Recoils</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The swarms of nindoru butterflies are drawn back into Kugaptee’s flesh as his arm is pulled down into the ground, and with it, the mind-numbing telepathic roar of his anguish and fear at being drawn back into death blasts even thought itself to shreds. Each PC takes @Damage[5d6[mental]] damage (@Check[will|dc:30|basic] save). If a PC carries The Wisdom of the Seven Sages, the truths carried in the scroll bolster their minds and ground them in reality. The scroll vanishes, and all the PCs are unaffected by this stage of Kugaptee’s death.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>4: The Final Death</h2>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">As Kugaptee’s talons slide back into the ground, his roar is cut off, and the PCs gain a momentary glimpse into the very nature of death. Each PC takes @Damage[5d6[void]] damage (DC 30 basic save; a PC can choose to endure this damage with a @Check[fortitude|dc:30|basic] save, avoid it with a @Check[reflex|dc:30|basic] save, or shield their souls with a @Check[will|dc:30|basic] save). If a PC carries the preserved camellia flower and ribbon, the flower blooms with new life, and a feeling of belonging to the world of the living protects the PCs. The flower and ribbon vanish, and all the PCs are unaffected by this final stage of Kugaptee’s death.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Heh Shan-Bao Freed": {
              "name": "和善保 解放者 Heh Shan-Bao Freed",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">和善保获得解放</span>\n</h3>\n<p>若PC与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的影响至少达到7，他们就能打动他并说服他抛弃苦迦菩提，不过他们仍得击败两名未复起者——只有当他们的影响达到10时，才能放逐未复起者并不经战斗就解放善保。</p>\n<p>他获得解放时，如释重负地叹了口气，用双手捂住脸的上半部，惊讶地揉着复原的双眼。他扭曲的形体缓缓消解，恢复为原本的人类外貌；除非PC的影响达到10，否则他只披着褴褛衣衫，若影响达到10，则身着华美服饰。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“我感谢你们。”他低声说道。原本就瘦削的身形，随着他继续开口而开始变得愈发虚无缥缈，“感谢你们给我自由。也感谢你们纠正我太过软弱而无法阻止的错误，并以我曾以为自己能做到的方式引领柳岸镇。我失败了，这是我最大的耻辱。我只能希望神祇裁定我已为此受够了苦，因为我现在要去接受他们的审判。”</p>\n</div>\n<p>若PC的影响达到7至9，他的表情会骤然转为惊恐，并喊道：“苦迦菩提！他在这里！”片刻之后，他在痛苦的哀号中，逐渐消散的身体猛然炸裂成一团猩红的灵堕魔蝴蝶，随即迅速淡去。PC阻止了苦迦菩提重获生命，却付出了和善保永恒灵魂的代价。</p>\n<p>若PC的影响达到10，他的神情会变得安宁平和。“我看见苦迦菩提了，”他低声说道，“但我如今知道，他无法接触我的永恒灵魂。谢谢你们……谢谢你们……”片刻之后，他彻底消散，灵魂前往骨园接受审判——是转世、升格，还是惩罚，唯有@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}（以及你这位GM）才能断言。</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Heh Shan-Bao Freed</span>\n</h3>\n<p>If the PCs reach at least Influence 7 with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, they get through to him and convince him to cast aside Kugaptee, although they’ll still have to defeat the two unrisen—only if they reach Influence 10 do they banish the unrisen and free Shan-Bao without a fight.</p>\n<p>As he is freed, he sighs in relief and claps his hands over the upper half of his face, rubbing at his restored eyes with astonishment. His warped form slowly dissolves, restoring him to his original human appearance, clad in rags unless the PCs reached Influence 10, in which case he wears resplendent attire.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“I thank you,” he whispers. His form, slight to begin with, begins to fade into insubstantiality as he continues, “I thank you for my freedom. I thank you, too, for righting the wrong I was too weak to prevent and for leading Willowshore in the way that I once believed I could. I failed, and it is my greatest shame. I can only hope the gods decree that I have suffered enough for it, for I go to their judgment now.”</p>\n</div>\n<p>If the PCs reached Influence 7 through 9, his expression suddenly turns to horror, and he cries out, “Kugaptee! He’s here!” A moment later, he wails in anguish as his fading body bursts into an explosion of crimson nindoru butterflies that swiftly fades away. The PCs have prevented Kugaptee from returning to life, but at the cost of Heh Shan-Bao’s eternal soul.</p>\n<p>If the PCs reached Influence 10, his expression becomes one of serene peace. “I see Kugaptee,” he whispers, “But I know now he cannot touch my eternal soul. Thank you... thank you...” A moment later, he fades away entirely, his soul traveling to the Boneyard to be judged—be it reincarnation, ascension, or punishment, only @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} (and you as the GM) can say.</p>"
            },
            "Speaking with Heh Shan-Bao": {
              "name": "与和善保说话 Speaking with Heh Shan-Bao",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">与和善保交谈</span>\n</h3>\n<p>如果PC与@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}交谈，他们可以按自己认为合适的方式回应他的挑衅。对话应当自然展开，和善保会以一种高高在上、居高临下的姿态回应PC。只要PC继续与他说话，他们就会逐渐磨损苦迦菩提的影响，并提醒和善保他曾经是人类。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shan-baohehmonstrousportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Heh Shan-Bao\" alt=\"曾被称为和善保的恶魔\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shan-baohehmonstrousportrait.webp')\" />\n<p>这场影响遭遇的每一轮会在1分钟内进行。PC起始有1分钟，并会根据队伍携带了多少条与督抚前世相关的线索而获得额外轮数。他们可能发现了四条潜在线索：位于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c2courtyard000]{C2}区域的朽坏的欧锦珠肖像、位于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4}区域的《七贤智慧》、在那卷轴中发现的信件、以及位于@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}区域的保存完好的花与缎带。队伍中任何人携带上述任意一件物品，都会让队伍获得额外1分钟来影响和善保——若他们把四条线索全都带在身上，他们就能获得最大值5个影响轮来触及这位饱受折磨的督抚。</p>\n<p>如果PC在本遭遇最后一轮结束前未能至少达到影响7，和善保的耐心就会崩断。“去死吧，冒牌货，”他咆哮道，“去死吧，然后永远被锁链束缚在灵魂轮回之外。”此时他发起攻击——按与和善保战斗处理，见前一页。如果PC达到影响7但在遭遇结束前未能达到影响10，他们会说服他抛弃苦迦菩提，但两段未活之生仍然存在——那两名未起者会立刻同时攻击，必须先将其击败，PC才能继续进行“和善保获释”。如果PC在任何时候达到影响10，影响遭遇立即结束。两名未起者会在痛苦中哀号后消失，和善保将苦迦菩提抛到一旁——继续进行“和善保获释”。</p>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>和善保</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">幻觉</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">心灵</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">苦迦菩提的初生容器</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +23</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>意志</strong> +21</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:29|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[society|dc:30|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:32|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响技能</strong> @Check[nindoru-lore|dc:28|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（警告他关于灵堕魔与苦迦菩提的真实本性），@Check[religion|dc:30|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（说话说明他与苦迦菩提的牵连具有自我毁灭性），@Check[society|dc:32|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（提醒他成为更大社会中富有成效的一员是怎样的感受），@Check[diplomacy|dc:30|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]，@Check[intimidation|dc:31|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]，@Check[deception|dc:33|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响4</strong> PC设法触及和善保仍鲜活的记忆。从这一点开始，明显携带<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>所带来的不利（见下文“减值”）将被抵消，但PC仍可通过把钥匙交给他来获得加值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响7</strong> 和善保泪崩，他的愤怒骤然被悲伤取代。他的灵魂仍被交付给苦迦菩提，而当他获释时，这灵魂会被邪魔吞噬——他无法被复活，也没有来世。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响10</strong> 和善保止住泪水，变得极其决心；影响遭遇结束。继续进行下方@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15hehshanbaofr00]{和善保获释}。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>抗力</strong> 和善保对任何暗示他出于自身私利行事、而非（以某种方式）为了拯救柳岸镇的说法都极为反感。任何时候只要PC暗示或声称他的行为给城镇带来了伤害，该次影响检定的DC提高2。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>弱点</strong> 若某名PC明显携带四件与和善保前世相关物品中的一件（锦珠的肖像、<em>《七贤智慧》</em>、卷轴中的信件、或保存完好的花），该PC用以影响和善保的DC降低2。若某名PC将<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>交给和善保（从而暗示他们即便如今也视他为统治者），影响他的所有DC再额外降低2。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>减值</strong> 和善保傲慢地将自己视为柳岸镇唯一真正的统治者。若某名PC明显携带獠牙与钥匙，这种对其统治权的隐含挑战会让他更为顽固。该PC用于影响和善保的DC提高2，即使该PC之后藏起或放弃獠牙与钥匙也一样——除非该PC将<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>交给和善保；在这种情况下，影响他的DC反而对所有PC降低2；该降低可与上文其他弱点所给予的DC降低叠加。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Speaking with Heh Shan-Bao</span>\n</h3>\n<p>If the PCs speak to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, they can reply to his challenge as they see fit. The conversation should play out naturally, with Heh Shan-Bao reacting to the PCs with an air of superiority and condescension. As long as the PCs continue to speak to him, they’ll wear away at Kugaptee’s influence and remind Heh Shan-Bao that he was once human.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shan-baohehmonstrousportrait.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Heh Shan-Bao\" alt=\"the fiend formerly known as Heh Shan-Bao\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shan-baohehmonstrousportrait.webp')\" />\n<p>Each round of this influence encounter plays out over the course of 1 minute. PCs start with 1 minute and gain additional rounds depending on how many links to the governor’s previous life the party carries. There are four potential links they could’ve discovered: the ruined portrait of Ok Jinju from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c2courtyard000]{C2}, The Wisdom of the Seven Sages from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4}, the letter found within that scroll, and the preserved flower and ribbon from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}. Each one of these items that someone in the group carries grants the party 1 additional minute to influence Heh Shan-Bao—if they all four links with them, they’ll have the maximum possible of 5 influence rounds to reach the tormented governor.</p>\n<p>If the PCs fail to reach at least Influence 7 by the final round of this encounter, Heh Shan-Bao’s patience snaps. “Die, pretenders,” he roars, “die, and be chained outside the cycle of souls forevermore.” At this point, he attacks—proceed with Fighting with Heh Shan-Bao, see previous page. If the PCs reach Influence 7 but fail to reach Influence 10 by the end of the encounter, they convince him to abandon Kugaptee, but the two Unlived Lives remain—the two unrisen attack at once and must be defeated before the PCs can proceed with Heh Shan-Bao Freed. If the PCs reach Influence 10 at any point, the influence encounter ends immediately. Both unrisen cry out in anguish before vanishing, and Heh Shan-Bao casts Kugaptee aside—proceed with Heh Shan-Bao Freed.</p>\n<section class=\"action\" style=\"padding-bottom:1ch\">\n  <h2 class=\"split\">\n    <span>Heh Shan-Bao</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">unique</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Illusion</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Mental</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Nascent vessel for Kugaptee</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +23</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Will</strong> +21</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:29|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[society|dc:30|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:32|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence Skills</strong> @Check[nindoru-lore|dc:28|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to warn him about the true nature of nindorus and Kugaptee), @Check[religion|dc:30|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to speak about how his association with Kugaptee is self-destructive), @Check[society|dc:32|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to remind him of what it was like to be a productive part of a larger society), @Check[diplomacy|dc:30|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:31|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:33|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 4</strong> The PCs manage to reach Heh Shan-Bao’s living memories. At this point onward, the disadvantage for visibly carrying the <em>Fang and Key</em> (see “Penalty,” below) is negated, but the PCs can still gain a bonus by giving him the key.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 7</strong> Heh Shan-Bao breaks down in tears, his anger suddenly replaced by grief. His soul is still consigned to Kugaptee, and when he’s freed, it is consumed by the fiend—he can’t be restored to life and has no afterlife.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 10</strong> Heh Shan-Bao stanches his tears and grows fiercely determined; the influence encounter ends. Proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15hehshanbaofr00]{Heh Shan-Bao Freed} below.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Resistances</strong> Heh Shan-Bao bristles against any implication that he acted for his own self-interest and not, in some way, to save Willowshore. Any time a PC implies or states that his actions have brought harm to the town, the DC for that Influence check is increased by 2.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Weaknesses</strong> If a PC visibly carries one of the four items that link to Heh Shan-Bao’s past life (Jinju’s portrait, <em>The Wisdom of the Seven Sages</em>, the scroll’s letter, or the preserved flower), the DCs for that PC to Influence Heh Shan-Bao are reduced by 2. If a PC gives Heh Shan-Bao the <em>Fang and Key</em> (thereby implying that they view him as their ruler even now), all DCs to Influence him are reduced by an additional 2.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Penalty</strong> Heh Shan-Bao arrogantly views himself as Willowshore’s only true ruler. If a PC visibly carries the Fang and Key, the implied challenge to his rule makes him grow even more stubborn. The DCs for that PC to Influence Heh Shan-Bao are increased by 2, even if that PC later hides or relinquishes the Fang and Key—unless the PC gives the <em>Fang and Key</em> to Heh Shan-Bao, in which case the DCs to Influence him are instead reduced by 2 for all PCs; this reduction stacks with the DC reduction granted for the other Weaknesses above.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Fighting with Heh Shan-Bao": {
              "name": "与和善保战斗 Fighting with Heh Shan-Bao",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">与和善保并肩作战</span>\n</h3>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-monstrous-shan-bao-heh.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">与和善保并肩作战</span> <span class=\"keepme\">极难 12</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.U8XsqkUGeomC67b3]{Heh Shan-Bao} @UUID[Actor.yH76LIxgrsHWyllN]{Unlived Lives (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>和善保派出两名未起者与PC交锋。战斗开始时，它们以“可怖逼近”踉跄向前，分开行动，各自将近战攻击集中在不同的PC身上。（虽然和善保会被未起者的“痛苦嚎叫”所伤害，但他不受它们“可怖逼近”景象的影响。）</p>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unlived-life.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Unlived Life\" alt=\"mangled conglomeration of splintered bones, decaying organs, and rotting flesh\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unlived-life.webp')\" />\n  <p>战斗伊始，和善保会先退在后方，在最初几轮用他的自发法术对付PC，之后才改用利爪。如果某位PC成为“窃取灵魂”的合适目标，他会迅速移动过去利用这一局势（若尝试失败，这会让和善保恼怒到不再犯同样的错误，并且不再对PC使用这一战术）。</p>\n  <p><strong>已释放的转世的灵魂：</strong>PC每释放三名被锁链束缚的转世的灵魂中的一名，当未起者在“再度起身”时，将其生命值减少20；若三名灵魂全部被释放，则未起者在“再度起身”时仅有40点生命值。此外，PC每释放三名灵魂中的一名，和善保的传说就会动摇。若释放了1名灵魂，他失去“气势凶猛”。若释放了2名灵魂，他失去“气势凶猛”，并失去其打击的挥砍伤害。若释放了3名灵魂全部，他失去“气势凶猛”、其打击的挥砍伤害，以及对物理伤害的抗力。</p>\n  <p><strong>击败和善保：</strong>当他的生命值降至0后，和善保倒地，似乎已经死亡。只要两名未活之命仍在，战斗就会继续，直到它们也被彻底击败。此时，和善保的尸体会猛然抽动着再度苏醒，勉强维持片刻，让他在爆裂成一团迅速消散的猩红灵堕魔蝴蝶之前，发出一声痛苦的尖叫——他的灵魂已被苦迦菩提吞噬。继续阅读@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15kugapteesfin00]{Kugaptee’s Final Death}。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Fighting with Heh Shan-Bao</span>\n</h3>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-monstrous-shan-bao-heh.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Fighting with Heh Shan-Bao</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 12</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.U8XsqkUGeomC67b3]{Heh Shan-Bao} @UUID[Actor.yH76LIxgrsHWyllN]{Unlived Lives (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Heh Shan-Bao sends the two unrisen to clash with the PCs. As combat begins, they lurch forward with an Awful Approach, splitting up to each focus their melee attacks against a different PC. (While Heh Shan-Bao can be harmed by an unrisen’s Agonized Howl, he’s unaffected by the sight of their Awful Approach.)</p>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unlived-life.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Unlived Life\" alt=\"mangled conglomeration of splintered bones, decaying organs, and rotting flesh\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-unlived-life.webp')\" />\n  <p>Heh Shan-Bao hangs back at the start of a fight, using his innate spells against the PCs for the first few rounds before switching to his claws. If a PC becomes a viable target for Steal Soul, he quickly moves to take advantage of that situation (if the attempt fails, this frustrates Heh Shan-Bao enough that he won’t make that mistake again and no longer uses this tactic against the PCs).</p>\n  <p><strong>Released Souls: </strong>For each of the three chained souls the PCs released, reduce an unrisen’s Hit Points when they Rise Again by 20; if all three souls are released, an unrisen has only 40 Hit Points upon Rising Again. In addition, for each of the three souls the PCs released, Heh Shan-Bao’s legend falters. If one soul has been released, he loses his frightful presence. If two souls are released, he loses frightful presence and the slashing damage from his Strikes. If all three souls are released, he loses frightful presence, the slashing damage from his Strikes, and his resistance to physical damage.</p>\n  <p><strong>Defeating Heh Shan-Bao:</strong> Once he’s reduced to 0 Hit Points, Heh Shan-Bao collapses to the ground, apparently dead. As long as the unlived lives remain, combat continues until they too are fully defeated. At this point, Heh Shan-Bao’s body lurches back to life long enough for him to shriek in pain an instant before he bursts into a cloud of crimson nindoru butterflies that swiftly fades—his soul has been consumed by Kugaptee. Proceed with @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15kugapteesfin00]{Kugaptee’s Final Death}.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Heh Shan-Bao Arrives": {
              "name": "和善保抵达 Heh Shan-Bao Arrives",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">和善保到来</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">严重 12</span>\n</h2>\n<p>最后一只煞星魔被杀死的瞬间，庭院上方那只高耸的巨爪猛然发出雷鸣般的一抽动，手指屈伸，仿佛要把月亮从天上摘下来。那股屈伸的力量沿着肢体一路传递下来，引得庭院一阵震颤——还不至于把PC震得倒地，但依然令人心惊。</p>\n<p>片刻之后，通往庭院的一扇门打开，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}迈步而入，身旁还跟着两个对他外貌的可怖拙劣模仿——扭曲、呜咽的残骸，踉跄着用手脚在地上爬行，躯体带着骇人的创口，四肢以别扭而不自然的角度弯折。它们行动起来更像蜘蛛而非人类，但每一张脸都是和善保的面孔。这些是“未升者”，代表着和善保曾经经历过的一段失败人生。他左侧的未升者身着华美长袍，佩戴着你可能会在一位成功的总督身上看到的精致饰物，象征着若他没有尝试那场注定使柳岸镇毁灭的命运仪式，本可过上的人生。他右侧的未升者穿着朴素却舒适的学者长袍，象征着若他彻底避开政治、始终作为学者，本可过上的人生。两者都对站在它们之间的、妖鬼形态的和善保绝对而盲目地忠诚。</p>\n<p>若PC尚未释放任何被锁链束缚的魂魄，和善保会带着怜爱伸手轻抚木瘤上被钉穿的眼睛；他最初与PC交谈时，声音平静而居高临下。反之，若这些眼睛缺失了部分或全部，和善保会怒视那些空缺之处，并以几乎压不住怒火的声音对PC说话。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“所以，你们终于站在我面前了，立于我上方主君的阴影之下。他归来的时代已至，你们无论做什么都无法阻止，可你们还是……来了。你们凭什么胆敢插手统治者与神祇的事务？”</p>\n</div>\n<p>在此时此刻，PC有机会将和善保从苦迦菩提的影响中解救出来。他们的成功取决于他们从修复后的庄园中找回了多少物品，以及他们运用这些物品来对付他的技能。若他们未能将他解救出来，与总督及其失败的过往人生（由两名未升者的存在所显现）的一战，仍能阻止苦迦菩提归来。</p>\n<p>除非PC试图离开，否则和善保不会主动开始战斗。除此之外，只有在PC挑起战斗，或谈判失败导致局势破裂时，他才会出手。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Heh Shan-Bao Arrives</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Severe 12</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As soon as the last shisagishin is slain, the towering claw looming over the courtyard gives a thunderous twitch, its fingers flexing as if attempting to pluck the moon from the sky. That flex translates down the limb’s length to rock the courtyard with a tremor—not violent enough to knock the PCs prone, but frightening nonetheless.</p>\n<p>A moment later, one of the doors into the courtyard opens, and in steps @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, accompanied by two horrific parodies of his appearance—twisted, mewling wreckages that stagger and crawl on their hands and knees, their bodies bearing gruesome wounds and limbs bending in awkward, unnatural angles. They move more like spiders than humans, yet each one’s face is that of Heh Shan-Bao. These are unrisen representing a failed life that Heh Shan-Bao lived. The one to his left wears fine robes and elegant accoutrements one might expect of a successful governor, symbolizing the life he could’ve lived had he not attempted the fateful ritual that doomed Willowshore. The unrisen to his right wears plain but comfortable scholar’s robes, symbolizing the life he could’ve lived had he avoided politics entirely and remained a scholar. Both are completely and mindlessly loyal to the yohoi version of Heh Shan-Bao who stands between them.</p>\n<p>If the PCs haven’t released any of the chained spirits, Heh Shan-Bao lovingly reaches out to caress the eyes impaled on the wooden burl, and when he initially speaks to the PCs, his voice is calm and condescending. On the other hand, if some or all of these eyes are missing, Heh Shan-Bao regards the missing spots with fury and addresses the PCs with a voice that barely restrains his outrage.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“And so, you finally stand before me, in the shadow of my lord above. His time of return has come, and there is nothing you can do to stop it, yet still... here you are. By what right do you dare meddle in the affairs of rulers and gods?”</p>\n</div>\n<p>At this juncture, the PCs have an opportunity to free Heh Shan-Bao from Kugaptee’s influence. Their success depends on how many items they recovered from the restored manor and on their own skill in using these items against him. If they fail to free him, a fight against the governor and his failed past lives (manifested by the presence of the two unrisen) can still prevent Kugaptee’s return.</p>\n<p>Heh Shan-Bao doesn’t start combat unless the PCs attempt to leave. Otherwise, he fights only if the PCs start a battle, or as a result of failed negotiations.</p>"
            },
            "Below Kugaptee’s Claw": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提之爪下方 Below Kugaptee’s Claw",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提之爪下</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">12级（变化）</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一汪闪着光的血池、一座骨制花园喷泉，以及成簇的病变枝叶，把庄园的核心变成了一场噩梦。朦胧可见的生物在血色池塘中泼溅，而红翅蝴蝶在枝叶间聚集。四下里，几具看着眼熟的尸体散落在地上。庭院边缘、环绕柱廊的屋檐下，挂着一些既骇人却又做工精良的灯笼——它们由被剥下的人脸皮制成。头顶的夜空被一轮巨大、形如红色眼睛的月亮照亮。在那座怪异城市北侧的山顶上，一只高耸的巨爪拔地而起，阴影笼罩着庭院，仿佛几乎要将月亮托在掌中。</p>\n  <p>在庭院北端，两张芦席之间的地面上放着一团树瘤。树瘤的根须向上扭曲，像攫握的触须般伸展，每一条都被鲜血浸得发亮。</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>北边的树瘤是苦迦菩提那恶魔之心的实体显化。如果PC们已经将所有被谋杀的受害者从他们的镣铐中释放（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15thechainedsp00]{被锁链束缚的魂魄}），那么树瘤向上伸展的根须就只是染着血迹。每有一个魂魄仍被镣铐束缚，就会有一双眼睛被钉穿在两条不同的根须上，悲伤地凝望着庭院。</p>\n<p>散落在庭院中的尸体看起来很眼熟，因为它们似乎是PC们在这条冒险路径的过程中逐渐喜欢上的NPC们的遗体。这些尸体并不真实，但看上去却像真的一样。它们大多不过是苦迦菩提布置在此的心理战争要素，但其中有些并不止于此。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-shisagishin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提之爪下</span> <span class=\"keepme\">12级（变化）</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.pqi2xSTYoXw5MtwN]{煞星魔（2至4）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>这里的部分尸体实际上是伪装成死者的煞星魔灵堕魔。尸体中出现的煞星魔数量取决于PC们释放了多少被锁链束缚的魂魄。如果他们一个都没释放，那么这里有四具尸体是煞星魔（12级极限遭遇）。如果PC们至少释放了其中一个被锁链束缚的魂魄，那么死者中只有三只煞星魔（12级严重遭遇）。如果PC们释放了全部三个被锁链束缚的魂魄，他们将只面对两只煞星魔（12级中等遭遇）。</p>\n  <p>一旦任意一个煞星魔“尸壳”被触碰，该煞星魔就会使用其<strong>死中暴起</strong>反应动作（）来尝试对触碰它的PC进行一次<strong>打击</strong>——随后所有灵堕魔都为先攻掷骰其潜行。若在1分钟内无人触碰伪装的煞星魔，或当庭院内最后一个人离开该区域时（以先发生者为准），灵堕魔为先攻掷骰其潜行，并从它们的尸壳中起身发动攻击，但不会利用<strong>死中暴起</strong>。灵堕魔会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Below Kugaptee’s Claw</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Varies 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A glistening pool of blood, a bone garden fountain, and clusters of diseased foliage turn the heart of the manor into a nightmare. Barely glimpsed creatures splash in the bloody pond, while red-winged butterflies gather in the foliage. Here and there, familiar looking bodies lie strewn on the ground. Grisly yet well-made lanterns crafted with skinned human faces hang along the edges of the courtyard from the eaves of the surrounding colonnade. The night sky above shines with the light of an immense red eye-shaped moon. From the hilltop north of the strange city, the towering claw rises, looming over the courtyard as it appears almost to cradle the moon in its grasp.</p>\n  <p>At the courtyard’s northern end, a wood burl sits on the ground between two reed mats. The roots of the burl twist upward like grasping tendrils, and each glistens with blood.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>The burl of wood to the north is a physical manifestation of Kugaptee’s fiendish heart. If the PCs have released all of the murdered victims from their shackles (see @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15thechainedsp00]{The Chained Spirits}), then the upward reaching roots of the burl are merely bloodstained. For each soul that remains shackled, a pair of eyes are impaled upon two different roots, staring mournfully out into the courtyard.</p>\n<p>The corpses sprawled across the courtyard appear familiar, for they seem to be the bodies of NPCs the PCs have grown fond of over the course of this Adventure Path. These bodies aren’t real, but they appear as if they are. Most of them serve as little more than psychological warfare elements placed here by Kugaptee, but some of them are more than that.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-shisagishin.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Below Kugaptee's Claw</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Varies 12</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.pqi2xSTYoXw5MtwN]{Shisagishins (2 to 4)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A number of the corpses here are actually shisagishin nindorus disguised as the dead. The number of shisagishin present among the corpses depends on how many of the chained spirits the PCs released. If they released none of them, then four of the bodies here are shisagishins (an Extreme 12 encounter). If the PCs released at least one of the chained spirits, then only three shisagishins are among the dead (a Severe 12 encounter). If the PCs released all three chained spirits, they’ll face only two shisagishins (a Moderate 12 encounter).</p>\n  <p>Once any of the shisagishin Corpse Shells are touched, that shisagishin uses its Burst From Death reaction to attempt a Strike on the PC who touched it—all of the nindorus then roll Stealth for initiative. If no one touches a disguised shisagishin after a minute or when the last person in the courtyard leaves the area (whichever comes first), the nindorus roll Stealth for initiative and rise up from their Corpse Shells to attack without taking advantage of Burst From Death. The nindorus fight to the death.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "The Governor’s Den": {
              "name": "总督之穴 The Governor’s Den",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">总督的巢穴</span>\n</h1>\n<p>当区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d4springspat00]{D4}北端的门被打开时，一片闪烁的薄雾遮蔽了门后的一切。那薄雾翻涌而出，充满整座建筑群，片刻之后又消散，显露出PC们如今正站在总督府邸的区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c1manorentra00]{C1}。滑动纸墙挡住了看向府邸庭院的视线，但这一次，情况更令人不安，因为PC们发现自己正处于苦迦菩提那铺天盖地的影响的核心。</p>\n<p>此处的府邸墙壁上覆满了数百只看上去阴森的红色眼睛，它们在PC之间随机扫视。这些眼睛的察觉加值为+26；若它们发现入侵者，正于府邸庭院中等待PC的@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}便会察觉到他们。</p>\n<p>PC们现在必须做出选择：他们可以穿过南面的门退回去，返回苦迦菩提之攫（从总督府邸的废墟进入那处思维空间，就像他们最初抵达时那样——他们需要再次穿越苦迦菩提之墓，才能回到此处），或者他们也可以进一步深入府邸。</p>\n<p>\n  这些区域看起来与区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c3servantsqu00]{C3}– @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}相同，只是其中没有生物、危害与宝藏。只要PC们打开任何一扇通往庭院的门，他们就会触发《<em>鬼季</em>》冒险路径的最终遭遇。继续阅读下方“苦迦菩提之爪下”。\n</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Governor’s Den</span>\n</h1>\n<p>When the doors at the northern end of area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d4springspat00]{D4} are opened, a shimmering haze obscures what lies beyond. That haze billows out to fill the entire complex, fading a moment later to reveal the PCs now standing in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c1manorentra00]{C1} of the governor’s manor. Sliding paper walls block the view into the manor’s courtyard, but this time, things are more unsettling, for the PCs now find themselves at the very heart of Kugaptee’s overwhelming influence.</p>\n<p>The manor walls here are covered with hundreds of sinister-looking red eyes that glance randomly between the PCs. These eyes have a Perception bonus of +26; if they spot intruders, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, who awaits the PCs in the manor courtyard, becomes aware of them.</p>\n<p>The PCs have a choice to make now: they can step back through the door to the south and return to Kugaptee’s Grasp (emerging into that mindscape from the ruins of the governor’s manor, just as they did when they first arrived—they’ll need to make a return journey through Kugaptee’s Grave to reach this point again), or they can move further into the manor.</p>\n<p>\n  These areas appear as in areas @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c3servantsqu00]{C3}– @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}, except that they’re empty of creatures, hazards, and treasures. As soon as the PCs open any door into the courtyard, they trigger the final encounter of the <em>Season of Ghosts</em>\n  Adventure Path. Proceed with Below Kugaptee’s Claw below.\n</p>"
            },
            "Spring’s Path": {
              "name": "春之路 Spring’s Path",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D4. 春之道</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>陡峭的崖壁向两侧延伸，上方直抵无云的夜空，下方则坠入令人眩晕的、云雾翻涌的深渊。一条十尺宽的岩架沿着崖壁蜿蜒前行，途中两次借由五尺宽的天然石桥跨越裂隙，最终向北通往一扇嵌入石壁的木门。诡异的低语与遥远、哀伤的哭号从下方雾霭中回荡而上，浓雾遮蔽了对地面的任何视线。</p>\n</div>\n<p>PC们应能很快认出这条狭窄裂谷正是他们在本幕早些时候走过的蛛纱之道。虽然他们身后通往区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d3lordofwint00]{D3} 的门是一扇朴素的石门，但北面的那扇门由木制成，一眼便能认出那正是 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保} 庄园的入口门。</p>\n<p>若有PC从岩架边缘跌落，将会向下坠落100尺，落到被浓雾笼罩的荒凉岩地上；要阻止这种坠落，角色必须在一次 @Check[reflex|dc:25|traits:manipulate,action:grab-an-edge|name:Grab an Edge] 豁免中成功，以抓住岩架边缘。角色可以通过成功的 @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] 检定来攀爬崖壁。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>随着PC们在该区域中移动，这条岩架与蛛纱之道的相似之处愈发明显——一对行道女从岩壁中现身，占据房间中点处那座横跨岩架的石桥两端的位置。与他们在蛛纱之道上交谈过的那位不同，这些行道女是从苦迦菩提的死寂梦境中抽出的造物；每一位身旁盘旋成群的红色蝴蝶云团，暗示了这一点。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D4. 春之道</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.ncYJqnROvZMNBU7Q]{行道女（2）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>与PC们先前交谈过的行道女不同，这些苦迦菩提的爪牙对讨论毫无兴趣，除了命令PC们“回头——这条路尽头的东西不属于你们！”若PC们不立刻返回区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d3lordofwint00]{D3}（或者他们确实返回了，但只是为了之后再回来这里），两名行道女会立刻发动攻击。</p>\n  <p>先前遭遇的那位行道女拥有“蔑视命运”和“复仇狂暴”能力，而这些行道女则改为拥有“亵渎灵光”（在视觉上表现为成群蝴蝶的云雾）与“腐化疑心”能力。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D4. Spring’s Path</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Sheer cliff walls stretch in both directions, up to a cloudless night sky above and down into a dizzying cloudy depth below. A ten-foot-wide ledge winds along the cliffs, crossing twice via five-foot-wide natural stone bridges as it winds its way north to a set of wooden doors built into the stone wall. Eerie whispers and distant, mournful cries echo up from the mists below, which obscure any sight of the ground.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The PCs should quickly recognize this narrow rift as the Gossamer Path they walked earlier in this act. While the door behind them leading back to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d3lordofwint00]{D3} is a plain stone door, the one to the north is made of wood and is immediately recognizable as being the entrance door to @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s manor.</p>\n<p>A PC who falls off the ledge plummets 100 feet down to a barren rocky floor below, shrouded in thick fog; a character must succeed at a @Check[reflex|dc:25|traits:manipulate,action:grab-an-edge|name:Grab an Edge] save to Grab the Edge of a ledge to stop such a fall. Characters can Climb the cliff walls with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:30|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb] check.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> The resemblance of this ledge to the Gossamer Path only grows as the PCs move through the area, as a pair of path maidens emerge from the rock walls to take up position at either end of the stone bridge that crosses the ledges at the midpoint of the room. Unlike the one they spoke with on the Gossamer Path, these path maidens are creations drawn from Kugaptee’s dead dreams, as the fluttering clouds of red butterflies that swarm around each one implies.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D4. Spring’s Path</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.ncYJqnROvZMNBU7Q]{Path Maidens (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>Unlike the path maiden the PCs spoke to earlier, these minions of Kugaptee aren’t interested in discussion other than to order the PCs to “turn back—what lies beyond this path is not for you!” If the PCs don’t immediately return to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d3lordofwint00]{D3} (or if they do, only to return here later), the two path maidens attack at once.</p>\n  <p>While the path maiden encountered earlier has the Scorn Fate and Vengeful Frenzy abilities, these path maidens instead have the Blasphemous Aura (visually represented by clouds of swarming butterflies) and Corrupting Doubt abilities.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Lord of Winter": {
              "name": "寒冬领主 Lord of Winter",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D3. 冬之领主</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这座杂草丛生的花园被一圈环形石墙围住。树木沿着边缘生长，而中央是一口敞开的石井，井水几乎满到井沿。头顶乌云密布，暴雨倾盆，抽打着整片区域，把地面变成一片杂草与泥泞的沼烂之地；南侧则立着一顶由杆子支起的大型棚盖，为暴雨提供些许遮蔽。色彩鲜艳的帐篷下方放着几条同样缤纷的毯子、一张小桌，桌上摆着一套茶具与四只银杯，以及一把带金色坐垫的大椅子。</p>\n</div>\n<p>PC们应当立刻认出此地与唐入的中央庭院相似，只是没那么整齐有序。这里湿滑的泥地属于困难地形，而倾盆大雨冰冷刺骨，其中还夹带着某种超自然的灌注，凝聚了冬季最糟糕的部分。任何角色若在暴雨中暴露并结束其回合，必须成功通过一次@Check[fortitude|dc:27]豁免以抵抗变为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{力竭 2}（大失败则为@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{力竭 2}），持续至其下一回合结束——这场雨让他们感觉自己仿佛在可怕的冬季风暴中跋涉了数小时。</p>\n<p>站在南侧的布质棚盖下可完全免受这场暴雨影响，但站在某棵树下只能获得部分遮蔽，使该豁免获得+2环境加值。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>有两名“住客”在此等候PC——其中一位是PC应当立刻认出的熟面孔：孙海；另一位则是PC在本战役中曾见过、但之后已死亡的一名NPC。该NPC恭敬地站在孙海身旁，显然将其奉为上级，因此你最好选择一名PC曾视作盟友或朋友的NPC。孙海坐在棚盖下的椅子上，啜饮着茶水、悠然放松；但与第10章的上一次遭遇不同，这次他似乎完全没有携带武器。他看见PC后向仆从点了点头，那仆从便邀请PC过来在帐篷下避雨，并为他们奉上盛在银杯里的茶。若某位PC精通茶学识，会自动注意到用银制茶杯是多么反常（因为银的导热性远胜于传统材质），这或许会让他们意识到事情不对劲。</p>\n<p>事实上，这两名身影都是伪装起来的灵堕魔——孙海是一名稽折魔灵堕魔，施展了@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.i35dpZFI7jZcRoBo]{幻象伪装}来呈现为PC的旧日宿敌；而他的仆从则是一名恪尸魔，显现出一具与那名死去NPC相符的躯体。若PC没有立刻动手，孙海希望他们每个人都从仆从手中接过一杯茶，然后祝贺PC一路走到这一步，深入了苦迦菩提的死之梦境。他邀请PC将银制茶杯当作礼物收下，并从南门前往区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d4springspat00]{D4}。</p>\n<p>四只银制茶杯全都带有稽折魔的感染银诅咒（见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21argyrzeihead00]{此处}）；他希望PC拿着这些“礼物”继续前往区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d4springspat00]{D4}，期间他会观察任何携带被诅咒茶杯的人，并尾随其后。若稽折魔觉得出现了对他出手的绝佳时机，他与仆从会加速追上PC——至少，若他们未先被击败，他们将会在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}一侧加入战斗。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-argyrzei.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D3. 冬之领主</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.obZ0KzlwyaZYuJxB]{稽折魔} @UUID[Actor.vLKeku6p1ZmUZR7L]{恪尸魔}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>若PC拒绝或发动攻击，两名灵堕魔便会愤怒咆哮并展开攻击，以欺瞒掷骰进行先攻。当稽折魔的第一回合开始时，生效中的幻象伪装会让人看起来像是他的人类躯体正在融化消失，露出其真形：一头无头怪物，迅速从脖颈断桩处抽出一把闪亮的银剑发动攻击。战斗一旦开始，灵堕魔将死战到底。由于暴雨对他们的影响可能与对PC的一样大，他们若可行更倾向在棚盖的遮蔽下作战。</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">效果</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">将@UUID[Item.SHQR9YToBxrci94Q]{\"孙海\" 真形}效果拖入以关闭他的伪装</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.bdk0kZ9ZrFiBNVsv]{茶杯} @UUID[Actor.i7rZJzFqFbf9UOqu]{被杀死的灵堕魔}<br />\n  每只精致的银制茶杯都是价值50 gp的艺术品，但同样地，每一只都带有稽折魔的感染银诅咒。\n</p>\n<p>当稽折魔被杀死时，它的躯体会融化成一堆血肉碎污，很快汇流在一起并变形为一件闪亮的银制武器——这更多是此诡异领域与苦迦菩提之间关联的结果，而非灵堕魔真正与生俱来的能力。这件银制武器应当是一把劈砍武器，类型应为某位PC偏好的那种，并且是一把带有感染银诅咒（@Check[will|dc:33]豁免）的<em>+2高等强击银制武器</em>。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D3. Lord of Winter</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This overgrown garden is surrounded by a circular stone wall. Trees grow around the perimeter, while in the center sits an open stone well that’s nearly full to the brim with water. Above, storm clouds fill the sky, pelting the area with driving rain and turning the ground into a morass of weeds and mud, while to the south stands a large canopy erected on poles that offers some shelter from the downpour. Below the brightly colored tent rest several colorful blankets, a small table atop which sits a tea set with four silver cups, and a large chair with a golden cushion.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The PCs should immediately recognize this area as being similar to the central courtyard of Karahai, although less organized. The wet muddy ground here is difficult terrain, and the driving rain is freezing cold and carries within it a supernatural infusion of the worst parts of winter. A character who ends their turn exposed to the rain must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:27] save to resist becoming @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 2} (@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.MIRkyAjyBeXivMa7]{Enfeebled 2} on a critical failure) until the end of their next turn, as the rain makes them feel like they’ve spent hours trudging through a terrible winter storm.</p>\n<p>Standing under the fabric canopy to the south provides total protection from this downpour, but standing under one of the trees only provides partial protection, affording a +2 circumstance bonus to the Fortitude save.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of occupants awaits the PCs in this room—a familiar figure the PCs should immediately recognize as Mago Kai and an NPC whom the PCs have met before in this campaign but who has since died. This NPC stands deferentially at Mago Kai’s side, obviously treating him as their superior, so it’s best if the NPC you choose is someone who the PCs regarded as an ally or friend. Kai sits on the chair under the canopy, sipping tea and relaxing, but unlike their previous encounter in Chapter 10, he seems to be completely unarmed. He nods to his servant as he spots the PCs, and that servant invites them over to take shelter under the tent and offers them cups of tea served in silver cups. A PC who’s master at Tea Lore automatically notes how unusual it is to have a silver teacup (as silver conducts heat much more than more traditional material), perhaps indicating to them that something strange is afoot.</p>\n<p>In truth, both of these figures are disguised nindorus—Mago Kai is an argyrzei nindoru who has used @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.i35dpZFI7jZcRoBo]{Illusory Disguise} to appear as the PCs’ old nemesis, while his servant is an akashti who has manifested a body to match the dead NPC. If the PCs don’t attack at once, Mago Kai hopes each of them accepts a cup of tea from his servant, then congratulates the PCs on making it this far into Kugaptee’s dead dreams. He invites the PCs to keep the silver teacups as gifts and to proceed through the southern door on to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d4springspat00]{D4}.</p>\n<p>The four silver teacups are all cursed with the argyrzei’s infected silver (See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21argyrzeihead00]{Here}); he hopes the PCs take the “gifts” and move on to area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15d4springspat00]{D4}, during which he observes anyone who carries one of the cursed teacups and follows along behind them. The argyrzei and his servant speed up to reach the PCs if he ever feels there’s a particularly advantageous time for him to strike against them—at the very least, they’ll join the fight at @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s side if not defeated first.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-argyrzei.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D3. Lord of Winter</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.obZ0KzlwyaZYuJxB]{Argyrzei} @UUID[Actor.vLKeku6p1ZmUZR7L]{Akashti}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If the PCs refuse or attack, both nindorus roar in anger and attack, rolling Deception for initiative. When the argyrzei’s first turn begins, the illusory disguise in effect makes it appear that his human body is melting away to reveal his true form: a headless monster that swiftly pulls a gleaming silver sword from the stump of its neck to attack. Once battle begins, the nindorus fight to the death. Since the rain can potentially affect him as much as the PCs, they prefer to fight from under the shelter of the canopy if possible.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Effect</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">Drag on the @UUID[Item.SHQR9YToBxrci94Q]{\"Mago Kai\" True Form} Effect to turn off his disguise</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.bdk0kZ9ZrFiBNVsv]{Teacups} @UUID[Actor.i7rZJzFqFbf9UOqu]{Slain Nindoru}<br />\n  Each of the elegant silver teacups is a work of art worth 50 gp, but again, each bears the argyrzei’s infected silver curse.\n</p>\n<p>When the argyrzei is slain, its body melts into a pile of gore that quickly flows together and transforms into a gleaming silver weapon—a result of this strange realm’s association with Kugaptee more than any real inborn ability possessed by the nindoru. This silver weapon should be a slashing weapon of a type favored by one of the PCs and is a <em>+2 greater striking silver weapon</em> that bears the infected silver curse (@Check[will|dc:33] save).</p>"
            },
            "A Fallen Tree": {
              "name": "一棵倒下的树 A Fallen Tree",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D2. 倒下的树</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>门穿过一堵正在崩塌、爬满藤蔓的石墙打开，通向一处杂草丛生的寺院庭院。地面上长满厚密纠结的荆棘与杂草；而左侧与右侧，一道由密密层层树木组成的“墙”挡住去路。杂草丛生的庭院对面那堵墙上还有另一扇古老的石门；庭院中央则耸立着一棵参天巨树，树干病腐、枝桠光秃。它的上半截看起来与其说像树，不如说更像一只扭曲的利爪伸向上方阴云密布的天空。</p>\n</div>\n<p>PC们会立刻认出这里是谭杉寺的庭院，只是长在区域中央的那棵杉树显然已经死了。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-corpsewood.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Corpseroot\" alt=\"a rotten, undead tree sporting bright-red poisonous fruit\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-corpsewood.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>当PC们进入该区域时，让他们尝试一次 @Check[perception|dc:38] 检定；若成功，他们会发现那棵死杉树发霉的树皮上，仿佛长出了几十张人脸的朦胧轮廓，每张脸的嘴都张开着，像是在无声尖叫。这个细节可能让PC们意识到，一股强大的不死存在——尸根——已由树干的一部分形成。若大成功或大失败为大成功，他们会在那些脸上看到几只眼睛抽动着，随着PC们的靠近而转动，以不祥的怒视盯着他们。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-corpsewood.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D2. 倒下的树</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.v1Nf0CsNFXJAF4pw]{尸杉} @UUID[Actor.rwpq77CuinvdTFIh]{痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>如果PC们没有意识到危险，尸杉会猛然复苏，从死杉树上撕扯着挣脱出来，并将死树的大量材质一并带走，蹒跚着向前移动。在此过程中，还会发生另外两件事。首先，树皮里嵌着的四张脸也会被扯离出来，同时拖拽出成束的枯枝与树皮。这些是披着长袍的痂苦魔灵堕魔，长袍看起来与谭杉寺那些腐化僧侣所穿的相似。所有这些生物都以潜行进行先攻投掷。与此同时，那棵高大的杉树会轰然倒下，树干在尸根破出后留下的空隙周围裂开。尸根能够控制树倒下的方向，并会这么做，以便尽可能多地把PC们卷入从房间中心喷射而出的 @Template[type:cone|distance:40] 范围内。处在该区域内的角色受到 [[/r 8d6[bludgeoning]]] 伤害（@Check[reflex|dc:27|basic] 豁免），且任何在该豁免中大成功或大失败为大失败的人都会被倒下的树 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{禁足}（逃脱 DC 27）。</p>\n  <p>如果PC们察觉危险并抢先攻击，尸杉与灵堕魔以察觉进行先攻投掷。在这种情况下，当死杉倒下时，尸根无法引导其倒下方向，树会朝随机决定的方向倾倒（任何被卷入该区域的PC在对抗树倒下的反射豁免上获得+4环境加值）。</p>\n  <p>不论由谁先开战，灵堕魔都会尖叫道：“闯入者！异端！杀了他们！”随后蹒跚向前发动攻击。它们在战斗开始时就已经显化出成束的枝条、细枝与树皮。尽管上方的红色天空只提供昏暗照明，但这对四只痂苦魔以及阴影啃咬的潜在目标来说都绰绰有余，足以让他们投下阴影。</p>\n  <p>当尸杉发动攻击时，一张脸会从它的树干上长出来——那是欣月充满憎恨的面容，PC们在冬季曾于谭杉寺深处地下的房间里击败过她。确实，这名腐化僧侣的灵魂协助驱动了这棵不死之树，并以其怨毒目的灌注其中；在战斗时，它会对PC们咒骂，并发出充满愤怒、要施以折磨的许诺，尤其是对那位曾在寺院战斗中击败她的PC。这些生物会一直战斗到被摧毁为止。</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.DZ6o0wYy4pjWMo0R]{杉树倒下}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D2. A Fallen Tree</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The door opens through a crumbling, vine-covered stone wall into an overgrown monastery courtyard. Thick tangles of brambles and weeds grow on the ground, while to the left and right, a wall of densely packed trees blocks the way. A wall on the opposite side of the overgrown courtyard has another old stone door, while in the middle rises a single towering tree, its trunk diseased and its branches bare. The upper half looks more like a twisted claw reaching up into the overcast sky above than anything else.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The PCs automatically recognize this place as the courtyard of the Tan Sugi Monastery, save that the tree that grows in the middle of the area is obviously dead.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-corpsewood.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Corpseroot\" alt=\"a rotten, undead tree sporting bright-red poisonous fruit\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-corpsewood.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> As the PCs enter this area, allow them to attempt a @Check[perception|dc:38] check; on a success, they spot what appear to be the vague shapes of dozens of human faces growing from the dead sugi tree’s moldy bark, each mouth open in a silent scream. This detail might let the PCs realize that a powerful undead presence—a corpseroot—has formed from a portion of the tree’s trunk. On a critical success, they spot a few eyes in those faces that twitch to follow the PCs’ approach with a baleful glare.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(3.6)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-corpsewood.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D2. A Fallen Tree</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.v1Nf0CsNFXJAF4pw]{Corpse Sugi} @UUID[Actor.rwpq77CuinvdTFIh]{Kagekuma(4)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If the PCs don’t realize the danger, the corpse sugi lurches to unlife and rips free from the dead sugi tree, taking with it much of the dead tree’s material as it lumbers forward. As it does so, two other things occur. First, four of the faces embedded in the bark rip free as well, dragging bundles of dead branches and bark with them. These are kagekuma nindorus clad in robes that look similar to those worn by the corrupted monks from the Tan Sugi Monastery. All of these creatures roll for initiative using Stealth. At the same time, the towering sugi tree topples over, its trunk splitting apart around the gap left by the corpseroot’s emergence. The corpseroot can control the direction of the tree’s fall, and does so to catch as many of the PCs as possible in a @Template[type:cone|distance:40] shooting out from the center of the room. Characters in this area take [[/r 8d6[bludgeoning]]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:27|basic] save), and anyone who critically fails this save becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{Immobilized} by the fallen tree (Escape DC 27)..</p>\n  <p>If the PCs recognize the danger and attack first, the corpse sugi and nindorus roll for initiative using Perception. In this case, when the dead sugi falls, the corpseroot can’t direct its fall, and the tree topples over in a randomly determined direction (and any PCs caught in the area gain a +4 circumstance bonus to their Reflex save against the tree’s fall).</p>\n  <p>Regardless of who starts the fight, the nindorus shriek out, “Interlopers! Unbelievers! Slay them!” as they lurch forward to attack. They begin the battle with bundles of branches and twig and bark already manifested. While the red sky above only provides dim illumination, it’s more than enough for the four kagekumas and potential targets of Shadow Bite to all cast shadows.</p>\n  <p>As the corpse sugi attacks, a face grows from its trunk—the hate-filled visage of Xin Yue, whom the PCs defeated back in winter in the chamber deep below the Tan Sugi Monastery. Indeed, the corrupted monk’s soul helps to animate this undead tree and fills it with its hateful purpose, and as it fights, it issues curses and angry promises of torment to the PCs, particularly to the PC who defeated her in combat at the monastery. All of these creatures fight until destroyed.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes2\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.DZ6o0wYy4pjWMo0R]{Sugi Tree Falls}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "Summertime Guard": {
              "name": "盛夏守卫 Summertime Guard",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">D1. 盛夏守卫</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>门打开后，外面不是预想中的建筑，而是一座熟悉的宽阔石桥——晨步桥。桥栏之外，是柳岸镇在去年春天时的全景，包括当时困扰城镇的诡异浓雾。向北与向南，两道带双开门的木制路障遮断了桥外的视线；而在头顶，夜空中悬着一轮形如红色眼睛的月亮。在桥的北端中央，一座巨大的金色王座被建造成端坐恶魔的模样，配着深紫色坐垫，披挂毛皮与成片刺绣绸缎。</p>\n</div>\n<p>尽管这间房间的边界被限制在桥上，PC们仍可从桥的边缘向外望去，看到第一幕开端时的柳岸镇——浓雾缠绕，绯红月光洒落其上。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-gurglegut.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Gurglegut\" alt=\"a drunk male buso spitting fire\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-gurglegut.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>在这场战役的开始，晨步桥由一个名叫辘肠的醉酒武僧与他那群金金跟班守卫。当PC们进入该区域时，他们将面对一个由同一个武僧的灵魂锻造而成、却比他先前化身强大许多的辘肠版本。他坐着的王座比他过去用的那一座更大、更华丽——而当辘肠从王座起身与PC们对话时，他的身形足足是先前的两倍高：站起来足有13英尺。侍立在这名巨型武僧身旁的不再是小魔怪（特征），而是一队四名山鬼，它们两两并列，站在王座与南侧入口之间——也就是PC们踏上桥面的地方。其中一对站在王座近旁，另一对则离南侧入口仅20英尺。</p>\n<p>一看到PC们，辘肠便放声大笑，举起一大壶米酒向他们致意。读出或转述以下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“看哪，我们又见面了，柳岸镇的英雄们——但这一次，你们休想趁我不备。这一次，我的守卫能干得很。这一次，我既不醉也不走神。等一切尘埃落定时，我会嚼碎你们的骨头，吃光你们的肉！”</p>\n</div>\n<p>辘肠很快就会下令发动攻击，但如果PC们回应得足够迅速，他们有一轮时间与这名武僧交涉。他的初始态度为敌对——如果他们能在不到一轮内把他的态度调整到至少不关心（注意：建立印象与胁迫通常需要1分钟才能进行，因此角色必须拥有类似于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.ar2DUlvDK4LDcH9J]{Quick Coercion}的专长，才有机会在如此短的时间内调整这名武僧的态度；由于这不是一次轻松的遭遇，像Glad Hand这样的专长不适用）。魔法（如@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{Charm}）同样可行，但前提是四名鬼胁都在同一时间被安抚，或者它们没有意识到有人用魔法操纵了它们的首领。</p>\n<p>如果PC们阻止了战斗，辘肠承认自己并不渴望再打一场——尽管他如今更强大了，但他也知道PC们同样如此；若PC们愿意送他一份礼物，他同意放行。任何价值至少2,000 gp的宝藏或魔法物品（若礼物与食物或饮酒有关，则1,000 gp即可）都足以买到通行权；但PC们也可以尝试对辘肠说谎，以说服他放他们通过。交涉在这里用处不大，但若一次胁迫尝试取得大成功或大失败中的大成功，某位PC便能吓住这名武僧，使其不经冲突就放PC们通过。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/onidoshi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D1. 盛夏守卫</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.byoe8fUg98AJyTk2]{辘肠} @UUID[Actor.HVznCS1H5CTJZ5TM]{山鬼（4）}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>若战斗开始，最南边的两名山鬼上前与PC们进行近战，而后方的两名则在辘肠的王座前摆出防御姿态，用短弓攻击；当出现不会把友军卷入范围效果的时机时，它们便改用魔法。战斗开始时，辘肠从王座上站起，用他的弩不断骚扰PC们。若辘肠被打到剩余40点生命值或更少，他会撤到桥的远端，让他的山鬼继续战斗；但若在此被逼到绝境，或四名山鬼全数被杀，他就会乞求饶命。此时任何仍活着的山鬼都会因辘肠的怯懦而怒吼，转而把攻击对准他。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>如果PC们饶辘肠一命（并保护他不被暴怒的山鬼杀死），这名武僧会缩小体型，变回PC们在第一幕所遭遇的那个版本（@UUID[Actor.EFX5AOuSEa0cxcj1]{辘肠}）。他一边流泪抽噎，一边解释自己一直被“伟大而光辉的苦迦菩提”囚禁在此，但现在只想安宁度日。他绝不会陪PC们继续深入苦迦菩提之墓，但他愿意把自己的魔法装备交给他们，并警告他们“当心尸体，因为苦迦菩提的玩物喜欢用死人来做伪装！”不幸的是，辘肠仍深陷苦迦菩提的领域之中，因此在他还来不及给PC们更多忠告时，他突然露出惊骇之色，仿佛刚注意到有什么东西正从PC们身后升起。一名朝那个方向瞥去的PC什么也看不见；但片刻之后，辘肠便在极度恐惧中尖叫，他的头颅猛然爆裂成一团绯红的蝴蝶，旋舞于空中，随即化作烟雾消散，留下这名武僧终于、也永远地死去。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">D1. Summertime Guard</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The door opens not into the expected building, but instead onto a familiar, wide stone bridge—Dawnstep Bridge. The panorama of Willowshore as it existed last spring lies beyond the bridge’s rails, including the eerie fog that plagued the town. To the north and south, wooden barricades set with double doors prevent sight beyond the bridge, while above, a moon in the shape of a red eye looms in the night sky. In the middle of the northern end of the bridge, an immense golden throne has been built to resemble a seated demon, fitted with deep purple cushions, and draped with furs and swaths of embroidered silks.</p>\n</div>\n<p>While the borders of this room are constrained to the bridge, the PCs can look out over its edges to behold a version of Willowshore as it existed during the start of the first act—wreathed in fog and under the light of a crimson moon.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-gurglegut.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Gurglegut\" alt=\"a drunk male buso spitting fire\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-gurglegut.webp')\" />\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> At the start of this campaign, Dawnstep Bridge was protected by a drunken buso named Gurglegut and his jinkin toadies. When the PCs enter this area, they face a version of Gurglegut forged from the same buso’s soul but greatly enhanced over his previous incarnation. The throne he’s seated upon is much larger and more ornate than the one he used before—and Gurglegut towers at twice his previous height, standing at 13 feet tall once he rises from his throne to address the PCs. The immense buso is attended not by gremlins, but by a group of four mountain oni who stand two abreast between the throne and the southern entrance, where the PCs emerge onto the bridge. One pair of oni stands near the throne, while the others stand a mere 20 feet away from the southern entrance.</p>\n<p>Upon spotting the PCs, Gurglegut roars in laughter and raises a large jug of rice wine in salute to them. Read or paraphrase the following.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>“And here we are again, heroes of Willowshore, only this time you shall not catch me at a disadvantage. This time, my guardians are competent. This time, I am not drunk and distracted. This time, I will be eating your flesh and crunching your bones when all is said and done!”</p>\n</div>\n<p>Gurglegut is quick to order the attack, but if the PCs respond to him quickly, they have a round to engage with the buso. His initial attitude is hostile—if they’re able to adjust his attitude to at least indifferent in less than a round (note that Make an Impression and Coerce normally take a minute to perform, so a character must have a feat like @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.ar2DUlvDK4LDcH9J]{Quick Coercion} to have a chance to adjust the buso’s attitude in such a short time period; as this isn’t a casual encounter, a feat like Glad Hand doesn’t apply). Magic (such as @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{Charm}) will work as well, but only if the four onidoshi are all placated at the same time or don’t realize that magic was used to manipulate their leader.</p>\n<p>If the PCs forestall a fight, Gurglegut admits he isn’t eager for a rematch—while he’s more powerful now, he knows the PCs are as well, and he agrees to let them pass if they offer him a gift. Any treasure or magic item worth at least 2,000 gp (or 1,000 gp if the gift has something to do with food or drink) suffices to buy passage, but PCs can also attempt to Lie to Gurglegut to convince him to let them pass as well. Diplomacy has little use here, but on a critical success at a Coercion attempt, a PC cows the buso, who lets the PCs pass without conflict.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/onidoshi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">D1. Summertime Guard</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.byoe8fUg98AJyTk2]{Gurglegut} @UUID[Actor.HVznCS1H5CTJZ5TM]{Mountain Oni (4)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If combat begins, the two southernmost mountain oni step forward to engage the PCs in melee, while those further back take a defensive stance before Gurglegut’s throne and use their shortbows to attack, switching to magic as the chance to do so without catching allies in areas of effect presents itself. Gurglegut stands up from his throne as the battle begins, harrying the PCs with his crossbow. If Gurglegut is reduced to 40 Hit Points or less, he retreats to the far end of the bridge and lets his oni continue the fight, but if cornered here, or if all four oni are slain, he begs for mercy. Any still-living oni at this point roar in rage at Gurglegut’s cowardice and redirect their attacks to him.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>If the PCs grant Gurglegut mercy (and protect him from being slain by enraged oni), the buso shrinks down in size, returning to the version of himself the PCs encountered in Act 1 (@UUID[Actor.EFX5AOuSEa0cxcj1]{Gurglegut}). Through tears and sobs, he explains that he’s been held captive here by “Great and Glorious Kugaptee” but now wants only to be left in peace. He absolutely won’t accompany the PCs further into Kugaptee’s Grave, but he does offer them his magical gear along with a warning to “be aware of dead bodies, for the playthings of Kugaptee enjoy using the dead as disguises!” Unfortunately for Gurglegut, he’s still deep within Kugaptee’s domain, so before he can give much more advice to the PCs, he suddenly grows horrified, as if he just noticed something rising up beyond the PCs. A PC who glances in that direction sees nothing, but a few moments later, Gurglegut shrieks in terror before his head bursts into a plume of crimson butterflies that swirls through the air then fades to smoke, leaving the buso finally and forever dead.</p>"
            },
            "Entering Kugaptee’s Grave": {
              "name": "进入苦迦菩提之墓 Entering Kugaptee’s Grave",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">进入苦迦菩提之墓</span>\n</h2>\n<p>当PC们在接近巨爪时穿行于苦迦菩提之握蜿蜒的街道，或是在释放了被锁缚的灵魂中的第三个之后在街上游荡时，一件怪事发生了。周围的建筑似乎变得更高，街道变得更窄，而头顶的天空似乎在下压。PC们移动得越快，这种变化就越明显；但即便他们站着不动，用不了多久，即使最宽阔的街道也会让人觉得像狭窄的巷道。头顶天空的视野被压缩成一条狭窄的带状，只能从那些高耸逼人的建筑之间看到；这些建筑挨得极近，让人感觉它们更像洞窟的墙壁，而非街边的立面。</p>\n<p>一旦PC们踏入这片洞窟般的构造物，他们可以沿着进入时所走的道路向南行进1分钟来离开，并返回柳岸镇的“本可能发生的版本”；但任何其他试图接近巨爪的尝试，都会把他们直接送回这个诡异的迷宫。此区域由一连串更像洞窟隧道而非街巷的“巷道”组成。这些区域的地面类似夯实的泥土，而墙壁则是建筑立面，间或点缀着上锁的门或紧闭的窗。上方，血红的天空压迫着，使该区域光线昏暗。试图砸穿这些墙壁或向下挖掘都是徒劳，因为它们之外什么也不存在——在这里，苦迦菩提之握的思维空间被缩减成一条单一路径。角色可以在成功的@Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb]后攀爬墙壁，但当高度达到30英尺时，攀爬者会发现屋顶线依然无法通过，仿佛有一堵不可穿透的玻璃墙挡住了他们通往最后几英尺、爬上屋顶所需的路径。在四个厅室中，这道“天花板”高度达到100英尺。</p>\n<p>沿着这些街道，唯一能起作用的门是那些通往室内地点的门——对PC们而言幸运的是，这些门并不藏在各条街道两侧的一排门之中，而是标示着一条蜿蜒巷道的尽头。在这些房间内，照明各不相同，外观也各异——从外面看可能像一栋建筑的东西，门后或许是一座大洞窟、一条户外小径，或任何其他事物。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Entering Kugaptee’s Grave</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As the PCs navigate the twisting streets of Kugaptee’s Grasp on their approach to the claw, or as they wander the streets after releasing the third of the shackled souls, a strange thing takes place. The surrounding buildings seem to grow taller, the streets grow narrower, and the sky above seems to lower. The transformation increases the more quickly the PCs move, but even if they stand still, it won’t be long before even the widest street feels like a narrow alleyway. The view of the sky above is reduced to a narrow strip visible between looming, towering buildings packed so closely together that they feel more like the walls of a cavern than a street-side facade.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs step into this cave-like construct, they can leave and return to the could-have-been version of Willowshore by traveling south along the road they entered by for 1 minute, but any other attempt to approach the claw sends them right back into this strange maze. This area consists of a series of “alleys” that function more like cavern tunnels. The ground in these areas resembles packed earth, while the walls are building facades, periodically adorned with locked doors or closed windows. Above, the blood-red sky looms, leaving the area dimly lit. Attempts to smash through these walls or dig below are fruitless, as nothing exists beyond them—here, the mindscape of Kugaptee’s Grasp has been reduced to a single path. A character can Climb the walls with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:20|traits:move,skill,action:climb|name:Climb], but at a height of 30 feet, the climber finds that the roofline remains impassable, as if a wall of impenetrable glass bars their way to the last few feet needed to clamber up to a roof. In the four chambers, this “ceiling” reaches a height of 100 feet.</p>\n<p>The only doors that function along these streets are those that open into interior locations—fortunately for the PCs, these doors aren’t hidden among those that line the sides of each street, but instead mark the end of a winding alleyway. Within these rooms, illumination varies, as does the appearance—what might look like a building from the outside might be a large cavern, an outdoor path, or anything else beyond its door.</p>"
            },
            "Kugaptee’s Grave": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提之墓 Kugaptee’s Grave",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提之墓</span>\n</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>与记忆作战</h1>\n  <p>苦迦菩提之墓中的四个遭遇区域旨在以战斗挑战PC，但也要唤起他们对之前各季的记忆。如果在你的游戏里，先前冒险中的其他部分更令人难忘，可以考虑用取自先前各幕的地图替换这里的遭遇，并让不同的敌人登场。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>尽管苦迦菩提之握的景象令人不安，这座奇异地空荡的“本可以存在”的城市里却几乎没有什么会危及PC，但当他们越接近思维空间中最令人心惊的地标时，这一点就会改变——那条伸向苍穹的梦魇之臂，曾经大尊柳就生长在那儿。此臂是苦迦菩提自身的具现；若事态遂其所愿，他手臂的末日般活动将预示他转生回到现世：它撕裂头顶的天空，并令这片思维空间走向终结。</p>\n<p>巨爪是苦迦菩提之握最引人注目的特征，光是它就足以把PC吸引过去。如果他们使用<em>天牙水晶</em>尝试追踪 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}，这些努力的结果会将他们引向巨爪。由你决定，PC交谈过的任何被锁缚的转世的灵魂都可以告诉PC：将他们变成这样的那个人在北方，“就在握本身的下方”。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.dXdUI7ShEBwPh1c7]{苦迦菩提之墓天气变化}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>不过，即使PC最终并未靠近此地，随着时间推移，它也会来找上他们。一旦三名被锁缚的转世的灵魂都获救，和善保——并通过他，苦迦菩提——就会寻求与PC迅速对决。灵堕魔不打算避开他们，而是希望把他们引入一处扭曲的领域来将其了结——一座由柳岸镇之城构成的洞窟般空间，一片令人不安、诡异离奇的区域，名为苦迦菩提之墓。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Kugaptee’s Grave</span>\n</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Battling Memories</h1>\n  <p>The four encounter areas within Kugaptee’s Grave are meant to challenge the PCs in combat, but also to evoke their memories of the previous seasons. If a different part of previous adventures played a more memorable role in your game, consider replacing encounters here with maps taken from prior acts and featuring different foes.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>While the visuals of Kugaptee’s Grasp are unsettling, there’s little in the strangely empty “could have been” city to endanger the PCs, but that changes the closer they come to the most disturbing landmark in the mindscape—the nightmare arm that reaches for the heavens where once the Great Willow grew. This arm is a physical manifestation of Kugaptee himself, and if events go his way, an apocalyptic animation of his arm presages his reincarnation into the living world as it rips the skies above apart and brings this mindscape to an end.</p>\n<p>The claw is the most noteworthy feature of Kugaptee’s Grasp, and it alone might be enough to draw the PCs toward it. If they use the <em>skyfang crystal</em> to try to Track @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, the results of those efforts lead them toward the claw. At your discretion, any of the shackled souls the PCs speak to can tell the PCs that the one who did this to them lies to the north, “below the Grasp itself.”</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes1\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macro</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.dXdUI7ShEBwPh1c7]{Kukaptee's Grave Weather Change}</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p>But even if the PCs don’t eventually approach this site, in time, it comes to them. Once all three of the shackled souls have been freed, Heh Shan-Bao—and through him, Kugaptee—seeks a swift confrontation with the PCs. Rather than avoid them, the nindoru hopes to finish them off by drawing them into a twisting realm—a sort of cavern made from the city of Willowshore, an unnerving and uncanny region known as Kugaptee’s Grave.</p>"
            },
            "The Herbalist’s Final Creation": {
              "name": "草药师的最终杰作 The Herbalist’s Final Creation",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">草药师的最终造物</span>\n</h3>\n<p>第三个被镣铐束缚的灵魂属于尤素珍，她被锁链拴在自己店铺里的炼金工作台上，不断尝试却屡屡失败，想要调制出更强力的<em>银魂炸弹</em>。这份混合物不时噼啪作响、闪光四溅，常常会戏剧性地爆炸，让尤素珍痛苦不堪；但随后一切又会“重置”，迫使她从头再来。她的工作爆炸时不会对PC造成伤害，但目睹这一切仍令人胆寒。</p>\n<p>如果PC与尤素珍交谈，她会告诉他们：“我几乎已经完善了我最新的发明，它会协助你们击败敌人……可这最后一步不管我怎么做都会失控！”为了释放她，PC可以通过帮助她完成工作，以一次@Check[crafting|dc:28]检定来解放她被镣铐束缚的灵魂；或通过标准的@Check[diplomacy|dc:32]或@Check[intimidation|dc:32]检定来帮助她逃脱。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>如果PC解放了她，尤素珍如释重负地叹了口气，为最终的炸弹封上盖子。她的眼睛回到眼眶里，手腕上的镣铐随她再度如释重负地叹息而逐渐消散，她也随之消失。与此同时，带着清新春日林地气息的蒸汽充满整间房间，强化每名PC的生命力——在本次冒险的剩余时间里，他们的强韧豁免获得+2状态加值（@UUID[Item.6o3yLo9g5DsaYPxY]{Soul Blessing (Fortitude Saves)}）。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>因释放尤素珍的灵魂，给予PC 80 XP。</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Herbalist’s Final Creation</span>\n</h3>\n<p>The third shackled soul, that of You So-Jin, is chained to her alchemy workstation at her shop, where she continues to try and fail at crafting a more powerful <em>silversoul bomb</em>. The concoction sputters and flashes, often exploding dramatically to cause You So-Jin great pain, only for everything to “reset” and force her to start over from scratch. When her work explodes, it causes no harm to the PCs but is nevertheless harrowing to witness.</p>\n<p>If the PCs speak to You So-Jin, she tells them, “I’ve almost perfected my latest invention, and it will aid you in defeating your enemies... but this last bit always spirals out of control, no matter what I do!” In order to release her, the PCs can Free her Shackled Soul by helping her finish her work with a @Check[crafting|dc:28] check, or via the standard @Check[diplomacy|dc:32] or @Check[intimidation|dc:32] checks to help her escape.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs free her, You So-Jin caps the final bomb with a sigh of relief. Her eyes return to her skull, and the shackles on her wrists fade as she vanishes with a sigh of relief. As she does, vapors smelling of fresh spring woodlands fill the chamber, bolstering each PC’s vitality—for the remainder of this adventure, they gain a +2 status bonus to Fortitude saves (@UUID[Item.6o3yLo9g5DsaYPxY]{Soul Blessing (Fortitude Saves)}).</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP for releasing You So-Jin’s soul.</p>"
            },
            "The Wandering Grave Keeper": {
              "name": "漫游的坟墓守护者 The Wandering Grave Keeper",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">徘徊的守墓人</span>\n</h3>\n<p>一旦PC们遭遇乌诺，他们就应当意识到，其他谋杀受害者也可能同样需要救助。第二名谋杀受害者伊丽泽丝·坎多的灵魂，被锁链拴在司魂娘娘庙后方的墓园里——但在苦迦菩提之握，法拉丝玛大教堂不过是一片坍塌的废墟，其上覆满亵渎性的涂鸦。墓园也遭到类似的亵渎：每一块墓碑都被砸碎，每一座坟墓都被掘开且空空如也。伊丽泽丝以蜗牛般的速度在墓园中游荡；她的镣铐锁链似乎埋在泥土之下，而当她艰难向前挪动时，锁链在她身后于地面犁出一道沟壑，使她那毫无希望的旅程仍在继续的同时进一步亵渎着土壤。她时不时会在一座被亵渎的坟前停下，举起随身携带的长笛，但当她试图吹奏时，长笛便会散架。她尽其所能将断裂的长笛拼凑回去，然后走向另一座被亵渎的坟墓，如此周而复始，一遍又一遍地重复同样的过程。</p>\n<p>若PC们与伊丽泽丝交谈，她会哀叹没有长笛就无法为被亵渎的亡者带来安宁。她举起那支破碎的长笛，修补之处显然摇摇欲坠、漏洞百出，并说道：“要是我的长笛没这么破损，我就能让这些受折磨的转世的灵魂获得片刻安宁！”为了释放她，PC们可以通过协助她进行一次@Check[performance|dc:28]检定来解救她那被镣铐束缚的灵魂，或使用标准的@Check[diplomacy|dc:32]或@Check[intimidation|dc:32]检定来帮助她逃脱。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们解救了她，这名牧师举起长笛，吹奏出最后一支哀婉的挽歌。她的眼睛回到骷髅眼眶中，手腕上的镣铐随她长舒一口气而消散无踪。她的乐音余韵仍在回荡，令PC们充满活力与对生命的爱情——在本次冒险的剩余时间里，他们的反射豁免获得+2状态加值（@UUID[Item.vtekpq80GirC6714]{Soul Blessing (Reflex Saves)}）。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>PC们释放伊丽泽丝的灵魂可获得80 XP。</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Wandering Grave Keeper</span>\n</h3>\n<p>Once the PCs encounter Oono, they should realize that other murder victims might need rescuing as well. The soul of Elizeth Candor, the second murder victim, is chained in the graveyard behind Her Fluvial Lady of Souls—but the Pharasmin cathedral is little more than a crumbled ruin covered with blasphemous graffiti in Kugaptee’s Grasp. The graveyard has been similarly defaced, with every marker smashed and every grave dug up and empty. Elizeth wanders the graveyard at a snail’s pace; her shackle chains appear to be buried in the earth, and as she pushes forward, the chains leave a furrow in the ground behind her, further defiling the soil even as she continues her hopeless journey. Now and then, she pauses at a defiled grave to lift the flute she carries, but when she tries to play it, the flute falls apart. She cobbles the fractured flute back together as best she can, then moves on to a different defiled grave to repeat the process over and over.</p>\n<p>If the PCs speak to Elizeth, she bemoans the fact that without her flute, she can’t bring peace to the defiled dead. She holds up her shattered flute, its repairs obviously tenuous and faulty, and says, “If only my flute were not so broken, I could bring a moment of peace to these tormented souls!” In order to release her, the PCs can Free her Shackled Soul by helping her perform with a @Check[performance|dc:28] check, or via the standard @Check[diplomacy|dc:32] or @Check[intimidation|dc:32] checks to help her escape.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs free her, the priest raises her flute and plays out one final mournful dirge. Her eyes return to her skull, and the shackles on her wrists fade as she vanishes with a sigh of relief. Lingering notes of her music persist, filling the PCs with energy and a love of life—for the remainder of this adventure, they gain a +2 status bonus to Reflex saves (@UUID[Item.vtekpq80GirC6714]{Soul Blessing (Reflex Saves)}).</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP for releasing Elizeth’s soul.</p>"
            },
            "The Silenced Songbird": {
              "name": "沉默的歌鸟 The Silenced Songbird",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">沉默的歌鸟</span>\n</h3>\n<p>大野和马被镣铐束缚的魂魄被锁在他的写字台上；这名失明的狐妖无休止地修订着《织水者纪事》的剧本——他正在处理的这份副本，实际上就是从他家中被偷走的那一本。工作时，他会喃喃自语，因自己所有的辛勤劳动被人篡改而感到挫败，并压低声音怨毒地抱怨什么“爱插手的自我膨胀之徒”和“玻璃心的政客”。他对PC们的到来毫无反应；任何从他身后探看的人都能看到：他正在把先前手写的注释改回去，那些注释把剧中主要反派塑造成了@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的明显讽刺漫画，但他的改动随即又会消褪，于是他不得不从头再来。</p>\n<p>若PC与大野和马交谈，他会不耐烦地挥手打发他们，说：“我只有几个小时能把这些改动做完，所以除非你们有什么高见，否则请保持安静！”要解放他，PC们必须通过一场讨论，让这出戏的后续走向令他满意，从而解开他的束缚之魂。进行一次@Check[deception|dc:28]检定来帮助他把讽刺写得更含蓄即可奏效；同样也可以使用标准的@Check[diplomacy|dc:32]或@Check[intimidation|dc:32]检定。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>若PC们解放了他，这名狐妖会对剧本做出最后一次编辑改动，剧本随即化为一部完整作品。他的眼睛回到眼眶中，手腕上的镣铐也随之消散；他长舒一口气，随之消失。他的作品仍留在原地；若任何PC触碰它，《织水者纪事》便会消失，回到现实世界中大野和马办公室书架上的原位；与此同时，它会强化PC们的心智——在本次冒险的剩余时间里，他们的意志豁免获得+2状态加值（@UUID[Item.c0KoUPqbW6EtPXLn]{魂魄祝福（意志豁免）}）。</p>\n<p><strong>奖励：</strong>因解放大野和马的魂魄，给予PC们80 XP。</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Silenced Songbird</span>\n</h3>\n<p>Kazuma Oono’s shackled spirit is chained to his writing desk, where the blinded kitsune endlessly revises a playbook for <em>The Chronicle of the Water-Weaver</em>—the copy he works on is, in fact, the one stolen from his home. As he works, he mutters to himself about being frustrated that all of his hard work is being tampered with, bitterly complaining under his breath about “meddling egos” and “thin-skinned politicians.” He doesn’t react to the PCs’ arrival; anyone who looks over his shoulder can watch as he revises previous handwritten notes to the play that cast the play’s main villain as an obvious caricature of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, only for his adjustments to fade away so that he must start all over again.</p>\n<p>If the PCs speak to Oono, he impatiently waves them off and says, “I only have a few hours to get these changes made, so unless you’ve got some bright ideas, please keep quiet!” In order to release him, the PCs must Free his Shackled Soul via a discussion about how to move forward with the play to his satisfaction. A @Check[deception|dc:28] check to help him make his satire more subtle will work, as will the standard @Check[diplomacy|dc:32] or @Check[intimidation|dc:32] checks.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> If the PCs free him, the kitsune makes one final editorial change to the play, which suddenly transforms into a complete work. His eyes return to his skull, and the shackles on his wrists fade as he vanishes with a sigh of relief. His work remains behind, and if any PC touches it, <em>The Chronicle of the Water-Weaver</em> vanishes as it returns to its shelf in the real-world version of Oono’s office; when it does, it bolsters the PCs’ minds—for the remainder of this adventure, they gain a +2 status bonus to Will saves (@UUID[Item.c0KoUPqbW6EtPXLn]{Soul Blessing (Will Saves)}).</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Grant the PCs 80 XP for releasing Oono’s soul.</p>"
            },
            "The Chained Spirits": {
              "name": "锁链魂魄 The Chained Spirits",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">被锁链束缚的灵体</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>避免的谋杀</h1>\n  <p>如果PC们在第12章期间设法阻止了三起谋杀中的任意一起发生，他们会自动获得该灵魂未被纳入苦迦菩提之攫的益处：在他们的一类豁免类别上获得对应的+2状态加值，并在本幕高潮处获得所述的优势。给予PC们这些灵魂被释放时本应获得的奖励，以及他们进入苦迦菩提之攫后也应获得的奖励。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>柳岸镇的所有建筑并非都被枝条人像占据。被@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}谋杀的那些人的灵魂，被连同他一起拉入了思维空间，在他们各自死亡地点附近化作啜泣的幽影，被束缚在那里。</p>\n<p>PC们可能不会想到要去拜访这些地点，但第一个地点——鸣禽剧院——就在PC们进入苦迦菩提之攫的出口附近。当PC们适应这诡异的新现实时，让他们每人尝试一次@Check[perception|dc:30]检定（携带<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>的PC在该检定上获得+4物品加值）。成功时，一名PC会听见从鸣禽剧院传来的熟悉嗓音的闷响——大野和马的声音——正在大声说话；该剧院位于他们进入苦迦菩提之攫处西南方不到200尺处。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-chainedspirit.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Chained Spirit\" alt=\"a kitsune spirit chained to a desk\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-chainedspirit.webp')\" />\n<p>本节中的三名灵体都被和善保谋杀，因为他害怕这些人生前可能有能力伤害他。讽刺的是，他背叛自己的恐惧并将他们杀害，反而给了每个灵体一件PC们可用来对付他的潜在武器。然而，PC们只有释放这些灵体，才能获得这些武器。</p>\n<p>在这些地点的每一处，PC们都可以与被锁链束缚的灵体互动，并使用一件个人物品来唤回该灵体对其生前身份的一部分记忆，从而打破善保的法术，进而将其解放。这样做会使灵体得以逃离思维空间，前往真正的来世，并使他们被偷走的眼睛从苦迦菩提祭坛上消失；其后果在本章末尾描述。此外，每个被释放的灵魂都会作为交换，向PC们提供一项益处。</p>\n<p>注意，尽管这三名被困住的灵魂不是生物，也没有数据表，但他们确实算作灵体，因此如有需要，PC们可以用<em>天牙水晶</em>追踪其中任意一个到其所在位置。如果和善保谋杀的受害者超过三人，PC们可以在第12章中发现尸体的地点附近找到那些被锁链束缚的灵体——以以下遭遇为指导，根据需要创建额外的遭遇。</p>\n<p>在每一种情况下，为了解放一名被镣铐束缚的灵魂，PC们必须进行以下行动。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>解放被镣铐束缚的灵魂</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">听觉</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">专注</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">探索</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">语言</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">精神</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你与一名被镣铐束缚的灵魂交谈10分钟，并通过提醒他们生前所爱之物来帮助他们摆脱枷锁。每次尝试都需要一次DC 28的技能检定，具体使用哪项技能取决于该灵魂本身（并会在下列各遭遇中提及），或者进行一次@Check[diplomacy|dc:32]或@Check[intimidation|dc:32]检定。若你携带并展示一件从该灵魂的谋杀现场取来的重要信物，你在此检定上获得+3物品加值。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大成功</strong>你说服灵魂摆脱镣铐；在其从苦迦菩提之攫中消散前，它会如后续遭遇所述奖励你。你的言辞极具感染力，以至于你不是让灵魂前往来世，而是让灵魂回到柳岸镇的生命之中，如同受到@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kqhPt9344UkcGVYO]{Resurrect}仪式的效果，且该仪式被升阶至第7环。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>成功</strong>同大成功，但灵魂不会复活；相反，它会前往骨园进入来世，并在生者世界中保持死亡。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>失败</strong>你未能说服灵魂摆脱镣铐，但你可以再次尝试。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>大失败</strong>灵魂在对苦迦菩提的束缚中越陷越深。除非和善保被击败，否则它无法被解放（届时，被镣铐束缚的灵魂会自动被解放并前往来世）；无法再对该被镣铐束缚的灵魂尝试“解放”。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Chained Spirits</span>\n</h2>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Murders Avoided</h1>\n  <p>If the PCs managed to prevent any of the three murders from taking place during Chapter 12, they’ll automatically receive the benefit of that soul’s absence from Kugaptee’s Grasp, gaining the associated +2 status bonus to one of their saving throw categories and earning the advantages detailed at this act’s climax. Grant the PCs the rewards they would’ve earned for releasing these souls as well as once they enter Kugaptee’s Grasp.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>Wicker effigies do not occupy all of Willowshore’s buildings. The souls of those who @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} murdered have been pulled into the mindscape with him, where they’re bound as weeping shades near the sites of their deaths.</p>\n<p>The PCs might not think about visiting these sites, but the first of them, Songbird Theater, is close to where the PCs emerge into Kugaptee’s Grasp. As the PCs acclimate to the strange new reality, have them each attempt a @Check[perception|dc:30] check (a PC carrying the <em>Fang and Key</em> gains a +4 item bonus to the check). On a success, a PC hears the muffled sounds of a familiar voice—Kazuma Oono’s—talking aloud from Songbird Theater, not quite 200 feet to the southwest of where they emerge into Kugaptee’s Grasp.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-chainedspirit.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Chained Spirit\" alt=\"a kitsune spirit chained to a desk\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-chainedspirit.webp')\" />\n<p>Each of the three spirits in this section was murdered by Heh Shan-Bao because he feared the possibility that the person, in life, might be able to hurt him. Ironically, by betraying his fears and murdering them, he gave each spirit a potential weapon that the PCs can use against him. However, the PCs can obtain these weapons only by releasing the spirits.</p>\n<p>At each of these sites, the PCs can free the chained spirit by interacting with it and using a personal item that restores some of the spirit’s memories of who they were in life, thereby breaking Shan-Bao’s spell. Doing so permits the spirit to flee the mindscape for the true afterworld and causes their stolen eyes to vanish from Shan-Bao’s altar to Kugaptee, with repercussions described at the end of this chapter. Additionally, each freed soul has a benefit to grant the PCs in exchange for its release.</p>\n<p>Note that while these three trapped souls aren’t creatures and don’t have stat blocks, they do count as spirits, so the PCs can use the <em>skyfang crystal</em> to track any of them to their locations if needed. If Heh Shan-Bao murdered more than three victims, the PCs can find those chained spirits near where their bodies were discovered in Chapter 12—use the following encounters as guidelines for creating additional ones as needed.</p>\n<p>In each case, to free a shackled soul, the PCs must perform the following activity.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>Free Shackled Soul</h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Auditory</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Concentrate</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Exploration</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Linguistic</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Mental</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You speak to a shackled soul for 10 minutes and help them to cast off their bonds by reminding them of what they loved in life. Each attempt requires a DC 28 skill check that’s specific to the soul in question (and mentioned in each of the following encounters), or a @Check[diplomacy|dc:32] or @Check[intimidation|dc:32] check. If you carry and display a significant token taken from the soul’s murder scene, you gain a +3 item bonus to this check.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Success</strong> You convince the soul to cast off its shackles; it rewards you as detailed in the following encounters before it fades away from Kugaptee’s Grasp. Your words have been so compelling that rather than moving on to the afterlife, you allow the soul to return to life in Willowshore, as if from the effects of a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.kqhPt9344UkcGVYO]{Resurrect} ritual that had been heightened to 7th rank.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the soul doesn’t resurrect; instead, it moves on to the Boneyard for its afterlife and remains dead in the living world.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Failure</strong> You fail to convince the soul to cast off its shackles but can attempt to do so again.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The soul spirals even deeper into its bondage to Kugaptee. It can’t be freed until Heh Shan-Bao is defeated (upon which the shackled soul is freed automatically to the afterlife); no further attempts to Free this Shackled Soul can be attempted.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Curiosities and Nightmares": {
              "name": "奇珍异事与梦魇 Curiosities and Nightmares",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">奇观与梦魇</span>\n</h2>\n<p>苦迦菩提之握里充斥着致幻的碎片。其中一些会如同一处@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE]{幻象场景}的效果般显现，并在PC们靠近时自动触发。下面详述三个例子。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>木材秤</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>触发</strong> PC们接近一片工业区域。</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>描述</strong> 附近矗立着一台木材场用的秤，由扭曲、焦黑的梁木与锈蚀的铁链搭成。它的横梁上蹲着一只食腐乌鸦，体型有小马那么大。乌鸦不断呕吐出人类骨骸，落到秤的高端托盘上。那一侧的托盘被穿出一个大洞，使得所有骨头都笔直落下，托盘也永远不会下沉。就在骨头将要砸到地面时，它们消失不见。另一侧低贴地面，堆着一堆木材与白银。</p>\n  <p>在较低的托盘旁，站着一个闪烁不定的柳条人形，疯狂地在银锭与成堆木材中翻找，执拗到手指都磨损得不成样子。那张圆圆的木头脸被粗劣地涂画成和善保的模样。它胸腔里堆满红翼的死蝴蝶，彼此碰撞，发出凄哀的窸窣声，无尽重复着：“你们在哪儿？我的宝贝们，你们在哪儿？你们一定在这儿。所有我珍视的一切都在这儿。”</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>荣耀贩子</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>触发</strong> PC们进入一处集市或商贸区域。</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>描述</strong> 在街角站着一个柳条人形，头是一颗木球，上面用孩童般的笔触涂画出一张脸。尽管画得笨拙，那张脸看起来像是和善保。</p>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-peddler-of-glories.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Peddler of Glories\" alt=\"a wicker figure with a childishly painted wooden ball for a head\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-peddler-of-glories.webp')\" />\n  <p>那人形披着帝国传令使华服的破烂残片，手里拿着一卷黄封卷轴，上面覆满毫无意义的涂写。它发出咔嗒与哐啷声，仿佛胸腔里有发条齿轮在滴答作响；但从它躯壳的缝隙里窥视进去，只能看到少量红翼枯萎的死蝴蝶彼此碰撞。任何活着的生物一靠近，柳条人形就转向那人，张开柳条双臂，仿佛在宣读官方告示。它那蝴蝶残壳的嘎啦声隐约像是在反复吟唱：“向最荣耀的总督致敬，荣耀加身！他何其荣耀！他曾何其荣耀！他终将再度荣耀！”</p>\n  <p>若成功通过一次@Check[society|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识，PC便知道：龙华帝国的传令使通常不会以“荣耀”来颂扬一位总督——荣耀从不被视作值得鼓吹的品质。真正配得上称颂的总督会因德行、智慧，或对律法的光荣服从而被赞美。这个传令使只会空洞、机械地谈论“荣耀”，还对着一座空村庄如此行事；在龙华贤者眼中，这会被视为愚者的悲剧。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>木偶母亲</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>触发 </strong>PC们穿过一片住宅区。</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>描述</strong> 路边站着一个柳条人形，仰着头伸长脖子望向窗户，双手合拢，满怀赞叹。它穿着农妇那种褴褛的裹衣与虫蛀的披巾，但它圆木头脑袋上那张带笑、笨拙涂画的脸却是和善保。空 hollow 的胸腔里红翼死蝴蝶彼此碰撞作响，它们尸体相互敲击的声音像是重复的吟唱：“我的儿子。我的好儿子。我多么为我的好儿子骄傲！”</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Curiosities and Nightmares</span>\n</h2>\n<p>Kugaptee’s Grasp is rife with hallucinatory fragments. Some of them manifest akin to the effects of an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE]{Illusory Scene} that triggers automatically as the PCs approach. Three examples are detailed below.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>The Lumber Scales</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs approach an industrial area.</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>Description</strong> A lumberyard scale built of warped, blackened beams and rusting chains stands nearby. On its crosspiece perches a carrion crow the size of a small pony. The crow vomits an unending stream of human bones onto the high side of the scale. The dish on that side is pierced through with a large hole so that all of the bones fall straight through, and the dish never lowers. Just as the bones would strike the ground, they disappear. On the other side, low to the ground, is a heap of lumber and silver.</p>\n  <p>A flickering image of a wicker figure stands beside the lower dish, digging frantically through the silver ingots and piled lumber with such determination that its fingers are frayed to ruins. The figure’s round wooden face has been crudely painted to resemble Heh Shan-Bao. Dead butterflies with red wings are heaped up inside its chest, and they rattle against one another to create a plaintive susurration that unendingly repeats: “Where are you? My precious ones, where are you? You must be here. All that is precious to me is here.”</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>The Peddler of Glories</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs enter a marketplace or mercantile area.</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>Description</strong> On a street corner stands a wicker figure with a childishly painted wooden ball for a head. Although it’s clumsily rendered, the face appears to be Heh Shan-Bao’s.</p>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-peddler-of-glories.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Peddler of Glories\" alt=\"a wicker figure with a childishly painted wooden ball for a head\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-peddler-of-glories.webp')\" />\n  <p>The figure is clad in the rags of an imperial herald’s finery and carries a yellow-sealed scroll covered with meaningless scribbles. It clicks and clatters as though it had clockwork gears ticking in its chest, but peering in through the shell of its body reveals only a handful of dead butterflies with withered red wings rattling against one another. Upon being approached by any living creature, the wicker figure turns toward that person and stretches its wicker arms wide, as though reciting an official proclamation. The rattle of its butterfly husks vaguely resembles a repeated chant: “All hail the most glorious of governors, in all his glory! Glorious he is! Glorious he was! Glorious he will be again!”</p>\n  <p>With a successful @Check[society|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC knows that a herald of Imperial Lung Wa wouldn’t ordinarily celebrate a governor for “glory,” which was never considered a quality worth touting. A truly worthy governor would be celebrated for virtue, wisdom, or honorable obedience to the law. The fact that this herald speaks only of “glory,” and does so mindlessly, to an empty village would be considered a fool’s tragedy by the sages of Lung Wa.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2>The Puppet Mother</h2>\n\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>Trigger </strong>The PCs move through a residential area.</p>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\"><strong>Description</strong> A wicker figure stands at the side of the road, craning its head up toward the windows and clasping its hands admiringly. It wears the shabby wrap and moth-eaten shawl of a peasant woman, but the smiling, clumsily painted face on its round wooden head is Heh Shan-Bao’s. Dead red-winged butterflies rattle in its hollow chest, and the sound of their corpses ticking against one another sounds like a repetitive chant: “My son. My wonderful son. How proud I am of my wonderful son!”</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Kugaptee’s Grasp Features": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提之握 特性 Kugaptee’s Grasp Features",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提之掌的特征</span>\n</h2>\n<p>当PC们穿行于苦迦菩提之掌时，你可以将第10页提供的柳岸镇地图作为指引，但务必让玩家明白：他们家乡的这个版本要大得多，也拥挤得多。接下来的页面呈现了数个可能在这座诡异城市中发生的遭遇，其中有几场能帮助PC了解他们需要做什么才能击败和善保。无论PC只是探索苦迦菩提之掌，还是专注于前往某个特定地点，你都可以按需使用这些遭遇——每一场都附有一个建议的“触发”来推动其发生，但若你的游戏需要，它们也都可以在任何时候登场。</p>\n<p>这里主要的“居民”是一群没有面孔、如同魅影般的镇民；他们似乎照常过着日子，但姿态中透出疲惫与抑郁。他们不说话，也不会接近PC或对PC的存在作出反应。这些魅影不过是由思维空间维持的幻象，任何试图将注意力集中在他们身上的尝试，都会揭示他们仅仅只是虚影。</p>\n<p>这些建筑空无一物，且呈现出二维平面感，仿佛是一个冷漠的舞台设计师草草摆上的布景。它们没有任何家具，墙上只有随意涂绘的暗示。装饰屏风与花卉摆设都被简化为含糊的色彩污迹。书籍、卷轴与信件上只有无法辨认的潦草涂写，储藏间里也只有稻壳与变质的水——因为这个世界出自@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}的想象，而他对平民的生活从来兴趣寥寥。</p>\n<p>柳岸镇的店铺粗制滥造，货品稀少。若店内本可能陈列出足以引起总督兴趣的奢侈品，那么那些区域如今都空空如也，只剩告示牌写着：“所有货物均将送往至高无上的总督之掌。”</p>\n<p>这些苦迦菩提之掌的幻影从不进入这些住宅与店铺，使其内无人居住，里面只有柳条编成的人形偶像，脑袋则是一个圆圆的、塞满稻草的篮子。柳条人偶穿着村民那种具有特色、十分好认的服饰——而且，如果PC去到青天茶馆，甚至可能找到他们自己的塑像。在那里，他们会发现“自己”穿着对自身衣物与道具拙劣而毫无价值的仿制品，篮子脑袋上还套着麻袋；麻袋上画着他们的脸，却是以和善保那种简陋、幼稚的笔触描绘出来的相貌。</p>\n<p>这便是和善保退守的思维空间。在这里，他统治着一处扭曲的拙劣仿品——而苦迦菩提承诺将把这一切在现实中上演；并且，在总督的帮助下，或许很快就会成真。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Kugaptee’s Grasp Features</span>\n</h2>\n<p>As the PCs travel through Kugaptee’s Grasp, you can use the map of Willowshore presented on page 10 as a guide but make sure that the players understand this version of their home town is much larger and densely packed. The following pages present several encounters that can take place in the eerie city, several of which can help inform the PCs what they need to do to defeat Heh Shan-Bao. Whether the PCs are simply exploring Kugaptee’s Grasp or they’re focused on traveling to a specific location, you can use these encounters as you see fit—each has a recommended “trigger” to set them in motion, but any of them can work at any time if your game calls for them.</p>\n<p>The primary “inhabitants” here are faceless phantomlike townspeople who appear to go about their day normally, although with postures that imply exhaustion and depression. They don’t speak, and none approach the PCs or react to their presence. These phantoms are little more than illusions maintained by the mindscape, and any attempt to focus concentration on them reveals the fact that they’re merely figments.</p>\n<p>The buildings are vacant and two-dimensional, as if they’d been hastily placed by a disinterested stage designer. They contain no furniture, only carelessly painted suggestions on the walls. Decorative screens and floral arrangements are reduced to vague smudges of color. Books, scrolls, and letters contain illegible scribbles, and pantries hold only rice husks and stale water, for this world is of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s imagination, and he never had much interest in the lives of commoners.</p>\n<p>Willowshore’s shops are slapdash and sparse. If they might have held luxuries of interest to the governor, then those sections of the shops are empty, except for placards saying, “ALL GOODS TO BE SENT TO THE MOST GLORIOUS GOVERNOR’S GRASP.”</p>\n<p>None of these phantasms of Kugaptee’s Grasp ever enter these homes and shops, leaving them devoid of people and containing only wicker figures with round straw-stuffed baskets for heads. The wicker figures have been dressed in the villagers’ characteristic, recognizable clothing—and, indeed, the PCs might even find effigies of themselves if they visit the Cerulean Teahouse. There, they’ll find “themselves” dressed in worthless imitations of their own clothes and gear with sacks pulled over their basket heads, onto which their faces have been painted as simple, childish likenesses of Heh Shan-Bao.</p>\n<p>This is the mindscape to which Heh Shan-Bao retreated. Here, he rules over a warped mockery that Kugaptee promises to enact in reality—and, with the governor’s help, might soon come to realize.</p>"
            },
            "Kugaptee’s Grasp": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提之攫握 Kugaptee’s Grasp",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">苦迦菩提之握</span>\n</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>寻找和善保</h1>\n  <p>在“苦迦菩提之握”中的一些遭遇会向PC揭示和善保藏身之处，但他们也可以使用天牙水晶——如果他们在区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c5guestquart00]{C5}取回了它——来追踪和善保。这样做会把他们引向思维空间北部、苦迦菩提之墓的入口。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>在被腐化的思维空间中，柳岸镇的边界之外什么都不存在。在这里，苦迦菩提的影响并非滋长于谭杉寺在思维空间中的对应之物，而是从那棵高耸的柳树之下蔓延，并一路向上侵入它；那棵柳树在现实世界的柳岸镇北缘如哨兵般矗立守望。在这个思维空间里，那棵树已经消失了，取而代之的是一只高耸的利爪巨臂直插天穹，仿佛要撕裂苍穹。这个阴森地标正是此思维空间名称的来源，也正因如此，居住其中的存在——皆为苦迦菩提思想与梦境的显现——都称此地为“苦迦菩提之握”。</p>\n<p>PC一踏入区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}的思维空间之门，便会立刻第一次目睹这诡异而恐怖的现实。他们出现在看似柳岸镇镇区的地方，仿佛是从总督宅邸的正门走出；然而当他们环顾四周，所见仍是他们在思维空间里经历过的同一片空荡广场——只有一个例外：同一扇思维空间之门矗立在广场中央，PC可以用它返回被修复的宅邸并回到活人的世界——一旦被<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>解锁，这扇思维空间之门从此刻起将一直对PC保持解锁状态。</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">场景注记</span><span class=\"keepme\">宏 / 氛围</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.ogYjqncZ6aQvQPob]{Willowshore to Kugaptee's Grasp} @UUID[Macro.Jz8MIw7gUsCW19TY]{Reset Willowshore} | @UUID[Playlist.FGK5jsYreqU1AR5o.PlaylistSound.sJR9BjRNOb6CqqbC]{Dark Willowshore}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>将柳岸镇场景的光照改为红色。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>在PC第一次看到“苦迦菩提之握”时，朗读或意译以下内容。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>门外铺展开一片噩梦般的景象，天空仿佛煮沸的血。云层翻涌成一团团青紫与赤红的淤伤色块，见不到太阳。天空没有星辰，取而代之的是无数巨大、发光的眼睛点缀其间。有些似乎会转动视线，追随着下方景观中移动的身影；另一些则空洞地凝视着仿佛不存在的事物。其中最大的一只眼睛像月亮般俯视着你们。</p>\n  <p>在那异样的天空之下，是柳岸镇的地貌——却只剩地形还与现实相同。这片广袤的柳岸镇仿佛在百年扩张后形成的模样，如今已成横亘大地的巨城，所过之处几乎不留自然之物。河流与湖泊成为毫无生机的黑色虚空，水面既无波浪也无流动，只是死寂地躺在河床里。建筑的木墙渗出焦油般、恶臭的树脂，沿着墙面淌下，像黑色的泪。柳岸镇所有的天然植被、农作物与园艺植物，都被矮小、扭曲、饱受折磨的仿制品所取代——它们显然不可能还活着。</p>\n  <p>北方远处，曾经大尊柳屹立于林木覆盖的丘陵之巅之处，如今升起一片巨大的城市蔓延区；其上方盘踞着一条庞大而畸形的手臂，扭曲的利爪向上伸展，仿佛要撕裂上方刺目的天空。</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>PC一抵达思维空间，每个人都会发现自己的手腕被幽魂般的锁链环绕，其上有昏暗、难以辨认的符文在发光——这些符文与形状与他们在凶案受害者手腕上看到的烙痕极其相似。若成功通过一次DC 30的辨识魔法检定，PC便理解：只要PC仍身处“苦迦菩提之握”，他们的灵魂本身就处于危险之中，并获得@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.3uh1r86TzbQvosxv]{毁灭（状态） 1}；且只要该PC仍在“苦迦菩提之握”内，他们的毁灭（状态）数值就不能低于1。若大成功或大失败，该PC会进一步揭示：若有角色在此思维空间内死亡，苦迦菩提将夺取其灵魂。类似于被灵堕魔杀死的生物会遭受灵魂撕裂，任何试图让被镣铐束缚的PC复活、或将其作为不死生物驱使的尝试，都会导致“苦迦菩提之握”试图反制该尝试（反制调整值+23，反制阶位7）。</p>\n<p>逃离这些镣铐有两种方式。击败@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}后，镣铐会立刻消散。不过，还有一种更容易达成的方法：携带一件与和善保前世相关的联结之物。携带这些物品之一的PC（区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c2courtyard000]{C2}中毁坏的玉瑾珠肖像、区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4}中的<em>七贤智慧</em>、该卷轴内发现的信件、或区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}中的保存花朵与缎带）会感到一股温暖的守护感从该物品涌入全身；片刻之后，幽魂镣铐便会消退，他们也不再处于毁灭（状态）。若PC身上不再携带这些物品之一，镣铐会立刻重新出现；该物品不必握在手中，但必须被穿戴，或放在PC携带或穿戴的容器中。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Kugaptee’s Grasp</span>\n</h1>\n<aside class=\"sidebar float-right\">\n  <h1>Seeking Heh Shan-Bao</h1>\n  <p>While some of the encounters in Kugaptee’s Grasp will reveal to the PCs where Heh Shan-Bao is hiding, they can also use the skyfang crystal, if they recovered it from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c5guestquart00]{C5}, to Track Heh Shan-Bao. Doing so leads them to the entrance to Kugaptee’s Grave in the north part of the mindscape.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>In the corrupted mindscape, nothing beyond the borders of Willowshore exists. Here, Kugaptee’s influence grows not in a mindscape version of Tan Sugi Monastery, but below and up into the towering willow tree that stands sentinel above the northern reaches of real-world Willowshore. In this mindscape, that tree has vanished, replaced by a towering clawed arm reaching up to the sky as if to rend the firmament. This looming landmark is the source of the mindscape’s name and why those who dwell within—all manifestations of Kugaptee’s thoughts and dreams—call the place Kugaptee’s Grasp.</p>\n<p>The PCs get their first view of this strange and horrifying reality as soon as they step through the mindscape door in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}. They emerge into what seems like downtown Willowshore, as if they’d stepped out of the front door of the governor’s manor, yet when they look around, all they see is the same empty plaza that existed in their mindscape—with one exception. The same mindscape door stands in the middle of the plaza and can be used by the PCs to return to the restored manor and back to the living world—once unlocked by the <em>Fang and Key</em>, this mindscape door remains unlocked for the PCs from this point onward.</p>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital Studio\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Scene Notes</span><span class=\"keepme\">Macros / Ambiance</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Macro.ogYjqncZ6aQvQPob]{Willowshore to Kugaptee's Grasp} @UUID[Macro.Jz8MIw7gUsCW19TY]{Reset Willowshore} | @UUID[Playlist.FGK5jsYreqU1AR5o.PlaylistSound.sJR9BjRNOb6CqqbC]{Dark Willowshore}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Change the Willowshore scene lighting to red.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>Read or paraphrase the following upon the PCs’ first sight of Kugaptee’s Grasp.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Beyond the door sprawls a nightmarish landscape under a sky that looks like boiled blood. The clouds are churning masses of bruised violet and red, devoid of a sun. Instead of stars, the sky is spangled with enormous, glowing eyes. Some seem to shift their gaze to follow those that move about the landscape below, while others stare blankly at seemingly nothing. The largest of these eyes looks down like a moon.</p>\n  <p>Beneath that alien sky lies the landscape of Willowshore, yet only the topography remains the same. This sprawling Willowshore appears as the town might have after a century of growth, now a massive city that spreads out across the land, leaving little of the natural world in its wake. The river and lake are lifeless black voids, and the water has neither waves nor currents; it sits motionless in its bed. The buildings’ wooden walls leak a tarry, foul-smelling sap that seeps down their sides like black tears. All of Willowshore’s natural vegetation, farm crops, and garden plants have been replaced by stunted, tortured replicas that, surely, can’t still be alive.</p>\n  <p>In the distance to the north, where once stood Great Willow atop a forested hill, rises a massive urban sprawl over which looms an immense, disfigured arm, its twisted talons reaching up as if to rip at the glaring sky above.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>As soon as the PCs arrive in the mindscape, each finds their wrists encircled by spectral chains with dim, illegible runes glowing on them—runes and shapes very similar to those they found burned onto the wrists of the murder victims. With a successful DC 30 check to Identify Magic, a PC understands that as long as the PCs remain in Kugaptee’s Grasp, their very souls are in danger and they become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.3uh1r86TzbQvosxv]{Doomed 1}, and as long as the PC remains in Kugaptee’s Grasp, their doomed condition value can’t go lower than 1. With a critical success, that PC reveals that if a character does die while within this mindscape, Kugaptee will claim their soul. In much the same way a creature killed by a nindoru is subjected to Soul Shred, any attempt that seeks to return a shackled PC to life or to animate them as undead causes Kugaptee’s Grasp to try to counteract the attempt (counteract modifier +23, counteract rank 7).</p>\n<p>There are two ways to escape these shackles. By defeating @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}, the shackles fade immediately. A much more available method, though, is to carry a link to Heh Shan-Bao’s previous life. A PC who carries one of these items (the ruined portrait of Ok Jinju from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c2courtyard000]{C2}, The <em>Wisdom of the Seven Sages</em> from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4}, the letter found within that scroll, or the preserved flower and ribbon from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}) feels a warm, protective sensation rising through their body from that item, and a moment later, the spectral shackles fade and they’re no longer doomed. The shackles reappear immediately if the PC is no longer carrying one of these items on their person; the item need not be held in hand, but must be either worn or located in a container the PC carries or wears.</p>"
            },
            "Heh Shan-Bao’s Plan": {
              "name": "和善保的计划 Heh Shan-Bao’s Plan",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">和善保的计划</span>\n</h2>\n<p>在他以堕落的柳岸镇思维空间“不死统治者”的新化身之身——如今此地被称为“苦迦菩提之握”（或简称“掌握”）——@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}一直在设法积攒足够的力量，好为苦迦菩提提供一具可供施展转生术的新躯体；但要完成这项任务，他必须等待自己的领域“追上”玩家角色进入的现实世界。也就是说：当玩家角色逃离思维空间时，能够一下子“跳跃”到115年后的未来；而和善保却不得不（在他看来）以真实时间度过这段漫长岁月。在这段期间，他作为苦迦菩提容器而不断增长的力量在周遭处处显现，将“掌握”从一座城镇改造成了一座城市。如今，为完成目标，他所需的只是在现实世界中收集足够多的转世的灵魂，让它们在他的巢穴中“成熟”；待它们准备就绪时，便会成为他彻底将自身交付给苦迦菩提、令其得以转生的催化剂，使灵堕魔得以扳倒谭杉，并自坟冢中崛起。</p>\n<p>以他当前的形态，和善保既强大又可悲。苦迦菩提将可怖的力量与亵渎的权能灌注于他，却也剥离了这位知府的大部分人格。善保已化作一头被愤怒与困惑本能驱使的生物，无法分辨自身模糊的记忆与苦迦菩提借由他传递的冲动。属于他的自我所剩无几，以至于他用镇民的恐惧与想象来填补缺失的自我认知。灵堕魔希望他永远维持这种状态；因为一旦和善保找回过多被遗忘的人性，忆起自己曾怀抱的希望、志向与理想，他便可能意识到自己失去了什么，并反抗恶魔的掌控。</p>\n<p>然而，在这层怪物般的伪装深处，真正的和善保仍然存在——被囚、迷失，并迫切渴求援助。若玩家角色能触及他，并带来合适的手段，他们便能引导这位前知府回归现实；如此一来，便可将苦迦菩提再度打入谭杉根系之下的又一个年代的沉眠之中。</p>\n<p>尽管和善保已接近完成他的计划（他在上一章谋杀的三名受害者，代表他完成仪式所需的最低转世的灵魂数量），但本章并不严格受计时器限制。若玩家角色拖延，和善保会杀害更多人以加速进程；不过，只要玩家角色完成《鬼季》冒险路径最后这部分的时间不超过一个月，他们应当仍有充足时间击败并拯救和善保。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Heh Shan-Bao’s Plan</span>\n</h2>\n<p>In his new incarnation as the deathless ruler of the corrupted Willowshore mindscape—now known as Kugaptee’s Grasp (or just the Grasp)—@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} has worked to gather enough power to afford Kugaptee a new body to reincarnate into, but to complete this task, he had to wait for his domain to “catch up” to the living world into which the PCs have entered. In effect, while the PCs were able to “jump” 115 years into the future when they escaped the mindscape, Heh Shan-Bao had to wait that out in (as perceived by him) real time. During that period, his growing power as Kugaptee’s vessel manifested all around him, transforming the Grasp from a town into a city. Now, all he needs to complete his goal is to gather enough souls from the living world, let them ripen in his lair, and when they’re ready, they’ll be the catalyst he needs to fully give himself over to Kugaptee to be reincarnated, allowing the nindoru to topple the Tan Sugi and rise from the grave.</p>\n<p>In his current form, Heh Shan-Bao is a creature at once both mighty and wretched. Kugaptee has imbued him with terrible strength and unholy power but has stripped away much of the governor’s personality. Shan-Bao has become a creature of angry, confused instincts, unable to distinguish his blurred memories from the impulses that Kugaptee sends through him. So little of his identity remains that he has adopted the townsfolk’s fears and imaginings in place of his missing sense of self. The nindoru wants him to remain in such a state, for if Heh Shan-Bao were to regain too much of his forgotten humanity and remember the hopes, aspirations, and ideals that he once held, he might realize what he has lost and rebel against the fiend’s grasp.</p>\n<p>For somewhere deep inside this monstrous facade, the real Heh Shan-Bao remains—trapped, lost, and desperate for help. If the PCs can reach him, and if they bring the right tools, they can guide their ex-governor back to reality and, in so doing, consign Kugaptee to another age of dormancy below the roots of the Tan Sugi.</p>\n<p>While Heh Shan-Bao is close to completing his plan (the three victims he murdered in the previous chapter representing the minimum amount of souls he needs to finish), this final chapter isn’t strictly on a timer. If the PCs dawdle, Heh Shan-Bao murders more and quickens the process, but assuming the PCs don’t take more than a month to complete this final portion of the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em>, they should have plenty of time to defeat and rescue Heh Shan-Bao.</p>"
            },
            "Into the Corruption": {
              "name": "深入腐化 Into the Corruption",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">深入腐化</span>\n</h1>\n<p>在过去的115年里，当柳岸镇的思维空间将PC们困住之时，苦迦菩提在现实世界中的存在缓慢地毒害并腐化了生长在他坟墓之上的苏木树。去年孙海将思维空间搅入混乱后，被打破的保持平衡使苦迦菩提的腐化得以更快速地扩散。若非PC们在本战役第二幕的深秋将尽之际击败了他的高阶祭司欣月，这股腐化本会让他得以在现实世界中完全转生。</p>\n<p>但击败欣月并未终结苦迦菩提的腐化影响——只是将其导向了别处。当PC们将自己与柳岸镇一并迁渡回现实世界后，他们在思维空间留下的灵性真空被那股影响所淹没。此后，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}被吸引进入此境界，被他自身的羞愧与罪疚所牵引。</p>\n<p>思维空间随之收缩，焦点不再是荒野边境，而是小镇本身。对和善保而言，接下来的115年里，他扮演着不朽统治者的角色，统治着一座由镇成长为城的聚落；城中居民并非凡人，而是不死、邪魔与怪物——它们与和善保的新化身（作为一名妖魄）一样，皆由苦迦菩提死去的梦所塑成。PC们很快将发现一种“如果……会怎样”的柳岸镇版本：若柳岸镇在115年的时光中成长为一座由怪物盘踞的庞大城市，并由一名暴君统治，而这暴君注定将成为某位邪魔神祇的新化身，它便会是如今这副模样。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Into the Corruption</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Over the past 115 years, while the Willowshore mindscape kept the PCs trapped, Kugaptee’s presence in the living world slowly poisoned and corrupted the sugi tree that grew over his grave. When Mago Kai threw the mindscape into chaos last year, the upset balance allowed Kugaptee’s corruption to spread more quickly. Had the PCs not defeated his high priest Xin Yue near the end of fall during this campaign’s second act, this corruption would’ve allowed him to reincarnate fully into the living world.</p>\n<p>But defeating Xin Yue didn’t put an end to Kugaptee’s corrupting influence—it merely redirected it. When the PCs transmigrated themselves and the town of Willowshore out into the living world, the spiritual vacuum they left behind in the mindscape became flooded with that influence. Thereafter, @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} was drawn into this realm, pulled in by his own shame and guilt.</p>\n<p>The mindscape shrank, focusing on the town rather than the hinterlands. For Heh Shan-Bao, the next 115 years played out with him in the role of an immortal ruler over a town that grew into a city, populated not by mortals but by undead, fiends, and monsters formed—like Heh Shan-Bao’s new incarnation as a yohoi—from Kugaptee’s dead dreams. What the PCs will soon find is a sort of “what if” version of Willowshore as it could’ve existed if it had grown over the course of 115 years into a sprawling city of monsters ruled by a tyrant destined to become the new incarnation of a fiendish god.</p>"
            },
            "Through the Mindscape Door": {
              "name": "穿过思维空间之门 Through the Mindscape Door",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">穿过思维空间之门</span>\n</h3>\n<p>北墙上的门是一扇永久性的思维空间之门，允许任何正统统治者从修复后的庄园旅行至受诅咒的柳岸镇思维空间。@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}可以随意来去，但PC必须将<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>接触到门锁上才能打开。这样做会在1分钟内解锁大门，之后它会再次上锁——如果PC穿门而过，他们会发现自己回到了<em>鬼季冒险路径</em>开始的地方，也就是柳岸镇思维空间……但思维空间在他们待在其中的这段时间里已经发生了很大的变化！</p>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Through the Mindscape Door</span>\n</h3>\n<p>The door in the northern wall is a permanent mindscape door that allows anyone to travel from the restored manor to the cursed Willowshore mindscape, but only if they’re rightful rulers. @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} can come and go as he pleases, but the PCs must touch the <em>Fang and Key</em> to the door’s lock to open it. Doing so unlocks the door for 1 minute, after which it locks again—if the PCs step through, they find themselves back where the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em> began, in the Willowshore mindscape... but the mindscape has changed much since their time spent therein!</p>"
            },
            "Master Bedroom": {
              "name": "主卧室 Master Bedroom",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C8. 主卧室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间陈设奢华的卧室里散发着纵情享乐的气息。带帷幔的床上托盘里摆着吃到一半的橘子、甜米糕与蜜饯坚果的残余。附近的书写台上放着一幅未完成的书法卷轴，旁边架子上则搁着干涸的墨盂。床右侧的墙上是一扇用上等柏木制成的大门。门把手上扣着一把华丽的金锁，锁面雕成一张丑恶的恶魔脸。</p>\n</div>\n<p>当PC们进入此房间时，任何携带着<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>的人都会感觉物品猛烈地向北门的锁拉扯。这扇门在PC们以往任何一次造访宅邸时都不存在，而且越是观察，越会觉得它忽明忽暗、不断扭动，好像这扇门并不完全属于这个现实。它是一扇思维空间之门，提供通往被腐化的柳岸镇思维空间的许可——@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}正是通过这扇门来去；有了<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>，PC们也可以如此。</p>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>在PC们能够继续前进检查大门之前，他们必须先应付这间房的住客：它蹲在门前，正嗅着锁。这是一只食厄精，一种以诅咒为食的昆虫样精类。这只特定的食厄精名为伊希尼亚克（Ithiniak），在化为废墟的柳岸镇栖身多年，并享受着弥漫在区域中的余留诅咒。他避开了孙海的驱邪者，但当PC们转渡回生者世界、总督宅邸以废墟形态回归后，伊希尼亚克发现自己被困在这座宅邸的小型思维空间版本之中。伊希尼亚克不知道自己为何会被困在这里，但他痴迷于从北门上锁的钥匙孔中飘出的“无比强烈的诅咒的芬芳”。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-imprecasia.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C8. 主卧室</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">微不足道 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Ejd4kDTxJ55sXiQ2]{伊希尼亚克}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>食厄精一注意到PC们，便立刻直起身打量他们；若PC们发动攻击，伊希尼亚克知道自己无处可逃，便会战至死。因此，这只食厄精更愿意与PC们交谈而不是战斗：他先问PC们是否知道是什么造成了从钥匙孔里飘出的“这股美味的气味”，接着问他该如何逃离此地。PC们可以直接护送这名精类离开宅邸；如此一来，他会一声不吭地迅速逃入周围的树林，连一句感谢都没有。</p>\n</section>\n<p>聪明或谨慎的PC们也许会花时间向这名精类打听。他能证实和善保的来去，并指出自己总是躲着那道骇人的身影；而且每当那位前任总督穿过此处这扇香气宜人的门出入时，门外一瞥既令他胆寒，又令他兴奋。他所能提供的细节不多，只提到曾瞥见红色的天空、被压迫的城市，以及一只爪子自山顶伸出，探入上方云海之中；但他也补充道：“那地方看起来再糟，闻起来却……太……美味了！”</p>\n<p>伊希尼亚克最初的态度为不关心。作为被带出宅邸的回报，他会同意尝试移除PC们可能承受的任何诅咒；然而，除非至少让他变为友善，否则当他这么做时，他会使用吞噬诅咒来“品出完整的味道”，在过程中可能会把对方吸干。若此次遭遇以和平方式结束，伊希尼亚克会告诉PC们他会在此等候。他还请求PC们在处理完门后区域的事务后，如果在门外发现更多诅咒，请带回来给他吃。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-flowerandribbon.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Camellia Flower and Ribbon\" alt=\"a withered camellia flower carefully preserved in a cushioned box\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-flowerandribbon.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.Qlo52vuimLWjRjNT]{壁龛} @UUID[Actor.sDG7VfWujAH2INrX]{衣柜} <br />\n  书写台下方的壁龛里放着和善保的私人日记，记录了他对自身所面临困境的反思、对在魔法仪式中赌上性命的恐惧，以及他最终决定修改仪式的缘由——他用自我辩解的说法称，若事情变糟，“众人都付出一些，无人付出全部。”\n</p>\n<p>在善保衣柜的深处，有一朵粉色山茶花，被小心地保存在带衬垫的盒子里。花茎用一条金色、写满书法的缎带缠绕，其上有一只纤细的手写着：“夏之美德永不凋零。”进行一次成功的@Check[society|dc:30]或@Check[academia-lore|dc:30]检定后，PC认出这句引文出自<em>《阿达维莎公主的哀歌》</em>，一部古典爱情传奇，讲述一位异乡公主爱上贫寒天朝学生的故事。两人明白社会地位使他们无法成婚，于是恋人共度一夏后分别；公主劝诫她的学者以践行龙华的传统美德，来纪念他们的爱情。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C8. Master Bedroom</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This lavishly furnished bedroom reeks of decadent trappings. Remnants of half-eaten oranges, sweet rice cakes, and candied nuts lie on a platter atop the canopied bed. A nearby writing stand holds an unfinished calligraphy scroll, and dry inkwells sit on the side shelf. The wall to the right side of the bed features a large door made of fine cypress wood. An ornate golden lock worked into a hideous fiend’s face is clasped around the door’s handle.</p>\n</div>\n<p>As the PCs enter this room, anyone carrying the <em>Fang and Key</em> feels the item tug violently toward the lock in the northern door. This door didn’t exist in any previous visit the PCs made to the manor, and the more one observes it, the more it seems to flicker and shift as if the door weren’t wholly part of this reality. It’s a mindscape door that provides access to the corrupted Willowshore mindscape—it’s through this door that @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} comes and goes, and with the <em>Fang and Key</em>, the PCs can do so as well.</p>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> Before the PCs can move forward to examine the door, they’ll need to contend with this room’s occupant, who crouches before the door and is sniffing the lock. This is an imprecasia, an insectile fey that feeds on curses. This particular imprecasia is named Ithiniak and dwelled in the ruined Willowshore for many years and enjoyed the lingering curse that infused the area. He avoided contact with Mago Kai’s exorcists, but when the PCs transmigrated back to the living world and the governor’s manor returned in its ruined form, Ithiniak found himself trapped within this small mindscape version of the manor. Ithiniak has no idea how he came to be trapped here but is obsessed with the scent of a “gloriously potent curse” that wafts through the northern door’s locked keyhole.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-imprecasia.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C8. Master Bedroom</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Trivial 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.Ejd4kDTxJ55sXiQ2]{Ithiniak}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The imprecasia straightens up quickly to regard the PCs once he notices them; if the PCs attack, Ithiniak knows he has nowhere to flee to and fights to the death. As such, the imprecasia is more willing to speak to the PCs than fight, first asking them if they know what’s causing “this delectable smell” wafting through the keyhole, then asking them how he can escape this place. The PCs can simply escort the fey out of the manor, in which case he quickly flees into the surrounding woods without so much as a thank you.</p>\n</section>\n<p>Wise or canny PCs might take the time to learn from the fey. He can confirm Heh Shan-Bao’s comings and goings, noting that he’s always hidden from the frightening figure, and that each time the former governor arrived or left through the lovely-smelling door in this room, the glimpse beyond both chilled and excited him. He can offer little more than mentioning a glimpse of red skies, an oppressed city, and a claw reaching from atop a hill into the clouds above, but he also notes that “as bad as the place looks, it smells... so... delicious!”</p>\n<p>Ithiniak’s initial attitude is indifferent. He’ll agree to try to remove any curses the PCs might be suffering in return for being led out of the manor; however, unless he’s been made at least friendly, when he does so, he’ll use Devour Curse to “get the full flavor” from the PC’s curse, potentially draining them in the process. If the PCs come to a peaceful conclusion in this encounter, Ithiniak lets the PCs know he’ll wait here. He also asks that if they find any more curses beyond the door to please bring them back to him to eat, once the PCs conclude their business in the area beyond.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-flowerandribbon.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Camellia Flower and Ribbon\" alt=\"a withered camellia flower carefully preserved in a cushioned box\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-flowerandribbon.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.Qlo52vuimLWjRjNT]{Nook} @UUID[Actor.sDG7VfWujAH2INrX]{Wardrobe} <br />\n  The nook beneath the writing stand holds Heh Shan-Bao’s private diary, containing his reflections on the dilemma he faced, his fears about risking his own life in the magical ritual, and his ultimate decision to modify the ritual with the self-justifying excuse that, if things go bad, “all pay some, and none pays all.”\n</p>\n<p>In the back of Shan-Bao’s wardrobe is a pink camellia flower carefully preserved in a cushioned box. The flower’s stem is wrapped in a gold, calligraphed ribbon, upon which a delicate hand has written: “Summer’s virtues never fade.” With a successful @Check[society|dc:30] or @Check[academia-lore|dc:30] check, a PC identifies the quotation as being from <em>Princess Adavisha’s Lament</em>, a classical romance about an outlander princess who fell in love with an impoverished Tian student. Knowing that their social positions made it impossible for them to marry, the lovers shared a single summer and then parted, with the princess exhorting her scholar to embody the traditional virtues of Lung Wa as a way of honoring the memory of their love.</p>"
            },
            "Storage Rooms": {
              "name": "储藏室 Storage Rooms",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C7. 储藏室</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">低 12</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这三个房间的描述都很相似；根据 PC 正在探索的具体房间，按需调整下方的朗读文本。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间储藏室的墙壁被一摞摞的木桶、箱子和其他容器遮得严严实实，所有东西上都覆着厚厚一层灰尘。</p>\n</div>\n<p>其中两间储藏室（区域 <strong>C7a</strong> 与 <strong>C7b</strong>）几乎没有什么值钱东西，但第三间（区域 <strong>C7c</strong>）则是个明显的例外，因为 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}曾用它来存放某些贵重物品。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/occult-living-rune.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C7. 储藏室</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.uuymk3S6erY8ebf7]{活化符文（神秘）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>一枚神秘活化符文守卫着西北侧的储藏室（区域 <strong>C7c</strong>），它潜伏在北侧一幅从竹制框架上垂下的大型壁卷上伺机而动。这幅卷轴描绘了一名身着护甲的女剑士，护甲表明她效忠于龙华帝国；她头顶的太阳中以通用语写着一个字：“Protection（守护）”。这便是那枚神秘活化符文；若有人未念出其停用真言便进入房间，它会在对方进入后的第 1 轮发起攻击。</p>\n  <p>若 PC 在区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4} 发现了被涂抹的停用真言，他们便可将其作为一个具有听觉与专注（特征）的 2 动作行动来进行，并尝试一次 @Check[occultism|dc:37|traits:auditory,concentrate|name:Deactivation Mantra] 检定。成功时，神秘活化符文会回到卷轴上的位置并保持不活跃状态，直到它遭到攻击，或房间空置 1 分钟后再有人重新进入为止。大成功或大失败：大成功时，停用真言会摧毁神秘活化符文；但大失败时，神秘活化符文会对未来使用该真言进行停用的尝试免疫。由你决定，若 PC 使用了非同寻常的手段来检查或修复区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4} 中被涂抹的指示，本次检定的 DC 最多可降低 10。</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.IWJJcS3f0Xawf8XO]{储藏室} <br />\n  曾存放在此处的大部分贵重物品，都在和善保为其毁灭的仪式做准备时被消耗掉了，但他最近购得的三把强力武器仍留在这里储存——若 PC 在此处花费 10 分钟来进行搜寻，他们会自动发现：一把<em>龙火半弓</em>、一把<em>四虎刀</em>与一把<em>雷怒大刀</em>。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C7. Storage Rooms</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 12</span>\n</h2>\n<p>All three of these rooms have similar descriptions; adjust the read aloud text below as needed depending on the one the PCs are exploring.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The walls of this storage room are hidden behind stacks of barrels, crates, and other containers, all of which are coated in thick layers of dust.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Two of these storage rooms (areas <strong>C7a</strong> and <strong>C7b</strong>) contain little of value, but the third (area <strong>C7c</strong>) is a significant exception, as @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} used it as storage for certain valuables.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/occult-living-rune.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C7. Storage Rooms</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.uuymk3S6erY8ebf7]{Living Rune (Occult)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> An occult living rune watches over the northwestern storage room (area <strong>C7c</strong>), lying in wait on a large wall scroll that hangs from a bamboo frame to the north. This scroll depicts a female swordfighter clad in armor that identifies her as serving Imperial Lung Wa; the sun above her head contains a single character in Common: “Protection.” This is the occult living rune, and it attacks on the first round after anyone enters the room without performing its deactivation mantra.</p>\n  <p>If the PCs discovered the smudged deactivation mantra in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4}, they can perform it as a 2-action activity with the auditory and concentrate traits and then attempt a @Check[occultism|dc:37|traits:auditory,concentrate|name:Deactivation Mantra] check. On a success, the occult living rune returns to its position on the scroll and remains inactive until it’s attacked or until the room is empty for 1 minute and then reentered. On a critical success, the deactivation mantra destroys the occult living rune, but on a critical failure, the occult living rune becomes immune to future attempts to deactivate it using the mantra. At your option, if the PCs used extraordinary means to examine or restore the smudged instructions from area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4}, the DC for this check can be reduced by up to 10.</p>\n</section>\n\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.IWJJcS3f0Xawf8XO]{Storage Room} <br />\n  Most of the valuables once kept here were expended during Heh Shan-Bao’s preparation for his doomed ritual, but three potent weapons he’d recently acquired remain in storage here—they’re automatically discovered if the PCs take 10 minutes to Search here: a <em>dragonfire halfbow</em>, a <em>four-tiger blade</em>, and a <em>thundering fury dadao</em>.\n</p>"
            },
            "Dining Area": {
              "name": "用餐区 Dining Area",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C6. 用餐区</span>\n<span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间房屋的墙面精细灰泥装饰被塑造成森林里柳树枝头栖息的鸟群。主用餐区摆着三张木桌，配有软垫长凳；从北边厨房敞开的门口飘来一阵烹饪盛宴的诱人香气。</p>\n</div>\n<p>在春季最后一天，@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}尝试进行他的仪式时，宅邸厨房正忙得不可开交，筹备着一场盛宴——他打算在次日举办，以庆祝仪式成功。如今，在这座被修复的宅邸所构成的思维空间中，这场盛宴永远在烹饪，却始终无法完成，使这片区域充满了令人垂涎却又令人沮丧的气味：一顿永远不可能到来的饭菜。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C6. 用餐区</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">中等 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.TzgqhLfOPvWiOeBa]{僵尸（3）}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Provincial Jiang-shi\" alt=\"provincial jiang-shi vampire\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>生物：</strong>三名僵尸吸血鬼（特征）潜伏在用餐区。表面上它们是宅邸守卫，但这三名吸血鬼（特征）已被烹饪食物的香气、以及为一场即将到来却永远不会到来的盛宴而摆好的餐桌所引发的忧郁情绪淹没。来自区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4} 中陷阱的哀号声会惊动它们；除此之外，当PC进入房间时，他们会发现这三名不死在此缓慢徘徊、漫无目的地游荡。它们无视任何交谈尝试，但若遭到攻击，吸血鬼（特征）会反击。战斗开始时，它们在1分钟内处于@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{呆滞 2}（注意这会使它们用于先攻的察觉加值承受–2减值），随后在接下来的1分钟内暂时免疫苦涩顿悟。它们会战斗至被摧毁为止。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C6. Dining Area</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>The fine plasterwork of this room’s walls has been molded into the shapes of birds roosting in the branches of willow trees in a forest. Three wooden tables with padded benches sit in the main dining area, and the appetizing scent of a cooking feast wafts through the open doors from the kitchen to the north.</p>\n</div>\n<p>When @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} attempted his ritual on the last day of spring, the manor kitchens were in full use, preparing a feast he intended to throw the next day to celebrate the successful ritual. Now, in the mindscape that is the restored manor, this feast is perpetually cooking but never quite completed, filling the area with the tantalizing but frustrating scents of a meal that will never be.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C6. Dining Area</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Moderate 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.TzgqhLfOPvWiOeBa]{Jiang-shi (3)}</span>\n  </div>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Provincial Jiang-shi\" alt=\"provincial jiang-shi vampire\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp')\" />\n  <p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A group of three jiang-shi vampires lurk in the dining area. Ostensibly serving as manor guards, these three vampires have become overwhelmed with melancholia at the scent of the cooking food and the tables set for an imminent feast that will never arrive. The sound of the wail from the trap in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c4meetingare00]{C4} rouses them, but otherwise, when the PCs enter the room, they find the three undead slowly milling about, aimlessly, in this room. They ignore any attempt to converse, but if they’re attacked, the vampires fight back. When combat begins, they are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 2} for 1 minute (note that this imparts a –2 penalty to their Perception bonus for initiative) but are temporarily immune to Bitter Epiphany for 1 minute thereafter. They fight until destroyed.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Guest Quarters": {
              "name": "客房 Guest Quarters",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C5. 客房</span>\n</h2>\n<p>这套客房的装潢都同样凌乱不堪；你可以对三间客房都使用以下朗读文本，但需要根据每间客房不同的大小相应调整描述。</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>这间陈设考究的卧室具备一位旅行中的贵族所期望的一切舒适设施，包括独立浴室和可上锁的私人箱柜。一把钥匙——很可能是给客人用来打开箱柜的——就放在容器合拢的盖子上。</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  在那场失败的仪式发生时，来自天京森杭寺的重要宾客住在区域<strong>C5a</strong>，但他们今天并不在这里——他们的尸体与魂魄在本章更早时已在荒废庄园中以战缚灵的形式遭遇过（见 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a5guestquart00]{这里}）。尽管如此，这间客房看起来最近仍有人使用：空气中残留着熏香的气味，床上的床单也有轻微的褶皱与凌乱。\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.LuTsRFPYNLZvSpNb]{床} @UUID[Actor.8vs8YrIBGUTUf8xU]{床单下面} <br />\n  虽然在现实世界的废墟里，它已作为被毁坏的物品存在过，但宾客带来的<em>天牙水晶</em>在这座复原后的庄园里仍完好无损地留在原处——几乎像是被随手丢弃一般，放在区域<strong>C5a</strong>其中一张床的床面上。它曾经的携带者将其作为护身之物，而它用来搜索魂魄的力量，会在PC们进入被腐化的柳岸镇思维空间后派上用场。\n</p>\n<p>在区域<strong>C5a</strong>另一张床的床单下面，塞着一块从谭杉寺取回的冥想曼荼罗，其中一位天京祭司一直在研究它。它显然是本地制品：以柏木雕刻成传统神门村落的样式，再涂上明亮的蓝色与紫色颜料，并非天京的遗物。天京祭司们并不知道，这块曼荼罗属于一位追随其领袖步入灾害的僧侣。曼荼罗可以作为项链或手链佩戴；除此之外，它的功能相当于一件<em>反制魅惑术</em>，其中目前封存着一个<em>扭曲心智</em>法术。它也可以用来解救本章中的那些被腐化的僧侣。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C5. Guest Quarters</span>\n</h2>\n<p>This suite of guest quarters all feature decor in a similar state of disarray; you can use the following read-aloud text for all three, but adjust each description as needed to account for the differing size of each guest quarter.</p>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>This finely appointed bedroom features all the comforts a traveling aristocrat would’ve expected, including amenities such as private baths and lockable personal chests. A key, likely for the guest’s use of the chest, sits atop the container’s closed lid.</p>\n</div>\n<p>\n  At the time of the botched ritual, important guests from the Senhang Monastery of Tianjing were staying in area\n  <strong>C5a</strong>, but they aren’t present here today—their bodies and souls were encountered in the ruined manor earlier in the act as war wraiths (See @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog13willow.JournalEntryPage.13a5guestquart00]{Here}). Still, this guest room appears to have been recently used, with a lingering fragrance of incense and beds that have slightly rumpled sheets.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.LuTsRFPYNLZvSpNb]{Bed} @UUID[Actor.8vs8YrIBGUTUf8xU]{Under Sheets} <br />\n  While it existed in the real-world ruins as a destroyed item, the <em>skyfang crystal</em> brought here by the guests remains in place here in the restored manor, sitting almost as if carelessly discarded atop one of the beds in area <strong>C5a</strong>. While its one-time carrier kept it for protection, its power to seek spirits will come in handy once the PCs enter the corrupted Willowshore mindscape.\n</p>\n<p>Stuffed under the sheets in a different bed in area <strong>C5a</strong> is a meditation mandala recovered from the Tan Sugi Monastery, which one of the Tianjing priests had been studying. It is obviously of local make, having been carved from cypress wood in a traditional Shenmen village design and then painted with bright blue and purple pigments, and isn’t a Tianjing artifact. Unbeknownst to the Tianjing priests, the mandala belonged to one of the monks who followed their leader into disaster. The mandala can be worn as a necklace or bracelet but otherwise functions as a <em>countering charm</em> that currently contains a <em>warp mind</em> spell. It can also be used to free the corrupted monks in this chapter.</p>"
            },
            "Meeting Area": {
              "name": "会面区域 Meeting Area",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C4. 会议区</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>精致的灯笼将这间房间照得通明。一对又长又矮的会议桌占据了房间的大部分空间；墙边的架子沿墙排开，塞满了整齐分隔的格子，用来分类存放官僚用的卷宗与公文。西南角的架子下方放着一只厚重的青铜保险箱，箱锁深嵌在一只庄严的金色狮子张开的口中，看上去令人望而生畏。南墙上挂着一个空的武器展示架。</p>\n</div>\n<p>墙上的武器展示架在现实世界里曾陈列着一把木材领主的斧头，但在这里仍然是空的。狮口保险箱上着锁（需要进行四次 @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] 来开锁），但只要以一次交互动作用<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>接触它，就会立刻解锁——携带钥匙并走到距离保险箱10尺以内的PC会感到钥匙在轻微震动，仿佛在期待什么。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">会议区</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.CpeKbIOrLrDJr1sj]{Witherweird Runes}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>危害：</strong>保险箱内部有一个暗格，藏着额外的宝藏，但这个暗格也受一处强力的超自然陷阱保护。</p>\n</section>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-wisdomofthesevensages.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Wisdom of the Seven Sages\" alt=\"a carefully rolled and secured scroll\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-wisdomofthesevensages.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.gmfmZ4nQ487Ceeip]{Shelves} @UUID[Actor.qDjiAK1irwhbRM8O]{Safe} @UUID[Actor.YdhSB5Ufiegaq2DT]{Hidden Compartment}<br />\n  除了数量惊人的过时且寻常的官僚文书之外，这里的架子上还放着一些和善保还为人类时最珍视的私人物品。如今，这些曾被珍爱的物件被弃置一旁，无人理会，只在架子上积满尘埃。一个角色若花至少10分钟搜寻这些架子，就会发现<em>《七贤之智》</em>，一部龙华著名的古典论著。和善保在通过最后一次大学考试时，父亲将这份卷轴赠予他。卷轴里夹着一封来自和善保父母的信，信中表达了他们对儿子的骄傲，并坚信他将证明自己是一位睿智而公正的龙座臣仆，配得上他们教导他的所有理想。这些物品会令<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>生出一阵识别般的颤动，并且它们可用于稍后帮助解放和善保的魂魄。</p>\n<p>保险箱里有10个丝绸钱袋，每个装有100 gp，另有数十张早已过期、如今一文不值的凭券与债券。PC在搜刮时若通过一次 @Check[perception|dc:30] 察觉检定，会注意到保险箱后壁内建的藏匿（并设有陷阱的）暗格。</p>\n<p>保险箱内的暗格里有第二套账簿，证明和善保曾非法售卖木材以中饱私囊，并将这笔收入对龙华帝国的上级隐瞒。账簿表明，他已习惯一种若无这条额外收入便无法维持的生活方式。最后几条记录暗示，他曾试图在不依赖木材钱的情况下维持奢侈开销，但未能做到。账簿接近末尾的一条记录揭示：和善保挪用了一大笔钱，从一名无良的龙华秘术师手中购得一枚神秘的活化符文，作为他“近期战争收藏品”的守卫。笔记指出，他暂时将活化符文（以及它所守护的武器）放在西北的储藏室里，并计划在“西北方遗迹里的邪恶魂魄这件事”结束后再购入更多。对PC而言，最直接有用的是一条不幸被抹花的记录，上面写着进入该房间时用来解除活化符文的“停用真言”。虽然字迹模糊，PC仍可利用这份残缺信息来尝试使活化符文失能（详见区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c7storageroo00]{C7c}）。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C4. Meeting Area</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Elaborate lanterns generously illuminate this room. A pair of long, low meeting tables fills most of the room, with shelves along the walls packed with regimented compartments for the organization of bureaucratic scrolls and missives. A stout bronze safe with a formidable-looking lock recessed inside a stern golden lion’s maw sits under the shelves in the southwest corner. An empty weapon display hangs on the southern wall.</p>\n</div>\n<p>The weapon display on the wall held a lumber lord’s axe in the real world, but here, it remains empty. The lion safe is locked (four @Check[thievery|dc:30|traits:manipulate,skill,action:pick-a-lock|name:Pick a Lock] checks to Pick the Lock), but a touch from the <em>Fang and Key</em> as an Interact action unlocks it immediately—a PC who carries the key and approaches within 10 feet of the safe feels the key vibrate as if in anticipation.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1.2)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/hazard.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Meeting Area</span> <span class=\"keepme\"></span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.CpeKbIOrLrDJr1sj]{Witherweird Runes}</span>\n  </div>\n  <p><strong>Hazard:</strong> A secret compartment inside the safe hides additional treasures, but this compartment is also protected by a potent supernatural trap.</p>\n</section>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-wisdomofthesevensages.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Wisdom of the Seven Sages\" alt=\"a carefully rolled and secured scroll\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-wisdomofthesevensages.webp')\" />\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.gmfmZ4nQ487Ceeip]{Shelves} @UUID[Actor.qDjiAK1irwhbRM8O]{Safe} @UUID[Actor.YdhSB5Ufiegaq2DT]{Hidden Compartment}<br />\n  Apart from a staggering amount of outdated and mundane bureaucratic documents, the shelves here contained some of Shan-Bao’s most prized personal possessions from when he was human. Now, these once-adored belongings are ignored, left to gather dust on these shelves. A character who Searches the shelves for at least 10 minutes comes across <em>The Wisdom of the Seven Sages</em>, a famous classical treatise of Lung Wa. Shan-Bao’s father gave him the scroll when he passed his final university exams. Folded into the scroll is a letter from Shan-Bao’s parents expressing their pride in their son and their conviction that he’ll prove to be a wise, fair servant of the Dragon Throne, worthy of all the ideals they taught him. These items draw a shiver of recognition from the <em>Fang and Key</em>, and they can be used to help free Heh Shan-Bao’s spirit later.\n</p>\n<p>The safe contains 10 silk pouches, each containing 100 gp, along with dozens of long-expired and now worthless vouchers and bonds. A PC who succeeds at a @Check[perception|dc:30] check while looting notices the hidden (and trapped) compartment built into the safe’s back wall.</p>\n<p>The hidden compartment inside the safe contains a second set of ledgers that prove that Heh Shan-Bao was illegally selling lumber to enrich himself personally and was concealing this income from his superiors in Imperial Lung Wa. These ledgers establish that he’d grown accustomed to a lifestyle that he wouldn’t be able to sustain without the extra income stream. A few of the final entries suggest that he was trying to find a way to maintain his luxury expenditures without the lumber money but failed to do so. Near the end of the ledgers, an entry reveals that Shan-Bao diverted a large amount of this money to purchase an occult living rune from an unscrupulous Lung Wa occultist to serve as a guardian for his “most recent wartime collectibles.” The notes indicate that he placed the living rune (and the weapons it guards) into the northwest storage room for the time being and that he plans to acquire more “once this matter with the evil spirit in the ruins to the northwest” is behind him. Of most immediate note to the PCs is an unfortunately smudged note containing the “deactivation mantra” for the living rune, to be used whenever Shan-Bao wished to enter the chamber. While smudged, the PCs can use this partial information to potentially incapacitate the living rune (see area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c7storageroo00]{C7c} for details).</p>"
            },
            "Servants’ Quarters": {
              "name": "仆役宿舍 Servants’ Quarters",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C3. 仆役寝室</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">低 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>尽管装饰朴素，这些仆役寝室看起来依然舒适而诱人，即便没有任何装饰来赋予它们各自的个性也是如此。</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>生物：</strong>一对僵尸吸血鬼（曾是为山宝效力的账房）栖身于此区域。它们各自占据两间寝室之一（<strong>C3b</strong>与<strong>C3c</strong>区域）作为自己的地盘，但当PC进入宅邸时，它们正在<strong>C3a</strong>区域，试图在桌上翻检成摞的文件与账簿并将其整理归类——这项工作永远不可能完成，因为它们总在按日期、按主题、按作者或其他分类方式之间反复改变主意，而这些分类方式又总会在它们完成最新一轮整理之前就被遗忘。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C3. 仆役寝室</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">低 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.TzgqhLfOPvWiOeBa]{僵尸 (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>如果它们注意到PC，两只僵尸会移动到@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c1manorentra00]{C1}区域迎接PC，并询问PC是如何在此之前找到进入领主宅邸的方法，随后要求PC立刻离开。吸血鬼几乎没有耐心，除迅速离开宅邸之外的任何举动都会促使它们发动攻击；它们会战斗至死。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C3. Servants’ Quarters</span>\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Low 12</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>Although they’re plainly decorated, these servants’ quarters look comfortable and inviting, even without any sort of decor to give them personalities of their own.</p>\n</div>\n<p><strong>Creatures:</strong> A pair of jiang-shi vampires (once accountants who served Shan-Bao) dwell in this area. Each has claimed one of the two quarters (areas <strong>C3b</strong> and <strong>C3c</strong>) as their own, but they’re in area <strong>C3a</strong> when the PCs enter the manor, sifting through stacks of documents and ledgers on the table in an attempt to organize them—a task they’ll never complete, as they keep changing their minds as to whether to sort the documents by date, by topic, by author, or by some other categorization that’s inevitably forgotten before they complete their latest sorting attempt.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(2.4)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/tokens/pzo90199-jiang-shi.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\">\n      <span class=\"keepme\">C3. Servants’ Quarters</span>\n      <span class=\"keepme\">Low 12</span>\n    </h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">@UUID[Actor.TzgqhLfOPvWiOeBa]{Jiang-shi (2)}</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>If they notice the PCs, the two jiang-shi move to greet the PCs in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c1manorentra00]{C1} and ask how the PCs found a way into the lord’s home before demanding the PCs leave at once. The vampires have very little patience, and anything other than swiftly leaving the manor prompts them to attack; they fight to the death.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Courtyard": {
              "name": "庭院 Courtyard",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C2. 庭院</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一泓闪耀的池水、一座假山庭园喷泉与精心布置的花木，使宅邸的核心化作一处雅致庭院。锦鲤在池中懒洋洋地游弋，鸣禽在灌木间啁啾歌唱。无数发着红光的灯笼沿庭院边缘悬挂在四周龙华式柱廊的檐下；而上方无月的夜空繁星满布。柱廊内侧墙面上装饰着装裱精美的画轴，描绘着龙、凤凰与显贵之士，但其中位于北侧中央墙面的一幅已被撕得粉碎。</p>\n</div>\n<p>这座庭院里永远都是晴朗无月之夜。若有PC飞出庭院上方，会在15尺高度撞上一道不可通行的屏障，无法看清周围地形。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-portraitscrap.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Portrait Scrap\" alt=\"torn portrait of a lovely young woman with dark hair\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-portraitscrap.webp')\" />\n<p>调查可发现，这幅画轴原本描绘的是一位黑发、目光庄重的可爱年轻女子，身着嬛郭一位公主的礼服。这幅画像的画框已被砸成碎片，画轴边缘也被利爪撕裂，但女子的容貌依然完好无损。破坏画框的东西似乎不敢触碰她的脸。若携带着<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>的PC接近这幅受损画轴至10尺以内，他们会感到钥匙微微颤动并轻轻震动。</p>\n<p>通过一次成功的 @Check[society|dc:30|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] 检定来进行回忆知识，PC可以辨认出画像中的女子是嬛郭的玉真珠公主——一位小贵族，在现代已去世多年。玉真珠公主曾是在 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保} 投身政治之前就读的那所大学里的同窗。尽管她只是远离王位的旁支公主，她的社会地位仍远高于当年尚为青年学者的善保，两人都明白他们的关系注定不可能。学业结束后，公主返回嬛郭。临别之际，她将山茶花与金丝绶带赠与善保，而他至今仍将其珍藏在卧室里（区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8}）——这朵山茶花与绶带在此处残存的画像中也清晰可见。</p>\n<p>善保担任总督时，曾委托绘制这幅画像，以致敬一位来访的嬛郭显贵；但实际上，这是因为他仍将她视为自己一生至爱。如今他已变成怪物，又因自己对柳岸镇所做之事而饱受罪疚折磨，善保几乎无法忍受直视公主的肖像。他撕毁她画像的行为源自极其强烈的情绪，以至于连宅邸的复原魔法也无法修复；然而即便在最狂怒之时，善保也无法忍心伤害画像的面容。</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>宝藏：</strong> @UUID[Actor.QlxKiUt5eSXPms8k]{Ruined Frame} <br />\n  画像残片可以轻易从画框中取出。它是能够用来解救善保的关键物体之一；然而它本身没有力量，且在受损状态下其价值不超过5 gp。\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C2. Courtyard</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A sparkling pool, a rock garden fountain, and artfully arranged foliage turn the manor’s heart into an elegant courtyard. Koi swim lazily in the pool, while songbirds sing in the shrubbery. Numerous glowing red lanterns hang along the edges of the courtyard from the eaves of the surrounding Lung Wa-style colonnade, while the moonless night sky above is filled with stars. Elegant, framed scrolls depicting dragons, phoenixes, and dignitaries adorn the inner walls of the colonnade, but one of them on the central northern wall has been torn apart.</p>\n</div>\n<p>It’s always a clear, moonless night in this courtyard. A PC who flies up out of the courtyard finds themselves hitting an impassible barrier at a height of 15 feet, preventing a good view of the surrounding terrain.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-portraitscrap.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Portrait Scrap\" alt=\"torn portrait of a lovely young woman with dark hair\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-portraitscrap.webp')\" />\n<p>An investigation reveals that the scroll once showed a lovely young woman with dark hair and solemn eyes wearing the ceremonial dress of a princess of Hwanggot. The frame of this portrait has been smashed to flinders, and claw swipes have torn the edges of the scroll, but the woman’s likeness remains pristine. Whatever damaged the frame doesn’t seem to have dared to touch her face. If a PC carrying the <em>Fang and Key</em> approaches within 10 feet of this damaged scroll, they’ll feel the key quiver and vibrate slightly.</p>\n<p>With a successful @Check[society|dc:30|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC identifies the woman in the portrait as Princess Ok Jinju of Hwanggot, a minor aristocrat who, in the modern era, is long dead. Princess Ok Jinju was a fellow student at the university where @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} studied before he got into politics. Although she was only a minor princess, far from the throne, she still belonged to a vastly higher social station than Shan-Bao could claim as a young scholar, and both of them knew that their relationship was impossible. After their studies came to an end, the princess returned to Hwanggot. In parting, she gave Shan-Bao the camellia and gold ribbon that he still keeps as prized possessions in his bedroom (area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c8masterbedr00]{C8})— that camellia and ribbon are fully visible in the portrait that remains here.</p>\n<p>When he was governor, Shan-Bao commissioned this portrait to honor a visiting dignitary from Hwanggot, but in reality, because he still considered her the great love of his life. Now that he has become a monster and is wracked with guilt for what he did to Willowshore, Shan-Bao can hardly bear to look at the princess’s likeness. His efforts to tear apart her portrait are rooted in such powerful emotion that they withstood the mansion’s restorative magic, but even in the worst of his rages, Shan-Bao couldn’t bear to damage the portrait’s face.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Treasure:</strong> @UUID[Actor.QlxKiUt5eSXPms8k]{Ruined Frame} <br />\n  The portrait scrap can be easily removed from the frame. It’s one of the key objects that can be used to free Shan-Bao; however, it has no power, and in its damaged state, it isn’t worth more than 5 gp.\n</p>"
            },
            "Manor Entrance": {
              "name": "庄园入口 Manor Entrance",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">C1. 庄园入口</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>一对石狮分立在庄园入口两侧，双眼闪烁着猩红的光芒。向北望去，滑动的纸墙挡住了通往庄园内院的视线。</p>\n</div>\n<p>在这座破败庄园的其他地方完全不见踪影的两尊石狮，就立在此处；当PC们进入房间时，它们似乎会动起来，抬起前爪致意，随后又回到原先的位置。石狮的举止透着如释重负，仿佛赋予它们行动的某种魂魄很高兴在长期疏于照料之后，宅邸终于落到值得信赖之人手中——它们本身并不危险。</p>\n<p>当PC们进入庄园时，除非他们屏住呼吸或试图潜行，否则位于区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c3servantsqu00]{C3a} 的僵尸仆役会自动注意到他们的进入。这些僵尸会暂时放下手头的工作，前去“迎接”PC们，详见区域 @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c3servantsqu00]{C3}。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">C1. Manor Entrance</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"read-aloud\">\n  <p>A pair of stone lions flanks the manor’s entrance, their eyes shimmering with crimson light. To the north, sliding paper walls block the view into the manor’s inner courtyard.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Completely missing from the ruined manor, the two stone lions found here appear to animate as the PCs enter the room, raising their forepaws in salute before returning to their original positions. The lions’ manner suggests relief, as if whatever spirit animates them is glad to have the mansion in trustworthy hands after a long history of neglect—they aren’t dangerous in and of themselves.</p>\n<p>When the PCs enter the manor, unless they’re holding their breath or attempting to be stealthy, the jiang-shi servants in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c3servantsqu00]{C3a} will automatically notice their entrance. The jiang-shi set aside their tasks to go “greet” the PCs as detailed in area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c3servantsqu00]{C3}.</p>"
            },
            "Manor Features": {
              "name": "庄园特征 Manor Features",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">宅邸特征</span>\n</h2>\n<p>\n  与本幕开始时不同，PC们可以毫无畏惧地接近已修复的宅邸。虽然拥有<em>尖牙与钥匙</em>将有助于解开已修复宅邸的某些谜团，但PC进入宅邸并不要求必须持有它。PC在宅邸外专注一轮后，会自动发现自己可以转换其“焦点”，观察宅邸在现代世界中实际存在的样子（作为废墟），或观察其完全修复的样子；但一旦PC进入已修复的宅邸，他们就无法在这些现实之间切换。通过一次成功的@Check[arcana|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[occultism|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]回忆知识检定，PC可以确认这座已修复的宅邸是思维空间的一种形式；那些合法统治柳岸镇的人可以随意进出其中。\n</p>\n<p>如果PC们进行实验，他们会发现：当他们进出已修复宅邸时，任何与他们保持接触的生物都能在现实世界与已修复宅邸的思维空间之间旅行；但若没有这种接触，这些生物就无法进入宅邸，或若被遗弃在宅邸内也无法离开。@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}正是通过这种方式安置了已修复宅邸的守卫。</p>\n<p>在修复状态下，很容易看出这座宅邸显然由健壮的木材建成，并以彩绘与瓦片精美装饰；但所有华丽工艺的银质点缀都已被剥除，只留下裸露的木材或石材。宅邸内的格栅纸墙上绘有自然、狩猎与社交聚会的美丽图景。无数灯笼使室内被诡异的红光照得通明——任何窥视这些灯笼内部的人都会看到，光源是一团扭动的发光灵堕魔蝴蝶球。</p>\n<p>虽然已修复宅邸的内部墙壁与窗户可以照常被强行打开，但外部的却不行。任何试图这么做的行为都只会让PC进入现实世界中那座废墟宅邸。同样地，任何试图从上方进入已修复宅邸庭院的行为，都会导致角色只是进入了废墟宅邸。只有通过区域@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c1manorentra00]{C1}的宅邸正门，PC才能在已修复宅邸与现实世界之间进出。</p>\n<h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">Manor Features</span>\n</h2>\n<p>\n  Unlike at the start of this act, the PCs can approach the restored manor without fear. While having the\n  <em>Fang and Key</em> will help unlock some of the restored manor’s mysteries, possession isn’t required for a PC to enter the manor. A PC who concentrates for a round while outside of the manor automatically finds that they can shift their “focus” to observe the manor as it actually exists in the modern world (as a ruin) or as it exists fully restored, but once a PC enters the restored manor, they can’t change between these realities. With a successful @Check[arcana|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[occultism|dc:25|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge, a PC confirms that this restored manor is a form of mindscape, one that can be entered or exited at will by those who rightfully rule Willowshore.\n</p>\n<p>If the PCs experiment, they’ll find that any creature they’re in contact with when they come or go from the restored manor can travel between the real world and the restored manor’s mindscape, but without this contact, such creatures can’t enter the manor or, if abandoned within the manor, can’t leave. It was via this method that @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao} installed the restored manor’s guardians.</p>\n<p>In its restored condition, it’s easy to see that the manor was clearly built from hearty woods and is beautifully adorned with paint and tiles, but all of the ornately worked silver accents have been stripped away, leaving bare wood or stone in their place. The latticed paper walls within the manor are decorated with beautiful images of nature, hunts, and social gatherings. Numerous lanterns keep the interiors brightly lit with eerie red light—anyone who peers within any of these lanterns sees that the source of light is a writhing sphere of glowing nindoru butterflies.</p>\n<p>While the restored manor’s interior walls and windows can be forced open normally, the exterior ones can’t. Any attempt to do so only allows the PCs to enter the ruined real-world manor. Likewise, any attempt to enter the restored manor’s courtyard from above results in the character simply entering the ruined manor. Only by using the manor’s front doors at area @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog15afiend.JournalEntryPage.15c1manorentra00]{C1} can a PC come or go from the restored manor to the real world.</p>"
            },
            "The Restored Manor": {
              "name": "修复后的庄园 The Restored Manor",
              "text": "<span class=\"keepme\">复原的庄园</span>\n</h1>\n<p>一旦PC被任命为柳岸镇的管理者，他们就能进入一座以超自然力量复原的总督庄园。镇上唯一还能看见这一变化的其他人，是PC在春季曾协助扶上柳岸镇领袖之位的镇中长老；但即便如此，在PC被任命为管理者之前，那位长老也看不见复原后的庄园，因为直到那时为止，他们在现代时代被任命为总督的任命并不算正式。若PC没有自行展开调查，你可以让长老带着“庄园怎么会重建起来”的疑问来找他们，以此推动PC去调查复原的庄园。</p>\n<p>这一切都是@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}为阻止入侵者回到如今已被腐化、由他统治的柳岸镇思维空间而制定的计划的一部分。他通过限制这两种现实之间的通行，希望能限制他人获得接近他的许可，却没预料到一只络新妇会如此急切地将PC抬举到现代神门政府中合法领导职位的高度。</p>\n<p>尽管<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>仍不过是一枚发光的官职徽记，但在复原的庄园内，它却如同一把隐喻性的钥匙，能够开启更深层的秘密——并最终帮助PC发现：他们曾居住过的柳岸镇思维空间依旧存在，只是已经发生了巨大改变，变得更加骇人可怖。</p>\n<h1 class=\"no-toc split\">\n  <span class=\"keepme\">The Restored Manor</span>\n</h1>\n<p>Once the PCs are made stewards of Willowshore, they can enter a supernaturally restored version of the governor’s manor. The only other person in town capable of seeing this change is the town elder whom the PCs helped install as Willowshore’s leader back in the spring, but even then, that town elder won’t see the restored manor until the PCs are made stewards since, until that point, their appointment to the role of governor wasn’t official in the modern era. You can use the town elder to spur the PCs to investigate the restored manor if they don’t pursue an investigation on their own by having the elder approach them with questions about how the manor got rebuilt.</p>\n<p>All of this is part of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}’s plan to prevent intruders from making their way back into the now-corrupted Willowshore mindscape where he rules. By restricting passage between these realities, he hoped to limit access to himself, not anticipating a jorogumo’s eagerness to elevate the PCs to positions of legal leadership in modern Shenmen’s government.</p>\n<p>While the <em>Fang and Key</em> remains little more than a glowing badge of office, within the restored manor, it functions as a metaphorical key that can unlock further secrets—and eventually help the PCs discover that the Willowshore mindscape they once dwelt in still exists, albeit in a much changed and much more horrific manner.</p>"
            },
            "A Fiend in Two Worlds": {
              "name": "双界恶魔 A Fiend in Two Worlds",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"A Fiend in Two Worlds\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">第13章：</span>\n  <span>横跨两界的恶魔</span>\n</h1>\n<p>如果PC们在事件7：最终季中向行道女问对了问题，他们应当会意识到，谋杀案的凶手是@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{和善保}——或者至少是某个戴着他面孔的生物。此外，幻象中那句“唯有正统的统治者方能携带通往我领域的钥匙！”意在揭示：一旦PC们成为管事（因此正式成为现代柳岸镇“正统统治者”的一员），他们就能返回和善保的庄园，使用<em>獠牙与钥匙</em>直接与他对峙。</p>\n<p>当然，PC们也可能通过其他调查得出和善保就是凶手的结论；但如果他们难以理清他与此事的关联，你可以让任美璃提出这种可能性。如果PC们将行道女赐予的镜中幻象告诉她，任美璃可以作出如下评述：“既然我已经让你们成为正统的统治者，或许是时候再去拜访你们那位前总督的庄园了？”</p>\n<p>只要任何一名如今已是柳岸镇管事的PC，接近那座破败的总督庄园遗迹30尺以内，射程内的那些PC便会目睹一件惊人的景象。对他们而言，并且只要他们仍在庄园墙壁30尺以内，这座建筑看起来就完全恢复如初。屋檐下挂着灯笼，点燃着令人不安的红光；又有更多红光从窗内透出。庄园似乎已被修复，但PC凝视得越久，心中就越发不安。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-nindoru-ambush.webp\" alt=\"Nindoru Ambush\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"A Fiend in Two Worlds\">\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Chapter 13:</span>\n  <span>A Fiend in Two Worlds</span>\n</h1>\n<p>If the PCs asked the right question of the path maiden during Event 7: The Final Season, they should realize that the perpetrator of the murders is @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21hehshanbao0001]{Heh Shan-Bao}—or some creature wearing his face, at the very least. Furthermore, the vision’s reference that “only a rightful ruler shall carry the key to my domain!” is meant to reveal that once the PCs become stewards (and thus are officially among the “rightful rulers” of modern Willowshore), they can return to Heh Shan-Bao’s manor and use the <em>Fang and Key</em> to confront him directly.</p>\n<p>The PCs might have come to the conclusion that Heh Shan-Bao is the murderer through other investigations, of course, but if they’re struggling to figure out his involvement, you can have Ren Mei Li suggest the possibility. If the PCs tell her of the vision in the mirror granted by the path maiden, Ren Mei Li can make the following observation: “Now that I’ve made you rightful rulers, perhaps it’s time to revisit your ex-governor’s manor?”</p>\n<p>As soon as any of the PCs, now stewards of Willowshore, approach within 30 feet of the dilapidated ruins that are the governor’s manor, those PCs in range witness something astounding. To them, and as long as they remain within 30 feet of the manor’s walls, the structure appears fully restored. Lanterns lit by an unsettling red light hang from the eaves, and additional red light glows from within its windows. The manor seems to be restored, but the longer a PC looks, the more unsettled they feel.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Continuing the Campaign": {
          "name": "继续战役 Continuing the Campaign",
          "pages": {
            "Into Kugaptee’s Mind": {
              "name": "进入苦迦菩提的心灵 Into Kugaptee’s Mind",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Into Kugaptee’s Mind\">进入苦迦菩提的心灵</h1>\n<p>PC们必须决定：是将苦迦菩提的坟墓留待后世处理，还是冒险与灵堕魔展开最后一次、正面的对决。若选择后者，他们必须前往天京的森杭寺院——散奎会的所在地，而和善保曾试图拉拢该会。</p>\n<p>在天京，PC们会被卷入当地的权谋之中。尤其是，布拉阔——一类四处游历的圣职之人，以10年为一任，担任信仰的守护者——试图拉拢PC们，好让他们关于各地涌现危险的报告更具分量。天京偏远边境持续遭受古魔试图突破该国诸多神圣封印的攻击，但首都的执政机构“尼恩仁议会”始终轻视这一威胁。</p>\n<p>无论PC们是否援助布拉阔，他们最终都会旅行前往偏远山地中的森杭寺院，并发现那里同样已屈服于古魔的渗透。寺院已被古魔彻底吞噬，仅剩少数仍保有人类面孔的同谋者在外人面前遮掩真相、阻止他人深究。</p>\n<p>若PC们在布拉阔中结交了盟友，他们或许能获得击败古魔的宝贵见解与工具。否则，PC们只能独自穿行于被腐化的废墟之中杀出一条路，并在那里找到散奎会最后的幸存者在死前设法保全的圣遗物。其中一些守卫者是守护魂魄或发条自动机，身上涂抹了神圣药膏以抵御古魔的侵蚀；若他们认为这些闯入者值得相助，便可能帮助PC们。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kugaptee.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kugaptee\" alt=\"Kugaptee\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kugaptee.webp')\" />\n<p>在寺院废墟中，PC们可以取回特缪的圣锣、数瓶发光的天火墨，以及能在对抗苦迦菩提时派上用场的祝圣物品。天火墨可用于在进入灵堕魔那死亡却仍在做梦的心灵之前，用祷告派涂覆自身；也可用来在丝带上描绘圣徽，然后将其绑在额头周围，以保护自己免受苦迦菩提思维空间造物的侵害。特缪的圣锣必须在灵堕魔被击败之时敲响，以确保天庭得知其覆灭，并立刻夺取其魂魄送往来世。</p>\n<p>PC们进入苦迦菩提那被死亡笼罩的思维空间的方法，应当需要他们在《鬼季》中已学到的诸多仪式之上进一步构筑。当他们终于进入灵堕魔内化的思维空间时，映入眼帘的是一座令人痛苦的迷宫。重力与逻辑皆无意义；超现实的物体与扭曲的面孔漂浮于无尽虚空；生者与死者彼此难分。PC们不仅必须在弯曲、荒诞的走廊中摸索前进，还得击败苦迦菩提以意志凭空塑造、并用被吞噬的转世的灵魂碎片赋予其生命的各类怪物。若没有从散奎会获得的工具，他们必将迷失。</p>\n<p>在尽头，PC们将与灵堕魔本人正面相对：一个近乎神祇的存在，因那些剥夺了他太多的英雄而被仇恨吞没。高潮之战应当足以传颂千秋；而在其终局，PC们将可安心确信自己已清除对天夏的一大威胁……否则，便是将自己永远囚禁，沦为魔神的玩物。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Into Kugaptee’s Mind\">Into Kugaptee’s Mind</h1>\n<p>The PCs must decide whether to leave Kugaptee’s grave alone for future generations to handle or risk a final, direct confrontation with the nindoru. Should they choose the latter, they must visit the Senhang Monastery in Tianjing, home of the Fellowship of Sankuei, whom Heh Shan-Bao attempted to enlist.</p>\n<p>In Tianjing, the PCs find themselves embroiled in local intrigues. In particular, the bulakho, a class of wandering holy people serving 10-year terms as defenders of the faith, try to enlist the PCs to add gravity to their reports of dangers arising across the countryside. The remote borders of Tianjing have faced continuous attacks from qlippoth trying to break through the nation’s many holy seals, but the ruling Nyenreng Conclave in the capital has consistently discounted the threat.</p>\n<p>Whether or not the PCs aid the bulakho, they’ll eventually travel to the remote, mountainous Senhang Monastery and discover that it, too, has succumbed to qlippoth infiltration. The monastery has been entirely consumed by qlippoth, with just a few human-faced conspirators discouraging scrutiny from outsiders.</p>\n<p>If the PCs have made allies among the bulakho, they might gain valuable insights and tools in defeating the qlippoth. Otherwise, the PCs are on their own in fighting their way through the corrupted ruins, where they can find relics that the last survivors of the Fellowship of Sankuei managed to safeguard before perishing. Some of these guardians are protective spirits or clockwork automatons smeared with holy unguents to protect them from qlippoth corrosion, and they might assist the PCs if they believe the interlopers to be worthy.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kugaptee.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Kugaptee\" alt=\"Kugaptee\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-kugaptee.webp')\" />\n<p>In the monastery’s ruins, the PCs can retrieve the Sacred Gong of Temyo, bottles of luminous skyfire ink, and blessed items that will aid them against Kugaptee. The skyfire ink can be used to cover themselves with prayers before entering the nindoru’s dead but dreaming mind, as well as to paint holy sigils onto silken bands they can bind about their brows to protect themselves from Kugaptee’s mindscape constructs. The Sacred Gong of Temyo must be sounded when the nindoru is defeated, to ensure that the Heavenly Court hears of his demise and seizes his soul for the afterworld at once.</p>\n<p>The method by which the PCs enter Kugaptee’s death-shrouded mindscape should require them to build upon the many rituals they already learned during <em>Season of Ghosts</em>. When they finally enter the nindoru’s internalized mindscape, the PCs find themselves in a torturous labyrinth. Gravity and logic are meaningless; surreal objects and grotesque faces float in an infinite void; the living and unliving are indistinguishable from one another. Not only must the PCs navigate through the twisting, nonsensical corridors, they must also defeat the various monstrosities that Kugaptee has willed into existence and animated with fragments of devoured souls. Without the tools gained from the Fellowship of Sankuei, they’ll surely be lost.</p>\n<p>At the end of it all, the PCs come face-to-face with the nindoru himself: a near-godlike entity consumed with hatred for the heroes who have denied him so much. The climactic fight should be one for the ages, but at the end of it, the PCs can rest confident that they have eliminated a grave threat to Tian Xia... or else consigned themselves to an eternity imprisoned as a fiend-god’s playthings.</p>"
            },
            "The Ghostly Governor": {
              "name": "幽灵总督 The Ghostly Governor",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Ghostly Governor\">幽灵总督</h1>\n<p>威胁柳岸镇的祸患并不只有苦迦菩提。如今小镇已回归现代时代，附近被诅咒的思泽城的幽灵总督周冥瑕也注意到了此事。她长久以来一直觊觎生长在柳岸腹地的珍贵木材，尤其是山中的杉树；木材大亨孙海在前一年未能将这批货交付到她的木材堆场，很可能会招致她更直接的行动。若果真如此，周冥瑕会在PC们重返生者世界后的第一个夏季的某个时点，尝试对柳岸镇主张权利。</p>\n<p>周冥瑕的阴谋基于龙华旧法中一条鲜为人知的条款：若一位总督任命不合法，或对其封地疏于治理达一年又一日，那么为了保护民众并确保政局稳定，另一位经合法任命的总督便可对该领地提出主张。柳岸镇在消失115年后离奇重返世间，冥瑕宣称这条规定已被违反超过百次，并据此声称自己理应有权统治这座小镇（及其区域资源），将其视为己有。</p>\n<p>由于周冥瑕是个妄想的幽灵，她的主张在现实中是否站得住脚并不重要。她只需要一层薄得不能再薄的借口，就能把不死仆从派往柳岸镇——而一旦她在自己心中确信主张正当，她就会这么做。PC们应当刚好有足够时间在她派出不死军队吞并柳岸镇之前收到警告，而他们的首要任务就是击溃这支军队。</p>\n<p>若PC们击败了这支入侵部队，周冥瑕会花些时间思考下一步动作。此时，本地律师骆熙旸想到了一条或许能永久击败幽灵的计策。难得的是，这位律师对如今已过时的龙华律法的深厚熟稔终于派上用场：她援引了一种可剥夺冥瑕总督之位的法律机制，并相信幽灵的内在逻辑会迫使她屈从该裁定，从而永久解除她，并将思泽从她可怖的控制中解放出来。</p>\n<p>要将冥瑕赶下台，PC们必须从思泽周边的每一位总督那里取得一致的“不信任”表决，然后将他们的签名汇集成一卷正式的谴责卷轴。面对这卷轴，周冥瑕将别无选择，只能羞愧退位——因为龙华律法白纸黑字如此规定。</p>\n<p>然而，取得签名绝非易事。除PC们之外，还有三位总督的印玺与签名必须到手。</p>\n<p><strong>牡丹白夫人</strong>是一只络新妇，自称白芳山为其领地。她虚荣而嗜好奢华，是典型的络新妇，深深沉溺于其宫廷的权谋之中。要赢得她的印玺，很可能需要一笔可观的贿赂，或是在宫廷的阴谋赌博中与牡丹白夫人的对手周旋。</p>\n<p><strong>乌帕罗·卡总督</strong>是乌帕罗家族年迈的家主，统治着雅姆镇。PC们造访此镇时，会发现乌帕罗祖宅已被遗弃。贵族与仆役尽数消失，只留下他们的牙齿。枕头上、厨房台面上等处散落着牙齿，景象诡异至极。</p>\n<p>通过与雅姆村民交谈并研究宅邸中留下的线索，PC们可以确定：这一家人大约在一年前的无月之夜消失，而村民们因惧怕络新妇而不敢将此事上报。要找到并营救乌帕罗家族，PC们必须在一次日全食期间，于满月之下请一位@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.aTYy1WHwAZiuei4h]{月夜}的祭司用神圣经文为他们全身绘身。如此一来，他们便能进入魂魄世界，查明乌帕罗家族究竟遭遇了什么——也就是乌帕罗·卡被一名伪装成凡人顾问的萨基尔所害，在不经意间允许对方将他整个家族拖入西巴尔巴——萨基尔在灵界中的国度。如今，乌帕罗全族皆被囚于折磨之中，PC们必须找到并救出他们，才能获得他的表决。</p>\n<p><strong>伊琪·苏萨鲁夫人</strong>是夜莺谷的统治者，也是PC们必须请求的最后一位总督。伊琪夫人优雅却满怀苦涩，如今已近七十；只有在PC们找回并复活她的儿子欧博鲁的遗骨后，她才会在卷轴上签名——欧博鲁多年前被络新妇掳走。</p>\n<p>为完成此事，PC们必须在阴司察夕的地下宫殿之下的尸骨堆中找出他的遗骸。欧博鲁是在30年前被带走的，他在络新妇手中活过一年以上的可能性不大。若掳走他的人没有夺去那件物品，那么唯有一条小小的银质夜莺项链或许能用来辨认他的骨骸。尽管辨认、取回并复原欧博鲁几乎是不可能的任务，伊琪夫人却寸步不让：若PC们想要她的帮助，就必须满足这项要求。她认为，如此强大的人物理应做得到。</p>\n<p>一旦PC们集齐三份签名，便可进军思泽，击败其不死守卫与死灵结界，并直面周冥瑕总督。在卷轴与龙华律法条文的逼迫下，冥瑕必须承认自己已失去权柄，而她的魂魄终于得以迈向来世。</p>\n<p>自此，思泽获得自由——并将需要一位新的总督。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Ghostly Governor\">The Ghostly Governor</h1>\n<p>Kugaptee wasn’t the only menace threatening Willowshore. Now that the town has returned to the modern era, Chou Mingxia, the ghostly governor of the nearby cursed city of Sze, takes note. She has long coveted the precious lumber that grows in Willowshore’s hinterlands, particularly the sugi trees in its mountains; the lumber lord Mago Kai’s failure to deliver this product to her stockyards the previous year may well result in more direct action. If so, Chou Mingxia attempts to assert a claim against Willowshore at some point during the first summer the PCs spend in the living world.</p>\n<p>Chou Mingxia’s scheme is based on a little-known provision in the old laws of Lung Wa, which state that if a governor is illegitimately appointed or neglects their fiefdom for a year and a day, then in the interest of protecting the citizenry and ensuring stable governance, another duly appointed governor can lay claim to that territory. With the strange return of Willowshore to the world after 115 years, Mingxia claims that the provision has been violated more than a hundred times and takes the stance that she should be entitled to govern the town (and its regional resources) as her own.</p>\n<p>Because Chou Mingxia is a deluded ghost, the actual merits of her claim aren’t important. She needs only the thinnest of pretexts to send her undead minions into Willowshore, which she does as soon as she’s satisfied in her own mind that her claim is legitimate. The PCs should have just enough time to be warned of Mingxia’s plans before she sends an army of undead to annex Willowshore, and their first task is defeating this army.</p>\n<p>If the PCs defeat this invading force, Chou Mingxia takes some time to consider her next actions. At this point, local lawyer Luo Xi Yang hits upon a stratagem that might permanently defeat the ghost. For once, the lawyer’s deep familiarity with the now-outdated laws of Lung Wa pays off: she cites a legal mechanism for stripping Mingxia of her governorship, and she believes that the ghost’s internal logic will force her to bow to this decision, which will permanently dispel her and free Sze from her awful grip.</p>\n<p>To remove Mingxia from power, the PCs must secure a unanimous vote of no confidence from every governor around Sze, then gather their signatures into an official scroll of condemnation. When faced with this scroll, Chou Mingxia will have no choice but to abdicate in shame, for it’s written in the laws of Lung Wa.</p>\n<p>Securing the signatures, however, won’t be easy. In addition to the PCs, there are three governors whose seals and signatures must be obtained.</p>\n<p><strong>Lady Mudan Bai</strong> is a jorogumo who claims White Fragrance Mountain as her domain. Vain and fond of luxury, she’s a typical jorogumo and deeply immersed in the schemes of their court. Winning her seal is likely to require either a significant bribe or playing courtly games of intrigue against Lady Mudan’s rivals.</p>\n<p><strong>Governor Uparo Ka</strong>, the elderly patriarch of House Uparo, rules over the town of Yamu. Upon visiting this town, the PCs find that the ancestral Uparo estate has been abandoned. The nobles and servants have vanished, leaving only their teeth behind. It’s a strange sight to find teeth lying on pillows, fallen on kitchen countertops, and so forth.</p>\n<p>By talking to the villagers of Yamu and studying clues left in the house, the PCs can ascertain that the family vanished on a moonless night approximately one year ago, and that the villagers were too afraid of the jorogumo to bring this occurrence to their attention. To find and rescue the Uparo family, the PCs must have their entire bodies painted with holy sutras by a priest of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.aTYy1WHwAZiuei4h]{Tsukiyo} during a full solar eclipse. Doing so will enable them to pass into the spirit world and find out what happened to the Uparo family—namely, that Uparo Ka fell victim to a sahkil posing as a mortal advisor and inadvertently permitted them to drag his entire household into Xibalba, the sahkils’ realm on the Ethereal Plane. Now, the entire Uparo household is imprisoned in torment, and the PCs must find and rescue them to secure his vote.</p>\n<p><strong>Lady Ichi Susarru</strong>, the ruler of Nightingales’ Hollow, is the final governor to whom the PCs must appeal. Lady Ichi is an elegant but embittered woman, now in her late sixties, who will sign the scroll only if the PCs recover and resurrect the bones of her son, Oboru, who was seized by the jorogumo years before.</p>\n<p>To accomplish this task, the PCs must find his remains amid the charnel heaps beneath the subterranean palaces of Yin-Sichasi. Oboru was taken 30 years ago, and it’s unlikely that he survived more than a year with the jorogumo. Only a small, silver nightingale necklace might identify his bones, if his captors didn’t take it. Although the task of identifying, retrieving, and restoring Oboru is nigh impossible, Lady Ichi is immovable: if the PCs want her help, then they must fulfill this demand. Such powerful people, she reasons, should be able to do it.</p>\n<p>Once the PCs have secured all three signatures, they can march on Sze, defeat its undead guardians and necromantic wards, and confront Governor Chou Mingxia. Faced with the scroll and the dictates of Lung Wa’s laws, Mingxia must concede the loss of her authority, and her spirit finally moves on to the afterlife.</p>\n<p>Thereafter, Sze is free—and will need a new governor.</p>"
            },
            "Shinzo’s Legacy": {
              "name": "神藏的遗产 Shinzo’s Legacy",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Legacy\">神藏的遗产</h1>\n<p>神秘的神藏在他最后一次造访柳岸镇之前，向PC揭示了自身本质的真相——他是@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}麾下的一名强大代理者，被称为死神——随后便前往柳岸镇完成最终的到访。随着小镇重返活人世界，他亲自纠正一切的牵挂也已结束；若PC不再进一步行动，他的故事将不再与他们的人生交汇。</p>\n<p>然而，PC或许已与这位神秘商人建立起友谊的羁绊。如今他们已守护住柳岸镇，并强大到足以开始穿行诸位面，他们也许会去寻找这位老友，看看自己是否能回报他在<em>鬼季</em>中给予他们的恩惠。</p>\n<p>神藏对柳岸镇的兴趣，部分源自数十年前他对法莱斯玛犯下的一桩旧过失——那是在小镇陷入其思维空间之前的事。在被指派给他的招魂者伊克斯的某种“监护”下，神藏被禁止直接干预凡人的生死命运；但被困在柳岸镇的人既非生者亦非死者。被夹在两者之间，神藏希望自己能尽力提供力所能及的协助（而且只能间接出手，以免进一步激怒法莱斯玛），从而重新赢回女神的信任。</p>\n<p>若PC前往骨园寻找他，那么法莱斯玛是否已将他的工作视为偿还过失的代价，以及这过失究竟为何，皆由你决定。也许神藏擅自处决了他认为“不配活着”的凡人，因此越过了自己作为公正死亡裁决者的职责；也许他的贪欲驱使他收受本该死去之人的报酬，让他们得以苟延残喘多活几年；又或许他爱上了一名凡人，并采取手段确保爱人得以长久活着，而不是在死后冒着转变成某种全新存在的风险。</p>\n<p>若你决定神藏尚未还清债务，那么当PC前去寻找他时，他们应当得知：法莱斯玛已派他去执行一项极其危险的任务，以完成赎罪。这项危险差事应与他的过失性质相呼应。若神藏曾是苛刻的处决者，他也许会被指派去监督一个注定毁灭的偏远世界走向终末，而其居民则在徒劳挣扎、试图避免末日；若神藏贪婪成性，他可能被派去骨园某处一座藏匿的宝库守望警戒——那宝库如今正遭邪恶魂魄围攻；若神藏曾爱过并失去一名凡人，他也许会被派往一个世界，在那里他昔日的爱人已转世的灵魂，而他必须遵从命令，只能观察对方的一生却不得施加影响，如此他才能最终见证自己那段爱情的故事本应如何结束。当PC终于追上神藏时，他们应当发现这位死神正深陷矛盾、几近失败。PC选择强化他、保护他或为他提供忠告，将决定他是否还能再次不受限制地为法莱斯玛效力，抑或将作为最终惩罚被转化为纯粹的原初本质。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinzo’s Legacy\">Shinzo’s Legacy</h1>\n<p>The mysterious Shinzo reveals to the PCs the truth of his nature—that he’s a powerful agent of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} known as a shinigami—before he pays his final visit to Willowshore. With the town’s return to the living world, his personal stake in setting things right has concluded, and without further action on the PCs’ behalf, his story will no longer intersect with their own.</p>\n<p>Yet the PCs might have formed a bond of friendship with the mysterious merchant, and now that they’ve secured Willowshore and become powerful enough to begin traveling the planes, they might seek out their old friend to see if they can return the favor he extended to them during <em>Season of Ghosts</em>.</p>\n<p>Part of Shinzo’s interest in Willowshore ties back to an old infraction against Pharasma he made decades before the town became mired in its mindscape. With the psychopomp Yix assigned to him as a minder of sorts, Shinzo was barred from directly intervening in the fate of mortal lives, but those trapped in Willowshore were neither living nor dead. Trapped in between, Shinzo hoped that by providing what aid he could (and only indirectly assisting so he would not further aggravate Pharasma), he could earn back the goddess’s trust.</p>\n<p>If the PCs seek him out in the Boneyard, whether or not Pharasma has accepted his work as payment for his infraction is left to you to decide, as is the nature of the infraction in the first place. Perhaps Shinzo took it upon himself to execute mortals he judged as being unworthy of life, and in so doing stepped out of his role as an impartial arbiter of death. Maybe his greed pushed him to accept payments from those who should’ve died so they could eke out a few more years of life. Or perhaps he fell in love with a mortal and took steps to ensure his lover’s lasting life rather than risk their transformation after death into something new.</p>\n<p>If you decide that Shinzo hasn’t yet paid his debt, then when the PCs seek him out, they should learn Pharasma has sent him on a particularly dangerous mission to complete his penance. This dangerous task should match the nature of his infraction. If Shinzo was a judgmental executioner, he might be assigned the task of overseeing the end of a remote world destined for destruction while its inhabitants scramble to prevent their doom. An avaricious Shinzo could be assigned to stand vigil over a hidden vault somewhere in the Boneyard that has become besieged by evil spirits. If Shinzo loved and lost a mortal, he might be sent to a world where his one-time lover has reincarnated and must comply with orders to observe their life without influencing it, so he can finally witness how his love’s story was supposed to end. When the PCs finally catch up with Shinzo, they should find the shinigami at odds and about to fail. Their decision to bolster, protect, or advise him should mean the difference in whether he’s ever allowed to serve Pharasma without restriction again or if he shall be transformed into raw quintessence as a final punishment.</p>"
            },
            "Continuing the Campaign": {
              "name": "继续战役 Continuing the Campaign",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Continuing the Campaign\">继续战役</h1>\n<p>随着柳岸镇重归现世、和善保的灵魂得以解脱，以及苦迦菩提再次安静地长眠于坟墓之中，PC们的故乡已然安全，但他们的冒险不必就此画上句号。</p>\n<p>本节概述了一些在天夏延伸队伍冒险的选项。这些建议应被视为继续开展一场符合你PC们兴趣与优先事项之战役的起点，而不是一张刻在石头上的线性路线图。</p>\n<p>由于PC们在继续前行之前，理应有充足机会在柳岸镇休息、放松并庆祝胜利，本纲要将何时以及是否要继续他们的征程留给他们自行决定。如果他们对已取得的成果感到满意，故事也可以在此结束。</p>\n<p>不过，倘若他们决定继续前进……</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-corrupted-monastery.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Corrupted Monastery\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Continuing the Campaign\">Continuing the Campaign</h1>\n<p>With Willowshore returned to the living world, Heh Shan-Bao’s soul set free, and Kugaptee once more quiet in his grave, the PCs’ hometown is safe, but their adventures don’t have to come to an end.</p>\n<p>This section outlines some options for extending the party’s adventures in Tian Xia. These suggestions should be taken as a starting point to continue with a campaign that suits your PCs’ interests and priorities, not as a railroad map etched in stone.</p>\n<p>Because the PCs should have ample opportunity to rest, relax, and celebrate their victories in Willowshore before moving on, this outline leaves it up to them to decide when and if they want to continue their quest. If they’re content with the result they’ve achieved, the story can end there.</p>\n<p>However, should they decide to press on...</p>"
            }
          }
        },
