            "Player Character Options": {
              "name": "玩家角色选项 Player Character Options",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Player Character Options\">玩家角色选项</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-lifes-flowing-river.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Life's Flowing River\" alt=\"Life's Flowing River\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>\n    追随善解之道，或研读包含善解秘密的典籍与传说（例如谭杉寺的@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{藏匿图书馆}中所收藏的资料）的PC，将获得这些罕见的玩家角色选项的许可。\n  </p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Player Character Options\">Player Character Options</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-lifes-flowing-river.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Life's Flowing River\" alt=\"Life's Flowing River\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>\n    A PC who follows the ways of Sangpotshi or studies texts and lore containing Sangpotshi secrets (such as those\n    found in the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog09inther.JournalEntryPage.09e11hiddenlib00]{Hidden Library} of the Tan Sugi Monastery) gains access to these uncommon player character\n    options.\n  </p>"
            },
            "Nindorus": {
              "name": "灵堕魔 Nindorus",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindorus\">灵堕魔</h2>\n<p>灵堕魔是转世与善解理念最强大的敌人之一。一段面向GM的灵堕魔讨论从@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog19cycles]{此处}开始，而各个灵堕魔个体则出现在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia]{怪物图鉴}中。PC可以像对任何生物那样通过回忆知识来了解各个灵堕魔，但若想进一步了解这些相对冷门的怪物，可以尝试进行一次@Check[nindoru-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[religion|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]或@Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge]检定来回忆知识。成功会揭示此处给出的常识，而大成功或大失败也会揭示更深层的知识。</p>\n<p><strong>成功—常识：</strong>这些邪魔形态各异，但许多都具有可辨识的特征，例如断裂而细长的四肢、头颅被困在篮子或笼子里或干脆被其替代、伤口渗出血红色蝴蝶的云雾，或使用被邪异力量勉强拼合在一起的破损武器与工具。它们体内的腐化深入骨髓，以至于对失去之物的渴求变得扭曲，最终化作对转世的灵魂的贪食，凌驾于一切之上。</p>\n<p><strong>大成功或大失败—更深层的知识：</strong>这些邪魔能放大自身自私的念头，使其具现为物体，甚至是只为它们效劳的仆从。最强大的个体仅凭思绪便能具现出整个社会或领域。灵堕魔将这些造物视作珍贵的私有物，但一旦它们被摧毁，便立刻将其遗忘。有些学者认为这种行为是在嘲弄转世，并将个体的一生与邪魔工具短暂的存在相提并论。此类推测源于灵堕魔表现得仿佛是善解秘修者的破坏性对立面。它们拥有类似的秘法法术库，并倾向于潜伏在神殿，以及自然与文明的边界——这些也正是善解秘修者常巡守的地点。此类理论的批评者指出，这些地点同样是灵堕魔能找到其偏好猎物之处，并坚持认为驱动灵堕魔的是本能，因而否定它们具有任何有组织目的的说法。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindorus\">Nindorus</h2>\n<p>Nindorus are among the greatest enemies of reincarnation and the Sangpotshi philosophy. A GM-facing discussion on nindorus begins @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog19cycles]{Here}, while individual nindorus appear in the @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia]{Bestiary}. A PC can learn more about individual nindorus by Recalling Knowledge as with any creature, but one who wishes to know more about these relatively obscure monsters can attempt a @Check[nindoru-lore|dc:15|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[religion|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] or @Check[occultism|dc:20|traits:concentrate,secret,skill,action:recall-knowledge|name:Recall Knowledge] check to Recall Knowledge. A success reveals the common knowledge given here, and a critical success also revels the deeper knowledge as well.</p>\n<p><strong>Success—Common Knowledge:</strong> These fiends take many forms, but many share identifiable traits, such as long broken limbs, heads trapped or replaced by baskets or cages, wounds that seep clouds of blood-red butterflies, or the utilization of broken weapons and tools held together by sinister forces. Corruption runs so deep within them that their yearning for what they’ve lost becomes twisted, manifesting as an appetite for reincarnated souls above all others.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Success—Deeper Knowledge:</strong> These fiends can amplify their selfish thoughts to manifest objects or even minions that serve them alone. The most powerful can manifest entire societies or realms from only their thoughts. Nindorus treat these creations as prized possessions but forget about them as soon as they’re destroyed. Some scholars see this behavior as a mockery of reincarnation, drawing a parallel between an individual’s life and the ephemeral existence of a fiend’s tool. Such speculation comes from nindorus behaving as the destructive opposites of Sangpotshi mystics. They have access to similar repertoires of occult spells, and they tend to stalk temples and boundaries between nature and civilization—the same places Sangpotshi mystics often patrol. Critics of such theories point out that those locations are also where nindorus can find their preferred prey and insist that base instincts drive nindorus, dismissing the notion that they have any organized purpose.</p>"
            },
            "Cycles of Life": {
              "name": "生命轮回 Cycles of Life",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Cycles of Life\">生命轮回</h2>\n<p>善解以长远的眼光看待生命。其典籍描述了映照生命、死亡与重生的循环——文明的兴衰、灾害之后自然的复苏，以及人们在面对变化时会回归的熟悉行为模式。</p>\n<p>有些循环具有建设性，应当被保留，但另一些则延续着苦难，而这未必是个体所能打破的。即便是负面的循环，也能帮助转世的灵魂成长，迈向最终的开悟；例如，持续的经济困境所带来的种种艰难便是其中之一。尽管如此，追随善解的人一致认为，毫无疑问，贫困会造成巨大的苦难，应该加以对抗。与此同时，命运也决定了，不同的行为与信念会导向不平等的结果。善解的信徒会尽其所能对抗不平等，同时也接受必须与其存在的现实共处。他们鼓励那些哀叹自身处境的人审视自己能从经历中学到什么。这种内省能够引向开悟与改变。如果人人彼此善待，或许终有一日能消除贫困。善解的准则帮助信徒培育正向循环，并逃脱或对抗负向循环。</p>\n<p>信徒也谨慎地守护自然世界与城市化世界之间的保持平衡。他们将一切活着的生物视为行于同一路径，并以自己也希望在回合中得到的尊严来对待它们。帮助他人是一项使命，但他们也会谨慎地以能让他人学习与成长、而非依赖外来协助的方式去伸出援手。他们提倡可持续的生活方式，只取所需，并以将伤害术降到最低的方法行事。这些选择旨在保留既有的循环，使未来世代能获得与过去世代相同的机会。这种想要守护并扶持他人的愿望意味着，暴力是最后手段，但它并非禁忌。破坏性的力量试图腐化轮回的循环，而善解的信徒会动用一切可用手段来守卫生命之河。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Cycles of Life\">Cycles of Life</h2>\n<p>Sangpotshi takes a long view on life. Its texts describe cycles that mirror life, death, and rebirth—the rise and fall of civilizations, the renewal of nature after a disaster, and the familiar behaviors people fall back on when confronted with change.</p>\n<p>Some cycles are constructive and should be preserved, but others perpetuate suffering that might not be within the power of individuals to break. Even negative cycles can help souls grow toward eventual enlightenment, with the difficulties that arise from constant economic peril being one such example. Nonetheless, those who follow Sangpotshi agree that, without a doubt, poverty causes immense suffering and should be counteracted. At the same time, fate dictates that different behaviors and beliefs lead to unequal outcomes. Followers of Sangpotshi do what lies within their power to combat inequality while accepting that one must live with the reality of its existence. They encourage those who lament their situation to examine what they can learn from their experiences. This introspection can lead to enlightenment and change. If everyone treats each other well, they might eventually eliminate poverty. Sangpotshi’s guidelines help followers nurture positive cycles and escape or counter negative ones.</p>\n<p>Followers are also careful to protect the balance between the natural and urbanized worlds. They see all living creatures as on the same path and treat them with the dignity they would want to receive in turn. Helping others is a duty, though they’re careful to assist in ways that allow others to learn and grow rather than become reliant on external aid. They promote sustainable methods of living, taking only what one needs and in ways that minimize harm. Such choices aim to preserve existing cycles so that future generations have access to the same opportunities that past ones did. This desire to preserve and uplift means that violence is a last resort, but it isn’t anathema. Destructive forces seek to corrupt the cycle of reincarnation, and Sangpotshi followers defend the River of Life through all means at their disposal.</p>"
            },
            "Past Life Curiosity": {
              "name": "好奇前世 Past Life Curiosity",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Past Life Curiosity\">好奇前世</h3>\n<p>那么，为什么会有人想了解自己的过去呢？也许有人觉得自己处在不公的境地，已经再也无法忍受。举个例子，一个在专横老板手下做工的工人。这样的人可能会去找一位秘术师，询问老板是否因为他们在前世做过什么而压迫他们。答案可能是否定的；若是如此，工人也许会觉得自己可以自由离开现状，去寻找更好的工作环境。</p>\n<p>如果答案是肯定的，工人可能会因为知道自己的苦难有其意义而感到宽慰，并留下来以了结自己的灵性债务。如果他们离开，未来可能又会再次在这位老板手下工作，或者更糟，在来世与对方产生亲缘关系，那时就没那么容易逃脱自己的债务了。也许秘术师看见他们的麻烦只会再持续一年；若他们耐心等下去，他们与老板的关系将会改善，或是老板会离开。秘术师也可能看见另一种偿还债务的方式，比如告诉他们老板为何如此愤怒，从而让此人能够去直面老板，直接解决问题。当秘术师担心无知会导致不良结果时，他们就会分享某人前世的细节。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Past Life Curiosity\">Past Life Curiosity</h3>\n<p>So why would anyone ever want to know about their past? Perhaps someone feels they’re in an unjust situation and can’t tolerate it any longer. Take the example of a worker under an oppressive boss. Such a person might seek out a mystic and ask if the boss oppresses them because of something they did in a past life. The answer might be no, in which case the worker might feel free to leave their situation to find a better working environment.</p>\n<p>If the answer is yes, the worker might find comfort in knowing their suffering has a purpose and stay so that they can end their spiritual debt. If they leave, they could find themselves working under the boss again in the future or, worse, become related to them in a future life where they can’t escape their debt so easily. Perhaps the mystic sees that their troubles will only last another year, and if they wait it out, their relationship with their boss will improve or the boss will leave. The mystic might also see another way to resolve the debt, such as telling them why their boss is so angry, enabling the person to confront their boss and resolve their problems directly. Mystics share details about someone’s past life when they fear that ignorance will result in a bad outcome.</p>"
            },
            "Spiritual Connections": {
              "name": "精魂结缘 Spiritual Connections",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Spiritual Connections\">精魂结缘</h2>\n<p>天夏的人们有时会在生活中遭遇困难时去寻求一位善解的秘术师，以了解这些困难是否源于精魂结缘。在天夏的大多数文化中，这类关系中的某些类型相当常见，几乎是常识。人们往往会在不同的前世今生中反复遭遇那些曾经影响过自己的人。</p>\n<p>至亲的羁绊源于那些在前世建立了强烈连结的人，尽管这种连结的性质各不相同。他们可能曾是家人、挚友或同袍，例如一同耕作公田的农民，或在同一支战团中并肩作战的士兵。这些关系可能带来吉缘，也可能充满对立。两个在前世彼此照拂的朋友，如今可能会以配偶或亲子之名形成一段吉缘。然而，由于精魂之债，同样的关系也可能转为对立。也许某个骗子骗走了他人的毕生积蓄，导致对方早逝——这段关系可能在来世显现为一位配偶或子女，并造成巨大的财务损失。这种损失可能是蓄意的，例如偷窃；也可能是间接的，例如因健康危机而产生的开销。</p>\n<p>秘术师会谨慎地告诫人们，不要把精魂关系当作合理化怨恨的借口，也不要擅自揣测究竟存在哪些精魂纽带。回到前述的对立例子：会偷窃的配偶可能是在潜意识里为前世的失窃复仇；也可能是在原本并不存在仇怨之处，开启一段新的愤怒与怨怼循环。</p>\n<p>友谊可能是一段新关系的开端，也可能是较弱精魂纽带的再现。短暂的友谊可能源于前世的一次单独精魂牵系；当这份牵系得到化解后，转世的灵魂便会各自分离。也许在前世，有两位陌生人曾出手协助某人。他们在来世会在自己曾帮助过的那位灵魂的指导下成为同窗；而当他们学会了实现梦想职业所需的技能后，便渐渐疏远。</p>\n<p>良善的命运能改善一个人出生时的处境。前世的一位大英雄，可能因赢得许多转世的灵魂的善意，而在来世出生于富裕家庭。然而，过去并不决定未来；善解告诫你应当依据人们的行为而非地位去尊重他人。一位富裕的继承人也可能在新一世变得残酷而贪婪，因为他缺乏对他人的同理心。</p>\n<p>善解的追随者相信，有些降生于恶劣处境是命运使然，但他们同样警告：做出这种假设很危险。有些强大的秘术师会选择转生术到艰难的环境中，因为这可能使他们的力量更快显现。另一些即将成为善者的转世的灵魂会立下自我牺牲的誓言，选择承受厄运，以避免其坠落在无辜的转世的灵魂身上。转世的灵魂被分配到新躯体的方式在许多方面都不可知。一根坠落的树枝无法选择自己会漂到哪里搁浅，正如生命之河中的一个灵魂无法选择自己会在何处重返生命。命运能够提高一个人出生于某些处境或在一生中遭遇特定事件的概率，但它从不保证这些事情必然发生。</p>\n<p>在善解与命运之道中，人们如何回应自己当下的处境是最重要的性相。以谦卑之心接受好运，以积极的态度面对困境。善解教导人们尽可能行善，保持良好判断，并遵循一条准则：以你希望他人对待你的方式去对待他人。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Spiritual Connections\">Spiritual Connections</h2>\n<p>People in Tian Xia sometimes seek out a Sangpotshi mystic when they encounter difficulties in their life to learn if those difficulties are the result of a spiritual connection. Some types of these relationships occur frequently and are common knowledge in most Tian Xia cultures. Individuals tend to encounter the same people who impacted them in prior incarnations.</p>\n<p>Kindred ties arise from those who developed strong connections in previous lives, though the nature of those connections varies. They might have been family, close friends, or compatriots, such as farmers working communal land together or soldiers fighting in the same war band. These relationships can be propitious or antagonistic. Two friends who took care of each other throughout a previous life could now have a propitious relationship as spouses or parent and child. Those same relationships can also be antagonistic due to a spiritual debt. Perhaps a con artist stole someone’s life savings, causing their premature death—that relationship can manifest in the next life as a spouse or child who causes great financial loss. Such a loss can be deliberate, such as through theft, or indirect, such as due to a health crisis.</p>\n<p>Mystics are careful to warn people not to use spiritual relationships as an excuse to justify resentment, nor to make assumptions about what spiritual bonds exist. Going back to the previous antagonistic example, a spouse who steals could be subconsciously taking revenge for a theft in a previous life, or they could be starting a new cycle of anger and resentment where none existed before.</p>\n<p>Friendships can be the start of new relationships or the recurrence of weaker spiritual bonds. Ephemeral friendships might be due to a single spiritual bond from a previous life that results in the souls parting once resolved. Perhaps two strangers came to someone’s aid in a previous life. They become study partners in their next life under the tutelage of the soul they helped, and when they learn the skills they need to attain their dream jobs, they then drift apart.</p>\n<p>A good destiny can improve one’s position at birth. A great hero from a previous life might be born into a wealthy family in the next because of the good will they incurred from many other souls. The past doesn’t dictate the future, though, and Sangpotshi warns that you should respect people for their behavior, not their status. A wealthy heir could become cruel and greedy in their new life because they lack empathy for others.</p>\n<p>Sangpotshi followers believe some births into bad situations result from fate, but they again warn that it’s dangerous to make such assumptions. Some powerful mystics choose to reincarnate into difficult circumstances because it can cause their powers to manifest more quickly. Other souls that are close to becoming Sangpots take oaths of self-sacrifice, choosing to suffer ill fortune to prevent it from falling on innocent souls. The assignment of souls into new bodies is unknowable in many respects. A fallen branch can choose where it washes ashore no more than a soul in the River of Life chooses where it reenters life. Fate can improve one’s odds of being born into certain circumstances or encountering specific events in one’s life, but it never guarantees such occurrences.</p>\n<p>How one responds to their current situation is the most important aspect of Sangpotshi and fate. Receive good fortune with humility and face trouble with a positive attitude. Sangpotshi tells people to do good whenever possible, exercise good judgment, and live by the rule of treating others as you would want others to treat you.</p>"
            },
            "The Nature of Reincarnation": {
              "name": "轮回的本质 The Nature of Reincarnation",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Nature of Reincarnation\">轮回的本质</h1>\n<p>关于哪些因素决定转世之魂的境遇，众说纷纭；而最流行的思想流派被称为各条“道”，每一条都有其独特的修行方式。<strong>天道</strong>源自伏陀罗哲学家波阇潘迪尼的教诲；他相信神祇会评判凡人如何度过一生，并据此安排他们来世的位阶。</p>\n<p><strong>地道</strong>的拥护者相信命运是一种自然现象。动作在一生之内会产生可观察的结果，因此合乎逻辑的结论是：命运在多次生命之间同样遵循这些规则。人们彼此如何对待，才是最重要的。</p>\n<p><strong>人道</strong>是最后一种主要修行。人道并不专注于哲学上的追求，而是鼓励以亲身探索的方式去体悟存在的本质。此道的追随者以同名的善者为榜样——这些开悟之人对宇宙获得了极其深刻的理解，以至于与宇宙融为一体。</p>\n<p>也有人认为，轮回的真正本质介于这些信念之间。灵魂的命运与宿命并不是一种可量化、可测量的力量，正如你无法衡量存在之中善意或苦难的总量。相反，它最适合被想象成一册册由个人持有的账簿，任何人都可以在其上记上一笔。某位神祇的忠诚信徒可能会从神圣代表那里得到一条正向记录；受害者则可能在施害者的账簿上记下一笔债；而一名因自身行为而深感愧疚的罪犯，即使社会与受害者早已原谅他，他也可能在很久之后仍为自己留下记过。同样，是否要对这些记录采取行动，也取决于登记之人；因为并不存在一个客观的外来者来强制执行这些裁决。这不过是人们相信彼此与自己“欠”了什么的总和，以及他们付诸行动的动机强弱。</p>\n<p>正是这种信念，或许构成了让相信轮回之人能够选择再度降生的力量。纵观历史，最伟大的英雄与恶棍，都是那些完成了他们相信自己必须去做之事的人。从这个意义上说，命运是可塑的，而每一条道都能找到大量证据来印证其教义。每条道中最强大的祭司与秘术师都宣称自己能够看见一个人在所有生世中与他人累积的宿缘联系。他们循着这些丝线，理解人与人之间行为模式与清算的循环。他们的知识使他们能够辨识人们最深层的欲望，裁决灵魂之间的争端，并要求立即进行命运的清算。</p>\n<p>善解的另一项关键教义，是遵守中道。善解的最终目标，是成为理想的自我，并超越凡俗之苦。善解的秘术师教导：苦难源于欲望。他们并不评判某个具体欲望是善是恶，但他们指出，欲望会制造对凡世的执著，使灵魂停滞并受苦。例如，一个人若对某个目标变得痴迷，当无法达成时便会不快乐；他可能为了追逐目标而损害生活的其他面向。反之，若一个人实现了某个欲望，他又可能害怕失去已得之物，将心力放在维持现状，而不是满足于自己所拥有的东西。</p>\n<p>摒弃欲望并不意味着放弃人生目标或社会责任。善解不赞同那些为了避免执著而抛弃义务的人，认为那同样是一种极端；不过，若不伤害他人，追随者有时也会选择暂时搁置自身处境。相反，这一哲学提供神导术，教人如何在自身处境中好好生活，并了结自己的灵性账目。这份神导术也包括：不要过度沉溺于前世。大多数善解的追随者认为，多数人（轮回者除外）不记得前世是有原因的。他们明白，重生给予自己一次机会去清空旧账，摆脱那些已经走到尽头或变得不健康的执著。善解的秘术师珍视自己获得前世信息的能力，但也谨慎地以中道运用；只有在他们认为这些信息与某个正在困扰当事人的现实问题相关时，才会稍稍窥探过去。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"The Nature of Reincarnation\">The Nature of Reincarnation</h1>\n<p>Theories abound about what factors determine the lot of a reincarnated soul, and the most popular schools of thought exist as “paths,” each with unique practices. The <strong>Heavens Path</strong> originates from the teachings of Vudrani philosopher Bhoja Pandiri, who believed gods judge how mortals lived and assign their station in their next life.</p>\n<p>Adherents of the <strong>Earthly Path</strong> believe fate is a natural occurrence. Actions have observable consequences within a single lifetime, so the logical conclusion is fate follows the same rules across multiple lifetimes. How people treat each other is what matters most.</p>\n<p>The <strong>Traveler’s Path</strong> is the final major practice. Rather than focus on philosophical pursuits, the Traveler’s Path encourages the physical act of exploring the nature of existence. Adherents of this path find role models in the eponymous Sangpots, enlightened individuals who gained such a profound understanding of the universe that they merged with it.</p>\n<p>Some believe that the true nature of reincarnation lies somewhere between these various beliefs. A soul’s fate and destiny isn’t a quantifiable force that can be measured any more than one can measure the total amount of good will or suffering in existence. It can instead be best imagined as individual ledgers in which anyone can write an entry. The faithful servant of a deity might receive a positive entry from a divine representative, while a victim might place a debt on the ledger of their aggressor, and a criminal who feels intense guilt for their actions might leave a demerit on themselves long after society and their victims have forgiven them. It’s also up to those submitting entries to act on them, for there’s no objective outsider enforcing these judgments. It’s simply the sum of what people believe they owe each other and themselves, and the extent of their motivation to act on those beliefs.</p>\n<p>Such convictions might be the force that allows those who believe in reincarnation to choose to be born anew. The greatest heroes and villains throughout history are those who accomplished what they believed they must do. In that sense, fate is malleable, and each path can find substantial evidence to validate its teachings. The most powerful priests and mystics of every path claim to be able to see the fated connections an individual has accumulated with others all of their lifetimes. They follow those threads to understand patterns of behavior and cycles of reckoning between people. Their knowledge enables them to identify people’s deepest desires, arbitrate disputes between souls, and demand immediate fateful reckoning.</p>\n<p>Another key tenet of Sangpotshi is adherence to moderation. The end goal of Sangpotshi is to become an ideal version of oneself and to transcend mortal suffering. Sangpotshi mystics teach that suffering comes from desire. They don’t pass judgment on whether individual desires are good or bad, but they point out that desires create attachments to the mortal realm that cause souls to stagnate and suffer. Someone who becomes obsessed with a goal, for example, becomes unhappy if they can’t accomplish it. They might pursue their goal to the detriment of other aspects of their life. Alternatively, someone who achieves a desire might fear losing what they’ve acquired, focusing on preserving the status quo instead of being satisfied with what they possess.</p>\n<p>Spurning desire doesn’t mean abandoning life goals or societal responsibilities. Sangpotshi frowns on those who abandon their obligations to avoid attachments, viewing that as its own extreme, though followers sometimes choose to set aside their circumstances if doing so doesn’t harm others. The philosophy instead provides guidance on how to live well within one’s circumstances and settle one’s spiritual accounts. That guidance includes not diving too deeply into past lives. Most followers of Sangpotshi believe there’s a reason most people—samsarans excluded—don’t remember their previous lives. They understand that rebirth gives them an opportunity to wipe their slate clean and shed attachments that have run their course or become unhealthy. Sangpotshi mystics prize their ability to access information about prior incarnations but are careful to use it in moderation. They only peek into the past when they believe it’s relevant to a problem plaguing someone in the present.</p>"
            },
            "Sangpotshi": {
              "name": "善解 Sangpotshi",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Sangpotshi\">\n  <span>善解</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sangpotshi-follower.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Sangpotshi Follower\" alt=\"Sangpotshi Follower\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sangpotshi-follower.webp')\" />\n<p>对轮回循环的信仰在天夏广泛流传，而 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.WfqLY2Fm1LGCcG5X]{善解}则是关于轮回如何运作及其目的为何的组织性哲学。大多数追随者并不将善解视为与对既有神祇的崇拜相竞争的信条，而是认为它能补充这些信仰。该哲学关注的是如何把凡人的一生过好。有些人对这种修行持怀疑态度，认为它是在试图“作弊”，规避来世的常规秩序，但天夏的神祇及其信徒则持不同观点。毕竟，轮回与灵魂可能面对的任何裁决一样合理。善解教导追随者，轮回是一场对信念的考验；因为每一世既提供了无数偏离自身戒律的契机，也提供了同样多自我提升的机会。</p>\n<p>善解也被称为生命之河。这个名称并非隐喻——它描述的是与灵魂之河相对应的另一条河流；灵魂之河将逝者的转世的灵魂载往 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}的骨园。相信轮回的人教导说，这些转世的灵魂会改为进入生命之河；河流的水势会将转世的灵魂一次又一次送回凡世，次数取决于其命定需继续重生循环多久。所有人生中所作所为的累积效果，会决定一个灵魂下一世的境遇。天夏的神祇、他们的代表以及志同道合的盟友会保护生命之河，抵御那些会在灵魂过境时掠食的破坏力量，但他们并不总能成功。超自然操弄的影响或不死性的污染，可能将一个灵魂撕离轮回循环，使其转化为灵堕魔——一种具破坏性的邪魔类别，试图扰乱轮回循环，并通过将灵魂从通往觉悟的道路上引向腐化与残忍，来摧毁凡人生命的长久功业。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-the-cycle-of-life.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Cycle of Life\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Sangpotshi\">\n  <span>Sangpotshi</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sangpotshi-follower.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Sangpotshi Follower\" alt=\"Sangpotshi Follower\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sangpotshi-follower.webp')\" />\n<p>Faith in the cycle of reincarnation is widespread across Tian Xia, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.WfqLY2Fm1LGCcG5X]{Sangpotshi} is the organizing philosophy around how reincarnation works and what purpose it serves. Most followers don’t see Sangpotshi as a belief that competes with worship of existing gods, but rather complements these faiths. The philosophy focuses on how to live a mortal life well. Some are skeptical about the practice, seeing it as an attempt to “cheat” the regular order of the afterlife, but Tian deities and their followers hold a different perspective. After all, reincarnation is as valid a judgment as any that a soul might face. Sangpotshi teaches followers that reincarnation is an exercise in conviction, for each life presents as many occasions to stray from one’s tenets as it does opportunities to improve oneself.</p>\n<p>Sangpotshi is also known as the River of Life. The name isn’t metaphorical—it describes a parallel to the River of Souls, which carries the souls of the dead to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}’s Boneyard. Those who believe in reincarnation teach that these souls enter the River of Life instead, whose currents carry souls back to mortal life as many times as they’re destined to continue the cycle of rebirth. The cumulative effects of lived actions across all lives determine the circumstances of a soul’s next life. Tian deities, their representatives, and like-minded allies protect the River of Life from disruptive forces who would prey on souls in transit, but they don’t always succeed. The influence of supernatural manipulation or the taint of undeath can tear a soul from the cycle of reincarnation, transforming it into a nindoru—a destructive category of fiend that seeks to disrupt the cycle of reincarnation and to destroy the lasting works of mortal life by diverting a soul from its path to enlightenment into corruption and cruelty.</p>"
            }
          }
        },
        "Cycles of Destruction": {
          "name": "毁灭的轮回 Cycles of Destruction",
          "pages": {
            "Nindorus in the World": {
              "name": "世界中的灵堕魔 Nindorus in the World",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindorus in the World\">世界中的灵堕魔</h1>\n<p>与其他邪魔相比，灵堕魔在格拉利昂的踪迹相对罕见且分布有限。它们起源于天夏，这在很大程度上使其影响力至今仍主要局限于这片大陆。以下地点是值得注意的灵堕魔行动区域。</p>\n<p><strong>楚叶：</strong>这个由鬼族统治的王国中盛行的残酷作风对灵堕魔颇具吸引力；楚叶境内栖居着数个大型灵煞，它们与恒将军的代理人合作，以镇压任何叛乱的迹象。这些合作关系很可能源于双方共同崇拜 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{文业王}，以及鬼族作为被腐化的神灵而诞生的起源，与灵堕魔源自被腐化的凡人转世的灵魂这两者之间的相似性。</p>\n<p><strong>神门：</strong>神门阴郁荒凉的边境是灵堕魔理想的狩猎场，它们沉溺于国民的苦难。由于神门主要由分散各地的村落构成，而失踪人口又不幸屡见不鲜，这些邪魔常在一个社区与另一个社区之间迅速穿梭，缓慢地逐个猎杀当地居民。苦迦菩提在此统御着众多追随者，所有人都在等待主人挣脱束缚的那一天。</p>\n<p><strong>天景：</strong>那些喜欢吞食受神祇触及之灵魂的灵堕魔会在天景安家，它们以异界入侵与匪徒夺权为乐——这些事件让这片土地因创伤而格外“甜美”。天景神子之森中枯萎腐败的区域是许多灵煞的藏身处，而研究者推测，当地对西格克的崇敬或许与邪魔的腐化有关。</p>\n<p><strong>兹哈：</strong>出于对轮回者由来已久的憎恨，若有可能，灵堕魔会成千上万地涌入兹哈。多山的地形与善德勇的防御在很大程度上遏止了实体入侵，但崇拜穆萨加尼的灵堕魔常试图复刻那位苦行者的入侵，并在寻找通往开悟群峰腹地的地下通道。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindorus in the World\">Nindorus in the World</h1>\n<p>Compared to other fiends, nindorus are relatively rare and limited in their presence in Golarion. Their origins in Tian Xia have largely kept their influence to this continent so far. The following locations are notable sites of nindoru activity.</p>\n<p><strong>Chu Ye:</strong> The cruelty in this oni-ruled kingdom appeals to nindorus, and Chu Ye is home to several large ninsats that work with the agents of Shogun Tsuneni to quell any signs of rebellion. These partnerships are likely fostered due to a shared worship of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{Fumeiyoshi}, as well as similarities between an oni’s genesis as a corrupted kami and a nindoru’s source being from a corrupted mortal soul.</p>\n<p><strong>Shenmen:</strong> The dreary reaches of Shenmen are ideal hunting grounds for nindorus, who relish the misery of the nation’s citizenry. Since Shenmen is largely composed of spread-out villages where missing persons are unfortunately commonplace, these fiends often dart from community to community, slowly picking off locals. Kugaptee commands many followers here, all waiting for the day that their master breaks free.</p>\n<p><strong>Tianjing:</strong> Nindorus who enjoy feeding on god-touched souls make their home in Tianjing, relishing the extraplanar incursions and bandit takeovers that have made the land sweet with trauma. The blighted portions of Tianjing’s Kaimuko Wood are a hideout for many ninsats, and researchers speculate that the local veneration of Sigek may be tied to fiendish corruption.</p>\n<p><strong>Zi Ha:</strong> Fueled by their long-standing hatred of samsarans, nindorus would rush into Zi Ha by the thousands if they could. The mountainous terrain and Sangpo-Jong’s defenses largely keep physical incursions at bay, but nindorus who worship Musagani frequently attempt to replicate the Ascetic’s invasion and are searching for underground routes into the very heart of the Enlightened Peaks.</p>"
            },
            "Sigek": {
              "name": "西格克 Sigek",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Sigek\">西格克</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-statue-of-sigek.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Statue of Sigek\" alt=\"a statue of a nindoru ascetic\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-statue-of-sigek.webp')\" />\n<p>与西格克作为灵堕魔苦行者归来相关的证据，直到7214 ic才被最近发现：一群探路者击败了三只以轮回者语社群为目标的灵煞，地点在天景。每只灵煞都有一处巢穴，巢穴里摆放着数十具尸体，围绕着蓝色雕像；这些雕像看上去像是长着多张大口、却具有人类面部特征的灵堕魔。当探路者抵达时，这些灵堕魔正处于狂乱之中，并一边反复吟诵“西格克将再次诞生！”，一边战斗至死。所有雕像都被运往过峡的灯笼会馆，并一直被严密上锁保管至今。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>关注领域</strong> 背叛、寄生虫、肉体痛苦、怪异变形</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>典范</strong> 背叛你的上级与盟友、使他人承受致残痛苦、寄宿寄生虫</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>禁忌</strong> 治愈他人的寄生虫感染、维持一段联盟超过一年、让非灵堕魔生物复生</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣属性</strong> 体质或智力</p>\n<h3>信徒增益</h3>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>牧师法术</strong> 1环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.gfPjmG6Fe6D3MFjl]{Pest Form}，3环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.XI6Lzd2B5pernkPd]{Insect Form}，5环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.d9sBzPOXX3KT8uTu]{Grisly Growths}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神授涌能</strong> 伤害术</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣圣化</strong> 必须选择不洁</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣技能</strong> 医学</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>领域</strong> 变化、痛苦、隐秘、诡计</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>偏好武器</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.tH5GirEy7YB3ZgCk]{Rapier}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>宗教圣徽</strong> 滴血的尖刺蛹壳</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Sigek\">Sigek</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-statue-of-sigek.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Statue of Sigek\" alt=\"a statue of a nindoru ascetic\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-statue-of-sigek.webp')\" />\n<p>Evidence related to Sigek’s return as a nindoru Ascetic was only recently discovered in 7214 ic, when a group of Pathfinders defeated three ninsats targeting samsaran communities in Tianjing. Each ninsat had a lair where dozens of corpses were placed around blue statues that resembled a multi-mawed nindoru with human facial features. The nindorus were in a frenzy when the Pathfinders arrived and fought to the death while repeatedly chanting the phrase “Sigek will be born again!” All the statues were transported to Goka’s Lantern Lodge, where they remain under lock and key to this day.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong> betrayals, parasites, physical agony, strange transformations</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Edicts</strong> betray your superiors and allies, cause crippling pain in others, host parasites</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Anathema</strong> cure parasitic infections in others, maintain an alliance longer than a year, restore a non-nindoru creature to life</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Attribute</strong> Constitution or Intelligence</p>\n<h3>Devotee Benefits</h3>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Cleric Spells</strong> 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.gfPjmG6Fe6D3MFjl]{Pest Form}, 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.XI6Lzd2B5pernkPd]{Insect Form}, 5th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.d9sBzPOXX3KT8uTu]{Grisly Growths}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Font</strong> harm</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Sanctification</strong> must choose unholy</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Skill</strong> Medicine</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Domains</strong> change, pain, secrecy, trickery</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Favored Weapon</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.tH5GirEy7YB3ZgCk]{Rapier}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong> blood-dripping spiky chrysalis</p>"
            },
            "Musagani": {
              "name": "穆萨加尼 Musagani",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Musagani\">穆萨加尼</h2>\n<p>巨大的穆萨加尼是所有已知灵堕魔中体型最大的一位，它率领一支灵煞于6778 ic渗透进入紫哈国。在那段时期，穆萨加尼夺走了数百名受害者的性命，直到最终在骨城与朱尼珀的巨人之手下迎来终结。在这次放逐术之前，穆萨加尼吸收了66名巨人的转世的灵魂，膨胀到庞然巨物的规模，而在此后数百年间再没有任何灵堕魔能复现这一点。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>关注领域</strong> 混乱、灵魂吞噬、巨型怪物、战争</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>典范</strong> 破坏组织、杀死比你更大的生物、阻止复活或转生</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>禁忌</strong> 向轮回者语提供援助、让非灵堕魔生物起死回生、自愿缩小你的体型</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣属性</strong> 力量或魅力</p>\n<h3>信徒增益</h3>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>牧师法术</strong> 1环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.i35dpZFI7jZcRoBo]{幻象伪装}，2环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.wzctak6BxOW8xvFV]{Enlarge}，4环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.LiGbewa9pO0yjbsY]{Confusion}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神授源泉</strong> 伤害术</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣祝圣</strong> 必须选择不洁</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣技能</strong> 威吓</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>领域</strong> 迷乱、力量、暴政、热忱</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>偏好武器</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.NufKswitJjxDCX8f]{Naginata}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>宗教圣徽</strong> 紧握着一颗碎裂头骨的拳头</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Musagani\">Musagani</h2>\n<p>Immense Musagani, the largest of all known nindorus, led a ninsat that infiltrated the nation of Zi Ha in 6778 ic, during which Musagani claimed hundreds of victims before finally meeting an end at the hands of the City of Bone and Juniper’s giants. Prior to this banishment, Musagani absorbed the souls of 66 giants, swelling to behemoth proportions that no nindoru has replicated in the centuries since.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong> chaos, consumption of souls, immense monsters, warfare</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Edicts</strong> disrupt organizations, slay creatures larger than you, prevent resurrection or reincarnation</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Anathema</strong> provide aid to a samsaran, restore a non-nindoru creature to life, willingly reduce your size</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Attribute</strong> Strength or Charisma</p>\n<h3>Devotee Benefits</h3>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Cleric Spells</strong> 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.i35dpZFI7jZcRoBo]{Illusory Disguise}, 2nd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.wzctak6BxOW8xvFV]{Enlarge}, 4th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.LiGbewa9pO0yjbsY]{Confusion}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Font</strong> harm</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Sanctification</strong> must choose unholy</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Skill</strong> Intimidation</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Domains</strong> disorientation, might, tyranny, zeal</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Favored Weapon</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.NufKswitJjxDCX8f]{Naginata}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong> fist clenching a shattering skull</p>"
            },
            "Kugaptee": {
              "name": "苦迦菩提 Kugaptee",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Kugaptee\">苦迦菩提</h2>\n<p>苦迦菩提是过去一千年间最为可怖的灵堕魔之一。据说他有四颗头与四条手臂，各自代表一年中的一个季节。他对天夏中部一处偏远地区的统治于6223 ic被女英雄谭隋靖终结，尽管她在击败他的同一场战斗中也不幸殒命。她的灵魂转世的灵魂为一棵巨大的杉树，生长在苦迦菩提的坟墓之上，确保只要树仍在，这个死去的邪魔就永远无法转世并重返此世。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>关注领域</strong> 诅咒、亵渎的坟墓、闹鬼的荒野，以及季节性灾害</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>典范</strong> 诅咒活着的生物、亵渎墓地与田园般的自然地区、</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>禁忌</strong> 施行旨在让亡者安息的埋葬仪式、为自己以外的任何人解除诅咒、使非灵堕魔的生物复活</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣属性</strong> 敏捷或感知</p>\n<h3>信徒增益</h3>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>牧师法术</strong> 1环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{魅惑术}，4环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VuPDHoVEPLbMfCJC]{兽化诅咒}，6环：@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.u5FAOOXuqK7fLqKW]{四季之树}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣灌注</strong> 伤害术</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣祝圣</strong> 必须选择不洁</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>神圣技能</strong> 自然</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>领域</strong> 憎恶、死亡、自然、梦魇</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>偏好武器</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.D6E4VaKVG05G26Rm]{锁镰}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>宗教圣徽</strong> 扭曲盘结的木根</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Kugaptee\">Kugaptee</h2>\n<p>Kugaptee was one of the most formidable nindorus of the last millennium. Said to have four heads and four arms, each representing one of the seasons of the year, his reign over a remote reach of central Tian Xia was brought to an end in 6223 ic by the heroine Tan Sui-Jing, although she perished in the same battle where she defeated him. Her soul, reincarnated as an immense sugi tree, grows above Kugaptee’s grave, ensuring the dead fiend will never reincarnate and return to this world while the tree remains.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong> curses, defiled graves, haunted wildlands, and seasonal disasters</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Edicts</strong> curse living creatures, defile graveyards and pastoral natural regions,</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Anathema</strong> perform a burial ritual meant to provide peace to the dead, remove a curse from anyone other than yourself, restore a non-nindoru creature to life</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Attribute</strong> Dexterity or Wisdom</p>\n<h3>Devotee Benefits</h3>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Cleric Spells</strong> 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{Charm}, 4th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VuPDHoVEPLbMfCJC]{Bestial Curse}, 6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.u5FAOOXuqK7fLqKW]{Tree of Seasons}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Font</strong> harm</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Sanctification</strong> must choose unholy</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Divine Skill</strong> Nature</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Domains</strong> abomination, death, nature, nightmares</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Favored Weapon</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.D6E4VaKVG05G26Rm]{Kusarigama}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong> twisted knot of wooden roots</p>"
            },
            "Nindoru Ascetics": {
              "name": "灵堕魔苦行者 Nindoru Ascetics",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindoru Ascetics\">灵堕魔苦行者</h1>\n<p>在灵堕魔之中，存在着更为危险、执掌神力的实体。由于其过于隐秘，尚未建立任何广泛流传的信仰，这些被统称为“苦行者”的灵堕魔半神在很大程度上仍是个谜。最广为人知的三位苦行者本身亦是谜团，且多已被现代社会遗忘。然而，在他们活跃的地区，他们的存在不容忽视。</p>\n<p>灵堕魔苦行者的牧师极其罕见，但确实存在——通常以孤身狂信徒的身份出现，或作为非牧师灵堕魔邪教的领袖。随着时代推移，某位灵堕魔苦行者的信仰规模也有可能扩大，尤其是在你的<em>鬼季</em>战役以灾害收场、而苦迦菩提重返人间之时！</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindoru Ascetics\">Nindoru Ascetics</h1>\n<p>There exists among nindorus much more dangerous entities wielding divine powers. Obscure enough to not have established any widespread faiths, these nindoru demigods, known collectively as the Ascetics, are largely a mystery. The three most well-known Ascetics are themselves enigmas largely forgotten by modern society. Yet in the regions where they’re active, their presence can’t be ignored.</p>\n<p>Clerics of nindoru ascetics are incredibly rare, but they do exist—typically in the role of lone fanatics or leaders of non-cleric nindoru cults. Over time, though, it’s possible for a nindoru ascetic’s faith to potentially grow larger, particularly if the events of your <em>Season of Ghosts</em> campaign end in disaster and Kugaptee returns to the living world!</p>"
            },
            "About Nindorus": {
              "name": "关于灵堕魔 About Nindorus",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"About Nindorus\">关于灵堕魔</h1>\n<p>虽然确实存在更广泛种类的灵堕魔，但本书在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nindoru0000000]{此处}详述了最常见、最常遇到的那些。</p>\n<p>作为游戏中相对较新的补充，玩家可能并不熟悉灵堕魔——这很好！发现这种新类型的恶魔，是<em>鬼季</em>核心谜团的重要组成部分。信奉善解的PC可能会对它们有所了解，详见@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo.JournalEntryPage.18nindorus000000]{此处}。不应有任何PC在本冒险路径开始时就受训于“灵堕魔学识”，但当他们在第1幕末期或第2幕初期了解到这些恶魔后，你应当让玩家知道这对他们的PC而言是一个可选项，甚至可以鼓励部分人利用本战役中大量的休整模式，将其重训为这种尤其有用的学识。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"About Nindorus\">About Nindorus</h1>\n<p>While a wider range of nindorus certainly exist, this book details those the most commonly encountered @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog21bestia.JournalEntryPage.21nindoru0000000]{Here}.</p>\n<p>As relatively new additions to the game, players might not be familiar with nindorus—this is good! The discovery of this new type of fiend is a big part of <em>Season of Ghosts</em>’ central mystery. A PC who is a follower of Sangpotshi might know something about them, as detailed @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog18sangpo.JournalEntryPage.18nindorus000000]{Here}. No PC should begin this Adventure Path trained in Nindoru Lore, but once they learn about these fiends near the end of Act 1 or early in Act 2, you should let the players know this is an option for their PCs and perhaps even encourage some to take advantage of this campaign’s copious amounts of downtime to retrain into this particularly useful Lore.</p>"
            },
            "Society": {
              "name": "协会 Society",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Society\">社会</h1>\n<p>现存关于灵堕魔社会结构的大多数信息都支离破碎。由来自神门的匿名阴暗守卫与来自子哈的轮回者撰写的巨著<em> 诅咒之地的恶魔，幽灵和妖怪 </em>，包含了目前最为详尽的可用信息。</p>\n<p>根据该书所述，灵堕魔最常以小群体形式出没；但当同一地区聚集了足够数量的灵堕魔时，它们会结成由十到五十个成员组成的游牧单位。这些群体通常由大量较弱的灵堕魔构成，并由少数更危险的变种率领。这种结社被称为“灵煞”（ninsat）——是对“灵那萨提”（ninashsati）的讹变；后者是一个古老的轮回者语词汇，意为“家庭”。尽管名称如此，许多灵堕魔群体中常见的关照与同志情谊在此几乎不存在。相反，灵煞强调传播腐化、腐朽、失落与毁灭。</p>\n<p>灵煞的构成会经常改变，因为成员会四散游走以追随各自的强迫冲动，或寻找新的狩猎场。灵煞也会在这些邪魔罕见地陷入内斗时发生变动——通常由争夺猎物引发。灵堕魔不会犹豫去谋杀同类，但它无法从这种杀戮中汲取养分，因此多数个体会把怒火留给更为美味的灵魂。</p>\n<p>灵堕魔对凡人的信仰或诸神的事务几乎毫无兴趣，尽管侍奉少数已知灵堕魔半神者（亦称为@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog19cycles.JournalEntryPage.19nindoruascet00]{灵堕魔苦行者}）是显著的例外。灵堕魔往往无视其他神祇的作为，但有两个例外。它们对@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.aTYy1WHwAZiuei4h]{月夜}——月之主、@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{文业王}复生的兄弟——以及@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{法莱斯玛}怀有格外凶残的蔑视。饰有月夜翡翠月徽的神龛，或受法莱斯玛螺旋标记守护的墓地，常会被某个灵堕魔或整支灵煞选为领地；它们从以屠戮亵渎这些区域的暴行中获得扭曲的快感。</p>\n<p>谈到同样嗜好杀戮的相近邪魔时，灵堕魔对合作毫无兴趣，甚至同样可能与恶魔、魔鬼或其他邪魔为敌。然而，那些将宇宙视作自身领域的存在——例如罗刹——有时会处在可能寻求与灵堕魔结盟的立场。无论如何，灵堕魔能够容忍与其他生物合作，尤其是当对方以丰厚的灵魂供给作为报酬时。讽刺的是，人们也曾目击灵堕魔与不死并肩出现——而不死正是最常被拿来与灵堕魔混淆的生物类型。在这些合作关系中，灵堕魔通常充当领袖，指挥食尸鬼、僵尸吸血鬼，或将无心智的不死当作躯壳加以占据，并将其改造为不死与灵堕魔生命特质交织的诡异混合体。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Society\">Society</h1>\n<p>Most of the information that exists on nindoru social structure is fragmented. <em> Demons, Ghosts and Yokai of the Cursed Lands </em>, a tome penned by anonymous Gloom Wardens from Shenmen and samsarans from Zi Ha, contains the most detailed information available at the moment.</p>\n<p>According to this text, nindorus are most often encountered in small groups, but when enough of them gather in a single region, they band together in nomadic units ranging from ten to fifty. These groups are typically made up of a large number of less powerful nindorus led by a few of the more dangerous variants. This grouping is known as a “ninsat”—a mangling of “ninashsati,” an archaic samsaran term for “family.” Despite the name, there is little in the way of the care and camaraderie found in many nindoru groups. Instead, ninsats emphasize spreading corruption, decay, loss, and ruin.</p>\n<p>The makeup of ninsats changes on a regular basis as members wander off to follow their own compulsions or seek fresh hunting grounds. Ninsats also shift during the rare occasions that the fiends fall into infighting, usually caused by disputes over prey. While a nindoru won’t hesitate to murder its kin, it’s unable to take nourishment from such kills, so most choose to save their rage for more delicious souls.</p>\n<p>Nindorus have little interest in the faiths of mortals or the affairs of the gods, although those who serve some of the few known nindoru demigods (known also as @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog19cycles.JournalEntryPage.19nindoruascet00]{Nindoru Ascetics}) are notable exceptions. Nindorus tend to ignore the works of other deities, with two exceptions. They feel particularly vicious contempt for @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.aTYy1WHwAZiuei4h]{Tsukiyo}, lord of the moon and the resurrected brother of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{Fumeiyoshi}, as well as @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}. Shrines emblazoned with Tsukiyo’s jade moon or graveyards protected by Pharasma’s spiral are often sought out as territories by a nindoru or entire ninsats, who derive perverse pleasure from desecrating such areas with carnage.</p>\n<p>When it comes to similar fiends with a shared appetite for bloodshed, nindorus have no interest in cooperation and are as likely to fight against demons, devils, or other fiends. Those who call the Universe their domain, though, such as rakshasas, sometimes find themselves in positions where they might seek an alliance with nindorus. Regardless, nindorus can tolerate cooperation with other creatures, especially if offered a bountiful supply of souls as payment. Ironically, nindorus have also been seen alongside undead, the creature type they are most often confused with. In these partnerships, nindorus usually act as leaders commanding ghouls, jiang-shi vampires, or using mindless undead as husks to inhabit and transform into strange amalgamations of undeath and nindoru life.</p>"
            },
            "Ecology": {
              "name": "生态 Ecology",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Ecology\">生态</h1>\n<p>灵堕魔存在于自然法则之外，但它们仍存在于自然世界之中——与大多数恶魔不同，它们的关联对象是宇宙本身，而非浩瀚众界中的另一个位面。尽管它们本身并不内在地遵循生态系统的法则，却仍被驱使以一种几乎会形成相同生态位的方式去扰乱环境——只不过那种“角色”看起来完全是自我毁灭的。每一种灵堕魔都体现了某个特定循环的断裂，此外还体现了创造它们的生死循环那种普遍性的破碎。</p>\n<p>灵堕魔被驱使去吞食转世的灵魂，但只有那些在善解的循环之流中漂流过多次的灵魂，才接近满足它们的饥渴。对灵堕魔而言，理想的灵魂是那种已转世多次、正在现世生活，同时还保有前世记忆（不论是部分还是完整）者。对灵堕魔来说，浸透了多世集体经验与智慧的灵魂，就像一瓶恰到好处陈年的佳酿。</p>\n<p>沿着这条阴森的类比继续延伸，人们可以想象灵堕魔拥有相当于侍酒师那样分辨葡萄酒原料的技能。它们能凭直觉判断某个灵魂是否经历过转世。那些在与灵堕魔的遭遇中幸存的人经常报告说，这些恶魔会就所谓的前世发表令人不寒而栗、极其私密的言论。多数人永远无法验证这些说法是否属实，因为能回忆前世是一种少数人才具备的天赋。具志坚吉一是第一位在《开拓者编年史》中发表灵堕魔详尽记录的人；他称那只恶魔告诉他，他的灵魂“有古老血迹的颜色”，并曾寄居于一名武士的身体中——那名武士在八桥之战中被利刃将头颅劈成两半而死。尽管无法证实，这一说法仍令吉一从骨子里为之震颤。</p>\n<p>灵堕魔会在肉体死亡之际吞食灵魂，在其从被杀害的血肉中离去时以形而上的方式将其“撕碎”，使该灵魂难以被送回——无论是回到生命还是不死。灵堕魔只吞噬该灵魂能量的一小部分，因此这些灵魂并不会被阻止前往来世或再次转世；然而，那些在遭受此类攻击后复活的人，往往会过上更为艰难的生活，并经历一些可能让他们觉得自己受了诅咒、毁灭，或只是单纯倒霉的事情。某些在被灵堕魔吞食后转世、怨念尤深的灵魂，若途中寻不到开悟，甚至可能会选择回归为灵堕魔本身。</p>\n<p>所有灵堕魔都具备将思绪具现为实体之物的能力，不过其中最弱者仅能具现武器、护甲或工具。更强大的灵堕魔能具现生物、改变它们的环境，或具现情绪与记忆而非有形的物体。这些具现物无论本质如何，外观总是破败、破损、令人不适——但当由其创造者使用时，它们的运作效果至少与完整无损时相当，甚至更佳。有人报告了这种力量中一种尤为令人毛骨悚然的变体：当与灵堕魔在战斗中对峙时，他们会目睹灵堕魔从对手自身的过往中具现出破损的武器、工具，甚至是人，然后用该物体或生物来对付他们。这种情感操控是某些更强大灵堕魔使用的计谋；它们可能具现出最喜爱的童年玩具、已故父母的褪色影像，或爱人的戒指。灵堕魔一边利用这份具现物取得优势，一边同时侵蚀敌人的决心。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Ecology\">Ecology</h1>\n<p>Nindorus exist outside the laws of nature, yet they still exist within the natural world–unlike most fiends, their association is with the Universe itself, rather than another plane of the Great Beyond. While they themselves do not intrinsically obey the laws of an ecosystem, they are compelled to disrupt environments in a way that almost results in the same sort of role—if only a role that seems entirely self-destructive. Each type of nindoru epitomizes the fracture of a specific cycle in addition to the generalized fracturing of the life and death cycle that created them.</p>\n<p>Nindorus are compelled to feast on souls, but only souls who have drifted through the recurrent stream of Sangpotshi multiple times come close to satisfying their hunger. A nindoru’s ideal soul is one that has reincarnated several times and is currently living a life while having memories (either partial or full) of previous lives. To a nindoru, a soul imbued with the collective experience and wisdom of multiple lives is like a fine wine allowed to age just right.</p>\n<p>To take this morbid analogy further, one can imagine that nindorus possess the equivalent of a sommelier’s skill at discerning a wine’s ingredients. They can intuit whether a soul has been reincarnated or not. Those who have survived encounters with nindorus often report that the demons made disturbingly intimate statements about so-called past lives. Most will never be able to verify whether or not these statements were true, as the ability to recall past lives is a gift few possess. Gushiken Giichi, the first to publish a detailed account of a nindoru in the Pathfinder Chronicles, said the fiend told him his soul “was the color of an ancient bloodstain” and had once been housed in the body of a warrior who died during the Battle of Eight Bridges after a blade cleaved his head in two. While impossible to confirm, the claim still shook Giichi to his core.</p>\n<p>The nindoru feeds on a soul upon the death of its body, metaphysically “shredding” the soul as it exits the slain flesh and rendering it difficult for that soul to be returned—either to life or undeath. These souls are not prevented from traveling on to the afterlife or being reincarnated, for nindorus feed on only a fraction of that soul’s energy, but those who come back to life after suffering such an attack often live harsher lives and experience things that might make them feel cursed, doomed, or simply unlucky. Particularly bitter souls reincarnated after being devoured by nindorus might even choose to return as nindorus themselves if they can’t find enlightenment along the way.</p>\n<p>All nindorus have the ability to manifest physical things from their thoughts, although the least powerful of their kind are limited to the manifestation of weapons, armor, or tools. More powerful nindorus can manifest creatures, alter their environments, or manifest emotions or memories instead of physical objects. These manifestations, regardless of their nature, always appear decrepit, broken, and unpleasant—yet when used by their creators they function as well, if not better, than they would if they were whole. Some report a particularly unnerving variant of this power, in which those facing a nindoru in battle witness them manifesting broken weapons, tools, or even people from the person’s own past, only to use that object or creature against them. This emotional manipulation is a stratagem used by some of the more powerful nindorus; they might manifest a favorite childhood toy, faded image of a long-deceased parent, or a loved one’s ring. The nindoru uses this manifestation to its advantage while simultaneously eroding its foe’s resolve.</p>"
            },
            "Appearance": {
              "name": "外观 Appearance",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Appearance\">外貌</h1>\n<p>灵堕魔的种类繁多，形态各异，但它们也共享某些共同特征。多数灵堕魔拥有大致类人的轮廓，却常因其枯槁的身形、破损或脱臼的肢体，以及宛如伤口的特征而被误认为是不死。外行人常以为灵堕魔与食尸鬼有关；而《帝国的亵渎者》——一本由龙华生物学家出版的天文文献——其中关于这些生物的条目竟错误地将灵堕魔认定为“不同寻常的丧尸变种”。灵堕魔的影响确实能将丧尸这类无智不死强化为更为骇人的形态与躯体，这当然无助于澄清误解。事实上，这种混淆或许也导致多年来缺乏对灵堕魔的适当研究——这一危险的疏忽所幸如今正被纠正。</p>\n<p>若对灵堕魔进行近距离观察，便会发现许多完全独有的特征。即便是外形最怪诞者，通常也会在其躯体上嵌入某种类人要素：或是在本不该有手臂之处长出手臂，或是在身体的藏匿部位——例如喉咙深处——出现一张隐约的面孔狞笑。灵堕魔往往似乎双目失明、受损，或干脆失去的眼睛，却依旧能清晰视物，展现出那些已从灵魂轮回中脱离的生物无法拥有此类器官。</p>\n<p>无论采取何种形态，灵堕魔的躯体都映照着毁灭的本质，并象征其打破生死循环的角色。其手臂与双腿常呈现痛苦般的拉长、断裂或脱臼，却仍保有与健康凡人肢体相当（甚至更强）的力量与敏捷。其血肉常显得蜡黄、腐朽，甚至布满可怖创伤。这些特征正是许多人将灵堕魔误认作不死的主因，但它们确实是活着的——其超自然的身体不受生物学与健康法则的束缚。其他灵堕魔则可能完全缺失身体中理应存在的部分，例如胸腔，甚至整颗头颅——并常以藤编笼、闪烁提灯或其他通常无生命的物体来替代这些部位。</p>\n<p>当灵堕魔着装或使用武器与工具时，它们无一例外偏好破损、黯淡或彻底毁坏的饰物与器具。多数会使用武器的灵堕魔挥舞的都是残破兵器，并由其超自然本质将之强化为魔法之物。当这些武器被其脱臼的手掌挥动时，足以造成严重创伤；但一旦松手，便会崩解成尘。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nindoru-butterfly.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nindoru Butterfly\" alt=\"an eerie blood-red butterfly\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nindoru-butterfly.webp')\" />\n<p>灵堕魔由那些抛弃“转世”或“死后仍有来生”这一观念的灵魂直接成形，并以完全成熟的姿态出现。最危险、最强大的灵堕魔往往源自殒落的善者或轮回者之魂——它们背弃了生死循环；但没有任何灵魂会“意外”变成灵堕魔。选择放弃循环、让自身不朽之魂暴露于此等命运，往往是通过参与复杂仪式来确保灵魂从世界中挣脱而发生；且此决定必须始终在生前出于自愿作出（尽管欺骗与诡计可能诱使悲剧人物在未完全理解后果的情况下作出选择）。</p>\n<p>许多灵堕魔共享的一个奇异要素，是那些令人毛骨悚然的血红蝴蝶：它们会聚集在灵堕魔躯体的空腔之中，或似乎完整成形地自其血肉中爬出。对许多人而言，蝴蝶象征蜕变与改变；然而从未有人见过与灵堕魔相关的毛虫，这暗示这些“蝴蝶”并非表面所见那般简单。有人认为灵堕魔蝴蝶是灵堕魔破损灵魂的具现，也有人相信它们是灵堕魔逸散思绪的化身。这些蝴蝶一旦从其恶魔般的宿主身旁振翅离去，便很少能存活太久，往往化作红色烟雾消散，或在墙面与地面留下如血渍般的痕迹。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Appearance\">Appearance</h1>\n<p>The various types of nindorus have a wide variety of forms, yet all of them share certain features in common. The majority have vaguely humanoid shapes and are often mistaken for undead due to their emaciated frames, broken or disjointed limbs, and wound-like features. The uninitiated often assume that nindorus are related to ghouls, and an entry on the creatures in Defilers of the Empire, a Tian text published by Lung Wa biologists, incorrectly identified nindorus as “unusual zombie variants.” The fact that nindoru influence can empower mindless undead like zombies into even more horrific shapes and forms certainly doesn’t help with this misconception. In fact, this confusion may have contributed to the lack of proper nindoru research over the years, a dangerous oversight that’s thankfully now being rectified.</p>\n<p>A close inspection of nindorus reveals many characteristics that are entirely their own. Even those with the most bizarre forms usually incorporate some humanoid feature in their shape, be it the growth of arms where no arms should be or the presence of a vaguely face leering from a hidden part of the body, such as the depths of the throat. Nindorus often seem to have blinded, damaged, or entirely missing eyes, yet see with perfect clarity, displaying how creatures who have broken away from the cycle of souls can’t possess such organs.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the shape they take, a nindoru’s body reflects the nature of destruction and symbolizes their role in breaking the cycle of life and death. Arms and legs often appear painfully elongated, broken, or dislocated, yet retain as much (if not more) strength and agility as healthy mortal limbs. Flesh often appears sallow, decaying, or even grievously wounded. These features are the primary reason many mistake nindorus for undead, yet they are very much alive—their supernatural bodies not being bound to the laws of biology and health. Other nindorus might be entirely missing an expected part of the body, such as the chest or even the entire head—often replacing such body parts with wicker cages, flickering lanterns, or other normally inanimate objects.</p>\n<p>When a nindoru dresses or uses weapons or tools, they invariably prefer accessories and devices that are broken, tarnished, or outright destroyed. Most nindorus who use weapons wield broken armaments that their supernatural nature empowers to become magical. When brandished in their disjointed hands, these weapons can inflict grievous wounds, but upon being released, they crumble into dust.</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nindoru-butterfly.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nindoru Butterfly\" alt=\"an eerie blood-red butterfly\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nindoru-butterfly.webp')\" />\n<p>Nindorus form fully grown from souls who have abandoned the very concept of reincarnation or life after death. The most dangerous and powerful nindorus tend to rise from the souls of fallen Sangpots or samsarans who have turned their back on the cycle of life and death, but no soul can “accidentally” become a nindoru. The choice to abandon the cycle and expose one’s immortal soul to such a fate often occurs through participation in complex rituals to ensure their soul breaks free from the world, and it must always be made freely while alive (although deception and trickery can delude tragic figures into making this choice without realizing the full ramifications).</p>\n<p>One strange element shared by many nindorus are the eerie blood-red butterflies that gather in the hollow spaces in a nindoru’s body or seem to crawl, fully formed, from their flesh. To many, the butterfly is a symbol of transformation and change, yet no caterpillar has ever been seen in association with a nindoru, suggesting that these “butterflies” are something more than they appear. Some suggest that nindoru butterflies are a physical manifestation of the nindoru’s broken soul, while others believe them to be incarnations of the nindoru’s stray thoughts. These butterflies rarely live long after fluttering away from their fiendish host, fading into red smoke or bloodstain-like markings on the wall or floor.</p>"
            },
            "Cycles of Destruction": {
              "name": "毁灭的轮回 Cycles of Destruction",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Cycles of Destruction\">\n  <span>毁灭的轮回</span>\n</h1>\n\n<p>不同于大多数恶魔——其起源可追溯至时间长河的幽深处，甚至常常早于“凡人生存”这一概念本身——灵堕魔在宇宙舞台上算是相对较新的来客。然而，随着时间推移，他们的存在仍有可能扩散到现实的每一个角落。</p>\n<p>史料显示，最初的灵堕魔诞生于三千多年前天夏仪兴帝国的鼎盛时期。在那个年代，一名人类孩子出生于轮回者父母之家，但不久后便被交给了一个人类社群抚养——他的生身父母希望自己的儿子能过上和谐的生活，并在下一个生命轮回中转生为轮回者之躯。可结果却事与愿违：这个孩子长成了名为西格克的愤怒青年，因父母抛弃自己而心怀怨恨。他在青年时期寻到他们，但当他发现父母甚至都不是人类时，他的苦涩迅速膨胀，迁怒于所有轮回者，尤其是那些追随善解之人。西格克质问：为何“觉悟”只能通过缓慢的死亡与重生达成，而业力却以一种武断的姿态，裁决灵魂的命运。</p>\n<p>随着成长，西格克执迷于在善解的轮回之外实现完美。他拜许多强大的施法者为师，最终长期侍奉于一名名为灵堕魔的巫妖。那巫妖向这个易受影响的年轻人灌输不死的种种可能，告诉他不死是一种无需将阅历与智慧奉献给繁重转生之无常摆布、便能达到的完美状态。西格克为之心动，但他认为灵魂之笼将成为他无法承受的弱点。研习五年后，西格克背叛了灵堕魔并摧毁了巫妖，随后盗走昔日主人的灵魂之笼用于实验，将巫妖的灵魂困在笼中多年。那些年里，西格克聚集起一群志同道合的学者与拒斥善解教义之人，并愈发崇敬@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{文业王}——天夏的坟墓守护神祇。公元4444年，西格克率领规模可观的会众举行了一场亵渎的仪式，意图强迫被囚的灵堕魔之魂转生为某种全新的事物——某种不在既定生死轮回之内的存在。西格克承诺，这将“粉碎善解之轮，让我们所有人从转生的牢笼中解脱。”</p>\n<p>关于西格克计划施行该仪式的记录至今仍存，也有文献记述他在选定举行仪式之日前的生平。然而，在那决定命运的一天之后，关于西格克、他的实验或其教团的一切便再无可寻。他与追随者仿佛凭空消失，像是被逐出了现实本身。可就在同年晚些时候，关于灵堕魔恶魔的最早记载开始出现，而多数人都认为这两件事在时间上的相近绝非巧合。数百年来，人们相信西格克以某种方式将其祈求者转变为最初的灵堕魔，而那些恶魔随后谋杀了他们的创造者。但近期证据揭示了灵堕魔半神的存在，其中甚至有一位冠以“西格克”之名——这或许暗示，那位幻灭的人类以将自身化作毁灭的化身之方式，达成了一种扭曲的觉悟。</p>\n<p>当然，最强大的灵堕魔自有不同说法：他们宣称自己始终存在于创世造物之外，而正是西格克的行为终于让他们得以进入这段现实的轮回——而恶魔们如今承诺，这将是最后一次轮回；因为当他们得逞之时，唯有灵堕魔会留存于世。</p>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-nindoru-fight.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Nindoru Fight\" class=\"chapter-image\" />\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here=\"Cycles of Destruction\">\n  <span>Cycles of Destruction</span>\n</h1>\n\n<p>Unlike most fiends, whose origins date back to the depths of time and often predate the very concept of mortal life itself, nindorus are a relatively new arrival on the cosmic stage. In time, however, their presence could potentially spread throughout all corners of reality.</p>\n<p>Historical documents suggest that the first nindorus came into being during the height of Tian Xia’s Yixing empire over three thousand years ago. In that era, a human child was born to samsaran parents only to be given over to a human community shortly thereafter, as his birth parents hoped their son would live a harmonious existence and reincarnate into a samsaran body during his next life cycle. Instead, this child grew into an angry youth named Sigek who resented his parents for abandoning him. He sought them out as a young adult, but upon discovering his parents weren’t even human, his bitterness swiftly bloomed to encompass all samsarans, especially those who followed Sangpotshi. Sigek demanded to know why enlightenment was only achievable via a slow process of death and rebirth, with karma serving as an arbitrary judge of a soul’s fate.</p>\n<p>As he matured, Sigek became obsessed with achieving perfection outside the cycle of Sangpotshi. He apprenticed himself to a host of powerful spellcasters, eventually entering into a lasting servitude under a lich named Nindoru. The lich filled the impressionable young man’s mind with the possibilities of undeath, telling him it was a perfect state that could be achieved without sacrificing experience and wisdom to the laborious whims of reincarnation. Sigek was intrigued, but concluded that a soul cage would be a vulnerability he could not afford. After five years of study, Sigek betrayed Nindoru and destroyed the lich, then stole his former master’s soul cage for experimentation, keeping the lich’s soul trapped within its cage for years. Over those years, Sigek gathered a sizable following of like-minded scholars and those who rejected the teachings of Sangpotshi while increasingly venerating @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.6O4UGWcYERDEugzk]{Fumeiyoshi}, Tian Xia’s patron of graves. In 4444 ic, Sigek led his sizable congregation in a blasphemous ritual intended to force Nindoru’s trapped soul to reincarnate into something new, something outside of the established cycle of life and death. This, Sigek promised, would “Shatter the wheel of Sangpotshi and free us all from the cage of reincarnation.”</p>\n<p>Records of Sigek’s plans to perform the ritual still exist, as well as documents chronicling his life before the date he chose to perform the rite. But after that fateful day, nothing can be found about Sigek, his experiments, or his cult. He and his followers seemed to have simply vanished, as if cast out of reality itself. Yet later that same year, the first accounts of nindoru fiends began to appear, and most agree that the timing of these two events is no coincidence. For centuries, it was believed that Sigek somehow managed to transform his supplicants into the first nindorus, and the fiends subsequently murdered their creator. But recent evidence has revealed the existence of nindoru demigods, including one bearing the name Sigek—perhaps a sign that the disillusioned human achieved a twisted version of enlightenment by transforming himself into an incarnation of his own destruction.</p>\n<p>The most powerful of the nindorus themselves, of course, hold different beliefs, for they claim to have always existed beyond the creation of creation itself, and it was only Sigek’s actions that finally allowed them into this cycle of reality—a cycle that the fiends now promise will be the last, for when they have had their way, only the nindorus will remain.</p>"
            }
          }
