            "Zhi Hui": {
              "name": "智惠 Zhi Hui",
              "text": "<span><strong>智惠大师</strong></span>\n<span class=\"chapter\">善良的寺庙幽灵</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihui.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zhi Hui\" alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihui.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>在智惠来到后来将被称为谭杉寺的地方之前，她曾被一个小村庄（如今早已被遗忘）的村民遗弃在幽魂之森，以此平息愤怒的灵体。此后，她作为游牧者在幽魂之森的诸灵之间生活。智惠并未屈服于怪物，而是被神灵发现并抚养长大。她遵循他们的指引，在15岁时开悟，随后独自踏上探索幽魂之森的旅程。多年后，她听闻一片杉树林的传说：那里的杉树高耸于林海之上，树干之粗足以媲美整间小屋。她不禁好奇，为何杉树能长到如此极端，于是出发去寻找那片树林。又过了三年，她才找到那些树——因为幽魂之森的这一带荒蛮而未经探索——但即便尚不知其含义，她也明白自己遇见了一处意义非凡之地。</p>\n<p>当智惠最初建立谭杉寺与柳岸镇时，她只是希望能创造一处所在，让善解的弟子们得以将一生奉献给追求开悟。那片杉树林令她心生敬畏，她发现灵性能量的高度汇聚使树木异常巨大。她很快揭开树林阴森的秘密——一股大恶沉眠于树根之下，唯有一位英魂的灵性抗力（其已转世为林中最高的那棵树）才将那邪恶压在死亡之中，阻止其逃脱。发现此事后，她搜罗自己可用的一切资源，并联络天夏各地的友人，终于查明那邪恶的本质：一位名为苦迦菩提的宁多鲁半神被埋在大杉树之下。她遂立誓守护这些杉树——而杉树反过来守护所有村民免受这魔裔之害。</p>\n<p>智惠大师逝世后，她的灵体起初仍与寺庙相系，以监督对杉树林的守护；但随着追随者离去或堕落，她的灵体也被困在苦迦菩提的掌控之中。如今，她几乎无力阻止正将事态推向危局的诸般发展：苦迦菩提的苏醒。</p>\n<h2>战役角色</h2>\n<p>当PC们净化寺庙中的雕像时，智惠便能回答他们更多的问题，并为他们施放法术；一旦四尊雕像全都被净化，她便可随意施放法术与回答问题，甚至还能在战斗中提供协助——只要战斗发生在包含已净化雕像的某个遭遇区域内。PC们可能向智惠提出的某些问题，答案如下。</p>\n<p><strong>苦迦菩提是谁/是什么？</strong>“苦迦菩提是一名宁多鲁魔裔，其存在与善解的哲理相悖。近千年前，他被谭隋靖击败。她也在那场战斗中殒命，但她的灵魂转世为一棵参天的杉树，生长在苦迦菩提的遗骸之上，作为封印将他的灵魂困住。寺庙中央的那棵杉树正是此树。但它已染病，因为苦迦菩提正渴求重生。他的影响正是你们一直面对的诸般怪异之源。这座寺庙曾是一处神圣之地，僧侣们照看着土地、动物与灵体。与此同时，甚至在寺庙建立之前，这里就是一处将苦迦菩提的滔天邪恶封在地底的所在。我原以为这座寺庙会守卫苦迦菩提之墓许多世代，却没能预见自己的死亡会如何影响追随者。无人准备好接替我。更糟的是，我的一名弟子，欣月，被苦迦菩提所腐化，甚至如今仍在他的墓穴下方劳作，只为让那魔裔的灵魂重生。现在，聚集于此的魔裔正在亵渎散落于寺庙各处的雕像，以放大苦迦菩提的影响。”</p>\n<p><strong>关于折磨柳岸镇的诅咒，你能告诉我们什么？</strong>“这座寺庙建于这片神圣的树木林地之中，但我当时并不知晓，大杉树封印着一名强大而邪恶的魔裔——苦迦菩提。正是这魔裔的影响引发了如今正在上演的悲剧。困住你们与柳岸镇的，并非寻常诅咒。时间本身被从你们身上夺走。我们都被困在一个循环的思维空间里，它每年重复：从夏季的第一天开始，到春季的最后一天结束。每一次循环重启，你们的记忆都会被重置。我保留着记忆，但我不知道循环已重复了多少次；直到如今，我也无法看清苦迦菩提的黑暗之外的事物。但我知道是谁开启了这一切——你们的总督，和善保。他企图强化谭杉寺，但它并不需要强化。他的尝试适得其反，打开了通往苦迦菩提之墓的裂隙——那些裂隙将我们所有人都投入这循环的思维空间之中。这甚至足以把和善保从束缚其余所有人的这片思维空间里卷走。尽管我无法说出我们重复了这一循环多少年，但我确知这一次有了变化——无论是苦迦菩提日益增长的力量所致，还是其他外力所致。重要的是，你们获得了改变我们命运的机会；若你们想解放我们所有人，就绝不能浪费这次机会。要终止循环，你们必须揭开事情真相，而这要从终结苦迦菩提对这片思维空间的影响开始。”</p>\n<p><strong>我们该如何逃离？</strong>“我不知道你们想要的答案。若有人知道，那必是和善保。他造成了这一切，但如今他也被困在自己的思维空间之中。一旦苦迦菩提的影响被削弱，你们就会发现可循的踪迹与可寻的线索，它们必将引领你们找到你们的总督去了何处。找到和善保，你们就会更接近理解当下正在发生什么，以及该如何逃离这恶意的循环。”</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.uFg1TnTBpXNYGF9o]{Zhi Hui}</span>\n    <span>生物 7</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">幽灵</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">虚体</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵体</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不死生物</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>Zhi Hui</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Benevolent Monastic Ghost</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihui.webp\" data-tooltip=\"Zhi Hui\" alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-zhihui.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>Before Zhi Hui arrived at what would become the Tan Sugi monastery, she lived as a nomad among the spirits of the Specterwood after being abandoned there to appease angry spirits by the villagers of a small, now long-forgotten village. Rather than succumb to monsters, Zhi Hui was instead discovered and raised by kami. She followed their guidance and achieved enlightenment at the age of 15 before setting out on her own to explore Specterwood. Years later, she heard the story of a grove of sugi trees that towered over the rest of the forest, with trunks as large as entire huts. Wondering how sugi trees could grow to such extremes, Zhi Hui set out to find the grove. It took her three more years to find the trees, for this part of Specterwood was wild and unexplored, but she knew she’d come across a place of immense significance even if she didn’t yet know what it meant.</p>\n<p>When Zhi Hui initially founded both the Tan Sugi monastery and Willowshore, she’d simply hoped to create a place where disciples of Sangpotshi could dedicate their lives to the pursuit enlightenment. The sugi grove instilled a sense of awe in her, and she discovered that a high concentration of spiritual energy caused the trees to grow abnormally large. She soon uncovered the grove’s sinister secret—that a great evil slumbered beneath its roots and only the spiritual resistance of a heroic soul who’d reincarnated as the tallest tree in the grove kept that evil from escaping its death. Following this discovery, she scoured the resources available to her and reached out to friends throughout Tian Xia before finally determining the nature of the evil. A nindoru demigod named Kugaptee was buried beneath the Great Sugi, and she dedicated herself to protecting the sugi trees that in turn protected all of the villagers from the fiend.</p>\n<p>After Master Zhi Hui’s passing, her spirit initially remained tied to the monastery to oversee the protection of the grove, but as her followers left or became corrupted, her spirit became trapped in Kugaptee’s clutches as well. Now, she can do little to stop the events that unfold and are leading to a dire situation: Kugaptee’s awakening.</p>\n<h2>Campaign Role</h2>\n<p>As the PCs purify statues in the monastery, Zhi Hui can answer more of their questions and cast spells on them; once all four statues are purified, she can cast spells and answer questions at will and can even aid in combat as long as the fight takes place in one of the encounter areas that contains a purified statue. Certain questions the PCs might ask Zhi Hui are answered as follows.</p>\n<p><strong>Who/What is Kugaptee?</strong> “Kugaptee is a nindoru fiend whose existence stands in opposition to the philosophy of Sangpotshi. Nearly a thousand years ago, he was defeated by Tan Sui-Jing. She perished in the fight as well, but her soul reincarnated as a towering sugi tree that grew over Kugaptee’s remains, serving as a seal that would keep his soul trapped. The central sugi tree in this monastery is that very tree. But it has sickened, for Kugaptee strives for rebirth. His influence is the source of the monstrosities you’ve been facing. This monastery was once a sacred place, with monks who cared for the land, the animals, and the spirits. At the same time, and even before the monastery, it has been a site that kept Kugaptee’s immense evil sealed away beneath the surface. I had hoped that this monastery would stand guard over Kugaptee’s grave for many generations to come, but I failed to see how my own death would affect my followers. No one was ready to take my place. Worse, one of my students, Xin Yue, became corrupted by Kugaptee and even now toils below in his grave to see the fiend’s soul reborn. Now, the fiends who have gathered here have been desecrating the statues scattered throughout the monastery to amplify Kugaptee’s influence.”</p>\n<p><strong>What can you tell us of the curse that afflicts Willowshore?</strong> “This monastery was built in this sacred grove of trees, but unknown to me at the time, the Great Sugi seals away a powerful and evil fiend named Kugaptee. It is this fiend’s influence that has caused the tragedy unfolding now. It is no mere curse that traps you and Willowshore. Time itself has been stolen from you. We are all trapped in a cycling mindscape that repeats every year, beginning on the first day of summer and ending on the last day of spring. Each time the cycle repeats, your memories have been reset. I retain my memories, but I know not how often the cycle has repeated and, until now, have not been able to see further than Kugaptee’s darkness. But I know who started it—your governor, Heh Shan-Bao. He sought to bolster the Tan Sugi, but it needed no bolstering. His attempt backfired and opened cracks into Kugaptee’s grave—cracks that plunged us all into this cyclic mindscape. It was enough to whisk Heh Shan-Bao away even from this mindscape that traps the rest of us. While I cannot say how many years we’ve repeated this cycle, I do know that something has changed this time—whether due to Kugaptee’s growing strength or other outside forces. What is important is that you have been given the chance to change our fates, and you must not waste this opportunity if you wish to free us all. To stop the cycle, you must uncover the truth of what happened, and that begins with ending Kugaptee’s influence over this mindscape.”</p>\n<p><strong>How can we escape?</strong> “I do not know the answer you seek. If anyone does, it would be Heh Shan-Bao. He caused all of this, but he is now trapped within his own mindscape. Once Kugaptee’s influence has been diminished, there will be trails to follow and clues to seek that will surely lead you to where your governor has gone. Find Heh Shan-Bao, and you will get closer to understanding what is happening now and how to escape from this cycle of malice.”</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.uFg1TnTBpXNYGF9o]{Zhi Hui}</span>\n    <span>Creature 7</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Ghost</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Incorporeal</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Spirit</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Undead</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Xin Yue": {
              "name": "新月 Xin Yue",
              "text": "<span><strong>心月</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">苦迦菩提的女祭司</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyue.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyue.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>心月记得自己所有的前世。起初，她将这种能力视为诸神的赐福，使她能在每一次死亡并转世的过程中，运用累积的知识来改善自己的人生境遇。她略微偏好转世为女性，因为那更符合她的第一具身体，但她很快也开始享受以男性之躯度过的生活。归根结底，对心月而言，只要灵魂仍然完整，身体的具体形态并不重要。</p>\n<p>作为善解的信徒，她所度过的每一世都让她离开悟更近一步。她与寿命悠长的灵体结为朋友，那些灵体总是乐于见到她以最新的身体前来造访。随着她的生命不断延续，她最终得以开悟。正是在本应是她最后一次转世时，她来到谭杉寺，并引起了苦迦菩提的注意。尽管在智慧逝去时苦迦菩提被困于谭杉之下的死亡之中，他仍在心月悲恸最深之际，将自己的影响潜入她的梦境。在随后那段可怕的数月里，灵堕魔对心月的影响日益加深。在这些梦中，心月与苦迦菩提愈发频繁地就转世的价值展开激烈辩论；久而久之，这种腐化发展到心月将自己奉献给那位灵堕魔半神的地步——她已将其视为那位“让她看清开悟之虚浮”的主宰。</p>\n<p>随后，心月将注意力转向寺中所剩无几的僧侣，并开始引诱他们改为崇拜苦迦菩提。然而，直到心月在其他僧侣眼前将自己献给那头恶魔作为祭品——却又转世成如今的身体——他们才也一并改信。对他们而言，心月揭示了谭杉寺并非宁静之地，而是一座牢笼般的墓冢；若他们能释放其中被束缚的囚徒，便能立刻获得巨大的力量与奖励，而不必为了某个甚至可能永远无法赢得的机会，去等待无数次转世。</p>\n<p>心月如今的身体是一名矮个的人类女性，齐肩短发，另有一条长长的黑色辫子垂至小腿。她总以愉快的态度、面带温和的微笑说出可怖之语，从而在追随者心中树立令人畏惧的敬意。她一贯的礼貌并非伪装，即便在她威胁并许诺惩罚之时亦然。她以尽可能漫长且痛苦的方式屠宰受害者时，会对他们微笑，并真诚地感谢他们的牺牲。</p>\n<p>当总督和善保的仪式屠杀了柳岸镇的人民，并将这片地区拖入思维空间时，心月与她的僧侣也一同死去。然而，他们并未在思维空间中复生。他们与苦迦菩提的接近与虔诚使他们无法重获生命，于是过去115年的每一次循环里，他们都以不死生物的形态存在。对心月而言，这具新的身体是一种可耻而恐怖的负担；她只寄望于协助苦迦菩提达成所欲——利用他昔日宿敌之躯的化身，如今覆盖其坟茔生长的杉树，作为塑造全新活体之躯的原始材料——从而让她也能重生为新的形态。她对自己会得到何种身体兴趣不大，只要那是活生生的血肉之躯即可。</p>\n<h2>战役角色</h2>\n<p>心月伪造了谭杉寺覆灭与苦迦菩提苏醒的种种因由，自那以后便一直为他的复活而努力。与英雄们一样，心月在过去115年间被困在思维空间里，但由于她与苦迦菩提的联系，她保留了每一次循环流逝的记忆。她一直监视着柳岸镇的镇民，但在一个世纪里屡次失败、始终无法打破自身循环之后，她便不再将他们视为对自己事业的威胁。因此，当她从苦迦菩提那里得到异象，看到PC们打开鬼打墙时，她确实感到震惊。</p>\n<p>尽管外表近乎骷髅般的不死生物，心月仍保持着她的礼貌；她丝毫不掩饰自己的意图。她对英雄们并无个人怨念。尽管她可能显得通情达理，但只要苦迦菩提的存在仍留在思维空间中，就无法通过劝说让她停止追求；她会为达成目标而战至最后一刻。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ExTKQvgLI72XGk98]{心月}</span>\n    <span>生物 7</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不死生物</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>Xin Yue</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Priestess of Kugaptee</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyue.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-xinyue.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>Xin Yue remembers all of their previous lives. They originally saw this ability as a blessing from the gods that allowed them to use their accumulated knowledge to better their station in life each time they died and were reincarnated. While they slightly preferred being reincarnated as a woman, because it matched their first body, they quickly grew to enjoy their lives in a man’s body as well. Ultimately, to Xin Yue, the actual form of their body was unimportant as long as their soul remained whole.</p>\n<p>As a follower of Sangpotshi, each lifetime they lived saw them growing ever-nearer to enlightenment. They befriended long-lived spirits who were always happy for them to visit in their latest body. As their lives continued on, they eventually attained enlightenment. It was during what would’ve been her final reincarnation that she came to the Tan Sugi monastery and drew Kugaptee’s attention. Though trapped in death below the Tan Sugi when Zhi Hui passed away, Kugaptee crept his influence into Xin Yue’s dreams when her grief was most profound. Over the awful months to follow, the nindoru’s influence over Xin Yue grew. In these dreams, Xin Yue and Kugaptee increasingly engaged in lively debates over the value of reincarnation, and over time, this corruption grew to the point that Xin Yue dedicated herself to the nindoru demigod, whom she had come to consider as the Lord who “opened her eyes to the frivolity of enlightenment.”</p>\n<p>Xin Yue then turned her attention to the few remaining monks at the monastery and began to lure them over to the worship of Kugaptee. However, it wasn’t until Xin Yue offered herself as a sacrifice to the fiend before the other monks’ eyes—only to be reincarnated into her current body—that they converted as well. To them, Xin Yue had revealed that the Tan Sugi monastery wasn’t a place for peace, but a cage-tomb that, if they could release its bound prisoner, would grant great power and rewards immediately, rather than waiting for countless reincarnations for a chance at something they might never even earn.</p>\n<p>Xin Yue’s current body has the form of a human woman with a short build, shoulder-length cropped hair and a long black braid that hangs to her calves. She strikes fearful respect into her followers by saying terrible things with a cheery attitude and a kind smile on her face. Her perpetual politeness isn’t a facade, even as she threatens and promises punishment. While butchering her victims in the most prolonged and painful way possible, she smiles at them and earnestly thanks them for their sacrifice.</p>\n<p>When Governor Heh Shan-Bao’s ritual slew the people of Willowshore and plunged the region into a mindscape, Xin Yue and her monks perished as well. However, they didn’t return to life within the mindscape. Their proximity and devotion to Kugaptee kept them from life, and they’ve spent each cycle of the past 115 years as undead. To Xin Yue, this new body is a shameful and horrific burden, and she only hopes that by helping Kugaptee to achieve what he desires—using the incarnation of his old enemy’s body, now the sugi tree that grows over his grave, as the raw building blocks of a new living body—that she too shall be reborn into a new form. She has little interest in what kind of body she might attain, just that it be one of living flesh.</p>\n<h2>Campaign Role</h2>\n<p>Xin Yue fabricated the circumstances for the Tan Sugi monastery to fall and for Kugaptee to awaken, and she’s been working toward his revival ever since. Like the heroes, Xin Yue has been trapped in the mindscape for the past 115 years, but due to her connection with Kugaptee, she retained the memories of each passing cycle. She’s kept tabs on the townsfolk of Willowshore, but after a century of repeated failures to break their own cycle, she discounted them as a threat to her work. As such, she was truly surprised when she received a vision from Kugaptee that showed the PCs opening the Wall of Ghosts.</p>\n<p>Despite her nearly skeletal, undead appearance, Xin Yue continues to foster her politeness; she doesn’t hide her intent in any way. She has no personal grudge against the heroes. Although she might come across as reasonable, as long as Kugaptee’s presence remains within the mindscape, she can’t be reasoned with to stop her pursuits and fights to the bitter end to achieve her goal.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ExTKQvgLI72XGk98]{Xin Yue}</span>\n    <span>Creature 7</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Undead</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Ren Mei Li": {
              "name": "任美璃 Ren Mei Li",
              "text": "<span><strong>任美璃</strong></span>\n<span class=\"chapter\">柳岸镇的络新妇公主</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-mei-li-ren.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-mei-li-ren.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>任美璃是一位有耐心且狡猾的阴谋家，决心扩大自己在神门的影响范围。她培植不走寻常路的代理人与手段，最终目光锁定在夺取阴司察夕的王座。</p>\n<p>任美璃出生于阴司察夕的宫城，自睁眼起便浸没在络新妇低语的阴谋诡计之中。然而，在她成年不久后，她便对姐妹们的行事方式感到幻灭，主要是因为那妨碍了她沉溺于自己偏爱的乐趣。在预言破灭之年伊始，络新妇宫廷夺取神门的控制权时，任美璃同样残忍且善于操控，宛如她的姐妹们；但岁月将会让这些特质发生变化。</p>\n<p>在让惊恐的臣民俯首称臣、并建立自己在宫廷中的影响力时，任美璃确实感到某种吸引力；但她真正的挚爱是演出。无论是黑焚岗的烟火、皮影戏、剑丝舞剧，还是遍布天夏的各类戏剧艺术，都令她心醉神迷。她乔装为人类女子，离开神门、横跨大陆去观赏最上乘的表演；然而更多时候，当她试图劝诱自己最喜爱的表演者前往神门、为她的姐妹们献艺时，对方都会拒绝。她们告诉她，再多的白银也不值得拿命去冒险踏入那片闹鬼之地；而且她们无法信任该国的络新妇统治者能保证她们的安全——却从未意识到，与她们交谈的那位女子本身就是络新妇。</p>\n<p>任美璃没有作出防御性的回应，而是从他们的角度思考问题，很快便得出结论：表演者的顾虑合情合理。神门确实危险，而且许多络新妇都不可靠。正是在她愿意理解这一视角的过程中，她意识到这里蕴藏着一个能极大巩固自己权力根基的机会。</p>\n<p>任美璃的新理念很简单：若她遵守自己所有的承诺，人们就会明白她值得依靠。若她避免代表其他络新妇作出任何许诺，并明确表示自己不替同族其余成员说话，那么她赢得的信任就只会局限在任美璃本人身上。这种安排既能巩固忠于她之人的忠诚，也能确保他们不信任她的对手。</p>\n<p>若她审慎治理、投入基础改善，并避免对臣民施加过度残酷，那么她的封地将变得更具生产力、也更能盈利，使她能够在自己所爱的奢侈品上挥霍得更为阔绰。感激之情会强化民众的忠诚，让对手更难破坏她的根基，并减少诸如因饥饿与失序而滋生的匪患等问题。久而久之，或许表演者也不会再对受邀到神门分享艺术如此犹豫。</p>\n<p>经过数十年的高强度经营，任美璃已发展出一张可信赖的代理人与代表网络。她挑选代表时首先看重能力——这在神门是极为罕见的——而且大多数人都忠诚效命。这份忠诚是双向的：任美璃会迅速保护自己的资产，因为她明白，整个网络的力量取决于她的代理人是否相信她也会为他们付出同样的努力。</p>\n<p>她的一些仆从是理想主义者，但任美璃本人并非如此。她是一个以自身利益为先的务实主义者；她追求善政，是因为那对她有利，而不是因为她格外关心她的人民。对她而言，改善自己领地之外任何臣民的境遇毫无意义，因为她认为，在神门其他地区，那些络新妇反复无常的残酷与她表面上的仁善形成鲜明对比，正是她的一项关键优势。</p>\n<p>然而，她发现假装并非如此颇有用处。任美璃最终且深藏不露的目标，是从朗洛依夫人手中夺取阴司察夕的丝绸王座。公开场合，她否认自己有此野心，但私下里这已是她多年来的终局计划。为达成此目的，她已在当地农民、野心勃勃的商人以及外国使节之间铺陈基础，让他们相信她登基极可能为神门带来一个开明统治的黄金时代。若她的派系最终登上权力之巅，这些星光般的美梦或许真的会实现——至少在任美璃觉得它们有用的范围内会如此。</p>\n<h2>战役角色</h2>\n<p>任美璃在第12章中是PC的关键盟友，并且可能也会在他们于神门的长期抱负上提供助力。尽管她的动机自私，她的行为却往往让她的人民受益。任美璃本性与其统治实际效果之间的这种二分，可能会为某些团体带来有趣的问题与两难。然而，应当明确的是：无论她采纳这些政策的理由是什么，她的政策确实为困在这片险恶之地的普通人创造出一处相对安全的避风港。</p>\n<p>在这场冒险中，任美璃不会在战斗中与PC并肩作战——同样地，如果他们愚蠢地向她发起决斗挑战，她会尽力避免造成不可挽回的伤害，而是运用魔法尝试缓和敌意，施放 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{Charm} 和 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.qwlh6aDgi86U3Q7H]{暗示术}。若这些手段失败，她会使用 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate} 或白银雾行撤退，给PC时间冷静下来；之后她会尝试通过中间人，或干脆伪装成完全不同的人再次与他们接触。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ONN4yz1NzvvCGBUv]{任美璃}</span>\n    <span>生物 16</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">唯一</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人形</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>Ren Mei Li</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Jorogumo Princess of Willowshore</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-mei-li-ren.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-mei-li-ren.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>A patient and cunning schemer, Ren Mei Li is determined to increase her sphere of influence in Shenmen. She cultivates unorthodox agents and approaches with an eye, ultimately, toward claiming the throne of Yin-Sichasi.</p>\n<p>Born in the palace-city of Yin-Sichasi, Ren Mei Li was immersed in the whispering intrigues of the jorogumo from the time she opened her eyes. Soon after reaching her majority, however, she became disillusioned with her sisters’ ways, chiefly because it impeded her ability to indulge her preferred tastes. When the jorogumo court seized control of Shenmen at the onset of the Age of Lost Omens, Ren Mei Li was as cruel and manipulative as her sisters, but time would see these traits change.</p>\n<p>While securing obeisance from terrified subjects and building her courtly influence did have a certain appeal, Ren Mei Li’s true love was performances. Be they Hei Fengan fireworks, shadow puppet plays, sword-and-silk dance operas, or any of the theatrical arts displayed across Tian Xia, they all delighted her. Disguised as a human woman, she traveled beyond Shenmen and across the continent to attend the finest shows, but more often than not, when she tried to coax her favorite performers to visit Shenmen and perform for her sisters, they refused. No price in silver was worth risking their lives in that haunted land, they told her, and they couldn’t trust the country’s jorogumo rulers to keep them safe, never realizing the woman who they spoke to was a jorogumo herself.</p>\n<p>Rather than respond defensively, Ren Mei Li considered the problem from their point of view and soon concluded that the performers’ qualms were justified. Shenmen was dangerous, and so many jorogumo were unreliable. In her willingness to understand this perspective, she realized there was a great opportunity to strengthen her base of power.</p>\n<p>Ren Mei Li’s new philosophy was simple: if she honored all her promises, then people would learn that she could be relied on. If she refrained from promising anything on behalf of other jorogumo, and indeed made it clear that she didn’t speak for the rest of her kind, then the trust she would earn would be limited to Ren Mei Li personally. This arrangement would both bolster her loyalists’ allegiances and ensure they distrusted her rivals.</p>\n<p>If she governed prudently, invested in basic improvements, and refrained from excessive cruelty to her subjects, then her fiefdom would become more productive and profitable, enabling her to spend even more lavishly on the luxuries she loved. Gratitude would strengthen her people’s loyalty, making it more difficult for her rivals to undermine her and reducing problems, such as banditry, that stemmed from hunger and disorder. And in time, perhaps performers wouldn’t be so hesitant toward invitations to share their art in Shenmen.</p>\n<p>After decades of intensive work, Ren Mei Li has developed a trusted network of agents and delegates. Her representatives are chosen for ability above all, a rarity in Shenmen, and for the most part, they serve faithfully. This loyalty runs both ways: Ren Mei Li is quick to protect her assets, knowing that the strength of her entire network depends on her agents believing she’ll exert similar efforts on their behalf.</p>\n<p>While some of her servants are idealists, Ren Mei Li herself isn’t. She’s a self-interested pragmatist who pursues good governance because it benefits her, not because she particularly cares about her people. Ren Mei Li has no interest in improving the lot of any subject outside her own domain since she considers the contrast between her seeming benevolence and the capricious cruelty of the other jorogumo elsewhere in Shenmen to be one of her key advantages.</p>\n<p>However, she’s found it useful to pretend otherwise. Ren Mei Li’s ultimate, deeply hidden goal is to seize the silken throne of Yin-Sichasi from Lady Lang Loi. Publicly, she denies any such ambition, but it’s secretly been her endgame for years. To achieve this end, she’s laid groundwork among local peasants, ambitious traders, and foreign envoys to view the prospect of her ascension as likely to usher in a golden age of enlightened rule in Shenmen. Should her faction rise to ascendance, these starry dreams might possibly even come true, at least to the extent that Ren Mei Li finds them useful.</p>\n<h2>Campaign Role</h2>\n<p>Ren Mei Li is a key ally for the PCs in Chapter 12, and potentially for their longer-term ambitions in Shenmen. Although her motivations are selfish, her actions tend to benefit her people. This dichotomy between Ren Mei Li’s nature and the actual effect of her rule might present interesting questions and dilemmas for some groups. However, it should be clear that whatever her reasons for adopting them, her policies do create a comparative safe haven for ordinary people trapped in a treacherous land.</p>\n<p>In this adventure, Ren Mei Li doesn’t fight alongside the PCs in battle—likewise, if they foolishly challenge her to combat, she’ll do her best to avoid doing lasting harm, instead using her magic to try to defuse the hostilities using @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{Charm} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.qwlh6aDgi86U3Q7H]{Suggestion}. If these fail, she’ll use @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate} or Silver Mistwalk to retreat and give the PCs time to calm down, after which she’ll attempt to engage with them again via intermediaries or while disguised as a different person entirely.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ONN4yz1NzvvCGBUv]{Ren Mei Li}</span>\n    <span>Creature 16</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "“Old” Matsuki Shou": {
              "name": "“老头”松木胜 “Old” Matsuki Shou",
              "text": "<span><strong>“老”松木胜</strong></span>\n<span class=\"chapter\">备受拥戴的本地老前辈</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-old-matsuki.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-old-matsuki.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>松木胜在10岁稚龄时就已在家族木匠生意里帮工，并参与修建寺院。今年他离99岁生日只差几周；胜是柳岸镇仅存的、亲身经历过村庄全部历史的人类。他怀念朝圣者挤满街道的兴盛岁月，称赞那十年间外出谋生时的同乡工友，并对龙瓦的接管满腹牢骚。</p>\n<p>表面上，老松木是个好斗的老头，更爱酒不爱茶，认定北岭人派系总在搞鬼，并哀叹妓院变成了旅店。私下里，人人都知道他对柳岸镇的文化、传统与人民的未来格外上心。怪物入侵期间，他头脑依旧敏锐专注，组织南岸巩固阵地，为幸存的村民争取宝贵时间，以便想办法夺回柳岸镇。</p>\n<h1>战役用途</h1>\n<p>如果胜成为柳岸镇的临时镇长，他会偏袒南岸的农民与传统。这一发展让PC更容易为即将到来的冬天筹备城镇的粮食储备，但代价是在接下来数月里无法提前着手加固城镇防御。</p>\n<p>当柳岸镇在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}开头恢复安全后，PC可以使用影响力（子系统）与老松木互动，该子系统见于《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》第187–189页。与老松木的影响遭遇是3级挑战，与他进行一次影响轮需要1小时。若任何一次对他施加影响的尝试导致大失败，且PC与他之间少于5点影响点，他不久后就会对该PC使用他的“尊重长辈！”能力。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>松木胜</span>\n    <span>等级 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人生物</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">松木木匠家的粗声家长，也是南岸农民的代言人</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +12（+10 视觉）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>强韧</strong> +10，<strong>意志</strong> +12</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[farming-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:18]（另见下方弱点），@Check[society|dc:16], @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:16]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响技能</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（理解并分享“旧日好时光”的故事），@Check[alcohol-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（分享对喜爱饮品的看法），@Check[diplomacy|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:20|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响 2</strong> 老松木修正了他最初对PC不尊重传统的判断，并承认（哪怕只是在心里）他们其实挺讨人喜欢。这份较好印象的开端使PC在南岸获得1点声望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响 5</strong> 老松木开始喜欢PC，并从他们身上看到了柳岸镇未来的光明希望。为庆祝他希望能发展为长久友谊的关系，他既赠予每位PC一剂自己特制的药酒，也将其配方分享给他们。@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.5lhQ79p0Z3j1VsY3]{松木药酒}。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响 7</strong> 老松木如今完全信任PC，并重视他们的意见。若PC请求他撤回自己竞逐柳岸镇领导之位的主张，他会点头表示理解并照办，相信PC会以柳岸镇的最大利益为念。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>抗力</strong> 老松木鄙夷那些要他信任年轻一代的说辞。在谈话中运用此类主题，会使所有对他施加影响的尝试DC提高2。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>弱点</strong> 对老松木进行发现检定且大成功的PC，会注意到他对精致美食与佳酿的欣赏。若PC请求在他们准备的一顿晚餐上与松木交谈（并成功通过一次@Check[crafting|dc:16]检定令他印象深刻），那么在餐后结束起最多3小时内，所有对他施加影响的尝试获得+1物品加值（若制作精致餐点的工艺检定大成功，则为+2物品加值）。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>背景</strong> 经验丰富的木匠；老松木沉着冷静的天性使他成为天生的领袖。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>外貌</strong> 老松木是位精神矍铄的老人，穿着朴素的工作袍，腰带上挂着多件木工工具。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>性格</strong> 过去他曾更为平和，但在最近十年里老松木变得相当直言不讳。他依旧深深爱着柳岸镇；只是他不再克制，尽情抱怨——因为他觉得自己时日无多。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>惩罚</strong> 老松木在所有影响轮期间都会喝酒。每次影响轮结束后，他必须成功通过一次@Check[fortitude|dc:15]豁免——每增加一轮，DC提高1。若他豁免失败，他会醉得心满意足地昏睡过去，且当天的影响遭遇结束。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.KhGtAbhgupqJyqET]{松木胜}</span>\n    <span>生物 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人生物</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>“Old” Matsuki Shou</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Popular Local Old-Timer</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-old-matsuki.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-old-matsuki.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-6em\" />\n<p>At the tender age of 10, Matsuki Shou was already part of the family carpentry business and participating in the construction of the monastery. A few weeks short of being 99 years old this year, Shou is the only human left in Willowshore who’s experienced the village’s entire history in person. He fondly remembers the vibrant days when pilgrims filled the streets, speaks highly of his fellow migrant workers in the decade when they sought work outside the village, and grumbles about Lung Wa’s takeover.</p>\n<p>Outwardly, Old Matsuki is a belligerent elderly man who prefers alcohol over tea, thinks the Northridge faction is always up to no good, and laments at the brothel’s transformation into an inn. In private, everyone knows he has a soft spot for the future of Willowshore’s culture, traditions, and people. During the monster invasion, his mind remains sharp and focused as he organizes Southbank to fortify their position, buying precious time for the surviving villagers to figure out how they might take Willowshore back.</p>\n<h1>Campaign Use</h1>\n<p>If Shou becomes Willowshore’s interim governor, he favors Southbank’s farmers and traditions. This development makes it easier for the PCs to prepare the town’s food stores for the coming winter, but at the cost of not having a head start at shoring up the town’s defenses in the coming months.</p>\n<p>Once the town of Willowshore is safe at the start of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}, the PCs can attempt to interact with Old Matsuki using the influence subsystem, described on pages 187–189 of the <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>. An influence encounter with Old Matsuki is a 3rd-level challenge, and an influence round with him takes 1 hour. If any attempt to Influence him results in a critical failure and the PCs have fewer than 5 Influence Points with him, he uses his Respect your Elders! ability against that PC soon thereafter.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>Matsuki Shou</span>\n    <span>Level 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Gruff patriarch of the Matsuki carpenters and spokesman for Southbank’s farmers</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +12 (+10 visual)</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Fort</strong> +10, <strong>Will</strong> +12</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[farming-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[perception|dc:18] (plus see Weaknesses below), @Check[society|dc:16], @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:16]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence Skills</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to understand and share stories of the “good old days”), @Check[alcohol-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to share opinions about favorite drinks), @Check[diplomacy|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[intimidation|dc:20|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 2</strong> Old Matsuki revises his initial assumption that the PCs have no respect for tradition and admits (if only to himself) they’re likable sorts. The start of this better impression grants the PCs 1 Reputation Point with Southbank.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 5</strong> Old Matsuki grows fond of the PCs and sees in them a bright promise for Willowshore’s future. To celebrate what he hopes will continue to develop into a lasting friendship, he both gifts each PC with a dose of his special medicinal wine and shares the formula for it with them. @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.5lhQ79p0Z3j1VsY3]{Matsuki's Medicinal Wine}.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 7</strong> Old Matsuki now fully trusts the PCs and values their input. If the PCs ask him to retract his bid for leadership of Willowshore, he does so with a nod of understanding, trusting the PCs have Willowshore’s best interests in mind.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Resistances</strong> Old Matsuki disdains appeals asking him to trust the younger generation. Utilizing such themes in conversation increases the DCs for all attempts to Influence him by 2.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Weaknesses</strong> A PC who critically succeeds at a Discovery check against Old Matsuki notes his appreciation for fine food and drink. If the PCs ask to speak to Matsuki over a dinner they prepare (and succeed at a @Check[crafting|dc:16] check to impress him), all attempts to Influence him for up to 3 hours after the meal concludes gain a +1 item bonus (or a +2 item bonus on a critical success to Craft a fine meal).</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Background</strong> An experienced carpenter, Old Matsuki’s levelheaded nature makes him a natural leader.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Appearance</strong> Old Matsuki is a spry elderly man in a simple work robe with several carpentry tools on his belt.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Personality</strong> A calmer person once upon a time, Old Matsuki has become quite vocal in the last decade. He still deeply loves Willowshore; he just no longer holds back and indulges in complaining as he believes he doesn’t have many years left in him.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Penalty</strong> Old Matsuki drinks wine during all influence rounds. After every influence round, he must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save—the DC increases by 1 with each additional round. If he fails this save, he passes out, happily drunk, and the influence encounter ends for the day.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.KhGtAbhgupqJyqET]{Matsuki Shou}</span>\n    <span>Creature 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Mago Kai": {
              "name": "孙海 Mago Kai",
              "text": "<span><strong>孙海</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">猎鬼的木业大亨</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kai-mago.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kai-mago.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-4em\" />\n<p>孙海一生都在侍奉死者。他出生在由鬼魂统治的司泽城中的一个活人家庭，自幼在恐惧与服从中长大。然而他挺了过来，并一路在城中的官僚体系里向上爬，躲开那些幽灵廷臣腐败的算计。他学会了理解鬼魂，尤其是如何利用它们思维的循环与僵固的执念为自己牟利。尽管他厌恶自己所效力的对象，但他能轻易将这种情绪藏在对他们对手同等的鄙夷之后。当他身边的人不是走狗就是敌人时，他可以相对轻松地对他们的垮台不屑一顾，甚至乐在其中。那并不是幸福的生活，但孙海确实如鱼得水。</p>\n<p>最终，孙海的成功引起了司泽不死统治者周冥瑕的注意。周冥瑕生前无能，死后更甚，她痴迷于将神门的森林彻底砍伐，把木材运回龙华，从帝国首都赚取一大笔财富。孙海很清楚那个传说中的帝国早已不复存在，但木材就是木材，白银就是白银，几份伪造文件就足以让货物卖给邻国，赚上一笔可观的利润。再加上司泽的鬼魂无法亲自核查他的营运情况，他也很容易在各处顺手“抽成”一点。</p>\n<p>对孙海而言，起初只是为了活命的愿望，如今已长成对权力的野心。但最近，就连他的野心也开始让位于另一种东西：希望——希望有朝一日他能拥有足够的资源，将司泽的亡者彻底清除。他竭力压下这种感觉，告诉自己这种感伤会害死人，可他以往的成功让这些偶尔冒出的念头变得难以忽视。他认为自己足够优秀，能够做到这一点，而仅仅是这种想法，就足以让他注定会去尝试。</p>\n<p>为此，孙海已聚集了一小批佣兵、祭司与驱魔人追随他。来自伐木收成的白银足以贿赂任何因而不悦的本地络新妇，其中一些如今甚至与这位木业领主及其小小的军队关系友善。他眼下的挫折令人懊恼，但孙海很早就学会了如何承受打击。他会想出办法的。他一向如此。</p>\n<h2>战役角色</h2>\n<p>PC们首次与孙海对峙时，他会提出停战，因为他迫切想了解那些让他手下驱魔人吃尽苦头的灵体。他对你来我往的讨论没兴趣，只想要答案。若PC们同意与他交谈，他会提出以下问题。他允许每位PC都有机会回答；若至少有一位PC成功，则该问题就会得到令他满意的答复。若PC们有苦迦菩提影响的确凿证据（例如能证明他的一名驱魔人已被一名nindoru替换），则PC们在所有这些技能检定中获得+2环境加值。</p>\n<p><strong> “你们到底想从我这里得到什么？为什么不干脆去你们的来世？是什么让你们如此执着于那座破败小镇？” </strong>用 @Check[deception|dc:27]、@Check[occultism|dc:30] 或 @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:28] 回答。</p>\n<p><strong> “每个鬼都想要东西。要是把你们想要的一切都给你们，活人就什么都不剩了。你们凭什么特别到让我在乎？” </strong>用 @Check[deception|dc:27]、@Check[diplomacy|dc:29] 或 @Check[intimidation|dc:29] 回答。</p>\n<p><strong> “司泽的总督周冥瑕要这些林子。要是我交不出来，她大概会砍了我的脑袋。你们能给我什么，值得我冒这个险？” </strong>用 @Check[diplomacy|dc:29]、@Check[nature|dc:30] 或 @Check[society|dc:28] 回答。</p>\n<p><strong>“嗯，我不知道。要是我放弃计划，我怎么获利？”</strong>用 @Check[crafting|dc:30]、@Check[intimidation|dc:29] 或 @Check[mercantile-lore|dc:27] 回答。</p>\n<p>若PC们在任意问题中提到苦迦菩提，孙海会提出以下额外问题。</p>\n<p><strong> “你们提到的这个邪灵，苦迦菩提。既然他死了，他还能对我们所有人造成什么威胁？砍掉长在他坟上的树，为什么会是坏事？” </strong>用 @Check[occultism|dc:26]、@Check[nindoru-lore|dc:27] 或 @Check[religion|dc:28] 回答。</p>\n<p>若孙海得知PC们曾被困在思维空间里，并且他们掌握了一种可能让整个小镇复活的方法，“拯救”如此多鬼魂的念头会打动他。他会在互动的最后提出以下问题。</p>\n<p><strong> “这么说，要是我允许你们用这个仪式复活，我就算是柳岸镇的英雄了，对吧？那里会有我的位置吗？一个配得上我的天赋与地位的角色？还是说，我会后悔让你们都复活？” </strong>用 @Check[deception|dc:31]、@Check[diplomacy|dc:26] 或 @Check[religion|dc:28] 回答。</p>\n<h3>孙海的决定</h3>\n<p>孙海问完问题后，统计PC们给出的令他满意的回答数量。</p>\n<p><strong>2个或更少满意回答：</strong>“不，我不这么认为。不管哪个行省，你们这些鬼都一个样。”他扛起斧头并发动攻击。</p>\n<p><strong>3或4个满意回答：</strong>“哈！我告诉你们吧。你们把害我损失的都补回来。然后我就关掉那该死的铃，把你们的火焰还给你们。成交吗？”孙海要求PC们归还他们从要塞偷走的任何物品，并补偿他们对唐入造成的任何破坏、他们造成的任何伤害，以及因他们的行动导致的任何死亡。若PC们同意，孙海会信守承诺，关掉守护铃；但即便新近复活的柳岸镇居民提出抗议，他仍会继续伐木作业；这将在冒险路径的终幕中引发后果。</p>\n<p><strong>5或6个满意回答：</strong>“你们知道吗？我不需要这个。我得把几套计划赶一赶，但我还有足够多其他能赚钱的地方。我不干了。给你们。祝你们对付周冥瑕好运。她下一个派来的人会绝望得多。”说完这番话，孙海把敲铃器扔到PC们脚边，走回住处收拾文件与随身物品，并带着他的驱魔人离开。他假装没听见PC们后续的任何问题。PC们有可能在第4幕再次遇到他；若是如此，这种和平解决方式可能会带来意想不到的优势。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.skJTZHJZgIAZ9oGN]{孙海}</span>\n    <span>生物 11</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>Mago Kai</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Ghost-Hunting Lumber Baron</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kai-mago.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kai-mago.webp');width:60%;margin-right:-4em\" />\n<p>For the entirety of his life, Mago Kai has served the dead. Born to a living family in the ghost-ruled city of Sze, he had a childhood defined by fear and obedience. Yet he endured and worked his way up the city’s bureaucracy, dodging the corrupt machinations of its spectral courtiers. He learned to understand ghosts, especially how to exploit their mental loops and static fixations for his own gain. Though he despised those he worked for, he could easily hide it behind his equal contempt for their rivals. When everyone around him was either a lackey or enemy, he could shrug off, even relish, their downfall with relative ease. It wasn’t a happy life, but Mago Kai did thrive.</p>\n<p>Eventually, Kai’s success caught the attention of Chou Mingxia, Sze’s undead ruler. Incompetent in life and doubly so in death, Mingxia was obsessed with the idea of clear-cutting the forests of Shenmen and sending the lumber back to Lung Wa, pulling in a fortune from the empire’s capital. Kai knew well enough the fabled empire was no more, but lumber was lumber, silver was silver, and a few forged documents could see the goods sold to neighboring nations for a tidy profit. With the ghosts of Sze unable to personally check his operations, it was also easy enough to skim a little off the top here and there.</p>\n<p>For Mago Kai, what started as merely a desire for survival has grown into ambition for power. But lately, even his ambition has started to give way to something else: hope—hope that one day he’ll have the resources to purge Sze of the dead. He does his best to squash this feeling, telling himself that sort of sentimentality is what gets people killed, but his previous successes have made such stray thoughts hard to ignore. He thinks he’s good enough to do it, and that alone makes it inevitable that he’ll try.</p>\n<p>To this end, Kai has amassed a small cadre of mercenaries, priests, and exorcists to his cause. Silver from his lumber harvests proved sufficient to bribe any local jorogumo who took umbrage, and some of them are now even on friendly terms with the lumber lord and his tiny army. His current setbacks have been frustrating, but Kai learned long ago how to roll with the punches. He’ll figure something out. He always does.</p>\n<h2>Campaign Role</h2>\n<p>When first confronted by the PCs, Mago Kai calls for a truce, as he’s eager to know more about the spirits who have been giving his exorcists such trouble. He isn’t interested in a back-and-forth discussion and is simply looking for answers. If the PCs agree to speak to him, he asks the following questions. He allows each PC a chance to answer, and if at least one PC succeeds, they answer the question his satisfaction. If the PCs have concrete evidence of Kugaptee’s influence (such as proof that one of his exorcists has been replaced by a nindoru), the PCs gain a +2 circumstance bonus to all these skill checks.</p>\n<p><strong> “What is it you want from me? Why don’t you just move along to your afterlives? What is it that makes you cling to your ruined town so?” </strong> Answer with @Check[deception|dc:27], @Check[occultism|dc:30], or @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:28].</p>\n<p><strong> “Every ghost wants things. If we gave you everything you wanted, there’d be nothing left for the living. What makes you so special that I should care?” </strong> Answer with @Check[deception|dc:27], @Check[diplomacy|dc:29], or @Check[intimidation|dc:29].</p>\n<p><strong> “The governor of Sze, Chou Mingxia, demanded these woods. If I don’t deliver, she’ll probably cut my head off. What’s in this for me that’s worth risking my neck?” </strong> Answer with @Check[diplomacy|dc:29], @Check[nature|dc:30], or @Check[society|dc:28].</p>\n<p><strong>“Hmm, I don’t know. If I were to abandon my plans, how would I profit?”</strong> Answer with @Check[crafting|dc:30], @Check[intimidation|dc:29], or @Check[mercantile-lore|dc:27].</p>\n<p>If the PCs mention Kugaptee in any of their questions, Kai asks the following bonus question.</p>\n<p><strong> “This evil spirit you mention, Kugaptee. What threat does he pose us all if he’s dead? Why would chopping down a tree growing over his grave be a bad thing?” </strong> Answer with @Check[occultism|dc:26], @Check[nindoru-lore|dc:27], or @Check[religion|dc:28].</p>\n<p>If Kai learns that the PCs have been trapped in a mindscape and that they have a method that might be able to return their entire town to life, the idea of “saving” that many ghosts appeals to him. He asks the following question at the very end of the interaction.</p>\n<p><strong> “So, if I allow you to use this ritual to come back to life, I’d be something of a hero to Willowshore, wouldn’t I? Would there be a place for me there? A role worthy of my gifts and position? Or would I regret letting you all come back to life?” </strong> Answer with @Check[deception|dc:31], @Check[diplomacy|dc:26], or @Check[religion|dc:28].</p>\n<h3>Mago Kai’s Decision</h3>\n<p>Once Kai has asked his questions, total the number of satisfactory answers the PCs gave him.</p>\n<p><strong>2 or Fewer Satisfactory Answers:</strong> “No, I don’t think so. No matter the province, you ghosts are all the same.” He hefts his axe and attacks.</p>\n<p><strong>3 or 4 Satisfactory Answers:</strong> “Huh! I tell you what. You make amends for everything you’ve cost me. Then I’ll turn off the damn bell and give you back your flame. Do we have a deal?” Kai demands the PCs return any items they’ve stolen from the fortress as well as compensate him for any damage done to Karahai, any injuries they’ve caused, and any deaths that have resulted from their actions. If the PCs agree, Kai is true to his word and turns off the warding bell, but he does continue his lumber operations despite any protests from the newly resurrected Willowshore residents; this will have repercussions in the final act of the Adventure Path.</p>\n<p><strong>5 or 6 Satisfactory Answers:</strong> “You know what? I don’t need this. I’ll have to rush a few plans, but I’ve got enough other profitable sites. I’m done. Here you go. Good luck with Chou Mingxia. The next person she sends will be a lot more desperate.” With that pronouncement, Kai tosses the bell ringer at the PCs’ feet, walks to his quarters to collect his papers and belongings, and leaves with his exorcists. He pretends not to hear any further questions from the PCs. It’s possible that the PCs might encounter him again in Act 4, in which case this peaceful resolution might result in an unexpected advantage.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.skJTZHJZgIAZ9oGN]{Mago Kai}</span>\n    <span>Creature 11</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Heh Shan-Bao": {
              "name": "和善保 Heh Shan-Bao",
              "text": "<span><strong>和善保</strong></span>\n<span class=\"chapter\">抱恨终天的柳岸镇镇长</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-bao-heh.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-bao-heh.webp')\" />\n<p>如果和善保在现代的天夏仍留有任何痕迹，他本可以很好地作为晚期帝国龙和官员的典型，为历史学家提供范本。他出身于一个由小官僚与公职人员组成的绵延家族。他的科举成绩极为出色。他严苛、专断，熟稔经典，必要时甚至能显得颇具魅力。但他也彻底腐败——这一特质可悲地进一步证明了他在龙和摇摇欲坠的政权中有多么“典型”。他替朋友与上司办理政治人情的习惯，在公众眼中几乎算不上不当之举。然而，他与他人妻子私通的习惯就没那么容易被原谅，并最终成了他的败亡之因——尽管直到善保在一场小规模的官场争执中押错了宝，这一切才真正酿成后果。被降职、遭同僚嘲弄之后，他发现自己竟成了申门偏僻水乡里，柳岸镇这个小村落的卑微镇长。</p>\n<p>尽管他缺点累累（而且确实多得数不清），和善保镇长从未将自己的困境归咎于柳岸镇的居民。村民对和善保所知甚少，只知道他是外来者，而且他们不喜欢他——这反倒让他的流放成了一种重新开始。善保明白，柳岸镇的种种缺陷几乎不能怪镇民——那是治理的问题；而他身为地方官，自当负责补救。若柳岸镇要成为一个配得上他居住的地方，就必须拥有更好的基础设施：贸易路线得以维护，本地产业需要扶持，得设法吸引教育者来教导有前途的年轻人，还必须处理附近谭杉寺废墟之下所埋藏的、挥之不去的邪恶威胁。最重要的是，必须维持帝国的法律与秩序。柳岸镇的偏僻带来了许多本可解决的麻烦，而善保喜欢解决麻烦。</p>\n<p>然而，一切在四年内彻底崩塌——与龙和帝国一起。官吏渎职与臃肿贵族从内部将其腐蚀殆尽，一连串灾害在7106 ic年对任何集中化的帝国权威残影都造成了最后一击。帝国覆灭之后，其边陲被抛下自生自灭。柳岸镇的偏远在申门的强盗与怪物逼近之际，确实让小镇得以保全，但随后消息传开：络新妇已开始掌控申门。和善保无需猜测接下来会发生什么。他的灵性侍从警告他，络新妇会向其臣民索取何等贪婪的贡赋。更糟的是，这个国家的新统治者中，有些还偏爱栖居于申门的恶毒灵体。</p>\n<p>镇长的忧惧再次指向那座破败寺院下方被囚的邪恶。他担心一旦络新妇发现它，后果将不堪设想：无论是这片土地的新统治者惩罚柳岸镇“窝藏”潜在竞争者，还是络新妇统治者利用苦迦菩提来增强自身力量，和善保镇长都将尽快解决这一迫近的难题作为首要之务。</p>\n<p>任何认识和善保的人，都不会称他为有操守之人。然而，与本地伐木头目及其他官员不同的是，他从未动过逃跑、任柳岸镇自取灭亡的念头。相反，他将自己相当扎实的魔法训练用于寻找治愈谭杉树的方法：翻检古老文献，召唤灵体为他出谋划策。他找到的唯一万无一失之法，是一场仪式：捕获一名拥有神秘力量的无辜者，并在圣树根基处以仪式终结其生命。</p>\n<p>和善保镇长摧毁了所有可能用来施行这等可怖仪式的典籍与器具。他的罪过向来只是凡人之罪；但他的骄傲在这种卑劣仪式面前划下了一条绝不可越过的界线。于是，他从内部拆解该仪式，试图以另一种方式重建，使其能够在远方恢复谭杉树，而无需他亲赴那危险之地，也无需牺牲无辜者。</p>\n<p>不幸的是，他严重低估了苦迦菩提的力量。当他施行自以为能强化谭杉的仪式时，所做的不过是让自己直接暴露在苦迦菩提的影响之下。他世俗且沾满罪污的灵魂无力抵抗那魔物，被封印的恐怖将他彻底吞噬。善保所施行、又因其凄惨谋杀而遭玷污的仪式，与苦迦菩提的力量相互交织，向柳岸镇的人民释放出饥饿鬼魂与宁多鲁邪魔的漩涡，将他们尽数屠戮，继而把一切封存在两个彼此分离的思维空间之中——一个属于毫不知情的镇民，一个属于镇长。凭借这两段被封瓶的现实，苦迦菩提被囚的力量便能在年复一年不断重复的岁月里缓慢积蓄，直至最终强大到足以撕裂谭杉的根系，脱困而出，并以转生术重临世间。</p>\n<p>善保如今也被困在他自己的思维空间牢狱中。他带着这份认知度过了多到数不清的循环；但即便到了现在，他仍继续朝着救赎努力——而在没有外界援助的情况下，这是他永远无法达成的目标。</p>\n<h2>战役角色</h2>\n<p>在这条冒险路径中，和善保是个复杂人物——而这是刻意为之。他从来都不是个好人，他作为官员的所作所为，让无数帝国子民的生活更加糟糕。他与苦迦菩提那场注定失败的对抗，直接导致PC的死亡与柳岸镇的苦难。要谴责他并继续前进很容易，而且或许那样的决定也没错。然而，和善保在柳岸镇的所有失败，都直接源自他拒绝为了自身利益而牺牲镇民。他之所以被判永恒的沉沦与湮灭，只因为他试图做正确的事，却缺乏将其贯彻到底的技艺、信念与怜悯——一个悲剧人物，PC可以在适当的时候按自己的意愿谴责或宽恕他。</p>\n<p>PC在第三幕所遭遇的善保版本无法从其牢狱中获救——当PC令柳岸镇迁渡时，善保也将一并重生，但不再是PC在第三幕遇见的那个人。他重返生命时，将以一个被苦迦菩提牢牢奴役的妖骸形态归来——关于他变为妖骸后的命运详情，见第四幕以及第354–355页的相关条目。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.bIoWSQbvs2yeL7PG]{和善保}</span>\n    <span>生物 9</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">类人生物</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>Heh Shan-Bao</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Guilt-Racked Governor of Willowshore</span>\n</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-bao-heh.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shan-bao-heh.webp')\" />\n<p>Had any trace of Heh Shan-Bao survived into modern day Tian Xia, he could’ve served historians well as a model of a late Imperial Lung Wa official. He came from a long family line of minor bureaucrats and government workers. His civil exam results were brilliant. He was strict, authoritarian, and well-educated in the classics, and he could even be charming when he needed to be. He was also completely corrupt—a trait that sadly reinforced how typical he was among Lung Wa’s crumbling regime. His habit of performing political favors for friends and superiors barely registered as improper conduct to the public. However, his habit of carrying on affairs with other people’s wives was viewed less charitably and ultimately proved his downfall, though not until Shan-Bao made the error of backing the wrong horse in a minor government spat. Demoted and mocked by his colleagues, he found himself serving as the petty governor of Willowshore, a village in the backwaters of Shenmen.</p>\n<p>For all his faults (and they were many), Governor Heh never blamed the citizens of Willowshore for his predicament. The villagers knew very little of Heh Shan-Bao, save that he was foreign and they didn’t like him, which meant that his exile served as a fresh start of a kind. Shan-Bao knew that the townsfolk were hardly to blame for Willowshore’s deficiencies—that was an issue of government, and as the local government official, it fell on him to remedy it. If Willowshore was to be a location suitable for him to inhabit, it needed better infrastructure. Trade routes had to be maintained, local industry needed to be promoted, educators would need to be lured in to tutor promising youths, and the threat of a lingering evil buried below the ruins of the nearby Tan Sugi monastery would have to be addressed. Most importantly, imperial law and order needed to be upheld. Willowshore’s obscurity caused numerous problems that could be solved, and Shan-Bao liked solving problems.</p>\n<p>It all fell apart in four years, alongside the Lung Wa empire. Rotted from the inside by government malfeasance and a bloated aristocracy, a series of disasters proved the final blow to any semblance of centralized imperial authority in 7106 ic. In the aftermath of the empire’s fall, its peripheries were abandoned to fend for themselves. Willowshore’s remote nature helped to keep the town safe as the bandits and monsters of Shenmen closed in, but then news spread that jorogumo had begun to take control of Shenmen. Governor Heh didn’t need to guess at what would happen next. His spiritual servitors warned him of the voracious tithes that the jorogumo demanded of their subjects. Worse yet, some of the nation’s new rulers had an affinity for the malevolent spirits that inhabited Shenmen.</p>\n<p>The governor’s fears returned to the imprisoned evil below the ruined monastery, and he worried that, should the jorogumo discover it, the repercussions would be dire. Whether the land’s new rulers punished Willowshore for “harboring” a potential competitor or whether the jorogumo rulers used Kugaptee to bolster their own power, Governor Heh focused on solving this looming problem as swiftly as he could.</p>\n<p>No one who ever knew Heh Shan-Bao would’ve called him a man of character. Yet, unlike the local lumber bosses and other officials, he never once considered fleeing and leaving Willowshore to its fate. Instead, he turned his considerable magical training toward finding a way to heal the Tan Sugi tree, rifling through ancient documents and summoning spirits to advise him. The only surefire method he found was a ceremony that involved capturing an innocent with mystic power and ritually ending their life at the base of the sacred tree.</p>\n<p>Governor Heh destroyed every text and implement that could’ve enacted such an awful ceremony. His sins had always been human, yet his pride drew a sharp line that wouldn’t be crossed when it came to such vile rites. Instead, he deconstructed the rite from within, then sought to rebuild it in a way that would restore the Tan Sugi tree from afar, without the need for him to travel to the dangerous site or to sacrifice an innocent.</p>\n<p>Unfortunately, he vastly underestimated Kugaptee’s power, and when he performed the rite he hoped would bolster the Tan Sugi, all he did was open himself up to Kugaptee’s direct influence. His worldly and sin-stained soul was unable to resist the fiend, and the sealed horror utterly consumed him. The ritual Shan-Bao performed, tainted by his grisly murder, combined with Kugaptee’s power and unleashed a vortex of hungry ghosts and nindoru fiends upon the people of Willowshore, slaughtering them all and then capturing everything in two separate mindscapes—one for the unknowing citizens of the town and one for the governor. With these two bottled realities, Kugaptee’s imprisoned power could slowly build over the repeating years until, finally, he would be strong enough to rip free from the Tan Sugi’s roots and reincarnate into the world.</p>\n<p>Shan-Bao, now trapped in a mindscape prison of his own, has lived with this knowledge for more cycles than he knows, but even now, he continues to work toward redemption—a goal he’ll never achieve without outside help.</p>\n<h2>Campaign Role</h2>\n<p>Heh Shan-Bao is a complex figure in this Adventure Path, and deliberately so. He was never a good man, and his actions as a government official worsened the lives of innumerable imperial subjects. His ill-fated confrontation with Kugaptee is directly responsible for the PCs’ deaths and Willowshore’s plight. It would be easy to condemn him and move on, and perhaps such a decision would be correct. However, Governor Heh’s failures in Willowshore all stemmed directly from his refusal to sacrifice the townsfolk for his own benefit. He’s been condemned to eternal damnation and oblivion solely because he tried to do the right thing but lacked the skill, conviction, and compassion to see it through, a tragic figure whom the PCs can condemn or forgive in time as they see fit.</p>\n<p>The version of Shan-Bao the PCs encounter in Act 3 can’t be rescued from his prison—when the PCs transmigrate Willowshore, Shan-Bao will be reborn as well, but not as the man the PCs meet in Act 3. When he returns to life, he does so as a yohoi firmly in Kugaptee’s thrall—see Act 4 and the entry on pages 354–355 for further details of his fate after transforming into a yohoi.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.bIoWSQbvs2yeL7PG]{Heh Shan-Bao}</span>\n    <span>Creature 9</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "“Granny” Hu Ban-niang": {
              "name": "“太婆”胡板娘 “Granny” Hu Ban-niang",
              "text": "<span><strong>“胡婆婆”胡板娘</strong></span>\n<span class=\"chapter\">退休的帝国卫队长</span>\n</h1>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-granny-hu.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-granny-hu.webp')\" />\n\n<p>胡板娘在司泽作为街头孤儿长大，逐渐把其他孤儿视为自己的兄弟姐妹。她先以敲诈勒索为生，带着他们也带着自己熬到成年，随后又谋得帝国士兵卫队的一席之位。她的兄弟姐妹仍留在犯罪世界里，却始终忠于这位姊妹，充当线人和金主，帮助她在城卫队的阶梯上步步高升。</p>\n<p>为自己终有一日年老体衰、只想享受所积累的财富与权势而早作打算，当龙瓦开始伐木营生时，板娘自愿前往当时仍是“穷乡僻壤”的柳岸镇，担任首任村卫队长。她一干就是二十余年，于7088 ic退休；但到那时，她已对这座曾被她嗤之以鼻的偏僻小镇生出感情，便在退休后留了下来。她刻意塑造“胡婆婆”的形象，装作岁月已磨平她的野心；然而实际上，她掌握着许多人的阴暗秘密，并不惮于利用这些情报操纵他人。</p>\n<h1>战役用途</h1>\n<p>如果胡婆婆成为柳岸镇的临时镇长，她会偏袒北岭人的生意与目标。这一变化会让PC在接下来的数月里更容易加强小镇防务，但代价是难以高效筹备越冬的粮食储备。</p>\n<p>当柳岸镇在@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{第3章}开头变得安全后，PC可以尝试使用影响力（子系统）与胡婆婆互动；该子系统见《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》第187–189页。与胡婆婆的影响遭遇为3级挑战，而与胡婆婆的一次影响轮耗时1小时。若任意一次对胡婆婆的影响尝试导致大失败，且PC与她之间少于5点影响点，她会在不久之后对该PC使用她的“你听说了没？”能力。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>胡板娘</span>\n    <span>3级</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">人形生物</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">退休的龙瓦卫队队长</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>察觉</strong> +11</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>意志</strong> +13</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>发现</strong> @Check[perception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[society|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[underworld-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响技能</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（承认帝国卫队维持治安的主张）, @Check[crafting|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]（准备并奉茶以示手段、博得好感）, @Check[intimidation|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[diplomacy|dc:18|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响力2</strong> 胡婆婆修正了她对PC的最初看法——她原本认为他们大体上要么对她无用、要么可能在谋划损害她的利益。这一更佳印象的开始使PC获得北岭人1点声望点。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响力5</strong> 胡婆婆相信PC把北岭人的最大利益放在心上。她邀请PC加入她的人脉网络，并提议让露达为任何感兴趣的PC施加@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.F4jOdM3qhYELTz1I]{彼岸花刺青}。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>影响力7</strong> 胡婆婆信任PC并重视他们的意见。若PC请求她撤回竞逐领导权的尝试，她会在（几乎）不抱怨的情况下照做，因为她相信PC是在为柳岸镇的最大利益着想。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>抗力</strong> 尽管胡婆婆在法律问题上有着斑驳复杂的过去，她正试图改过自新，并把柳岸镇的安危放在心上。任何试图影响她、且包含贿赂或依赖她犯罪过往的尝试，都会使该检定DC提高2。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>弱点</strong> 虽然胡婆婆更专注于加固柳岸镇的防务，她也清楚小镇将难以维持生计。任何使用欺瞒、交涉或威吓来影响她、且内容涉及对柳岸镇可能面临粮食短缺等问题的担忧的尝试，都会使该检定DC降低2。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>背景</strong> 胡婆婆悲惨的童年把她磨砺成一位工于心计、渴求权力的退休者；只有把柳岸镇的一切事务都攥在手里，她才感到安全。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>外貌</strong> 胡婆婆温和的微笑让人觉得她平易近人，仿佛随时准备倾听你的烦忧；但她眼中那抹坚硬的光芒又告诉你，她绝不是好拿捏的人。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>性格</strong> 尽管举止温顺而有礼，胡婆婆的谋划与散布流言却可能十分狠毒。</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>惩罚</strong> 试图敲诈胡婆婆会适得其反。虽然这不会直接影响影响力挑战，但她会使用她的“真要试试看？”反应，这使她可能在之后与PC的决斗中、当PC尝试对其决斗对手进行一次打击时，再使用她的“你确定要这样？”反应。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.0QfL4oXQrDfhfZDs]{胡板娘}</span>\n    <span>生物 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">独特</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">人类</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">人形生物</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\">\n  <span><strong>“Granny” Hu Ban-niang</strong></span>\n  <span class=\"chapter\">Retired Imperial Guard</span>\n</h1>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-granny-hu.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-granny-hu.webp')\" />\n\n<p>Growing up a street urchin in Sze, Hu Ban-niang came to view other urchins as her siblings. She pulled them and herself through to adulthood by working as a racketeer before securing a position as an imperial soldier guard. Her siblings remained in the criminal world but retained loyalty to their sister and acted as informants and financiers to help her climb the ranks of the city watch.</p>\n<p>Planning ahead for the day when she grew old and frail and simply wanted to enjoy the wealth and power she’d amassed, Ban-niang volunteered to be an inaugural village guard captain in the “backwaters” that was Willowshore when Lung Wa started its lumber operations. Occupying the position for over two decades, Ban-niang retired in 7088 ic but, by that point, had grown fond of the town she’d once dismissed as a backwater and stayed in her retirement. She’s cultivated her image of “Granny Hu,” pretending to let age mellow her ambitions, but in fact, she knows many folks’ shady secrets and isn’t afraid to use this knowledge to manipulate others.</p>\n<h1>Campaign Use</h1>\n<p>If Granny Hu becomes Willowshore’s interim governor, she favors Northridge’s businesses and goals. This development makes it easier for the PCs to bolster the town’s defenses in the coming months, but at the cost of being able to efficiently prepare food stores for the coming winter.</p>\n<p>Once the town of Willowshore is safe at the start of @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog05thewil]{Chapter 3}, the PCs can attempt to interact with Granny Hu using the influence subsystem, described on pages 187–189 of the <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>. An influence encounter with Granny Hu is a 3rd-level challenge, and an influence round with Granny Hu takes 1 hour. If any attempt to Influence Granny Hu results in a critical failure and the PCs have fewer than 5 Influence Points with her, she uses her So Have You Heard? ability against that PC soon thereafter.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>Hu Ban-Niang</span>\n    <span>Level 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Retired Lung Wa guard captain</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Perception</strong> +11</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Will</strong> +13</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Discovery</strong> @Check[perception|dc:18|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[society|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[underworld-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover], @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:16|traits:concentrate,secret,action:discover|name:Discover]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence Skills</strong> @Check[willowshore-lore|dc:14|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to acknowledge the imperial guard’s claim to keep peace), @Check[crafting|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence] (to prepare and serve tea to impress), @Check[intimidation|dc:16|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[diplomacy|dc:18|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence], @Check[deception|dc:20|traits:concentrate,linguistic,action:influence|name:Influence]</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 2</strong> Granny Hu revises her initial opinion that the PCs are largely either useless to her or possibly plotting against her interests. The start of this better impression grants the PCs 1 Reputation Point with Northridge.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 5</strong> Granny Hu trusts that the PCs have Northridge’s best interests at heart. She invites the PCs to become a member of her network and offers to let Luda apply a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.F4jOdM3qhYELTz1I]{Spider Lily Tattoo} on any PC who’s interested.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Influence 7</strong> Granny Hu trusts the PCs and values their input. If the PCs ask her to retract her bid for leadership, she does so without (much) complaint, trusting the PCs have Willowshore’s best interests in mind.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Resistances</strong> While Granny Hu has a checkered past when it comes to the law, she’s trying to turn over a new leaf and keep Willowshore’s safety in mind. Any attempts to Influence her that includes bribing her or relies on her criminal past increases the DC of that check by 2.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Weaknesses</strong> While Granny Hu is more focused on shoring up Willowshore’s defenses, she’s aware that the town will struggle to subsist. Any attempt to Influence her that uses Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation and that involves fears that Willowshore might face food shortages or the like reduces the DC of that check by 2.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Background</strong> Granny Hu’s awful childhood hardened her into a scheming and power-hungry retiree who only feels secure if she has a hold on all Willowshore affairs.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Appearance</strong> Granny Hu’s gentle smile makes her feel approachable, as if she’s ready to listen to your woes, but the hard glint in her eyes lets you know she’s no pushover.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Personality</strong> While mild-mannered and polite, Granny Hu’s schemes and rumor-mongering can be vicious.</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Penalty</strong> Attempting to blackmail Granny Hu backfires. While it has no direct impact on the influence challenge, she uses her Want to Try Me? reaction, which allows her to potentially later use her Are You Sure About That? reaction during the duel against a PC when they attempt a Strike against their dueling partner.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.0QfL4oXQrDfhfZDs]{Hu Ban-Niang}</span>\n    <span>Creature 5</span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait unique\">Unique</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Human</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Humanoid</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Red-Hooded Thatchling": {
              "name": "红头草人 Red-Hooded Thatchling",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Red-Hooded Thatchling\">红头草人</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-red-hooded-tatchling.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-red-hooded-tatchling.webp')\" />\n<p>当一个注定会变成草人的灵魂在极度痛苦的折磨中死去时，他们可能会在死后以红头草人的形态回归。这些复仇的草人在远处看起来像是戴着红色兜帽，但走近后便会揭露可怖的真相——他们的头颅被鲜血浸透。与其他草人不同，红头草人擅长欺诈；他们能通过幻术魔法伪装成活着的类人生物，这使得他们更容易把毫无戒心的旅人引诱进伏击圈。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.N69YhHyRWfpfvESy]{红头草人}</span>\n    <span>生物 2</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">小型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">不死</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪秽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">永远无感</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>草人诅咒会夺走受其影响者的方向感，并由此在神门衍生出一整类侮辱性说法，用“草人感”来比喻某人把事情办成的能力。例如，一个很难交到朋友的人可能会被说成有“草人感的交友能力”；而一个总把饭菜搞砸的人则可能会被说成有“草人感的厨房直觉”。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Red-Hooded Thatchling\">Red-Hooded Thatchling</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-red-hooded-tatchling.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-red-hooded-tatchling.webp')\" />\n<p>When a soul doomed to become a thatchling dies in the throes of great anguish, they can return after death as a red-hooded thatchling. These vengeful thatchlings appear to wear red hoods when viewed at a distance, but up close, the grisly truth—that their heads are blood-soaked—is revealed. Unlike other thatchlings, red-hooded thatchlings are skilled at trickery, and their ability to appear as a living humanoid through illusion magic allows them to lure unsuspecting travelers into ambushes much more easily.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.N69YhHyRWfpfvESy]{Red-Hooded Thatchling}</span>\n    <span>Creature 2</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Small</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Undead</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Forever Senseless</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>The thatchling’s curse robs the sense of direction from those it falls upon, leading to a whole category of insults in Shenmen that compare someone’s ability to get something done to “a thatchling’s sense.” For example, someone who has a hard time making friends might be said to have “a thatchling’s sense of friendship,” while someone who constantly ruins meals might be said to have “a thatchling’s kitchen sense.”</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Thatchling": {
              "name": "草人 Thatchling",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Thatchling\">草人</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-thatchling.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-thatchling.webp')\" />\n<p>在神门的乡间，善解的某些支系警告人们：如果一个注定要转世的灵魂被阻止进入灵魂之河、无法重新加入轮回，会发生什么。这些灵魂会先变得沮丧、困惑，随后因他们觉得自己理应拥有的躯体被剥夺而愤怒，并反过来强迫植被充当他们的新身体。也有人推测，当尸体被埋在浅坟里时，向下生长进遗骸的草根会缠住并捕获灵魂。</p>\n<p>草人很聪明，也有能力说话，但很少这么做——对那些他们觊觎其生命的人，他们通常没什么可说的。偶尔，有草人会试图呼唤他人求助，引诱对方进入一片高草区或矮丛环境中茂密之处，但它们几乎没有欺骗的技能，因此这类伎俩并不能很好地让它们看起来像是真正需要帮助的活生物。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">老友</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>柳岸镇的草人之所以出现，原因很简单：那些通常会在死后转世的灵魂无法如此，因此会起身成为草人。当然，由于每年都会“重置”一切，当年死去并变成草人的人，会在每个夏季的第一天再次作为活人重生，且不记得他们先前那段毁灭的灵魂存在。尽管它们仍受本能驱使去攻击活物，柳岸镇的草人确实也会感到一丝悔意——如果GM认为特别合适，它们对自己生前认识的生物进行攻击检定与豁免骰时，可能会承受–2环境减值。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Thatchling\">Thatchling</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-thatchling.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-thatchling.webp')\" />\n<p>In rural Shenmen, some branches of Sangpotshi warn of what can happen if a soul bound for reincarnation is prevented from entering the River of Souls and rejoining the cycle. These souls become frustrated, confused, and then furious at what they feel is a denial of the body they deserve, and in turn, they force vegetation to serve as their new body. Others theorize that when a body is buried in a shallow grave, the roots of grass growing down into the remains can tangle the soul and capture it.</p>\n<p>Thatchlings are intelligent and capable of speaking but rarely do so—they generally have little to say to those whose lives they covet. Rarely, one might attempt to lure someone into an area of tall grass or dense undergrowth by calling out to them for aid, but they have little skill at deception, so such tactics aren’t particularly effective at making them seem like actual living creatures in need of help.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Old Friends</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>The source of Willowshore’s thatchlings is the simple fact that the souls who would normally have been reincarnated upon death can’t do so, thus rising as thatchlings. Of course, since each year “resets” things, those who died during the year and became thatchlings are reborn alive once more on every first day of summer, with no memories of their previous doomed existence. While still driven by instinct to attack the living, Willowshore’s thatchlings do feel a sense of remorse—if the GM judges it especially appropriate, they might take a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and saving throws against creatures they knew in life.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Stone Spider": {
              "name": "石蜘蛛 Stone Spider",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Stone Spider\">石蜘蛛</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-stone-spider.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-stone-spider.webp')\" />\n<p>将蜘蛛奉为抵御害虫、虫害与一般邪祟之护的传统，远早于当代络新妇的统治时代；石蜘蛛在其中扮演的角色与@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-monster-core-2.Actor.ZLqdudajQtI8dkTT]{石狮}相似。石蜘蛛守护兽常见于城镇与村落入口附近的基座上，伫立不动——有些甚至一站就是好几代——以至于许多当地人早已忘记自家的守护者并非只是装饰品。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.4iZxxQFySmU6EOfn]{石蜘蛛}</span>\n    <span>生物 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">大型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">天界</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">思维空间增益</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>当在现代时代，守护柳岸镇的石蜘蛛“丑小乖”被杀死，且其绑定容器被摧毁时，他们并不会消散。相反，他们会在柳岸镇的思维空间中苏醒，并与自己的容器完全融合。身处思维空间时，丑小乖能像操纵活体一样移动自己的石质身躯。他们始终如同处于“栖居于其容器”状态般运作，并且无法停止“栖居于其容器”。若丑小乖在思维空间中被摧毁，他们将保持被摧毁状态，无法重新构成；不过，若思维空间重置，丑小乖也会随之复活，再次完全“栖居于其容器”。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Stone Spider\">Stone Spider</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-stone-spider.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-stone-spider.webp')\" />\n<p>The tradition of venerating spiders as wards against vermin, pests, and evil in general far predates the modern jorogumo rule, with stone spiders filling a role similar to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-monster-core-2.Actor.ZLqdudajQtI8dkTT]{Stone Lions}. Stone spider guardian beasts can be found perched on plinths near town and village entrances, standing motionless—for generations in some cases—so that many locals have forgotten their local guardian is anything more than a decoration.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.4iZxxQFySmU6EOfn]{Stone Spider}</span>\n    <span>Creature 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Large</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Celestial</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Mindscape Perks</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>When Ugly Cute, the stone spider who protects Willowshore, is slain in the modern era and their bonded vessel is destroyed, they don’t dissipate. Instead, they awaken in Willowshore’s mindscape, fully merged with their vessel. While in the mindscape, Ugly Cute can move their stone body as if it were a living body. They function at all times as if Inhabiting their Vessel, and they’re unable to cease Inhabiting their Vessel. If Ugly Cute is destroyed in the mindscape, they remain destroyed and can’t reconstitute, although if the mindscape were to reset, Ugly Cute would return to life as well, once more fully Inhabiting their Vessel.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Silsyche": {
              "name": "逝宅神 Silsyche",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Silsyche\">逝宅神</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silsyche.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silsyche.webp')\" />\n<p>当一座世代有人居住的房屋被遗弃后，有时建筑本身会因失去家人而悲恸至极，以至于引来一位尚未认领护所的神灵之怜悯。类似于付丧神显现的方式（《怪物图鉴3》276），这种魂魄之力的结合可能会促成逝宅神的形成——一种渴求陪伴的废弃居所之魂魄。逝宅神从不会意图直接伤害那些进入其所由成形之房屋的人。他们只是极度渴望建立联系，却无法理解多数人并不乐见被囚禁。</p>\n<p>逝宅神的真实形态是一名纤细、孩童般的闪烁身影，头饰酷似其最初显现的建筑结构。这些对逝宅神第一座家宅的呈现，映照着他们所渴求的温暖与欢迎，甚至可能展示早已离去的住户所留下的纪念物。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.Qmg2GRJivmrKxJ4C]{逝宅神}</span>\n    <span>生物 6</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">小型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">虚体</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">神灵</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">魂魄</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">额外学识占据范围</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>多数逝宅神会与一座房屋建立羁绊，通常是仅有一到两层的小型建筑。更强大的逝宅神能与更大的结构建立羁绊，例如要塞或城堡，甚至是诸如航行船只之类的大型载具。关于整座城镇被单个极其强大的逝宅神所占据的传说，至今仍在故事中流传。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Silsyche\">Silsyche</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silsyche.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-silsyche.webp')\" />\n<p>When a home is abandoned after it has been lived in for generations, sometimes the building itself mourns the loss of its family so greatly that it attracts the pity of a kami who has yet to claim a ward. Similar to how a tsukumogami manifests (Pathfinder Bestiary 3 276), such a conjoining of spiritual power can result in the formation of a silsyche—a spirit of an abandoned home who craves companionship. A silsyche never aims to outright harm those who enter the homes they form from. They are merely desperate for connection and lack the understanding that most others don’t take kindly to captivity.</p>\n<p>The silsyche’s true form is a slender, childlike shimmering figure with a headpiece resembling the structure they initially manifested from. These representations of the silsyche’s first home reflect the warmth and welcome they yearn for, potentially even displaying mementos of the house’s inhabitants that have long gone.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.Qmg2GRJivmrKxJ4C]{Silsyche}</span>\n    <span>Creature 6</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Small</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Incorporeal</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Kami</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Spirit</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Range of Possession</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Most silsyches bond with a single home, typically a small building with one or two floors. More powerful silsyches can bond with larger structures, like fortresses or castles, or even large vehicles like sailing ships. Legends of entire towns being claimed by a single, incredibly powerful silsyche persist in stories to this day.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Shinigami": {
              "name": "死神 Shinigami",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinigami\">死神</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinigami.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinigami.webp')\" />\n<p>即使是神灵这样的不朽者也无法免于死亡。当一位神灵或同等强大的存在拒绝回应骨园的召唤时，便会召唤死神前来，将这些顽固的灵魂制伏。死神精准而迅捷，以高效而冷静的方式执行死亡的裁决而闻名。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.5GZ9o5DlIQIZgLb8]{死神}</span>\n    <span>生物 17</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">大型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">监察者</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">生命循环的守护者</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>死神负责调查并处理那些扰乱生命自然流动的广泛现象。他们可能被指派去解决问题，或被告知等待、观察，并提供最小限度的援助。尽管大多数死神能在如此漫长的守望中保持公正超然，但也有一些远非无情无感，最终在怜悯或残酷之间动摇。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shinigami\">Shinigami</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinigami.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-shinigami.webp')\" />\n<p>Even immortals such as kami aren’t immune to death. When a kami or equally powerful entity refuses the call of the Boneyard, a shinigami is summoned to bring these stubborn souls to heel. Exact and swift, shinigami are known to dispense the judgment of death efficiently and dispassionately.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.5GZ9o5DlIQIZgLb8]{Shinigami}</span>\n    <span>Creature 17</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Large</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Monitor</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Guardians of the Cycle of Life</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Shinigami are responsible for investigating and dealing with widespread phenomena that disrupt the natural flow of life. They might be tasked with solving the issue or be told to wait, observe, and provide minimal assistance. While most shinigami can retain their impartiality during such long vigils, some are far from emotionless and end up wavering toward mercy or cruelty.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Shimmerthief": {
              "name": "窃光者 Shimmerthief",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shimmerthief\">窃光者</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shimmerthief.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shimmerthief.webp')\" />\n<p>窃光者是失明、形似蜥蜴的穴居生物，对吞食稀有珍馐——光——有着永不满足的渴望。这份饥饿驱使它们离开地下巢穴前往地表觅食，并在所经之处留下片片黑暗。</p>\n<p>窃光者绝非愚笨，但它们更倾向于避开其他有感知生物，因为它们知道许多人会觉得自己令人不适。它们在年纪尚轻时便会独立生活，却也会保护同类；条件允许时，它们会结成小群一同旅行。谨慎的窃光者会尽量避免在繁忙区域吞食光，但这些地方同样最具诱惑力——熙攘的人群意味着更多的光源。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.OoTnmIkunSTCPet3]{Shimmerthief}</span>\n    <span>生物 7</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">野兽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">额外学识替代饮食</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>有些窃光者会逐渐喜好并获得吞食比光更为阴险的能量形式的能力，使它们转而以生命能量或思维能量为食。对大多数窃光者而言，这种行为被视为骇人听闻，也是遭到放逐的原因。具有这些癖好的窃光者是危险的掠食者；它们依然保有吞食光的能力，并会刻意制造片片黑暗，用以困住并吞食受害者。以生命能量为食的窃光者会用其颚部造成虚空伤害；而以思维能量为食的窃光者则会用其颚部造成心灵伤害。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Shimmerthief\">Shimmerthief</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shimmerthief.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-shimmerthief.webp')\" />\n<p>Shimmerthieves are blind, lizard-like cave dwellers with an insatiable yearning to consume the rare delicacy of light. This hunger compels them to travel beyond their subterranean lairs to the surface to feed, leaving pockets of darkness behind as they go.</p>\n<p>Shimmerthieves are far from unintelligent yet prefer to avoid other sapient creatures, aware that many find them off-putting. They become independent at a young age but are protective of their kind, and they travel in small groups when able. Prudent shimmerthieves try to avoid feeding on light in busy areas, but such places are also the most tempting, as bustling populations mean more light sources.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.OoTnmIkunSTCPet3]{Shimmerthief}</span>\n    <span>Creature 7</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Beast</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Alternate Diets</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Some shimmerthieves develop a taste for and the capacity to consume energy forms far more insidious than light, allowing them to instead feed on life energy or thought energy. Such behavior is considered monstrous by most shimmerthieves and is a reason for exile. Shimmerthieves with these proclivities are dangerous predators who maintain the ability to feed on light and purposely create pockets of darkness to trap and feed on victims. A shimmerthief who feeds on life energy deals void damage with their jaws, while one that feeds on thought energy deals mental damage with their jaws.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Path Maiden": {
              "name": "行道女 Path Maiden",
              "text": "<h1 data-split-here=\"Path Maiden\">行道女</h1>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">行道游民</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>行道女几乎总是以女性形态显现。那些以男性形态显现者则被称为行道游民。这些不死生物拥有相同的能力，但往往会走得更远；它们代表的是背弃法拉丝玛作为预言者与命运操弄者的职责，而非背弃她对生与死的司掌。</p>\n</section>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp')\" />\n<p>申门中有些信徒将每一口气息都奉献给 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma}，却在临终的最后一刻违逆女神；他们有时会在死后转化为行道女。所有行道女所穿的衣装，是她们昔日信仰留下的最后残迹，也是一种永恒的提醒，昭示着她们的耻辱。</p>\n<h2>创造行道女</h2>\n<p>最好根据冒险需求来创建自定义的行道女。</p>\n<h3>行道女能力</h3>\n<p>行道女具有虚体、灵体、不死生物与邪秽（特征）特征。所有行道女都会获得以下能力。那些允许豁免骰或法术攻击者，使用《<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>》第121页所列的高DC与高法术攻击调整数值。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>黑暗视觉</strong></p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>心灵感应</strong> 100尺</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>豁免骰</strong> 对抗活力的所有豁免获得+1状态加值</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>虚无医疗</strong></p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>免疫</strong> 流血、死亡效果、疾病、麻痹、毒素、精确、昏迷</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>抗力</strong> 所有伤害5（除力场、幽冥、灵体或活力；对非魔法伤害的抗力加倍）。该抗力在第9级时提升至10，在第16级时提升至15。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.igFRStfWiTekB9cU]{监禁坟墓}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.gTORJ6OyH2GvfJLC]{有限飞行}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.SPNfbhNa46L3V2NQ]{叛教者寿衣}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>异能内在法术</strong> 所有行道女都拥有数量有限的异能内在法术。典型的行道女有6个内在法术——2个法术环阶等于其实际等级除以2（向下取整），然后在接下来低两个法术环阶中各再有2个。此外，所有行道女都拥有以下戏法（以其最高环阶内在法术的等级施放）：幻景、识路术、光亮术、念动手、念动射弹。所有行道女都知晓唤起死灵仪式。</p>\n<h3>特殊能力</h3>\n<p>从以下能力中选择两个；若行道女为16级或更高，也可以选择三个。你也可以自由创造主题相近的能力，用于你自行设计的独特行道女。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.3H0xMglx23V5PP2N]{亵渎灵光}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.VupsXjJEpavg5ByS]{腐化疑心}。</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.UQ2ZvIag5gPL2QiU]{蔑视命运}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.rB3msRRnN5M9z5Vm]{堕化胜利}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.w5wDTUUeGHAAoZH1]{复仇狂暴}</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>行道女</h2>\n<p>下文展示的是一个典型的行道女。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.USMiwD8crKdeFybh]{行道女}</span>\n    <span>生物 12</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">虚体</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵体</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">不死生物</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪秽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo2102-treasure-icon.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">罗网绶带</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>申门的络新妇有时会将这些白与紫的绶带赠予那些向她们求助、希望能联系行道女以寻求建议的人。</p>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Q3ZYTbPGPDG6WINq]{罗网绶带}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">物品 11</span></h2>\n    <ul class=\"traits\">\n      <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">消耗品</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">幻术</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">魔法</li>\n    </ul>\n  </section>\n</section>\n<h1 data-split-here=\"Path Maiden\">Path Maiden</h1>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Path Nomads</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Path maidens almost always manifest in feminine forms. Those who manifest in masculine forms are instead known as path nomads. These undead have the same abilities but tend to travel more widely; they represent turning one’s back on Pharasma’s role as a prophet and manipulator of destiny rather than of her roles over birth and death.</p>\n</section>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-path-maiden.webp')\" />\n<p>Worshippers in Shenmen who devote their every breath to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.deities.Item.QZD0u1jxwz0kj8uI]{Pharasma} only to defy the goddess with their last sometimes transform, upon death, into path maidens. The garments all path maidens wear are the last vestiges of their former faith, a permanent reminder of their disgrace.</p>\n<h2>Creating a path maiden</h2>\n<p>It’s best to create custom path maidens to fill an adventure’s needs.</p>\n<h3>Path Maiden Abilities</h3>\n<p>A path maiden has the incorporeal, spirit, undead, and unholy traits. All path maidens gain the following abilities. Those that allow saving throws or spell attacks use the High DC and High Spell Attack Modifier values, as listed on page 121 of <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Darkvision</strong></p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Telepathy</strong> 100 feet</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Saving Throws</strong> +1 status to all saves vs. vitality</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Void Healing</strong></p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Immunities</strong> bleed, death effects, disease, paralyzed, poison, precision, unconscious</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Resistances</strong> All damage 5 (except force, ghost touch, spirit, or vitality; double resistance to non-magical). This resistance increases to 10 at 9th level and 15 at 16th level.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.igFRStfWiTekB9cU]{Imprisoning Grave}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.gTORJ6OyH2GvfJLC]{Limited Flight}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.SPNfbhNa46L3V2NQ]{Apostate's Shroud}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Occult Innate Spells</strong> All path maidens have a limited selection of occult innate spells. A typical path maiden has six innate spells—two of a spell rank equal to their actual level divided by 2 (rounded down), and then two more for the next two spell ranks below that. In addition, all path maidens have the following cantrips (cast at a level equal to their highest-rank innate spell): figment, know the way, light, telekinetic hand, and telekinetic projectile. All path maidens know the create undead ritual.</p>\n<h3>Special Abilities</h3>\n<p>Select two of the following abilities, or potentially three if the path maiden is 16th level or higher. Feel free to create similarly-themed abilities for unique path maidens of your own design.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.3H0xMglx23V5PP2N]{Blasphemous Aura}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.VupsXjJEpavg5ByS]{Corrupting Doubt}.</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.UQ2ZvIag5gPL2QiU]{Scorn Fate}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.rB3msRRnN5M9z5Vm]{Sour Victory}</p>\n<p class=\"hanging-indent\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.w5wDTUUeGHAAoZH1]{Vengeful Frenzy}</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc>path maiden</h2>\n<p>Presented below is a typical path maiden.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.USMiwD8crKdeFybh]{Path Maiden}</span>\n    <span>Creature 12</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Incorporeal</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Spirit</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Undead</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo2102-treasure-icon.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Gossamer Sash</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>The jorogumo of Shenmen sometimes grant these white and violet sashes to those who ask them for aid in contacting path maidens for advice.</p>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Q3ZYTbPGPDG6WINq]{Gossamer Sash}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Item 11</span></h2>\n    <ul class=\"traits\">\n      <li class=\"trait rare\">rare</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">Consumable</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">Illusion</li>\n\n      <li class=\"trait\">Magical</li>\n    </ul>\n  </section>\n</section>"
            },
            "Impersonator Roles": {
              "name": "模仿者角色 Impersonator Roles",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Impersonator Roles\">模仿者角色</h3>\n<p>无面鬼模仿者会扮演三种角色之一；你需要根据被模仿的PC来决定每个模仿者的角色。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.AsfjgDmWkUxPI6m8]{无面鬼模仿者（武斗）}</h2>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.3KNblm2fWM6XLiS7]{无面鬼模仿者（技能）}</h2>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>施法模仿者</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.QSa1PbcvbgDv8Zpr]{无面鬼模仿者（奥术）}</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.dqsQutshiegWaFPQ]{无面鬼模仿者（神术）}</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.Mt053Q3jCVLXp6us]{无面鬼模仿者（秘术）}</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.6UkZJRICusE2EOhS]{无面鬼模仿者（原初）}</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Impersonator Roles\">Impersonator Roles</h3>\n<p>A noppera-bo impersonator plays one of three roles; you’ll need to decide what each impersonator’s role is depending on the PC being impersonated.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.AsfjgDmWkUxPI6m8]{Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Martial)}</h2>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.3KNblm2fWM6XLiS7]{Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Skilled)}</h2>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc>Spellcasting Impersonator</h2>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.QSa1PbcvbgDv8Zpr]{Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Arcane)}</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.dqsQutshiegWaFPQ]{Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Divine)}</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.Mt053Q3jCVLXp6us]{Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Occult)}</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\" style=\"padding-left:4ch\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.6UkZJRICusE2EOhS]{Noppera-Bo Impersonator (Primal)}</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Noppera-bo Impersonator": {
              "name": "无面鬼模仿者 Noppera-bo Impersonator",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Noppera-bo Impersonator\">无面鬼模仿者</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-impersinator.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-impersinator.webp')\" />\n<p>无面鬼是没有面孔的妖怪，以戏弄他人为乐。本次冒险中出现的无面鬼模仿者，是苦迦菩提在总督和善保的思维空间中残留存在的直接具现。当这一次的思维空间循环开始时，居住在该思维空间里的那些重复PC与其他镇民一样——虚幻但无害。随着PC在柳岸镇的思维空间中力量增长，和善保思维空间中的邪恶思想能量产生反应，将PC的复制体转化为危险的怪物：无面鬼模仿者。</p>\n<h3>额外学识调整模仿者</h3>\n<p>由于每个<em>鬼季</em>战役中的PC组合各不相同，此处的数据应按需调整，以尽可能贴近每名PC。无需过于担心完全匹配每个角色的规则选项，因为怪物遵循的规则与PC不同——相反，应着眼于如何以能让这些生物像怪物般复制体的方式来呈现它们。每个无面鬼模仿者都没有脸，但它们的道具与装备应当与PC抵达和善保的思维空间时所拥有的一模一样。当然，这些装备的大部分都只是幻象的一部分——当无面鬼模仿者被杀死时，它们的道具会移位并变形为破烂、破损的道具，仅在模糊的程度上类似于各个PC所携带与使用的物品。</p>\n<p>请注意，你可以使用<em>Pathfinder GM Core</em>中关于怪物制作的规则，调整下方给出的无面鬼模仿者的数据，以挑战不同等级的其他PC。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.AsfjgDmWkUxPI6m8]{无面鬼模仿者}</span>\n    <span>生物 6</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">异怪</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">冒充NPC</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>本次冒险中的无面鬼模仿者专注于复制PC，但它们同样擅长在世界中复制并取代NPC。有时，无面鬼模仿者以伪装NPC、身居要职的身份所扮演的角色，能持续多年，甚至几十年。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Noppera-bo Impersonator\">Noppera-bo Impersonator</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-impersinator.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-noppera-bo-impersinator.webp')\" />\n<p>Noppera-bos are faceless yokai who delight in tricking others. The noppera-bo impersonators present in this adventure are direct manifestations of Kugaptee’s lingering presence in Governor Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape. When this latest mindscape cycle began, the duplicate PCs who dwelled in this mindscape were like the other townsfolk—phantasmal but harmless. As the PCs grew in power in the Willowshore mindscape, the sinister thought energy in Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape reacted and transformed the PCs’ duplicates into dangerous monsters: noppera-bo impersonators.</p>\n<h3>Impersonator Adjustments</h3>\n<p>Since the exact mix of PCs in each <em>Season of Ghosts</em> campaign will vary, the statistics here should be adjusted as needed to match each PC as closely as possible. Don’t worry too much about exactly matching each character’s rules choices since monsters follow different rules than PCs do—rather, look at ways you can present these creatures in ways that make them feel like monstrous duplicates. Each noppera-bo impersonator is faceless, but their gear and equipment should look identical to what the PCs have when they arrive in Heh Shan-Bao’s mindscape. Of course, the bulk of this equipment is all part of the illusion—when a noppera-bo impersonator is slain, their gear shifts and transforms into ragged, broken props that only vaguely resemble the items carried and used by each PC.</p>\n<p>Note that you can adjust the statistics of the noppera-bo impersonator presented below, using the rules for monster creation found in <em>Pathfinder GM Core</em> to challenge other PCs of different levels.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.AsfjgDmWkUxPI6m8]{Noppera-bo Impersonator}</span>\n    <span>Creature 6</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Aberration</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Impersonating NPCs</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>The noppera-bo impersonators in this adventure focus on duplicating PCs, but they’re just as adept at duplicating and replacing NPCs in the world. Sometimes, a noppera-bo impersonator’s role as a disguised NPC in a position of power can last for years or even decades.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Noppera-bo Occultist": {
              "name": "无面鬼秘术师 Noppera-bo Occultist",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Noppera-bo Occultist\">无面鬼秘术师</h2>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp');width:40%\" />\n<p>一些无面鬼会运用其与生俱来的魔法，以进一步恐吓受害者。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.zhw2TOrXkWyvle5S]{无面鬼秘术师}</span>\n    <span>生物 2</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">异怪</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">无面鬼起源</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>关于无面鬼的起源有许多理论——从变形能力出错的化狸，到被诅咒扭曲的人形生物，再到自然诞生的妖怪。有些人甚至推测，这种状态曾经是一种可传播的诅咒，如同兽化症一般。多数无面鬼不记得自己的起源，并且往往更热衷于假扮成完全不同的其他人。</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Noppera-bo Occultist\">Noppera-bo Occultist</h2>\n\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp\" data-tooltip alt=\"\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-noppera-bo-occultist.webp');width:40%\" />\n<p>Some noppera-bos harness their natural magic to further frighten victims.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.zhw2TOrXkWyvle5S]{Noppera-bo Occultist}</span>\n    <span>Creature 2</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n\n    <li class=\"trait\">Aberration</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Noppera-bo Origins</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>There are many theories on the origins of noppera-bos—from tanuki whose Change Shape ability went wrong, to humanoids who were warped by curses, to naturally spawning yokai. Some even theorize this condition was once a transmissible curse like lycanthropy. Most noppera-bos don’t recall their origins and are often more interested in pretending to be someone else entirely.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Noppera-bo Trickster": {
              "name": "无面鬼骗子 Noppera-bo Trickster",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>无面鬼骗子</h1>\n<p>这些无面鬼已精通伪装的艺术。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.APu2EqTJ4QdHkwtR]{无面鬼骗子}</span>\n    <span>生物 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">畸变</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Noppera-bo Trickster</h1>\n<p>These noppera-bos have mastered the art of disguise.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.APu2EqTJ4QdHkwtR]{Noppera-bo Trickster}</span>\n    <span>Creature 1</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Aberration</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Noppera-bo Grunt": {
              "name": "无面鬼士兵 Noppera-bo Grunt",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>无面鬼士兵</h1>\n\n<p>无面鬼士兵缺乏必要的社交礼仪，无法用他人的脸完全伪装自己。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.52dTAJPXCnE48a5a]{无面鬼士兵}</span>\n    <span>生物 0</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">畸变</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-noppera-bo-grunt.webp\" title=\"Noppera-bo Grunt\" data-tooltip=\"Noppera-bo Grunt\" alt=\"Noppera-bo Grunt\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-noppera-bo-grunt.webp');width:40%\" />\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Noppera-bo Grunt</h1>\n\n<p>Noppera-bo grunts lack the social graces necessary to fully disguise themselves with another person’s face.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.52dTAJPXCnE48a5a]{Noppera-bo Grunt}</span>\n    <span>Creature 0</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Aberration</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>"
            },
            "Noppera-bo": {
              "name": "无面鬼 Noppera-bo",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>无面鬼</h1>\n<p>无面鬼从背后看起来像是普通人，甚至可能长得像你认识的人——直到它们转过身来，露出一张没有任何五官的脸。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">炉火纯青的专业人士</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>典型的无面鬼残忍成性，乐于以惊吓或折磨类人生物为乐，但它们并非全都沉溺于邪恶。有些无面鬼更喜欢当恶作剧者，用自己的能力去欺骗与捉弄；而更为罕见的无面鬼则用能力去致敬并崇拜自己钦佩之人，同时把自己的时间专注于提升自身在艺术上的技能，或制作和平之器。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Noppera-bo</h1>\n<p>Noppera-bos appear to be regular humans from behind, and might even resemble someone you know, until they turn to reveal a featureless face.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Consummate Professionals</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>While the typical noppera-bo is cruel and revels in the act of frightening or tormenting humanoid creatures, not all of them wallow in evil. Some noppera-bos prefer roles as pranksters and use their abilities to trick and tease, while even rarer noppera-bos use their abilities to honor and idolize those they admire while focusing their own time on developing their skills at art or crafting tools of peace.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Argyrzei (Headless Nindoru)": {
              "name": "稽折魔（无头灵堕魔） Argyrzei (Headless Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>稽折魔（无头灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-argyrzei.webp\" title=\"Argyrzei\" data-tooltip=\"Argyrzei\" alt=\"Argyrzei\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-argyrzei.webp')\" />\n<p>大多数灵堕魔会被银伤害，但稽折魔不会。相反，稽折魔会把银当作传播病痛与折磨的方法，并借此操弄那些在不知不觉间落入其受感染赋礼诅咒之人的心智。它们乐于乔装打扮，然后向受害者出售或赠送带感染的银。其他灵堕魔尤其畏惧稽折魔对银的精通，因为它们知道稽折魔能够用银刃造成痛苦的创口。</p>\n<p>稽折魔外形类人，但双脚朝后，且没有头。它们发着红光的断颈里塞满了各式各样的刀具、刃器与金属碎片。这些灵堕魔象征着艺术被创造、毁灭，并被回收再制成新艺术的循环。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.1zClr6JrKhMo2xCu]{稽折魔}</span>\n    <span>生物 13</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪秽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">祸银</h2>\n  </div>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h3 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">感染之银</span> <span class=\"keepme\">诅咒 13</span></h3>\n    <ul class=\"traits\">\n      <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n      <li class=\"trait\">诅咒</li>\n      <li class=\"trait\">魔法</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>使用</strong> 诅咒银制物品</p>\n    <hr />\n    <p class=\"no-indent\">携带感染之银1分钟后，它会与你纠缠在一起。你陷入 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{笨拙 1}，并在诅咒持续期间一直如此。只要你仍受诅咒影响，你对抗由灵堕魔制造的心灵效果时的所有豁免骰都会承受–2状态减值。</p>\n  </section>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Argyrzei (Headless Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-argyrzei.webp\" title=\"Argyrzei\" data-tooltip=\"Argyrzei\" alt=\"Argyrzei\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-argyrzei.webp')\" />\n<p>Most nindorus are harmed by silver, but not the argyrzei. Instead, argyrzeis use silver as a method of spreading sickness and pain, and to help them manipulate the minds of those who unwittingly fall under the curse of their infected gifts. They delight in disguising themselves and then selling or giving infected silver to victims. Other nindorus particularly fear argyrzeis for their mastery over silver, knowing that they’re capable of causing painful wounds with their silver blades.</p>\n<p>Argyrzeis appear humanoid, but their feet point backward, and they have no heads. Their glowing red neck stumps are stuffed with a wide assortment of knives, blades, and shards of metal. These nindorus represent the cycle of art being created, destroyed, and recycled into new art.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.1zClr6JrKhMo2xCu]{Argyrzei}</span>\n    <span>Creature 13</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Cursed Silver</h2>\n  </div>\n  <section class=\"action\">\n    <h3 class=\"no-toc split\"><span class=\"keepme\">Infected Silver</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Curse 13</span></h3>\n    <ul class=\"traits\">\n      <li class=\"trait rare\">rare</li>\n      <li class=\"trait\">Cursed</li>\n      <li class=\"trait\">Magical</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Usage</strong> curses silver item</p>\n    <hr />\n    <p class=\"no-indent\">After 1 minute of carrying infected silver, it fuses to you. You become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{Clumsy 1} and remain so as long as the curse persists. As long as you remain cursed, you take a –2 status penalties to all saving throws against mental effects created by nindorus.</p>\n  </section>\n</section>"
            },
            "Shisagishin (Crooked Nindoru)": {
              "name": "煞星魔（畸形灵堕魔） Shisagishin (Crooked Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>煞星魔（畸形灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shisagishin.webp\" title=\"Shisagishin\" data-tooltip=\"Shisagishin\" alt=\"Shisagishin\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shisagishin.webp')\" />\n<p>煞星魔乐于渗透进某个社群，然后把自己伪装成某位挚爱之人或受人爱戴的公众人物那可怖腐烂或残缺的遗骸——只为在葬礼服务期间以其真正形态骤然复活（一个多臂的人形体，空洞的头颅从内部发光，如同灯笼）。煞星魔体现了腐朽孕育新生的循环。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.MNqc1mJwPOOfjoVr]{Shisagishin}</span>\n    <span>生物 12</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪秽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">手作栖地</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>煞星魔更喜欢在本就冲突频仍、事故隐患重重的区域游荡，但若有需要，它也乐于亲手打造这样的地点。它可能会向水井投放毒素、把疾病带给健康的家畜，甚至与腐败的人类合作——只要这能换来杀戮的自由。被诅咒的小镇或闹鬼的道路，有时便是这类煞星魔的游乐场。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Shisagishin (Crooked Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shisagishin.webp\" title=\"Shisagishin\" data-tooltip=\"Shisagishin\" alt=\"Shisagishin\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-shisagishin.webp')\" />\n<p>The shisagishin takes delight in infiltrating a community and then disguising themself as the horribly decayed or mutilated remains of a loved one or adored public figure, only to spring to life in their true form (a many-limbed humanoid with a hollow head that glows from within like a lantern) during funeral services. A shisagishin epitomizes the cycle of decay giving rise to new life.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.MNqc1mJwPOOfjoVr]{Shisagishin}</span>\n    <span>Creature 12</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Handmade Habitats</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>A shisagishin prefers to roam areas already rife with conflict and potential accidents, but they’ll happily create such a location if needed. They might poison wells, introduce disease to healthy livestock, or even collaborate with corrupt humans if it means the freedom to kill. Cursed towns or haunted roads are sometimes the playground of such a shisagishin.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Akashti (Sobbing Nindoru)": {
              "name": "恪尸魔（哭泣灵堕魔） Akashti (Sobbing Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>恪尸魔（哭泣灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-akashti-nindoru.webp\" title=\"Akashti\" data-tooltip=\"Akashti\" alt=\"Akashti\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-akashti-nindoru.webp')\" />\n<p>恪尸魔是善于操控的邪魔，以哀悼之人为食；它们会化作最近死去的挚爱之人，以便潜入家庭，随后谋杀并吞噬悲恸家庭成员转世的灵魂。恪尸魔有时被称为“复制尸体”，其真身看起来像一具覆着皮肤的骷髅，手指上长着锋利的爪，鲜血般的泪水从其无眼睑的眼中滴落。它的头骨像碗一样敞开，里面栖着一把把深红色的蝴蝶。当恪尸魔躲藏在其显现出的躯体之内时，仔细调查有时能揭露真相：那位“死而复生”的挚爱之人的头皮会微微起伏鼓胀，仿佛其中的蝴蝶在扭动翻搅。</p>\n<p>恪尸魔体现了哀伤的复杂循环。虽然它们通常更喜欢独自行动，但若某地遭受了重大灾害，尸体众多——因此哀悼者也众多——煞星魔招募数只恪尸魔来协助也并非闻所未闻，以便加以利用。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>恪尸魔</span>\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ozi0MnBHVjQQbfNJ]{Akashti}</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不圣</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">额外学识已死的入侵者</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>有时，恪尸魔伏击并谋杀目标并非为了沉浸于其挚爱之人的悲恸之中，而是为了取而代之，化作其形，从内部渗透某个组织，腐化既有的同袍情谊。然而，这些恪尸魔终究会厌倦欺瞒，并将它们的新盟友引入陷阱，任其被屠戮。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Akashti (Sobbing Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-akashti-nindoru.webp\" title=\"Akashti\" data-tooltip=\"Akashti\" alt=\"Akashti\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-akashti-nindoru.webp')\" />\n<p>Akashtis are manipulative fiends who prey on those in mourning; they assume the form of a recently deceased loved one so they can infiltrate homes, then murder and consume the souls of grieving families. Sometimes called a “copycorpse,” an akashti in their true form appears as a skin-covered skeleton with sharp talons on their fingers and tears of blood dripping from their lidless eyes. Their skull appears open like a bowl, and inside nest handfuls of crimson butterflies. When an akashti hides within their manifested body, close investigation can sometimes reveal the truth when the scalp of the supposed beloved one returned to life seems to subtly ripple and bulge as the butterflies within writhe.</p>\n<p>Akashtis embody the complex cycle of grief. While they typically prefer to work on their own, it’s not unheard of for a shisagishin to recruit the aid of a few akashtis when a region has suffered a great disaster, and there are a large number of bodies—and thus a large number of mourners—to take advantage of.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>Akashti</span>\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ozi0MnBHVjQQbfNJ]{Akashti}</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Deathly Invaders</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Sometimes, akashtis ambush and murder targets not to bask in the grief of their loved ones, but instead to assume their form and infiltrate an organization from within to corrupt established bonds of camaraderie. Inevitably, though, these akashtis grow bored with deception and lead their new allies into a trap for slaughter.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Kagekuma (Lurking Nindoru)": {
              "name": "痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔） Kagekuma (Lurking Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kagekuma-nindoru.webp\" title=\"Kagekuma\" data-tooltip=\"Kagekuma\" alt=\"Kagekuma\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kagekuma-nindoru.webp')\" />\n<p>痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）游离于社会边缘，潜伏在其偏爱猎物——工人阶级与受压迫者——的阴影之中。在某些地区，它们被称为“影祟”。这种灵堕魔能够在拥挤人群中化身为毫不起眼的角色，使其即便在有人居住的区域也能觅食。痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）的外形是一个弓背的人形生物，长颈獠口；但当它们背着一捆包裹时，生物的头与颈会紧紧缩入双肩之间，从而被完全遮蔽。痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）体现了在复杂关系进程中，信任一次次建立又一次次破损的循环。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.183L006AcuLnHJbY]{痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）}</span>\n    <span>生物 8</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">恶魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪秽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">额外学识痂苦魔的捆子</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>痂苦魔（潜伏灵堕魔）的捆子不仅仅是伪装与护甲——它还是一种具象的标记，表明它们夺去了多少性命，以及它们吞啜了多少转世的灵魂。无论这捆子由稻草、绳索、头发或其他材料构成，其中每一段都象征着某种“死神的收割”；捆子里的每一缕都代表一条被这灵堕魔斩断并收集的隐喻生命线——以至于被夺去的无数生命，反而淹没了灵堕魔自身在世间的存在感。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Kagekuma (Lurking Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kagekuma-nindoru.webp\" title=\"Kagekuma\" data-tooltip=\"Kagekuma\" alt=\"Kagekuma\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90198-kagekuma-nindoru.webp')\" />\n<p>A kagekuma exists in the periphery of society, lurking in the very shadows of their favored prey—the working class and downtrodden. Known in some regions as “shadefiends,” this nindoru’s ability to appear as uninteresting figures in the crowd allows them to feed even in populated areas. A kagekuma appears as a hunched over humanoid with a long neck and a fanged mouth, but when wearing a bundle, the creature’s head and neck tuck in tight between their shoulders to become entirely obscured. The kagekuma personifies the cycle of trust being built and broken over and over again through the course of a complex relationship.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.183L006AcuLnHJbY]{Kagekuma}</span>\n    <span>Creature 8</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Kagekuma Bundles</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>A kagekuma’s bundle is more than just a disguise and armor—it’s a physical indication of how many lives they’ve cut short and how many souls they’ve supped upon. Whether the bundle is composed of straw, ropes, hair, or other materials, the individual lengths symbolize a sort of “reaper’s harvest,” with each strand in the bundle representing a metaphorical lifeline that the nindoru has severed and collected—to an extent that the multitude of lives taken overwhelms the nindoru’s own presence in the world.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Ijda (Forgetful Nindoru)": {
              "name": "爱怛魔（健忘灵堕魔） Ijda (Forgetful Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>爱怛魔（健忘灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-ijda.webp\" title=\"Ijda\" data-tooltip=\"Ijda\" alt=\"Ijda\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-ijda.webp')\" />\n<p>爱怛魔是健忘的生物。它们诞生于那些曾经开悟、却又背弃开悟并放弃自己在转世轮回中职责的转世的灵魂；它们诅咒自身存在的徒劳，并以引导他人走向同样的命运为乐。</p>\n<p>爱怛魔看上去是高耸的人形，其身体不断迸裂出灵堕魔蝴蝶。它们的手臂过于修长且严重破损，扭动起来更像触手，使其战斗风格令人不安，并拥有比大多数大型生物更远的触及。它们身披由发霉稻草编成的衣物与斗篷，挥舞着破损的长剑，碎裂的剑刃仍大致悬浮在原位。它们最令人毛骨悚然的特征是完全没有头；本该是头的位置，取而代之的是一只柳条编成的笼子，里面充满翻涌的蝴蝶云团。然而它们依旧能看、能听、能说，仿佛头颅仍在原处一般。</p>\n<p>由于形成时没有头，甚至没有大脑，爱怛魔的心智由其头笼中的蝶群或从其身体迸出的蝶群共享；而每当这些昆虫中的一只逃逸并消散，这些健忘的魔物就会失去一个潜在的念头。它们无法学习新事物，所采取的任何动作都源自刻进其灵魂的记忆，或是它们盲目遵从的、来自其他灵堕魔或它们已接受为上级的生物的指令。它们的移动、言语与反应动作（）全都通过一种“肌肉记忆”来完成，这种记忆基于其灵魂认为自己应当如何回应外界刺激。结果是，其中大多数如今都充当残暴的守卫，因为它们的健忘也使其无法睡眠术。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.QCTOHTwnEo6eq82T]{爱怛魔}</span>\n    <span>生物 6</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">大型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">亵渎</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">偏好武器</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>此处展示的若干灵堕魔会偏好挥使特定类型的武器，甚至可能拥有与该类武器相关联的特殊能力。使用不同武器的灵堕魔仍然可以运用这些相关能力，但应视情况对该能力的叙述风味做出相应调整。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Ijda (Forgetful Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-ijda.webp\" title=\"Ijda\" data-tooltip=\"Ijda\" alt=\"Ijda\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-ijda.webp')\" />\n<p>Ijdas are creatures of forgetfulness. Born from souls who were once enlightened but then renounced it and their role in the cycle of reincarnation, they curse the futility of their existence and find pleasure in leading others to the same fate.</p>\n<p>Ijdas appear as towering humanoids, their bodies constantly bursting with nindoru butterflies. Their arms are overly long and so broken as to writhe more like tentacles, affording them an unsettling combat style with greater reach than most large creatures enjoy. They wear clothing and capes made of moldy straw and wield broken swords whose shattered blades still float roughly in place. Their most unsettling features are their complete lack of heads; instead, where a head should be sits a wicker cage filled with a writhing cloud of butterflies. Yet still, they see, hear, and speak without issue, as if their heads remained in place.</p>\n<p>Formed without heads or even brains, an ijda’s mind is shared among the flocks of butterflies in their head cages or bursting from their bodies, and as each of these insects escapes and fades away, these forgetful fiends lose another potential thought. Unable to learn new things, any actions they take stem from memories etched into their souls or directives they blindly follow from other nindorus or creatures they’ve come to accept as superiors. Their movements, words, and reactions are all conducted via a type of muscle memory based on how their souls believe they should respond to their external stimuli. As a result, most now serve as brutal guardians since their forgetfulness also prevents them from being able to sleep.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.QCTOHTwnEo6eq82T]{Ijda}</span>\n    <span>Creature 6</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Large</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Weapons of Choice</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Several of the nindorus presented here have preferred types of weapons to wield and might even have special abilities associated with that type of weapon. A nindoru who wields a different weapon can still make use of those associated abilities, but the flavor of that ability should be adjusted as appropriate.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Guhdggi (Wandering Nindoru)": {
              "name": "孤寂魔（游荡灵堕魔） Guhdggi (Wandering Nindoru)",
              "text": "<div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">灵堕魔叛徒</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>尽管大多数灵堕魔在本质上纯粹邪恶且不洁，但传说中有极其罕见的灵堕魔设法逃离自身天性并得以升华，在死后转生为神灵或其他更仁善的魂魄，并在这一过程中摆脱灵堕魔特征。当然，这些“叛徒”在那些被抛下的灵堕魔眼中，被视为能想象到的最美味佳肴。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>孤寂魔（游荡灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi-bestiary.webp\" title=\"Guhdggi\" data-tooltip=\"Guhdggi\" alt=\"Guhdggi\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi-bestiary.webp')\" />\n<p>孤寂魔由那些在多次人生中踏过同一朝圣路线之人的堕化转世的灵魂所形成。这种灵堕魔看起来像一只臃肿的青蛙，前肢位置却长着细长的人类手臂而非前腿。它们的眼睛鼓胀、似乎失明，却仍具备视力。孤寂魔背上绑着一个巨大的柳条笼，腹部与两侧则被数十根绳索与皮带固定着一堆破损的武器、工具与物品。它们行走时会借助夹在前臂中的两支长矛，步态笨拙、踉跄跳跃。孤寂魔最令人不安的特征是它们的第二张脸：当蛙形的嘴张开时，会露出喉咙里一张人脸，周围纠缠着一团蝴蝶的巢。这张脸有着长而深色、仿佛有生命般舞动的头发，能抽打出令人疼痛的鞭挞；当它们闭上嘴唇时，那些发丝的末端会从青蛙嘴角垂落。</p>\n<p>尽管孤寂魔已不再具备像多数类人生物那样迅捷的移动能力，它们仍喜爱旅行，同时对那些能更轻松做到这一点的存在怀有凶暴的嫉恨。不过，可别低估孤寂魔那踉跄的摇晃步伐！这种恶魔尤其喜欢潜伏在朝圣路线的偏僻路段，伏击旅人，把受害者关进笼子里，并以俘虏的心智与对曾经造访之地的记忆为食。</p>\n<p>孤寂魔体现了重复旅途的循环，以及“每一段旅程的终点即下一段旅程的起点”这一概念。这一概念的核心，是“没有任何旅程会真正开始或结束——它们只是从前一段旅程中涌现而出”。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.Z97fXdQ6kTe7PUIr]{Guhdggi}</span>\n    <span>生物 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">大型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">恶魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不洁</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">灵堕魔蝴蝶</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>各类灵堕魔最奇异的共同特征之一，是那些仿佛会跟随其左右、栖巢于其身体之上，或周期性地从其伤口中涌出的血红色蝴蝶。这些令人不安的昆虫是灵堕魔思想的实体显化，并象征着它们曾经历却又背弃的无数前世。灵堕魔蝴蝶一旦飞离其源头超过几英尺便不会存在太久，会逐渐淡去化作烟雾，并迅速消散在空气中。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Nindoru Traitors</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>While most nindorus are purely evil and unholy in nature, legends tell of exceptionally rare nindorus who manage to escape their own nature and ascend, reincarnating after death into kami or other more benevolent spirits and shedding the nindoru trait as they do so. Of course, these “traitors” are regarded as the most delicious meals imaginable by the nindorus left behind.</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Guhdggi (Wandering Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi-bestiary.webp\" title=\"Guhdggi\" data-tooltip=\"Guhdggi\" alt=\"Guhdggi\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-guhdggi-bestiary.webp')\" />\n<p>A guhdggi forms from the corrupted souls of those who have trod the same pilgrimage route through multiple lives. This type of nindoru looks like a bloated frog with long, slender human arms instead of front legs. Their eyes appear bulbous and blind yet are capable of sight. A guhdggi carries a large wicker cage strapped to their back, while dozens of cords and straps affix a trove of broken weapons, tools, and items to their belly and flanks. When they walk, they do so with the aid of two long spears clutched in their forearms, stumbling and hopping in an ungainly gait. The most unsettling feature of the guhdggi is their second face, revealed when the frog-like mouth opens to reveal a human face peering from their throat amid a tangled nest of butterflies. This face has long, dark, animated hair capable of inflicting painful lashes, the lengths of which hang from the corner of the frog’s mouth when their lips are closed.</p>\n<p>While the guhdggi is no longer capable of movement as swift as most humanoids walk, they still enjoy traveling while harboring a ferocious jealousy of those who can do so with greater ease. One would do well not to underestimate the stumbling stagger of a guhdggi, though! The fiend particularly delights in lying in wait along isolated sections of pilgrimage routes to ambush travelers, trapping victims in their cages and feeding upon their captive’s mind and memories of previously visited places.</p>\n<p>Guhdggis embody the cycles of repeated journeys and the concept that every journey taken ends at the start of the next. Central to this concept is the notion that no journey ever truly begins or ends—they just emerge from the previous one.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.Z97fXdQ6kTe7PUIr]{Guhdggi}</span>\n    <span>Creature 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Large</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Nindoru Butterflies</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>One of the strangest shared traits of the various types of nindoru are the blood-red butterflies that seem to follow them around, nest on their bodies, or periodically emerge from their wounds. These unnerving insects are physical manifestations of the nindorus’ thoughts and symbolize the countless past lives they once lived but turned their backs on. Nindoru butterflies never last long once they flutter more than a few feet from their source, fading away into smoke that quickly dissipates into the air.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Sojiruh (Shrieking Nindoru)": {
              "name": "索闹魔（尖叫灵堕魔） Sojiruh (Shrieking Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>索闹魔（尖叫灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sojiruh.webp\" title=\"Sojiruh\" data-tooltip=\"Sojiruh\" alt=\"Sojiruh\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sojiruh.webp')\" />\n<p>索闹魔的诞生源于这样一种情况：某个生物在多次生命中都致力于追求开悟，却在临死前背弃这些目标，并蓄意将自己的灵魂从转世轮回中硬生生撕离。这些怪物般的生物是最常见的灵堕魔，也最受善解追随者的憎恨，因为许多这类邪魔都源自该哲学体系中堕落的成员。</p>\n<p>这类灵堕魔沉醉于多次转世的灵魂之味，并认为当肉体仍活着、仍在尖叫时吞噬其生命力最为鲜美。对索闹魔而言，它们进食的躯体发出的完美尖叫之声，就如同与晚餐完美搭配的一杯美酒。</p>\n<p>索闹魔的嘴被一缕缕自己的头发缝死。即便如此，它们仍能自在说话，那空洞的声音会从被封住的双唇间清晰传出。只有当它们选择发出尖啸与惨叫时，才会拉扯这些缝线。它们的手臂修长而仿佛破损，胸腔几乎只剩肋骨，其间塞满红色湿漉漉的蝴蝶；这些蝴蝶在生物的肋骨与脏器间爬行并依附其上。当索闹魔尖叫时，它们胸中蝴蝶的翅膀会疯狂颤动。</p>\n<p>索闹魔象征着转世轮回在失却纯净、分崩离析之后的模样——无论在精神上还是肉体上，都已无可救药地深陷于腐朽与堕落之中。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.TVi4RDeqw7GDsxp0]{索闹魔}</span>\n    <span>生物 4</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不洁</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">灵堕魔半神</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>最强大的灵堕魔是半神，尽管它们的邪教相当罕见。灵堕魔半神在死后倾向于再度转世；像苦迦菩提这样的灵堕魔半神，更恰当的称呼是“灵堕魔苦行者”。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Sojiruh (Shrieking Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sojiruh.webp\" title=\"Sojiruh\" data-tooltip=\"Sojiruh\" alt=\"Sojiruh\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-sojiruh.webp')\" />\n<p>A sojiruh comes into existence when a creature who has dedicated multiple lives to achieving enlightenment turns their back on these goals and deliberately tears themself away from the cycle of reincarnation before their death. These monstrous creatures are the most common nindoru and are also the most hated by followers of Sangpotshi since so many of these fiends rise from fallen members of that very philosophy.</p>\n<p>This type of nindoru relishes the flavor of an oft-reincarnated soul and finds this life force tastes best when consumed while the physical body still lives and screams. To sojiruhs, the sound of a perfect scream from the body they feed upon is akin to the perfect wine pairing with dinner.</p>\n<p>A sojiruh’s mouth is stitched shut with lengths of their own hair. Despite this, they can speak freely, their hollow-sounding voices issuing clearly from sealed lips. They only stretch these stitches when they choose to shriek and scream. Their arms are long and broken-looking, while their chests are little more than rib cages filled with red wet butterflies that crawl through and cling to the creature’s ribs and organs. When a sojiruh screams, the wings of the butterflies in their chest flutter frantically.</p>\n<p>Sojiruhs symbolize the cycle of reincarnation after it has come undone from its purity and has become hopelessly mired in decay and corruption—both spiritually and physically.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.TVi4RDeqw7GDsxp0]{Sojiruh}</span>\n    <span>Creature 4</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Nindoru Demigods</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>The most powerful nindorus are demigods, although their cults are quite rare. Prone to reincarnation after death, nindoru demigods like Kugaptee are more properly known as “nindoru ascetics.”</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Meokdan (Hungry Nindoru)": {
              "name": "莫啖魔（饥饿灵堕魔） Meokdan (Hungry Nindoru)",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>莫啖魔（饥饿灵堕魔）</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-meokdan.webp\" title=\"Meokdan\" data-tooltip=\"Meokdan\" alt=\"Meokdan\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-meokdan.webp')\" />\n<p>作为同类中最弱小的一支，莫啖魔承受着持续而痛苦的饥饿，因为它们缺乏更强大的灵堕魔那种从转世的灵魂中汲取养分的能力。这种饥饿驱使莫啖魔不断寻找食物，并常常迫使它们吞食泥土、石块与垃圾，这些东西几乎不提供（如果有的话）任何营养价值。无论它们吃下多少，莫啖魔的体态始终瘦削得令人痛苦。无论它们有多饿，它们都不会饿死。</p>\n<p>莫啖魔消瘦的躯体外形看似人类，浓密纠结的头发从它们的面部以及头部其余部位直接生长出来，只留下莫啖魔那张大张的嘴巴可见。它们的手臂看起来像是断裂了一般，既不自然地细长，手指也同样修长，末端长着参差不齐的指甲。它们的皮肤上布满细小的开放性溃疡。</p>\n<p>莫啖魔体现了食物循环的极致：从摄食开始，最终生物自身也会在终结时被吞噬——无论是被掠食者吞食，还是被从其残骸中滋长的环境所吞没。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.k77t59tuHjiDEXRm]{莫啖魔}</span>\n    <span>生物 2</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">灵堕魔</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不洁</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">转世的灵魂</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>在某些情况下，你会知道某个灵堕魔攻击的生物是否拥有转世的灵魂。像轮回者这样的族裔总是转世的灵魂，而PC的背景故事，甚至他们的背景，往往也能表明其存在前世。《鬼季》冒险路径中的所有PC都符合转世的灵魂这一条件，因为他们在数十年间一次又一次地重过自己的人生。如果你需要为了裁定灵堕魔的能力而判断某个生物的灵魂是否为转世的灵魂，进行一次@Check[flat|dc:11]——若成功，则其拥有转世的灵魂。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Meokdan (Hungry Nindoru)</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-meokdan.webp\" title=\"Meokdan\" data-tooltip=\"Meokdan\" alt=\"Meokdan\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-meokdan.webp')\" />\n<p>As the least of their kind, meokdans suffer a constant and painful hunger, for they lack the ability of more powerful nindorus to derive nourishment from a reincarnated soul. This hunger drives meokdans to constantly seek food and often compels them to eat dirt, stones, and refuse that offer little (if any) nutritional value. Regardless of how much they eat, meokdans always remains painfully thin in stature. Regardless of how hungry they get, they never starve to death.</p>\n<p>A meokdan’s emaciated frame appears human in shape, with thick, tangled hair that grows directly from their face as well as the rest of their head, leaving only the meokdan’s gaping mouth visible. Their arms appear to be broken and unnaturally long, with equally long fingers tipped with ragged nails. Small, open sores pockmark their skin.</p>\n<p>Meokdans epitomize the cycle of food, from consumption to the creatures themselves being consumed in the end, be it by predators or the environment growing from their remains.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.k77t59tuHjiDEXRm]{Meokdan}</span>\n    <span>Creature 2</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">Rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fiend</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Nindoru</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Reincarnated Souls</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>In some cases, you’ll know if a creature a nindoru attacks has a reincarnated soul. Ancestries like samsarans are always reincarnated souls, and a PC’s backstory or even their background can often indicate the presence of a previous life. All of the PCs in the <em>Season of Ghosts Adventure Path</em> qualify as reincarnated souls, as they’ve relived their lives over and over for decades. If you ever need to determine if a creature’s soul is reincarnated for the purpose of adjudicating a nindoru’s ability, attempt a @Check[flat|dc:11]—on a success, it has a reincarnated soul.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Nindoru": {
              "name": "灵堕魔 Nindoru",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindoru\">灵堕魔</h1>\n<p>当一个已多次转世的邪恶凡人灵魂被从灵魂轮回中生生扯出并遭到腐化时，它可能会经历骇人的变形，化作一种名为灵堕魔的邪魔。作为熵与打破循环的力量，灵堕魔是丑恶的生物，身体常呈现扭曲变形；它们挥舞已被击碎却仍能运作的武器；其真实面容也常常不让人看见。它们显露出人们会在不死生物身上见到的特征，例如腐烂的血肉或破损的骨骼，然而灵堕魔确确实实仍是活物。</p>\n<p>每一只灵堕魔都体现着某一特定循环的断裂，无论那循环源自自然界还是社会根源。对灵堕魔而言，没有什么比吞食一个已多次转世的生物更为甘美；而那些理论上即将升至真正开悟者，则是最可口的一餐。被灵堕魔杀死的存在也会被从循环中撕裂——幸运者会前往骨园接受审判，但更多的则会被腐化，化作更多这般恐怖的邪魔。</p>\n<p>善解的追随者尤其憎恶灵堕魔，并将其视为最可怕的威胁之一。灵堕魔最常见于世上转世循环最强盛的地区；它们与罗刹相似，其关联最紧密的是宇宙本身，而非浩瀚众界中的任何一处邪恶位面。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">灵堕魔特征</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>灵堕魔是不洁的邪魔，由转世灵魂轮回遭受腐化而生，并栖居于宇宙之中。尽管它们外貌上常有让人觉得像不死的要素，但它们实际上是活体。大多数灵堕魔具有黑暗视觉，免疫死亡效果，对银具有弱点，并拥有将自身思想中的物体或生物具现化的力量。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here=\"Nindoru\">Nindoru</h1>\n<p>When an evil mortal soul that has been reincarnated multiple times is wrenched from the cycle of souls and corrupted, it can undergo a horrific transformation into a fiend known as a nindoru. A force for entropy and the breaking of cycles, nindorus are hideous creatures whose bodies often appear distorted, who wield weapons that have been shattered yet still function, and whose true face is often hidden from view. They display traits one might expect to see in an undead creature, such as decaying flesh or broken bones, yet nindorus are very much still alive.</p>\n<p>Each nindoru epitomizes the fracture of a specific cycle, be it one from the natural world or from societal traditions. To nindorus, nothing is more delicious than the consumption of a creature who has reincarnated multiple times, with those who are theoretically about to ascend to true enlightenment presenting the tastiest meal. Those slain by a nindoru are themselves torn from the cycle—the lucky ones move on to the Boneyard for judgment, but many are instead corrupted to form more of these horrific fiends.</p>\n<p>Followers of Sangpotshi find nindorus to be particularly abhorrent and count them among the greatest threats imaginable. Most commonly found in regions of the world where the reincarnation cycle is strongest, nindorus are, like rakshasas, associated most strongly with the Universe and not one of the unholy planes of the Great Beyond.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Nindoru Trait</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Nindorus are unholy fiends who rise from corruptions to the cycle of reincarnating souls and live within the Universe. Although they often have elements in their appearance that make them seem undead, they’re actually living beings. Most nindorus have darkvision, are immune to death effects, have weakness to silver, and possess the power to manifest objects or creatures from their thoughts.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Imprecasia": {
              "name": "食厄精 Imprecasia",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>食厄精</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-imprecasia.webp\" title=\"Imprecasia\" data-tooltip=\"Imprecasia\" alt=\"Imprecasia\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-imprecasia.webp')\" />\n<p>食厄精（IMPRECASIA），俗称食咒者，是一种独居的妖精，被诅咒所散发的能量吸引。它们看起来像骨瘦如柴的人形生物，长着阴影般的翅膀；细长的手上有锋利的爪；昆虫般的头颅上长着羽状的触角。</p>\n<p>食厄精出现在某个地区往往意味着当地的土地正受困扰，但它们并不招人厌。恰恰相反，食厄精的行踪是令人垂涎的情报，因为它们有能力将物体与生物上的诅咒彻底吞食。许多背负诅咒重担的人会去寻找食咒者；其中大多数会乐于接收毁灭的物体，或出于善意为某个人摧毁其诅咒。</p>\n<p>食厄精永远不会接受“治愈一片被诅咒的土地或受灾的地区”这种想法。它们甚至可能试图强化某个地区的苦难，只为确保稳定的食物来源。更大胆的食厄精会追踪被诅咒的家族跨越数代，以他们的不幸为食，直到诅咒终结或血脉断绝。任何试图摧毁此类诅咒的人，都可能成为食厄精的敌人——因为它们会捍卫自己的食物来源。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.K68BqK1Ero3x8NsK]{Imprecasia}</span>\n    <span>生物 11</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">妖精</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">规则与建议以物品为目标</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>食厄精可以对受诅咒的物品施放 cleanse affliction，而不是对生物施放，但它们不能对其使用吞噬诅咒。它们只能对等级等于或低于自身等级的物品这么做；成功时，若该物品的等级等于或高于食厄精等级–4，则物品在24小时内解除诅咒；若其等级更低，则永久解除诅咒。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Imprecasia</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-imprecasia.webp\" title=\"Imprecasia\" data-tooltip=\"Imprecasia\" alt=\"Imprecasia\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-imprecasia.webp')\" />\n<p>An imprecasia, commonly known as a curse eater, is a solitary fey drawn to the energy emanating from curses. They appear as an emaciated humanoid creature with shadowy wings, long thin hands with sharp claws, and an insectile head with feathery antennae.</p>\n<p>An imprecasia’s appearance in a region signifies the land is troubled, but they’re not unpopular creatures. On the contrary, an imprecasia’s whereabouts are coveted information, as they have the ability to fully consume curses on objects and creatures. Many carrying the weight of a curse seek out curse eaters, most of whom will gladly accept doomed objects or charitably destroy an individual’s curse.</p>\n<p>An imprecasia will never accept the idea of healing a cursed land or blighted region. One might even seek to strengthen the afflictions on a region simply to ensure a regular supply of food. A bolder imprecasia tracks cursed families over generations, feeding off their misfortune until the curse ends or the bloodline dies off. Any who attempts to destroy such curses might become the enemy of an imprecasia defending their source of sustenance.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.K68BqK1Ero3x8NsK]{Imprecasia}</span>\n    <span>Creature 11</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Fey</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Targeting Items</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>An imprecasia can cast cleanse affliction on a cursed item rather than on a creature, but they can’t use Devour Curse on it. They can only do so on an item that’s of a level equal to or less than their own level; on a success, the item is uncursed for 24 hours if it’s of a level equal to or higher than the imprecasia’s level – 4, or uncursed permanently if it’s lower level than that.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Dalgyal Gwishin": {
              "name": "蛋脸鬼 Dalgyal Gwishin",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>蛋脸鬼</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-gwishin.webp\" title=\"Dalgyal Gwishin\" data-tooltip=\"Dalgyal Gwishin\" alt=\"Dalgyal Gwishin\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-gwishin.webp')\" />\n<p>蛋脸鬼是一种无面、不死的魂魄，佩戴着一张石面具。这个凄凉的不死者由孤独死去、无人记得的凡人灵魂形成，也同样无法记起自己生前的样貌。蛋脸鬼徘徊于生者的土地上，搜寻任何能证明自己生前是谁的痕迹。它们满怀愤怒，仍嫉妒那些被人爱戴或声名远播、身边围绕着亲密朋友与仰慕者的人——那种绝不会落得与蛋脸鬼同样下场的人。</p>\n<p>蛋脸鬼除了一具由雾构成的幽魂之躯外几乎一无所有，但它头上所戴的无特征石面具却是坚实的。就连它们夺来的面孔也只是短暂之物，会在一天后龟裂剥落，形成看起来类似脆弱瓷制死亡面具的东西。有些孤独的魂魄会保留这些面具，并将它们加入自己在偏远而凄凉的巢穴中的收藏，期望在这不断增长的无声面孔陈列中找到陪伴。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ELmJu6nt0nW1hvqz]{蛋脸鬼}</span>\n    <span>生物 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">罕见</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">虚体</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">不死</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">邪秽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">无面骇物</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>蛋脸鬼最显著的外形特征——没有脸——也见于被称为noppera-bo的活体异怪。尽管共享这一特征且都拥有窃取面容的能力，这两种生物并不合作，反而更常是势同水火的敌人。任何被蛋脸鬼杀死的人都会留下令人不安的无面尸体。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Dalgyal Gwishin</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-gwishin.webp\" title=\"Dalgyal Gwishin\" data-tooltip=\"Dalgyal Gwishin\" alt=\"Dalgyal Gwishin\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-gwishin.webp')\" />\n<p>A dalgyal gwishin is a faceless, undead spirit that wears a stone mask. This forlorn undead forms from the soul of a mortal who died a lonely death with no one to remember them and is similarly unable to remember what it looked like in life. A dalgyal gwishin wanders the land of the living in search of any trace of who they were when they were alive. Full of anger, they remain envious of well-loved or famous individuals who are surrounded by close friends and admirers—the type of people who would never share the dalgyal gwishin’s fate.</p>\n<p>While a dalgyal gwishin has little more than a ghostly body made of mist, the featureless stone mask it wears on its head is solid. Even the stolen faces it claims are transitory, cracking off after a day to form what looks akin to a fragile porcelain death mask. Some of these lonely spirits keep these masks and add them to a collection in a remote and forlorn lair, hoping to find companionship in an ever-growing display of silent faces.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.ELmJu6nt0nW1hvqz]{Dalgyal Gwishin}</span>\n    <span>Creature 5</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Incorporeal</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Undead</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Unholy</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Faceless Horror</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>The dalgyal gwishin’s most significant physical trait—the lack of a face—is shared with the living aberrations known as noppera-bos. Despite this shared feature and the ability to steal faces, the two creatures don’t cooperate and are more often bitter enemies. Anyone slain by a dalgyal gwishin leaves behind an unnerving faceless corpse.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Bakeneko": {
              "name": "化猫 Bakeneko",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>化猫</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-bakeneko.webp\" title=\"Bakeneko\" data-tooltip=\"Bakeneko\" alt=\"Bakeneko\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-bakeneko.webp')\" />\n<p>当一只猫的生命被延长到超过其正常寿命时，化猫便会诞生——无论是由于难以置信的好运、魔法，还是其他手段。随着年岁增长，这只猫科动物会变得越来越怪异可怖：体型增大、智力提升，并逐渐获得对魔法的亲和力。最终，它们能够用后腿直立行走，培养新的爱好，并学习语言。尽管智力大幅增长，许多化猫仍更愿意在升格后的最初几十年里照常生活，继续当一只（尤其是体型过大的）家猫。有些化猫这么做是因为它们想获取作为猫时无法理解的世界知识；而另一些则只是想在迈向下一阶段之前，与当下的家人和所爱之人共度余生。</p>\n<p>在所有乐趣之中，化猫最爱跳舞；它们无法抗拒随音乐点头、用爪子打拍子或摇摆尾巴。它们常常只是为了看尸体跳舞而让尸体动起来——若不死从化猫的控制中挣脱，这种消遣往往会给附近的聚居地带来麻烦。化猫通常顽皮又爱恶作剧；虽然它们并非天生邪恶的生物，但因其让尸体活动以及命令火焰的能力而仍令人畏惧。村民们常被看见一只燃烧的猫与一具行走的尸体并行的景象吓得半死；它们与不死与秘术的关联，也使天夏的某些村庄将所有猫都妖魔化。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.BK4gQmGPX4BW4hyb]{化猫}</span>\n    <span>生物 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">小型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">野兽</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">猫又</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>化猫大多把它们所驱动但毫无心智的丧尸当作玩物，不过也会将其用作守卫，甚至作为复仇的执行者。即便如此，它们仍会尽力确保自己驱使的不死不会被放任四处游荡。大多数关于“邪恶化猫”的故事，其实指的是一种相似但危险得多的生物：猫又——化猫的中型变体，等级为6，其咬击会导致一种令人衰弱的精神疾病。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Bakeneko</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-bakeneko.webp\" title=\"Bakeneko\" data-tooltip=\"Bakeneko\" alt=\"Bakeneko\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-bakeneko.webp')\" />\n<p>A bakeneko comes into existence when the life of a cat is extended past its normal lifespan, whether through incredible fortune, magic, or other means. With each passing year, the feline becomes more and more monstrous—growing in size, becoming more intelligent, and gaining an affinity for magic. Eventually, they become able to walk upright on their rear legs, pursue new hobbies, and learn languages. Despite this expanded intellect, many bakenekos prefer to enjoy the first decades of their ascension continuing their lives as usual as a (particularly oversized) house cat. For some, they do so because they want to acquire knowledge of the world that they couldn’t comprehend as cats, but for others, it’s just a desire to live out their lives with their current families and loved ones before moving on to what comes next.</p>\n<p>Bakenekos enjoy dancing above all other pleasures and can’t resist nodding their heads, tapping their paws, or swishing their tails in time to music. They often animate corpses simply to watch them dance—a pastime that often spells trouble for nearby settlements should the undead get free from the bakeneko’s control. Bakenekos typically have a playful and mischievous demeanor, and while they aren’t inherently evil creatures, they’re still feared for their ability to animate corpses and command fire. Villagers are often frightened half to death by the sight of a flaming cat strolling alongside a walking corpse, and their association with undead and the occult has caused some villages in Tian Xia to vilify all cats.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.BK4gQmGPX4BW4hyb]{Bakeneko}</span>\n    <span>Creature 3</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">rare</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Small</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Beast</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-pf-lore.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Nekomatas</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>Bakenekos mostly see their animated but mindless zombies as amusements, though they also use them as guardians or even as agents for revenge. Still, they do their best to ensure that undead they animate aren’t left to wander free. Most tales of “evil bakenekos” in fact refer to a similar and much more dangerous creature, the nekomata—a level 6 Medium-sized variant of the bakeneko whose bite causes a debilitating disease of the mind.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Algriever": {
              "name": "哀伤者 Algriever",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>哀护蛛灵</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-algriever.webp\" title=\"Algriever\" data-tooltip=\"Algriever\" alt=\"Algriever\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-algriever.webp')\" />\n<p>有些人会把这些蛛形魂魄误认为是在废弃神龛中搜刮的拾荒者，但事实恰恰相反：它们是被遗忘礼拜之所的自封守卫，捍卫被丢弃信仰的神圣性，并照料那些无人看管的地点。有时，哀护蛛灵的职责带着哀伤与悲恸，因为它们会悼念曾经前来它们所选神龛参拜的人。另一些则充满挫败与愤怒，将任何误闯其神龛之人视作最轻也不过是怠惰的信徒，最坏则是亵渎者——理应受罚的罪人。</p>\n<p>哀护蛛灵对活着的生物兴趣不大，除非对方闯入它们的领地。一旦哀护蛛灵的神龛被侵入，它们便会封锁通路，直到闯入者表达敬意。好斗的哀护蛛灵会从旅人身上偷窃，或挟持人质，直到它们索要供奉的要求得到满足。当哀护蛛灵怀疑有人犯下亵渎之举时，再多的赠礼也无法平息它们对复仇的渴望。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.amLD0YfFcG8ejrME]{Algriever}</span>\n    <span>生物 9</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">非普通</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">中型</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">野兽</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">魂魄</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">规则与建议反应惩罚</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>哀护蛛灵遵循它们所绑定神龛之神祇或信仰的典范与禁忌，尽管它们在大多数其他议题上仍不表态。无论神龛有多大，哀护蛛灵都会在神龛中选择三件中型或更小的物体，作为它们防卫的焦点，并且可以对任何触碰或扰乱这些物体的生物使用助祭防御。</p>\n</section>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Algriever</h1>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-algriever.webp\" title=\"Algriever\" data-tooltip=\"Algriever\" alt=\"Algriever\" class=\"float-right\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-algriever.webp')\" />\n<p>Some mistake these spiderlike spirits as scavengers looking to loot abandoned shrines, but they’re actually the opposite: self-appointed guardians of forgotten places of worship, defending the sanctity of discarded faiths and tending sites that have no caretakers. Sometimes, an algriever’s duties are tinged with sadness and grief, as they mourn the loss of those who once attended their chosen shrine. Others are filled with frustration and rage, viewing any who stumble upon their shrine as lapsed faithful at best or blasphemers at worse—sinners who deserve punishment.</p>\n<p>Algrievers have little interest in living creatures until they wander into their territory. Once an algriever’s shrine has been breached, they block passage until the interlopers pay their respects. Aggressive algrievers steal from travelers or take hostages until their demands for an offering are satisfied. When algrievers suspect someone of committing blasphemy, no gifts can slake their thirst for vengeance.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">\n    <span>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.season-of-ghosts-bestiary.Actor.amLD0YfFcG8ejrME]{Algriever}</span>\n    <span>Creature 9</span>\n  </h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait uncommon\">Uncommon</li>\n    <li class=\"trait size\">Medium</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Beast</li>\n    <li class=\"trait\">Spirit</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"encounter\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo92102-rules.webp\" />\n    <h2 class=\"no-toc split\">Reactive Punishment</h2>\n  </div>\n  <p>An algriever follows the edicts and anathemas of the deity or faith of the shrine to which they’re bonded, although they remain uncommitted in most other topics. Regardless of how large the shrine is, an algriever chooses three Medium or smaller objects in the shrine as their own focus for defense and can use Acolyte’s Defense against any creature that touches or disturbs those objects.</p>\n</section>"
            },
