        "Player's Guide": {
          "name": "玩家指南 Player's Guide",
          "pages": {
            "The Great Willow": {
              "name": "大尊柳 The Great Willow",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W37. 大尊柳</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇坐落在一片山地的山脚下，该区域在地理上被称为三山，因区域内三座主要山峰而得名。在她的回忆录中，智惠大师记述她如何在其中最低那座山的山顶，发现了一棵体型异常巨大的古老柳树。在与守护这棵树的木灵神结为友伴之后，智惠大师得知了至关重要的信息，这些信息最终引领她前往西面的谭杉林。多年来，因这份知识，那棵被称作“大尊柳”的木灵神一直受到柳岸镇居民与来访朝圣者的深切敬仰。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>采集的食物与非金属原材料</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W37. The Great Willow</h3>\n<p>Willowshore rests at the foot of a mountainous region known geographically as the Trimountains, named due to the three major peaks in the area. In her memoir, Master Zhi Hui noted how she found an ancient willow tree of unusual size at the summit of the lowest of these mountains. After befriending the kodama kami who protected the tree, Master Zhi Hui learned vital information that eventually led her to the Tan Sugi grove to the west. For this knowledge, the kodama of the so-called “Great Willow” has received much reverence from both Willowshore and visiting pilgrims over the years.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> foraged foods and nonmetallic raw materials</p>"
            },
            "Bones of the Forgotten": {
              "name": "受弃者之骨 Bones of the Forgotten",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W36. 受弃者之骨</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇和许多偏远村落一样，有自己的一套法律。重罪通常会被放逐，除非此人的技能或知识有用——那样惩罚就会改为永久监禁。处决很少见，因为被放逐进幽魂之森往往本身就等同于死刑。</p>\n<p>尤其卑劣的罪犯会被在头皮上刺上罪印，而在其死后，这一纹身会通过刻划转移到骨头上，这意味着即便死亡并腐朽，印记依然存在。带有罪印的尸体——无论来自柳岸镇、其他村庄，还是龙华——都只能埋葬在这片杂草丛生、无人打理的区域里。</p>\n<p>过去的坟墓并没有标记，但最近立起了几根木桩，上面挂着纸制手里剑，似乎是在无声抗议，认为埋在下面的人也许死得不公。又或者，这是在试图阻止某个怨恨、复仇的幽灵（特征）出现。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W36. Bones of the Forgotten</h3>\n<p>Willowshore, like many remote villages, has its own set of laws. Grievous crimes were punished with exile unless the individual’s skill or knowledge was needed—the punishment was then permanent imprisonment. Executions were rare, as being exiled into Specterwood was often a death sentence in itself.</p>\n<p>Particularly vile criminals had a Mark of Crime tattooed onto their scalp, and after death, this tattoo was transferred to the bones through carving, meaning even in death and decomposition, the mark remained. Bodies with a Mark of Crime—be it from Willowshore, another village, or Lung Wa—can only be buried in this overgrown and unkept area.</p>\n<p>While graves were unmarked in the past, a few wooden posts have been erected recently and paper shuriken hung off them, seemingly in silent protest that the ones buried beneath might have died an unjust death. Or perhaps this is an attempt to stave off the rise of a bitter, vengeful ghost.</p>"
            },
            "The Leshy’s Saloon": {
              "name": "莱西茶铺 The Leshy’s Saloon",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W35. 莱西茶铺</h3>\n<p>当地的莱西族不记得自己何时来到这片地区，只记得那是在柳岸镇建立之前很久。他们直到聚落扩张到让此事不可避免时，才正式加入柳岸镇。在盟友家族替他们挡住贪婪的伐木领主之后，莱西族建立了自己的茶园生意，背着长方形竹制背包上路，包里藏着泡好的茶与茶具。有些会高喊口号，另一些则用简单的木鱼来通知顾客他们到了。这些走街串巷的商贩很快成了柳岸镇生活中的一景与必不可少的一部分。自从青天茶馆关闭后，<strong>山峰草</strong>（举止不拘、无性别的莱西族制茶师）——这支莱西族队伍的首领——越来越专注于为他们偏爱的本地顾客定制专属的茶道拼配。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>陶制茶具、茶叶</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W35. The Leshy’s Saloon</h3>\n<p>The local leshies don’t recall when they came to the region, just that it was long before Willowshore was founded. They didn’t officially join Willowshore until the expansion of the settlement made it inevitable. With allied families keeping the greedy lumber lords away, the leshies built their own tea farm business, taking to the roads with brewed tea and teaware stashed in rectangular bamboo backpacks. Some would shout slogans, while others used a simple temple block to inform customers of their arrival. These traveling merchants soon became an attraction and staple of Willowshore life. Ever since the Cerulean Teahouse closed, <strong>Mountain Summit Grass</strong> (irreverent agender leshy teamaker), the leader of this band of leshies, has been increasingly focusing on creating bespoke blends of tea for individual local customers they favor.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> clay pottery tea ware, tea leaves</p>"
            },
            "Spider Gate": {
              "name": "蜘蛛门 Spider Gate",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W33. 蜘蛛门</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp\" alt=\"长明灯\" data-tooltip=\"长明灯\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>在断刀夜之后，柳岸镇的镇长屈从于在镇入口处设置一盏新灯笼的要求，以加强镇中心长明灯所提供的防护。最初的计划是让柳岸镇的木匠建造一座鸟居门或嬛族语—舒国式的门楼，以便悬挂灯笼；但一位龙华贵族提出无偿提供他花园里的一只石制守护蜘蛛，因为它已不再符合花园的装饰风格。</p>\n<p>多数柳岸镇居民认为这尊巨大的雕像是他们见过最丑的东西。尽管如此，他们仍假定雕像里栖居着一位守护魂魄，并因此对它表示敬重。随着时间推移，村民们接受了这位独特的入口守护者，甚至把它当作吉祥物，并给它取名为“丑小乖”。丑小乖用獠牙叼着的灯笼是一盏普通灯笼，不像晨步桥上的那盏长明灯，但柳岸镇的人民同样珍视它，并努力让它始终保持点亮。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W33. Spider Gate</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp\" alt=\"Eternal Lantern\" data-tooltip=\"Eternal Lantern\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90199-eternallantern.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>After the Night of Broken Blades, Willowshore’s governor caved to the demand for a new lantern at the entrance of the town to augment the protection afforded by the Eternal Lantern at the town’s heart. While the original plan was for the carpenters of Willowshore to build a tori gate or Tian-shu gateway on which lanterns could be hung, a Lung Wa aristocrat offered a free stone guardian spider from his garden since it no longer fit in with the garden’s decorations.</p>\n<p>Most Willowshorers thought the giant statue was the ugliest thing they’d ever seen. Nevertheless, they assumed the statue housed a guardian spirit and respected it accordingly. In time, villagers accepted their unique entrance guardian, even adopting it as their mascot and naming it “Ugly Cute.” The lantern Ugly Cute holds in its fangs is a regular lantern, unlike the Eternal Lantern found at Dawnstep Bridge, but the people of Willowshore value it just as much and strive to keep it lit at all times.</p>"
            },
            "The Mushroom House": {
              "name": "蘑菇房 The Mushroom House",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W32. 蘑菇房</h3>\n<p>这座偏远的砖砌农舍散发着腐败与粪肥的气味。不过，人人都知道，农舍里生长的并不只有蘑菇。只要价格合适，蘑菇房几乎什么都能“种”出来。<strong>卢达·巴马</strong>（善于操纵的女性半身人走私者）是一位身手矫健的半身人老妇人，她在胡太婆的明确许可下，掌管并经营着这处非法市场。</p>\n<p><strong>货品：</strong>冒险道具、毒品、毒素、纹身</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W32. The Mushroom House</h3>\n<p>This remote brick farmhouse smells of decay and manure. Everyone knows that mushrooms aren’t the only things growing in the farmhouse, though. For the right price, the Mushroom House can grow almost anything. <strong>Luda Bama</strong> (manipulative female halfling smuggler), a spry, elderly halfling woman, is the head of this illicit market, which she runs with the explicit permission of Granny Hu.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> adventuring gear, drugs, poisons, tattoos</p>"
            },
            "Dock": {
              "name": "码头 Dock",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W31. 码头</h3>\n<p>在水坝建成后，柳岸镇的旧码头被封堵，因此必须在木棉河入海口建造一座新码头。新码头由<strong>拉祖尔·萨姆杜拉</strong>（沉静的男性那伽吉造船匠）运营与管理；他是木棉河-杜月江瓦市因其造船技能而专门雇用的。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>河船租赁与出售</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W31. Dock</h3>\n<p>After the construction of the dam, Willowshore’s old dock was blocked off, thus requiring the construction of a new dock at the mouth of the Ceiba River. The new dock is operated and managed by <strong>Rajul Samudra</strong> (serene male nagaji shipwright), who was hired by the Ceiba-Duyue Exchange specifically for his boat-building skills.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> river boat rentals and sales</p>"
            },
            "Fisheries": {
              "name": "渔场 Fisheries",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W30. 渔场</h3>\n<p>鱼类是柳岸镇的重要食物来源。当地人传统上会捕捞整群的鱼，将超过一定体型的鱼加以保存，并在自家后院的池塘里养殖小鱼。如今，这种做法已得到扩展，不过渔民们尚未达到让这里的渔场池塘能够无限期维持下去的程度。</p>\n<p><strong>座泽</strong>（机警的鼠人女性渔民）是柳岸镇首屈一指的养鱼人；她感知天气变化的能力让她在这一行当中具备完美优势。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>风干或熏制的鱼和虾、肥料、钓鱼道具、昆虫鱼饵</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W30. Fisheries</h3>\n<p>Fish is an important food source for Willowshore. Locals traditionally capture entire schools of fish, preserve those above a certain size, and raise small ones in their backyard ponds. Today, this practice has been expanded, though the fishers have yet to reach a point where the fishery ponds here can be maintained indefinitely.</p>\n<p><strong>Zataku</strong> (observant female ratfolk fisher) is Willowshore’s foremost fish keeper; her ability to sense weather changes gives her the perfect edge in her occupation.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> dried or smoked fish and shrimp, fertilizer, fishing gear, insect bait</p>"
            },
            "The Ceiba-Duyue Exchange": {
              "name": "木棉河-杜月江瓦市 The Ceiba-Duyue Exchange",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W29. 木棉河-杜月江瓦市</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp\" alt=\"胡太婆\" data-tooltip=\"胡太婆\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>当和善保总督在柳岸镇就任时，他下令在此修建数座新仓库与一座贸易栈，希望扩展城镇的产业，并加强与海岸要塞唐入之间的联系。在胡太婆的建议下，和善保亲自挑选当地国府幸的祭司<strong>金具元</strong>（耐心的男性人类牧师）担任瓦市经理一职。具元勉强接受了这份工作，因为他知道胡太婆握有足以要挟他的把柄，他根本无法拒绝。</p>\n<p><strong>货物：</strong>饮品、神术卷轴、食物与香料、符箓、矿石原料、纺织品</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W29. The Ceiba-Duyue Exchange</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp\" alt=\"Granny Hu\" data-tooltip=\"Granny Hu\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-grannyhu.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>When Governor Heh Shan-Bao took office in Willowshore, he ordered several new warehouses and a trade office to be built here, hoping to expand the town’s industry and connection with the coastal fortress of Karahai. On Granny Hu’s advice, Shan-Bao handpicked the local Kofusachi priest, <strong>Kim Gu-won</strong> (patient male human cleric), to take the post of Exchange Manager. Gu-won reluctantly accepted the job, knowing that with what Granny Hu has on him, he wouldn’t be able to refuse.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> beverages, divine scrolls, foods and spices, fulus, raw mineral, textiles</p>"
            },
            "Mother’s Coil": {
              "name": "主母之绾 Mother’s Coil",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W28. 主母之绾</h3>\n<p>在柳岸镇，魔法传统上被视为神明赐福的显现、与魂魄世界的联系，或只是手法与心智的把戏。直到苏萨杜斯的安贾尔——一位老年纳迦基巫师——到来之前，大多数人都不太理解它是一门需要研究与学习的学问。大约15年前，安贾尔来到此地，发现柳岸镇的天气对他们的干鳞症状态很温和，于是从一位打算迁往伺城的农民手中买下了一块地。一夜之间，一座纳迦乔尔风格的深色玄武岩高塔拔地而起，令村民们惊叹不已。</p>\n<p>尽管对魔法感到好奇，大多数村民仍认为这门学问艰深难近，更不用说不切实际了。因此，安贾尔只有一名学徒——十兵卫。她还是个孩子时，被一对不负责任的“父母”遗弃在柳岸镇；那两人伪装成富裕商人，之后却未付清欠款便逃离了镇子。因竟有人胆敢如此置孩子于险境而怒不可遏，安贾尔出于其纳里尼瓦提亚的信念，将受惊的十兵卫收为己出。</p>\n<p>此后，十兵卫已成长为能干的年轻人。虽然安贾尔去年的去世令人悲痛，但十兵卫决心继续通过养父母遗留下来的书籍研习奥术艺术。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>奥术与异术卷轴、配方与食谱、魔杖</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W28. Mother’s Coil</h3>\n<p>Magic was traditionally seen in Willowshore as either a manifestation of divine blessing, one’s connection to the spirit world, or just a trick of the hand and mind. Most folks didn’t quite understand it as a topic to be studied and learned until the arrival of Anjal of Thulsadus, an old nagaji wizard. Arriving about 15 years ago, Anjal found the weather of Willowshore to be gentle on their dryscale condition and thus bought a plot of land from a farmer looking to relocate to the city of Sze. Overnight, a Nagajor-styled tower of dark basalt appeared, much to the awe of the villagers.</p>\n<p>Though curious about magic, most villagers find the topic to be formidable and unapproachable, not to mention impractical. Thus, Anjal had only one apprentice, Jubei, a child they raised after she was abandoned in Willowshore by a pair of irresponsible “parents” who posed as well-off merchants but then fled town without paying their bills. Infuriated that anyone dared endanger a child so, Anjal’s Nalinivatian beliefs prompted the old wizard to take the terrified Jubei in as their own.</p>\n<p>Jubei has since grown into a capable young adult. While Anjal’s death last year was tragic, Jubei is determined to continue studying the arcane arts through the books her adopted parent left behind.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> arcane and occult scrolls, formulas and recipes, wands</p>"
            },
            "The Hand of Spring": {
              "name": "妙手回春 The Hand of Spring",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W27. 妙手回春</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp\" alt=\"Dami\" data-tooltip=\"Dami\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>柳岸镇在达米汉西格·玛巴邦洛奥布医生（和蔼的男性人类医生）到来之前，医疗护理主要依赖家传偏方、草药煎剂以及巡回的祭司；大家都简称他为达米。达米运用针灸、提纯化学制剂与外科手术相结合的方式提供诊疗。尽管他的疗法并非柳岸镇人习惯的那一套，达米却因其乐善好施、比起金钱更关心病患而声名远扬。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>炼金治疗物品、医疗工具包补给、非魔法治疗物品</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W27. The Hand of Spring</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp\" alt=\"Dami\" data-tooltip=\"Dami\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-dahan.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>Willowshore relied heavily on home remedies, herbal droughts, and traveling priests for medical care until the arrival of Doctor <strong>Damihansig Mababangloob</strong> (kindly male human doctor), whom everyone calls Dami for short. Dami uses a mix of acupuncture, purified chemicals, and surgery to provide care. Though his treatments aren’t what Willowshore is used to, Dami has developed quite a reputation for being a charitable doctor who cares more about his patients than monetary gain.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> alchemical healing items, healer’s kit supplies, nonmagical healing items</p>"
            },
            "Second Best": {
              "name": "二等优 Second Best",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W26. 二等优</h3>\n<p>当<strong>霍天哲</strong>（谦逊的人类男性发明家）在五年前与父亲从唐入（柳岸镇东方最近的邻近聚落）来到镇上，协助维护柳岸镇大坝时，这个出身城市的儿子原以为自己马上就能教会“乡下二流铁匠”该怎么把事情办成。很快，天哲就意识到自己的技能甚至不如永焰最年轻的学徒，而他那些设计花哨的农用小装置，与其说是奇迹机器，不如说更像玩具。受到打击后，天哲请求父亲留在柳岸镇，好让他学习成为“一名有用的铁匠”。天哲的父亲不情不愿地答应了这个请求，但仍给了儿子一把金币，让他去订做一块新的店招。为了提醒自己，天哲干脆把自己的工坊大胆命名为“二等优”。</p>\n<p>天哲的产品已经赢得了一些忠实顾客，而他对机械的知识也打动了雍武秀，以至于这位老铁匠将大坝的维护工作交给了他。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>冒险工具、炼金弹药、炼金炸弹、发条小器具，以及简易护甲、金属武器和盾牌</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W26. Second Best</h3>\n<p>When <strong>Huo Tian-Zhe</strong> (humble male human inventor) arrived in town with his father from Karahai (Willowshore’s closest neighboring settlement to the east) five years ago to assist with the maintenance of Willowshore’s dam, the urban-born son thought he was about to show the “second-rated smiths of the countryside” how to get things done. Quickly, Tian-Zhe realized his skills were subpar to even the youngest apprentice of the Eternal Blaze and that his fancily-designed farm gadgets were more akin to toys than machines of marvels. Humbled, Tian-Zhe asked his father to stay in Willowshore so he could learn to be a “smith of use.” Begrudgingly accepting the request, Tian-Zhe’s father nevertheless gave his son a handful of gold to order a new shop sign. As a reminder to himself, Tian-Zhe boldly named his workshop “Second Best.”</p>\n<p>Tian-Zhe’s products have garnered some loyal customers, and his knowledge of machinery won over Yong Wu-Xiu such that the old smith tasked him with the maintenance of the dam.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> adventuring tools, alchemical ammunition, alchemical bombs, clockwork gadgets, and simple armor, metal weapons, and shields</p>"
            },
            "Mercantile Street": {
              "name": "商业街 Mercantile Street",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W25. 商业街</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇较新的商家，尤其是与木雕有关的，多分布在商业街沿线的一栋红砖建筑里。为确保木材大亨不会偏袒任何人，木雕师们联合起来成立了一家公会，通过该公会，年轻学徒在学徒期内有机会在不同店铺实习。<strong>云梦昂</strong>（才华横溢的人类女性木雕师）是木雕师现任民选公会领袖，也是这种培训的成果。尽管她的工作备受称赞，但昂更愿意成为一名画家或珠宝匠。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>艺术品、木制物品、木制宗教符号</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W25. Mercantile Street</h3>\n<p>Willowshore’s newer businesses, particularly those associated with woodcarving, are mostly found in one of the red-brick buildings along Mercantile Street. To ensure the lumber lords would never favor anyone, the woodcarvers came together to form a guild, through which young apprentices have the opportunity to intern at different shops during their apprenticeship. <strong>Yun Mong-Un</strong> (talented female human woodcarver), the woodcarver’s current elected guild leader, is a product of such training. Though heaped with praise for her work, Mong-Un would rather be a painter or jewelry maker.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> artwork, wood items, wooden religious symbols</p>"
            },
            "Abandoned Estates": {
              "name": "被遗弃的庄园 Abandoned Estates",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W23. 被遗弃的庄园</h3>\n<p>这些木材大亨的宅邸在被彻底洗劫一空后，就被遗弃下来，偶尔成了发泄室或胆量挑战的场所。其中一栋房子里坐落着一座德丝娜的废弃神龛，许多人都在疑惑，是否该有人将这位女神迎入家中，而不是让她孤零零地留在庄园废墟里。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W23. Abandoned Estates</h3>\n<p>The abandoned lumber lords’ estates, after being thoroughly picked clean, were left to serve as the occasional rage room or dare challenge. An abandoned shrine to Desna sits in one of the houses, and many have questioned if someone should accept the goddess into their home instead of leaving her bereft in the estate ruins.</p>"
            },
            "The Cerulean Teahouse": {
              "name": "青天茶馆 The Cerulean Teahouse",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W22. 青天茶馆</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇的木材老板们自视甚高，与“平民百姓”厮混的想法令他们心生厌恶。贵族庆麦莱的解决之道，便是在这些木材大亨庄园附近建立了这座精美的建筑。</p>\n<p>青天茶馆凭借丰盛的奢华菜肴、饮品与表演迅速走红。然而，新鲜感一过，生意便很快冷清下来。尽管如此，麦莱依旧坚持不懈：先将茶馆的重心改为茶饭承办，继而与莱西茶铺合作，将其作为门面，最后又转型为可灵活经营的民宿。就在麦莱终于还清这处地产贷款后的短短几天，龙华崩塌的消息传到了柳岸镇。麦莱随即宣布收手并退休，但当她试图将茶馆的控制权转交给家人时却遇到麻烦，因为显然她的亲属中无人愿意移动到柳岸镇。麦莱于前一个冬季初去世时，这家生意的所有权仍未确定，因为麦莱从未提交意志。如今，青天茶馆空置无人，正缓慢坠落为废墟。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W22. The Cerulean Teahouse</h3>\n<p>Willowshore’s lumber bosses thought very highly of themselves, and the idea of mingling with the “common folk” rankled them. Aristocrat Qing Mai-Lai’s solution was the establishment of this fine structure, close to the lumber lords’ estates.</p>\n<p>The Cerulean Teahouse took off quickly, thanks to its plentiful offerings of extravagant food, drinks, and performances. However, once the novelty wore off, business quickly died. Still, Mai-Lai persevered, first by changing the teahouse’s focus to banquet catering, then by collaborating with The Leshy’s Salon as a storefront, and finally as a flexible bed-and-breakfast. Just days after Mai-Lai finally paid off the loan on the property, news of Lung Wa’s collapse reached Willowshore. Mai-Lai called it quits at that point and announced her retirement, but her attempts to transfer control of the Teahouse to family met with complications after it became apparent that none of her relations wanted to move to Willowshore. When Mai-Lai passed away early in the previous winter, ownership of the business was still undetermined, for Mai-Lai never submitted a will. Today, the Cerulean Teahouse stands vacant and is slowly falling into ruin.</p>"
            },
            "Luo and Laws": {
              "name": "骆氏状所 Luo and Laws",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W20. 骆氏状所</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp\" alt=\"Luo Xi Yang\" data-tooltip=\"Luo Xi Yang\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>龙华的法律在一代又一代自私自利的统治者手中被反复修订，成了一团自相矛盾的乱麻，使得独立律师——例如<strong>骆熙旸</strong>（热忱的女性人类律师）——得以靠着试图理清这些条文来过上体面的生活。邀请她来此的伐木领主向她保证乡村生活压力会更小，熙旸因此只带着那部必需的10卷《帝国律摘要》便启程前来。很快，这位律师便发现柳岸镇的法律问题丝毫不比她此前在伺城遇到的简单，甚至更加复杂；于是她的图书馆规模也随之扩张，变成了她旧居里那间图书馆的两倍。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W20. Luo and Laws</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp\" alt=\"Luo Xi Yang\" data-tooltip=\"Luo Xi Yang\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-xiyangluo.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>Lung Wa’s laws, after being revised time and time again by self-serving rulers, are a bag of contradictions allowing independent lawyers, such as <strong>Luo Xi Yang</strong> (eager female human lawyer), to make a decent living attempting to make sense of them. Promised by the lumber lords who invited her here that rural life would be less stressful, Xi Yang arrived with only the essential 10-volume Imperial Compendium. Quickly, the lawyer discovered that Willowshore’s legal issues were as complicated, if not more so, than what she’d previously encountered in the city of Sze, and thus her library grew to a size that doubled the one in her former home.</p>"
            },
            "Downtown Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇镇区 Downtown Willowshore",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W19. 柳岸镇镇区</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp\" alt=\"Zheng Peng\" data-tooltip=\"Zheng Peng\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>柳岸镇镇区仍是镇上的主要行动中心。东北方矗立着总督的宅邸与办公处，同时也兼作村子的银行与金库。庄园南边是帝国营房，由<strong>郑鹏</strong>（坚毅的男性人类巡守军官）统领。十字路口北侧是村里每周舒剧演出的舞台，它是由<strong>大野和马</strong>（和蔼健谈的男性狐妖导演）主持的七彩鸣鸾剧院的一部分。附近道路两侧相对而立的是柳岸镇最繁忙的商铺之一树雀居，以及柳岸镇唯一的公共澡堂乐天河童。树雀居是一家家族经营的杂货铺，由<strong>三美奈户弥</strong>（友善的女性人类家族女族长）打理；而乐天河童的主人<strong>华德歌</strong>（健谈的男性半身人澡堂老板）则因他对清洁的痴迷而在镇上闻名。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>酒精、沐浴用品、娱乐、谷物、家居用品与工具、腌渍食品、口粮</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W19. Downtown Willowshore</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp\" alt=\"Zheng Peng\" data-tooltip=\"Zheng Peng\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-zhengpeng.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>Downtown Willowshore remains a major hub of activity in town. To the northeast stands the governor’s home and office, which also serves as the village’s bank and treasury. South of the manor lie the imperial barracks, commanded by <strong>Zheng Peng</strong> (stoic male human watch officer). To the north of the crossroad is the stage for the village’s weekly Shu Opera performance, which is part of the Seven-Colored Songbird theater, a venue officiated over by <strong>Kazuma Oono</strong> (gregarious male kitsune director). Nearby on opposite sides of the road is one of Willowshore’s busiest stores, Treesparrow’s Rest, and Willowshore’s only public bathhouse, the Happy Kappa. Treesparrow’s is a family-owned grocery store run by <strong>Nadoya Sanmi</strong> (friendly female human family matriarch), while the Happy Kappa’s owner, <strong>De-Ge Hua</strong> (chatty male halfling bathhouse owner) is famous in town for his obsession with cleanliness.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> alcohol, bathing, entertainment, grains, household supplies and tools, preserved foods, rations</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Dam": {
              "name": "柳岸镇大坝 Willowshore Dam",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W18. 柳岸镇大坝</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇的大坝是一项小型工程奇迹。其主体由巨大、精密拼接的深灰色大理石板构成，并雕刻出经过精心计算的弧度。大坝有两扇巨大的木闸门，可关闭或开启以降低湖水水位。转动控制闸门的轮盘会自动引发钟声响起，提醒下游的任何人移动至安全处。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W18. Willowshore Dam</h3>\n<p>Willowshore’s dam is a minor engineering marvel. Its main body is constructed out of immense, precisely fitted slabs of dark-gray marble, carved with a carefully calculated curvature. The dam has two giant wooden gates that can be closed or opened to lower the level of the lake. Turning the wheel that controls the gates automatically causes a bell to ring, signaling anyone downriver to move away to safety.</p>"
            },
            "Woodraft Lake": {
              "name": "木筏湖 Woodraft Lake",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W17. 木筏湖</h3>\n<p>龙华任命到柳岸镇的第一任总督曾试图通过各种工程壮举来驯服臭名昭著的木棉河。其中一部分努力，再加上对木材湿储的需求，促成了柳岸镇大坝——以及随之而来的木筏湖——的修建。</p>\n<p>起初许多人抗议这项工程，因为形成的湖泊会淹没一些住宅与农田——其中包括村里供奉难婆的神龛。又关押了几个人之后，所有抱怨都消失了。大坝在预定时间内完工。那位总督因此升迁，不久后离开了柳岸镇，但还没来得及享受成果，就在一个晴朗的日子里被山体滑坡掩埋。尽管这则故事的真实性颇为可疑，后来的总督从未阻止柳岸镇的村民将这座湖当作供奉苦难寡妇的神龛。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W17. Woodraft Lake</h3>\n<p>The first governor appointed to Willowshore by Lung Wa made an effort to tame the notorious Ceiba River through various engineering feats. Part of that effort, plus the demand for wet storage for wood, led to the construction of the Willowshore Dam—and by extension, Woodraft Lake.</p>\n<p>Many protested the construction at first, as the resulting lake would submerge some homes and farmlands—including the village’s shrine to Lady Nanbyo. A few imprisonments later, all complaints ceased. The dam was completed in due time. While the governor earned themself a promotion and left Willowshore soon after, they didn’t get to enjoy before a landslide buried them on a bright sunny day. While the story’s veracity is somewhat dubious, subsequent governors have never stopped Willowshore’s villagers from treating the lake as a shrine to the Widow of Suffering.</p>"
            },
            "Nine Ear Shrine": {
              "name": "九耳神社 Nine Ear Shrine",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W16. 九耳神社</h3>\n<p>这座泥墙小屋从外面看像是一座谷仓。其内部向地下延伸10英尺，通往一处以石头砌衬的封闭空间，中央矗立着一尊15英尺高的九尾狐大理石雕像。一条用干草编成的巨大魂魄之绳挂在它的脖子上。地下室的墙面饰有彩绘浮雕，描绘着大狐女的故事。</p>\n<p>十五年前，当欧跋鸣家族被一名腐败的守卫围捕并准备处决时，一位走投无路的母亲把她的婴儿藏在这里。等守卫们发现少了个孩子时，一大群狐狸已经包围了神社。守卫们不愿招致神圣狂怒，便撤退了。家族的盟友很快赶来营救婴儿，就在那时狐狸们消失无踪。</p>\n<p>那个婴儿，<strong>欧跋鸣</strong>（虔诚的人类女性祭司），在远亲的照料下长大。尽管她显露出欧跋鸣家族崇敬自然的倾向，欧跋鸣仍希望通过侍奉大狐女来偿还她所欠的救命之恩。虽然有人质疑她的意图，但柳岸村的大多数人都支援她的奉献。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>符箓、卷轴、护符</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W16. Nine Ear Shrine</h3>\n<p>This mud-wall hut looks like a grain storage hut from the outside. Its interior descends 10 feet underground into an enclosed space lined with stone, in the middle of which sits a 15-foot-tall marble statue of a nine-tailed fox. A large spiritual rope made of hay hangs off its neck. The walls of the basement are decorated with painted carvings that depict stories of Daikitsu.</p>\n<p>Fifteen years ago, a desperate mother of the Ouh family hid her baby here as the family was rounded up for execution by a corrupt guard. By the time the guards learned about the missing offspring, a large skulk of foxes had surrounded the temple. Unwilling to tempt divine wrath, the guards retreated. Allies of the family soon arrived to rescue the baby, at which point the foxes vanished.</p>\n<p>That baby, <strong>Ba-Ming Ouh</strong> (devoted female human priest), grew up under the care of distant relatives. While she shows signs of the Ouh family’s inclinations toward the veneration of nature, Ba-Ming wishes to return her life debt by serving Daikitsu. While some question her intentions, most Willowshorers support her dedication.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> fulus, scrolls, talismans</p>"
            },
            "Industrial District": {
              "name": "工业区 Industrial District",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W13-W15. 工业区</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇的龙华木材老板还经营着许多与从林地获取的材料相关的其他生意。许多产业工人明确是为这份工作来到柳岸镇，把家人和朋友留在了身后。</p>\n<p>木材老板离开后，赫赫总督夺取了控制权，并命令劳工继续工作。由于在这件事上别无选择而感到愤怒，他们一直在深夜聚集，在<strong>川冈</strong>（忠诚的男性天狗公会领袖）——一位资深赌注登记员——的领导下，讨论他们该如何与总督谈判，以释放那些想离开的人，并公平地支付选择留下的人。</p>\n<p>随着龙华的崩溃，这里许多曾经兴盛的生意都已关门歇业。唯一仍在运作的只有云纸屋（由川冈经营的造纸厂）、玉液琼浆（一家酿酒厂）以及里氏制革厂（一家制革厂）。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>酒精、精油与香水、玻璃器皿与玻璃物品、皮革与皮制品、纸张与纸制品，例如法术书与配方簿</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W13-W15. Industrial District</h3>\n<p>Willowshore’s Lung Wa lumber bosses had a host of other businesses related to materials taken from the woods. Many industrial workers came to Willowshore explicitly for this work, leaving family and friends behind.</p>\n<p>After the lumber bosses left, Governor Heh seized control and ordered the laborers to continue working. Upset that they had no choice in the matter, they’ve been gathering late at night under the guidance of <strong>Kawaka</strong> (devoted male tengu guild leader), a senior bookmaker, to discuss how they should negotiate with the governor to release those who want to leave and fairly pay those who elect to stay.</p>\n<p>With the collapse of Lung Wa, many of the businesses that once thrived here have closed up shop. The only ones still functioning are Cloud Paper House (a paper mill run by Kawaka), Jadeite Essentials (a distillery), and Rebel’s Leatherworks (a tannery).</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> alcohol, essential oils and perfume, glassware and glass items, hide and leather items, paper and paper products such as spellbooks and formula books</p>"
            },
            "Dawnstep Bridge": {
              "name": "晨步桥 Dawnstep Bridge",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W11. 晨步桥</h3>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>长明灯</h1>\n  <p>这件次级神器是一件无法移动的物体，由谭杉寺的创建者智惠赠予柳岸镇。贯穿柳岸镇的整个历史，长明灯一直矗立在聚居地核心附近守望；自从智惠在其中放入几枚铜钱后，它的光芒从未动摇。有人相信，只要将铜钱投入长明灯，便能从那些其神龛坐落于柳岸镇的神祇处获得祝福，以换取额外的庇护；但总体而言，柳岸镇的人民早已习惯了晨步桥南侧台阶上那盏永不熄灭的灯笼。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>在三福青楼建立之后（但在它成为旅店之前），柳岸镇的人口规模已增长到按神门的标准足以被视为一座城镇——这意味着在镇内靠近入口处、主要十字路口或桥梁处，必须始终维持一盏点亮的灯笼。在这些地点之一缺少点亮的灯笼，暗示着城镇已被遗弃；人们相信这会招来害兽、幽灵（特征）、危险的野兽，以及更糟糕的东西。如今，柳岸镇有两盏这样的灯笼，但矗立于此的这盏——长明灯——既是最古老的，也是最引人注目的。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W11. Dawnstep Bridge</h3>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>The Eternal Lantern</h1>\n  <p>This minor artifact is an immobile object gifted to the town of Willowshore by the founder of the Tan Sugi monastery, Zhi Hui. For the town’s entire history, the Eternal Lantern has stood sentinel near the settlement’s heart, its light never wavering after Zhi Hui placed a few copper coins within it. Some believe that it’s possible to receive blessings from the deities whose shrines stand in Willowshore by placing copper coins within the Eternal Lantern in exchange for additional protection, but for the most part, the people of Willowshore have become used to the ever-burning lantern at the southern steps of Dawnstep Bridge.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>After the Thrice-Blessed Brothel was established (but before it became an inn), Willowshore’s population had grown enough in size to be considered a town by Shenmen standards, meaning that a lit lantern must be maintained at all times within the town near the entrance, at a major crossroads, or at a bridge. The lack of a lit lantern at one of these locations suggests that the town is abandoned, which is believed to invite vermin, ghosts, dangerous beasts, and worse. Today, Willowshore features two such lanterns, but the one that stands here, the Eternal Lantern, is both its oldest and most notable.</p>"
            },
            "Lady of Souls": {
              "name": "司魂娘娘 Lady of Souls",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W9. 司魂娘娘</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp\" alt=\"伊丽丝·堪多拉\" data-tooltip=\"伊丽丝·堪多拉\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>龙华人在最初将势力扩张到柳岸镇时，最主要的担忧之一就是降低不死暴动的可能性。他们通过建造一座供奉法莱斯玛的大教堂解决了这个问题。</p>\n<p><strong>伊丽丝·堪多拉</strong>（富有同理心的人类女性牧师），来自过峡的第二代塔尔丹人，是此地现任女祭司。小时候曾到访过柳岸镇与谭杉寺的伊丽丝，从未想过自己成为法莱斯玛的牧师后，竟会得到机会永久回到这个她记忆犹新的村镇。她将这份巧合视作法莱斯玛之手安排的命运，因此尽责而勤勉地侍奉。她喜欢独自在墓园里与长笛为伴，常在那儿吹奏，以帮助安抚那些最近葬于此处之人的魂魄。</p>\n<p><strong>货物：</strong>消耗性宗教物品、神术卷轴</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W9. Lady of Souls</h3>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp\" alt=\"Elizeth Candora\" data-tooltip=\"Elizeth Candora\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90197-elizethcandora.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>One of Lung Wa’s chief concerns when they first expanded into Willowshore was to reduce the likelihood of an undead uprising. They solved it by building a cathedral to Pharasma.</p>\n<p><strong>Elizeth Candora</strong> (empathetic female human cleric), a second-generation Taldan from Goka, is the current priestess here. Having once visited Willowshore and the Tan Sugi monastery as a child, Elizeth never imagined that becoming a cleric of Pharasma would lead to an opportunity for her to permanently return to the village she vividly recalls. She sees the coincidence as fate arranged by Pharasma’s hands and therefore serves dutifully and diligently. She’s fond of spending time alone in the graveyard with her flute and often plays the instrument there to help soothe the spirits of those recently buried therein.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> consumable religious items, divine scrolls</p>"
            },
            "Milling Houses": {
              "name": "磨坊 Milling Houses",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W8. 磨坊</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇有许多磨坊，其中两座由水力驱动，三座由风力驱动，十座由人力或役用动物驱动。数量充裕，确保即便因例行维护或故障而停用一两座磨，也不会危及村子的需求。</p>\n<p>磨坊的工作强度很大，而且由于每天需求不同，工时可能不规律。磨坊工人的领头人<strong>乔春虎</strong>（乐于支持的男性人类磨坊工）以鼓励来维持士气，抵制不合理的要求，保持工资稳定，并提供午夜点心。</p>\n<p><strong>货物：</strong>脱壳谷物、谷物面粉、石制物体</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W8. Milling Houses</h3>\n<p>Willowshore has numerous millhouses, including two powered by water, three by wind, and ten powered by people or draft animals. The abundance ensures that losing one or two mills to routine maintenance or malfunction never jeopardizes the village’s needs.</p>\n<p>Work at the mills is intense, and the hours can be irregular due to the demand each day. The millers’ leader, <strong>Choe Chung-hu</strong> (supportive male human miller), keeps morale high with encouragement, pushing back against unreasonable demands, keeping wages stable, and offering midnight snacks.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> De-husked grain, grain flour, stone objects</p>"
            },
            "Silvermist Lodges": {
              "name": "银雾斋 Silvermist Lodges",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W7. 银雾斋</h3>\n<p>银雾斋分布在镇子以南树林里的两处小型院落中。每处地点的屋舍木作都顺着木纹走势而制，使建筑呈现出一种有机的外观，这也与精灵的建筑风格相契合。在柳岸镇最初尝试实现自给自足的那些日子里，有八名精灵冒险者来到此地，并接受了在村里定居的提议；以他们的寿命而言，他们将这一请求视作一份短期契约。尽管最初的八名精灵如今都已不再居住在柳岸镇，但他们留下了许多子嗣与后代。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>动物部件、捕兽套索用品</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W7. Silvermist Lodges</h3>\n<p>The Silvermist Lodges are split between two small compounds in the woods south of town. At each location, the lodges’ woodwork conforms to the grain of the wood, giving the buildings an organic look associated with elven architecture. In the days when Willowshore first tried to become self-sufficient, eight elven adventurers came and took up an offer to settle in the village, seeing the request as a short-term contract given their life spans. Though none of these original eight elves live in Willowshore anymore, they left many offspring and descendants behind.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> animal parts, snare supplies</p>"
            },
            "Thrice-Blessed Inn": {
              "name": "三福客栈 Thrice-Blessed Inn",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W6. 三福客栈</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇的三福客栈最初是三福青楼，因为它由三位分别信奉国府幸、卡莉丝翠与莎琳的牧师共同创立。政治上的纠葛迫使青楼的主人奥蒂丝妈妈（精明的性别流动半精灵客栈老板）在龙华崩溃前几年就关闭了这家店。在柳岸镇当地律师骆熙旸的协助下，奥蒂丝妈妈得以援引一条鲜为人知的法律，避免被驱逐，并获准继续将这栋建筑作为客栈经营。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W6. Thrice-Blessed Inn</h3>\n<p>Willowshore’s Thrice-Blessed Inn began as the Thrice-Blessed Brothel, for it was founded by three clerics of Kofusachi, Calistria, and Shelyn. Political complications forced the brothel’s owner, Mother Otis (canny genderfluid half-elf innkeeper), to shut down the establishment only a few years before Lung Wa’s collapse. With the aid of Willowshore’s local lawyer, Luo Xi Yang, Mother Otis was able to rely upon an obscure law that prevented their eviction and allowed them to continue to operate the building as an inn.</p>"
            },
            "Matsuki Estate": {
              "name": "松木宅 Matsuki Estate",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W5. 松木宅</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇人称为<strong>“老”松木</strong>的那名男子（怀旧的人类男性木匠）曾做过谭杉寺首席木匠的学徒。在向师父告辞后，他带领家人建造了一座大型嬛族语/密凯安式宅邸，好让他们二十来口人都能住在一起。据说，这位迷信的家主随后还特意让人用掺有祝圣盐与圣水的石灰石来粉刷外墙。如今，老松木是柳岸镇南岸派系中最有影响力的人物，并担任该派系的发言人。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W5. Matsuki Estate</h3>\n<p>The man that Willowshore calls <strong>“Old” Matsuki</strong> (nostalgic male human carpenter) once apprenticed to the head carpenter of the Tan Sugi monastery. After taking leave from his master, he led his family to construct a large Tian-shu/Minkaian estate to house all two dozen of them. Reportedly, the superstitious patriarch then made sure that the outer walls were whitewashed with limestone containing blessed salts and holy water. Today, Old Matsuki is the most influential of Willowshore’s Southbank faction and serves as the faction’s spokesman.</p>"
            },
            "Abadar Shrine": {
              "name": "财神爷神龛 Abadar Shrine",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W4. 财神爷神龛</h3>\n<p>这座雅致的神龛里供奉着一尊3英尺高的石灰岩阿巴达尔雕像，雕像一手握着铁锹，另一手拿着泥刀。据说这尊雕像最初被带到过峡，先在大银行举行仪式以祈请阿巴达尔的神圣祝福，随后才被运回柳岸镇。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W4. Abadar Shrine</h3>\n<p>This elegant shrine houses a 3-foot-tall limestone statue of Abadar that holds a shovel in one hand and a trowel in the other. The statue was reportedly taken to Goka first to ritualistically invite Abadar’s divine blessings at the Grand Bank before being ferried back to Willowshore.</p>"
            },
            "Graveside Manners": {
              "name": "坟边居 Graveside Manners",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W3. 坟边居</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇的居民在早期实行火葬以防止不死生物出现。这座古老墓地里的坟墓安放着许多早期定居者的骨灰瓮。如今，只有少数家族仍将坟边居作为埋葬之地。墓碑上几乎不见地衣与苔藓，这多亏了墓园的守墓人尤素珍（神秘的女性精灵草药师）。素珍曾是一名常去谭杉寺朝圣的香客；寺院崩塌后，她在柳岸镇定居，并经营着一家草药店——这也是如今人们前来坟边居的主要原因。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>炼金灵药与工具、炼金试剂、新鲜与干燥草药</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W3. Graveside Manners</h3>\n<p>Willowshore’s residents practiced cremation in its early days to prevent undeath. The tombs in this old cemetery house the urns of many of those early settlers. Today, only a few families use Graveside Manners as a burial ground. The headstones remain free of lichen and moss thanks to the graveyard’s keeper, You So-Jin (mysterious female elf herbalist). Once a pilgrim who frequented the Tan Sugi monastery, So-Jin settled in Willowshore after the monastery’s collapse and maintains an herbalist shop—the primary reason anyone visits Graveside Manners today.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> alchemical elixirs and tools, alchemical reagents, fresh and dried herbs</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Stables": {
              "name": "柳岸镇马场 Willowshore Stables",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W2. 柳岸镇马场</h3>\n<p>柳岸镇马场是镇上为家养动物、宠物和牲畜提供兽医服务的设施。顺带一提，柳岸镇马场将牲畜用作役畜的做法影响了村子的饮食文化，导致许多家庭避免食用牛肉。其主人昆舜重（和蔼的男性人类兽医）与他十几岁的儿子蒙松（尽责的男性人类兽医）以他们友善的态度以及对各种动物的慈爱而闻名。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>动物租赁、坐骑护甲、鞍囊、陆地载具</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W2. Willowshore Stables</h3>\n<p>Willowshore Stables is the town’s veterinary facility for household animals, pets, and livestock. Incidentally, Willowshore Stables’ use of livestock as beasts of burden influenced the village’s food culture, causing many households to avoid the consumption of beef. The owner, Kum Soon-chong (caring male human veterinarian), and his teenage son, Meng-sung (dutiful male human veterinarian), are well-known for their affable attitudes and compassion for all kinds of animals.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> animal rentals, barding, saddle bags, land vehicles</p>"
            },
            "Eternal Blaze Ironworks": {
              "name": "永火铁厂 Eternal Blaze Ironworks",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W1. 永火铁厂</h3>\n<p>在修道院建造的那些日子里，永火铁厂负责制作各种金属物品，从炊具、木工工具到小型金属零件，例如用于箱子的铰链、锁和钥匙。<strong>雍武秀</strong>（勤劳的女性狐妖铁匠）大约在十年前从父亲手中继承了这门生意。</p>\n<p><strong>商品：</strong>金属制品、冒险道具（尤其是炊具）、金属护甲、金属武器、金属盾牌</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>W1. Eternal Blaze Ironworks</h3>\n<p>In the days of the monastery’s construction, the Eternal Blaze Ironworks was responsible for creating metal items from cookware, woodworking tools, and small metal parts, such as hinges, locks, and keys for chests. <strong>Yong Wu-Xiu</strong> (industrious female kitsune blacksmith) inherited the business from her father about a decade ago.</p>\n<p><strong>Wares:</strong> metalworks, adventuring gear (especially cookware), metal armor, metal weapons, metal shields</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Locations": {
              "name": "柳岸镇地点 Willowshore Locations",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>柳岸镇地点</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇中的重要建筑与关键人物详述于以下页面，其编号对应城镇地图上的地点。未标注的建筑为木结构，可能是商店、住宅、农舍、储藏室，或会因其所处位置而有其他用途；并且在GM许可下，可被选作任何PC的住所。</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">重新编号</span><span class=\"keepme\">日志</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">《玩家指南》中地点的顺序与编号已被调整，以与GM在完整冒险文本中所见内容一致，从而更好地促进在共享的柳岸镇场景中的沟通。这意味着下方内容会与玩家指南pdf存在细微差异。</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Willowshore Locations</h2>\n<p>Significant buildings and important people found in Willowshore are detailed on the following pages, with numbers corresponding to the locations on the town map. Unlabeled buildings are wooden structures that might be shops, homes, farmhouses, storerooms, or have other usage depending on their location and, with the GM’s permission, can be selected as homes for any PC.</p>\n<section class=\"encounter\" data-scroll=\"scenenotes\">\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <img style=\"transform:scale(1);filter:drop-shadow(1px 1px 2px black)\" src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/metamorphic-logo.svg\" alt=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" title=\"MetaMorphic Digital\" />\n    <h2 class=\"split no-toc\"><span class=\"keepme\">Renumbering</span><span class=\"keepme\">Journal</span></h2>\n    <span class=\"link\">The order and numbering of locations have been changed in the Player's Guide to match what the GM sees in the full adventure text, to better facilitate communication on the shared Willowshore Scene. That means that the below will have small differences from the player's guide pdf.</span>\n  </div>\n</section>"
            },
            "People of Willowshore": {
              "name": "柳岸镇的人民 People of Willowshore",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>柳岸镇的人民</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇的大多数居民，会以自家何时最初在镇上定居来区分身份；这往往也会影响他们住在木棉河的哪一岸。最早一批镇民，要么在修道院工作，要么受修道院雇佣来柳岸镇定居。这些人最初住在河的南岸，因此被称为南岸人。另一方面，在龙瓦掌权之后才来到此地的人，则定居在河的北岸；由于那里坡势明显，被称为北岭人。这些定居者包括为木材大亨工作的工人、希望便捷取得木材的商家，以及帝国卫队。</p>\n<p>尽管如今柳岸镇的这两派使用“南岸”与“北岭”之名，但一个人的归属并不完全由其居住或工作的地点决定。南岸居民偏向传统主义者，热衷于维护柳岸镇的文化，并以朴素的方式依靠土地生活。北岭居民则更注重务实与城镇发展。北岭的许多人对让络新妇统治神门这一想法持开放态度，而南岸人则基于原则认为络新妇是邪恶的怪物，最好敬而远之。</p>\n<p>尽管存在分歧，双方仍一致认为应将柳岸镇的生存与安全置于首位。许多居民有着既不偏向任何一方的看法，并认为自己不隶属于任何派系。总体而言，柳岸镇重视倾尽所有、竭尽所能的付出。在许多方面，尤其随着这场冒险中的事件逐步展开，村子也别无选择。</p>\n<p>在你游玩《鬼季》时，你们作为一个团体的行动与选择，将在这两派之中建立名声；你的 GM 拥有追踪名声并在游戏进程中实施其效果所需的全部规则与指引。</p>\n<p>目前柳岸镇的热门话题集中在木材领主近期的出走、有关络新妇夺取国家控制权的传闻，以及为即将到来的鬼季所做的准备。</p>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">柳岸镇</span> <span class=\"keepme\">聚居地 4</span></h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp\" alt=\"“老”松木胜\" data-tooltip=\"“老”松木胜\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp');max-width:200px\" class=\"float-right\" />\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">城镇</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">与世隔绝的伐木镇</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>政府</strong> 委任总督（和善保）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>人口</strong> 225（73% 人类，6% 半精灵，4% 半身人，4% 狐族，3% 精灵，3% 天狗，2% 那伽裔，5% 其他）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>语言</strong> 通用语（天语）、精灵语、半身人语、米纳坦语、那伽裔语、天狗语、天华语、天民语</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>宗教</strong> 阿巴达，黛奇图，难婆，法拉丝玛，善解，其他（以小神龛的形式呈现）</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>威胁</strong> 恶意灵体，贪食的害虫，艰难的自给自足，超自然影响，护地盘的野兽</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>共克时艰</strong> 柳岸镇的居民尽管彼此有分歧，仍会互相帮助。即使另一位柳岸镇居民对你不关心或不友善，你仍可以尝试向其提出“请求”以获得帮助，但你会承受 –2 环境减值。</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“奶奶”胡板娘</strong>（令人生畏的天书女性，退休的帝国卫队长）退休的帝国卫队长</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“老”松木胜</strong>（怀旧的天书男性，家族族长）退休木匠与柳岸镇的活历史</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>和善保</strong>（紧张的天书男性，总督）柳岸镇的委任行政官</p>\n</section>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>People of Willowshore</h2>\n<p>Most of Willowshore’s citizens identify by when their family first settled in town, often affecting which bank of the Ceiba River they live on. The first wave of townspeople were either those who worked on the monastery or were paid to settle in Willowshore by the monastery. These folks originally lived south of the river and are thus referred to as Southbankers. Those who arrived after Lung Wa took control, meanwhile, settled on the river’s northern banks, called Northridge due to its prominent incline. These settlers included workers for the lumber bosses, businesses that wanted convenient access to the lumber, and imperial guards.</p>\n<p>Though these two factions in Willowshore today use the names Southbank and Northridge, one’s allegiance isn’t solely determined by where they live or work. Southbank residents are traditionalists, keen on maintaining Willowshore’s culture and living simply off the land. Northridge residents, meanwhile, focus on pragmatism and urban growth. Many in Northridge are open to the idea of jorogumo ruling Shenmen, while Southbankers on principle think jorogumo are evil monsters and best avoided.</p>\n<p>Despite disagreements, both sides have a consensus on putting Willowshore’s survival and safety first. Plenty of residents have their own opinions that lean in neither direction and consider themselves unaffiliated with either faction. Overall, Willowshore values giving all one has to offer. In many ways, the village has no choice, especially as the events of this adventure evolve.</p>\n<p>As you play Season of Ghosts, your actions and choices as a group will build reputation with these two factions; your GM has all the rules and guidance needed to track reputation and implement its effects in the game as play progresses.</p>\n<p>Current trending topics in Willowshore focus on the recent exodus of the lumber lords, rumors of jorogumo seizing control of the nation, and preparations for the upcoming season of ghosts.</p>\n\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">Willowshore</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Settlement 4</span></h2>\n  <img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp\" alt=\"“Old” Matsuki Shou\" data-tooltip=\"“Old” Matsuki Shou\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-oldmatsuki.webp');max-width:200px\" class=\"float-right\" />\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait\">Town</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\">Isolated lumber town</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Government</strong> Appointed governor (Heh Shan-Bao)</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Population</strong> 225 (73% humans, 6% half-elves, 4% halflings, 4% kitsune, 3% elves, 3% tengu, 2% nagaji, 5% others)</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Languages</strong> Common (Tien), Elven, Halfling, Minatan, Nagaji, Tengu, Tian-hwa, Tian-min</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Religions</strong> Abadar, Daikitsu, Lady Nanbyo, Pharasma, Sangpotshi, others (represented by small shrines)</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Threats</strong> malicious spirits, ravenous vermin, struggling self-sufficiency, supernatural influences, territorial beasts</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Teeth-Clenching Teamwork</strong> Willowshore’s residents help one another despite differences. You can attempt to Request help from another Willowshore resident even if they’re indifferent or unfriendly, but you do so with a –2 circumstance penalty.</p>\n  <hr />\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“Granny” Hu Ban-niang</strong> (intimidating female Tian-shu retired guard captain) retired imperial guard captain</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>“Old” Matsuki Shou</strong> (nostalgic male Tian-shu family patriarch) retired carpenter and Willowshore’s living history</p>\n  <p class=\"hanging-indent\"><strong>Heh Shan-Bao</strong> (nervous male Tian-shu governor) appointed administrator of Willowshore</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Willowshore Gazetteer": {
              "name": "柳岸镇地名志 Willowshore Gazetteer",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>柳岸镇地理志</h1>\n<p>7020年，一位名为智惠的善解僧侣建立了谭杉寺。谭杉寺围绕一棵据说具有神秘性质的古老杉树而建，位置极其偏远，坐落在幽魂之森一处尚未定居、林木茂密的山谷中。柳岸镇最初建立是为了支援建造寺院的人们，而连接城镇与寺院的那条漫长小路后来被称为朝圣之径。寺院建造完成后，柳岸镇的重心转向日益自给自足的生活方式，只需偶尔支援寺中僧侣。</p>\n<p>智惠于7054年去世；随着寺中僧侣开始陆续离开，柳岸镇本身也把重心转向伐木业。到7060年，寺院已被遗弃；但在7062年，当一群樵夫试图采伐在那里生长的古老杉树时，悲剧发生了。那天傍晚，樵夫们带着破损的武器与不死的尸体回到柳岸镇；尽管这些不死樵夫在次日清晨便被击败，仍有数十名镇民在搏斗中丧生。此事如今被称为“断刀夜”，此后46年间，几乎没有访客再踏上前往那座废墟寺院的旅程。如今那里被视为遭到诅咒、闹鬼，或更糟。</p>\n<p>岁月流逝，神门正式征募柳岸镇，使其成为龙华伐木开采野心的一部分。起初进展顺利，修建了包括桥梁与水坝在内的基础设施。然而，负责开采作业的伐木头目很快因对柳岸镇清苦过往的利用而遭人憎恨。更糟的是，他们开始将这处聚落（如今已名正言顺称为城镇）包装成供龙华贵族“度假”的去处，让其以狩猎取乐，并恣意享用以帝国之名强行征取的食物与酒水。</p>\n<p>当龙华于7106年崩溃时，柳岸镇的伐木领主携其财富离去，抛下庄园并逃亡。驻扎在镇上的大多数士兵要么返回神门的首都，要么擅离职守，只留下那些已在当地扎根的人。柳岸镇的偏远使其免于猖獗的匪患与外部政治冲突——这些问题已开始困扰神门；但正如你在开始游玩鬼季时不久便会发现的那样，柳岸镇直面新世界的时代已经到来。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Willowshore Gazetteer</h1>\n<p>In 7020, the Tan Sugi monastery was founded by a Sangpotshi monk named Zhi Hui. Built around an ancient sugi tree said to have mystic properties, the Tan Sugi monastery was incredibly remote, nestled in a wooded valley within an unsettled reach of Specterwood. Willowshore was originally founded to support those who built the monastery, and the long trail that connected the town to the monastery became known as the Pilgrim’s Path. Once construction of the monastery ended, Willowshore’s focus shifted to an increasingly self-sufficient lifestyle that only periodically needed to support the monks.</p>\n<p>Zhi Hui passed away in 7054, and as the monks of the monastery began to drift away, Willowshore itself shifted focus to the lumber industry. By 7060, the monastery had been abandoned, but when a group of woodcutters attempted to harvest the ancient sugi trees that grew there in 7062, tragedy struck. The woodcutters returned to Willowshore with broken weapons and unliving bodies that evening, and while these undead woodcutters were defeated by morning, dozens of townsfolk had perished during the struggle. The event is remembered today as the “Night of Broken Blades,” and few visitors have made the journey to the ruined monastery in the 46 years since. The place is regarded now as cursed, haunted, or worse.</p>\n<p>As the years wore on, Shenmen officially enlisted Willowshore to become part of Lung Wa’s lumber harvesting ambitions. Things started out well, with the construction of infrastructure including bridges and a dam. However, the lumber bosses who ran the harvesting operation soon became loathed for their exploitation of Willowshore’s ascetic past. Worse, they began to present the settlement (now properly called a town) as a “getaway” for Lung Wa aristocrats to hunt for sport and indulge in food and drinks forcefully seized in the empire’s name.</p>\n<p>When Lung Wa collapsed in 7106, Willowshore’s lumber lords took their wealth, abandoned their estates, and fled. Most of the soldiers stationed in town returned to Shenmen’s capital or deserted their posts, leaving behind those who had put down local roots. Willowshore’s remoteness saved it from rampant banditry and external political conflicts that had begun to plague Shenmen, but as you will soon discover when you begin to play Season of Ghosts, the time has come for Willowshore to face the new world.</p>"
            },
            "Suggested Character Options": {
              "name": "推荐的角色选项 Suggested Character Options",
              "text": "<h3 class=\"no-toc table\">建议的角色选项</h3>\n<table style=\"font-size:0.85rem;margin-left:-30px;margin-right:-30px;width:calc(100% + 60px)\">\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th></th>\n      <th>族裔</th>\n      <th>职业</th>\n      <th>语言</th>\n      <th>技能</th>\n      <th>变体</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p><strong>强烈推荐</strong></p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>人类、精灵、半精灵、半身人、狐妖、莱西、纳迦吉、天狗</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>泛灵师、吟游诗人、武僧、德鲁伊、调查员、武僧、神谕者、游侠、游荡者、奇械师、女巫</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>通用语（嬛族语）</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>运动、交涉、自然、宗教、社会、柳岸镇学识</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>仪式师</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p><strong>推荐</strong></p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>其他核心族裔、吸血裔（特征）、冥人（特征）、大地精、莱西、涅菲林、鼠人、轮回者</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>炼金术士、牧师、战士、魔战士、灵能者、术士、召唤师、剑客、法师</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>邪灵语、地底语、精灵语、妖精语、半身人语、狐妖语、死灵语</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>奥秘、制作、欺瞒、威吓、神秘、求生、盗窃</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>天眷者、赏金猎人、决斗家、草药师、元帅、武术家、魂魄战士、流浪厨师</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p><strong>合适</strong></p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>所有其他族裔（除以下者）</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>所有其他职业（除以下者）</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>龙语、天界语、地精语、嬛族语、民凯语、纳迦吉语、安魂语、轮回者语、天狗语</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>特技、医术、表演、隐匿</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>所有其他变体（除以下者）</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <strong>不<br />推荐</strong>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>机械人、水栖族裔</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>枪手</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>所有其他</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>—</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>刺客、枪手多职、海盗、义警、维京人</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h3 class=\"no-toc table\">Suggested Character Options</h3>\n<table style=\"font-size:0.85rem;margin-left:-30px;margin-right:-30px;width:calc(100% + 60px)\">\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th></th>\n      <th>Ancestries</th>\n      <th>Classes</th>\n      <th>Languages</th>\n      <th>Skills</th>\n      <th>Archetypes</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p><strong>Strongly Recommended</strong></p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Humans, Elves, Half-elves, Halflings, Kitsunes, Leshies, Nagajis, Tengus</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Animist, Bard, Champion, Druid, Investigator, Monk, Oracle, Ranger, Rogue, Thaumaturge, Witch</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Common (Tian)</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Athletics, Diplomacy, Nature, Religion, Society, Willowshore Lore</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Ritualist</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p><strong>Recommended</strong></p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Other core ancestries, Dhampirs, Duskwalkers, Hobgoblins, Leshies, Nephilim, Ratfolk, Samsarans</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Alchemist, Cleric, Fighter, Magus, Psychic, Sorcerer, Summoner, Swashbuckler, Wizard</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Aklo, Chthonian, Elven, Fey, Halfling, Kitsune, Necril</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Arcana, Crafting, Deception, Intimidation, Occultism, Survival, Thievery</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Blessed One, Bounty Hunter, Duelist, Herbalist, Marshal, Martial artist, Spirit Warrior, Wandering Chef</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p><strong>Appropriate</strong></p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>All other ancestries (save those below)</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>All other classes (save those below)</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Draconic, Empyrean, Goblin, Hwan, Minkaian, Nagaji, Requian, Samsaran, Tengu</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Acrobatics, Medicine, Performance, Stealth</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>All other archetypes (save those below)</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <strong>Not<br />Recommended</strong>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Androids, Aquatic Ancestries</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Gunslinger</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>All others</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>—</p>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <p>Assassin, Gunslinger multiclass, Pirate, Vigilante, Viking</p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
            },
            "Home and Heirloom": {
              "name": "故乡与传家宝 Home and Heirloom",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>家与传家宝</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>八项守则</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇的人民在夏季最初几周——鬼季——遵循这八条忠告。这些信念主要是当地迷信，至于它们在与任何恶意灵体的遭遇中是否真能帮上忙，人们争论不休。</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li>不要把鬼叫做“鬼”；如果非得称呼它们，就用友善的问候语。</li>\n    <li>不要拍别人的头或肩膀。</li>\n    <li>附近有鬼时，避免进入任何水域。</li>\n    <li>不要吃从食物里伸出两根棒状物的食物。</li>\n    <li>白天不要倚靠墙壁。</li>\n    <li>夜里不要吹口哨。</li>\n    <li>夜里不要把洗好的衣物晾在外面。</li>\n    <li>如果夜里听到有人从你身后喊你的名字，不要回头。</li>\n  </ol>\n</aside>\n\n<p>创建你的鬼季角色的最后一步，是选择你在柳岸镇的居所。第16页所示的城镇地图展示了柳岸镇的所有建筑。如果你选择了一个鬼季背景，该选择会暗示你家最可能位于柳岸镇的哪里，但你不必受此暗示限制——你可以把地图上任何未标注的小型建筑选作你角色的家（注意：你的GM可能对某些建筑有建议或计划，超出这场冒险的预期范围，因此在你最终确定住所之前，需要得到GM许可）。</p>\n<p>选定住所后，从下列四组宝藏中选择一组。当你开始鬼季时，你所选的宝藏仍存放在家中。虽然在第一段冒险开始时你无法使用它，但用不了多久，每位PC都会有机会回家取回家族宝藏以供使用！</p>\n<p>选择这些宝藏时，每位玩家必须选择不同的选项——只有当队伍中玩家超过四人时，你才可以选择已被其他玩家选过的宝藏。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>两瓶下等治疗药水，以及一件由该PC自选、价值不超过2 gp的普通冒险道具。</li>\n  <li>一枚可预见的银币，以及一支小瓶，内含1剂潜能油。</li>\n  <li>制作警报圈套的材料、10 sp，以及两枚次级镇魂炸药。</li>\n  <li>一块价值10 gp的寒铁块。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Home and Heirloom</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>The Eight Practices</h1>\n  <p>The people of Willowshore follow these eight bits of advice during the first several weeks of summer—the season of ghosts. These beliefs are primarily local superstitions, and their capacity to actually help in an encounter with any sort of malicious spirit is hotly debated.</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li>Do not call a ghost a ghost; instead, address them with friendly greetings if you must.</li>\n    <li>Do not pat people on the head or shoulders.</li>\n    <li>Avoid entering bodies of water when a ghost is nearby.</li>\n    <li>Do not eat food that has two stick-like objects protruding from it.</li>\n    <li>Do not lean against walls during the day.</li>\n    <li>Do not whistle at night.</li>\n    <li>Do not leave laundry out at night.</li>\n    <li>If you hear someone call your name from behind you at night, do not turn around.</li>\n  </ol>\n</aside>\n\n<p>The final step for creating your Season of Ghosts character is to choose where you live in Willowshore. The town map presented on page 16 shows all of the buildings in Willowshore. If you chose a Season of Ghosts background, that choice suggests where in Willowshore your home is most likely to be located, but you need not be limited by this suggestion—you can pick any unlabeled smaller building on the map as your character’s home (note that your GM might have suggestions or plans for certain buildings beyond the expected scope of the adventure, so before you settle on your home, you’ll need GM approval).</p>\n<p>Once you’ve chosen your home, pick one of the following four sets of treasure. When you start Season of Ghosts, the treasure you selected is still stored back home. While you won’t have access to it when the first adventure begins, it won’t be long into the adventure before each PC will have the opportunity to return home and gather their family treasures for use!</p>\n<p>When selecting these treasures, each player must choose a different option—only if there are more than four players in the group can you choose a treasure already selected by another player.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Two minor healing potions and one piece of common adventuring gear worth 2 gp or less of the PC’s choice.</li>\n  <li>One predictable silver piece and a vial containing one dose of oil of potency.</li>\n  <li>Supplies for an alarm snare, 10 sp, and two lesser ghost charges.</li>\n  <li>One cold-iron chunk worth 10 gp.</li>\n</ul>"
            },
            "Background Adjustments": {
              "name": "背景调整 Background Adjustments",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>背景调整</h3>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>关于你的家人</h1>\n  <p>尽管柳岸镇是你角色的家，而且他们可能有近亲住在镇上，但《鬼季》完全不会把任何潜在的PC家人纳入冒险剧情之中。如果你的角色在柳岸镇与父母、兄弟姐妹、子女、恋爱伴侣或其他家人同住，请与GM讨论：你是否希望他们只扮演纯粹的背景角色，或在GM协助下，在战役剧情中占据更关键的部分。尤其要让GM知道，你是否能接受家人可能会受到《鬼季》中某些要素的威胁，并确保其他玩家也能接受这一要素。同样地，《鬼季》中没有任何剧情要素会直接危及任何PC的家人（除了所有柳岸镇居民都面临的生存层面的危机），但对某些玩家与团体而言，让家人参与这类故事，能让体验更具挑战性，也更有回报。</p>\n</aside>\n\n<p>你可以将以下两项调整之一添加到任何背景（包括普通背景）上，以进一步修改你的选择，使其更符合你对PC的构想。</p>\n<p><strong>家人：</strong>你与另一名（或多名）PC是关系亲密的家人（兄弟姐妹、亲子、已婚等）。如果你选择此调整，作为你家人的其他PC也必须选择此调整。从下列选项中选择一项，用以替换你原本会从背景获得的技能专长。（你和你的兄弟姐妹不必做出相同选择——想保留其背景技能专长的兄弟姐妹可以从列表中选择“典型”。）</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>斗嘴：</strong>你与兄弟姐妹之间有一段由来已久的口角与不和。每当你的兄弟姐妹在一次重要的技能检定或攻击掷骰上大失败，且你目睹了他们的失败时，你会在暗自（或也许并不那么暗自）幸灾乐祸之下，在你的下一回合结束前，获得对你的豁免骰的+1状态加值。</li>\n  <li><strong>亲密无间：</strong>你与兄弟姐妹配合默契，当他们重伤时你会全力协助他们。当你对兄弟姐妹进行协助或施行急救时，其DC比正常值低5。</li>\n  <li><strong>典型：</strong>你与兄弟姐妹的关系很普通；不改变你背景的技能专长。</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>弃儿：</strong>你并非柳岸镇的本地人，但你确实在镇里长大。你可能有养父母，或你可能在街头长大。从下列选项中选择一项，用以替换你原本会从背景获得的额外专长。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>愤懑：</strong>你欣赏柳岸镇，但仍对导致你被遗弃或被留在镇上的处境心怀怨恨。你获得金刚怒目技能专长。</li>\n  <li><strong>神秘： </strong>你守口如瓶，柳岸镇中很少有人（若有的话）知道你在定居于镇上之前的经历，部分原因在于你习惯以观察而非交谈来了解柳岸镇。你获得人情练达技能专长。</li>\n  <li><strong>外向：</strong>你感激柳岸镇镇民给予你的归属感，并总是尽力回报那份善意。每周一次，当你尝试进行一次技能检定，以解决一项可能使柳岸镇受益的休整模式行动（其中几项行动在冒险中有详细说明；若是其他行动是否符合条件，也总可以由你的GM裁定），且你在该检定中失败时，你改为成功；或者若你在该检定中大失败时，你改为仅仅失败。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Background Adjustments</h3>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>About Your Family</h1>\n  <p>Although Willowshore is your character’s home, and they might have close family dwelling in town, Season of Ghosts doesn’t incorporate any potential PC family members into the adventure plots at all. If your character has parents, siblings, children, romantic partners, or other family living with them in Willowshore, talk with your GM about whether you’d like them to play purely a background role or, with the GM’s aid, take up a more integral part of the campaign’s plot. In particular, let your GM know if you’re comfortable potentially having family members become threatened by elements in Season of Ghosts, and make sure the other players are okay with this element as well. Again, there are no plot elements in Season of Ghosts that directly imperil any PC’s family (beyond the existential peril facing all of Willowshore’s inhabitants), but for some players and groups, involving family in stories like this one can make the experience more challenging and rewarding.</p>\n</aside>\n\n<p>You can add one of the following two adjustments to any background (including a Common one) to further modify your choice to match your vision for your PC.</p>\n<p><strong>Family:</strong> You and one (or more) other PCs are close family members (siblings, parent/child, married, etc.). If you take this adjustment, the other PC(s) who are your family must also take this adjustment. Choose one of the following to replace the skill feat you otherwise would’ve gained from your background. (You and your sibling need not share the same choice—a sibling who wants to keep their background’s skill feat can pick “Typical” from the list.)</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Bickering:</strong> You have a long-standing feud with your sibling(s). Whenever your sibling(s) critically fail a significant skill check or attack roll and you witness their failure, you gain a +1 status bonus to your saving throws until the end of your next turn as you secretly (or perhaps not so secretly) delight in their failure.</li>\n  <li><strong>Close-Knit:</strong> You and your sibling(s) work well together, and you go all-out to help them when they’re badly hurt. When you provide Aid or Administer First Aid to your sibling(s), the DC is 5 lower than normal.</li>\n  <li><strong>Typical:</strong> You have a standard relationship with your sibling(s); don’t change your background’s skill feat.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Foundling:</strong> You aren’t a native to Willowshore, but you did grow up in the town. You might have adoptive parents, or you could’ve grown up on the streets. Choose one of the following to replace the bonus feat you otherwise would’ve gained from your background.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Bitter:</strong> You appreciate the town of Willowshore but still resent the conditions that resulted in you being abandoned or left in the town. You gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat.</li>\n  <li><strong>Mysterious: </strong>You keep secrets, and very few in Willowshore (if anyone) know your history before you settled in the town, in part because you’ve taken to learning about Willowshore by watching rather than engaging in conversation. You gain the Streetwise skill feat.</li>\n  <li><strong>Outgoing:</strong> You’re grateful for the sense of belonging the townsfolk of Willowshore have extended to you and always do your best to repay that kindness. Once per week when you attempt a skill check to resolve a downtime activity that could benefit Willowshore (several of these activities are detailed in the adventures, and your GM can always make the call if another activity would qualify) and you fail that check, you instead succeed at the check, or if you critically fail at that check, you instead simply fail that check.</li>\n</ul>"
            },
            "Season of Ghosts Backgrounds": {
              "name": "鬼季背景 Season of Ghosts Backgrounds",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>鬼季背景</h3>\n<p>接下来几页中介绍的6个新背景，适用于《鬼季》冒险路径中的所有角色。每个稀有背景都是为配合本冒险路径的主题而量身打造，并包含一些关于重现节的风味描述，以及你为何会被选为庆典的绑架对象之一。</p>\n<p><strong>季节恩赐：</strong>这些背景中的每一个都会给予你一个季节恩赐。你可以在任何时间以自由动作使用季节恩赐（其触发条件如你的背景所述），但每个季节只能使用一次（夏、秋、冬、春——对应《鬼季》冒险路径的四个幕次；你的GM会告诉你何时进入新的幕次，而你的恩赐也会再次可用一次）。如果你在某一幕次中没有使用季节恩赐，该次使用就会作废——未使用的季节恩赐不会延续到下一幕次。</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.uker8dnTA7WhzXSR]{Close Ties}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">背景</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">你与柳岸镇的一位知名市民建立了亲密友谊，并形成了悠久的传统：一边分享茶饮，一边聊共同的兴趣、未来计划、镇上八卦或其他值得一提的事情。与GM合作，从《柳岸镇志》中提到的NPC里选择一位（胡婆婆或老松木除外）——你的GM可能会建议哪个NPC最适合你的角色，或是知道某位NPC在战役后续将扮演的角色，从而为你的角色提供一个引人入胜的剧情节拍。你可能是这位NPC的雇员或学徒、亲近的亲属或朋友，甚至在某种意义上是友好的竞争对手。</p>\n  <p>你的住处很可能离你的NPC盟友的店铺或住处相对较近。</p>\n  <p>在重现节期间，你很可能与这位NPC盟友共度了一些时光，并可能约定在次日——也就是夏季第一天——再聚一聚，也许一起喝茶。你之所以在重现节期间被选为绑架对象，可能是因为你的NPC朋友或盟友认为这会很有趣或对你有益；也可能是因为他们在你去年的怂恿下参与过，而现在“轮到你了”。</p>\n  <p>选择两次属性提升。其中一次必须给魅力或智力，另一次为自由属性提升。</p>\n  <p>你受训于交涉（技能）与茶学识。你获得独门手艺技能专长（选择一个与你的盟友NPC相关的专长），并且你的盟友NPC对队伍的初始态度为友善（而非冷漠；冷漠是所有柳岸镇NPC的常规初始态度）。</p>\n  <p>季节恩赐 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> 触发 队伍中的某人使柳岸镇的一名NPC变为友善；效果 你的名声在外，即使并非由你尝试影响该NPC也一样。该NPC改为变为乐于助人而非友善。让NPC变为乐于助人可以解锁他们在柳岸镇所属地点提供的额外支持——你的GM会提供更多关于该机制的信息。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.ia5aFzfmfnMjhcms]{Folklore Enthusiast}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">背景</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">柳岸镇是申门乡村地区的一座小镇，但这并不意味着它能与怪奇与未解之事隔绝。围绕柳岸镇或柳岸腹地，有许多神秘事件与萦绕不散的传说；在你成长经历的影响下，你对进一步了解这些事格外感兴趣。虽然许多地方民俗源自柳岸镇诸多宗教与本地信仰之一（你可能是其中的虔诚信众；也可能只是以世俗角度对这些学识感兴趣），但你注意到，这些信念也会以他们自己或许都未曾意识到的方式影响工匠与手艺人。你确信许多本地信仰都扎根于某个意义重大的更深层历史事件，并希望有朝一日能更了解柳岸镇真正的历史。</p>\n  <p>如果你有宗教信仰，你的家很可能在与你信仰相关的一处神龛附近——如果柳岸镇的神龛中没有你的信仰，请与GM讨论，看看是否能在你家中或附近设置一处供奉你信仰的神龛。</p>\n  <p>在重现节期间，你很可能花时间与他人聊鬼故事、分享阴森的传说与怪谈。你在重现节期间并非“被选中”成为绑架对象，而是热切地自愿争取这个机会——你甚至可能在往年就作为绑架对象参与过！</p>\n  <p>选择两次属性提升。其中一次必须给智力或感知，另一次为自由属性提升。</p>\n  <p>你受训于宗教（技能）与艺术学识。你获得异常察觉技能专长。</p>\n  <p>季节恩赐 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> 触发 你即将进行任何回忆知识检定；效果 当你回想起一则古老寓言、晦涩传说或与眼前主题相关的故事时，你灵光一闪。该次回忆知识检定失去秘传特质。将你这次回忆知识检定的结果提高一个成功等级。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.2nt2nsQMBXgQRlOu]{Northridge Scholar}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">背景</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">北岭这一政治派系专注于现代务实主义与城市发展。尽管该派系中确实有人将南岸的人看作乡巴佬、笨拙的土包子，或顽固的传统派、宁愿柳岸镇永远别发展，但追随这一地方派系的大多数人，反而将精力投入到建设柳岸镇之中，憧憬着小镇有朝一日能成长为重要的贸易枢纽。你的兴趣则更偏向把柳岸镇当作学习之地——一所学校、图书馆，甚至一座小型大学，都能为你的家乡带来巨大改变！当然，学习研究固然令人振奋，你也明白要以这种方式扩展柳岸镇需要大量艰苦工作；而你童年时帮忙打地基或搭建房屋的经历，让你拥有不同于典型学者的体格。</p>\n  <p>你的家很可能在塞巴河的北岸，位于柳岸镇镇区以东的某处。</p>\n  <p>在重现节期间，你很可能帮忙运作一些庆典活动，或只是坐着观察人群。你自愿在重现节成为绑架对象，因为参与这项城镇延续最久的传统之一，是你一直渴望体验的荣誉。</p>\n  <p>选择两次属性提升。其中一次必须给体质或力量，另一次为自由属性提升。</p>\n  <p>你受训于社会与学术学识。你获得额外学识专长。</p>\n  <p>季节恩赐 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> 触发 队伍在北岭的声望提高；效果 使队伍在北岭的声望额外提高2点（你的GM掌握有关柳岸镇声望的信息）。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.GyFfqCZZVtazmwPD]{Outskirt Dweller}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">背景</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">柳岸镇虽是个可爱的城镇，但哪怕只有200人，对你来说也有点太多了。无论你是在镇子外围长大，还是因镇上生活令人烦闷与不堪重负而决定搬到边缘地带，你只有被大自然环绕时才真正有归属感。你并不轻视住在镇上的人；你可能是猎人、捕兽者、渔夫或采药人之一，为那些缺乏林业技能的人提供重要支持。</p>\n  <p>你的家在柳岸镇郊外，甚至可能在地图上并没有实际建筑标示。经GM许可，你甚至可以住在更远一些的柳岸腹地里的一间小屋，但距离城镇不超过几里。</p>\n  <p>在重现节期间，你可能来得很晚，本来也不打算久留，但你的朋友与盟友（其他PC）说服你留下。你在重现节临近结束时被选为绑架对象，因为有人不得不临时退出（也许是宴会上吃喝过度所致），而你的朋友（其他PC）又说服你加入他们，把这当作一次有趣的共同体验。既然这包含在林中星空下露宿，那可真是结束夜晚的美妙方式！</p>\n  <p>选择两次属性提升。其中一次必须给敏捷或感知，另一次为自由属性提升。</p>\n  <p>你受训于自然与狩猎学识。你获得地形专家（森林）技能专长。</p>\n  <p>季节恩赐 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> 触发 你即将投掷先攻；效果 某些状况触发了你的防备，让你能更快应对突如其来的危险。你在先攻检定上获得一个状态加值，其数值等于自你开始鬼季以来经过的季节数（夏季为+1，至多在冒险路径最后一幕的春季达到+4）。若你能向其他PC传达警告，他们的先攻也获得该加值。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.2W2jadmj4gPNfdQ9]{Southbank Traditionalist}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">背景</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">南岸这一政治派系代表柳岸镇的最初创立者——一群坚韧的拓荒定居者，其技能与重心更偏向质朴与务实。尽管该派系中确实有人将北岭视为肤浅的城里人、商贩与渴求权力的政客，但南岸的大多数人把精力投入在确保柳岸镇有饭吃、尊重其悠久传统，并尽量保持自给自足。你对柳岸镇历史的兴趣，与务农传统、用自己双手建造所需之物，以及参与这片地区共同的口述历史紧密相连。无论是与本地长者谈古论今，还是帮助新来者学习柳岸镇的行事方式，你总是热切地想协助守护小镇传统。</p>\n  <p>你的家很可能位于塞巴河以南，在城镇最南端的郊外。</p>\n  <p>在重现节期间，你很可能花时间帮忙布置宴席、协助举办部分活动，并在幕后做了不少工作。你在重现节被选为绑架对象，是因为你打赌输了、欠了人情，或以其他方式被家人、朋友或同事施压或骗去担任该角色。也许原本要当绑架对象的人在最后一刻不得不退出，于是你最终顶替了他的位置。</p>\n  <p>选择两次属性提升。其中一次必须给魅力或体质，另一次为自由属性提升。</p>\n  <p>你受训于手艺（技能）与农耕学识。你获得交际花专长。</p>\n  <p>季节恩赐 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> 触发 队伍在南岸的声望提高；效果 使队伍在南岸的声望额外提高2点（你的GM掌握有关柳岸镇声望的信息）。</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.0oTvU8dNFcT42CWV]{Willowshore Urchin}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">背景</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">稀有</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">任何聚居地都一样：并非柳岸镇的所有居民都生来生活轻松。你在镇上的街头长大，要么是孤儿，要么是家境困顿、年纪轻轻就被迫帮家里糊口的孩子。你也许名义上有自己的家，但出于种种原因，你在童年大部分时间里都在墙外生活，或更愿意如此。你可能与一群孩子结伙（其中一些甚至可能是其他PC），也可能是个独行者，却仍在万般不利中活了下来。不管怎样，你的童年充满被迫的机智、绝望与体力活。几乎没有哪个星期你不用临时拼凑个方案来解决某个问题，或在事态升级前仅凭反射神经或蛮力迅速摆平局面。即使你长大后或许已将旧日生活抛在身后，你在柳岸镇街头度过的岁月仍塑造了如今的你。</p>\n  <p>你也许在法律意义上仍是无家可归者，靠街头度日，从不连续两晚睡在同一个地方。你也可能在镇里某处保有一间小棚屋或藏身处。也有可能，尽管童年如此，你仍足够幸运地找到一个家庭或一个家，那么你的住处可能在柳岸镇的任何地方。</p>\n  <p>在重现节期间，你很可能很享受狂欢……也许有点过头了！在你的童年里，节庆总是令人兴奋的时刻，而这次也不例外。你在重现节被选为绑架对象纯属巧合——也许你的名字是闭眼抽签选中的；也许有人激你参加；又或者你只是渴望成为焦点。</p>\n  <p>选择两次属性提升。其中一次必须给敏捷或力量，另一次为自由属性提升。</p>\n  <p>你受训于运动（技能）与工程学识。你获得迷人骗子专长。</p>\n  <p>季节恩赐 <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> 触发 你（或一名相邻PC）即将进行复苏检定；效果 你无需投掷复苏检定，而是自动获得一次大成功——你强健的体格、顽强的意志，或仅仅是运气，一如童年那样继续帮你活下去。若你相邻于一名即将进行复苏检定的PC，你也可以改为使用此恩赐，将该效果赋予他们。</p>\n</section>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Season of Ghosts Backgrounds</h3>\n<p>The six new backgrounds presented on the following pages are available to all characters in the Season of Ghosts Adventure Path. Each of these rare backgrounds is tailor-made to match the themes of this Adventure Path and includes a bit of flavor about the Reenactment Festival and why you were chosen to be one of the festival’s abductees.</p>\n<p><strong>Seasonal Boon:</strong> Each of these backgrounds grants you a seasonal boon. You can use a seasonal boon at any time as a free action (with a trigger as described in your background), but only once per season (summer, fall, winter, spring—corresponding to the four acts of the Season of Ghosts Adventure Path; your GM can let you know when a new act begins and your boon is available for use once more). If you don’t use a seasonal boon during an act, that use is lost—unused seasonal boons don’t carry over into the next act.</p>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.uker8dnTA7WhzXSR]{Close Ties}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Background</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">You’ve forged a close friendship with one of Willowshore’s notable citizens, and you have a long tradition of sharing tea with each other while chatting about shared interests, plans for the future, town gossip, or other matters of note. Work with your GM to choose one of the NPCs mentioned in the Willowshore Gazetteer (other than Granny Hu or Old Matsuki)—your GM might have suggestions for which NPC makes the most sense for your character or might know something about an NPC’s eventual role in the campaign that would give your character a compelling story beat. You could be an employee or apprentice of this NPC, a close relation or friend, or even a friendly competitor in some way.</p>\n  <p>Your home is likely relatively close to the place of business or home of your NPC ally.</p>\n  <p>During the Reenactment Festival, you likely spent time with your NPC ally and might have made plans to get together the next day on the first day of summer, perhaps to have tea together. You were chosen to be an abductee during the Reenactment Festival because your NPC friend or ally suggested the experience would be fun or good for you, or because they’d done it the previous year at your urging and now “it’s your turn.”</p>\n  <p>Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Charisma or Intelligence, and one is a free attribute boost.</p>\n  <p>You’re trained in the Diplomacy skill and the Tea Lore skill. You gain the Specialty Crafting skill feat (choose a specialty associated with your allied NPC), and your allied NPC begins with an attitude of friendly toward the party (rather than indifferent, which is the initial norm for all Willowshore NPCs).</p>\n  <p>Seasonal Boon <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> Trigger Someone in the party makes an NPC in Willowshore friendly; Effect Your reputation precedes you, even if you aren’t the one making the attempt to influence an NPC. The NPC is made helpful instead of friendly. Making an NPC helpful can unlock additional support from their location in Willowshore—your GM has more information about this mechanic.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.ia5aFzfmfnMjhcms]{Folklore Enthusiast}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Background</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">Willowshore is a small town in a rural part of Shenmen, but that doesn’t exempt it from the world of the strange and unexplained. There are plenty of mysterious events and haunting legends about Willowshore or its hinterlands, and as a result of your upbringing, you’ve become particularly interested in learning more about them. While much of the regional folklore comes from one of Willowshore’s many religions and local faiths (of which you might be a practicing member or perhaps instead have a secular interest in the lore), you’ve noticed that these beliefs also influence artisans and crafters in ways they might not even realize. You’re convinced that many of these local beliefs have roots in a deeper, historical event of great significance and hope one day to learn more about Willowshore’s true history.</p>\n  <p>If you’re religious, your home is likely near a shrine associated with your faith—if your faith isn’t represented among Willowshore’s shrines, speak with your GM about potentially having a shrine to your faith in or near to your home.</p>\n  <p>During the Reenactment Festival, you likely spent time chatting with others about ghost stories and sharing spooky legends and tales. You weren’t chosen to be an abductee during the Reenactment Festival so much as you volunteered, eagerly, for the chance—you might have even participated in previous years as an abductee!</p>\n  <p>Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Intelligence or Wisdom, and one is a free attribute boost.</p>\n  <p>You’re trained in the Religion skill and the Art Lore skill. You gain the Oddity Identification skill feat.</p>\n  <p>Seasonal Boon <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> Trigger You’re about to roll any check to Recall Knowledge; Effect You have a flash of insight as you recall an old parable, obscure legend, or applicable tale to the topic at hand. This Recall Knowledge check loses the secret trait. Increase the result of your check to Recall Knowledge by one degree of success.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.2nt2nsQMBXgQRlOu]{Northridge Scholar}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Background</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The political faction of Northridge is focused on modern pragmatism and urban growth. While there are certainly those in this faction who regard those of Southshore as rubes, bumbling yokels, or stubborn traditionalists who would prefer Willowshore never grow, most of those following this local faction instead put their energy into developing Willowshore, envisioning a time when the town might grow into an important hub for trade. Your interests lie more along the concept of Willowshore as a place for learning—a school, library, or even small university could do so much for your town! Of course, as invigorating as it is to study and learn, you also understand that expanding Willowshore in such a way will require lots of hard work, and your childhood helping to lay foundations or raise buildings has given you a physique that eludes the typical scholar.</p>\n  <p>Your home is likely somewhere along the northern banks of the Ceiba River to the east of downtown Willowshore.</p>\n  <p>During the Reenactment Festival, you likely helped to run some of the festivities or spent time simply sitting back to people-watch. You volunteered to be an abductee during the Reenactment Festival because the experience of taking part in one of the town’s longest-running traditions is an honor you’ve always wanted to experience.</p>\n  <p>Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Constitution or Strength, and one is a free attribute boost.</p>\n  <p>You’re trained in the Society skill and the Academia Lore skill. You gain the Additional Lore feat.</p>\n  <p>Seasonal Boon <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> Trigger The party’s reputation with Northridge increases; Effect Increase the party’s reputation with Northridge by an additional 2 points (your GM has information about Willowshore reputation).</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.GyFfqCZZVtazmwPD]{Outskirt Dweller}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Background</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">While Willowshore is a lovely small town, even a population of 200 is a bit much for you. Whether you grew up in the town’s outskirts, or you grew frustrated and overwhelmed with town life and decided to move to the fringes, you’re only really at home when you’re surrounded by nature. You don’t look down on those who live in town, and you might be among the hunters, trappers, fishers, or herbalists who provide important support to those who lack such forestry skills.</p>\n  <p>Your home is on the outskirts of Willowshore and might not even be represented by an actual building on the map. With the GM’s permission, you might even dwell in a small building further out in the Willowshore hinterlands, but no further than a couple of miles from town.</p>\n  <p>During the Reenactment Festival, you likely showed up late and weren’t intending to stay for long, but your friends and allies (the other PCs) convinced you to stick around. You were chosen to be an abductee during the Reenactment Festival at the last minute when someone else had to back out (perhaps as a result of overindulging during the feast), and your friends (the other PCs) convinced you to join them on what would be a fun, shared experience. Since it involves sleeping out under the stars in the woods, well, that’s a pretty lovely way to end an evening!</p>\n  <p>Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Dexterity or Wisdom, and one is a free attribute boost.</p>\n  <p>You’re trained in the Nature skill and the Hunting Lore skill. You gain the Terrain Expertise (forest) skill feat.</p>\n  <p>Seasonal Boon <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> Trigger You’re about to roll initiative; Effect Something about the situation triggers your defenses, allowing you to react to sudden peril more quickly. You gain a status bonus to your initiative roll equal to the number of seasons since you’ve started Season of Ghosts (+1 during summer, up to a maximum of +4 during spring in the Adventure Path’s final act). If you can communicate a warning to other PCs, they gain this bonus to their initiative as well.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.2W2jadmj4gPNfdQ9]{Southbank Traditionalist}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Background</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">The political faction of Southbank represents the original founders of Willowshore, a hearty band of settlers whose skills and focus tend toward the earthly and humble. While there are certainly those in this faction who regard Northridge as vapid urbanites, merchants, and power-hungry politicians, most in Southbank devote their energy to helping Willowshore stay fed, honoring its long-standing traditions, and remaining relatively self-sufficient. Your interests in Willowshore’s history are closely tied to the traditions of farming and building what you need with your own two hands, as well as taking part in the shared oral history of the region. Whether it’s enjoying discussions with local elders about the past or helping newcomers learn Willowshore’s ways, you’re always eager to help uphold the town’s traditions.</p>\n  <p>Your home is likely located south of the Ceiba River, on the southernmost outskirts of town.</p>\n  <p>During the Reenactment Festival, you likely spent time helping to set up the feasts, assisted in running some of the events, and otherwise worked behind the scenes. You were chosen to be an abductee during the Reenactment Festival because you lost a bet, owed a favor, or otherwise got pressured or tricked into the role by a family member, friend, or coworker. Perhaps someone who was going to be one of the abductees but had to back out at the last moment, so you ended up taking their place.</p>\n  <p>Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Charisma or Constitution, and one is a free attribute boost.</p>\n  <p>You’re trained in the Crafting skill and the Farming Lore skill. You gain the Hobnobber feat.</p>\n  <p>Seasonal Boon <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> Trigger The party’s reputation with Southbank increases; Effect Increase the party’s reputation with Southbank by an additional 2 points (your GM has information about Willowshore reputation).</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\">\n  <h2 data-no-toc class=\"split\"><span class=\"keepme\">@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.backgrounds.Item.0oTvU8dNFcT42CWV]{Willowshore Urchin}</span> <span class=\"keepme\">Background</span></h2>\n  <ul class=\"traits\">\n    <li class=\"trait rare\">RARE</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"no-indent\">As with any settlement, not all of Willowshore’s citizens are born into easy lives. You grew up on the town streets, either as an orphan or hardscrabble youth who was forced at a young age to help provide for your family. You might technically have had a home of your own, but for various reasons, you had, or preferred, to live most of your childhood outside of those walls. You might have run with a gang of kids (some of whom might even be fellow PCs), or you could’ve been a loner who managed to survive against all odds. Regardless, your childhood was one of forced ingenuity, desperation, and physicality. Hardly a week would’ve passed without you having to jury-rig a solution to some problem or to simply use your reflexes or brawn to solve a situation quickly before things escalated. While you might have left your old life behind you now that you’re all grown up, the time you spent on Willowshore’s streets has made you the person you are today.</p>\n  <p>You might still be technically homeless, subsisting on the street and never sleeping in the same place twice in a row. You might keep a small shanty or hideout somewhere in town as well. It’s also possible that, despite your childhood, you’ve been fortunate enough to find a family or home, in which case your home could be anywhere in Willowshore.</p>\n  <p>During the Reenactment Festival, you likely enjoyed the revelry... perhaps a bit too much! Festivals were always times of excitement in your childhood, and this one is no exception. You were chosen to be an abductee during the Reenactment Festival simply by chance—maybe your name was selected by a blind draw, or perhaps someone dared you to take part, or you could simply have craved the attention.</p>\n  <p>Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Dexterity or Strength, and one is a free attribute boost.</p>\n  <p>You’re trained in the Athletics skill and the Engineering Lore skill. You gain the Charming Liar feat.</p>\n  <p>Seasonal Boon <span class=\"pf2-icon\">f</span> Trigger You (or an adjacent PC) are about to roll a recovery check; Effect You gain an automatic critical success on the recovery check rather than rolling it as your hearty physique, tenacious attitude, or just plain old luck continues to help you survive the way it had during your childhood. If you’re adjacent to a PC who’s about to roll a recovery check, you can instead use this boon to grant them this effect.</p>\n</section>"
            },
            "Standard Background": {
              "name": "标准背景 Standard Background",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>标准背景</h3>\n<p>如果你希望直接从《玩家核心》中选择一个标准背景，那么适合《鬼季》的良好主题选择包括：工匠、赏金猎人、江湖骗子、厨师、罪犯、侦探、表演者、农场工人、赌徒、守卫、草药师、隐士、猎人、劳工、武学弟子、商人、学者、教师、街头孤儿，以及战士。</p>\n<p>《玩家核心 2》中还提供了额外的标准背景；该书中适合的主题选择包括：朝圣者、根术师、仆人，或受护者。</p>\n<p><strong>季节恩惠：</strong>你不再获得一个特定的季节恩惠（选择《鬼季》背景的角色会获得的额外益处），而是改为获得如下选项：每个季节一次（夏、秋、冬或春——因此在《鬼季》中每幕一次），你可以在为解决任意休整模式行动而进行的检定中获得+4状态加值；你可以在你掷骰之后再决定是否应用此加值。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Standard Background</h3>\n<p>If you wish to simply pick a standard background from Player Core, good thematic choices for Season of Ghosts include artisan, bounty hunter, charlatan, cook, criminal, detective, entertainer, farmhand, gambler, guard, herbalist, hermit, hunter, laborer, martial disciple, merchant, scholar, teacher, street urchin, and warrior.</p>\n<p>Additional standard backgrounds are available in Player Core 2; good thematic choices from that book include pilgrim, root worker, servant, or ward.</p>\n<p><strong>Seasonal Boon:</strong> Instead of gaining a specific seasonal boon (an additional benefit that characters who choose Season of Ghosts backgrounds gain), you instead gain the option to, once per season (summer, fall, winter, or spring—thus, once per act during Season of Ghosts), gain a +4 status bonus to a check attempted to resolve any downtime activity; you can choose to apply this bonus after you roll the check.</p>"
            },
            "Backgrounds": {
              "name": "背景 Backgrounds",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>背景</h2>\n<p>与大多数冒险道不同，《鬼季》的故事几乎完全发生在柳岸镇及其附近，并默认PC们都是这座聚居地的长期居民。因此，你的PC很可能在镇上有家人或密友——你应该与GM合作创建这些额外的NPC，以帮助充实柳岸镇！本《玩家指南》中提供的每个自定义背景都附带暗示，说明你的PC在镇上住在哪里；你可以利用这些信息来帮助你决定角色的直系亲属中哪些人在镇上，哪些人可能不在。不过请记住，如果你决定让重要的家庭成员位于柳岸腹地之外，你在这场战役期间很可能无法去探望他们！</p>\n<p>当你为《鬼季》创建角色时，你可以用以下两种方法之一来选择角色的背景。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Backgrounds</h2>\n<p>Unlike most Adventure Paths, Season of Ghosts takes place almost entirely in and near the town of Willowshore and assumes the PCs are all long-term citizens of this settlement. As such, it’s likely that your PC has family or close friends in town—you should work with your GM to create these additional NPCs to help populate Willowshore! Each of the custom backgrounds offered in this Player’s Guide comes with suggestions as to where your PC lives in town, so you can use this to help you decide who in your character’s immediate family is in town and who might not be. Keep in mind, though, if you decide to have important family members located outside of the Willowshore hinterlands, you likely won’t be able to visit them during this campaign!</p>\n<p>When you create a character for Season of Ghosts, you can choose one of the following two methods for selecting your character’s background.</p>"
            },
            "Gear": {
              "name": "道具 Gear",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>道具</h2>\n<p>鬼季发生在天夏，因此，《玩家核心》中以下非常见武器在创建角色时对每位PC均可用：镰、武士刀、锡杖、双节棍、钗、手里剑，以及寺院剑。</p>\n<p>《玩家核心2》中以下非常见武器在创建角色时对每位PC均可用：大弓（高级武器）、天狗疾风刃，以及胁差。</p>\n<p>此外，《失落预兆：天夏角色指南》第127页所列出的所有武器，在创建角色时也对每位PC可用。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Gear</h2>\n<p>Season of Ghosts takes place in Tian Xia, and as such, the following uncommon weapons from Player Core are accessible to every PC upon character creation: kama, katana, khakkara, nunchaku, sai, shuriken, and temple sword.</p>\n<p>The following uncommon weapons from Player Core 2 are accessible to every PC upon character creation: daikyu (advanced weapon), tengu gale blade, and wakizashi.</p>\n<p>Additionally, all of the weapons listed on page 127 of the Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide are available to every PC upon character creation.</p>"
            },
            "Archetypes": {
              "name": "变体 Archetypes",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>变体</h2>\n<p>随着你变得更强大，选择一个变体的选项可以帮助你进一步自定义你的角色，并使其在主题上更契合《鬼季》。大多数多职业变体都很适合《鬼季》战役（枪手除外），而《玩家核心 2》中其他同样贴合主题的变体还包括：受祝者（与柳岸镇中设有神龛的某位神祇相关）、赏金猎人或决斗家（尤其适合用来塑造浪人主题的角色）、草药师、元帅或武术家。仪式师变体尤其适合本战役，因为《鬼季》包含种类繁多的仪式，并提供了许多使用它们的机会。《失落预兆：天夏角色指南》中一些同样稳妥的额外选择包括魂魄武者与流浪厨师。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Archetypes</h2>\n<p>As you grow more powerful, the option to select an archetype can help you further customize your character and make them more thematically appropriate for Season of Ghosts. Most multiclass archetypes work well for a Season of Ghosts campaign (with the exception of gunslinger), while other thematically appropriate archetypes from Player Core 2 include the following: blessed one (associated with one of the deities who have shrines in Willowshore), bounty hunter or duelist (particularly when used to create a ronin-themed character), herbalist, marshal, or martial artist. The ritualist archetype is particularly well-suited to this campaign, as Season of Ghosts features a wide number of rituals and offers many opportunities to use them. Additional archetypes from Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide that are solid choices include spirit warrior and wandering chef.</p>"
            },
            "Skills and Feats": {
              "name": "技能与专长 Skills and Feats",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>技能与专长</h2>\n<p>在《鬼季》中，你将面对范围广泛的挑战与机遇，尤其是在休整时间方面。毕竟，这条冒险路径横跨整整一年，而你也会时不时地一连数周投入到各种休整时间行动中。那些在战斗遭遇（或紧随其后）经常派上用场的技能——例如特技、运动、医疗与隐匿——在整个战役中都会持续有用；其中一些（尤其是运动）在各种休整时间追求中还有显著的其他用途。</p>\n<p>在与魔法根源相关的四项技能中，自然与宗教将在整条冒险路径中拥有大量大放异彩的机会。奥术学与神秘学则会在这四部曲战役的后半段更能发挥其价值。</p>\n<p>有助于社交互动的技能——例如交涉、威吓与社会——在《鬼季》全程都会频繁使用。当然，欺瞒在遭遇模式中也经常有用，可用于制造佯动或虚招；但在战役前半段，它在战斗之外大显身手的机会很少（虽仍很重要）——到了后半段，欺瞒技能的重要性会大幅提升。</p>\n<p>能够自给自足，或以相同目标帮助偏远的柳岸镇，使得生存成为贯穿战役的重要技能。盗窃也同样非常有用：既能用于处理危害，也会周期性地在某些休整时间行动中，或在需要更隐秘手段的挑战里派上用场。</p>\n<p>在第一幕结束后，制作会成为一项重要技能。此后，你在休整时间的事件与行动中将越来越常被要求去建造、修理或以其他方式运用这项技能。虽然用表演来达成目标的机会较少见，但每段冒险都会有几个时刻，让这方面的本领能够轻松解决问题。</p>\n<p>大量学识（技能）在这场战役中都很有帮助。当某项休整时间行动可用时，某个特定的学识（技能）往往会比欺瞒或社会这类更泛用的技能拥有更低的DC。这条冒险路径中最重要的学识（技能）是柳岸镇学识——对一场几乎完全发生在这座小镇及其周边的战役来说，这也在情理之中！战役中还有不少其他重要的学识（技能），会有不止一两次大放异彩的机会，包括学术、艺术、工程、务农、狩猎、图书馆、善解以及茶学识。只会有一两次机会派上用场的学识（技能）包括：任何与非茶类食物或饮品相关的学识，以及建筑、烹饪、钓鱼、占卜、游戏、族谱、行会、草药、络新妇、劳工、商贸、产妇、气中、河流、航海、侦察、剧场、地底与战争学识。</p>\n<p>还有一项值得注意的新学识（技能）：它未收录于《玩家核心》，但会在本战役中变得越来越有用；它与《鬼季》中引入的一类新怪物家族相关。一旦你们的小队发现这种新怪物，接受其学识训练将有助于你们为与它们的战斗做准备，或研究之后将出现的剧情要素。话虽如此，当你开始《鬼季》时未受过这项特定学识（技能）的任何训练不仅完全没问题，而且也是战役剧情逐步展开的一部分。这里提到它，只是为了让那些喜欢提前规划角色升级选择的玩家，能为未来的机会做好准备。</p>\n<p>你应当避免选择那些在大城市中最能发挥效果，或依赖于超出你几天内所能完成的长距离旅行的专长，因为这些要素在《鬼季》中不会发挥作用。相比之下，那些能帮助你与其他镇民互动、增强你自给自足能力，或总体而言对任何在偏远林地小镇生活一整年的人都有用的专长，会比平时更有价值。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Skills and Feats</h2>\n<p>You’ll face a wide range of challenges and opportunities in Season of Ghosts, particularly when it comes to downtime. This Adventure Path spans an entire year, after all, and now and then, you’ll be spending weeks at a time pursuing various downtime activities. Skills that feature often in combat encounters (or immediately following), such as Acrobatics, Athletics, Medicine, and Stealth, will be consistently useful throughout the campaign, with some of them (particularly Athletics) having significant other applications during various downtime pursuits.</p>\n<p>Of the four skills associated with magical traditions, Nature and Religion will have significant opportunities to shine throughout the entire Adventure Path. Arcana comes into its own more in the second half of this four-part campaign, as does Occultism.</p>\n<p>Skills that help with social interaction, such as Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Society, will see constant use throughout Season of Ghosts. Deception will often be useful in encounter mode, of course, to Create a Diversion or Feint, but its chances to shine outside of combat are minimal (if important) during the first half of the campaign—in the second half, skill at Deception becomes much more important.</p>\n<p>Being able to subsist or to help the remote town of Willowshore with the same goals makes Survival an important skill throughout the campaign. Thievery will likewise be of great use, both in dealing with hazards but also periodically for certain downtime activities or for challenges that might require more subtlety.</p>\n<p>Crafting becomes an important skill after the first act concludes. Thereafter, you’ll increasingly be called upon during downtime events and activities to build, repair, or otherwise use this skill. While opportunities to use Performance to accomplish goals will be less common, each adventure will have a few moments where skill in this area can solve problems with ease.</p>\n<p>An extensive number of Lore skills are helpful in this campaign. When a downtime activity becomes available, a specific Lore skill will often have a lower DC than more generalized skills like Deception or Society. The most important Lore skill in this Adventure Path is Willowshore Lore, as one would expect of a campaign set almost entirely within and around this small town! Other important Lore skills that will have more than a couple of opportunities to shine in the campaign include Academia, Art, Engineering, Farming, Hunting, Library, Sangpotshi, and Tea Lore. Lore skills that will have only one or two chances to shine include any to do with non-tea food or drink, Architecture, Cooking, Fishing, Fortune-Telling, Games, Genealogy, Guild, Herbalism, Jorogumo, Labor, Mercantile, Midwifery, Qi-Zhong, River, Sailing, Scouting, Theater, Underworld, and Warfare Lore.</p>\n<p>One new lore skill worthy of note that isn’t represented in Player Core but that will become increasingly useful in this campaign is one associated with a specific family of new monster introduced in Season of Ghosts. Once your group discovers this new type of monster, becoming trained in its lore will help you prepare for combat against them or otherwise research plot elements to come. That said, not having any particular training in this specific Lore skill when you begin Season of Ghosts is not only fine, but part of the unfolding plot of the campaign. It’s mentioned here merely to prepare you for future opportunities for those players who enjoy building their character’s level choices out beforehand.</p>\n<p>You should avoid feats that work best in large cities or that rely on long-distance travel beyond what you could do in a few days, as these elements don’t play a role in Season of Ghosts. Feats that help you to interact with other townsfolk, that would bolster your ability to be self-sufficient, or that would generally prove useful to anyone living out a year of their life in a remote woodland town will be more useful than normal.</p>"
            },
            "License": {
              "name": "许可 License",
