            "Beyond the Hinterlands": {
              "name": "远离荒野之地 Beyond the Hinterlands",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>腹地之外</h2>\n<p>《鬼季》的故事几乎完全发生在柳岸镇及其紧邻的柳岸腹地内，如地图所示，但在地图边界之外还有整个世界！当事件可能将你带到柳岸腹地之外时，你的GM会提供所需信息；不过，在寻求灵感来创建你的角色时，把注意力集中在柳岸镇及其腹地最为容易。</p>\n<p>以下简要概述了沿着六条通往地图外的道路与小路，腹地之外分别有什么。</p>\n<p><strong>中央北路：</strong>这条部分毁坏的道路蜿蜒穿过数片荒芜的田地，周围是多年前被遗弃的一座村庄的废墟；最终，它在一片大型湿地处走到尽头。那片湿地名为月沼，因为那里生长的橙色夜开花会在月光下闪耀。</p>\n<p><strong>东北路：</strong>这条道路将柳岸镇与幽魂之森中散布的许多小而遥远的村落与城镇相连，并最终通向罗网山脉。沿路最近的聚落是狐谷，但要旅行三天，而且规模比柳岸镇还小。</p>\n<p><strong>东路：</strong>这条道路通往贸易要塞唐入，是柳岸镇与神门其余地区之间的主要经济纽带。唐入附近还有一个小村落（比柳岸镇小得多）——而这座贸易要塞本身则是幽海西岸众多经济枢纽之一。</p>\n<p><strong>东北方向的道路：</strong>这条道路通往一处新近建立的农庄，位于俯瞰幽海的峭壁上；那里还有一座牧牛场，属于一名以冷酷无情而臭名昭著的外来政客，此人来自伺城，与柳岸镇并无太多往来。</p>\n<p><strong>西北小路：</strong>这条古老而杂草丛生的小路通向森林深处；大多数人认为它通往一座早已废弃的神龛，但如今很少有人在这条偏僻的路径上旅行。</p>\n<p><strong>南路：</strong>南路是一条漫长的陆路，最终会与更易维护的道路相连，并通往更南方数日旅行之外人口更稠密的村落与城镇；但柳岸镇的大多数人称它为“苹果之路”，因为它通往一片野苹果树林，每到秋天都会结出格外美味的果实。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Beyond the Hinterlands</h2>\n<p>Season of Ghosts takes place almost entirely within the town of Willowshore and its immediate hinterlands, as presented on the map, but there’s a whole world out there beyond the borders of the map! When events might send you beyond the Willowshore hinterlands, your GM will have the information you need, but it’s easiest to focus on Willowshore and its hinterlands when seeking inspiration to create your character.</p>\n<p>Brief notes about what lies beyond the hinterlands down the six roads and trails that lead off the map are summarized below.</p>\n<p><strong>Central Northern Road:</strong> This partially ruined road winds through several fields that have gone fallow amid the ruins of a village that was abandoned many years ago, then eventually comes to an end at a large wetland known as Moon Marsh for the way the orange, night-blooming flowers that grow there shine under the moonlight.</p>\n<p><strong>Eastern Northern Road:</strong> This road connects Willowshore with numerous small but distant villages and towns scattered throughout Specterwood and eventually finds its way to the Gossamer Mountains. The next closest settlement down this road is Foxhollow, but it’s three days’ travel and even smaller than Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Eastern Road:</strong> This road leads to the trade fortress of Karahai and represents Willowshore’s major economic link to the rest of Shenmen. Karahai has a small village (quite a bit smaller than Willowshore) nearby—the trade fortress itself being one of many economic hubs along the west coast of the Sea of Ghosts.</p>\n<p><strong>Northeastern Road: </strong>This road leads to a recently established farmstead on a bluff overlooking the Sea of Ghosts, a cattle ranch owned by a notoriously ruthless expatriate politician from the city of Sze who doesn’t have much to do with Willowshore.</p>\n<p><strong>Northwest Trail:</strong> This old overgrown trail leads off into the forest; most folks believe it leads to a long-abandoned shrine, but few travel this remote path today.</p>\n<p><strong>Southern Road: </strong>The southern road is a long overland route that eventually connects to better maintained roads and more populous villages and towns several days’ travel to the south, but most in Willowshore call it the “Apple Road,” as it leads to a grove of wild apple trees that produce particularly delicious fruit every fall.</p>"
            },
            "Willowshore Hinterlands": {
              "name": "柳岸腹地 Willowshore Hinterlands",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>柳岸腹地</h2>\n<p>越过小镇的边界，便是崎岖的腹地地形——向西是起伏的林木丘陵，逐渐抬升为葱郁群山；而向东，这片区域最大的河流最终汇入幽海。在这条河与海相接之处，坐落着柳岸镇最近的邻居：名为唐入的沿海要塞化集市；但即便是这里，距小镇也有一天的骑程。</p>\n<p>紧邻小镇的腹地分布着一些小型的景点。杜月江是本地区最大的水道，而柳岸镇则建立在其一条支流——木棉河——的河畔。另一条更浅的支流蜻蜓溪蜿蜒向南，通往一片遍布嶙峋岩石的开阔地，称为尖牙峡——一处天然采石场，为柳岸镇的道路与地基提供了石材。位于柳岸镇下游的葫芦湖钓鱼极佳，但凡要在湖中行舟者，最好向栖居于湖底、并在南岸嬉闹的河童献上供品。青丝峰海拔近2,000英尺，是腹地的最高点；而被称作文业双眼的天然塌陷坑则恰恰相反——那是寸草不生的荒芜深坑，池着混着砂砾的积水。</p>\n<p>在柳岸镇之外，这片区域的人类定居痕迹十分稀少，但并非完全没有，而且多已荒废。东北方矗立着一座被焚毁的废弃驿站遗迹，曾名为玉鸟客栈；而在杜月江源头附近，则有一间偏远的猎户小屋。北方还能找到一处旧日扩建区，原本打算用来支援柳岸镇，但当人们发现流经此处的小溪每年都会在毫无征兆的时间段干涸后，那些建筑与农场很快便被弃置。西边靠近木棉河源头处，是旧伐木营地的残迹；数年前，这里被当地木材领主们废弃，如今正被森林缓慢收回。而在小镇西北的低矮群山中，沿着名为朝圣之径的小径尽头，坐落着谭杉寺的废墟——据说如今那里成了怪物、幽灵或更可怕之物的巢穴。</p>\n<p>环绕柳岸镇的森林属于更为广袤的林地——幽魂之森——不过在柳岸腹地这一区域，那些以侵扰林地而臭名昭著的怨灵与鬼影并没有那么危险。此地野生动物极为丰富，鹿与野猪是主要的大型猎物；而黑熊、狼、巨锹甲虫与巨型蜘蛛等更危险的掠食者，则构成了腹地对那些离开道路太远、或在入夜后探索荒野之人的更大威胁。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Willowshore Hinterlands</h2>\n<p>Beyond the town’s borders lies the rugged terrain of its hinterlands—rolling forested hills rising to verdant mountains to the west, while to the east, the region’s largest river eventually flows into the Sea of Ghosts. Where this river meets the sea stands Willowshore’s closest neighbor, the coastal fortified market called Karahai, yet even this location is a day’s ride from town.</p>\n<p>The immediate hinterlands feature a number of minor sites of interest. The Duyue River is the largest waterway in the region with Willowshore founded on one of its tributaries, the Ceiba River. A shallower tributary, Dragonfly Creek, winds south to an open area of rugged stone known as the Gorge of Fangs and Teeth—a natural quarry that supplied the stone for Willowshore’s roads and foundations. Gourd Lake, downriver from Willowshore, provides excellent fishing, but those who would ply its waters would do well to make offerings to the kappas who dwell in its depths and cavort on its southern shores. Green Silk Peak, nearly 2,000 feet high, is the highest point of elevation in the hinterlands, while the natural sinkholes known as the Eyes of Fumeiyoshi are the opposite—barren pits in the ground where nothing grows and gritty water has pooled.</p>\n<p>Signs of habitation beyond Willowshore are sparse in the region, but they do exist and are largely abandoned. To the northeast stand the burnt-out ruins of an abandoned roadhouse once known as Canary Inn, while a remote Hunter’s Hut stands near the headwaters of the Duyue River. To the north can be found an old expansion once intended to support Willowshore, but these buildings and farms were soon abandoned when it became apparent the stream that flowed through the area tended to dry up at random intervals each year. To the west, near the source of the Ceiba River, are the remains of the old Lumber Camp abandoned a few years ago by the local lumber lords—a location that’s slowly being reclaimed by the forest. And in the low mountains northwest of town, at the far end of the trail known as Pilgrim’s Path, stand the ruins of the Tan Sugi monastery—a place reputed today to be the den of monsters, ghosts, or worse.</p>\n<p>The forest surrounding Willowshore is part of the much larger woodland known as Specterwood, although here in Willowshore’s hinterlands, the haunts and ghosts notorious for plaguing these woods aren’t as dangerous. Wildlife is abundant with deer and boars making up the primary large game in the region, and more dangerous predators like black bears, wolves, giant stag beetles, and enormous spiders comprise the greater perils of the hinterlands to those who travel too far from the roads or explore the wilds after dark.</p>"
            },
            "Languages": {
              "name": "语言 Languages",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>语言</h2>\n<p>在《鬼季》中，主要使用的语言是天夏语——在本《玩家指南》以及整个《鬼季》冒险路径中，这门语言被称为通用语。上文所列任意常见族裔的语言（精灵语、半身人语、狐妖语、娜迦吉语与天狗语）也可能经常派上用场。</p>\n<p>一些实用的通用语言包括邪灵语、地底语、妖精语和死灵语。</p>\n<p>还有一些更特定的语言，虽然对整场战役而言没那么有用，但在少数遭遇中可能会因情境而变得重要，包括龙语、天界语、地精语、环语、民凯语、安魂语与轮回者语。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Languages</h2>\n<p>In Season of Ghosts, the primary language spoken is Tien—this language is referred to as Common in this Player’s Guide and throughout the Season of Ghosts Adventure Path. The languages of any of the common ancestries listed above (elven, halfling, kitsune, nagaji, and tengu) might find frequent use as well.</p>\n<p>General-use languages that will be handy to know include Aklo, Chthonian, Fey, and Necril.</p>\n<p>More specific languages that aren’t as useful for the entire campaign but might become situationally important for a small number of encounters include Draconic, Empyrean, Goblin, Hwan, Minkaian, Requian, and Samsaran.</p>"
            },
            "Faiths": {
              "name": "信仰 Faiths",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>信仰</h2>\n<p>柳岸镇有两座神殿——一座供奉大狐女，另一座供奉法莱斯玛——但镇民的信仰要多元得多。除这两种信仰之外，阿巴达尔与难婆也各自拥有许多信徒，而大多数镇民也会向更广泛的其他神祇致敬。镇上散布着大量供奉不同信仰的小神龛，正反映出这种崇拜风貌。其中一些神龛——例如供奉大狐女与法莱斯玛的——位于众所周知的地点，但更多则是私人神龛，或几乎已被遗忘的神龛。</p>\n<p>柳岸镇内可见下列神祇的神龛；如果你的角色信奉其中一位神祇，那么他们会自动知道对应神龛的位置：阿巴达尔、卡莉丝翠、大狐女、黛丝娜、克忒菲斯、国府幸、难婆、姥姝婆、莲花天女、法莱斯玛、齐仲、谢琳、希兹露、月夜与夜神。若你选择信奉未列于此的神祇，请与GM沟通——你的信仰甚至可能会让柳岸镇的神龛名单上新增一处神龛！</p>\n<p>请注意，某些信仰——例如阿拉兹尼、卡桑达莉或诺克提库拉的信仰——要么尚未出现，要么尚未经历自预言破灭之年开始后约一百年间所发生的重大变化。同样地，尽管阿罗登之死距今也不过数年，但他的信仰在天夏并不显著——在柳岸镇更是如此。由于冒险路径的时间线，你的角色应避免崇拜此类神祇。</p>\n<p>除镇上所崇敬的众多神祇之外，柳岸镇还有许多人追随善解。事实上，镇子的最初建立者便是这一信念的拥护者。他们在西侧丘陵中修建了谭杉寺，作为远离尘嚣、藉由此哲学追求开悟之所；而柳岸镇最初的设立，是为了支援那些辛劳建造寺院的人，后来则发展为支援僧侣的贸易枢纽。谭杉寺如今已被遗弃，任其荒废（并且，有人坚称那里也被各类幽魂与怪物所盘踞），但柳岸镇仍有许多人继续走在善解之道上。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Faiths</h2>\n<p>Willowshore features two temples—one devoted to Daikitsu and one to Pharasma—but the townsfolk are much more diverse in their faith. In addition to these two faiths, both Abadar and Lady Nanbyo count many worshippers among their flock, and most townsfolk pay homage to a wide range of other deities. Their worship is reflected in the large number of small shrines to various faiths scattered throughout town. Some of these shrines, like those devoted to Daikitsu and Pharasma, are in well-known locations, but many are private shrines or shrines that have been all but forgotten.</p>\n<p>Shrines to the following deities are found in Willowshore; if your character worships one of these deities, then they’ll automatically know the location of that shrine: Abadar, Calistria, Daikitsu, Desna, Ketephys, Kofusachi, Lady Nanbyo, Lao Shu Po, Nalinivati, Pharasma, Qi Zhong, Shelyn, Shizuru, Tsukiyo, and Yaezhing. If you choose to worship a deity beyond those listed here, speak with your GM—your faith might even result in another shrine being added to Willowshore’s list!</p>\n<p>Note that certain faiths, such as those of Arazni, Casandalee, or Nocticula, either don’t yet exist or haven’t yet undergone the significant changes they made in the hundred or so years after the start of the Age of Lost Omens. Likewise, while Aroden’s death is only a few years in the past, his faith isn’t significant in Tian Xia—and certainly not in Willowshore. Your character should avoid worshipping such deities because of Adventure Path’s timeline.</p>\n<p>Beyond the town’s wide range of deities, many in Willowshore are followers of Sangpotshi. Indeed, the original founders of the town were adherents to this belief. They built the Tan Sugi monastery up in the hills to the west as a remote place to pursue enlightenment through this philosophy, and they founded Willowshore first to support those who toiled to build the monastery and later as a trade hub to support the monks. The Tan Sugi monastery is now abandoned and has been left to ruin (and, some maintain, to various ghosts and monsters), but many in Willowshore still follow the path of Sangpotshi.</p>"
            },
            "Classes": {
              "name": "职业 Classes",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>职业</h2>\n<p>在《鬼季》中，你的角色被默认是柳岸镇的居民。尽管柳岸镇的人口只有225人（不包括你们的PC！），但小镇的历史与地理位置使它对多种潜在的角色职业都相当开放，足以让这些职业由新一代英雄阵容来呈现。</p>\n<p><strong>炼金术师</strong>在柳岸镇备受尊敬与喜爱，既因为他们作为草药师的技艺，也因为他们擅长为节庆制作奇巧的消遣物。坟边居的本地草药师尤·素锦更偏重炼金创新中的草药学一侧；但只要你赢得她的支持与友谊，能使用她的炼金实验室与物资，将在整个战役中对你大有裨益。对柳岸镇的炼金术师而言，“医师”研究领域在主题上最贴切，但在《鬼季》中，任何研究领域都会同样实用。</p>\n<p><strong>泛灵师</strong>和神谕者一样，是《鬼季》非常契合主题的选择，尤其适合那些以通灵者或萨满方式修行的人。与乡野环境或古老民间传统相关的显现体是最合适的主题选择，包括林苑与花园的守护者、失落时刻的回声、隐秘之处的冒名者、昏暗枝桠中的潜行者、古战的见证者。此外，参见第9页的“信仰”，以获取关于宗教的更多指引。</p>\n<p><strong>野蛮人</strong>在《鬼季》中可能是个较复杂的选择，因为该地区缺乏任何已建立的野蛮人部族。虽然柳岸镇没有这类NPC，但本地仍有许多人喜欢狠狠干上一架，或欣赏强健的体魄。拥有动物本能的野蛮人可能因其狩猎技能而受重视；而拥有灵体本能的野蛮人则可能作为对抗当地人所畏惧的邪灵的守护者而受敬重（并且他们更容易伤害虚体敌人的能力，在《鬼季》的许多战斗遭遇中肯定会是极大的助益！）其他本能与柳岸镇并无特别的主题关联，但总体而言，对这条冒险路径来说也都不算差的选择。</p>\n<p><strong>吟游诗人</strong>在《鬼季》中会有许多机会影响NPC、打造独一无二的表演，或在不同节点利用音乐为自己争取优势；但在这条冒险路径里，没有哪一种特定构筑会明显优于其他。如果你选择“谜团”作为你的缪斯，<strong>谭穗静</strong>（一位古老的民间英雄，其过往功业如今已成为柳岸镇遗产的一部分）或<strong>大尊柳</strong>（与镇北山丘上那棵同名高大柳树相关联的奇异木灵神）会是有趣的选择——与GM交流，看看是否还有其他神秘缪斯也合理可用。在柳岸镇，经营七彩鸣鸾剧院的导演大野和马以会不定期试镜演员而闻名。</p>\n<p><strong>武德勇士</strong>都适合《鬼季》，前提是其事业不至于让他们与队伍其他成员发生冲突。经典的“浪人定居小镇并成为其守护者”的形象，正是像《鬼季》这类战役中武德勇士的标志性角色。虽然这条冒险路径里并不常有必须让PC骑乘作战的遭遇，但在城市与荒野环境中，仍会有大量场合让坐骑在战斗中派上用场。</p>\n<p><strong>牧师</strong>应参考“信仰”条目中的补充信息，以了解应崇拜哪位神祇的指引。</p>\n<p><strong>指挥官</strong>在主题上并不算与《鬼季》特别契合，但和战士一样，他们在战斗中会有许多发光发热的机会。尽管如此，请记住这条冒险路径里有大量非战斗挑战，因此可考虑将部分技能提升投入到制作、交涉、威吓与社交等选项上。</p>\n<p><strong>德鲁伊</strong>会在《鬼季》中拥有大量表现机会，因为这条冒险路径聚焦于一年四季的更迭，而柳岸镇又是乡野地区。本冒险路径所呈现的主要自然地形为温带森林。动物、树叶与风暴三大德鲁伊教团在主题上最为贴切，但所有教团都能在本战役中找到闪光点。以下动物在柳岸镇周边地区最为常见，因此若你选择其中之一作为你的动物伙伴，也会很符合主题（若你想选择不同的动物伙伴，可与GM讨论该动物如何在不寻常的情况下成为你的伙伴）：树精幼苗、獾、蝙蝠、熊、甲虫、鸟、野猪、猫、马、蛇或狼。</p>\n<p><strong>典范</strong>可能会与《鬼季》的小镇主题与舞台发生一定冲突，因此务必将这条冒险路径的乡村背景牢记在心。同样，由于本冒险路径发生在《神陨》事件的一百多年前，你需要与GM合作决定你的神圣火花来源于何处。选择称号时，可参考第9页“技能”中的建议；你也可以与GM一起缩小选项范围，以便他们在需要时提供经过筛选、且不剧透的指引。</p>\n<p><strong>战士</strong>在《鬼季》中会有大量机会大显身手，但重要的是要记住，这条冒险路径包含许多城市与休整期要素。考虑加强你在制作、交涉、威吓或社交等技能上的训练，好让你在冒险路径的非战斗部分也仍有机会出彩。</p>\n<p><strong>守护者</strong>在这条冒险路径中将面临与指挥官类似的主题挑战，尤其是在《鬼季》中数量众多的非战斗挑战面前。与指挥官和战士一样，确保你受训于制作、交涉、威吓与社交等技能，以便在战役这些环节仍有抓手可用。</p>\n<p><strong>枪手</strong>在主题上并不特别适合这条冒险路径；除此之外，柳岸镇也缺乏可供枪手依赖的资源。如果你想扮演枪手，请先与GM讨论，但或许最好把枪手PC的构想留到另一场战役里。</p>\n<p><strong>发明家</strong>在神门并不常见，但也绝非闻所未闻；而他们拼装装置与提出创意解法的本领，在柳岸镇这类乡野地区尤为宝贵——因为那里不一定能获得更广泛的稀有或专用工具与装备。的确，柳岸镇铁匠铺“第二好”的霍天哲以其装置与造物而著称，对发明家PC来说，他会是极佳的盟友或朋友。在《鬼季》中，并不存在某种发明家革新比另一种更或更不合适的情况。</p>\n<p><strong>调查员</strong>在《鬼季》的历程中会有大量机会研究信息、追踪线索并揭开谜团，使其总体而言成为这条冒险路径的特别优秀选择。炼金科学与法医学两种方法论在主题上最为贴切。</p>\n<p><strong>动能使</strong>是《鬼季》的不错选择，尽管柳岸镇对元素或动能使风味的主题支撑并不多——若你想扮演动能使，可与GM讨论是否以某种方式进行调整。尤其是，“木对抗金属”的主题在本战役中以微妙方式贯穿始终；柳岸镇的人民更偏向木，而金属则更明显地与某些构成战役对立面的要素相呼应。</p>\n<p><strong>魔战士</strong>会发现自己的能力在《鬼季》全程都很有用，但在主题上并不特别贴合这条冒险路径的剧情。当然，这也意味着魔战士角色在选择如何增强力量时，相对不易发生主题冲突！</p>\n<p><strong>武僧</strong>是柳岸镇非常契合主题的强力选择，因为这座小镇最初就是为了支持一座偏远修道院而建立的。尽管那处所在——谭杉寺——如今已成废墟且不再运作，但武僧的生活方式在柳岸镇本地仍可能带来非凡的收获，哪怕仅仅是作为小镇丰厚历史与遗产的一部分。参见第9页“信仰”，以获得关于宗教或信念的更多指引。</p>\n<p><strong>神谕者</strong>就神圣施法者而言，在《鬼季》中或许比牧师更契合主题。大多数神谕者奥秘在本冒险路径中都很贴合主题，其中以战斗、宇宙与烈焰最不贴合。此外，参见第9页的“信仰”，以获取关于宗教的更多指引。</p>\n<p><strong>灵能者</strong>在柳岸镇居民中并不多见，但他们的魔法修行为人所知且受人敬佩。那些将研究与力量集中在传说、探寻古老秘密，或对抗超自然势力等主题上的人，会在《鬼季》中发现机会多得用不完。</p>\n<p><strong>游侠</strong>在柳岸镇的人民中非常受重视，因为他们的野外求生能力与狩猎本领能帮助小镇在筹措食粮方面保持自给自足。镇上的银雾斋是本地游侠传统上的聚会地点，但在今天，游侠几乎可以以镇上任何区域或更外侧的腹地为据点。若你获得动物伙伴，请参考第7页为德鲁伊列出的建议。若你选择“偏好地形”专长，森林地形无疑是你在《鬼季》中最常面对的地形。水域（以湖泊与河流的形式）与山地地形所占比重小得多；再之后，平原、天空、沼泽与地下的比重更小。《鬼季》中不包含极地或沙漠地形。</p>\n<p><strong>游荡者</strong>会在《鬼季》中发现自己的技能大有用武之地，尤其是在应对乡村小镇政治等方面。选择将训练重点放在哪里时，可参考第9页“技能”中的建议。</p>\n<p><strong>术士</strong>是这条冒险路径极佳的主题选择，因为柳岸镇浸润于诸多超自然与神秘传统之中。所有术士血脉在《鬼季》中都可能同样有趣，但最贴合主题的是帝国或不死。</p>\n<p><strong>召唤师</strong>在构建其侍神时应考虑当地的区域环境（森林为主，伴有一些低矮山地，以及大量河流与湖泊），除此之外，他们会发现自己在《鬼季》中拥有非常广泛的选择空间。本冒险路径中最契合主题的侍神选择是：怒怨幻灵、野兽、奉献幻灵、植物或引魂使。</p>\n<p><strong>侠客</strong>与战士类似，会在本战役的战斗中有大量机会展示本领，但他们也应考虑训练其他方向，以便在休整期或城市区域中、当战斗并非最佳解决方案时仍能有所探索与施展。</p>\n<p><strong>奇械师</strong>是《鬼季》的极佳选择。和调查员一样，他们将面对大量谜团与古老秘密，需要探索并揭开真相。所有奇械师法器都能在本战役中找到可供构筑的主题关联，但或许没有哪一种比提灯更贴切——考虑到柳岸镇与其@UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog22sogpgh.JournalEntryPage.00w11dawnstepb00]{长明灯}之间深厚的传统联系。虽然你无法选择这盏特定的提灯作为你的法器，但制作一盏仿其形制的提灯会非常合适！</p>\n<p><strong>女巫</strong>由于其与神秘庇护主的联系，以及该职业内建的近恐怖主题，对《鬼季》而言，作为施法者的主题适配度甚至可能比术士更高。选择你的庇护主时与GM沟通以获得更多指引；其中，“信仰的守焰者”“怨憎”“雪中寂静”或“荒野监护者”等庇护主主题，永远是这条冒险路径的优秀选择。选择魔宠时，请记住柳岸镇与一位传统守护者相关联。来访者可以在小镇东缘沿路旁的一座神龛中见到一尊巨大的石蜘蛛雕像——因此，选择蜘蛛魔宠会非常符合主题！</p>\n<p><strong>法师</strong>会发现，只要他们的研究重点不落在令人不安与恐惧之物上，柳岸镇的人民会非常看重他们对魔法的精通！不过，所有魔法学派在这条冒险路径中都会有大量用武之地。法师PC或许会希望与主母之绾的井川十兵卫建立同盟或友谊；他是柳岸镇常驻的法师，也是研究一切魔法事物的学者。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Classes</h2>\n<p>In Season of Ghosts, your characters are assumed to be citizens of Willowshore. While Willowshore only has a population of 225 (excluding your PCs!), the town’s history and placement make it open toward a wide range of potential character classes to be represented by its newest cast of heroes.</p>\n<p><strong>Alchemists</strong> are respected and adored in Willowshore for both their skill as herbalists and talent in crafting fanciful distractions for festivals. Local herbalist You So-Jin of Graveside Manners focuses more on the herbalism side of alchemical innovation, but access to her alchemist’s lab and supplies, should you earn her support and friendship, will be of great use to you during the campaign. The chirurgeon research field is the most appropriate thematic choice for a Willowshore alchemist, but any research field will be of equal use in Season of Ghosts.</p>\n<p><strong>Animists</strong> are, like oracles, a strong thematic choice for Season of Ghosts, particularly those who practice as mediums or shamans. Apparitions associated with rural settings or old folk traditions are the best thematic choices, including Custodian of Groves and Gardens, Echo of Lost Moments, Impostor in Hidden Places, Stalker in Darkened Boughs, and Witness to Ancient Battles. Also, see Faiths on page 9 for additional guidance on religions.</p>\n<p><strong>Barbarians</strong> might be a complex choice for Season of Ghosts considering the lack of any established barbarian clans in the region. Though there are no such NPCs in Willowshore, there are plenty of locals who enjoy a good fight or appreciate physical strength. An animal instinct barbarian might be valued for their skills at hunting, while a spirit instinct barbarian might find themselves respected as a defender against the evil spirits that locals fear (and will certainly find their ability to harm incorporeal foes more easily to be a great boon during many combat encounters in Season of Ghosts!) Other instincts don’t have a particular thematic tie to Willowshore, but none of them are particularly poor choices overall for this Adventure Path.</p>\n<p><strong>Bards</strong> will have many opportunities to influence NPCs, craft singular performances, or use music to their advantage at various points during Season of Ghosts, but no specific build is more advantageous over another in this Adventure Path. If you select enigma as your muse, <strong>Tan Sui-Jing</strong> (an ancient folk hero whose accomplishments in the past are now a part of Willowshore’s legacy) or <strong>Great Willow</strong> (the strange kodama kami associated with the towering willow tree of the same name that looms atop a hill north of town) might be fun choices—speak with your GM to find out if any other mysterious muses might make sense. In Willowshore, Kazuma Oono, the director who runs the Seven-Colored Songbird theater, is known to periodically audition performers.</p>\n<p><strong>Champions</strong> are all appropriate for Season of Ghosts, provided their cause doesn’t set them up to clash against the rest of the party. The classic example of a ronin who settles in a small town and becomes its protector is an iconic role for a champion in a campaign like Season of Ghosts. While there aren’t many encounters in this Adventure Path that require the PCs to be mounted, there are be plenty of opportunities in both urban and wilderness areas where having a mount in combat could be helpful.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerics</strong> should consider the additional information presented under Faiths for guidelines on which deity to worship.</p>\n<p><strong>Commanders</strong> aren’t particularly strong thematic matches for Season of Ghosts, but like fighters, they’ll find many chances to shine during combat. Still, remember that there are a lot of non-combat challenges in this Adventure Path, so consider focusing some of your skill increases on options like Crafting, Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Society.</p>\n<p><strong>Druids</strong> will have ample opportunity to excel in Season of Ghosts as a result of the Adventure Path’s focus on a year’s worth of seasons and the town of Willowshore being a rural location. Temperate forests are the primary natural terrain featured in this Adventure Path. The druid orders of animal, leaf, and storm are the most thematically appropriate choices for this Adventure Path, but all orders will find opportunities to shine in this campaign. The following animals are the most common in the region surrounding Willowshore, so choosing one of them as your animal companion will also be on theme (if you wish to choose a different animal companion, speak to your GM about how this animal might have become your companion under unusual circumstances): arboreal sapling, badger, bat, bear, beetle, bird, boar, cat, horse, snake, or wolf.</p>\n<p><strong>Exemplars</strong> might find themselves clashing with the small-town themes and setting of Season of Ghosts, so make sure to keep the Adventure Path’s rural setting in mind. Likewise, since this Adventure Path takes place over a century before the events of Godsrain, you’ll want to work with your GM to determine where your divine spark comes from. When choosing epithets, consider the advice featured in Skills on page 9; you can work with your GM to narrow down choices as well so that they can provide curated, non-spoiler guidance as needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Fighters</strong> will find ample opportunity to shine in Season of Ghosts, but it’s important to remember that there are a lot of urban and downtime elements in this Adventure Path. Consider bolstering your training in a skill like Crafting, Diplomacy, Intimidation, or Society so that you’ll still have moments to shine during the noncombat portions of this Adventure Path.</p>\n<p><strong>Guardians</strong> will face similar thematic challenges in this Adventure Path as commanders do, particularly when confronted by the numerous non-combat challenges in Season of Ghosts. As with commanders and fighters, make sure you’re trained in skills like Crafting, Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Society so you still have something to work with during these portions of the campaign.</p>\n<p><strong>Gunslingers</strong> aren’t a particularly good choice, thematically, for this Adventure Path, and beyond that, there are no resources for gunslingers to rely upon in the town of Willowshore. If you want to play a gunslinger, talk to your GM first, but it’s probably best to save your ideas for a gunslinger PC for another campaign.</p>\n<p><strong>Inventors</strong> aren’t common in Shenmen, but they’re hardly unknown, and their knack for rigging up contraptions and creative solutions can be quite valuable in a rural area like Willowshore where access to a wider range of rare or specialized tools and gear aren’t guaranteed. Indeed, Huo Tian-Zhe of Willowshore’s smithy, Second Best, is well-known for his contraptions and creations, and he could make for an excellent ally or friend to a PC inventor. There’s no inventor innovation that’s more or less appropriate for Season of Ghosts than another.</p>\n<p><strong>Investigators</strong> will find plenty of opportunities to research information, track clues, and unravel mysteries during the course of Season of Ghosts, making them a particularly excellent choice for this Adventure Path overall. The methodologies of alchemical sciences and forensic medicine are the most thematically appropriate options for this Adventure Path.</p>\n<p><strong>Kineticists</strong> are a fine choice for Season of Ghosts, although there isn’t much thematic support in Willowshore for an elemental or kineticist flavor—if you wish to play a kineticist, speak with your GM about potentially adjusting that in some way. In particular, a theme of “wood against metal” plays a subtle underlying role in this campaign; the people of Willowshore more align toward wood, while metal aligns more noticeably with certain elements that form a part of the campaign’s opposition.</p>\n<p><strong>Magi</strong> will find their abilities useful throughout Season of Ghosts but aren’t particularly tied, thematically, to this Adventure Path’s plot. Of course, that also means a magus character will be relatively free from thematic clashes when making choices about their increasing power!</p>\n<p><strong>Monks</strong> are a strong thematic choice for Willowshore, as the town was originally founded to serve as support for a remote monastery. While that place, the Tan Sugi monastery, is now in ruins and no longer operational, a monk’s lifestyle can still be exceptionally rewarding in Willowshore proper, if only as part of the town’s rich history and legacy. See Faiths on page 9 for additional guidance on religion or belief.</p>\n<p><strong>Oracles</strong> are perhaps an even stronger thematic choice for Season of Ghosts than clerics as far as divine spellcasters are concerned. Most oracle mysteries are strong thematic choices in this Adventure Path, with Battle, Cosmos, and Flames being the least so. Also, see Faiths on page 9 for additional guidance on religions.</p>\n<p><strong>Psychics</strong> aren’t well represented among Willowshore’s citizens, but their magical practices are known and admired. Those who focus their studies and powers on themes associated with lore, discovering ancient secrets, or battling supernatural forces will find themselves with no shortage of opportunity in Season of Ghosts.</p>\n<p><strong>Rangers</strong> are quite valued among Willowshore’s people, as their survivalist abilities and hunting acumen help the town maintain its self-sufficiency when it comes to gathering food. The town’s Silvermist Lodges are the traditional locations where local rangers would gather, but today, a ranger could be based out of nearly any part of town or the hinterlands beyond. If you gain an animal companion, consult the suggestions listed for druids on page 7. If you take the Favored Terrain feat, the terrain of Forest is far and above the most common terrain you’ll face during Season of Ghosts. The aquatic (in the form of lakes and rivers) and Mountain terrains have much more minor roles to play, after which there are even lesser roles for Plains, Sky, Swamp, and Underground. Season of Ghosts doesn’t feature arctic or desert terrains.</p>\n<p><strong>Rogues</strong> will find many uses for their skills in Season of Ghosts, particularly when it comes to those associated with navigating the politics of a small rural town. Consider the advice for Skills on page 9 when choosing where to focus your training.</p>\n<p><strong>Sorcerers</strong> are an excellent thematic choice for this Adventure Path, as Willowshore is steeped in many supernatural and mysterious traditions. All sorcerer bloodlines could be equally interesting in Season of Ghosts, but the most thematically appropriate ones are imperial or undead.</p>\n<p><strong>Summoners</strong> should consider the local regions (forests, with some low mountains and plenty of rivers and lakes) when building their eidolon, but apart from that, they’ll find they have a wide range of choices available to them during Season of Ghosts. The most thematic selections for eidolons in this Adventure Path are anger phantom, beast, devotion phantom, plant, or psychopomp.</p>\n<p><strong>Swashbucklers</strong> are like fighters in that they’ll find plenty of chances to show their stuff in this campaign’s battles, but they should consider also training other options to explore during downtime or while in urban areas when fighting isn’t the best solution.</p>\n<p><strong>Thaumaturges</strong> are excellent choices for Season of Ghosts. Like the investigator, they’ll be faced with a wide range of mysteries and ancient secrets to explore and uncover. All thaumaturge implements could find thematic links to build from in this campaign, but perhaps none more so than the lantern, considering Willowshore’s strong tradition with its @UUID[JournalEntry.pf2apsog22sogpgh.JournalEntryPage.00w11dawnstepb00]{Eternal Lantern}. While you can’t select this particular lantern as your implement, a lantern crafted in its image would fit right in!</p>\n<p><strong>Witches</strong> are perhaps an even more thematically appropriate choice for a spellcaster than sorcerer for Season of Ghosts due to their ties to a mysterious patron and the horror-adjacent themes built right into the class. Speak with your GM when choosing your patron to receive additional guidance, but the patron themes of Faith’s Flamekeeper, The Resentment, Silence in Snow, or Wilding Steward are always going to be excellent choices for this Adventure Path. When choosing a familiar, keep in mind that Willowshore is associated with a traditional guardian. Visitors can find a large stone spider statue in a shrine just off the road along the town’s eastern edge—as such, choosing a spider familiar is quite on theme!</p>\n<p><strong>Wizards</strong> will find their mastery over magic to be something the people of Willowshore quite value, provided their focus isn’t on something unsettling and frightening! That said, all schools of magic will have ample opportunities for use during this Adventure Path. A PC wizard might wish to pursue an alliance or friendship with Igawa Jubei of Mother’s Coil, who is Willowshore’s resident wizard and a scholar of all things magical.</p>"
            },
            "Inappropriate Ancestries": {
              "name": "不恰当的族裔 Inappropriate Ancestries",
              "text": "<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>不合适的族裔</h3>\n<p>水栖族裔会发现在《鬼季》中自己真的不在适合发挥的环境里，因为几乎没有多少时刻能让这类角色大放异彩。柳岸镇坐落在一条河流的河岸上，镇子中心还有一座湖，因此确实有水域可供栖居，但在为你的角色做出这种选择之前，请先与你的GM沟通。</p>\n<p>仿生人同样不适合本战役。由于《鬼季》的时间点大约设定在《钢铁巨神》冒险路径事件发生前约100年，仿生人还没有扩散到足以在纽梅利亚边境之外的地方被合理地遇见。如果你希望在《鬼季》中扮演仿生人，你需要与GM合作，按需调整你们游戏的正史设定，以便为仿生人出现在柳岸镇提供一个合乎世界内逻辑的理由。</p>\n<p>最后，正如人们从这条冒险路径的标题就能猜到的那样，不死族裔在《鬼季》中会显得格外尴尬，因此不应被PC选择。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Inappropriate Ancestries</h3>\n<p>Aquatic ancestries will find themselves literally out of their element in Season of Ghosts, as there are very few moments for such characters to shine. Willowshore is located on the banks of a river and has a lake at its heart, so there is a source of water to dwell in, but speak with your GM before making such a choice for your character.</p>\n<p>Androids are inappropriate for this campaign as well. Since Season of Ghosts is set roughly 100 years before the events of the Iron Gods Adventure Path, androids simply haven’t spread far enough beyond the borders of Numeria to be logically encountered elsewhere in the world. If you wish to play an android in Season of Ghosts, you’ll need to work with your GM to adjust your game’s canon as needed to provide a logical in-world reason for an android’s presence in Willowshore.</p>\n<p>Finally, as one might guess from the title of this Adventure Path, undead ancestries would make for particularly awkward choices in Season of Ghosts and should not be chosen for a PC.</p>"
            },
            "Ancestries": {
              "name": "祖源 Ancestries",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>族裔</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>天狗的敌意</h1>\n  <p>柳岸镇的人民并不会对本镇的天狗居民抱有任何根深蒂固的反感（事实上，其中一些人，比如川冈山人，还是备受尊敬的商号东主），但当代申门的统治者——络新妇——却憎恨天狗，并且一旦与天狗对峙，往往会暴怒到起杀心。由于《鬼季》的故事发生在络新妇开始统治申门之初，偏远的柳岸镇迄今尚未遇到任何络新妇访客；因此，天狗PC通常不必频繁应对这种苦涩的敌意。若在战役中出现络新妇将造访柳岸镇的流言或消息，扮演天狗角色的玩家应当留意——你的GM在各段冒险中给出了如何处理此类情况的建议，所以如果你对扮演天狗PC有所顾虑，就和你的GM谈谈，好让他们以自己觉得舒适的方式，提供适合你们团桌的定制建议。</p>\n</aside>\n<p>作为柳岸镇的镇民，最合适的PC族裔选择，是那些在镇上有相当代表性的族裔。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>常见族裔</h3>\n<p>以下族裔在柳岸镇都在一定程度上有所分布。<strong>人类</strong>无疑是柳岸镇数量最多的族裔，天夏的各个人类族群皆可在此见到。申门与金人、观来等国的近邻关系，使得国内城镇里有相当数量的<strong>精灵</strong>、<strong>半精灵</strong>、<strong>植裔</strong>与<strong>天狗</strong>居住，柳岸镇也不例外。塔尔丹族裔的人类与<strong>半身人</strong>（大多是从申门正北方的阿玛南达移民而来）在柳岸镇同样存在。<strong>狐妖</strong>与<strong>那迦裔</strong>在申门境内并不如前述族裔那般普遍，但在柳岸镇也有少量人口；请注意，这两种族裔在《Pathfinder Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide》中还有更多可选项！</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>罕见族裔</h3>\n<p>这些族裔在柳岸镇不那么常见——镇上可能只住着寥寥几位，或除潜在PC外根本没有，但它们在主题上仍然很适合《鬼季》。在选择这些族裔之一之前，你或许应当先与GM沟通，好让他们有机会对战役作出调整，并让你的选择在柳岸镇居民之中获得更多呈现。</p>\n<p><strong>矮人</strong>、侏儒、地精与兽人并未在柳岸镇形成显著规模，但这些族群中的任何一支都可能从阿玛南达向南迁徙并在此定居。</p>\n<p><strong>吸血裔</strong>会是像《鬼季》这种恐怖主题战役的绝佳选择，尤其是儒尸血脉（Ancestry Guide 26）：他们将吸血鬼血统追溯至一位僵尸。柳岸镇也有一些鼠人（又称鼠族；Player Core 2 28）居住，同样会是合适的PC选择。</p>\n<p><strong>涅斐林</strong>（尤其是从幽海对岸之国天景来到申门的天界裔）也可能已在申门定居。居住在申门的坎比安常被柳岸镇的人以恐惧与猜疑相待，但在《鬼季》中，任何此类族裔的PC都已被其他镇民视为对“常理预期”的“例外”；若你打算将这样的角色融入本战役，请与GM沟通，以便他们在需要时调整战役的某些方面来体现你的选择。</p>\n<p><strong>大地精</strong>PC可能从西方的高岭来到柳岸镇，但和坎比安一样，他们也常被人以恐惧或猜疑看待。</p>\n<p>尽管柳岸镇目前没有任何<strong>冥人（特征）</strong>、<strong>付丧神木偶</strong>、<strong>轮回者</strong>、<strong>影灵</strong>或<strong>妖怪</strong>居住，这些族裔依然契合《鬼季》的某些主题。若你有兴趣扮演这些族裔之一，请与GM商量，因为他们可能会给你更多建议。</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>稀有族裔</h3>\n<p>任何上文未提及的族裔（或下方“不适合的族裔”中列出的）都视为稀有——这些族裔当然能从游戏平衡的角度运作良好，但并不特别契合《鬼季》的主题。若你想扮演稀有族裔，请先与GM沟通。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Ancestries</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Tengu Animosity</h1>\n  <p>While the people of Willowshore harbor no intrinsic dislike of their tengu citizens (and indeed, some of them, like Kawaka Myna, are well-respected business owners), the rulers of modern Shenmen, the jorogumo, loathe tengu and are known to fly into murderous rages when confronted by them. Since Season of Ghosts is set at the onset of jorogumo rule over Shenmen, remote Willowshore has yet to face any jorogumo visitors; as such, tengu PCs won’t need to navigate this bitter animosity often. Should rumors or news of a jorogumo visit to Willowshore arise in the campaign, players of tengu characters should take note—your GM has advice in the adventures on how to handle such situations, so if you have concerns about playing a tengu PC, speak to your GM so they can provide advice customized to your table in a way they feel comfortable with.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>As a citizen of the town of Willowshore, the most appropriate ancestries to choose for a PC are those that are represented significantly in the town.</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Common Ancestries</h3>\n<p>The following ancestries are all represented to a certain degree in Willowshore. <strong>Humans</strong> are far and away the most numerous ancestry in Willowshore, with all of Tian Xia’s human ethnicities being represented. Shenmen’s proximity to nations like Jinin and Kwanlai has ensured that a noticeable number of <strong>elves</strong>, <strong>half-elves</strong>, <strong>leshies</strong>, and <strong>tengu</strong> live in the nation’s towns, and Willowshore is no exception. Humans of Taldan ethnicity and <strong>halflings</strong> (largely folk emigrated from the nation of Amanandar just north of Shenmen) are present in Willowshore as well. <strong>Kitsune</strong> and <strong>nagaji</strong> aren’t as widespread throughout Shenmen, but they’re present in small numbers in Willowshore; note that both of these ancestries have a few more options to choose from in Pathfinder Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide!</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Uncommon Ancestries</h3>\n<p>These ancestries are less common in Willowshore—there might only be a handful living in town or none at all besides potential PCs, but they’re still thematically appropriate for Season of Ghosts. You might wish to speak to your GM before selecting one of these ancestries to give them a chance to potentially adjust the campaign and give your choice more visibility among Willowshore’s citizens.</p>\n<p><strong>Dwarves</strong>, gnomes, goblins, and orcs aren’t present in notable numbers in Willowshore, but any of these peoples could have emigrated south from Amanandar to settle there.</p>\n<p><strong>Dhampirs</strong> would make an excellent thematic choice for a horror-themed campaign like Season of Ghosts, particularly those of the ru-shi lineage (Ancestry Guide 26), who trace their vampiric bloodline to a jiang-shi. Some ysoki (aka ratfolk; Player Core 2 28) live in Willowshore and would also make appropriate PCs.</p>\n<p><strong>Nephilim</strong> (particularly empyreans who have traveled to Shenmen from the nation of Tianjing on the opposite shore of the Sea of Ghosts) might have settled in Shenmen as well. Cambions who dwell in Shenmen are often regarded with fear and suspicion by those in Willowshore, but any PCs of such an ancestry in Season of Ghosts is already known to the other townsfolk as an “exception” to the expectation—speak to your GM about integrating such a character into this campaign in the event they wish to adjust certain aspects of the campaign to reflect your choice.</p>\n<p><strong>Hobgoblins</strong> PCs might have come to Willowshore from the western nation of Kaoling, but like cambions, they are often regarded with fear or suspicion.</p>\n<p>While there aren’t any <strong>duskwalkers</strong>, <strong>tsukumogami poppets</strong>, <strong>samsarans</strong>, <strong>wayangs</strong>, or <strong>yaoguai</strong> currently living in Willowshore, these ancestries still match certain themes in Season of Ghosts. Speak with your GM if you’re interested in playing one of these ancestries, as they might have additional advice for you.</p>\n<h3 data-no-toc data-split-here>Rare Ancestries</h3>\n<p>Any other ancestry not mentioned above (or in Inappropriate Ancestries below) is considered rare—while these ancestries can certainly work from a game balance perspective, they aren’t particularly on theme for Season of Ghosts. If you wish to play a rare ancestry, speak with your GM first.</p>"
            },
            "Edicts and Anathemas": {
              "name": "典范与禁忌 Edicts and Anathemas",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>典范与禁忌</h2>\n<p>《鬼季》的核心在于柳岸镇——一座由两三百人组成的乡村社区，居民的信念与性格各不相同。尽管如此，柳岸镇的主流态度明显远离残酷与其他邪恶行径，而本《冒险路径》的相当一部分也仰赖PC出于同情心而受到激励，在并无任何特定金钱奖励承诺的情况下保护同镇的乡亲。因此，鼓励邪恶行为、或不允许与你的同镇居民合作的典范与禁忌，在主题上并不太适合本《冒险路径》。不过一如既往，只要各个PC能够协力合作，并且（在本例中）希望确保他们共同家乡的繁荣与存续，那么大多数典范与禁忌都能正常运作。如果你怀疑你PC的典范与禁忌可能不太适合当个小镇英雄，请与GM一起商量！</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Edicts and Anathemas</h2>\n<p>The heart of Season of Ghosts lies in the town of Willowshore, a rural community made up of a couple hundred people with varying beliefs and personalities. That said, the primary attitude in Willowshore skews markedly away from cruelty and other evil acts, and a fair amount of this Adventure Path relies on the PCs being motivated through compassion to protect their fellow townsfolk without any particular promise of monetary rewards. As a result, edicts and anthemas that promote evil actions or don’t allow for cooperation with your fellow townsfolk aren’t a great thematic fit for this Adventure Path. As always, though, as long as the individual PCs are able to work together and (in this case) wish to ensure the prosperity and survival of their shared hometown, most edicts and anathemas will function just fine. Work with your GM if you suspect your PC’s edicts and anathemas might not be a good fit for a small-town hero!</p>"
            },
            "Character Suggestions": {
              "name": "角色建议 Character Suggestions",
              "text": "<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>角色建议</h1>\n<p>以下信息为创建与柳岸镇及神门的主题相契合的角色提供背景，并帮助你构建一个能很好融入《鬼季》整体剧情线的角色。</p>\n<h1 data-no-toc data-split-here>Character Suggestions</h1>\n<p>The following information provides context for creating characters that fit well with the themes present in the town of Willowshore and the nation of Shenmen and also helps you to build a character that will fit well in the overall storyline of Season of Ghosts.</p>"
            },
            "Horror and Consent": {
              "name": "恐怖与同意 Horror and Consent",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>恐怖与同意</h2>\n<p>鬼季是一场以恐怖为主题的战役，因此，随着这条冒险路径展开，GM与玩家应当共同合作，确保所呈现的主题适合该游戏桌。如果你对恐怖类型中常见的某些套路或主题感到不适，请在开始鬼季之前与GM及其他玩家沟通，以便达成共识，让桌上每个人都能同样享受这场战役。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>Horror and Consent</h2>\n<p>Season of Ghosts is a horror-themed campaign, and as such, the GM and players should work together to ensure that the themes presented as this Adventure Path unfolds are appropriate for the game table. If you aren’t comfortable with certain tropes or themes common to the horror genre, speak with your GM and the other players before beginning Season of Ghosts so you can arrive at a common ground where everyone at your table can enjoy the campaign equally.</p>"
            },
            "About Shenmen": {
              "name": "关于神门 About Shenmen",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>关于神门</h2>\n<p>虽然天夏的一些国家受到某些现实文化的启发，但神门主要受恐怖根源启发，这些根源取材自范围广泛的现实世界故事。它是一个虚构国家，并不意在代表除这些超自然恐怖根源之外的任何事物。在神门的历史中，它曾被龙华征服，接纳过来自花国的移民，并被络新妇夺取统治。因此，这里呈现出文化的混合；其人民在姓名与地名上也采纳了多种语言中的词语。在神门，幽灵与怪物是生活中非常真实的一部分，而其人民所采用的种种做法源自必要性，而非迷信。</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>About Shenmen</h2>\n<p>While some nations in Tian Xia are inspired by certain real-life cultures, Shenmen is primarily inspired by horror traditions taken from a wide range of real-world stories. It’s a fictional nation and isn’t meant to represent more than these traditions of supernatural horror. During Shenmen’s history, it was conquered by Lung Wa, picked up immigrants from Hwanggot, and was taken over by jorogumo. It features a mix of cultures as a result, and its people have adopted words from multiple languages for their names and places. In Shenmen, ghosts and monsters are a very real part of life, and the practices employed by its people arise from necessity, not superstition.</p>"
            },
            "In the Year 7108": {
              "name": "在 7108 年 In the Year 7108",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>在7108年</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp\" alt=\"Governor Shan-Bao Heh\" data-tooltip=\"Governor Shan-Bao Heh\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>《鬼季》开始于7108年的夏季第一天，比其他冒险之道所默认的“当前年份”早了一个多世纪。把战役安排在如此久远的过去，可能需要大量工作来修订格拉利昂各地的设定；但《鬼季》在这方面几乎不需要费什么力——柳岸镇是一处偏远的乡村地点，在预言破灭之年的最初几年里，这里基本被忽视，任其自生自灭。</p>\n<p>预言破灭之年始于7106年；那段时期，强烈风暴肆虐格拉利昂的大部分地区。柳岸镇也不例外，席卷该区域的冬季风暴是记忆中最严重的一批。如今两年过去，柳岸镇的人民对即将到来的冬季多少有些紧张。尽管7107年的冬天相对温和，但7106年的大雪、狂风与倾盆暴雨仍令人记忆犹新。</p>\n<p>龙华帝国的崩溃对柳岸镇而言并非迫在眉睫的忧虑，尽管从更宏观的区域尺度来看，这场政治动荡是塑造现代天夏的最重要事件之一。神门在龙华治下的统治于7106年结束；然而，小镇如柳岸镇在传统上一直被龙华典范所任命的总督所忽视、放任自理，这一事实在很大程度上使柳岸镇免于承受帝国崩溃带来的后果。柳岸镇很幸运：帝国指派的总督——名为和善保的人——就根源而言相对温和；甚至可以说，由于每年的税吏或其他帝国访客不再前来，这座乡村小镇迎来了更为恬静的季节。与此同时，一个崩溃帝国的混乱在更城市化的区域引发了暴力与动荡。龙华崩溃对柳岸镇造成的最大变化，是镇子被各路木材领主抛弃：他们宁可离开自己的庄园与旧伐木营地，也不愿继续满足离柳岸镇最近的大型聚居地——赭城——的需求。对柳岸镇的人民而言，这些令人不快的长期访客的离去几乎被一致视为解脱；而那些访客的庄园与旧伐木营地也被搁置不管——部分原因是担心他们随时可能回来，但更多是因为本地人相信，让这些建筑与地点被森林重新吞没，才是将龙华对柳岸镇的影响体面地送入记忆的最尊重方式。</p>\n<p>至于络新妇已经掌控神门的说法，此时仍不过是“鬼故事”或“可怕的传闻”。至今还没有络新妇造访过柳岸镇……至少，据人们所知是如此。同样，关于赭城的统治者死亡后以幽灵（特征）之身归来的消息终于传到了镇上，但并非所有人都相信这些故事。柳岸镇的人民满足于继续照旧过日子——至少暂时如此！</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>In the Year 7108</h2>\n<img src=\"modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp\" alt=\"Governor Shan-Bao Heh\" data-tooltip=\"Governor Shan-Bao Heh\" style=\"shape-outside:url('modules/pf2e-season-of-ghosts/assets/art/pzo90196-governorshanbaoheh.webp')\" class=\"float-right\" />\n<p>Season of Ghosts begins on the first day of summer in the year 7108, over a century before the current year assumed for other Adventure Paths. While playing a campaign this far in the past could result in significant work to revise the setting in various parts of Golarion, Season of Ghosts requires very little work in this regard—Willowshore is a remote rural location that, for the first several years of the Age of Lost Omens, was largely ignored and left to its own devices.</p>\n<p>The Age of Lost Omens began in 7106, a time during which powerful storms wracked much of Golarion. Willowshore was no exception, and the winter storms that blasted the region were among the worst in memory. Now, two years later, the people of Willowshore are somewhat nervous about the coming winter season. Even though the winter of 7107 was relatively mild, memories of the snow, high winds, and torrential rains of 7106 linger.</p>\n<p>The collapse of the Lung Wa Empire is a less immediate concern to Willowshore, even though on a larger regional scale, this political upheaval is one of the most important events to shape modern Tian Xia. While Shenmen’s rule under Lung Wa ended in 7106, the fact that small towns like Willowshore had traditionally been ignored and left to their own devices under governors installed by Lung Wa edicts has largely sheltered Willowshore from suffering from the ramifications of the empire’s collapse. Willowshore is fortunate that the governor assigned by the empire, a man named Heh Shan-Bao, is relatively benign as far as tradition goes, and if anything, the lack of a yearly tax collector or other imperial visitors has resulted in idyllic seasons in the rural town. Meanwhile, the mayhem of a collapsed empire has led to violence and upheaval in more urban areas. The largest change that hit Willowshore as the result of Lung Wa’s collapse was the abandonment of the town by various lumber lords, who left their estates and lumber camps rather than continue to supply the demands of the city of Sze, the closest large settlement to Willowshore. For the people of Willowshore, the loss of these unpleasant long-term visitors has been seen almost universally as a relief, and the visitors’ manors and lumber camps have been left alone, in part out of fear that they could return at any time, but mostly because locals believe letting these buildings and locations be reclaimed by the woods is the most respectful way to usher Lung Wa’s influence over Willowshore into memory.</p>\n<p>The notion that jorogumo have taken control of Shenmen remains, at this point, a “ghost story” or “scary rumor.” No jorogumo has visited Willowshore yet... at least, as far as anyone knows. Likewise, news that the ruler of Sze died and returned as a ghost has finally reached town, but not everyone believes these stories. The people of Willowshore are content to live as they always have—for now!</p>"
            },
            "What is the Season of Ghosts?": {
              "name": "什么是“鬼季”？ What is the Season of Ghosts?",
              "text": "<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>什么是鬼季？</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>在格拉利昂的哪里（以及何时）？</h1>\n  <p>《鬼季》冒险道仅发生在天夏大陆中央、闹鬼之国神门的一小片乡村地区。具体而言，本次冒险的大部分内容发生在柳岸镇及其周边；关于该城镇的更多细节自第15页起展开介绍。</p>\n  <p>更值得注意的是《鬼季》发生的时间——不同于其他冒险道，《鬼季》的事件大致跨越一年，从夏季第一天开始：纪元7108年ic（内海地区纪元4608年ar）。尤其值得一提的是，本作设定在一百年前，且仅在预言破灭之年开始后的短短数年！</p>\n</aside>\n<p>《鬼季》冒险道得名于神门的一段传统时期，发生在夏季最初的几周；在这段时间里，林地中的作祟事件、魂魄与不死的活动会显著增加。尽管这些作祟增加的原因尚不明确，但这些幽魂常会诱使人们走向死亡。</p>\n<p>在柳岸镇，每年春末最后一天都会举行一场盛大的宴会与节庆，名为“重现节”。这场庆典不仅用来庆祝春天结束，也意在欺骗人们认为会在夏季最初几周从林中现身的邪灵与鬼魂。随着节庆宴席接近尾声，小镇会重演受害者被“鬼魂”（由戴着纸面具的镇民扮演）掳走的情景。未参与这场假绑架的人则假装陷入集体恐慌；指定的哭号者会大声哀悼，其他人则演出搜寻与救援行动。镇民相信，这场闹剧会让真正的鬼魂以为聚落已经被“闹过”，并在次日鬼季开始时（也就是夏季第一天）引诱它们去寻找更“快乐”的村庄施加痛苦。</p>\n<p>命运弄人的是，今年你的PC们被选中扮演镇上被掳走的人——他们被绑走的理由已写入《鬼季》的各个背景中；因此，如果你在创建角色时未选用这些背景之一，请与GM合作，创造一个与其中所示类似的理由，解释你为何会成为节庆的“被掳者”。</p>\n<p>当你在宴席上被“掳走”后，“绑匪”会把你卷进草席里，抬到小镇外围的一处林间空地；你被要求在那里过夜。随着夏季第一道曙光到来，“被掳者”会由当年负责重现节的人“赎回”。今年这份荣誉落在乔春虎身上——他是柳岸镇磨坊工人们深受爱戴的领袖。他承诺次日清晨会把“赎金”（一批美味的早餐点心）带到林间空地给PC们享用，然后带他们返回小镇，宣布重现节大获成功。</p>\n<p>尽管夏季常常下雨，你们运气不错，在星空下度过了相对舒适的一夜。当然，在任何林地中过夜都带着一定风险，而你们都有充分时间为此做准备。你可以在被掳走时随身携带你在创建角色时确定的所有初始物品与装备。任何未随身带走的物品都会在你回到家后等着你。</p>\n<p>《鬼季》冒险道从你与其他PC在夏季第一天于林间空地醒来时开始……但你们看不到乔春虎的踪影，也不见他承诺的早餐！</p>\n<h2 data-no-toc data-split-here>What is the Season of Ghosts?</h2>\n<aside class=\"float-right\">\n  <h1 data-no-toc>Where (and When) on Golarion?</h1>\n  <p>The Season of Ghosts Adventure Path takes place exclusively in a small part of rural Shenmen, a haunted nation in the middle of the continent of Tian Xia. Specifically, the bulk of this adventure takes place in and around the town of Willowshore, which is presented in further detail beginning on page 15.</p>\n  <p>Of greater note is the time in which Season of Ghosts takes place—unlike other Adventure Paths, the events of Season of Ghosts occur roughly over the course of a year, starting on the first day of summer in the year 7108 ic (4608 ar in the Inner Sea region). Notably, it is set a hundred years in the past and only a few years after the start of the Age of Lost Omens!</p>\n</aside>\n<p>The Season of Ghosts Adventure Path is named for a traditional period in Shenmen that takes place during the first few weeks of summer, when the woodlands see an increase in hauntings, spirits, and undead. While the cause of these increased hauntings is uncertain, these ghosts often lure people to their deaths.</p>\n<p>In Willowshore, a massive feast and festival takes place on the last day of spring. Called the “Reenactment Festival,” this gala is meant not only to celebrate the end of spring, but also to trick the evil spirits and ghosts believed to come out of the woods during the first few weeks of summer. As the festival’s feast concludes, the town reenacts victims being snatched away by “ghosts” (played by townsfolk in paper masks). Those not involved in the faux abduction pretend to plunge into collective panic as designated wailers mourn loudly and others play out a search and rescue effort. The townfolk believe this farce tricks real ghosts into thinking that someone has already haunted the settlement and that it entices them into seeking happier villages to inflict misery on once the season of ghosts begins the next day (on the first day of summer).</p>\n<p>As fate would have it, your PCs are chosen this year to play the role of the town’s abductees—reasons for their abduction are built in to the various Season of Ghosts backgrounds, so if you don’t use one of these backgrounds for your character, work with the GM to create a reason similar to those presented there to explain why you’re among the festival’s abductees.</p>\n<p>Once you’re “abducted” from the feast, your captors roll you up in straw mats and carry you off into a forest clearing on the town’s outskirts, where you’re expected to stay overnight. With the first dawn of summer, the “abductees” are ransomed by whoever is in charge of that year’s Reenactment Festival. This year, that honor falls to Choe Chun-hu, the beloved leader of Willowshore’s millers. He has promised to bring the “ransom” (a selection of delicious breakfast delicacies) to the PCs in the forest clearing the next morning for them to enjoy before leading them back to town to proclaim the Reenactment Festival a grand success.</p>\n<p>While it often rains during the summer, you luck out and spend a relatively comfortable night under the stars. Of course, staying overnight in any woodland carries some risk, and you’ve all have plenty of time to prepare for it. You can bring all your starting items and gear, as determined during character creation, with you during your abduction. Any items not brought along will be waiting for you back at home.</p>\n<p>The Season of Ghosts Adventure Path begins when you and the other PCs awaken in a forest clearing on the first day of summer... but there’s no sign of Choe Chun-hu or the breakfast he promised!</p>"
            },
            "Player’s Guide": {
              "name": "玩家指南 Player’s Guide",
              "text": "<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here><span class=\"chapter\">玩家指南</span></h1>\n\n<h1 data-no-toc>如何使用本指南</h1>\n<p>欢迎来到《鬼季》冒险路径！</p>\n<p>本《玩家指南》将帮助你为一场恐怖主题的战役做好准备。战役设定在神门国的乡野地区，你的角色是家乡英雄，必须挺身而出，保护柳岸镇的人民免受险恶诅咒与各种超自然威胁的侵害，同时还要为一个可能格外残酷的冬季做准备。你将从1级角色开始；如果他们并非在柳岸镇度过一生，那么他们也在不久前来到镇上后，已被视为并欢迎为本地人。</p>\n<p>本冒险路径分为四个部分，每一部分都发生在不同的季节。随着每个月流逝，你们的PC会变得更加强大，而柳岸镇面临的威胁也会愈发致命、愈发骇人。《鬼季》包含一些尤为重大的剧情反转与真相揭示，因此如果你已经提前得知了其中一些惊喜，请在透露本冒险路径后续部分等待发现的秘密之前，先顾及其他玩家的体验！</p>\n<p>要游玩这场战役，你只需要《Pathfinder 玩家核心》和一张角色卡。在你的游戏主持人允许的情况下，你也可以使用《Pathfinder》第二版的增补规则书、战役设定书以及其他配件来进一步定制你的角色——尤其因为本战役设定在天夏大陆，在那里，最常见的祖裔、信仰与其他要素，并不与设定在内海地区的战役所默认的那些相同。</p>\n<p>在接下来的页面中，你会找到一些具体的建议，帮助你为《鬼季》创建一名新角色。本《玩家指南》分为以下几个部分。</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>角色建议：</strong>用于创建一名能与本战役无缝衔接的1级角色的指引、实用建议与具体提示。</li>\n  <li><strong>柳岸镇概览：</strong>你（以及你的角色）需要了解的关于你们家乡柳岸镇的大部分信息都收录在这份概览中。如果本节未包含你需要的信息，你的GM还掌握关于这座城镇的额外资料。</li>\n</ul>\n<h1 class=\"chapter-heading no-toc\" data-split-here><span class=\"chapter\">Player’s Guide</span></h1>\n\n<h1 data-no-toc>How to Use This Guide</h1>\n<p>Welcome to the Season of Ghosts Adventure Path!</p>\n<p>This Player’s Guide will help you prepare for a horror-themed campaign set in the rural regions of the nation of Shenmen, where your characters are hometown heroes who must rise to the occasion and defend the people of Willowshore from a sinister curse and from all manner of supernatural threats, all while also preparing for what might be a particularly cruel winter season. You’ll begin as 1st-level characters who, if they haven’t lived in Willowshore their whole lives, have come to be recognized and welcomed as locals after arriving in town in the recent past.</p>\n<p>This Adventure Path is split into four parts, each taking place during a different season. With every passing month, your PCs grow more powerful and the threats facing Willowshore grow deadlier and more shocking. Season of Ghosts features some particularly significant plot twists and revelations, so if you’ve had some of these surprises revealed to you already, please consider other players’ experiences before spoiling the secrets that await discovery during the later parts of this Adventure Path!</p>\n<p>To play in this campaign, all you need is Pathfinder Player Core and a character sheet. With your Game Master’s permission, you can also use Pathfinder Second Edition supplemental rulebooks, campaign setting books, and other accessories to further customize your character, especially since this campaign is set on the continent of Tian Xia, where the most common ancestries, faiths, and other elements aren’t the same as those assumed in a campaign set in the Inner Sea region.</p>\n<p>On the following pages, you’ll find specific suggestions to help you create a new character for Season of Ghosts. This Player’s Guide is organized into the following sections.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Character Suggestions:</strong> Guidance, practical advice, and specific tips for creating a 1st-level character that fits seamlessly into this campaign.</li>\n  <li><strong>Willowshore Gazetteer:</strong> Much of what you (and your character) need to know about your hometown of Willowshore is presented in this gazetteer. Your GM has additional information about this town, should information you need not be present in this section.</li>\n</ul>"
            }
          }
